window.__SE_ATLAS__={"papers":[{"id":"p00487","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FlowScope: Non-Intrusive Distributed Tracing with Method-Level Delay Estimation for Microservices Troubleshooting","tz":"FlowScope：面向微服务故障排查、带方法级延迟估计的非侵入式分布式追踪","a":"Microservices’ inherent complexity creates significant troubleshooting challenges, particularly in user request analysis. While nonintrusive distributed tracing addresses this by monitoring cross-service execution without code instrumentation, current frameworks still exhibit critical deficiencies: Current approaches suffer from language-dependent instrumentation that restricts multienvironment adaptability and kernel-to-user space data transfers, introducing prohibitive overhead. Furthermore, their inability to model request causality in concurrent environments frequently produces distorted traces, particularly under asynchronous execution patterns. To address these limitations, we propose DeepTrace, a non-intrusive distributed tracing framework for microservices that leverages method-level delay distribution estimation to optimize trace reconstruction. DeepTrace employs a hybrid architecture combining kernel and user-space processing: low-complexity protocol parsing is offloaded to the kernel via eBPF to minimize overhead, while user-space components handle computationally intensive protocol analysis. The framework integrates cross-correlation method delay distributions with method relationship constraints, enabling precise causal inference for trace reconstruction. This approach ensures both efficiency in data collection and accuracy in modeling request causality across concurrent execution paths. Our testbed results indicate that, compared to state-of-the-art frameworks (e.g., DeepFlow, TreaceWeaver), DeepTrace reduces collection overhead by 89% with a 51% accuracy improvement.","az":"微服务固有的复杂性带来了显著的故障排查挑战，尤其是在用户请求分析方面。非侵入式分布式追踪通过在不做代码插桩的情况下监控跨服务执行来应对这一问题，但现有框架仍存在关键缺陷：当前方法依赖与语言相关的插桩，限制了多环境适配能力，且存在内核态到用户态的数据传输，引入了难以承受的开销。此外，它们无法在并发环境中建模请求因果关系，常常产生失真的调用链，在异步执行模式下尤为明显。为解决这些局限，我们提出 DeepTrace，一个面向微服务的非侵入式分布式追踪框架，它利用方法级延迟分布估计来优化调用链重建。DeepTrace 采用内核态与用户态相结合的混合架构：低复杂度的协议解析通过 eBPF 下沉到内核以最小化开销，而计算密集的协议分析交由用户态组件处理。该框架将互相关的方法延迟分布与方法关系约束相结合，从而实现用于调用链重建的精确因果推断。这一方法同时保证了数据采集的高效性与跨并发执行路径建模请求因果关系的准确性。我们的测试床结果表明，与当前最优框架（如 DeepFlow、TraceWeaver）相比，DeepTrace 将采集开销降低了 89%，准确率提升了 51%。","tl":"用 eBPF 加方法级延迟分布做因果推断，重建并发请求调用链。","au":["gyt","Han Zhang","Zhiheng Wu","Yahui Li","Jilong Wang","Xia Yin"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["distributed tracing","microservices troubleshooting","eBPF","trace reconstruction","delay distribution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/1/x"},{"id":"p00488","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Designing Abandabot: When Does Open Source Dependency Abandonment Matter?","tz":"设计 Abandabot：开源依赖被弃维护何时才真正要紧？","a":"Despite the inevitable risk that depending on abandoned open source dependencies poses, many developers feel a lack of resources and guidance on how to deal with this. Automated detection of abandonment is feasible, but not all abandoned dependencies impact a downstream project equally.In this paper, we perform a need-finding interview study with 22 open source maintainers to explore what makes the abandonment of certain dependencies impactful to their project, as well as their information needs and design requirements for such an automated notification tool. We find four main factors, the depth of integration, the availability of alternatives, the importance of the functionality, and external environmental pressures. Using this emerging theory, we then build an LLM-based classifier to predict the impact of a dependency’s abandonment in a given context, and evaluate it with an independent user study with 124 open source maintainers. Our results show that the classifier is effective at predicting whether a dependency’s abandonment would be impactful to a project, and that theory-based explanations given by the LLM are useful to developers when making judgments about the potential impactfulness of a given dependency’s abandonment.","az":"尽管依赖已被弃维护的开源组件不可避免地带来风险，许多开发者仍感到缺乏处理这一问题的资源与指导。自动检测“弃维护”是可行的，但并非所有被弃维护的依赖对下游项目的影响都相同。在本文中，我们对 22 位开源维护者开展了一项需求发现访谈研究，以探究是什么使某些依赖的弃维护对其项目产生影响，以及他们对这类自动通知工具的信息需求与设计要求。我们发现了四个主要因素：集成的深度、替代方案的可得性、该功能的重要性，以及外部环境压力。基于这一初步理论，我们随后构建了一个基于大语言模型的分类器，用于在给定上下文中预测某个依赖被弃维护的影响，并通过一项面向 124 位开源维护者的独立用户研究对其进行评估。结果表明，该分类器能有效预测某个依赖的弃维护是否会对项目产生影响，而且 LLM 给出的基于理论的解释在开发者判断某依赖弃维护的潜在影响程度时是有用的。","tl":"从访谈提炼四因素理论，并用 LLM 分类器预测依赖弃维护的影响。","au":["Courtney Miller","Hao He","Weigen Chen","Elizabeth Lin","Chenyang Yang","Bogdan Vasilescu","Christian Kästner"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["human-study","llm-based"],"kw":["dependency abandonment","open source maintainers","need-finding interviews","LLM classifier","user study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/2/x"},{"id":"p00489","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Views on Internal and External Validity in Empirical Software Engineering: 10 Years Later and Beyond","tz":"实证软件工程中关于内部效度与外部效度的看法：十年之后与展望","a":"Ten years ago, a survey (ICSE’15) revealed an unsatisfactory picture among key players of the software engineering research community: There was dissent and confusion on how to approach empirical research. Specifically, researchers were divided on the tradeoff between internal and external validity, holding strong and often opposing opinions, which cannot be a basis for stringent scientific progress. Clearly, the field has progressed over the last decade, but did the views progress, as well, or is the community still divided and confused? Our study addresses these questions by repeating the original survey among current key players of the field. Analyzing 790 open answers learning how perspectives have changed over the past ten years, we found that, despite increased awareness of the intricacies of conducting empirical studies, not nearly enough has changed to address the wide range of opinions on what a good study is and how that can be reflected in the review process. Specifically, participants disagree on balancing internal, external, and ecological validity, and while there is consensus on the need for replication studies, the specifics of when, how, and what to replicate remain unclear. Our results suggest the need for a more sophisticated review process, incorporating clear empirical standards for various methods and fostering honest discussions on what is worth replicating.","az":"十年前，一项调查（ICSE'15）揭示了软件工程研究社区关键参与者中一幅不尽如人意的图景：在如何开展实证研究上存在异见与混乱。具体而言，研究者在内部效度与外部效度的取舍上意见分裂，各执强硬且常常对立的观点，而这无法成为严谨科学进步的基础。显然，该领域在过去十年间取得了进展，但观念是否也随之进步，抑或社区依旧分裂而混乱？我们的研究通过在当下该领域的关键参与者中重做原始调查来回答这些问题。通过分析 790 条开放式回答以了解视角在过去十年中的变化，我们发现：尽管人们对开展实证研究之复杂性的认识有所提高，但改变远远不足以解决关于“什么是好的研究”以及这如何体现在评审过程中的广泛意见分歧。具体来说，参与者在内部效度、外部效度与生态效度之间的平衡上意见不一；虽然在复现研究的必要性上存在共识，但何时复现、如何复现、复现什么仍不清楚。我们的结果表明，需要一套更精细的评审流程，纳入针对各类方法的明确实证标准，并促成关于什么值得复现的坦诚讨论。","tl":"十年后重做 ICSE'15 调查，发现效度分歧与复现困惑依旧未解。","au":["Alina Mailach","Janet Siegmund","Sven Apel","Norbert Siegmund"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["human-study","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["internal and external validity","empirical software engineering","survey replication","review process","replication studies"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/3/x","pu":"https://sws.informatik.uni-leipzig.de/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/10-years-validity.pdf"},{"id":"p00490","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evolving Trends, Patterns, and Hidden Pitfalls: Unveiling JavaScript Feature Usage in the Wild","tz":"演化趋势、使用模式与隐藏陷阱：揭示真实世界中的 JavaScript 特性使用","a":"JavaScript offers a wide range of language features, providing developers with multiple ways—known as feature alternatives—to accomplish tasks. While this flexibility is beneficial, improper usage of feature alternatives can lead to code being bug-prone and challenging to maintain. Therefore, exploring how language feature alternatives are utilized in the wild is vital to providing valuable insights for the language community. Existing research has studied individual JavaScript features; however, there is still a gap in understanding the negative patterns that arise from the improper or combined use of feature alternatives. To fill this gap, we collected 3066 open-source project versions and conducted a comprehensive empirical analysis of 12 JavaScript (and TypeScript) features with alternative implementations, revealing the language feature alternatives’ evolving trends (RQ1), usage patterns (RQ2), and code smell issues (RQ3). To support this study, we also designed DiTU, a query-based heuristic feature usage analysis method to detect feature usage from large-scale repositories. Our study revealed 12 usage patterns, with seven of them further evaluated as code smell patterns. Additionally, we introduced nine insightful metrics that provide a deeper understanding of these patterns. Our results benefit language designers, users, and tool developers in navigating the evolving landscape of JavaScript.","az":"JavaScript 提供了范围广泛的语言特性，为开发者完成任务提供了多种方式——即所谓的特性替代方案（feature alternatives）。这种灵活性虽有益处，但不当使用特性替代方案会导致代码易出错且难以维护。因此，探究语言特性替代方案在真实世界中如何被使用，对于为语言社区提供有价值的洞见至关重要。已有研究考察过单个 JavaScript 特性，但对于不当使用或组合使用特性替代方案所产生的负面模式，仍存在理解上的空白。为填补这一空白，我们收集了 3066 个开源项目版本，对 12 个具有替代实现的 JavaScript（及 TypeScript）特性进行了全面的实证分析，揭示了语言特性替代方案的演化趋势（RQ1）、使用模式（RQ2）与代码坏味问题（RQ3）。为支撑该研究，我们还设计了 \\emph{DiTU}，一种基于查询的启发式特性使用分析方法，用于从大规模仓库中检测特性使用情况。我们的研究揭示了 12 种使用模式，其中 7 种被进一步评估为代码坏味模式。此外，我们提出了 9 个富有洞见的度量指标，以更深入地理解这些模式。我们的结果有助于语言设计者、使用者和工具开发者把握 JavaScript 不断演化的格局。","tl":"首次系统刻画 JS 特性替代方案的组合误用并归纳 7 类坏味。","au":["Dawei Chen","Wuxia Jin","Hui Guo","Guanlin Qiao","Peng Di","Ting Liu"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["JavaScript language features","feature alternatives","code smells","empirical analysis","TypeScript"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/4/x"},{"id":"p00491","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Generating Energy-Efficient Code via Large-Language Models - Where are we now?","tz":"用大语言模型生成节能代码——我们现在走到哪一步了？","a":"Context . The rise of Large Language Models (LLMs) has led to their widespread adoption in development pipelines. Goal . We empirically assess the energy efficiency of Python code generated by LLMs against human-written code and code developed by a Green software expert. Method . We test 363 solutions to 9 coding problems from the EvoEval benchmark using 6 widespread LLMs with 4 prompting techniques, and comparing them to human-developed solutions. Energy consumption is measured on three different hardware platforms: a server, a PC, and a Raspberry Pi for a total of ≈881h (36.7 days). Results . Human solutions are 16% more energy-efficient on the server and 3% on the Raspberry Pi, while LLMs outperform human developers by 25% on the PC. Prompting does not consistently lead to energy savings, where the most energy-efficient prompts vary by hardware platform. The code developed by a Green software expert is consistently more energy-efficient by at least 17% to 30% against all LLMs on all hardware platforms. Conclusions . Even though LLMs exhibit relatively good code generation capabilities, no LLM-generated code was more energy-efficient than that of an experienced Green software developer, suggesting that as of today there is still a great need of human expertise for developing energy-efficient Python code.","az":"背景。大语言模型（LLM）的兴起使其在开发流水线中被广泛采用。目标。我们实证评估 LLM 生成的 Python 代码相对于人类编写的代码以及由绿色软件专家开发的代码的能效。方法。我们使用 6 个广泛使用的 LLM 配合 4 种提示技术，测试了取自 EvoEval 基准的 9 个编程问题的 363 个解法，并与人类开发的解法进行比较。能耗在三种不同的硬件平台上测量：一台服务器、一台 PC 和一块 Raspberry Pi，总计约 881 小时（36.7 天）。结果。在服务器上人类解法的能效高出 16%，在 Raspberry Pi 上高出 3%；而在 PC 上 LLM 比人类开发者高出 25%。提示并不必然带来能耗节省，最节能的提示因硬件平台而异。由绿色软件专家开发的代码在所有硬件平台上都稳定地比所有 LLM 的代码更节能，优势至少为 17% 到 30%。结论。尽管 LLM 展现出相对不错的代码生成能力，但没有任何 LLM 生成的代码比一位经验丰富的绿色软件开发者所写的更节能，这表明就目前而言，开发节能的 Python 代码仍然极其需要人类专业知识。","tl":"跨三种硬件实测 881 小时：LLM 生成代码仍不如绿色软件专家节能。","au":["Radu Apsan","Vincenzo Stoico","Michel Albonico","Rudra Dhar","Karthik Vaidhyanathan","Ivano Malavolta"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["energy efficiency","LLM code generation","prompting techniques","EvoEval","green software"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/5/x","pu":"https://www.ivanomalavolta.com/files/papers/ICSE_2026.pdf"},{"id":"p00492","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"InferLog: Accelerating LLM Inference for Online Log Parsing via ICL-oriented Prefix Caching","tz":"InferLog：通过面向 ICL 的前缀缓存加速在线日志解析的 LLM 推理","a":"Modern software systems generate massive volumes of runtime logs, necessitating efficient and accurate log parsing to enable critical downstream tasks such as anomaly detection and root cause analysis. Recently, large language models (LLMs) have achieved advanced accuracy on log parsing, but their deployment in production environments faces two major limitations: 1) the privacy risks associated with commercial LLMs, driving the adoption of locally deployment, and 2) the stringent latency and throughput requirements imposed by high-volume log streams, which existing LLM-based parsers fail to meet. Although recent efforts have reduced the number of LLM queries, they overlook the high latency of the LLM invocations, where concurrent log parsing requests can cause serve performance degradation of LLM inference system. In this study, we present InferLog, the first LLM inference optimization method for online log parsing. InferLog accelerate inference by designing 1) A prefix-aware ICL refinement policy to refine the examples and permutation of in-context learning to improve the prefix caching efficiency. 2) A rapid and task-specific configuration tuning pipeline based on meta-learning to find the optimal LLM scheduling-relate configuration for dynamic log parsing workloads. The experimental results based on Loghub-2k dataset and vLLM demonstrate that InferLog significantly outperforms existing inference optimization methods and markedly accelerates the state-of-the-art LLM-based log parser without compromising parsing accuracy.","az":"现代软件系统会产生海量的运行时日志，因而需要高效而准确的日志解析，以支撑异常检测和根因分析等关键下游任务。近来，大语言模型（LLM）在日志解析上达到了先进的准确率，但其在生产环境中的部署面临两大限制：1）商用 LLM 带来的隐私风险，推动了本地部署的采用；2）高流量日志流施加的严苛延迟与吞吐要求，现有基于 LLM 的解析器无法满足。尽管近期工作减少了 LLM 查询次数，却忽视了 LLM 调用本身的高延迟——并发的日志解析请求会严重拖累 LLM 推理系统的性能。在本研究中，我们提出 InferLog，首个面向在线日志解析的 LLM 推理优化方法。InferLog 通过以下设计加速推理：1）一种前缀感知的 ICL 精化策略，对上下文学习的示例及其排列进行精化，以提升前缀缓存效率；2）一条基于元学习的快速且任务专用的配置调优流水线，为动态日志解析负载寻找最优的 LLM 调度相关配置。基于 Loghub-2k 数据集与 vLLM 的实验结果表明，InferLog 显著优于已有的推理优化方法，并在不牺牲解析准确率的前提下明显加速了当前最优的基于 LLM 的日志解析器。","tl":"用前缀感知的 ICL 示例重排加元学习调参提升日志解析推理吞吐。","au":["Yilun Wang","Pengfei Chen","Haiyu Huang","Zilong He","Gou Tan","Chuanfu Zhang","Jingkai He","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["log parsing","LLM inference optimization","prefix caching","in-context learning","vLLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/6/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.08523"},{"id":"p00493","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Order Matters! An Empirical Study on Large Language Models' Input Order Bias in Software Fault Localization","tz":"顺序很重要！大语言模型在软件缺陷定位中输入顺序偏置的实证研究","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) show great promise in software engineering tasks like Fault Localization (FL) and Automatic Program Repair (APR). This study examines how input order and context size affect LLM performance in FL, a key step for many downstream software engineering tasks. We test different orders for methods using Kendall Tau distances, including “perfect” (where ground truths come first) and “worst” (where ground truths come last), using two benchmarks that consist of both Java and Python projects. Our results indicate a significant bias in order; Top-1 FL accuracy in Java projects drops from 57% to 20%, while in Python projects it decreases from 38% to approximately 3% when we reverse the code order. Breaking down inputs into smaller contexts helps reduce this bias, narrowing the performance gap in FL from 22% and 6% to just 1% on both benchmarks. We then investigated whether the bias in ordering was caused by data leakage by renaming the method names with more meaningful alternatives. Our findings indicated that the trend remained consistent, suggesting that the bias was not due to data leakage. We also look at ordering methods based on traditional FL techniques and metrics. Ordering using DepGraph’s ranking achieves 48% Top-1 accuracy, which is better than more straightforward ordering approaches like CallGraph_DFS. These findings underscore the importance of how we structure inputs, manage contexts, and choose ordering methods to improve LLM performance in FL and other software engineering tasks.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在缺陷定位（FL）和自动程序修复（APR）等软件工程任务中展现出巨大潜力。本研究考察输入顺序和上下文规模如何影响 LLM 在缺陷定位中的表现——缺陷定位是许多下游软件工程任务的关键一步。我们在包含 Java 与 Python 项目的两个基准上，使用 Kendall Tau 距离测试了方法的不同排列顺序，包括“最佳”（真值排在最前）和“最差”（真值排在最后）。结果表明存在显著的顺序偏置：当我们颠倒代码顺序时，Java 项目的 Top-1 缺陷定位准确率从 57% 降至 20%，Python 项目则从 38% 降至约 3%。把输入拆分成更小的上下文有助于减轻这种偏置，使两个基准上的缺陷定位性能差距分别从 22% 和 6% 缩小到仅 1%。随后我们通过把方法名重命名为更有意义的替代名称，调查顺序偏置是否由数据泄漏造成。我们的发现表明趋势保持一致，说明该偏置并非源于数据泄漏。我们还考察了基于传统缺陷定位技术与度量的排序方法。使用 DepGraph 的排名进行排序可达到 48% 的 Top-1 准确率，优于 CallGraph_DFS 等更简单的排序方式。这些发现凸显了在改进 LLM 于缺陷定位及其他软件工程任务中的表现时，如何组织输入、管理上下文和选择排序方法的重要性。","tl":"揭示 LLM 定位准确率随代码顺序剧烈波动，且非数据泄漏所致。","au":["Md Nakhla Rafi","Dong Jae Kim","Tse-Hsun (Peter) Chen","Shaowei Wang"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["fault localization","input order bias","context size","Kendall Tau","data leakage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/7/x"},{"id":"p00494","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Do Unit Proofs Work? An Empirical Study of Compositional Bounded Model Checking for Memory Safety Verification","tz":"单元证明有效吗？面向内存安全验证的组合式有界模型检验实证研究","a":"Memory safety defects pose a major threat to software reliability, enabling cyberattacks, outages, and crashes. To mitigate these risks, organizations adopt Compositional Bounded Model Checking (BMC), using unit proofs to formally verify memory safety. However, methods for creating unit proofs vary across organizations and are inconsistent within the same project, leading to errors and missed defects. In addition, unit proofing remains understudied, with no systematic development methods or empirical evaluations. This work presents the first empirical study on unit proofing for memory safety verification. We introduce a systematic method for creating unit proofs that leverages verification feedback and objective criteria. Using this approach, we develop 73 unit proofs for four embedded operating systems and evaluate their effectiveness, characteristics, cost, and generalizability. Our results show unit proofs are cost-effective, detecting 74% of recreated defects, with an additional 9% found with increased BMC bounds, and 19 new defects exposed. We also found that embedded software requires small unit proofs, which can be developed in 87 minutes and executed in 61 minutes on average. These findings provide practical guidance for engineers and empirical data to inform tooling design.","az":"内存安全缺陷严重威胁软件可靠性，可能引发网络攻击、服务中断和崩溃。为缓解这些风险，各组织采用组合式有界模型检验（BMC），用单元证明（unit proof）来形式化验证内存安全。然而，创建单元证明的方法在不同组织之间各不相同，即使在同一项目内部也不一致，从而导致错误和漏检缺陷。此外，单元证明本身仍缺乏研究，既没有系统化的开发方法，也没有实证评估。本工作首次对面向内存安全验证的单元证明开展实证研究。我们提出了一种系统化的单元证明构造方法，它利用验证反馈和客观准则。采用该方法，我们为四个嵌入式操作系统开发了 73 个单元证明，并评估了它们的有效性、特征、成本与可推广性。结果表明单元证明具有成本效益：它们检出了 74% 的复现缺陷，在增大 BMC 边界后又多发现 9%，并暴露出 19 个新缺陷。我们还发现嵌入式软件所需的单元证明规模较小，平均可在 87 分钟内开发完成、61 分钟内执行完毕。这些发现为工程师提供了实用指导，也为工具设计提供了实证数据。","tl":"首次实证评估单元证明：系统化构造方法并在嵌入式 OS 上挖出 19 个新缺陷。","au":["Paschal Amusuo","Owen Cochell","Taylor Le Lievre","Parth Vinod Patil","Aravind Machiry","James C. Davis"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["unit proofs","bounded model checking","memory safety verification","embedded operating systems","compositional verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/8/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13762"},{"id":"p00495","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Breaking Strong Encapsulation: A Comprehensive Study of Java Module Abuse","tz":"打破强封装：Java 模块滥用的全面研究","a":"As an increasing number of software systems reach sizes of hundreds of millions of lines of code, relying solely on code-level abstractions is impractical, posing profound challenges to software maintenance. Java Module Platform System (JPMS) provides architectural abstractions that enable Java engineers to control the required and provided interfaces of a module. Despite numerous advantages of enforced strong encapsulation provided by JPMS, developers still break those encapsulations to access the internal elements of a module. Such practice is referred to as Breaking the Strong Encapsulation (BSE). This behavior not only complicates the migration to newer versions (e.g., Java 9) but also threatens the integrity and safety of software projects. Since the BSE problem is still underexplored, in this work, we conduct the first empirical study to identify and characterize this widespread and impactful problem. We first collect a comprehensive dataset containing 4,079 GitHub issues and then investigate those issues from various perspectives, including symptoms, abuse sources, desired functionalities, and resolutions. Our empirical study highlights a tension in the Java module system: module developers aim to enforce strong encapsulation while module users frequently attempt to break the encapsulation. Our finding also emphasizes the need for both practitioners and researchers to develop effective strategies to mitigate these problems, offering an understanding of BSE characteristics to inform future detection and repair efforts.","az":"随着越来越多的软件系统达到数亿行代码的规模，仅依赖代码层面的抽象已不现实，这给软件维护带来了深刻挑战。Java 模块平台系统（JPMS）提供了架构层面的抽象，使 Java 工程师能够控制模块所需要和所提供的接口。尽管 JPMS 强制的强封装带来诸多好处，开发者仍会打破这些封装以访问模块内部元素。这种做法被称为打破强封装（Breaking the Strong Encapsulation, BSE）。该行为不仅使向新版本（如 Java 9）的迁移变得复杂，也威胁软件项目的完整性与安全性。由于 BSE 问题尚未被充分探索，本工作开展了首个实证研究来识别并刻画这一普遍且影响深远的问题。我们首先收集了一个包含 4,079 个 GitHub issue 的综合数据集，然后从多个视角考察这些 issue，包括症状、滥用来源、期望的功能以及解决方案。我们的实证研究凸显了 Java 模块系统中的一种张力：模块开发者力图强制实施强封装，而模块使用者却频繁试图打破封装。我们的发现还强调，实践者与研究者都需要制定有效策略来缓解这些问题，并提供了对 BSE 特征的理解，以指导未来的检测与修复工作。","tl":"首个 JPMS 强封装被突破现象的大规模 issue 实证刻画。","au":["Yirui He","Yongbo Chen","Jessy Ayala","Yecheng Zhou","Qiran Wang","Joshua Garcia"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Java Platform Module System","strong encapsulation","internal API access","empirical study","GitHub issues"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/9/x"},{"id":"p00496","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Testora: Using Natural Language Intent to Detect Behavioral Regressions","tz":"Testora：利用自然语言意图检测行为回归","a":"As software is evolving, code changes can introduce regression bugs or affect the behavior in other unintended ways. Traditional regression test generation is impractical for detecting unintended behavioral changes, because it reports all behavioral differences as potential regressions. However, most code changes are intended to change the behavior in some way, e.g., to fix a bug or to add a new feature. This paper presents Testora, an automated approach that detects regressions by comparing the intentions of a code change against behavioral differences caused by the code change. Given a pull request (PR), Testora queries an LLM to generate tests that exercise the modified code, compares the behavior of the original and modified code, and classifies any behavioral differences as intended or unintended. For the classification, we present an LLM-based technique that leverages the natural language information associated with the PR, such as the title, description, and commit messages – effectively providing a natural language oracle for regression testing. Applying Testora to PRs of complex and popular Python projects, we find 19 regression bugs and 11 PRs that, despite having another intention, coincidentally fix a bug. Out of 13 regressions reported to the developers, 10 have been confirmed and 8 have already been fixed. The costs of using Testora are acceptable for real-world deployment, with 12.3 minutes to check a PR and LLM costs of only $0.003 per PR. We envision our approach to be used before or shortly after a code change gets merged into a code base, providing a way to early on detect regressions that are not caught by traditional approaches.","az":"随着软件不断演化，代码变更可能引入回归缺陷或以其他非预期的方式改变行为。传统的回归测试生成难以用于检测非预期的行为变化，因为它会把所有行为差异都报告为潜在回归。然而，大多数代码变更本就意在以某种方式改变行为，例如修复缺陷或添加新功能。本文提出 Testora，一种自动化方法，通过将代码变更的意图与该变更引起的行为差异进行比较来检测回归。给定一个拉取请求（PR），Testora 查询 LLM 生成能够执行被修改代码的测试，比较原始代码与修改后代码的行为，并将任何行为差异分类为预期或非预期。对于分类，我们提出一种基于 LLM 的技术，利用与该 PR 关联的自然语言信息，如标题、描述和提交信息——从而有效地为回归测试提供了一个自然语言预言。我们把 Testora 应用于复杂而流行的 Python 项目的 PR，发现了 19 个回归缺陷，以及 11 个虽有其他意图却顺带修复了缺陷的 PR。在向开发者报告的 13 个回归中，10 个已被确认，8 个已被修复。使用 Testora 的成本对于真实部署是可接受的：检查一个 PR 需要 12.3 分钟，LLM 成本仅为每个 PR 0.003 美元。我们设想这一方法可在代码变更合并进代码库之前或之后不久使用，从而及早发现传统方法无法捕捉的回归。","tl":"把 PR 标题与描述当作自然语言预言，区分预期与非预期行为差异。","au":["Michael Pradel"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["behavioral regression","natural language oracle","pull request intent","LLM test generation","regression testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/10/x"},{"id":"p00497","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Comprehensive Study of Deep Learning Model Fixing Approaches","tz":"深度学习模型修复方法的全面研究","a":"Deep Learning (DL) has been widely adopted in diverse industrial domains, including autonomous driving, intelligent healthcare, and aided programming. Like traditional software, DL systems are also prone to faults, whose malfunctioning may expose users to significant risks. Consequently, numerous approaches have been proposed to address these issues. In this paper, we conduct a large-scale empirical study on 16 state-of-the-art DL model fixing approaches, spanning model-level, layer-level, and neuron-level categories, to comprehensively evaluate their performance. We assess not only their fixing effectiveness (their primary purpose) but also their impact on other critical properties, such as robustness, fairness, and backward compatibility. To ensure comprehensive and fair evaluation, we employ a diverse set of datasets, model architectures, and application domains within a uniform experimental setup for experimentation. We summarize several key findings with implications for both industry and academia. For example, model-level approaches demonstrate superior fixing effectiveness compared to others. No single approach can achieve the best fixing performance while improving accuracy and maintaining all other properties. Thus, academia should prioritize research on mitigating these side effects. These insights highlight promising directions for future exploration in this field.","az":"深度学习（DL）已在自动驾驶、智能医疗和辅助编程等多样的工业领域被广泛采用。与传统软件一样，DL 系统同样容易出现缺陷，其失灵可能让用户面临重大风险。因此，已有大量方法被提出以解决这些问题。本文对 16 种当前最先进的 DL 模型修复方法开展了大规模实证研究，涵盖模型级、层级和神经元级三类，以全面评估其性能。我们不仅评估其修复有效性（即其主要目的），还评估其对鲁棒性、公平性和向后兼容性等其他关键属性的影响。为确保全面而公平的评估，我们在统一的实验设置下采用了多样的数据集、模型架构和应用领域进行实验。我们总结了若干对产业界和学术界都有启示的关键发现。例如，模型级方法相比其他方法展现出更优的修复有效性；没有任何单一方法能在提升准确率并保持所有其他属性的同时取得最佳修复效果。因此，学术界应优先研究如何缓解这些副作用。这些洞见为该领域未来的探索指明了有前景的方向。","tl":"首次统一评测 16 种 DL 模型修复方法及其对鲁棒性公平性的副作用。","au":["Hanmo You","Zan Wang","Zishuo Dong","Luanqi Mo","Jianjun Zhao","Junjie Chen"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["DL model fixing","empirical evaluation","robustness and fairness","backward compatibility","model repair"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/11/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00498","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FORGE: An LLM-driven Framework for Large-Scale Smart Contract Vulnerability Dataset Construction","tz":"FORGE：一个用于大规模构建智能合约漏洞数据集的 LLM 驱动框架","a":"High-quality smart contract vulnerability datasets are critical for evaluating security tools and advancing smart contract security research. Two major limitations of current manual dataset construction are (1) labor-intensive and error-prone annotation processes limiting the scale, quality, and evolution of the dataset, and (2) absence of standardized classification rules results in inconsistent vulnerability categories and labeling results across different datasets. To address these limitations, we present FORGE, the first automated approach for constructing smart contract vulnerability datasets. FORGE leverages an LLM-driven pipeline to extract high-quality vulnerabilities from real-world audit reports and classify them according to the Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE), the most widely recognized classification in software security. FORGE employs a divide-and-conquer strategy to extract structured and self-contained vulnerability information from unstructured audit reports. Additionally, it uses a tree-of-thoughts technique to classify the vulnerability information into the hierarchical CWE classification. To evaluate FORGE’s effectiveness, we run FORGE on 6,454 real-world audit reports and generate a dataset comprising 81,390 solidity files and 27,497 vulnerability findings across 296 CWE categories. Manual assessment of the dataset demonstrates high extraction precision and classification consistency with human experts (precision of 95.6% and inter-rater agreement k- of 0.87). We further validate the practicality of our dataset by benchmarking 13 existing security tools on our dataset. The results reveal the significant limitations in current detection capabilities. Furthermore, by analyzing the severity-frequency distribution patterns through a unified CWE perspective in our dataset, we highlight inconsistency between the current smart contract research focus and the priorities identified from real-world vulnerabilities. This analysis also reveals key differences from traditional software security concerns, providing practical implications for improving the smart contract security ecosystem.","az":"高质量的智能合约漏洞数据集对于评估安全工具、推进智能合约安全研究至关重要。当前人工构建数据集存在两大局限：（1）标注过程耗费人力且易出错，限制了数据集的规模、质量与演进；（2）缺乏标准化的分类规则，导致不同数据集之间漏洞类别与标注结果不一致。为解决这些局限，我们提出 FORGE，首个用于构建智能合约漏洞数据集的自动化方法。FORGE 利用一条 LLM 驱动的流水线，从真实世界的审计报告中抽取高质量漏洞，并依据软件安全领域最被广泛认可的分类体系——通用弱点枚举（CWE）——对其进行分类。FORGE 采用分而治之的策略，从非结构化的审计报告中抽取结构化且自包含的漏洞信息；此外，它使用思维树（tree-of-thoughts）技术把漏洞信息归入层次化的 CWE 分类。为评估 FORGE 的有效性，我们在 6,454 份真实审计报告上运行 FORGE，生成了一个包含 81,390 个 Solidity 文件和横跨 296 个 CWE 类别的 27,497 条漏洞发现的数据集。对该数据集的人工评估表明抽取精度高、分类与人类专家高度一致（精度 95.6%，评分者间一致性 k-α 为 0.87）。我们进一步在该数据集上对 13 个现有安全工具进行基准测试，以验证数据集的实用性，结果揭示了当前检测能力的显著不足。此外，通过在统一的 CWE 视角下分析数据集中严重性—频次的分布模式，我们指出当前智能合约研究关注点与真实世界漏洞所反映的优先级之间存在不一致。该分析还揭示了与传统软件安全关切的关键差异，为改善智能合约安全生态提供了实践启示。","tl":"用 LLM 从审计报告自动抽取并按 CWE 分类，建成 2.7 万条漏洞数据集。","au":["Jiachi Chen","Yiming Shen","Jiashuo Zhang","Zihao Li","John Grundy","Zhenzhe Shao","Yanlin Wang","Jiashui Wang","Ting Chen","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["smart contract vulnerability dataset","audit reports","CWE classification","tree-of-thoughts","security tool benchmarking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/12/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.18795"},{"id":"p00499","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Back to the Basics: Rethinking Issue-Commit Linking with LLM-Assisted Retrieval","tz":"回归本源：用 LLM 辅助检索重新思考 Issue-Commit 链接恢复","a":"Issue-commit linking, which connects issues with commits that fix them, is crucial for software maintenance. Existing approaches have shown promise in automatically recovering these links. Evaluations of these techniques assess their ability to identify genuine links from plausible but false links. However, these evaluations overlook the fact that, in reality, when a repository has more commits, the presence of more plausible yet unrelated commits may interfere with the tool in differentiating the correct fix commits. To address this, we propose the Realistic Distribution Setting (RDS) and use it to construct a more realistic evaluation dataset that includes 20 open-source projects. By evaluating tools on this dataset, we observe that the performance of the state-of-the-art deep learning-based approach drops by more than half, while the traditional Information Retrieval method, VSM, outperforms it. Inspired by these observations, we propose EasyLink, which utilizes a vector database as a modern Information Retrieval technique. To address the long-standing problem of the semantic gap between issues and commits, EasyLink leverages a large language model to rerank the commits retrieved from the database. Under our evaluation, EasyLink achieves an average Precision@1 of 75.91%, improving over the state-of-the-art by over four times. Additionally, this paper provides practical guidelines for advancing research in issue-commit link recovery.","az":"Issue-commit 链接把 issue 与修复它们的提交关联起来，对软件维护至关重要。已有方法在自动恢复这些链接方面展现出前景。对这些技术的评估考察它们从看似合理但错误的候选链接中识别出真实链接的能力。然而，这些评估忽视了一个现实：当一个仓库拥有更多提交时，更多看似合理却无关的提交会干扰工具区分正确的修复提交。为解决这一点，我们提出现实分布设定（Realistic Distribution Setting, RDS），并用它构建了一个包含 20 个开源项目的更贴近现实的评测数据集。在该数据集上评测各类工具时，我们观察到当前最优的基于深度学习的方法性能下降超过一半，而传统信息检索方法 VSM 反而优于它。受这些观察启发，我们提出 \\textbf{EasyLink}，它把向量数据库用作现代信息检索技术。为解决 issue 与提交之间语义鸿沟这一长期问题，EasyLink 利用大语言模型对从数据库中检索到的提交进行重排。在我们的评测中，EasyLink 取得了平均 75.91% 的 Precision@1，比当前最优方法提升了四倍以上。此外，本文还为推进 issue-commit 链接恢复研究提供了实用指南。","tl":"提出现实分布评测设定，揭示深度学习方法失效并用向量库加 LLM 重排反超。","au":["Huihui Huang","Ratnadira Widyasari","Ting Zhang","Ivana Clairine Irsan","Jieke Shi","Han Wei Ang","Frank Liauw","Eng Lieh Ouh","Lwin Khin Shar","Hong Jin Kang","David Lo"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["issue-commit link recovery","realistic distribution setting","vector database retrieval","LLM reranking","traceability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/13/x"},{"id":"p00500","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Six Million (Suspected) Fake Stars on GitHub: A Growing Spiral of Popularity Contests, Spams, and Malware","tz":"GitHub 上六百万个（疑似）虚假 Star：人气竞赛、垃圾内容与恶意软件的螺旋上升","a":"GitHub, the de-facto platform for open-source software development, provides a set of social-media-like features to signal high-quality repositories. Among them, the star count is the most widely used popularity signal, but it is also at risk of being artificially inflated (i.e., faked), decreasing its value as a decision-making signal and posing a security risk to all GitHub users. In this paper, we present a systematic, global, and longitudinal measurement study of fake stars in GitHub. To this end, we build StarScout, a scalable tool able to detect anomalous starring behaviors across the entire GitHub metadata in the last five years. Analyzing the data collected using StarScout, we find that: (1) fake-star-related activities have rapidly surged since 2024; 2) the accounts and repositories in fake star campaigns have highly trivial activity patterns; (3) the majority of fake stars are used to promote short-lived phishing malware repositories; the remaining ones are mostly used to promote AI/LLM, blockchain, tool/application, and tutorial/demo repositories; (4) while repositories may have acquired fake stars for growth hacking, fake stars only have a promotion effect in the short term (i.e., less than two months) and become a liability in the long term. Our study has implications for platform moderators, open-source practitioners, and supply chain security researchers.","az":"GitHub 作为开源软件开发的事实标准平台，提供了一套类社交媒体的功能来标示高质量仓库。其中，star 数是被最广泛使用的人气信号，但它也面临被人为抬高（即“刷假”）的风险，这削弱了它作为决策信号的价值，并对所有 GitHub 用户构成安全风险。本文对 GitHub 上的虚假 star 开展了系统的、全球性的纵向测量研究。为此，我们构建了 StarScout，一个可扩展的工具，能够在过去五年的整个 GitHub 元数据中检测异常的加星行为。分析用 StarScout 收集的数据后我们发现：（1）与虚假 star 相关的活动自 2024 年以来迅速激增；（2）参与虚假 star 活动的账号与仓库具有高度琐碎的活动模式；（3）大多数虚假 star 被用来推广短命的钓鱼恶意软件仓库，其余的大多用于推广 AI/LLM、区块链、工具/应用和教程/演示类仓库；（4）虽然仓库可能通过获取虚假 star 来做增长黑客，但虚假 star 只在短期（即不到两个月）内有推广效果，长期来看反而成为一种负担。我们的研究对平台审核者、开源实践者和供应链安全研究者都有启示。","tl":"用 StarScout 全网测出六百万虚假 star，多数在推广钓鱼恶意仓库。","au":["Hao He","Haoqin Yang","Philipp Burckhardt","Alexandros Kapravelos","Bogdan Vasilescu","Christian Kästner"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["fake stars","GitHub popularity signals","phishing malware repositories","anomaly detection","supply chain security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/14/x"},{"id":"p00501","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Measuring the Influence of Incorrect Code on Test Generation","tz":"度量错误的被测代码对测试生成的影响","a":"It is natural to suppose that a Large Language Model is more likely to generate correct test cases when prompted with correct code under test, compared to incorrect code under test. However, the size of this effect has never been previously measured, despite its obvious importance for both practicing software engineers and researchers. To answer the question, we conducted a comprehensive empirical study on 5 open source and 6 closed source language models, with 3 widely-used benchmark data sets together with 41 repo-level real-world examples from two different real-world data sets. Our results reveal that, when compared to incorrect code under test, LLMs prompted with correct code achieve improvements in test accuracy, code coverage, and bug detection of 57%, 12%, and 24% respectively. We further show that these scientific conclusions carry over from the three benchmark data sets to the real-world code, where tests generated for incorrect code experience a 47% worse bug detection rate. Finally, we report that improvements of +18% in accuracy, +4% coverage, and +34% in bug detection can be achieved by providing natural language code descriptions. These findings have actionable conclusions. For example, the 47% reduction in real-world bug detection is a clear concern. Fortunately, it is a concern for which our findings about the added value of descriptions offer an immediately actionable remedy.","az":"人们很自然地会认为，当提示中给出正确的被测代码时，大语言模型比给出错误的被测代码时更可能生成正确的测试用例。然而，尽管这一效应对实践中的软件工程师和研究者都显然重要，其大小此前从未被度量过。为回答这一问题，我们在 5 个开源和 6 个闭源语言模型上开展了全面的实证研究，使用了 3 个被广泛使用的基准数据集，以及来自两个不同真实世界数据集的 41 个仓库级真实样例。我们的结果表明，与错误的被测代码相比，以正确代码提示 LLM 时，测试准确率、代码覆盖率和缺陷检测能力分别提升了 57%、12% 和 24%。我们进一步表明，这些科学结论可以从三个基准数据集迁移到真实世界代码上：针对错误代码生成的测试，其缺陷检测率要差 47%。最后，我们报告：通过提供自然语言的代码描述，可以获得准确率 +18%、覆盖率 +4%、缺陷检测 +34% 的提升。这些发现具有可操作的结论。例如，真实世界缺陷检测率下降 47% 显然令人担忧；所幸的是，我们关于代码描述附加价值的发现，为这一担忧提供了可立即付诸实践的补救手段。","tl":"首次量化被测代码正误对 LLM 测试生成的影响，并给出用自然语言描述补救的方案。","au":["Dong Huang","Jie M. Zhang","Mark Harman","Mingzhe Du","Heming Cui"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["test generation","incorrect code under test","LLM","bug detection","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/15/x"},{"id":"p00502","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Empirical Study of WebAssembly Usage in Node.js","tz":"Node.js 中 WebAssembly 使用情况的实证研究","a":"WebAssembly code executes within a host environment, such as JavaScript running on Node.js. Despite the increasing popularity of mixed JavaScript-WebAssembly applications, the interactions between these two languages and the effect of WebAssembly usage on the NPM ecosystem, are currently not well understood, forcing developers of program analyses and runtime engines and ecosystem tooling authors to make assumptions that may not hold in practice. Moreover, there currently is no executable dataset of WebAssembly modules that allows for studying how WebAssembly is used at runtime within Node.js packages. This paper presents the first comprehensive study of WebAssembly usage in Node.js code. The study is enabled by a novel dataset that we collect comprising 510 executable Node.js packages that exercise 217 unique WebAssembly modules. We study dependencies among packages that use WebAssembly, how JavaScript and WebAssembly interoperate, and the implications for security, efficiency and reliability in the WebAssembly-JavaScript ecosystem. The study provides several insights and future research opportunities, including: (i) a lack of maintenance of WebAssembly binaries that are ports of C/C++/Rust libraries, which motivates future work on cross-language package maintenance, (ii) a lack of testing of WebAssembly usage from JavaScript, which motivates work on targeted testing techniques; (iii) relatively little dynamism in WebAssembly usage, allowing for pragmatic assumptions in program analyses; and (iv) untapped optimization opportunities in engine caching and client-specific debloating. Beyond these insights, we envision our dataset to provide a basis for future studies, program analyses, and work on WebAssembly engine design.","az":"WebAssembly 代码在宿主环境中执行，例如运行在 Node.js 上的 JavaScript。尽管 JavaScript 与 WebAssembly 混合的应用日益流行，这两种语言之间的交互以及 WebAssembly 的使用对 NPM 生态的影响目前仍缺乏充分理解，这迫使程序分析与运行时引擎的开发者、以及生态工具的作者作出在实践中可能并不成立的假设。此外，目前也没有可执行的 WebAssembly 模块数据集，用于研究 WebAssembly 在 Node.js 包中运行时是如何被使用的。本文首次对 Node.js 代码中的 WebAssembly 使用进行了全面研究。该研究得益于我们收集的一个新数据集，它包含 510 个可执行的 Node.js 包，这些包共调用了 217 个不同的 WebAssembly 模块。我们研究了使用 WebAssembly 的包之间的依赖关系、JavaScript 与 WebAssembly 如何互操作，以及这对 WebAssembly-JavaScript 生态在安全性、效率与可靠性方面的影响。该研究提供了若干洞见与未来研究机会，包括：(i) 由 C/C++/Rust 库移植而来的 WebAssembly 二进制缺乏维护，这促使未来开展跨语言包维护的工作；(ii) 缺乏对从 JavaScript 调用 WebAssembly 的测试，这促使研究有针对性的测试技术；(iii) WebAssembly 的使用中动态性相对较少，使得程序分析可以做出务实的假设；(iv) 引擎缓存与面向特定客户端的代码瘦身存在尚未开发的优化机会。除这些洞见之外，我们也期望该数据集能为未来的研究、程序分析以及 WebAssembly 引擎设计工作提供基础。","tl":"首个 Node.js 中 WebAssembly 使用的可执行数据集与全面实证刻画。","au":["Michelle Thalakottur","Maxwell Bernstein","Daniel Lehmann","Michael Pradel","Frank Tip"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["WebAssembly","Node.js","NPM ecosystem","JavaScript interoperability","executable dataset"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/16/x"},{"id":"p00503","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Repair Ingredients Are All You Need: Improving Large Language Model-Based Program Repair via Repair Ingredients Search","tz":"修复素材才是关键：通过修复素材搜索改进基于大语言模型的程序修复","a":"Automated Program Repair (APR) that aims to automatically fix buggy programs has attracted much attention and blooms various kinds of techniques. Among these, Large Language Model-based (LLM-based) approaches have shown great promise. Recent advances demonstrate that directly leveraging LLMs (e.g., ChatGPT) without reliance on training data can achieve leading results. However, these techniques remain suboptimal in generating contextually relevant and accurate patches, as they often overlook repair ingredients crucial for practical program repair. In this paper, we propose ReinFix, a novel agent-based framework that enables LLMs to autonomously search for repair ingredients throughout both the reasoning and solution phases of bug fixing. In the reasoning phase, ReinFix integrates static analysis tools to retrieve internal ingredients, such as variable definitions, to assist the LLM in root cause analysis when it encounters difficulty understanding the context. During the solution phase, when the LLM lacks experience in fixing specific bugs, ReinFix searches for external ingredients from historical bug fixes with similar bug patterns, leveraging both the buggy code and its root cause to guide the LLM in identifying appropriate repair actions, thereby increasing the likelihood of generating correct patches. Evaluations on two popular benchmarks (Defects4J V1.2 and V2.0) demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach over SOTA baselines. Notably, ReinFix fixes 146 bugs, which is 32 more than the baselines on Defects4J V1.2. On Defects4J V2.0, ReinFix fixes 38 more bugs than the SOTA. Importantly, when evaluating on the new benchmarks that are free of data leakage risk, ReinFix also maintains the best performance.","az":"旨在自动修复有缺陷程序的自动程序修复（APR）已受到广泛关注，并催生了各类技术。其中，基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法展现出巨大潜力。近期进展表明，不依赖训练数据、直接利用 LLM（如 ChatGPT）即可取得领先结果。然而，这些技术在生成上下文相关且准确的补丁方面仍不够理想，因为它们往往忽视了对实际程序修复至关重要的修复素材。本文提出 ReinFix，一个新颖的基于智能体的框架，使 LLM 能够在缺陷修复的推理阶段和求解阶段自主搜索修复素材。在推理阶段，ReinFix 集成静态分析工具来检索内部素材（如变量定义），在 LLM 难以理解上下文时辅助其进行根因分析。在求解阶段，当 LLM 缺乏修复特定缺陷的经验时，ReinFix 会从具有相似缺陷模式的历史缺陷修复中搜索外部素材，并结合缺陷代码及其根因来引导 LLM 识别恰当的修复动作，从而提高生成正确补丁的可能性。在两个流行基准（Defects4J V1.2 与 V2.0）上的评估表明，我们的方法优于当前最先进的基线。值得注意的是，ReinFix 修复了 146 个缺陷，在 Defects4J V1.2 上比基线多修 32 个；在 Defects4J V2.0 上比 SOTA 多修 38 个。重要的是，在不存在数据泄露风险的新基准上评估时，ReinFix 同样保持了最佳性能。","tl":"让 LLM 智能体在推理与求解两阶段自主检索内外部修复素材。","au":["Jiayi Zhang","Kai Huang","Jian Zhang","Yang Liu","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["automated program repair","repair ingredients","LLM agent","static analysis","Defects4J"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/17/x"},{"id":"p00504","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Breaking Single-Tester Limits: Multi-Agent LLMs for Multi-User Feature Testing","tz":"打破单测试者的局限：用多智能体 LLM 测试多用户交互功能","a":"The growing dependence on mobile phones and their apps has made multi-user interactive features—like chat calls, live streaming, and video conferencing—indispensable for bridging the gaps in social connectivity caused by physical and situational barriers. However, automating these interactive features for testing is fraught with challenges, owing to their inherent need for timely, dynamic, and collaborative user interactions, which current automated testing methods inadequately address. Inspired by the concept of agents designed to autonomously and collaboratively tackle problems, we propose MAdroid, a novel multi-agent approach powered by the Large Language Models (LLMs) to automate the multi-user interactive task for app feature testing. Specifically, MAdroid employs two functional types of multi-agents: user agents (Operator) and supervisor agents (Coordinator and Observer). Each agent takes a specific role: the Coordinator directs the interactive task; the Operator mimics user interactions on the device; and the Observer monitors and reviews the task automation process. Our evaluation, which included 41 multi-user interactive tasks, demonstrates the effectiveness of our approach, achieving 82.9% of the tasks with 96.8% action similarity, outperforming the ablation studies and state-of-the-art baselines. Additionally, a preliminary investigation underscores MAdroid’s practicality by helping identify 11 multi-user interactive bugs during regression app testing, confirming its potential value in real-world software development contexts.","az":"人们对手机及其应用的依赖日益加深，使得聊天通话、直播、视频会议等多用户交互功能成为跨越物理与情境障碍、弥合社交连接鸿沟的必需品。然而，为测试而自动化这些交互功能困难重重，因为它们本质上需要及时、动态且协作的用户交互，而当前的自动化测试方法对此支持不足。受“智能体可自主并协作地解决问题”这一概念的启发，我们提出 MAdroid，一种由大语言模型驱动的新型多智能体方法，用于自动化多用户交互任务以进行应用功能测试。具体而言，MAdroid 使用两类功能性的多智能体：用户智能体（Operator）与监督智能体（Coordinator 与 Observer）。每个智能体承担特定角色：Coordinator 指挥交互任务；Operator 在设备上模拟用户交互；Observer 监控并复审任务自动化过程。我们的评估涵盖 41 个多用户交互任务，结果表明该方法有效，完成了 82.9% 的任务、动作相似度达 96.8%，优于消融实验与最先进的基线。此外，一项初步调查凸显了 MAdroid 的实用性：它在回归应用测试中帮助发现了 11 个多用户交互缺陷，证实了其在真实软件开发场景中的潜在价值。","tl":"用协调者-操作者-观察者多智能体自动化多设备多用户交互测试。","au":["Sidong Feng","Changhao Du","huaxiao liu","Qingnan Wang","Zhengwei Lv","Mengfei Wang","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["multi-agent testing","multi-user interactive features","Android GUI testing","LLM agents","regression testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/18/x"},{"id":"p00505","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Synthesizing Hardware-Specific Instructions for Efficient Code Generation of Simulink","tz":"为 Simulink 高效代码生成综合硬件专用指令","a":"Simulink has become a pivotal tool in embedded scenarios, offering a model-driven approach for embedded software development. Given the tight performance and resource constraints in embedded applications, it is crucial to ensure the efficiency of the code generated from Simulink models. Code generators implement various optimizations to enhance performance. However, they neglect the potential of hardware-specific instructions available in modern processors, such as saturation-type instructions, which accomplish complex operations in fewer cycles. Moreover, relying on state-of-the-art compilers to use these instructions is also not as effective as expectation, due to their complex semantics. This paper proposes AMICA, an efficient code generator for Simulink models with hardware-specific instruction synthesis. The key insight of AMICA is to leverage model semantics to effectively synthesize the appropriate instructions. AMICA first converts the model into the dataflow graph and crafts a series of optimization rules represented as dataflow subgraph with constraints related to block parameters, data types, and other critical properties. Then, AMICA iteratively matches these rules with dataflow graph to obtain the optimizable candidates. The candidate that maximizes latency reduction is chosen to update the dataflow graph. Finally, AMICA synthesizes the appropriate instructions for optimizable blocks in accordance with instruction syntax and block properties. We implemented and evaluated AMICA on benchmark Simulink models. Compared with the state-of-the-art code generators Simulink Embedded Coder and Mercury, the code generated by AMICA is 1.20 - 6.54 faster in terms of execution time across different platforms. Besides, AMICA reduces 6% - 53% assembly code size of the compiled programs, while performing similarly in terms of data segment size and BSS segment size.","az":"Simulink 已成为嵌入式场景中的关键工具，为嵌入式软件开发提供了模型驱动的方法。鉴于嵌入式应用中严格的性能与资源约束，确保由 Simulink 模型生成的代码的效率至关重要。代码生成器实现了各种优化以提升性能，但它们忽视了现代处理器中可用的硬件专用指令的潜力，例如饱和类指令——这类指令能以更少的周期完成复杂运算。此外，由于这些指令语义复杂，依赖最先进的编译器来使用它们的效果也不如预期。本文提出 AMICA，一个面向 Simulink 模型、具备硬件专用指令综合能力的高效代码生成器。AMICA 的关键洞见是利用模型语义来有效综合合适的指令。AMICA 首先将模型转换为数据流图，并设计一系列以带约束的数据流子图表示的优化规则，这些约束与模块参数、数据类型及其他关键属性有关。随后，AMICA 迭代地将这些规则与数据流图进行匹配，以获得可优化的候选；选择延迟削减最大的候选来更新数据流图。最后，AMICA 依据指令语法与模块属性，为可优化的模块综合合适的指令。我们在基准 Simulink 模型上实现并评估了 AMICA。与最先进的代码生成器 Simulink Embedded Coder 和 Mercury 相比，AMICA 生成的代码在不同平台上的执行时间快 1.20 倍至 6.54 倍；同时，AMICA 将编译后程序的汇编代码体积减少了 6% 至 53%，而在数据段与 BSS 段大小方面表现相当。","tl":"用模型语义驱动的数据流规则匹配，为 Simulink 代码综合饱和类硬件指令。","au":["Zehong Yu","Zhuo Su","Rui Wang","Yu Jiang"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Simulink code generation","hardware-specific instructions","dataflow graph optimization","embedded software","Embedded Coder"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/19/x"},{"id":"p00506","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Decades of GNU Patch and Git Cherry-Pick: Can We Do Better?","tz":"GNU patch 与 Git cherry-pick 的数十年：我们能做得更好吗？","a":"Patching is a fundamental software maintenance and evolution task enabling the (semi-)automated propagation of changes across different software versions. Established and widely used language-agnostic patchers, such as GNU patch and Git cherry-pick, work on textual artifact representations (i.e., files) and typically rely on line numbers and contexts (i.e., surrounding unchanged text) to apply changes. This strategy often fails if source and target of a patch differ: Some required changes may be rejected, others may be applied to the wrong location; provoking cumbersome manual effort. In this paper, we study the effectiveness of commonly-used patchers, and propose a novel technique that significantly increases the level of patch automation. First, we curate and analyze a large dataset of more than 400,000 patch scenarios (i.e., cherry picks) from 5,000 GitHub projects. Next, we examine the effectiveness of established patchers on the gathered patch scenarios, observing that patchers often fail to apply changes correctly. Third, we develop a novel language-agnostic patch technique, mpatch , that utilizes a source-to-target matching to determine suitable change locations. By comparing mpatch to other patchers, we find that it can correctly apply 44% more patches automatically than other language-agnostic patchers, while it also requires fewer manual fixes in cases that cannot be automated completely. Thus, mpatch considerably reduces the burden of manually fixing failed patches in practice, specifically in projects with frequent patch applications.","az":"打补丁是一项基础的软件维护与演化任务，它支持在不同软件版本之间（半）自动地传播变更。GNU patch、Git cherry-pick 等成熟且广泛使用的语言无关打补丁工具，作用于制品的文本表示（即文件），通常依赖行号和上下文（即周围未改动的文本）来应用变更。当补丁的源与目标存在差异时，这一策略常常失败：某些必需的变更可能被拒绝，另一些可能被应用到错误的位置，从而引发繁琐的人工工作。本文研究了常用打补丁工具的有效性，并提出一种显著提升补丁自动化水平的新技术。首先，我们从 5,000 个 GitHub 项目中整理并分析了一个包含超过 400,000 个打补丁场景（即 cherry-pick）的大规模数据集。其次，我们在所收集的场景上检验了成熟打补丁工具的有效性，发现它们经常无法正确应用变更。第三，我们开发了一种新的语言无关打补丁技术 mpatch，它利用源到目标的匹配来确定合适的变更位置。通过将 mpatch 与其他打补丁工具比较，我们发现它能够自动正确应用的补丁比其他语言无关工具多 44%，并且在无法完全自动化的情况下所需的人工修复也更少。因此，mpatch 在实践中显著减轻了人工修复失败补丁的负担，尤其是在频繁应用补丁的项目中。","tl":"用源到目标匹配替代行号上下文定位，自动正确打补丁率提升 44%。","au":["Alexander Schultheiß","Alexander Boll","Paul Maximilian Bittner","Sandra Greiner","Thomas Thüm","Timo Kehrer"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["patching","git cherry-pick","change propagation","language-agnostic patcher","mpatch"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/20/x","pu":"https://lanpirot.github.io/publications/Decades_of_GNU_Patch_and_Git_Cherry-Pick_Can_We_Do_Better.pdf"},{"id":"p00507","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Think Outside the Box: Automating Inter-App Functionality Testing via Memory Implanting and Reasoning","tz":"跳出单应用之框：通过记忆植入与推理自动化跨应用功能测试","a":"Inter-app functionality requires multiple apps to collaborate to complete a functional task, which has become essential in modern software ecosystems. However, due to the dynamic updates and openness of modern apps, automated GUI testing based on predefined interaction models or trained on historical data is difficult to achieve inter-app testing. The low fault tolerance and context-dependent characteristics of inter-app functionality paths, lead the LLM-based GUI testing to have UI semantic mapping ambiguity and irreversible operation generating problem. To address these challenges, this paper proposes InterDroid, an automated GUI testing approach that enhances inter-app testing by implanting structured semantic knowledge into LLM’s memory. InterDroid retrieves relevant historical inter-app interactions using a multimodal retrieval method that integrates visual and textual GUI information, significantly improving retrieval accuracy. Inspired by the research on memory implantation in cognitive psychology, we design a memory implanting mechanism: global memory presents inter-app paths in a conversational form, simulating prior testing experience, and local memory tracks real-time state transitions. Additionally, InterDroid proposes a testing monitor that dynamically tracks testing progress and detects deviations, ensuring comprehensive test execution. InterDroid is designed as an integrable module that activates upon detecting the transition of the app to another app, allowing existing automated GUI testing tools to continue seamlessly after inter-app testing is completed. We evaluate InterDroid on 100 inter-app functionalities across 63 apps, comparing it with state-of-the-art GUI testing baselines. InterDroid achieves up to 133% improvement in page coverage, 124% in action coverage, and 268% in exact match accuracy over the best baseline. Furthermore, InterDroid detects 43 new crash bugs in real-world apps from Google Play, with 31 fixed and 12 confirmed by developers, demonstrating InterDroid’s effectiveness.","az":"跨应用功能需要多个应用协作完成一项功能任务，这在现代软件生态中已变得不可或缺。然而，由于现代应用的动态更新与开放性，基于预定义交互模型或在历史数据上训练的自动化 GUI 测试难以实现跨应用测试。跨应用功能路径具有容错性低、依赖上下文的特点，导致基于 LLM 的 GUI 测试存在 UI 语义映射歧义与生成不可逆操作的问题。为应对这些挑战，本文提出 InterDroid，一种通过将结构化语义知识植入 LLM 记忆来增强跨应用测试的自动化 GUI 测试方法。InterDroid 采用融合视觉与文本 GUI 信息的多模态检索方法来检索相关的历史跨应用交互，显著提升了检索准确率。受认知心理学中记忆植入研究的启发，我们设计了一种记忆植入机制：全局记忆以对话形式呈现跨应用路径，模拟先前的测试经验；局部记忆则跟踪实时的状态转移。此外，InterDroid 提出了一个测试监控器，动态跟踪测试进度并检测偏离，确保测试执行的全面性。InterDroid 被设计为可集成模块，在检测到应用切换至另一应用时激活，使现有自动化 GUI 测试工具能够在跨应用测试完成后无缝继续。我们在 63 个应用的 100 项跨应用功能上评估 InterDroid，并与最先进的 GUI 测试基线比较。相比最佳基线，InterDroid 在页面覆盖率上最高提升 133%，动作覆盖率提升 124%，精确匹配准确率提升 268%。此外，InterDroid 在 Google Play 的真实应用中发现了 43 个新的崩溃缺陷，其中 31 个已被修复、12 个已被开发者确认，证明了 InterDroid 的有效性。","tl":"用全局/局部记忆植入与多模态检索攻克跨应用 GUI 测试。","au":["Mengzhuo Chen","Zhe Liu","Chunyang Chen","Junjie Wang","Yangguang Xue","Boyu Wu","Libin Wu","Qing Wang"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"agent-memory-context-and-retrieval","tg":["llm-based","agentic","multimodal"],"kw":["inter-app testing","GUI testing","memory implanting","multimodal retrieval","crash bugs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/21/x"},{"id":"p00508","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Predicting Failures in Smart Human-Centric EcoSystems","tz":"预测智能以人为中心生态系统中的失效","a":"Smart cities, smart grids, and in general Smart Human-centric Ecosystems (SHEs) emerge from the co-existence of many systems that operate according to independently owned specifications, and evolve over time. SHEs may fail despite the correct behavior of the systems that comprise the SHE. Fully testing SHEs on testbed to prevent failures in production is impossible, and scenarios that may lead to catastrophic SHE failures are unavoidable. In this paper we frame the core issues of SHE failures, and propose Smart human-centric Ecosystem Monitoring, SEM, an approach that predicts SHE failures to enable corrective actions for mitigating the catastrophic effects of failures. SEM identifies failure-prone scenarios from the reconstruction error of SHE indicators, that is, metric values that SEM collects from the SHE at constant frequency. SEM computes the reconstruction error with a suitably trained denoising autoencoder combined with a Transformer architecture. The results of experimenting with a peer-to-peer ride-sharing ecosystem operating in San Francisco confirm that SEM can effectively predict SHE failures early enough to activate preventing actions, and indicate the generalizability of SEM with continual learning. The main contributions of the paper are the definition and the exemplification of the impact of failures in SHEs, and an approach to detect incoming failures before otherwise inevitable disruptive effects.","az":"智慧城市、智能电网，以及一般意义上的智能以人为中心生态系统（SHE），产生于众多按照各自独立拥有的规范运行并随时间演化的系统的共存。即使构成 SHE 的各个系统行为都正确，SHE 仍可能失效。在测试床上完整测试 SHE 以防止生产环境中的失效是不可能的，可能导致灾难性 SHE 失效的场景不可避免。本文界定了 SHE 失效的核心问题，并提出 SEM（智能以人为中心生态系统监控），一种预测 SHE 失效、从而启用纠正措施以缓解失效灾难性后果的方法。SEM 通过 SHE 指标的重构误差来识别易发生失效的场景，这些指标即 SEM 以固定频率从 SHE 采集的度量值。SEM 使用经过恰当训练的去噪自编码器结合 Transformer 架构来计算重构误差。在旧金山运营的点对点拼车生态系统上的实验结果证实，SEM 能够足够早地有效预测 SHE 失效以启动预防措施，并表明结合持续学习后 SEM 具备泛化能力。本文的主要贡献是对 SHE 中失效影响的定义与实例化，以及一种在不可避免的破坏性后果发生前检测即将到来的失效的方法。","tl":"用去噪自编码器加 Transformer 的重构误差提前预测智能生态系统失效。","au":["Niccolò Puccinelli","Davide Molinelli","Noura El Moussa","Matteo Ciniselli","Mauro Pezze"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["smart human-centric ecosystems","failure prediction","denoising autoencoder","monitoring","continual learning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/22/x"},{"id":"p00509","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"\"Making Our Life Less Monotonous\" or \"Just Tick Things Off\": An Exploratory Multi-Method Study of Toil","tz":"“让生活不那么单调”还是“只是打勾了事”：一项关于 toil 的探索性多方法研究","a":"Google introduced Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) as a DevOps approach focused on service reliability. A key concept in SRE is toil defined as manual, repetitive, automatable, and reactive tasks that arise in production service management, scale with service growth, and provide no lasting value. As SRE adoption expands beyond Google, organisations adapt SRE practices and terminology, leading to inconsistencies in how toil is defined and perceived. Understanding toil is crucial, as it is assumed to directly impact both operational efficiency and well-being of engineers, ultimately influencing the reliability and scalability of production services. In this study, we examine toil in light of Google’s claim that “less toil is better\". We explore how different developers define toil, its perceived impact, and whether reducing toil is seen as beneficial. To this end, we analyse grey literature, for a broad, practical perspective of toil and its effects, and conduct semi-structured interviews at the Company to triangulate the previous findings. We observe that while Google’s toil definition has been widely adopted, it has been expanded to include additional technical attributes (e.g., routine, time-consuming, persistent) and human aspects (e.g., mundane, not just unwanted work). Practitioners generally view toil negatively, citing its impact on organisations’ growth, teams’ efficiency, and morale. However, while toil elimination is generally praised, we also observe resistance stemming from concerns over cost, complexity, and the possible negative impact this elimination can have on employees predominantly working on toil.","az":"谷歌提出了站点可靠性工程（SRE）作为一种聚焦服务可靠性的 DevOps 方法。SRE 中的一个关键概念是 toil（琐务），其定义为在生产服务管理中出现的手工、重复、可自动化且被动响应的任务，这类任务随服务增长而扩大，且不产生持久价值。随着 SRE 的采纳超出谷歌范围，各组织调整了 SRE 实践与术语，导致 toil 的定义与认知出现不一致。理解 toil 至关重要，因为人们假定它直接影响运维效率与工程师的福祉，并最终影响生产服务的可靠性与可扩展性。本研究结合谷歌“toil 越少越好”的主张来考察 toil。我们探究不同开发者如何定义 toil、其被感知的影响，以及减少 toil 是否被视为有益。为此，我们分析了灰色文献以获得关于 toil 及其影响的广泛而实用的视角，并在一家公司开展半结构化访谈以对前述发现进行三角验证。我们观察到，虽然谷歌的 toil 定义已被广泛采纳，但它被扩展为包含更多技术属性（如例行、耗时、持续存在）与人的方面（如乏味、并非只是不受欢迎的工作）。从业者普遍对 toil 持负面看法，指出其对组织成长、团队效率与士气的影响。然而，尽管消除 toil 总体上被称许，我们也观察到阻力，其根源在于对成本、复杂度，以及消除 toil 可能对主要从事此类工作的员工产生负面影响的担忧。","tl":"用灰色文献加访谈揭示 toil 定义的扩展与“消除 toil”遭遇的阻力。","au":["Tom Kafoe","Lina Ochoa","Sharath Siravuru","Alexander Serebrenik"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["human-study","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["toil","site reliability engineering","DevOps","grey literature","semi-structured interviews"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/23/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00510","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Global Matches for Third-Party Library Detection in Android","tz":"迈向全局匹配的 Android 第三方库检测","a":"The detection of third-party libraries (TPLs) is pivotal in upholding the security of Android supply chains. A significant hurdle in this domain pertains to ensuring accurate detection, particularly in the face of prevalent code obfuscation techniques. Recently, multiple research endeavors have advocated for the adoption of fuzzy library signatures to accommodate specific code features that can be affected by code obfuscation. Despite the potential promise of this approach, the use of such abstractions often results in the identification of multiple candidates that bear a striking resemblance. Unfortunately, prevailing methodologies tend to rely on local maxima of similarity matches, disregarding the broader contextual knowledge encapsulated within surrounding classes. This oversight culminates in suboptimal matching outcomes. The key observation motivating our research is that knowledge about surrounding library classes can significantly enhance matching accuracy. In this regard, we aim to establish a correspondence between sets of classes in a given app and target library—leveraging this contextual information from surrounding classes enables a transition from local matches to global matches. We implemented our idea in a TPL detection tool, called LibScope. LibScope refines obfuscation-resilient library signatures and introduces a strategic iterative process (i.e., a back-and-forth game), thereby elevating the pairwise similarity between independent classes to similarities among sets of classes. We extensively evaluated LibScope with state-of-the-art TPL detection approaches published at top venues. The comparative results on two representative public benchmarks reveal that LibScope significantly outperforms its counterparts in terms of recall, precision, and accuracy in library version detection.","az":"第三方库（TPL）检测对于维护 Android 供应链的安全至关重要。该领域的一大障碍在于确保检测的准确性，尤其是在代码混淆技术普遍存在的情况下。近期多项研究工作提倡采用模糊的库签名，以适应那些会被代码混淆影响的特定代码特征。尽管这一思路潜力可观，但使用此类抽象往往会导致识别出多个高度相似的候选。遗憾的是，现有方法往往依赖相似度匹配的局部极大值，忽略了周围类所蕴含的更广泛的上下文知识，这导致匹配结果并非最优。启发我们研究的关键观察是：关于周围库类的知识能够显著提升匹配准确性。为此，我们旨在在给定应用与目标库的类“集合”之间建立对应关系——利用来自周围类的上下文信息，使匹配从局部匹配转变为全局匹配。我们将这一想法实现于一个名为 LibScope 的 TPL 检测工具中。LibScope 改进了抗混淆的库签名，并引入了一种策略性的迭代过程（即一种来回博弈），从而将独立类之间的成对相似度提升为类集合之间的相似度。我们将 LibScope 与发表在顶级会议上的最先进 TPL 检测方法进行了广泛评估。在两个具有代表性的公开基准上的对比结果表明，LibScope 在库版本检测的召回率、精确率与准确率方面显著优于同类方法。","tl":"把类级局部相似匹配提升为类集合的全局匹配以抗混淆识别第三方库。","au":["Lige Zhan","Jiang Ming","Chenke Luo","Guojun Peng","Jianming Fu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["third-party library detection","Android","code obfuscation","library signatures","global matching"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/24/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3764541"},{"id":"p00511","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Dually Hierarchical Drift Adaptation for Online Configuration Performance Learning","tz":"面向在线配置性能学习的双重层次化漂移适应","a":"Modern configurable software systems need to learn models that correlate configuration and performance. However, when the system operates in dynamic environments, the workload variations, hardware changes, and system updates will inevitably introduce concept drifts at different levels. As such, existing offline and trans- fer learning approaches can struggle to adapt to these implicit and unpredictable changes in real-time, rendering configuration performance learning challenging. To address this, we propose DHDA, an online configuration performance learning framework designed to capture and adapt to these drifts at different levels. The key idea is that DHDA adapts to both the local and global drifts using dually hierarchical adaptation: at the upper level, we redivide the data into different divisions, within each of which the local model is retrained, to handle global drifts only when necessary. At the lower level, the local models of the divisions can detect local drifts and adapt themselves asynchronously. To balance responsiveness and efficiency, DHDA combines incremental updates with periodic full retraining to minimize redundant computation when no drifts are detected. Through evaluating eight software systems and against state-of-the-art approaches, we show that DHDA achieves considerably better accuracy and can effectively adapt to drifts with up to 2.91× improvements, while incurring reasonable overhead and is able to improve different local models in handling concept drift.","az":"现代可配置软件系统需要学习将配置与性能关联起来的模型。然而，当系统运行在动态环境中时，工作负载变化、硬件更换与系统更新不可避免地会在不同层级引入概念漂移。因此，现有的离线与迁移学习方法难以实时适应这些隐式且不可预测的变化，使配置性能学习颇具挑战。为此，我们提出 DHDA，一个旨在捕捉并适应不同层级漂移的在线配置性能学习框架。其核心思想是，DHDA 采用双重层次化适应来同时应对局部与全局漂移：在上层，我们将数据重新划分为不同的分区，并在每个分区内重训局部模型，仅在必要时处理全局漂移；在下层，各分区的局部模型可以检测局部漂移并异步地自我适应。为平衡响应性与效率，DHDA 将增量更新与周期性完整重训相结合，以在未检测到漂移时尽量减少冗余计算。通过在八个软件系统上评估并与最先进方法比较，我们表明 DHDA 取得了显著更好的准确率，能有效适应漂移，最高提升达 2.91 倍，同时开销合理，并且能够改进不同局部模型处理概念漂移的能力。","tl":"上层重划分区、下层异步自适应的双层漂移适应在线性能建模。","au":["Zezhen Xiang","Jingzhi Gong","Tao Chen"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["configuration performance learning","concept drift","online learning","hierarchical adaptation","configurable systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/25/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.08730"},{"id":"p00512","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Temporal Specification Oriented Fuzzing for Trigger-Action-Programming Smart Home Integrations","tz":"面向触发-动作编程智能家居集成的时序规约导向模糊测试","a":"The convergence of Internet of Things (IoT) and Home Automation (HA) has revolutionized human-device interaction, typically through Trigger-Action Programming paradigms such as If This Then That (IFTTT). While empowering user-customized automation, this integration introduces critical challenges: unexpected behaviors from improper rule configurations, and cybersecurity threats propagated through interconnected rule chains. Although existing research demonstrates that linear temporal logic (LTL) specifications can formally characterize these risks for model checking verification, conventional methodologies suffer from two fundamental limitations: the inherent state space explosion problem constraining efficiency, and restricted expressiveness of model patterns hindering scalability. Furthermore, the HA-IoT domain notably lacks standardized benchmark datasets for validating LTL-related methods. To address these critical gaps, we propose HAFuzz - an innovative framework that synergizes formal modeling with adaptive fuzzing techniques for efficient temporal specification violation detection. We further incorporate manually curated specifications with large language model (LLM)-driven mutation generation, enabling systematic test case augmentation. Experimental evaluations demonstrate HAFuzz achieves violation detection within 50ms per integration under typical scenarios, showing superior efficiency improvement compared with conventional model checking approaches. Comprehensive validation involving 3,343 LTL specifications confirms HAFuzz’s accuracy and effectiveness in identifying critical violations, particularly in large-scale deployments characterized by intricate rule interdependencies and specifications that feature complex temporal logic patterns.","az":"物联网（IoT）与家庭自动化（HA）的融合革新了人机设备交互，通常通过诸如 IFTTT 的触发-动作编程范式实现。这种集成在赋能用户自定义自动化的同时，也带来了关键挑战：不当的规则配置会导致意料之外的行为，网络安全威胁会沿着相互关联的规则链传播。尽管已有研究表明线性时序逻辑（LTL）规约能够形式化刻画这些风险以供模型检验验证，传统方法仍存在两个根本局限：固有的状态空间爆炸问题限制了效率，模型模式的表达能力受限阻碍了可扩展性。此外，HA-IoT 领域明显缺乏用于验证 LTL 相关方法的标准基准数据集。为填补这些关键空白，我们提出 HAFuzz——一个将形式化建模与自适应模糊测试技术协同起来、用于高效检测时序规约违规的创新框架。我们进一步将人工整理的规约与大语言模型（LLM）驱动的变异生成相结合，实现系统化的测试用例扩充。实验评估表明，在典型场景下 HAFuzz 能在每个集成 50 毫秒内完成违规检测，相比传统模型检验方法在效率上有显著提升。涵盖 3,343 条 LTL 规约的全面验证确认了 HAFuzz 在识别关键违规方面的准确性与有效性，尤其是在具有复杂规则相互依赖以及包含复杂时序逻辑模式的规约的大规模部署中。","tl":"用自适应模糊测试替代模型检验，毫秒级检出智能家居规则的 LTL 违规。","au":["Jinglin Dai","Yifan Xiong","Lezhi Ma","Shangqing Liu","Lei Bu"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","security","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["trigger-action programming","smart home","LTL specification","fuzzing","IFTTT"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/26/x"},{"id":"p00513","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FM4MC: Improving Feature Models for Microservice Chains—Towards More Efficient Configuration and Validation","tz":"FM4MC：改进微服务链的特征模型——迈向更高效的配置与验证","a":"AI-based applications deployed as microservice chains pose challenging configuration problems, as their Feature Models (FMs) quickly grow to sizes where state-of-the-art validation approaches become infeasible. We propose FM4MC, a correctness-preserving method that validates such models efficiently by (i) slicing them into Partial Feature Models (PFMs) and (ii) applying SAT solving selectively based on estimated complexity. This combination drastically reduces the number of solver calls while retaining exact results. Our evaluation on synthetic FMs, sampled to reflect realistic heavy-tail size distributions, shows that FM4MC validates large models up to 23× faster in typical scenarios, reaches speedups of more than 100×, and scales in extreme cases even to 1,000× faster than state-of-the-art techniques. These results demonstrate that FM4MC makes configuration and validation feasible for microservice-based AI applications under mission-critical time constraints, where existing approaches become impractical.","az":"以微服务链形式部署的基于 AI 的应用带来了具有挑战性的配置问题，因为其特征模型（FM）很快会增长到当前最先进的验证方法难以处理的规模。我们提出 FM4MC，一种保持正确性的方法，它通过 (i) 将模型切片为部分特征模型（PFM），以及 (ii) 基于估计的复杂度选择性地应用 SAT 求解，来高效验证此类模型。这一组合在保留精确结果的同时大幅减少了求解器调用次数。我们在合成特征模型上的评估（采样时反映了真实的重尾规模分布）表明，FM4MC 在典型场景下验证大型模型的速度最高快 23 倍，加速比可超过 100 倍，在极端情况下甚至可扩展到比最先进技术快 1,000 倍。这些结果表明，FM4MC 使得在任务关键的时间约束下，对基于微服务的 AI 应用进行配置与验证成为可行，而现有方法在此类场景中并不实用。","tl":"用特征模型切片加按复杂度选择性 SAT，把大模型验证加速至千倍。","au":["Uwe Gropengießer","Paul Wolfart","Julian Liphardt","Max Mühlhäuser"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["feature models","microservice chains","SAT solving","configuration validation","partial feature models"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/27/x"},{"id":"p00514","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"The Cost vs the Benefit of Adding an Extra Code Reviewer to Mitigate Developer Turnover through Reviewer Recommenders","tz":"通过评审者推荐器增加一名额外代码评审者以缓解开发者流失：成本与收益","a":"Developer turnover is inevitable in software projects, leading to knowledge loss, reduced productivity, and increased defects. Prior works have quantified the knowledge distribution ability of reviewer recommenders at the replacement level. However, they did not consider adding reviewers. In this work, we target pull requests containing abandoned or hoarded files, which are more prone to significant knowledge loss from developer turnover, i.e. Pull Requests with Knowledge at Risk to Turnover (PRKRs). On PRKRs, we know that the knowledge is not distributed across the team. In this study, we aim to suggest an extra reviewer for PRKRs to spread their knowledge more broadly among the developers while limiting the additional work for the development team. Our most aggressive recommender is TurnoverRec++, which adds an extra reviewer to all PRKRs. This recommender achieves an average reduction of -82% in turnover risk, however, there is a significant cost, with extra reviewers being added to an average 16.6% of all pull requests. Our simulations show a tight trade-off between reducing the number of files at risk of turnover and the extra reviews. We also show that this trade-off is non-linear, and it is possible to significantly decrease the turnover risk with relatively few extra reviews. For example, the novel recommender, FarAwareRec, reduces files at risk to turnover by -42% but only adds an extra reviewer to 1.9%. Ultimately, our results show that managers should determine which strategy best suits their situation by considering factors such as turnover rates and available budgets. Our scripts and data are available in our replication package.","az":"开发者流失在软件项目中不可避免，会导致知识流失、生产力下降与缺陷增加。已有工作在“替换”层面量化了评审者推荐器分散知识的能力，但没有考虑“增加”评审者。在本工作中，我们针对包含被遗弃或被囤积文件的拉取请求，这类请求更容易因开发者流失而造成显著的知识损失，我们称之为“知识面临流失风险的拉取请求”（PRKR）。在 PRKR 上，我们知道知识并未在团队中分散。本研究旨在为 PRKR 建议一名额外评审者，以在限制开发团队额外工作量的前提下，将其知识更广泛地扩散到开发者中。我们最激进的推荐器是 TurnoverRec++，它为所有 PRKR 都增加一名额外评审者。该推荐器使流失风险平均降低 82%，但代价显著：平均有 16.6% 的全部拉取请求被追加了额外评审者。我们的仿真表明，在减少面临流失风险的文件数量与额外评审量之间存在紧张的权衡。我们还表明这一权衡是非线性的：用相对较少的额外评审即可显著降低流失风险。例如，新提出的推荐器 FarAwareRec 将面临流失风险的文件减少了 42%，却只为 1.9% 的拉取请求增加了额外评审者。最终，我们的结果表明管理者应结合流失率与可用预算等因素，判断哪种策略最适合自身情况。我们的脚本与数据可在复现包中获取。","tl":"首次量化“增派评审者”降低知识流失风险的非线性成本收益权衡。","au":["Mohammadali Sefidi Esfahani","Fahimeh Hajari","Peter Rigby"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["reviewer recommendation","developer turnover","knowledge loss","pull requests","code review"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/28/x"},{"id":"p00515","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AgentSpec: Customizable Runtime Enforcement for Safe and Reliable LLM Agents","tz":"AgentSpec：面向安全可靠 LLM 智能体的可定制运行时强制执行","a":"Agents built on LLMs are increasingly deployed across diverse domains, automating complex decision-making and task execution. However, their autonomy introduces safety risks, including security vulnerabilities, legal violations, and unintended harmful actions. Existing mitigation methods, such as model-based safeguards and early enforcement strategies, fall short in robustness, interpretability, and adaptability. To address these challenges, we propose AgentSpec, a lightweight domain-specific language for specifying and enforcing runtime constraints on LLM agents. With AgentSpec, users define structured rules that incorporate triggers, predicates, and enforcement mechanisms, ensuring agents operate within predefined safety boundaries. We implement AgentSpec across multiple domains, including code execution, embodied agents, and autonomous driving, demonstrating its adaptability and effectiveness. Our evaluation shows that AgentSpec successfully prevents unsafe executions in over 90% of code agent cases, eliminates all hazardous actions in embodied agent tasks, and enforces 100% compliance by autonomous vehicles (AVs). Despite its strong safety guarantees, AgentSpec remains computationally lightweight, with overheads in milliseconds. By combining interpretability, modularity, and efficiency, AgentSpec provides a practical and scalable solution for enforcing LLM agent safety across diverse applications. We also automate the generation of rules using LLMs and assess their effectiveness. Our evaluation shows that the rules generated by OpenAI o1 achieve a precision of 95.56% and recall of 70.96% for embodied agents, successfully identify 87.26% of the risky code, and prevent AVs from breaking laws in 5 out of 8 scenarios.","az":"基于大语言模型构建的智能体正越来越多地部署于各类领域，自动化复杂的决策与任务执行。然而，其自主性带来了安全风险，包括安全漏洞、法律违规与意料之外的有害行为。现有的缓解方法，如基于模型的防护与早期强制执行策略，在鲁棒性、可解释性与适应性方面均有不足。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 AgentSpec，一种用于指定并强制执行 LLM 智能体运行时约束的轻量级领域专用语言。借助 AgentSpec，用户可以定义包含触发条件、谓词与强制执行机制的结构化规则，确保智能体在预定义的安全边界内运行。我们在多个领域实现了 AgentSpec，包括代码执行、具身智能体与自动驾驶，展示了其适应性与有效性。评估表明，AgentSpec 在超过 90% 的代码智能体案例中成功阻止了不安全执行，在具身智能体任务中消除了全部危险动作，并使自动驾驶车辆（AV）达成 100% 合规。尽管提供了强有力的安全保证，AgentSpec 在计算上仍然轻量，开销在毫秒级。通过结合可解释性、模块化与效率，AgentSpec 为在多样化应用中强制执行 LLM 智能体安全提供了实用且可扩展的解决方案。我们还使用 LLM 自动生成规则并评估其效果。评估显示，OpenAI o1 生成的规则在具身智能体上达到 95.56% 的精确率与 70.96% 的召回率，成功识别出 87.26% 的风险代码，并在 8 个场景中的 5 个里阻止了自动驾驶车辆违法。","tl":"用轻量 DSL 定义触发-谓词-执行规则，在运行时拦截智能体的不安全动作。","au":["Haoyu Wang","Chris Poskitt","Jun Sun"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","tg":["security","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["runtime enforcement","LLM agent safety","domain-specific language","guardrails","autonomous driving"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/29/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.18666"},{"id":"p00516","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Empirical Study on Static Application Security Testing (SAST) Tools for Python","tz":"面向 Python 的静态应用安全测试（SAST）工具实证研究","a":"Python is currently the most popular programming language and ensuring the security of Python applications has become a critical concern. Static Application Security Testing (SAST) tools have been introduced to address this need, claiming to support a wide range of Common Weakness Enumerations (CWEs). However, the ability of these tools to detect real-world vulnerabilities in Python programs has not been comprehensively evaluated. In this paper, we selected eight SAST tools from 117 existing ones based on well-designed criteria. Based on the synthetic and real-world dataset, we evaluated and compared these SAST tools from different perspectives including effectiveness and efficiency. Our results reveal significant limitations in current SAST tools: although perform well on the synthetic dataset, a single tool detects no more than 40% of the vulnerabilities in our real-world dataset. Even when aggregating the outputs of all evaluated tools, only 66.7% of the real-world vulnerabilities are identified. To further understand these shortcomings, we performed a root cause analysis of the detection results and identified useful insights for both SAST tool developers and users, focusing on tool development, evaluation, and selection.","az":"Python 目前是最流行的编程语言，确保 Python 应用的安全已成为关键议题。静态应用安全测试（SAST）工具被引入以满足这一需求，并声称支持广泛的通用缺陷枚举（CWE）。然而，这些工具在 Python 程序中检测真实世界漏洞的能力尚未得到全面评估。本文基于精心设计的标准，从现有的 117 个工具中挑选出 8 个 SAST 工具。基于合成数据集与真实世界数据集，我们从有效性与效率等不同角度对这些工具进行了评估与比较。我们的结果揭示了当前 SAST 工具的显著局限：尽管它们在合成数据集上表现良好，但在我们的真实世界数据集上，单个工具检测到的漏洞不超过 40%；即便汇总所有被评估工具的输出，也仅识别出 66.7% 的真实世界漏洞。为进一步理解这些不足，我们对检测结果进行了根因分析，并为 SAST 工具的开发者与使用者在工具开发、评估与选择方面提炼出有价值的洞见。","tl":"实测 8 款 Python SAST 工具：真实漏洞单工具检出率不足 40%。","au":["Liu Zhuohang","Zhi Wang","Haotong Liu","Wanpeng Li"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["SAST tools","Python security","CWE","empirical evaluation","real-world vulnerabilities"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/30/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00517","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CombCT: Compiler Testing via Combinatorial Testing","tz":"CombCT：通过组合测试进行编译器测试","a":"Compilers, as fundamental software, are essential for various applications, making their reliability crucial. Modern compilers like GCC and LLVM offer numerous optimizations to improve performance. Empirical studies present that most bugs occur during compiler optimization, especially with specific optimization sequences, yet little attention has been paid to this in compiler testing. The vast optimization sequence space challenges existing methods, leaving this important research direction in its early stages and in need of effective solutions. In this work, we propose a novel and effective compiler testing approach dubbed CombCT, aimed at boosting compiler testing. CombCT is the first approach that leverages the power of combinatorial testing for compiler testing, making it be capable of effectively exploring optimization sequences. Besides, CombCT incorporates three new techniques, i.e., dynamic optimization sequence adaption, partial sequence selection, and diversity augmentation, to enhance its effectiveness. Extensive experiments on various versions of GCC and LLVM demonstrate that CombCT detects much more unique bugs, which are caused by certain optimization sequences, than current state-of-the-art methods, indicating its superiority. Moreover, CombCT has disclosed 14 previously unknown bugs in the latest versions of GCC and LLVM, 13 of which have been confirmed or fixed, showing its practical value.","az":"编译器作为基础软件，对各类应用至关重要，因此其可靠性极为关键。GCC 与 LLVM 等现代编译器提供了大量优化以提升性能。实证研究表明，大多数缺陷发生在编译器优化期间，尤其与特定的优化序列有关，然而编译器测试对此鲜有关注。庞大的优化序列空间对现有方法构成挑战，使这一重要研究方向仍处于早期阶段，亟需有效的解决方案。在本工作中，我们提出一种新颖且有效的编译器测试方法 CombCT，旨在提升编译器测试效果。CombCT 是首个将组合测试的威力用于编译器测试的方法，使其能够有效探索优化序列。此外，CombCT 融合了三项新技术，即动态优化序列适配、部分序列选择与多样性增强，以增强其有效性。在 GCC 与 LLVM 多个版本上的大量实验表明，CombCT 检测到的由特定优化序列引发的唯一缺陷远多于当前最先进的方法，显示了其优越性。此外，CombCT 在最新版本的 GCC 与 LLVM 中披露了 14 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 13 个已被确认或修复，体现了其实用价值。","tl":"首次用组合测试系统探索编译器优化序列空间以挖掘缺陷。","au":["Chuan Luo","Shaoke Cui","Jiahao Yan","Junjie Chen","Chenyao Suo","Wei Wu","Chanjuan Liu","Chunming Hu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["compiler testing","combinatorial testing","optimization sequences","GCC","LLVM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/31/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/31/CombCT-Compiler-Testing-via-Combinatorial-Testing"},{"id":"p00518","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RealityCraft: Automated Synthesis of Extended Reality Device Interaction Scripts from Natural Language Instructions","tz":"RealityCraft：从自然语言指令自动合成扩展现实设备交互脚本","a":"Extended Reality (XR) technologies have emerged as transformative tools across diverse domains, resulting in a rapidly growing market expected to exceed $200 billion by 2025. Despite this growth, the increasing complexity of XR software systems poses significant challenges for reliability and usability, particularly in automated testing and interaction processes. Unlike traditional software, XR applications operate in three-dimensional space with multi-modal inputs, making it difficult to translate natural language instructions into executable system commands. This paper addresses this fundamental challenge by introducing RealityScript, a novel domain-specific language designed specifically for XR applications that captures the unique spatial, temporal, and interactive characteristics of extended reality environments. We also present RealityCraft, an innovative approach that leverages large language models to analyze complex natural language instructions and translate them into executable RealityScript code through a process of semantic decomposition, rule-based parsing, and verification. Our evaluation demonstrates that this approach significantly outperforms existing methods in translating natural language instructions for XR applications, providing a robust foundation for automated testing and interaction in spatial computing environments. This work represents an important step toward enhancing the reliability and usability of XR software through improved automation of testing processes.","az":"扩展现实（XR）技术已成为各领域的变革性工具，带来了快速增长的市场，预计到 2025 年将超过 2000 亿美元。尽管增长迅速，XR 软件系统日益增加的复杂性对可靠性与可用性构成了重大挑战，尤其是在自动化测试与交互过程中。与传统软件不同，XR 应用在三维空间中运行并接受多模态输入，这使得将自然语言指令翻译为可执行的系统命令变得困难。本文通过引入 RealityScript 来应对这一根本挑战，这是一种专为 XR 应用设计的新型领域专用语言，能够刻画扩展现实环境独有的空间、时间与交互特性。我们还提出 RealityCraft，一种创新方法，它利用大语言模型分析复杂的自然语言指令，并通过语义分解、基于规则的解析与验证的流程，将其翻译为可执行的 RealityScript 代码。我们的评估表明，该方法在为 XR 应用翻译自然语言指令方面显著优于现有方法，为空间计算环境中的自动化测试与交互提供了稳健的基础。这项工作代表着通过改进测试过程自动化来提升 XR 软件可靠性与可用性的重要一步。","tl":"提出 XR 专用 DSL 并用 LLM 把自然语言指令译为可执行脚本。","au":["Shuqing Li","Yun Peng","Yige Chen","Dingyuan Xue","Yepang Liu","Michael Lyu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["extended reality","domain-specific language","natural language to script","LLM","XR testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/32/x"},{"id":"p00519","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Think Like Human Developers: Harnessing Community Knowledge for Structured Code Reasoning","tz":"像人类开发者那样思考：利用社区知识实现结构化代码推理","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have significantly advanced automated code generation, yet they struggle with complex coding tasks requiring multi-step logical reasoning. High-quality reasoning data is crucial for improving LLMs’ reasoning capabilities, but such datasets remain scarce. Existing approaches either rely on computationally expensive reinforcement learning (RL) or error-prone reasoning chains synthesized by LLMs, posing challenges in scalability and accuracy. To address this challenge, we propose SVRC (Structured and Validated Reasoning Chains for Code Generation), a novel framework that mines, restructures, and enriches reasoning chains from community-driven discussions on software engineering platforms. SVRC refines unstructured and incomplete discussions of coding problems by aligning them with Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) principles, ensuring that reasoning chains capture real-world problem-solving strategies and support iterative refinement. To evaluate the effectiveness of SVRC, we introduce CodeThinker, an LLM fine-tuned on 12,444 reasoning-augmented samples generated by SVRC. Experiments on LiveCodeBench show that CodeThinker surpasses its base model by 42.86% on medium-level code problems in terms of pass@1 and outperforms GPT-4o-mini and GPT-4o by 73.14% and 115.86%, respectively. Our ablation study further highlights that each component of SVRC contributes to the reasoning capabilities of CodeThinker.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）显著推进了自动代码生成，但在需要多步逻辑推理的复杂编码任务上仍有困难。高质量的推理数据对提升 LLM 的推理能力至关重要，但此类数据集依然稀缺。现有方法要么依赖计算昂贵的强化学习（RL），要么依赖由 LLM 合成、易出错的推理链，在可扩展性与准确性方面存在挑战。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 SVRC（面向代码生成的结构化且经验证的推理链），一个从软件工程平台上社区驱动的讨论中挖掘、重构并丰富推理链的新框架。SVRC 通过将编码问题的非结构化、不完整讨论与软件开发生命周期（SDLC）原则对齐来加以提炼，确保推理链捕捉真实世界的问题求解策略并支持迭代精化。为评估 SVRC 的有效性，我们引入 CodeThinker，一个在 SVRC 生成的 12,444 个推理增强样本上微调的 LLM。在 LiveCodeBench 上的实验表明，CodeThinker 在中等难度代码问题的 pass@1 上超过其基座模型 42.86%，并分别比 GPT-4o-mini 与 GPT-4o 高出 73.14% 与 115.86%。我们的消融实验进一步表明，SVRC 的每个组件都对 CodeThinker 的推理能力有所贡献。","tl":"从社区讨论按 SDLC 原则重构出经验证推理链作为微调数据。","au":["Chengran Yang","Zhensu Sun","Hong Jin Kang","Jieke Shi","David Lo"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["reasoning chains","community knowledge","fine-tuning","code generation","LiveCodeBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/33/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00520","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fuzzing JavaScript Engines by Fusing JavaScript and WebAssembly","tz":"通过融合 JavaScript 与 WebAssembly 对 JavaScript 引擎进行模糊测试","a":"JavaScript engines are a fundamental part of modern browsers, and many efforts have been invested in testing them to enhance their security. However, the incorporation of WebAssembly into JavaScript engines introduces new attack surfaces that have not received sufficient attention. Existing fuzzers for JavaScript engines primarily focus on JavaScript, neglecting WebAssembly code and its interactions with JavaScript. We introduce Mad-Eye, the first fuzzer that can test the JavaScript-WebAssembly interaction using a novel cross-language code fusion technique. Evaluations of Mad-Eye on V8, SpiderMonkey, and JavaScriptCore detected 21 previously unknown vulnerabilities, with 18 confirmed and 13 fixed and merged into mainstream browsers, who acknowledged our reports with vulnerability bounties.","az":"JavaScript 引擎是现代浏览器的基础组成部分，人们已投入大量精力对其进行测试以增强其安全性。然而，将 WebAssembly 纳入 JavaScript 引擎带来了尚未获得足够关注的新攻击面。现有的 JavaScript 引擎模糊测试器主要聚焦于 JavaScript，忽视了 WebAssembly 代码及其与 JavaScript 的交互。我们提出 Mad-Eye，首个能够通过新颖的跨语言代码融合技术测试 JavaScript 与 WebAssembly 交互的模糊测试器。在 V8、SpiderMonkey 与 JavaScriptCore 上对 Mad-Eye 的评估检测出 21 个此前未知的漏洞，其中 18 个已确认、13 个已修复并合入主流浏览器，相关厂商以漏洞赏金确认了我们的报告。","tl":"用跨语言代码融合首次针对 JS-Wasm 交互面做引擎模糊测试。","au":["Jiayi Lin","Changhua Luo","Mingxue Zhang","Lanteng Lin","Penghui Li","Chenxiong Qian"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["JavaScript engine fuzzing","WebAssembly","cross-language code fusion","browser vulnerabilities","V8"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/34/x"},{"id":"p00521","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PromiseTune: Unveiling Causally Promising and Explainable Configuration Tuning","tz":"PromiseTune：揭示因果上有希望且可解释的配置调优","a":"The high configurability of modern software systems has made configuration tuning a crucial step for assuring system performance, e.g., latency or throughput. However, given the expensive measurements, large configuration space, and rugged configuration landscape, existing tuners suffer ineffectiveness due to the difficult balance of budget utilization between exploring uncertain regions (for escaping from local optima) and exploiting guidance of known good configurations (for fast convergence). The root cause is that we lack knowledge of where the promising regions lay, which also causes challenges in the explainability of the results. In this paper, we propose PromiseTune that tunes configuration guided by causally purified rules. PromiseTune is unique in the sense that we learn rules, which reflect certain regions in the configuration landscape, and purify them with causal inference. The remaining rules serve as approximated reflections of the promising regions, bounding the tuning to emphasize these places in the landscape. This, as we demonstrate, can effectively mitigate the impact of the exploration and exploitation trade-off. Those purified regions can then be paired with the measured configurations to provide spatial explainability at the landscape level. We evaluate PromiseTune against 10 state-of-the-art tuners on 12 systems and varying budgets, revealing that it performs significantly better than the others on 86% cases while providing richer information to explain the hidden system characteristics.","az":"现代软件系统的高度可配置性，使配置调优成为保障系统性能（例如延迟或吞吐量）的关键步骤。然而，由于测量代价高昂、配置空间庞大且配置景观崎岖，现有调优器在预算利用上难以平衡：既要探索不确定区域（以逃离局部最优），又要利用已知优良配置的指引（以快速收敛），因而效果不佳。其根本原因在于我们缺乏关于“有希望区域”在何处的知识，这也给结果的可解释性带来挑战。本文提出 PromiseTune，一种由经因果提纯的规则引导的配置调优方法。PromiseTune 的独特之处在于，我们学习能够反映配置景观中特定区域的规则，并用因果推断对其进行提纯。剩余的规则可作为有希望区域的近似映射，将调优约束到景观中的这些位置。正如我们所展示的，这能有效缓解探索与利用权衡的影响。随后，这些被提纯的区域可与已测量的配置配对，从而在景观层面提供空间上的可解释性。我们在 12 个系统与不同预算下将 PromiseTune 与 10 个最先进的调优器进行比较，结果表明它在 86% 的情形下显著优于其他方法，同时提供了更丰富的信息来解释系统的隐藏特性。","tl":"用因果提纯的规则圈定“有希望区域”，兼顾调优效果与可解释性。","au":["Pengzhou Chen","Tao Chen"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["configuration tuning","causal inference","rule learning","explainability","configurable systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/35/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.05995"},{"id":"p00522","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM Test Generation via Iterative Hybrid Program Analysis","tz":"通过迭代式混合程序分析实现 LLM 测试生成","a":"Automating unit test generation remains a significant challenge, particularly for complex methods in real-world projects. While Large Language Models (LLMs) have made strides in code generation, they struggle to achieve high branch coverage due to their limited ability to reason about intricate control flow structures. To address this limitation, we introduce Panta, a technique that emulates the iterative process human developers follow when analyzing code and constructing test cases. Panta integrates static control flow analysis and dynamic code coverage analysis to systematically guide LLMs in identifying uncovered execution paths and generating better test cases. By incorporating an iterative feedback-driven mechanism, our technique continuously refines test generation based on static and dynamic path coverage insights, ensuring more comprehensive and effective testing. Our empirical evaluation, conducted on classes with high cyclomatic complexity from open-source projects, demonstrates that Panta achieves 26% higher line coverage and 23% higher branch coverage compared to the state-of-the-art.","az":"自动化单元测试生成仍是一项重大挑战，对真实项目中的复杂方法尤其如此。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在代码生成方面取得进展，但由于其对复杂控制流结构的推理能力有限，难以达到高分支覆盖率。为克服这一局限，我们提出 Panta，一种模拟人类开发者在分析代码与构造测试用例时所遵循的迭代过程的技术。Panta 将静态控制流分析与动态代码覆盖分析相结合，系统性地引导 LLM 识别未覆盖的执行路径并生成更好的测试用例。通过引入迭代式的反馈驱动机制，我们的技术基于静态与动态路径覆盖的洞见持续精化测试生成，确保更全面有效的测试。我们在开源项目中圈复杂度较高的类上开展的实证评估表明，与最先进方法相比，Panta 的行覆盖率提升 26%，分支覆盖率提升 23%。","tl":"用静动态路径覆盖反馈迭代引导 LLM 补齐未覆盖分支。","au":["Sijia Gu","Noor Nashid","Ali Mesbah"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unit test generation","hybrid program analysis","branch coverage","LLM","control flow analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/36/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/36/LLM-Test-Generation-via-Iterative-Hybrid-Program-Analysis"},{"id":"p00523","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Quantifying Memorization Advantage in Code LLMs","tz":"量化代码大模型中的记忆优势","a":"The lack of transparency regarding the code datasets used during LLM training creates substantial challenges in detecting, evaluating, and mitigating data leakage. This paper applies a perturbation-based approach to quantify the “membership advantage” of LLMs across various coding tasks by measuring the performance gap between a model’s handling of data it has likely encountered during training versus novel inputs. Our comprehensive analysis examines 8 open-source code LLMs, including StarCoder and QwenCoder, across 19 benchmark datasets spanning four distinct categories: standard code generation, code understanding, security vulnerability detection, and bug identification. The results reveal significant variations in the sensitivity patterns, with models like StarCoder exhibiting substantially higher sensitivity scores on certain benchmarks compared to models like QwenCoder, suggesting fundamental differences in their generalization process and their learned knowledge. Interestingly, our analysis of the widely-used CVEFixes and Defects4J benchmarks, frequently suspected of data leakage in the research community, reveals unexpectedly low membership advantage scores across all models. This finding challenges prevailing concerns about this dataset’s validity for evaluating code LLMs and suggests that models may be effectively generalizing from this data rather than merely memorizing it. Other findings provide critical insights into the generalization capabilities of code LLMs and emphasize the need for more robust evaluation frameworks when evaluating model performance, particularly in domains and tasks, such as security-related ones, where data leakage may significantly lead to a false sense of reliability.","az":"LLM 训练所用代码数据集缺乏透明性，给检测、评估与缓解数据泄露带来了巨大挑战。本文采用基于扰动的方法，通过度量模型在处理其训练中很可能见过的数据与处理全新输入之间的性能差距，来量化 LLM 在各类编码任务上的“成员优势”。我们的全面分析考察了 8 个开源代码 LLM（包括 StarCoder 与 QwenCoder），覆盖 19 个基准数据集，涉及四个不同类别：标准代码生成、代码理解、安全漏洞检测与缺陷识别。结果显示敏感度模式存在显著差异：在某些基准上，StarCoder 等模型的敏感度得分明显高于 QwenCoder 等模型，提示它们在泛化过程与所学知识上存在本质差别。有趣的是，我们对被研究社区频繁怀疑存在数据泄露的常用基准 CVEFixes 与 Defects4J 的分析表明，所有模型上的成员优势得分都出乎意料地低。这一发现挑战了当前关于该数据集用于评估代码 LLM 的有效性的普遍担忧，并提示模型可能确实是在从这些数据中有效泛化，而非仅仅记忆。其他发现则为代码 LLM 的泛化能力提供了关键洞见，并强调在评估模型性能时需要更稳健的评测框架，尤其是在安全相关等数据泄露可能严重造成可靠性假象的领域与任务中。","tl":"用扰动法量化成员优势，发现 CVEFixes/Defects4J 泄露担忧被高估。","au":["Alberick Euraste Djire","Abdoul Kader Kaboré","Jordan Samhi","Earl T. Barr","Jacques Klein","Tegawendé F. Bissyandé"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["memorization","membership advantage","data leakage","code LLMs","benchmark validity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/37/x"},{"id":"p00524","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PyXray: Practical Cross-Language Call Graph Construction through Object Layout Analysis","tz":"PyXray：通过对象布局分析实现实用的跨语言调用图构建","a":"A great number of software packages combine code in high-level languages, such as Python, with binary extensions compiled from low-level languages such as C, C++ or Rust to either boost efficiency or enable specific functionalities. In this context, high-level function calls can trigger native (binary) code execution. This setup introduces challenges for call graph generation. Accurate call graphs are essential for various applications, including vulnerability management and software maintenance, as they help track execution paths, assess security risks, and identify unused or redundant code. This work tackles the problem of cross-language call graph construction in Python. Instead of relying on static analysis, which struggles with identifying Python-native interactions, we propose a dynamic analysis technique which does not require inputs to execute code. Our approach is based on two key insights: (1) when a binary extension is imported from Python code, all its objects (e.g., functions) are loaded into memory, and (2) the layout of callable Python objects contains pointers to the native functions they invoke. By analyzing these memory layouts for every loaded object, we identify corresponding graph edges, which link Python functions to the native functions they eventually invoke. This is an essential element for constructing call graphs across language boundaries. We implement this approach in PyXray, a tool that efficiently analyzes massive Python packages such as NumPy and PyTorch in minutes, while significantly outpeforming existing static analysis methods in terms of precision and recall. PyXray enables two key applications: (1) cross-language vulnerability management, by identifying whether a Python package potentially calls a vulnerable native function and (2) cross-language bloat analysis, by quantifying unnecessary code across Python and native components.","az":"大量软件包将 Python 等高级语言的代码与由 C、C++ 或 Rust 等低级语言编译而来的二进制扩展相结合，以提升效率或实现特定功能。在这种情形下，高级语言的函数调用可以触发原生（二进制）代码的执行。这一结构给调用图生成带来了挑战。准确的调用图对各类应用至关重要，包括漏洞管理与软件维护，因为它们有助于追踪执行路径、评估安全风险并识别未使用或冗余的代码。本工作处理 Python 中跨语言调用图构建的问题。我们不依赖难以识别 Python 与原生交互的静态分析，而是提出一种无需输入即可执行代码的动态分析技术。我们的方法基于两个关键洞见：(1) 当从 Python 代码中导入一个二进制扩展时，它的所有对象（例如函数）都会被加载到内存中；(2) 可调用 Python 对象的布局中包含指向其所调用原生函数的指针。通过分析每个已加载对象的内存布局，我们识别出相应的图边，将 Python 函数与其最终调用的原生函数连接起来。这是构建跨越语言边界的调用图的关键要素。我们在 PyXray 工具中实现了该方法，它能够在数分钟内高效分析 NumPy、PyTorch 等大规模 Python 包，并在精确率与召回率上显著优于现有的静态分析方法。PyXray 支持两个关键应用：(1) 跨语言漏洞管理，判断某个 Python 包是否可能调用存在漏洞的原生函数；(2) 跨语言膨胀分析，量化 Python 与原生组件中不必要的代码。","tl":"靠内存中可调用对象布局的函数指针动态还原 Python-原生调用边。","au":["Georgios Alexopoulos","Thodoris Sotiropoulos","Georgios Gousios","Zhendong Su","Dimitris Mitropoulos"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["cross-language call graph","Python native extensions","object layout analysis","dynamic analysis","code bloat"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/38/x","pu":"https://grgalex.gr/assets/pdf/pyxray_icse26.pdf"},{"id":"p00525","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"The Hidden Cost of Readability: How Code Formatting Silently Consumes Your LLM Budget","tz":"可读性的隐性代价：代码格式化如何悄悄消耗你的 LLM 预算","a":"Source code is usually formatted with elements like indentation and newlines to improve readability for human developers. However, these visual aids do not seem to be beneficial for large language models (LLMs) in the same way since the code is processed as a linear sequence of tokens. Furthermore, these additional tokens can lead to increased computational costs and longer response times for LLMs. If such formatting elements are non-essential to LLMs, we can reduce such costs by removing them from the code. To figure out the role played by formatting elements, we conduct a comprehensive empirical study to evaluate the impact of code formatting on LLM performance and efficiency. Through large-scale experiments on Fill-in-the-Middle Code Completion tasks across four programming languages (Java, Python, C++, C#) and ten LLMs—including both commercial and open-source models—we systematically analyze token count and performance when formatting elements are removed. Key findings indicate that LLMs can maintain performance across formatted code and unformatted code, achieving an average input token reduction of 24.5% with negligible output token reductions. This makes code format removal a practical optimization strategy for improving LLM efficiency. Further exploration reveals that both prompting and fine-tuning LLMs can lead to significant reductions (up to 36.1%) in output code length without compromising correctness. To facilitate practical applications, we develop a bidirectional code transformation tool for format processing, which can be seamlessly integrated into existing LLM inference workflows, ensuring both human readability and LLM efficiency.","az":"源代码通常会用缩进、换行等元素进行格式化，以提升人类开发者的可读性。然而，这些视觉辅助对大语言模型（LLM）似乎并无同样的益处，因为代码是作为线性的 token 序列被处理的。此外，这些额外的 token 会导致 LLM 计算成本上升、响应时间变长。如果这类格式化元素对 LLM 而言并非必需，我们就可以通过将其从代码中移除来降低成本。为弄清格式化元素所起的作用，我们开展了一项全面的实证研究，以评估代码格式化对 LLM 性能与效率的影响。通过在四种编程语言（Java、Python、C++、C#）与十个 LLM（包括商业与开源模型）上进行的大规模“中间填充（Fill-in-the-Middle）代码补全”实验，我们系统分析了移除格式化元素后的 token 数量与性能。关键发现表明，LLM 在格式化代码与未格式化代码上都能保持性能，平均输入 token 减少 24.5%，而输出 token 的减少可忽略不计。这使得移除代码格式成为提升 LLM 效率的实用优化策略。进一步探索发现，对 LLM 进行提示与微调都能在不损害正确性的前提下显著减少输出代码长度（最高达 36.1%）。为便于实际应用，我们开发了一个用于格式处理的双向代码转换工具，它可无缝集成到现有的 LLM 推理流程中，同时保证人类可读性与 LLM 效率。","tl":"去掉缩进换行可省 24.5% 输入 token 而性能不降，并给出双向转换工具。","au":["Dangfeng Pan","Zhensu Sun","Cenyuan Zhang","David Lo","Xiaoning Du"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code formatting","token efficiency","fill-in-the-middle","code completion","LLM cost"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/39/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00526","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SeRe: A Security-Related Code Review Dataset Aligned with Real-World Review Activities","tz":"SeRe：一个与真实评审活动对齐的安全相关代码评审数据集","a":"Software security vulnerabilities can lead to severe consequences, making early detection essential. Although code review serves as a critical defense mechanism against security flaws, relevant feedback remains scarce due to limited attention to security issues or a lack of expertise among reviewers. Existing datasets and studies primarily focus on general-purpose code review comments, either lacking security-specific annotations or being too limited in scale to support large-scale research. To bridge this gap, we introduce SeRe, a security-related code review dataset, constructed using an active learning-based ensemble classification approach. The proposed approach iteratively refines model predictions through human annotations, achieving high precision while maintaining reasonable recall. Using the fine-tuned ensemble classifier, we extracted 6,732 security-related reviews from 373,824 raw review instances, ensuring representativeness across multiple programming languages. Statistical analysis indicates that SeRe generally aligns with real-world security-related review distribution. To assess both the utility of SeRe and the effectiveness of existing code review comment generation approaches, we benchmark state-of-the-art approaches on security-related feedback generation. By releasing SeRe along with our benchmark results, we aim to advance research in automated security-focused code review and contribute to the development of more effective secure software engineering practices.","az":"软件安全漏洞可能导致严重后果，因此尽早检测至关重要。尽管代码评审是抵御安全缺陷的关键防线，但由于评审者对安全问题关注不足或缺乏相关专业知识，与安全相关的评审反馈仍然稀缺。已有数据集和研究主要聚焦于通用的代码评审意见，要么缺少安全专属标注，要么规模太小、无法支撑大规模研究。为弥补这一空白，我们提出 SeRe，一个安全相关的代码评审数据集，它采用基于主动学习的集成分类方法构建。该方法通过人工标注迭代地改进模型预测，在保持合理召回率的同时实现了高精度。借助微调后的集成分类器，我们从 373,824 条原始评审实例中抽取出 6,732 条安全相关评审，并确保其在多种编程语言上的代表性。统计分析表明，SeRe 总体上与真实世界中安全相关评审的分布相吻合。为评估 SeRe 的实用价值以及现有代码评审意见生成方法的效果，我们在安全相关反馈生成任务上对当前最先进的方法进行了基准测试。通过发布 SeRe 及我们的基准测试结果，我们希望推动面向安全的自动化代码评审研究，并促进更有效的安全软件工程实践的发展。","tl":"用主动学习集成分类器筛出6732条真实安全评审并建基准。","au":["Zixiao Zhao","Yanjie Jiang","Hui Liu","Kui Liu","Lu Zhang"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["benchmark-dataset","security","empirical-study"],"kw":["code review","security review dataset","active learning","review comment generation","benchmark"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/40/x"},{"id":"p00527","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MazeBreaker: Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning for Dynamic Jailbreaking of LLM Security Defenses","tz":"MazeBreaker：用多智能体强化学习动态越狱大模型的安全防御","a":"In recent years, the application of Large Language Models~(LLMs) has become increasingly widespread, along with growing concerns about their security. To assess the security of LLMs, researchers have proposed various jailbreak attack algorithms, but only rely on the models’ internal information or face limitations in exploring the unsafe behavior, highlighting the need for a more adaptive and generalizable approach. Inspired by the game of rats escaping a maze, we introduce a novel jailbreak attack approach, MazeBreaker, where attackers dynamically learn to find the exit based on feedback and their accumulated experience to compromise the target LLMs’ security defenses. Our method is the first to systematically learn from the feedback of attack attempts on target LLMs through a multi-agent reinforcement learning system, enabling strategic exploration of the model’s unsafe boundaries without a reference oracle. We compared our approach with six state-of-the-art jailbreak attack methods, testing it on 13 different architectures of open-source and commercial models. The results show that our method performs exceptionally well in terms of attack effectiveness, especially for the commercial models (GPT-3.5-turbo, GPT-4o-mini, GLM-4-air and Claude-3.5-sonnet) with strong safety alignment. We hope this study will help academia and industry better test the security of large language models and promote adherence to safety and ethical standards. Code and data are available on our repository: https://anonymous.4open.science/r/MazeBreaker .","az":"近年来，大语言模型（LLM）的应用日益广泛，与之相伴的安全担忧也不断增长。为评估 LLM 的安全性，研究者提出了各种越狱攻击算法，但这些方法要么仅依赖模型的内部信息，要么在探索不安全行为方面存在局限，这凸显出需要一种更具适应性和泛化能力的方法。受老鼠逃出迷宫这一游戏的启发，我们提出一种新颖的越狱攻击方法 MazeBreaker：攻击者基于反馈与积累的经验动态学习如何找到出口，从而攻破目标 LLM 的安全防御。我们的方法首次系统性地通过多智能体强化学习系统从对目标 LLM 的攻击尝试反馈中学习，在没有参考预言的情况下实现对模型不安全边界的策略性探索。我们将该方法与六种最先进的越狱攻击方法进行比较，并在 13 种不同架构的开源与商业模型上进行测试。结果表明，我们的方法在攻击有效性方面表现优异，尤其是在安全对齐能力强的商业模型（GPT-3.5-turbo、GPT-4o-mini、GLM-4-air 和 Claude-3.5-sonnet）上。我们希望这项研究能帮助学术界和工业界更好地测试大语言模型的安全性，并推动对安全与伦理标准的遵守。代码和数据见我们的仓库：https://anonymous.4open.science/r/MazeBreaker 。","tl":"首次用多智能体强化学习从攻击反馈中学习越狱策略。","au":["Zhihao Lin","Wei Ma","Mingyi Zhou","Yanjie Zhao","Haoyu Wang","Yang Liu","Jun Wang","Li Li"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["cross-track-bridge","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["jailbreak attack","multi-agent reinforcement learning","LLM safety","red teaming","attack success rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/41/x"},{"id":"p00528","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AtPatch: Debugging Transformers via Hot-Fixing Over-Attention","tz":"AtPatch：通过热修复过度注意力来调试 Transformer","a":"Transformer-based deep neural networks (DNNs) affected by backdoor attacks and unfairness typically exhibit anomalous attention patterns, leading to over-attend to backdoor triggers or protected attributes. Existing neuron-editing mitigation strategies often struggle to handle such situation and most of them lack flexibility and tend to distort feature representations. Motivated by such over-attention phenomenon and software engineering paradigms such as delta debugging and hot patching, we propose AtPatch, a hot-fix method that dynamically redistributes attention maps during model inference. Specifically, for a given input, AtPatch first extracts the attention map from the model’s inference process. Then, it uses a pre-trained detector to identify anomalous columns and replace them with unified benign attention. Then, AtPatch rescales other columns to mitigate the impact of over-attention. Finally, AtPatch returns the redistributed attention map to the model for continued inference. Notably, if the detector does not report any anomalous columns, AtPatch directly returns the original attention map to the model. Unlike existing techniques, AtPatch selectively redistributes the attention map, making it better at preserving the model’s original functionality. Furthermore, AtPatch’s on-the-fly nature allows it to work without modifying model parameters or retraining, making it better suited for deployed models. We conducted extensive experiments to validate AtPatch. Experimental results show that, compared to existing methods, AtPatch can more effectively mitigate backdoor attacks and unfairness while better preserving the model’s original functionality.","az":"受后门攻击和不公平性影响的基于 Transformer 的深度神经网络（DNN）通常表现出异常的注意力模式，导致对后门触发器或受保护属性的过度关注。已有的神经元编辑缓解策略往往难以应对此类情形，且大多缺乏灵活性并容易扭曲特征表示。受这种过度注意力现象以及增量调试、热补丁等软件工程范式的启发，我们提出 AtPatch，一种在模型推理过程中动态重新分配注意力图的热修复方法。具体而言，对于给定输入，AtPatch 首先从模型的推理过程中提取注意力图；随后使用一个预训练的检测器识别异常列，并用统一的良性注意力替换它们；接着，AtPatch 重新缩放其他列以缓解过度注意力的影响；最后，AtPatch 将重新分配后的注意力图返回给模型以继续推理。值得注意的是，如果检测器未报告任何异常列，AtPatch 会直接把原始注意力图返回给模型。与已有技术不同，AtPatch 有选择地重新分配注意力图，因而能更好地保留模型的原有功能。此外，AtPatch 的即时（on-the-fly）特性使其无需修改模型参数或重新训练即可工作，更适用于已部署的模型。我们开展了大量实验来验证 AtPatch。实验结果表明，与已有方法相比，AtPatch 能更有效地缓解后门攻击和不公平性，同时更好地保持模型的原有功能。","tl":"推理期重分配注意力图即可热修复后门与不公平，无需重训。","au":["Shihao Weng","Yang Feng","Jincheng Li","Yining Yin","Xiaofei Xie","Jia Liu"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["attention redistribution","backdoor mitigation","fairness repair","hot patching","Transformer debugging"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/42/x"},{"id":"p00529","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Write Your Own Code Checker: An Automated Test-Driven Checker Development Approach with LLMs","tz":"自己动手写代码检查器：一种基于大模型的测试驱动检查器自动开发方法","a":"With the rising demand for code quality assurance, developers are not only utilizing existing static code checkers but also seeking custom checkers to satisfy their specific needs. Nowadays, various code-checking frameworks provide extensive checker customization interfaces to meet this need. However, both the abstract checking logic and the complex API usage of large-scale checker frameworks make this task challenging. To this end, automated code checker generation is anticipated to ease the burden of checker development. In this paper, we propose AutoChecker, an innovative LLM-powered approach that can write code checkers automatically based on only a rule description and a test suite. To achieve comprehensive checking logic, AutoChecker incrementally updates the checker’s logic by focusing on solving one selected case each time. To obtain precise API knowledge, during each iteration, it leverages fine-grained logic-guided API-context retrieval, where it first decomposes the checking logic into a series of sub-operations and then retrieves checker-related API-contexts for each sub-operation. For evaluation, we apply AutoChecker, five baselines, and three ablation methods using multiple LLMs to generate checkers for 20 randomly selected PMD rules. Experimental results show that AutoChecker significantly outperforms others across all effectiveness metrics, with an average test pass rate of 82.28%. Additionally, the checkers generated by AutoChecker can be successfully applied to real-world projects, matching the performance of official checkers.","az":"随着代码质量保障需求的上升，开发者不仅使用现成的静态代码检查器，还希望定制检查器以满足特定需求。如今，各种代码检查框架提供了大量的检查器定制接口来满足这一需求。然而，抽象的检查逻辑以及大型检查器框架复杂的 API 用法都使这项任务颇具挑战。为此，人们期待自动化的代码检查器生成来减轻检查器开发负担。本文提出 AutoChecker，一种由大语言模型驱动的创新方法，仅依据一条规则描述和一个测试套件即可自动编写代码检查器。为获得全面的检查逻辑，AutoChecker 每次聚焦于解决一个选定的用例，增量式地更新检查器逻辑。为获取精确的 API 知识，在每次迭代中它采用细粒度的逻辑引导式 API 上下文检索：先将检查逻辑分解为一系列子操作，再为每个子操作检索与检查器相关的 API 上下文。在评估中，我们使用多种大语言模型，让 AutoChecker、五个基线方法和三种消融方法为随机选取的 20 条 PMD 规则生成检查器。实验结果表明，AutoChecker 在所有有效性指标上都显著优于其他方法，平均测试通过率达 82.28%。此外，AutoChecker 生成的检查器可以成功应用于真实项目，性能与官方检查器相当。","tl":"用逻辑引导的API检索增量生成自定义静态检查器。","au":["Jun Liu","Yuanyuan Xie","Jiwei Yan","Jinhao Huang","Jun Yan","Jian Zhang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static code checker","checker generation","PMD rules","API context retrieval","test-driven"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/43/x"},{"id":"p00530","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Generator Solving for Symbolic Execution","tz":"面向符号执行的生成器求解","a":"Automated test input generation based on symbolic execution has garnered significant research interest. However, the main drawback of symbolic execution is its poor scalability. Since the overhead associated with constraint modeling and solving is high, generating only one test input per SMT query is inefficient. In this paper, we introduce the concept of generator solving. Instead of solving for only one particular solution, we propose to find a generator that can be called multiple times to continuously yield new test inputs. This approach offers several benefits: (1) it allows efficient generation of as many test inputs as needed, thereby significantly improving the input generation efficiency of symbolic execution methods; (2) the continuously generated inputs facilitate a more comprehensive exploration of the solution set, potentially triggering new program behaviors; and (3) compared to hybrid approaches based on mutation, using a generator ensures the satisfiability of the target constraints. We present three key techniques for generator solving: (1) reusing invertible model converters in Z3 as generators; (2) constructing hierarchical range-based samplers to sample solutions of range constraints; and (3) employing optimistic simplification strategies to enhance the generality of the solving process. We have implemented GenSlv, a prototypical generator solver specifically designed for automated test case generation based on symbolic execution. Evaluation results demonstrate that (1) GenSlv is effective in finding generators for constraints collected from real-world programs (specifically, GenSlv can find a generator for 97% of the constraints that have at least two different solutions), and (2) GenSlv significantly and consistently improves the performance of commonly used symbolic executors (including KLEE, Angr, TritonDSE, and SymCC) in terms of program coverage and vulnerability detection across various settings in symbolic execution and hybrid fuzzing tasks, with a maximum of more than twofold increase in branch coverage.","az":"基于符号执行的自动化测试输入生成已获得大量研究关注。然而，符号执行的主要缺陷在于可扩展性差。由于约束建模与求解的开销很高，每次 SMT 查询只生成一个测试输入的做法效率低下。本文提出“生成器求解”（generator solving）这一概念：不再只求解某一个特定解，而是寻找一个可以被多次调用、持续产出新测试输入的生成器。该方法带来若干好处：（1）可以按需高效生成任意多的测试输入，从而显著提升符号执行方法的输入生成效率；（2）持续生成的输入有助于更全面地探索解集，可能触发新的程序行为；（3）与基于变异的混合方法相比，使用生成器可确保目标约束的可满足性。我们提出生成器求解的三项关键技术：（1）复用 Z3 中可逆的模型转换器作为生成器；（2）构建基于区间的分层采样器，以对区间约束的解进行采样；（3）采用乐观化简策略以提升求解过程的通用性。我们实现了 GenSlv，一个专为基于符号执行的自动测试用例生成而设计的生成器求解器原型。评估结果表明：（1）GenSlv 能有效地为真实程序中收集到的约束找到生成器（具体而言，对于至少有两个不同解的约束，GenSlv 能为其中 97% 找到生成器）；（2）在符号执行与混合模糊测试任务的各种设置下，GenSlv 都显著且一致地提升了常用符号执行引擎（包括 KLEE、Angr、TritonDSE 和 SymCC）在程序覆盖率与漏洞检测方面的表现，分支覆盖率最高提升超过两倍。","tl":"求解出可反复调用的生成器，而非单个解，加速符号执行。","au":["Siwei Wei","Yan Cai"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic execution","constraint solving","generator solving","test input generation","hybrid fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/44/x"},{"id":"p00531","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Synthetic Repo-level Bug Dataset for Training Automated Program Repair Models","tz":"用于训练自动程序修复模型的合成仓库级缺陷数据集","a":"Automated program repair (APR) aims to autonomously fix software bugs, yet its effectiveness is hampered by the lack of diverse, real-world bug datasets essential for model training. Although combining large-scale mining with human effort can yield such datasets, the associated costs limit scalability. To address this, we introduce a novel, scalable synthetic data pipeline that leverages large language models (LLMs) to generate synthetic bugs through targeted LLM-based code rewriting. Our pipeline is also capable of synthesizing valuable intermediate repair steps and enriches the training signal toward correct fixes. Using our method, we create SWE-Synth, a large and contextually rich dataset of bug-fix pairs that are natural, scalable, automated verifiable, and contain intermediate repair steps. Training LLMs on our synthetic dataset yields context-aware repair strategies, that achieve repair accuracy equivalent to those trained on manually curated datasets from Github like SWE-Gym while delivering superior scalability with effortless bug synthesis, as demonstrated on popular benchmarks (SWE-Bench and BugsInPy).","az":"自动程序修复（APR）旨在自主修复软件缺陷，但其效果受限于缺乏模型训练所必需的多样化真实缺陷数据集。尽管把大规模挖掘与人工投入结合起来可以构造此类数据集，但相应成本限制了可扩展性。为此，我们提出一条新颖且可扩展的合成数据流水线，利用大语言模型（LLM）通过有针对性的基于 LLM 的代码改写来生成合成缺陷。我们的流水线还能合成有价值的中间修复步骤，从而丰富指向正确修复的训练信号。基于该方法，我们构建了 SWE-Synth，一个规模大、上下文丰富的缺陷-修复对数据集，其样本自然、可扩展、可自动验证，并包含中间修复步骤。在我们的合成数据集上训练 LLM 可获得具备上下文感知能力的修复策略，其修复准确率与在 SWE-Gym 这类从 GitHub 人工整理的数据集上训练所得相当，同时凭借轻松的缺陷合成带来更优的可扩展性——这一点已在常用基准（SWE-Bench 和 BugsInPy）上得到验证。","tl":"用LLM改写代码合成仓库级缺陷与中间修复步骤做训练数据。","au":["Minh V. T. Pham","Huy N. Phan","Hoang Nhat Phan","Cuong Chi Le","Tien N. Nguyen","Nghi D. Q. Bui"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["automated program repair","synthetic bug generation","SWE-Synth","training data pipeline","SWE-Bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/45/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00532","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SEAlign: Alignment Training for Software Engineering Agent","tz":"SEAlign：面向软件工程智能体的对齐训练","a":"Recent advances in code generation models have demonstrated impressive capabilities in automating software development tasks, yet these models still struggle in real-world software engineering scenarios. Although current training methods, particularly post-training, excel at solving competitive programming problems, they fail to adequately prepare models for the complexities of practical software development. This misalignment raises the critical question: Are existing alignment training methods well suited for real-world software engineering tasks? In this study, we identify this issue and propose SEAlign, a novel alignment framework designed to bridge the gap between code generation models and real-world software development tasks. SEAlign leverages the unique characteristics of software engineering processes, including high-quality workflow steps, to enhance model capabilities. Our framework further employs Monte Carlo Tree Search for fine-grained alignment in multi-step decision processes, followed by preference optimization on critical actions to ensure models meet real-world requirements. We evaluate SEAlign on three standard agentic benchmarks for real-world software engineering, including HumanEvalFix, SWE-Bench-Lite, and SWE-Bench-Verified. Experimental results demonstrate state-of-the-art performance with minimal training overhead. In addition, we develop an agent-based software development platform using SEAlign, which successfully automates the creation of several small applications. Human evaluations of these applications highlight significant improvements in both task performance and user experience. Our findings underscore the potential of SEAlign to accelerate the adoption of large code models in real-world software development. We believe that this research makes a meaningful step towards fully automated software engineering.","az":"代码生成模型的最新进展在自动化软件开发任务上展现了令人印象深刻的能力，但这些模型在真实的软件工程场景中仍然表现不佳。尽管当前的训练方法（尤其是后训练）在解决竞赛编程题上表现出色，却未能让模型充分应对实际软件开发的复杂性。这种错配引出一个关键问题：现有的对齐训练方法真的适合真实世界的软件工程任务吗？在本研究中，我们指出了这一问题，并提出 SEAlign，一个旨在弥合代码生成模型与真实软件开发任务之间差距的新型对齐框架。SEAlign 利用软件工程过程的独特特征（包括高质量的工作流步骤）来增强模型能力。我们的框架进一步采用蒙特卡洛树搜索在多步决策过程中进行细粒度对齐，随后对关键动作进行偏好优化，以确保模型满足真实需求。我们在三个面向真实软件工程的标准智能体基准上评估 SEAlign，包括 HumanEvalFix、SWE-Bench-Lite 和 SWE-Bench-Verified。实验结果表明其以极小的训练开销取得了最先进的性能。此外，我们基于 SEAlign 开发了一个基于智能体的软件开发平台，成功自动化地创建了若干小型应用。对这些应用的人工评估显示，其在任务表现与用户体验两方面都有显著提升。我们的发现凸显了 SEAlign 加速大型代码模型在真实软件开发中落地的潜力。我们相信这项研究朝着完全自动化的软件工程迈出了有意义的一步。","tl":"用MCTS对多步工作流细粒度对齐并对关键动作做偏好优化。","au":["Kechi Zhang","Huangzhao Zhang","Ge Li","Jinliang You","Jia Li","Yunfei Zhao","Zhi Jin"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["SE agent alignment","Monte Carlo Tree Search","preference optimization","SWE-Bench","post-training"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/46/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00533","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"D-BUNDLR: Destructing JavaScript Bundles for Effective Static Analysis","tz":"D-BUNDLR：拆解 JavaScript 打包产物以实现有效的静态分析","a":"Static analysis for vulnerability detection in JavaScript is an extensively studied research area. However, state-of-the-art approaches ignore bundling, an emerging development practice, akin to compilation, which allows developers to merge code from different providers, while also applying optimizations to reduce code size. A typical bundle heavily reuses single-letter identifiers and extensively relies on dynamic JavaScript features to emulate code dependencies, thus, hindering static analysis. In this work, we propose a reverse engineering approach that relies on domain-specific code transformations to unpack bundles and replace reidentified libraries with their source code. Our technique applies lightweight static analysis to dissect bundles into individual components, machine learning to identify libraries, and dynamic analysis to verify that libraries were correctly identified. We implement this approach in a tool called D-Bundlr, and evaluate it by comparing the output of CodeQL (a popular static analysis tool) before and after debundling. For a JavaScript code benchmark with known vulnerabilities, our approach allows CodeQL to recover 89% of the vulnerabilities and 83% of all alerts that were also detected in the source code, but were dormant in bundles. Similarly, for real-world bundles where we can retrieve the source code, D-Bundlr recovered 33% of the original alerts. When applied to bundles extracted from the 100,000 most popular websites, D-Bundlr identifies 34,445 instances corresponding to 63 unique libraries, and causes CodeQL to produce around 3.2K more security alerts than on packed bundles. We additionally illustrate how attackers can exploit some of our zero-day findings, causing unwanted security effects such as advertisement space hijacking.","az":"面向 JavaScript 漏洞检测的静态分析是一个被广泛研究的领域。然而，最先进的方法忽略了打包（bundling）这一新兴开发实践——它类似于编译，允许开发者把来自不同提供方的代码合并，同时施加各种优化以缩减代码体积。典型的打包产物大量复用单字母标识符，并大量依赖 JavaScript 的动态特性来模拟代码依赖，因而阻碍了静态分析。在本工作中，我们提出一种逆向工程方法，依靠领域专用的代码变换来解包 bundle，并用源代码替换重新识别出的库。我们的技术使用轻量级静态分析将 bundle 拆解为独立组件，使用机器学习识别库，并使用动态分析验证库被正确识别。我们在名为 D-Bundlr 的工具中实现了该方法，并通过比较 CodeQL（一个流行的静态分析工具）在解包前后的输出来评估它。对于一个已知漏洞的 JavaScript 代码基准，我们的方法使 CodeQL 恢复了 89% 的漏洞，以及在源代码中也能检测到、但在 bundle 中处于“休眠”状态的全部告警中的 83%。类似地，对于可以取得源代码的真实 bundle，D-Bundlr 恢复了 33% 的原始告警。当应用于从最流行的 10 万个网站中提取的 bundle 时，D-Bundlr 识别出对应 63 个不同库的 34,445 个实例，并使 CodeQL 相比在打包状态下多产生约 3.2K 条安全告警。我们还展示了攻击者如何利用我们发现的部分零日问题，造成诸如广告位劫持之类的有害安全后果。","tl":"解包并还原库源码，让CodeQL重新看见被打包掩盖的漏洞。","au":["Wenyuan Xu","Alexi Turcotte","Cristian-Alexandru Staicu"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["JavaScript bundling","debundling","static analysis","CodeQL","library identification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/47/x"},{"id":"p00534","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automating Just-In-Time Python Type Annotation Updating","tz":"自动化的 Python 类型注解即时更新","a":"Type annotations are more and more popular in Python projects to avoid type errors caused by Python’s dynamic typing feature. However, when developers change source code, these type annotations are often neglected or overlooked, resulting in outdated and inconsistent type annotations. Such obsolete type annotations can hinder program comprehension, mislead developers, and even introduce bugs in the future. Therefore, it is necessary to avoid and correct these inconsistent type annotations from the very beginning. In this work, we argue that obsolete type annotations can be reduced and even avoided by automatically updating type annotations alongside code changes. We refer to this task as “Just-In-Time (JIT) type annotation updating”. To solve this task, we propose a novel LLM-based approach named TypeUp (Type Annotation Updator) to automate this task. TypeUp can automatically generate new type annotations based on the old type annotations and corresponding code changes. Specifically, TypeUp guides LLM to perform type annotation updates by eliciting its knowledge and logical reasoning power and learning from similar code changes. The evaluation results show that TypeUp outperforms state-of-the-art type infer approach (i.e., TypeGen) by 41.9% on our task. Moreover, we conducted an in-the-wild evaluation with real-world software projects, 20 out of 25 type annotation updates generated by our approach have already been confirmed by developers, showing our approach’s practical value in real-world environments.","az":"为避免 Python 动态类型特性带来的类型错误，类型注解在 Python 项目中越来越流行。然而，当开发者修改源代码时，这些类型注解常常被忽视或遗漏，导致注解过时且不一致。这类陈旧的类型注解会妨碍程序理解、误导开发者，甚至在未来引入缺陷。因此，有必要从一开始就避免并纠正这些不一致的类型注解。在本工作中，我们主张通过在代码变更的同时自动更新类型注解，可以减少甚至避免过时注解。我们称该任务为“即时（JIT）类型注解更新”。为解决该任务，我们提出一种基于大语言模型的新方法 TypeUp（Type Annotation Updator）来实现自动化。TypeUp 能够基于旧的类型注解和相应的代码变更自动生成新的类型注解。具体而言，TypeUp 通过激发大模型的知识与逻辑推理能力、并从相似的代码变更中学习，来引导模型完成类型注解更新。评估结果表明，在我们的任务上 TypeUp 比最先进的类型推断方法（即 TypeGen）高出 41.9%。此外，我们在真实软件项目上开展了实地评估，我们的方法生成的 25 个类型注解更新中已有 20 个得到开发者确认，显示出该方法在真实环境中的实用价值。","tl":"提出随代码变更即时更新类型注解的新任务与LLM方法。","au":["Zhipeng Xue","Zhipeng Gao","Xing Hu","Jingyuan Chen","Xin Xia","Shanping Li"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["type annotation","just-in-time updating","Python typing","code change","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/48/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00535","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Smoke and Mirrors: Jailbreaking LLM-based Code Generation via Implicit Malicious Prompts","tz":"障眼法：通过隐式恶意提示越狱基于大模型的代码生成","a":"The proliferation of Large Language Models (LLMs) has revolutionized natural language processing and significantly impacted code generation tasks, enhancing software development efficiency and productivity. Notably, LLMs like GPT-4 have demonstrated remarkable proficiency in text-to-code generation tasks. However, the growing reliance on LLMs for code generation necessitates a critical examination of the security implications associated with their outputs. Existing research efforts have primarily focused on verifying functional correctness, overlooking the crucial aspect of code security. This paper introduces a jailbreaking approach, CodeJailbreaker, targeting LLM-based code generation to expose security vulnerabilities. The basic observation is that existing security mechanisms for LLMs are built through the instruction-following paradigm, where malicious intent is explicitly articulated within the instruction of the prompt. Consequently, CodeJailbreaker explores to construct a prompt whose instruction is benign and the malicious intent is implicitly encoded in a covert channel, i.e., the commit message, to bypass the safety mechanism. Experiments on the recently-released RMCBench benchmark demonstrate that CodeJailbreaker markedly surpasses the conventional jailbreaking strategy, which explicitly conveys malicious intents in the instructions, in terms of the attack effectiveness across three code generation tasks. This study challenges the traditional safety paradigms in LLM-based code generation, emphasizing the need for enhanced safety measures in safeguarding against implicit malicious cues.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的普及彻底改变了自然语言处理，并显著影响了代码生成任务，提升了软件开发的效率与生产力。值得注意的是，像 GPT-4 这样的 LLM 在文本到代码生成任务中展现出卓越的能力。然而，对 LLM 代码生成日益增长的依赖，要求我们审慎审视其输出所带来的安全影响。已有研究主要关注功能正确性的验证，忽视了代码安全这一关键方面。本文提出一种针对基于 LLM 的代码生成的越狱方法 CodeJailbreaker，用以暴露安全漏洞。其基本观察是：现有的 LLM 安全机制是围绕指令遵循范式构建的，即恶意意图被显式表述在提示的指令中。因此，CodeJailbreaker 探索构造这样一种提示——其指令是良性的，而恶意意图被隐式编码在一个隐蔽信道（即提交信息）中，以绕过安全机制。在最近发布的 RMCBench 基准上的实验表明，在三个代码生成任务上，CodeJailbreaker 的攻击有效性显著超过在指令中显式表达恶意意图的传统越狱策略。本研究挑战了基于 LLM 的代码生成中的传统安全范式，强调需要更强的安全措施来防范隐式的恶意线索。","tl":"把恶意意图藏进提交信息这一隐蔽信道即可绕过代码安全机制。","au":["Sheng Ouyang","Yihao Qin","Bo Lin","Liqian Chen","Xiaoguang Mao","Shangwen Wang"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["jailbreak","malicious code generation","covert channel","commit message","RMCBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/49/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.17953"},{"id":"p00536","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Portable Power Modeling with Transfer Learning on JVM-Based Applications","tz":"基于迁移学习的 JVM 应用可移植功耗建模","a":"Developing energy-aware applications is an important approach to promoting sustainable computing. This paper addresses a fundamental and challenging problem faced by developers and deployers: how to port a power model built for one machine to another? We present LucRETius, a novel approach toward portable power modeling through transfer learning, where a pre-trained power model on one machine can serve as a teacher to help construct a student model on another machine rapidly. The key insight that enables transfer learning is that the layer of application runtimes can abstract away the machine-specific details, so that two machines—despite different hardware and software system configurations—are unified with a common set of runtime events that can serve as features for transfer learning. We evaluate LucRETius through bi-directional transfers across 4 machines, and we show the power models built by LucRETius have a median percentage error of 1.01%-1.75% when used for predicting the energy consumption of 36 real-world JVM-based applications. Compared with training from scratch, LucRETius can lead to a speed up of 8.07! .","az":"开发能耗感知的应用是推动可持续计算的重要途径。本文探讨开发者与部署者面临的一个基础且具挑战性的问题：如何把为一台机器构建的功耗模型移植到另一台机器上？我们提出 LucRETius，一种通过迁移学习实现可移植功耗建模的新方法：在一台机器上预训练的功耗模型可作为“教师”，帮助在另一台机器上快速构建“学生”模型。使迁移学习成为可能的关键洞见是，应用运行时这一层可以抽象掉机器特有的细节，从而使两台机器——尽管硬件与软件系统配置不同——能够通过一组共同的运行时事件统一起来，这些事件可作为迁移学习的特征。我们在 4 台机器之间进行双向迁移来评估 LucRETius，结果显示 LucRETius 构建的功耗模型在预测 36 个真实 JVM 应用的能耗时，中位百分比误差为 1.01%–1.75%。与从零开始训练相比，LucRETius 可带来 8.07 倍的加速。","tl":"以运行时事件为共享特征迁移功耗模型，跨机器建模快8倍。","au":["Joseph Raskind","Timur Babakol","Yu David Liu"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["power modeling","transfer learning","JVM applications","energy consumption","sustainable computing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/50/x"},{"id":"p00537","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Accurate Inference of Termination Conditions","tz":"精确推断程序终止条件","a":"We present the first approach to infer accurate termination conditions of programs. It builds on a simple but effective framework where non-terminating states are iteratively identified and removed, and a termination prover is employed to validate the current condition. We instantiate the framework with data-driven provers and design a multi-way data sharing mechanism to enhance their interaction. Our proofs show that this method is correct, accurate, terminating, and relatively complete. Additionally, we introduce generalization techniques for recurrent sets to accelerate the iteration process. Evaluation on a benchmark of programs from the literature shows that our implementation significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art tool Acabar, producing much more accurate termination conditions, with the proposed techniques playing a crucial role in speeding up the convergence of the process.","az":"我们提出了首个用于推断程序精确终止条件的方法。它建立在一个简单但有效的框架之上：迭代地识别并剔除非终止状态，并使用终止性证明器来验证当前条件。我们用数据驱动的证明器实例化该框架，并设计了一种多路数据共享机制来增强它们之间的交互。我们的证明表明该方法是正确的、精确的、可终止的，并且是相对完备的。此外，我们引入了针对递归集（recurrent set）的泛化技术以加速迭代过程。在文献中的程序基准上的评估表明，我们的实现显著优于最先进的工具 Acabar，能产生精确得多的终止条件，而所提出的技术在加速过程收敛方面发挥了关键作用。","tl":"迭代剔除非终止状态并用证明器验证，首次推断精确终止条件。","au":["Biting Huang","Zhilei Han","Fei He"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["termination condition inference","termination prover","recurrent set","data-driven analysis","program analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/51/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00538","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evaluating Generated Commit Messages with Large Language Models","tz":"用大语言模型评估生成的提交信息","a":"Commit messages are essential in software development as they serve to document and explain code changes. Yet, their quality often falls short in practice, with studies showing significant proportions of empty or inadequate messages. While automated commit message generation has advanced significantly, particularly with Large Language Models (LLMs), the evaluation of generated messages remains challenging. Traditional reference-based automatic metrics like BLEU, ROUGE-L, and METEOR have notable limitations in assessing commit message quality, as they assume a one-to-one mapping between code changes and commit messages, leading researchers to rely on resource-intensive human evaluation. This study investigates the potential of LLMs as automated evaluators for commit message quality. Through systematic experimentation with various prompt strategies and state-of-the-art LLMs, we demonstrate that LLMs combining Chain-of-Thought reasoning with few-shot demonstrations achieve near human-level evaluation proficiency. Our LLM-based evaluator significantly outperforms traditional metrics while maintaining acceptable reproducibility, robustness, and fairness levels despite some inherent variability. This work conducts a comprehensive preliminary study on using LLMs for commit message evaluation, offering a scalable alternative to human assessment while maintaining high-quality evaluation.","az":"提交信息在软件开发中至关重要，因为它们用于记录并解释代码变更。然而在实践中其质量往往不尽如人意，已有研究表明存在相当比例的空白或不充分的提交信息。尽管自动提交信息生成（尤其是借助大语言模型）已取得显著进展，但对生成信息的评估仍然困难。诸如 BLEU、ROUGE-L 和 METEOR 之类传统的基于参考的自动指标在评估提交信息质量方面存在明显局限，因为它们假设代码变更与提交信息之间是一一对应的，这导致研究者不得不依赖资源密集的人工评估。本研究考察了将大语言模型用作提交信息质量自动评估者的潜力。通过对多种提示策略和最先进大模型的系统性实验，我们证明：将思维链推理与少样本示例相结合的大模型可以达到接近人类水平的评估能力。我们基于大模型的评估器显著优于传统指标，尽管存在一定固有波动，仍保持了可接受的可复现性、鲁棒性与公平性水平。本工作对使用大模型评估提交信息进行了全面的初步研究，在保持高质量评估的同时，为人工评估提供了一种可扩展的替代方案。","tl":"思维链加少样本的LLM评估器达到接近人类的提交信息评分。","au":["Qunhong Zeng","Yuxia Zhang","Zexiong Ma","Bo Jiang","Ningyuan Sun","Klaas-Jan Stol","Xingyu Mou","Hui Liu"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["commit message evaluation","LLM-as-a-judge","chain-of-thought","few-shot prompting","evaluation metrics"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/52/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.10906","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00539","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ConfLogger: Enhance Systems' Configuration Diagnosability through Configuration Logging","tz":"ConfLogger：通过配置日志增强系统的配置可诊断性","a":"Modern configurable systems offer customization via intricate configuration spaces, yet such flexibility introduces pervasive configuration-related issues such as misconfigurations and latent softwarebugs. Existing diagnosability supports focus on post-failure analysis of software behavior to identify configuration issues, but none of these approaches look into whether the software clue sufficient failure information for diagnosis. To fill in the blank, we propose the idea of configuration logging to enhance existing logging practices at the source code level. We develop ConfLogger, the first tool that unifies configuration-aware static taint analysis with LLM-based log generation to enhance software configuration diagnosability. Specifically, our method 1) identifies configuration-sensitive code segments by tracing configuration-related data flow in the whole project, and 2) generates diagnostic log statements by analyzing configuration code contexts. Evaluation results on eight popular software systems demonstrate the effectiveness of ConfLogger to enhance configuration diagnosability. Specifically, ConfLogger-enhanced logs successfully aid a log-based misconfiguration diagnosis tool to achieve 100% accuracy on error localization in 30 silent misconfiguration scenarios, with 80% directly resolvable through explicit configuration information exposed. In addition, ConfLogger achieves 74% coverage of existing logging points, outperforming baseline LLM-based loggers by 12% and 30%. It also gains 8.6% higher in precision, 79.3% higher in recall, and 26.2% higher in F1 compared to the state-of-the-art baseline in terms of variable logging while also augmenting diagnostic value. A controlled user study on 22 cases further validated its utility, speeding up diagnostic time by 1.25× and improving troubleshooting accuracy by 251.4%.","az":"现代可配置系统通过复杂的配置空间提供定制能力，但这种灵活性也带来了普遍存在的配置相关问题，如错误配置和潜伏的软件缺陷。现有的可诊断性支持主要关注对软件行为的事后失效分析以识别配置问题，但这些方法都没有考察软件本身是否给出了足够的失效诊断信息。为填补这一空白，我们提出“配置日志”的思想，在源代码层面增强现有的日志实践。我们开发了 ConfLogger，这是首个将配置感知的静态污点分析与基于大模型的日志生成统一起来、以提升软件配置可诊断性的工具。具体而言，我们的方法：1）通过在整个项目中追踪配置相关的数据流来识别配置敏感的代码片段；2）通过分析配置代码上下文来生成诊断性日志语句。在八个流行软件系统上的评估结果证明了 ConfLogger 在增强配置可诊断性方面的有效性。具体来说，经 ConfLogger 增强的日志成功帮助一款基于日志的错误配置诊断工具在 30 个静默错误配置场景中达到 100% 的错误定位准确率，其中 80% 可通过显式暴露的配置信息直接解决。此外，ConfLogger 覆盖了现有日志点的 74%，比基于大模型的日志基线分别高出 12% 和 30%。在变量日志方面，它相比最先进的基线精确率高 8.6%、召回率高 79.3%、F1 高 26.2%，同时还增强了诊断价值。一项针对 22 个案例的受控用户研究进一步验证了其实用性：诊断时间加快 1.25 倍，排障准确率提升 251.4%。","tl":"配置感知污点分析加LLM生成日志，使静默错配可被定位。","au":["Shiwen Shan","Yintong Huo","Yuxin Su","Zhining Wang","Dan Li","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["llm-based","human-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["configuration diagnosability","logging statement generation","taint analysis","misconfiguration","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/53/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/53/ConfLogger-Enhance-Systems-Configuration-Diagnosability-through-Configuration-Loggi"},{"id":"p00540","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Rusted Types: Static Detection of Rust Type Confusion Bugs","tz":"生锈的类型：Rust 类型混淆缺陷的静态检测","a":"Rust is a modern programming language designed for strict memory and concurrency safety. Despite the safety checks, unsafe code in Rust can introduce memory safety issues. Unsafe type conversion, which reinterprets data from one type to another type, can alter the type spatial and temporal properties, leading to memory safety and data corruption issues. Since an unsafely converted value could violate a programmer’s intended conversion semantics and allows attackers to access the sensitive memory, type confusion bugs have critical security implications. Despite the increasing number of Rust type confusion bugs, the problem has not been systematically studied and addressed by the Rust community. In this paper, we propose DeRust, the first and a novel static analysis tool for detecting Rust type confusion bugs. By precisely tracking the inter-procedural data flows from unsafe type conversions to sensitive operations, DeRust can effectively and efficiently identify type confusion bugs. Our evaluation shows that DeRust can detect all the type confusion bugs in the benchmark datasets, and further helped report 54 previously unknown bugs in the top 1,000 Rust packages with 13 RustSec IDs assigned. We plan to release the prototype implementation of DeRust and other artifacts to help improve the Rust ecosystem.","az":"Rust 是一门为严格的内存与并发安全而设计的现代编程语言。尽管有安全检查，Rust 中的 unsafe 代码仍可能引入内存安全问题。不安全的类型转换会把数据从一种类型重新解释为另一种类型，可能改变类型的空间与时间属性，从而导致内存安全与数据损坏问题。由于被不安全转换的值可能违反程序员意图的转换语义，并允许攻击者访问敏感内存，类型混淆缺陷具有严重的安全影响。尽管 Rust 类型混淆缺陷的数量不断增加，该问题尚未被 Rust 社区系统地研究和解决。本文提出 DeRust，首个用于检测 Rust 类型混淆缺陷的新型静态分析工具。通过精确追踪从不安全类型转换到敏感操作的过程间数据流，DeRust 能有效且高效地识别类型混淆缺陷。我们的评估显示，DeRust 能检出基准数据集中的所有类型混淆缺陷，并进一步帮助在排名前 1000 的 Rust 包中报告了 54 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 13 个被分配了 RustSec 编号。我们计划发布 DeRust 的原型实现及其他制品，以帮助改进 Rust 生态。","tl":"首个静态检测Rust类型混淆的工具，挖出54个未知缺陷。","au":["Zeyang Zhuang","Wei Meng","Michael Lyu"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Rust","type confusion","unsafe code","static analysis","memory safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/54/x"},{"id":"p00541","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Aligning Requirement for Large Language Model's Code Generation","tz":"为大语言模型的代码生成对齐需求规约","a":"Code generation refers to the automatic generation of source code based on a given programming specification, which has garnered significant attention particularly with the advancement of large language models (LLMs). However, due to the inherent complexity of real-world problems, the LLM-generated code often fails to fully align with the provided specification. While state-of-the-art agent-based techniques have been proposed to enhance LLM code generation, they overlook the critical issue of specification perception, resulting in persistent misalignment issues. Given that accurate perception of programming specifications serves as the foundation of the LLM-based code generation paradigm, ensuring specification alignment is particularly crucial. In this work, we draw on software requirement engineering to propose Specine, a novel specification alignment technique for LLM code generation. Its key idea is to identify misaligned input specifications, lift LLM-perceived specifications, and align them to enhance the code generation performance of LLMs. Our comprehensive experiments on four state-of-the-art LLMs across five challenging competitive benchmarks by comparing with ten state-of-the-art baselines, demonstrate the effectiveness of Specine. For example, Specine outperforms the most effective baseline, achieving an average improvement of 29.60% across all subjects in terms of Pass@1.","az":"代码生成是指基于给定的编程规约自动生成源代码，随着大语言模型（LLM）的发展，这一任务获得了极大关注。然而，由于现实问题固有的复杂性，LLM 生成的代码往往无法完全符合所提供的规约。虽然已有最先进的基于智能体的技术被提出以增强 LLM 代码生成，但它们忽视了规约感知这一关键问题，导致错配问题持续存在。鉴于准确感知编程规约是基于 LLM 的代码生成范式的基础，确保规约对齐尤为关键。在本工作中，我们借鉴软件需求工程，提出 Specine，一种面向 LLM 代码生成的新型规约对齐技术。其核心思想是识别错配的输入规约，提炼出 LLM 所感知到的规约，并将二者对齐，从而提升 LLM 的代码生成性能。我们在四个最先进的 LLM 上、跨五个具有挑战性的竞赛类基准，与十个最先进的基线方法进行了全面实验，证明了 Specine 的有效性。例如，在 Pass@1 指标上，Specine 超过了最有效的基线，在所有对象上平均提升 29.60%。","tl":"提炼并对齐模型感知到的规约与输入规约，Pass@1提升29.6%。","au":["Zhao Tian","Junjie Chen"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["specification alignment","code generation","requirement engineering","LLM","Pass@1"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/55/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.01313"},{"id":"p00542","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Scrub It Out! Erasing Sensitive Memorization in Code Language Models via Machine Unlearning","tz":"清除干净！通过机器遗忘擦除代码语言模型中的敏感记忆","a":"While Code Language Models (CLMs) have demonstrated superior performance in software engineering tasks such as code generation and code summarization, recent empirical studies reveal a critical privacy vulnerability: these models exhibit unintended memorization of sensitive training data, enabling verbatim reproduction of confidential information when specifically prompted. To address this issue, several approaches, including dataset deduplication and differential privacy augmentation, have been proposed. However, these methods require full-model retraining for deployed CLMs, which incurs substantial computational costs. In this paper, we aim to answer the following research question: Can sensitive information memorized by CLMs be erased effectively and efficiently? We conduct a pioneering investigation into erasing sensitive memorization in CLMs through machine unlearning—a post hoc modification approach that removes specific information from trained models without requiring full retraining. Specifically, we first quantify the memorization risks of sensitive data within CLM training datasets and curate a high-risk dataset of 50,000 sensitive memorization samples by identifying and selecting vulnerable elements as unlearning targets. We investigate two widely-used gradient ascent-based unlearning approaches: the vanilla method and the constraint-based method, and introduce an advanced variant, termed CodeEraser, which selectively unlearns sensitive memorization elements in code while preserving the structural integrity and functional correctness of the surrounding code. Extensive experiments on three families of CLMs, i.e., CodeParrot, CodeGen-Mono and Qwen2.5-Coder, validate the effectiveness and efficiency of CodeEraser in erasing targeted sensitive memorization while maintaining model utility.","az":"尽管代码语言模型（CLM）在代码生成、代码摘要等软件工程任务上表现优异，最近的实证研究揭示了一个关键的隐私脆弱性：这些模型会非预期地记忆敏感训练数据，在被特定提示时能够逐字复现机密信息。为解决该问题，人们提出了数据集去重、差分隐私增强等若干方法。然而，这些方法对已部署的 CLM 需要全模型重新训练，带来巨大的计算开销。本文旨在回答如下研究问题：CLM 所记忆的敏感信息能否被有效且高效地擦除？我们开创性地研究了通过机器遗忘（machine unlearning）来擦除 CLM 中敏感记忆——这是一种事后修改方法，可在不需要完整重训的前提下从已训练模型中移除特定信息。具体而言，我们首先量化了 CLM 训练数据集中敏感数据的记忆风险，并通过识别与筛选脆弱元素作为遗忘目标，构建了一个包含 50,000 条敏感记忆样本的高风险数据集。我们研究了两种广泛使用的基于梯度上升的遗忘方法：朴素方法与基于约束的方法，并提出了一个进阶变体 CodeEraser，它有选择地遗忘代码中的敏感记忆元素，同时保持周围代码的结构完整性与功能正确性。在三个系列的 CLM（即 CodeParrot、CodeGen-Mono 和 Qwen2.5-Coder）上的大量实验验证了 CodeEraser 在擦除目标敏感记忆的同时保持模型效用方面的有效性与高效性。","tl":"选择性遗忘代码中敏感片段，保住周边代码功能正确性。","au":["Zhaoyang Chu","Yao Wan","Zhikun Zhang","Di Wang","Zhou Yang","Hongyu Zhang","Pan Zhou","Xuanhua Shi","Hai Jin","David Lo"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"privacy-memorization-watermarking-and-unlearning","tg":["security","llm-based"],"kw":["machine unlearning","code language models","sensitive memorization","privacy","gradient ascent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/56/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13755"},{"id":"p00543","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM-based Vulnerability Discovery through the Lens of Code Metrics","tz":"从代码度量视角审视基于大模型的漏洞发现","a":"Large language models (LLMs) excel in many tasks of software engineering, yet progress in leveraging them for vulnerability discovery has stalled in recent years. To understand this phenomenon, we investigate LLMs through the lens of classic code metrics. Surprisingly, we find that a classifier trained solely on these metrics performs on par with state-of-the-art LLMs for vulnerability discovery. A root-cause analysis reveals a strong correlation and a causal effect between LLMs and code metrics: When the value of a metric is changed, LLM predictions tend to shift by a corresponding magnitude. This dependency suggests that LLMs operate at a similarly shallow level as code metrics, limiting their ability to grasp complex patterns and fully realize their potential in vulnerability discovery.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在许多软件工程任务上表现出色，但近年来利用它们进行漏洞发现的进展却停滞不前。为理解这一现象，我们通过经典代码度量的视角来考察 LLM。令人意外的是，我们发现仅基于这些度量训练的分类器在漏洞发现上的表现与最先进的 LLM 相当。根因分析揭示了 LLM 与代码度量之间存在强相关性以及因果效应：当某个度量的取值被改变时，LLM 的预测倾向于发生相应幅度的偏移。这种依赖关系表明，LLM 的运作层次与代码度量同样浅层，从而限制了它们把握复杂模式、在漏洞发现中充分发挥潜力的能力。","tl":"证明LLM漏洞检测与经典代码度量同样浅层且存在因果依赖。","au":["Felix Weissberg","Lukas Pirch","Erik Imgrund","Jonas Möller","Thorsten Eisenhofer","Konrad Rieck"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"interpretability-and-model-internals","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["vulnerability discovery","code metrics","LLM","causal analysis","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/57/x","pu":"https://mlsec.org/docs/2026-icse.pdf"},{"id":"p00544","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An LLM Agentic Approach for Legal-Critical Software: A Case Study for Tax Prep Software","tz":"面向法律关键型软件的大模型智能体方法：以报税软件为案例","a":"As Large Language Models (LLMs) continue to advance in their ability to process natural and programming languages, they show promise in complex translation tasks across domains with strict compliance requirements. However, ensuring consistency in legally critical domains remains challenging due to inherent limitations, such as natural language ambiguity and the tendency to generate hallucinations. This paper explores an agentic approach that leverages LLMs for legal-critical software development. We use U.S. federal tax preparation software as a representative case study, where natural language tax code must be precisely translated into executable logic, ensuring high fidelity to regulatory requirements. A fundamental challenge in developing legally critical software from specifications is the generation of test cases, which suffers from the oracle problem. Determining the correct output for a given scenario often requires interpreting legal statutes through a dialogic process, necessitating input from legal experts or independent reviewers. Prior research has proposed metamorphic testing as a potential solution by evaluating equivalence across similarly situated individuals. This paper adopts and extends this approach by introducing LLM agents specialized in generating metamorphic test cases. A key innovation of our work is a higher-order generalization of metamorphic tests, motivated by our case study of tax preparation software, wherein system outputs are analyzed across comparative shifts among similar individuals. Since manually generating such higher-order relations is tedious and error-prone, our agentic paradigm is well-suited for automating test case generation. We design and implement cohorts of LLM-based agents, each simulating roles in real-world software development teams handling legal documents. Our framework includes a metamorphic testing agent that provides counterexamples while translating tax code into executable software logic. Our findings indicate that our agentic approach, utilizing smaller language models (e.g., GPT-4o-mini), outperforms frontier models (e.g., GPT-4o and Claude-3.5) in complex tax code generation scenarios, achieving a worst-case pass rate of 45% compared to 9%–15%. Furthermore, our evaluations reveal that incorporating higher-order metamorphic testing improves the pass rate in the most challenging scenarios by up to 50%. Our results present a compelling case for using agentic LLM-driven methodologies to generate robust and trustworthy legal-critical software from natural language specifications.","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）在处理自然语言与编程语言方面不断进步，它们在合规要求严格的领域的复杂翻译任务上展现出潜力。然而，由于自然语言的歧义性和产生幻觉的倾向等固有局限，在法律关键领域确保一致性仍具挑战。本文探索一种利用 LLM 进行法律关键型软件开发的智能体方法。我们以美国联邦报税软件作为代表性案例研究，其中自然语言的税法条文必须被精确翻译为可执行逻辑，并高度忠实于监管要求。从规约开发法律关键型软件的一个根本挑战是测试用例的生成，它受制于预言（oracle）问题。要确定给定情境下的正确输出，往往需要通过对话式过程来解读法律条文，需要法律专家或独立评审者的输入。已有研究提出蜕变测试作为潜在解法，即评估处境相似的个体之间的等价性。本文采纳并扩展了这一思路，引入了专门生成蜕变测试用例的 LLM 智能体。我们工作的一项关键创新是对蜕变测试的高阶泛化，其动机来自报税软件案例：系统输出是在相似个体之间的对比性变化中被分析的。由于手工构造这类高阶关系既繁琐又易错，我们的智能体范式非常适合自动化测试用例生成。我们设计并实现了若干组基于 LLM 的智能体，各自模拟真实软件开发团队中处理法律文档的角色。我们的框架包含一个蜕变测试智能体，在把税法翻译为可执行软件逻辑的过程中提供反例。我们的发现表明，采用较小语言模型（如 GPT-4o-mini）的智能体方法在复杂税法代码生成场景中优于前沿模型（如 GPT-4o 和 Claude-3.5），最差情况下的通过率为 45%，而后者仅为 9%–15%。此外，我们的评估显示，引入高阶蜕变测试可将最具挑战场景下的通过率最多提升 50%。我们的结果为使用基于智能体的 LLM 方法从自然语言规约生成健壮且可信的法律关键型软件提供了有力论据。","tl":"提出高阶蜕变关系与智能体，破解法规软件的测试预言难题。","au":["Sina Gogani Khiabani","Ashutosh Trivedi","Diptikalyan Saha","Saeid Tizpaz-Niari"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["metamorphic testing","legal-critical software","tax preparation","LLM agents","oracle problem"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/58/x"},{"id":"p00545","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Are “Solved Issues” in SWE-bench Really Solved Correctly? An Empirical Study","tz":"SWE-bench 中“已解决的 Issue”真的解对了吗？一项实证研究","a":"Automated issue solving aims to resolve real-world issues in software repositories. The most popular benchmarks for automated issue solving are SWE-bench and its human-filtered subset SWEbench Verified, which are widely used to evaluate foundation models and software engineering agents. These benchmarks leverage testing to validate generated patches. However, because testing is rarely exhaustive, a patch may pass the tests but nevertheless fail to match the developers’ expectations. Unfortunately, it is currently unclear to what extent evaluations performed with SWE-bench suffer from such plausible but incorrect patches. This paper presents an in-depth empirical study of the correctness of plausible patches generated by three state-of-the-art issue-solving tools (CodeStory, LearnByInteract, and OpenHands) evaluated on SWE-bench Verified. We extensively test and inspect generated patches, and compare them against human-written ground truth patches. The core of our methodology is a novel technique PatchDiff for differential patch testing, which automatically exposes behavioral discrepancies between two patches. Our findings reveal critical weaknesses in SWE-bench’s patch validation mechanism, which causes 7.8% of all patches to count as “correct” while failing the developer-written test suite. Moreover, our novel automated technique reveals that even more (29.6%) plausible patches induce different behavior than the ground truth patches. These behavioral differences are often due to similar, but divergent implementations (46.8%) and due to generated patches that adapt more behavior than the ground truth patches (27.3%). Our manual inspection shows that 28.6% of behaviorally divergent patches are certainly incorrect. Combined, the different weaknesses lead to an inflation of reported resolution rates by 6.2 absolute percent points. Our findings are a call to arms for more robust and reliable evaluation of issue-solving tools. We envision our automated differential patch testing technique to be useful for this purpose.","az":"自动 Issue 求解旨在解决软件仓库中的真实问题。最流行的自动 Issue 求解基准是 SWE-bench 及其经人工筛选的子集 SWE-bench Verified，它们被广泛用于评估基础模型与软件工程智能体。这些基准依靠测试来验证生成的补丁。然而，由于测试很少是穷尽的，一个补丁可能通过测试却仍不符合开发者的预期。遗憾的是，目前尚不清楚基于 SWE-bench 的评估在多大程度上受到这类“看似可信但实则错误”的补丁的影响。本文对三款最先进的 Issue 求解工具（CodeStory、LearnByInteract 和 OpenHands）在 SWE-bench Verified 上生成的可信补丁的正确性开展了深入的实证研究。我们对生成的补丁进行了广泛的测试与检查，并将其与人工编写的基准真值补丁进行比较。我们方法论的核心是一项新技术 PatchDiff，用于差分补丁测试，它能自动暴露两个补丁之间的行为差异。我们的发现揭示了 SWE-bench 补丁验证机制的关键缺陷：有 7.8% 的补丁被计为“正确”，却无法通过开发者编写的测试套件。此外，我们的新型自动化技术揭示，更多（29.6%）的可信补丁所引发的行为与基准真值补丁不同。这些行为差异往往源于相似但有分歧的实现（46.8%），以及生成的补丁比基准真值补丁适配了更多行为（27.3%）。我们的人工检查显示，28.6% 行为发散的补丁确定是错误的。综合来看，这些不同的缺陷导致报告的解决率被虚高了 6.2 个百分点。我们的发现是对更健壮、更可靠的 Issue 求解工具评估的呼吁。我们设想我们的自动差分补丁测试技术将对此有所助益。","tl":"差分补丁测试揭示SWE-bench解决率虚高6.2个百分点。","au":["You Wang","Michael Pradel","Zhongxin Liu"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["SWE-bench","patch correctness","differential patch testing","plausible patches","benchmark validity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/59/x"},{"id":"p00546","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CoReX: Context-Aware Refinement-Based Slicing for Debugging Regression Failures","tz":"CoReX：面向回归失效调试的上下文感知精化式切片","a":"Troubleshooting regression failures is one of the most frequent yet time-consuming development tasks. To help with this task, numerous approaches aim to narrow down developers’ attention to the subset of code statements relevant to the failure. The most prominent of these approaches are based on program slicing, as slicing not only identifies a subset of relevant statements but also maintains the flow of information between these statements. By surveying more than 50 practitioners from eight different countries, we observe that existing dual-version slicing-based approaches have two main limitations: (a) to minimize the number of statements presented to the developer, they omit contextual information required to truly understand the failure and (b) to keep information propagation between the statements in the slice intact, they include lengthy computations that are not necessary to understand the failure. We use these observations to define a new dual-version slicing approach for regression scenarios, called CoReX. We quantitatively evaluate CoReX on a large number of subjects and metrics used in prior work, calculating the reduction rate it achieves and its alignment with developers’ expectations. The results of our evaluation show that CoReX outperforms other existing dual-version slicing techniques on both metrics. We believe our work provides grounds for efficient integration of slicing-based approaches into development workflows.","az":"排查回归失效是最频繁却也最耗时的开发任务之一。为帮助完成这一任务，众多方法致力于把开发者的注意力收敛到与失效相关的代码语句子集上。其中最突出的是基于程序切片的方法，因为切片不仅能识别相关语句的子集，还能保持这些语句之间的信息流。通过对来自八个国家的 50 多位从业者进行调研，我们观察到现有的双版本切片方法存在两个主要局限：（a）为了尽量减少呈现给开发者的语句数量，它们省略了真正理解失效所必需的上下文信息；（b）为了保持切片中语句之间信息传播的完整性，它们包含了理解失效并不必要的冗长计算。我们据此定义了一种针对回归场景的新型双版本切片方法，称为 CoReX。我们在大量对象和先前工作使用的指标上对 CoReX 进行定量评估，计算其达到的缩减率及其与开发者预期的契合度。评估结果表明，CoReX 在这两个指标上都优于其他现有的双版本切片技术。我们相信这项工作为把基于切片的方法高效集成到开发工作流中奠定了基础。","tl":"双版本切片补上理解失效所需上下文并剪掉冗长计算。","au":["Sahar Badihi","Julia Rubin"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","human-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["program slicing","regression failure","debugging","dual-version slicing","practitioner survey"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/60/x","pu":"https://people.ece.ubc.ca/~mjulia/publications/2026_CoReX_ICSE.pdf"},{"id":"p00547","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Agentic Predicates Reasoning for Directed Fuzzing","tz":"面向定向模糊测试的智能体式谓词推理","a":"Directed fuzzing aims to find program inputs that lead to specified target states, which has broad applications, such as debugging system crashes, confirming reported bugs, and generating exploits for potential vulnerabilities. This task is inherently challenging because target states are often deeply nested in the program, while the search space manifested by numerous possible program inputs and their corresponding execution paths is prohibitively large. Existing approaches rely on branch distances or manually-specified constraints to guide the search; however, the branches alone are often insufficient to precisely characterize progress toward reaching the target states, while the manually specified constraints are often tailored for specific bug types and thus difficult to generalize to diverse target states and programs. We present Locus, a novel framework to improve the efficiency of directed fuzzing. Our key insight is to represent the fuzzing progress as reaching semantically meaningful states — the synthetic intermediate milestones before reaching the target states. The predicates capturing these states, when used to instrument the program under fuzz, can early reject executions impossible to reach the target states, while providing additional coverage guidance. Generating these predicates requires sophisticated reasoning about the target states and an expert-level understanding of program behaviors. To automate this task and generalize to diverse programs, Locus features an agentic framework equipped with various program analysis tools to synthesize and iteratively refine the candidate predicates, while ensuring the predicates strictly relax the target states to prevent false rejection via symbolic execution. Our evaluation shows that Locus substantially improves the efficiency of eight state-of-the-art fuzzers in discovering real-world vulnerabilities, including six previously unknown bugs, achieving an average speedup of 50.4 . So far, Locus has found six previously unpatched bugs, with one already acknowledged with a draft patch.","az":"定向模糊测试旨在找到能够导致指定目标状态的程序输入，其应用广泛，例如调试系统崩溃、确认已报告的缺陷以及为潜在漏洞生成利用。这项任务本身颇具挑战，因为目标状态往往深藏于程序内部，而由大量可能的程序输入及其对应执行路径构成的搜索空间极为庞大。现有方法依赖分支距离或人工指定的约束来引导搜索；然而，仅凭分支往往不足以精确刻画朝目标状态推进的进展，而人工指定的约束通常是为特定缺陷类型定制的，因而难以推广到多样的目标状态和程序。我们提出 Locus，一个提升定向模糊测试效率的新框架。我们的关键洞见是把模糊测试的进展表示为到达语义上有意义的状态——即在抵达目标状态之前的合成中间里程碑。刻画这些状态的谓词在被插桩进被测程序后，能够尽早拒绝不可能到达目标状态的执行，同时提供额外的覆盖引导。生成这些谓词需要对目标状态进行复杂推理，以及专家级的程序行为理解。为自动化这一任务并泛化到多样的程序，Locus 采用一个配备了多种程序分析工具的智能体框架来合成并迭代精化候选谓词，同时通过符号执行确保谓词严格放松目标状态，以防止错误拒绝。我们的评估表明，Locus 大幅提升了八款最先进模糊测试器发现真实漏洞的效率，包括发现六个此前未知的缺陷，平均加速达 50.4 倍。迄今为止，Locus 已找到六个尚未修补的缺陷，其中一个已获确认并有了补丁草案。","tl":"智能体合成中间里程碑谓词做插桩，定向模糊测试提速50倍。","au":["Jie Zhu","Chihao Shen","Ziyang Li","Jiahao Yu","Yizheng Chen","Kexin Pei"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["agentic","llm-based","security"],"kw":["directed fuzzing","predicate synthesis","agentic framework","symbolic execution","program instrumentation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/61/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.21302"},{"id":"p00548","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Is My RPC Response Reliable? Detecting RPC Bugs in Blockchain Client under Context","tz":"我的 RPC 响应可靠吗？在上下文中检测区块链客户端的 RPC 缺陷","a":"Blockchain clients are fundamental software for running blockchain nodes. They provide users with various RPC (Remote Procedure Call) interfaces to interact with the blockchain. These RPC methods are expected to follow the same specification across different blockchain nodes, providing users with seamless interaction. However, there have been continuous reports on various RPC bugs that can cause unexpected responses or even Denial of Service weakness. Existing studies on blockchain RPC bug detection mainly focus on generating the RPC method calls for testing blockchain clients. However, a wide range of the reported RPC bugs are triggered in various blockchain contexts. To the best of our knowledge, little attention is paid to generating proper contexts that can trigger these context-dependent RPC bugs. In this work, we propose EthCRAFT, a Context-aware RPC Analysis and Fuzzing Tool for client RPC bug detection. EthCRAFT first proposes to explore the state transition program space of blockchain clients and generate various transactions to construct the context. EthCRAFT then designs a context-aware RPC method call generation method to send RPC calls to the blockchain clients. The responses of 5 different client implementations are used as cross-referring oracles to detect the RPC bugs. We evaluate EthCRAFT on real-world RPC bugs collected from the GitHub issues of Ethereum client implementations. Experiment results show that EthCRAFT outperforms existing client RPC detectors by detecting more RPC bugs. Moreover, EthCRAFT has found six new bugs in major Ethereum clients and reported them to the developers. One of the bug fixes has been written into breaking changes in the client’s updates. Three of our bug reports have been offered a vulnerability bounty by the Ethereum Foundation.","az":"区块链客户端是运行区块链节点的基础软件。它们为用户提供各种 RPC（远程过程调用）接口以与区块链交互。这些 RPC 方法本应在不同区块链节点上遵循相同的规范，为用户提供无缝的交互体验。然而，关于各类 RPC 缺陷的报告不断出现，它们可能导致非预期响应甚至拒绝服务弱点。已有的区块链 RPC 缺陷检测研究主要聚焦于生成 RPC 方法调用来测试区块链客户端。然而，大量已报告的 RPC 缺陷是在各种区块链上下文中被触发的。据我们所知，几乎没有工作关注如何生成能够触发这些上下文相关 RPC 缺陷的恰当上下文。在本工作中，我们提出 EthCRAFT，一个用于客户端 RPC 缺陷检测的上下文感知 RPC 分析与模糊测试工具。EthCRAFT 首先提出探索区块链客户端的状态转移程序空间，并生成各种交易来构造上下文。随后，EthCRAFT 设计了一种上下文感知的 RPC 方法调用生成方法，向区块链客户端发送 RPC 调用。5 种不同客户端实现的响应被用作交叉比对的预言来检测 RPC 缺陷。我们在从以太坊客户端实现的 GitHub issue 中收集的真实 RPC 缺陷上评估 EthCRAFT。实验结果表明，EthCRAFT 检出的 RPC 缺陷多于现有的客户端 RPC 检测器。此外，EthCRAFT 在主流以太坊客户端中发现了六个新缺陷并报告给开发者。其中一个缺陷修复已被写入客户端更新的破坏性变更中。我们的三份缺陷报告获得了以太坊基金会的漏洞赏金。","tl":"先造交易构建区块链上下文，再做跨客户端差分RPC模糊测试。","au":["Zhijie Zhong","Yuhong Nan","Mingxi Ye","Qing Xue","Jiashui Wang","Long Liu","Xinlei Ying","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["blockchain client","RPC bug detection","context-aware fuzzing","differential oracle","Ethereum"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/62/x"},{"id":"p00549","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Cognitive Biases in LLM-Assisted Software Development","tz":"大模型辅助软件开发中的认知偏差","a":"The widespread adoption of Large Language Models (LLMs) in software development is transforming programming from a generative activity into one dominated by prompt engineering and AI-generated solution evaluation. This shift opens the pathway for new cognitive challenges that amplify existing decision-making biases or create entirely novel ones. One such type of challenge is cognitive biases, which are thinking patterns that lead people away from logical reasoning, often resulting in errors, poor decisions, or sub-optimal actions. Despite LLMs becoming integral to modern development workflows, we lack a systematic understanding of how cognitive biases manifest and impact developer decision-making in these AI-collaborative contexts. This paper presents the first comprehensive study of cognitive biases in LLM-assisted programming using a mixed-methods approach of observational studies with n=14 student and professional developers, followed by surveys with n=22 additional developers. First, we qualitatively analyze our data based on bias categorization in the traditional non-LLM workflow reported in prior work. Our findings suggest that the traditional software development biases are inadequate to explain/understand why LLM-related actions are more likely to be biased. Through systematic analysis of 239 cognitive bias types, we develop a novel taxonomy of 15 bias categories of 90 biases specific to developer-LLM interactions, validated with cognitive psychologists. We found that 48.8% of total programmer actions are biased, and programmer-LLM interactions included 56.4% of biased actions. Based on our survey analysis, we present practical tools and practices for programmers, along with recommendations for LLM-based code generation tool builders to help mitigate cognitive biases in human-AI programming.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在软件开发中的广泛采用，正把编程从一种生成性活动转变为以提示工程和对 AI 生成方案的评估为主的活动。这一转变为新的认知挑战打开了通道，它们会放大既有的决策偏差，或制造全新的偏差。其中一类挑战就是认知偏差，即那些使人偏离逻辑推理的思维模式，常常导致错误、糟糕的决策或次优的行动。尽管 LLM 已成为现代开发工作流不可或缺的一部分，我们仍缺乏对认知偏差在这些人机协作情境中如何显现、以及如何影响开发者决策的系统性理解。本文采用混合方法首次对大模型辅助编程中的认知偏差开展了全面研究：先对 n=14 名学生与专业开发者进行观察性研究，随后对另外 n=22 名开发者进行问卷调查。首先，我们依据先前工作报告的传统非 LLM 工作流中的偏差分类对数据进行定性分析。我们的发现表明，传统的软件开发偏差不足以解释/理解为何与 LLM 相关的行为更容易带有偏差。通过对 239 种认知偏差类型的系统分析，我们提出了一个包含 15 个偏差类别、共 90 种偏差的新分类体系，专门针对开发者与 LLM 的交互，并由认知心理学家进行了验证。我们发现，程序员的全部操作中有 48.8% 带有偏差，而程序员与 LLM 的交互中有 56.4% 的操作带有偏差。基于问卷分析，我们为程序员提供了可操作的工具与实践，并为基于 LLM 的代码生成工具构建者提出建议，以帮助缓解人机协作编程中的认知偏差。","tl":"首次提出面向开发者-LLM交互的90种认知偏差分类体系。","au":["Xinyi Zhou","Zeinabsadat Saghi","Sadra Sabouri","Rahul Pandita","Mollie McGuire","Souti Chattopadhyay"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["human-study","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["cognitive bias","LLM-assisted programming","observational study","developer decision-making","taxonomy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/63/x"},{"id":"p00550","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CCLInsight: Unveiling Insights in GPU Collective Communication Libraries via Primitive-Centric Analysis","tz":"CCLInsight：以原语为中心的分析揭示 GPU 集合通信库的洞见","a":"As distributed AI workloads scale in complexity, GPU-based collective communication libraries (xCCLs) such as NCCL are becoming increasingly critical for efficient data movement across heterogeneous hardware. Characterizing and optimizing the interactions between hardware architectures, communication algorithm designs, and low-level primitive configurations is essential to fully utilize GPU and interconnect resources while ensuring scalability. However, existing analysis methods often lack depth, limiting optimization insights, leaving significant performance gains untapped, or lack generality. To address these limitations, we propose a novel primitive-based profiling and analysis method that integrates architectural, algorithmic, and primitive-level insights to comprehensively qualify and quantify performance-critical parameters in GPU-based CCLs that we implement and test in our tool CCLInsight. Evaluating three large-scale GPU clusters with diverse GPU architectures featuring up to 64 H100s, 64 RTX 5000s, and 256 A100s, CCLInsight uncovers critical parameter influences on communication efficiency and scalability, as well as exposing a new CCL performance scaling law. Adjusting parameters based on this analysis, we demonstrate a 43.90% improvement in NCCL and a 40.64× speedup in MSCCL over default configurations in the collective communication microbenchmark, while also improving NCCL and MSCCL performance on LLM training workloads (GPT- 3, LLaMA2, DeepSeek-R1) by up to 2.27× and 3.00×, respectively, on a 256-GPU H200 cluster. These contributions establish CCLInsight as a useful tool for xCCL characterization and optimization in distributed AI environments.","az":"随着分布式 AI 工作负载在复杂度上不断扩展，诸如 NCCL 之类基于 GPU 的集合通信库（xCCL）对于在异构硬件间高效搬运数据变得愈发关键。刻画并优化硬件架构、通信算法设计与底层原语配置之间的相互作用，对于充分利用 GPU 与互连资源并确保可扩展性至关重要。然而，现有分析方法往往深度不足，限制了优化洞见，使显著的性能收益未被挖掘，或者缺乏通用性。为突破这些限制，我们提出一种新颖的基于原语的剖析与分析方法，融合架构、算法与原语层面的洞见，全面地定性并定量刻画基于 GPU 的 CCL 中对性能起关键作用的参数；我们在工具 CCLInsight 中实现并测试了该方法。在三个大规模 GPU 集群（涵盖多样的 GPU 架构，分别最多包含 64 块 H100、64 块 RTX 5000 和 256 块 A100）上的评估中，CCLInsight 揭示了关键参数对通信效率与可扩展性的影响，并揭示出一条新的 CCL 性能扩展定律。基于该分析调整参数后，我们在集合通信微基准上相较默认配置实现了 NCCL 43.90% 的提升和 MSCCL 40.64 倍的加速；同时在 256 块 GPU 的 H200 集群上，把 NCCL 与 MSCCL 在 LLM 训练工作负载（GPT-3、LLaMA2、DeepSeek-R1）上的性能分别提升最多 2.27 倍和 3.00 倍。这些贡献确立了 CCLInsight 作为分布式 AI 环境中 xCCL 刻画与优化的实用工具。","tl":"以通信原语为中心剖析xCCL，揭示新的性能扩展定律。","au":["Liuyao Dai","Adam Weingram","Weicong Chen","Xiaoyi Lu"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["collective communication library","NCCL","GPU cluster","performance profiling","distributed training"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/64/x"},{"id":"p00551","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"The Software Infrastructure Attitude Scale (SIAS): A Questionnaire Instrument for Measuring Professionals’ Attitudes Toward Technical and Sociotechnical Infrastructure","tz":"软件基础设施态度量表（SIAS）：一种测量从业者对技术性与社会技术性基础设施态度的问卷工具","a":"Context: Recent software engineering (SE) research has highlighted the need for sociotechnical research, implying a demand for customized psychometric scales. Objective: We define the concepts of technical and sociotechnical infrastructure in software engineering, and develop and validate a psychometric scale that measures attitudes toward them. Method: Grounded in theories of infrastructure, attitudes, and prior work on psychometric measurement, we defined the target constructs and generated scale items. The scale was administered to 225 software professionals and evaluated using a split sample. We conducted an exploratory factor analysis (EFA) on one half of the sample to uncover the underlying factor structure and performed a confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) on the other half to validate the structure. Further analyses with the whole sample assessed face, criterion-related, and discriminant validity. Results: EFA supported a two-factor structure (technical and sociotechnical infrastructure), accounting for 65% of the total variance with strong loadings. CFA confirmed excellent model fit. Face and content validity were supported by the item content reflecting cognitive, affective, and behavioral components. Both subscales were correlated with job satisfaction, perceived autonomy, and feedback from the job itself, supporting convergent validity. Regression analysis supported criterion-related validity, while the Heterotrait-Monotrait ratio of correlations (HTMT), the Fornell-Larcker criterion, and model comparison all supported discriminant validity. Discussion: The resulting scale is a valid instrument for measuring attitudes toward technical and sociotechnical infrastructure in software engineering research. Our work contributes to ongoing efforts to integrate psychological measurement rigor into empirical and behavioral software engineering research.","az":"背景：近期的软件工程（SE）研究强调了开展社会技术研究的必要性，这意味着需要定制化的心理测量量表。目标：我们界定了软件工程中技术性基础设施与社会技术性基础设施的概念，并开发并验证了一套测量人们对它们态度的心理测量量表。方法：以基础设施理论、态度理论以及以往心理测量工作的研究为基础，我们定义了目标构念并生成了量表条目。该量表面向 225 名软件从业者施测，并采用分半样本进行评估。我们在一半样本上进行探索性因子分析（EFA）以揭示潜在的因子结构，并在另一半样本上进行验证性因子分析（CFA）以验证该结构。基于全样本的进一步分析评估了表面效度、效标关联效度与区分效度。结果：EFA 支持两因子结构（技术性基础设施与社会技术性基础设施），累计解释了总方差的 65%，且载荷较高。CFA 确认模型拟合优异。条目内容涵盖认知、情感与行为成分，支持了表面效度与内容效度。两个分量表均与工作满意度、感知自主性以及工作本身提供的反馈相关，支持了聚合效度。回归分析支持了效标关联效度，而异质-单质相关比（HTMT）、Fornell-Larcker 准则以及模型比较均支持了区分效度。讨论：所得量表是在软件工程研究中测量对技术性与社会技术性基础设施态度的有效工具。我们的工作为将心理测量的严谨性融入实证与行为软件工程研究的持续努力作出了贡献。","tl":"首个经效度验证的软件基础设施态度心理测量量表。","au":["Miikka Kuutila","Paul Ralph","Huilian Sophie Qiu","Ronnie de Souza Santos","Morakot Choetkiertikul","Amin Milani Fard","Rana Alkadhi","Xavier Devroey","Gregorio Robles","Hideaki Hata","Sebastian Baltes","Vladimir Kovalenko","Shalini Chakraborty","Eray Tüzün","Hera Arif","Gianisa Adisaputri","kelly Garces Pernett","Anielle Severo Lisboa de Andrade","Eyram Amedzor","Bimpe Ayoola","Keisha Gaspard-Chickoree","Arazoo Hoseyni"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","empirical-study"],"kw":["psychometric scale","sociotechnical infrastructure","factor analysis","behavioral software engineering","survey"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/65/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.00855"},{"id":"p00552","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Light over Heavy: Automated Performance Requirements Quantification with Linguistic Inducement","tz":"以轻胜重：借助语言学诱导的性能需求自动量化","a":"Elicited performance requirements need to be quantified for compliance in different engineering tasks, e.g., configuration tuning and performance testing. Much existing work has relied on manual quantification, which is expensive and error-prone due to the imprecision. In this paper, we present LQPR, a highly efficient automatic approach for performance requirements quantification. LQPR relies on a new theoretical framework that converts quantification as a classification problem. Despite the prevalent applications of Large Language Models (LLMs) for requirement analytics, LQPR takes a different perspective to address the classification: we observed that performance requirements can exhibit strong patterns and are often short/concise, therefore we design a lightweight linguistically induced matching mechanism. We compare LQPR against nine state-of-the-art learning-based approaches over diverse datasets, demonstrating that it is ranked as the sole best for 88% or more cases with two orders less cost. Our work proves that, at least for performance requirement quantification, specialized methods can be more suitable than the general LLM-driven approaches.","az":"已获取的性能需求需要被量化，以便在不同工程任务（例如配置调优和性能测试）中检查是否达标。已有的大量工作依赖人工量化，这既昂贵又因不精确而易出错。本文提出 LQPR，一种高效的性能需求自动量化方法。LQPR 基于一个新的理论框架，将量化转化为分类问题。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在需求分析中已被广泛应用，LQPR 却采用了不同视角来处理该分类问题：我们观察到性能需求往往表现出很强的模式性且通常简短、凝练，因此我们设计了一种轻量级的语言学诱导匹配机制。我们在多样化数据集上将 LQPR 与九种最先进的基于学习的方法进行了比较，结果表明它在 88% 及以上的情形中被评为唯一最优，且成本低两个数量级。我们的工作证明，至少在性能需求量化这一任务上，专用方法可能比通用的 LLM 驱动方法更为合适。","tl":"把性能需求量化转成分类，用轻量语言学匹配胜过 LLM。","au":["Shihai Wang","Tao Chen"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["performance requirements","requirements quantification","linguistic matching","lightweight classification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/66/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.03421"},{"id":"p00553","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evaluating and Improving Automated Repository-Level Rust Issue Resolution with LLM-based Agents","tz":"评估并改进基于 LLM 智能体的仓库级 Rust Issue 自动求解","a":"The Rust programming language presents a steep learning curve and significant coding challenges, making the automation of issue resolution essential for its broader adoption. Recently, LLM-powered code agents have shown remarkable success in resolving complex software engineering tasks, yet their application to Rust has been limited by the absence of a large-scale, repository-level benchmark. To bridge this gap, we introduce Rust-SWE-bench, a benchmark comprising 500 real-world, repository-level software engineering tasks from 34 diverse and popular Rust repositories. We then perform a comprehensive study on Rust-SWE-bench with four representative agents and four state-of-the-art LLMs to establish a foundational understanding of their capabilities and limitations in the Rust ecosystem. Our extensive study reveals that while ReAct-style agents are promising, i.e., resolving up to 21.2% of issues, they are limited by two primary challenges: comprehending repository-wide code structure and complying with Rust’s strict type and trait semantics. We also find that issue reproduction is rather critical for task resolution. Inspired by these findings, we propose RUSTFORGER, a novel agentic approach that integrates an automated test environment setup with a Rust metaprogramming-driven dynamic tracing strategy to facilitate reliable issue reproduction and dynamic analysis. The evaluation shows that RUSTFORGER using Claude-Sonnet-3.7 significantly outperforms all baselines, resolving 28.6% of tasks on Rust-SWE-bench, i.e., a 34.9% improvement over the strongest baseline, and, in aggregate, uniquely solves 46 tasks that no other agent could solve across all adopted advanced LLMs.","az":"Rust 编程语言学习曲线陡峭、编码挑战显著，这使得 issue 求解的自动化对其更广泛的普及至关重要。近来，LLM 驱动的代码智能体在解决复杂软件工程任务上取得了显著成功，但由于缺乏大规模的仓库级基准，它们在 Rust 上的应用受到限制。为弥补这一空白，我们提出 Rust-SWE-bench，一个包含来自 34 个多样且流行的 Rust 仓库的 500 个真实世界仓库级软件工程任务的基准。随后我们在 Rust-SWE-bench 上，使用四种代表性智能体和四个最先进的 LLM 开展了全面研究，以建立对它们在 Rust 生态中能力与局限的基础性认识。我们的广泛研究表明，尽管 ReAct 风格的智能体前景可期，即最多可解决 21.2% 的 issue，但它们受制于两大挑战：理解仓库范围的代码结构，以及遵守 Rust 严格的类型与 trait 语义。我们还发现 issue 复现对任务求解相当关键。受这些发现启发，我们提出 RUSTFORGER，一种新颖的智能体式方法，它将自动化测试环境搭建与 Rust 元编程驱动的动态追踪策略相结合，以促成可靠的 issue 复现与动态分析。评估表明，使用 Claude-Sonnet-3.7 的 RUSTFORGER 显著优于所有基线，在 Rust-SWE-bench 上解决了 28.6% 的任务，即较最强基线提升 34.9%；并且总体上独占性地解决了 46 个在所有采用的先进 LLM 下其他智能体都无法解决的任务。","tl":"首个 Rust 仓库级 issue 基准，并用元编程追踪提升复现与求解率。","au":["Jiahong Xiang","Wenxiao He","Xihua Wang","Hongliang Tian","Yuqun Zhang"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["Rust-SWE-bench","issue resolution","LLM agents","dynamic tracing","issue reproduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/67/x"},{"id":"p00554","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Unlocking the Silent Needs: Business-Logic-Driven Iterative Requirements Auto-completion","tz":"解锁沉默的需求：业务逻辑驱动的迭代式需求自动补全","a":"To tackle the dual challenges of incomplete requirements and hallucinations in large language models (LLMs), this paper proposes a business-logic-driven iterative requirements auto-completion approach named ReqCompleter. By treating the use case – entity– operation” triplet as the smallest computable closed loop, ReqCompleter adopts a model-driven iterative mechanism. First, a use-case model, an E-R diagram, and a CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) matrix are fused into a unified semantic framework. Next, gaps in the CRUD matrix act as triggers to iteratively detect missing functionalities, while the E-R diagram delimits entity boundaries to steer the LLM toward generating requirements within a controlled scope. We evaluate our approach across seven cases in e-commerce, logistics, public safety and other domains. Compared to general-purpose LLMs, it improves requirements completeness rate by 20%-88% while reducing hallucination rate by 2.4%-13.9%. To the best of our knowledge, this work represents the first tight coupling of classical requirements engineering models with generative AI, establishing an automated closed-loop system that delivers what’s missing, as needed\" under explicit business logic constraints. This opens a new and practical technical pathway for high-quality, explainable, and continuously evolvable requirements engineering.","az":"为应对需求不完整与大语言模型（LLM）幻觉这两大挑战，本文提出一种业务逻辑驱动的迭代式需求自动补全方法，名为 ReqCompleter。通过将“用例—实体—操作”三元组视为最小可计算闭环，ReqCompleter 采用模型驱动的迭代机制。首先，将用例模型、E-R 图和 CRUD（增、查、改、删）矩阵融合为统一的语义框架。其次，以 CRUD 矩阵中的空缺作为触发器，迭代地检测缺失功能，同时由 E-R 图界定实体边界，引导 LLM 在受控范围内生成需求。我们在电子商务、物流、公共安全等领域的七个案例上评估了该方法。与通用 LLM 相比，它将需求完整率提升了 20%–88%，同时将幻觉率降低了 2.4%–13.9%。据我们所知，本工作首次将经典需求工程模型与生成式 AI 紧密耦合，建立了在显式业务逻辑约束下“按需交付所缺内容”的自动化闭环系统。这为高质量、可解释且可持续演化的需求工程开辟了一条新的、实用的技术路径。","tl":"用 CRUD 矩阵空缺触发 LLM 迭代补全缺失需求并抑制幻觉。","au":["Zhujun Wu","Xiaohong Chen","Zhi Jin","Ming Hu","Dongming Jin"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["requirements completion","CRUD matrix","E-R diagram","LLM hallucination","requirements engineering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/68/x"},{"id":"p00555","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CREME: Robustness Enhancement of Code LLMs via Layer-Aware Model Editing","tz":"CREME：通过层感知模型编辑增强代码大模型的鲁棒性","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated impressive capabilities in code generation, where the natural language prompt plays a crucial role in conveying user intent to the model. However, prior studies have shown that LLMs are highly sensitive to prompt perturbations. Minor modifications in wording, syntax, or formatting can significantly reduce the functional correctness of generated code. As perturbations frequently occur in real-world scenarios, improving the robustness of LLMs to prompt perturbations is essential for ensuring reliable performance in practical code generation. In this paper, we introduce CREME (Code Robustness Enhancement via Model Editing), a novel approach that enhances LLM robustness through targeted parameter updates. CREME first identifies robustness-sensitive layers by comparing hidden states between an original prompt and its perturbed variant. Then, it performs lightweight parameter editing at the identified layer to reduce performance degradation. We evaluate CREME on two widely used code generation benchmarks (HumanEval and MBPP) along with their perturbed counterparts. Experimental results show that CREME improves Pass@1 accuracy by 63% on perturbed prompts while maintaining stable performance on clean inputs, with accuracy deviations within ±1%. Further analysis reveals that robustness-sensitive layers are primarily concentrated in the middle and deeper layers of the network, and their locations vary across different model architectures. These insights provide a valuable foundation for developing future robustness-oriented editing strategies.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在代码生成方面展现出令人印象深刻的能力，其中自然语言提示在向模型传达用户意图上起着关键作用。然而，已有研究表明 LLM 对提示扰动高度敏感：措辞、语法或格式上的细微改动都可能显著降低所生成代码的功能正确性。由于扰动在真实场景中频繁出现，提升 LLM 对提示扰动的鲁棒性对于保证实际代码生成中的可靠表现至关重要。本文提出 CREME（Code Robustness Enhancement via Model Editing），一种通过有针对性的参数更新来增强 LLM 鲁棒性的新方法。CREME 首先通过比较原始提示与其扰动变体之间的隐藏状态，识别出对鲁棒性敏感的层；随后在所识别的层上执行轻量级参数编辑，以减少性能下降。我们在两个广泛使用的代码生成基准（HumanEval 和 MBPP）及其扰动版本上评估了 CREME。实验结果表明，CREME 在扰动提示上将 Pass@1 准确率提升了 63%，同时在干净输入上保持性能稳定，准确率偏差在 ±1% 以内。进一步分析揭示，对鲁棒性敏感的层主要集中在网络的中层与深层，且其位置在不同模型架构之间存在差异。这些洞见为未来面向鲁棒性的编辑策略的开发提供了有价值的基础。","tl":"定位鲁棒性敏感层并做轻量参数编辑，抗提示扰动。","au":["Shuhan Liu","Xing Hu","Kerui Huang","Xiaohu Yang","David Lo","Xin Xia"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["model editing","prompt perturbation","code LLM robustness","layer localization","HumanEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/69/x"},{"id":"p00556","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Hey, ChatGPT, Look at My Work: Using Conversational AI in Requirements Engineering Education","tz":"“嘿 ChatGPT，看看我的作业”：在需求工程教学中使用对话式 AI","a":"The emergence of conversational AI tools in late 2022 practically changed the face of software engineering and software engineering education. Contemplating the question of how to best prepare and evaluate students in this new reality, we experimented with systematically introducing a conversational AI tool, ChatGPT, into the 2023 offering of an upper-level undergraduate project-based course on Software Engineering. In this course, 20 groups of four students each had to design and implement a project of their choice, with an Android-based mobile client and a Node.js-based cloud server. This paper discusses our goals, approach, and lessons learned from introducing ChatGPT into the first phase of the project development: scoping the work and defining the project requirements. Our experience shows that students can achieve comparable results using a variety of ChatGPT interaction modes and the success of each mode largely depends on students’ preferences, learning styles, and the invested effort. Yet, in any of the modes, with moderate effort, students can produce artifacts of a mid-range quality level of around 80%. Moving above this range requires substantial investment, which can be spent on brainstorming, crafting high-quality prompts, or critically assessing ChatGPT’s output. We also observe low prompting proficiency of the students: students can improve their prompting strategies by providing a more adequate description of their course and project setup, examples, and expected output format for their requests. Interestingly, students can often be “swayed” by ChatGPT’s projected confidence, even when their original ideas are, in fact, more appropriate than the proposed refinements. We hope that our experience and lessons learned will help spark further discussions on how to best embed AI tools into the software engineering curriculum and work practices.","az":"2022 年末对话式 AI 工具的出现实际上改变了软件工程与软件工程教育的面貌。为思考在这一新现实下如何最好地培养和评价学生，我们在 2023 学年一门面向高年级本科生、以项目为基础的软件工程课程中，系统性地引入了对话式 AI 工具 ChatGPT 并开展实验。在该课程中，20 个四人小组需自选并设计实现一个项目，包含基于 Android 的移动客户端和基于 Node.js 的云端服务器。本文讨论了我们在项目开发第一阶段——界定工作范围与定义项目需求——中引入 ChatGPT 的目标、做法与经验教训。我们的经验表明，学生使用多种 ChatGPT 交互模式都能取得可比的结果，而每种模式的成效在很大程度上取决于学生的偏好、学习风格与投入的努力。然而，在任何一种模式下，只要投入中等程度的努力，学生都能产出质量约为 80% 中等水平的制品。要超越这一区间则需要大量投入，这些投入可以用于头脑风暴、打磨高质量提示，或批判性地评估 ChatGPT 的输出。我们还观察到学生的提示能力较低：学生可以通过更充分地描述课程与项目背景、提供示例以及说明期望的输出格式来改进其提示策略。有趣的是，学生常常会被 ChatGPT 所表现出的自信“带偏”，即便他们原本的想法实际上比被建议的修改更为恰当。我们希望我们的经验与教训能够激发关于如何最好地将 AI 工具嵌入软件工程课程与工作实践的进一步讨论。","tl":"课堂实证：学生易被 ChatGPT 的自信带偏，提示能力普遍不足。","au":["Sahar Badihi","Michael Tegegn","Evelien Riddell","Krzysztof Czarnecki","Julia Rubin"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["human-study","llm-based"],"kw":["requirements engineering education","ChatGPT","student study","prompting proficiency","project-based course"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/70/x","pu":"https://people.ece.ubc.ca/~mjulia/publications/2026_AI_In_RE_ICSE.pdf"},{"id":"p00557","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"IntelliRadar: A Comprehensive Platform to Pinpoint Malicious Package Information from Cyber Intelligence","tz":"IntelliRadar：从网络情报中精准定位恶意软件包信息的综合平台","a":"Malicious packages in public registries have significantly threatened the software supply chain (SSC) security in modern software engineering. Current software component analysis (SCA) tools have been applied to detect and report these threats to protect downstream users. However, existing SCA tools rely heavily on databases of known malicious components, while existing databases such as OSV and Snyk often have delays in data updates and incomplete information. This inadequacy is particularly evident in their limited coverage of non-structured intelligence sources like social media platforms and developer forums, where emerging threats are often first reported. Consequently, the lifecycle of malicious packages is extended, posing serious threats to downstream users. To address this, we developed a novel and comprehensive approach to construct a platform IntelliRadar to pinpoint the collection, processing, and extraction of malicious components intelligence. Specifically, by exhaustively searching and snowballing the public sources of malicious package intelligence, and incorporating large language models (LLMs) with domain-specialized Least to Most prompts, IntelliRadar ensures the coverage, timeliness, and accurate information extraction of malicious package intelligence. As a result, we constructed a comprehensive malicious package database containing 34,313 malicious NPM and PyPI packages. Our evaluation shows that IntelliRadar achieves high performance (97.91% precision) on malicious package intelligence extraction. Compared to existing databases, IntelliRadar identifies 7,542 more malicious packages than OSV and 12,684 more than Snyk. Furthermore, 76.6% of NPM components and 70.3% of PyPI components in IntelliRadar were collected earlier than in Snyk’s database. IntelliRadar is also more cost-efficient, with a cost of $0.003 per piece of malicious package intelligence and only $7 per month for continuous monitoring. Furthermore, we identified and received confirmation for 1,981 malicious packages in downstream package manager mirror registries through the implementation of IntelliRadar.","az":"公共注册表中的恶意软件包已显著威胁到现代软件工程中的软件供应链（SSC）安全。当前的软件成分分析（SCA）工具被用于检测并上报这些威胁，以保护下游用户。然而，现有 SCA 工具严重依赖已知恶意组件数据库，而 OSV、Snyk 等现有数据库往往存在数据更新延迟与信息不完整的问题。这一不足在它们对社交媒体平台、开发者论坛等非结构化情报源的有限覆盖上尤为明显，而新兴威胁往往最先在这些渠道被披露。因此，恶意软件包的生命周期被延长，对下游用户构成严重威胁。为解决该问题，我们提出了一种新颖而全面的方法，构建了平台 IntelliRadar，用于精准地采集、处理和抽取恶意组件情报。具体而言，通过穷尽式搜索与滚雪球式扩展恶意包情报的公开来源，并将大语言模型（LLM）与领域专用的 Least-to-Most 提示相结合，IntelliRadar 确保了恶意包情报的覆盖度、时效性与信息抽取准确性。由此我们构建了一个包含 34,313 个恶意 NPM 与 PyPI 软件包的综合数据库。评估表明，IntelliRadar 在恶意包情报抽取上取得了高性能（97.91% 精确率）。与现有数据库相比，IntelliRadar 比 OSV 多识别出 7,542 个恶意包，比 Snyk 多识别出 12,684 个。此外，IntelliRadar 中 76.6% 的 NPM 组件和 70.3% 的 PyPI 组件比 Snyk 数据库更早被收录。IntelliRadar 的成本效益也更高：每条恶意包情报的成本为 0.003 美元，持续监控每月仅需 7 美元。此外，通过 IntelliRadar 的实施，我们在下游包管理器镜像注册表中识别出并获得确认的恶意包达 1,981 个。","tl":"用 LLM 从非结构化情报源构建更快更全的恶意包数据库。","au":["Wenbo Guo","Chengwei Liu","Limin Wang","Yiran Zhang","Wu Jiahui","Zhengzi Xu","Yang Liu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["malicious packages","software supply chain","threat intelligence","NPM and PyPI","LLM extraction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/71/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.15049"},{"id":"p00558","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Semantic-Enhanced Automatic Refinement of Architecture Recovery Results Using LLMs","tz":"使用 LLM 对架构恢复结果进行语义增强的自动精化","a":"Understanding the architecture is crucial for effectively maintaining and managing large software systems. However, discrepancies often exist between the designed and implemented architectures, which can pose significant risks. To identify these discrepancies, architects need to extract the architecture from the system implementation, which is both time-consuming and error-prone. To simplify this procedure, many automatic architecture recovery techniques have been developed. Yet, their accuracy is often limited. Architects must still invest significant effort in refining recovery results to ensure they accurately reflect the implemented architecture. To reduce such manual effort, we introduce SemRef, a framework that combines LLMs with dependency analysis to automatically refine architectures recovered by existing architecture recovery tools. By leveraging the LLM’s semantic understanding capabilities and integrating structural dependencies, SemRef enhances both the accuracy and the comprehension of recovered architectures. To evaluate SemRef, we tested on 9 projects with published ground-truth architectures and 10 state-of-the-art architecture recovery tools. 5 commonly used metrics are adopted to evaluate the effectiveness of SemRef. The results show that SemRef improves accuracy across various metrics, with normalized gains ranges from 17.72% to 43.35%. Specifically, for MoJoFM and $a2a_{adj}$ metrics, SemRef achieves relative improvements of 118.57% and 100.41%, respectively. Moreover, SemRef is highly scalable. It maintains stable performance across projects ranging from thousands to trillions of lines of code with the cost scale linearly with project size. Further, we test SemRef on various LLMs to demonstrate its generalizability across different models. Beyond improving accuracy, the integration of LLMs enables SemRef to provide a structured module hierarchy and hierarchical module summaries, which further enhance the comprehensibility of recovered architectures.","az":"理解架构对于有效维护和管理大型软件系统至关重要。然而，设计架构与实现架构之间常常存在差异，这可能带来重大风险。为识别这些差异，架构师需要从系统实现中提取架构，而这既耗时又易出错。为简化这一流程，人们开发了许多自动架构恢复技术，但其准确性往往有限。架构师仍须投入大量精力精化恢复结果，以确保其准确反映已实现的架构。为减少此类人工投入，我们提出 SemRef，一个将 LLM 与依赖分析相结合、自动精化由现有架构恢复工具所恢复架构的框架。通过利用 LLM 的语义理解能力并融合结构依赖关系，SemRef 同时提升了所恢复架构的准确性与可理解性。为评估 SemRef，我们在 9 个具有已公开真值架构的项目上、结合 10 种最先进的架构恢复工具进行了测试，并采用 5 个常用指标评估 SemRef 的有效性。结果表明，SemRef 在各项指标上均提升了准确性，归一化增益范围为 17.72% 至 43.35%。具体而言，在 MoJoFM 和 $a2a_{adj}$ 指标上，SemRef 分别取得了 118.57% 和 100.41% 的相对提升。此外，SemRef 具有高度可扩展性：在从数千行到万亿行代码规模的项目上都能保持稳定性能，且成本随项目规模线性增长。我们还在多种 LLM 上测试了 SemRef，以证明其在不同模型间的泛化性。除提升准确性外，LLM 的引入还使 SemRef 能够提供结构化的模块层次结构与分层模块摘要，进一步增强了所恢复架构的可理解性。","tl":"用 LLM 加依赖分析自动精化架构恢复结果并生成模块层次。","au":["Yiran Zhang","Chengwei Liu","Yuqiang Sun","Zhengzi Xu","Weisong Sun","Wenke Li","Wuxia Jin","Yang Liu"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["architecture recovery","dependency analysis","LLM refinement","MoJoFM","module hierarchy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/72/x"},{"id":"p00559","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Attention Pruning: Automated Fairness Repair of Language Models via Surrogate Simulated Annealing","tz":"注意力剪枝：基于代理模型模拟退火的语言模型公平性自动修复","a":"This paper explores pruning attention heads as a post-processing bias mitigation method for large language models (LLMs). Modern AI systems such as LLMs are expanding into sensitive social contexts and socio-economic decision-making where fairness concerns become especially crucial. Since LLMs develop their decision-making patterns by training on massive datasets of human-generated content, they naturally encode and perpetuate societal biases. While modifying training datasets and algorithms is expensive and requires significant resources, post-processing techniques—such as selectively deactivating attention heads in pre-trained LLMs—can provide feasible and effective approaches to improve fairness. However, identifying the optimal subset of parameters to prune presents a combinatorial challenge within the immense parameter space of LLMs, requiring efficient solutions that efficiently balance competing objectives across the frontiers of model fairness and utility. We explore a search-based program repair approach via simulated annealing to address the computational challenges. Given the prohibitive evaluation costs in billion-parameter LLMs, we develop surrogate deep neural networks that efficiently model the relationship between attention head states (active/inactive) and their corresponding fairness/utility metrics. This allows us to perform optimization over the surrogate models and efficiently identify optimal subsets of attention heads for pruning rather than directly searching through the LLM parameter space. This paper introduces Attention Pruning, a fairness-aware surrogate simulated annealing approach to prune attention heads in LLMs that disproportionately contribute to bias while minimally impacting overall model utility. Our experimental evaluation shows that Attention Pruning achieves a reduction of up to $40%$ in gender bias and outperforms state-of-the-art bias mitigation strategies. Warning: This paper contains content that some readers may find offensive and harmful.","az":"本文探索将剪枝注意力头作为大语言模型（LLM）的后处理偏见缓解方法。诸如 LLM 之类的现代 AI 系统正在扩展到敏感的社会情境与社会经济决策之中，公平性问题因而变得尤为关键。由于 LLM 是通过在海量人类生成内容数据集上训练来形成其决策模式的，它们自然会编码并延续社会偏见。修改训练数据集与算法代价高昂且需要大量资源，而后处理技术——例如有选择地停用预训练 LLM 中的注意力头——可以提供可行而有效的公平性改进途径。然而，在 LLM 巨大的参数空间中确定最优的待剪枝参数子集是一个组合难题，需要能在模型公平性与效用的前沿之间高效平衡相互竞争目标的解法。我们探索通过模拟退火的基于搜索的程序修复方法来应对这一计算挑战。鉴于在数十亿参数的 LLM 上评估成本高昂，我们开发了代理深度神经网络，以高效地建模注意力头状态（激活/停用）与其对应的公平性/效用指标之间的关系。这使我们能够在代理模型上进行优化，从而高效地识别出最优的待剪枝注意力头子集，而无需直接在 LLM 参数空间中搜索。本文提出 Attention Pruning，一种公平性感知的代理模拟退火方法，用于剪除那些对偏见贡献过大而对模型整体效用影响最小的注意力头。我们的实验评估表明，Attention Pruning 可将性别偏见降低多达 40%，并优于最先进的偏见缓解策略。警告：本文包含部分读者可能认为冒犯或有害的内容。","tl":"用代理模型加模拟退火搜索待剪注意力头以降偏见。","au":["Vishnu Asutosh Dasu","Md Rafi Ur Rashid","Vipul Gupta","Saeid Tizpaz-Niari","Gang (Gary) Tan"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["cross-track-bridge","llm-based"],"kw":["bias mitigation","attention head pruning","simulated annealing","surrogate model","fairness repair"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/73/x"},{"id":"p00560","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Scaling Security Testing by Addressing the Reachability Gap","tz":"通过解决可达性缺口来扩展安全测试","a":"In order to scale automated security testing, we must first solve the reachability bottleneck. Existing approaches to test specific features of a software system always assume some way of interacting with the system. For instance, the most popular approach, fuzzing, either assumes command line access, network access, an execution to amplify, or so-called fuzz drivers to send generated inputs to the system’s process or its components. Yet, scaling security testing requires so much more than sending inputs. To test a specific feature, we might need to enable specific configuration options in specific files, to set up a specific runtime environment, to write some source code to exchange messages with the system over the network, or to issue system calls to the OS kernel (e.g., to test a device driver). We call the challenge of producing both the environment and input required to trigger specific internal functionality in a system as the reachability bottleneck. In this paper, we investigate the use of Large Language Model (LLM) agents to address the reachability bottleneck in automated software testing. We introduce a novel end-to-end methodology that combines LLM-driven execution with invivo fuzzing, requiring only that the target software is installed and runnable—no manual harnesses or configuration. First, we evaluate whether an LLM agent can autonomously drive real-world programs into deep internal states. Then, we study the effectiveness of our full methodology: using invivo fuzzing to amplify executions produced by the agent. This approach results in increased code coverage and leads to the discovery of a previously unknown vulnerability in a widely used open source project.","az":"要扩展自动化安全测试，我们必须首先解决可达性瓶颈。现有用于测试软件系统特定功能的方法总是假定存在某种与系统交互的途径。例如，最流行的方法模糊测试要么假定有命令行访问、网络访问、可放大的一次执行，要么依赖所谓的 fuzz driver 把生成的输入送入系统进程或其组件。然而，扩展安全测试所需要的远不止发送输入。为测试某个特定功能，我们可能需要在特定文件中启用特定配置选项、搭建特定的运行时环境、编写一些通过网络与系统交换消息的源代码，或者向操作系统内核发出系统调用（例如为了测试设备驱动）。我们把“同时产生触发系统内部特定功能所需的环境与输入”这一挑战称为可达性瓶颈。本文研究使用大语言模型（LLM）智能体来解决自动化软件测试中的可达性瓶颈。我们提出了一种新颖的端到端方法论，将 LLM 驱动的执行与 in-vivo 模糊测试相结合，只要求目标软件已安装且可运行——无需人工编写 harness 或做配置。首先，我们评估 LLM 智能体能否自主地把真实世界程序驱动到很深的内部状态。随后，我们研究完整方法论的有效性：使用 in-vivo 模糊测试放大由智能体产生的执行。该方法带来了代码覆盖率的提升，并在一个广泛使用的开源项目中发现了一个此前未知的漏洞。","tl":"让 LLM 智能体自动把程序驱入深层状态，再做 in-vivo 模糊测试。","au":["Gaetano Sapia","Marcel Böhme"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["agentic","llm-based","security"],"kw":["reachability bottleneck","in-vivo fuzzing","LLM agent","security testing","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/74/x"},{"id":"p00561","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Large-Scale Empirical Study of Secret Key Leakage in Hugging Face Spaces","tz":"Hugging Face Spaces 中密钥泄露的大规模实证研究","a":"Hugging Face Spaces (Spaces) has become a leading platform for hosting AI applications, offering developers seamless integration of Git-based repositories and out-of-the-box web service deployment. However, as its adoption continues to expand, security concerns have come to light. Recent reports have pointed to the issue of accidental exposure of sensitive information, such as API tokens and database credentials, within Spaces-hosted code. Despite these concerns, the research community still lacks a comprehensive understanding of the scope and impact of these security risks. To bridge this gap, we present the first large-scale and systematic empirical study to quantify the extent of secret leakage in Spaces. We begin by compiling a comprehensive dataset of 313,647 public Spaces repositories created between March 2022 and December 2024. To detect exposed secrets, we introduce Secret Reviewer, an advanced framework that combines static analysis and Large Language Model (LLM)-assisted detection to identify leaked credentials. Applying Secret Reviewer, we identified 9,149 with secret leakage vulnerabilities and 11,557 unique keys—76% of which from leading AI service providers such as OpenAI and Groq. Our findings indicate that 30% of leaks were embedded in commit histories, and over 1,000 non-code files contained sensitive data. Further validation revealed that 30% of detected keys remained active, including 140 valid database credentials and 50% of access tokens with write permissions, underscoring significant security risks. Our study sheds light on critical security challenges in AI platform ecosystems and advocates for stronger security practices to mitigate these risks.","az":"Hugging Face Spaces（Spaces）已成为托管 AI 应用的领先平台，为开发者提供了基于 Git 的仓库的无缝集成与开箱即用的 Web 服务部署。然而，随着其采用范围不断扩大，安全问题逐渐显现。近期报告指出，Spaces 托管的代码中存在 API 令牌、数据库凭据等敏感信息被意外暴露的问题。尽管存在这些担忧，研究界仍缺乏对这些安全风险范围与影响的全面认识。为弥补这一空白，我们开展了首个大规模、系统化的实证研究，以量化 Spaces 中密钥泄露的程度。我们首先编制了一个包含 2022 年 3 月至 2024 年 12 月间创建的 313,647 个公开 Spaces 仓库的综合数据集。为检测暴露的密钥，我们提出 Secret Reviewer，一个将静态分析与大语言模型（LLM）辅助检测相结合以识别泄露凭据的先进框架。应用 Secret Reviewer，我们识别出 9,149 个存在密钥泄露漏洞的仓库和 11,557 个唯一密钥——其中 76% 来自 OpenAI、Groq 等领先 AI 服务提供商。我们的发现表明，30% 的泄露嵌入在提交历史中，且超过 1,000 个非代码文件包含敏感数据。进一步验证显示，所检测到的密钥中有 30% 仍然有效，包括 140 个有效的数据库凭据，以及 50% 具有写权限的访问令牌，凸显出重大的安全风险。我们的研究揭示了 AI 平台生态中的关键安全挑战，并倡导以更强的安全实践来缓解这些风险。","tl":"首次大规模量化 HF Spaces 密钥泄露，30% 泄露密钥仍有效。","au":["Shaoxuan Yun","Yuchao Zhang","Zhikun Shi","Liu Wang","Yi Wang","Yu Bai"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["secret leakage","Hugging Face Spaces","credential exposure","static analysis","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/75/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/75/A-Large-Scale-Empirical-Study-of-Secret-Key-Leakage-in-Hugging-Face-Spaces"},{"id":"p00562","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Why Attention Fails: A Taxonomy of Faults in Attention-Based Neural Networks","tz":"注意力为何失效：基于注意力的神经网络故障分类体系","a":"Attention mechanisms are at the core of modern neural architectures, powering systems ranging from ChatGPT to autonomous vehicles and driving a major economic impact. However, high-profile failures, such as ChatGPT’s nonsensical outputs or Google’s suspension of Gemini’s image generation due to attention weight errors, highlight a critical gap: existing deep learning fault taxonomies might not adequately capture the unique failures introduced by attention mechanisms. This gap leaves practitioners without actionable diagnostic guidance. To address this gap, we present the first comprehensive empirical study of faults in attention-based neural networks (ABNNs). Our work is based on a systematic analysis of 555 real-world faults collected from 96 projects across ten frameworks, including GitHub, Hugging Face, and Stack Overflow. Through our analysis, we develop a novel taxonomy comprising seven attention-specific fault categories, not captured by existing work. Our results show that over half of the ABNN faults arise from mechanisms unique to attention architectures. We further analyze the root causes and manifestations of these faults through various symptoms. Finally, by analyzing symptom–root cause associations, we identify four evidence-based diagnostic heuristics that explain 33.0% of attention-specific faults, offering the first systematic diagnostic guidance for attention-based models.","az":"注意力机制是现代神经架构的核心，支撑着从 ChatGPT 到自动驾驶汽车的各类系统，并带来了重大的经济影响。然而，诸如 ChatGPT 输出无意义内容、或 Google 因注意力权重错误而暂停 Gemini 图像生成之类的高关注度失败，凸显出一个关键空白：现有的深度学习故障分类体系可能未能充分刻画注意力机制所引入的独特失效。这一空白使从业者缺乏可操作的诊断指引。为填补该空白，我们提出了首个关于基于注意力的神经网络（ABNN）故障的全面实证研究。我们的工作基于对来自 GitHub、Hugging Face 和 Stack Overflow 等十个框架、96 个项目中收集的 555 个真实世界故障的系统性分析。通过分析，我们构建了一个由七类注意力特有故障类别组成的新颖分类体系，这些类别未被已有工作所覆盖。结果表明，超过半数的 ABNN 故障源于注意力架构所独有的机制。我们进一步通过各种症状分析了这些故障的根因与表现形式。最后，通过分析症状与根因的关联，我们识别出四条基于证据的诊断启发式规则，可解释 33.0% 的注意力特有故障，为基于注意力的模型提供了首套系统化的诊断指引。","tl":"首个注意力机制特有故障分类体系与四条诊断启发式规则。","au":["Sigma Jahan","Saurabhsingh Rajput","Tushar Sharma","Masud Rahman"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study"],"kw":["fault taxonomy","attention mechanism","deep learning bugs","root cause analysis","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/76/x","pu":"https://www.arxiv.org/abs/2508.04925"},{"id":"p00563","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Large Language Model-Aided Partial Program Dependence Analysis","tz":"大语言模型辅助的部分程序依赖分析","a":"Dependence analysis (DA) plays a critical role in software engineering, from code optimization to debugging. It is traditionally limited to scenarios where entire source code is available. In practice, however, developers often encounter incomplete or partial code snippets, as in StackOverflow (S/O) forums or during modular development, where program constructs are missing. This presents challenges for DA tools, which rely on syntactic and semantic correctness to correctly identify dependencies. Thus, existing DA tools for partial code often face trade-offs in precision and recall. In this work, we introduce L𝜆MDA, a framework that addresses these limitations by leveraging large language models (LLMs) as context augmenters to enrich partial code snippets with the program elements required for enabling such analyses. Through our evaluation, we showed that L𝜆MDA exhibits high correctness and completeness guarantees, yielding a higher recall than traditional approaches, and a higher precision than learning-based approaches. Overall, L𝜆MDA improves over all baselines in partial program dependence analysis by 5%-265% and 16%-331% across S/O benchmarks. Moreover, we show L𝜆MDA’s effectiveness in providing exception handling suggestions as well as exception-flow analysis.","az":"依赖分析（DA）在软件工程中扮演关键角色，从代码优化到调试皆有应用。传统上它仅适用于整份源代码可得的场景。然而在实践中，开发者常遇到不完整或部分的代码片段，例如 StackOverflow（S/O）论坛中的代码，或模块化开发过程中缺失程序构件的情形。这给依赖分析工具带来了挑战，因为它们依赖语法与语义的正确性才能正确识别依赖关系。因此，现有面向部分代码的 DA 工具往往要在精确率与召回率之间权衡。在本工作中，我们提出 LλMDA，一个通过将大语言模型（LLM）用作上下文增强器、为部分代码片段补足使此类分析得以进行所需程序元素的框架，从而解决上述局限。通过评估，我们表明 LλMDA 具备很高的正确性与完整性保证：其召回率高于传统方法，精确率高于基于学习的方法。总体而言，在 S/O 基准上，LλMDA 在部分程序依赖分析上较所有基线分别提升了 5%–265% 与 16%–331%。此外，我们还展示了 LλMDA 在提供异常处理建议以及进行异常流分析方面的有效性。","tl":"用 LLM 补全缺失程序元素，使部分代码也能做依赖分析。","au":["Xiaokai Rong","Aashish Yadavally","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["dependence analysis","partial code","LLM context augmentation","exception flow","Stack Overflow snippets"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/77/x","pu":"https://aashishyadavally.github.io/assets/pdf/pub-icse2026-(1).pdf"},{"id":"p00564","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"XRFix: Exploring Performance Bug Repair of Extended Reality Applications with Large Language Models","tz":"XRFix：用大语言模型探索扩展现实应用的性能缺陷修复","a":"As an emerging technology, Extended Reality (XR) provides end-users with an immersive experience of interacting with virtual and physical environments. Unlike traditional software, the execution of XR applications involves more computationally complex operations, such as 3D scene rendering, real-time animation, and process simulations. Inefficient coding practices during the software development of XR applications may cause various performance bugs, which can ultimately degrade user experience and even cause motion sickness. Thus, it is an urgent need to develop an automated program repair (APR) framework for fixing performance bugs in complex XR programs. However, it is non-trivial to achieve this goal due to several technical challenges: (1) a lack of a real-world XR codebase and bug dataset, (2) no accurate bug detection tool, and (3) no effective bug-fixing tool designed for XR performance bugs. To tackle these challenges, we present a novel large language model-based framework, namely XRFix, to repair performance bugs for open-source XR programs. To overcome the first challenge, we first construct a corpus of domain-specific performance bugs built on top of a codebase from 23 open-source XR projects and a dataset of XR-related bugs containing 104 real-world bugs. To address the second challenge, we tailor two static analysis tools for accurately detecting bugs in both C# scripts and asset files. To solve the third challenge, we design different prompts to instruct large language models (LLMs) to fix XR bugs in three types of bug scenarios with different complexities, i.e., single-line level, function level, and class level. We conduct extensive experiments on five off-the-shelf LLMs to evaluate the bug-fixing performance of XRFix. We also compare our XRFix with three state-of-the-art (SOTA) APR approaches. Through static analysis, reference answer comparison, and manual inspection, we demonstrate that our XRFix can effectively fix XR bugs, outperforming SOTA APR methods. For example, our XRFix achieves 67.3% fixing rate, i.e., 7.7% higher than the second-best method.","az":"作为一项新兴技术，扩展现实（XR）为终端用户提供了与虚拟与物理环境交互的沉浸式体验。与传统软件不同，XR 应用的执行涉及更为计算复杂的操作，例如 3D 场景渲染、实时动画与过程仿真。XR 应用开发中低效的编码实践可能导致各类性能缺陷，最终降低用户体验，甚至引发晕动症。因此，迫切需要为复杂 XR 程序中的性能缺陷开发自动程序修复（APR）框架。然而，实现这一目标并非易事，存在若干技术挑战：(1) 缺乏真实世界的 XR 代码库与缺陷数据集；(2) 没有准确的缺陷检测工具；(3) 没有为 XR 性能缺陷设计的有效修复工具。为应对这些挑战，我们提出一个新颖的基于大语言模型的框架 XRFix，用于修复开源 XR 程序的性能缺陷。针对第一个挑战，我们首先在来自 23 个开源 XR 项目的代码库之上构建了领域专用的性能缺陷语料库，以及一个包含 104 个真实缺陷的 XR 相关缺陷数据集。针对第二个挑战，我们定制了两款静态分析工具，用于在 C# 脚本与资产文件中准确检测缺陷。针对第三个挑战，我们设计了不同的提示，指导大语言模型（LLM）在三种复杂度不同的缺陷场景（单行级、函数级与类级）下修复 XR 缺陷。我们在五个现成 LLM 上开展了大量实验以评估 XRFix 的缺陷修复性能，并将 XRFix 与三种最先进（SOTA）的 APR 方法进行了比较。通过静态分析、参考答案比对与人工检查，我们证明 XRFix 能够有效修复 XR 缺陷，优于 SOTA 的 APR 方法。例如，XRFix 取得了 67.3% 的修复率，即比次优方法高 7.7%。","tl":"首个面向 XR 性能缺陷的数据集加 LLM 修复框架。","au":["Jingwen Wu","Hanyang Guo","Hong-Ning Dai","Xiapu Luo"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["extended reality","performance bugs","program repair","static analysis","Unity C#"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/78/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3773120"},{"id":"p00565","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Precise Static Identification of Ethereum Storage Variables","tz":"以太坊存储变量的精确静态识别","a":"Smart contracts are small programs that run autonomously on the blockchain, using it as their persistent memory. The predominant platform for smart contracts is the Ethereum VM (EVM). In EVM smart contracts, a problem with significant applications is to identify data structures (in blockchain state, a.k.a. ``storage''), given only the deployed smart contract code. The problem has been highly challenging and has often been considered nearly impossible to address satisfactorily. (For reference, the latest state-of-the-art research tool fails to recover nearly all complex data structures and scales to 50% of contracts.) Much of the complication is that the main on-chain data structures (mappings and arrays) have their locations derived dynamically through code execution. We propose sophisticated static analysis techniques to solve the identification of on-chain data structures with extremely high fidelity and completeness. Our analysis scales nearly universally and recovers deep data structures. Our techniques are able to identify the exact types of data structures with 95.70% precision and at least 94.96% recall, compared to a state-of-the-art tool managing 83.30% and 55.65% respectively. Strikingly, the analysis is often more complete than the storage description that the compiler itself produces, with full access to the source code.","az":"智能合约是在区块链上自主运行的小程序，并将区块链用作其持久化存储。智能合约的主流平台是以太坊虚拟机（EVM）。在 EVM 智能合约中，一个具有重要应用价值的问题是：仅给定已部署的智能合约代码，识别出区块链状态（即“storage”）中的数据结构。该问题极具挑战性，常被认为几乎不可能得到令人满意的解决。（作为参考，最新的最先进研究工具几乎无法恢复所有复杂数据结构，且仅能扩展到 50% 的合约。）复杂之处主要在于，主要的链上数据结构（映射与数组）的位置是通过代码执行动态推导出来的。我们提出了精巧的静态分析技术，以极高的保真度与完整度解决链上数据结构的识别问题。我们的分析几乎具有普适的可扩展性，并能恢复深层数据结构。我们的技术能够以 95.70% 的精确率和至少 94.96% 的召回率识别数据结构的确切类型，而最先进工具分别只能达到 83.30% 与 55.65%。令人惊讶的是，该分析往往比编译器自身在完全可访问源代码的情况下产生的 storage 描述还要完整。","tl":"静态分析近乎完整地恢复 EVM 字节码中的链上数据结构类型。","au":["Sifis Lagouvardos","Yannis Bollanos","Michael Debono","Neville Grech","Yannis Smaragdakis"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Ethereum","EVM bytecode","storage variables","static analysis","data structure recovery"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/79/x","pu":"https://sifislag.github.io/assets/papers/storage-modeling-full.pdf"},{"id":"p00566","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"HarnessLLM: Rust Verification Harness Generation with Large Language Models","tz":"HarnessLLM：用大语言模型生成 Rust 验证 harness","a":"Rust’s ownership model and type system offer strong memory safety guarantees, but unsafe code and runtime panics still present significant risks. Formal verification is essential to ensure memory safety, but developing verification harnesses remains a challenging and manual task. Although large language models (LLMs) have shown strong performance in various code analysis tasks, directly applying them to harness generation often results in inaccurate API invocations, inefficient nondeterministic data generation, and fabricated fixes. In this paper, we present HarnessLLM, an automated workflow that leverages LLMs to generate verification harnesses for Rust code directly from existing test suites. HarnessLLM automatically extracts calling scenarios from test cases, generates nondeterministic arguments based on dependency analysis, and incrementally synthesizes harnesses. It then iteratively refines the harnesses, preserving critical code regions and reporting fabricated types or functions to LLMs for correction. In our evaluation on 9 real-world Rust codebases, HarnessLLM extracted 294 calling scenarios from 494 test cases with 94.66% precision and generated harnesses for all scenarios in an average of 145 seconds each. It outperformed the existing approach, Autoharness, which succeeded on only 41% of those scenarios. Finally, 6 real-world memory safety bugs were detected using the generated harnesses, demonstrating the practical utility of our approach in verification. To our knowledge, this is the first work to use LLMs for generating harnesses aimed at memory safety verification in real-world Rust projects.","az":"Rust 的所有权模型与类型系统提供了强有力的内存安全保证，但 unsafe 代码与运行时 panic 仍带来显著风险。形式化验证对于确保内存安全至关重要，但开发验证 harness 仍是一项具有挑战性的手工任务。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在各类代码分析任务中表现出色，直接将其用于 harness 生成往往会导致不准确的 API 调用、低效的非确定性数据生成以及杜撰式的修复。本文提出 HarnessLLM，一个利用 LLM 直接从已有测试套件为 Rust 代码生成验证 harness 的自动化工作流。HarnessLLM 自动从测试用例中抽取调用场景，基于依赖分析生成非确定性参数，并增量式地合成 harness；随后迭代地精化这些 harness，保留关键代码区域，并把杜撰的类型或函数反馈给 LLM 进行纠正。在我们对 9 个真实世界 Rust 代码库的评估中，HarnessLLM 从 494 个测试用例中抽取出 294 个调用场景，精确率为 94.66%，并为所有场景生成了 harness，平均每个耗时 145 秒。它优于已有方法 Autoharness，后者仅在其中 41% 的场景上成功。最后，使用所生成的 harness 检测出 6 个真实世界的内存安全缺陷，证明了我们方法在验证中的实用价值。据我们所知，这是首个在真实 Rust 项目中使用 LLM 生成面向内存安全验证 harness 的工作。","tl":"从已有测试自动合成 Rust 内存安全验证 harness。","au":["Minghua Wang","Yuwei Liu","Lin Huang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Rust verification","harness generation","memory safety","LLM workflow","dependency analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/80/x"},{"id":"p00567","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"EMC: A Semantic-Enhanced Malware Classification Method with Robustness and Scalability","tz":"EMC：一种兼具鲁棒性与可扩展性的语义增强恶意软件分类方法","a":"Driven by substantial financial incentives, malware continues to evolve, posing persistent and growing threats. Malware classification has long been a vital research area, and numerous classification approaches have been proposed. However, existing methods still face limitations in performance and often lack robustness when dealing with complex analytical scenarios involving concept drift. In this paper, we propose a robust and scalable malware classification framework based on program semantic analysis and feature enhancement, and implement a prototype system named EMC. Our approach focuses on behavior-oriented semantic understanding of programs, constructing a more effective feature space while eliminating spurious correlations between features in a fine-grained manner to enhance robustness. EMC extracts behavior-oriented binary opcode sequences and employs a BERT sliding window mechanism for semantic understanding and feature space construction. Furthermore, it combines random Fourier features and weighted resampling techniques to remove dependencies between features, and leverages mutual information to purify features. These enhancements enable the classification model to more accurately capture the intrinsic characteristics of malicious programs, thereby improving both accuracy and robustness. Compared with nine mainstream malware classification methods, EMC achieves F1 score improvements ranging from 1.51% to 12.06% under standard conditions, and from 17.36% to 50.35% in scenarios involving concept drift.","az":"在巨大经济利益的驱动下，恶意软件持续演化，构成了持久且不断增长的威胁。恶意软件分类长期以来都是一个重要研究领域，已有大量分类方法被提出。然而，现有方法在性能上仍存在局限，并且在面对涉及概念漂移的复杂分析场景时往往缺乏鲁棒性。本文提出一个基于程序语义分析与特征增强的鲁棒且可扩展的恶意软件分类框架，并实现了名为 EMC 的原型系统。我们的方法聚焦于面向行为的程序语义理解，构建更有效的特征空间，同时以细粒度方式消除特征之间的伪相关，以增强鲁棒性。EMC 提取面向行为的二进制操作码序列，并采用 BERT 滑动窗口机制进行语义理解与特征空间构建。此外，它结合随机傅里叶特征与加权重采样技术以去除特征间的依赖，并利用互信息来提纯特征。这些增强使分类模型能够更准确地捕捉恶意程序的内在特征，从而同时提升准确性与鲁棒性。与九种主流恶意软件分类方法相比，EMC 在标准条件下的 F1 分数提升幅度为 1.51% 至 12.06%，在涉及概念漂移的场景下提升幅度为 17.36% 至 50.35%。","tl":"用操作码语义加去伪相关，让恶意软件分类抗概念漂移。","au":["Haojun Zhao","Yueming Wu","Zhen Li","Deqing Zou"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["malware classification","opcode sequences","concept drift","random Fourier features","spurious correlation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/81/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/81/EMC-A-Semantic-Enhanced-Malware-Classification-Method-with-Robustness-and-Scalabilit"},{"id":"p00568","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Staying or Leaving? How Job Satisfaction, Embeddedness and Antecedents Predict Turnover Intentions of Software Professionals","tz":"留下还是离开？工作满意度、嵌入度及其前因如何预测软件从业者的离职意向","a":"Context: Voluntary turnover is common in the software industry, increasing recruitment and onboarding costs and the risk of losing organizational and tacit knowledge. Objective: This study investigates how job satisfaction, work-life balance, job embeddedness, and their antecedents, including job quality, personality traits, attitudes toward technical and sociotechnical infrastructure, and perceptions of organizational justice, relate to software professionals’ turnover intentions. Method: We conducted a geographically diverse cross-sectional survey of software professionals (N = 224) and analyzed the data using partial least squares structural equation modeling (PLS-SEM). Our model includes both reflective and formative constructs and tests 15 hypotheses grounded in occupational psychology and software engineering literature. Results: Job satisfaction and embeddedness were significantly negatively associated with software professionals’ turnover intentions, while work-life balance showed no direct effect. The strongest antecedents for job satisfaction were work-life balance and job quality, while organizational justice was the strongest predictor of job embeddedness. Discussion: The resulting PLS-SEM model has considerably higher explanatory power for key outcome variables than previous work conducted in the software development context, highlighting the importance of both psychological (e.g., job satisfaction, job embeddedness) and organizational (e.g., organizational justice, job quality) factors in understanding turnover intentions of software professionals. Our results imply that improving job satisfaction and job embeddedness is the key to retaining software professionals. In turn, enhancing job quality, supporting work-life balance, and ensuring high organizational justice can improve job satisfaction and embeddedness, indirectly reducing turnover intentions.","az":"背景：自愿离职在软件行业十分常见，它增加了招聘与入职成本，并带来组织知识与隐性知识流失的风险。目标：本研究考察工作满意度、工作-生活平衡、工作嵌入度及其前因（包括工作质量、人格特质、对技术性与社会技术性基础设施的态度，以及对组织公平的感知）如何与软件从业者的离职意向相关联。方法：我们对软件从业者开展了一项地域多样化的横断面调查（N = 224），并使用偏最小二乘结构方程模型（PLS-SEM）分析数据。我们的模型同时包含反映型与形成型构念，并检验了 15 个基于职业心理学与软件工程文献提出的假设。结果：工作满意度与嵌入度均与软件从业者的离职意向显著负相关，而工作-生活平衡未表现出直接效应。工作满意度最强的前因是工作-生活平衡与工作质量，而组织公平是工作嵌入度最强的预测因子。讨论：所得 PLS-SEM 模型对关键结果变量的解释力显著高于以往在软件开发情境中开展的工作，凸显了心理因素（如工作满意度、工作嵌入度）与组织因素（如组织公平、工作质量）在理解软件从业者离职意向中的重要性。我们的结果意味着，提升工作满意度与工作嵌入度是留住软件从业者的关键；进而，改善工作质量、支持工作-生活平衡并确保高水平的组织公平可以提升满意度与嵌入度，从而间接降低离职意向。","tl":"PLS-SEM 证实满意度与嵌入度决定离职意向，平衡无直接效应。","au":["Miikka Kuutila","Paul Ralph","Huilian Sophie Qiu","Ronnie de Souza Santos","Morakot Choetkiertikul","Amin Milani Fard","Rana Alkadhi","Xavier Devroey","Gregorio Robles","Hideaki Hata","Sebastian Baltes","Hera Arif","Vladimir Kovalenko","Shalini Chakraborty","Eray Tüzün","Gianisa Adisaputri"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","empirical-study"],"kw":["turnover intention","job satisfaction","job embeddedness","PLS-SEM","software professionals"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/82/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.00869"},{"id":"p00569","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Test Flimsiness: Characterizing Flakiness Induced by Mutation to the Code Under Test","tz":"测试脆性：刻画由被测代码变异引发的不稳定性","a":"Flaky tests, those that fail non-deterministically against the same version of code, pose a well-established challenge to software developers. In this paper, we characterize the overlooked phenomenon of test FLIMsiness: FLakiness Induced by Mutations to the code under test. These mutations are generated by the same operators found in out-of-the-box mutation testing tools. Flimsiness has profound implications for researchers in software testing. While previous work analyzed the impact of pre-existing flaky tests on mutation testing, we reveal that mutations themselves can induce flakiness, exposing a previously neglected threat. This has impacts beyond mutation testing, calling into question the reliability of any technique that relies on deterministic test outcomes in response to mutations. On the other hand, flimsiness also presents an opportunity to surface potential flakiness that may otherwise remain hidden. Where prior work has perturbed the execution environment to augment rerunning or the test code to support benchmarking, our work advances these efforts by perturbing a third major source of flakiness: the code under test. We conducted an empirical study on over half a million test suite executions across 28 diverse Python projects. Our robust statistical analysis on more than 30 million mutant-test pairs unveiled flimsiness in 54% of projects, highlighting its prevalence. We found that augmenting the standard rerunning flaky test detection strategy with mutations to the code under test detects a substantially larger number of flaky tests (median 740 vs. 163) and uncovers many that the standard strategy is unlikely to detect.","az":"不稳定测试（flaky test），即在同一版本代码上非确定性失败的测试，是软件开发者面临的一个公认挑战。本文刻画了一个被忽视的现象——测试 FLIMsiness：由对被测代码施加变异（mutation）所引发的不稳定性（FLakiness Induced by Mutations）。这些变异由现成变异测试工具中的同一批算子生成。脆性对软件测试研究者具有深远意义。以往工作分析了既有不稳定测试对变异测试的影响，而我们揭示出变异本身也能引发不稳定性，暴露了一个此前被忽视的威胁。这一影响超出了变异测试本身，使任何依赖“测试对变异产生确定性结果”的技术的可靠性受到质疑。另一方面，脆性也提供了一个机会：它能暴露原本可能隐藏的潜在不稳定性。以往工作通过扰动执行环境来增强重跑，或扰动测试代码以支持基准构建；我们的工作在此基础上更进一步，扰动了不稳定性的第三大来源：被测代码。我们在 28 个多样化的 Python 项目上对超过五十万次测试套件执行开展了实证研究。我们在超过 3000 万个“变异体—测试”对上的稳健统计分析揭示，54% 的项目存在脆性，凸显了其普遍性。我们发现，用对被测代码的变异来增强标准的重跑式不稳定测试检测策略，能够检测出数量显著更多的不稳定测试（中位数 740 对 163），并发现许多标准策略不太可能检出的不稳定测试。","tl":"发现变异本身会诱发不稳定测试，并可反用于检出隐藏 flaky。","au":["Owain Parry","Gregory Kapfhammer","Michael Hilton","Phil McMinn"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["flaky tests","mutation testing","test flimsiness","empirical study","Python projects"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/83/x"},{"id":"p00570","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"E-Test: E'er-Improving Test Suites","tz":"E-Test：持续改进的测试套件","a":"Test suites are inherently imperfect, and testers can always enrich a suite with new test cases that improve its quality and, consequently, the reliability of the target software system. However, finding test cases that explore execution scenarios beyond the scope of an existing suite can be extremely challenging and labor-intensive, particularly when managing large test suites over extended periods. In this paper, we propose E-Test, an approach that reduces the gap between the execution space explored with a test suite and the executions experienced after testing by augmenting the test suite with test cases that explore execution scenarios that emerge in production. E-Test (i) identifies executions that have not yet been tested from large sets of scenarios, such as those monitored during intensive production usage, and (ii) generates new test cases that enhance the test suite. E-Test leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) to pinpoint scenarios that the current test suite does not adequately cover, and augments the suite with test cases that execute these scenarios. Our evaluation on a dataset of 1,975 scenarios, collected from highly-starred open-source Java projects already in production and Defects4J, demonstrates that E-Test retrieves not-yet-tested execution scenarios significantly better than state-of-the-art approaches. While existing regression testing and field testing approaches for this task achieve a maximum F1-score of 0.34, and vanilla LLMs achieve a maximum F1-score of 0.39, E-Test reaches 0.55. These results highlight the impact of E-Test in enhancing test suites by effectively targeting not-yet-tested execution scenarios and reducing manual effort required for maintaining test suites.","az":"测试套件天然是不完美的，测试人员总能用新的测试用例丰富套件，从而提升其质量，进而提升目标软件系统的可靠性。然而，寻找那些探索超出既有套件范围的执行场景的测试用例可能极具挑战且耗费人力，尤其是在长期维护大型测试套件时。本文提出 E-Test，一种通过为测试套件补充能够探索生产环境中涌现执行场景的测试用例，来缩小“测试套件所探索的执行空间”与“测试之后实际经历的执行”之间差距的方法。E-Test 能够 (i) 从大量场景（例如在密集生产使用过程中监控到的场景）中识别出尚未被测试的执行，并 (ii) 生成增强测试套件的新测试用例。E-Test 利用大语言模型（LLM）来精确定位当前测试套件未能充分覆盖的场景，并用执行这些场景的测试用例扩充套件。我们在一个包含 1,975 个场景的数据集（收集自已投入生产的高星标开源 Java 项目以及 Defects4J）上的评估表明，E-Test 在检索尚未被测试的执行场景方面显著优于最先进的方法。现有的回归测试与现场测试方法在该任务上的最高 F1 分数为 0.34，原生 LLM 的最高 F1 分数为 0.39，而 E-Test 达到了 0.55。这些结果凸显了 E-Test 在通过有效瞄准尚未测试的执行场景来增强测试套件、并减少维护测试套件所需人工投入方面的影响力。","tl":"用生产场景找出未测执行并自动补充测试用例。","au":["Ketai Qiu","Luca Di Grazia","Leonardo Mariani","Mauro Pezze"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test suite augmentation","field testing","untested scenarios","LLM","Defects4J"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/84/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.19860"},{"id":"p00571","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AssertFlip: Reproducing Bugs via Inversion of LLM-Generated Passing Tests","tz":"AssertFlip：通过反转 LLM 生成的通过型测试来复现缺陷","a":"Bug reproduction is critical in the software debugging and repair process, yet the majority of bugs in open-source and industrial settings lack executable tests to reproduce them at the time they are reported, making diagnosis and resolution more difficult and time-consuming. To address this challenge, we introduce AssertFlip, a novel technique for automatically generating Bug Reproducible Tests (BRTs) using large language models (LLMs). Unlike existing methods that attempt direct generation of failing tests, AssertFlip first generates passing tests on the buggy behaviour and then inverts these tests to fail when the bug is present. We hypothesize that LLMs are better at writing passing tests than ones that crash or fail on purpose. Our results show that AssertFlip outperforms all known techniques in the leaderboard of SWT-Bench, a benchmark curated for BRTs. Specifically, AssertFlip achieves a fail-to-pass success rate of 43.6% on the SWT-Bench-Verified subset.","az":"缺陷复现在软件调试与修复流程中至关重要，但在开源与工业场景中，大多数缺陷在被报告时都缺乏可执行的复现测试，这使诊断与解决更加困难和耗时。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 AssertFlip，一种使用大语言模型（LLM）自动生成缺陷复现测试（BRT）的新技术。与试图直接生成失败测试的现有方法不同，AssertFlip 先针对缺陷行为生成通过型测试，然后将这些测试反转，使其在缺陷存在时失败。我们的假设是：LLM 更擅长编写通过型测试，而不是刻意崩溃或失败的测试。我们的结果表明，AssertFlip 在为 BRT 精心构建的基准 SWT-Bench 的排行榜上优于所有已知技术。具体而言，AssertFlip 在 SWT-Bench-Verified 子集上取得了 43.6% 的 fail-to-pass 成功率。","tl":"先写通过型测试再反转断言，从而更可靠地复现缺陷。","au":["Lara Khatib","Noble Saji Mathews","Mei Nagappan"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["bug reproducible tests","assertion inversion","SWT-Bench","LLM test generation","fail-to-pass"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/85/x"},{"id":"p00572","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"On Interaction Effects in Greybox Fuzzing","tz":"论灰盒模糊测试中的交互效应","a":"A greybox fuzzer is an automated software testing tool that generates new test inputs by applying randomly chosen mutators (e.g., flipping a bit or deleting a block of bytes) to a seed input in random order, and adds all coverage-increasing inputs to the corpus of seeds. We hypothesize that the order in which mutators are applied to a seed input has an impact on the effectiveness of greybox fuzzers. In our experiments, we fit a linear model to a dataset that contains the effectiveness of all possible mutator pairs and indeed observe the conjectured interaction effect. This points us to more efficient fuzzing by choosing the most promising mutator sequence with higher likelihood. We propose MuoFuzz, a greybox fuzzer that learns and chooses the most promising mutator sequences. MuoFuzz learns the conditional probability that the next mutator will yield an interesting input given the previously selected mutator. Then, it samples from the learned probability using a random walk to generate mutator sequences. We compare the performance of MuoFuzz to AFL++, which uses a fixed selection probability, and MOPT, which optimizes the selection probability of each mutator in isolation. Experimental results on the FuzzBench and MAGMA benchmarks show that MuoFuzz achieves the highest code coverage, and finds four bugs missed by AFL++ and one missed by both AFL++ and MOPT.","az":"灰盒模糊测试工具是一种自动化软件测试工具，它通过以随机顺序对种子输入施加随机选择的变异算子（例如翻转一个比特或删除一段字节）来生成新的测试输入，并把所有能提升覆盖率的输入加入种子语料库。我们假设：变异算子施加到种子输入上的顺序会影响灰盒模糊测试的有效性。在我们的实验中，我们对一个包含所有可能变异算子对的有效性数据集拟合了线性模型，确实观察到了所猜想的交互效应。这提示我们可以通过以更高概率选择最有希望的变异算子序列来实现更高效的模糊测试。我们提出 MuoFuzz，一个学习并选择最有希望的变异算子序列的灰盒模糊测试工具。MuoFuzz 学习在给定前一个被选中的变异算子的条件下，下一个变异算子产出有趣输入的条件概率；随后，它使用随机游走从所学得的概率中采样，以生成变异算子序列。我们将 MuoFuzz 的性能与使用固定选择概率的 AFL++ 以及孤立地优化每个变异算子选择概率的 MOPT 进行了比较。在 FuzzBench 与 MAGMA 基准上的实验结果表明，MuoFuzz 取得了最高的代码覆盖率，并发现了 AFL++ 漏掉的四个缺陷以及 AFL++ 和 MOPT 都漏掉的一个缺陷。","tl":"首次实证变异算子顺序的交互效应并据此学习变异序列。","au":["Konstantinos Kitsios","Marcel Böhme","Alberto Bacchelli"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["greybox fuzzing","mutator scheduling","interaction effects","AFL++","FuzzBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/86/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.19984"},{"id":"p00573","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Issue2Test: Generating Reproducing Test Cases from Issue Reports","tz":"Issue2Test：从 Issue 报告生成复现测试用例","a":"Automated tools for solving GitHub issues are receiving significant attention by both researchers and practitioners, e.g., in the form of foundation models and LLM-based agents prompted with issues. A crucial step toward successfully solving an issue is creating a test case that accurately reproduces the issue. Such a test case can guide the search for an appropriate patch and help validate whether the patch matches the issue’s intent. However, existing techniques for issue reproduction show only moderate success. This paper presents Issue2Test, an LLM-based technique for automatically generating a reproducing test case for a given issue report. Unlike automated regression test generators, which aim at creating passing tests, our approach aims at a test that fails, and that fails specifically for the reason described in the issue. To this end, Issue2Test performs three steps: (1) understand the issue and gather context (e.g., related files and project-specific guidelines) relevant for reproducing it; (2) generate a candidate test case; and (3) iteratively refine the test case based on compilation and runtime feedback until it fails and the failure aligns with the problem described in the issue. We evaluate Issue2Test on the SWT-bench-lite dataset, where it successfully reproduces 32.9% of the issues, achieving a 16.3% relative improvement over the best existing technique. Our evaluation also shows that Issue2Test reproduces 20 issues that four prior techniques fail to address, contributing a total of 60.4% of all issues reproduced by these tools. We envision our approach to contribute to enhancing the overall progress in the important task of automatically solving GitHub issues.","az":"用于解决 GitHub issue 的自动化工具正受到研究者与从业者的高度关注，例如以基础模型和以 issue 作为提示的 LLM 智能体的形式出现。成功解决一个 issue 的关键一步是创建能够准确复现该 issue 的测试用例。这样的测试用例既能指导对合适补丁的搜索，也有助于验证补丁是否符合 issue 的意图。然而，现有的 issue 复现技术只取得了中等程度的成功。本文提出 Issue2Test，一种基于 LLM、为给定 issue 报告自动生成复现测试用例的技术。与旨在创建通过型测试的自动回归测试生成器不同，我们的方法追求的是一个失败的测试，并且是恰恰因为 issue 中所描述的原因而失败。为此，Issue2Test 执行三个步骤：(1) 理解该 issue 并收集与复现相关的上下文（例如相关文件和项目特定的规范）；(2) 生成候选测试用例；(3) 基于编译与运行时反馈迭代精化该测试用例，直至它失败且失败原因与 issue 中描述的问题相符。我们在 SWT-bench-lite 数据集上评估 Issue2Test，它成功复现了 32.9% 的 issue，较现有最佳技术实现了 16.3% 的相对提升。我们的评估还表明，Issue2Test 复现了 20 个此前四种技术都未能处理的 issue，在这些工具复现的全部 issue 中贡献了 60.4%。我们期望我们的方法能推动“自动解决 GitHub issue”这一重要任务的整体进展。","tl":"迭代利用编译与运行反馈，生成因 issue 原因而失败的测试。","au":["Noor Nashid","Islem BOUZENIA","Michael Pradel","Ali Mesbah"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["issue reproduction","reproducing test generation","SWT-bench","LLM","runtime feedback"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/87/x"},{"id":"p00574","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automating API Documentation from Crowdsourced Knowledge","tz":"从众包知识自动生成 API 文档","a":"API documentation is crucial for developers to learn and use APIs. However, it is known that many official API documents are obsolete and incomplete. To address this challenge, we propose a new approach called AutoDoc that generates API documents with API knowledge extracted from online discussions on Stack Overflow (SO). AutoDoc leverages a fine-tuned dense retrieval model to identify seven types of API knowledge from SO posts. Then, it uses GPT-4o to summarize the API knowledge in these posts into concise text. Meanwhile, we designed two specific components to handle LLM hallucination and redundancy in generated content. We evaluated AutoDoc against five comparison baselines on 48 APIs of different popularity levels. Our results indicate that the API documents generated by AutoDoc are up to 77.7% more accurate, 11.5% less duplicated, and contain 34.4% knowledge uncovered by the official documents. We also measured the sensitivity of AutoDoc to the choice of different LLMs. We found that while larger LLMs produce higher-quality API documents, AutoDoc enables smaller open-source models (e.g., Mistral-7B-v0.3) to achieve comparable results. Finally, we conducted a user study to evaluate the usefulness of the API documents generated by AutoDoc. All participants found API documents generated by AutoDoc to be more comprehensive, concise, and helpful than the comparison baselines. This highlights the feasibility of utilizing LLMs for API documentation with careful design to counter LLM hallucination and information redundancy.","az":"API 文档对开发者学习和使用 API 至关重要。然而众所周知，许多官方 API 文档已经过时且不完整。为应对这一挑战，我们提出一种名为 AutoDoc 的新方法，利用从 Stack Overflow（SO）在线讨论中抽取的 API 知识来生成 API 文档。AutoDoc 利用经过微调的稠密检索模型，从 SO 帖子中识别七类 API 知识；随后使用 GPT-4o 将这些帖子中的 API 知识总结为简洁的文本。同时，我们设计了两个专门组件来处理 LLM 幻觉与生成内容中的冗余。我们在 48 个不同流行度水平的 API 上，将 AutoDoc 与五个对比基线进行了评估。结果表明，AutoDoc 生成的 API 文档准确性最多高出 77.7%，重复内容减少 11.5%，并包含官方文档未覆盖的 34.4% 的知识。我们还测量了 AutoDoc 对不同 LLM 选择的敏感性，发现虽然更大的 LLM 能产出质量更高的 API 文档，但 AutoDoc 使较小的开源模型（例如 Mistral-7B-v0.3）也能取得可比的结果。最后，我们开展了一项用户研究以评估 AutoDoc 生成的 API 文档的有用性。所有参与者都认为 AutoDoc 生成的 API 文档比对比基线更全面、更简洁、更有帮助。这凸显了在精心设计以对抗 LLM 幻觉与信息冗余的前提下，利用 LLM 进行 API 文档生成的可行性。","tl":"从 Stack Overflow 抽七类 API 知识生成去冗余的文档。","au":["Bonan Kou","Zijie Zhou","Muhao Chen","Tianyi Zhang"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["API documentation","Stack Overflow","dense retrieval","LLM hallucination","user study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/88/x"},{"id":"p00575","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Bayesian Multi-Level Performance Models for Multi-Factor Variability of Configurable Software Systems","tz":"面向可配置软件系统多因素变异性的贝叶斯多层性能模型","a":"Tuning a software system’s configuration is essential to meet performance requirements. However, not only do configuration options affect performance, but also the system’s interaction with external factors such as the workload. Hence, tuning requires understanding how a specific setting of external factors (e.g., a specific workload) in combination with the system configuration influences performance. Current performance modeling approaches usually do not incorporate external factors, for good reasons: training a separate model per setting is costly and is unlikely to generalize, whereas a single model trained on multiple settings fails to capture variations that are specific to a certain setting . To address this shortcoming, we propose HyPerf, a Bayesian multi-level performance modeling approach that systematically distinguishes between setting-invariant and setting-variant influences, that is, influences that remain consistent across settings versus those that exhibit substantial variation. For this purpose, HyPerf employs a hierarchical structure: The upper level captures general performance trends across multiple settings (e.g., across different workloads), while the lower level refines these estimates with setting-specific deviations (e.g., workload-specific performance variations). With HyPerf, we aim at balancing accuracy and efficiency , achieving robust performance predictions with significantly fewer training samples. Unlike the state of the art, HyPerf is able to identify a minimal set of settings that captures essential performance variations, so that developers can approximate whether all setting-variant influences have been accounted for. Empirical evaluations on ten real-world software systems across up to 35 workloads demonstrates that HyPerf matches or outperforms state-of-the-art approaches while requiring fewer measurements. Notably, HyPerf enables interpretable performance reasoning and can identify minimal workload subsets that capture essential performance variations.","az":"调优软件系统的配置对于满足性能需求至关重要。然而，影响性能的不仅是配置选项，还有系统与工作负载等外部因素的交互。因此，调优需要理解外部因素的某一特定设定（例如某个特定工作负载）如何与系统配置共同影响性能。当前的性能建模方法通常不纳入外部因素，这是有原因的：为每种设定训练单独的模型代价高昂且不太可能泛化，而在多种设定上训练单一模型又无法捕捉某一设定所特有的变化。为弥补这一不足，我们提出 HyPerf，一种贝叶斯多层性能建模方法，它系统性地区分设定不变的影响与设定可变的影响，即在不同设定间保持一致的影响与呈现显著差异的影响。为此，HyPerf 采用层次结构：上层捕捉跨多种设定（例如跨不同工作负载）的一般性能趋势，下层则以设定特定的偏差（例如工作负载特有的性能变化）来精化这些估计。借助 HyPerf，我们旨在平衡准确性与效率，用显著更少的训练样本实现稳健的性能预测。与现有最先进方法不同，HyPerf 能够识别出捕捉关键性能变化的最小设定集合，使开发者可以近似判断是否已涵盖所有设定可变的影响。在十个真实世界软件系统、多达 35 种工作负载上的实证评估表明，HyPerf 在所需测量更少的情况下达到或超过了最先进方法。值得注意的是，HyPerf 支持可解释的性能推理，并能识别出捕捉关键性能变化的最小工作负载子集。","tl":"分层贝叶斯区分设定不变与可变影响，少样本预测配置性能。","au":["Johannes Dorn","Stefan Mühlbauer","Stefan Jahns","Sven Apel","Norbert Siegmund"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["configurable systems","performance prediction","Bayesian hierarchical model","workload variability","sampling efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/89/x"},{"id":"p00576","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Eye for AI: Eye-Tracking the Micro-Interruptions of GenAI Code Suggestions","tz":"AI 之眼：用眼动追踪刻画 GenAI 代码建议造成的微打断","a":"Generative AI code suggestion tools, such as GitHub Copilot, are increasingly integrated into developer workflows. While these tools promise productivity gains, the actual impact on developer cognition and task performance has been mixed. In this paper, we present the first in-depth eye-tracking study of how developers interact with generative AI code suggestions during programming. We recruited 35 professionals and student developers and recorded their gaze behavior, code suggestion interactions, and code editing activity during programming sessions. By combining high-resolution eye-tracking data with fine-grained logging of AI-generated suggestions, we quantify the cognitive costs of reviewing code suggestions. Our findings show that approximately half of the generated suggestions are not even looked at. From the suggestions that were looked at, over 75% are not used. Although suggestions are only reviewed briefly (~0.9 seconds on average), each suggestion introduces a micro-interruption that disrupts developer flow. We discuss opportunities for more efficient and context-aware generative AI code suggestions that minimize cognitive overhead.","az":"以 GitHub Copilot 为代表的生成式 AI 代码建议工具正越来越多地融入开发者工作流。虽然这些工具承诺带来生产力提升，但其对开发者认知与任务表现的实际影响却褒贬不一。本文首次深入开展眼动追踪研究，考察开发者在编程过程中如何与生成式 AI 代码建议交互。我们招募了 35 名专业开发者与学生开发者，记录了他们在编程会话中的注视行为、代码建议交互以及代码编辑活动。通过将高分辨率眼动数据与 AI 生成建议的细粒度日志相结合，我们量化了审阅代码建议的认知成本。研究发现，约有一半的生成建议甚至根本没有被看过；在被看过的建议中，超过 75% 未被采用。尽管建议只被短暂审阅（平均约 0.9 秒），但每条建议都会带来一次打断开发者心流的「微打断」。我们进而讨论了如何设计更高效、更具上下文感知能力、从而将认知开销降到最低的生成式 AI 代码建议。","tl":"首个眼动实验量化 AI 代码建议带来的微打断成本。","au":["Tarek Alakmeh","Sarah D'Angelo","Thomas Fritz"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","llm-based"],"kw":["eye tracking","code suggestions","GitHub Copilot","developer cognition","micro-interruption"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/90/x","pu":"https://eye-for-ai.hasel.dev/download/an-eye-for-ai-icse2026-preprint.pdf"},{"id":"p00577","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Actionable Warning Is Not Enough: Recommending Valid Actionable Warnings with Weak Supervision","tz":"仅有可执行告警还不够：用弱监督推荐真正有效的可执行告警","a":"The use of static analysis tools has gained increasing popularity among developers in the last few years. However, the widespread adoption of static analysis tools is hindered by their high false alarm rates (up to 90%). Previous studies have introduced the concept of actionable warnings and built machine-learning method to distinguish actionable warnings from false alarms. However, according to our empirical observation, the current assumption used for actionable warning(s) collection is rather shaky and inaccurate, leading to a large number of invalid actionable warnings. To address this problem, in this study, we build the first large actionable warning dataset by mining 68,274 reversions from Top-500 GitHub C repositories, we then take one step further by assigning each actionable warning a weak label regarding its likelihood of being a real bug. Following that, we propose a two-stage framework called ACWRecommender to automatically identify actionable warnings and recommend the actionable warnings with high probability to be real bugs (AWHB). Our approach warms up the pre-trained model UniXcoder to identify actionable warnings (coarse-grained detection stage) and rerank AWHB to the top by weakly supervised learning (fine-grained reranking stage). Experimental results show that our proposed model outperforms several baselines by a large margin in terms of nDCG and MRR for AWHB recommendation. Moreover, we ran our tool on 10 randomly selected projects and manually checked the top-ranked warnings from 2,197 reported warnings, we reported top-60 recommended warnings to developers, 27 of them were already confirmed by developers as real bugs. Developers can quickly find real bugs among the massive amount of reported warnings, which verifies the practical usage of our tool.","az":"近年来静态分析工具在开发者中日益流行。然而，其高达 90% 的误报率阻碍了静态分析工具的广泛采用。已有研究提出了「可执行告警（actionable warning）」的概念，并构建机器学习方法来区分可执行告警与误报。但根据我们的实证观察，当前用于收集可执行告警的假设相当脆弱且不准确，导致大量无效的可执行告警。为解决该问题，本研究从 GitHub Top-500 的 C 语言仓库中挖掘 68,274 个修订版本，构建了首个大规模可执行告警数据集；我们进一步为每条可执行告警赋予一个弱标签，刻画其成为真实缺陷的可能性。在此基础上，我们提出名为 ACWRecommender 的两阶段框架，自动识别可执行告警，并把极可能是真实缺陷的可执行告警（AWHB）推荐出来。我们的方法先对预训练模型 UniXcoder 进行预热以识别可执行告警（粗粒度检测阶段），再通过弱监督学习把 AWHB 重排到前列（细粒度重排阶段）。实验结果表明，在 AWHB 推荐的 nDCG 与 MRR 指标上，我们的模型大幅超越多个基线。此外，我们在随机选取的 10 个项目上运行工具，对 2,197 条报告告警中排名靠前的告警进行人工检查，向开发者上报了排名前 60 的推荐告警，其中 27 条已被开发者确认为真实缺陷。开发者可以在海量告警中快速找到真实缺陷，这验证了该工具的实用价值。","tl":"用弱标签重构可执行告警数据集并两阶段重排推荐真缺陷。","au":["Zhipeng Xue","Zhipeng Gao","Tongtong Xu","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Shanping Li"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["actionable warning","static analysis","weak supervision","false alarm","UniXcoder"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/91/x"},{"id":"p00578","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ModularEvo: Evolving Multi-Task Models via Neural Network Modularization and Composition","tz":"ModularEvo：通过神经网络模块化与组合来演化多任务模型","a":"Training a general multi-task deep neural network (DNN) model, such as a large language model, and deploying it across diverse downstream tasks has become a common practice. In long-term deployment scenarios, downstream tasks can change over time, such as new data distributions and requirements, leading to the fine-tuning of the model accordingly, i.e., evolving the model. However, traditional full-parameter fine-tuning methods adapt the model to individual tasks, resulting in degradation of the original knowledge. Although parameter-efficient fine-tuning methods could mitigate this problem, they still isolate new knowledge in external, separate parameters. As a result, the base model gains little cumulative benefit from downstream updates. These limitations stem from the indiscriminate model deployment and fine-tuning. Inspired by modular design principles in software engineering, we propose ModularEvo, a framework that enables on-demand deployment and co-evolution of multi-task models and modules across diverse downstream tasks. ModularEvo first decomposes the model into task-specific modules, each retaining a subset of relevant weights and functionality. These modules, instead of the entire model, are deployed on downstream tasks on demand. During long-term deployment, each module is independently optimized to adjust to the change of the corresponding task. Unlike conventional fine-tuning methods, ModularEvo applies modular fine-tuning to update only the task-relevant weights within modules. Furthermore, new knowledge acquired by modules is periodically integrated into the model, enabling the co-evolution of both the model and modules. We evaluate ModularEvo through extensive experiments on three Transformer models and six downstream tasks involving both classification and generation tasks. Results demonstrate the effectiveness of ModularEvo in model performance and inference efficiency in evolution scenarios. Compared to state-of-the-art baselines, ModularEvo achieves an absolute performance gain of 2.34% in multi-round evolution scenarios, and a 2.22 times speedup in inference.","az":"训练一个通用多任务深度神经网络（DNN）模型（例如大语言模型）并将其部署到多种下游任务，已经成为常见做法。在长期部署场景中，下游任务会随时间变化，例如出现新的数据分布与新需求，从而需要相应地微调模型，即让模型不断演化。然而，传统的全参数微调方法只针对单个任务适配模型，会导致原有知识退化。虽然参数高效微调方法能缓解该问题，但它们仍把新知识隔离在外部的独立参数中，结果基础模型几乎无法从下游更新中累积获益。这些局限源于不加区分的模型部署与微调。受软件工程中模块化设计原则的启发，我们提出 ModularEvo 框架，支持多任务模型与模块在多样下游任务上的按需部署与协同演化。ModularEvo 首先把模型分解为任务特定的模块，每个模块保留相关权重与功能的一个子集；部署到下游任务的是这些模块而非整个模型，且按需部署。在长期部署过程中，每个模块独立优化以适应对应任务的变化。与常规微调方法不同，ModularEvo 采用模块化微调，仅更新模块内与任务相关的权重。此外，模块新学到的知识会被周期性地整合回模型，实现模型与模块的协同演化。我们在三个 Transformer 模型和六个下游任务（涵盖分类与生成任务）上进行了大量实验评估。结果表明 ModularEvo 在演化场景下于模型性能与推理效率方面均有效：相比最新基线，在多轮演化场景中取得 2.34% 的绝对性能提升，并实现 2.22 倍的推理加速。","tl":"把模型拆成任务模块按需部署并回灌知识实现协同演化。","au":["Wenrui Long","Binhang Qi","Hailong Sun","ZongZhen Yang","Ruobing Zhao","Xiang Gao"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["model modularization","multi-task model","modular fine-tuning","model evolution","inference efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/92/x"},{"id":"p00579","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Does Core Contributor Disengagement Impact Open Source Project Activity? A Quasi-Experiment","tz":"核心贡献者退出如何影响开源项目活跃度？一项准实验研究","a":"The sustainability of Open Source Software (OSS) projects often depends on a small group of core contributors. When these contributors disengage, projects may face disruption; however, the consequences of such disengagement on OSS contribution workflows remain underexplored. This paper presents a large-scale quasi-experimental study quantifying the impact of core contributor disengagement on pull request (PR) throughput, acceptance rate, and time to merge. We analyzed over 35 million PRs across 50,804 GitHub repositories, identifying 95,958 disengagement bursts (one or more core contributors becoming inactive for >365 days within the same week) involving 174,887 contributors. Using Difference-in-Differences with matched control groups, we found that the impact varies substantially with contributor and project characteristics. Disengagements of contributors with a high share of commits lead to pronounced declines in throughput and acceptance, while long-tenured contributors’ disengagements have milder effects on those metrics but increase merge time, suggesting loss of tacit project knowledge. These findings provide empirical evidence of how core contributors’ disengagement influences OSS workflows and highlight structural factors associated with project resilience.","az":"开源软件（OSS）项目的可持续性往往依赖一小群核心贡献者。当这些贡献者退出时，项目可能陷入动荡；然而这种退出对开源贡献工作流的后果仍缺乏研究。本文开展了一项大规模准实验研究，量化核心贡献者退出对拉取请求（PR）吞吐量、接受率与合并时间的影响。我们分析了 50,804 个 GitHub 仓库中的 3,500 多万个 PR，识别出 95,958 次「退出潮」（同一周内一名或多名核心贡献者进入超过 365 天的不活跃状态），涉及 174,887 名贡献者。采用带匹配对照组的双重差分方法，我们发现影响随贡献者与项目特征差异显著：提交占比高的贡献者退出会导致吞吐量与接受率明显下降，而任期长的贡献者退出对这两个指标影响较温和，却会增加合并时间，提示隐性项目知识的流失。这些发现为核心贡献者退出如何影响开源工作流提供了实证证据，并凸显了与项目韧性相关的结构性因素。","tl":"用双重差分量化不同类型核心贡献者退出的差异化冲击。","au":["Yunqi Chen","Klaas-Jan Stol","Fabio Marcos De Abreu Santos","Daniel M. German","Bianca Trinkenreich"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["open source sustainability","core contributor disengagement","difference-in-differences","pull request throughput","quasi-experiment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/93/x"},{"id":"p00580","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Configuration-Sensitive Linux Kernel Fuzzing","tz":"配置敏感的 Linux 内核模糊测试","a":"Fuzzing operating system kernels to discover deep and complex bugs is difficult to accomplish, as kernels reside between hardware and user applications, exposing a variety of input vectors that affect their internal state. Previous approaches mainly use a kernel’s system call interface to deliver test payloads into the kernel, but reaching states and triggering bugs also require collaborative efforts from other input vectors, such as runtime parameters. Kernel runtime parameters greatly affect the execution behavior of the kernel under test, as they alter internal execution flows and thus require kernel fuzzers to manipulate them in conjunction with invoking system calls to effectively root out bugs. In this paper, we present CSGO, a kernel fuzzer that discovers more in-depth bugs through fuzzing kernel runtime parameters in conjunction with system calls. CSGO’s approach is achieved through the following designs. First, CSGO generates valid test case generation syntax for kernel configurations by extracting available parameters exposed by the kernel. Then, for the extracted parameters, CSGO statically deduces relations between the configurations and kernel system calls for initial generation guidance. Finally, during fuzzing, CSGO dynamically refines the relations between the configurations and system calls by interpreting execution feedback. We implemented CSGO and evaluated its approach on recent versions of the Linux kernel. Our results show that CSGO achieves an average of 21% improvement in overall coverage compared with existing state-of-the-art kernel fuzzers and triggers 21 previously unknown bugs, with 8 fixed by kernel maintainers.","az":"对操作系统内核做模糊测试以发现深层复杂缺陷相当困难，因为内核位于硬件与用户应用之间，暴露出多种会影响其内部状态的输入向量。以往方法主要通过内核的系统调用接口把测试载荷送入内核，但要到达特定状态并触发缺陷，还需要其他输入向量（例如运行时参数）的协同作用。内核运行时参数会极大影响被测内核的执行行为，因为它们会改变内部执行流，因此内核模糊测试器必须在调用系统调用的同时操纵这些参数，才能有效挖出缺陷。本文提出 CSGO，一个通过联合模糊测试内核运行时参数与系统调用来发现更深层缺陷的内核模糊测试器。CSGO 的方案包含以下设计：首先，CSGO 通过提取内核暴露的可用参数，为内核配置生成合法的测试用例生成语法；其次，针对提取出的参数，CSGO 静态推导配置与内核系统调用之间的关系，用于初始生成的引导；最后，在模糊测试过程中，CSGO 通过解读执行反馈动态细化配置与系统调用之间的关系。我们实现了 CSGO，并在近期版本的 Linux 内核上评估其方法。结果显示，相比现有最先进的内核模糊测试器，CSGO 在整体覆盖率上平均提升 21%，并触发了 21 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 8 个已被内核维护者修复。","tl":"首次把内核运行时参数与系统调用联合变异做模糊测试。","au":["Yuheng Shen","Jianzhong Liu","Yuhan Chen","Yifei Chu","Qiang Zhang","Guoyu Yin","Heyuan Shi","Yu Jiang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","security"],"kw":["kernel fuzzing","runtime parameters","syscall generation","coverage feedback","Linux kernel"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/94/x"},{"id":"p00581","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Enhancing Issue Localization Agent with Tool-Interactive Training","tz":"用工具交互式训练增强 Issue 定位智能体","a":"Issue localization, the process of identifying code locations that need modification to resolve software issues, is a critical yet challenging task in software development. The semantic gap between natural language issue descriptions and faulty code requires complex multi-hop reasoning through code dependencies. Existing LLM-based agents attempt to address this by integrating repository retrieval tools, which poses a higher demand for LLMs to effectively utilize various tools during multi-step reasoning for issue localization. To tackle this challenge, we present ToolTrain, a two-stage tool-interactive training framework combining rejection-sampled supervised fine-tuning and tool-interactive reinforcement learning to enhance LLMs’ ability to use retrieval tools for issue localization. Experimental results show that ToolTrain-trained models achieve state-of-the-art performance, with our 32B model even surpassing Claude-3.7 on function-level localization. The results also show that improved localization performance translates to better end-to-end issue resolution performance. This further demonstrates that training for issue localization is a viable and effective strategy for improving automated software development.","az":"Issue 定位，即找出为解决软件 issue 需要修改的代码位置，是软件开发中关键而困难的任务。自然语言 issue 描述与缺陷代码之间的语义鸿沟，要求在代码依赖上进行复杂的多跳推理。已有基于 LLM 的智能体尝试通过集成仓库检索工具来应对，但这对 LLM 在多步推理中有效使用各种工具提出了更高要求。为应对该挑战，我们提出 ToolTrain，一个两阶段的工具交互式训练框架，结合拒绝采样的监督微调与工具交互式强化学习，以增强 LLM 使用检索工具进行 issue 定位的能力。实验结果表明，经 ToolTrain 训练的模型达到了当前最佳性能，我们的 32B 模型在函数级定位上甚至超过了 Claude-3.7。结果还显示，定位性能的提升可以转化为更好的端到端 issue 求解性能，这进一步说明针对 issue 定位进行训练是提升自动化软件开发的可行且有效的策略。","tl":"拒绝采样 SFT 加工具交互式 RL 训练出的定位智能体超越 Claude-3.7。","au":["Zexiong Ma","Chao Peng","Qunhong Zeng","Pengfei Gao","Yanzhen Zou","Bing Xie"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["issue localization","tool-interactive training","reinforcement learning","rejection sampling SFT","repository retrieval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/95/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.03012"},{"id":"p00582","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RusyFuzz: Unhandled Exception Guided Fuzzing for Rust OS Kernel","tz":"RusyFuzz：面向 Rust 操作系统内核的未处理异常引导模糊测试","a":"Rust’s strong type system and ownership model eliminate many traditional memory safety issues in OS kernels. However, logic errors—such as unchecked indexing and failed unwrap operations—can still cause panic!s that crash the entire system. Existing kernel fuzzers, designed primarily for C-based kernels and reliant on KCOV, treat all crashes uniformly and fail to account for Rust-specific failure modes. We present RusyFuzz, the first fuzzing framework tailored to Rust OS kernels that explicitly targets panic-prone code paths using an unhandled-exception-guided strategy. RusyFuzz analyzes the compiler-inserted assertions within the Rust MIR, performs backward slicing to link these assertions to system call arguments, and uses constraint solving to synthesize inputs that trigger panics. In the absence of built-in coverage support, RusyFuzz employs a lightweight, log-based instrumentation method to enable coverage-guided fuzzing. We evaluate RusyFuzz on three emerging Rust-based kernels: Asterinas, Redox OS, and RuxOS. RusyFuzz discovers 70 previously unknown and developer-confirmed vulnerabilities. Compared to Trinity, it uncovers over twice as many bugs while improving line coverage by 14.4%. These results demonstrate that unhandled-exception-guided fuzzing is critical for uncovering logic bugs and enhancing the reliability of Rust OS kernels, providing the first systematic methodology for detecting such vulnerabilities.","az":"Rust 强大的类型系统与所有权模型消除了操作系统内核中许多传统的内存安全问题。然而，诸如未检查索引、unwrap 操作失败之类的逻辑错误仍会引发 panic!，导致整个系统崩溃。现有内核模糊测试器主要面向 C 语言内核设计并依赖 KCOV，它们对所有崩溃一视同仁，无法考虑 Rust 特有的失效模式。我们提出 RusyFuzz，这是首个专门面向 Rust 操作系统内核的模糊测试框架，采用未处理异常引导策略显式地瞄准易 panic 的代码路径。RusyFuzz 分析 Rust MIR 中由编译器插入的断言，进行后向切片以把这些断言与系统调用参数关联起来，并利用约束求解合成能触发 panic 的输入。在缺少内置覆盖率支持的情况下，RusyFuzz 采用轻量级的基于日志的插桩方法，以实现覆盖率引导的模糊测试。我们在三个新兴的 Rust 内核 Asterinas、Redox OS 和 RuxOS 上评估 RusyFuzz，共发现 70 个此前未知且被开发者确认的漏洞。与 Trinity 相比，它发现的缺陷数量是其两倍以上，同时行覆盖率提升 14.4%。这些结果表明，未处理异常引导的模糊测试对于揭示逻辑缺陷、提升 Rust 操作系统内核可靠性至关重要，并提供了检测此类漏洞的首个系统性方法论。","tl":"用 MIR 断言后向切片与约束求解定向触发 Rust 内核 panic。","au":["Yuwei Liu","Yanhao Wang","Minghua Wang","Lin Huang","Purui Su","Tao Wei"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","security"],"kw":["Rust OS kernel","panic-guided fuzzing","MIR assertions","backward slicing","coverage instrumentation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/96/x"},{"id":"p00583","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"VDBFuzz: Understanding and Detecting Crash Bugs in Vector Database Management Systems","tz":"VDBFuzz：理解并检测向量数据库管理系统中的崩溃缺陷","a":"Vector Database Management Systems~(VDBMSs) have become critical in LLM-integrated applications, powering tasks such as Retrieval-Augmented Generation~(RAG) and long-term memory. However, their inherent complexity—stemming from high-dimensional data structures, diverse indexing strategies, and heterogeneous implementations—makes them prone to reliability issues, particularly crash bugs caused by boundary condition failures such as invalid configurations and mismatched data dimensions. These bugs can result in severe consequences, including data loss, corrupted indexes, and cascading downstream failures. To address this gap, we propose VDBFuzz, the first fuzzing framework specifically designed to detect crash bugs in VDBMSs through systematic boundary value testing. VDBFuzz systematically leverages techniques to collect high-quality seeds, generate edge-case inputs, and explore complex API interactions. We evaluated VDBFuzz on 8 representative VDBMSs, including native systems (e.g., Weaviate, Milvus), libraries (e.g., Faiss, hnswlib), and extended systems (e.g., pgvector, sqlite-vec). VDBFuzz achieved up to 3x higher code coverage compared to state-of-the-art tools such as RESTler and Schemathesis, uncovering 19 previously unknown crash bugs, including 13 memory corruption and 6 runtime exceptions. These results highlight VDBFuzz’s effectiveness in improving the robustness and reliability of VDBMSs.","az":"向量数据库管理系统（VDBMS）已成为 LLM 集成应用的关键组件，支撑检索增强生成（RAG）与长期记忆等任务。然而，其固有的复杂性——源自高维数据结构、多样的索引策略以及异构实现——使其易出现可靠性问题，尤其是由无效配置、数据维度不匹配等边界条件失败引发的崩溃缺陷。这些缺陷可能造成严重后果，包括数据丢失、索引损坏以及级联的下游故障。为填补这一空白，我们提出 VDBFuzz，这是首个专门为通过系统化边界值测试来检测 VDBMS 崩溃缺陷而设计的模糊测试框架。VDBFuzz 系统性地运用多种技术来收集高质量种子、生成边界用例输入并探索复杂的 API 交互。我们在 8 个有代表性的 VDBMS 上评估 VDBFuzz，包括原生系统（如 Weaviate、Milvus）、库（如 Faiss、hnswlib）以及扩展型系统（如 pgvector、sqlite-vec）。相比 RESTler、Schemathesis 等最新工具，VDBFuzz 的代码覆盖率最高提升 3 倍，发现 19 个此前未知的崩溃缺陷，其中 13 个为内存破坏、6 个为运行时异常。这些结果凸显了 VDBFuzz 在提升 VDBMS 健壮性与可靠性方面的有效性。","tl":"首个面向向量数据库的边界值模糊测试框架，挖出 19 个崩溃缺陷。","au":["Shenao Wang","Zhao Liu","Yanjie Zhao","Quanchen Zou","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["vector database","crash bugs","boundary value testing","fuzzing","API interaction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/97/x"},{"id":"p00584","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Beyond Final Code: A Process-Oriented Error Analysis of Software Development Agents in Real-World GitHub Scenarios","tz":"超越最终代码：真实 GitHub 场景中软件开发智能体的过程导向错误分析","a":"AI-driven software development has rapidly advanced with the emergence of software development agents that leverage large language models (LLMs) to tackle complex, repository-level software engineering tasks. These agents go beyond just generation of final code; they engage in multi-step reasoning, utilize various tools for code modification and debugging, and interact with execution environments to diagnose and iteratively resolve issues. However, most existing evaluations focus primarily on static analyses of final code outputs, yielding limited insights into the agents’ dynamic problem-solving processes. To fill this gap, we conduct an in-depth empirical study on 3,977 solving-phase trajectories and 3,931 testing-phase logs from 8 top-ranked agents evaluated on 500 GitHub issues in the SWE-Bench benchmark. Our exploratory analysis shows that Python execution errors during the issue resolution phase correlate with lower resolution rates and increased reasoning overheads. We have identified the most prevalent errors—such as ModuleNotFoundError and TypeError—and highlighted particularly challenging errors like OSError and database-related issues (e.g., IntegrityError) that demand significantly more debugging effort. Furthermore, we have discovered 3 bugs in the SWE-Bench platform that affect benchmark fairness and accuracy; these issues have been reported to and confirmed by the maintainers. To promote transparency and foster future research, we publicly share our datasets and analysis scripts.","az":"随着利用大语言模型（LLM）处理复杂的仓库级软件工程任务的软件开发智能体出现，AI 驱动的软件开发迅速发展。这些智能体不只是生成最终代码；它们会进行多步推理、使用各种工具修改与调试代码，并与执行环境交互以诊断并迭代地解决问题。然而，现有评测大多只关注对最终代码产物的静态分析，对智能体动态解题过程的洞察有限。为填补这一空白，我们对 8 个排名靠前的智能体在 SWE-Bench 基准 500 个 GitHub issue 上产生的 3,977 条求解阶段轨迹与 3,931 条测试阶段日志开展了深入实证研究。我们的探索性分析显示，issue 求解阶段的 Python 执行错误与更低的解决率、更高的推理开销相关。我们识别出最常见的错误，如 ModuleNotFoundError 与 TypeError，并指出了 OSError 以及数据库相关问题（如 IntegrityError）等特别棘手、需要显著更多调试投入的错误。此外，我们还发现了 SWE-Bench 平台中影响基准公平性与准确性的 3 个缺陷，这些问题已上报并获维护者确认。为促进透明度并推动后续研究，我们公开了数据集与分析脚本。","tl":"从近四千条轨迹揭示执行错误类型如何拖垮智能体解题率。","au":["Zhi Chen","Wei Ma","Lingxiao Jiang"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["software development agents","trajectory analysis","SWE-Bench","execution errors","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/98/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.12374"},{"id":"p00585","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Debugging Performance Issues in WebAssembly Runtimes via Mutation-based Inference","tz":"通过基于变异的推断调试 WebAssembly 运行时的性能问题","a":"Performance debugging in WebAssembly (Wasm) runtimes is essential for ensuring the robustness of Wasm, especially since performance issues have frequently occurred in Wasm runtimes, which can significantly degrade the capabilities of hosted services. Many performance issues in Wasm runtimes result from suboptimal compilation of input Wasm programs, for which existing performance debugging methods primarily designed for application-level inefficiencies are not well-suited. In this paper, we present WarpL, a novel mutation-based approach that aims to identify the exact suboptimal instruction sequences responsible for the performance issues in Wasm runtimes, thereby narrowing down the root causes. Specifically, WarpL obtains a functionally similar mutant in which the performance issue does not manifest, and isolates the exact suboptimal instructions by comparing the machine code of the original and mutated programs. We implement WarpL as an open-source tool and evaluate it on 12 real-world performance issues across three widely used Wasm runtimes. WarpL identified the exact causes in 10 out of 12 issues. Notably, we have used WarpL to successfully diagnose six previously unknown performance issues in Wasmtime.","az":"WebAssembly（Wasm）运行时的性能调试对保障 Wasm 的健壮性至关重要，尤其是因为 Wasm 运行时中频繁出现性能问题，会显著削弱其承载服务的能力。Wasm 运行时中的许多性能问题源自对输入 Wasm 程序的次优编译，而现有主要面向应用层低效问题的性能调试方法并不适用。本文提出 WarpL，一种新颖的基于变异的方法，旨在识别导致 Wasm 运行时性能问题的确切次优指令序列，从而缩小根因范围。具体而言，WarpL 获得一个功能相似但不再表现出该性能问题的变异体，并通过比较原始程序与变异程序的机器码来隔离出确切的次优指令。我们将 WarpL 实现为开源工具，并在三个广泛使用的 Wasm 运行时上针对 12 个真实性能问题进行评估。WarpL 在 12 个问题中的 10 个里准确识别出了根因。值得注意的是，我们已用 WarpL 成功诊断出 Wasmtime 中六个此前未知的性能问题。","tl":"用功能等价变异体差分机器码，精确定位次优指令序列。","au":["Ruiying Zeng","Shuyao Jiang","Wenxuan Zhao","Yangfan Zhou"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["WebAssembly runtime","performance debugging","mutation-based inference","root cause isolation","Wasmtime"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/99/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/99/Debugging-Performance-Issues-in-WebAssembly-Runtimes-via-Mutation-based-Inference"},{"id":"p00586","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When AI Takes the Wheel: Security Analysis of Framework-Constrained Program Generation","tz":"当 AI 掌舵：框架受限程序生成的安全性分析","a":"In recent years, the AI wave has grown rapidly in software development. Even novice developers can now design and generate complex framework-constrained software systems based on their high-level requirements with the help of Large Language Models (LLMs). However, when LLMs gradually “take the wheel” of software development, developers may only check whether the program works. They often miss security problems hidden in how the generated programs are implemented. In this work, we investigate the security properties of framework-constrained programs generated by state-of-the-art LLMs. We focus specifically on Chrome extensions due to their complex security model involving multiple privilege boundaries and isolated components. To achieve this, we built ChromeSecBench, a dataset with 140 prompts based on known vulnerable extensions. We used these prompts to instruct nine state-of-the-art LLMs to generate complete Chrome extensions, and then analyzed them for vulnerabilities across three dimensions: scenario types, model differences, and vulnerability categories. Our results show that LLMs produced vulnerable programs at alarmingly high rates (18%-50%), particularly in Authentication & Identity and Cookie Management scenarios (up to 83% and 78% respectively). Most vulnerabilities exposed sensitive browser data like cookies, history, or bookmarks to untrusted code. Interestingly, we found that advanced reasoning models performed worse, generating more vulnerabilities than simpler models. These findings highlight a critical gap between LLMs’ coding skills and their ability to write secure framework-constrained programs.","az":"近年来，AI 浪潮在软件开发中迅速兴起。借助大语言模型（LLM），即使是新手开发者如今也能基于高层需求设计并生成复杂的框架受限软件系统。然而，当 LLM 逐渐「掌舵」软件开发时，开发者可能只检查程序是否能跑通，却常常忽视隐藏在生成程序实现方式中的安全问题。本工作中，我们考察了当前最先进 LLM 生成的框架受限程序的安全属性。我们特别聚焦 Chrome 扩展，因为其安全模型复杂，涉及多重权限边界与隔离组件。为此，我们基于已知的脆弱扩展构建了包含 140 条提示的数据集 ChromeSecBench。我们用这些提示指示九个最先进的 LLM 生成完整的 Chrome 扩展，然后从场景类型、模型差异与漏洞类别三个维度分析其漏洞。结果显示，LLM 生成脆弱程序的比例高得惊人（18%–50%），在「认证与身份」和「Cookie 管理」场景中尤为严重（分别高达 83% 与 78%）。大多数漏洞会把 cookie、历史记录或书签等敏感浏览器数据暴露给不可信代码。有趣的是，我们发现高级推理模型表现更差，生成的漏洞比简单模型更多。这些发现凸显了 LLM 的编码能力与其编写安全的框架受限程序的能力之间存在关键鸿沟。","tl":"发现推理模型写的 Chrome 扩展反而漏洞更多，最高 83%。","au":["Yue Liu","Zhenchang Xing","Shidong Pan","Kla Tantithamthavorn"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["framework-constrained generation","Chrome extension security","ChromeSecBench","LLM code security","privilege boundary"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/100/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16823"},{"id":"p00587","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Enhancing LLM Code Generation with Ensembles: A Similarity-Based Selection Approach","tz":"用集成提升 LLM 代码生成：一种基于相似度的选择方法","a":"Ensemble learning has been widely used in machine learning to improve model robustness, accuracy, and generalization, but has not yet been applied to code generation tasks with large language models (LLMs). We propose an ensemble approach for LLMs in code generation. Instead of relying on the output of a single model, we generate multiple candidate programs from different LLMs and apply a structured voting mechanism to select the most reliable solution. For voting, we compute syntactic and semantic similarity using CodeBLEU and behavioral equivalence using CrossHair’s differential behavior analysis. By aggregating these similarity scores, we select the program that best aligns with the consensus among the candidates. We show through experiments that our ensemble approach consistently outperforms standalone LLMs on the well-known HumanEval and the more challenging LiveCodeBench datasets, achieving an accuracy of 90.2% and 50.2%, respectively, on the two datasets. In comparison, the best-performing LLM (GPT-4o) has an accuracy of 83.5% and 43.4%, respectively. Furthermore, even when restricted to free open source models, our method achieves an accuracy of 80.5% and 41.6%, respectively, demonstrating the viability of our approach in resource-constrained settings.","az":"集成学习在机器学习中被广泛用于提升模型的健壮性、准确性与泛化能力，但尚未被应用于大语言模型（LLM）的代码生成任务。我们提出一种面向 LLM 代码生成的集成方法：不依赖单一模型的输出，而是从不同 LLM 生成多个候选程序，并应用结构化投票机制来选出最可靠的解。在投票中，我们使用 CodeBLEU 计算语法与语义相似度，并使用 CrossHair 的差分行为分析计算行为等价性；通过聚合这些相似度得分，我们选出与候选集共识最吻合的程序。实验表明，我们的集成方法在著名的 HumanEval 与更具挑战性的 LiveCodeBench 数据集上持续优于单一 LLM，两个数据集上的准确率分别达到 90.2% 与 50.2%；相比之下，表现最好的单一模型 GPT-4o 的准确率分别为 83.5% 与 43.4%。此外，即便仅限使用免费的开源模型，我们的方法也分别达到 80.5% 与 41.6% 的准确率，证明了该方法在资源受限场景下的可行性。","tl":"用 CodeBLEU 加差分行为等价做跨模型投票选代码。","au":["Tarek Mahmud","Bin Duan","Corina S. Păsăreanu","Guowei Yang"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["ensemble code generation","CodeBLEU","behavioral equivalence","CrossHair","candidate voting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/101/x"},{"id":"p00588","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AdapTrack: Constrained Decoding without Distorting LLM's Output Intent","tz":"AdapTrack：不扭曲 LLM 输出意图的受限解码","a":"Language model-based code generation and completion tools have been widely adopted, but they may sometimes produce code that does not meet necessary constraints, such as syntactic correctness or API existence. Constrained decoding techniques are developed to help the model generate code that adheres to the constraints by greedily eliminating generation options that violate constraints at each step of the generation process. However, there is a severe limitation of constrained decoding, that it distorts the model’s output intent, forcing it to produce code that may satisfy the constraint but does not match the development intent and is therefore incorrect. In response to this challenge, we propose AdapTrack. By incorporating backtracking into the generation process, AdapTrack avoids distorting the output intent of the language model, thereby producing results that are not only constraint-compliant but also more semantically aligned with model’s output intent. On our synthetic API completion dataset, AdapTrack can achieve up to 360.87% improvement compared to constrained decoding; on the real-world API completion dataset we collect that exhibits similar issues, AdapTrack can also achieve an improvement of up to 38.93% over constrained decoding; in general code genration benchmarks, compared to constrained decoding, AdapTrack can achieve up to 7.84% improvement on HumanEval, and up to 6.42% improvement on MBPP. This indicates that, simply by better adhering to the model’s output intent, AdapTrack can achieve significant improvements. We provide a theoretical proof that the distribution produced by AdapTrack aligns with the model’s distribution given the generated tokens, thereby ensuring that the model’s output intent is not distorted. Experiments on domain-specific language problems show that, compared to existing methods, our approach can provide generation results that are more consistent with the language model’s distribution.","az":"基于语言模型的代码生成与补全工具已被广泛采用，但它们有时会产生不满足必要约束的代码，例如语法正确性或 API 是否存在。受限解码技术被提出，通过在生成过程的每一步贪心地剔除违反约束的生成选项，帮助模型产出符合约束的代码。然而受限解码存在一个严重局限：它会扭曲模型的输出意图，迫使模型产出虽满足约束却与开发意图不符、因而错误的代码。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 AdapTrack。通过在生成过程中引入回溯，AdapTrack 避免扭曲语言模型的输出意图，从而产出既符合约束、又在语义上更贴合模型输出意图的结果。在我们的合成 API 补全数据集上，相比受限解码，AdapTrack 最高可带来 360.87% 的提升；在我们收集的、表现出类似问题的真实 API 补全数据集上，相比受限解码也可取得最高 38.93% 的提升；在通用代码生成基准上，相比受限解码，AdapTrack 在 HumanEval 上最高提升 7.84%，在 MBPP 上最高提升 6.42%。这表明，仅仅通过更好地遵循模型的输出意图，AdapTrack 就能取得显著提升。我们给出理论证明：在已生成 token 的条件下，AdapTrack 所产生的分布与模型分布一致，从而保证模型输出意图不被扭曲。在领域专用语言问题上的实验表明，相比现有方法，我们的方法能给出与语言模型分布更一致的生成结果。","tl":"在受限解码中引入回溯，理论上保证不偏离模型原分布。","au":["Yongmin Li","Jia Li","Ge Li","Zhi Jin"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["constrained decoding","backtracking","API completion","output intent","code generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/102/x"},{"id":"p00589","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"WhyFlow: Interrogative Debugger for Sensemaking Taint Analysis","tz":"WhyFlow：面向污点分析意义建构的问答式调试器","a":"Taint analysis is a security analysis technique used to track the flow of potentially dangerous data through an application and its dependent libraries. Investigating why certain unexpected flows appear and why expected flows are missing is an important sensemaking process during end-user taint analysis. Existing taint analysis tools often do not provide this end-user debugging capability, where developers can ask why, why-not, and what-if questions about dataflows and reason about the impact of configuring sources and sinks, and models of 3rd-party libraries that abstract permissible and impermissible data flows. Furthermore, a tree-view or a list-view used in existing taint-analyzer’s visualization makes it difficult to reason about the global impact on connectivity between multiple sources and sinks. Inspired by the insight that sensemaking tool-generated results can be significantly improved by a QA inquiry process, we propose WhyFlow, a first end-user question-answer style debugging interface for taint analysis. It enables a user to ask why, why-not, and what-if questions to investigate the existence of suspicious flows, the non-existence of expected flows, and the global impact of third-party library models. WhyFlow performs speculative what-if analysis, to help a user in debugging how different connectivity assumptions affect overall results. A user study with 12 participants shows that participants using WhyFlow achieved 21% higher accuracy on average, compared to CodeQL. They also reported a 45% reduction in mental demand (NASA-TLX) and rated higher confidence in identifying relevant flows using WhyFlow. This shows WhyFlow’s potential to significantly reduce sensemaking effort.","az":"污点分析是一种安全分析技术，用于追踪潜在危险数据在应用及其依赖库中的流动。在终端用户使用污点分析时，探究为何出现某些意料之外的数据流、为何缺失预期的数据流，是一个重要的意义建构（sensemaking）过程。现有污点分析工具通常不提供这种面向终端用户的调试能力，即开发者可以就数据流提出 why、why-not 与 what-if 问题，并推理配置源点、汇点以及第三方库模型（用于抽象允许与不允许的数据流）所带来的影响。此外，现有污点分析器可视化中使用的树状视图或列表视图，使人难以推理多个源点与汇点之间连通性的全局影响。受「工具生成结果可通过问答式探询过程显著改进」这一洞见启发，我们提出 WhyFlow，首个面向污点分析的终端用户问答式调试界面。它让用户可以提出 why、why-not 与 what-if 问题，以调查可疑数据流为何存在、预期数据流为何不存在，以及第三方库模型的全局影响。WhyFlow 执行推测式的 what-if 分析，帮助用户调试不同连通性假设如何影响整体结果。一项包含 12 名参与者的用户研究表明，与使用 CodeQL 相比，使用 WhyFlow 的参与者平均准确率高出 21%，他们还报告心智负荷（NASA-TLX）降低 45%，并对使用 WhyFlow 识别相关数据流更有信心。这展示了 WhyFlow 显著降低意义建构成本的潜力。","tl":"首个支持 why/why-not/what-if 提问的污点分析交互调试界面。","au":["Burak Yetiştiren","Hong Jin Kang","Miryung Kim"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["human-study","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["taint analysis","interrogative debugging","sensemaking","what-if analysis","user study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/103/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.07198"},{"id":"p00590","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PTV: Scalable Version Detection of Web Libraries and its Security Application","tz":"PTV：可扩展的 Web 库版本检测及其安全应用","a":"Identifying the libraries used by a web application is an important task for sales intelligence, website profiling, and web security analysis. Recent work uses tree structures to represent the property relationships of the library at runtime, realizing automatic library identification without pinpointing versions. But when assessing the security risks associated with these web libraries or conducting fine-grained software analysis, it becomes essential to determine the specific version of the library in use. However, existing tree-based methods are not directly applicable to version detection due to the huge storage requirements for maintaining separate trees for a large number of versions. This paper proposes a novel algorithm to find the most unique structure out of each tree in a forest so that the footprint of the features can be greatly minimized. We implement this algorithm into a web library detection tool. Experimental evaluations on 556 web libraries, encompassing 30,810 versions, reveal that our tool reduces space requirements by up to 99%, achieves more precise version detection compared to existing tools, and detects 190 vulnerabilities on 200 top-traffic websites.","az":"识别 Web 应用所使用的库，对销售情报、网站画像与 Web 安全分析都是重要任务。近期工作使用树结构表示库在运行时的属性关系，实现了无需确定版本的自动库识别。但在评估这些 Web 库的安全风险或进行细粒度软件分析时，确定所用库的具体版本就变得必不可少。然而，由于为大量版本各自维护一棵树所需的存储开销巨大，现有基于树的方法无法直接用于版本检测。本文提出一种新算法，从森林中的每棵树里找出最具唯一性的结构，从而极大压缩特征的存储占用。我们将该算法实现为一个 Web 库检测工具。在涵盖 30,810 个版本的 556 个 Web 库上的实验评估显示，我们的工具将空间需求最多降低 99%，相比现有工具实现了更精确的版本检测，并在 200 个高流量网站上检测出 190 个漏洞。","tl":"用最具唯一性子结构把版本指纹压缩 99% 仍能精确定版。","au":["Xinyue Liu","Haipeng Cai","Lukasz Ziarek"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["web library detection","version identification","software composition analysis","property tree","vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/104/x"},{"id":"p00591","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Context-Free Grammar Inference for Complex Programming Languages in Black Box Settings","tz":"黑盒设定下面向复杂编程语言的上下文无关文法推断","a":"Grammar inference for complex programming languages remains a significant challenge, as existing approaches fail to scale to real-world datasets within practical time constraints. In our experiments,none of the state-of-the-art tools, including Arvada, Treevada and Kedavra were able to infer grammars for complex languages such as C, C++, and Java within 48 hours. Arvada and Treevada perform grammar inference directly on full-length input examples, which proves inefficient for large files commonly found in such languages. While Kedavra introduces data decomposition to create shorter examples for grammar inference, its lexical analysis still relies on the original inputs. Additionally, its strict no-overgeneralization constraint limits the construction of complex grammars. To overcome these limitations, we propose Crucio, which builds a decomposition forest to extract short examples for lexical and grammar inference via a distributional matrix. Experimental results show that Crucio is the only method capable of successfully inferring grammars for complex programming languages (where the number of nonterminals is up to 17× greater than in prior benchmarks) within reasonable time limits. On the prior simple benchmark, Crucio achieves an average recall improvement of 1.37× and 1.19× over Treevada and Kedavra, respectively, and improves F1 scores by 1.21× and 1.13×.","az":"复杂编程语言的文法推断仍是重大挑战，现有方法无法在可接受的时间内扩展到真实数据集。在我们的实验中，包括 Arvada、Treevada 与 Kedavra 在内的最先进工具，没有一个能在 48 小时内为 C、C++、Java 等复杂语言推断出文法。Arvada 与 Treevada 直接在完整长度的输入样例上做文法推断，对这类语言中常见的大文件而言效率低下；Kedavra 虽引入数据分解以生成更短的样例用于文法推断，但其词法分析仍依赖原始输入，且其严格的「不过度泛化」约束限制了复杂文法的构建。为克服这些局限，我们提出 Crucio，它构建分解森林，借助分布矩阵提取短样例以进行词法与文法推断。实验结果表明，Crucio 是唯一能在合理时间内成功推断复杂编程语言文法的方法（其非终结符数量最高可达以往基准的 17 倍）。在此前的简单基准上，Crucio 相比 Treevada 与 Kedavra 的平均召回率分别提升 1.37 倍与 1.19 倍，F1 分数分别提升 1.21 倍与 1.13 倍。","tl":"用分解森林加分布矩阵首次在合理时间内推断出 C/C++/Java 文法。","au":["Feifei Li","Xiao Chen","xiaoyu sun","Xi Xiao","Shaohua Wang","Yong Ding","Sheng Wen","Qingli"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["grammar inference","context-free grammar","black-box","decomposition forest","lexical inference"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/105/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12385"},{"id":"p00592","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Revisiting \"Revisiting Neuron Coverage for DNN Testing: A Layer-Wise and Distribution-Aware Criterion\": A Critical Review and Implications on DNN Coverage Testing","tz":"再审视《Revisiting Neuron Coverage for DNN Testing: A Layer-Wise and Distribution-Aware Criterion》：批判性评述及其对 DNN 覆盖测试的启示","a":"We present a critical review of Neural Coverage (NLC), a state-of-the-art DNN coverage criterion by Yuan et al. at ICSE 2023. While NLC proposes to satisfy eight design requirements and demonstrates strong empirical performance, we question some of their theoretical and empirical assumptions. We observe that NLC deviates from core principles of coverage criteria, such as monotonicity and test suite order independence, and could more fully account for key properties of the covariance matrix. Additionally, we note threats to the validity of the empirical study, related to the ground truth ordering of test suites. Through our empirical validation, we substantiate our claims and propose improvements for future DNN coverage metrics. Finally, we conclude by discussing the implications of these insights.","az":"我们对 Yuan 等人在 ICSE 2023 提出的最先进 DNN 覆盖准则 Neural Coverage（NLC）进行批判性评述。虽然 NLC 宣称满足八项设计要求并展现出很强的实证表现，但我们对其部分理论与实证假设提出质疑。我们观察到，NLC 偏离了覆盖准则的核心原则，例如单调性与测试套件顺序无关性，并且本可更充分地考虑协方差矩阵的关键性质。此外，我们指出其实证研究中与测试套件真值排序有关的效度威胁。通过实证验证，我们佐证了上述论断，并为未来的 DNN 覆盖度量提出改进建议。最后，我们讨论了这些洞见的意义。","tl":"指出 NLC 违背单调性与顺序无关性等覆盖准则基本性质。","au":["Jinhan Kim","Nargiz Humbatova","Gunel Jahangirova","Shin Yoo","Paolo Tonella"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["reproducibility-replication","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["neuron coverage","DNN testing","coverage criterion","critical review","monotonicity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/106/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.08729"},{"id":"p00593","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Learning From Software Failures: A Case Study at a National Space Research Center","tz":"从软件失效中学习：某国家级航天研究中心的案例研究","a":"Software failures can have significant consequences, making learning from failures a critical aspect of software engineering. While software organizations are recommended to conduct postmortems to learn from failures, the effectiveness and adoption of these practices vary widely. Understanding how engineers gather, document, and share & reuse lessons from failures is essential for improving software reliability and preventing recurring failures. High-reliability organizations (HROs) often develop software systems where failures carry catastrophic risks, requiring continuous learning practices to ensure reliability. These organizations provide a valuable setting to examine practices and challenges for learning from software failures. Such insight could help develop processes and tools to improve reliability and to prevent recurring failures. However, we lack in-depth industry perspectives on the practices and challenges associated with failure analysis and learning. To address this gap, we conducted a case study through 10 in-depth interviews with research software engineers at a national space research center. We examine how they gather, document, and share & reuse lessons from failures. To assess the transferability of our findings, we include data from 5 additional interviews at other HROs. Our findings provide insight on how software engineers learn from failures in practice. To summarize our findings: (1) failure learning is informal, ad-hoc, and inconsistently integrated into SDLC; (2) recurring failures persist due to the absence of structured processes; and (3) key challenges—including time constraints, knowledge loss due to team turnover and fragmented documentation, and weak process enforcement, which undermine efforts to systematically learn from failures. Our findings contribute to a deeper understanding of how software engineers learn from failures and offer guidance for improving failure management practices.","az":"软件失效可能造成严重后果，因而从失效中学习是软件工程的关键一环。尽管人们建议软件组织通过复盘（postmortem）来从失效中学习，但这些实践的有效性与采纳程度差异很大。理解工程师如何收集、记录、共享与复用失效教训，对提升软件可靠性、防止失效重演至关重要。高可靠性组织（HRO）常常开发那些失效会带来灾难性风险的软件系统，因而需要持续学习实践来保障可靠性，这为考察从软件失效中学习的实践与挑战提供了有价值的场景。然而，我们缺乏关于失效分析与学习相关实践和挑战的深入行业视角。为填补这一空白，我们通过对某国家级航天研究中心的研究型软件工程师进行 10 次深度访谈，开展了一项案例研究，考察他们如何收集、记录、共享与复用失效教训。为评估发现的可迁移性，我们还纳入了来自其他高可靠性组织的 5 次访谈数据。我们的发现揭示了软件工程师在实践中如何从失效中学习，概括为：（1）失效学习是非正式、临时性的，并未一致地融入软件开发生命周期；（2）由于缺乏结构化流程，失效反复发生；（3）关键挑战包括时间压力、团队人员流动造成的知识流失与文档碎片化、以及流程约束薄弱，它们共同削弱了系统性地从失效中学习的努力。我们的发现有助于更深入地理解软件工程师如何从失效中学习，并为改进失效管理实践提供指导。","tl":"访谈揭示高可靠性组织的失效学习仍是临时非正式流程。","au":["Dharun Anandayuvaraj","Tanmay Singla","Zain Alabedin Haj Hammadeh","Andreas Lund","Alexandra Holloway","James C. Davis"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["human-study","industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study"],"kw":["learning from failures","postmortem","high-reliability organization","interview study","software reliability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/107/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.06301"},{"id":"p00594","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"“I need to learn better searching tactics for privacy policy laws.” Investigating Software Developers’ Behavior When Using Sources on Privacy Issues","tz":"「我需要学会更好的隐私政策法规检索技巧」：考察软件开发者在隐私问题上使用信息源的行为","a":"Since the introduction of the European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), software developers increasingly have to make privacy-related decisions during system design and implementation. However, past research showed that they often lack legal expertise and struggle with privacy-compliant development. To shed light on how effective current information sources are in supporting them with privacy-sensitive implementation, we conducted a qualitative study with 30 developers. Participants were presented with a privacy-sensitive scenario and asked to identify privacy issues and suggest measures using their knowledge, online resources, and an AI assistant. We observed developers’ decision-making in think-aloud sessions and discussed it in follow-up interviews. We found that participants struggled with all three sources: personal knowledge was insufficient, web content was often too complex, and while AI assistants provided clear and user-tailored responses, they lacked contextual relevance and failed to identify scenario-specific issues. Our study highlights major shortcomings in existing support for privacy-related development tasks. Based on our findings, we offer recommendations for more accessible, understandable, and actionable privacy resources for developers.","az":"自欧盟《通用数据保护条例》（GDPR）与《加州消费者隐私法案》（CCPA）出台以来，软件开发者在系统设计与实现过程中越来越需要做出与隐私相关的决策。然而以往研究表明，他们往往缺乏法律专业知识，在隐私合规开发上举步维艰。为弄清当前的信息源在支持隐私敏感实现方面究竟有多有效，我们对 30 名开发者开展了一项定性研究。参与者面对一个隐私敏感场景，被要求利用自身知识、在线资源与一个 AI 助手来识别隐私问题并提出应对措施。我们在出声思考（think-aloud）环节观察开发者的决策过程，并在后续访谈中加以讨论。我们发现参与者在这三类信息源上都遇到困难：个人知识不足；网络内容往往过于复杂；而 AI 助手虽然给出清晰且贴合用户的回答，却缺乏上下文相关性，未能识别出场景特有的问题。我们的研究揭示了现有隐私相关开发任务支持手段的重大缺陷，并据此提出了让隐私资源更易获取、更易理解、更可执行的建议。","tl":"实验发现 AI 助手答得清楚却抓不到场景特有的隐私问题。","au":["Stefan Albert Horstmann","Sandy Hong","Maziar Niazian","Cristiana Santos","Alena Naiakshina"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["human-study","security"],"kw":["privacy compliance","developer study","think-aloud","GDPR","AI assistant"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/108/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.08059"},{"id":"p00595","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Bytecode-centric Detection of Known-to-be-vulnerable Dependencies in Java Projects","tz":"以字节码为中心检测 Java 项目中的已知脆弱依赖","a":"On average, 71% of the code in typical Java projects comes from open-source software (OSS) dependencies, making OSS dependencies the dominant component of modern software code bases. This high degree of OSS reliance comes with a considerable security risk of adding known security vulnerabilities to a code base. To remedy this risk, researchers and companies have developed various dependency scanners , which try to identify inclusions of known-to-be-vulnerable OSS dependencies. However, there are still challenges that modern dependency scanners do not overcome, especially when it comes to dependency modifications, such as re-compilations, re-bundlings or re-packagings, which are common in the Java ecosystem. To overcome these challenges, we present Jaralyzer, a bytecode-centric dependency scanner for Java. Jaralyzer does not rely on the metadata or the source code of the included OSS dependencies being available but directly analyzes a dependency’s bytecode. Our evaluation across 56 popular OSS components demonstrates that Jaralyzer outperforms other popular dependency scanners in detecting vulnerabilities within modified dependencies. It is the only scanner capable of identifying vulnerabilities across all the above mentioned types of modifications. But even when applied to unmodified dependencies, Jaralyzer outperforms the current state-of-the-art code-centric scanner Eclipse Steady by detecting 28 more true vulnerabilities and yielding 29 fewer false warnings.","az":"在典型的 Java 项目中，平均 71% 的代码来自开源软件（OSS）依赖，使得 OSS 依赖成为现代软件代码库的主要组成部分。这种高度依赖伴随着相当大的安全风险，即把已知安全漏洞引入代码库。为缓解该风险，研究者与企业开发了各种依赖扫描器，试图识别已知脆弱 OSS 依赖的引入。然而，现代依赖扫描器仍面临挑战，尤其是在 Java 生态中常见的依赖修改场景，如重新编译、重新打包（re-bundling）与重新封装（re-packaging）。为克服这些挑战，我们提出 Jaralyzer，一个面向 Java、以字节码为中心的依赖扫描器。Jaralyzer 不依赖所包含 OSS 依赖的元数据或源码是否可得，而是直接分析依赖的字节码。我们在 56 个流行 OSS 组件上的评估表明，在检测被修改依赖中的漏洞方面，Jaralyzer 优于其他流行依赖扫描器，是唯一能够识别上述所有修改类型下漏洞的扫描器。即便应用于未修改的依赖，Jaralyzer 也优于当前最先进的以代码为中心的扫描器 Eclipse Steady：多检出 28 个真实漏洞，并少报 29 个误报。","tl":"直接分析字节码，识别重打包依赖中被现有扫描器漏掉的漏洞。","au":["Stefan Schott","Serena Elisa Ponta","Wolfram Fischer","Jonas Klauke","Eric Bodden"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["dependency scanner","Java bytecode","vulnerable dependency","software composition analysis","re-packaging"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/109/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.19393"},{"id":"p00596","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"One Size Does Fit All: Kernel-Assisted Fine-Grained Debloating and Layout Randomization for Shared Libraries","tz":"一刀确实可以切所有：面向共享库的内核辅助细粒度裁剪与布局随机化","a":"Prevalent software engineering practices, such as code reuse and the “one-size-fits-all” methodology, have significantly contributed to code bloat. Code debloating, which targets the reduction of extraneous code, emerges as a promising solution to combat this issue. However, current methods that depend on redundant code deletion are at odds with the foundational design philosophy of reusable code components, regardless of whether they are applied offline or at runtime. In this paper, we introduce a kernel-assisted debloating framework, K-Polarizer, that aligns with the “one-size-fits-all” design philosophy of shared libraries. Starting from scratch, K-Polarizer progressively appends dependencies on demand to the underlying page cache associated with offline-reconstructed shared libraries, enabling it to practice the hybrid debloating strategy of “cutting unwanted pages while loading needed functions.” This allows for code sharing among processes while minimizing the global code base, keeping the visible code base for each process to an approximate minimum. Additionally, K-Polarizer integrates layout randomization at load-time to enhance security further. We have thoroughly evaluated K-Polarizer using real-world shared libraries, including musl-libc, glibc, and libFLAC. The results indicate that K-Polarizer operates transparently, preserving the original functionality of the libraries. Furthermore, K-Polarizer provides security guarantees (76.1% gadget reduction on musl-libc) comparable to the leading debloating technique with acceptable overhead, while gracefully handling the scenario of dynamic library loading. Meanwhile, it offers resilience against memory disclosures.","az":"代码复用与「一刀切」方法论等主流软件工程实践，极大地助长了代码膨胀。代码裁剪（debloating）以削减冗余代码为目标，成为应对该问题的有前景方案。然而，现有依赖删除冗余代码的方法，无论离线还是运行时应用，都与可复用代码组件的基础设计哲学相冲突。本文提出一个内核辅助的裁剪框架 K-Polarizer，它与共享库「一刀切」的设计哲学相契合。K-Polarizer 从零开始，按需逐步向离线重构的共享库所对应的底层页缓存追加依赖，从而实践「一边裁掉不需要的页、一边加载所需函数」的混合裁剪策略。这使得进程之间仍可共享代码，同时最小化全局代码基，把每个进程可见的代码基保持在近似最小。此外，K-Polarizer 在加载时集成了布局随机化以进一步增强安全性。我们使用 musl-libc、glibc 与 libFLAC 等真实共享库对 K-Polarizer 进行了充分评估。结果表明 K-Polarizer 运行透明，保持了库的原有功能；它在可接受开销下提供了与领先裁剪技术相当的安全保障（在 musl-libc 上减少 76.1% 的 gadget），并能优雅地处理动态库加载场景，同时对内存泄露（memory disclosure）具有抵抗力。","tl":"在页缓存粒度按需裁剪共享库，兼顾代码共享与攻击面收缩。","au":["Ziyi Lin","Haoyu Ma","Kexin Liu","Bowen Li","Jinku Li","Jianfeng Ma"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code debloating","shared libraries","layout randomization","kernel-assisted","gadget reduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/110/x"},{"id":"p00597","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RefAgent: A Multi-agent LLM-based Framework for Automatic Software Refactoring","tz":"RefAgent：面向自动软件重构的多智能体 LLM 框架","a":"Recent advancements in Large Language Models (LLMs) have substantially influenced various software engineering tasks, including code generation, program repair, and software maintenance. Indeed, in the case of software refactoring, traditional LLMs have shown the ability to reduce development time and enhance code quality. However, these LLMs often rely on static, detailed instructions for specific tasks. In contrast, LLM-based agents can dynamically adapt to evolving contexts and autonomously make decisions by interacting with software tools and executing workflows. In this paper, we explore the potential of LLM-based agents in supporting refactoring activities. Specifically, we introduce RefAgent, a multi-agent LLM-based framework for end-to-end software refactoring. RefAgent consists of specialized agents responsible for planning, executing, testing, and iteratively refining refactorings using self-reflection and tool-calling capabilities. We evaluate RefAgent on eight open-source Java projects, comparing its effectiveness against a single-agent approach, a search-based refactoring tool, and historical developer refactorings. Our assessment focuses on: (1) the impact of generated refactorings on software quality, (2) the ability to identify refactoring opportunities, and (3) the contribution of each LLM agent through an ablation study. Our results show that RefAgent achieves a median unit test pass rate of 90%, reduces code smells by a median of 52.5%, and improves key quality attributes (e.g., reusability) by a median of 8.6%. Additionally, it closely aligns with developer refactorings and the search-based tool in identifying refactoring opportunities, attaining a median F1-score of 79.15% and 72.7%, respectively. Compared to single-agent approaches, RefAgent improves the median unit test pass rate by 64.7% and the median compilation success rate by 40.1%. These findings highlight the promise of multi-agent architectures in advancing automated software refactoring.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展已显著影响代码生成、程序修复、软件维护等多项软件工程任务。在软件重构方面，传统 LLM 确实展现出缩短开发时间、提升代码质量的能力。然而，这些 LLM 往往依赖针对特定任务的静态、详尽指令。相比之下，基于 LLM 的智能体可以动态适应不断变化的上下文，通过与软件工具交互并执行工作流来自主决策。本文探索基于 LLM 的智能体在支持重构活动方面的潜力。具体而言，我们提出 RefAgent，一个用于端到端软件重构的多智能体 LLM 框架。RefAgent 由若干专职智能体组成，分别负责规划、执行、测试，并借助自我反思与工具调用能力迭代地精化重构。我们在八个开源 Java 项目上评估 RefAgent，将其有效性与单智能体方法、一种基于搜索的重构工具以及历史上开发者的重构进行对比。我们的评估关注：（1）生成的重构对软件质量的影响；（2）识别重构机会的能力；（3）通过消融实验考察各 LLM 智能体的贡献。结果显示，RefAgent 的单元测试通过率中位数达 90%，代码坏味中位数减少 52.5%，关键质量属性（如可复用性）中位数提升 8.6%。此外，在识别重构机会方面，它与开发者的重构以及基于搜索的工具高度吻合，F1 分数中位数分别为 79.15% 与 72.7%。与单智能体方法相比，RefAgent 将单元测试通过率中位数提升 64.7%，编译成功率中位数提升 40.1%。这些发现凸显了多智能体架构在推进自动软件重构方面的前景。","tl":"规划-执行-测试-反思的多智能体框架把重构测试通过率拉到 90%。","au":["Khouloud Oueslati","Maxime Lamothe","Foutse Khomh"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated refactoring","multi-agent LLM","code smells","self-reflection","tool calling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/111/x"},{"id":"p00598","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"WhisperCatcher: Demystifying Unauthorized and Encrypted Private Data Transmission in Android Applications","tz":"WhisperCatcher：揭示 Android 应用中未经授权的加密隐私数据传输","a":"The privacy issues associated with Android apps are increasingly raising our concerns. Unfortunately, a large portion of privacy breaches in Android apps cannot be accurately detected by existing approaches, especially private data that is collected without consent and transmitted in encrypted form. Even if existing studies are able to break the encryption at protocol level to recover the structure and content of traffic packets, they are still unable to understand the code layer encrypted data. To solve this problem, we propose WhisperCatcher, an automated tool for analyzing unauthorized and encrypted private data transmitted by apps. For each app, WhisperCatcher first captures the raw traffic generated during the app’s startup phase, before the user consents to the privacy policy, and then extracts the semantic information. Furthermore, it utilizes the traffic semantics to guide static code analysis and extracts transmission-related key functions. Finally, it performs dynamic instrumentation analysis and recovers the encrypted data, thereby identifying unauthorized private data transmissions. Extensive evaluations show that WhisperCatcher significantly outperforms existing tools, and it achieves the recall of 91.38% and F1-Score of 95.49%, respectively. In addition, we conduct a large-scale measurement analysis on 14,879 apps and WhisperCatcher identifies 13,966 traffic flows from 4,966 apps that transmit private data prior to obtaining user consent, among which 3,838 (27.48%) flows contain app-encrypted data. Our findings highlight the potential privacy leakage risks in Android apps, which should be brought to the attention of the community.","az":"Android 应用相关的隐私问题日益引发关注。遗憾的是，现有方法无法准确检测其中很大一部分隐私泄露，尤其是那些未经用户同意即被收集、并以加密形式传输的隐私数据。即便已有研究能在协议层破解加密、还原流量包的结构与内容，它们仍无法理解代码层加密的数据。为解决该问题，我们提出 WhisperCatcher，一个自动分析应用所传输的未经授权加密隐私数据的工具。对每个应用，WhisperCatcher 首先在应用启动阶段、用户同意隐私政策之前捕获原始流量，并提取语义信息；随后利用流量语义引导静态代码分析，抽取与传输相关的关键函数；最后执行动态插桩分析还原加密数据，从而识别未经授权的隐私数据传输。大量评估表明，WhisperCatcher 显著优于现有工具，召回率达 91.38%，F1 分数达 95.49%。此外，我们对 14,879 个应用开展了大规模测量分析，WhisperCatcher 从 4,966 个应用中识别出 13,966 条在获得用户同意前即传输隐私数据的流量流，其中 3,838 条（27.48%）包含应用自行加密的数据。我们的发现凸显了 Android 应用中潜在的隐私泄露风险，值得社区重视。","tl":"流量语义引导静态分析加动态插桩，还原应用自加密的隐私外传。","au":["Zhaoyu Qiu","Ming Fan","Bocan Ma","Yutian Tang","Lei Xue","Haijun Wang","Ting Liu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Android privacy leakage","encrypted traffic","dynamic instrumentation","static analysis","user consent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/112/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00599","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"\"Maybe We Need Some More Examples:\" Individual and Team Drivers of Developer GenAI Tool Use","tz":"「也许我们还需要更多示例」：开发者使用生成式 AI 工具的个体与团队驱动因素","a":"Despite the widespread availability of generative AI tools in software engineering, developer adoption remains uneven. This unevenness is problematic because it hampers productivity efforts, frustrates management’s expectations, and creates uncertainty around the future roles of developers. Through paired interviews with 54 developers across 27 teams – one frequent and one infrequent user per team – we demonstrate that differences in usage result primarily from how developers perceive the tool (as a collaborator vs. feature), their engagement approach (experimental vs. conservative), and how they respond when encountering challenges (with adaptive persistence vs. quick abandonment). Our findings imply that widespread organizational expectations for rapid productivity gains without sufficient investment in learning support creates a “Productivity Pressure Paradox” undermining the very productivity benefits that motivate adoption.","az":"尽管生成式 AI 工具在软件工程中已广泛可得，开发者的采纳程度仍参差不齐。这种不均衡是个问题，因为它阻碍了提升生产力的努力、让管理层的期望落空，并给开发者未来的角色带来不确定性。我们对 27 个团队中的 54 名开发者进行了配对访谈（每个团队一名高频使用者与一名低频使用者），结果表明使用差异主要源于开发者如何看待该工具（视之为协作者还是功能）、他们的参与方式（实验型还是保守型），以及他们在遇到困难时的反应（适应性坚持还是迅速放弃）。我们的发现意味着，组织普遍期待快速获得生产力收益却未在学习支持上投入足够资源，由此产生了一种「生产力压力悖论」，反而侵蚀了推动采纳的那些生产力收益本身。","tl":"配对访谈揭示采纳差异源于认知、参与方式与遇挫反应。","au":["Courtney Miller","Rudrajit Choudhuri","Mara Ulloa","Sankeerti Haniyur","Robert DeLine","Margaret-Anne Storey","Emerson Murphy-Hill","Christian Bird","Jenna L. Butler"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["human-study","llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["GenAI adoption","paired interviews","developer teams","productivity pressure","tool perception"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/113/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.21280","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00600","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Good are Input Grammar Miners? An Empirical Study","tz":"输入文法挖掘器到底有多好？一项实证研究","a":"To generate valid test inputs for a system, one needs a specification of its input language—typically a context-free grammar that describes input syntax. But where can one get such a grammar from? In the past years, the field of input grammar mining has emerged, with creative approaches to extract input grammars from inputs, code, or both. But how good are these approaches? In particular; How accurate are the grammars they mine? In this study, we systematically evaluate grammar miners for these questions. Notably, we find that the previous evaluations conducted by the respective authors—producing a set of inputs from a golden grammar and having them checked by the mined grammar, or vice versa—are insufficient, as they have a strong bias towards short, possibly unrealistic inputs. We therefore also measure the diversity of the mined grammars using k-path coverage with varying depths~k to find how many combinations of grammar elements are actually represented. Ideally, a mined grammar should have perfect precision and recall regardless of the depth k. However, our results show that for all approaches presented so far, precision and recall can drop significantly compared to reported results when increasing~k and thus checking for ``deeper'' diversity, especially for complex input languages such as Lisp, JSON, or Tiny-C. For instance, the Tiny-C grammar mined by Arvada achieves a precision of 75% when considering k-paths with k = 1 (the originally reported precision was 73%), but this drops to 46% for k = 5. White-box approaches based on program analysis, such as Mimid and Stalagmite, are more stable with varying depth k, but can be challenged by complex parsers such as mjs. Raising the bars for evaluation, our study shows that there is still room for improvement in grammar mining.","az":"要为一个系统生成有效的测试输入，需要其输入语言的规约——通常是一部描述输入语法的上下文无关文法。可这样的文法从哪里来？近年来，输入文法挖掘领域应运而生，出现了从输入、代码或二者中提取输入文法的各种创造性方法。但这些方法究竟有多好？特别是，它们挖掘出的文法有多准确？本研究系统评估了文法挖掘器在这些问题上的表现。值得注意的是，我们发现各方法作者此前采用的评估方式——用黄金文法生成一批输入再用挖掘出的文法检查，或反之——是不充分的，因为它们强烈偏向短小、可能不现实的输入。因此我们还使用不同深度 k 的 k-path 覆盖来度量挖掘文法的多样性，考察实际被覆盖的文法元素组合有多少。理想情况下，挖掘出的文法无论深度 k 为何都应具备完美的精确率与召回率。然而我们的结果显示，对目前提出的所有方法而言，当 k 增大、即检查更「深」的多样性时，精确率与召回率相比已报告结果都会显著下降，对 Lisp、JSON、Tiny-C 等复杂输入语言尤为如此。例如，Arvada 挖掘出的 Tiny-C 文法在 k = 1 的 k-path 下精确率为 75%（原报告精确率为 73%），但在 k = 5 时降至 46%。基于程序分析的白盒方法（如 Mimid 与 Stalagmite）在 k 变化时更稳定，但会被 mjs 这类复杂解析器难住。本研究提高了评估标准，表明文法挖掘仍有很大改进空间。","tl":"用 k-path 覆盖揭示现有文法挖掘评估高估精度、深度一增就崩。","au":["Leon Bettscheider","Andreas Zeller"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["grammar mining","k-path coverage","input grammar","empirical evaluation","precision and recall"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/114/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/114/How-Good-are-Input-Grammar-Miners-An-Empirical-Study"},{"id":"p00601","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Small Changes, Big Trouble: Demystifying and Parsing License Variants for Incompatibility Detection in the PyPI Ecosystem","tz":"小改动，大麻烦：解析 PyPI 生态中的许可证变体以检测许可证不兼容","a":"Open-source licenses establish the legal foundation for software reuse, yet license variants, including both modified standard licenses and custom-created alternatives, introduce significant compliance complexities. Despite their prevalence and potential impact, these variants are poorly understood in modern software systems, and existing tools do not account for their existence, leading to significant challenges in both effectiveness and efficiency of license analysis. To fill this knowledge gap, we conduct a comprehensive empirical study of license variants in the PyPI ecosystem. Our findings show that textual variations in licenses are common, yet only 2% involve substantive modifications. However, these license variants lead to significant compliance issues, with 10.7% of their downstream dependencies found to be license-incompatible. Inspired by our findings, we introduce LV-Parser, a novel approach for efficient license variant analysis leveraging diff-based techniques and large language models, along with LV-Compat, an automated pipeline for detecting license incompatibilities in software dependency networks. Our evaluation demonstrates that LV-Parser achieves an accuracy of 0.936 while reducing computational costs by 30%, and LV-Compat identifies 5.2 times more incompatible packages than existing methods with a precision of 0.98. This work not only provides the first empirical study into license variants in software packaging ecosystem but also equips developers and organizations with practical tools for navigating the complex landscape of open-source licensing.","az":"开源许可证为软件复用奠定了法律基础，然而许可证变体——既包括被修改过的标准许可证，也包括自定义创建的替代许可证——带来了显著的合规复杂性。尽管这类变体十分普遍且潜在影响巨大，但在现代软件系统中人们对它们的理解仍然很少，现有工具也没有考虑它们的存在，导致许可证分析在有效性和效率两方面都面临重大挑战。为填补这一认知空白，我们对 PyPI 生态中的许可证变体开展了全面的实证研究。我们的发现表明，许可证文本层面的差异非常常见，但其中只有 2% 涉及实质性修改。然而，这些许可证变体确实引发了严重的合规问题：其下游依赖中有 10.7% 被发现存在许可证不兼容。受这些发现启发，我们提出了 LV-Parser——一种结合 diff 技术与大语言模型的高效许可证变体分析方法，以及 LV-Compat——一条用于在软件依赖网络中检测许可证不兼容的自动化流水线。评估表明，LV-Parser 在将计算成本降低 30% 的同时达到了 0.936 的准确率，而 LV-Compat 在 0.98 精确率下识别出的不兼容包数量是现有方法的 5.2 倍。这项工作不仅首次对软件打包生态中的许可证变体进行了实证研究，也为开发者和组织提供了应对复杂开源许可格局的实用工具。","tl":"首次量化 PyPI 许可证变体，并用 diff+LLM 高效检测不兼容。","au":["Weiwei Xu","Hengzhi Ye","Kai Gao","Minghui Zhou"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["license variants","license incompatibility","PyPI ecosystem","dependency network","compliance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/115/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.14594"},{"id":"p00602","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM-based API Argument Completion with Knowledge-Augmented Prompts","tz":"基于知识增强提示的 LLM API 参数补全","a":"Application Programming Interfaces (API) are fundamental to modern software development, yet accurately completing API method arguments remains a challenging task. Existing methods, such as information retrieval and hybrid program analysis with language models, often struggle with static code patterns and limited domain-specific knowledge. To this end, in this paper, we introduce APICopilot, a novel approach that enhances LLM-based API argument completion using dynamically generated, context-rich prompts. First, it creates an input knowledge graph (KG) from the preceding code for the to-be-complete API invocation, and a targeted knowledge graph from a collection of similar code files, both representing the anticipated API call. Second, it quantifies structural and semantic alignment between the two KGs and retrieves relevant subgraphs from the targeted graph. These subgraphs provide crucial structural context for in-context learning, enabling significantly more accurate and context-specific argument completions. Finally, we integrate the subgraphs into prompts and request LLMs to recommend API arguments. Our evaluation results on 54,000 Java files suggest that the proposed approach outperforms the state-of-the-art approach, improving precision, recall, and mean reciprocal rank by 38%, 36% and 23%, respectively.","az":"应用程序编程接口（API）是现代软件开发的基础，但准确补全 API 方法的参数仍然是一项富有挑战的任务。现有方法（如信息检索，以及将程序分析与语言模型结合的混合方法）常常受限于静态的代码模式和有限的领域特定知识。为此，本文提出 APICopilot，一种通过动态生成的、上下文丰富的提示来增强基于 LLM 的 API 参数补全的新方法。首先，它从待补全 API 调用之前的代码构建一个输入知识图谱（KG），并从一组相似代码文件中构建一个目标知识图谱，二者都刻画了预期的 API 调用。其次，它量化两个知识图谱之间的结构与语义对齐程度，并从目标图谱中检索相关子图。这些子图为上下文学习提供了关键的结构性上下文，从而实现显著更准确、更贴合上下文的参数补全。最后，我们将子图整合进提示中，请求 LLM 推荐 API 参数。在 54,000 个 Java 文件上的评估结果表明，所提方法优于最先进的方法，在精确率、召回率和平均倒数排名上分别提升了 38%、36% 和 23%。","tl":"用输入/目标知识图谱对齐检索子图来提示 LLM 补全 API 参数。","au":["Waseem Akram","Yanjie Jiang","Haris Ali Khan","Furqan Jalil","Hui Liu"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["API argument completion","knowledge graph","in-context learning","prompt construction","code completion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/116/x"},{"id":"p00603","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PredicateFix: Repairing Static Analysis Alerts with Bridging Predicates","tz":"PredicateFix：用桥接谓词修复静态分析告警","a":"Fixing static analysis alerts in source code with Large Language Models (LLMs) is becoming increasingly popular. However, LLMs often hallucinate and perform poorly for complex and less common alerts. Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) aims to solve this problem by providing the model with a relevant example, but existing approaches face the challenge of unsatisfactory quality of such examples. To address this challenge, we utilize the predicates in the analysis rule, which serve as a bridge between the alert and relevant code snippets within a clean code corpus, called key examples. Based on this insight, we propose an algorithm to retrieve key examples for an alert automatically, and build PredicateFix as a RAG pipeline to fix alerts from two static code analyzers: CodeQL and GoInsight. Evaluation with multiple LLMs shows that PredicateFix increases the number of correct repairs by 27.1% ~ 69.3%, significantly outperforming other baseline RAG approaches.","az":"使用大语言模型（LLM）修复源代码中的静态分析告警正变得越来越流行。然而，LLM 经常产生幻觉，并且在复杂且不常见的告警上表现不佳。检索增强生成（RAG）试图通过为模型提供相关示例来解决这一问题，但现有方法面临示例质量不理想的挑战。为应对该挑战，我们利用分析规则中的谓词，它们在告警与干净代码语料库中的相关代码片段（我们称之为关键示例）之间充当桥梁。基于这一洞见，我们提出了一种自动为告警检索关键示例的算法，并构建了 PredicateFix 这一 RAG 流水线，用于修复来自 CodeQL 和 GoInsight 两个静态代码分析器的告警。在多个 LLM 上的评估显示，PredicateFix 将正确修复的数量提高了 27.1%～69.3%，显著优于其他基线 RAG 方法。","tl":"用分析规则谓词检索关键示例，显著提升告警修复正确率。","au":["Yuan-An Xiao","Weixuan Wang","Dong Liu","Junwei Zhou","Shengyu Cheng","Yingfei Xiong"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static analysis alerts","CodeQL","retrieval-augmented generation","alert repair","analysis predicates"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/117/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.12205"},{"id":"p00604","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MINES: Explainable Anomaly Detection through Web API Invariant Inference","tz":"MINES：通过 Web API 不变量推断实现可解释的异常检测","a":"Detecting the anomalies of web applications, important infrastructures for running modern companies and governments, is crucial for providing reliable web services. Many modern web applications operate on web APIs (e.g., RESTful, SOAP, and WebSockets), their exposure invites intended attacks or unintended illegal visits, causing abnormal system behaviors. However, such anomalies can share very similar logs (sometimes even identical logs) with normal logs, missing crucial information (which could be in database) for log discrimination. Further, log instances can be also noisy, which can further mislead the state-of-the-art log learning solutions to learn spurious correlation, resulting superficial models and rules for anomaly detection. In this work, we propose MINES which infers explainable API invariants for anomaly detection from the schema level instead of detailed raw log instances, which can (1) significantly discriminate noise in logs to identify precise normalities and (2) detect abnormal behaviors beyond the instrumented logs (e.g., regarding the database state or session state). Our learned invariants can capture API preconditions such as (1) what is the legitimate database state to initiate the call events? and (2) what are the constraints to satisfy between different API calls? Then we translate the invariants into executable Python code to verify its consistency with the runtime logs. Technically, MINES (1) converts API signatures into table schema to enhance the original database shema; and (2) infers the potential database constraints (such as reference constraint and check constraints) on the enhanced database schema to capture the potential relationships between APIs and database tables. MINES uses LLM for extracting potential relationship based on two given table structures; and use normal log instances to reject and accept LLM-generated invariants. Finally, MINES translates the inferred constraints into invariants to generate Python code for verifying the runtime logs. We extensively evaluate MINES on 76 types of web-tamper attacks on the benchmarks of Train-Ticket, NiceFish, Gitea, Mastodon, and NextCloud against baselines such as LogRobust, LogFormer, and WebNorm. The results show that MINES achieves high recall (more than 14% over LogRobust, LogFormer, and WebNorm) for the anomalies while introducing almost zero false positives, indicating a new state-of-the-art.","az":"Web 应用是现代企业和政府运转的重要基础设施，检测其异常对于提供可靠的 Web 服务至关重要。许多现代 Web 应用基于 Web API（如 RESTful、SOAP 和 WebSockets）运行，其暴露面招致有意攻击或无意的非法访问，导致系统行为异常。然而，这类异常的日志可能与正常日志非常相似（有时甚至完全相同），缺失了用于区分日志的关键信息（这些信息可能存在于数据库中）。此外，日志实例还可能含噪，从而进一步误导最先进的日志学习方案去学习虚假相关性，产生表面化的异常检测模型与规则。在本工作中，我们提出 MINES，它不是从细粒度的原始日志实例出发，而是从模式（schema）层面推断可解释的 API 不变量用于异常检测，从而能够：(1) 显著区分日志中的噪声以识别精确的正常行为；(2) 检测超出已插桩日志范围的异常行为（例如涉及数据库状态或会话状态的异常）。我们学到的不变量可以刻画 API 的前置条件，例如：(1) 发起调用事件时合法的数据库状态是什么？(2) 不同 API 调用之间需要满足哪些约束？随后我们将这些不变量翻译为可执行的 Python 代码，以验证其与运行时日志的一致性。在技术上，MINES 首先将 API 签名转换为表模式以增强原始数据库模式；其次在增强后的数据库模式上推断潜在的数据库约束（如引用约束与检查约束），以刻画 API 与数据库表之间的潜在关系。MINES 使用 LLM 基于两张给定的表结构抽取潜在关系，并利用正常日志实例来接受或拒绝 LLM 生成的不变量。最后，MINES 将推断出的约束转化为不变量，生成用于验证运行时日志的 Python 代码。我们在 Train-Ticket、NiceFish、Gitea、Mastodon 和 NextCloud 基准上针对 76 类 Web 篡改攻击，与 LogRobust、LogFormer 和 WebNorm 等基线进行了广泛评估。结果表明，MINES 对异常取得了高召回率（比 LogRobust、LogFormer 和 WebNorm 高出 14% 以上），同时几乎没有误报，达到了新的最优水平。","tl":"从数据库与 API 模式推断可执行不变量，近零误报检测 Web 异常。","au":["Wenjie Zhang","Yun Lin","Kwok Chun Fung Amos","Xiwen Teoh","Xiaofei Xie","Frank Liauw","Hongyu Zhang","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["security","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["anomaly detection","web API invariants","log analysis","database constraints","runtime verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/118/x"},{"id":"p00605","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GPTrace: Effective Crash Deduplication Using LLM Embeddings","tz":"GPTrace：利用 LLM 嵌入实现高效崩溃去重","a":"Fuzzing is a highly effective method for uncovering software vulnerabilities, but analyzing the resulting data typically requires substantial manual effort. This is amplified by the fact that fuzzing campaigns often find a large number of crashing inputs, many of which share the same underlying bug. Crash deduplication is the task of finding such duplicate crashing inputs and thereby reducing the data that needs to be examined. Many existing deduplication approaches rely on comparing stack traces or other information that is collected when a program crashes. Although various metrics for measuring the similarity of such pieces of information have been proposed, many do not yield satisfactory deduplication results. In this work, we present GPTrace, a deduplication workflow that leverages a large language model to evaluate the similarity of various data sources associated with crashes by computing embedding vectors and supplying those as input to a clustering algorithm. We evaluate our approach on over 300 000 crashing inputs belonging to 50 ground truth labels from 14 different targets. The deduplication results produced by GPTrace show a noticeable improvement over hand-crafted stack trace comparison methods and even more complex state-of-the-art approaches that are less flexible.","az":"模糊测试是发现软件漏洞的高效手段，但分析其产生的数据通常需要大量人工投入。模糊测试活动往往会发现大量导致崩溃的输入，其中许多共享同一个底层缺陷，这进一步加剧了分析负担。崩溃去重的任务就是找出这些重复的崩溃输入，从而减少需要人工检查的数据量。许多现有去重方法依赖于比较程序崩溃时收集的栈回溯或其他信息。尽管已经提出了各种度量此类信息相似度的指标，但许多指标的去重效果并不令人满意。在本工作中，我们提出 GPTrace，一种去重工作流：它利用大语言模型计算与崩溃相关的多种数据源的嵌入向量，以评估其相似度，并将这些向量输入聚类算法。我们在来自 14 个不同目标、隶属于 50 个真实标签的超过 300,000 个崩溃输入上评估了该方法。GPTrace 产生的去重结果相比人工设计的栈回溯比较方法有明显提升，甚至优于更复杂但灵活性较差的最先进方法。","tl":"用 LLM 嵌入聚类崩溃数据，去重效果超越栈回溯相似度方法。","au":["Patrick Herter","Vincent Ahlrichs","Ridvan Açilan","Julian Horsch"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["crash deduplication","fuzzing triage","LLM embeddings","stack trace similarity","clustering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/119/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.01609"},{"id":"p00606","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automatic Dockerfile Generation with Large Language Models","tz":"用大语言模型自动生成 Dockerfile","a":"Project maintainers on platforms like GitHub usually provide a document (e.g., a Readme) describing how to build and use their software, whose instructions, often written in natural language, might sometimes be ambiguous or platform-specific. This task can be eased by containerization, which allows developers to define the build environments required for their software and to enable automatic builds. Docker is the leading platform in this field and relies on Dockerfiles for correct execution. Practitioners who want to use and build projects that do not include a Dockerfile need to develop it themselves. They often need to perform multiple builds by trial and error to discover the correct build steps and build dependencies (e.g., third-party library necessary for software builds). To address this challenge, we propose a novel approach and tool called Dockerfile Refinement and Fixing Tool (DRAFT), which can automatically generate a working Dockerfile by a Large Language Model (LLM). The core idea of DRAFT is that it emulates developers’ behavior iteratively. Specifically, DRAFT is used to iteratively generate prompts to instruct the LLM to generate patches for an initially generated Dockerfile until it executes successfully. Subsequently, it attempts to optimize the Dockerfile to reduce the size of the im- age it builds. We evaluated DRAFT on 35 projects and compared it with the Dockerfiles generated by Copilot (based on ChatGPT 4.0), Actions_remaker, Repo2docker, Boxing, and Starter in five different languages (C, Java, Go, Python, and Ruby). The evaluation results show that DRAFT can successfully generate Dockerfiles for 31 projects, resulting in a success rate of 80%, which is much higher than all compared tools. The time consumed by DRAFT on generating Dockerfiles is 19.57 minutes at maximum with the median at 33.78s. Using DRAFT can reduce image size by 67.14% and build time by 3.62%. DRAFT relieves practitioners from the burden of manually creating build specifications.","az":"GitHub 等平台上的项目维护者通常会提供一份文档（如 Readme）来说明如何构建和使用其软件，但这些用自然语言写成的说明有时含糊不清或依赖特定平台。容器化可以缓解这一问题：它允许开发者定义软件所需的构建环境并支持自动构建。Docker 是该领域的主流平台，其正确执行依赖于 Dockerfile。想要使用和构建不含 Dockerfile 的项目的实践者只能自行编写，往往需要反复试错、多次构建，才能摸清正确的构建步骤和构建依赖（例如软件构建所需的第三方库）。为解决这一难题，我们提出了一种新方法与工具 DRAFT（Dockerfile Refinement and Fixing Tool），它能够借助大语言模型（LLM）自动生成可用的 Dockerfile。DRAFT 的核心思想是迭代地模拟开发者的行为：具体而言，它迭代生成提示，指示 LLM 为最初生成的 Dockerfile 生成补丁，直到该 Dockerfile 能够成功执行；随后，它还会尝试优化 Dockerfile 以减小所构建镜像的体积。我们在 35 个项目上评估了 DRAFT，并与 Copilot（基于 ChatGPT 4.0）、Actions_remaker、Repo2docker、Boxing 和 Starter 在五种语言（C、Java、Go、Python 和 Ruby）上生成的 Dockerfile 进行比较。评估结果显示，DRAFT 成功为 31 个项目生成了 Dockerfile，成功率达 80%，远高于所有对比工具。DRAFT 生成 Dockerfile 的耗时最长为 19.57 分钟，中位数为 33.78 秒。使用 DRAFT 可将镜像体积减少 67.14%，构建时间减少 3.62%。DRAFT 将实践者从手工编写构建规约的负担中解放出来。","tl":"迭代提示 LLM 打补丁直至构建成功，并进一步压缩镜像体积。","au":["Jun Lyu","He Zhang","Yusong Yuan","Lanxin Yang","Yue Li","Manuel Rigger"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Dockerfile generation","Infrastructure-as-Code","build environment","iterative repair","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/120/x"},{"id":"p00607","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Retrieval-Augmented Test Generation: How Far Are We?","tz":"检索增强的测试生成：我们到了哪一步？","a":"Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) has advanced software engineering tasks but remains underexplored in unit test generation. To bridge this gap, we investigate the efficacy of RAG-based unit test generation for machine learning (ML/DL) APIs and analyze the impact of different knowledge sources on their effectiveness. We examine three domain-specific sources for RAG: (1) API documentation (official guidelines), (2) GitHub issues (developer-reported resolutions), and (3) StackOverflow Q&As (community-driven solutions). Our study focuses on five widely used Python-based ML/DL libraries, TensorFlow, PyTorch, Scikit-learn, Google JAX, and XGBoost, targeting the most-used APIs. We evaluate four state-of-the-art LLMs: LLMs—GPT-3.5-Turbo, GPT-4o, Mistral MoE 8x22B, and Llama 3.1 405B, across three strategies: basic instruction prompting, Basic RAG, and API-level RAG. Quantitatively, we assess syntactical and dynamic correctness and line coverage. While RAG does not enhance correctness, RAG improves line coverage by 6.5% on average. We found that GitHub issues result in the best improvement in line coverage by providing edge cases from various issues. We also found that these generated unit tests can help detect new bugs. Specifically, 28 bugs were detected, 24 unique bugs were reported to developers, ten were confirmed, four were rejected, and ten are awaiting developers’ confirmation. Our findings highlight RAG’s potential in unit test generation for improving test coverage with well-targeted knowledge sources. Future work should focus on retrieval techniques that identify documents with unique program states to optimize RAG-based unit test generation further.","az":"检索增强生成（RAG）已推动了多项软件工程任务的发展，但在单元测试生成方面仍未被充分探索。为填补这一空白，我们研究了基于 RAG 的单元测试生成在机器学习（ML/DL）API 上的效果，并分析了不同知识源对其有效性的影响。我们考察了三类面向领域的 RAG 知识源：(1) API 文档（官方指南）；(2) GitHub issues（开发者报告的解决方案）；(3) StackOverflow 问答（社区驱动的解决方案）。我们的研究聚焦五个广泛使用的基于 Python 的 ML/DL 库——TensorFlow、PyTorch、Scikit-learn、Google JAX 和 XGBoost，针对其最常用的 API。我们评估了四个最先进的 LLM：GPT-3.5-Turbo、GPT-4o、Mistral MoE 8x22B 和 Llama 3.1 405B，并比较了三种策略：基础指令提示、基础 RAG 和 API 级 RAG。在量化层面，我们评估语法正确性、动态正确性和行覆盖率。虽然 RAG 并未提升正确性，但它平均将行覆盖率提高了 6.5%。我们发现 GitHub issues 带来的行覆盖率提升最大，因为它们提供了来自各类问题的边界用例。我们还发现这些生成的单元测试有助于发现新缺陷：具体而言，共检测到 28 个缺陷，其中 24 个唯一缺陷已报告给开发者，10 个被确认，4 个被拒绝，10 个仍在等待开发者确认。我们的发现凸显了 RAG 在单元测试生成中借助精准知识源提升测试覆盖率的潜力。未来工作应聚焦于能识别出具有独特程序状态的文档的检索技术，以进一步优化基于 RAG 的单元测试生成。","tl":"实证表明 RAG 不提升测试正确性，但 GitHub issues 最能提高覆盖率。","au":["Jiho Shin","Nima Shiri Harzevili","Reem Aleithan","Hadi Hemmati","Song Wang"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["retrieval-augmented generation","unit test generation","ML/DL APIs","line coverage","bug detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/121/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.12682"},{"id":"p00608","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Causal Perspective on Measuring, Explaining and Mitigating Smells in LLM-Generated Code","tz":"因果视角下 LLM 生成代码中代码异味的测量、解释与缓解","a":"Recent advances in large language models ( LLMs ) have accelerated their adoption in software engineering contexts. However, concerns persist about the structural quality of the code they produce. In particular, LLMs often replicate poor coding practices, introducing code smells (i.e., patterns that hinder readability, maintainability, or design integrity). Although prior research has examined the detection or repair of smells, we still lack a clear understanding of how and when these issues emerge in generated code. This paper addresses this gap by systematically measuring , explaining and mitigating smell propensity in LLM -generated code. We build on the Propensity Smelly Score ( PSC ), a probabilistic metric that estimates the likelihood of generating particular smell types, and establish its robustness as a signal of structural quality. Using PSC as an instrument for causal analysis, we identify how generation strategy, model size, model architecture and prompt formulation shape the structural properties of generated code. Our findings show that prompt design and architectural choices play a decisive role in smell propensity and motivate practical mitigation strategies that reduce its occurrence. A user study further demonstrates that PSC helps developers interpret model behavior and assess code quality, providing evidence that smell propensity signals can support human judgement. Taken together, our work lays the groundwork for integrating quality-aware assessments into the evaluation and deployment of LLMs for code.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展加速了它们在软件工程场景中的采用。然而，人们仍然担忧其生成代码的结构质量。特别是，LLM 常常复刻糟糕的编码实践，引入代码异味（即妨碍可读性、可维护性或设计完整性的模式）。尽管已有研究考察了异味的检测或修复，我们仍然缺乏对这些问题在生成代码中如何以及何时出现的清晰理解。本文通过系统地测量、解释与缓解 LLM 生成代码中的异味倾向来填补这一空白。我们以 Propensity Smelly Score（PSC）为基础——这是一种估计生成特定异味类型可能性的概率度量——并确立了它作为结构质量信号的稳健性。以 PSC 作为因果分析的工具，我们识别了生成策略、模型规模、模型架构和提示表述如何塑造生成代码的结构属性。我们的发现表明，提示设计与架构选择对异味倾向具有决定性作用，并据此提出了可降低其发生率的实用缓解策略。一项用户研究进一步表明，PSC 有助于开发者解读模型行为并评估代码质量，为异味倾向信号可以支撑人类判断提供了证据。总体而言，我们的工作为将质量感知评估纳入代码 LLM 的评价与部署奠定了基础。","tl":"用 PSC 度量做因果分析，揭示提示与架构决定代码异味倾向。","au":["Alejandro Velasco","Daniel Rodriguez-Cardenas","Dipin Khati","David Nader Palacio","Lutfar Rahman Alif","Denys Poshyvanyk"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","human-study"],"kw":["code smells","LLM-generated code","propensity smelly score","causal analysis","prompt design"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/122/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15817"},{"id":"p00609","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"JEDI: Java Evaluation of Declarative and Imperative Queries - Benchmarking the Java Stream API","tz":"JEDI：声明式与命令式查询的 Java 评测——Java Stream API 基准套件","a":"The Java Stream API aims at increasing developer productivity thanks to an easy-to-read declarative syntax to express computations. It also simplifies parallel computing, providing a high-level abstraction on top of common parallelization aspects such as data partitioning, synchronization, and merging operations of thread-local computations. Unfortunately, there is a lack of benchmarks specifically targeting stream-based applications. Such a lack of benchmarks makes it difficult for researchers and developers of the Java class library to optimize the Stream API. Moreover, in the absence of dedicated benchmarks, it is difficult for researchers to analyze the performance of streams to suggest developers how to write efficient code using the API. In this work we present JEDI, a new benchmark suite that targets the Java Stream API. JEDI is automatically generated by converting SQL benchmarks into Java benchmarks. Our code generator supports the generation of different implementations (both stream-based and imperative) for the same query. The ultimate goal of our benchmark suite - and the main contribution of this work - is to analyze the performance of the different implementations to spot inefficient code structures and better alternatives, suggesting best practices to Java developers. Among the multiple implementations we generate, we focus on different parallelization strategies and explain the most efficient parallelization strategies based on characteristics of the processed data. Finally, the code generation producing imperative code helps in the definition of a baseline that can guide researchers and Java implementers to optimize the performance of the Stream API.","az":"Java Stream API 通过易读的声明式语法来表达计算，旨在提升开发者生产力。它还简化了并行计算，为数据划分、同步以及线程局部计算的合并等常见并行化环节提供了高层抽象。遗憾的是，目前缺乏专门针对基于 stream 的应用的基准测试。基准的缺失使得研究人员和 Java 类库开发者难以优化 Stream API；而且在没有专用基准的情况下，研究人员也难以分析 stream 的性能，从而难以向开发者建议如何用该 API 编写高效代码。在本工作中，我们提出 JEDI，一个面向 Java Stream API 的新基准套件。JEDI 通过将 SQL 基准转换为 Java 基准自动生成。我们的代码生成器支持为同一查询生成不同实现（既有基于 stream 的，也有命令式的）。我们基准套件的最终目标——也是本工作的主要贡献——是分析不同实现的性能，以发现低效的代码结构和更优的替代方案，从而向 Java 开发者提出最佳实践建议。在我们生成的多种实现中，我们重点关注不同的并行化策略，并基于被处理数据的特征解释哪些并行化策略最为高效。最后，生成命令式代码有助于定义一个基线，指导研究人员和 Java 实现者优化 Stream API 的性能。","tl":"由 SQL 基准自动生成 Java stream/命令式实现，对比并行化性能。","au":["Filippo Schiavio","Walter Binder"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["benchmark-dataset","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Java Stream API","benchmark suite","parallelization strategy","performance analysis","code generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/123/x"},{"id":"p00610","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"EchoFuzz: Empowering Smart Contract Fuzzing with Large Language Models","tz":"EchoFuzz：用大语言模型增强智能合约模糊测试","a":"Smart contracts, serving as the cornerstone of decentralized applications on blockchain platforms, autonomously manage trillion-dollar digital assets across diverse domains, making them prime targets for malicious exploits. Fuzzing has emerged as a promising technique for detecting vulnerabilities in smart contracts, yet existing methods face two main challenges. (1) The logical gap in state transitions and combinatorial redundancy hinders effective tradeoffs between bug detection efficiency and state space exploration cost, leading to critical execution paths to be overlooked. (2) Rule-based sequence mutation strategies suffer from path redundancy and inadequate guidance from contract logic, resulting in performance bottlenecks that stall the exploration of in-depth vulnerability-oriented paths. To tackle these challenges, we propose EchoFuzz, an LLM-guided fuzzing framework that introduces Vulnerable Function Call Sequences (VFCS) - minimal, behavior-preserving execution paths that expose bugs through essential state transitions. EchoFuzz consists of two key procedures. First, we develop a chain-guided LLM approach that mimics the workflow of expert auditors, combining static analysis with logical understanding to generate contract-specific VFCS candidates that eliminate combinatorial redundancy. Second, we adopt an iterative fuzzing strategy that employs LLMs to adaptively promote exploration, taking advantage of the real-time feedback to steer the fuzzer towards unexplored branches. Experimental results show that EchoFuzz significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art methods, achieving 29% improvement in branch coverage and discovering 62% more vulnerabilities than the top competitors. In addition, EchoFuzz has discovered 37 previously unknown vulnerabilities in real-world smart contract projects, underscoring its robust performance and practicality.","az":"智能合约作为区块链平台上去中心化应用的基石，自主管理着跨多个领域的万亿美元级数字资产，因而成为恶意攻击的主要目标。模糊测试已成为检测智能合约漏洞的有前景技术，但现有方法面临两大挑战：(1) 状态转移中的逻辑鸿沟与组合冗余，使得缺陷检测效率与状态空间探索成本之间难以有效权衡，导致关键执行路径被忽略；(2) 基于规则的序列变异策略存在路径冗余，且缺乏来自合约逻辑的充分引导，形成性能瓶颈，阻碍了面向深层漏洞路径的探索。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 EchoFuzz，一个由 LLM 引导的模糊测试框架，引入了易受攻击函数调用序列（Vulnerable Function Call Sequences，VFCS）——即通过关键状态转移暴露缺陷的、最小且保持行为的执行路径。EchoFuzz 包含两个关键过程：首先，我们设计了一种链式引导的 LLM 方法，模拟专家审计人员的工作流程，将静态分析与逻辑理解相结合，生成针对具体合约的 VFCS 候选，消除组合冗余；其次，我们采用一种迭代模糊测试策略，利用 LLM 自适应地促进探索，借助实时反馈将 fuzzer 导向尚未探索的分支。实验结果表明，EchoFuzz 显著优于最先进方法，在分支覆盖率上提升 29%，发现的漏洞数量比最强竞争者多 62%。此外，EchoFuzz 在真实世界智能合约项目中发现了 37 个此前未知的漏洞，凸显了其稳健的性能与实用性。","tl":"用 LLM 生成最小易漏函数调用序列引导合约模糊测试。","au":["Juanen Li","Peng Qian","Guanyan Li","Rui Wang","Peixin Wang","Zhiqing Tang","Fuchen Ma","Yuanliang Chen","Lun Zhang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract fuzzing","vulnerable function call sequence","LLM-guided fuzzing","branch coverage","blockchain security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/124/x"},{"id":"p00611","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Rethinking the Capability of Fine-Tuned Language Models for Automated Vulnerability Repair","tz":"重新审视微调语言模型在自动漏洞修复中的能力","a":"Learning-based automated vulnerability repair (AVR) techniques that utilize fine-tuned language models have shown promise in generating vulnerability patches. However, questions remain about their ability to repair unseen vulnerabilities. Our empirical study reveals that state-of-the-art models are often overfit to the training set and are evaluated using training, validation, and test sets that are not mutually exclusive. Furthermore, relying on match-based metrics that compare generated patches to reference fixes at the token level have some limitations, failing to account for the possibility of multiple valid ways to patch the vulnerability. In this paper, we examine the capabilities of state-of-the-art fine-tuned AVR models and the adequacy of match-based evaluation metrics in three ways. First, we apply semantic-preserving transformations to test sets to determine whether models truly learn robust vulnerability-repair patterns or simply rely on spurious features. Second, we resplit the training, validation and test sets to be mutually exclusive and evaluate the models on the revised test set to assess their generalization capabilities. Third, we introduce L-AVRBench, a test-based benchmark tailored for learning-based AVR, to overcome the limitations of match-based metrics and examine the AVR models’ true repair capabilities.","az":"利用微调语言模型的基于学习的自动漏洞修复（AVR）技术在生成漏洞补丁方面展现出前景。然而，它们修复未见过漏洞的能力仍存疑问。我们的实证研究发现，最先进的模型常常对训练集过拟合，并且所用的训练集、验证集与测试集之间并非互斥。此外，依赖在词元级别将生成补丁与参考修复进行比较的匹配式指标存在局限，未能考虑修复同一漏洞可能存在多种有效方式。本文从三个方面考察最先进的微调 AVR 模型的能力以及匹配式评测指标的适当性。第一，我们对测试集施加保持语义的变换，以判断模型是否真正学到了稳健的漏洞修复模式，还是仅仅依赖虚假特征。第二，我们重新划分训练、验证与测试集使其互斥，并在修订后的测试集上评估模型以考察其泛化能力。第三，我们提出 L-AVRBench，一个为基于学习的 AVR 量身定制的、基于测试的基准，以克服匹配式指标的局限并考察 AVR 模型真实的修复能力。","tl":"揭示 AVR 模型过拟合与数据泄漏，并提出基于测试的 L-AVRBench。","au":["Woorim Han","Yeongjun Kwak","miseon Yu","Kyeongmin Kim","Younghan Lee","Hyungon Moon","Yunheung Paek"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["automated vulnerability repair","fine-tuned language models","data leakage","semantic-preserving transformation","L-AVRBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/125/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.22633"},{"id":"p00612","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Sapling: Quantifying and Measuring the Maturity of the RISC-V Software Ecosystem","tz":"Sapling：量化与度量 RISC-V 软件生态的成熟度","a":"Open-source technology has enabled RISC-V to emerge as a cost-effective alternative for processor manufacturers by reducing intellectual property expenses. A key factor influencing its broader application is the maturity of the RISC-V software ecosystem. However, quantifying this maturity remains challenging due to the complexity of the ecosystem. In this study, we introduce Sapling, an automated oracle designed to systematically evaluate the maturity of the RISC-V software ecosystem. Our framework categorizes the ecosystem into five domains comprising thirty software components, each assessed across six dimensions. These evaluations are then aggregated within each domain and further analyzed through a cross-layer evaluation. Our findings indicate that while the RISC-V software ecosystem remains in its developmental phase, it is steadily advancing, demonstrating strong potential for sustained growth and broader industry application. Furthermore,~thirteen key insights and five strategic recommendations are presented to advance the maturity of the RISC-V software ecosystem. We hope that this study contributes to a deeper understanding of the maturity of the RISC-V software ecosystem and offers valuable guidance for its effective enhancement.","az":"开源技术通过降低知识产权开销，使 RISC-V 成为处理器厂商颇具性价比的替代方案。影响其更广泛应用的一个关键因素是 RISC-V 软件生态的成熟度。然而，由于生态的复杂性，量化这种成熟度仍然困难。在本研究中，我们提出 Sapling，一个用于系统评估 RISC-V 软件生态成熟度的自动化预言。我们的框架将该生态划分为五个领域、共三十个软件组件，每个组件从六个维度进行评估；随后在每个领域内汇总这些评估，并进一步通过跨层评估加以分析。我们的发现表明，虽然 RISC-V 软件生态仍处于发展阶段，但正在稳步前进，展现出持续增长和更广泛产业应用的强劲潜力。此外，我们给出了十三条关键洞见和五项战略建议，以推动 RISC-V 软件生态的成熟。我们希望本研究有助于加深对 RISC-V 软件生态成熟度的理解，并为其有效提升提供有价值的指导。","tl":"提出五领域三十组件六维度的自动化生态成熟度评估框架。","au":["Yuhang Liu","Chenchen Ji","Haoquan Li","Jiageng Yu","Mingyu Chen","Yanjun Wu","Yungang Bao"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["RISC-V","software ecosystem maturity","automated oracle","cross-layer evaluation","empirical assessment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/126/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/126/Sapling-Quantifying-and-Measuring-the-Maturity-of-the-RISC-V-Software-Ecosystem"},{"id":"p00613","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LoopSCC: Summarizing Complex Multi-branch Nested Loops via Periodic Oscillation Interval","tz":"LoopSCC：通过周期振荡区间对复杂多分支嵌套循环进行摘要","a":"Analyzing programs with loops is a challenging task, suffering from potential issues such as the indeterminate number of iterations and exponential growth of control flow complexity. Loop summarization based on static symbolic analysis receives increasing focus in the field of loop program analysis. However, current loop summarization methods are only suitable for single-branch loops or multi-branch loops with simple cycles and fail to handle complex multi-branch nested loops with intricate non-functional variables and irregular jumps between multiple branches. In this paper, we propose a novel loop summarization approach based on symbolic analysis to address the complex loops mentioned above and develop a tool named LoopSCC. For a non-nested loop, LoopSCC constructs an SPath Graph, where each node represents a path from entry to exit of the control flow graph of the loop and contracts it to an acyclic graph by collapsing each strongly connected component (SCC) into a single node. The summarization of a loop is the disjunction of the summaries of each path in the acyclic graph. For non-functional variables and irregular jumps, we iteratively model a valid value and refine the conditions until reaching the minimum. We introduce the oscillation interval, within which SPaths in the SCC can jump between one another. Outside this interval, no such jumps occur. This allows us to transform loop iteration transitions into a piecewise function, then summarize the interest variables according to the piecewise function. For nested loops, we construct summaries using the approaches above and apply them sequentially from the innermost loop to the outermost. Comparing state-of-the-art loop summarization tools, LoopSCC can handle more types of loops with 100% precision. We integrated LoopSCC with the symbolic execution tool, Angr, to enhance its efficiency, which enabled the detection of 18 previously unknown vulnerabilities across 11 IoT projects, 7 of which were assigned CVEs. The LoopSCC is publicly available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/LoopSCC-386F .","az":"分析含循环的程序是一项富有挑战的任务，面临迭代次数不确定和控制流复杂度指数级增长等潜在问题。基于静态符号分析的循环摘要在循环程序分析领域日益受到关注。然而，当前的循环摘要方法只适用于单分支循环或具有简单环的多分支循环，无法处理带有复杂非功能变量和多分支间不规则跳转的复杂多分支嵌套循环。本文提出一种基于符号分析的新型循环摘要方法以应对上述复杂循环，并开发了名为 LoopSCC 的工具。对于非嵌套循环，LoopSCC 构建一个 SPath 图，其中每个节点表示循环控制流图中从入口到出口的一条路径，并通过把每个强连通分量（SCC）坍缩为单个节点，将其收缩为无环图。循环的摘要即为无环图中各路径摘要的析取。对于非功能变量和不规则跳转，我们迭代地建模有效取值并细化条件，直至达到最小。我们引入了振荡区间的概念：在该区间内，SCC 中的 SPath 可以相互跳转；在该区间之外则不会发生此类跳转。这使我们能够将循环迭代转移转化为分段函数，进而依据分段函数对关注变量进行摘要。对于嵌套循环，我们使用上述方法构建摘要，并从最内层循环向最外层依次应用。与最先进的循环摘要工具相比，LoopSCC 能处理更多类型的循环且精度达到 100%。我们将 LoopSCC 与符号执行工具 Angr 集成以提升其效率，从而在 11 个 IoT 项目中检测出 18 个此前未知的漏洞，其中 7 个获得了 CVE 编号。LoopSCC 已公开发布于 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/LoopSCC-386F 。","tl":"用 SCC 收缩与振荡区间把循环转移建模为分段函数实现精确摘要。","au":["Kai Zhu","Haofeng Li","Kuihao Yan","Rongqing Wang","Jiaming Guo","Haoran Yang","Jie Lu","Lei Yu","Xiaoqi Jia","Chenkai Guo","Haichao Du","Qingjia Huang","Yamin Xie","Jing Tang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["loop summarization","symbolic analysis","strongly connected component","oscillation interval","symbolic execution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/127/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/127/LoopSCC-Summarizing-Complex-Multi-branch-Nested-Loops-via-Periodic-Oscillation-Inter"},{"id":"p00614","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Comparison of Conversational Models and Humans in Answering Technical Questions: the Firefox Case","tz":"对话式模型与人类回答技术问题的比较：以 Firefox 为例","a":"The use of Large Language Models (LLMs) to support tasks in software development has steadily increased over recent years. From assisting developers in coding activities to providing conversational agents that answer newcomers’ questions. In collaboration with the Mozilla Foundation, this study evaluates the effectiveness of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in assisting developers within the Mozilla Firefox project. We conducted an empirical analysis comparing responses from human developers, a standard GPT model, and a GPT model enhanced with RAG, using real queries from Mozilla’s developer chat rooms. To ensure a rigorous evaluation, Mozilla experts assessed the responses based on helpfulness, comprehensiveness, and conciseness. The results show that RAG-assisted responses were more comprehensive than human developers (62.50% to 54.17%) and almost as helpful (75.00% to 79.17%), suggesting RAG’s potential to enhance developer assistance. However, the RAG responses were not as concise and often verbose. The results show the potential to apply RAG-based tools to Open Source Software (OSS) to minimize the load to core maintainers without losing answer quality. Toning down retrieval mechanisms and making responses even shorter in the future would enhance developer assistance in massive projects like Mozilla Firefox.","az":"近年来，使用大语言模型（LLM）支持软件开发任务的情况稳步增加，从协助开发者编码，到提供回答新手问题的对话式智能体。本研究与 Mozilla 基金会合作，评估检索增强生成（RAG）在 Mozilla Firefox 项目中协助开发者的有效性。我们开展了一项实证分析，使用来自 Mozilla 开发者聊天室的真实提问，比较人类开发者、标准 GPT 模型以及经 RAG 增强的 GPT 模型的回答。为确保评估严谨，Mozilla 的专家从有用性、全面性和简洁性三方面评估这些回答。结果显示，RAG 辅助的回答比人类开发者更全面（62.50% 对 54.17%），有用性也几乎持平（75.00% 对 79.17%），表明 RAG 有潜力增强对开发者的支持。然而，RAG 的回答不够简洁，往往显得冗长。结果显示，将基于 RAG 的工具应用于开源软件（OSS）有望在不损失回答质量的前提下减轻核心维护者的负担。未来若适度收敛检索机制并使回答更简短，将进一步提升在 Mozilla Firefox 这类大型项目中对开发者的支持效果。","tl":"专家评估显示 RAG 回答比人类更全面，但过于冗长。","au":["João Correia","Daniel Coutinho","Marco Castelluccio","Caio Barbosa","Igor Steinmacher","Marco Gerosa","Alessandro Garcia","Rafael de Mello","Anita Sarma"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["human-study","llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["retrieval-augmented generation","developer question answering","Mozilla Firefox","expert evaluation","open source support"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/128/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.21933"},{"id":"p00615","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A First Look at Model Supply Chain: From the Risk Perspective","tz":"模型供应链初探：风险视角","a":"The rapid proliferation of publicly available artificial intelligence models on platforms such Hugging Face has formed a complex model supply chain, where base models are continually transformed, e.g., by fine-tuning, quantization, and merging, into new derived models. Despite its critical importance for reuse, provenance, and risk management, this supply chain remains poorly characterized at scale. We construct the first comprehensive model supply chain based on models on Hugging Face as of June 25, 2025, which consists of 1.82 million models as well as 0.54 million dependency relations. Then, we conduct the first systematic study to characterize the usage, evolution, quality, and risk of this model supply chain. Finally, we provide actionable implications for model maintainers, consumers, platform designers, and researchers to foster this new direction in the era of AI.","az":"Hugging Face 等平台上公开可用的人工智能模型迅速激增，形成了一条复杂的模型供应链：基础模型不断通过微调、量化和合并等方式被改造为新的衍生模型。尽管这条供应链对复用、溯源和风险管理至关重要，但其在大规模层面上仍缺乏刻画。我们基于截至 2025 年 6 月 25 日 Hugging Face 上的模型，构建了首个全面的模型供应链，包含 182 万个模型和 54 万条依赖关系。随后，我们开展了首个系统性研究，刻画该模型供应链的使用情况、演化、质量与风险。最后，我们为模型维护者、使用者、平台设计者和研究人员给出了可操作的启示，以推动这一 AI 时代的新方向。","tl":"首次构建 182 万模型的 HF 供应链图谱并刻画其风险。","au":["Ziqian Chen","Zekai Chen","Susheng Wu","Bihuan Chen","Wenyan Song","Yiheng Huang","Zhuotong Zhou","Yiheng Cao","Xin Peng"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","security"],"kw":["model supply chain","Hugging Face","pre-trained model reuse","provenance","risk characterization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/129/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/129/A-First-Look-at-Model-Supply-Chain-From-the-Risk-Perspective"},{"id":"p00616","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"\"Game Changer\" or \"Overenthusiastic Drunk Acquaintance\"? Generative AI Use by Blind and Low Vision Software Professionals in the Workplace","tz":"“改变游戏规则”还是“热情过头的醉汉熟人”？盲人与低视力软件从业者在职场中对生成式 AI 的使用","a":"The software development workplace poses numerous technical and collaborative accessibility challenges for blind and low vision software professionals (BLVSPs). Though Generative AI (GenAI) is increasingly adopted within the software development industry and has been a rapidly growing topic of interest in research, to date, the unique perspectives of BLVSPs have yet to be consulted. We report on a qualitative study involving 39 semi-structured interviews with BLVSPs about what the introduction of GenAI has meant for their work. We found that BLVSPs used GenAI for many software development tasks, resulting in benefits such as increased productivity and accessibility. However, significant costs were also accompanied by GenAI use as they were more vulnerable to hallucinations than their sighted colleagues. Sometimes, organizational policies prevented use. Based on our findings, we discuss the higher-risks and higher-returns that BLVSPs had to carefully weigh when deciding whether and when to use GenAI tools for work.","az":"软件开发的工作场所为盲人与低视力软件从业者（BLVSPs）带来了大量技术性与协作性的无障碍挑战。尽管生成式 AI（GenAI）在软件开发行业中被日益采用，并成为研究中快速升温的话题，但迄今为止，BLVSPs 的独特视角尚未被征询。我们报告了一项定性研究，对 39 名 BLVSPs 进行了半结构化访谈，了解 GenAI 的出现对他们的工作意味着什么。我们发现 BLVSPs 将 GenAI 用于许多软件开发任务，带来了生产力与无障碍性提升等益处。然而，使用 GenAI 也伴随着显著代价：相比视力正常的同事，他们更容易受到幻觉的伤害。有时，组织政策还会禁止使用。基于这些发现，我们讨论了 BLVSPs 在决定是否以及何时在工作中使用 GenAI 工具时，必须谨慎权衡的更高风险与更高回报。","tl":"39 场访谈揭示盲低视力开发者用 GenAI 的高风险高回报权衡。","au":["Yoonha Cha","Victoria Jackson","Lauren Shu","Stacy Branham","Andre van der Hoek"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","tg":["human-study","accessibility-inclusion"],"kw":["blind and low vision developers","generative AI","accessibility","qualitative interview study","workplace adoption"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/130/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.24462"},{"id":"p00617","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PreServe: Intelligent Management for LMaaS Systems via Hierarchical Prediction","tz":"PreServe：通过分层预测实现 LMaaS 系统的智能管理","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have revolutionized fields such as natural language processing and software engineering, fueling the growth of Language-Model-as-a-Service (LMaaS) platforms hosted by industry leaders like OpenAI. These platforms handle millions of queries daily, requiring efficient management to reduce serving latency and meet Service Level Objectives (SLOs) while optimizing resource utilization. However, conventional cloud service management techniques, originally designed for traditional workloads, are suboptimal for LMaaS due to its dynamic service workloads and variable request loads. To address this, we propose PreServe, a tailored LMaaS management framework centered on hierarchical prediction. PreServe incorporates a service workload predictor to estimate periodic token density at a coarse granularity and a novel request load predictor to assess the resource demand of individual LLM requests, enabling the construction of a load anticipator for each LLM instance. By integrating both long-term and short-term predictions, PreServe adjusts resource allocation in advance, mitigating the risks of instance under- or over-provisioning. Moreover, PreServe optimizes request routing by considering both current and anticipated future instance loads, ensuring balanced load distribution across instances. Evaluations on real-world LMaaS production datasets demonstrate that PreServe outperforms state-of-the-art approaches, achieving over 41.3% reduction in tail latency, an average 49.38% decrease in resource consumption, and incurring only 0.23% additional overhead.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已经变革了自然语言处理和软件工程等领域，推动了由 OpenAI 等行业领导者托管的“语言模型即服务”（LMaaS）平台的增长。这些平台每天处理数百万次查询，需要高效管理以降低服务延迟、满足服务级目标（SLO），同时优化资源利用率。然而，传统云服务管理技术最初是为传统负载设计的，面对 LMaaS 动态的服务负载和多变的请求负载并不理想。为此，我们提出 PreServe，一个以分层预测为核心、为 LMaaS 量身定制的管理框架。PreServe 包含一个服务负载预测器，用于在粗粒度上估计周期性的 token 密度；以及一个新颖的请求负载预测器，用于评估单个 LLM 请求的资源需求，从而为每个 LLM 实例构建负载预判器。通过融合长期与短期预测，PreServe 提前调整资源分配，缓解实例资源不足或过度配置的风险。此外，PreServe 在优化请求路由时同时考虑实例当前与预期未来的负载，确保各实例之间负载均衡。在真实 LMaaS 生产数据集上的评估表明，PreServe 优于最先进方法，将尾延迟降低超过 41.3%，资源消耗平均减少 49.38%，而仅引入 0.23% 的额外开销。","tl":"分层预测 token 密度与单请求负载，提前调配资源并均衡路由。","au":["Zhihan Jiang","Yujie Huang","Guangba Yu","Junjie Huang","Jiazhen Gu","Michael Lyu"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["LMaaS","LLM serving","workload prediction","resource allocation","request routing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/131/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00618","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SustainDiffusion: Optimising the Social and Environmental Sustainability of Stable Diffusion Models","tz":"SustainDiffusion：优化 Stable Diffusion 模型的社会与环境可持续性","a":"Background: Text-to-image generation models are widely used across numerous domains. Among these models, Stable Diffusion (SD) – an open-source text-to-image generation model – has become the most popular, producing over 12 billion images annually. However, the widespread use of these models raises concerns regarding their social and environmental sustainability. Aims: To reduce the harm that SD models may have on society and the environment, we introduce SustainDiffusion, a search-based approach designed to enhance the social and environmental sustainability of SD models. Method: SustainDiffusion searches the optimal combination of hyperparameters and prompt structures that can reduce gender and ethnic bias in generated images while also lowering the energy consumption required for image generation. Importantly, SustainDiffusion maintains image quality comparable to that of the original SD model. Results: We conduct a comprehensive empirical evaluation of SustainDiffusion, testing it against six different baselines using 56 different prompts. Our results demonstrate that SustainDiffusion can reduce gender bias in SD3 by 68%, ethnic bias by 59%, and energy consumption (calculated as the sum of CPU and GPU energy) by 48%. Additionally, the outcomes produced by SustainDiffusion are consistent across multiple runs and can be generalised to various prompts. Conclusions: With SustainDiffusion, we demonstrate how enhancing the social and environmental sustainability of text-to-image generation models is possible without fine-tuning or changing the model’s architecture.","az":"背景：文本到图像生成模型已在众多领域被广泛使用。其中，Stable Diffusion（SD）这一开源的文本到图像生成模型最为流行，每年生成超过 120 亿张图像。然而，这类模型的广泛使用引发了对其社会与环境可持续性的担忧。目标：为降低 SD 模型可能对社会和环境造成的危害，我们提出 SustainDiffusion，一种基于搜索的方法，旨在增强 SD 模型的社会与环境可持续性。方法：SustainDiffusion 搜索超参数与提示结构的最优组合，以在降低生成图像中的性别与种族偏见的同时，降低图像生成所需的能耗。重要的是，SustainDiffusion 保持了与原始 SD 模型相当的图像质量。结果：我们对 SustainDiffusion 进行了全面的实证评估，使用 56 条不同提示与六个不同基线进行对比。结果表明，SustainDiffusion 可将 SD3 中的性别偏见降低 68%、种族偏见降低 59%，并将能耗（按 CPU 与 GPU 能耗之和计算）降低 48%。此外，SustainDiffusion 的结果在多次运行中保持一致，并可泛化到各种提示。结论：借助 SustainDiffusion，我们证明了无需微调或改变模型架构，也能提升文本到图像生成模型的社会与环境可持续性。","tl":"搜索超参与提示结构组合，同时降低扩散模型偏见与能耗。","au":["Giordano d'Aloisio","Tosin Fadahunsi","Jay Choy","Rebecca Moussa","Federica Sarro"],"top":"generative-and-multimodal-models","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["cross-track-bridge","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Stable Diffusion","search-based optimization","gender and ethnic bias","energy consumption","sustainability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/132/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.15663"},{"id":"p00619","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"On the Robustness of Fairness Practices: A Causal Framework for Systematic Evaluation","tz":"论公平性实践的稳健性：一个用于系统评估的因果框架","a":"Machine learning (ML) algorithms are increasingly deployed to make critical decisions in socioeconomic applications such as finance, criminal justice, and autonomous driving. However, due to their data-driven and pattern-seeking nature, ML algorithms may develop decision logic that disproportionately distributes opportunities, benefits, resources, or information among different population groups, potentially harming marginalized communities. In response to such fairness concerns, the software engineering and ML communities have made significant efforts to establish the best practices for creating fair ML software. These include fairness interventions for training ML models such as including sensitive features, selecting non-sensitive attributes, and applying bias mitigators. But how reliably can software professionals tasked with developing data-driven systems depend on these recommendations? And how well do these practices generalize in the presence of faulty labels, missing data, or distribution shifts? These questions form the core theme of this paper. We present a testing tool and technique based on causality theory to assess the robustness of best practices in fair ML software development. Given a practice—specified as a first-order logic property—and a socio-critical dataset that satisfies the property, our goal is to search for neighborhood datasets to determine whether the property continues to hold. This process is akin to testing the robustness of a neural network for image classification, except that the “image\" is an entire dataset, and its “neighbors\" are datasets in which certain causal hypotheses are altered. Since computing neighborhood datasets while accounting for various factors—such as noise, faulty labeling, and demographic shifts—is challenging, we utilize causal graph representations of the dataset and leverage a search algorithm to explore equivalent causal graphs to generate datasets. Our results across various fairness-sensitive tasks, derived from prevalent fairness-sensitive applications, identify best practices that preserve robustness under the varying factors.","az":"机器学习（ML）算法正被越来越多地部署到金融、刑事司法和自动驾驶等社会经济应用中做关键决策。然而，由于其数据驱动和寻找模式的本质，ML 算法可能形成在不同人群之间不成比例地分配机会、利益、资源或信息的决策逻辑，从而可能伤害边缘化群体。为回应这些公平性担忧，软件工程与 ML 社区做出了大量努力来确立创建公平 ML 软件的最佳实践，包括面向 ML 模型训练的公平性干预，如纳入敏感特征、选择非敏感属性以及应用偏见缓解器。但是，负责开发数据驱动系统的软件从业者能在多大程度上可靠地依赖这些建议？在存在错误标签、数据缺失或分布偏移的情况下，这些实践的泛化性又如何？这些问题构成了本文的核心主题。我们提出了一种基于因果理论的测试工具与技术，用以评估公平 ML 软件开发中最佳实践的稳健性。给定一条实践——以一阶逻辑性质的形式给出——以及一个满足该性质的社会关键数据集，我们的目标是搜索邻域数据集，判断该性质是否依然成立。这一过程类似于测试用于图像分类的神经网络的稳健性，只不过此处的“图像”是整个数据集，而其“邻居”是某些因果假设被改变后的数据集。由于在考虑噪声、错误标注和人口结构偏移等多种因素的同时计算邻域数据集颇具挑战，我们利用数据集的因果图表示，并借助搜索算法探索等价的因果图来生成数据集。我们在源自常见公平性敏感应用的各类公平性敏感任务上的结果，识别出了在各种变动因素下仍能保持稳健的最佳实践。","tl":"把数据集当测试对象，用等价因果图搜索检验公平性实践稳健性。","au":["Verya Monjezi","Ashish Kumar","Ashutosh Trivedi","Gang (Gary) Tan","Saeid Tizpaz-Niari"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["fairness practices","causal testing","robustness","bias mitigation","socio-critical datasets"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/133/x"},{"id":"p00620","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Exploring and Improving Real-World Vulnerability Data Generation via Prompting Large Language Models","tz":"通过提示大语言模型探索并改进真实世界漏洞数据的生成","a":"Data-driven approaches have proven to be promising for vulnerability analysis, contingent on quality and sizable training data being available. Several dedicated vulnerability data generation techniques have demonstrated impressive merits, yet they are limited to simple (single-line injection induced) vulnerabilities only and suffer from overfitting to seed samples. Large language models (LLMs) may overcome these fundamental limitations as they are known to be effective at generative tasks. yet it remains unclear how they would fare for the task of vulnerable sample generation. In this paper, we explore the potentials and gaps of seven state-of-the-art (SOTA) LLMs for that task via prompting. We reveal that the LLMs are capable of injecting vulnerabilities, with advanced prompting strategies such as few-shot in-context learning and our new vulnerability-introducing code-change semantics (VICS) guided prompting boosting the effectiveness, achieving up to 93% success rate on a synthetic dataset and 88% on real-world code. The LLMs can effectively perform both single- and multi-line injections, addressing a key limitation of prior work. Notably, they exhibit a strong preference to replacement edits, different from ground-truth patterns, and their effectiveness varies across CWE types. Furthermore, LLMs, particularly with VICS, outperform existing SOTA vulnerability generators %(VulGen and VGX) with success rate improvements of up to 210%-343%. Crucially, the LLM-generated data substantially improves the performance of downstream DL-based vulnerability analysis models, especially with multi-line injections, boosting their accuracy by up to 36.2%. The generated samples also enhances the effectiveness of other LLMs for vulnerability analysis via RAG, with multi-line-injected samples yielding up to 16.5% gains. Most importantly, our findings reveal that, augmenting existing DL models with high-quality, LLM-generated data can lead to vulnerability analysis performance (up to 67.50% accuracy) superior to those of even the most advanced LLMs performing the same analysis (up to 27.40%), indicating the usefulness of the LLM-generated vulnerability data at present and in longer term.","az":"数据驱动的方法已被证明在漏洞分析中很有前景，但其前提是有高质量且规模足够的训练数据。若干专门的漏洞数据生成技术展现了令人印象深刻的优点，但它们仅限于简单的（由单行注入引起的）漏洞，并且容易对种子样本过拟合。大语言模型（LLM）以擅长生成式任务著称，可能克服这些根本局限，但它们在生成含漏洞样本这一任务上的表现仍不清楚。本文通过提示的方式，探索七个最先进（SOTA）LLM 在该任务上的潜力与差距。我们发现 LLM 有能力注入漏洞，而少样本上下文学习以及我们提出的“引入漏洞的代码变更语义（VICS）”引导式提示等高级提示策略进一步提升了效果，在合成数据集上成功率高达 93%，在真实代码上达到 88%。LLM 能够有效执行单行与多行注入，解决了先前工作的一个关键局限。值得注意的是，它们强烈偏好替换式编辑，与真实模式不同，且其效果因 CWE 类型而异。此外，LLM（尤其是配合 VICS 时）优于现有 SOTA 漏洞生成器，成功率提升高达 210%–343%。至关重要的是，LLM 生成的数据显著提升了下游基于深度学习的漏洞分析模型的性能，尤其是在多行注入的情况下，准确率提升最高达 36.2%。所生成的样本还通过 RAG 增强了其他 LLM 进行漏洞分析的效果，多行注入样本带来最高 16.5% 的收益。最重要的是，我们的发现表明，用高质量的 LLM 生成数据增强现有深度学习模型，可使漏洞分析性能（准确率高达 67.50%）优于最先进的 LLM 直接执行同样分析的表现（最高 27.40%），说明 LLM 生成的漏洞数据在当下和长期都具有实用价值。","tl":"提出 VICS 引导提示让 LLM 注入多行漏洞，显著提升下游检测。","au":["Guangbei Yi","Yu Nong","Minzhang Li","Haipeng Cai"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","empirical-study"],"kw":["vulnerability data generation","prompting strategies","VICS","multi-line injection","deep learning vulnerability analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/134/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3773176"},{"id":"p00621","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Energy-Efficient Software Development: A Multi-dimensional Empirical Analysis of Stack Overflow","tz":"能效软件开发：对 Stack Overflow 的多维度实证分析","a":"Energy consumption of software applications has emerged as a critical concern for developers to contemplate in their daily development processes. Previous studies have surveyed a limited number of developers to understand their viewpoints on energy consumption. We complement these studies by analyzing a meticulously curated dataset of 1,193 Stack Overflow (SO) questions concerning energy consumption. These questions capture real-world energy-related challenges in practice. To understand practitioners’ perceptions, we investigate the intentions behind these questions, semantic topics, and associated technologies (e.g., programming languages). Our results reveal that: (i) the most prevalent energy consumption topic is about balancing Positioning usage; (ii) efficiently handling data is particularly challenging, with these questions having the longest response times; (iii) practitioners primarily ask questions to understand a concept or API related to energy consumption; and (iv) practitioners are concerned about energy consumption across multiple levels—hardware, operating systems, and programming languages—during energy efficient software development. Our findings raise awareness about energy consumption’s impact on software development. We also derive actionable implications for energy optimization at different levels (e.g., optimizing API usage or hardware accesses) during energy-aware software development.","az":"软件应用的能耗已成为开发者在日常开发过程中必须考虑的关键问题。以往研究调查了数量有限的开发者以了解他们对能耗的看法。我们对此加以补充，分析了一个精心整理的、包含 1,193 个与能耗相关的 Stack Overflow（SO）问题的数据集，这些问题捕捉了实践中真实的能耗挑战。为理解从业者的认知，我们考察了这些问题背后的意图、语义主题以及相关技术（如编程语言）。我们的结果表明：(i) 最常见的能耗主题是关于平衡定位服务（Positioning）的使用；(ii) 高效地处理数据尤其具有挑战性，这类问题的响应时间最长；(iii) 从业者提问主要是为了理解与能耗相关的某个概念或 API；(iv) 在能效软件开发过程中，从业者关注硬件、操作系统和编程语言等多个层面的能耗问题。我们的发现提高了人们对能耗影响软件开发的认识，我们也为能耗感知软件开发中不同层面的能耗优化（例如优化 API 使用或硬件访问）提炼了可操作的启示。","tl":"挖掘 1193 个 SO 问题，刻画多层面能耗开发挑战与意图。","au":["Bihui Jin","Heng Li","Pengyu Nie","Ying Zou"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["energy consumption","Stack Overflow mining","energy-efficient development","developer perception","empirical analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/135/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.19222"},{"id":"p00622","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Cobblestone: A Divide-and-Conquer Approach for Automating Formal Verification","tz":"Cobblestone：一种分而治之的形式化验证自动化方法","a":"Formal verification using proof assistants, such as Coq, is an effective way of improving software quality, but requires significant effort and expertise. Machine learning can automatically synthesize proofs, but such tools are able to prove only a fraction of desired software properties. We introduce Cobblestone, a divide-and-conquer approach for proof synthesis. Cobblestone uses a large language model (LLM) to generate potential proofs, uses those proofs to break the problem into simpler parts, automatically identifies which of those parts were successfully proven, and iterates on the remaining parts to build a correct proof that is guaranteed to be sound, despite the reliance on unsound LLMs. We evaluate Cobblestone on four benchmarks of open-source Coq projects, controlling for training data leakage. Fully automatically, Cobblestone outperforms state-of-the-art non-LLM tools, and proves many theorems that other LLM-based tools cannot, and on many benchmarks, outperforms them. Each Cobblestone run costs only $1.25 and takes 14.7 minutes, on average. Cobblestone can also be used with external input, from a user or another tool, providing a proof structure or relevant lemmas. Evaluated with such an oracle, Cobblestone proves up to 58% of theorems. Overall, our research shows that tools can make use of partial progress and external input to more effectively automate formal verification.","az":"使用 Coq 等证明助手进行形式化验证是提升软件质量的有效途径，但需要大量投入与专业知识。机器学习可以自动合成证明，但此类工具只能证明所需软件性质中的一小部分。我们提出 Cobblestone，一种分而治之的证明合成方法。Cobblestone 使用大语言模型（LLM）生成候选证明，利用这些证明将问题拆解为更简单的部分，自动识别其中哪些部分已被成功证明，并对剩余部分进行迭代，从而构建出正确的证明；尽管依赖的是不可靠（unsound）的 LLM，最终证明的可靠性仍有保证。我们在四个开源 Coq 项目的基准上评估 Cobblestone，并控制了训练数据泄漏。在完全自动的设置下，Cobblestone 优于最先进的非 LLM 工具，证明了许多其他基于 LLM 的工具无法证明的定理，并在多个基准上优于它们。Cobblestone 每次运行平均仅花费 1.25 美元、耗时 14.7 分钟。Cobblestone 还可以使用来自用户或另一工具的外部输入，这些输入提供证明结构或相关引理。在这种预言式设置下评估，Cobblestone 能证明多达 58% 的定理。总体而言，我们的研究表明，工具可以利用部分进展和外部输入来更有效地自动化形式化验证。","tl":"把 LLM 的部分成功证明拆解迭代，组合出可靠的 Coq 证明。","au":["Saketh Ram Kasibatla","Arpan Agrawal","Yuriy Brun","Sorin Lerner","Talia Lily Ringer","Emily First"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["proof synthesis","Coq","formal verification","divide-and-conquer","large language model"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/136/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3773178"},{"id":"p00623","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"StorFuzz: Using Data Diversity to Overcome Fuzzing Plateaus","tz":"StorFuzz：利用数据多样性突破模糊测试平台期","a":"Fuzzing is widely used to discover software bugs and vulnerabilities. Unfortunately, real-world long-running fuzzing campaigns often plateau and no progress can be made anymore, leaving code areas untested. State-of-the-art fuzzers leverage code coverage to measure progress and reach new areas, but this is insufficient to capture all program behavior, as code coverage may be the same for different behavior, thus preventing progress and masking bugs. In this paper, we introduce StorFuzz, a novel technique to overcome fuzzing plateaus and improve on code coverage by leveraging our new data coverage. StorFuzz automatically identifies and instruments memory stores to capture changes in program behavior invisible to control flow, which it uses to diversify the saturated corpora of plateaued campaigns. StorFuzz leverages this diversified corpus of test cases that changed internal states to improve navigation of the input space, which also enables conventional fuzzers to improve their code coverage. We implement StorFuzz in LibAFL and evaluate on FuzzBench, starting from a corpus, which is saturated by multimonth OSS-Fuzz fuzzing campaigns and LibAFL. We show that StorFuzz successfully generates new coverage for plateauing campaigns of widely-used and well-fuzzed software, leading to the discovery of 50 new bugs in 7 OSS-Fuzz projects, like VLC and PHP, with some bugs having been present in the code for 14 years . Our approach significantly outperforms both the state-of-the-art fuzzer LibAFL and data-guided fuzzer DDFuzz in 11 of 23 FuzzBench benchmarks, while performing equally on all others. StorFuzz is also complementary to WingFuzz, an approach guided by static data, as both fuzzers cover distinct code regions. We make StorFuzz and our artifacts available as open source to aid reproducibility and allow easy reuse by future work.","az":"模糊测试被广泛用于发现软件缺陷与漏洞。遗憾的是，真实世界中长期运行的模糊测试活动常常进入平台期，无法再取得进展，使部分代码区域未被测试。最先进的 fuzzer 利用代码覆盖率衡量进展并到达新区域，但这不足以刻画所有程序行为，因为不同的行为可能具有相同的代码覆盖，从而阻碍进展并掩盖缺陷。本文提出 StorFuzz，一种借助我们提出的数据覆盖来突破模糊测试平台期并改进代码覆盖率的新技术。StorFuzz 自动识别并插桩内存写入（store），以捕获控制流不可见的程序行为变化，并用它来多样化已陷入平台期的饱和语料库。StorFuzz 利用这一由改变内部状态的测试用例组成的多样化语料库，改进对输入空间的探索，这也使传统 fuzzer 能够提升其代码覆盖率。我们在 LibAFL 中实现了 StorFuzz，并在 FuzzBench 上进行评估，起始语料库来自数月之久的 OSS-Fuzz 模糊测试活动与 LibAFL 所达到的饱和语料。我们证明 StorFuzz 能为广泛使用且已被充分模糊测试的软件中陷入平台期的活动生成新的覆盖，从而在 VLC 和 PHP 等 7 个 OSS-Fuzz 项目中发现 50 个新缺陷，其中一些缺陷已在代码中存在 14 年之久。我们的方法在 23 个 FuzzBench 基准中的 11 个上显著优于最先进的 fuzzer LibAFL 和数据引导的 fuzzer DDFuzz，在其余基准上表现相当。StorFuzz 与由静态数据引导的 WingFuzz 方法也具有互补性，因为两个 fuzzer 覆盖了不同的代码区域。我们将 StorFuzz 及相关制品开源，以帮助可复现性并便于后续工作复用。","tl":"插桩内存写入获得数据覆盖，使饱和语料重新产生新覆盖。","au":["Leon Weiß","Tobias Holl","Kevin Borgolte"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["fuzzing plateau","data coverage","memory store instrumentation","corpus diversification","LibAFL"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/137/x","pu":"https://softsec.rub.de/files/pdf/icse2026-storfuzz.pdf"},{"id":"p00624","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Dependency-aware Residual Risk Analysis","tz":"考虑依赖关系的残余风险分析","a":"However much we test a software system, some residual risk of undiscovered bugs always remains. If we model test generation as a sampling process, a residual risk can be defined as the probability that the next test input reveals a bug. This risk is upper-bounded by the discovery probability (DP), i.e., the probability that the next test input covers new code, which itself is upper-bounded by the coverage rate, i.e., the expected number of new coverage elements per test input. Prior work introduced the Good-Turing estimator (GoTu) to estimate residual risk via coverage rate. However, we find that GoTu substantially overestimates, leading to undue optimism in bug finding because (i) the coverage rate is only a loose upper bound, and (ii) it ignores dependencies among coverage elements. We propose dependency-aware DP estimation for residual risk analysis. Our estimator directly estimates DP and accounting for coverage dependencies using Ma and Chao’s sample coverage estimation. A naive implementation requires space proportional to the number of coverage elements and executions, which can be prohibitively large. To make it practical, we introduce two optimizations: dependency-aware node removal, which reduces the number of coverage elements to observe, and online singleton cluster maintenance, which eliminates the need to record observed coverage elements in each execution. A comparison of our estimator and GoTu on real-world software from FuzzBench demonstrates a substantial reduction in estimation error. If we stopped the campaign when the estimate of residual risk falls below a certain threshold, GoTu would lead a tester to waste 7 more time than our estimator before deciding to stop. Our estimator achieves a median absolute error of only one-fifth that of GoTu. Finally, our bug-based analysis shows that our estimator achieves one to two orders of magnitude lower error than GoTu in residual risk estimation.","az":"无论我们如何充分地测试一个软件系统，总会残留一些未被发现的缺陷，即残余风险。如果把测试生成建模为一个抽样过程，残余风险可定义为下一个测试输入揭示缺陷的概率。该风险的上界是发现概率（DP），即下一个测试输入覆盖新代码的概率；而 DP 本身又以覆盖率速率（即每个测试输入带来的新覆盖元素的期望数量）为上界。先前工作引入了 Good-Turing 估计器（GoTu），通过覆盖率速率来估计残余风险。然而我们发现 GoTu 会大幅高估，导致对缺陷发现过于乐观，原因在于：(i) 覆盖率速率只是一个松弛的上界；(ii) 它忽略了覆盖元素之间的依赖关系。我们提出面向残余风险分析的、考虑依赖关系的 DP 估计方法。我们的估计器直接估计 DP，并利用 Ma 与 Chao 的样本覆盖估计来考虑覆盖依赖关系。朴素实现所需空间与覆盖元素数量和执行次数成正比，可能大到无法承受。为使其实用，我们引入两项优化：依赖感知的节点移除，用以减少需要观测的覆盖元素数量；以及在线单例簇维护，从而无需记录每次执行中观测到的覆盖元素。在来自 FuzzBench 的真实软件上，我们的估计器与 GoTu 的对比表明估计误差大幅下降。如果在残余风险估计值低于某一阈值时停止测试活动，GoTu 会让测试者在决定停止之前多浪费 7 倍的时间。我们的估计器的绝对误差中位数仅为 GoTu 的五分之一。最后，基于缺陷的分析显示，在残余风险估计上，我们的估计器的误差比 GoTu 低一到两个数量级。","tl":"直接估计发现概率并考虑覆盖依赖，大幅降低残余风险估计误差。","au":["Seongmin Lee","Marcel Böhme"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["residual risk","discovery probability","Good-Turing estimator","coverage dependency","fuzzing stopping rule"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/138/x","pu":"https://nimgnoeseel.github.io/assets/pdf/structrr-paper.pdf"},{"id":"p00625","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Connected to Stay: Gender Homophily and Its Role in Open-Source Software Developer Retention","tz":"因连接而留下：性别同质性及其在开源软件开发者留存中的作用","a":"Understanding how social connections shape participation is critical for sustaining open-source software (OSS) communities. We analyze longitudinal collaboration networks of 1.6 million developers over 14 years (2008–2022) using the World of Code dataset, focusing on gender homophily, developers’ preference to collaborate with others of the same gender, and its relationship to retention. We find strong evidence of gender homophily beyond demographic baselines, with same-gender ties among women exceeding random expectations by over 200%. While women tend to form homophilous ties, men show a preference for cross-gender collaboration, and these patterns shift over time as the OSS ecosystem evolves. Most notably, we find that developers—especially women—who collaborate with other women experience significantly lower dropout risk, with hazard rates up to 20.7% lower. These retention effects only become visible after accounting for activity levels, revealing a Simpson’s Paradox in prior analyses. Our results suggest that homophilous ties offer social support that improves developer persistence, highlighting the importance of inclusive, gender-diverse networks for sustaining participation in OSS projects.","az":"理解社会连接如何塑造参与，对于维系开源软件（OSS）社区至关重要。我们使用 World of Code 数据集，分析了 160 万名开发者在 14 年间（2008–2022）的纵向协作网络，重点关注性别同质性（即开发者更倾向于与同性别者协作）及其与留存的关系。我们发现，性别同质性的证据强于人口统计基线：女性之间的同性别连接超出随机预期 200% 以上。虽然女性倾向于形成同质性联系，男性却更偏好跨性别协作，并且随着 OSS 生态的演化，这些模式会随时间变化。最值得注意的是，我们发现与女性协作的开发者（尤其是女性本身）退出风险显著更低，风险率最多降低 20.7%。这些留存效应只有在控制活跃度水平之后才会显现，揭示了先前分析中存在的辛普森悖论。我们的结果表明，同质性联系提供了有助于提升开发者坚持度的社会支持，凸显了包容且性别多元的网络对维系 OSS 项目参与的重要性。","tl":"160 万开发者数据显示与女性协作显著降低退出风险。","au":["Tielin Katy Yu","Huilian Sophie Qiu","Patrick Park","Laura Dabbish","Bogdan Vasilescu"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["empirical-study","accessibility-inclusion","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["gender homophily","developer retention","open source collaboration networks","World of Code","survival analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/139/x"},{"id":"p00626","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Characterizing Regression Bug‑Inducing Changes and Improving LLM‑Based Regression Bug Detection","tz":"刻画引入回归缺陷的代码变更并改进基于 LLM 的回归缺陷检测","a":"Regression bugs are common in real-world software projects. Although several studies have characterized various aspects of these bugs, a detailed analysis of the characteristics of code changes that introduce regression bugs is still lacking. It is also not clear whether and how regression bugs can be identified, in the era of wide usage of large language models (LLMs), in code commits during software development in the first place. To fill this gap, our study systematically analyzes 280 regression bugs from open-source Java projects, examining both the root causes and the associated development activities of regression bug-inducing changes, while also evaluating the effectiveness of LLMs in detection such commits and explaining their underlying causes. Our findings indicate that regression bugs are usually triggered by a single atomic development activity, with feature changes or additions, and bug fixes appearing more frequently in regression bug-inducing commits. Additionally, performance improvements and refactoring are often responsible for the introduction of bugs. We develop a taxonomy that categorizes the root causes of regression bugs into two types: intrinsic errors, such as logic errors and unchecked null references, and compatibility errors, where otherwise correct changes inadvertently violate assumptions or dependencies in other parts of the system. Furthermore, we verify that LLMs have limited ability to detect regression bugs. Based on our findings, we construct LLM4Reg that substantially improves the precision, recall, and explanation capabilities of LLM-based regression bug detection.","az":"回归缺陷在真实软件项目中十分常见。尽管已有若干研究刻画了这类缺陷的各个方面，但对于引入回归缺陷的代码变更的特征，仍缺乏细致的分析。同时，在大语言模型（LLM）被广泛使用的今天，软件开发过程中的代码提交里究竟能否、以及如何识别出回归缺陷，也仍不清楚。为填补这一空白，我们的研究系统分析了来自开源 Java 项目的 280 个回归缺陷，考察了引入回归缺陷的变更的根因及其关联的开发活动，同时评估了 LLM 在检测此类提交并解释其根本原因方面的有效性。我们的发现表明，回归缺陷通常由单一的原子开发活动触发，其中特性变更或新增特性以及缺陷修复在引入回归缺陷的提交中出现得更为频繁。此外，性能改进和重构也常常是引入缺陷的原因。我们构建了一个分类体系，将回归缺陷的根因分为两类：内在错误（如逻辑错误、未检查的空引用）和兼容性错误（即本身正确的变更却无意中违反了系统其他部分的假设或依赖）。进一步地，我们验证了 LLM 检测回归缺陷的能力有限。基于上述发现，我们构建了 LLM4Reg，显著提升了基于 LLM 的回归缺陷检测的精确率、召回率与解释能力。","tl":"首次系统刻画回归缺陷诱因变更，并据此造出 LLM4Reg 提升检测。","au":["Xuezhi Song","Yijian Wu","Bihuan Chen","Zhengjie Lu","Shuning Liu","Xin Peng"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["regression bugs","bug-inducing changes","root cause taxonomy","LLM-based bug detection","Java open source"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/140/x","pu":"https://github.com/FudanSELab/LLM4Reg/blob/master/icse26_preprint_Regression_Bug_Inducing_Changes.pdf"},{"id":"p00627","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Efficient Strong Updates For Path Sensitive Data Dependence Analysis","tz":"面向路径敏感数据依赖分析的高效强更新","a":"Path-sensitive data dependence analysis is a powerful technique widely used in static vulnerability detection. One of the central challenges is how to resolve indirect data dependencies induced by pointer operations: the value loaded from a memory location may depend on different values stored before. Resolving indirect data dependencies in a path-sensitive manner significantly improves the analysis precision, but also induces high overhead that limits its scalability. We observe that much of the computation effort in path-sensitive data dependence analysis is spent on performing strong updates during load-store matching: a stored value propagates to a load statement only if it is not overwritten by other values stored to the same memory location during the propagation. Answering this question path-sensitively is extremely challenging and often leads to a state explosion that precludes efficient static analysis. To improve the efficiency for performing strong updates in path-sensitive data dependence analysis, our key insight is that the relation among multiple store statements could be determined in stages: most of the easy cases are handled efficiently by inferring a must-kill relation among the heap store statements, reserving the computationally expensive path-sensitive analysis for the rest. We design a tree-like data structure to encode both the control flow and alias information, which incrementally updates the relation during the analysis. Experiments have shown significant speed-ups and improved state coverage in static analysis through the algorithmic improvements of path-sensitive strong updates.","az":"路径敏感的数据依赖分析是一种强大的技术，被广泛用于静态漏洞检测。其核心挑战之一是如何解析由指针操作引发的间接数据依赖：从某个内存位置加载的值可能依赖于此前存入的不同值。以路径敏感的方式解析间接数据依赖能显著提升分析精度，但同时带来很高的开销，限制了其可扩展性。我们观察到，路径敏感数据依赖分析中的大量计算开销花在了 load-store 匹配时的强更新上：只有当某个已存储的值在传播过程中没有被写入同一内存位置的其他值覆盖时，它才能传播到某条 load 语句。以路径敏感方式回答这一问题极为困难，往往导致状态爆炸，使高效静态分析无法进行。为提升路径敏感数据依赖分析中强更新的效率，我们的关键洞见是：多条 store 语句之间的关系可以分阶段确定——大多数简单情形可以通过推断堆上 store 语句之间的 must-kill 关系来高效处理，而把计算代价高昂的路径敏感分析留给其余情形。我们设计了一种树状数据结构来同时编码控制流与别名信息，在分析过程中增量地更新这些关系。实验表明，通过对路径敏感强更新的算法改进，静态分析获得了显著的加速并提升了状态覆盖率。","tl":"用 must-kill 关系分阶段处理强更新，大幅加速路径敏感依赖分析。","au":["Yiyuan Guo","Charles Zhang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["path-sensitive analysis","data dependence","strong update","alias analysis","static vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/141/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3773183"},{"id":"p00628","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Scalable and Interpretable Mobile App Risk Analysis via Large Language Models","tz":"借助大语言模型实现可扩展且可解释的移动应用风险分析","a":"Mobile application marketplaces are responsible for vetting apps to identify and mitigate security risks. Current vetting processes are labor-intensive, relying on manual analysis by security professionals aided by semi-automated tools. To address this inefficiency, we propose Mars, a system that leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) for automated risk identification and profiling. Mars is designed to concurrently analyze multiple applications across diverse risk categories with minimal human intervention. To enhance analytical precision and operational efficiency, Mars leverages a pre-constructed risk identification tree to extract relevant indicators from high-dimensional application features. This initial step filters the data, reducing the input volume for the LLM and mitigating the potential for model hallucination induced by irrelevant features. The extracted indicators are then subjected to LLM analysis for final risk determination. Furthermore, Mars automatically generates a comprehensive evidence chain for each assessment, documenting the analytical process to provide transparent justification. These chains are designed to facilitate subsequent manual review and to inform enforcement decisions, such as application delisting. The performance of Mars was evaluated on a real-world dataset from a partner Android marketplace. The results demonstrate that Mars attained an F1-score of 0.838 in risk identification and an F1-score of 0.934 in evidence retrieval. To assess its practical applicability, a user study involving 20 expert analysts was conducted, which indicated that Mars yielded a substantial efficiency gain, ranging from 60% to 90%, over conventional manual analysis.","az":"移动应用市场有责任对上架应用进行审核，以识别并缓解安全风险。当前的审核流程高度依赖人力，需要安全专业人员在半自动化工具辅助下进行人工分析。为解决这一低效问题，我们提出了 Mars，一个利用大语言模型（LLM）进行自动化风险识别与画像的系统。Mars 被设计为能够在极少人工介入的情况下，跨多种风险类别并发分析多个应用。为提升分析精度与运行效率，Mars 利用预先构建的风险识别树，从高维应用特征中抽取相关指标。这一初始步骤过滤了数据，减少了输入 LLM 的数据量，并缓解了无关特征引发模型幻觉的可能。随后，抽取出的指标交由 LLM 分析以做出最终风险判定。此外，Mars 会为每次评估自动生成完整的证据链，记录分析过程以提供透明的判定依据。这些证据链旨在便于后续人工复核，并为下架应用等执法决策提供支撑。我们在一个合作 Android 应用市场的真实数据集上评估了 Mars 的性能。结果表明，Mars 在风险识别上取得了 0.838 的 F1 值，在证据检索上取得了 0.934 的 F1 值。为评估其实际可用性，我们开展了一项有 20 名专家分析师参与的用户研究，结果显示相比传统人工分析，Mars 带来了 60% 到 90% 的效率提升。","tl":"风险识别树先筛特征再交 LLM 判定，并自动产出可审计证据链。","au":["Yu Yang","Zhenyuan Li","Xiandong Ran","Jiahao Liu","Jiahui Wang","Bo Yu","Shouling Ji"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale","human-study"],"kw":["mobile app vetting","risk identification","LLM analysis","evidence chain","Android marketplace"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/142/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/142/Towards-Scalable-and-Interpretable-Mobile-App-Risk-Analysis-via-Large-Language-Models"},{"id":"p00629","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SAINT: Service-level Integration Test Generation with Program Analysis and LLM-based Agents","tz":"SAINT：结合程序分析与 LLM 智能体的服务级集成测试生成","a":"Enterprise applications are typically tested at multiple levels, with service-level testing playing an important role in validating application functionality. Existing service-level testing tools, especially for RESTful APIs, often employ fuzzing and/or depend on OpenAPI specifications which are not readily available in real-world enterprise codebases. Moreover, they fail to generate functional tests that exercise meaningful scenarios. In this work, we present SAINT, a novel white-box testing approach for service-level testing of enterprise Java applications. SAINT combines static analysis, large language models (LLMs), and LLM-based agents to automatically generate endpoint and scenario-based tests. The approach builds two key models: an endpoint model, capturing syntactic and semantic information about service endpoints, and an operation dependency graph, capturing inter-endpoint ordering constraints. SAINT then employs LLM-based agents to generate tests. Endpoint-focused tests aim to maximize code and database interaction coverage. Scenario-based tests are synthesized by extracting application use cases from code and refining them into executable tests via planning, action, and reflection phases of the agentic loop. We evaluated SAINT on eight Java applications, including a proprietary enterprise application. Our results illustrate the effectiveness of SAINT in coverage, fault detection, and scenario generation. Moreover, a developer survey provides strong endorsement of the scenario-based tests generated by SAINT. Overall, our work shows that combining static analysis with agentic LLM workflows enables more effective, functional, and developer-aligned service-level test generation.","az":"企业应用通常在多个层次上进行测试，其中服务级测试在验证应用功能方面扮演着重要角色。现有的服务级测试工具，尤其是针对 RESTful API 的工具，往往采用模糊测试和/或依赖 OpenAPI 规范，而在真实企业代码库中这类规范并不总是现成可用。此外，它们无法生成能够覆盖有意义场景的功能性测试。在本文中，我们提出了 SAINT，一种面向企业 Java 应用服务级测试的新型白盒测试方法。SAINT 结合静态分析、大语言模型（LLM）以及基于 LLM 的智能体，自动生成端点测试与基于场景的测试。该方法构建两个关键模型：一个端点模型，刻画服务端点的语法与语义信息；一个操作依赖图，刻画端点间的时序约束。随后 SAINT 使用基于 LLM 的智能体生成测试。面向端点的测试旨在最大化代码覆盖率与数据库交互覆盖率。基于场景的测试则通过从代码中抽取应用用例，并经由智能体循环的规划、执行与反思阶段将其细化为可执行测试来合成。我们在八个 Java 应用（包括一个专有企业应用）上评估了 SAINT。结果表明 SAINT 在覆盖率、故障检测与场景生成方面均具有良好效果。此外，一项开发者调查对 SAINT 生成的场景测试给予了高度认可。总体而言，我们的工作表明，将静态分析与智能体式 LLM 工作流相结合，能够实现更有效、更具功能性且更贴合开发者期望的服务级测试生成。","tl":"用端点模型加操作依赖图驱动智能体生成场景级服务测试。","au":["Rangeet Pan","Raju Pavuluri","Ruikai Huang","Tyler Stennett","Rahul Krishna","Alessandro Orso","Saurabh Sinha"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["service-level testing","integration test generation","operation dependency graph","LLM agents","static analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/143/x"},{"id":"p00630","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Prompts Go Wrong: Evaluating Code Model Robustness to Ambiguous, Contradictory, and Incomplete Task Descriptions","tz":"当提示出错时：评估代码模型对含歧义、矛盾与不完整任务描述的鲁棒性","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated impressive performance in code generation tasks under idealized conditions, where task descriptions are clear and precise. However, in practice task descriptions frequently exhibit ambiguity, incompleteness, or internal contradictions. In this paper, we present the first empirical study examining the robustness of state of the art code generation models when faced with such unclear task descriptions. We extend the HumanEval and MBPP benchmarks by systematically introducing realistic task descriptions flaws through guided mutation strategies, producing a dataset that mirrors the messiness of informal developer instructions. We evaluate multiple LLMs of varying sizes and architectures, analyzing their functional correctness and failure modes across task descriptions categories. Our findings reveal that even minor imperfections in task description phrasing can cause significant performance degradation, with contradictory task descriptions resulting in numerous logical errors. Moreover, while larger models tend to be more resilient than smaller variants, they are not immune to the challenges posed by unclear requirements. We further analyze semantic error patterns and identify correlations between description clarity, model behavior, and error types. Our results underscore the critical need for developing LLMs that are not only powerful but also robust to the imperfections inherent in natural user tasks, highlighting important considerations for improving model training strategies, designing more realistic evaluation benchmarks, and ensuring reliable deployment in practical software development environments.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在理想条件下（任务描述清晰精确）的代码生成任务中展现了令人印象深刻的性能。然而在实践中，任务描述经常表现出歧义、不完整或自相矛盾。在本文中，我们首次开展实证研究，考察当面对这类不清晰的任务描述时，最先进代码生成模型的鲁棒性。我们扩展了 HumanEval 与 MBPP 基准，通过有引导的变异策略系统性地引入真实的任务描述缺陷，构建出一个能够反映非正式开发者指令之混乱程度的数据集。我们评估了多种规模与架构的 LLM，分析其在各类任务描述类别下的功能正确性与失败模式。我们的发现揭示：即使是任务描述措辞中的微小瑕疵也会导致显著的性能下降，其中自相矛盾的任务描述会造成大量逻辑错误。此外，虽然更大的模型往往比小模型更具韧性，但它们同样无法免疫于不清晰需求带来的挑战。我们进一步分析了语义错误模式，并识别出描述清晰度、模型行为与错误类型之间的相关性。我们的结果强调：亟需开发不仅强大、而且对自然用户任务中固有瑕疵具备鲁棒性的 LLM，并为改进模型训练策略、设计更贴近现实的评测基准以及确保在实际软件开发环境中可靠部署提供了重要参考。","tl":"用引导变异造出含缺陷任务描述，量化代码模型的需求鲁棒性。","au":["Maya LARBI","Amal Akli","Mike Papadakis","Rihab BOUYOUSFI","Maxime Cordy","Federica Sarro","Yves Le Traon"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["ambiguous task description","robustness","code generation","HumanEval / MBPP mutation","failure modes"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/144/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.20439"},{"id":"p00631","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TraceCoder: A Trace-Driven Multi-Agent Framework for Automated Debugging of LLM-Generated Code","tz":"TraceCoder：面向 LLM 生成代码自动调试的轨迹驱动多智能体框架","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) often generate code with subtle yet critical bugs, particularly for complex tasks. Existing automated methods for repairing LLM-generated code are limited by their reliance on superficial outcomes, such as simple pass/fail results. This {black-box} approach offers little insight into the program’s internal dynamics, hindering precise error localization. Furthermore, the absence of a mechanism to learn from past failures leads to inefficient repair cycles that often repeat the same mistakes. To address these limitations, we introduce TraceCoder, a collaborative multi-agent framework that mimics the observe-analyze-repair process of human experts. The framework first instruments the code with diagnostic print statements to capture fine-grained runtime traces, providing deep visibility into its internal execution. It then conducts causal analysis on these traces to accurately identify the root cause of the error. This process is further enhanced by a novel Historical Lesson Learning Mechanism, which distills insights from prior failed repair attempts to inform subsequent correction strategies and prevent recurrence of similar mistakes. To ensure stable convergence, a Rollback Mechanism enforces that each repair iteration constitutes a strict improvement toward the correct solution. Comprehensive empirical evaluations demonstrate that TraceCoder achieves up to a 34.43% relative improvement in Pass@1 accuracy over state-of-the-art baselines. Ablation studies verify the significance of each system component, with the iterative repair process alone contributing a 65.61% relative gain in accuracy. Furthermore, TraceCoder significantly outperforms leading iterative methods in terms of both accuracy and cost-efficiency.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）生成的代码常常包含细微却关键的缺陷，在复杂任务上尤其如此。现有的修复 LLM 生成代码的自动化方法受限于其对表层结果（如简单的通过/失败结果）的依赖。这种“黑盒”方式几乎无法洞察程序的内部动态，妨碍了精确的错误定位。此外，缺乏从以往失败中学习的机制，导致修复循环低效并反复犯同样的错误。为克服这些局限，我们提出了 TraceCoder，一个模仿人类专家“观察—分析—修复”过程的协作式多智能体框架。该框架首先在代码中插桩诊断性打印语句，以捕获细粒度的运行时轨迹，从而深入观察其内部执行。随后，它对这些轨迹进行因果分析，准确定位错误的根本原因。这一过程由一种新颖的历史教训学习机制（Historical Lesson Learning Mechanism）进一步增强，该机制从此前失败的修复尝试中提炼洞见，以指导后续的纠正策略并防止类似错误重现。为确保稳定收敛，一个回滚机制强制每次修复迭代都必须是朝正确解的严格改进。全面的实证评估表明，TraceCoder 相比最先进基线在 Pass@1 准确率上取得了最高 34.43% 的相对提升。消融实验验证了各系统组件的重要性，其中仅迭代修复过程就贡献了 65.61% 的相对准确率增益。此外，TraceCoder 在准确率与成本效率两方面都显著优于主流的迭代式方法。","tl":"插桩取运行轨迹做因果分析，并用历史失败教训指导后续修复。","au":["Jiangping Huang","Wenguang Ye","Weisong Sun","Jian Zhang","Mingyue Zhang","Yang Liu"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["automated debugging","runtime trace","multi-agent repair","historical lesson learning","Pass@1"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/145/x"},{"id":"p00632","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"What’s in a Software Engineering Job Posting?","tz":"软件工程招聘启事里究竟写了什么？","a":"A well-rounded software engineer is often defined by technical prowess and the ability to deliver on complex projects. However, the narrative around the ideal Software Engineering (SE) candidate is evolving, suggesting that there is more to the story. This article explores the non-technical aspects emphasized in SE job postings, revealing the sociotechnical and organizational expectations of employers. Our Thematic Analysis of 100 job postings shows that employers seek candidates who align with their sense of purpose, fit within company culture, pursue personal and career growth, and excel in interpersonal interactions. This study contributes to ongoing discussions in the SE community about the evolving role and workplace context of software engineers beyond technical skills. By highlighting these expectations, we provide relevant insights for researchers, educators, practitioners, and recruiters. Additionally, our analysis offers a valuable snapshot of SE job postings in 2023, providing a scientific record of prevailing trends and expectations.","az":"一名全面的软件工程师常被定义为具备技术实力并能够交付复杂项目的人。然而，围绕理想软件工程（SE）候选人的叙事正在演变，暗示故事远不止于此。本文探讨了 SE 招聘启事中所强调的非技术性方面，揭示了雇主的社会技术与组织层面的期望。我们对 100 份招聘启事所做的主题分析表明，雇主寻找的是那些认同其使命感、契合公司文化、追求个人与职业成长并在人际互动中表现出色的候选人。本研究为 SE 社区中关于软件工程师角色演变及其工作场所情境（超越技术技能）的持续讨论做出了贡献。通过凸显这些期望，我们为研究者、教育者、从业者与招聘方提供了相关洞见。此外，我们的分析提供了 2023 年 SE 招聘启事的宝贵快照，为当时的主流趋势与期望留下了科学记录。","tl":"主题分析 100 份招聘启事，揭示雇主重视的非技术期望。","au":["Marvin Wyrich","Lloyd Montgomery"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["empirical-study"],"kw":["job postings","thematic analysis","non-technical skills","sociotechnical expectations","SE job market"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/146/x","pu":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.13656"},{"id":"p00633","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LSPRAG: LSP-Guided RAG for Language-Agnostic Real-Time Unit Test Generation","tz":"LSPRAG：面向语言无关实时单元测试生成的 LSP 引导式 RAG","a":"Automated unit test generation is essential for robust software development, yet existing approaches struggle to generalize across multiple programming languages and operate within real-time development. While Large Language Models (LLMs) offer a promising solution, their ability to generate high coverage test code depends on prompting a concise context of the focal method. Current solutions, such as Retrieval-Augmented Generation, either rely on imprecise similarity-based searches or demand the creation of costly, language-specific static analysis pipelines. To address this gap, we present LSPRAG, a framework for concise-context retrieval tailored for real-time, language-agnostic unit test generation. LSPRAG leverages off-the-shelf Language Server Protocol (LSP) back-ends to supply LLMs with precise symbol definitions and references in real time. By reusing mature LSP servers, LSPRAG provides an LLM with language-aware context retrieval, requiring minimal per-language engineering effort. We evaluated LSPRAG on open-source projects spanning Java, Go, and Python. Compared to the best performance of baselines, LspRag increased line coverage by up to 174.55% for Golang, 213.31% for Java, and 31.57% for Python.","az":"自动化单元测试生成对稳健的软件开发至关重要，但现有方法难以跨多种编程语言泛化，也难以在实时开发过程中运行。虽然大语言模型（LLM）提供了一条有前景的路径，但其生成高覆盖率测试代码的能力取决于是否能在提示中提供目标方法的简洁上下文。现有方案，例如检索增强生成（RAG），要么依赖不够精确的基于相似度的搜索，要么要求构建代价高昂且与语言绑定的静态分析流水线。为填补这一空白，我们提出 LSPRAG，一个为实时、语言无关的单元测试生成量身定制的简洁上下文检索框架。LSPRAG 利用现成的语言服务器协议（LSP）后端，实时向 LLM 提供精确的符号定义与引用。通过复用成熟的 LSP 服务器，LSPRAG 以极少的单语言工程投入为 LLM 提供了语言感知的上下文检索。我们在涵盖 Java、Go 和 Python 的开源项目上评估了 LSPRAG。与基线的最佳性能相比，LspRag 在 Golang 上将行覆盖率最高提升了 174.55%，在 Java 上提升了 213.31%，在 Python 上提升了 31.57%。","tl":"复用 LSP 服务器提供精确符号上下文，实现语言无关测试生成。","au":["Gwihwan Go","Quan Zhang","Chijin Zhou","Zhao Wei","Yu Jiang"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unit test generation","Language Server Protocol","retrieval-augmented generation","language-agnostic","line coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/147/x"},{"id":"p00634","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DNN Modularization via Activation-Driven Training","tz":"通过激活驱动训练实现 DNN 模块化","a":"Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) tend to accrue technical debt and suffer from significant retraining costs when adapting to evolving requirements. Modularizing DNNs offers the promise of improving their reusability. Previous work has proposed techniques to decompose DNN models into modules both during and after training. However, these strategies yield several shortcomings, including significant weight overlaps and accuracy losses across modules, restricted focus on convolutional layers only, and added complexity and training time by introducing auxiliary masks to control modularity. In this work, we propose MODA, an activation-driven modular training approach. MODA promotes inherent modularity within a DNN model by directly regulating the activation outputs of its layers based on three modular objectives: intra-class affinity, inter-class dispersion, and compactness. MODA is evaluated using three well-known DNN models and five datasets with varying sizes. This evaluation indicates that, compared to the existing state-of-the-art, using MODA yields several advantages: (1) MODA accomplishes modularization with 22% less training time; (2) the resultant modules generated by MODA comprise up to 24x fewer weights and 37x less weight overlap while (3) preserving the original model’s accuracy without additional fine-tuning; in module replacement scenarios, (4) MODA improves the accuracy of a target class by 12% on average while ensuring minimal impact on the accuracy of other classes.","az":"深度神经网络（DNN）在适应不断演化的需求时，往往会积累技术债并承受高昂的重训练成本。将 DNN 模块化有望改善其可复用性。已有工作提出了在训练期间以及训练之后分解 DNN 模型的技术。然而这些策略存在若干不足，包括模块间显著的权重重叠与准确率损失、仅局限于卷积层，以及因引入辅助掩码来控制模块化而带来的额外复杂度与训练时间。在本工作中，我们提出 MODA，一种激活驱动的模块化训练方法。MODA 通过依据三个模块化目标——类内亲和性、类间离散性与紧致性——直接调控各层的激活输出，从而促进 DNN 模型内部固有的模块化。我们使用三个知名 DNN 模型与五个规模不一的数据集对 MODA 进行评估。评估表明，与现有最先进方法相比，MODA 具有多项优势：(1) MODA 以少 22% 的训练时间完成模块化；(2) MODA 生成的模块权重数量最多减少 24 倍、权重重叠最多减少 37 倍；同时 (3) 在无需额外微调的情况下保持原模型的准确率；在模块替换场景中，(4) MODA 使目标类别的准确率平均提升 12%，同时对其他类别准确率的影响极小。","tl":"直接调控层激活即可获得内生模块化，无需辅助掩码。","au":["Tuan Ngo","Abid Hassan","Saad Shafiq","Nenad Medvidović"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DNN modularization","activation-driven training","module reuse","weight overlap","module replacement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/148/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.01074"},{"id":"p00635","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SecureReviewer: Enhancing Large Language Models for Secure Code Review through Secure-Aware Fine-Tuning","tz":"SecureReviewer：通过安全感知微调增强大语言模型的安全代码评审能力","a":"Identifying and addressing security issues during the early phase of the development lifecycle is critical for mitigating the long-term negative impacts on software systems. Code review serves as an effective practice that enables developers to check their teammates’ code before integration into the codebase. To streamline the generation of review comments, various automated code review approaches have been proposed, where Large Language Model (LLM)-based methods have significantly advanced the capabilities of automated review generation. However, existing models primarily focus on general-purpose code review, their effectiveness in identifying and addressing security-related issues remains underexplored. Moreover, adapting existing code review approaches to target security issues faces substantial challenges, including data scarcity and inadequate evaluation metrics. To address these limitations, we propose SecureReviewer, a novel approach designed for enhancing LLMs’ ability to identify and resolve security-related issues during code review. Specifically, we first construct a dataset tailored for training and evaluating secure code review capabilities. Leveraging this dataset, we fine-tune LLMs to generate code review comments that can effectively identify security issues and provide fix suggestions with our proposed secure-aware fine-tuning strategy. To mitigate hallucination in LLMs and enhance the reliability of their outputs, we integrate the Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) technique, which grounds the generated comments in domain-specific security knowledge. Additionally, we introduce SecureBLEU, a new evaluation metric designed to assess the effectiveness of review comments in addressing security issues. Experimental results demonstrate that SecureReviewer outperforms state-of-the-art baselines in both security issue detection accuracy and the overall quality and practical utility of generated review comments.","az":"在开发生命周期的早期识别并处理安全问题，对于减轻其对软件系统的长期负面影响至关重要。代码评审是一种有效实践，使开发者能够在代码合入代码库之前检查队友的代码。为简化评审意见的生成，已有多种自动化代码评审方法被提出，其中基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法显著推进了自动评审生成的能力。然而，现有模型主要聚焦于通用代码评审，它们在识别与处理安全相关问题上的有效性仍未被充分研究。此外，将现有代码评审方法适配到安全问题上面临巨大挑战，包括数据稀缺与评估指标不足。为解决这些局限，我们提出 SecureReviewer，一种旨在增强 LLM 在代码评审中识别并解决安全相关问题能力的新方法。具体而言，我们首先构建了一个为训练与评估安全代码评审能力而定制的数据集。基于该数据集，我们采用所提出的安全感知微调策略对 LLM 进行微调，使其生成能够有效识别安全问题并给出修复建议的评审意见。为缓解 LLM 的幻觉并提升其输出的可靠性，我们集成了检索增强生成（RAG）技术，将生成的意见锚定在领域特定的安全知识之上。此外，我们引入了 SecureBLEU，一种用于评估评审意见在解决安全问题方面有效性的新指标。实验结果表明，SecureReviewer 在安全问题检测准确率以及所生成评审意见的整体质量与实用价值上，均优于最先进的基线方法。","tl":"安全感知微调加 RAG 生成安全评审意见，并提出 SecureBLEU 指标。","au":["Fang Liu","Simiao Liu","Yinghao Zhu","Xiaoli Lian","Li Zhang"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","security","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["secure code review","review comment generation","secure-aware fine-tuning","RAG","SecureBLEU"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/149/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.26457"},{"id":"p00636","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"What Makes Code Generation Ethically Sourced?","tz":"是什么让代码生成具备合乎伦理的来源？","a":"Several code generation models have been proposed to help reduce time and effort in solving software-related tasks. To ensure responsible AI, there are growing interests over various ethical issues (e.g., unclear licensing, privacy, fairness, and environment impact). These studies have the overarching goal of ensuring ethically sourced generation, which has gained growing attentions in speech synthesis and image generation. In this paper, we introduce the novel notion of Ethically Sourced Code Generation (ES-CodeGen) to refer to managing all processes involved in code generation model development from data collection to post-deployment via ethical and sustainable practices. To build a taxonomy of ES-CodeGen, we perform a two-phase literature review where we read 803 papers across various domains and specific to AI-based code generation. We identified 71 relevant papers with 10 initial dimensions of ES-CodeGen. To refine our dimensions and gain insights on consequences of ES-CodeGen, we surveyed 32 practitioners, which include six developers who submitted GitHub issues to opt-out from the Stack dataset (these impacted users have real-world experience of ethically sourcing issues in code generation models). The results lead to 11 dimensions of ES-CodeGen with a new dimension on code quality as practitioners have noted its importance. We also identified consequences, artifacts, and stages relevant to ES-CodeGen. Our post-survey reflection showed that most practitioners tend to ignore social-related dimensions despite their importance. Most practitioners either agreed or strongly agreed that our survey help improve their understanding of ES-CodeGen. Our study calls for attentions of various ethical issues towards ES-CodeGen.","az":"已有多个代码生成模型被提出，用以减少解决软件相关任务所需的时间与精力。为确保负责任的 AI，人们越来越关注各类伦理问题（例如不明确的许可、隐私、公平性与环境影响）。这些研究的总体目标是确保“合乎伦理来源的生成”，这一议题在语音合成与图像生成领域已获得越来越多关注。本文引入了“合乎伦理来源的代码生成”（Ethically Sourced Code Generation, ES-CodeGen）这一新概念，指的是以合乎伦理且可持续的实践来管理代码生成模型开发中从数据收集到部署后的全部流程。为构建 ES-CodeGen 的分类体系，我们开展了两阶段文献综述，阅读了跨多个领域以及专门针对基于 AI 的代码生成的 803 篇论文。我们识别出 71 篇相关论文，并归纳出 ES-CodeGen 的 10 个初始维度。为细化这些维度并了解 ES-CodeGen 带来的后果，我们调查了 32 名从业者，其中包括六名曾向 GitHub 提交 issue 以退出 The Stack 数据集的开发者（这些受影响用户对代码生成模型中的伦理来源问题有真实经历）。调查结果最终形成了 ES-CodeGen 的 11 个维度，并新增了“代码质量”这一维度，因为从业者指出了它的重要性。我们还识别出与 ES-CodeGen 相关的后果、制品与阶段。我们的调查后反思显示，尽管社会相关维度很重要，大多数从业者却倾向于忽视它们。多数从业者同意或强烈同意我们的调查有助于提升他们对 ES-CodeGen 的理解。我们的研究呼吁各界关注 ES-CodeGen 所涉及的各类伦理问题。","tl":"提出 ES-CodeGen 概念与 11 维分类，并用从业者调查验证。","au":["Zhuolin Xu","Chenglin Li","Qiushi Li","Shin Hwei Tan"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["human-study","position-vision"],"kw":["ethically sourced code generation","taxonomy","practitioner survey","licensing and privacy","responsible AI"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/150/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00637","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automated Network-Level Fault Injection Testing of Microservice Architectures","tz":"微服务架构的自动化网络级故障注入测试","a":"Microservice architectures are inherently vulnerable to partial failures, and they rely on resilience patterns to tolerate them. However, it is challenging to design and implement the resilience logic. Unforeseen interactions with faulty services can lead to errors in dependent services, resulting in incorrect system behavior. Fault injection testing techniques aim to uncover these errors by examining the system’s behavior in response to different fault combinations. However, existing automated techniques primarily focus on service-level fault injection, which limits their broader applicability. We present an automated fault-injection testing method that operates at the network level, enabling broad applicability. The method models the system’s resilience behaviors dynamically through the observed test executions and uses this information to reduce the set of fault combinations to explore. We implemented our method in a prototype tool, called Reynard. Our evaluation demonstrates that Reynard efficiently explores system executions by significantly reducing the number of fault combinations to test. It incurs minimal overhead and can be easily integrated into existing benchmarks. Furthermore, we applied Reynard to test an industrial system, showcasing its applicability and effectiveness in a real-world context. Moreover, we uncovered a previously unknown resilience bug.","az":"微服务架构天然容易出现部分失效，并依赖韧性模式来容忍这些失效。然而，设计并实现韧性逻辑颇具挑战。与故障服务之间未被预见的交互可能在依赖服务中引发错误，导致系统行为不正确。故障注入测试技术旨在通过考察系统对不同故障组合的响应行为来揭示这些错误。但现有的自动化技术主要聚焦于服务级的故障注入，限制了其更广泛的适用性。我们提出了一种在网络层面运行的自动化故障注入测试方法，从而具备广泛的适用性。该方法通过观察到的测试执行动态地建模系统的韧性行为，并利用这些信息来缩减需要探索的故障组合集合。我们在一个名为 Reynard 的原型工具中实现了该方法。我们的评估表明，Reynard 通过显著减少需要测试的故障组合数量，高效地探索了系统执行。它带来的开销极小，并可轻松集成到现有基准之中。此外，我们将 Reynard 应用于测试一个工业系统，展示了其在真实场景中的适用性与有效性。而且，我们还发现了一个此前未知的韧性缺陷。","tl":"在网络层注入故障并动态建模韧性行为以裁剪故障组合空间。","au":["Delano Flipse","Hakan Simsek","Jérémie Decouchant","Burcu Kulahcioglu Ozkan"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["fault injection testing","microservices","resilience patterns","network-level faults","combination reduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/151/x","pu":"https://burcuku.github.io/home/assets/pdf/icse26.pdf"},{"id":"p00638","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Closing the Chain: How to reduce your risk of being SolarWinds, Log4j, or XZ Utils","tz":"闭合链条：如何降低成为 SolarWinds、Log4j 或 XZ Utils 的风险","a":"Software supply chain frameworks, such as the US NIST Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF), detail what tasks software development organizations are recommended or mandated to adopt to reduce security risk. However, to further reduce the risk of similar attacks occurring, software organizations benefit from knowing what tasks mitigate attack techniques the attackers are currently using to address specific threats, prioritize tasks, and close mitigation gaps. The goal of this study is to aid software organizations in reducing the risk of software supply chain attacks by systematically synthesizing how framework tasks mitigate the attack techniques used in the SolarWinds, Log4j, and XZ Utils attacks. We qualitatively analyzed 106 Cyber Threat Intelligence (CTI) reports of the 3 attacks to gather the attack techniques. We then systematically constructed a mapping between attack techniques and the 73 tasks enumerated in 10 software supply chain frameworks. Afterward, we established and ranked priority tasks that mitigate attack techniques. The three mitigation tasks with the highest scores are role-based access control, system monitoring, and boundary protection. Additionally, three mitigation tasks were missing from all ten frameworks, including sustainable open-source software and environmental scanning tools. Thus, software products would still be vulnerable to software supply chain attacks even if organizations adopted all recommended tasks.","az":"软件供应链框架，例如美国 NIST 的安全软件开发框架（SSDF），详细规定了软件开发组织被推荐或被强制采纳以降低安全风险的任务。然而，为进一步降低类似攻击再次发生的风险，软件组织需要知道哪些任务能够缓解攻击者当前正在使用的攻击技术，从而应对特定威胁、对任务排定优先级并弥补缓解措施的缺口。本研究的目标是通过系统性地综合分析框架任务如何缓解 SolarWinds、Log4j 与 XZ Utils 攻击中所使用的攻击技术，帮助软件组织降低软件供应链攻击的风险。我们对这三起攻击的 106 份网络威胁情报（CTI）报告进行了定性分析，以收集其中的攻击技术。随后，我们系统地构建了攻击技术与 10 个软件供应链框架中列举的 73 项任务之间的映射。之后，我们确立并排序了能够缓解攻击技术的优先任务。得分最高的三项缓解任务是基于角色的访问控制、系统监控与边界防护。此外，有三项缓解任务在全部十个框架中都缺失，包括可持续的开源软件与环境扫描工具。因此，即便组织采纳了所有被推荐的任务，软件产品仍然可能遭受软件供应链攻击。","tl":"把三起著名供应链攻击技术映射到 73 项框架任务并排出优先级。","au":["Sivana Hamer","Jacob Bowen","Md Nazmul Haque","Robert Hines","Chris Madden","Laurie Williams"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["software supply chain","SSDF","attack techniques","cyber threat intelligence","mitigation mapping"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/152/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.12192"},{"id":"p00639","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CoBrA: Context-, Branch-sensitive Static Analysis for Detecting Taint-style Vulnerabilities in PHP Web Applications","tz":"CoBrA：面向 PHP Web 应用污点式漏洞检测的上下文与分支敏感静态分析","a":"PHP, a widely-used programming language in Web development, contains powerful dynamic features (e.g., dynamic function name construction), making static detection of taint-style vulnerabilities like SQL injection and Cross-Site Scripting challenging. State-of-the-art static approaches perform call graph-guided backward dataflow tracking, thus failing to analyze those dynamic PHP features like variable functions and control change statements, which results in high false positives and negatives. In this paper, we design and implement CoBrA, a context-, branch-sensitive approach to detect taint-style vulnerabilities in PHP-based Web applications. The key innovations are the abstract domain graph (ADG), which is used to efficiently guide the analysis and “stretch-relax” algorithm, which enables accurate resolution of PHP dynamic features and efficient inter-procedural taint propagation. Our evaluation of CoBrA’s prototype identified 54 zero-day vulnerabilities in 19 real-world applications with eight Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) identifiers assigned, achieved $88.66%$ detection rate with under $0.3%$ false positives on a PHP tarpits dataset, and outperformed four state-of-the-art tools across all test datasets with reasonable time and space consumption.","az":"PHP 是 Web 开发中广泛使用的编程语言，包含强大的动态特性（例如动态函数名构造），这使得对 SQL 注入和跨站脚本等污点式漏洞进行静态检测颇具挑战。最先进的静态方法执行调用图引导的后向数据流追踪，因而无法分析诸如变量函数与控制变更语句之类的 PHP 动态特性，导致高误报与高漏报。本文设计并实现了 CoBrA，一种上下文敏感、分支敏感的方法，用于检测基于 PHP 的 Web 应用中的污点式漏洞。其关键创新在于抽象域图（ADG），用于高效引导分析；以及“拉伸—松弛”（stretch-relax）算法，可实现对 PHP 动态特性的精确解析与高效的过程间污点传播。我们对 CoBrA 原型的评估在 19 个真实应用中发现了 54 个零日漏洞，并获分配了八个通用漏洞披露（CVE）编号；在 PHP tarpits 数据集上达到了 88.66% 的检测率、误报率低于 0.3%；并在所有测试数据集上以合理的时间与空间开销超越了四个最先进工具。","tl":"抽象域图加 stretch-relax 算法精确解析 PHP 动态特性做污点分析。","au":["Yichao Xu","Mingqing Kang","Neil Thimmaiah","Rigel Gjomemo","V. N. Venkatakrishnan","Yinzhi Cao"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["taint-style vulnerabilities","PHP web applications","context- and branch-sensitive analysis","abstract domain graph","zero-day detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/153/x"},{"id":"p00640","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Perspective-Taking in Software Engineering: A Study on its Relationship to Team Performance","tz":"软件工程中的换位思考：其与团队绩效关系的研究","a":"As software engineering (SE) becomes increasingly collaborative and cross-functional, teams must navigate differences in expertise, role priorities, and communication styles. While team diversity is often associated with greater innovation and creativity, it can also lead to misalignment, conflict, and diminished performance. Perspective-taking (PT), the cognitive process of understanding others’ viewpoints, has been studied in other fields as a way to convert diversity into improved team performance outcomes, yet its role in SE remains underexplored. In this work, we address this gap through an empirical study examining how PT operates in SE teams, and how it relates to team performance. We conducted semi-structured interviews with 33 software professionals across a range of roles and organizations, and used thematic analysis to identify common patterns in how participants described PT’s influence on performance outcomes such as team output, team morale, and software quality. Our findings suggest that perspective-taking fosters more motivation and inclusion, and more productive task-based conflict, all of which shape how teams reason, deliberate, and deliver. Given that PT can be difficult in practice, we also identify several factors that help overcome barriers to PT, such as psychological safety and open communication. By improving our understanding of how PT contributes to team performance in SE, and how it can be supported, this work advances efforts to create software that better serves diverse users and a more inclusive SE industry.","az":"随着软件工程（SE）日益走向协作化与跨职能化，团队必须应对专业背景、角色优先级与沟通风格上的差异。虽然团队多样性常与更强的创新与创造力相关联，但它也可能导致目标错位、冲突与绩效下降。换位思考（perspective-taking, PT），即理解他人观点的认知过程，在其他领域已被研究为将多样性转化为更好团队绩效的途径，但其在 SE 中的作用仍未被充分探索。在本工作中，我们通过一项实证研究填补这一空白，考察 PT 在 SE 团队中如何运作，以及它与团队绩效之间的关系。我们对来自不同角色与组织的 33 名软件专业人士进行了半结构化访谈，并使用主题分析识别参与者描述 PT 如何影响团队产出、团队士气与软件质量等绩效结果的共同模式。我们的发现表明，换位思考能够激发更强的动机与包容感，并带来更具建设性的任务型冲突，而这些都会塑造团队的推理、审议与交付方式。鉴于 PT 在实践中往往不易实现，我们还识别出若干有助于克服 PT 障碍的因素，例如心理安全感与开放沟通。通过增进对 PT 如何促进 SE 团队绩效以及如何加以支持的理解，本工作推动了打造更好服务多样用户的软件以及更具包容性的 SE 行业的努力。","tl":"33 次访谈揭示换位思考经由动机与建设性冲突提升团队绩效。","au":["Kezia Devathasan","Jayani Samaraweera","Dana Damian"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","empirical-study"],"kw":["perspective-taking","team performance","semi-structured interviews","thematic analysis","psychological safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/154/x"},{"id":"p00641","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SEER: Enhancing Chain-of-Thought Code Generation through Self-Exploring Deep Reasoning","tz":"SEER：通过自我探索式深度推理增强思维链代码生成","a":"Code generation, the task of creating executable programs from natural language requirements, has recently seen tremendous advances through Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning, which enables Large Language Models (LLMs) to develop high-level reasoning plans before writing code. Recent research has proposed various methods to enhance models’ CoT reasoning for code generation such as prompt engineering and supervised fine-tuning. However, existing approaches still face three critical limitations: (1) limited exploration of diverse reasoning paths, which constrains generalization across various programming scenarios, (2) lack of quality assessment for intermediate reasoning steps, which hampers the reliability of the generated plans and code, and (3) the potential negative impact of “overthinking”, potentially leading to unnecessarily complex and incorrect solutions. To address these limitations, we frame CoT code generation as a decision making problem and present SEER, a SElf-Exploring deep Reasoning framework that enables accurate and adaptive reasoning for code generation. SEER introduces three key components: (1) Diverse reasoning path exploration, which aims at exploring diverse reasoning paths and annotating intermediate steps without relying on manual experts or closed-source proprietary models; (2) Reasoning quality-aware model training, which trains a policy model for generating candidate reasoning steps and a value model for assessing their quality; and (3) Adaptive CoT reasoning, which dynamically switches between direct generation and step-by-step reasoning for different problems. Experiments on state-of-the-art code LLMs DeepSeek-Coder and Qwen2.5-Coder demonstrate that SEER achieves remarkable performance gains across three popular code generation benchmarks, consistently outperforming all baseline methods and achieving absolute improvements by 4.2% ∼ 9.3% in MBPP, 1.9% ∼ 9.1% in HumanEval and 3.5% ∼ 5.3% in LiveCodeBench, respectively.","az":"代码生成，即从自然语言需求创建可执行程序的任务，近期借助思维链（CoT）推理取得了巨大进展——CoT 使大语言模型（LLM）能够在写代码之前先制定高层推理计划。近期研究提出了多种增强模型 CoT 推理以用于代码生成的方法，例如提示工程与有监督微调。然而，现有方法仍面临三大关键局限：(1) 对多样推理路径的探索有限，制约了在各种编程场景中的泛化能力；(2) 缺乏对中间推理步骤的质量评估，损害了所生成计划与代码的可靠性；(3) “过度思考”可能带来负面影响，进而导致不必要复杂且错误的解法。为解决这些局限，我们将 CoT 代码生成建模为一个决策问题，并提出 SEER，一个自我探索式深度推理（SElf-Exploring deep Reasoning）框架，可实现面向代码生成的精确且自适应的推理。SEER 引入三个关键组件：(1) 多样推理路径探索，旨在探索多样的推理路径并标注中间步骤，而不依赖人工专家或闭源专有模型；(2) 推理质量感知的模型训练，训练一个策略模型用于生成候选推理步骤，以及一个价值模型用于评估其质量；(3) 自适应 CoT 推理，针对不同问题在直接生成与逐步推理之间动态切换。在最先进代码 LLM DeepSeek-Coder 与 Qwen2.5-Coder 上的实验表明，SEER 在三个流行代码生成基准上取得了显著性能提升，持续优于所有基线方法，在 MBPP 上取得 4.2%~9.3%、在 HumanEval 上取得 1.9%~9.1%、在 LiveCodeBench 上取得 3.5%~5.3% 的绝对提升。","tl":"自探索标注推理步骤训练策略与价值模型，并自适应决定是否深推。","au":["Shuzheng Gao","Chaozheng Wang","Cuiyun Gao","Michael Lyu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["chain-of-thought code generation","reasoning path exploration","value model","adaptive reasoning","overthinking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/155/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/155/SEER-Enhancing-Chain-of-Thought-Code-Generation-through-Self-Exploring-Deep-Reasonin"},{"id":"p00642","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"One Signature, Multiple Payments: Demystifying and Detecting Signature Replay Vulnerabilities in Smart Contracts","tz":"一次签名，多次支付：揭示并检测智能合约中的签名重放漏洞","a":"Smart contracts have significantly advanced blockchain technology, and digital signatures are crucial for reliable verification of contract authority. Through signature verification, smart contracts can ensure that signers possess the required permissions, thus enhancing security and scalability. However, lacking checks on signature usage conditions can lead to repeated verifications, increasing the risk of permission abuse and threatening contract assets. We define this issue as the Signature Replay Vulnerability (SRV). In this paper, we conducted the first empirical study to investigate the causes and characteristics of the SRVs. From 1,419 audit reports across 37 blockchain security companies, we identified 108 with detailed SRV descriptions and classified five types of SRVs. To detect these vulnerabilities automatically, we designed LASiR, which utilizes the general semantic understanding ability of Large Language Models (LLMs) to assist in the static taint analysis of the signature state and identify the signature reuse behavior. It also employs path reachability verification via symbolic execution to ensure effective and reliable detection. To evaluate the performance of LASiR, we conducted large-scale experiments on 15,383 contracts involving signature verification, selected from the initial dataset of 918,964 contracts across four blockchains: Ethereum, Binance Smart Chain, Polygon, and Arbitrum. The results indicate that SRVs are widespread, with affected contracts holding 4.76 million in active assets. Among these, 19.63% of contracts that use signatures on Ethereum contain SRVs. Furthermore, manual verification demonstrates that LASiR achieves an F1-score of 87.90% for detection. Ablation studies and comparative experiments reveal that the semantic information provided by LLMs aids static taint analysis, significantly enhancing LASiR’s detection performance.","az":"智能合约极大推动了区块链技术的发展，而数字签名对于可靠地验证合约权限至关重要。通过签名验证，智能合约可以确保签名者拥有所需权限，从而增强安全性与可扩展性。然而，若缺少对签名使用条件的检查，就可能导致重复验证，增加权限滥用的风险并威胁合约资产。我们将这一问题定义为签名重放漏洞（Signature Replay Vulnerability, SRV）。本文首次开展实证研究，探究 SRV 的成因与特征。我们从 37 家区块链安全公司的 1,419 份审计报告中，识别出 108 份包含详细 SRV 描述的报告，并将 SRV 分为五类。为自动检测这些漏洞，我们设计了 LASiR，它利用大语言模型（LLM）的通用语义理解能力来辅助对签名状态的静态污点分析，识别签名重用行为；同时通过符号执行进行路径可达性验证，以确保检测的有效与可靠。为评估 LASiR 的性能，我们在 15,383 份涉及签名验证的合约上开展了大规模实验，这些合约是从 Ethereum、Binance Smart Chain、Polygon 与 Arbitrum 四条链上初始的 918,964 份合约中筛选得到的。结果表明 SRV 相当普遍，受影响合约持有 476 万美元的活跃资产；其中，Ethereum 上使用签名的合约有 19.63% 含有 SRV。此外，人工验证表明 LASiR 的检测 F1 值达到 87.90%。消融实验与对比实验揭示，LLM 提供的语义信息有助于静态污点分析，显著提升了 LASiR 的检测性能。","tl":"首次定义签名重放漏洞并用 LLM 辅助污点分析大规模检出。","au":["Zexu Wang","Jiachi Chen","Zewei Lin","Wenqing Chen","Kaiwen Ning","Jianxing Yu","Yuming Feng","Yu Zhang","Weizhe Zhang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["signature replay vulnerability","smart contracts","static taint analysis","symbolic execution","audit report study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/156/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09134"},{"id":"p00643","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TaintP2X: Detecting Taint-Style Prompt-to-Anything Injection Vulnerabilities in LLM-Integrated Applications","tz":"TaintP2X：检测 LLM 集成应用中的污点式 Prompt-to-Anything 注入漏洞","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have revolutionized numerous domains, enabling the development of LLM-integrated applications that autonomously plan and act through tool calling. While these applications demonstrate remarkable capabilities, their ability to invoke sensitive operations, such as file system interactions, code execution, and database queries, introduces critical security risks. In particular, prompt injection vulnerabilities, combined with security-sensitive sink functions, can lead to a broad class of attacks we define as Prompt-to-Anything Injection (P2Xi). These vulnerabilities, stemming from the misuse of LLM-generated outputs without proper validation, can result in severe consequences such as Remote Command Execution (RCE), file injection, SQL injection, and Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF). To address this emerging threat, we propose TaintP2X, a novel static taint analysis framework that models LLM-generated outputs as taint sources, tracks their propagation through sensitive sink functions, and employs LLM-assisted analysis to prune false positives. TaintP2X achieves high precision and scalability, systematically identifying P2Xi vulnerabilities. In evaluations, TaintP2X demonstrated a 77.1% recall on a ground truth dataset of 35 vulnerabilities, outperforming state-of-the-art methods, and uncovered 101 taint paths across 75 GitHub repositories, with several vulnerabilities confirmed by developers. These findings highlight the prevalence and impact of P2Xi vulnerabilities and establish TaintP2X as a practical solution for securing LLM-integrated ecosystems.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已革新众多领域，催生了能够通过工具调用自主规划与行动的 LLM 集成应用。尽管这类应用展现出卓越能力，但它们调用敏感操作（如文件系统交互、代码执行与数据库查询）的能力引入了严重的安全风险。特别是，提示注入漏洞与安全敏感的汇聚点函数相结合，会导致我们所定义的一大类攻击——Prompt-to-Anything 注入（P2Xi）。这些漏洞源自未经适当校验就使用 LLM 生成的输出，可能造成远程命令执行（RCE）、文件注入、SQL 注入与服务端请求伪造（SSRF）等严重后果。为应对这一新兴威胁，我们提出 TaintP2X，一个新颖的静态污点分析框架：它将 LLM 生成的输出建模为污点源，追踪其经由敏感汇聚点函数的传播，并借助 LLM 辅助分析来剪除误报。TaintP2X 兼具高精度与可扩展性，能够系统性地识别 P2Xi 漏洞。在评估中，TaintP2X 在包含 35 个漏洞的真值数据集上取得了 77.1% 的召回率，优于最先进方法，并在 75 个 GitHub 仓库中发现了 101 条污点路径，其中若干漏洞已获开发者确认。这些发现凸显了 P2Xi 漏洞的普遍性与影响，并确立了 TaintP2X 作为保护 LLM 集成生态实用方案的地位。","tl":"把 LLM 输出当污点源做静态追踪，系统揭示 P2X 注入漏洞。","au":["HeJunjie","Shenao Wang","Yanjie Zhao","Xinyi Hou","Zhao Liu","Quanchen Zou","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["prompt injection","LLM-integrated applications","static taint analysis","sensitive sink functions","RCE / SSRF"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/157/x"},{"id":"p00644","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"NB2P: Generating Data Science Pipelines from Computational Notebooks","tz":"NB2P：从计算笔记本生成数据科学流水线","a":"Computational notebooks empower data scientists to explore data, perform analytics, and share their findings. During data exploration, the scientist uses notebooks to construct and refine data pipelines that process data in multiple stages. Extracting pipelines from a given notebook is useful in understanding the notebook’s semantics and in migrating it to production systems. However, the nature of the data exploration process, and the lack of sufficient documentation in the notebook, present two challenges in extracting the pipelines. First, notebook cells can be executed in any order, making it difficult to capture the data flow between pipeline stages. Second, data transformation operations belonging to a stage may not be cleanly separated, making it difficult to extract cohesive pipeline components. In this paper, we propose NB2P, a novel system that automatically extracts data science pipelines from notebooks. Given an input notebook, NB2P first parses it into an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST). It then performs analysis on the AST to recover the execution order, thereby addressing the first challenge above. Next, it groups the data operations into pipeline stages based on their semantics. This step is called semantic segmentation, and it addresses the second challenge using a tree-based, learned encoding-decoding algorithm that captures the data flow and fine-grained hierarchical information in the notebook. Finally, NB2P assembles the stages and constructs the final pipeline that can be deployed into production systems. We train NB2P on a large notebook corpus from Kaggle. We compare NB2P against baselines that use state-of-the-art large language models and other machine learning models for source code segmentation. The experimental results show that NB2P consistently outperforms the baselines while incurring low overhead.","az":"计算笔记本让数据科学家能够探索数据、开展分析并分享成果。在数据探索过程中，科学家使用笔记本来构建并细化分多个阶段处理数据的流水线。从给定笔记本中抽取流水线，对于理解笔记本的语义以及将其迁移到生产系统都很有用。然而，数据探索过程的本质以及笔记本中缺乏充分文档，给流水线抽取带来了两大挑战。首先，笔记本单元格可以按任意顺序执行，使得难以捕捉流水线各阶段之间的数据流。其次，属于同一阶段的数据转换操作可能并未被清晰地分隔，使得难以抽取内聚的流水线组件。本文提出 NB2P，一个能够自动从笔记本中抽取数据科学流水线的新系统。给定一个输入笔记本，NB2P 首先将其解析为抽象语法树（AST）；接着对 AST 进行分析以恢复执行顺序，从而解决上述第一个挑战；然后，它依据语义将数据操作归并为流水线阶段，这一步称为语义分割，它采用一种基于树的学习式编码—解码算法，捕捉笔记本中的数据流与细粒度层次信息，从而解决第二个挑战；最后，NB2P 将各阶段组装起来，构造出可部署到生产系统的最终流水线。我们在来自 Kaggle 的大规模笔记本语料上训练 NB2P，并将其与使用最先进大语言模型及其他机器学习模型进行源码分割的基线进行比较。实验结果表明，NB2P 在开销很低的同时持续优于这些基线。","tl":"恢复执行顺序加树式语义分割，把乱序笔记本变成可投产流水线。","au":["Haotian Gao","Quang Trung Ta","Tien Tuan Anh Dinh","Nhut Minh Ho","Zhiyong Huang","Beng Chin Ooi"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["computational notebooks","data science pipeline extraction","semantic segmentation","abstract syntax tree","production migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/158/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/158/NB2P-Generating-Data-Science-Pipelines-from-Computational-Notebooks"},{"id":"p00645","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"UniCoR: Modality Collaboration for Robust Cross-Language Hybrid Code Retrieval","tz":"UniCoR：面向鲁棒跨语言混合代码检索的模态协同","a":"Effective code retrieval is indispensable and it has become an important paradigm to search code in hybrid mode using both natural language and code snippet. Nevertheless, it remains unclear whether existing approaches can effectively leverage such hybrid queries, particularly in cross-language contexts. We conduct a comprehensive empirical study of representative code models and reveal three challenges: (1) insufficient semantic understanding; (2) inefficient fusion in hybrid code retrieval; and (3)weak generalization in cross-language scenarios. To address these challenges, we propose UniCoR, a novel self-supervised framework that learns unified code representation representations framework designed to learn unified and robust code representations. Firstly, we design a multi-perspective supervised contrastive learning module to enhance semantic understanding and modality fusion. It aligns representations from multiple perspectives, including code-to-code, natural language-to-code, and natural language-to-natural language, enforcing the model to capture a semantic essence among modalities. Secondly, we introduce a representation distribution consistency learning module to improve cross-language generalization, which explicitly aligns the feature distributions of different programming languages, enabling language-agnostic representation learning. Extensive experiments on both empirical benchmark and large-scale benchmark show that UniCoR outperforms all baseline models, achieving an average improvement of 8.64% in MRR and 11.54% in MAP over the best-performing baseline. Furthermore, UniCoR exhibits stability in hybrid code retrieval and generalization capability in cross-language scenarios.","az":"高效的代码检索不可或缺，使用自然语言与代码片段共同构成的混合模式来搜索代码已成为一种重要范式。然而，现有方法能否有效利用这类混合查询，尤其是在跨编程语言的场景下，仍不清楚。我们对代表性代码模型开展了全面的实证研究，揭示出三项挑战：(1) 语义理解不足；(2) 混合代码检索中的模态融合效率低下；(3) 跨语言场景下泛化能力弱。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 UniCoR，一个新颖的自监督框架，旨在学习统一且鲁棒的代码表示。首先，我们设计了多视角有监督对比学习模块，以增强语义理解与模态融合。它从代码到代码、自然语言到代码、自然语言到自然语言等多个视角对齐表示，促使模型捕捉跨模态的语义本质。其次，我们引入表示分布一致性学习模块以提升跨语言泛化能力，显式对齐不同编程语言的特征分布，实现语言无关的表示学习。在实证基准与大规模基准上的大量实验表明，UniCoR 优于所有基线模型，相比表现最好的基线在 MRR 上平均提升 8.64%、在 MAP 上平均提升 11.54%。此外，UniCoR 在混合代码检索中表现稳定，并在跨语言场景下展现出良好的泛化能力。","tl":"多视角对比加分布一致性学习，统一自然语言与代码混合检索表示。","au":["Yang Yang","Li Kuang","Jiakun Liu","Zhongxin Liu","Yingjie Xia","David Lo"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["empirical-study","multimodal"],"kw":["hybrid code retrieval","cross-language generalization","contrastive learning","code representation","modality fusion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/159/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00646","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Unified Software Engineering agent as AI Software Engineer","tz":"作为 AI 软件工程师的统一软件工程智能体","a":"The growth of Large Language Model (LLM) technology has raised expectations for automated coding. However, software engineering is more than coding and is concerned with activities including maintenance and evolution of a project. In this context, the concept of LLM agents has gained traction, which utilize LLMs as reasoning engines to invoke external tools autonomously. But is an LLM agent the same as an AI software engineer? In this paper, we seek to understand this question by developing a Unified Software Engineering agent or USEagent. Unlike existing work which builds specialized agents for specific software tasks such as testing, debugging, and repair, our goal is to build a unified agent which can orchestrate and handle multiple capabilities. This gives the agent the promise of handling complex scenarios in software development such as fixing an incomplete patch, adding new features, or taking over code written by others. We envision USEagent as the first draft of a future AI Software Engineer which can be a team member in future software development teams involving both AI and humans. To evaluate the efficacy of USEagent, we build a Unified Software Engineering bench (USEbench) comprising of myriad tasks such as coding, testing, and patching. USEbench is a judicious mixture of tasks from existing benchmarks such as SWE-bench, SWT-bench, and REPOCOD. In an evaluation on USEbench consisting of 1,271 repository-level software engineering tasks, USEagent shows improved efficacy compared to existing general agents such as OpenHands CodeActAgent. For specific tasks such as issue resolution in SWE-bench, USEagent demonstrates efficacy comparable to agents such as AutoCodeRover (which are focused on software maintenance), while maintaining applicability to a broader range of software engineering tasks. There exist gaps in the capabilities of USEagent for certain coding tasks, which provides hints on further developing the AI Software Engineer of the future.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）技术的发展提高了人们对自动化编码的期待。然而，软件工程不仅仅是编码，还涉及项目的维护与演化等活动。在此背景下，LLM 智能体的概念获得了关注——它们把 LLM 用作推理引擎来自主调用外部工具。但是，一个 LLM 智能体等同于一名 AI 软件工程师吗？本文通过开发一个统一软件工程智能体（Unified Software Engineering agent, USEagent）来探索这一问题。与已有为测试、调试、修复等特定软件任务构建专用智能体的工作不同，我们的目标是构建一个能够编排并处理多种能力的统一智能体。这使该智能体有望应对软件开发中的复杂场景，例如修补一个不完整的补丁、添加新特性，或接手他人编写的代码。我们把 USEagent 设想为未来 AI 软件工程师的第一版草稿，它可以成为未来由 AI 与人类共同组成的软件开发团队中的一员。为评估 USEagent 的效能，我们构建了统一软件工程基准（USEbench），它涵盖编码、测试、打补丁等众多任务。USEbench 是对 SWE-bench、SWT-bench 与 REPOCOD 等现有基准中任务的审慎混合。在包含 1,271 个仓库级软件工程任务的 USEbench 评估中，USEagent 相比 OpenHands CodeActAgent 等现有通用智能体展现出更好的效能。在 SWE-bench 的 issue 求解等特定任务上，USEagent 的效能可与 AutoCodeRover 等（专注于软件维护的）智能体相媲美，同时还适用于更广泛的软件工程任务。USEagent 在某些编码任务上的能力仍存在差距，这为进一步打造未来的 AI 软件工程师提供了线索。","tl":"用一个统一智能体编排多类 SE 任务，并配套 USEbench 评测。","au":["Leonhard Applis","Yuntong Zhang","Shanchao Liang","Nan Jiang","Lin Tan","Abhik Roychoudhury"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["unified SE agent","USEbench","issue resolution","test and patch tasks","AI software engineer"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/160/x"},{"id":"p00647","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Hallucinating Certificates: Differential Testing of TLS Certificate Validation Using Generative Language Models","tz":"幻觉出的证书：使用生成式语言模型对 TLS 证书校验进行差分测试","a":"Certificate validation is a crucial step in Transport Layer Security (TLS), the de facto standard network security protocol. Prior research has shown that differentially testing TLS implementations with synthetic certificates can reveal critical security issues, such as accidentally accepting untrusted certificates. Leveraging known techniques, like random input mutations and program coverage guidance, prior work created corpora of synthetic certificates. By testing the certificates with multiple TLS libraries and comparing the validation outcomes, they discovered new bugs. In this paper, we introduce a new approach, MLCerts, to generate synthetic certificates for differential testing that leverages generative language models to more extensively test implementations. Recently, these models have become (in)famous for their applications in generating content, writing code, and conversing with users, as well as for “hallucinating” syntactically correct yet semantically nonsensical output. In our work, we provide and leverage two novel insights: (a) TLS certificates can be expressed in natural-like language, as they can be defined in the X.509 standard that aids human readability, and (b) differential testing can benefit from hallucinated malformed test cases. Using our approach MLCerts, we find significantly more distinct discrepancies between the five TLS implementations OpenSSL, LibreSSL, GnuTLS, MbedTLS, and MatrixSSL than the state-of-the-art benchmark Transcert (+30%; 20 vs 26, out of a maximum possible of 30) and an order of magnitude more than the seminal work Frankencerts (+1,200%; 2 vs 26). Finally, we show that the diversity of MLCerts-generated certificates reveals a range of previously unobserved and interesting behavior with security implications.","az":"证书校验是传输层安全协议（TLS，事实上的标准网络安全协议）中的关键环节。已有研究表明，用合成证书对 TLS 实现进行差分测试可以揭示严重的安全问题，例如意外接受不受信任的证书。借助随机输入变异与程序覆盖引导等已知技术，先前工作构建了合成证书语料库；通过在多个 TLS 库上测试这些证书并比较校验结果，他们发现了新的缺陷。本文提出一种新方法 MLCerts，利用生成式语言模型为差分测试生成合成证书，从而更充分地测试各实现。近来，这类模型因其在生成内容、编写代码与和用户对话上的应用而声名（狼藉地）大噪，也因“幻觉”出语法正确却语义荒谬的输出而广为人知。在我们的工作中，我们提出并利用了两条新洞见：(a) TLS 证书可以用类自然语言表达，因为它们可由旨在便于人类阅读的 X.509 标准定义；(b) 差分测试可以从被幻觉出的畸形测试用例中获益。使用我们的方法 MLCerts，我们在 OpenSSL、LibreSSL、GnuTLS、MbedTLS 与 MatrixSSL 这五个 TLS 实现之间发现的不同差异数量，显著多于最先进基准 Transcert（+30%；20 对 26，最大可能为 30），并比开创性工作 Frankencerts 多一个数量级（+1,200%；2 对 26）。最后，我们表明 MLCerts 生成证书的多样性揭示了一系列此前未被观察到、且具有安全影响的有趣行为。","tl":"把 X.509 视作类自然语言，让模型“幻觉”出畸形证书做差分测试。","au":["Muhammad Talha Paracha","Kyle Posluns","Kevin Borgolte","Martina Lindorfer","David Choffnes"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["TLS certificate validation","differential testing","generative language models","synthetic certificates","hallucination"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/161/x","pu":"https://talhaparacha.com/icse_preprint.pdf"},{"id":"p00648","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Efficient Build Dependency Verification Using eBPF and Incremental Analysis","tz":"使用 eBPF 与增量分析实现高效的构建依赖验证","a":"Build systems are fundamental to modern software development, but maintaining correct dependency specifications remains a significant challenge. Dependency-related errors, including missing and redundant dependencies, account for over 50% of build errors in large-scale software projects. Existing tools for detecting such errors suffer from two major limitations: high runtime overhead due to ptrace-based system call tracing, and the need to verify all edges in the build dependency graph. This paper presents mkcheck2, a novel approach that combines extended Berkeley Packet Filter (eBPF)-based system call tracing with incremental analysis to enable efficient dependency verification. Our evaluation on a diverse set of open-source projects demonstrates that mkcheck2 reduces the overhead of dependency error detection by up to 99.7% compared to existing ptrace-based approaches while maintaining detection accuracy. Across the entire 300-project Make corpus, the incremental analysis technique lowers the mean analysis time per commit from 1267.49 seconds to just 23.56 seconds, making continuous dependency verification practical in real-world development environments.","az":"构建系统是现代软件开发的基础，但维护正确的依赖声明仍是一大挑战。依赖相关的错误，包括缺失依赖与冗余依赖，在大规模软件项目中占构建错误的 50% 以上。现有的检测此类错误的工具存在两大局限：基于 ptrace 的系统调用追踪带来的高运行时开销，以及必须验证构建依赖图中的所有边。本文提出 mkcheck2，一种将基于扩展伯克利包过滤器（eBPF）的系统调用追踪与增量分析相结合的新方法，以实现高效的依赖验证。我们在一组多样的开源项目上的评估表明，与现有基于 ptrace 的方法相比，mkcheck2 将依赖错误检测的开销最多降低 99.7%，同时保持检测准确性。在整个包含 300 个项目的 Make 语料上，增量分析技术把每次提交的平均分析时间从 1267.49 秒降至仅 23.56 秒，使得在真实开发环境中进行持续依赖验证成为可能。","tl":"用 eBPF 追踪加增量分析，把每次提交的依赖验证降到 23 秒。","au":["Yuta Saito","Kazunori Sakamoto","Hironori Washizaki"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["build systems","dependency verification","eBPF syscall tracing","incremental analysis","missing and redundant dependencies"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/162/x"},{"id":"p00649","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Diffploit: Facilitating Cross-Version Exploit Migration for Open Source Library Vulnerabilities","tz":"Diffploit：促进开源库漏洞的跨版本利用代码迁移","a":"Exploits are commonly used to demonstrate the presence of library vulnerabilities and validate their impact across different versions. However, their direct application to alternative versions often fails due to breaking changes introduced during evolution. These failures stem from both changes in triggering conditions (e.g., API refactorings) and broken dynamic environments (e.g., build or runtime errors), which are challenging to interpret and adapt manually. Existing techniques primarily focus on code-level trace alignment through fuzzing, which is both time-consuming and insufficient for handling environment-level failures. Moreover, they often fall short when dealing with complicated triggering condition changes across versions. To overcome this, we propose Diffploit, an iterative, diff-driven exploit migration method structured around two key modules: the Context Module and the Migration Module. The Context Module dynamically constructs contexts derived from analyzing behavioral discrepancies between the target and reference versions, which capture the failure symptom and its related diff hunks. Leveraging these contexts, the Migration Module guides an LLM-based adaptation through an iterative feedback loop, balancing exploration of diff candidates and gradual refinement to resolve reproduction failures effectively. We evaluate Diffploit on a large-scale dataset containing 102 Java CVEs and 689 version-migration tasks across 79 libraries. Diffploit successfully migrates 84.2% exploits, outperforming the change-aware test repair tool TARGET by 52.0% and the rule-based tool in IDEA by 61.6%. Beyond technical effectiveness, Diffploit identifies 5 CVE reports with incorrect affected version ranges, three of which have been confirmed. It also discovers 111 unreported vulnerable versions in the GitHub Advisory Database.","az":"利用代码（exploit）常被用于证明库漏洞的存在并验证其在不同版本上的影响。然而，将其直接应用到其他版本往往会失败，原因是演化过程中引入的破坏性变更。这些失败既源于触发条件的变化（例如 API 重构），也源于动态环境被破坏（例如构建或运行时错误），二者都难以人工解读与适配。现有技术主要聚焦于通过模糊测试实现代码级的轨迹对齐，既耗时又不足以处理环境级失败；而且在面对跨版本复杂的触发条件变化时往往力不从心。为克服这一点，我们提出 Diffploit，一种迭代式、差异驱动的利用代码迁移方法，围绕两个关键模块构建：上下文模块与迁移模块。上下文模块通过分析目标版本与参考版本之间的行为差异，动态构建上下文，捕捉失败症状及其相关的 diff 代码块。迁移模块利用这些上下文，通过迭代反馈循环引导基于 LLM 的适配，在探索候选 diff 与逐步细化之间取得平衡，从而有效解决复现失败。我们在一个大规模数据集上评估了 Diffploit，该数据集包含 79 个库上的 102 个 Java CVE 与 689 个版本迁移任务。Diffploit 成功迁移了 84.2% 的利用代码，比变更感知的测试修复工具 TARGET 高出 52.0%，比 IDEA 中的基于规则的工具高出 61.6%。除技术效果之外，Diffploit 还识别出 5 份受影响版本范围有误的 CVE 报告，其中三份已获确认；它还在 GitHub Advisory Database 中发现了 111 个此前未被报告的易受攻击版本。","tl":"用行为差异构建上下文，迭代引导 LLM 把 exploit 迁移到其他版本。","au":["Zirui Chen","Zhipeng Xue","Jiayuan Zhou","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Xiaohu Yang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["exploit migration","cross-version reproduction","library vulnerabilities","diff-driven context","GitHub Advisory Database"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/163/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.12950"},{"id":"p00650","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"HoarePrompt: Structural Reasoning About Program Correctness in Natural Language","tz":"HoarePrompt：以自然语言进行程序正确性的结构化推理","a":"While software requirements are often expressed in natural language, verifying the correctness of a program against such requirements is a hard and underexplored problem. Large language models (LLMs) are promising candidates for addressing this challenge, however our experience shows that they are ineffective in this task, often failing to detect even straightforward bugs. To address this gap, we introduce HoarePrompt, a novel approach that adapts fundamental ideas from program verification to natural language artifacts. Inspired from the strongest postcondition calculus, HoarePrompt employs a systematic, step-by-step process in which an LLM generates natural language descriptions of reachable program states at various code points. To manage loops, we propose few-shot-driven k-induction, an adaptation of the k-induction method widely used in model checking. Once program states are described, HoarePrompt leverages the LLM to assess whether the program, annotated with these state descriptions, conforms to the natural language requirements. For evaluating the quality of classifiers of program correctness with respect to natural language requirements, we constructed CoCoClaNeL, a challenging dataset of solutions to programming competition problems. Our experiments show that HoarePrompt improves the MCC by 61% compared to directly using Zero-shot-CoT prompts for correctness classification. Furthermore, HoarePrompt outperforms a classifier that assesses correctness via LLM-based test generation by an MCC increase of 106%. The inductive reasoning mechanism contributes a 26% boost to MCC, underscoring its effectiveness in managing loops.","az":"软件需求常以自然语言表达，但针对这类需求验证程序的正确性是一个困难且未被充分探索的问题。大语言模型（LLM）是应对这一挑战的有力候选，然而我们的经验表明它们在该任务上效果不佳，常常连直白的缺陷都检测不出来。为填补这一空白，我们提出 HoarePrompt，一种把程序验证的基本思想迁移到自然语言制品上的新方法。受最强后置条件演算启发，HoarePrompt 采用系统化的逐步流程，让 LLM 生成对程序在各个代码点可达状态的自然语言描述。为处理循环，我们提出少样本驱动的 k-归纳（few-shot-driven k-induction），这是对模型检验中广泛使用的 k-归纳方法的一种改造。在程序状态被描述之后，HoarePrompt 利用 LLM 评估带有这些状态描述标注的程序是否符合自然语言需求。为评估“针对自然语言需求判定程序正确性”的分类器质量，我们构建了 CoCoClaNeL，一个由编程竞赛题解构成的高难度数据集。我们的实验表明，与直接使用 Zero-shot-CoT 提示做正确性分类相比，HoarePrompt 将 MCC 提升了 61%。此外，HoarePrompt 比通过基于 LLM 的测试生成来评估正确性的分类器在 MCC 上高出 106%。归纳推理机制为 MCC 带来了 26% 的提升，凸显了其在处理循环方面的有效性。","tl":"用自然语言版最强后置条件与 k-归纳判定程序是否满足需求。","au":["Dimitrios Stamatios Bouras","Yihan Dai","Tairan Wang","Yingfei Xiong","Sergey Mechtaev"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["program correctness classification","strongest postcondition","k-induction","natural language requirements","CoCoClaNeL"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/164/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00651","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Reflections on the Reproducibility of Commercial LLM Performance in Empirical Software Engineering Studies","tz":"对实证软件工程研究中商用 LLM 性能可复现性的反思","a":"Large Language Models have gained remarkable interest in industry and academia. The increasing interest in LLMs in academia is also reflected in the number of publications on this topic over the last years. For instance, alone 78 of the around 425 publications at ICSE 2024 performed experiments with LLMs. Conducting empirical studies with LLMs remains challenging and raises questions on how to achieve reproducible results, for both other researchers and practitioners. One important step towards excelling in empirical research on LLM and their application is to first understand to what extent current research results are eventually reproducible and what factors may impede reproducibility. This investigation is within the scope of our work. We contribute an analysis of the reproducibility of LLM-centric studies, provide insights into the factors impeding reproducibility, and discuss suggestions on how to improve the current state. In particular, we studied the 86 articles describing LLM-centric studies, published at ICSE 2024 and ASE 2024. Of the 86 articles, 18 provided research artefacts and used OpenAI models. We attempted to replicate those 18 studies. Of the 18 studies, only five were fit for reproduction. For none of the five studies, we were able to fully reproduce the results. Two studies seemed to be partially reproducible, and three studies did not seem to be reproducible. Our results highlight not only the need for stricter research artefact evaluations but also for more robust study designs to ensure the reproducible value of future publications.","az":"大语言模型在工业界和学术界都引起了极大的兴趣。学术界对 LLM 日益增长的兴趣也体现在近年来该主题的论文数量上。例如，仅 ICSE 2024 约 425 篇论文中就有 78 篇开展了 LLM 实验。使用 LLM 开展实证研究依然充满挑战，并引出了如何为其他研究者和从业者取得可复现结果的问题。在 LLM 及其应用的实证研究中追求卓越，第一步是理解当前研究结果在多大程度上最终是可复现的，以及哪些因素会阻碍可复现性。这一考察正是我们工作的范围。我们贡献了一项对以 LLM 为中心的研究的可复现性分析，给出了阻碍可复现性因素的洞见，并讨论了改进现状的建议。具体而言，我们研究了发表于 ICSE 2024 和 ASE 2024 的 86 篇以 LLM 为中心的论文。在这 86 篇论文中，有 18 篇提供了研究制品并使用了 OpenAI 模型。我们尝试复制这 18 项研究。在这 18 项研究中，只有 5 项适合复现。对于这 5 项研究，我们均无法完全复现其结果。其中 2 项研究似乎部分可复现，3 项研究似乎不可复现。我们的结果不仅凸显了更严格的研究制品评审的必要性，也凸显了更稳健的研究设计对保障未来论文可复现价值的必要性。","tl":"首次系统复现 ICSE/ASE 2024 的 LLM 研究，发现无一可完全复现。","au":["Florian Angermeir","Maximilian Amougou","Mark Kreitz","Andreas Bauer","Matthias Linhuber","Davide Fucci","Fabiola Moyón","Daniel Mendez","Tony Gorschek"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["reproducibility-replication","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["reproducibility","empirical software engineering","LLM studies","research artifacts","OpenAI models"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/165/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.25506"},{"id":"p00652","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Argus: A Multi-agent Sensitive Information Leakage Detection Framework Based on Hierarchical Reference Relationships","tz":"Argus：基于层次化引用关系的多智能体敏感信息泄露检测框架","a":"Sensitive information leakage in code repositories has emerged as a critical security challenge. Traditional detection methods—relying on regular expressions, fingerprint features, and high-entropy calculations-suffer from high false-positive rates, which not only reduce detection efficiency but also significantly increase the manual screening burden on developers. Recent advances in large language models(LLMs) and multi-agent collaborative architectures have demonstrated remarkable potential in tackling complex tasks, offering a novel technological perspective for sensitive information detection. In response to these challenges, we propose Argus, a multi-agent collaborative framework for detecting sensitive information. Argus employs a three-tier detection mechanism that integrates key content, file context, and project reference relationships to effectively reduce false positives and enhance overall detection accuracy. To comprehensively evaluate Argus in real-world repository environments, we developed two new benchmarks—one to assess genuine leak detection capabilities and another to evaluate false-positive filtering performance. Experimental results show that Argus achieves up to 94.86% accuracy in leak detection,with a precision of 96.36%, recall of 94.64%, and an F1 score of 0.955.Moreover, the analysis of 97 real repositories incurred a total cost of only 2.21.All code implementations and related datasets are publicly available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/Argus-3C01 for further research and application.","az":"代码仓库中的敏感信息泄露已成为一项关键的安全挑战。传统检测方法依赖正则表达式、指纹特征和高熵值计算，存在很高的误报率，这不仅降低了检测效率，也显著加重了开发者人工筛查的负担。大语言模型（LLM）与多智能体协作架构的最新进展在应对复杂任务上展现出显著潜力，为敏感信息检测提供了新的技术视角。针对上述挑战，我们提出 Argus，一个用于检测敏感信息的多智能体协作框架。Argus 采用三层检测机制，融合关键内容、文件上下文与项目引用关系，有效降低误报并提升整体检测准确率。为了在真实仓库环境中全面评估 Argus，我们构建了两个新基准：一个评估真实泄露的检测能力，另一个评估误报过滤性能。实验结果表明，Argus 在泄露检测上达到最高 94.86% 的准确率，精确率 96.36%，召回率 94.64%，F1 分数 0.955。此外，对 97 个真实仓库的分析总成本仅为 2.21 美元。所有代码实现与相关数据集均已公开于 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/Argus-3C01 ，以供进一步研究与应用。","tl":"用三层引用关系的多智能体协作把密钥泄露检测的误报大幅压低。","au":["Bin Wang","Hui Li","Liyang Zhang","Qijia Zhuang","Ao Yang","Dong Zhang","Xijun Luo","Bing Lin"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","agentic","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["sensitive information leakage","multi-agent framework","false positive reduction","secret detection","code repository security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/166/x"},{"id":"p00653","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SpecGuru: Hierarchical LLM-Driven API Points-to Specification Generation with Self-Validation","tz":"SpecGuru：分层 LLM 驱动、带自验证的 API 指向规约生成","a":"Static analysis is a fundamental technique for ensuring software safety and reliability. However, when analyzing client code that invokes third-party APIs, proper handling of API source code becomes critical. A common approach is to utilize API specifications that approximate the essential behaviors of the API while avoiding direct analysis of the implementation. Existing methods for constructing API specifications often fail to adequately address challenges presented by complex semantics, syntax, and edge cases. In this paper, we introduce SpecGuru, a framework that leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) to automatically generate points-to API specifications. SpecGuru employs a novel bottom-up approach that begins with leaf functions (those without dependencies) and progressively builds specifications through rigorous validation. These validated specifications subsequently serve as abstractions at call sites of higher-level functions along the call hierarchy, effectively eliminating the need to process complex source code directly with LLMs. Our approach incorporates a robust self-validation mechanism using automatically synthesized test cases for differential testing throughout the specification inference process, which prevents error propagation and ensures incremental correctness of the generated specifications. Our experimental evaluation on 15 third-party C libraries shows that SpecGuru significantly outperforms existing specification inference tools, generating 21% more specifications than Spectre and 46% more than c-summary. Moreover, our bottom-up abstraction technique combined with automated testing methodology enables the discovery of a more comprehensive set of specifications while effectively preventing error propagation, achieving analysis results comparable to those obtained using complete API source code.","az":"静态分析是保障软件安全性与可靠性的基础技术。然而，在分析调用第三方 API 的客户端代码时，如何恰当处理 API 源码变得至关重要。一种常见做法是利用 API 规约来近似 API 的关键行为，从而避免直接分析其实现。现有的 API 规约构建方法往往无法充分应对复杂语义、语法和边界情形带来的挑战。本文提出 SpecGuru，一个利用大语言模型（LLM）自动生成指向（points-to）类 API 规约的框架。SpecGuru 采用一种新颖的自底向上方法：从叶子函数（无依赖的函数）出发，通过严格验证逐步构建规约。这些经过验证的规约随后在调用层次中作为上层函数调用点处的抽象，从而无需让 LLM 直接处理复杂源码。我们的方法在规约推断全过程中引入了稳健的自验证机制，利用自动合成的测试用例进行差分测试，防止错误传播并确保生成规约的增量正确性。在 15 个第三方 C 库上的实验评估表明，SpecGuru 显著优于现有规约推断工具，生成的规约比 Spectre 多 21%，比 c-summary 多 46%。此外，我们的自底向上抽象技术结合自动化测试方法，能够发现更全面的规约集合，同时有效防止错误传播，所得分析结果可与使用完整 API 源码时相媲美。","tl":"自底向上加差分测试自验证，让 LLM 稳健推出 API 指向规约。","au":["Shuangxiang Kan","Yuekang Li","Xiao Cheng","Yulei Sui"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["points-to specification","static analysis","specification inference","differential testing","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/167/x"},{"id":"p00654","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Repairing LLM Executions for Secure Automatic Programming","tz":"修复 LLM 的执行过程以实现安全的自动编程","a":"While automatic code generation using Large Language Models (LLMs) has advanced significantly, these models frequently produce code containing security vulnerabilities. Existing approaches to improve the security of automatically generated code, such as fine-tuning or prompt engineering, have shown limited success and provide minimal insight into the underlying mechanisms causing these vulnerabilities. We propose an approach grounded in mechanistic interpretability to analyze and mitigate vulnerable code generation in LLMs. We begin by examining the knowledge stored inside LLMs, identifying and disentangling knowledge representations that contribute to generating vulnerable code. Next, we leverage these insights to repair model execution in real time: when the model attempts to access vulnerability-inducing representations during inference, our method intercepts and modifies this access, improving the security of the generated code. We implement our methodology in a tool called thea and evaluate it on the CyberSecEval benchmark using Llama 3.1. Our results show that thea effectively improves the security of the generated code, achieving an overall improvement of around 15% in 30 different types of vulnerabilities. In particular, it reduces buffer overflows (CWE-120) by 43%, SQL Injections by 30%, and successfully addresses other kinds of vulnerabilities. Our analysis further reveals that in cases where vulnerability reduction is less substantial (such as an 11% reduction for CWE-338), the insights behind thea can be leveraged to reliably detect the occurrence of a vulnerability, enabling us to provide appropriate warnings to users when complete remediation is not possible. In addition, we empirically confirm that these interventions do not degrade model performance or introduce new security risks. Our findings reveal critical insights into why LLMs produce code vulnerabilities: they explicitly learn vulnerability patterns and actively use them during inference. We repair the LLM executions to avoid such vulnerability patterns.","az":"尽管使用大语言模型（LLM）进行自动代码生成已取得长足进展，这些模型仍频繁产出包含安全漏洞的代码。现有改进自动生成代码安全性的方法（如微调或提示工程）成效有限，且对导致漏洞的底层机制几乎没有提供洞见。我们提出一种基于机制可解释性的方法来分析并缓解 LLM 的漏洞代码生成。我们首先考察 LLM 内部存储的知识，识别并解耦那些促成漏洞代码生成的知识表示。随后，我们利用这些洞见在运行时修复模型执行：当模型在推理过程中试图访问诱发漏洞的表示时，我们的方法会拦截并修改这一访问，从而提升所生成代码的安全性。我们将该方法实现为工具 thea，并在 CyberSecEval 基准上使用 Llama 3.1 进行评估。结果显示 thea 有效提升了生成代码的安全性，在 30 种不同类型的漏洞上取得约 15% 的整体改进。其中，缓冲区溢出（CWE-120）减少 43%，SQL 注入减少 30%，并成功处理了其他多类漏洞。我们的分析进一步表明，在漏洞削减幅度较小的情形下（例如 CWE-338 仅减少 11%），thea 背后的洞见仍可用于可靠地检测漏洞的出现，从而在无法完全修复时向用户发出适当告警。此外，我们通过实验确认这些干预不会削弱模型性能，也不会引入新的安全风险。我们的发现揭示了 LLM 为何产生代码漏洞的关键洞见：它们显式地学习了漏洞模式，并在推理时主动使用这些模式。我们通过修复 LLM 的执行过程来规避此类漏洞模式。","tl":"证明 LLM 显式存有漏洞模式，并在推理时拦截该表示访问。","au":["Ali El Husseini","Yacine Izza","Blaise Genest","Abhik Roychoudhury"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["secure code generation","mechanistic interpretability","CWE","inference-time intervention","CyberSecEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/168/x"},{"id":"p00655","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RepoScope: Leveraging Call Chain-Aware Multi-View Context for Repository-Level Code Generation","tz":"RepoScope：利用调用链感知的多视图上下文进行仓库级代码生成","a":"Repository-level code generation aims to generate code within the context of a specified repository. Existing approaches typically employ retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) techniques to provide LLMs with relevant contextual information extracted from the repository. However, these approaches often struggle with effectively identifying truly relevant contexts that capture the rich semantics of the repository, and their contextual perspectives remains narrow. Moreover, most approaches fail to account for the structural relationships in the retrieved code during prompt construction, hindering the LLM’s ability to accurately interpret the context. To address these issues, we propose RepoScope, which leverages call chain-aware multi-view context for repository-level code generation. RepoScope constructs a Repository Structural Semantic Graph (RSSG) and retrieves a comprehensive four-view context, integrating both structural and similarity-based contexts. We propose a novel call chain prediction method that utilizes the repository’s structural semantics to improve the identification of callees in the target function. Additionally, we present a structure-preserving serialization algorithm for prompt construction, ensuring the coherence of the context for the LLM. Notably, RepoScope relies solely on static analysis, eliminating the need for additional training or multiple LLM queries, thus ensuring both efficiency and generalizability. Evaluation on widely-used repository-level code generation benchmarks (CoderEval and DevEval) demonstrates that RepoScope outperforms state-of-the-art methods, achieving up to a 36.35% relative improvement in pass@1 scores. Further experiments emphasize RepoScope’s potential to improve code generation across different tasks and its ability to integrate effectively with existing approaches. We provide the replication package at https://github.com/Lorien1128/RepoScope .","az":"仓库级代码生成旨在在指定仓库的上下文中生成代码。现有方法通常采用检索增强生成（RAG）技术，为 LLM 提供从仓库中抽取的相关上下文信息。然而，这些方法往往难以有效识别真正相关、能够刻画仓库丰富语义的上下文，其上下文视角也较为狭窄。此外，多数方法在构造提示时未考虑所检索代码之间的结构关系，妨碍了 LLM 准确理解上下文。为解决这些问题，我们提出 RepoScope，利用调用链感知的多视图上下文进行仓库级代码生成。RepoScope 构建仓库结构语义图（RSSG），并检索包含结构性与相似性上下文在内的四视图综合上下文。我们提出一种新颖的调用链预测方法，利用仓库的结构语义来改进对目标函数被调用者的识别。此外，我们提出一种用于提示构造的保结构序列化算法，确保提供给 LLM 的上下文具有连贯性。值得注意的是，RepoScope 仅依赖静态分析，无需额外训练或多次 LLM 查询，从而兼具效率与泛化性。在广泛使用的仓库级代码生成基准（CoderEval 与 DevEval）上的评估表明，RepoScope 优于最先进方法，pass@1 相对提升最高达 36.35%。进一步实验强调了 RepoScope 在不同任务上改进代码生成的潜力，以及与现有方法有效集成的能力。复现包见 https://github.com/Lorien1128/RepoScope 。","tl":"用仓库结构语义图预测调用链，组装保结构的四视图上下文。","au":["Yang Liu","Li Zhang","Fang Liu","Zhuohang Wang","Donglin Wei","Zhishuo Yang","Kechi Zhang","Jia Li","Lin Shi"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["repository-level code generation","call chain prediction","retrieval-augmented generation","static analysis","structural context"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/169/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.14791"},{"id":"p00656","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fuzzing Java Optimizing Compilers with Complex Inter-Class Structures Guided by Heterogeneous Program Graphs","tz":"以异构程序图引导、面向复杂类间结构的 Java 优化编译器模糊测试","a":"Modern Java compilers, such as Just-In-Time (JIT) and Ahead-OfTime (AOT) compilers, often infer and analyze complex inter-class structures to perform program optimizations while preserving semantic correctness. However, incorrect inference of these structures during compilation can lead to critical bugs, as observed in production compilers like HotSpot and R8. Despite their significance, existing Java fuzzing tools fail to adequately explore inter-class relationships, focusing instead on simpler intra-class or intra-method constructs. To bridge this gap, we present InterFuzz, the first fuzzing framework designed to systematically generate Java test cases with complex inter-class structures. InterFuzz introduces a novel concept of Heterogeneous Program Graph (HPG) to abstract and manipulate inter-class relationships. It then employs Inter-Class Mutators to construct intricate interactions, and utilizes Graph Complexity to guide test generation toward high-diversity code. Our evaluation shows that InterFuzz effectively uncovers compiler bugs that elude traditional fuzzers, having discovered 24 new bugs across HotSpot, ART, and R8, with 20 confirmed by developers—16 of which hinge on intricate inter-class structures.","az":"现代 Java 编译器（如即时编译器 JIT 与提前编译器 AOT）通常需要推断并分析复杂的类间结构，以在保持语义正确性的同时执行程序优化。然而，编译期间对这些结构的错误推断可能导致严重缺陷，这在 HotSpot 和 R8 等生产级编译器中已有体现。尽管意义重大，现有的 Java 模糊测试工具未能充分探索类间关系，而是聚焦于更简单的类内或方法内构造。为弥合这一空白，我们提出 InterFuzz，首个专门用于系统性生成具有复杂类间结构的 Java 测试用例的模糊测试框架。InterFuzz 引入了异构程序图（HPG）这一新颖概念来抽象和操纵类间关系，随后使用类间变异算子构造复杂的交互，并利用图复杂度引导测试生成走向高多样性代码。评估表明，InterFuzz 能有效发现传统模糊测试工具难以触及的编译器缺陷，在 HotSpot、ART 和 R8 中共发现 24 个新缺陷，其中 20 个已被开发者确认，16 个依赖于复杂的类间结构。","tl":"首次用异构程序图系统构造类间结构来测 Java 编译器。","au":["Shiyu Qiu","Ming Wen","Zifan Xie","Hai Jin"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["compiler fuzzing","JIT compiler","inter-class structure","heterogeneous program graph","HotSpot"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/170/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/170/Fuzzing-Java-Optimizing-Compilers-with-Complex-Inter-Class-Structures-Guided-by-Heter"},{"id":"p00657","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TypeCare: Boosting Python Type Inference Models via Context-Aware Re-Ranking and Augmentation","tz":"TypeCare：通过上下文感知的重排序与扩充增强 Python 类型推断模型","a":"Type annotations improve Python code quality by enabling better readability, static analysis, and developer productivity. However, manually annotating existing code is labor-intensive and error-prone. While recent learning-based models have advanced automatic type inference, they struggle with rare or complex types that are underrepresented in training data. We present TypeCare, a model-agnostic post-processing technique that refines the outputs of existing type inference models using code context, without requiring retraining or fine-tuning. TypeCare combines two key components: (1) Re-Ranking, which prioritizes semantically and syntactically relevant types, and (2) Augmentation, which generates additional contextually plausible candidates. Applied to three state-of-the-art type inference models—TypeT5, Tiger, and TypeGen—TypeCare consistently improves top-1 accuracy, achieving up to 40.1% gains on complex types that existing models often fail to predict correctly.","az":"类型注解通过提升可读性、静态分析能力和开发者生产力来改善 Python 代码质量。然而，手工为已有代码添加注解既费力又易出错。虽然近期基于学习的模型推进了自动类型推断，它们在训练数据中代表性不足的稀有或复杂类型上仍表现不佳。我们提出 TypeCare，一种与模型无关的后处理技术，利用代码上下文来精化已有类型推断模型的输出，无需重新训练或微调。TypeCare 结合两个关键组件：（1）重排序，优先考虑语义和句法上相关的类型；（2）扩充，生成额外的、上下文上合理的候选类型。将 TypeCare 应用于三个最先进的类型推断模型 TypeT5、Tiger 和 TypeGen 后，top-1 准确率持续提升，在现有模型常常预测失败的复杂类型上最高提升 40.1%。","tl":"免训练的后处理重排+候选扩充，专攻稀有复杂类型推断。","au":["Wonseok Oh","Hakjoo Oh"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Python type inference","type annotation","re-ranking","post-processing","rare types"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/171/x"},{"id":"p00658","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FreshBrew: A Benchmark for Evaluating AI Agents on Java Code Migration","tz":"FreshBrew：评测 AI 智能体完成 Java 代码迁移的基准","a":"AI coding assistants are rapidly becoming integral to modern software development. A key challenge in this space is the continual need to migrate and modernize codebases in response to evolving software ecosystems. Traditionally, such migrations have relied on rule-based systems and human intervention. With the advent of powerful large language models (LLMs), AI-driven agentic frameworks offer a promising alternative—but their effectiveness remains underexplored. In this paper, we introduce FreshBrew, a novel benchmark for evaluating AI agents on project-level Java migrations, with a specific focus on measuring an agent’s ability to preserve program semantics and avoid reward hacking, which we argue requires projects with high test coverage for a rigorous and reliable evaluation. We benchmark several state-of-the-art LLMs, and compare their performance against established rule-based tools. Our evaluation of AI agents on this benchmark of 228 repositories shows that the top-performing model, Gemini 2.5 Flash, can successfully migrate 54.3% of projects to JDK 17. Our empirical analysis reveals novel insights into the critical strengths and limitations of current agentic approaches, offering actionable insights into their real-world applicability. By releasing FreshBrew publicly upon acceptance, we aim to facilitate rigorous, reproducible evaluation and catalyze progress in AI-driven codebase modernization.","az":"AI 编程助手正迅速成为现代软件开发不可或缺的一部分。该领域的一个关键挑战是，为应对不断演化的软件生态，代码库需要持续迁移和现代化。传统上，此类迁移依赖基于规则的系统和人工介入。随着强大的大语言模型（LLM）出现，AI 驱动的智能体框架提供了一种有前景的替代方案，但其有效性仍未被充分探索。本文提出 FreshBrew，一个用于评测 AI 智能体完成项目级 Java 迁移的新基准，尤其关注衡量智能体保持程序语义、避免奖励攻击（reward hacking）的能力；我们认为这要求所选项目具有高测试覆盖率，才能做出严格可靠的评估。我们对若干最先进的 LLM 进行了基准测试，并将其表现与成熟的基于规则的工具进行比较。我们在包含 228 个仓库的该基准上对 AI 智能体的评估显示，表现最佳的模型 Gemini 2.5 Flash 能成功将 54.3% 的项目迁移到 JDK 17。我们的实证分析揭示了当前智能体方法关键优势与局限的新洞见，为其真实世界的适用性提供了可操作的启示。我们将在论文被接收后公开 FreshBrew，以促进严格、可复现的评测，并推动 AI 驱动的代码库现代化进展。","tl":"以高覆盖率项目为准，揭穿迁移智能体的语义破坏与奖励攻击。","au":["Victor May","Diganta Misra","Yanqi Luo","Anjali Sridhar","Justine Gehring","Silvio Soares Ribeiro Junior"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["code migration benchmark","Java modernization","AI agents","reward hacking","JDK 17"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/172/x"},{"id":"p00659","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Online and Interactive Bayesian Inference Debugging","tz":"在线交互式贝叶斯推断调试","a":"Probabilistic programming is a rapidly developing programming paradigm which enables the formulation of Bayesian models as programs and the automation of posterior inference. It facilitates the development of models and conducting Bayesian inference, which makes these techniques available to practitioners from multiple fields. Nevertheless, probabilistic programming is notoriously difficult as identifying and repairing issues with inference requires a lot of time and deep knowledge. Through this work, we introduce a novel approach to debugging Bayesian inference that reduces time and required knowledge significantly. We discuss several requirements a Bayesian inference debugging framework has to fulfill, and propose a new tool that meets these key requirements directly within the development environment. We evaluate our results in a study with 18 experienced participants and show that our approach to online and interactive debugging of Bayesian inference significantly reduces time and difficulty on inference debugging tasks.","az":"概率编程是一种快速发展的编程范式，它使贝叶斯模型能够以程序形式表达，并自动完成后验推断。它便利了模型开发与贝叶斯推断的实施，使这些技术可以被多个领域的从业者使用。然而，概率编程以困难著称，因为识别并修复推断中的问题需要大量时间和深厚知识。通过这项工作，我们提出一种调试贝叶斯推断的新方法，显著降低了所需时间与知识门槛。我们讨论了贝叶斯推断调试框架必须满足的若干需求，并提出一个直接在开发环境中满足这些关键需求的新工具。我们在一项有 18 名经验丰富的参与者的研究中评估了结果，表明我们的在线交互式贝叶斯推断调试方法显著降低了推断调试任务的耗时与难度。","tl":"把贝叶斯推断诊断做成 IDE 内的在线交互式调试器。","au":["Nathanael Nussbaumer","Markus Böck","Jürgen Cito"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["human-study","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["probabilistic programming","Bayesian inference debugging","interactive debugging","IDE tool","user study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/173/x"},{"id":"p00660","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Optimization-Aware Test Generation for Deep Learning Compilers","tz":"面向深度学习编译器的优化感知测试生成","a":"Deep Learning (DL) compilers have been widely utilized to optimize DL models for efficient deployment across various hardware. Due to their vital role in the DL ecosystem, ensuring their reliability is critical. Such model optimizations are often designed to match specific computational graph structures of a model. However, existing DL compiler fuzzing techniques do not generate tests for each optimization aware of its matched graph structures. In this paper, we proposed OATest, a novel technique that synthesizes optimization-aware tests by extracting patterns from documented tests and integrating them into diverse computational graph contexts. To address the key technical challenge of synthesizing valid and optimization-aware computational graphs, OATest introduces two synthesis strategies: (1) reusing compatible inputs/outputs from existing nodes and (2) creating new nodes with compatible inputs/outputs, establishing effective connections between patterns and contexts. OATest is evaluated on two popular DL compilers, TVM and ONNXRuntime, regarding the bugs revealed by crashes and inconsistencies. The experimental results show that OATest significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art DL compiler fuzzing techniques by detecting more bugs and covering more optimization code in TVM and ONNXRuntime. Particularly, OATest uncovers 56 previously unknown bugs, 42/24 of which have been confirmed/fixed by developers.","az":"深度学习（DL）编译器被广泛用于优化 DL 模型，以便在各种硬件上高效部署。由于其在 DL 生态中的关键作用，确保其可靠性至关重要。模型优化往往是针对特定计算图结构设计的，然而现有的 DL 编译器模糊测试技术并未针对每项优化、结合其所匹配的图结构来生成测试。本文提出 OATest，一种新技术，通过从有文档记录的测试中提取模式，并将其整合进多样的计算图上下文，来合成优化感知的测试。为解决合成有效且优化感知的计算图这一关键技术挑战，OATest 引入两种合成策略：（1）复用已有节点中兼容的输入/输出；（2）创建具有兼容输入/输出的新节点，从而在模式与上下文之间建立有效连接。我们在两个流行的 DL 编译器 TVM 和 ONNXRuntime 上评估 OATest，考察由崩溃和不一致所揭示的缺陷。实验结果显示，OATest 显著优于最先进的 DL 编译器模糊测试技术，在 TVM 和 ONNXRuntime 中检测到更多缺陷并覆盖了更多优化代码。特别地，OATest 发现了 56 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 42 个/24 个已被开发者确认/修复。","tl":"从文档测试提取优化模式再嵌入多样计算图上下文做测试合成。","au":["Qingchao Shen","Zan Wang","Haoyang Ma","Yongqiang Tian","Lili Huang","Zibo Xiao","Junjie Chen","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DL compiler testing","optimization-aware test synthesis","TVM","ONNXRuntime","computational graph"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/174/x"},{"id":"p00661","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Rethinking the Evaluation of Secure Code Generation","tz":"重新思考安全代码生成的评测方式","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are widely used in software development. However, the code generated by LLMs often contains vulnerabilities. Several secure code generation methods have been proposed to address this issue, but their current evaluation schemes leave several concerns unaddressed. Specifically, most existing studies evaluate security and functional correctness separately, using different datasets. That is, they assess vulnerabilities using security-related code datasets while validating functionality with general code datasets. In addition, prior research primarily relies on a single static analyzer, CodeQL, to detect vulnerabilities in generated code, which limits the scope of security evaluation. In this work, we conduct a comprehensive study to systematically assess the improvements introduced by four state-of-the-art secure code generation techniques. Specifically, we apply both security inspection and functionality validation to the same generated code and evaluate these two aspects together. We also employ three popular static analyzers and two LLMs to identify potential vulnerabilities in the generated code. Our study reveals that existing techniques often compromise the functionality of generated code to enhance security. Their overall performance remains limited when evaluating security and functionality together. In fact, many techniques even degrade the performance of the base LLM by more than 50%. Our further inspection reveals that these techniques often either remove vulnerable lines of code entirely or generate ``garbage code'' that is unrelated to the intended task. Moreover, the commonly used static analyzer CodeQL fails to detect several vulnerabilities, further obscuring the actual security improvements achieved by existing techniques. Our study serves as a guideline for a more rigorous and comprehensive evaluation of secure code generation performance in future work.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在软件开发中被广泛使用。然而，LLM 生成的代码常常包含漏洞。已有若干安全代码生成方法被提出以应对这一问题，但它们当前的评测方案留下了若干未解的疑虑。具体而言，多数现有研究使用不同数据集分别评估安全性与功能正确性：用与安全相关的代码数据集评估漏洞，而用通用代码数据集验证功能。此外，以往研究主要依赖单一静态分析器 CodeQL 来检测生成代码中的漏洞，这限制了安全评估的范围。在本工作中，我们开展了一项全面研究，系统评估四种最先进的安全代码生成技术所带来的改进。具体地，我们对同一批生成代码同时施加安全检查与功能验证，并将这两方面一并评估。我们还使用三种流行的静态分析器和两个 LLM 来识别生成代码中的潜在漏洞。我们的研究表明，现有技术往往以牺牲生成代码的功能性来换取安全性提升；在将安全与功能一并评估时，它们的总体表现仍然有限。事实上，许多技术甚至使基础 LLM 的性能下降超过 50%。进一步检视发现，这些技术往往要么完全删除有漏洞的代码行，要么生成与预期任务无关的“垃圾代码”。此外，常用的静态分析器 CodeQL 未能检测出若干漏洞，进一步掩盖了现有技术实际取得的安全改进。我们的研究为未来更严格、更全面地评测安全代码生成性能提供了指南。","tl":"安全与功能同表评测，揭示现有安全生成技术多以功能崩塌换安全。","au":["Shih-Chieh Dai","Jun Xu","Guanhong Tao"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication","llm-based"],"kw":["secure code generation","evaluation methodology","static analyzers","CodeQL","security-functionality trade-off"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/175/x"},{"id":"p00662","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Well Begun is Half Done: Location-Aware and Trace-Guided Iterative Automated Vulnerability Repair","tz":"良好的开端是成功的一半：位置感知与轨迹引导的迭代式自动漏洞修复","a":"The advances of large language models (LLMs) have paved the way for automated software vulnerability repair approaches, which iteratively refine the patch until it becomes plausible. Nevertheless, existing LLM-based vulnerability repair approaches face notable limitations: 1) they ignore the concern of locations that need to be patched but only concerning the repair content. 2) they lack quality assessment for generated candidate patches in the iterative process. To tackle the two limitations, we propose LoopRepair, an LLM-based approach that provides information about where should be patched first. Furthermore, LoopRepair improves the iterative repair strategy by assessing the quality of test-failing patches and selecting the best patch for the next iteration. We introduce two dimensions to assess the quality of patches: whether they introduce new vulnerabilities and the taint statement coverage. We evaluated LoopRepair on a real-world C/C++ vulnerability repair dataset VulnLoc+, which contains 40 vulnerabilities and their Proof-of-Vulnerability. The experimental results demonstrate that LoopRepair exhibits substantial improvements compared with the Neural Machine Translation (NMT)-based, Program Analysis-based, and LLM-based state-of-the-art vulnerability repair approaches. Specifically, LoopRepair is able to generate 27 plausible patches, which is comparable to or even 8 to 22 more plausible patches than the baselines. In terms of correct patch generation, LoopRepair repairs 8 to 13 additional vulnerabilities compared with existing approaches.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的进展为自动软件漏洞修复方法铺平了道路，这类方法会迭代地精化补丁直至其变得可信。然而，现有基于 LLM 的漏洞修复方法面临明显局限：1）它们忽视了需要打补丁的位置，只关注修复内容；2）它们在迭代过程中缺乏对生成候选补丁的质量评估。为应对这两个局限，我们提出 LoopRepair，一种基于 LLM 的方法，先提供关于“应在何处打补丁”的信息。此外，LoopRepair 通过评估测试失败补丁的质量、并选择最佳补丁进入下一轮迭代，改进了迭代修复策略。我们引入两个维度来评估补丁质量：补丁是否引入新漏洞，以及污点语句覆盖率。我们在真实世界的 C/C++ 漏洞修复数据集 VulnLoc+ 上评估了 LoopRepair，该数据集包含 40 个漏洞及其漏洞证明（Proof-of-Vulnerability）。实验结果表明，LoopRepair 相比基于神经机器翻译（NMT）、基于程序分析和基于 LLM 的最先进漏洞修复方法有实质性提升。具体而言，LoopRepair 能生成 27 个可信补丁，与基线相当甚至多出 8 至 22 个可信补丁。在正确补丁生成方面，LoopRepair 比现有方法多修复 8 至 13 个漏洞。","tl":"先定位再修，并用“是否引新漏洞+污点覆盖”筛选迭代补丁。","au":["Zhenlei Ye","Xiaobing Sun","Sicong Cao","Lili Bo","Bin Li"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated vulnerability repair","patch localization","taint coverage","iterative refinement","C/C++ vulnerabilities"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/176/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00663","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Are Humans and LLMs Confused by the Same Code? An Empirical Study on Fixation-Related Potentials and LLM Perplexity","tz":"人类和 LLM 会被同样的代码搞糊涂吗？关于注视相关电位与 LLM 困惑度的实证研究","a":"Already today, humans and programming assistants based on large language models (LLMs) collaborate in everyday programming tasks. Clearly, a misalignment between how LLMs and programmers comprehend code can lead to misunderstandings, inefficiencies, low code quality, and bugs. A key question in this space is whether humans and LLMs are confused by the same kind of code. This would not only guide our choices of integrating LLMs in software engineering workflows, but also inform about possible improvements of LLMs. To this end, we conducted an empirical study comparing an LLM to human programmers comprehending clean and confusing code. We operationalized comprehension for the LLM by using LLM perplexity, and for human programmers using neurophysiological responses (in particular, EEG-based fixation-related potentials). We found that LLM perplexity spikes correlate both in terms of location and amplitude with human neurophysiological responses that indicate confusion. This result suggests that LLMs and humans are similarly confused about the code. Based on these findings, we devised a data-driven, LLM-based approach to identify regions of confusion in code that elicit confusion in human programmers.","az":"如今，人类与基于大语言模型（LLM）的编程助手已在日常编程任务中协同工作。显然，LLM 与程序员在理解代码方式上的不一致会导致误解、低效、低代码质量和缺陷。该领域的一个关键问题是：人类和 LLM 是否会被同一类代码搞糊涂？这不仅能指导我们如何将 LLM 集成进软件工程工作流，也能启示 LLM 可能的改进方向。为此，我们开展了一项实证研究，比较一个 LLM 与人类程序员在理解清晰代码与令人困惑代码时的表现。我们用 LLM 困惑度（perplexity）来操作化 LLM 的理解，用神经生理响应（具体为基于 EEG 的注视相关电位）来操作化人类程序员的理解。我们发现，LLM 困惑度的峰值在位置和幅度上都与指示困惑的人类神经生理响应相关。该结果表明 LLM 与人类会被代码以相似方式困惑。基于这些发现，我们设计了一种数据驱动、基于 LLM 的方法，用于识别代码中会引发人类程序员困惑的区域。","tl":"EEG 注视电位与 LLM 困惑度峰值相关，可据此定位困惑代码区。","au":["Youssef Abdelsalam","Norman Peitek","Anna-Maria Maurer","Mariya Toneva","Sven Apel"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["human-study","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["code comprehension","EEG fixation-related potentials","LLM perplexity","confusing code","human-LLM alignment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/177/x","pu":"https://www.se.cs.uni-saarland.de/publications/docs/APM+26.pdf"},{"id":"p00664","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ProxyWar: Dynamic Assessment of LLM Code Generation in Game Arenas","tz":"ProxyWar：在游戏竞技场中动态评估 LLM 代码生成","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have revolutionized automated code generation, yet the evaluation of their real-world effectiveness remains limited by static benchmarks and simplistic metrics. We present ProxyWar , a novel framework that systematically assesses code generation quality by embedding LLM-generated agents within diverse, competitive game environments. Unlike existing approaches, ProxyWar evaluates both functional correctness and strategic performance, combining automated testing, iterative code repair, and multi-agent tournaments to provide a holistic view of code quality. Applied to a range of state-of-the-art coders and games, our approach uncovers notable discrepancies between benchmark scores and actual performance in dynamic settings, revealing overlooked limitations and opportunities for improvement. These findings highlight the need for richer, competition-based evaluation of code generation. Looking forward, ProxyWar lays a foundation for research into LLM-driven algorithm discovery and adaptive problem solving, including the potential for models to outperform hand-crafted agents. All code and evaluation environments will be released to foster further research and reproducibility.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已经彻底改变了自动代码生成，但对其真实世界有效性的评估仍受限于静态基准和过于简单的指标。我们提出 ProxyWar，一个新颖框架，通过将 LLM 生成的智能体嵌入多样的竞技游戏环境来系统评估代码生成质量。与现有方法不同，ProxyWar 同时评估功能正确性与策略性能，结合自动化测试、迭代代码修复和多智能体锦标赛，从而给出代码质量的整体视图。将该方法应用于一系列最先进的代码模型和游戏后，我们发现基准分数与动态环境中实际表现之间存在显著差异，揭示了被忽视的局限与改进机会。这些发现凸显了对代码生成开展更丰富的、基于竞争的评测的必要性。展望未来，ProxyWar 为 LLM 驱动的算法发现与自适应问题求解研究奠定了基础，包括模型超越手工编写智能体的潜力。所有代码与评测环境都将发布，以促进后续研究与可复现性。","tl":"用竞技游戏对战替代静态基准，同时考功能正确性与策略强度。","au":["Xinyu Wang","Wenjun Peng","Qi Wu"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","agentic"],"kw":["dynamic evaluation","game arena","code generation assessment","multi-agent tournament","benchmark limitations"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/178/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00665","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MaCTG: Multi-Agent Collaborative Thought Graph for Automatic Programming","tz":"MaCTG：面向自动编程的多智能体协作思维图","a":"With the rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs), LLM-based approaches have demonstrated strong problem-solving capabilities across various domains. However, in automatic programming, a single LLM is typically limited to function-level code generation, while multi-agent systems composed of multiple LLMs often suffer from inefficient task planning. This lack of structured coordination can lead to cascading hallucinations, where accumulated errors across agents result in suboptimal workflows and excessive computational costs. To overcome these challenges, we introduce MaCTG (Multi-Agent Collaborative Thought Graph), a novel multi-agent framework that employs a dynamic graph structure to facilitate precise task allocation and controlled collaboration among LLM agents. MaCTG autonomously assigns agent roles based on programming requirements, dynamically refines task distribution through context-aware adjustments, and systematically verifies and integrates project-level code, effectively reducing hallucination errors and improving overall accuracy. MaCTG enhances cost-effectiveness by implementing a hybrid LLM deployment, where proprietary models handle complex reasoning, while open-source models are used for routine coding and validation tasks. To evaluate MaCTG’s effectiveness, we applied it to traditional image processing auto-programming tasks, achieving a state-of-the-art accuracy of 94.44%. Additionally, by leveraging its hybrid LLM configuration, MaCTG significantly reduced operational costs by 89.09% compared to existing multi-agent frameworks, demonstrating its efficiency, scalability, and real-world applicability. Our project can be found at https://github.com/MaCTG2025/MaCTG .","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）的快速发展，基于 LLM 的方法在各领域展现出强大的问题求解能力。然而在自动编程中，单个 LLM 通常局限于函数级代码生成，而由多个 LLM 组成的多智能体系统又常常受困于低效的任务规划。这种缺乏结构化协调的情况会导致级联幻觉：跨智能体累积的错误造成次优工作流与过高的计算成本。为克服这些挑战，我们提出 MaCTG（多智能体协作思维图），一个新颖的多智能体框架，采用动态图结构来促进 LLM 智能体之间精确的任务分配与受控的协作。MaCTG 依据编程需求自主分配智能体角色，通过上下文感知的调整动态精化任务分布，并系统性地验证与整合项目级代码，有效减少幻觉错误并提升整体准确率。MaCTG 通过混合 LLM 部署提升成本效益：专有模型负责复杂推理，开源模型用于常规编码与验证任务。为评估 MaCTG 的有效性，我们将其应用于传统图像处理类自动编程任务，取得了 94.44% 的最先进准确率。此外，借助其混合 LLM 配置，MaCTG 相比现有多智能体框架将运行成本显著降低 89.09%，展示了其效率、可扩展性与现实适用性。项目见 https://github.com/MaCTG2025/MaCTG 。","tl":"动态思维图分派角色，配合专有/开源模型混部把成本降 89%。","au":["Zixiao Zhao","Jing Sun","Zhe Hou","Wei Zhiyuan","ChengHao Cai","Miao Qiao","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["multi-agent framework","thought graph","task allocation","automatic programming","hybrid LLM deployment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/179/x"},{"id":"p00666","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"No Shot in the Dark: Efficient Context-Free Language Reachability via Context-Aware Tabulation","tz":"不打无准备之仗：通过上下文感知制表实现高效的上下文无关语言可达性","a":"Context-free language (CFL) reachability is a widely used framework for formulating static program analyses. Operating over edge-labeled graphs, the standard algorithm performs context-free tabulation by iteratively deriving new edges that summarize paths whose labels conform to the production rules of a context-free grammar. However, as the term ``context-free'' suggests, these derivations are made without considering the surrounding context of inferred edges, often resulting in unproductive edges that do not contribute to the final reachability result. In this paper, we present context-aware tabulation (CAT), a novel approach that incorporates a restricted form of context sensitivity into CFL-reachability analysis to eliminate such unproductive edges. Comprehensive experiments on three widely studied clients show that CAT significantly accelerates reachability solving—achieving speedups of 1.75x, 1.49x, and 2.13x—and also reduces memory usage by 33.28%, 24.24%, and 50.15%, respectively, compared to a state-of-the-art solver.","az":"上下文无关语言（CFL）可达性是一个被广泛用于表达静态程序分析的框架。标准算法在带边标签的图上运行，通过迭代推导新边来进行上下文无关制表，这些新边概括了标签符合上下文无关文法产生式规则的路径。然而，正如“上下文无关”一词所暗示的，这些推导在做出时并不考虑被推导边的周围上下文，常常产生对最终可达性结果毫无贡献的无效边。本文提出上下文感知制表（CAT），一种将受限形式的上下文敏感性引入 CFL 可达性分析、以消除此类无效边的新方法。在三个被广泛研究的客户分析上的全面实验表明，CAT 显著加速了可达性求解，相比最先进求解器分别取得 1.75 倍、1.49 倍和 2.13 倍的加速，并分别减少 33.28%、24.24% 和 50.15% 的内存占用。","tl":"给 CFL 可达性加入受限上下文敏感性，剪掉无效边大幅提速。","au":["Chenghang Shi","Lian Li"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["CFL reachability","context-aware tabulation","static analysis","context sensitivity","performance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/180/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/180/No-Shot-in-the-Dark-Efficient-Context-Free-Language-Reachability-via-Context-Aware-T"},{"id":"p00667","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Understanding and Characterizing Vulnerabilities in Intelligent Connected Vehicles through Real-World Exploits","tz":"通过真实世界漏洞利用理解与刻画智能网联汽车中的漏洞","a":"Intelligent Connected Vehicles (ICVs) are a core component of modern transportation systems, and their security is crucial as it directly relates to user safety. Despite prior research, most existing studies focus only on specific sub-components of ICVs due to their inherent complexity. As a result, there is a lack of systematic and comprehensive understanding of ICV vulnerabilities. Moreover, much of the current literature relies on human subjective analysis, such as surveys and interviews, which tends to be high-level and unvalidated, leaving a significant gap between theoretical findings and real-world attacks. To address this issue, we conducted the first large-scale empirical study on ICV vulnerabilities. We began by analyzing existing ICV security literature and summarizing the prevailing taxonomies in terms of vulnerability locations and types. To evaluate their real-world relevance, we collected a total of 649 exploitable vulnerabilities, including 592 from eight ICV vulnerability discovery competitions, Anonymous Cup, between January 2023 and April 2024, covering 48 different vehicles. The remaining 57 vulnerabilities were submitted daily by researchers. Based on this dataset, we assessed the coverage of existing taxonomies and identified several gaps, discovering one new vulnerability locations and 13 new vulnerability types. We further categorized these vulnerabilities into 6 threat types (e.g., privacy data breach) and 4 risk levels (ranging from low to critical), and analyzed common attack surfaces in ICVs. This study provides a comprehensive and data-driven analysis of ICV vulnerabilities, offering actionable insights for researchers, industry practitioners, and policymakers. To support future research, we have made our vulnerability dataset publicly available.","az":"智能网联汽车（ICV）是现代交通系统的核心组成部分，其安全性至关重要，因为它直接关系到用户安全。尽管已有相关研究，由于 ICV 固有的复杂性，多数现有研究只聚焦于其特定子组件。因此，业界缺乏对 ICV 漏洞系统而全面的理解。此外，当前文献大量依赖人的主观分析（如问卷与访谈），往往流于高层且未经验证，在理论结论与真实攻击之间留下显著鸿沟。为解决该问题，我们开展了首个关于 ICV 漏洞的大规模实证研究。我们首先分析已有 ICV 安全文献，总结其在漏洞位置与类型方面的主流分类法。为评估这些分类法的现实相关性，我们共收集了 649 个可利用漏洞，其中 592 个来自 2023 年 1 月至 2024 年 4 月间的八场 ICV 漏洞挖掘竞赛（Anonymous Cup），覆盖 48 款不同车型；其余 57 个由研究者日常提交。基于该数据集，我们评估了现有分类法的覆盖情况并识别出若干空白，发现了一个新的漏洞位置和 13 种新的漏洞类型。我们进一步将这些漏洞归入 6 类威胁（如隐私数据泄露）和 4 个风险等级（从低到严重），并分析了 ICV 中常见的攻击面。本研究提供了对 ICV 漏洞全面、数据驱动的分析，为研究者、工业从业者和政策制定者提供了可操作的洞见。为支持未来研究，我们已公开漏洞数据集。","tl":"用 649 个真实可利用漏洞补全智能网联汽车漏洞分类法空白。","au":["Yuelin Wang","Yuqiao Ning","Yanbang Sun","Xiaofei Xie","Zhihua Xie","Yang Chen","Zhen Guo","Shihao Xue","Junjie Wang","Sen Chen"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","security","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["intelligent connected vehicles","vulnerability taxonomy","real-world exploits","attack surface","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/181/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00668","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"What to Retrieve for Effective Retrieval-Augmented Code Generation? An Empirical Study and Beyond","tz":"有效的检索增强代码生成应该检索什么？一项实证研究及其延伸","a":"Repository-level code generation remains challenging due to complex code dependencies and the limitations of large language models (LLMs) in processing long contexts. While retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) frameworks are widely adopted, the effectiveness of different retrieved information sources—contextual code, APIs, and similar snippets—has not been rigorously analyzed. Through an empirical study on two benchmarks, we demonstrate that in-context code and potential API information significantly enhance LLM performance, whereas retrieved similar code often introduces noise, degrading results by up to 15%. Based on the preliminary results, we propose AllianceCoder, a novel context-integrated method that employs chain-of-thought prompting to decompose user queries into implementation steps and retrieves APIs via semantic description matching. Through extensive experiments on CoderEval and RepoExec, AllianceCoder achieves state-of-the-art performance, improving Pass@1 by 10–20% over existing approaches.","az":"由于复杂的代码依赖以及大语言模型（LLM）处理长上下文的局限，仓库级代码生成依然充满挑战。虽然检索增强生成（RAG）框架被广泛采用，但不同检索信息源（上下文代码、API 和相似代码片段）的有效性尚未得到严格分析。通过在两个基准上的实证研究，我们证明上下文内代码与潜在 API 信息能显著提升 LLM 性能，而检索到的相似代码往往引入噪声，使结果最多退化 15%。基于这些初步结果，我们提出 AllianceCoder，一种新颖的上下文集成方法：采用思维链提示将用户查询分解为实现步骤，并通过语义描述匹配检索 API。在 CoderEval 与 RepoExec 上的大量实验表明，AllianceCoder 取得了最先进的性能，Pass@1 相比现有方法提升 10–20%。","tl":"实证指出相似代码是噪声，改以 API 语义匹配加步骤分解检索。","au":["Wenchao Gu","Juntao Chen","Yanlin Wang","Tianyue Jiang","Xingzhe Li","Mingwei Liu","Xilin Liu","Yuchi Ma","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["retrieval-augmented code generation","repository-level generation","API retrieval","chain-of-thought","empirical analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/182/x"},{"id":"p00669","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Same Same But Different: Preventing Refactoring Attacks on Software Plagiarism Detection","tz":"貌合神离：防范针对软件抄袭检测的重构攻击","a":"Plagiarism detection in programming education faces growing challenges due to increasingly sophisticated obfuscation techniques, particularly automated refactoring-based attacks. While code plagiarism detection systems used in education practice are resilient against basic obfuscation, they struggle against structural modifications that preserve program behavior, especially caused by refactoring-based obfuscation. This paper presents a novel and extensible framework that enhances state-of-the-art detectors by leveraging code property graphs and graph transformations to counteract refactoring-based obfuscation. Our comprehensive evaluation of real-world student submissions, obfuscated using both algorithmic and AI-based obfuscation attacks, demonstrates a significant improvement in detecting plagiarized code.","az":"由于混淆技术日益复杂，尤其是基于自动重构的攻击，编程教育中的抄袭检测正面临越来越大的挑战。虽然教育实践中使用的代码抄袭检测系统能够抵御基础混淆，但它们难以应对保持程序行为的结构性修改，特别是由基于重构的混淆造成的修改。本文提出一个新颖且可扩展的框架，利用代码属性图和图变换来对抗基于重构的混淆，从而增强最先进的检测器。我们在真实学生提交上的全面评估（这些提交同时使用算法式和基于 AI 的混淆攻击进行了混淆）表明，被抄袭代码的检测能力得到显著提升。","tl":"用代码属性图变换归一化重构混淆，恢复抄袭检测能力。","au":["Robin Maisch","Larissa Schmid","Timur Sağlam","Nils Niehues"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["plagiarism detection","code obfuscation","refactoring attack","code property graph","programming education"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/183/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.25057"},{"id":"p00670","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TaCoS: Generated Context Summaries for Task Resumption","tz":"TaCoS：用于任务恢复的自动生成上下文摘要","a":"Interruptions are a frequent challenge in software development, requiring developers to reconstruct both the mental and working context of their tasks. While prior work has proposed visual timelines or manual notes to aid resumption, these approaches either require effort or lack support for mental context reconstruction. Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) offer new opportunities to support task resumption through automatically generated summaries. We present TaCoS, an IDE-integrated tool that generates task context summaries from IDE and browser activity, combining inferred intent, implementation steps, and links to relevant artifacts. We evaluated TaCoS in a controlled lab study with 32 software developers who resumed three programming tasks. Each task was resumed using one of three cues: a manual note, a timeline of recent edits, or a TaCoS-generated summary. The generated summary led to the shortest resumption and edit lag, and was rated as the most helpful cue overall. However, the timeline condition achieved the highest task success rate. Participants valued the summaries’ structured, low-effort presentation of past activity, but noted that they often lacked forward-looking information, which was typically present in the self-authored manual notes. These findings highlight the potential of combining automated summarization with lightweight user annotations to support task resumption in development environments.","az":"中断是软件开发中的常见挑战，迫使开发者重建任务的心智上下文与工作上下文。以往工作提出了可视化时间线或手工笔记来辅助恢复，但这些方法要么需要额外投入精力，要么无法支持心智上下文的重建。大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展为通过自动生成的摘要来支持任务恢复提供了新机会。我们提出 TaCoS，一个集成于 IDE 的工具，可从 IDE 与浏览器活动生成任务上下文摘要，融合推断出的意图、实现步骤以及指向相关制品的链接。我们在一项有 32 名软件开发者参与的受控实验室研究中评估了 TaCoS，参与者需恢复三项编程任务。每项任务使用三种线索之一来恢复：手工笔记、近期编辑的时间线，或 TaCoS 生成的摘要。生成的摘要带来了最短的恢复时延与编辑时延，并被总体评为最有帮助的线索。然而，时间线条件取得了最高的任务成功率。参与者认可摘要以结构化、低投入方式呈现过往活动，但指出摘要常常缺少前瞻性信息，而这类信息通常存在于自己撰写的手工笔记中。这些发现凸显了将自动摘要与轻量级用户标注相结合以支持开发环境中任务恢复的潜力。","tl":"IDE 活动自动生成上下文摘要，实验证明恢复最快但缺前瞻信息。","au":["Alexander Lill","Valentin Hollenstein","Roy Rutishauser","André N. Meyer","Thomas Fritz"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["human-study","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["task resumption","interruption","context summary","IDE tool","controlled experiment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/184/x"},{"id":"p00671","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Unlocking LLM Repair Capabilities Through Cross-Language Translation and Multi-Agent Refinement","tz":"通过跨语言翻译与多智能体精化释放 LLM 的修复能力","a":"Recent advances in leveraging LLMs for APR have demonstrated impressive capabilities in fixing software defects. However, current LLM-based approaches predominantly focus on mainstream programming languages like Java and Python, neglecting less prevalent but emerging languages such as Rust due to expensive training resources, limited datasets, and insufficient community support. This narrow focus creates a significant gap in repair capabilities across the programming language spectrum, where the full potential of LLMs for comprehensive multilingual program repair remains largely unexplored. To address this limitation, we introduce a novel cross-language program repair approach LANTERN that leverages LLMs’ differential proficiency across languages through a multi-agent iterative repair paradigm. Our technique strategically translates defective code from languages where LLMs exhibit weaker repair capabilities to languages where they demonstrate stronger performance, without requiring additional training. A key innovation of our approach is an LLM-based decision-making system that dynamically selects optimal target languages based on bug characteristics and continuously incorporates feedback from previous repair attempts. We evaluate our method on xCodeEval, a comprehensive multilingual benchmark comprising 5,068 bugs across 11 programming languages. Results demonstrate significant enhancement in repair effectiveness, particularly for underrepresented languages, with Rust showing a 22.09% improvement in Pass@10 metrics. Our research provides the first empirical evidence that cross-language translation significantly expands the repair capabilities of LLMs and effectively bridges the performance gap between programming languages with different levels of popularity, opening new avenues for truly language-agnostic automated program repair.","az":"利用 LLM 进行自动程序修复（APR）的最新进展在修复软件缺陷上展现出令人印象深刻的能力。然而，当前基于 LLM 的方法主要聚焦于 Java、Python 等主流编程语言，而忽视了 Rust 等不那么流行但正在兴起的语言，原因在于训练资源昂贵、数据集有限以及社区支持不足。这种狭窄的关注造成了跨编程语言谱系的修复能力鸿沟，LLM 在全面的多语言程序修复上的全部潜力仍基本未被探索。为解决这一局限，我们提出一种新颖的跨语言程序修复方法 LANTERN，它通过多智能体迭代修复范式来利用 LLM 在不同语言上的能力差异。我们的技术有策略地将缺陷代码从 LLM 修复能力较弱的语言翻译到其表现更强的语言，且无需额外训练。该方法的一个关键创新是基于 LLM 的决策系统，它依据缺陷特征动态选择最优目标语言，并持续吸纳先前修复尝试的反馈。我们在 xCodeEval 上评估了该方法，这是一个涵盖 11 种编程语言、包含 5,068 个缺陷的综合多语言基准。结果表明修复有效性显著提升，尤其是对代表性不足的语言，Rust 在 Pass@10 指标上提升 22.09%。我们的研究首次提供了实证证据，表明跨语言翻译能显著扩展 LLM 的修复能力，并有效弥合不同流行度编程语言之间的性能差距，为真正语言无关的自动程序修复开辟了新途径。","tl":"把缺陷代码译到模型更擅长的语言再修，Rust 修复率大涨。","au":["Wenqiang LUO","Jacky Keung","Boyang Yang","Jacques Klein","Tegawendé F. Bissyandé","Haoye Tian","Xuan-Bach D. Le"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","agentic","low-resource-or-non-english"],"kw":["automated program repair","cross-language translation","multi-agent refinement","xCodeEval","Rust"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/185/x"},{"id":"p00672","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MioHint: LLM-Assisted Request Mutation for Whitebox REST API Testing","tz":"MioHint：面向白盒 REST API 测试的 LLM 辅助请求变异","a":"Cloud applications heavily rely on APIs to communicate with each other and exchange data. To ensure the reliability of cloud applications, cloud providers widely adopt API testing techniques. Unfortunately, existing API testing approaches are insufficient to reach strict conditions, a problem known as fitness plateaus, due to the lack of a gradient provided by coverage metrics. To address this issue, we propose MioHint, a novel white-box API testing approach that leverages the code comprehension capabilities of LLM to boost API testing. The key challenge of LLM-based API testing lies in system-level testing, which emphasizes the dependencies between requests and targets across functions and files, thereby making the entire codebase the object of analysis. However, feeding the entire codebase to an LLM is impractical due to its limited context length and short memory. MioHint addresses this challenge by synergizing static analysis with LLMs. We retrieve relevant code with data-dependency analysis at the statement level, including def-use analysis for variables used in the target and function expansion for subfunctions called by the target. To evaluate the effectiveness of our method, we conducted experiments across 16 real-world REST API services. The findings reveal that MioHint achieves an average increase of 4.95% in line coverage compared to the baseline, EvoMaster, alongside a remarkable factor of 67x improvement in mutation accuracy. Furthermore, our method successfully covers over 57% of hard-to-cover targets, while in the baseline, the coverage is less than 10%.","az":"云应用高度依赖 API 相互通信并交换数据。为确保云应用的可靠性，云服务商广泛采用 API 测试技术。遗憾的是，由于覆盖率指标无法提供梯度，现有 API 测试方法难以触及严格条件，这一问题被称为适应度平台期（fitness plateaus）。为解决该问题，我们提出 MioHint，一种新颖的白盒 API 测试方法，利用 LLM 的代码理解能力来增强 API 测试。基于 LLM 的 API 测试的关键挑战在于系统级测试：它强调请求与目标之间跨函数、跨文件的依赖关系，从而使整个代码库都成为分析对象。然而，由于上下文长度有限且记忆较短，将整个代码库喂给 LLM 并不现实。MioHint 通过将静态分析与 LLM 协同来应对这一挑战：我们在语句级别用数据依赖分析检索相关代码，包括对目标中所用变量的定义-使用（def-use）分析，以及对目标所调用子函数的函数展开。为评估方法有效性，我们在 16 个真实 REST API 服务上开展实验。结果显示，MioHint 相比基线 EvoMaster 平均提升 4.95% 的行覆盖率，同时变异准确率提升高达 67 倍。此外，我们的方法成功覆盖了超过 57% 的难覆盖目标，而基线的覆盖率不足 10%。","tl":"用语句级数据依赖检索喂 LLM 做请求变异，突破覆盖平台期。","au":["Jia Li","Jiacheng Shen","Yuxin Su","Michael Lyu"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["REST API testing","white-box testing","request mutation","data-dependency analysis","fitness plateau"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/186/x"},{"id":"p00673","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ConfuGuard: Using Metadata to Detect Active and Stealthy Package Confusion Attacks Accurately and at Scale","tz":"ConfuGuard：利用元数据准确且大规模地检测活跃且隐蔽的软件包混淆攻击","a":"Package confusion attacks such as typosquatting threaten software supply chains. Attackers make packages with names that syntactically or semantically resemble legitimate ones, tricking engineers into installing malware. While prior work has developed defenses against package confusions in some software package registries, notably NPM, PyPI, and RubyGems, gaps remain: high false-positive rates, generalization to more software package ecosystems, and insights from real-world deployment. In this work, we introduce ConfuGuard, a state-of-art detector for package confusion threats. We begin by presenting the first empirical analysis of benign signals derived from prior package confusion data, uncovering their threat patterns, engineering practices, and measurable attributes. Advancing existing detectors, we leverage package metadata to distinguish benign packages, and extend support from three up to seven software package registries. Our approach significantly reduces false positive rates (from 80% to 28%), at the cost of an additional 14𝑠 average latency to filter out benign packages by analyzing the package metadata. ConfuGuard is used in production at our industry partner, whose analysts have already confirmed 630 real attacks detected by ConfuGuard.","az":"诸如域名/包名抢注（typosquatting）之类的软件包混淆攻击威胁着软件供应链。攻击者制作名称在句法或语义上与合法包相似的软件包，诱骗工程师安装恶意软件。虽然已有工作为部分软件包注册中心（特别是 NPM、PyPI 和 RubyGems）开发了针对包混淆的防御，但仍存在空白：高误报率、向更多软件包生态的推广，以及来自真实部署的洞见。在本工作中，我们提出 ConfuGuard，一个面向包混淆威胁的最先进检测器。我们首先给出对既往包混淆数据中良性信号的首个实证分析，揭示其威胁模式、工程实践与可度量属性。在推进现有检测器的基础上，我们利用软件包元数据来区分良性包，并将支持范围从三个扩展到七个软件包注册中心。我们的方法显著降低了误报率（从 80% 降至 28%），代价是通过分析包元数据过滤良性包所引入的平均 14 秒额外延迟。ConfuGuard 已在我们的工业合作伙伴处投入生产使用，其分析人员已确认 ConfuGuard 检测到的 630 起真实攻击。","tl":"用包元数据识别良性信号，把包名混淆检测误报从 80% 降到 28%。","au":["Wenxin Jiang","Berk Çakar","Mikola Lysenko","James C. Davis"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["package confusion","typosquatting","software supply chain","package metadata","false positive reduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/187/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.20528"},{"id":"p00674","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Variability-Aware Fuzzing","tz":"可变性感知的模糊测试","a":"Modern software systems often provide a vast configuration space to enhance reusability and adaptability, but this configurability also significantly complicates bug finding. While existing static and dynamic variability-aware analysis approaches systematically explore the configuration space, they often suffer from scalability limitations. Conversely, grey-box fuzzing has demonstrated remarkable success in vulnerability detection through lightweight, iterative input space exploration, yet the state-of-the-art configuration fuzzers overlook the potential of integrating variability-aware analysis within the fuzzing process. In this paper, we present VAFuzz, a novel variability-aware fuzzer that integrates principled dynamic variability-aware analysis within the fuzzing process to enhance configuration space exploration. VAFuzz introduces new variability-aware seed selection and mutations to drive the fuzzing process. These are enabled by a new presence condition seed queue that tracks coverage and crash contributions across the configuration space, and a map that captures the relationship between data seeds and presence conditions. Our evaluation on a diverse set of programs show that VAFuzz outperforms the state-of-the-art configuration fuzzers on 21 out of 25 programs in terms of code coverage. It also detects more vulnerabilities than these baselines, including previous unknown bugs.","az":"现代软件系统常常提供庞大的配置空间以增强可复用性与适应性，但这种可配置性也显著增加了缺陷发现的难度。现有的静态与动态可变性感知分析方法虽能系统地探索配置空间，却往往受限于可扩展性。相反，灰盒模糊测试凭借轻量、迭代的输入空间探索在漏洞检测上取得了显著成功，但最先进的配置模糊测试工具忽视了在模糊测试过程中集成可变性感知分析的潜力。本文提出 VAFuzz，一种新颖的可变性感知模糊测试工具，它在模糊测试过程中集成了有原则的动态可变性感知分析，以增强配置空间探索。VAFuzz 引入了新的可变性感知种子选择与变异策略来驱动模糊测试过程；这得益于一个新的存在条件（presence condition）种子队列（用于跟踪配置空间中的覆盖与崩溃贡献），以及一个刻画数据种子与存在条件之间关系的映射。我们在一组多样化程序上的评估显示，VAFuzz 在 25 个程序中的 21 个上在代码覆盖率方面优于最先进的配置模糊测试工具，并且比这些基线检测出更多漏洞，包括此前未知的缺陷。","tl":"把存在条件引入种子队列与变异，让模糊测试兼顾配置空间。","au":["Meah Tahmeed Ahmed","Arnab Dev","Shiyi Wei"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["variability-aware fuzzing","configuration space","presence condition","seed selection","greybox fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/188/x","pu":"https://chaoticcross12.github.io/papers/Variability-Aware%20Fuzzing.pdf"},{"id":"p00675","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Empirical Study on the Robustness of Android Third-Party Library Detection Tools Against Advanced Obfuscation","tz":"关于 Android 第三方库检测工具抵御高级混淆鲁棒性的实证研究","a":"Third-party libraries (TPLs) play a crucial role in Android app development by providing reusable functionalities, improving development efficiency, and reducing time-to-market. However, detecting and analyzing TPLs is essential, as their vulnerabilities, outdated versions, or malicious modifications can introduce security risks and compromise the integrity of Android apps. Existing TPL detection approaches struggle against code obfuscation, a prevalent practice in Android apps. While prior research has explored obfuscation-resistant detection methods, they largely overlook advanced obfuscation techniques such as package hierarchy obfuscation. To bridge this gap, we first investigate the prevalence of advanced obfuscation in contemporary Android apps using ObfDetector, a novel static analysis tool capable of detecting identifier renaming, package hierarchy obfuscation, and code optimization. Our large-scale study on 77,504 closed-source Google Play apps and 619 widely used apps reveals extensive obfuscation adoption. We further evaluate the resilience of state-of-the-art TPL detection tools under realistic obfuscation conditions using a newly constructed benchmark dataset, exposing significant performance deficiencies, with F1-scores dropping below 50% for library-level detection and under 10% for version-level identification. Finally, we conduct a systematic failure analysis to uncover key architectural limitations in existing TPL detection frameworks and propose design guidelines for next-generation detection tools. We release our obfuscation detection tool and benchmark dataset to support further research in Android security.","az":"第三方库（TPL）通过提供可复用功能、提升开发效率并缩短上市时间，在 Android 应用开发中扮演关键角色。然而，检测与分析 TPL 十分必要，因为其漏洞、过时版本或恶意修改会引入安全风险并破坏 Android 应用的完整性。现有的 TPL 检测方法难以应对代码混淆，而混淆在 Android 应用中十分普遍。尽管以往研究探索过抗混淆的检测方法，它们大多忽视了诸如包层次结构混淆等高级混淆技术。为弥合这一空白，我们首先使用 ObfDetector（一种能够检测标识符重命名、包层次结构混淆与代码优化的新型静态分析工具）考察当代 Android 应用中高级混淆的流行程度。我们对 77,504 个闭源 Google Play 应用和 619 个广泛使用的应用开展的大规模研究揭示了混淆的广泛采用。我们进一步使用新构建的基准数据集，在真实混淆条件下评估最先进 TPL 检测工具的鲁棒性，暴露出显著的性能缺陷：库级检测的 F1 分数降至 50% 以下，版本级识别更低于 10%。最后，我们进行了系统的失败分析，揭示现有 TPL 检测框架的关键架构局限，并为下一代检测工具提出设计准则。我们公开了混淆检测工具与基准数据集，以支持 Android 安全的后续研究。","tl":"大规模实测显示高级混淆下 TPL 版本识别 F1 跌破 10%。","au":["Dahan Pan","Zhuohao Zhang","Yunjia Min","Runhan Feng","Yuanyuan Zhang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["third-party library detection","Android obfuscation","package hierarchy obfuscation","benchmark","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/189/x"},{"id":"p00676","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SAFE: Harnessing LLM for Scenario-Driven ADS Testing from Multimodal Crash Data","tz":"SAFE：利用 LLM 从多模态碰撞数据驱动自动驾驶系统的场景化测试","a":"Ensuring the safety of Autonomous Driving Systems (ADS) requires realistic and reproducible test scenarios, yet extracting such scenarios from multimodal crash reports remains a major challenge. Large Language Models (LLMs) often hallucinate and lose map structure, resulting in unrealistic road layouts and vehicle behaviors. To address this, we introduce SAFE, a novel Scenario-based ADS testing Framework via multimodal Extraction, which leverages Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), knowledge-grounded prompting, Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning, and self-validation to improve scenario reconstruction from multimodal crash data. SAFE achieves 93.8% accuracy in extracting road network details, 80.0% for actor information, and 100% for environmental context. In human studies, SAFE outperforms LCTGen and AC3R in reconstructing consistent road networks and vehicle behaviors. Under identical ADS and simulator settings, SAFE detects 39 and 71 more safety violations than LCTGen and AC3R, respectively, and reproduces 12 more real world crash cases than LCTGen. On 19 cases supported by AC3R, SAFE reproduces one additional crash case with statistically significant gains across five runs. It generates scenarios within 25 seconds and triggers violations after just 1 case (IDM), 3 cases (PPO), and 1 case (BeamNG). Unlike AC3R, SAFE is ontology-free and generalizes to a broader range of crash scenarios. Code: https://anonymous.4open.science/r/SAFE-8404/README.md","az":"保障自动驾驶系统（ADS）的安全需要真实且可复现的测试场景，然而从多模态碰撞报告中抽取此类场景仍是一大挑战。大语言模型（LLM）常常产生幻觉并丢失地图结构，导致不真实的道路布局与车辆行为。为解决该问题，我们提出 SAFE——一个基于多模态抽取的场景化 ADS 测试框架，它利用检索增强生成（RAG）、知识锚定提示、思维链（CoT）推理以及自我校验，来改进从多模态碰撞数据中重建场景的效果。SAFE 在抽取道路网络细节上达到 93.8% 的准确率，行为体信息达到 80.0%，环境上下文达到 100%。在人类被试研究中，SAFE 在重建一致的道路网络与车辆行为方面优于 LCTGen 和 AC3R。在相同的 ADS 与仿真器设置下，SAFE 分别比 LCTGen 和 AC3R 多检测出 39 和 71 条安全违规，并比 LCTGen 多复现 12 个真实世界碰撞案例。在 AC3R 支持的 19 个案例上，SAFE 多复现了一个碰撞案例，且在五次运行中取得统计显著的提升。它能在 25 秒内生成场景，并分别在 1 个案例（IDM）、3 个案例（PPO）和 1 个案例（BeamNG）后就触发违规。与 AC3R 不同，SAFE 无需本体（ontology-free），并可泛化到更广泛的碰撞场景。代码：https://anonymous.4open.science/r/SAFE-8404/README.md","tl":"用 RAG 加自校验从多模态碰撞报告重建可复现 ADS 测试场景。","au":["Siwei Luo","Yang Zhang","Yao Deng","Linfeng Liang","Xi Zheng"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving testing","scenario reconstruction","multimodal crash reports","retrieval-augmented generation","safety violation detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/190/x"},{"id":"p00677","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Minimizing Breaking Changes and Redundancy in Mitigating Technical Lag for Java Projects","tz":"以最小的破坏性变更与冗余来缓解 Java 项目的技术滞后","a":"Re-using open-source software (OSS) can avoid reinventing the wheel, but failing to keep it up-to-date can lead to missing new features and persistent bugs or vulnerabilities that have already been resolved. The use of outdated OSS introduces technical lag, necessitating timely upgrades. However, maintaining up-to-date libraries is challenging, as it may introduce incompatibility issues that break the project or redundant dependencies that unnecessarily increase the size of the project. These issues discourage developers from upgrading libraries, highlighting the need for a fully automated solution that balances version upgrades, reduces technical lag, ensures compatibility, and avoids redundant dependencies. To this end, we propose DepUpdater, which ensures that upgrades minimize technical lag as much as possible while avoiding incompatibility issues and redundant dependencies. The comparison with existing dependency management tools demonstrates that DepUpdater more effectively reduces technical lag while ensuring compatibility and pruning redundant dependencies. Additionally, an ablation study highlights the potential benefits of considering pruning requirements during upgrades to mitigate incompatibility issues. Finally, leveraging DepUpdater, we investigate the impact of transitive dependency upgrades on client compatibility, providing insights for future research.","az":"复用开源软件（OSS）可以避免重复造轮子，但若不能保持其及时更新，就会错失新特性并遗留已被修复的缺陷或漏洞。使用过时的 OSS 会引入技术滞后（technical lag），因而需要及时升级。然而，保持库的最新状态颇具挑战，因为升级可能引入破坏项目的不兼容问题，或引入不必要增大项目体积的冗余依赖。这些问题令开发者不愿升级库，凸显了对一种全自动方案的需求：该方案需在版本升级、降低技术滞后、保证兼容性与避免冗余依赖之间取得平衡。为此，我们提出 DepUpdater，它在避免不兼容问题与冗余依赖的同时，尽可能地最小化技术滞后。与现有依赖管理工具的比较表明，DepUpdater 能更有效地降低技术滞后，同时保证兼容性并裁剪冗余依赖。此外，消融实验凸显了在升级过程中考虑裁剪需求以缓解不兼容问题的潜在收益。最后，我们利用 DepUpdater 研究了传递依赖升级对客户端兼容性的影响，为未来研究提供了洞见。","tl":"升级依赖时同时优化滞后、兼容性与冗余三者。","au":["Rui Lu","Lyuye Zhang","Kaixuan Li","Min Zhang","Yixiang Chen"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["technical lag","dependency upgrade","breaking changes","redundant dependencies","Java build"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/191/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.06762"},{"id":"p00678","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"BFix: Automated Safe Memory-Leak Fixing for Binary Code","tz":"BFix：面向二进制代码的安全内存泄漏自动修复","a":"Fixing memory leaks in software is crucial to improving system efficiency, reliability, and stability. Nevertheless, manually fixing memory leaks is not only time-consuming but also error-prone. Recent research has proposed program repair techniques to fix memory leaks automatically. However, a common limitation of prior techniques is that they cannot tackle memory leaks in binary code. Given the huge popularity of binary code, it is highly necessary to fix its hidden memory leaks. To this end, this paper presents BFix, the first-ever binary-level memory-leak fixing tool. BFix creates effective binary analysis techniques to overcome the unique technical challenges of automatically and safely fixing memory leaks in binaries. Our experiments show that BFix can achieve promising fixing effectiveness and efficiency, comparable to state-of-the-art source-level fixing tools. Meanwhile, it has a negligible impact on binary code size and performance.","az":"修复软件中的内存泄漏对于提升系统效率、可靠性与稳定性至关重要。然而，手工修复内存泄漏不仅耗时，而且容易出错。近期研究提出了自动修复内存泄漏的程序修复技术，但既有技术的共同局限在于无法处理二进制代码中的内存泄漏。鉴于二进制代码的广泛存在，修复其中隐藏的内存泄漏非常必要。为此，本文提出 BFix——首个二进制层面的内存泄漏修复工具。BFix 设计了有效的二进制分析技术，以克服在二进制中自动且安全地修复内存泄漏所面临的独特技术挑战。实验表明，BFix 能取得可观的修复效果与效率，可与最先进的源码级修复工具相媲美；同时，它对二进制代码体积与性能的影响可忽略不计。","tl":"首个在二进制层面安全修复内存泄漏的工具。","au":["Wen Zhang","Botang Xiao","Qingchen Kong","Boyang Yi","Suxin Ji","Yage Hu","Songlan Wang","Wenwen Wang"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["memory leak repair","binary analysis","automated program repair","safe patching"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/192/x"},{"id":"p00679","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Remediating Superfluous Re-Rendering in React Applications","tz":"修复 React 应用中的冗余重渲染","a":"React is an extremely popular framework for constructing user interfaces (UIs). A React UI is organized as a tree of components, each of which is defined by a function that returns a literal written in JSX, a syntactic extension of JavaScript consisting of a combination of XML tags, executable JavaScript code, and references to sub-components. React supports incremental re rendering by maintaining an in-memory representation of a web page’s Document Object Model (DOM) and automatically calculating a set of minimal changes that must be applied to the DOM when state changes occur. However, React’s semantics are complex and subtle, and programmers often write code that gives rise to unnecessary re-rendering, which hurts performance and responsiveness. We identify 5 React anti-patterns that give rise to unnecessary re-rendering, present a static analysis for detecting them, and rewrite rules that suggest how to refactor the code to improve rendering performance. The static analysis is potentially unsound, so developers should carefully review the suggested refactorings. A survey of 7,758 React repositories showed that 92.1% of them exhibit at least one anti-pattern, and careful experimental evaluation on 23 React projects revealed that the suggested refactoring reduces the number of rendering operations by 33.3% on average while preserving application behavior in all but one case. With a small increase in code complexity, we find an average reduction in rendering time of 20.54%, and three case studies reveal that the refactorings can greatly improve application responsiveness as the number of components scales.","az":"React 是构建用户界面（UI）的极为流行的框架。React 的 UI 被组织为组件树，每个组件由一个返回 JSX 字面量的函数定义；JSX 是 JavaScript 的语法扩展，由 XML 标签、可执行 JavaScript 代码以及对子组件的引用组合而成。React 通过在内存中维护网页文档对象模型（DOM）的表示，并在状态变化时自动计算必须施加到 DOM 上的最小变更集合，来支持增量重渲染。然而，React 的语义复杂而微妙，程序员常常写出导致不必要重渲染的代码，从而损害性能与响应性。我们识别出 5 种会引发不必要重渲染的 React 反模式，提出用于检测它们的静态分析，以及提示如何重构代码以提升渲染性能的重写规则。该静态分析可能是不健全（unsound）的，因此开发者应仔细审阅建议的重构。对 7,758 个 React 仓库的调查显示，其中 92.1% 至少存在一种反模式；在 23 个 React 项目上的细致实验评估表明，所建议的重构平均减少 33.3% 的渲染操作，且除一个案例外均保持了应用行为。在代码复杂度略有增加的代价下，我们发现渲染时间平均减少 20.54%，三个案例研究显示这些重构能在组件数量增长时显著提升应用响应性。","tl":"识别 5 类 React 反模式并重构，平均减少 33.3% 渲染。","au":["Farideh Khalili","Satyajit Gokhale","Alexi Turcotte","Dale Xu","Frank Tip"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["React","re-rendering","anti-patterns","static analysis","refactoring rules"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/193/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3773235","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00680","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Training on Clean Data but Getting Backdoored Models! A Poisoning Attack on Code Encoders","tz":"在干净数据上训练却得到带后门的模型！针对代码编码器的投毒攻击","a":"Transformer-based code encoders like CodeBERT learn general knowledge from vast amounts of unlabeled source code. These encoders can convert input code into meaningful representations (i.e., code embeddings) and support a series of downstream tasks. Specifically, users can fine-tune a code encoder on certain datasets and obtain strong model performance on corresponding tasks. Re cent studies have exposed critical security vulnerabilities in this widely-adopted paradigm: attackers can inject backdoors into mod els by poisoning the fine-tuning datasets with carefully crafted triggers (e.g., dead code snippets), causing the model to produce attacker-specified outputs when these triggers are present. However, backdoor attacks rely on a strong and often unrealistic assumption: attackers can directly poison the fine-tuning data and developers will unknowingly use these compromised datasets. It motivates us to propose a novel method and expose a new stealthy backdoor attack scenario: attackers can directly poison and release poisoned encoders; even when users fine-tune the poisoned encoder on clean datasets, the obtained model inherits the backdoor! This method bypasses the aforementioned unrealistic assumption and is thus easier to operate. Additionally, it fundamentaly undermines existing defenses that focus on detecting user-side data poisoning as the latter does not happen at all. As a proof-of-concept, we evaluate the proposed attack on three popular pre-trained models across three software engineering tasks. Experiments show that the attack is both (1) effective: the average attack success rate can reach 91.62% and (2) stealthy: the decrease in model performance is 1.26%, unnoticeable by users. We additionally show that existing popular defenses cannot alarm the users when triggers appear in model inputs. These findings expose a critical blind spot in pre-trained code models and highlight the urgent need for automated defenses.","az":"像 CodeBERT 这样基于 Transformer 的代码编码器从海量无标注源码中学习通用知识。这些编码器可以将输入代码转换为有意义的表示（即代码嵌入），并支撑一系列下游任务。具体而言，用户可以在特定数据集上微调代码编码器，从而在相应任务上获得强劲的模型性能。近期研究揭示了这一被广泛采用范式中的关键安全漏洞：攻击者可以通过用精心构造的触发器（例如死代码片段）投毒微调数据集，向模型中注入后门，使模型在触发器出现时产生攻击者指定的输出。然而，后门攻击依赖一个很强且往往不现实的假设：攻击者能够直接投毒微调数据，并且开发者会在不知情的情况下使用这些被污染的数据集。这促使我们提出一种新方法并揭示一种新的隐蔽后门攻击场景：攻击者可以直接投毒并发布被污染的编码器；即使用户在干净数据集上微调这个被投毒的编码器，所得到的模型仍会继承后门！该方法绕过了上述不现实的假设，因而更易实施。此外，它从根本上瓦解了那些聚焦于检测用户侧数据投毒的现有防御，因为用户侧投毒根本没有发生。作为概念验证，我们在三个流行的预训练模型上、跨三项软件工程任务评估了所提出的攻击。实验表明该攻击既（1）有效：平均攻击成功率可达 91.62%，又（2）隐蔽：模型性能下降仅 1.26%，用户难以察觉。我们还进一步表明，现有的流行防御在触发器出现于模型输入时无法向用户报警。这些发现暴露了预训练代码模型中的一个关键盲点，并凸显了对自动化防御的迫切需求。","tl":"投毒编码器本身，干净微调后后门仍被继承。","au":["Yiran Xiao","Xiangyue Liu","Zhou Yang","Lili Bo","Xiaobing Sun"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","llm-based"],"kw":["backdoor attack","code encoder","poisoned pre-trained model","CodeBERT","attack success rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/194/x"},{"id":"p00681","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Bounded Exhaustive Random Program Generation for Testing Solidity Compilers","tz":"面向 Solidity 编译器测试的有界穷举随机程序生成","a":"By July 2025, smart contracts have collectively overseen assets about $120 billion. Since Solidity is the leading language for developing smart contracts, ensuring the correctness of Solidity compilers is critically important. However, Solidity compilers are prone to bugs, with recent studies revealing that combinations of qualifiers in Solidity programs are the primary cause of compiler crashes, accounting for 40.48% of all historical crashes. While random program generators are widely used for compiler testing, they are less effective at finding Solidity compiler bugs because they explore the unbounded space of possible programs rather than concentrating on the specific subspace related to bug-prone qualifiers. A promising idea for finding qualifier-related bugs is to bound the search space based on empirical evidence of where such bugs are likely to occur, specifically focusing test generation to target subspaces with rich combinations of qualifiers. To address this, we propose bounded exhaustive random program generation, a novel approach that dynamically bounds the search space, enhancing the likelihood of uncovering Solidity compiler bugs. Specifically, our method bounds the search space by generating valid program templates that abstract those programs using bug-prone qualifiers and then applies these templates to guide program generation for compiler testing. Mechanisms are devised to address the technical challenges regarding validity and efficiency. We have implemented our novel generation approach in a new tool, Erwin. We have used Erwin to find and report 26 bugs across two Solidity compilers, solc and solang, and one Solidity static analyzer, slither. Among these, 23 were previously unknown, 18 have been confirmed, and 10 have been fixed. Evaluation results demonstrate that Erwin outperforms state-of-the-art Solidity fuzzers in bug detection and complements developer-written test suites by covering 4,599 edges and 14,824 lines of the solc compiler that were missed by solc’s unit tests.","az":"截至 2025 年 7 月，智能合约共计管理着约 1200 亿美元的资产。由于 Solidity 是开发智能合约的主流语言，保证 Solidity 编译器的正确性至关重要。然而，Solidity 编译器容易出现缺陷，近期研究显示 Solidity 程序中限定符（qualifier）的组合是编译器崩溃的主要原因，占历史崩溃的 40.48%。虽然随机程序生成器被广泛用于编译器测试，但它们在发现 Solidity 编译器缺陷方面效果较差，因为它们探索的是无界的程序空间，而非聚焦于与易出错限定符相关的特定子空间。发现限定符相关缺陷的一个有前景的思路是：依据关于此类缺陷易出现位置的经验证据来限定搜索空间，即将测试生成聚焦到限定符组合丰富的子空间。为此，我们提出有界穷举随机程序生成——一种动态限定搜索空间的新方法，以提升发现 Solidity 编译器缺陷的可能性。具体而言，我们的方法通过生成有效的程序模板来限定搜索空间，这些模板对使用易出错限定符的程序进行抽象，随后应用这些模板来指导用于编译器测试的程序生成。我们设计了相应机制以应对有效性与效率方面的技术挑战。我们在新工具 Erwin 中实现了这一新颖的生成方法，并用 Erwin 在两个 Solidity 编译器（solc 与 solang）以及一个 Solidity 静态分析器（slither）中发现并报告了 26 个缺陷。其中 23 个此前未知，18 个已被确认，10 个已被修复。评估结果表明，Erwin 在缺陷检测上优于最先进的 Solidity 模糊测试工具，并能补充开发者编写的测试套件——它覆盖了 solc 单元测试未覆盖的 4,599 条边和 14,824 行代码。","tl":"用限定符模板有界穷举生成程序，挖出 23 个新编译器缺陷。","au":["Haoyang Ma","Alastair F. Donaldson","Qingchao Shen","Yongqiang Tian","Junjie Chen","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Solidity compiler testing","random program generation","bounded exhaustive","qualifier combinations","solc"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/195/x"},{"id":"p00682","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"HistoryFinder: Advancing Method-Level Source Code History Generation with Accurate Oracles and Enhanced Algorithm","tz":"HistoryFinder：以准确的标准答案与增强算法推进方法级源码历史生成","a":"Reconstructing a method’s change history efficiently and accurately is critical for many software engineering tasks, including maintenance, refactoring, and comprehension. Despite the availability of method history generation tools such as CodeShovel and CodeTracker, existing evaluations of their effectiveness are limited by inaccuracies in the ground truth oracles used. In this study, we systematically construct two new oracles—the corrected CodeShovel oracle and a newly developed HistoryFinder oracle—by combining automated analysis with expert-guided manual validation. We also introduce HistoryFinder, a new method history generation tool designed to improve not only the accuracy and completeness of method change histories but also to offer competitive runtime performance. Through extensive evaluation across 400 methods from 40 open-source repositories, we show that HistoryFinder consistently outperforms CodeShovel, CodeTracker, IntelliJ, and Git-based baselines in terms of precision, recall, and F1 score. Moreover, HistoryFinder achieves competitive runtime performance, offering the lowest mean and median execution times among all the research-based tools. While Git-based tools exhibit the fastest runtimes, this efficiency comes at the cost of significantly lower precision and recall—leaving HistoryFinder as the best overall choice when both accuracy and efficiency are important. To facilitate adoption, we provide a web interface, CLI, and Java library for flexible usage.","az":"高效而准确地重建一个方法的变更历史，对许多软件工程任务（包括维护、重构与理解）都至关重要。尽管已有 CodeShovel 和 CodeTracker 等方法历史生成工具，但对其有效性的既有评估因所用标准答案（oracle）不准确而受限。在本研究中，我们通过将自动化分析与专家指导的人工验证相结合，系统性地构建了两个新的 oracle——修正后的 CodeShovel oracle 与全新开发的 HistoryFinder oracle。我们还提出了 HistoryFinder，一个新的方法历史生成工具，旨在不仅提升方法变更历史的准确性与完整性，还提供有竞争力的运行时性能。通过在来自 40 个开源仓库的 400 个方法上的广泛评估，我们表明 HistoryFinder 在精确率、召回率与 F1 分数上一致地优于 CodeShovel、CodeTracker、IntelliJ 以及基于 Git 的基线。此外，HistoryFinder 取得了有竞争力的运行时性能，在所有研究型工具中拥有最低的平均与中位执行时间。虽然基于 Git 的工具运行最快，但这种效率是以显著更低的精确率与召回率为代价的——因此在同时看重准确性与效率时，HistoryFinder 是整体上的最佳选择。为便于采用，我们提供了 Web 界面、命令行工具与 Java 库以供灵活使用。","tl":"重建更准的方法历史 oracle，并给出更优的生成工具。","au":["Md Shahidul Islam","S M Ashik Aowal","Md Sharif Uddin","Shaiful Chowdhury"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","benchmark-dataset","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["method history generation","code change tracking","ground truth oracle","CodeShovel","repository mining"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/196/x"},{"id":"p00683","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Metronome: Differentiated Delay Scheduling for Serverless Functions","tz":"Metronome：面向无服务器函数的差异化延迟调度","a":"Function-as-a-Service (FaaS) computing is an emerging cloud computing paradigm for its ease-of-management and elasticity. However, optimizing function scheduling in serverless environments remains challenging due to their dynamic and event-driven nature. While data locality has been proven effective in traditional cluster computing systems through delay scheduling, its application in serverless platforms remains largely unexplored. In this paper, we systematically evaluate existing delay scheduling methods in serverless environments and identify three key observations: 1) delay scheduling benefits vary significantly based on function input characteristics; 2) serverless computing exhibits more complex locality patterns than traditional cluster computing systems, encompassing both data locality and infrastructure locality; and 3) heterogeneous function execution times make rule-based delay thresholds ineffective. Based on these insights, we propose Metronome, a differentiated delay scheduling framework that employs predictive mechanisms to identify optimal locality-aware nodes for individual functions. Metronome leverages an online Random Forest Regression model to forecast function execution times across various nodes, enabling informed delay decisions while preventing SLA violations. Our implementation on OpenLambda demonstrates that Metronome significantly outperforms baseline approaches, achieving 64.88%-95.83% reduction in mean execution time for functions, while maintaining performance advantages under increased concurrency levels and ensuring SLA compliance.","az":"函数即服务（FaaS）因易于管理与弹性伸缩而成为新兴的云计算范式。然而，由于其动态与事件驱动的本质，优化无服务器环境中的函数调度仍具挑战。虽然数据局部性已在传统集群计算系统中通过延迟调度被证明有效，但其在无服务器平台中的应用在很大程度上仍未被探索。本文系统评估了无服务器环境中现有的延迟调度方法，并得出三点关键观察：1）延迟调度的收益随函数输入特征的不同而显著变化；2）无服务器计算展现出比传统集群计算系统更复杂的局部性模式，同时涵盖数据局部性与基础设施局部性；3）函数执行时间的异构性使得基于规则的延迟阈值失效。基于这些洞见，我们提出 Metronome——一个差异化延迟调度框架，采用预测机制为各个函数识别最优的局部性感知节点。Metronome 利用在线随机森林回归模型预测函数在不同节点上的执行时间，从而在避免违反 SLA 的同时做出有依据的延迟决策。我们在 OpenLambda 上的实现表明，Metronome 显著优于基线方法，使函数的平均执行时间降低 64.88%–95.83%，并在更高并发水平下保持性能优势且确保 SLA 合规。","tl":"按函数预测执行时间做差异化延迟调度，兼顾局部性与 SLA。","au":["Zhuangbin Chen","Juzheng Zheng","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["serverless","delay scheduling","data locality","FaaS","execution time prediction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/197/x"},{"id":"p00684","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Memory-Efficient Large Language Models for Program Repair with Semantic-Guided Patch Generation","tz":"面向程序修复的内存高效大语言模型：语义引导的补丁生成","a":"Fixing software bugs is crucial yet demands significant resources from developers. Automated Program Repair (APR) is a promising solution to address this challenging task. The emergence of Large Language Models (LLMs) has opened a new era of LLM-based APR, substantially advancing the APR field further. LLM-based APR methods face significant challenges regarding memory inefficiency, hindering their scalability and effectiveness. This is largely due to the beam search utilized in the patch generation phase of LLM-based APR, which requires large beam sizes to search for more potentially good repair candidates. In this paper, we first show that increases in beam size, even for small-sized LLMs (1B-7B params), require extensive GPU usage, leading to up to 80% of recurring crashes due to memory overloads in LLM-based APR. Seemingly simple solutions to reduce memory consumption are (1) to quantize LLM models, i.e., converting the weights of an LLM from high-precision values to lower-precision ones, and (2) to make beam search sequential, i.e., forwarding each beam through the model sequentially and then concatenating them back into a single output. However, we show that these approaches still do not work via both theoretical analysis and experiments. To address this, we introduce FLAMES, a novel LLM-based APR technique that employs semantic-guided patch generation to enhance repair effectiveness and memory efficiency. Unlike conventional methods that rely on beam search, FLAMES utilizes greedy decoding to enhance memory efficiency while steering the search towards more potentially good repair candidates via a semanticguided best-first search algorithm. At each decoding step, FLAMES uses semantic feedback from test validation, such as the number of passing and failing test cases, to select the most promising token to explore further. Our empirical evaluation on Defects4J shows that FLAMES substantially reduces memory consumption by up to 83% compared to LLM-based APR without compromising time efficiency. Moreover, FLAMES correctly fixes 133 bugs on Defects4J, fixing 10 bugs more than the best baseline. Additionally, these improvements also generalize to the HumanEval-Java and TransformedD4J datasets, where FLAMES generates 12% and 36.5% more correct patches, respectively, than the best baseline.","az":"修复软件缺陷至关重要，却要消耗开发者大量资源。自动程序修复（APR）是应对这一挑战性任务的有前景的方案。大语言模型（LLM）的出现开启了基于 LLM 的 APR 新时代，进一步大幅推进了 APR 领域。基于 LLM 的 APR 方法在内存效率方面面临重大挑战，阻碍了其可扩展性与有效性。这主要源于基于 LLM 的 APR 在补丁生成阶段所使用的束搜索（beam search）：为搜索到更多潜在优质的修复候选，需要很大的束宽。本文首先表明，即使对小规模 LLM（10 亿到 70 亿参数），增大束宽也需要大量 GPU 资源，导致基于 LLM 的 APR 中高达 80% 的重复崩溃源于内存过载。看似简单的降低内存消耗的方案有两种：（1）量化 LLM 模型，即将 LLM 权重从高精度数值转换为低精度数值；（2）将束搜索改为串行，即逐个束依次前向通过模型再拼接回单一输出。然而，我们通过理论分析与实验表明这些方法仍然行不通。为此，我们提出 FLAMES——一种新颖的基于 LLM 的 APR 技术，采用语义引导的补丁生成来同时提升修复有效性与内存效率。与依赖束搜索的传统方法不同，FLAMES 使用贪心解码来提升内存效率，同时通过语义引导的最佳优先搜索算法将搜索导向更有潜力的修复候选。在每个解码步骤，FLAMES 利用来自测试验证的语义反馈（例如通过与失败测试用例的数量）来选择最有希望进一步探索的 token。我们在 Defects4J 上的实证评估表明，与基于 LLM 的 APR 相比，FLAMES 将内存消耗最多降低 83%，且不牺牲时间效率。此外，FLAMES 在 Defects4J 上正确修复了 133 个缺陷，比最佳基线多修复 10 个。这些改进同样推广到 HumanEval-Java 与 TransformedD4J 数据集上，FLAMES 分别比最佳基线多生成 12% 与 36.5% 的正确补丁。","tl":"用测试语义反馈的最佳优先贪心解码替代束搜索，省 83% 显存。","au":["Thanh Le-Cong","Xuan-Bach D. Le","Toby Murray"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated program repair","beam search memory","semantic-guided search","greedy decoding","Defects4J"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/198/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/198/Memory-Efficient-Large-Language-Models-for-Program-Repair-with-Semantic-Guided-Patch-"},{"id":"p00685","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Demystifying the CVE Ecosystem: Community-Perceived Impacts and Problems","tz":"揭秘 CVE 生态：社区感知到的影响与问题","a":"The Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) system plays a critical role in global cybersecurity by standardizing the identification and cataloging of software and hardware vulnerabilities. However, recent high-profile incidents highlight the potential pitfall of the system, indicating the space for improvement. Despite significant interests in and substantial studies on CVE system, there is a lack of understanding to what extent the participants are impacted, and what problems are exactly in the CVE ecosystem. To bridge the knowledge gap, we extensively collect blog posts, community discussions and editorial articles from various sources including Reddit, LWN.net and GitHub, and employ thematic analysis approach to identify the perceived adverse impact on participants as well as the inherent problems within the CVE ecosystem. Then we conducted a follow-up community survey with 77 participants for validation. The results unveil the impacts on various participants within the prevailing CVE ecosystem and for the first time comprehensively trace and elucidate the problems that may cause these impacts. Based on the findings and survey results, we propose a series of implications to mitigate existing problems within the CVE ecosystem, aiming to enhance its efficiency and health.","az":"通用漏洞披露（CVE）系统通过标准化软硬件漏洞的标识与编目，在全球网络安全中发挥着关键作用。然而，近期若干高关注度事件凸显了该系统的潜在隐患，说明仍有改进空间。尽管学界对 CVE 系统兴趣浓厚且已有大量研究，但对于参与者受到多大程度的影响、以及 CVE 生态中究竟存在哪些问题，仍缺乏理解。为弥合这一知识空白，我们从 Reddit、LWN.net 与 GitHub 等多种来源广泛收集博客文章、社区讨论与评论文章，并采用主题分析方法识别参与者所感知到的不利影响以及 CVE 生态中的固有问题。随后，我们开展了一项有 77 名参与者的后续社区问卷调查以进行验证。结果揭示了当前 CVE 生态中对各类参与者的影响，并首次全面追溯与阐明了可能导致这些影响的问题。基于这些发现与问卷结果，我们提出了一系列启示，以缓解 CVE 生态中的现有问题，从而提升其效率与健康度。","tl":"首次系统追溯 CVE 生态的问题及其对各类参与者的影响。","au":["Yiliang Zhao","Hengzhi Ye","Minghui Zhou","Huaimin Wang"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","human-study"],"kw":["CVE ecosystem","thematic analysis","community survey","vulnerability disclosure","security practice"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/199/x"},{"id":"p00686","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Scalpel: Automotive Deep Learning Framework Testing via Assembling Model Components","tz":"Scalpel：通过装配模型组件测试车载深度学习框架","a":"Deep learning (DL) plays a key role in autonomous driving systems. DL models support perception modules, equipped with tasks such as object detection and sensor fusion. These DL models en- able vehicles to process multi-sensor inputs to understand complex surroundings. Deploying DL models in autonomous driving systems faces stringent challenges, including real-time processing, limited computational resources, and strict power constraints. To address these challenges, automotive DL frameworks (e.g., PaddleInference) have emerged to optimize inference efficiency. However, these frameworks encounter unique quality issues due to their more complex deployment environments, such as crashes stemming from limited scheduled memory and incorrect memory allocation. Unfortunately, existing DL framework testing methods fail to detect these quality issues due to the failure in deploying generated test input models, as these models lack three essential capabilities: (1) multi-input/output tensor processing, (2) multi-modal data processing, and (3) multi-level data feature extraction. These capabilities necessitate specialized model components, which existing testing methods neglect during model generation. To bridge this gap, we propose Scalpel, an automotive DL frameworks testing method that generates test input models at the model component level. Scalpel generates models by assembling model components (heads, necks, backbones) to support capabilities required by autonomous driving systems. Specifically, Scalpel maintains and updates a repository of model components, generating test inputs by selecting, mutating, and assembling them. Successfully generated models are added back to enrich the repository. Newly generated models are then deployed within the autonomous driving system to test automotive DL frameworks via differential testing. The experimental results demonstrate that Scalpel outperforms existing methods in both effectiveness and efficiency. In Apollo, Scalpel detects 16 crashes and 21 NaN & inconsistency bugs. All detected bugs have been reported to open-source communities, with 10 crashes confirmed. Scalpel achieves 27.44 and 8.5 improvements in model generation efficiency and bug detection efficiency. Additionally, Scalpel detects nine crashes and 16 NaN & inconsistency bugs in Autoware, which shows its excellent generalization.","az":"深度学习（DL）在自动驾驶系统中扮演关键角色。DL 模型支撑感知模块，承担目标检测与传感器融合等任务。这些 DL 模型使车辆能够处理多传感器输入以理解复杂环境。在自动驾驶系统中部署 DL 模型面临严苛挑战，包括实时处理、有限的计算资源与严格的功耗约束。为应对这些挑战，车载 DL 框架（如 PaddleInference）应运而生以优化推理效率。然而，由于部署环境更为复杂，这些框架会遭遇独特的质量问题，例如因调度内存有限与内存分配错误导致的崩溃。遗憾的是，现有的 DL 框架测试方法无法检出这些质量问题，原因在于生成的测试输入模型无法被成功部署——这些模型缺乏三项必备能力：（1）多输入/输出张量处理，（2）多模态数据处理，（3）多层级数据特征抽取。这些能力需要专门的模型组件，而现有测试方法在模型生成时忽略了它们。为弥合这一空白，我们提出 Scalpel，一种在模型组件层面生成测试输入模型的车载 DL 框架测试方法。Scalpel 通过装配模型组件（head、neck、backbone）来生成模型，以支持自动驾驶系统所需的能力。具体而言，Scalpel 维护并更新一个模型组件库，通过选择、变异与装配组件来生成测试输入；成功生成的模型会被加回库中以丰富组件库。随后将新生成的模型部署到自动驾驶系统中，通过差分测试来测试车载 DL 框架。实验结果表明，Scalpel 在有效性与效率上均优于现有方法。在 Apollo 中，Scalpel 检测出 16 个崩溃以及 21 个 NaN 与不一致缺陷；所有检出的缺陷均已报告给开源社区，其中 10 个崩溃已被确认。Scalpel 在模型生成效率与缺陷检测效率上分别取得 27.44 倍与 8.5 倍的提升。此外，Scalpel 在 Autoware 中检测出 9 个崩溃与 16 个 NaN 及不一致缺陷，显示出出色的泛化能力。","tl":"以 head/neck/backbone 组件装配生成可部署模型来测车载 DL 框架。","au":["Yinglong Zou","Juan Zhai","Chunrong Fang","An Guo","Jiawei Liu","Zhenyu Chen"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["DL framework testing","model component assembly","differential testing","autonomous driving","Apollo"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/200/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/200/Scalpel-Automotive-Deep-Learning-Framework-Testing-via-Assembling-Model-Components"},{"id":"p00687","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Project-Level Resource Leak Detection through Agent-based Ownership Analysis and Repair Pattern Verification","tz":"通过基于智能体的所有权分析与修复模式验证实现项目级资源泄漏检测","a":"Resource leaks cause system performance degradation and crashes. Traditional static analysis approaches rely on predefined rules, limiting their ability to find unknown leaks. Emerging LLM-based methods can locate APIs but face challenges in large-scale projects, including high costs and numerous false positives. To address these limitations, we propose AROP, the first project-level resource leak detection framework integrating LLM-based agents. AROP first extracts project-level metadata to efficiently filter resource-related files. It then employs a detection agent to identify acquisition/release operations, followed by a validation agent and data-flow dependency analysis to reduce false positives. Finally, it determines leaks through leak repair pattern analysis. We evaluated the effectiveness of our tool on the JLeaks benchmark and 6 large-scale real-world open-source projects. On JLeaks, AROP achieved a recall of 66.1% with a precision of 91.0%, which outperformed the current state-of-the-art, INFERROI, surpassing it by 18.2% in precision while maintaining a comparable recall. In evaluation on real-world projects, AROP discovered 106 previously unknown resource leak defects with a precision of 71.3%. We submitted patches for 28 of these defects, all of which have been confirmed and merged by developers.","az":"资源泄漏会导致系统性能下降与崩溃。传统静态分析方法依赖预定义规则，限制了其发现未知泄漏的能力。新兴的基于 LLM 的方法能够定位 API，但在大规模项目上面临成本高与误报多等挑战。为克服这些局限，我们提出 AROP——首个集成基于 LLM 的智能体的项目级资源泄漏检测框架。AROP 首先抽取项目级元数据以高效筛选与资源相关的文件；随后使用检测智能体识别获取/释放操作，再通过验证智能体与数据流依赖分析来降低误报；最后通过泄漏修复模式分析来判定泄漏。我们在 JLeaks 基准与 6 个大规模真实开源项目上评估了工具的有效性。在 JLeaks 上，AROP 取得 66.1% 的召回率与 91.0% 的精确率，超越当前最先进的 INFERROI——在精确率上高出 18.2%，同时保持相当的召回率。在真实项目的评估中，AROP 发现了 106 个此前未知的资源泄漏缺陷，精确率为 71.3%。我们为其中 28 个缺陷提交了补丁，全部已被开发者确认并合入。","tl":"检测+验证双智能体加修复模式分析，项目级查资源泄漏。","au":["Chengxin Xu","xiu zhang","Xiaorui Gong"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["resource leak detection","LLM agents","ownership analysis","false positive reduction","JLeaks"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/201/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/201/Project-Level-Resource-Leak-Detection-through-Agent-based-Ownership-Analysis-and-Repa"},{"id":"p00688","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Supporting Open Source Library Maintainers with Community-Based Analytics","tz":"用社区化分析支持开源库维护者","a":"Open-source software (OSS) is a pillar of modern software development. Its success depends on the dedication of maintainers who work constantly to keep their libraries stable, adapt to changing needs, and support a growing community. Yet, they receive little to no continuous feedback on how the projects that rely on their libraries actually use their APIs. We believe that gaining these insights can help maintainers make better decisions, such as refining testing strategies, understanding the impact of changes, and guiding the evolution of their libraries more effectively. We propose the use of community-based analytics to analyze how an OSS library is used across its dependent ecosystem. We conduct an empirical study of 10 popular Java libraries and each with their respective dependent ecosystem of 50 projects. Our results reveal that while library developers offer a wide range of API methods, only 16% on average are actively used by their dependent ecosystem. Moreover, only 73% of the used API methods are partially or fully covered by their library test suite. We propose two metrics to help developers evaluate their test suite according to the APIs used by their community, and we conduct a survey on open-source practitioners to assess the practical value of these insights in guiding maintenance decisions.","az":"开源软件（OSS）是现代软件开发的支柱。它的成功依赖于维护者的付出——他们持续工作以保持库的稳定、适应不断变化的需求并支撑日益壮大的社区。然而，对于依赖其库的项目究竟如何使用其 API，维护者几乎得不到任何持续的反馈。我们认为，获得这些洞见能帮助维护者做出更好的决策，例如优化测试策略、理解变更的影响，以及更有效地引导库的演化。我们提出使用社区化分析（community-based analytics）来分析一个开源库在其依赖生态中的使用方式。我们对 10 个流行的 Java 库开展实证研究，每个库各配以由 50 个项目构成的依赖生态。结果显示，尽管库开发者提供了范围广泛的 API 方法，但平均只有 16% 被其依赖生态实际使用。此外，被使用的 API 方法中只有 73% 被库的测试套件部分或完全覆盖。我们提出两项指标，帮助开发者依据社区实际使用的 API 来评估其测试套件，并开展了一项面向开源从业者的问卷调查，以评估这些洞见在指导维护决策方面的实用价值。","tl":"依生态实际 API 使用量重评库的测试覆盖，仅 16% API 被用。","au":["Rachna Raj","Diego Elias Costa"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","human-study"],"kw":["API usage analytics","OSS maintainers","dependent ecosystem","test coverage metrics","Java libraries"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/202/x"},{"id":"p00689","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Understanding DevOps Security of Google Workspace Apps","tz":"理解 Google Workspace 应用的 DevOps 安全","a":"Cloud-based workspace systems, such as Google Workspace and Microsoft OneDrive, have enabled third-party developers to create and upload functionality-rich applications (referred to as add-ons). Existing studies have primarily examined user-centric data protection and permission management of this emerging ecosystem, but the underlying DevOps mechanisms that regulate add-on development, deployment, and operation remain largely unexplored. In this work, we conduct the first developer-centric investigation of these DevOps mechanisms. We propose a hybrid method that combines a static analysis to abstract development and integration (i.e., deployment) (Dev) models and a dynamic analysis to add-ons’ runtime operation workflows (Ops). It yields insights into the DevOps lifecycle of add-ons, unveiling associated attack surfaces and multiple types of security vulnerabilities, including source code leakage, code tampering and secret key exposure. Our large-scale evaluation of 5,300 Google Workspace add-ons reveals a concerning status quo of the ecosystem: 274 add-ons are subject to source code leakage, including widely-used ones with over 100,000 users. Among them, 96 (around one third) expose the secret keys of developers, e.g., PayPal merchant secret key and secret keys to access the developer’s back-end databases.","az":"诸如 Google Workspace 与 Microsoft OneDrive 之类的云端工作空间系统，使第三方开发者能够创建并上传功能丰富的应用（称为插件，add-on）。已有研究主要考察了这一新兴生态中以用户为中心的数据保护与权限管理，但规范插件开发、部署与运行的底层 DevOps 机制在很大程度上仍未被探索。在本工作中，我们首次对这些 DevOps 机制开展以开发者为中心的调查。我们提出一种混合方法：用静态分析抽象开发与集成（即部署）（Dev）模型，用动态分析刻画插件的运行时操作工作流（Ops）。该方法揭示了插件 DevOps 生命周期的内在规律，暴露了相关的攻击面与多种类型的安全漏洞，包括源码泄露、代码篡改与密钥泄露。我们对 5,300 个 Google Workspace 插件的大规模评估揭示了该生态令人担忧的现状：274 个插件存在源码泄露，其中包括用户数超过 10 万的广泛使用的插件。在这些插件中，96 个（约三分之一）泄露了开发者的密钥，例如 PayPal 商户密钥以及访问开发者后端数据库的密钥。","tl":"首次从开发者视角剖析插件 DevOps，5300 个应用中大量泄密钥。","au":["Liuhuo Wan","Chuan Yan","Zicong Liu","Haoyu Wang","Guangdong Bai"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["Google Workspace add-ons","DevOps security","source code leakage","secret key exposure","static and dynamic analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/203/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/203/Understanding-DevOps-Security-of-Google-Workspace-Apps"},{"id":"p00690","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"STEM-EF: A Model for Assessing Scrum Team Effectiveness Based on Emotional Factors","tz":"STEM-EF：一个基于情绪因素评估 Scrum 团队效能的模型","a":"Background: Team effectiveness is critical to Agile Software Development (ASD), particularly within the Scrum framework. Existing models focus on behavioral and structural dimensions such as communication, coordination, and shared leadership, but largely overlook emotional dynamics. Objective: This study proposes the Scrum Team Effectiveness Model – Emotional Factors (STEM-EF), a novel instrument designed to assess team effectiveness in Scrum by incorporating emotional constructs. Method: STEM-EF was developed around four emotional factors—Emotional Intelligence (EI), Interpersonal Skills (IS), Conflict Resolution (CR), and Psychological Safety (PS)—and tailored to Scrum events, roles, and artifacts. Validation followed a mixed-methods approach: content validity was assessed using the Content Validity Index (CVI), while perceived utility was evaluated through the Technology Acceptance Model (TAM). Data were collected from 11 Scrum experts, 56 team members, and 2 psychologists via interviews, focus groups, and surveys. Results: STEM-EF demonstrated high content validity across relevance, coherence, and simplicity (S-CVI-Relevance = 1.00, S-CVI-Coherence = 1.00, S-CVI-Simplicity = 0.99). TAM results indicated favorable perceptions of usefulness and intention to adopt the instrument. Conclusion: STEM-EF is a content-validated and practically promising instrument for integrating emotional assessment into Scrum team evaluations. It offers both researchers and practitioners a structured means to explore and support emotional dynamics that may affect team performance.","az":"背景：团队效能对敏捷软件开发（ASD）至关重要，在 Scrum 框架中尤甚。现有模型关注沟通、协调与共享领导等行为与结构维度，却在很大程度上忽略了情绪动态。目标：本研究提出 Scrum 团队效能模型——情绪因素（STEM-EF），这是一种通过纳入情绪构念来评估 Scrum 团队效能的新型工具。方法：STEM-EF 围绕四个情绪因素构建——情绪智力（EI）、人际技能（IS）、冲突解决（CR）与心理安全（PS）——并针对 Scrum 的事件、角色与工件进行了定制。验证采用混合方法：用内容效度指数（CVI）评估内容效度，用技术接受模型（TAM）评估感知效用。数据通过访谈、焦点小组与问卷，从 11 位 Scrum 专家、56 名团队成员与 2 位心理学家处收集。结果：STEM-EF 在相关性、连贯性与简明性上均展现出高内容效度（S-CVI-相关性 = 1.00，S-CVI-连贯性 = 1.00，S-CVI-简明性 = 0.99）。TAM 结果显示受访者对该工具的有用性与采用意愿评价良好。结论：STEM-EF 是一个经过内容效度验证、在实践中颇具前景的工具，可将情绪评估整合进 Scrum 团队评价。它为研究者与从业者提供了一种结构化手段，用以探索并支持可能影响团队绩效的情绪动态。","tl":"把情绪智力等四类情绪因素做成可验证的 Scrum 团队效能量表。","au":["Ramon Nóbrega dos Santos","Hyggo Almeida","Mirko Perkusich","Danyllo Albuquerque","Felipe Cunha","Thiago Rique","Ademar Sousa Neto","Angelo Perkusich"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["human-study","empirical-study"],"kw":["Scrum team effectiveness","emotional intelligence","psychological safety","content validity index","technology acceptance model"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/204/x"},{"id":"p00691","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Is Call Graph Pruning Really Effective? An Empirical Re-evaluation","tz":"调用图剪枝真的有效吗？一次实证再评估","a":"Recently proposed call graph pruning techniques, which use machine learning to predict and reduce false positives in static call graphs, have reported impressive results and demonstrated practicality for downstream analyses. However, as we research the methodology of how datasets are created and how evaluation is conducted in these research projects, we identify many risk factors that may make the reported results incomplete or even invalid. We further investigate these factors and provide empirical evidence to demonstrate they indeed result in misleading results. Motivated by these findings, we propose an empirical re-evaluation of existing call graph pruning techniques to assess their effectiveness. We first construct a new dataset of real-world programs, applying three complementary labeling approaches, resulting in 41,952 labels. To provide a full picture of these techniques, we utilize three popular call graph analysis frameworks (WALA, Doop, and OPAL) and seven tool configurations. Our results show that pruning is not as effective as reported in prior work, improving precision at the cost of significant coverage loss. We further train more general models across analysis tools and configurations, and explore the impact of data splitting and balancing. We find these models often match or outperform the existing configuration-specific ones, indicating their applicability in more general settings. Finally, we highlight the open challenges and potential solutions, including the need for better datasets as well as improved feature engineering.","az":"近期提出的调用图剪枝技术使用机器学习预测并减少静态调用图中的误报，报告了令人印象深刻的结果，并展示了其在下游分析中的实用性。然而，当我们研究这些研究项目中数据集如何构建、评估如何开展的方法论时，我们识别出许多可能使所报告结果不完整甚至无效的风险因素。我们进一步考察这些因素，并提供实证证据表明它们确实会导致误导性的结果。受这些发现的驱动，我们提出对现有调用图剪枝技术进行实证再评估，以评判其有效性。我们首先构建了一个由真实世界程序组成的新数据集，应用三种互补的标注方法，共得到 41,952 条标签。为全面刻画这些技术，我们使用了三个流行的调用图分析框架（WALA、Doop 与 OPAL）以及七种工具配置。结果表明，剪枝并不像先前工作所报告的那样有效：它以显著的覆盖损失为代价换取精确率的提升。我们进一步跨分析工具与配置训练了更通用的模型，并探究了数据划分与数据平衡的影响。我们发现这些模型往往能够匹配甚至超过既有的特定配置模型，表明它们在更一般的场景中同样适用。最后，我们指出了尚待解决的挑战与可能的解决方案，包括对更好数据集以及改进特征工程的需求。","tl":"重做数据集与评估，发现调用图剪枝以大幅丢覆盖换精确率。","au":["Mohammad Rafieian","Vlad Birsan","Kunal Katiya","Dylan Zhong","Shiyi Wei"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["reproducibility-replication","empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["call graph pruning","re-evaluation","static analysis","WALA / Doop / OPAL","dataset labeling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/205/x","pu":"https://mohpydev.github.io/papers/call-graph-pruning-preprint.pdf"},{"id":"p00692","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Knowledge-Augmented Log Anomaly Detection with Large Language Models","tz":"知识增强的大语言模型日志异常检测","a":"Log anomaly detection is critical for maintaining system reliability, yet existing large language model (LLM)-based methods suffer from limited accuracy, high computational costs, and poor explainability. In this paper, we introduce LogPipe, a novel framework that enhances LLM-based log anomaly detection by integrating a dynamic knowledge base. LogPipe constructs a knowledge base using discrete and semantic log patterns, augmented by dynamic patterns that are generated by a sentiment dictionary and frequent pattern mining. During inference, log sequences are matched against the knowledge base to provide specific guidance to the LLM, improving detection accuracy and generating detailed explanations. A continuous update mechanism ensures the knowledge base remains relevant while minimizing redundant LLM queries, significantly reducing inference costs. Evaluated on eight public datasets, LogPipe achieves an average F1 score of 97.5%, outperforming state-of-the-art models, with reduced token consumption. Additionally, LogPipe excels in fault localization, which enhances the explainability of detected anomalies.","az":"日志异常检测对维持系统可靠性至关重要，但现有基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法存在准确率有限、计算成本高与可解释性差的问题。本文提出 LogPipe，一种通过集成动态知识库来增强基于 LLM 的日志异常检测的新框架。LogPipe 使用离散日志模式与语义日志模式构建知识库，并辅以由情感词典与频繁模式挖掘生成的动态模式。在推理阶段，日志序列与知识库进行匹配，为 LLM 提供具体指导，从而提升检测准确率并生成详细的解释。持续更新机制确保知识库保持时效性，同时最大限度减少冗余的 LLM 查询，显著降低推理成本。在八个公开数据集上的评估显示，LogPipe 取得 97.5% 的平均 F1 分数，优于最先进的模型，且 token 消耗更低。此外，LogPipe 在故障定位方面表现优异，增强了所检测异常的可解释性。","tl":"用可持续更新的日志模式知识库指导 LLM，F1 达 97.5%。","au":["Yongliang Tao","Hongyu Zhang","Van-Hoang Le","Yi Xiao"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["log anomaly detection","knowledge base","pattern mining","LLM inference cost","fault localization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/206/x"},{"id":"p00693","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RulePilot: An LLM-Powered Agent for Security Rule Generation","tz":"RulePilot：一个由 LLM 驱动的安全规则生成智能体","a":"The real-time demand for system security leads to the detection rules becoming an integral part of the intrusion detection life-cycle. Rule-based detection often identifies malicious logs based on the predefined grammar logic, requiring experts with deep domain knowledge for rule generation. Therefore, automation of rule generation can result in significant time savings and ease the burden of rule-related tasks on security engineers. In this paper, we propose RulePilot, which mimics human expertise via LLM-based agent for addressing rule-related challenges like rule creation or conversion. Using RulePilot, the security analysts do not need to write down the rules following the grammar, instead, they can just provide the annotations such as the natural-language-based descriptions of a rule, our RulePilot can automatically generate the detection rules without more intervention. RulePilot is equipped with the intermediate representation (IR), which abstracts the complexity of config rules into structured, standardized formats, allowing LLMs to focus on generation rules in a more manageable and consistent way. We present a comprehensive evaluation of RulePilot in terms of textual similarity and execution success abilities, showcasing RulePilot can generate high-fidelity rules, outperforming the baseline models by up to 107.4% in textual similarity to ground truths and achieving better detection accuracy in real-world execution tests. We perform a case study from our industry collaborators, showcasing that RulePilot can help junior analysts/general users in the rule creation process.","az":"对系统安全的实时需求使检测规则成为入侵检测生命周期中不可或缺的一环。基于规则的检测通常依据预定义的语法逻辑来识别恶意日志，规则生成需要具备深厚领域知识的专家。因此，规则生成的自动化能够显著节省时间，并减轻安全工程师在规则相关任务上的负担。本文提出 RulePilot，它通过基于 LLM 的智能体模拟人类专家，以应对规则创建或规则转换等与规则相关的挑战。使用 RulePilot 时，安全分析师无需按照语法编写规则，只需提供注释（例如对规则的自然语言描述），RulePilot 便能自动生成检测规则而无需更多干预。RulePilot 配备了中间表示（IR），将配置规则的复杂性抽象为结构化、标准化的格式，使 LLM 能以更可控、更一致的方式专注于生成规则。我们从文本相似度与执行成功能力两方面对 RulePilot 进行了全面评估，结果显示 RulePilot 能生成高保真度的规则，在与标准答案的文本相似度上最多超出基线模型 107.4%，并在真实执行测试中取得更好的检测准确率。我们还展示了与工业合作方的案例研究，说明 RulePilot 能在规则创建过程中帮助初级分析师与普通用户。","tl":"用中间表示让 LLM 智能体从自然语言描述生成检测规则。","au":["Hongtai Wang","Ming Xu","Yanpei Guo","Weili Han","Hoon Wei Lim","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["llm-based","agentic","security"],"kw":["security rule generation","intrusion detection","LLM agent","intermediate representation","rule conversion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/207/x"},{"id":"p00694","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"More with Less: An Empirical Study of Turn-Control Strategies for Efficient Coding Agents","tz":"少即是多：高效编程智能体轮次控制策略的实证研究","a":"LLM-powered coding agents, which operate in iterative loops (turns) to solve software engineering tasks, are becoming increasingly powerful. However, their practical deployment is hindered by significant and unpredictable costs. This challenge arises from a combination of factors: quadratically growing token counts with each turn, the high price of state-of-the-art models, the large number of turns required for real-world tasks, and the tendency of agents to take inefficient or unnecessary actions. While existing research focuses on optimizing individual turns, the strategic control of the total number of turns remains an underexplored area for managing agent performance and cost. To address this gap, we conduct a comprehensive empirical study on the SWE-bench benchmark using three state-of-the-art models (Claude 4 Sonnet, Gemini 2.5 Pro, and GPT 4.1). We systematically evaluate the impact of three distinct turn-control strategies: an unrestricted baseline, a fixed-turn limit with reminders, and a novel dynamic-turn strategy that grants extensions on-demand. Our findings first reveal a fundamental trade-off in the unrestricted setting, where no single model excels across performance, cost, and turn efficiency. We then show that a fixed-turn limit, specifically at the 75th percentile of the baseline, serves as a “sweet spot”, substantially reducing costs (by 24%-68%) with minimal impact on solve rates. Most significantly, our proposed dynamic-turn strategy consistently outperforms fixed-limit approaches, achieving comparable or better solve rates while further reducing costs by an additional 12%-24% by intelligently allocating resources only to tasks that need them. This work provides the first systematic analysis of turn-control strategies, offering simple yet effective guidelines for developers to balance cost and efficacy. We demonstrate that dynamic resource allocation is a superior, easy-to-implement approach for deploying powerful yet economically viable coding agents.","az":"以 LLM 驱动、在迭代循环（轮次）中解决软件工程任务的编程智能体正变得日益强大。然而，其实际部署受到高昂且不可预测成本的阻碍。这一挑战源于多重因素的叠加：token 数量随每一轮次二次增长、最先进模型的高昂价格、真实任务所需的大量轮次，以及智能体倾向于采取低效或不必要的动作。现有研究聚焦于优化单个轮次，而对总轮次数的策略性控制——作为管理智能体性能与成本的手段——仍是一个未被充分探索的领域。为填补这一空白，我们在 SWE-bench 基准上使用三个最先进的模型（Claude 4 Sonnet、Gemini 2.5 Pro 与 GPT 4.1）开展了一项全面的实证研究。我们系统评估了三种不同轮次控制策略的影响：无限制基线、带提醒的固定轮次上限，以及一种按需授予延长的新型动态轮次策略。我们的发现首先揭示了无限制设置下的一个根本性权衡：没有任何单一模型能在性能、成本与轮次效率上全面胜出。随后我们表明，固定轮次上限——具体取基线的第 75 百分位——是一个“甜点”，能在对解决率影响极小的情况下大幅降低成本（24%–68%）。最重要的是，我们提出的动态轮次策略始终优于固定上限方法：在取得相当或更好解决率的同时，通过仅向真正需要的任务智能分配资源，进一步额外降低 12%–24% 的成本。这项工作首次对轮次控制策略做了系统分析，为开发者平衡成本与效能提供了简单而有效的指南。我们证明，动态资源分配是部署强大且经济可行的编程智能体的更优、且易于实现的方法。","tl":"按需延长轮次的动态策略，在保解决率下再省 12%-24% 成本。","au":["Pengfei Gao","Chao Peng"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["coding agent cost","turn control","SWE-bench","dynamic budget","token efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/208/x"},{"id":"p00695","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evaluating the effectiveness of LLM-based interoperability","tz":"评估基于 LLM 的互操作性的有效性","a":"Background: Systems of systems are becoming increasingly dynamic and heterogeneous, and this adds pressure on the long-standing challenge of interoperability. Besides its technical aspect, interoperability has also an economic side, as development time efforts are required to build the interoperability artifacts. Objectives: With the recent advances in the field of large language models (LLMs), we aim at analyzing the effectiveness of LLM-based strategies to make systems interoperate autonomously, at runtime, without human intervention. Method: We selected 13 open source LLMs and curated four versions of a dataset in the agricultural interoperability use case. We performed three runs of each model with each version of the dataset, using two different strategies. Then we compared the effectiveness of the models and the consistency of their results across multiple runs. Results: qwen2.5-coder:32b was the most effective model using both strategies DIRECT (average pass@1 ≥ 0.99) and CODEGEN (average pass@1 ≥ 0.89) in three out of four dataset versions. In the fourth dataset version, which included an unit conversion, all models using the strategy DIRECT failed, whereas using CODEGEN qwen2.5-coder:32b succeeded with an average pass@1 = 0.75. Conclusion: Some LLMs can make systems interoperate autonomously. Further evaluation in different domains is recommended, and further research on reliability strategies should be conducted.","az":"背景：系统之系统（systems of systems）正变得日益动态与异构，这加剧了互操作性这一长期存在的挑战。除技术层面外，互操作性还有经济层面的问题，因为构建互操作性制品需要投入开发时间。目标：随着大语言模型（LLM）领域的最新进展，我们旨在分析基于 LLM 的策略在无人干预的情况下、于运行时让系统自主互操作的有效性。方法：我们选取了 13 个开源 LLM，并在农业互操作性用例中整理了四个版本的数据集。我们使用两种不同策略，让每个模型在每个数据集版本上各运行三次；随后比较各模型的有效性以及其结果在多次运行间的一致性。结果：qwen2.5-coder:32b 在两种策略下都是最有效的模型——在四个数据集版本中的三个上，DIRECT 策略的平均 pass@1 ≥ 0.99，CODEGEN 策略的平均 pass@1 ≥ 0.89。在包含单位换算的第四个数据集版本上，所有使用 DIRECT 策略的模型均告失败，而使用 CODEGEN 策略的 qwen2.5-coder:32b 成功达到平均 pass@1 = 0.75。结论：某些 LLM 能够让系统自主互操作。建议在不同领域开展进一步评估，并应就可靠性策略开展进一步研究。","tl":"对比 DIRECT 与 CODEGEN 两策略，发现生成代码更能应对单位换算。","au":["Rodrigo Falcão","Stefan Schweitzer","Julien Siebert","Emily Calvet","Frank Elberzhager"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["interoperability","systems of systems","open-source LLMs","pass@1","code generation strategy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/209/x"},{"id":"p00696","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DeFT: Maintaining Determinism and Extracting Unit Tests for Autonomous Driving Planning","tz":"DeFT：为自动驾驶规划模块保持确定性并抽取单元测试","a":"An Autonomous Driving System (ADS) is a complex software system often composed of multiple modules, each responsible for its own set of tasks. The ADS planning module is responsible for planning the future driving trajectories (i.e., making decisions on how to drive) of the autonomous vehicle and is historically the most buggy ADS module. In recent years, many approaches have been proposed to test an ADS in complex virtual scenarios through simulation, and these scenarios have been effective in revealing ADS’ suboptimal decisions. However, due to the randomness of events that occur during the real-time execution of an ADS, test scenarios tend to produce varying outcomes and, in turn, make ADS testing non-deterministic, flaky, and unpredictable. To address this challenge, we propose and evaluate DeFT, an approach that extracts deterministic test cases for the ADS planning module from non-deterministic system-level scenario tests. DeFT monitors the messages being exchanged by ADS modules during executions of system-level scenario tests and reconstructs inputs to reproduce the executions of the planning module. By using DeFT, we find planning module tests can (1) more accurately reproduce planning module executions that occurred during system-level scenario tests, (2) be used to deterministically detect the same 658 collision failures revealed by system-level scenario tests, and (3) reduced time needed to reproduce failure by 43.69% to 77.64%.","az":"自动驾驶系统（ADS）是一个复杂的软件系统，通常由多个模块组成，每个模块负责各自的一组任务。ADS 的规划（planning）模块负责规划自动驾驶车辆未来的行驶轨迹（即决定如何驾驶），历史上也是缺陷最多的 ADS 模块。近年来，人们提出了许多通过仿真在复杂虚拟场景中测试 ADS 的方法，这些场景在揭示 ADS 的次优决策方面颇为有效。然而，由于 ADS 实时执行期间发生事件的随机性，测试场景往往产生不同的结果，进而使 ADS 测试变得非确定性、不稳定（flaky）且不可预测。为应对这一挑战，我们提出并评估了 DeFT——一种从非确定性的系统级场景测试中为 ADS 规划模块抽取确定性测试用例的方法。DeFT 监控系统级场景测试执行期间 ADS 各模块之间交换的消息，并重建输入以复现规划模块的执行。使用 DeFT，我们发现规划模块的测试可以（1）更准确地复现系统级场景测试中发生的规划模块执行，（2）确定性地检测出系统级场景测试所揭示的同样的 658 个碰撞失败，（3）将复现失败所需的时间减少 43.69% 至 77.64%。","tl":"回放模块间消息，把非确定性场景测试变成确定性规划单元测试。","au":["Yuqi Huai","Yuntianyi Chen","Ziwen Wan","Alfred Chen","Joshua Garcia"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["autonomous driving planning","deterministic tests","test flakiness","unit test extraction","failure reproduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/210/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3773252"},{"id":"p00697","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Verification of Multi-Model Stochastic Systems","tz":"多模型随机系统的验证","a":"Given its ability to analyse stochastic models ranging from discrete and continuous-time Markov chains to Markov decision processes and stochastic games, probabilistic model checking (PMC) is widely used to verify system dependability and performance properties. However, modelling the behaviour of, and verifying these properties for many software-intensive systems requires the joint analysis of multiple interdependent stochastic models of different types, which existing PMC techniques and tools cannot handle. To address this limitation, we introduce a tool-supported UniversaL stochasTIc Modelling, verificAtion and synThEsis (ULTIMATE) framework that supports the representation, verification and synthesis of heterogeneous multi-model stochastic systems with complex model interdependencies. Through its unique integration of multiple PMC paradigms, underpinned by a novel verification method that handles model interdependencies, ULTIMATE unifies—for the first time—the modelling of probabilistic and nondeterministic uncertainty, discrete and continuous time, partial observability, and the use of both Bayesian and frequentist inference to exploit domain knowledge and data about the modelled context. A comprehensive suite of case studies and experiments confirm the generality and effectiveness of our novel verification framework.","az":"由于能够分析从离散与连续时间马尔可夫链到马尔可夫决策过程与随机博弈等各类随机模型，概率模型检验（PMC）被广泛用于验证系统的可信性与性能属性。然而，对许多软件密集型系统而言，建模其行为并验证这些属性需要对多个不同类型、彼此依赖的随机模型进行联合分析，而现有的 PMC 技术与工具无法处理这种情形。为突破这一局限，我们提出了有工具支持的 ULTIMATE（通用随机建模、验证与合成）框架，支持对具有复杂模型间依赖关系的异构多模型随机系统进行表示、验证与合成。通过对多种 PMC 范式的独特整合，并以一种能够处理模型间依赖的新颖验证方法为支撑，ULTIMATE 首次统一了概率性与非确定性不确定性的建模、离散与连续时间的建模、部分可观测性，以及对贝叶斯与频率派推断的使用，从而充分利用关于所建模场景的领域知识与数据。一整套全面的案例研究与实验验证了我们这一新颖验证框架的通用性与有效性。","tl":"首次统一多范式概率模型检验并处理模型间依赖。","au":["Radu Calinescu","Simos Gerasimou","Sinem Getir Yaman","Gricel Vázquez","Micah Bassett"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["probabilistic model checking","stochastic models","multi-model verification","synthesis","partial observability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/211/x","pu":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1icMGEs1cx92BAeRUiJ4-2nV06Y3aunUX/view"},{"id":"p00698","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Using a Sledgehammer to Crack a Nut? Revisiting Automated Compiler Fault Isolation","tz":"杀鸡用牛刀？重新审视编译器缺陷自动隔离","a":"Background: Compilers are fundamental to software development, translating high-level source code into executable software systems. Faults in compilers can have severe consequences and thus effective localization and resolution of compiler bugs are crucial. Problem: In practice, developers often examine version history to identify and investigate bug-inducing commit (BIC) for fixing bugs. However, while numerous sophisticated Spectrum-Based Fault Localization (SBFL) techniques have been proposed for compiler fault isolation, their effectiveness has not been evaluated against the BIC-based strategies widely adopted by developers. Objective: This study aims to address the gap by directly comparing the BIC-based strategy named BASIC with established SBFL techniques in the domain of compiler fault localization. The BIC-based strategy aligns closely with developer practices, which directly identifying the BIC and treating its associated files as faulty candidates. Method: The BASIC technique identifies the most recent good release and earliest bad release, employing a binary search to pinpoint the bug-inducing commit. All files modified in this commit are flagged as potentially faulty. We rigorously compare BASIC against SBFL-based techniques using identical datasets and evaluation metrics. Result: Our analysis reveals that BASIC outperforms existing SBFL-based techniques in most cases, particularly in the critical Top-1 and Top-5 ranking metrics. Conclusion: This study contributes to a deeper understanding of the practical efficacy of SBFL-based techniques in real-world scenarios. We recommend that future research should adopt BASIC as a baseline for comparison when developing new compiler fault isolation methods.","az":"背景：编译器是软件开发的基础，它将高级源代码翻译为可执行的软件系统。编译器中的故障可能造成严重后果，因此有效定位与解决编译器缺陷至关重要。问题：在实践中，开发者常通过检查版本历史来识别并调查引入缺陷的提交（BIC）以修复缺陷。然而，尽管已有众多复杂的基于频谱的缺陷定位（SBFL）技术被提出用于编译器缺陷隔离，其有效性从未与开发者广泛采用的基于 BIC 的策略进行过对比评估。目标：本研究旨在填补这一空白，在编译器缺陷定位领域中直接比较名为 BASIC 的基于 BIC 的策略与成熟的 SBFL 技术。基于 BIC 的策略与开发者实践高度契合，即直接识别 BIC 并将其涉及的文件视为疑似缺陷候选。方法：BASIC 技术识别最近的一个“正常版本”与最早的一个“异常版本”，并采用二分查找来精确定位引入缺陷的提交；该提交中修改的所有文件都被标记为潜在缺陷文件。我们使用相同的数据集与评估指标，严格地将 BASIC 与基于 SBFL 的技术进行比较。结果：我们的分析显示，BASIC 在大多数情况下优于现有的基于 SBFL 的技术，在关键的 Top-1 与 Top-5 排名指标上尤为明显。结论：本研究有助于更深入地理解基于 SBFL 的技术在真实场景中的实际效用。我们建议未来研究在提出新的编译器缺陷隔离方法时，应采用 BASIC 作为比较基线。","tl":"二分查找引入缺陷提交的朴素策略反而胜过复杂的 SBFL。","au":["Yibiao Yang","Qingyang Li","Maolin Sun","Jiangchang Wu","Yuming Zhou"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["reproducibility-replication","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["compiler fault isolation","spectrum-based fault localization","bug-inducing commit","bisection","baseline comparison"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/212/x"},{"id":"p00699","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Code to Correctness: Closing the Last Mile of Code Generation with Hierarchical Debugging","tz":"从代码到正确性：用分层调试打通代码生成的最后一公里","a":"While large language models have made significant strides in code generation, the pass rate of the generated code is bottlenecked on subtle errors, often requiring human intervention to pass tests, especially for complex problems. Existing LLM-based debugging systems treat generated programs as monolithic units, failing to address bugs at multiple levels of granularity, from low-level syntax errors to high-level algorithmic flaws. In this paper, we introduce Multi-Granularity Debugger (MGDebugger), a hierarchical code debugger that isolates, identifies, and resolves bugs at various levels of granularity. MGDebugger decomposes problematic code into a hierarchical tree structure of subfunctions, with each level representing a particular granularity of error. During debugging, it analyzes each subfunction and iteratively resolves bugs in a bottom-up manner. To effectively test each subfunction, we propose an LLM-simulated Python executor, which traces code execution and tracks important variable states to pinpoint errors accurately. Extensive experiments with both open-source and commercial LLMs demonstrate that MGDebugger significantly outperforms existing debugging systems, achieving up to 18.9% improvement in accuracy over seed generations in HumanEval and a 97.6% repair success rate in HumanEvalFix. Furthermore, MGDebugger effectively generalizes to real-world software defects, fixing 129 bugs in Defects4J v1.2 and 64 bugs in Defects4J v2.0, outperforming state-of-the-art program repair approaches by 13.2% and 8.5% respectively. These results demonstrate MGDebugger’s robustness and effectiveness across different scenarios, establishing it as a powerful tool for closing the last mile of code generation.","az":"尽管大语言模型在代码生成上取得了长足进步，所生成代码的通过率仍受制于细微错误，往往需要人工干预才能通过测试，复杂问题尤甚。现有基于 LLM 的调试系统将生成的程序视为单体单元，无法在从低级语法错误到高级算法缺陷的多个粒度层次上处理缺陷。本文提出多粒度调试器（MGDebugger），一种分层的代码调试器，能够在不同粒度层次上隔离、识别并修复缺陷。MGDebugger 将有问题的代码分解为子函数的层次树结构，每一层代表某一特定粒度的错误。在调试过程中，它分析每个子函数，并以自底向上的方式迭代修复缺陷。为有效测试每个子函数，我们提出了一个由 LLM 模拟的 Python 执行器，它追踪代码执行并跟踪重要变量状态，从而精确定位错误。在开源与商用 LLM 上的大量实验表明，MGDebugger 显著优于现有调试系统：在 HumanEval 上相较种子生成结果最多提升 18.9% 的准确率，在 HumanEvalFix 上取得 97.6% 的修复成功率。此外，MGDebugger 能有效泛化到真实世界的软件缺陷，在 Defects4J v1.2 中修复 129 个缺陷、在 Defects4J v2.0 中修复 64 个缺陷，分别比最先进的程序修复方法高出 13.2% 与 8.5%。这些结果证明了 MGDebugger 在不同场景下的鲁棒性与有效性，使其成为打通代码生成最后一公里的有力工具。","tl":"把代码拆成子函数树，自底向上分粒度定位并修复缺陷。","au":["Yuling Shi","Songsong Wang","Chengcheng Wan","Wang Min","Xiaodong Gu"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["hierarchical debugging","self-debugging","subfunction decomposition","LLM-simulated executor","HumanEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/213/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01215"},{"id":"p00700","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Let the Trial Begin: A Mock-Court Approach to Vulnerability Detection using LLM-Based Agents","tz":"开庭审理：一种用于漏洞检测的法庭式 LLM 多智能体方法","a":"Detecting vulnerabilities in source code remains a critical yet challenging task, especially when benign and vulnerable functions share significant similarities. In this work, we introduce VulTrial, a courtroom-inspired multi-agent framework designed to enhance automated vulnerability detection. It employs four role-specific agents, which are a security researcher, a code author, a moderator, and a review board. Through extensive experiments using GPT-3.5 and GPT-4o, we demonstrate that VulTrial outperforms single-agent and multi-agent baselines. Using GPT-4o, VulTrial improves the number of pairs that are correctly labeled by 41 and 37 (around double) over its respective baseline. Additionally, we show that role-specific instruction tuning in VulTrial with small quantities of data (50 pair samples) improves the number of pairs that are correctly labeled by 56 and 52 points. Furthermore, we analyze the impact of increasing the number of agent interactions on VulTrial’s overall performance. While multi-agent setups inherently incur higher costs due to increased token usage, our findings reveal that applying VulTrial to a cost-effective model like GPT-3.5 can improve its performance compared to GPT-4o in a single-agent setting, at a lower overall cost.","az":"检测源代码中的漏洞仍是一项关键而艰巨的任务，尤其当良性函数与含漏洞函数高度相似时。在本工作中，我们提出 VulTrial，一个受法庭启发的多智能体框架，用于增强自动化漏洞检测。它采用四个角色专属的智能体：安全研究员、代码作者、主持人以及评审委员会。通过使用 GPT-3.5 与 GPT-4o 开展的大量实验，我们证明 VulTrial 优于单智能体与多智能体基线。使用 GPT-4o 时，VulTrial 相较各自基线将正确标注的样本对数量分别提升了 41 对与 37 对（约为两倍）。此外，我们表明在 VulTrial 中使用少量数据（50 个样本对）进行角色专属的指令微调，可将正确标注的样本对数量分别提升 56 和 52 个点。我们还分析了增加智能体交互次数对 VulTrial 整体性能的影响。虽然多智能体设置因 token 用量增加而必然带来更高成本，但我们的发现表明，将 VulTrial 应用于 GPT-3.5 这类高性价比模型，能以更低的总体成本取得优于单智能体设置下 GPT-4o 的性能。","tl":"以法庭四角色辩论提升漏洞检测，且角色专属微调再加分。","au":["Ratnadira Widyasari","Martin Weyssow","Ivana Clairine Irsan","Han Wei Ang","Frank Liauw","Eng Lieh Ouh","Lwin Khin Shar","Hong Jin Kang","David Lo"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","multi-agent framework","role-specific instruction tuning","GPT-4o","cost analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/214/x"},{"id":"p00701","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RISE: Rule-Driven SQL Dialect Translation via Query Reduction","tz":"RISE：基于查询化简的规则驱动 SQL 方言翻译","a":"Translating SQL dialects across different relational database management systems (RDBMSs) is crucial for migrating RDBMS-based applications to the cloud. Traditional SQL dialect translation tools rely on manually-crafted rules, necessitating significant manual effort to support new RDBMSs and dialects. Although large language models (LLMs) can assist in translating SQL dialects, they often struggle with lengthy and complex SQL queries. In this paper, we propose RISE, a novel LLM-based SQL dialect translation approach that can accurately handle lengthy and complex SQL queries. Given a complex source query 𝑄𝑐 that contains a SQL dialect 𝑑, we first employ a dialect-aware query reduction technique to derive a simplified query 𝑄𝑠 by removing 𝑑-irrelevant SQL elements from 𝑄𝑐. Subsequently, we utilize LLMs to translate 𝑄𝑠 into 𝑄𝑠′, and automatically extract the translation rule 𝑟𝑑 for dialect 𝑑 based on the relationship between 𝑄𝑠 and 𝑄𝑠′. By applying 𝑟𝑑 to 𝑄𝑐, we can effectively translate the dialect 𝑑 within 𝑄𝑐, thereby bypassing the complexity of the source query 𝑄𝑐. We evaluate RISE on two real-world benchmarks, i.e., TPC-DS and SQLProcBench, comparing its performance against both the traditional rule-based tools and the LLM-based approaches with respect to translation accuracy. RISE achieves accuracies of 97.98% on TPC-DS and 100% on SQLProcBench, outperforming the baselines by an average improvement of 24.62% and 238.41%, respectively.","az":"在不同关系型数据库管理系统（RDBMS）之间翻译 SQL 方言，对于将基于 RDBMS 的应用迁移上云至关重要。传统的 SQL 方言翻译工具依赖人工编写的规则，支持新的 RDBMS 和方言需要大量人工投入。尽管大语言模型（LLM）可以辅助翻译 SQL 方言，但它们在处理冗长且复杂的 SQL 查询时往往力不从心。本文提出 RISE，一种新颖的基于 LLM 的 SQL 方言翻译方法，能够准确处理冗长复杂的 SQL 查询。给定一个包含 SQL 方言 d 的复杂源查询 Qc，我们首先采用一种方言感知的查询化简技术，从 Qc 中移除与 d 无关的 SQL 元素，从而得到简化查询 Qs。随后，我们利用 LLM 将 Qs 翻译为 Qs'，并基于 Qs 与 Qs' 之间的关系自动抽取出方言 d 的翻译规则 rd。将 rd 应用于 Qc，即可有效翻译 Qc 中的方言 d，从而绕过源查询 Qc 本身的复杂性。我们在两个真实基准（TPC-DS 和 SQLProcBench）上评估 RISE，在翻译准确率方面与传统基于规则的工具以及基于 LLM 的方法进行对比。RISE 在 TPC-DS 上达到 97.98% 的准确率，在 SQLProcBench 上达到 100%，分别平均超出基线 24.62% 和 238.41%。","tl":"用方言感知查询化简自动抽取翻译规则，再回用于复杂查询。","au":["Xudong Xie","Yuwei Zhang","Wensheng Dou","Yu Gao","Ziyu Cui","Jiansen Song","Rui Yang","Jun Wei"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["SQL dialect translation","query reduction","LLM","database migration","translation rules"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/215/x"},{"id":"p00702","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Code Changes to Quality Gains: An Empirical Study in Python ML Systems with PyQu","tz":"从代码变更到质量提升：借助 PyQu 对 Python 机器学习系统的实证研究","a":"In an era shaped by Generative Artificial Intelligence for code generation and the rising adoption of Python-based Machine Learning systems (MLS), software quality has emerged as a major concern. As these systems grow in complexity and importance, a key obstacle lies in understanding exactly how specific code changes affect overall quality—a shortfall aggravated by the lack of quality assessment tools and a clear mapping between ML systems code changes and their quality effects. Although prior work has explored code changes in MLS, it mostly stops at what the changes are, leaving a gap in our knowledge of the relationship between code changes and the MLS quality. To address this gap, we conducted a large-scale empirical study of 3,340 open-source Python ML projects, encompassing more than 3.7 million commits and 2.7 trillion lines of code. We introduce PyQu, a novel tool that leverages low-level software metrics to identify quality-enhancing commits with an average accuracy, precision, and recall of 0.84 and 0.85 of average F1 score. Using PyQu and a thematic analysis, we identified 61 code changes, each demonstrating a direct impact on enhancing software quality, and we classified them into 13 categories based on contextual characteristics. 41% of the changes are newly discovered by our study and have not been identified by state-of-the-art Python changes detection tools. Our work offers a vital foundation for researchers, practitioners, educators, and tool developers, advancing the quest for automated quality assessment and best practices in Python-based ML software.","az":"在生成式人工智能用于代码生成、以及基于 Python 的机器学习系统（MLS）被日益广泛采用的时代，软件质量已成为一个重大关切。随着这些系统的复杂性和重要性不断增长，一个关键障碍在于准确理解具体的代码变更如何影响整体质量——而质量评估工具的缺失以及 ML 系统代码变更与其质量影响之间缺乏清晰映射，进一步加剧了这一问题。尽管已有工作探讨过 MLS 中的代码变更，但大多止步于“变更是什么”，在代码变更与 MLS 质量之间关系的认识上仍存在空白。为填补这一空白，我们对 3,340 个开源 Python ML 项目开展了大规模实证研究，涵盖超过 370 万次提交和 2.7 万亿行代码。我们提出 PyQu，一种利用底层软件度量来识别质量提升型提交的新工具，其平均准确率、精确率和召回率为 0.84，平均 F1 分数为 0.85。借助 PyQu 与主题分析，我们识别出 61 种代码变更，每一种都对提升软件质量有直接影响，并依据上下文特征将其归为 13 个类别。其中 41% 的变更是本研究新发现的，尚未被最先进的 Python 变更检测工具识别。我们的工作为研究者、从业者、教育者和工具开发者提供了重要基础，推动了 Python 机器学习软件中自动化质量评估与最佳实践的探索。","tl":"大规模挖掘提交，识别出 61 种真正提升质量的代码变更。","au":["Mohamed Almukhtar","Anwar Ghammam","Marouane Kessentini","Hua Ming"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["code change","software quality","Python ML systems","mining software repositories","PyQu"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/216/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.02827"},{"id":"p00703","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SmartC2Rust: Iterative, Feedback-Driven C-to-Rust Translation via Large Language Models for Safety and Equivalence","tz":"SmartC2Rust：借助大语言模型进行迭代式、反馈驱动的 C 到 Rust 翻译，兼顾安全性与语义等价","a":"Memory safety vulnerabilities remain prevalent in today’s software systems and one promising solution to mitigate them is to adopt memory-safe languages such as Rust. Due to legacy code written in memory unsafe C, there is strong motivation to translate legacy C code into Rust. Prior works have already shown promise in using Large Language Models (LLMs) for such translations. However, significant challenges persist for LLM-based translation: the translated code often fails to compile, let alone reduce unsafe statements and maintain the semantic functionalities due to inherent limitations of LLMs such as limited token size and inconsistent outputs. In this paper, we design an automated C-to-Rust translation system, called SmartC2Rust, to segment and convert the C code to Rust with memory safety and semantic equivalence. The key insight is to iteratively refine the output Rust code with additional feedback, e.g., compilation errors, segmentation contexts, semantic discrepancies, and memory unsafe statements. Such feedback will gradually improve the quality of generated Rust code, thus mitigating unsafety, inconsistency, and semantic issues. Our evaluation shows that SmartC2Rust significantly decreases the unsafe statements and outperforms prior works in security and semantic equivalence.","az":"内存安全漏洞在当今软件系统中依然普遍存在，缓解它们的一个有前景的方案是采用 Rust 这类内存安全语言。由于大量遗留代码是用内存不安全的 C 编写的，将遗留 C 代码翻译为 Rust 的动机十分强烈。已有工作已经展示了使用大语言模型（LLM）进行此类翻译的潜力。然而，基于 LLM 的翻译仍面临重大挑战：由于 LLM 固有的局限（如有限的 token 长度和输出不一致），翻译出的代码往往无法编译，更谈不上减少 unsafe 语句并保持语义功能。本文设计了一个自动化的 C 到 Rust 翻译系统 SmartC2Rust，它将 C 代码切分并转换为具备内存安全性和语义等价性的 Rust 代码。核心洞见是利用额外反馈（例如编译错误、切分上下文、语义差异以及内存不安全语句）来迭代式地优化输出的 Rust 代码。这些反馈将逐步提升生成的 Rust 代码质量，从而缓解不安全性、不一致性和语义问题。评估表明，SmartC2Rust 显著减少了 unsafe 语句，并在安全性与语义等价性方面优于以往工作。","tl":"用编译与语义差异反馈迭代修正，降低译出 Rust 的 unsafe 语句。","au":["Momoko Shiraishi","Yinzhi Cao","Takahiro Shinagawa"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["C-to-Rust translation","memory safety","LLM","semantic equivalence","iterative feedback"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/217/x"},{"id":"p00704","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"INTENTFIX: Automated Logic Vulnerability Repair via LLM-Driven Intent Modeling","tz":"INTENTFIX：通过 LLM 驱动的意图建模实现逻辑漏洞自动修复","a":"Logic vulnerabilities, which arise from semantic gaps between a developer’s intent and the actual code, represent a critical and growing challenge in software security. Unlike syntactic bugs, these vulnerabilities pass traditional testing while harboring critical security flaws that can lead to severe breaches. We introduce INTENTFIX, a novel framework that automatically repairs logic vulnerabilities through intent-centric security analysis. INTENTFIX first leverages a Large Language Model (LLM) to systematically extract and formalize the developer’s implicit intent into a structured model. It then performs a differential analysis between this intent model and the implementation to precisely identify semantic gaps. Finally, it synthesizes and refines a patch through a multi-aspect, LLM-driven reasoning process. We evaluated INTENTFIX on a comprehensive dataset of 1,107 real-world CVE cases across five vulnerability types and 19 programming languages, achieving a patch accuracy of 64.5%, a 1.97× improvement over strong Chain-of-Thought (CoT) LLM baselines. This work makes three primary contributions: (1) We formalize intent-centric analysis as a new theoretical foundation for logic vulnerability repair. (2) We introduce a novel, structured framework that effectively harnesses an LLM’s reasoning capabilities for security. (3) We provide extensive empirical evidence validating our approach and offering new insights into the role of context in automated program repair.","az":"逻辑漏洞源于开发者意图与实际代码之间的语义鸿沟，是软件安全中一个关键且日益严峻的挑战。与语法缺陷不同，这类漏洞能够通过传统测试，却潜藏着可能导致严重安全事故的关键缺陷。我们提出 INTENTFIX，一个通过以意图为中心的安全分析来自动修复逻辑漏洞的新框架。INTENTFIX 首先利用大语言模型（LLM）系统性地抽取开发者的隐含意图并将其形式化为结构化模型；随后在该意图模型与实现之间执行差分分析，以精确定位语义鸿沟；最后通过多方面的、LLM 驱动的推理过程合成并精化补丁。我们在一个涵盖五类漏洞、19 种编程语言、共 1,107 个真实 CVE 案例的综合数据集上评估 INTENTFIX，补丁准确率达到 64.5%，相比强大的思维链（CoT）LLM 基线提升 1.97 倍。本工作有三项主要贡献：(1) 我们将以意图为中心的分析形式化为逻辑漏洞修复的新理论基础；(2) 我们提出了一个新颖的结构化框架，有效驾驭 LLM 的安全推理能力；(3) 我们提供了广泛的实证证据验证该方法，并就上下文在自动程序修复中的作用给出新见解。","tl":"把开发者意图形式化后做差分，定位并修补语义鸿沟型逻辑漏洞。","au":["Jinseok Heo","Dongwook Choi","Jinyoung Kim","Misoo Kim","Eunseok Lee"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["logic vulnerability repair","intent modeling","CVE","differential analysis","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/218/x"},{"id":"p00705","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"BTreeFuzz: Enhanced Feedback Mechanism for ROS Program Fuzzer Based on Behavior Tree","tz":"BTreeFuzz：基于行为树的 ROS 程序模糊测试反馈机制增强","a":"Robots are increasingly taking on human roles and functions, and societal expectations for these machines to perform critical tasks and eliminate the problem of human error continue to rise. The robot operating system (ROS) is considered the de facto standard that has been widely used to develop robotic programs. However, even though robot malfunctions should be minimized, it remains highly challenging to develop ROS programs without software vulnerabilities. As a result, many ROS programs still contain software vulnerabilities that can lead to serious malfunctions. To address this concern, researchers have recently presented several fuzzing techniques to automatically detect these vulnerabilities in ROS programs. A feedback mechanism for fuzzing requires a specific metric tailored to the features of ROS programs. However, existing ROS program fuzzers have been unable to provide adequate feedback mechanisms to make this possible. For instance, ROFER, a state-of-the-art ROS program fuzzer, cannot correctly differentiate between multiple distinct robot statuses based on its feedback mechanism metric, and often mistakenly identifies identical statuses as being different from each other, making it ineffective at detecting unique crashes. In this paper, we propose a new ROS program fuzzer named BTreeFuzz, which incorporates a novel feedback mechanism metric. BTreeFuzz collects a behavior tree log to track the sequence of the robot’s executed tasks and their statuses. Based on the log, BTreeFuzz constructs a status graph that represents the robot’s state transitions and its status as dictated by the status graph. Using the degree of similarity between the status graphs, BTreeFuzz determines whether the corresponding inputs are interesting or not. Compared to other state-of-the-art ROS program fuzzers, BTreeFuzz differentiates robot statuses more precisely and detects 49.31% more unique crashes per run on average. Finally, we present 35 bugs that BTreeFuzz found, 11 of which were previously unknown.","az":"机器人正越来越多地承担人类的角色与职能，社会对这些机器执行关键任务、消除人为错误问题的期待持续上升。机器人操作系统（ROS）被视为开发机器人程序的事实标准并被广泛使用。然而，尽管机器人故障理应被最小化，开发不含软件漏洞的 ROS 程序依然极具挑战。因此，许多 ROS 程序仍包含可能导致严重故障的软件漏洞。为应对这一问题，研究者近期提出了若干模糊测试技术以自动检测 ROS 程序中的漏洞。模糊测试的反馈机制需要一个针对 ROS 程序特性量身定制的度量指标。然而，现有的 ROS 程序模糊测试器无法提供足够充分的反馈机制。例如，最先进的 ROS 程序模糊测试器 ROFER 无法基于其反馈机制指标正确区分多个不同的机器人状态，常常错误地把相同状态识别为彼此不同，因而在检测唯一崩溃方面效果不佳。本文提出一个新的 ROS 程序模糊测试器 BTreeFuzz，它引入了一种新颖的反馈机制度量。BTreeFuzz 收集行为树日志以追踪机器人已执行任务的序列及其状态；基于该日志，BTreeFuzz 构建状态图来表示机器人的状态转移及其由状态图刻画的状态。利用状态图之间的相似程度，BTreeFuzz 判定对应输入是否“有价值”。与其他最先进的 ROS 程序模糊测试器相比，BTreeFuzz 能更精确地区分机器人状态，平均每轮多检出 49.31% 的唯一崩溃。最后，我们展示了 BTreeFuzz 发现的 35 个缺陷，其中 11 个此前未知。","tl":"用行为树日志构建状态图作为模糊测试反馈，精确区分机器人状态。","au":["Hee Yeon Kim","Gyunghoon Kim","Dong Hoon Lee","Wonsuk Choi"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["ROS fuzzing","behavior tree","feedback mechanism","robot status graph","unique crashes"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/219/x"},{"id":"p00706","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Semantic-based Optimization Approach for Repairing LLMs: Case Study on Code Generation","tz":"一种基于语义的大模型修复优化方法：以代码生成为例","a":"Language Models (LMs) are widely used in software engineering for code generation, but they may produce code with errors. Rather than repairing the generated code, a more thorough way is to address the underlying failures of models. LM repair offers a lightweight solution to this challenge: it requires minimal data, reduces computational costs, and reduces the side effects. Unlike full retraining, LM repair focuses on applying tailored updates to targeted neurons, making it ideal for scenarios with limited resources, high-performance demands, or strict safety requirements. In this paper, we propose {S}emantic {T}argeting for {A}nalytical {R}epair (STAR), a pioneering and novel semantic-based optimization approach for repairing LLMs. STAR realizes the main operations of repairing LMs in an optimization process, including locating buggy neurons'', solving neuron patches'', and patching ``buggy neurons''. Correspondingly, it computes the deltas of weight matrix as the prior information to guide optimization; and attributes the targeted layers and neurons leveraging statistical insights. The neuron patches are computed with a solid semantic-based analytical formula, which directly bridges the changes to logits with the deltas of neurons, by steering latent representations. Compared to the prior work of LM repair (MINT) and optimization methods (SGD), STAR integrates their strengths while mitigating their limitations. By implementing LM repair as an optimization-based process, STAR supports solving multiple failures together, significantly improving the usefulness. Evaluated on coding tasks using popular code LMs, STAR demonstrates superior effectiveness compared with the state-of-the-art. For instance, on CoNaLa, STAR obtained 10.5% 19.9% improvements in ExactMatch score. Besides, STAR exhibits better efficiency, achieving an average speedup of 2.4 7.0 times in solving each model failure. In terms of side effects, namely the balance between generalization and specificity, STAR outperforms prior work by a significant margin. Additionally, we conducted assessments on the overfitting risk of LM repair as well as the cumulative impact. Further, we analyzed the differences with pipeline-based methods and explained the reason why STAR is better and how it mitigated the common limitations of LM repair.","az":"语言模型（LM）在软件工程中被广泛用于代码生成，但它们可能产生含错误的代码。与其修复生成出的代码，更彻底的方式是处理模型底层的失败。LM 修复为此提供了一种轻量级方案：所需数据极少、计算成本更低、副作用更小。与完整重训不同，LM 修复聚焦于对目标神经元施加定制化更新，因而非常适合资源受限、性能要求高或安全要求严格的场景。本文提出 STAR（Semantic Targeting for Analytical Repair），一种开创性的、新颖的基于语义的大模型修复优化方法。STAR 在一个优化过程中实现了 LM 修复的主要操作，包括定位“有缺陷的神经元”、求解“神经元补丁”以及为“有缺陷的神经元”打补丁。相应地，它计算权重矩阵的增量作为先验信息来引导优化，并利用统计洞见归因到目标层与目标神经元。神经元补丁由一个扎实的、基于语义的解析公式计算得出，该公式通过引导潜在表示，直接把 logits 的变化与神经元的增量联系起来。与此前的 LM 修复工作（MINT）以及优化方法（SGD）相比，STAR 融合了它们的长处并缓解了各自的局限。通过把 LM 修复实现为基于优化的过程，STAR 支持同时求解多个失败，显著提升了实用性。在使用流行代码 LM 的编程任务上评估显示，STAR 相比最先进方法效果更优。例如在 CoNaLa 上，STAR 在 ExactMatch 分数上取得 10.5%~19.9% 的提升。此外，STAR 效率更高，在求解每个模型失败上平均加速 2.4~7.0 倍。在副作用方面，即泛化性与特异性之间的平衡上，STAR 大幅优于以往工作。我们还评估了 LM 修复的过拟合风险以及累积影响，并进一步分析了与基于流水线方法的差异，解释了 STAR 为何更优、以及它如何缓解 LM 修复的常见局限。","tl":"用解析式语义公式直接求解神经元补丁，一次修复多个模型失败。","au":["Jian Gu","Aldeida Aleti","Chunyang Chen","Hongyu Zhang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["LM repair","neuron patching","model editing","code generation","semantic optimization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/220/x"},{"id":"p00707","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SSAR: A Novel Software Architecture Recovery Approach Enhancing Accuracy and Scalability","tz":"SSAR：一种兼顾准确性与可扩展性的新型软件架构恢复方法","a":"Software architecture is critical for software development and maintenance. As software evolves, its architecture may drift from the original design, resulting in architectural degradation that negatively affects software quality. To effectively manage and maintain software systems, architects need an accurate understanding of the current architecture, but manual analysis is time-consuming and error-prone. Therefore, numerous automated architecture recovery techniques have been developed to facilitate this process. However, existing techniques often face limitations in either accuracy or efficiency, especially when dealing with large-scale software systems. In this paper, we propose a novel architecture recovery approach that integrates semantic similarity and structural dependencies between files to construct a weighted graph. Then it applies an optimized community detection algorithm to partition the graph for software modularization. To evaluate the effectiveness of our approach, we selected nine open-source projects with ground-truth architectures and compared our approach against six state-of-the-art architecture recovery techniques. Experimental results have shown that our approach improves accuracy ranging from 5.0% to 90.9%, 3.8% to 16.9%, and 12.5% to 500% in the three well-known architecture similarity metrics (𝑀𝑜 𝐽𝑜𝐹𝑀, 𝑎2𝑎, and 𝑐2𝑐𝑐𝑣𝑔), respectively. Additionally, it reduces the average execution time by 5% to 99%. In conclusion, our approach not only achieves a more precise recovery of software architecture but also significantly cuts down the time and effort required for the recovery process.","az":"软件架构对软件开发与维护至关重要。随着软件演化，其架构可能偏离最初设计，导致架构退化，进而损害软件质量。为有效管理和维护软件系统，架构师需要准确理解当前架构，但人工分析既耗时又易出错。因此，已有大量自动化架构恢复技术被提出以辅助这一过程。然而，现有技术在准确性或效率上常存在局限，尤其在处理大规模软件系统时。本文提出一种新颖的架构恢复方法，它整合文件之间的语义相似度与结构依赖关系来构建加权图，随后应用一种优化的社区发现算法对该图进行划分，实现软件模块化。为评估方法有效性，我们选取了九个具有真实架构标注的开源项目，并与六种最先进的架构恢复技术进行对比。实验结果显示，我们的方法在三项知名架构相似度指标（MoJoFM、a2a 和 c2ccvg）上分别取得 5.0%~90.9%、3.8%~16.9% 和 12.5%~500% 的准确率提升，同时将平均执行时间降低 5% 至 99%。总之，我们的方法不仅实现了更精确的软件架构恢复，还显著削减了恢复过程所需的时间与人力。","tl":"融合语义相似与结构依赖建加权图，用社区发现做架构恢复。","au":["Wei Ding","Ran Mo","Chaochao Wu","Haopeng Song"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["architecture recovery","software modularization","community detection","semantic similarity","structural dependency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/221/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/221/SSAR-A-Novel-Software-Architecture-Recovery-Approach-Enhancing-Accuracy-and-Scalabil"},{"id":"p00708","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Enhancing Symbolic Execution with Self-Configuring Parameters","tz":"用自配置参数增强符号执行","a":"We present ParaSuit, a self-configuring technique that enhances symbolic execution by autonomously adjusting its parameters tailored to each program under test. Modern symbolic execution tools are typically equipped with various external parameters to effectively test real-world programs. However, the need for users to fine-tune a multitude of parameters for optimal testing outcomes makes these tools harder to use and limits their potential benefits. Despite recent efforts to improve this tuning process, existing techniques are not self-configuring; they cannot dynamically identify which parameters to tune for each target program, and for each manually selected parameter, they sample a value from a fixed, user-defined set of candidate values that is specific to that parameter and remains unchanged across programs. The goal of this paper is to automatically configure symbolic execution parameters from scratch for each program. To this end, ParaSuit begins by automatically identifying all available parameters in the symbolic execution tool and evaluating each parameter’s impact through interactions with the tool. It then applies a specialized algorithm to iteratively select promising parameters, construct sampling spaces for each, and update their sampling probabilities based on data accumulated from symbolic execution runs using sampled parameter values. We implemented ParaSuit on KLEE and assessed it across 12 open-source C programs. The results demonstrate that ParaSuit significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art method without self-configuring parameters, achieving an average of 26% higher branch coverage. Remarkably, ParaSuit identified 11 unique bugs, four of which were exclusively discovered by ParaSuit.","az":"我们提出 ParaSuit，一种自配置技术，通过针对每个被测程序自主调整参数来增强符号执行。现代符号执行工具通常配备了各种外部参数，以便有效测试真实世界程序。然而，用户需要为获得最优测试结果而精调大量参数，这使这些工具更难使用，也限制了它们的潜在收益。尽管近期已有改进该调参过程的努力，现有技术并非自配置：它们无法针对每个目标程序动态识别应调哪些参数，而且对每个人工选定的参数，只能从一个固定的、用户定义的、特定于该参数且跨程序保持不变的候选值集合中采样。本文的目标是为每个程序从零开始自动配置符号执行参数。为此，ParaSuit 首先自动识别符号执行工具中所有可用参数，并通过与工具交互评估每个参数的影响；随后应用一种专门算法迭代地选择有前景的参数、为每个参数构建采样空间，并根据使用采样参数值运行符号执行所积累的数据更新其采样概率。我们在 KLEE 上实现了 ParaSuit，并在 12 个开源 C 程序上进行评估。结果表明，ParaSuit 显著优于不具备自配置能力的最先进方法，平均分支覆盖率高出 26%。值得注意的是，ParaSuit 识别出 11 个唯一缺陷，其中 4 个仅被 ParaSuit 发现。","tl":"从零自动识别并迭代采样符号执行参数，无需人工指定候选值。","au":["Minjong Kim","Sooyoung Cha"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic execution","parameter tuning","self-configuring","KLEE","branch coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/222/x"},{"id":"p00709","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Seed to Scope: Reasoning to Identify Change Impact Sets","tz":"从种子到范围：用推理识别变更影响集","a":"Change impact analysis (IA), which identifies the set of co-changed program elements (i.e., impact set), is critical for several software engineering tasks. However, existing IA approaches struggle with a trade-off between precision (correctly detecting impacted elements) and recall (detecting all relevant ones). More importantly, they are limited in intent-aware settings, where co-changing elements are determined by a given change intent. In this work, we propose RIPPLE, an intent-aware IA approach that leverages large language models (LLMs) to capture change dependencies by linking intent to program elements and estimating their co-change relationships. To address the precision-recall tradeoff, we adopt a two-phase design: (1) a seed-to-scope expansion strategy that expands the impact set using evolutionary and dependence coupling to improve recall, and (2) a plan-then-predict strategy where an LLM-generated change plan refines impact estimation for higher precision. We evaluate RIPPLE on real-world commits from Apache projects, achieving a 39.7%-380.8% improvement in F1-score over existing IA approaches. In addition, RIPPLE introduces flexibility, allowing users to prioritize higher precision or recall based on their preferences.","az":"变更影响分析（IA）识别协同变更的程序元素集合（即影响集），对多项软件工程任务至关重要。然而，现有 IA 方法在精确率（正确检出受影响元素）与召回率（检出全部相关元素）之间难以兼顾。更重要的是，它们在意图感知的场景下能力有限——在这种场景中，协同变更的元素由给定的变更意图决定。本文提出 RIPPLE，一种意图感知的 IA 方法，利用大语言模型（LLM）通过把意图与程序元素相关联并估计它们之间的协同变更关系来捕获变更依赖。为解决精确率—召回率的权衡，我们采用两阶段设计：(1) 一种“从种子到范围”的扩展策略，利用演化耦合与依赖耦合扩展影响集以提升召回率；(2) 一种“先规划后预测”的策略，由 LLM 生成的变更计划来精化影响估计以获得更高精确率。我们在 Apache 项目的真实提交上评估 RIPPLE，相比现有 IA 方法在 F1 分数上提升 39.7%~380.8%。此外，RIPPLE 具备灵活性，允许用户根据偏好优先侧重精确率或召回率。","tl":"先按耦合扩召回、再用 LLM 变更计划提精度的意图感知影响分析。","au":["Aashish Yadavally","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["change impact analysis","impact set","co-change","LLM","intent-aware"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/223/x","pu":"https://aashishyadavally.github.io/assets/pdf/pub-icse2026-(2).pdf"},{"id":"p00710","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Enforcing Control Flow Integrity on DeFi Smart Contracts","tz":"为 DeFi 智能合约强制实施控制流完整性","a":"Smart contracts power decentralized financial (DeFi) services but are vulnerable to complex security exploits that can lead to significant financial losses. Existing security measures often fail to adequately protect these contracts due to the composability of DeFi protocols and the increasing sophistication of attacks. Through a large-scale empirical study of historical transactions from the 37 hacked DeFi protocols, we discovered that while benign transactions typically exhibit a limited number of unique control flows, in stark contrast, attack transactions consistently introduce novel, previously unobserved control flows. Building on these insights, we developed CrossGuard, a novel framework that enforces control flow integrity in real-time to secure smart contracts. Crucially, CrossGuard does not require prior knowledge of specific hacks; instead, it dynamically enforces control flow whitelisting policies and applies simplification heuristics at runtime. This approach monitors and prevents potential attacks by reverting all transactions that do not adhere to the established control flow whitelisting rules. Our evaluation demonstrates that CrossGuard effectively blocks 35 of the 37 analyzed attacks when configured only once prior to contract deployment, maintaining a low false positive rate of 0.26% and minimal additional gas costs. These results underscore the efficacy of applying control flow integrity to smart contracts, significantly enhancing security beyond traditional methods and addressing the evolving threat landscape in the DeFi ecosystem.","az":"智能合约驱动着去中心化金融（DeFi）服务，但易受复杂安全攻击的影响，可能造成重大经济损失。由于 DeFi 协议的可组合性以及攻击手法日益精巧，现有安全措施往往无法充分保护这些合约。通过对 37 个被攻击 DeFi 协议历史交易的大规模实证研究，我们发现良性交易通常只表现出数量有限的唯一控制流，而与之形成鲜明对比的是，攻击交易始终会引入此前从未观察到的新控制流。基于这些洞见，我们开发了 CrossGuard，一个实时强制控制流完整性以保护智能合约的新框架。关键在于，CrossGuard 不需要关于具体攻击的先验知识；相反，它在运行时动态执行控制流白名单策略并应用化简启发式。该方法通过回滚所有不符合既定控制流白名单规则的交易来监控并阻止潜在攻击。评估表明，在合约部署前仅配置一次的情况下，CrossGuard 有效阻断了所分析的 37 起攻击中的 35 起，误报率低至 0.26%，额外 gas 开销也极小。这些结果凸显了将控制流完整性应用于智能合约的有效性，其安全性显著超越传统方法，并应对了 DeFi 生态中不断演变的威胁态势。","tl":"发现攻击交易必引入新控制流，据此做运行时白名单拦截。","au":["Zhiyang Chen","Sidi Mohamed Beillahi","Pasha Barahimi","Cyrus Minwalla","Han Du","Andreas Veneris","Fan Long"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["control flow integrity","DeFi","smart contract security","runtime enforcement","attack transactions"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/224/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.05509"},{"id":"p00711","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CodeMapper: A Language-Agnostic Approach to Mapping Code Regions Across Commits","tz":"CodeMapper：一种语言无关的跨提交代码区域映射方法","a":"The evolution of software involves numerous code changes. To follow changes made by others, developers are commonly facing the problem of mapping a specific code region from one commit to another. For example, they may want to determine how the condition of an if-statement, a specific line in a configuration file, or the definition of a function is changing. We call this problem the code mapping problem. Existing techniques, such as git diff, address this problem insufficiently because they show all changes made to a file, instead of focusing on a code region of the developer’s choice. Other techniques focus on specific code elements and programming languages, e.g., methods in Java, limiting their applicability. This paper introduces CodeMapper, an approach to address the code mapping problem in a way that is independent of specific program elements and programming languages. Given a code region in one commit, CodeMapper finds the corresponding region in another commit. The approach consists of two phases: (i) computing candidate regions by analyzing diffs, detecting code movements, and searching for specific code fragments, and (ii) selecting the most likely target region by calculating similarities. Our evaluation applies CodeMapper to four datasets: two new, hand-annotated datasets, each containing 100 code region pairs of different sizes, written in ten popular programming languages, a dataset of 187 evolving comments used to suppress static analysis warnings in Python, and a dataset of 2,005 pairs of code elements from prior work. CodeMapper correctly identifies the expected target region (i.e., exact match rate) in 71.0%–94.5% of all cases, improving over the best available baselines by 1.5–58.8 absolute percent points.","az":"软件演化涉及大量代码变更。为跟进他人所做的修改，开发者常面临把某个特定代码区域从一个提交映射到另一个提交的问题。例如，他们可能想确定某个 if 语句的条件、配置文件中的某一行，或某个函数的定义是如何变化的。我们把这一问题称为代码映射问题。现有技术（如 git diff）对该问题的处理并不充分，因为它们展示对一个文件所做的全部变更，而非聚焦于开发者所选的某个代码区域。另一些技术则只针对特定代码元素和编程语言（例如 Java 中的方法），限制了其适用性。本文提出 CodeMapper，一种以独立于特定程序元素和编程语言的方式解决代码映射问题的方法。给定某个提交中的一个代码区域，CodeMapper 在另一个提交中找到对应区域。该方法包含两个阶段：(i) 通过分析 diff、检测代码移动并搜索特定代码片段来计算候选区域；(ii) 通过计算相似度选出最可能的目标区域。我们的评估把 CodeMapper 应用于四个数据集：两个新的人工标注数据集（各含 100 对不同规模的代码区域，涉及十种流行编程语言）、一个包含 187 条用于抑制 Python 静态分析告警的演化注释的数据集，以及一个来自先前工作的 2,005 对代码元素的数据集。CodeMapper 在 71.0%~94.5% 的情况下正确识别出预期目标区域（即完全匹配率），比可得的最佳基线绝对提升 1.5~58.8 个百分点。","tl":"不依赖语言与元素类型，把任意代码区域跨提交对齐。","au":["Huimin Hu","Michael Pradel"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["code mapping","code region","commit evolution","language-agnostic","code movement detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/225/x"},{"id":"p00712","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Beyond Adoption: Examining the Evolution and Impact of Codes of Conduct on Open-Source Communities","tz":"超越采纳：考察行为准则在开源社区中的演化与影响","a":"While open source software (OSS) communities thrive on collaboration, conflicts such as toxic behavior and discrimination can surface, threatening the sustainability of these projects. To address these concerns, many communities have adopted a Code of Conduct (CoC) as a mechanism for governing and moderating members’ behavior. Previous research has explored the motivations behind CoC adoption and the content changes made, but it remains unclear how different communities are using and maintaining CoCs over time after the initial adoption and how the presence of a CoC impacts a community. To bridge these gaps, our study compiles a large-scale dataset of CoCs along with their change histories in OSS repositories on GitHub to quantitatively (1) understand the evolution of CoC content and identify change patterns across different communities, and (2) investigate the potential impact of CoC adoption on community engagement. Our results show that OSS communities with a CoC attract more new contributors and decrease the number of existing contributors disengaging from the community in the long term. The insights from this study provide guidance on best practices for maintaining CoCs in OSS communities and offer statistically significant evidence of their impact.","az":"开源软件（OSS）社区以协作为生命线，但诸如有毒行为和歧视等冲突仍可能浮现，威胁项目的可持续性。为应对这些问题，许多社区采纳了行为准则（Code of Conduct, CoC）作为治理和规范成员行为的机制。以往研究探讨过采纳 CoC 的动机以及内容上的变化，但在初次采纳之后，不同社区如何随时间使用和维护 CoC、以及 CoC 的存在对社区产生何种影响，仍不清楚。为填补这些空白，我们的研究汇编了一个大规模数据集，涵盖 GitHub 上开源仓库中的 CoC 及其变更历史，用以定量地：(1) 理解 CoC 内容的演化并识别不同社区间的变更模式；(2) 考察采纳 CoC 对社区参与度的潜在影响。结果表明，拥有 CoC 的开源社区吸引了更多新贡献者，并在长期内减少了既有贡献者的流失。本研究的洞见为开源社区维护 CoC 的最佳实践提供了指导，并给出了其影响在统计意义上显著的证据。","tl":"量化证明采纳行为准则能吸引新贡献者并减少流失。","au":["Jiayi Sun","Hongbo Fang","Junming Zhang","Jiakai Shi","Ruitao Lai","Anita Ihuman","Richard Littauer","Shurui Zhou"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["code of conduct","open source community","governance","contributor engagement","GitHub mining"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/226/x","pu":"https://jys-sun.github.io/website/resources/ICSE26.pdf"},{"id":"p00713","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM-based Agents for Automated Bug Fixing: How Far Are We?","tz":"面向自动缺陷修复的 LLM 智能体：我们走到哪一步了？","a":"Large language models (LLMs) and LLM-based Agents have been applied to fix bugs automatically, demonstrating the capability in addressing software defects by engaging in development environment interaction, iterative validation and code modification. However, systematic analysis of these agent systems remain limited, particularly regarding performance variations among top-performing ones. In this paper, we examine six repair systems on the SWE-bench Verified benchmark for automated bug fixing. We first assess each system’s overall performance, noting the instances solvable by all or none of these systems, and explore the capabilities of different systems. We also compare fault localization accuracy at file and code symbol levels and evaluate bug reproduction capabilities. Through analysis, we concluded that further optimization is needed in both the LLM capability itself and the design of Agentic flow to improve the effectiveness of the Agent in bug fixing.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）以及基于 LLM 的智能体已被用于自动修复缺陷，展现出通过与开发环境交互、迭代验证和代码修改来处理软件缺陷的能力。然而，对这些智能体系统的系统性分析仍然有限，尤其是在表现最好的系统之间的性能差异方面。本文在 SWE-bench Verified 基准上考察六个用于自动缺陷修复的修复系统。我们首先评估每个系统的整体性能，指出所有系统都能解决和都无法解决的实例，并探究不同系统的能力。我们还在文件级和代码符号级比较了缺陷定位准确率，并评估了缺陷复现能力。通过分析，我们得出结论：要提升智能体在缺陷修复中的有效性，LLM 自身能力和 Agentic 流程的设计都还需要进一步优化。","tl":"拆解六大修复智能体在定位与复现环节的能力差异与共同盲区。","au":["Xiangxin Meng","Zexiong Ma","Pengfei Gao","Chao Peng"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["SWE-bench Verified","bug fixing agents","fault localization","bug reproduction","empirical comparison"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/227/x"},{"id":"p00714","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Parse this! Summoning Context-Sensitive Inputs with Goblin","tz":"Parse this！用 Goblin 召唤上下文敏感的输入","a":"Grammar-based fuzzers have shown immense promise in identifying bugs in software systems that have highly-structured and intricate input formats ( , XML). Many of the existing grammar-based fuzzers rely on context-free grammars (CFGs) to represent the target’s input structure. CFGs, however, are often insufficient to precisely capture many application input formats containing context-sensitive constraints. Application-specific fuzzers, albeit effective, lack generality to be adapted to new applications. In this paper, we present Goblin, a new input generation language and tool that helps bridge this gap. Given a context-free grammar annotated with semantic constraints, Goblin generates inputs that both conform to the grammar and satisfy the constraints. While a few prior techniques target this problem, our method is distinguished by: (i) support for constraint solving over arbitrary SMT theories (e.g., bitvectors, integers, strings); (ii) a minimal core input language with formal semantics that is smaller and less complex than prior work; and (iii) a shift from global constraints to local, production rule constraints, which enables easier integration with certain fuzzing workflows. Goblin’s input generation approach is inspired by DPLL-style SAT solvers and enjoys the following formal guarantees: solution soundness, solution completeness, and refutation soundness. In addition to comparing Goblin with prior work, we demonstrate its effectiveness by incorporating it into a grammar-based network protocol fuzzer.","az":"基于文法的模糊测试器在识别输入格式高度结构化且复杂（例如 XML）的软件系统中的缺陷方面展现出巨大潜力。许多现有的基于文法的模糊测试器依赖上下文无关文法（CFG）来表示目标的输入结构。然而，CFG 往往不足以精确刻画许多包含上下文敏感约束的应用输入格式。面向特定应用的模糊测试器虽然有效，却缺乏推广到新应用的通用性。本文提出 Goblin，一种有助于弥合这一鸿沟的新输入生成语言与工具。给定一个带有语义约束标注的上下文无关文法，Goblin 生成既符合文法又满足约束的输入。虽然此前已有少数技术针对该问题，我们的方法的独特之处在于：(i) 支持在任意 SMT 理论（如位向量、整数、字符串）上进行约束求解；(ii) 提供一个带形式化语义的极简核心输入语言，比以往工作更小也更简单；(iii) 从全局约束转向局部的产生式规则约束，使其更易与某些模糊测试工作流集成。Goblin 的输入生成方法受 DPLL 风格 SAT 求解器启发，并享有以下形式化保证：解的可靠性（solution soundness）、解的完备性（solution completeness）以及反驳可靠性（refutation soundness）。除了与以往工作的对比之外，我们还将其集成进一个基于文法的网络协议模糊测试器，展示了其有效性。","tl":"把语义约束下放到产生式并用 SMT 求解，生成上下文敏感输入。","au":["Robert Lorch","Muhammad Daniyal Pirwani Dar","Cesare Tinelli","Omar Chowdhury"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["grammar-based fuzzing","context-sensitive constraints","SMT solving","input generation language","protocol fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/228/x"},{"id":"p00715","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Top General Performance = Top Domain Performance? DomainCodeBench: A Multi-domain Code Generation Benchmark","tz":"通用能力强就等于领域能力强吗？DomainCodeBench：一个多领域代码生成基准","a":"With the rapid advancement of large language models (LLMs), extensive research has been conducted to investigate the code generation capabilities of LLMs. However, existing efforts primarily focus on general-domain tasks, leaving LLMs’ code generation performance in real-world application domains underexplored. This raises a critical question: can a model’s general-domain coding ability reliably represent its ability in specialized domains? In this paper, we introduce DomainCodeBench, a multi-domain code generation benchmark designed to systematically evaluate LLMs across 12 software application domains and 15 programming languages. DomainCodeBench contains 2,400 manually verified tasks with ground-truth, human-annotated docstrings, and fine-grained dependency information to ensure more coverage of domain-specific challenges. Specifically, we first identify the most popular application domains by topic mining. Then, we curate coding tasks based on commonly used frameworks and platforms in each domain. We obtain several findings through extensive experiments on DomainCodeBench with ten mainstream LLMs. (1) Performance decoupling: experiments reveal that top general-domain models do not consistently excel in specific application domains; (2) Domain-specific weaknesses: LLMs often fail due to domain knowledge gaps and third-party library misusage; (3) Contextual enhancement: we show that augmenting prompts with domain-specific knowledge improves performance by around 38.17%, providing actionable insights for performance optimization. Our replication package, including the benchmark, source code, and experimental results, is available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/DomainCodeBench-E8E0 .","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）的快速发展，已有大量研究考察 LLM 的代码生成能力。然而，现有工作主要聚焦通用领域任务，对 LLM 在真实应用领域中的代码生成表现探索不足。这引出一个关键问题：模型的通用领域编码能力能否可靠地代表其在专门领域中的能力？本文提出 DomainCodeBench，一个多领域代码生成基准，旨在系统评估 LLM 在 12 个软件应用领域和 15 种编程语言上的表现。DomainCodeBench 包含 2,400 个人工验证的任务，配有标准答案、人工标注的文档字符串以及细粒度的依赖信息，以确保更充分覆盖领域特定挑战。具体而言，我们首先通过主题挖掘识别最热门的应用领域，然后基于各领域常用的框架与平台策划编码任务。通过在 DomainCodeBench 上对十个主流 LLM 进行大量实验，我们获得若干发现：(1) 性能解耦：实验显示顶尖的通用领域模型在特定应用领域中并不总是表现出色；(2) 领域特定弱点：LLM 常因领域知识缺失和第三方库误用而失败；(3) 上下文增强：我们表明在提示中补充领域特定知识可使性能提升约 38.17%，为性能优化提供了可操作的洞见。我们的复现包（含基准、源码与实验结果）发布于 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/DomainCodeBench-E8E0 。","tl":"揭示通用编码能力与领域编码能力解耦，且补领域知识可提升 38%。","au":["Dewu Zheng","Yanlin Wang","Ensheng Shi","Xilin Liu","Yuchi Ma","Hongyu Zhang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["multi-domain benchmark","code generation","domain knowledge","third-party library misuse","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/229/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/229/Top-General-Performance-Top-Domain-Performance-DomainCodeBench-A-Multi-domain-Cod"},{"id":"p00716","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Assessing Coherency and Consistency of Code Execution Reasoning by Large Language Models","tz":"评估大语言模型代码执行推理的连贯性与一致性","a":"This paper proposes CES, a task to evaluate the abilities of LLMs in simulating program execution and using that reasoning in programming tasks. Besides measuring the correctness of variable predictions during execution simulation, CES introduces the notion of coherence to determine whether the simulation complies with commonsense execution logic, even if the predicted values along the simulations are incorrect. This enables CES to rule out suspiciously correct output predictions due to reasoning shortcuts, hallucinations, or potential data leakage. CES also introduces a novel metric to measure reasoning consistency across tests with the same or different prime path coverage in a spectrum: strong, weak, and random. Evaluating 16 LLMs (including three reasoning LLMs) using CES indicates 81.42% coherent execution simulation on HumanEval, 46.92% and 53.08% of which result in correct and incorrect output predictions. Frontier LLMs such as GPT-4 and DeepSeek-R1 have the most incoherent execution reasoning, mostly due to natural language shortcuts. Despite relatively coherent execution simulation, LLMs’ reasoning performance across different tests is inconsistent, mostly random (48.87%) or weak (45.37%), potentially explaining their weakness in programming tasks that require path-sensitive program analysis to succeed. We also compare CES with bug prediction/localization/repair, which intuitively requires control- and data-flow awareness. We observe that LLMs barely incorporate execution reasoning into their analysis for bug-related tasks, and their success is primarily due to inherent abilities in pattern matching or natural language shortcuts, if not data leakage. Without reasoning, there is a threat to the generalizability of LLMs in dealing with unseen bugs or patterns in different contexts. CES can be used to vet the suspicious success of LLMs in these tasks systematically.","az":"本文提出 CES，一个用于评估 LLM 模拟程序执行、并把这种推理用于编程任务的能力的任务。除了度量执行模拟过程中变量预测的正确性之外，CES 还引入“连贯性”的概念，用以判定模拟是否符合常识性的执行逻辑——即便模拟过程中预测的值是错误的。这使 CES 能够排除因推理捷径、幻觉或潜在数据泄露而“可疑地正确”的输出预测。CES 还引入了一个新颖指标，在强、弱、随机这一谱系上度量在具有相同或不同主路径（prime path）覆盖的测试之间的推理一致性。使用 CES 评估 16 个 LLM（含三个推理型 LLM）表明，在 HumanEval 上有 81.42% 的执行模拟是连贯的，其中 46.92% 与 53.08% 分别对应正确与错误的输出预测。诸如 GPT-4 和 DeepSeek-R1 这样的前沿 LLM 执行推理最不连贯，主要源于自然语言捷径。尽管执行模拟相对连贯，LLM 在不同测试间的推理表现却不一致，多数为随机（48.87%）或弱（45.37%），这可能解释了它们在需要路径敏感程序分析才能成功的编程任务上的弱势。我们还把 CES 与缺陷预测/定位/修复进行比较——直觉上这些任务需要控制流与数据流意识。我们观察到，LLM 在缺陷相关任务的分析中几乎没有纳入执行推理，其成功主要源于模式匹配或自然语言捷径的固有能力，若非数据泄露的话。缺乏推理会威胁 LLM 在不同上下文中处理未见缺陷或模式时的泛化性。CES 可用于系统性地审视 LLM 在这些任务上可疑的成功。","tl":"提出连贯性与一致性指标，揭穿 LLM 执行推理中的捷径式正确。","au":["Changshu Liu","Yang Chen","Reyhaneh Jabbarvand"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["execution reasoning","coherence","consistency","prime path coverage","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/230/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.15079"},{"id":"p00717","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Context-Free Property Oriented Fuzzing","tz":"面向上下文无关性质的模糊测试","a":"Fuzzing is effective for finding software bugs. However, the bugs specified in context-free properties are difficult for the existing fuzzers. These bugs are triggered when the program execution contains specific sequences of operations, e.g., push and pop operations on the stack, and locking and unlocking operations on the lock. As far as we know, existing approaches do not support fuzzing for non-regular context-free properties, which are more expressive and can be used to specify bugs in many scenarios. This paper proposes a general runtime monitoring-based fuzzing framework for the bugs expressed as context-free properties. We propose two algorithms to improve fuzzing’s effectiveness and efficiency with respect to the context-free property. The algorithm for preserving input mutants leverages the state transition information of the property’s monitors. The other algorithm for mutating the input seed combines control flow information with state transition information to prioritize the different parts of the input. We have implemented our framework CFPOFuzz for C/C++ programs. The results of the extensive experiments on real-world C/C++ programs indicate our method’s effectiveness and efficiency. Compared with coverage-oriented fuzzing, our method achieves 3.83x speedups for generating the first target input triggering the bugs. Our method found 7 unknown zero-day bugs.","az":"模糊测试在发现软件缺陷方面很有效。然而，由上下文无关性质所刻画的缺陷对现有模糊测试器而言难以触及。这类缺陷在程序执行包含特定操作序列时才会被触发，例如栈上的 push 与 pop 操作、锁的加锁与解锁操作。据我们所知，现有方法并不支持针对非正则的上下文无关性质进行模糊测试，而这类性质表达能力更强，可用于刻画许多场景下的缺陷。本文提出一个通用的、基于运行时监控的模糊测试框架，用于以上下文无关性质表达的缺陷。我们提出两个算法以提升模糊测试针对上下文无关性质的有效性与效率：保留输入变体的算法利用性质监控器的状态转移信息；另一个用于变异输入种子的算法则结合控制流信息与状态转移信息，对输入的不同部分进行优先级排序。我们为 C/C++ 程序实现了框架 CFPOFuzz。在真实 C/C++ 程序上的大量实验结果表明了本方法的有效性与效率：与面向覆盖率的模糊测试相比，我们的方法在生成首个触发缺陷的目标输入上取得 3.83 倍加速，并发现了 7 个未知的零日缺陷。","tl":"用性质监控器的状态转移信息指导种子保留与变异优先级。","au":["Jiaqiang Yao","Meixi Liu","Zhenbang Chen","Yongchao Xing","Jinjian Luo","Yunlai Luo","Guofeng Zhang","Yufeng Zhang","Ji Wang"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["context-free property","runtime monitoring","fuzzing","seed mutation","state transition"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/231/x"},{"id":"p00718","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Input Reduction Enhanced LLM-based Program Repair","tz":"以输入缩减增强基于 LLM 的程序修复","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown great potential in Automated Program Repair (APR). Test inputs, being crucial for reasoning the root cause of failures, are always included in the prompt for LLM-based APR. Unfortunately, LLMs struggle to retain key information in long prompts. When the test inputs are extensive in the prompt, this may trigger the “lost-in-the-middle” issue, compromising repair performance. ReduceFix prompts an LLM to generate a reducer that minimizes failure-inducing test inputs without human effort, and then feeds the reduced failure-inducing inputs to guide patch generation. For targeted evaluation, we constructed LFTBench, the first long-input APR benchmark with 200 real bugs from 20 programming tasks, each paired with a failure‑inducing input whose median size is 1 MB. On this benchmark, ReduceFix shrinks inputs by 89.1% on average and improves overall pass@10 by up to 53.8% relative to a prompt that includes the original test, and by 17.6% compared with omitting the test entirely. Adding the same reduction step to ChatRepair and CREF increases their fix rate by 21.3% and 2.6%, respectively, without other changes. Our gains hold against a ddmin‑only reducing template baseline and transfer to repository‑level OSS‑Fuzz cases. Ablation studies further highlight the impact of input length and compressed failure information on repair success. These results underscore that automatically reducing failing inputs is a practical and powerful complement to LLM-based APR, significantly improving its scalability and effectiveness.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在自动程序修复（APR）中展现出巨大潜力。测试输入对于推断失败根因至关重要，因此在基于 LLM 的 APR 中总是被放入提示。遗憾的是，LLM 难以在长提示中保留关键信息。当提示中的测试输入十分庞大时，可能触发“迷失在中间”（lost-in-the-middle）问题，损害修复性能。ReduceFix 提示 LLM 生成一个归约器（reducer），无需人工投入即可最小化致错测试输入，然后把缩减后的致错输入用于引导补丁生成。为了有针对性地评估，我们构建了 LFTBench——首个长输入 APR 基准，包含来自 20 个编程任务的 200 个真实缺陷，每个缺陷都配有一个中位大小为 1 MB 的致错输入。在该基准上，ReduceFix 平均将输入缩小 89.1%，相较包含原始测试的提示，整体 pass@10 最多提升 53.8%；相较完全不包含测试的做法提升 17.6%。把同样的缩减步骤加入 ChatRepair 和 CREF，在不做其他改动的情况下分别使其修复率提升 21.3% 和 2.6%。我们的增益在与仅使用 ddmin 的归约模板基线对比中依然成立，并可迁移到仓库级的 OSS-Fuzz 案例。消融实验进一步凸显了输入长度与压缩后失败信息对修复成功率的影响。这些结果表明，自动缩减失败输入是对基于 LLM 的 APR 一种实用而有力的补充，显著提升了其可扩展性与有效性。","tl":"让 LLM 生成归约器压缩巨型致错输入，再喂给修复提示。","au":["Boyang Yang","Luyao Ren","Xin Yin","Jiadong Ren","Haoye Tian","Shunfu Jin"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["automated program repair","input reduction","lost-in-the-middle","LFTBench","failure-inducing input"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/232/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.15251"},{"id":"p00719","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Agent-Based Ensemble Reasoning for Repository-Level Issue Resolution","tz":"面向仓库级 Issue 求解的基于智能体的集成推理","a":"Software issue resolution is a critical challenge in software engineering and has garnered increasing attention in recent years. With the rapid advancement of large language models (LLMs), substantial progress has been made in addressing real-world software engineering tasks. Recent studies have introduced ensemble reasoning techniques to enhance the performance of LLM-based issue resolution. However, existing prompting-based methods still face limitations in effectively exploring large ensemble spaces and lack the capacity for repository-level understanding, both of which constrain their overall effectiveness. In this paper, we propose EnAgent, the first agent-based ensemble reasoning approach for repository-level issue resolution. EnAgent formulates our goal as an optimal solution search problem and addresses two key challenges, i.e., large ensemble spaces and repository-level understanding, through modular agents for generation, pruning, and selection. We conduct extensive experiments using three leading LLMs on the widely-adopted SWE-bench benchmark, comparing EnAgent against four state-of-the-art ensemble reasoning techniques. Experimental results demonstrate that EnAgent consistently achieves superior performance, with an average improvement of 10.22% over all baselines in terms of Pass@1. EnAgent has been integrated into Trae Agent, driving it to achieve first place on the SWE-bench Verified leaderboard as of January 2026, with a notable Pass@1 score of 78.80%.","az":"软件 issue 求解是软件工程中的关键挑战，近年来受到越来越多关注。随着大语言模型（LLM）的快速发展，在处理真实软件工程任务方面已取得长足进展。近期研究引入集成推理（ensemble reasoning）技术以提升基于 LLM 的 issue 求解性能。然而，现有基于提示的方法在有效探索庞大的集成空间方面仍有局限，且缺乏仓库级理解能力，二者共同制约了其整体效果。本文提出 EnAgent，首个面向仓库级 issue 求解的基于智能体的集成推理方法。EnAgent 将目标形式化为一个最优解搜索问题，并通过用于生成、剪枝和选择的模块化智能体来应对两大关键挑战：庞大的集成空间与仓库级理解。我们使用三个领先 LLM 在被广泛采用的 SWE-bench 基准上开展大量实验，将 EnAgent 与四种最先进的集成推理技术对比。实验结果表明 EnAgent 始终取得更优表现，在 Pass@1 上平均超出所有基线 10.22%。EnAgent 已集成进 Trae Agent，助其在 2026 年 1 月的 SWE-bench Verified 排行榜上位列第一，Pass@1 分数达到 78.80%。","tl":"把集成推理做成生成-剪枝-选择的智能体搜索，登顶 SWE-bench。","au":["Zhao Tian","Pengfei Gao","Junjie Chen","Chao Peng"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["issue resolution","ensemble reasoning","SWE-bench","agent modules","Pass@1"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/233/x","pu":"https://github.com/tianzhaotju/preprints/blob/main/ICSE'26%20-%20Agent-Based%20Ensemble%20Reasoning%20for%20Repository-Level%20Issue%20Resolution.pdf"},{"id":"p00720","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"NotDec: WebAssembly Decompilation With Inter-Procedural Type Recovery","tz":"NotDec：具备过程间类型恢复的 WebAssembly 反编译","a":"With WebAssembly widely supported in browsers, containers, IoT devices, and serverless platforms and increasingly adopted as a universal low‑level bytecode standard, auditing its hidden vulnerabilities and malicious intentions has become critical. Decompiling existing WebAssembly modules can help security researchers and end users understand binary behavior, but current tools suffer from verbose result, poor readability, and limited type recovery. We present NotDec, an advanced WebAssembly decompilation framework. NotDec extends the WebAssembly type checking algorithm to lift bytecode into an SSA‑based IR, applies the inter-procedural type recovery algorithm Retypd with pointer and numeric value differentiation methods to recover complex data structures, and leverages Memory SSA alongside semantics‑preserving structured control‑flow analysis to emit readable, semantically consistent C code. NotDec achieves 100% recompilation success rate on all 5,241 Juliet samples and all Howard dataset programs, significantly outperforming baselines including Ghidra (45.95% success rate). On type recovery accuracy, NotDec recovers 85.33% of struct member accesses in real-world programs, vastly exceeding Ghidra’s 9.24%. While the full inter-procedural version faces scalability challenges on large binaries, the intra-procedural variant NotDec_F demonstrates superior efficiency, consuming less than half of Ghidra’s memory and up to 97% less execution time on unoptimized binaries.","az":"随着 WebAssembly 在浏览器、容器、物联网设备和无服务器平台上获得广泛支持，并日益被采纳为通用的低层字节码标准，审计其隐藏漏洞与恶意意图变得至关重要。反编译现有 WebAssembly 模块可以帮助安全研究者和终端用户理解二进制行为，但当前工具存在结果冗长、可读性差、类型恢复能力有限等问题。我们提出 NotDec，一个先进的 WebAssembly 反编译框架。NotDec 扩展了 WebAssembly 类型检查算法，将字节码提升为基于 SSA 的中间表示；应用过程间类型恢复算法 Retypd，并结合指针与数值区分方法来恢复复杂数据结构；同时利用 Memory SSA 以及保语义的结构化控制流分析，输出可读且语义一致的 C 代码。NotDec 在全部 5,241 个 Juliet 样本和全部 Howard 数据集程序上达到 100% 的重编译成功率，显著优于包括 Ghidra（45.95% 成功率）在内的基线。在类型恢复准确率方面，NotDec 在真实程序中恢复了 85.33% 的结构体成员访问，远超 Ghidra 的 9.24%。虽然完整的过程间版本在大型二进制上面临可扩展性挑战，但过程内变体 NotDec_F 展现出更优的效率，在未优化二进制上内存消耗不到 Ghidra 的一半，执行时间最多减少 97%。","tl":"把 Wasm 提升为 SSA IR 并用 Retypd 做过程间类型恢复，出可编译 C。","au":["Jikai Wang","Ningyu He","Tianming Liu","Junhai Wang","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["WebAssembly decompilation","type recovery","Retypd","Memory SSA","control-flow structuring"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/234/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/234/NotDec-WebAssembly-Decompilation-With-Inter-Procedural-Type-Recovery"},{"id":"p00721","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Depradar: Agentic Coordination for Context-Aware Defect Impact Analysis in Deep Learning Libraries","tz":"DepRadar：面向深度学习库上下文感知缺陷影响分析的智能体协同","a":"Deep learning (DL) libraries like Transformers and Megatron are now widely adopted in modern AI programs. However, when these libraries introduce defects—ranging from silent computation errors to subtle performance regressions—it is often challenging for downstream users to assess whether their own programs are affected. Such impact analysis requires not only understanding the defect semantics but also checking whether the client code satisfies complex triggering conditions involving configuration flags, runtime environments, and indirect API usage. We present DepRadar, an agent coordination framework for fine-grained defect and impact analysis in DL library updates. DepRadar coordinates four specialized agents across three stages: (1) the PR Miner and Code Diff Analyzer extract structured defect semantics from commits or pull requests, (2) the Orchestrator Agent synthesizes these signals into a unified defect pattern with trigger conditions and minimal usage examples, and (3) the Impact Analyzer statically checks downstream programs to determine whether the defect can be triggered. To improve accuracy and explainability, DepRadar integrates static analysis with DL-specific domain rules for robust defect reasoning and client-side tracing. We evaluate DepRadar on 157 PRs and 70 commits across two representative DL libraries. It achieves 90% precision in defect identification and generates high-quality structured fields (average field score 1.6/2). On 122 client programs, DepRadar identifies affected cases with 90% recall and 80% precision—substantially outperforming other baselines. Case studies further demonstrate its ability to uncover silent defects missed by developers and support actionable mitigation decisions without version upgrades.","az":"诸如 Transformers 和 Megatron 之类的深度学习（DL）库如今在现代 AI 程序中被广泛采用。然而，当这些库引入缺陷——从静默计算错误到细微的性能回退——下游用户往往难以评估自己的程序是否受到影响。此类影响分析不仅需要理解缺陷语义，还需检查客户端代码是否满足涉及配置开关、运行时环境和间接 API 使用的复杂触发条件。我们提出 DepRadar，一个用于深度学习库更新中细粒度缺陷与影响分析的智能体协同框架。DepRadar 在三个阶段协调四个专门智能体：(1) PR Miner 与 Code Diff Analyzer 从提交或拉取请求中抽取结构化的缺陷语义；(2) Orchestrator Agent 把这些信号综合为统一的缺陷模式，包含触发条件和最小使用示例；(3) Impact Analyzer 静态检查下游程序以判定该缺陷是否可被触发。为提升准确性与可解释性，DepRadar 将静态分析与 DL 特定领域规则相结合，实现稳健的缺陷推理与客户端追踪。我们在两个代表性 DL 库的 157 个 PR 和 70 个提交上评估 DepRadar，其缺陷识别精确率达到 90%，并生成高质量的结构化字段（平均字段得分 1.6/2）。在 122 个客户端程序上，DepRadar 以 90% 的召回率和 80% 的精确率识别出受影响案例，大幅优于其他基线。案例研究进一步表明，它能够揭示被开发者遗漏的静默缺陷，并在不升级版本的前提下支持可操作的缓解决策。","tl":"四智能体协同抽取库缺陷触发条件，静态判定下游程序是否受影响。","au":["Yi Gao","Xing Hu","Tongtong Xu","Jiali Zhao","Xiaohu Yang","Xin Xia"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["defect impact analysis","deep learning libraries","agent coordination","trigger conditions","static analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/235/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.09440"},{"id":"p00722","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Enabling Global, Human-Centered Explanations for LLMs: From Tokens to Interpretable Code and Test Generation","tz":"为 LLM 提供全局的、以人为中心的解释：从 token 到可解释的代码与测试生成","a":"As Large Language Models for Code (LM4Code) become integral to software engineering, establishing trust in their output becomes critical. However, standard accuracy metrics obscure the underlying reasoning of generative models, offering little insight into how decisions are made. Although post-hoc interpretability methods attempt to fill this gap, they often restrict explanations to local, token-level insights, which fail to provide a developer-understandable global analysis. Our work highlights the urgent need for global, code-based explanations that reveal how models reason across code. To support this vision, we introduce code rationales (CodeQ), a framework that enables global interpretability by mapping token-level rationales to high-level programming categories. Aggregating thousands of these token-level explanations allows us to perform statistical analyses that expose systemic reasoning behaviors. We validate this aggregation by showing it distills a clear signal from noisy token data, reducing explanation uncertainty (Shannon entropy) by over 50%. Additionally, we find that a code generation model (codeparrot-small) consistently favors shallow syntactic cues (e.g., indentation) over deeper semantic logic. Furthermore, in a user study with 37 participants, we find its reasoning is significantly misaligned with that of human developers. These findings, hidden from traditional metrics, demonstrate the importance of global interpretability techniques to foster trust in LM4Code.","az":"随着面向代码的大语言模型（LM4Code）成为软件工程不可或缺的一部分，建立对其输出的信任变得至关重要。然而，标准的准确率指标掩盖了生成模型的底层推理，几乎无法揭示决策是如何做出的。尽管事后可解释性方法试图填补这一空白，它们常把解释局限于局部的、token 级的洞见，无法提供开发者可理解的全局分析。我们的工作强调了对全局的、基于代码的解释的迫切需求，以揭示模型如何跨代码进行推理。为支撑这一愿景，我们提出 code rationales（CodeQ）框架，通过把 token 级理由映射到高层编程范畴来实现全局可解释性。聚合成千上万条这样的 token 级解释，使我们能够开展统计分析，暴露系统性的推理行为。我们通过展示这种聚合能从嘈杂的 token 数据中提炼出清晰信号来验证其有效性——解释的不确定性（香农熵）降低超过 50%。此外，我们发现一个代码生成模型（codeparrot-small）始终偏好浅层的语法线索（例如缩进）而非更深的语义逻辑。更进一步，在一项有 37 名参与者的用户研究中，我们发现其推理与人类开发者的推理存在显著错位。这些被传统指标所掩盖的发现，证明了全局可解释性技术对于培育对 LM4Code 的信任的重要性。","tl":"把 token 级理由聚合到编程范畴，揭示模型偏好缩进等浅层线索。","au":["Dipin Khati","Daniel Rodriguez-Cardenas","David Nader Palacio","Alejandro Velasco","Michele Tufano","Denys Poshyvanyk"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"interpretability-and-model-internals","tg":["llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["global interpretability","code rationales","LM4Code","token-level explanation","user study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/236/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.16771v2"},{"id":"p00723","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FrameShift: Resizing Fuzzer Inputs Without Breaking Them","tz":"FrameShift：在不破坏输入的前提下调整模糊测试输入大小","a":"Coverage-guided fuzzers are powerful automated bug-finding tools. They mutate program inputs, observe coverage, and save any input that hits an unexplored path for future mutation. Unfortunately, without knowledge of input formats—for example, the relationship between formats’ data fields and sizes—fuzzers are prone to generate destructive frameshift mutations. These time-wasting mutations yield malformed inputs that are rejected by the target program. To avoid such breaking mutations, this paper proposes a novel, lightweight technique that preserves the structure of inputs during mutation by detecting and using relation fields. Our technique, FrameShift, is simple, fast, and does not require additional instrumentation beyond standard coverage feedback. We implement our technique in two state-of-the-art fuzzers, AFL++ and LibAFL, and perform a 12+ CPU-year fuzzer evaluation, finding that FrameShift improves the performance of the fuzzer in each configuration, sometimes increasing coverage by more than 50%. Furthermore, through a series of case studies, we show that our technique is versatile enough to find important structural relationships in a variety of formats, even generalizing beyond C/C++ targets to both Rust and Python.","az":"覆盖引导的模糊测试器是强大的自动化缺陷发现工具。它们变异程序输入、观察覆盖率，并保存任何命中未探索路径的输入以供后续变异。遗憾的是，在不了解输入格式（例如格式中数据字段与长度字段之间的关系）的情况下，模糊测试器容易生成破坏性的“移框”（frameshift）变异。这些浪费时间的变异产生畸形输入，会被目标程序拒绝。为避免此类破坏性变异，本文提出一种新颖的轻量级技术，通过检测并利用关系字段（relation fields）在变异过程中保持输入结构。我们的技术 FrameShift 简单、快速，除标准覆盖反馈外不需要额外插桩。我们在两个最先进的模糊测试器 AFL++ 和 LibAFL 中实现了该技术，并开展了超过 12 CPU 年的模糊测试评估，发现 FrameShift 在每种配置下都提升了模糊测试器的性能，有时覆盖率提升超过 50%。此外，通过一系列案例研究，我们表明该技术足够通用，能够在多种格式中发现重要的结构关系，甚至可以从 C/C++ 目标推广到 Rust 和 Python。","tl":"自动识别长度等关系字段，避免变异时产生破坏结构的移框。","au":["Harrison Green","Claire Le Goues","Fraser Brown"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["coverage-guided fuzzing","frameshift mutation","relation fields","AFL++","LibAFL"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/237/x"},{"id":"p00724","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"“Write in English, Nobody Understands Your Language Here”: A Study of Non-English Trends in Open-Source Repositories","tz":"“用英语写，这里没人懂你的语言”：开源仓库中非英语趋势研究","a":"The open-source software (OSS) community has historically been dominated by English as the primary language for code, documentation, and developer interactions. But with growing global participation and better support for non-Latin scripts through standards like Unicode, OSS is gradually becoming more multilingual. This study investigates the extent to which OSS is becoming more multilingual, analyzing 9.14 billion GitHub issues, pull requests, and discussions, and 62,500 repositories across 5 programming languages and 30 natural languages, covering the period from 2015 to 2025. We examine six research questions to track changes in language use across communication, code, and documentation. We find that multilingual participation has steadily increased, especially in Korean, Chinese, and Russian. This growth appears not only in issues and discussions but also in code comments, string literals, and documentation files. While this shift reflects greater inclusivity and language diversity in OSS, it also creates language tension. The ability to express oneself in a native language can clash with shared norms around English use, especially in collaborative settings. Non-English or multilingual projects tend to receive less visibility and participation, suggesting that language remains both a resource and a barrier, shaping who gets heard, who contributes, and how open collaboration unfolds.","az":"开源软件（OSS）社区历来以英语为代码、文档和开发者交流的主要语言。但随着全球参与度的增长，以及 Unicode 等标准对非拉丁文字的更好支持，OSS 正逐渐变得更加多语种化。本研究考察 OSS 多语种化的程度，分析了 91.4 亿条 GitHub issue、拉取请求与讨论，以及涵盖 5 种编程语言和 30 种自然语言的 62,500 个仓库，时间跨度为 2015 年至 2025 年。我们考察六个研究问题，以追踪语言使用在交流、代码与文档中的变化。我们发现多语种参与稳步上升，尤以韩语、中文和俄语为甚。这种增长不仅体现在 issue 和讨论中，也体现在代码注释、字符串字面量和文档文件中。尽管这一转变反映了 OSS 中更强的包容性与语言多样性，它同时也造成了语言张力：用母语表达自我的能力可能与围绕英语使用的共同规范相冲突，在协作场景中尤其如此。非英语或多语种项目往往获得更少的可见度与参与度，这表明语言既是资源也是障碍，塑造着谁被听见、谁来贡献，以及开放协作如何展开。","tl":"十年 91 亿条数据揭示 OSS 多语种化上升，但非英语项目可见度更低。","au":["Masudul Hasan Masud Bhuiyan","Manish Kumar Bala Kumar","Cristian-Alexandru Staicu"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","low-resource-or-non-english","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["multilingual OSS","non-English repositories","GitHub mining","language barrier","community participation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/238/x"},{"id":"p00725","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Panoptes: A Profile Clustering Framework for Context-Aware Binary Optimization","tz":"Panoptes：面向上下文感知二进制优化的性能剖析聚类框架","a":"Optimization strategies are widely employed to ensure efficient execution of applications. However, aggressive optimization strategies such as compiler autotuning and profile-guided optimization suffer from scalability issues when dealing with a large suite of programs. Clustering techniques become a focal point in this regard, as they can detect binaries with similar bottlenecks and promote reuse of optimizations between them. However, existing program clustering techniques fail to cluster at granularities that represent meaningful optimization targets, thus hindering their utility. To solve this, we introduce Panoptes, a clustering and visualization tool designed to identify common optimization targets across multiple binaries. Panoptes clusters Single-Entry-Single-Exit (SESE) regions – a granularity large enough to encompass program structures yet small enough to effectively pinpoint program hot spots. Our tool incorporates Dynamic Binary Instrumentation (DBI) techniques, to filter and prioritize high-impact candidates for optimization. Subsequently, a recurrent autoencoder generates embeddings from the filtered regions, thereby providing a compatible yet information-dense representation for clustering algorithms. The resulting clusters enable developers to identify effective optimizations that are applicable across an entire cluster. Additionally, Panoptes incorporates a Graphical User Interface (GUI) that enables the visualization and exploration of program clusters, assisting user-guided optimization efforts. To demonstrate the capabilities of Panoptes, we examine case studies that involve analyzing various benchmark suites to evaluate the framework’s efficiency in identifying, clustering, and visualizing areas of interest for optimizing binaries.","az":"优化策略被广泛用于确保应用的高效执行。然而，诸如编译器自动调优和基于剖析的优化（PGO）这类激进的优化策略，在处理大规模程序集合时会遇到可扩展性问题。在此背景下，聚类技术成为关注焦点，因为它们能检测出具有相似瓶颈的二进制，并促进优化在它们之间的复用。然而，现有的程序聚类技术无法在代表有意义优化目标的粒度上进行聚类，从而削弱了其实用性。为解决这一问题，我们提出 Panoptes，一个旨在跨多个二进制识别共同优化目标的聚类与可视化工具。Panoptes 对单入口单出口（SESE）区域进行聚类——这一粒度足够大以涵盖程序结构，又足够小以有效定位程序热点。我们的工具引入动态二进制插桩（DBI）技术，以筛选并优先排序高影响的优化候选。随后，一个循环自编码器从筛选出的区域生成嵌入，为聚类算法提供兼容且信息密集的表示。所得的簇使开发者能够识别在整个簇上都适用的有效优化。此外，Panoptes 还提供图形用户界面（GUI），支持对程序簇的可视化与探索，辅助用户引导的优化工作。为展示 Panoptes 的能力，我们通过案例研究分析多个基准套件，评估该框架在识别、聚类和可视化待优化区域方面的效率。","tl":"以 SESE 区域为粒度聚类二进制热点，让优化可跨程序复用。","au":["Edwin Kayang","Eric Jahns","Mishel Jyothis Paul","Michel Kinsy"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["profile clustering","binary optimization","SESE region","dynamic binary instrumentation","autoencoder embedding"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/239/x"},{"id":"p00726","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Change And Cover: Last-Mile, Pull Request-Based Regression Test Augmentation","tz":"Change And Cover：面向 Pull Request 的“最后一公里”回归测试增强","a":"Software is in constant evolution, with developers frequently submitting pull requests (PRs) to introduce new features or fix bugs. Testing newly added or modified code in PRs is critical to maintaining software quality. Yet, even in projects with extensive test suites, some of the code modified in PRs may remain untested, leaving a “last-mile” regression test gap. Existing automated test generators mostly focus on improving overall code coverage, but do not specifically target the uncovered lines in PRs. This paper presents Change And Cover (ChaCo), a novel, LLM-based test augmentation technique that specifically addresses the last-mile regression test gap in PRs. Our approach is enabled by three key contributions: (i) Instead of focusing on overall code coverage, ChaCo considers a specific PR and the lines left uncovered after applying the PR, offering developers augmented tests for code just when it is on the developers’ mind. (ii) We identify providing suitable test context as a crucial challenge for an LLM to generate useful tests, and present two techniques to extract relevant test content, such as existing test functions, fixtures, and data generators. (iii) To make augmented tests acceptable for developers, ChaCo carefully integrates them into the existing test suite, e.g., by matching the test’s structure and style with the existing tests, and generates a summary of the test addition for developer review. We evaluate ChaCo on 145 PRs from three popular, complex, and well-tested open-source projects—SciPy, Qiskit, and Pandas. The approach successfully helps 30% of PRs achieve full patch coverage, at the affordable cost of $0.11 per PR, demonstrating its effectiveness and feasibility. A qualitative assessment of the generated tests shows that human reviewers find the tests to be worth adding (4.53/5.0), well integrated (4.20/5.0), and relevant to the PR (4.70/5.0). In a contribution study, we submitted 12 tests to these projects, of which 8 have already been merged, and two previously unknown bugs were discovered and fixed. We envision our approach to be integrated into CI workflows, automating the last mile of regression test augmentation.","az":"软件处于持续演化之中，开发者频繁提交 Pull Request（PR）以引入新特性或修复缺陷。对 PR 中新增或修改的代码进行测试，对维持软件质量至关重要。然而，即便在拥有完备测试套件的项目中，PR 修改的部分代码仍可能未被测试，留下“最后一公里”的回归测试缺口。现有自动测试生成工具大多着眼于提升整体代码覆盖率，并不专门针对 PR 中未覆盖的代码行。本文提出 Change And Cover（ChaCo），一种基于大语言模型的新型测试增强技术，专门弥补 PR 中的最后一公里回归测试缺口。我们的方法建立在三项关键贡献之上：(i) ChaCo 不关注整体覆盖率，而是针对具体某个 PR 以及应用该 PR 后仍未覆盖的代码行，在开发者正思考这段代码时为其提供增强测试；(ii) 我们指出为大语言模型提供合适的测试上下文是生成有用测试的关键挑战，并提出两种技术来抽取相关测试内容，例如已有的测试函数、fixture 与数据生成器；(iii) 为使增强测试能被开发者接受，ChaCo 会将其谨慎地融入既有测试套件，例如让测试的结构与风格与既有测试保持一致，并生成测试新增内容的摘要供开发者评审。我们在三个流行、复杂且测试完善的开源项目——SciPy、Qiskit 和 Pandas——的 145 个 PR 上评估 ChaCo。该方法成功帮助 30% 的 PR 达成完整的补丁覆盖率，每个 PR 成本仅 0.11 美元，展示了其有效性与可行性。对生成测试的定性评估表明，人工评审者认为这些测试值得加入（4.53/5.0）、融合良好（4.20/5.0）且与 PR 相关（4.70/5.0）。在贡献研究中，我们向这些项目提交了 12 个测试，其中 8 个已被合并，并发现并修复了两个此前未知的缺陷。我们设想该方法可集成进 CI 工作流，自动完成回归测试增强的最后一公里。","tl":"把测试生成目标从整体覆盖率改为 PR 补丁未覆盖行，并做风格融合。","au":["Zitong Zhou","Matteo Paltenghi","Miryung Kim","Michael Pradel"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["regression test augmentation","pull request","patch coverage","LLM test generation","test context"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/240/x","pu":"https://zitongzhoueric.github.io/assets/files/chaco_cps_v2.pdf"},{"id":"p00727","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Knowledge Matters: Injecting Project and Testing Knowledge into LLM-based Unit Test Generation","tz":"知识很重要：将项目知识与测试知识注入基于 LLM 的单元测试生成","a":"Automated unit test generation using large language models (LLMs) holds great promise but often struggles with generating tests that are both correct and maintainable in real-world projects. This paper presents KTester, a novel framework that integrates project-specific knowledge and testing domain knowledge to enhance LLM-based test generation. Our approach first extracts project structure and usage knowledge through static analysis, which provides rich context for the model. It then employs a testing-domain-knowledge-guided separation of test case design and test method generation, combined with a multi-perspective prompting strategy that guides the LLM to consider diverse testing heuristics. The generated tests follow structured templates, improving clarity and maintainability. We evaluate KTester on multiple open-source projects, comparing it against state-of-the-art LLM-based baselines using automatic correctness and coverage metrics, as well as a human study assessing readability and maintainability. Results demonstrate that KTester significantly outperforms existing methods across all metrics, producing tests with clearer intent and higher practical value.","az":"利用大语言模型（LLM）自动生成单元测试前景广阔，但在真实项目中往往难以生成既正确又易于维护的测试。本文提出 KTester，一个融合项目专属知识与测试领域知识以增强基于 LLM 的测试生成的新框架。我们的方法首先通过静态分析抽取项目结构与用法知识，为模型提供丰富上下文；随后采用测试领域知识引导的“测试用例设计与测试方法生成”分离策略，并结合多视角提示策略，引导 LLM 考虑多样的测试启发式。生成的测试遵循结构化模板，提升了清晰度与可维护性。我们在多个开源项目上评估 KTester，使用自动化的正确性与覆盖率指标与最先进的基于 LLM 的基线进行比较，并通过人工研究评估可读性与可维护性。结果表明，KTester 在所有指标上都显著优于现有方法，生成的测试意图更清晰、实用价值更高。","tl":"用静态分析项目知识加测试领域知识分阶段提示提升单测质量。","au":["Anji Li","Mingwei Liu","Zhenxi Chen","Zheng Pei","Zike Li","Dekun Dai","Yanlin Wang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["unit test generation","project knowledge","static analysis context","multi-perspective prompting","test maintainability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/241/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.14224"},{"id":"p00728","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Boosting Gas Revenues of Ethereum Miners","tz":"提升以太坊矿工的 Gas 收益","a":"In cryptocurrency networks, transaction-fee revenue serves as the primary financial incentive for miners to participate in the consensus mechanism, securing the network by validating transactions and extending the blockchain. Maximizing this revenue is therefore a key optimization problem for miners. While this has been studied for UTXO blockchains like Bitcoin, where transaction fees are fixed, we focus on Ethereum, where the challenge is significantly greater. On Ethereum, the fee paid by a transaction depends on its execution cost (gas), which can change based on the ordering of preceding transactions in a block. This creates a combinatorial explosion, as miners must select not only a subset of transactions but also their optimal permutation to maximize revenue. In this work, we present a randomized framework to address this problem. Our approach first uses randomized testing, executing sample permutations of pending transactions to profile their gas usage. From this data, we employ decision trees to learn transaction interdependencies, identifying a small “neighborhood” of transactions that influence each other’s execution costs. These dependencies are then encoded as a set of logical rules that predict gas usage based on local transaction ordering. Finally, we translate these rules and other constraints (e.g., block gas limit, nonce ordering) into an integer linear programming (ILP) instance, which we solve to find a block composition that maximizes total tip revenue. Our experimental results demonstrate significant gains: our method outperforms real-world Ethereum miners by an average of 73.45 percent per block, which corresponds to roughly 63 million USD per annum.","az":"在加密货币网络中，交易手续费收入是矿工参与共识机制的主要经济激励，矿工通过验证交易与延长区块链来保障网络安全。因此，最大化这一收入是矿工的关键优化问题。该问题在比特币等 UTXO 区块链上已有研究（其手续费固定），而我们关注以太坊，其挑战显著更大。在以太坊上，一笔交易支付的费用取决于其执行开销（gas），而该开销会随区块中先前交易的排序而变化。这带来了组合爆炸：矿工不仅要选择交易的子集，还要选择其最优排列以最大化收益。本文提出一个随机化框架来解决该问题。我们的方法首先使用随机化测试，执行待处理交易的若干样本排列以刻画其 gas 使用情况；随后利用决策树学习交易间的相互依赖，识别出彼此影响执行开销的小规模交易“邻域”；这些依赖被编码为一组逻辑规则，用于根据局部交易顺序预测 gas 使用；最后，我们将这些规则以及其他约束（例如区块 gas 上限、nonce 顺序）转化为一个整数线性规划（ILP）实例并求解，得到能最大化总小费收入的区块组成。实验结果显示出显著收益：我们的方法平均每个区块比真实的以太坊矿工高出 73.45%，约合每年 6300 万美元。","tl":"用随机化测试加决策树学交易 gas 依赖，再用 ILP 求最优打包顺序。","au":["Togzhan Barakbayeva","Soroush Farokhnia","Amir K. Goharshady","Sergei Novozhilov"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["Ethereum","gas usage","transaction ordering","integer linear programming","miner revenue"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/242/x"},{"id":"p00729","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"End-to-End Model Generation with Large Language Models for Adaptive IoT Application Deployment","tz":"用大语言模型端到端生成模型以支持自适应 IoT 应用部署","a":"The deployment of AI-powered applications on resource-constrained edge devices presents a significant software engineering challenge. While Pruning and Neural Architecture Search (NAS) have shown promise in optimizing model efficiency, their application in edge device deployment is often limited by low levels of automation. In this paper, we introduce LLM-based Adaptive Model Generation (LAMDA), a novel framework that tackle the challenge of adaptive AI deployment as an automated model generation problem. LAMDA empowers an LLM to perform end-to-end design, refinement, and optimization of DNNs to meet the specific hardware constraints. Our approach makes two primary contributions. First, we introduce a serialization technique that transforms complex DNN computation graphs into a structured textual representation that makes model architectures comprehensible and manipulable by an LLM. Further, to ground the generation process in real-world hardware constraints, we integrate a feedback-driven optimization loop. This loop leverages an empirical performance model, trained to correlate architectural patterns with on-device latency, enabling the LLM to reason about and optimize for non-functional requirements. To mitigate architectural ``hallucinations'', we incorporate context management and validation to ensure valid generation. We evaluate LAMDA through extensive experiments on public benchmarks and real-world edge devices. The results demonstrate that our framework can autonomously generate and adapt DNNs that satisfy deployment-specific accuracy and latency constraints, significantly advancing the state-of-the-art in automated software adaptation for the AI-enabled edge devices.","az":"将 AI 驱动的应用部署到资源受限的边缘设备上是一项重大的软件工程挑战。尽管剪枝与神经架构搜索（NAS）在优化模型效率方面已展现出潜力，但它们在边缘设备部署中的应用常常受限于自动化程度过低。本文提出基于 LLM 的自适应模型生成框架 LAMDA，将自适应 AI 部署挑战建模为一个自动化的模型生成问题。LAMDA 使大语言模型能够端到端地设计、精化与优化 DNN，以满足特定硬件约束。我们的方法有两项主要贡献：第一，我们提出一种序列化技术，将复杂的 DNN 计算图转化为结构化的文本表示，使模型架构可被 LLM 理解与操作；第二，为了让生成过程扎根于真实硬件约束，我们引入了反馈驱动的优化回路。该回路利用一个经验性能模型（经训练以关联架构模式与设备端延迟），使 LLM 能够对非功能性需求进行推理与优化。为缓解架构“幻觉”，我们加入了上下文管理与校验以确保生成的有效性。我们在公开基准与真实边缘设备上对 LAMDA 进行了广泛实验。结果表明，我们的框架能够自主生成并适配满足部署特定精度与延迟约束的 DNN，显著推进了面向 AI 使能边缘设备的自动化软件自适应的最新水平。","tl":"把 DNN 计算图序列化成文本，让 LLM 带硬件反馈回路直接生成模型。","au":["ZHENYU WEN","Jintao Feng","Yao Nanjie","Di Wu","Cong Wang","Mincheng Wu","Jianbin Qin","Shibo He"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["edge deployment","neural architecture generation","LLM-driven optimization","latency constraints","computation graph serialization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/243/x"},{"id":"p00730","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AnchorDiff: Binary OSS Version Identification Method Based on Anchor Node Slicing","tz":"AnchorDiff：基于锚点切分的二进制开源软件版本识别方法","a":"Binary Open-Source Software (OSS) is commonly embedded as third-party code within firmware and downstream software architectures, for simplifying the development process. However, vulnerabilities existing in OSS can be propagated through code reuse into embedded firmware and software architectures, posing security risks to these devices. To mitigate the security risks in firmware and software architectures, researchers have identified the versions of extracted firmware or binary software to detect N-day vulnerabilities in OSS. Existing works have achieved several success, but new challenges of non-linear update and minor updates hinder the improvement of the accuracy of binary OSS version identification. In this paper, we propose AnchorDiff, an efficient and accurate framework of binary OSS version identification. AnchorDiff filters out versions with significant updates from all OSS versions as Anchor Nodes which serve as boundaries to partition the entire version chain into sub-regions. The target file’s sub-region is located based on the binary code similarity detection (BCSD) results with the Anchor Nodes ’ function libraries. Finally, AnchorDiff uses the Adaptive Weight Fine-grained Matching (AWM) algorithm to weight the fine-grained matching results and determine the true version of the target binary file. The experimental results show that AnchorDiff achieves the best performance in identifying binary OSS versions with complex compilation configurations in both small and large OSS datasets, with accuracies reaching 90.35% and 97.17% respectively, which are 2.76% and 20.99% higher than the current state-of-the-art (SOTA) work. In terms of database storage, AnchorDiff reduces storage requirements by a factor of 36, compared to the original binary files.","az":"二进制开源软件（OSS）常作为第三方代码嵌入固件与下游软件架构中，以简化开发流程。然而，OSS 中存在的漏洞会通过代码复用传播到嵌入它的固件与软件架构中，给设备带来安全风险。为缓解固件与软件架构中的安全风险，研究者通过识别提取出的固件或二进制软件的版本来检测 OSS 中的 N-day 漏洞。已有工作取得了一些成效，但非线性更新与小版本更新等新挑战阻碍了二进制 OSS 版本识别准确率的提升。本文提出 AnchorDiff，一个高效且准确的二进制 OSS 版本识别框架。AnchorDiff 从全部 OSS 版本中筛选出发生显著更新的版本作为锚点节点，以其为边界将整条版本链划分为若干子区间；再基于与锚点节点函数库的二进制代码相似度检测（BCSD）结果定位目标文件所属子区间；最后，AnchorDiff 使用自适应权重细粒度匹配（AWM）算法对细粒度匹配结果加权，判定目标二进制文件的真实版本。实验结果表明，在小规模与大规模 OSS 数据集上，AnchorDiff 在识别具有复杂编译配置的二进制 OSS 版本方面都取得了最佳性能，准确率分别达到 90.35% 与 97.17%，比当前最先进（SOTA）工作分别高出 2.76% 与 20.99%。在数据库存储方面，相较原始二进制文件，AnchorDiff 将存储需求降低了 36 倍。","tl":"用锚点版本切分版本链再加权细粒度匹配，解决小版本难辨问题。","au":["Zixuan Liang","Lei Zhou","Yongqiang Guo","Peihong Lin","Danjun Liu","Baosheng Wang","Xu Zhou"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["binary OSS version identification","anchor node slicing","binary code similarity detection","N-day vulnerability","firmware"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/244/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/244/AnchorDiff-Binary-OSS-Version-Identification-Method-Based-on-Anchor-Node-Slicing"},{"id":"p00731","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Atomizer: An LLM-based Collaborative Multi-Agent Framework for Intent-Driven Commit Untangling","tz":"Atomizer：一个基于 LLM 的意图驱动提交解缠协作式多智能体框架","a":"Composite commits, which entangle multiple unrelated concerns, are prevalent in software development and significantly hinder program comprehension and maintenance. Existing automated untangling methods, particularly state-of-the-art graph clustering-based approaches, are fundamentally limited by two issues. (1) They over-rely on structural information, failing to grasp the crucial semantic intent behind changes, and (2) they operate as single-pass'' algorithms, lacking a mechanism for the critical reflection and refinement inherent in human review processes. To overcome these challenges, we introduce Atomizer, a novel collaborative multi-agent framework for composite commit untangling. To address the semantic deficit, Atomizer employs an Intent-Oriented Chain-of-Thought (IO-CoT) strategy, which prompts large language models (LLMs) to infer the intent of each code change according to both the structure and the semantic information of code. To overcome the limitations of single-pass'' grouping, we employ two agents to establish a grouper-reviewer collaborative refinement loop, which mirrors human review practices by iteratively refining groupings until all changes in a cluster share the same underlying semantic intent. Extensive experiments on two benchmark C# and Java datasets demonstrate that Atomizer significantly outperforms several representative baselines. On average, it surpasses the state-of-the-art graph-based methods by over 6.0% on the C# dataset and 5.5% on the Java dataset. This superiority is particularly pronounced on complex commits, where Atomizer’s performance advantage widens to over 16%.","az":"复合提交（composite commit）将多个互不相关的关注点纠缠在一起，在软件开发中非常普遍，并严重阻碍程序理解与维护。已有的自动解缠方法，尤其是最先进的基于图聚类的方法，存在两点根本局限：（1）过度依赖结构信息，无法把握变更背后关键的**语义意图**；（2）以“单趟”算法方式运行，缺乏人类评审过程中固有的**批判性反思与精化机制**。为克服这些挑战，我们提出 Atomizer，一个用于复合提交解缠的新型协作式多智能体框架。针对语义缺失，Atomizer 采用**意图导向的思维链（IO-CoT）**策略，提示大语言模型（LLM）根据代码的结构与语义信息推断每处代码变更的意图。为突破“单趟”分组的局限，我们使用两个智能体建立**分组者—评审者协作精化回路**，模拟人类评审实践，迭代精化分组，直至同一簇中的所有变更共享相同的底层语义意图。在 C# 与 Java 两个基准数据集上的大量实验表明，Atomizer 显著优于多个代表性基线：平均而言，在 C# 数据集上超出最先进的基于图的方法 6.0% 以上，在 Java 数据集上超出 5.5% 以上。在复杂提交上这一优势尤为突出，性能领先幅度扩大到 16% 以上。","tl":"用意图思维链加分组者—评审者回路做语义级提交解缠。","au":["Kangchen Zhu","Zhiliang Tian","Shangwen Wang","mingyue leng","Xiaoguang Mao"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["commit untangling","composite commit","multi-agent framework","intent-oriented chain-of-thought","code change semantics"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/245/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/245/Atomizer-An-LLM-based-Collaborative-Multi-Agent-Framework-for-Intent-Driven-Commit-U"},{"id":"p00732","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM4Perf: Large Language Models Are Effective Samplers for Multi-Objective Performance Modeling","tz":"LLM4Perf：大语言模型是多目标性能建模的有效采样器","a":"The performance of modern software systems is critically dependent on their complex configuration options. Building accurate performance models to navigate this vast configuration space requires effective sampling strategies, yet existing methods often struggle with multi-objective optimization and fail to leverage semantic information from documentation. The recent success of Large Language Models (LLMs) motivates the central question of this work: Can LLMs serve as effective samplers for multi-objective performance modeling? To explore this question, we present a comprehensive empirical study investigating the capabilities and characteristics of LLM-driven sampling. We design and implement LLM4Perf, a feedback-based framework, and use it to systematically evaluate LLM-guided sampling across four highly configurable, real-world systems. Our study reveals that the LLM-guided approach outperforms traditional baselines in most cases. Quantitatively, LLM4Perf achieves the best performance in nearly 68.8% (77 out of 112) of all evaluation scenarios, demonstrating its superior effectiveness. We find that this effectiveness stems from the LLM’s dual capabilities: configuration space pruning and feedback-driven strategy refinement. The strength of the pruning mechanism is further validated by the fact that it also enhances the performance of baseline methods in 91.5% (410 out of 448) of cases. Furthermore, we analyze how the selection of LLMs for different components and hyperparameters within LLM4Perf affects its overall effectiveness. Overall, this paper provides strong empirical evidence that LLMs can serve as powerful and effective samplers in performance engineering and offers concrete insights into the mechanisms driving their success.","az":"现代软件系统的性能高度依赖其复杂的配置选项。构建准确的性能模型以导航这一庞大的配置空间需要有效的采样策略，但现有方法在多目标优化上往往力不从心，也未能利用文档中的语义信息。大语言模型（LLM）近来的成功引出了本工作的核心问题：LLM 能否充当多目标性能建模的有效采样器？为探究该问题，我们开展了一项全面的实证研究，考察 LLM 驱动采样的能力与特性。我们设计并实现了基于反馈的框架 LLM4Perf，并用它在四个高度可配置的真实系统上系统评估 LLM 引导的采样。研究发现，LLM 引导的方法在多数情况下优于传统基线。定量地看，LLM4Perf 在全部评估场景中的近 68.8%（112 个中的 77 个）取得最佳性能，展示了其卓越有效性。我们发现这种有效性源自 LLM 的双重能力：配置空间剪枝与反馈驱动的策略精化。剪枝机制的强大之处还进一步体现在：它在 91.5%（448 个中的 410 个）的情形下同样提升了基线方法的性能。此外，我们分析了 LLM4Perf 中不同组件的 LLM 选择与超参数如何影响整体有效性。总体而言，本文提供了有力的实证证据，表明 LLM 可以在性能工程中充当强大而有效的采样器，并对其成功背后的机制给出了具体洞见。","tl":"实证证明 LLM 可做配置采样器，其收益来自空间剪枝与反馈精化。","au":["Xin Wang","Zhenhao Li","Zishuo Ding"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["configurable systems","performance modeling","multi-objective sampling","configuration space pruning","LLM-guided sampling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/246/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.16070"},{"id":"p00733","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RBCTest: Leveraging LLMs to Mine and Verify Oracles of API Response Bodies for RESTful API Testing","tz":"RBCTest：利用 LLM 挖掘并验证 API 响应体预言以支持 RESTful API 测试","a":"In API testing, deriving logical constraints on API response bodies to be used as oracles is crucial in generating test cases and performing automated testing of RESTful APIs. However, existing approaches are restricted to dynamic analysis in which oracles are extracted via the execution of APIs as part of the system under test. In this paper, we propose a complementary LLM-based, static approach in which the constraints for API response bodies are mined from API specifications. We leverage large language models (LLMs) to comprehend the API specifications, mine constraints for response bodies, and generate test cases. To reduce LLMs’ hallucination, we apply an Observation-Confirmation (OC) scheme which uses initial prompts to contextualize constraints, allowing subsequent prompts to more accurately confirm their presence. Our empirical results show that RBCTest with OC prompting achieves high precision in constraint mining with the average from 85.1%–93.6%. It also performs well in generating test cases from mined constraints, with a precision from 86.4%–91.7%. We use the test cases generated by RBCTest to detect 46 mismatches between the API specification and actual response data for 19 real-world APIs. Four of the mismatches were, in fact, reported in developers’ forums.","az":"在 API 测试中，推导出可作为预言（oracle）的 API 响应体逻辑约束，对于生成测试用例、实现 RESTful API 自动化测试至关重要。然而，现有方法局限于动态分析，即通过执行被测系统中的 API 来提取预言。本文提出一种互补的、基于大语言模型的静态方法，从 API 规约中挖掘响应体约束。我们利用大语言模型（LLM）理解 API 规约、挖掘响应体约束并生成测试用例。为减少 LLM 的幻觉，我们采用“观察—确认”（OC）方案：先用初始提示为约束提供上下文，使后续提示能更准确地确认其存在。实证结果表明，采用 OC 提示的 RBCTest 在约束挖掘上取得高精度，平均为 85.1%–93.6%；在根据挖掘出的约束生成测试用例方面也表现良好，精度为 86.4%–91.7%。我们用 RBCTest 生成的测试用例，在 19 个真实世界 API 上检测出 46 处 API 规约与实际响应数据之间的不一致，其中 4 处确实曾被开发者在论坛中报告过。","tl":"改用静态规约挖掘响应体约束做预言，并用观察—确认提示抑制幻觉。","au":["Hieu Huynh","Quoc-Tri Le","Tu Nguyen","Viet Nguyen","Vu Nguyen","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["REST API testing","response body constraints","test oracle mining","API specification","observation-confirmation prompting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/247/x"},{"id":"p00734","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Inside Out: Uncovering How Comment Internalization Steers LLMs for Better or Worse","tz":"由内而外：揭示注释内化如何或好或坏地引导 LLM","a":"While comments are non-functional elements of source code, Large Language Models (LLM) frequently rely on them to perform Software Engineering (SE) tasks. Yet, where in the model this reliance resides, and how it affects performance, remains poorly understood. We present the first concept-level interpretability study of LLMs in SE, analyzing three tasks - code completion, translation, and refinement - through the lens of internal comment representation. Using Concept Activation Vectors (CAV), we show that LLMs not only internalize comments as distinct latent concepts but also differentiate between subtypes such as Javadocs, inline, and multiline comments. By systematically activating and deactivating these concepts in the LLMs’ embedding space, we observed significant, model-specific, and task-dependent shifts in performance ranging from -90% to +67%. Finally, we conducted a controlled experiment using the same set of code inputs, prompting LLMs to perform 10 distinct SE tasks while measuring the activation of the comment concept within their latent representations. We found that code summarization consistently triggered the strongest activation of comment concepts, whereas code completion elicited the weakest sensitivity. These results open a new direction for building SE tools and models that reason about and manipulate internal concept representations rather than relying solely on surface-level input.","az":"尽管注释是源代码中的非功能性元素，大语言模型（LLM）在执行软件工程（SE）任务时却经常依赖它们。然而，这种依赖存在于模型的哪个位置、又如何影响性能，人们仍知之甚少。我们提出首个面向 SE 的 LLM 概念级可解释性研究，从内部注释表征的视角分析三项任务——代码补全、代码翻译与代码精化。借助概念激活向量（CAV），我们表明 LLM 不仅将注释内化为独立的潜在概念，还能区分 Javadoc、行内注释与多行注释等子类型。通过在 LLM 的嵌入空间中系统地激活与去激活这些概念，我们观察到性能出现显著的、随模型与任务而异的变化，幅度从 -90% 到 +67%。最后，我们使用同一组代码输入开展受控实验，提示 LLM 执行 10 项不同的 SE 任务，同时测量其潜在表征中注释概念的激活程度。我们发现代码摘要始终触发最强的注释概念激活，而代码补全引发的敏感度最弱。这些结果为构建能够对内部概念表征进行推理与操控、而非仅依赖表层输入的 SE 工具与模型开辟了新方向。","tl":"首次用概念激活向量定位并操控 LLM 内部的“注释概念”。","au":["Aaron Imani","Mohammad Moshirpour","Iftekhar Ahmed"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"interpretability-and-model-internals","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["concept activation vectors","interpretability","code comments","latent representations","software engineering tasks"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/248/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.16790"},{"id":"p00735","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM4JMH: Studying the Use of LLMs for Generating Java Performance Microbenchmarks","tz":"LLM4JMH：研究使用 LLM 生成 Java 性能微基准","a":"Performance regressions pose a significant threat to software reliability. In recent years, smaller-scale performance testing, such as performance microbenchmarks, has been adopted in practice to detect such regressions in an early stage of development. Developing these microbenchmarks is costly, error-prone, and demands specialized expertise. Motivated by the recent progress of large language models (LLMs) in code-related tasks, we study whether LLMs can step in as performance experts to automate the generation of microbenchmarks for performance regression detection. While existing approaches typically depend on functional unit tests to generate performance microbenchmarks, we instead design an LLM-based approach, LLM4JMH, to assess the capability of LLMs in generating reliable and effective performance microbenchmarks directly from source code. We further explore how program analysis techniques, such as static analysis, can enhance the reliability and effectiveness of LLM-generated performance microbenchmarks. Experimental results show that LLM-generated performance microbenchmarks achieve comparable bug detection effectiveness to expert-written microbenchmarks, while reducing overall expected detection latency by up to 52.60% across RxJava, Eclipse Collections, and Zipkin. In the study, the generated tests can successfully identify six out of 11 real-world performance bugs in Apache Flink. These results demonstrate that LLM-based performance microbenchmark generation can automate early performance regression detection in continuous integration pipelines of the software development process and reduce reliance on expert-crafted tests, advancing performance-aware software engineering.","az":"性能回归对软件可靠性构成重大威胁。近年来，性能微基准等小规模性能测试已在实践中被采用，用于在开发早期检测此类回归。然而，开发这些微基准成本高、易出错，并且需要专门的专业知识。受大语言模型（LLM）在代码相关任务上近期进展的启发，我们研究 LLM 能否充当性能专家，自动化生成用于性能回归检测的微基准。现有方法通常依赖功能性单元测试来生成性能微基准，而我们设计了一种基于 LLM 的方法 LLM4JMH，用以评估 LLM 直接从源代码生成可靠且有效的性能微基准的能力。我们进一步探索了静态分析等程序分析技术如何提升 LLM 生成的性能微基准的可靠性与有效性。实验结果表明，LLM 生成的性能微基准在缺陷检测有效性上与专家编写的微基准相当，同时在 RxJava、Eclipse Collections 与 Zipkin 上将总体预期检测延迟最多降低 52.60%。在研究中，生成的测试成功识别出 Apache Flink 中 11 个真实性能缺陷中的 6 个。这些结果表明，基于 LLM 的性能微基准生成可以在软件开发过程的持续集成流水线中自动化早期性能回归检测，减少对专家编写测试的依赖，推动面向性能的软件工程发展。","tl":"直接从源码而非单元测试生成 JMH 微基准，并用静态分析提升可靠性。","au":["Zongxiong Chen","Derui Zhu","Kundi Yao","Weiyi Shang","Jinfu Chen","Jiahui Geng","Alexander Pretschner","Jens Grossklags","Manfred Hauswirth","Sonja Schimmler"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["performance microbenchmark","JMH","performance regression detection","LLM generation","static analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/249/x"},{"id":"p00736","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SpecOps: A Fully Automated AI Agent Testing Framework in Real-World GUI Environments","tz":"SpecOps：面向真实 GUI 环境的全自动 AI 智能体测试框架","a":"Autonomous AI agents powered by large language models (LLMs) are increasingly deployed in real-world applications, where reliable and robust behavior is critical. However, existing agent evaluation frameworks either rely heavily on manual efforts, operate within simulated environments, or lack focus on testing complex, multimodal, real-world agents. We introduce SpecOps, a novel, fully automated testing framework designed to evaluate GUI based AI agents in real-world environments. SpecOps, decomposes the testing process into four specialized phases—test case generation, environment setup, test execution, and validation—each handled by a distinct LLM-based specialist agent. This structured architecture addresses key challenges including end-to-end task coherence, robust error handling, and adaptability across diverse agent platforms including CLI tools, web apps, and browser extensions. In comprehensive evaluations across five diverse real-world agents, SpecOps, outperforms baselines including general-purpose agentic systems such as AutoGPT and LLM crafted automation scripts in planning accuracy, execution success, and bug detection effectiveness. SpecOps identifies 164 true bugs on the real-world agents with an F1 score of 0.89. Costing under $0.73 and runtime of under eight minutes per test, it demonstrates its practical viability and superiority in automated, real-world agent testing.","az":"由大语言模型（LLM）驱动的自主 AI 智能体正越来越多地部署于真实应用中，其行为的可靠性与鲁棒性至关重要。然而，现有的智能体评估框架要么严重依赖人工，要么只能在模拟环境中运行，要么缺乏对复杂、多模态、真实世界智能体的测试关注。我们提出 SpecOps，一个全新的全自动测试框架，用于在真实环境中评估基于 GUI 的 AI 智能体。SpecOps 将测试过程分解为四个专门阶段——测试用例生成、环境搭建、测试执行与验证——每个阶段由一个独立的基于 LLM 的专家智能体负责。这一结构化架构应对了若干关键挑战，包括端到端任务连贯性、健壮的错误处理，以及对 CLI 工具、Web 应用、浏览器扩展等多种智能体平台的适应性。在五个多样化真实智能体上的全面评估中，SpecOps 在规划准确率、执行成功率与缺陷检测有效性上都优于包括 AutoGPT 等通用智能体系统以及 LLM 编写的自动化脚本在内的基线。SpecOps 在真实智能体上识别出 164 个真实缺陷，F1 分数为 0.89。每次测试成本不到 0.73 美元、运行时间不到八分钟，展示了其在真实世界智能体自动化测试中的实用可行性与优越性。","tl":"用四阶段专家智能体在真实环境中自动测试 GUI 型 AI 智能体。","au":["Syed Yusuf Ahmed","Shiwei Feng","Chanwoo Bae","Calix Barrus","Xiangyu Zhang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["AI agent testing","GUI agents","automated test framework","bug detection","real-world environments"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/250/x"},{"id":"p00737","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Distance-Guided Search in Program Synthesis with Imperfect LLM Solutions","tz":"利用不完美的 LLM 解引导程序合成中的距离导向搜索","a":"Search-based program synthesis systematically explores a space of programs to find one that satisfies a given specification. While effective for small programs, it struggles with scalability due to the combinatorial explosion of the search space. In contrast, large language models (LLMs) can generate large programs but often produce solutions that are incorrect or fail to meet the specification. We propose a novel distance-guided search algorithm that leverages imperfect LLM-generated programs to guide both top-down and bottom-up synthesis. Using an anti-unification-based distance metric, we prioritize candidates in the top-down search that are structurally similar to the LLM output. For bottom-up synthesis, we generate components close to subexpressions of the LLM solution while preserving completeness and pruning efficiency. We implement our approach atop Trio, a bidirectional synthesizer for recursive functional programs, and evaluate it on 80 synthesis tasks. Our results show that distance-guided search effectively combines the strengths of LLMs and search-based methods, solving tasks beyond the reach of either technique alone.","az":"基于搜索的程序合成系统性地探索程序空间，以找到满足给定规约的程序。这类方法对小程序有效，但由于搜索空间的组合爆炸而难以扩展。相比之下，大语言模型（LLM）能够生成较大的程序，但产出的解常常不正确或不满足规约。我们提出一种新的距离导向搜索算法，利用不完美的 LLM 生成程序同时引导自顶向下与自底向上的合成。使用基于反合一（anti-unification）的距离度量，我们在自顶向下搜索中优先考虑在结构上与 LLM 输出相似的候选；对于自底向上合成，我们生成与 LLM 解的子表达式相近的组件，同时保持完备性与剪枝效率。我们在双向递归函数式程序合成器 Trio 之上实现了该方法，并在 80 个合成任务上进行评估。结果表明，距离导向搜索有效结合了 LLM 与基于搜索方法的优势，解决了任一技术单独都无法完成的任务。","tl":"用反合一距离让 LLM 的错误程序也能引导双向合成搜索。","au":["Hangyeol Cho","Jaehyung Lee","Woosuk Lee"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["program synthesis","search-based synthesis","anti-unification distance","LLM-guided search","bidirectional synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/251/x"},{"id":"p00738","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Insecure Ingredients? Exploring Dependency Update Patterns of Bundled JavaScript Packages on the Web","tz":"不安全的“原料”？探究 Web 上打包 JavaScript 包的依赖更新模式","a":"Reusable software components, typically distributed as packages, are a central paradigm of modern software development. The JavaScript ecosystem serves as a prime example, offering millions of packages with their use being promoted as idiomatic. However, download statistics on npm raise security concerns as they indicate a high popularity of vulnerable package versions while their real prevalence on production websites remains unknown. Package version detection mechanisms fill this gap by extracting utilized packages and versions from observed artifacts on the web. Prior research focuses on mechanisms for either hand-selected popular packages in bundles or for single-file resources utilizing the global namespace. This does not allow for a thorough analysis of modern web applications’ dependency update behavior at scale. In this work, we improve upon this by presenting Aletheia, a package-agnostic method which dissects JavaScript bundles to identify package versions through algorithms originating from the field of plagiarism detection. We show that this method clearly outperforms the existing approaches in practical settings. Furthermore, we crawl the Tranco top 100,000 domains to reveal that 5% - 20% of domains update their dependencies within 16 weeks. Surprisingly, from a longitudinal perspective, bundled packages are updated significantly faster than their CDN-included counterparts, with consequently up to 10 times fewer known vulnerable package versions included. Still, we observe indicators that few widespread vendors seem to be a major driving force behind timely updates, implying that quantitative measures are not painting a complete picture.","az":"以包形式分发的可复用软件组件是现代软件开发的核心范式。JavaScript 生态是典型代表，提供了数百万个包，其使用被视为惯用做法。然而，npm 上的下载统计引发了安全担忧：数据显示存在漏洞的包版本仍相当流行，但它们在生产网站上的真实普及程度尚不清楚。包版本检测机制可弥补这一空白，它从 Web 上观察到的制品中提取所使用的包及其版本。已有研究要么面向打包产物中人工挑选的流行包，要么面向使用全局命名空间的单文件资源，因而无法对现代 Web 应用的依赖更新行为进行大规模的深入分析。本工作对此加以改进，提出 Aletheia——一种与具体包无关的方法，借助源自剽窃检测领域的算法剖析 JavaScript 打包产物以识别包版本。我们表明该方法在实际场景中明显优于已有方法。此外，我们爬取了 Tranco 前 100,000 个域名，发现 5%–20% 的域名会在 16 周内更新其依赖。令人意外的是，从纵向视角看，打包引入的包比通过 CDN 引入的对应包更新得显著更快，因而包含的已知易受攻击包版本最多可少 10 倍。不过我们也观察到一些迹象表明，少数广泛使用的厂商似乎是及时更新的主要推动力，这意味着仅靠定量度量并不能勾勒出完整图景。","tl":"用剽窃检测算法做包无关的 bundle 版本识别，并大规模测量更新行为。","au":["Ben Swierzy","Marc Ohm","Michael Meier"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["JavaScript bundles","package version detection","dependency updates","vulnerable dependencies","web measurement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/252/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15447"},{"id":"p00739","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Software Vulnerability Management in the Era of Artificial Intelligence: An Industry Perspective","tz":"人工智能时代的软件漏洞管理：一个工业界视角","a":"Artificial Intelligence (AI) has revolutionized software development, particularly by automating repetitive tasks and improving developer productivity. While these advancements are well-documented, the use of AI-powered tools for Software Vulnerability Management (SVM), such as vulnerability detection and repair, remains underexplored in industry settings. To bridge this gap, our study aims to determine the extent of the adoption of AI-powered tools for SVM, identify barriers and facilitators to the use, and gather insights to help improve the tools to meet industry needs better. We conducted a survey study involving 60 practitioners from diverse industry sectors across 27 countries. The survey incorporates both quantitative and qualitative questions to analyze the adoption trends, assess tool strengths, identify practical challenges, and uncover opportunities for improvement. Our findings indicate that AI-powered tools are used throughout the SVM life cycle, with 69% of users reporting satisfaction with their current use. Practitioners value these tools for their speed, coverage, and accessibility. However, concerns about false positives, missing context, and trust issues remain prevalent. We observe a socio-technical adoption pattern in which AI outputs are filtered through human oversight and organizational governance. To support safe and effective use of AI for SVM, we recommend improvements in explainability, contextual awareness, integration workflows, and validation practices. We assert that these findings can offer practical guidance for practitioners, tool developers, and researchers seeking to enhance secure software development through the use of AI.","az":"人工智能（AI）已经变革了软件开发，尤其体现在自动化重复性任务与提升开发者生产力方面。尽管这些进展已被充分记录，但在工业界中使用 AI 驱动工具进行软件漏洞管理（SVM，如漏洞检测与修复）的情况仍缺乏研究。为弥补这一空白，我们的研究旨在确定 AI 驱动的 SVM 工具的采用程度，识别使用中的障碍与促进因素，并收集洞见以帮助改进工具、更好满足工业界需求。我们开展了一项调查研究，涵盖来自 27 个国家、不同行业领域的 60 位从业者。问卷结合定量与定性问题，用以分析采纳趋势、评估工具优势、识别实际挑战并发掘改进机会。我们的发现表明，AI 驱动的工具已贯穿 SVM 生命周期，69% 的使用者对当前使用情况表示满意。从业者看重这些工具的速度、覆盖面与易用性。然而，对误报、上下文缺失与信任问题的担忧仍然普遍存在。我们观察到一种社会—技术的采纳模式：AI 的输出会经过人工监督与组织治理的过滤。为支持安全有效地将 AI 用于 SVM，我们建议在可解释性、上下文感知、集成工作流与验证实践方面加以改进。我们认为这些发现可为希望通过 AI 提升安全软件开发的从业者、工具开发者与研究者提供实用指导。","tl":"首次用跨国从业者调查刻画 AI 漏洞管理工具的采纳与社会技术约束。","au":["M. Mehdi Kholoosi","Triet Le","Muhammad Ali Babar"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","tg":["human-study","security","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["software vulnerability management","AI-powered tools","practitioner survey","adoption barriers","human oversight"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/253/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.18261"},{"id":"p00740","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An empirical Analysis of Community and Coding Patterns in OSS4SG vs. Conventional OSS","tz":"OSS4SG 与常规开源项目中社区与编码模式的实证分析","a":"Open Source Software for Social Good (OSS4SG) projects aim to address critical societal challenges, such as healthcare access and community safety. Understanding the community dynamics and contributor patterns in these projects is essential for ensuring their sustainability and long-term impact. However, while extensive research has focused on conventional Open Source Software (OSS), little is known about how the mission-driven nature of OSS4SG influences its development practices. To address this gap, we conduct a large-scale empirical study of 1,039 GitHub repositories, comprising 422 OSS4SG and 617 conventional OSS projects, to compare community structure, contributor engagement, and coding practices. Our findings reveal that OSS4SG projects foster significantly more stable and “sticky” (63.4%) communities, whereas conventional OSS projects are more “magnetic” (75.4%), attracting a high turnover of contributors. OSS4SG projects also demonstrate consistent engagement throughout the year, while conventional OSS communities exhibit seasonal fluctuations. Additionally, OSS4SG projects rely heavily on core contributors for both code quality and issue resolution, while conventional OSS projects leverage casual contributors for issue resolution, with core contributors focusing primarily on code quality.","az":"面向社会公益的开源软件（OSS4SG）项目旨在应对医疗可及性、社区安全等重大社会挑战。理解这类项目中的社区动态与贡献者模式，对保障其可持续性与长期影响至关重要。然而，尽管已有大量研究关注常规开源软件（OSS），人们对 OSS4SG 的使命驱动特性如何影响其开发实践仍知之甚少。为填补这一空白，我们对 1,039 个 GitHub 仓库（包括 422 个 OSS4SG 项目与 617 个常规 OSS 项目）开展了大规模实证研究，比较其社区结构、贡献者参与度与编码实践。我们的发现表明，OSS4SG 项目培育出显著更稳定、更具“黏性”的社区（63.4%），而常规 OSS 项目更具“磁性”（75.4%），吸引大量贡献者但流动率高。OSS4SG 项目全年参与度保持稳定，而常规 OSS 社区呈现季节性波动。此外，OSS4SG 项目在代码质量与 issue 解决两方面都高度依赖核心贡献者，而常规 OSS 项目则借助临时贡献者解决 issue，核心贡献者主要专注于代码质量。","tl":"实证揭示公益开源社区更“黏”、常规开源更“磁”的结构差异。","au":["Mohamed Ouf","Shayan Noei","Zeph Van Iterson","Mariam Guizani","Ying Zou"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["OSS for social good","contributor engagement","community structure","GitHub mining","coding practices"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/254/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.03430"},{"id":"p00741","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ProofCoop: Collaborative Automated Formal Verification","tz":"ProofCoop：协作式自动形式化验证","a":"Formal verification using proof assistants, such as Coq or Lean, is an effective way of ensuring software correctness. Recent research has shown that machine learning can automate proof synthesis, but such approaches are only successful a fraction of the time. Methods for improving such proof synthesis include training more precise models, improving the model-driven synthesis search mechanisms, and effectively combining multiple models into synthesis search. This paper focuses on the latter and develops ProofCoop, for the first time demonstrating collaborative cooperation between models. Diva, the state-of-the-art method for combining models, uses a disparate search for each model. On the CoqGym benchmark of 68.5K theorems from 124 open-source Coq projects a Diva combination of five models automatically proves 3,287 (27.5%) of CoqGym’s 11.9K test set theorems, while the best individual model proves only 2,604 (21.8%). By contrast, our method, ProofCoop can use the same five models to fully automatically prove 3,932 (33.0%) theorems, meaning that ProofCoop is 19.6% more likely to prove a theorem, on average, than the prior state of the art combination method. ProofCoop allows its models to build on each other’s contributions and demonstrates that such collaboration significantly increases synthesis success. ProofCoop enables six different types of collaboration: joint model next-step prediction at each search step; preferential next-step prediction via voting, bidding, and stacking; sharing lemmas proven across models mid-search, and models completing each other’s partial proofs. Together with CoqHammer, ProofCoop synthesizes proofs for 36.0% of the theorems. Our research demonstrates that creative uses of learned models can lead to collaborative synthesis that is more effective than prior approaches, suggesting a powerful new research direction in automated formal verification.","az":"使用 Coq 或 Lean 等证明助手进行形式化验证，是确保软件正确性的有效途径。近期研究表明机器学习可以自动化证明合成，但此类方法只有一小部分情况能成功。改进证明合成的手段包括训练更精确的模型、改进模型驱动的合成搜索机制，以及有效地把多个模型组合进合成搜索。本文聚焦最后一点，提出 ProofCoop，首次展示了模型之间的协作式合作。当前最先进的模型组合方法 Diva 为每个模型使用彼此独立的搜索。在包含来自 124 个开源 Coq 项目的 68.5K 条定理的 CoqGym 基准上，Diva 组合五个模型可自动证明 CoqGym 测试集 11.9K 条定理中的 3,287 条（27.5%），而最佳单模型只能证明 2,604 条（21.8%）。相比之下，我们的方法 ProofCoop 使用同样的五个模型可全自动证明 3,932 条（33.0%）定理，意味着 ProofCoop 平均比此前最先进的组合方法证明一条定理的可能性高出 19.6%。ProofCoop 让各模型能够在彼此的贡献之上继续构建，证明了这种协作显著提升了合成成功率。ProofCoop 支持六种协作方式：在每个搜索步进行联合的模型下一步预测；通过投票、竞价与堆叠实现带偏好的下一步预测；在搜索中途共享各模型已证明的引理；以及模型互相补全彼此的部分证明。与 CoqHammer 结合后，ProofCoop 可为 36.0% 的定理合成证明。我们的研究表明，对已学习模型的创造性使用可以带来比以往方法更有效的协作式合成，昭示了自动形式化验证中一个有力的新研究方向。","tl":"让多个证明模型共享引理、互补部分证明，实现真正协作式证明合成。","au":["Zhanna Kaufman","Emily First","Alex Sanchez-Stern","Kyle Thompson","Sorin Lerner","Yuriy Brun"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["formal verification","proof synthesis","Coq","CoqGym","model collaboration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/255/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3787783"},{"id":"p00742","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Environment-Aware Code Generation: How far are We?","tz":"环境感知的代码生成：我们走到哪一步了？","a":"Recent progress in large language models (LLMs) has led to impressive code generation capabilities. However, existing evaluations of LLMs primarily focus on generating isolated, small-scale code units (e.g., single functions or statements) under default or unspecified software environments. As a result, it remains unclear whether LLMs can reliably generate executable code tailored to specific user environments.. To fill this knowledge gap, we make the first systematic study of Environment-Aware Code Generation (EACG), which requires generating code that is both functionally correct and directly executable under arbitrary software configurations. We introduce VersiBCB, a large-scale benchmark constructed from real-world Python projects, featuring diverse environment specifications and realistic, multi-package scenarios. Building on this benchmark, we develop three representative adaptation strategies for LLMs: retrieval-augmented generation (data-based), mixture-of-experts (parameter-based), and memory-augmented generation (cache-based). We empirically evaluate these methods across tasks including code completion, function repair, and API migration. Our results reveal that existing LLMs struggle with environment-specific code generation, but our adaptation strategies yield improvements in environment compatibility and executability. These findings highlight critical challenges and opportunities for deploying LLMs in practical, heterogeneous software engineering workflows, and underscore the need for further research into environment-aware AI-assisted programming.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展带来了令人印象深刻的代码生成能力。然而，现有对 LLM 的评估主要关注在默认或未指定软件环境下生成孤立的小规模代码单元（例如单个函数或语句）。因此，LLM 是否能可靠地生成契合特定用户环境的可执行代码，仍不清楚。为填补这一知识空白，我们首次系统研究了环境感知的代码生成（EACG），它要求生成的代码既功能正确，又能在任意软件配置下直接执行。我们提出 VersiBCB，一个由真实 Python 项目构建的大规模基准，涵盖多样的环境规格与真实的多包场景。基于该基准，我们为 LLM 开发了三种代表性适配策略：检索增强生成（基于数据）、专家混合（基于参数）与记忆增强生成（基于缓存）。我们在代码补全、函数修复与 API 迁移等任务上对这些方法进行了实证评估。结果表明，现有 LLM 在环境相关的代码生成上表现吃力，但我们的适配策略在环境兼容性与可执行性上带来了改进。这些发现凸显了在实际的异构软件工程工作流中部署 LLM 所面临的关键挑战与机遇，也强调了进一步研究环境感知的 AI 辅助编程的必要性。","tl":"提出 VersiBCB 基准并系统评测任意依赖环境下的可执行代码生成。","au":["Tongtong Wu","Rongyi Chen","Wenjie Du","Suyu Ma","Guilin Qi","Zhenchang Xing","Shahram Khadivi","Ramesh Periyathambi","Gholamreza Haffari"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["environment-aware code generation","VersiBCB","dependency versions","retrieval-augmented generation","API migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/256/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/256/Environment-Aware-Code-Generation-How-far-are-We-"},{"id":"p00743","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Filtering before Tuning: Robust Fine-Tuning of Large Code Models under Noisy Labels","tz":"先过滤再微调：噪声标签下大型代码模型的稳健微调","a":"Fine-tuning plays a crucial role in adapting large code models (LCMs) to specific software engineering tasks. However, fine-tuning LCMs requires perfectly labeled datasets, which are rarely available in practice. Noisy labels in the training data can significantly impair the generalization ability and overall performance of fine-tuned LCMs. Previous work has primarily focused on the problem of noisy labels in training models from scratch, while this problem remains largely unexplored in the context of fine-tuning LCMs. To fill this gap, this paper proposes RobustFT, the first approach for fine-tuning LCMs in the presence of noisy labels. The core of RobustFT is to distinguish noisy labels from clean ones based on training dynamics observed during the fine-tuning process. Our insight is that, during fine-tuning, the trajectories of mislabeled samples in the latent feature space are significantly longer than those of clean samples. After filtering out noisy labels, RobustFT restarts the fine-tuning process using only the selected clean samples, thus producing a more effective LCM. We evaluate RobustFT on 36 diverse subjects, covering multiple LCMs, code datasets, and varying types and ratios of noisy labels. The results show that RobustFT outperforms five baselines in both identifying noisy labels and enhancing the fine-tuning effectiveness of LCMs.","az":"微调在将大型代码模型（LCM）适配到特定软件工程任务中起着关键作用。然而，微调 LCM 需要标注完全正确的数据集，而这在实践中很少见。训练数据中的噪声标签会显著削弱微调后 LCM 的泛化能力与整体性能。以往工作主要关注从零训练模型时的噪声标签问题，而在微调 LCM 场景下该问题仍基本未被探索。为填补这一空白，本文提出 RobustFT，首个用于在存在噪声标签情况下微调 LCM 的方法。RobustFT 的核心是依据微调过程中观察到的训练动态来区分噪声标签与干净标签。我们的洞见是：在微调过程中，被错误标注样本在潜在特征空间中的轨迹显著长于干净样本。在过滤掉噪声标签之后，RobustFT 仅使用挑选出的干净样本重新启动微调过程，从而得到更有效的 LCM。我们在 36 个多样化的实验对象上评估 RobustFT，覆盖多种 LCM、代码数据集以及不同类型与比例的噪声标签。结果表明，RobustFT 在识别噪声标签与提升 LCM 微调效果两方面都优于五个基线方法。","tl":"用潜在空间训练轨迹长度识别错标样本，过滤后重启微调。","au":["Zhong Li","Yang Chen","Heng Yong","Yuanyi Lin","Jiali Zhao","Tongtong Xu","Minxue Pan","Tian Zhang","Xuandong Li"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["noisy labels","robust fine-tuning","large code models","training dynamics","sample filtering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/257/x"},{"id":"p00744","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Causal or Correlational? A Cohort Study on the Effects of Code Smells on Class Change- and Fault-Proneness","tz":"因果还是相关？关于代码坏味对类的变更倾向与缺陷倾向影响的队列研究","a":"Code smells are suboptimal design choices in source code that are conjectured to hinder software maintainability. Previous research has studied the impact of code smells on class change- and fault- proneness, yet, as in most mining studies, it has been limited to highlighting correlations rather than detecting causal relationships. This paper instantiates the cohort study design to software repository studies and presents a cohort study aimed at assessing whether code smells cause an increase or decrease in class change- and fault-proneness. By reusing data from the work of Khomh et al. [42 ] within a cohort study design, we investigate the causal effect of eleven types of code smells on class change- and fault-proneness. Our results show that, overall, the presence of code smells appears to be causing a significant increase in change-proneness, while, with few exceptions, fault-proneness appears unaffected. This work reinforces the principle that correlation does not imply causation: we partially confirmed some previous results on the effects of code smells, while challenging others. It also lays the groundwork for applying cohort study designs to other software properties and relationships previously studied using observational data.","az":"代码坏味是源代码中次优的设计选择，被认为会损害软件的可维护性。以往研究考察过代码坏味对类的变更倾向与缺陷倾向的影响，但与多数挖掘研究一样，这些工作仅止于揭示相关性，而非检测因果关系。本文将队列研究（cohort study）设计实例化到软件仓库研究中，开展了一项队列研究，评估代码坏味究竟会导致类的变更倾向与缺陷倾向上升还是下降。我们在队列研究设计下复用 Khomh 等人 [42] 工作中的数据，考察十一种代码坏味对类变更倾向与缺陷倾向的因果效应。结果表明，总体而言，代码坏味的存在似乎确实导致变更倾向显著上升，而除少数例外，缺陷倾向似乎未受影响。这项工作强化了“相关不蕴含因果”的原则：我们部分证实了以往关于代码坏味影响的一些结论，同时对另一些结论提出了质疑。它也为将队列研究设计应用于以往仅用观测数据研究过的其他软件属性与关系奠定了基础。","tl":"把流行病学队列设计引入仓库挖掘，区分坏味影响中的因果与相关。","au":["Sabato Nocera","Sira Vegas","Giuseppe Scanniello","Massimiliano Di Penta","Natalia Juristo"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["code smells","cohort study","causal inference","change-proneness","fault-proneness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/258/x","pu":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aPivADA0sNbBMq_Enjwy1u36uGVVrw7t/view?usp=sharing"},{"id":"p00745","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Defects4REST: A Benchmark of Real-World Defects to Enable Controlled Testing and Debugging Studies for REST APIs","tz":"Defects4REST：面向 REST API 的受控测试与调试研究的真实缺陷基准","a":"Existing research on REST API testing and debugging often relies on arbitrarily selected APIs for evaluation, leaving a critical gap in our understanding of real world defects in REST API based projects, particularly those that can be automatically detected or repaired. To address this gap, we present Defects4REST, the first public benchmark of defects in REST API projects, systematically mined from open source GitHub repositories. Using a semi-automated process that combines clustering, topic modeling, and manual validation, we build a dataset of 607 REST API defects from 50 projects and organize them into a taxonomy of 6 defect types and 13 sub-types. Each defect is linked to an issue report, the developer-modified versions of the patched files, and the corresponding commit messages. Defects4REST features easy access to the buggy and patched versions of projects for each defect and enables analysis of the associated artifacts. To evaluate current automated testing capabilities, we assess four state-of-the-art REST API testing tools on a sample of 30 defects from 11 projects. Our evaluation reveals that tools detect only 10% (3/30) of real-world defects due to nine fundamental limitations including semantic validation, stateful testing, and infrastructure-aware testing. We release both the benchmark and the issue mining framework to support reproducible research in REST APIs, enabling the development and evaluation of REST API testing and debugging techniques.","az":"现有关于 REST API 测试与调试的研究常常依赖任意选取的 API 进行评估，这使我们对基于 REST API 的项目中真实缺陷（尤其是那些可被自动检测或修复的缺陷）的理解存在关键空白。为填补这一空白，我们提出 Defects4REST，首个公开的 REST API 项目缺陷基准，系统性地从开源 GitHub 仓库中挖掘而来。我们采用结合聚类、主题建模与人工校验的半自动流程，构建了一个包含来自 50 个项目的 607 个 REST API 缺陷的数据集，并将其组织为包含 6 种缺陷类型与 13 种子类型的分类体系。每个缺陷都关联到一份 issue 报告、开发者修改后的补丁文件版本以及相应的提交信息。Defects4REST 便于访问每个缺陷对应项目的缺陷版本与修复版本，并支持对相关制品的分析。为评估当前的自动化测试能力，我们在来自 11 个项目的 30 个缺陷样本上评估了四款最先进的 REST API 测试工具。评估显示，这些工具仅检测出 10%（3/30）的真实缺陷，原因在于九项根本性局限，包括语义校验、有状态测试与基础设施感知测试等方面的不足。我们同时发布该基准与 issue 挖掘框架，以支持 REST API 领域可复现的研究，促进 REST API 测试与调试技术的开发与评估。","tl":"首个真实 REST API 缺陷基准，揭示现有测试工具仅能发现一成缺陷。","au":["Rahil Mehta","Pushpak Katkhede","Manish Motwani"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["REST API defects","benchmark","defect taxonomy","API testing tools","issue mining"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/259/x","pu":"https://mmotwani.com/publications/publication_sources/Mehta26icse.pdf"},{"id":"p00746","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"EmbedAgent: Benchmarking Large Language Models in Embedded System Development","tz":"EmbedAgent：面向嵌入式系统开发的大语言模型基准评测","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown promise in various tasks, yet few benchmarks assess their capabilities in embedded system development. In this paper, we introduce EmbedAgent, a paradigm designed to simulate real-world roles in embedded system development, such as Embedded System Programmer, Architect, and Integrator. This paradigm enables LLMs to be tested in tasks that bridge the gap between digital and physical systems, allowing for a more comprehensive assessment of their capabilities. To evaluate LLMs on these tasks, we propose EmbedBench, the first comprehensive benchmark for embedded system programming, circuit design, and cross-platform migration. EmbedBench consists of 126 cases, covering 9 electronic components across 3 hardware platforms. Through extensive experiments on 10 mainstream LLMs, we uncover several key findings. Surprisingly, despite the simplicity of the cases, DeepSeek-R1 achieves only a 55.6% pass@1 rate when provided with schematic information, and 50.0% when tasked with generating the schematics itself. In the cross-platform migration tasks, LLMs show relatively strong performance with MicroPython on the Raspberry Pi Pico (with the top model achieving 73.8% pass@1), but perform poorly on ESP-IDF, where the best model reaches only 29.4% pass@1. Interestingly, we observe that general-purpose chat LLMs like DeepSeek-V3 often fail to utilize relevant pre-trained knowledge in this domain, while reasoning LLMs tend to overthink and overlook efficient knowledge during pretraining. Based on these insights, we propose two strategies—retrieval augmented generation and compiler feedback-to enhance LLM performance. These strategies result in significant improvements, with Deepseek-R1 reaching a 65.1% pass@1 with correct schematics, and 53.1% without. Additionally, the accuracy of the Arduino to ESP32 migration task improves from 21.4% to 27.8%.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已在各类任务中展现潜力，但鲜有基准评估它们在嵌入式系统开发中的能力。本文提出 EmbedAgent，一种用于模拟嵌入式系统开发中真实角色（如嵌入式系统程序员、架构师与集成工程师）的范式。该范式使 LLM 能够在弥合数字系统与物理系统鸿沟的任务中接受测试，从而对其能力进行更全面的评估。为在这些任务上评估 LLM，我们提出 EmbedBench，首个覆盖嵌入式系统编程、电路设计与跨平台迁移的综合基准。EmbedBench 包含 126 个案例，覆盖 3 个硬件平台上的 9 种电子元件。通过对 10 个主流 LLM 的大量实验，我们得到若干关键发现。令人惊讶的是，尽管案例并不复杂，DeepSeek-R1 在提供电路原理图信息时 pass@1 仅为 55.6%，在需要自行生成原理图时仅为 50.0%。在跨平台迁移任务上，LLM 在 Raspberry Pi Pico 的 MicroPython 上表现相对较好（最佳模型 pass@1 达 73.8%），但在 ESP-IDF 上表现很差，最佳模型仅为 29.4% pass@1。有趣的是，我们观察到 DeepSeek-V3 等通用对话型 LLM 常常无法在该领域调用相关的预训练知识，而推理型 LLM 则倾向于过度思考、忽略预训练中高效的知识。基于这些洞见，我们提出两种策略——检索增强生成与编译器反馈——以提升 LLM 性能。这些策略带来显著改进：DeepSeek-R1 在有正确原理图时 pass@1 提升至 65.1%，无原理图时提升至 53.1%；此外，Arduino 到 ESP32 的迁移任务准确率从 21.4% 提升至 27.8%。","tl":"首个覆盖编程、电路设计与跨平台迁移的嵌入式开发 LLM 基准。","au":["Ruiyang Xu","Jialun Cao","Mingyuan Wu","Wenliang Zhong","Yaojie Lu","Ben He","Xianpei Han","Shing-Chi Cheung","Le Sun"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["embedded system development","EmbedBench","circuit design","cross-platform migration","compiler feedback"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/260/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/260/EmbedAgent-Benchmarking-Large-Language-Models-in-Embedded-System-Development"},{"id":"p00747","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Weak Programmers Need Not Apply, LLMs Welcome! Survey Screening in the AI Era","tz":"弱程序员请勿申请，LLM 欢迎光临！AI 时代的问卷筛选","a":"Quantitative research on software development practice often depends on the results of anonymous online surveys. However, it is difficult to be sure that the respondents to such surveys are, in fact, developers. The problem is greater if survey responses are paid for, incentivising respondents to game the system and attracting the attention of bots and professional survey farms. One solution is to include screening questions in the survey to assess respondents’ coding skills. However, this introduces the risk of unfairly excluding considered responses from developers who spent time and energy on the survey. It also risks skewing results by excluding hasty developers and those who are technically weak. We reviewed the responses of all 86 developers who were excluded from analysis of a large unpaid developer survey (n=1,100) because they answered screening questions incorrectly. Based on this review, we estimate that up to 86% of the developers who were excluded were genuine developers. The advent of LLMs casts further doubt on the use of screening questions. Investigating LLM ability, we found that five sample LLMs could answer the first code screening question correctly, and three were able to answer the second. We explored other screening questions and techniques that are typically used in SE surveys, finding that most are susceptible to fraud via LLM use, bots and survey farms. Recruitment strategy may be a better screening technique. We recommend that if survey respondents are compensated only known developers should be invited. Surveys that are widely distributed, e.g. on social media, should not compensate respondents. Instead, researchers should focus on good survey design and imaginative recruitment strategies.","az":"关于软件开发实践的定量研究常常依赖匿名在线问卷的结果。然而，很难确定这些问卷的受访者是否真的是开发者。如果问卷有报酬，问题会更严重：受访者有动机钻空子，还会吸引机器人与专业刷单团队。一种解决方案是在问卷中加入筛选题以评估受访者的编码能力。但这会带来不公平地排除那些认真作答、投入了时间与精力的开发者的风险，也可能因排除了匆忙作答者与技术较弱者而使结果发生偏倚。我们复核了在一项大型无偿开发者问卷（n=1,100）中因筛选题答错而被排除的全部 86 位开发者的作答。基于这一复核，我们估计被排除者中高达 86% 其实是真正的开发者。LLM 的出现进一步动摇了筛选题的可用性。在考察 LLM 能力时我们发现，五个样本 LLM 都能正确回答第一道代码筛选题，其中三个还能答对第二道。我们又探究了 SE 问卷中常用的其他筛选题与技术，发现大多数都易被 LLM、机器人与刷单团队所欺骗。招募策略也许是更好的筛选手段。我们建议：若对受访者给予报酬，则只应邀请已知的开发者；而在社交媒体等渠道广泛分发的问卷不应给予报酬，研究者应转而专注于良好的问卷设计与富有创意的招募策略。","tl":"证明 SE 问卷筛选题既误杀真开发者又挡不住 LLM，应改用招募策略。","au":["Ita Ryan","Utz Roedig","Klaas-Jan Stol"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["human-study","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["survey screening questions","developer surveys","LLM cheating","survey validity","recruitment strategy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/261/x"},{"id":"p00748","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Comprehensive Study of Concurrency Bugs in the Linux Kernel","tz":"Linux 内核并发缺陷的全面研究","a":"Concurrency bugs, which arise from unexpected instruction orderings of concurrent execution contexts, are notoriously difficult to detect and diagnose due to their non-deterministic nature. Studies of concurrency bugs in user-space applications have shed light on common concurrency bug characteristics, informing the design of effective solutions for their detection, diagnosis, and repair. However, far less is known about concurrency bugs in operating system kernels, where low-level systems programming and complex execution patterns introduce new challenges. To address this gap, this paper presents the first comprehensive study of concurrency bugs in the Linux kernel. Our study reveals that kernel concurrency bugs exhibit surprisingly different characteristics compared to their counterparts in applications. For instance, 27.0% of kernel concurrency bugs only occur when certain interrupts are handled, which are rarely considered by existing bug discovery approaches. In addition, half of the bugs involve kernel driver code, but about 69.3% of these happen due to concurrent device operations on the control paths, such as device registration and deregistration, which suggests the driver control path should be a primary focus for concurrency bug discovery. Our findings reveal challenges and gaps in the existing approaches to finding kernel concurrency bugs. By shedding light on these challenges, this work paves the way for new operating system designs, testing tools, and verification efforts that will make modern operating systems more reliable and secure.","az":"并发缺陷源于并发执行上下文之间出乎意料的指令顺序，因其非确定性而以难以检测和诊断著称。针对用户态应用并发缺陷的研究已揭示了常见的并发缺陷特征，为其检测、诊断与修复方案的设计提供了依据。然而，对于操作系统内核中的并发缺陷，人们了解得少得多——低层系统编程与复杂的执行模式在这里带来了新的挑战。为填补这一空白，本文提出首个针对 Linux 内核并发缺陷的全面研究。我们的研究表明，内核并发缺陷与应用中的同类缺陷呈现出出人意料的不同特征。例如，27.0% 的内核并发缺陷只有在处理特定中断时才会发生，而现有的缺陷发现方法很少考虑这一点。此外，半数缺陷涉及内核驱动代码，但其中约 69.3% 发生在控制路径上的并发设备操作（如设备注册与注销）之中，这表明驱动的控制路径应成为并发缺陷发现的首要关注点。我们的发现揭示了现有内核并发缺陷发现方法面临的挑战与空白。通过阐明这些挑战，本工作为新的操作系统设计、测试工具与验证工作铺平了道路，使现代操作系统更可靠、更安全。","tl":"首个 Linux 内核并发缺陷全面研究，揭示中断与驱动控制路径是盲区。","au":["Sishuai Gong","Chih-En Lin","Kevin Wu","Edwin Lu","Pedro Fonseca"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["concurrency bugs","Linux kernel","empirical study","interrupt handling","device drivers"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/262/x","pu":"https://sishuaigong.github.io/pdf/icse26-concurrencybugstudy.pdf"},{"id":"p00749","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Practitioner Views on Mobile App Accessibility: Practices and Challenges","tz":"从业者对移动应用无障碍的看法：实践与挑战","a":"As mobile applications (apps) become ubiquitous in everyday life, it is crucial for developers to prioritize accessibility for users with diverse abilities. While previous research has identified widespread accessibility issues and raised awareness of developer challenges, there remains a lack of cross-platform, globally representative insights into how practitioners approach accessibility in practice. This paper presents findings from a mixed-methods survey of 110 mobile app developers across 43 countries, examining how platform ecosystems (iOS vs. Android) and developer experience shape accessibility practices. Results show that while developers recognize the importance of accessibility, they often rely on platform-specific guidelines and typically perform compliance testing late in the development process. Developers primarily implement text-focused features while struggling with API limitations and organizational constraints. Through systematic cross-platform comparison, we identify novel platform-specific barriers and demonstrate how accessibility practices differ across developer experience levels. Our findings offer new insights into the challenges of achieving accessibility in practice and provide actionable steps for various stakeholders to promote more consistent and inclusive app development.","az":"随着移动应用（app）在日常生活中无处不在，开发者优先考虑不同能力用户的无障碍性变得至关重要。尽管以往研究已识别出普遍存在的无障碍问题并提升了对开发者挑战的认识，但关于从业者在实践中如何对待无障碍，仍缺乏跨平台、具全球代表性的洞见。本文呈现一项针对 43 个国家 110 位移动应用开发者的混合方法调查的结果，考察平台生态（iOS 与 Android）与开发者经验如何塑造无障碍实践。结果显示，尽管开发者认同无障碍的重要性，他们往往依赖平台特定的指南，并通常在开发流程后期才进行合规测试。开发者主要实现以文本为中心的特性，同时受困于 API 限制与组织层面的约束。通过系统的跨平台比较，我们识别出新的平台特有障碍，并展示了无障碍实践如何随开发者经验水平而不同。我们的发现为实践中实现无障碍所面临的挑战提供了新洞见，并为各类利益相关者提供了促进更一致、更具包容性的应用开发的可行步骤。","tl":"跨 43 国混合方法调查，首次系统比较 iOS 与 Android 无障碍实践差异。","au":["Amila Indika","Rick Kazman","Anthony Peruma"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","accessibility-inclusion","empirical-study"],"kw":["mobile accessibility","practitioner survey","cross-platform comparison","accessibility testing","developer experience"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/263/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.14131"},{"id":"p00750","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Better Linux Kernel Fault Localization: Leveraging Contrastive Reasoning and Hierarchical Context Analysis","tz":"迈向更好的 Linux 内核缺陷定位：结合对比推理与层次化上下文分析","a":"Debugging the Linux kernel remains a formidable challenge due to its vast codebase, complex architecture, and low-level programming intricacies. Effective fault localization (FL) is thus essential for effcient kernel debugging and maintenance. While existing FL techniques (both traditional and LLM-based) have shown promise in general-purpose software, they are ill-suited for the kernel context. In particular, recent LLM-based techniques often treat bug reports and source code as plain text, lacking deep integration of kernel-specific knowledge, which limits their ability to identify root causes and achieve fine-grained localization. We present CoHiKer, a novel LLM-based FL technique tailored to the Linux kernel. CoHiKer introduces two key innovations: (1) contrastive reasoning, which identifies root causes by analyzing the behavioral divergence between carefully mutated passing and failing test cases, and (2) hierarchical context analysis, which systematically narrows the localization scope from files to methods by integrating crash reports, syscall semantics, inter-file dependencies, and kernel-specific features. Unlike prior techniques that rely on static understanding and full-code input, CoHiKer decomposes the localization task and enables structured LLM prompting to reason semantically over meaningful contexts. We evaluate CoHiKer on an extended Linux kernel bug dataset against five state-of-the-art baselines. CoHiKer consistently outperforms all competitors, improving Top-1 localization accuracy by up to 26.07% at the file level and 56.85% at the method level over state-of-the-art LLM-based baselines, while achieving up to 8.84× and 28.9× reductions in token consumption, respectively. Furthermore, CoHiKer demonstrates strong generalizability on the non-kernel dataset, with comparable gains (15.5% and 5.3% in Top-1 at file and method levels). These results demonstrate the promise of CoHiKer as a practical and accurate solution for kernel FL.","az":"由于代码库庞大、架构复杂以及底层编程的精细性，调试 Linux 内核仍是一项艰巨挑战。因此，有效的缺陷定位（FL）对高效的内核调试与维护至关重要。虽然现有 FL 技术（无论传统还是基于 LLM）在通用软件上已展现潜力，但并不适用于内核场景。特别是，近期基于 LLM 的技术往往把缺陷报告与源代码当作纯文本处理，缺乏对内核特有知识的深度融合，限制了它们识别根因与实现细粒度定位的能力。我们提出 CoHiKer，一种为 Linux 内核量身定制的基于 LLM 的 FL 技术。CoHiKer 引入两项关键创新：（1）对比推理，通过分析经过精心变异的通过用例与失败用例之间的行为分歧来识别根因；（2）层次化上下文分析，通过整合崩溃报告、系统调用语义、跨文件依赖与内核特有特征，系统性地将定位范围从文件收窄到方法。与依赖静态理解和全量代码输入的既有技术不同，CoHiKer 对定位任务进行分解，使结构化的 LLM 提示能够在有意义的上下文上进行语义推理。我们在一个扩展的 Linux 内核缺陷数据集上，将 CoHiKer 与五个最先进的基线进行比较评估。CoHiKer 始终优于所有竞争者，相较最先进的基于 LLM 的基线，在文件级 Top-1 定位准确率上最多提升 26.07%，在方法级最多提升 56.85%，同时分别将 token 消耗降低最多 8.84 倍与 28.9 倍。此外，CoHiKer 在非内核数据集上展现出很强的泛化性，取得了相当的提升（文件级与方法级 Top-1 分别提升 15.5% 与 5.3%）。这些结果表明 CoHiKer 是一种实用且准确的内核缺陷定位方案。","tl":"用通过/失败用例的对比推理加层次化内核上下文做细粒度定位。","au":["Haichi Wang","Ruiguo Yu","Yesong Pang","Yingquan Zhao","Junjie Chen","Jiajun Jiang","Zan Wang"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["fault localization","Linux kernel","contrastive reasoning","hierarchical context","LLM-based debugging"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/264/x"},{"id":"p00751","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FlipFlop: A Static Analysis-based Energy Optimization Framework for GPU Kernels","tz":"FlipFlop：基于静态分析的 GPU Kernel 能耗优化框架","a":"Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications, such as Large Language Models, are primarily driven and executed by Graphics Processing Units (GPUs). These GPU programs (kernels) consume substantial amounts of energy, yet software developers often lack the hardware expertise and ad hoc knowledge required to optimize for power efficiency. We propose FlipFlop, a framework using static code analysis to predict energy consumption and recommend Pareto-optimal thread block configurations considering both power consumption and execution time. Our framework requires no runtime execution and analyzes PTX code, a low-level instruction set for CUDA-enabled GPUs. It is validated across a diverse set of GPUs and kernels, including multi-head attention, convolution, and matrix multiplication. FlipFlop achieves 83% accuracy in identifying locally optimal energy-efficient configurations, while also minimizing developer effort by reducing the optimization search space by 93.4%. For multi-head attention kernels, it yields up to 79% energy savings and 106% throughput gains relative to NVIDIA’s occupancy heuristic. By integrating static analysis with real-time monitoring and providing explainable optimization guidance, FlipFlop empowers developers to create sustainable, high-performance GPU software which minimizes environmental and computational costs.","az":"以大语言模型为代表的人工智能（AI）应用主要由图形处理器（GPU）驱动和执行。这些 GPU 程序（kernel）消耗大量能源，然而软件开发者往往缺乏优化功耗效率所需的硬件专业知识和经验性知识。我们提出 FlipFlop，一个利用静态代码分析来预测能耗、并在同时考虑功耗与执行时间的前提下推荐帕累托最优线程块（thread block）配置的框架。我们的框架无需运行时执行，只分析 PTX 代码——一种面向支持 CUDA 的 GPU 的低层指令集。该框架在多种 GPU 和 kernel 上得到验证，包括多头注意力、卷积和矩阵乘法。FlipFlop 在识别局部最优的高能效配置上达到 83% 的准确率，同时将优化搜索空间缩减 93.4%，从而显著降低开发者的工作量。对于多头注意力 kernel，相对于 NVIDIA 的占用率（occupancy）启发式方法，它带来最高 79% 的能耗节省和 106% 的吞吐量提升。通过将静态分析与实时监控相结合并提供可解释的优化指导，FlipFlop 帮助开发者构建可持续、高性能的 GPU 软件，最小化环境与计算成本。","tl":"首次仅靠 PTX 静态分析预测能耗并推荐帕累托最优线程块配置。","au":["Saurabhsingh Rajput","Alexander Brandt","Vadim Elisseev","Tushar Sharma"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GPU kernel","energy optimization","static analysis","PTX","thread block configuration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/265/x","pu":"https://tusharma.in/preprints/ICSE2026_FlipFlop.pdf"},{"id":"p00752","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fairness Is Not Just Ethical: Performance Trade-Off via Data Correlation Tuning to Mitigate Bias in ML Software","tz":"公平不只是伦理问题：通过数据相关性调优缓解 ML 软件偏见的性能权衡","a":"Traditional software fairness research typically emphasizes ethical and social imperatives, neglecting that fairness fundamentally represents a core software quality issue arising directly from performance disparities across sensitive user groups. Recognizing fairness explicitly as a software quality dimension yields practical benefits beyond ethical considerations, notably improved predictive performance for unprivileged groups, enhanced out-of-distribution generalization, and increased geographic transferability in real-world deployments. Nevertheless, existing bias mitigation methods face a critical dilemma: while pre-processing methods offer broad applicability across model types, they generally fall short in effectiveness compared to post-processing techniques. To overcome this challenge, we propose Correlation Tuning (CoT), a novel pre-processing approach designed to mitigate bias by adjusting data correlations. Specifically, CoT introduces the Phi-coefficient, an intuitive correlation measure, to systematically quantify correlation between sensitive attributes and labels, and employs multi-objective optimization to address the proxy biases. Extensive evaluations demonstrate that CoT increases the true positive rate of unprivileged groups by an average of 17.5% and reduces three key bias metrics, including statistical parity difference (SPD), average odds difference (AOD), and equal opportunity difference (EOD), by more than 50% on average. CoT outperforms state-of-the-art methods by three and ten percentage points in single attribute and multiple attributes scenarios, respectively. We will publicly release our experimental results and source code to facilitate future research.","az":"传统的软件公平性研究通常强调伦理与社会层面的要求，忽视了公平性本质上是一个核心软件质量问题——它直接源于不同敏感用户群体之间的性能差异。将公平性明确视为一个软件质量维度，会带来超越伦理考量的实际收益，尤其是对弱势群体预测性能的提升、更好的分布外泛化能力，以及在真实部署中更强的地域可迁移性。然而，现有的偏见缓解方法面临一个关键困境：预处理方法虽然对各类模型具有广泛适用性，但其效果通常不如后处理技术。为克服这一挑战，我们提出相关性调优（Correlation Tuning，CoT），一种通过调整数据相关性来缓解偏见的新型预处理方法。具体而言，CoT 引入 Phi 系数这一直观的相关性度量，系统性地量化敏感属性与标签之间的相关性，并采用多目标优化来处理代理偏见。大量实验评估表明，CoT 将弱势群体的真阳性率平均提高 17.5%，并将统计均等差（SPD）、平均几率差（AOD）和机会均等差（EOD）这三项关键偏见指标平均降低超过 50%。在单一敏感属性和多敏感属性场景下，CoT 分别比最先进方法高出三个和十个百分点。我们将公开发布实验结果与源代码，以便利后续研究。","tl":"用 Phi 系数量化相关性并多目标优化，做更强的预处理去偏。","au":["Ying Xiao","Shangwen Wang","Sicen Liu","Dingyuan Xue","Xian Zhan","Yepang Liu","Jie M. Zhang"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["software fairness","bias mitigation","pre-processing","Phi coefficient","multi-objective optimization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/266/x"},{"id":"p00753","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Imitation Game: Reproducing Deep Learning Bugs Leveraging an Intelligent Agent","tz":"模仿游戏：借助智能体复现深度学习缺陷","a":"Despite their wide adoption in various domains (e.g., healthcare, finance, software engineering), Deep Learning (DL)-based applications suffer from many bugs, failures, and vulnerabilities. Reproducing these bugs is essential for their resolution, but it is extremely challenging due to the inherent nondeterminism of DL models and their tight coupling with hardware and software environments. According to recent studies, only about 3% of DL bugs can be reliably reproduced using manual approaches. To address these challenges, we present RepGen, a novel, automated, and intelligent approach for reproducing deep learning bugs. RepGen constructs a learning-enhanced context from a project, develops a comprehensive plan for bug reproduction, employs an iterative generate-validate-refine mechanism, and thus generates such code using an LLM that reproduces the bug at hand. We evaluate RepGen on 106 real-world deep learning bugs and achieve a reproduction rate of 80.19%, a 19.81% improvement over the state-of-the-art measure. A developer study involving 27 participants shows that RepGen improves the success rate of DL bug reproduction by 23.35%, reduces the time to reproduce by 56.8%, and lowers participants’ cognitive load.","az":"尽管深度学习（DL）应用在医疗、金融、软件工程等众多领域被广泛采用，它们仍然存在大量缺陷、故障和漏洞。复现这些缺陷对于解决它们至关重要，但由于 DL 模型固有的非确定性以及它们与软硬件环境的紧密耦合，复现极其困难。根据近期研究，仅约 3% 的 DL 缺陷能够通过人工方法可靠复现。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 RepGen，一种用于复现深度学习缺陷的全新自动化智能方法。RepGen 从项目中构建学习增强的上下文，制定全面的缺陷复现计划，采用迭代式的“生成—验证—精化”机制，并据此使用大语言模型生成能够复现当前缺陷的代码。我们在 106 个真实世界的深度学习缺陷上评估 RepGen，取得 80.19% 的复现率，比当前最先进方法提升 19.81%。一项有 27 名参与者的开发者研究表明，RepGen 将 DL 缺陷复现的成功率提高 23.35%，将复现所需时间减少 56.8%，并降低了参与者的认知负荷。","tl":"用生成-验证-精化的 LLM 智能体自动复现 DL 缺陷，复现率达 80%。","au":["Mehil Shah","Masud Rahman","Foutse Khomh"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","agentic","human-study"],"kw":["deep learning bugs","bug reproduction","LLM agent","developer study","iterative refinement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/267/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.14990"},{"id":"p00754","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Securing the AI Supply Chain: What Can We Learn From Developer-Reported Security Issues and Solutions of AI Projects?","tz":"保护 AI 供应链：我们能从开发者上报的 AI 项目安全问题与解决方案中学到什么？","a":"The rapid growth of Artificial Intelligence (AI) models and applications has led to an increasingly complex security landscape. Developers of AI projects must contend not only with traditional software supply chain issues but also with novel, AI-specific security threats. However, little is known about what security issues are commonly encountered and how they are resolved in practice. This gap hinders the development of effective security measures for each component of the AI supply chain. We bridge this gap by conducting an empirical investigation of developer-reported issues and solutions, based on discussions from Hugging Face and GitHub. To identify security-related discussions, we develop a pipeline that combines keyword matching with an optimal fine-tuned distilBERT classifier, which achieved the best performance in our extensive comparison of various deep learning and large language models. This pipeline produces a dataset of 312,868 security discussions, providing insights into the security reporting practices of AI applications and projects. We conduct a thematic analysis of 753 posts sampled from our dataset and uncover a fine-grained taxonomy of 32 security issues and 24 solutions across four themes: (1) System and Software, (2) External Tools and Ecosystem, (3) Model, and (4) Data. We reveal that many security issues arise from the complex dependencies and black-box nature of AI components. Notably, challenges related to Models and Data often lack concrete solutions. Our insights can offer evidence-based guidance for developers and researchers to address real-world security threats across the AI supply chain.","az":"人工智能（AI）模型与应用的快速增长带来了日益复杂的安全格局。AI 项目的开发者不仅要应对传统的软件供应链问题，还要面对新型的、AI 特有的安全威胁。然而，人们对实践中常见的安全问题及其解决方式知之甚少。这一空白阻碍了针对 AI 供应链各组成部分制定有效的安全措施。我们通过对开发者上报的问题与解决方案开展实证调查来弥合这一空白，数据来自 Hugging Face 和 GitHub 上的讨论。为识别与安全相关的讨论，我们开发了一条将关键词匹配与经过微调的最优 distilBERT 分类器相结合的流水线；在我们对多种深度学习模型和大语言模型的广泛比较中，该分类器表现最佳。这条流水线产生了一个包含 312,868 条安全讨论的数据集，为理解 AI 应用与项目的安全上报实践提供了洞见。我们对从数据集中抽样的 753 条帖子进行主题分析，揭示出一个细粒度分类体系，涵盖四个主题下的 32 类安全问题和 24 类解决方案：(1) 系统与软件，(2) 外部工具与生态，(3) 模型，(4) 数据。我们发现许多安全问题源自 AI 组件复杂的依赖关系与黑箱特性。值得注意的是，与模型和数据相关的挑战往往缺乏具体的解决方案。我们的洞见可为开发者与研究者应对 AI 供应链中的真实安全威胁提供基于证据的指导。","tl":"首次基于 31 万条讨论给出 AI 供应链安全问题与解法的分类体系。","au":["The Anh Nguyen","Triet Le","Muhammad Ali Babar"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["AI supply chain","security issues","Hugging Face","thematic analysis","taxonomy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/268/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.23385"},{"id":"p00755","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Uncovering Failures in Cyber-Physical System State Transitions: A Fuzzing-Based Approach Applied to sUAS","tz":"揭示信息物理系统状态转移中的失效：一种应用于小型无人机系统的模糊测试方法","a":"The increasing deployment of small Uncrewed Aerial Systems (sUAS) in diverse and often safety-critical environments demands rigorous validation of onboard decision logic under various conditions. In this paper, we present SAFUS, a fuzzing pipeline that validates core behavior associated with state transitions, automated failsafes, and human operator interactions in sUAS applications operating under various timing conditions and environmental disturbances. We create fuzzing scenarios to detect behavioral deviations, and then dynamically generate associated Fault Trees to visualize states, modes, and environmental factors that contribute to the failure, thereby helping project stakeholders to analyze the failure and identify its root causes. We validated SAFUS against a real-world sUAS system and were able to identify several points of failure not previously detected by the system’s development team. The fuzzing was conducted in a high-fidelity simulation environment, and outcomes were validated on physical sUAS in a real-world field testing setting. The findings from the study demonstrated SAFUS’ ability to uncover diverse state transition failures, and to provide a practical and scalable solution for detecting a broad range of state-related failures in an sUAS application.","az":"小型无人驾驶航空系统（sUAS）在多样且往往安全攸关的环境中日益广泛部署，这要求对机载决策逻辑在各种条件下进行严格验证。本文提出 SAFUS，一条模糊测试流水线，用于验证 sUAS 应用在各种时序条件和环境扰动下与状态转移、自动失效保护（failsafe）以及人类操作员交互相关的核心行为。我们构造模糊测试场景以检测行为偏差，随后动态生成相应的故障树，以可视化导致失效的状态、模式和环境因素，从而帮助项目相关方分析失效并识别其根本原因。我们在一个真实的 sUAS 系统上验证了 SAFUS，能够识别出此前该系统开发团队未曾发现的若干失效点。模糊测试在高保真仿真环境中进行，其结果在真实场地测试中于物理 sUAS 上得到验证。研究结果表明，SAFUS 能够揭示多种状态转移失效，并为检测 sUAS 应用中广泛的状态相关失效提供了一种实用且可扩展的方案。","tl":"针对无人机状态转移与失效保护的模糊测试并自动生成故障树。","au":["Theodore Chambers","Arturo Miguel Russell Bernal","Michael Vierhauser","Jane Cleland-Huang"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["sUAS","fuzzing","state transition failures","fault tree","simulation-based testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/269/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.05449"},{"id":"p00756","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Multi-Location Software Model Completion","tz":"多位置软件模型补全","a":"In model-driven engineering and beyond, software models are key development artifacts. In practice, they often grow to substantial size and complexity, undergoing thousands of modifications over time due to evolution, refactoring, and maintenance. The rise of AI has sparked interest in how software modeling activities can be automated. Recently, LLM-based approaches for software model completion have been proposed, however, the state of the art supports only single-location model completion by predicting changes at a specific location. Going beyond, we aim to bridge the gap toward handling coordinated changes that span multiple locations across large, complex models. Specifically, we propose a novel global embedding-based next focus predictor, NextFocus, which is capable of multi-location model completion for the first time. The predictor consists of a neural network with an attention mechanism, which is trained on historical software model evolution data from real-world modeling repositories. Starting from an existing change, it predicts further model elements to change, potentially spanning across multiple parts of the model. We evaluate our approach on multi-location model changes that actually have been performed by developers in real-world projects. NextFocus achieves promising results for multi-location model completion even when changes are heavily spread across the model. It archives an average Precision@k score of 0.98 for k 10, significantly outperforming the three baseline approaches.","az":"在模型驱动工程及更广泛的场景中，软件模型是关键的开发制品。在实践中，它们往往规模庞大、结构复杂，并因演化、重构和维护而经历成千上万次修改。人工智能的兴起激发了人们对软件建模活动自动化的兴趣。近期已有基于大语言模型的软件模型补全方法被提出，但现有技术仅支持单一位置的模型补全，即预测某个特定位置的变更。我们更进一步，力图弥合处理跨越大型复杂模型多个位置的协同变更这一空白。具体而言，我们提出一种新颖的基于全局嵌入的下一焦点预测器 NextFocus，首次实现了多位置模型补全。该预测器由带注意力机制的神经网络构成，在来自真实建模仓库的历史软件模型演化数据上训练。它从一次已有变更出发，预测后续需要修改的模型元素，这些元素可能跨越模型的多个部分。我们在真实项目中开发者实际执行过的多位置模型变更上评估我们的方法。即使变更在模型中高度分散，NextFocus 在多位置模型补全上也取得了良好效果，在 $k \\leq 10$ 时平均 Precision@k 达到 0.98，显著优于三个基线方法。","tl":"首个能预测跨多个位置协同变更的软件模型补全器。","au":["Alisa Carla Welter","Christof Tinnes","Sven Apel"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["model-driven engineering","model completion","multi-location change","attention network","model evolution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/270/x"},{"id":"p00757","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GenDetect: Generalizing Reactive Detection for Resilience Against Imitative DeFi Attack Cascade","tz":"GenDetect：泛化反应式检测以抵御模仿型 DeFi 攻击级联","a":"As blockchain ecosystems grow, financially motivated attackers have increasingly exploited vulnerabilities in decentralized finance (DeFi) protocols, resulting in frequent and severe losses. Unlike conventional cyberattacks, DeFi exploits propagate rapidly due to the transparent and composable nature of smart contracts. In this setting, we identify a critical behavioral pattern: Imitative Attack Cascade, where an initial successful exploit is quickly followed by a flurry of mimicking transactions that reuse attack logic with minor modifications or parameter changes. Our empirical analysis shows that over 69% of DeFi attacks exhibit strong behavioral similarity to earlier incidents, often occurring within hours or days of the initial attack. This phenomenon highlights a fundamental limitation in current reactive detection workflows. While the initial attacks are often flagged through heuristic alerts, such as Tornado Cash traces, anomalous nonce usage, or known exploiter labels, these signals require manual validation and the construction of handcrafted detection rules through trace analysis. This process is labor-intensive and slow, resulting in unacceptable latency while follow-up attacks continue to spread. Motivated by this gap, our research goal is to ensure that once an attack has been observed, even a single instance, it can be rapidly abstracted into an actionable and generalizable detection rule, enabling scalable protection against imitative attacks. We decompose the problem into two core challenges: (I) abstracting the semantics of diverse, obscure function signatures, and (II) matching transaction logic in noisy, evasive traces. To address these, we leverage two key insights: (i) the open-source nature of most DeFi protocols enables high-fidelity semantic classification of function signatures; (ii) contract labels allow us to isolate essential logic by filtering irrelevant calls and classifying attack intent. Based on these, we develop a reactive detection framework, GenDetect, which achieves strong benchmark performance (ACC: 98%, FPR: 1%, FNR: 3%) and, critically, discovers 56 previously unrevealed attacks from the past three years, highlighting its practical effectiveness. Our source code and dataset are released on Github .","az":"随着区块链生态的发展，出于经济动机的攻击者越来越多地利用去中心化金融（DeFi）协议中的漏洞，造成频繁而严重的损失。与传统网络攻击不同，由于智能合约的透明性与可组合性，DeFi 攻击传播极快。在此背景下，我们识别出一种关键的行为模式：模仿型攻击级联（Imitative Attack Cascade）——一次成功的初始攻击之后，会迅速出现大量模仿交易，它们复用攻击逻辑并只做细微修改或参数改动。我们的实证分析表明，超过 69% 的 DeFi 攻击与此前事件表现出强烈的行为相似性，且往往发生在初始攻击后的数小时或数天内。这一现象凸显了当前反应式检测流程的根本局限。虽然初始攻击常能通过启发式告警（如 Tornado Cash 痕迹、异常 nonce 使用或已知攻击者标签）被标记出来，但这些信号需要人工验证，并需通过痕迹分析构建手工编写的检测规则。该过程耗时费力，导致在后续攻击持续扩散时产生难以接受的延迟。基于这一空白，我们的研究目标是：一旦观测到一次攻击（哪怕只有一个实例），就能迅速将其抽象为可执行、可泛化的检测规则，从而实现对模仿型攻击的可扩展防护。我们将问题分解为两个核心挑战：(I) 抽象各种晦涩函数签名的语义；(II) 在噪声大、具规避性的交易痕迹中匹配交易逻辑。为此我们利用两个关键洞见：(i) 大多数 DeFi 协议的开源特性使得对函数签名进行高保真语义分类成为可能；(ii) 合约标签使我们能够过滤无关调用并对攻击意图进行分类，从而分离出核心逻辑。基于此，我们开发了反应式检测框架 GenDetect，它取得了出色的基准性能（准确率 98%，误报率 1%，漏报率 3%），并且关键地发现了过去三年中 56 起此前未被揭露的攻击，凸显其实际有效性。我们的源码与数据集已在 GitHub 上发布。","tl":"把单次 DeFi 攻击抽象成可泛化检测规则，挖出 56 起未披露攻击。","au":["Bowen Cai","Weihng Bai","Youshui Lu","Haoran Xu","Yuannan Yang","Yajin Zhou","Kangjie Lu"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DeFi attacks","imitative attack cascade","reactive detection","transaction traces","smart contracts"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/271/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.26094"},{"id":"p00758","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Testing Deep Learning Libraries via Neurosymbolic Constraint Learning","tz":"通过神经符号约束学习测试深度学习库","a":"Deep Learning (DL) libraries (e.g., Pytorch) are popular in the development of AI applications. These libraries are complex and contain bugs. Researchers have proposed various bug-finding techniques for such libraries. Yet, there is much room for improvement. A key challenge in testing DL libraries is the lack of API specifications. Prior testing approaches often inaccurately model the input specifications of DL APIs, resulting in missing valid inputs that could reveal bugs or false alarms from invalid inputs. To address this challenge, we develop Centaur - the first neurosymbolic technique to test DL library APIs using dynamically learned input constraints. Centaur leverages the key idea that formal API constraints can be learned from a small number of seed inputs, and that the learned constraints can be solved using SMT solvers to generate valid and diverse test inputs for the API. We develop a novel grammar that represents first-order logic formulae over API parameters and expresses tensor-related properties (e.g., shape, data type, etc.) as well as relational properties between parameters. We use the grammar to guide a Large Language Model (LLM) to enumerate syntactically correct candidate rules, which are then validated using valid inputs. Further, we develop a custom refinement strategy to prune the set of learned rules to eliminate spurious or redundant rules. The learned constraints are then used to systematically generate valid and diverse inputs for the API by SMT solving (such as Z3) and a specialized sampling technique. We evaluate Centaur for testing PyTorch and TensorFlow. Our results show that Centaur generates constraints more accurately compared to prior approaches, namely DocTer and ACETest. In terms of coverage, Centaur covers 203, 149, and 9608 more branches than TitanFuzz, ACETest and Pathfinder, respectively. Using Centaur, we also detect 23 new bugs in PyTorch and TensorFlow, out of which 11 are already confirmed.","az":"深度学习（DL）库（如 PyTorch）在 AI 应用开发中广受欢迎。这些库结构复杂且含有缺陷。研究者已提出多种面向此类库的缺陷发现技术，但仍有很大改进空间。测试 DL 库的一个关键挑战是缺少 API 规约。以往的测试方法常常不准确地建模 DL API 的输入规约，导致遗漏可能暴露缺陷的有效输入，或因无效输入产生误报。为应对这一挑战，我们开发了 Centaur——首个利用动态学习到的输入约束来测试 DL 库 API 的神经符号技术。Centaur 的核心思想是：形式化的 API 约束可以从少量种子输入中学习得到，而学到的约束可用 SMT 求解器求解，从而为 API 生成有效且多样的测试输入。我们设计了一种新颖的文法，用以表示关于 API 参数的一阶逻辑公式，既能表达张量相关属性（如形状、数据类型等），也能表达参数之间的关系属性。我们用该文法引导大语言模型枚举语法正确的候选规则，再用有效输入对其进行验证。此外，我们设计了定制的精化策略来裁剪学到的规则集合，剔除虚假或冗余的规则。随后，学到的约束通过 SMT 求解（如 Z3）和一种专门的采样技术，被用于系统性地生成有效且多样的 API 输入。我们在 PyTorch 和 TensorFlow 上评估 Centaur。结果表明，与此前方法 DocTer 和 ACETest 相比，Centaur 生成的约束更准确。在覆盖率方面，Centaur 分别比 TitanFuzz、ACETest 和 Pathfinder 多覆盖 203、149 和 9608 个分支。使用 Centaur，我们还在 PyTorch 和 TensorFlow 中检测出 23 个新缺陷，其中 11 个已被确认。","tl":"用 LLM 枚举加 SMT 求解动态学习 DL API 输入约束来造测试。","au":["M M Abid Naziri","Shinhae Kim","Feiran Qin","Saikat Dutta","Marcelo d'Amorim"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["deep learning library testing","neurosymbolic","input constraints","SMT solving","PyTorch"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/272/x"},{"id":"p00759","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LogFold: Compressing Logs with Structured Tokens and Hybrid Encoding","tz":"LogFold：基于结构化 token 与混合编码的日志压缩","a":"Logs are essential for diagnosing failures and conducting retrospective studies, leading many software organizations to retain log messages for a long time. Nevertheless, the volume of generated log data grows rapidly as software systems grow, necessitating an effective compression method. Apart from general-purpose compressors (e.g., Gzip, Bzip2), many recent studies developed log-specific compression algorithms, but they offer suboptimal performance because of (1) overlooking redundancies within certain complex tokens, and (2) lacking a fine-grained encoding strategy for diverse token types. This work uncovers a new redundancy pattern in structured tokens and proposes a new type-aware encoding strategy to improve log compression. Building on this insight, we introduce LogFold, a novel log compression method consisting of four components: a token analyzer to classifies tokens as structured, unstructured, or static types; a processor that mines recurring patterns within structured tokens based on their delimiter skeletons; a hybrid encoder that tailors data representation according to token types; and a packer that compresses the output into an archive file. Extensive experiments on 16 public log datasets demonstrate that LogFold surpasses state-of-the-art baselines, achieving average compression ratio improvements by 11.11%, with a compression speed of 9.842 MB/s. Ablation studies further indicate the importance of each component. We also conduct sensitivity analyses to verify LogFold’s robustness and stability across various internal settings.","az":"日志对于诊断故障和开展回溯性研究至关重要，因此许多软件组织会长期保留日志消息。然而，随着软件系统的增长，生成的日志数据量迅速膨胀，亟需有效的压缩方法。除通用压缩器（如 Gzip、Bzip2）外，近期许多研究开发了面向日志的专用压缩算法，但它们性能欠佳，原因在于：(1) 忽视了某些复杂 token 内部的冗余；(2) 缺乏针对多样 token 类型的细粒度编码策略。本工作揭示了结构化 token 中的一种新冗余模式，并提出一种新的类型感知编码策略来改进日志压缩。基于这一洞见，我们提出 LogFold，一种新颖的日志压缩方法，包含四个组件：将 token 分类为结构化、非结构化或静态类型的 token 分析器；基于分隔符骨架挖掘结构化 token 内重复模式的处理器；根据 token 类型定制数据表示的混合编码器；以及将输出压缩为归档文件的打包器。在 16 个公开日志数据集上的大量实验表明，LogFold 超越了最先进的基线方法，平均压缩率提升 11.11%，压缩速度达 9.842 MB/s。消融实验进一步表明各组件的重要性。我们还进行了敏感性分析，验证了 LogFold 在各种内部设置下的鲁棒性与稳定性。","tl":"发现结构化 token 内新冗余模式并做类型感知混合编码压缩日志。","au":["Shiwen Shan","Yintong Huo","Hongzhan Zhong","Zhining Wang","Yuxin Su","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["log compression","structured tokens","hybrid encoding","delimiter skeleton","log analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/273/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/273/LogFold-Compressing-Logs-with-Structured-Tokens-and-Hybrid-Encoding"},{"id":"p00760","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Beyond Fuzzy Matching: Constraint-Guided Patch Presence Testing for Obfuscated Java Binaries","tz":"超越模糊匹配：面向混淆 Java 二进制的约束引导补丁存在性检测","a":"Patch presence testing (PPT) is critical for mitigating vulnerabilities introduced by the use of third-party libraries (TPLs) in Java programs. However, the widespread use of obfuscation significantly undermines its accuracy by altering patch-relevant features. To preserve feature consistency before and after obfuscation for reliable comparison, existing studies summarize patch digests using several representative fuzzy features. These fuzzy features, designed to generalize obfuscation-prone details, have proven effective in TPL detection. Nevertheless, this approach faces limitations when directly applied to PPT, where finer features are needed to capture subtle patch changes. Although patch digests facilitate feature matching under obfuscation-induced code changes with high efficiency, methods with similar semantic structures—common in TPLs due to factors such as overriding and inheritance—often exhibit identical digests. Relying solely on feature similarity without considering method constraints often results in inaccurate outcomes. To tackle the aforementioned challenges, this paper presents PScan, a constraint-guided patch presence testing tool capable of detecting patches in both standard and obfuscated Java binaries (i.e., executables of Java programs). PScan first defines a set of actual constraints that must be satisfied during Java method matching. Guided by these constraints, it maps methods containing critical patch information to their obfuscated counterparts and then leverages these mappings to refine the associated fuzzy features into concrete expressions. Furthermore, leveraging the formalized constraints, PScan formulates the patch digest matching process as a binary integer programming (BIP) model to precisely identify correct method matches. Extensive evaluations on public datasets show that PScan outperforms state-of-the-art methods, improving accuracy by at least 15.0 percentage points and achieving an overall accuracy of 97.1%. Our experiments also reveal that, with these constraints, PScan reduces the method mismatch rate to 1.5%, a 16.9 percentage point reduction relative to the baseline.","az":"补丁存在性检测（PPT）对于缓解 Java 程序中使用第三方库（TPL）引入的漏洞至关重要。然而，混淆的广泛使用会改变与补丁相关的特征，从而严重削弱其准确性。为在混淆前后保持特征一致以便可靠比较，现有研究使用若干具代表性的“模糊特征”来概括补丁摘要。这些为泛化易受混淆影响的细节而设计的模糊特征，已在 TPL 检测中被证明有效。然而，将其直接应用于 PPT 时会遇到局限，因为 PPT 需要更精细的特征来捕捉细微的补丁变更。尽管补丁摘要能够在混淆导致的代码变化下高效地进行特征匹配，但语义结构相似的方法——由于重写和继承等因素，在 TPL 中十分常见——往往具有相同的摘要。仅依赖特征相似度而不考虑方法约束，常常导致结果不准确。为应对上述挑战，本文提出 PScan，一种约束引导的补丁存在性检测工具，能够在标准和混淆的 Java 二进制（即 Java 程序的可执行文件）中检测补丁。PScan 首先定义了一组在 Java 方法匹配过程中必须满足的实际约束。在这些约束引导下，它将包含关键补丁信息的方法映射到其被混淆后的对应方法，然后利用这些映射把相关的模糊特征细化为具体表达式。此外，借助形式化的约束，PScan 将补丁摘要匹配过程建模为二元整数规划（BIP）模型，以精确识别正确的方法匹配。在公开数据集上的大量评估表明，PScan 优于最先进方法，准确率至少提升 15.0 个百分点，总体准确率达 97.1%。实验还表明，借助这些约束，PScan 将方法误匹配率降至 1.5%，相对基线下降 16.9 个百分点。","tl":"用方法匹配约束与二元整数规划精化模糊特征做补丁存在性检测。","au":["Lige Zhan","Jiang Ming","Chenke Luo","Letian Sha","Guojun Peng","Jianming Fu"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["patch presence testing","Java obfuscation","third-party libraries","binary integer programming","method matching"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/274/x","pu":"https://github.com/IMZGforever/PScan/blob/main/Beyond%20Fuzzy%20Matching%20Constraint-Guided%20Patch%20Presence%20Testing%20for%20Obfuscated%20Java%20Binaries.pdf"},{"id":"p00761","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Women’s Career Paths in the Nordic Software Industry: A Narrative Analysis Through Gender-Switched Personas","tz":"北欧软件行业女性的职业路径：基于性别互换人物志的叙事分析","a":"Recent data indicate that women are significantly more likely than men to leave the software engineering (SE) field or transition to other careers, with nearly half doing so by the age of 35. Despite ongoing efforts, retention strategies remain inadequate and insufficient. This study examines the career trajectories of women in the SE industry, with a specific focus on the Nordic context. We adopted a narrative research approach, using a storytelling framework to explore the lived experiences of women working in SE. We collected data through a questionnaire and semi-structured interviews. To challenge gender stereotypes and foster reflection, we present the findings through a gender-switched approach. The personas vary in background, nationality, and age, and highlight a range of personal and professional challenges. Key themes include self-doubt, mental health struggles, and what we refer to as the “good-girl syndrome”—a form of internalized pressure linked to perfectionism. For instance, Jakob, a non-native speaker, described how language barriers and the scarcity of women in the field affect career advancement. Andreas, a younger professional, expressed concerns about not being taken seriously due to age. The results underscore the importance of women-centered networks in sharing experiences and fostering a sense of safety, as well as the need for open communication and transparency from companies in their hiring practices, salary data, and representation of female leadership. Our study offers a new perspective on the career paths of women, inspiring future researchers and providing an actionable set of strategies to consider for addressing the retention of women in the SE field.","az":"近期数据显示，女性离开软件工程（SE）领域或转向其他职业的可能性显著高于男性，近半数女性在 35 岁前就已如此。尽管相关努力持续进行，留存策略仍然不足且不充分。本研究考察女性在软件工程行业中的职业轨迹，并特别聚焦北欧语境。我们采用叙事研究方法，使用讲故事的框架来探究在 SE 领域工作的女性的亲身经历。我们通过问卷和半结构化访谈收集数据。为挑战性别刻板印象并促进反思，我们以性别互换的方式呈现研究发现。这些人物志在背景、国籍和年龄上各不相同，凸显了一系列个人与职业层面的挑战。关键主题包括自我怀疑、心理健康困扰，以及我们称之为“乖女孩综合征”的现象——一种与完美主义相关联的内化压力。例如，非母语者 Jakob 描述了语言障碍以及该领域女性稀少如何影响职业晋升；较年轻的从业者 Andreas 则担忧因年龄而不被认真对待。研究结果强调了以女性为中心的网络在分享经验、营造安全感方面的重要性，以及企业在招聘实践、薪酬数据和女性领导层比例上保持开放沟通与透明的必要性。我们的研究为理解女性职业路径提供了新视角，启发未来研究者，并提供了一套可落地的策略以应对软件工程领域女性的留存问题。","tl":"用性别互换人物志叙事呈现北欧女性软件从业者的留存困境。","au":["Claudia Maria Cutrupi","Mia Bjørndal","Anh Nguyen-Duc","Letizia Jaccheri"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","accessibility-inclusion"],"kw":["women in software engineering","career paths","narrative analysis","personas","retention"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/275/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3787803"},{"id":"p00762","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Hybrid Fault-Driven Mutation Testing for Python","tz":"面向 Python 的混合式故障驱动变异测试","a":"Mutation testing is an effective technique for assessing the effectiveness of test suites by systematically injecting artificial faults into programs. However, existing mutation testing techniques fall short in capturing many types of common faults in dynamically-typed languages like Python. In this paper, we introduce a novel set of seven mutation operators that are inspired by prevalent anti-patterns in Python programs, designed to complement the existing general-purpose operators and broaden the spectrum of simulated faults. We propose a mutation testing technique that utilizes a hybrid of static and dynamic analyses to mutate Python programs based on these operators while minimizing equivalent mutants. We implement our approach in a tool called PyTation and evaluate it on 13 open-source Python applications. Our results show that PyTation generates mutants that complement those from general-purpose tools, exhibiting distinct behaviour under test execution and uncovering inadequacies in high-coverage test suites. We further demonstrate that PyTation produces a high proportion of unique mutants, a low cross-kill rate, and a low test overlap ratio relative to baseline tools, highlighting its novel fault model. PyTation also incurs few equivalent mutants, aided by dynamic analysis heuristics.","az":"变异测试是通过系统性地向程序注入人工故障来评估测试套件有效性的有效技术。然而，现有变异测试技术难以捕捉 Python 这类动态类型语言中的许多常见故障类型。本文引入一组七个新的变异算子，其灵感来自 Python 程序中普遍存在的反模式，旨在补充现有的通用算子并拓宽可模拟故障的范围。我们提出一种变异测试技术，结合静态与动态分析，基于这些算子对 Python 程序进行变异，同时最小化等价变异体。我们将该方法实现为工具 PyTation，并在 13 个开源 Python 应用上进行评估。结果表明，PyTation 生成的变异体与通用工具生成的变异体形成互补，在测试执行下表现出不同的行为，并揭示了高覆盖率测试套件中的不足。我们进一步表明，相对基线工具，PyTation 产生了高比例的独有变异体、较低的交叉杀死率和较低的测试重叠率，凸显其新颖的故障模型。得益于动态分析启发式方法，PyTation 产生的等价变异体也很少。","tl":"提出七个源自 Python 反模式的变异算子并用静动态混合分析去等价体。","au":["Saba Alimadadi","Golnaz Gharachorlu"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mutation testing","Python","mutation operators","equivalent mutants","static and dynamic analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/276/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.19088"},{"id":"p00763","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TestWeaver: Execution-aware, Feedback-driven Regression Testing Generation with Large Language Models","tz":"TestWeaver：执行感知、反馈驱动的大语言模型回归测试生成","a":"Regression testing ensures that code changes do not unintentionally break existing functionality. While recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have shown promise in automating test generation for regression testing, they often suffer from limited reasoning about program execution, resulting in stagnated coverage growth—a phenomenon known as the coverage plateau. In this paper, we present TestWeaver, a novel LLM-based approach that integrates lightweight program analysis to create a focused execution context that assists LLMs in better test generation versus existing passive re-prompting approaches. TestWeaver strategically chooses the following components to overcome LLMs’ limited reasoning on complex execution: (1) it reduces hallucinations and improves focus by supplying the LLM with the backward slice from the target line instead of a full program context; (2) it identifies and incorporates close test cases—those that share control-flow similarities with the path to the target line—to provide focused execution context within the LLM’s context window; and (3) it enhances LLM’s reasoning with execution in-line annotations that encode variable states as comments along the executed path. By equipping LLMs with these targeted and contextualized inputs, TestWeaver improves coverage-guided test generation and mitigates redundant explorations. Empirical results demonstrate that TestWeaver accelerates code coverage growth and generates more effective regression test cases than the state-of-the-art LLM-based approaches.","az":"回归测试确保代码变更不会无意中破坏已有功能。虽然大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展在自动化回归测试生成方面展现出潜力，但它们对程序执行的推理能力有限，导致覆盖率增长停滞——即所谓的覆盖率平台期现象。本文提出 TestWeaver，一种新颖的基于 LLM 的方法，它集成轻量级程序分析来构建聚焦的执行上下文，相比现有的被动重复提示方法，能更好地辅助 LLM 生成测试。TestWeaver 有策略地选择以下组件来克服 LLM 在复杂执行上推理能力的不足：(1) 向 LLM 提供从目标行出发的后向切片而非完整程序上下文，从而减少幻觉并提升聚焦度；(2) 识别并引入“相近测试用例”——那些与通往目标行的路径具有控制流相似性的测试——以在 LLM 上下文窗口内提供聚焦的执行上下文；(3) 通过执行内联注释增强 LLM 的推理，这些注释以注释形式沿执行路径编码变量状态。通过为 LLM 提供这些有针对性且上下文化的输入，TestWeaver 改进了覆盖率引导的测试生成，并缓解了冗余探索。实验结果表明，TestWeaver 相比最先进的基于 LLM 的方法加快了代码覆盖率增长，并生成了更有效的回归测试用例。","tl":"用后向切片、相近测试与变量状态内联注释打破 LLM 测试生成的覆盖率平台期。","au":["Cuong Chi Le","Cuong Duc Van","Tung Duy Vu","Minh V. T. Pham","Hoang Nhat Phan","Huy N. Phan","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["regression test generation","LLM","backward slice","coverage plateau","execution context"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/277/x"},{"id":"p00764","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Modeling Like Peeling an Onion: Layerwise Analysis-Driven Automatic Behavioral Model Generation","tz":"像剥洋葱一样建模：逐层分析驱动的自动行为建模","a":"As software complexity skyrockets and requirements evolve at breakneck speed, traditional human-centric behavioral modeling can no longer keep pace in terms of efficiency, accuracy, and scalability. While existing automated approaches can produce models, they still struggle with deep semantic understanding of textual requirements or with reasoning about intricate system logic, especially nested relationships. Inspired by the way experienced analysts “peel back” layers of a problem, we propose LATO, a Layerwise Analysis-Driven AuTomatic Behavioral MOdeling approach. It employs a progressive decomposition strategy to guide large language models in incrementally parsing requirement structures, deconstructing behavioral dependencies, and ultimately generating executable UML activity diagrams. Comprehensive evaluations on four open-source datasets and two real-world industrial systems show that LATO comprehensively outperforms state-of-the-art baselines in accuracy, completeness, and syntactic compliance: F_1 scores for behavioral node-extraction improve by up to 71.1%, relation-extraction F_1 by 52.4 % relatively, and syntactic pass rates remain above 96.67%. The framework also exhibits strong robustness to input perturbations, confirming its cross-domain generalizability. This paper is the first to tightly fuse human-inspired strategies with LLMs in behavior modeling, yielding an intelligent infrastructure that exhibits expert-level logical understanding and generalization. By closing the modeling-skills gap, LATO delivers a next-generation, low-cost, and explainable solution for requirements engineering and AI-native software development.","az":"随着软件复杂度急剧上升、需求以极快速度演变，传统以人为中心的行为建模在效率、准确性和可扩展性上已难以跟上。尽管现有自动化方法能够产出模型，它们仍难以深入理解文本需求的语义，或难以推理复杂的系统逻辑，尤其是嵌套关系。受经验丰富的分析师逐层“剥开”问题的方式启发，我们提出 LATO，一种逐层分析驱动的自动行为建模方法。它采用渐进式分解策略，引导大语言模型逐步解析需求结构、拆解行为依赖，并最终生成可执行的 UML 活动图。在四个开源数据集和两个真实工业系统上的全面评估表明，LATO 在准确性、完整性和语法合规性上全面超越最先进基线：行为节点抽取的 $F_1$ 分数最高提升 71.1%，关系抽取的 $F_1$ 相对提升 52.4%，语法通过率保持在 96.67% 以上。该框架对输入扰动也表现出很强的鲁棒性，验证了其跨领域泛化能力。本文首次将受人类启发的策略与大语言模型在行为建模中紧密融合，产出了一种具备专家级逻辑理解与泛化能力的智能基础设施。通过弥合建模技能鸿沟，LATO 为需求工程与 AI 原生软件开发提供了下一代低成本、可解释的解决方案。","tl":"用渐进式分解引导 LLM 逐层生成可执行 UML 活动图。","au":["Yike Huang","Ming Hu","Xiaohong Chen","Zhi Jin","Shuyuan Xiao"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["behavioral modeling","UML activity diagram","requirements analysis","LLM","progressive decomposition"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/278/x"},{"id":"p00765","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"VADA: A Multicultural Benchmark for Value-Aware Data Generation and Alignment Evaluation in LLMs","tz":"VADA：面向 LLM 价值感知数据生成与对齐评测的多文化基准","a":"As large language models (LLMs) are increasingly integrated into intelligent software systems that range from educational assistants to legal advisory tools, ensuring their alignment with diverse cultural values becomes a critical software engineering challenge. Traditional software engineering methods such as unit testing and formal verification fall short in specifying or validating complex normative expectations such as fairness, cultural sensitivity, and moral appropriateness. Addressing this gap, we introduce VADA, a value-aware development and evaluation framework for systematically testing and benchmarking LLMs under multiple cultural value systems. VADA incorporates a modular scenario-question generation pipeline that constructs culturally grounded test cases spanning 25 value dimensions across Chinese, European, and Islamic ethical frameworks. It further includes a Bayesian ensemble evaluation framework that aggregates alignment judgments from multiple diverse LLM-based evaluators, assigning dimension-specific trust weights based on their observed reliability. We also develop a lightweight supervised evaluator fine-tuned on VADA-generated data, providing a scalable and deployable alternative to multi-model ensemble evaluation. We construct a large-scale benchmark containing 11,865 automatically annotated cases, along with a human-labeled subset of 1000 instances for validation and evaluation. Empirical results demonstrate that VADA substantially outperforms existing prompting-based evaluators, achieving over 93.6 percent accuracy and high agreement with human annotations. Ablation studies confirm the complementary benefits of evaluator diversity and reliability-aware aggregation. Furthermore, VADA enables comparative audits of state-of-the-art LLMs, uncovering alignment inconsistencies across cultural dimensions. Results highlight VADA’s effectiveness as a foundation for robust value-aware evaluation and development of LLMs.","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）越来越多地被集成进从教育助手到法律咨询工具等各类智能软件系统，确保它们与多元文化价值观保持一致成为一项关键的软件工程挑战。单元测试和形式化验证等传统软件工程方法，难以规约或验证诸如公平性、文化敏感性和道德恰当性这类复杂的规范性期望。为填补这一空白，我们提出 VADA，一个价值感知的开发与评测框架，用于在多种文化价值体系下系统性地测试和基准化 LLM。VADA 包含一条模块化的场景—问题生成流水线，构建覆盖中国、欧洲和伊斯兰伦理框架下 25 个价值维度的、具文化根基的测试用例。它还包含一个贝叶斯集成评测框架，聚合多个不同 LLM 评测者的对齐判断，并依据其观测到的可靠性为各维度分配特定的信任权重。我们还开发了一个在 VADA 生成数据上微调的轻量级有监督评测器，作为多模型集成评测的可扩展、可部署替代方案。我们构建了一个包含 11,865 个自动标注案例的大规模基准，以及一个用于验证和评测的 1000 条人工标注子集。实证结果表明，VADA 大幅优于现有基于提示的评测器，准确率超过 93.6%，并与人工标注高度一致。消融实验证实了评测者多样性与可靠性感知聚合的互补收益。此外，VADA 支持对最先进 LLM 进行对比审计，揭示了跨文化维度的对齐不一致。结果凸显了 VADA 作为稳健的价值感知 LLM 评测与开发基础的有效性。","tl":"用贝叶斯集成评测者构建跨三大伦理体系的 25 维价值对齐基准。","au":["Zhenlun Zhang","Yang Feng","Shihao Weng","Yining Yin","Jincheng Li","Jia Liu"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["cross-track-bridge","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["value alignment","multicultural benchmark","LLM evaluators","Bayesian ensemble","scenario generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/279/x"},{"id":"p00766","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"META²V2V: Revealing Behavioural Deviations under Mutual Perception in Multi-Vehicle Autonomous Driving","tz":"META²V2V：揭示多车自动驾驶中互感知下的行为偏差","a":"In next-generation traffic, multiple intelligent vehicles equipped with autonomous driving systems (ADS) operate simultaneously. These vehicles share real-time information through vehicle-to-vehicle (V2V) communication during operation and make decisions based on this mutual perception. In this paper, we present a novel METAmorphic testing framework to evaluate ADS performance in multi-vehicle scenarios, addressing the META information shared during V2V communication (META²V2V). META²V2V interacts with the shared information by systematically injecting four types of controlled common perturbations into V2V data streams and observing how these disruptions affect the vehicles’ mutual perception and subsequent interactions. META²V2V assesses ADS decisions from two aspects: soundness and robustness, by introducing soundness metamorphic testing relations (S-MRs) and robustness metamorphic relations (R-MRs), respectively. Specifically, S-MRs claim that the performance of ADS under perfect information should outperform that under perturbations, whereas R-MRs claim that the performance of ADS should not degrade too much under information perturbations. Furthermore, META²V2V employs multi-objective search-based testing conducted from two directions to efficiently generate test groups that violate S-MRs and R-MRs, respectively. Experimental results demonstrate that, compared to random testing, our approach can identify 733.3% and 133.0% more violations that reveal soundness and robustness issues.","az":"在下一代交通中，多辆配备自动驾驶系统（ADS）的智能车辆同时运行。这些车辆在运行过程中通过车对车（V2V）通信共享实时信息，并基于这种互感知作出决策。本文提出一种新颖的蜕变测试框架，用于评估多车场景下的 ADS 性能，并聚焦 V2V 通信中共享的元信息（META²V2V）。META²V2V 通过系统性地向 V2V 数据流注入四类受控的常见扰动，并观察这些干扰如何影响车辆的互感知及后续交互，从而与共享信息发生交互。META²V2V 从两个方面评估 ADS 决策：健全性与鲁棒性，分别引入健全性蜕变关系（S-MRs）和鲁棒性蜕变关系（R-MRs）。具体而言，S-MRs 断言 ADS 在完美信息下的性能应优于在扰动下的性能，而 R-MRs 断言 ADS 的性能在信息扰动下不应退化过多。此外，META²V2V 采用从两个方向进行的多目标搜索式测试，以高效生成分别违反 S-MRs 和 R-MRs 的测试组。实验结果表明，与随机测试相比，我们的方法能够多识别出 733.3% 和 133.0% 的违例，分别揭示健全性与鲁棒性问题。","tl":"针对 V2V 共享信息扰动提出健全性与鲁棒性两类蜕变关系。","au":["Lejin Li","Xiao-Yi Zhang","Shuncheng Tang","Zhenya Zhang","Jianjun Zhao"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["metamorphic testing","autonomous driving","V2V communication","search-based testing","metamorphic relations"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/280/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/280/META-V2V-Revealing-Behavioural-Deviations-under-Mutual-Perception-in-Multi-Vehicle-A"},{"id":"p00767","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Learning without Forgetting: Towards Continual learning of Fault Localization Models in Industrial Software Systems","tz":"学而不忘：面向工业软件系统缺陷定位模型的持续学习","a":"Learning-based fault localization has achieved promising results. However, as software and tests are constantly evolving, models trained on old data become ineffective on new data. Particularly, in the context of system testing for large-scale software, each iteration generates a large volume of new data. This makes retraining the model from scratch incur an unacceptable time overhead, while merely fine-tuning on new data leads to catastrophic forgetting. Continual learning offers an effective method for models to avoid catastrophic forgetting during this iterative process. However, existing continual learning methods are not specifically designed for fault localization or for large-scale software system testing scenarios, which leads to their direct application yielding sub-optimal effectiveness. In response, we propose Canto, a novel continual learning framework specifically designed for large-scale software fault localization. Canto first extracts fine-grained program semantics from logs, then utilizes fault characteristics to enhance the weights of certain semantics. Finally, Canto uses an unsupervised algorithm to obtain corresponding embeddings and selects representative exemplars based on clustering. Subsequently, Canto mixes the representative exemplars with new samples for training and adjusts the loss weight according to the model’s degree of mastery over the sample. This allows the model to focus more on samples that are not yet well-mastered during the training process, thereby enabling it to learn new faults while mitigating the forgetting of old ones. In extensive evaluations against 6 continual learning baselines, Canto demonstrates superior performance, improving overall effectiveness by 17.30% to 45.23%.","az":"基于学习的缺陷定位已取得可喜成果。然而，由于软件和测试不断演化，在旧数据上训练的模型在新数据上会失效。特别是在大规模软件的系统测试场景中，每次迭代都会产生大量新数据。这使得从头重训模型带来难以接受的时间开销，而仅在新数据上微调又会导致灾难性遗忘。持续学习为模型在这一迭代过程中避免灾难性遗忘提供了有效方法。然而，现有持续学习方法并非专为缺陷定位或大规模软件系统测试场景设计，直接应用会导致效果欠佳。为此，我们提出 Canto，一个专为大规模软件缺陷定位设计的新型持续学习框架。Canto 首先从日志中提取细粒度的程序语义，然后利用故障特征增强某些语义的权重。最后，Canto 使用无监督算法获得相应的嵌入，并基于聚类选取代表性样例。随后，Canto 将代表性样例与新样本混合进行训练，并根据模型对样本的掌握程度调整损失权重。这使得模型在训练过程中更关注尚未充分掌握的样本，从而在学习新故障的同时缓解对旧故障的遗忘。在与 6 个持续学习基线的大量对比评估中，Canto 表现更优，整体效果提升 17.30% 至 45.23%。","tl":"用日志语义加权与代表性样例回放缓解缺陷定位模型的灾难性遗忘。","au":["Chun Li","Hui Li","Zhong Li","Minxue Pan","Xuandong Li"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["fault localization","continual learning","catastrophic forgetting","log semantics","industrial software"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/281/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/281/Learning-without-Forgetting-Towards-Continual-learning-of-Fault-Localization-Models-"},{"id":"p00768","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SWE-Debate: Competitive Multi-Agent Debate for Software Issue Resolution","tz":"SWE-Debate：面向软件 Issue 求解的竞争式多智能体辩论","a":"Issue resolution has made remarkable progress thanks to the advanced reasoning capabilities of large language models (LLMs). Recently, agent-based frameworks such as SWE-agent have further advanced this progress by enabling autonomous, tool-using agents to tackle complex software engineering tasks. While existing agent-based issue resolution approaches are primarily based on agents’ independent explorations, they often get stuck in local solutions and fail to identify issue patterns that span across different parts of the codebase. To address this limitation, we propose SWE-Debate, a competitive multi-agent debate framework that encourages diverse reasoning paths and achieves more consolidated issue localization. SWE-Debate first creates multiple fault propagation traces as localization proposals by traversing a code dependency graph. Then, it organizes a three-round debate among specialized agents, each embodying distinct reasoning perspectives along the fault propagation trace. This structured competition enables agents to collaboratively converge on a consolidated fix plan. Finally, this consolidated fix plan is integrated into an MCTS-based code modification agent for patch generation. Experiments on the SWE-bench benchmark show that SWE-Debate achieves new state-of-the-art results in open-source agent frameworks and outperforms baselines by a large margin.","az":"得益于大语言模型（LLM）先进的推理能力，issue 求解已取得显著进展。近来，SWE-agent 等基于智能体的框架通过让自主的、会使用工具的智能体处理复杂软件工程任务，进一步推动了这一进展。虽然现有基于智能体的 issue 求解方法主要依赖智能体各自独立的探索，但它们常常陷入局部解，无法识别跨越代码库不同部分的 issue 模式。为解决这一局限，我们提出 SWE-Debate，一个竞争式多智能体辩论框架，鼓励多样化的推理路径，并实现更加整合的 issue 定位。SWE-Debate 首先通过遍历代码依赖图创建多条故障传播路径作为定位提案。随后，它组织专门化智能体之间的三轮辩论，每个智能体沿着故障传播路径体现不同的推理视角。这种结构化竞争使智能体能够协同收敛到一个整合的修复方案。最后，该整合的修复方案被接入一个基于 MCTS 的代码修改智能体以生成补丁。在 SWE-bench 基准上的实验表明，SWE-Debate 在开源智能体框架中取得了新的最先进结果，并大幅超越基线。","tl":"沿故障传播路径组织三轮竞争辩论以整合 issue 定位方案。","au":["Han Li","Yuling Shi","Shaoxin Lin","Xiaodong Gu","Heng Lian","Wang Xin","Yantao Jia","huangtao","Qianxiang Wang"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["issue resolution","multi-agent debate","fault propagation trace","SWE-bench","MCTS patch generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/282/x"},{"id":"p00769","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evolving with AI: A Longitudinal Analysis of Developer Logs","tz":"与 AI 共同演化：开发者日志的纵向分析","a":"AI‑powered coding assistants are rapidly becoming fixtures in professional IDEs, yet their sustained influence on everyday development remains poorly understood. Prior research has focused on short-term use or self-reported perceptions, leaving open questions about how sustained AI use reshapes daily coding practices in the long term. We address this gap with a mixed-method study of AI adoption in IDEs, combining longitudinal two-year fine-grained telemetry from 800 developers with a survey of 62 professionals. We analyze five dimensions of workflow change: productivity, code quality, code editing, code reuse, and context switching. Telemetry reveals that AI users produce substantially more code but also delete significantly more. Meanwhile, survey respondents report productivity gains and perceive minimal changes in other dimensions. Our results offer empirical insights into the silent restructuring of software workflows and provide implications for designing future AI-augmented tooling.","az":"AI 驱动的编程助手正迅速成为专业 IDE 中的固定配置，但它们对日常开发的持续影响仍未被充分理解。以往研究聚焦于短期使用或自我报告的感受，留下了关于长期持续使用 AI 如何重塑日常编码实践的开放问题。我们通过一项关于 IDE 中 AI 采纳的混合方法研究来填补这一空白，结合了来自 800 名开发者为期两年的细粒度纵向遥测数据与对 62 名专业人员的问卷调查。我们分析了工作流变化的五个维度：生产力、代码质量、代码编辑、代码复用和上下文切换。遥测数据显示，AI 使用者产出的代码显著更多，但删除的代码也显著更多。与此同时，问卷受访者报告了生产力提升，并认为其他维度变化甚微。我们的结果为软件工作流的“静默重构”提供了实证洞见，并为设计未来的 AI 增强工具提供了启示。","tl":"两年遥测发现 AI 用户写得更多也删得更多，主观感知却变化甚微。","au":["Agnia Sergeyuk","Eric Huang","Dariia Karaeva","Anastasiia Serova","Yaroslav Golubev","Iftekhar Ahmed"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["AI coding assistants","longitudinal telemetry","developer workflow","mixed-method study","productivity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/283/x"},{"id":"p00770","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"3D Software Synthesis Driven by Constraint-Expressive Intermediate Representation","tz":"由约束表达型中间表示驱动的 3D 软件合成","a":"Graphical user interface (UI) software has undergone a fundamental transformation from traditional two-dimensional (2D) desktop/web/mobile interfaces to spatial three-dimensional (3D) environments. While existing work has made remarkable success in automated 2D software generation, such as HTML/CSS and mobile app interface code synthesis, the generation of 3D software still remains under-explored. Current methods for 3D software generation usually generate the 3D environments as a whole and cannot modify or control specific elements in the software. Furthermore, these methods struggle to handle the complex spatial and semantic constraints inherent in the real world. To address the challenges, we present Scenethesis, a novel requirement-sensitive 3D software synthesis approach that maintains formal traceability between user specifications and generated 3D software. Scenethesis is built upon ScenethesisLang, a domain-specific language that serves as a granular constraint-aware intermediate representation (IR) to bridge natural language requirements and executable 3D software. It serves both as a comprehensive scene description language enabling fine-grained modification of 3D software elements and as a formal constraint-expressive specification language capable of expressing complex spatial constraints. By decomposing 3D software synthesis into stages operating on ScenethesisLang, Scenethesis enables independent verification, targeted modification, and systematic constraint satisfaction. Our evaluation demonstrates that Scenethesis accurately captures over 80% of user requirements and satisfies more than 90% of hard constraints while handling over 100 constraints simultaneously. Furthermore, Scenethesis achieves a 42.8% improvement in BLIP-2 visual evaluation scores compared to the state-of-the-art method, establishing its effectiveness in generating high-quality 3D software that faithfully adheres to complex user requirements.","az":"图形用户界面（UI）软件已经历从传统二维（2D）桌面/网页/移动界面到空间三维（3D）环境的根本性转变。虽然已有工作在自动化 2D 软件生成（如 HTML/CSS 和移动应用界面代码合成）上取得显著成功，3D 软件的生成仍未被充分探索。当前的 3D 软件生成方法通常将 3D 环境作为整体生成，无法修改或控制软件中的特定元素。此外，这些方法难以处理现实世界中固有的复杂空间与语义约束。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 Scenethesis，一种新颖的需求敏感 3D 软件合成方法，在用户规约与生成的 3D 软件之间保持形式化可追溯性。Scenethesis 构建于 ScenethesisLang 之上——这是一种领域专用语言，作为细粒度、约束感知的中间表示（IR），桥接自然语言需求与可执行的 3D 软件。它既是一种全面的场景描述语言，支持对 3D 软件元素的细粒度修改；也是一种形式化的、具约束表达能力的规约语言，能够表达复杂的空间约束。通过将 3D 软件合成分解为在 ScenethesisLang 上操作的若干阶段，Scenethesis 实现了独立验证、定向修改与系统化的约束满足。我们的评估表明，Scenethesis 准确捕捉了超过 80% 的用户需求，并在同时处理超过 100 条约束的情况下满足了 90% 以上的硬约束。此外，与最先进方法相比，Scenethesis 在 BLIP-2 视觉评测得分上提升 42.8%，确立了其在生成忠实遵循复杂用户需求的高质量 3D 软件方面的有效性。","tl":"用约束表达型 DSL 作中间表示，使 3D 软件可细粒度修改与验证。","au":["Shuqing Li","Anson Y. Lam","Yun Peng","Wenxuan Wang","Michael Lyu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["3D software synthesis","domain-specific language","intermediate representation","spatial constraints","requirement traceability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/284/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.18625"},{"id":"p00771","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"The State of Open Science in Software Engineering Research: A Case Study of ICSE Artifacts","tz":"软件工程研究中开放科学的现状：ICSE 制品的案例研究","a":"Replication packages are crucial for enabling transparency, validation, and reuse in software engineering (SE) research. While artifact sharing is now a standard practice and even expected at premier SE venues such as ICSE, the practical usability of these replication packages remain underexplored. In particular, there is a marked lack of studies that comprehensively examine the executability and reproducibility of replication packages in SE research. In this paper, we aim to fill this gap by evaluating 100 replication packages published in ICSE proceedings over the past decade (2015 - 2024). We assess the (1) executability of the replication packages, (2) efforts and modifications required to execute them, (3) challenges that prevent executability, and (4) reproducibility of the original findings for those that are executable. We spent approximately 650 person-hours in total to execute the artifacts and reproduce the study findings. Our analysis shows that only 40 of the 100 evaluated artifacts were fully executable. Among these, 32.5% ran without any modification. However, even executable artifacts required varying levels of effort: 17.5% required low effort, while 82.5% required moderate to high effort to execute successfully. We identified five common types of modifications and 13 challenges that lead to execution failure, encompassing environmental, documentation, and structural issues. Among the executable artifacts, only 35% (14 out of 40) reproduced the original results. These findings highlight a notable gap between artifact availability, executability, and reproducibility. Our study proposes three actionable guidelines to improve the preparation, documentation, and review of research artifacts, thereby strengthening the rigor and sustainability of open science practices in SE research.","az":"复现包对于实现软件工程（SE）研究的透明性、验证与复用至关重要。尽管制品共享如今已是标准做法，甚至在 ICSE 等顶级 SE 会议上被预期，这些复现包的实际可用性仍未被充分研究。特别是，明显缺乏全面考察 SE 研究复现包可执行性与可复现性的工作。本文旨在填补这一空白，评估过去十年（2015—2024）发表于 ICSE 论文集中的 100 个复现包。我们评估：(1) 复现包的可执行性；(2) 执行它们所需的工作量与修改；(3) 阻碍可执行性的挑战；以及 (4) 对于可执行的那些包，原始发现的可复现性。我们总共花费约 650 人时来执行这些制品并复现研究发现。分析显示，在 100 个被评估的制品中，只有 40 个完全可执行。其中，32.5% 无需任何修改即可运行。然而，即使是可执行的制品也需要不同程度的工作量：17.5% 只需较低工作量，而 82.5% 需要中等至高强度的工作量才能成功执行。我们识别出五类常见修改以及 13 项导致执行失败的挑战，涵盖环境、文档和结构方面的问题。在可执行的制品中，只有 35%（40 个中的 14 个）复现了原始结果。这些发现凸显了制品可获得性、可执行性与可复现性之间的显著鸿沟。我们的研究提出三条可落地的指南，以改进研究制品的准备、文档与评审，从而加强 SE 研究中开放科学实践的严谨性与可持续性。","tl":"花 650 人时实测：ICSE 百个制品仅四成可跑、仅 14 个复现原结果。","au":["Al Muttakin","Saikat Mondal","Chanchal K. Roy"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study"],"kw":["replication package","artifact evaluation","reproducibility","open science","ICSE artifacts"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/285/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.02066"},{"id":"p00772","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FoundRoot: Towards Foundation Model for Root Cause Analysis via Structured Deep Thinking","tz":"FoundRoot：通过结构化深度思考迈向根因分析基础模型","a":"Root Cause Analysis (RCA) for service systems is critical for ensuring their reliability, while its application remains challenging because of the large number of metrics and the complex causal relationships. Classical RCA methods typically rely on statistical or rule-based approaches, making them difficult to generalize to unseen systems. The introduction of Large Language Models (LLMs) has partly addressed these challenges with their understanding of the domain-specific semantics of metrics and reasoning capabilities. However, they still struggle with incomplete or shallow reasoning when facing a large amount of metrics. To address these limitations, we present FoundRoot, a reinforcement learning (RL)-enhanced LLM foundation model for zero-shot RCA. FoundRoot features a novel structured deep thinking paradigm, which breaks down the RCA reasoning into several goal-oriented substeps, enhancing the completeness and reasoning capability of the causal relationship. We collect and curate diverse open-sourced RCA datasets across different systems and introduce a data augmentation technique to ensure data scalability. We design a two-stage training pipeline that includes supervised fine-tuning (SFT) and RL to align the LLM with the structured deep thinking paradigm, which significantly improves its reasoning quality. Extensive experiments on four datasets show that FoundRoot outperforms both classical and LLM-based methods in RCA accuracy on unseen systems, achieving 2.9%-42% mean reciprocal rank (MRR) improvements.","az":"服务系统的根因分析（RCA）对于保障其可靠性至关重要，但由于指标数量庞大且因果关系复杂，其实际应用仍具挑战。经典 RCA 方法通常依赖统计或基于规则的途径，难以泛化到未见过的系统。大语言模型（LLM）的引入凭借其对指标领域语义的理解和推理能力，部分缓解了这些挑战。然而，面对海量指标时，它们仍然存在推理不完整或流于表面的问题。为解决这些局限，我们提出 FoundRoot，一个用于零样本 RCA 的强化学习（RL）增强的 LLM 基础模型。FoundRoot 采用一种新颖的结构化深度思考范式，将 RCA 推理拆解为若干目标导向的子步骤，增强因果关系推理的完整性与能力。我们收集并整理了跨不同系统的多样化开源 RCA 数据集，并引入数据增强技术以确保数据的可扩展性。我们设计了包含有监督微调（SFT）和强化学习的两阶段训练流水线，使 LLM 与结构化深度思考范式对齐，显著提升其推理质量。在四个数据集上的大量实验表明，FoundRoot 在未见系统上的 RCA 准确率优于经典方法和基于 LLM 的方法，平均倒数排名（MRR）提升 2.9%–42%。","tl":"用结构化深度思考范式加 SFT+RL 训练出零样本根因分析基础模型。","au":["Zhe Xie","Zeyan Li","Xiao He","Shenglin Zhang","Longlong Xu","Yuzhuo Yang","Tieying Zhang","Jianjun Chen","Rui Shi","Dan Pei"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["root cause analysis","foundation model","reinforcement learning","structured reasoning","service systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/286/x"},{"id":"p00773","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automating Requirements Formalization: Using LLMs and Low-Complexity Distinguishing Traces for Semantic Validation","tz":"自动化需求形式化：用 LLM 与低复杂度区分痕迹进行语义验证","a":"Translating natural language (NL) requirements into formal specifications is critical for verifying safety-critical systems, but it is error-prone and time-consuming when done manually. While Large Language Models (LLMs) can automate this translation, they often produce incorrect outputs that require extensive validation. In this paper, we propose ARTEMIS, an LLM-based framework that translates unstructured NL requirements into formal temporal logic (TL) specifications. Our framework reduces validation effort through three synergistic, automated techniques: (i) LLM Translation to Structured NL: We use LLMs to translate unstructured NL requirements into structured NL, which has an unambiguous mapping to LTL. This intermediate representation reduces translation errors. (ii) Sub-Specification Generation: We generate low-complexity execution traces (i.e., system behaviors) that correspond to candidate specification fragments from the LLM translations. Users inspect these and accept or reject them. (iii) Balanced Distinguishing Trace Generation: We minimize the number of traces users need to inspect by pruning the candidate specification space. Each accepted or rejected trace eliminates candidates logarithmically. We evaluate ARTEMIS on five real-world safety-critical requirements datasets. The results show that it achieves 1.57X higher translation accuracy while reducing manual validation effort by up to 10.83X compared to state-of-the-art baselines.","az":"将自然语言（NL）需求翻译为形式化规约对于验证安全攸关系统至关重要，但人工完成时既易出错又耗时。虽然大语言模型（LLM）可以自动化这一翻译过程，但它们常常产生不正确的输出，需要大量验证。本文提出 ARTEMIS，一个基于 LLM 的框架，可将非结构化的自然语言需求翻译为形式化时序逻辑（TL）规约。我们的框架通过三项协同的自动化技术减少验证工作量：(i) LLM 翻译为结构化自然语言：我们使用 LLM 将非结构化 NL 需求翻译为结构化 NL，后者与 LTL 存在无歧义的映射，这一中间表示减少了翻译错误。(ii) 子规约生成：我们生成与 LLM 翻译得到的候选规约片段相对应的低复杂度执行痕迹（即系统行为），由用户检查并接受或拒绝。(iii) 平衡的区分性痕迹生成：我们通过裁剪候选规约空间，最小化用户需要检查的痕迹数量；每接受或拒绝一条痕迹，都会以对数级速度排除候选。我们在五个真实世界的安全攸关需求数据集上评估 ARTEMIS。结果表明，与最先进基线相比，它的翻译准确率提升 1.57 倍，同时将人工验证工作量最多减少 10.83 倍。","tl":"用结构化 NL 中间表示加区分性痕迹把人工验证成本降到十分之一。","au":["Daniel Mendoza","Anastasia Mavridou","Andreas Katis","Caroline Trippel"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["requirements formalization","temporal logic","LTL","distinguishing traces","semantic validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/287/x"},{"id":"p00774","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MutDafny: A Mutation-Based Approach to Assess Dafny Specifications","tz":"MutDafny：一种基于变异的 Dafny 规约评估方法","a":"This paper explores the use of mutation testing to reveal weaknesses in formal specifications written in Dafny. In verification-aware programming languages, such as Dafny, despite their critical role, specifications are as prone to errors as implementations. Flaws in specs can result in formally verified programs that deviate from the intended behavior. We present MutDafny, a tool that increases the reliability of Dafny specifications by automatically signaling potential weaknesses. Using a mutation testing approach, we introduce faults (mutations) into the code and rely on formal specifications for detecting them. If a program with a mutant verifies, this may indicate a weakness in the specification. We extensively analyze mutation operators from popular tools, identifying the ones applicable to Dafny. In addition, we synthesize new operators tailored for Dafny from bugfix commits in publicly available Dafny projects on GitHub. Drawing from both, we equipped our tool with a total of 32 mutation operators. We evaluate MutDafny’s effectiveness and efficiency in a dataset of 794 real-world Dafny programs and we manually analyze a subset of the resulting undetected mutants, identifying five weak real-world specifications (on average, one at every 241 lines of code) that would benefit from strengthening.","az":"本文探索使用变异测试来揭示用 Dafny 编写的形式化规约中的薄弱之处。在 Dafny 这类面向验证的编程语言中，规约尽管扮演关键角色，却和实现一样容易出错。规约中的缺陷会导致经过形式化验证的程序仍偏离预期行为。我们提出 MutDafny，一个通过自动标示潜在薄弱点来提升 Dafny 规约可靠性的工具。采用变异测试的思路，我们向代码中引入故障（变异），并依赖形式化规约来检测它们。如果含有变异体的程序仍能通过验证，这可能表明规约存在薄弱之处。我们广泛分析了主流工具中的变异算子，识别出适用于 Dafny 的那些算子。此外，我们从 GitHub 上公开可得的 Dafny 项目的缺陷修复提交中，综合出为 Dafny 量身定制的新算子。基于这两者，我们为工具配备了总计 32 个变异算子。我们在包含 794 个真实世界 Dafny 程序的数据集上评估 MutDafny 的有效性与效率，并人工分析了由此产生的未被检测出的变异体的一个子集，识别出五个薄弱的真实规约（平均每 241 行代码一个），它们需要被加强。","tl":"首次把变异测试用于评估 Dafny 形式化规约的强度，含 32 个算子。","au":["Isabel Amaral","Alexandra Mendes","José Campos"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mutation testing","Dafny","formal specifications","mutation operators","verification-aware language"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/288/x"},{"id":"p00775","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TARIPlay: A Test Framework for AR Applications based on Interactive Area Detection in Playback Videos","tz":"TARIPlay：基于回放视频交互区域检测的 AR 应用测试框架","a":"As Augmented Reality (AR) becomes more and more embedded in daily life, ensuring the quality, safety, and reliability of AR applications is increasingly important. However, AR apps present unique challenges for automated testing. Unlike static GUI layouts in traditional mobile apps, AR apps acquire their interaction interface from the surrounding environment, which is volatile and non-deterministic. Recent advancements like ARCore Playback and ARKit Replay allow developers to reuse real-world scenarios by recording and playing back enriched videos, enabling more feasible automated AR testing. However, using playback videos introduces two major challenges: test inputs must be timed precisely, and interactive areas in the video are dynamic, irregular, and difficult to identify. To address these challenges, we propose TARIPlay, a framework that analyzes playback videos to detect, track, and filter proper interactive areas over time for automated testing. In particular, TARIPlay identifies viable test opportunities based on criteria like stability and visibility, then feeds this information to an automated testing engine to simulate user interactions. We perform an experiment with four open-source AR apps and nine playback videos. Evaluation results show that TARIPlay significantly outperforms the existing tool Monkey in test coverage (55.8% over 41.98% on branch coverage) of AR-related code, and can also be used to assess the quality of playback videos for testing suitability.","az":"随着增强现实（AR）越来越深入地嵌入日常生活，确保 AR 应用的质量、安全性与可靠性愈发重要。然而，AR 应用给自动化测试带来了独特挑战。与传统移动应用中静态的 GUI 布局不同，AR 应用从周围环境中获取其交互界面，而环境是易变且非确定的。诸如 ARCore Playback 和 ARKit Replay 等最新进展允许开发者通过录制和回放富化视频来复用真实世界场景，使更可行的自动化 AR 测试成为可能。然而，使用回放视频带来了两大挑战：测试输入必须被精确计时；视频中的交互区域是动态、不规则且难以识别的。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 TARIPlay，一个分析回放视频以随时间检测、跟踪并筛选合适交互区域用于自动化测试的框架。具体而言，TARIPlay 基于稳定性和可见性等标准识别可行的测试时机，然后将这些信息送入自动化测试引擎以模拟用户交互。我们在四个开源 AR 应用和九段回放视频上开展实验。评测结果表明，TARIPlay 在 AR 相关代码的测试覆盖率上显著优于现有工具 Monkey（分支覆盖率 55.8% 对 41.98%），并且还可用于评估回放视频是否适合用于测试。","tl":"从 AR 回放视频中检测动态交互区域与时机来驱动自动化测试。","au":["Seyed Amir Mousavi","Xiaoyin Wang"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["AR application testing","playback video","interactive area detection","ARCore Playback","test coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/289/x"},{"id":"p00776","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Attention Distance: A Novel Metric for Directed Fuzzing with Large Language Models","tz":"注意力距离：一种用于大语言模型驱动定向模糊测试的新度量","a":"In the domain of software security testing, Directed Grey-Box Fuzzing (DGF) has garnered widespread attention for its efficient target localization and excellent detection performance. However, existing approaches measure only the physical distance between seed execution paths and target locations, overlooking logical relationships among code segments. This omission can yield redundant or misleading guidance in complex binaries, weakening DGF’s real-world effectiveness. To address this, we introduce attention distance, a novel metric that leverages a large language model’s contextual analysis to compute attention scores between code elements and reveal their intrinsic connections. Under the same AFLGo configuration—without altering any fuzzing components other than the distance metric—replacing physical distances with attention distances across 38 real vulnerability reproduction experiments delivers a 3.43× average increase in testing efficiency over the traditional method. Compared to state-of-the-art directed fuzzers DAFL and WindRanger, our approach achieves 2.89× and 7.13× improvements, respectively. To further validate the generalizability of attention distance, we integrate it into DAFL and WindRanger, where it also consistently enhances their original performance. All related code and datasets are publicly available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/Attention_Distance-4650 .","az":"在软件安全测试领域，定向灰盒模糊测试（DGF）因其高效的目标定位能力和出色的检测性能而受到广泛关注。然而，现有方法仅度量种子执行路径与目标位置之间的物理距离，忽视了代码片段之间的逻辑关系。这一缺失会在复杂二进制程序中产生冗余或具有误导性的引导，削弱 DGF 在真实场景中的有效性。为此，我们提出了**注意力距离（attention distance）**——一种利用大语言模型的上下文分析能力来计算代码元素之间注意力分数、从而揭示其内在关联的新度量。在相同的 AFLGo 配置下——除距离度量外不改动任何模糊测试组件——在 38 个真实漏洞复现实验中，用注意力距离替换物理距离带来了平均 **3.43×** 的测试效率提升。与最先进的定向模糊测试工具 DAFL 和 WindRanger 相比，我们的方法分别取得了 **2.89×** 和 **7.13×** 的提升。为进一步验证注意力距离的通用性，我们将其集成到 DAFL 与 WindRanger 中，同样持续提升了它们的原有性能。全部相关代码与数据集已公开于 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/Attention_Distance-4650 。","tl":"用 LLM 注意力分数取代物理距离来引导定向模糊测试。","au":["Bin Wang","Ao Yang","Kedan Li","Aofan Liu","Hui Li","Guibo Luo","Weixiang Huang","Yan Zhuang"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["directed greybox fuzzing","attention distance","AFLGo","LLM code analysis","vulnerability reproduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/290/x"},{"id":"p00777","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Accelerating IC3 Verification by Exploiting Unsatisfiable Cores and Satisfying Models","tz":"利用不可满足核与可满足模型加速 IC3 验证","a":"The IC3 algorithm represents a groundbreaking advancement in the field of model checking. However, its heavy reliance on numerous and frequent constraint-solving calls poses significant challenges when verifying complex programs. We observe that many of the constraints solved within IC3 share remarkable similarities. Based on this observation, we propose an IC3 acceleration verification method by reusing unsatisfiable cores and satisfying models of previous constraints. This method constructs an Unsatisfiable Core Library (UCL) and a Satisfying Model Library (SML) to store and index crucial unsatisfiable cores and satisfying models generated during the verification process. When a new constraint-solving request is received, our method preemptively determines the satisfiability of the constraint using the existing unsatisfiable cores and satisfying models. This approach can significantly reduce the number of required solver calls, thereby enhancing the verification efficiency. We have implemented our method on Kind2 and evaluated it on the standard benchmark suite of Kind2. Experimental evaluation demonstrates that, for those complex examples, our method can reduce the number of solver calls by an order of magnitude, and achieves a 4.35-fold speedup with even less memory consumption.","az":"IC3 算法是模型检验领域的一项突破性进展。然而，它对大量且频繁的约束求解调用的严重依赖，在验证复杂程序时带来了显著挑战。我们观察到，IC3 内部求解的许多约束之间存在高度相似性。基于这一观察，我们提出了一种通过复用先前约束的不可满足核（unsatisfiable core）与可满足模型（satisfying model）来加速 IC3 验证的方法。该方法构建了不可满足核库（UCL）与可满足模型库（SML），用于存储并索引验证过程中产生的关键不可满足核与可满足模型。当收到新的约束求解请求时，我们的方法会先利用已有的不可满足核与可满足模型预先判定该约束的可满足性。这一做法能显著减少所需的求解器调用次数，从而提升验证效率。我们在 Kind2 上实现了该方法，并在 Kind2 的标准基准套件上进行了评估。实验结果表明，对于那些复杂样例，我们的方法可将求解器调用次数减少一个数量级，并在内存消耗更低的情况下取得 4.35 倍加速。","tl":"复用不可满足核与可满足模型，减少 IC3 的求解器调用。","au":["Xinyi Gong","Liangze Yin","Yuhan Li","Ke Kang","Wei Dong","Shanshan Li","Ji Wang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["IC3","model checking","unsatisfiable core","SMT solving","Kind2"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/291/x","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00778","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Beyond Correctness: Exposing LLM-generated Logical Flaws in Reasoning via Multi-step Automated Theorem Proving","tz":"超越正确性：通过多步自动定理证明揭示 LLM 生成推理中的逻辑缺陷","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated impressive reasoning capabilities, leading to their adoption in high-stakes domains such as healthcare, law, and scientific research. However, their reasoning often contains subtle logical errors masked by fluent language, posing significant risks for critical applications. While existing approaches like fact-checking, self-consistency methods, and rule-based validation provide partial solutions, they fail to detect complex logical flaws in multi-step reasoning. To overcome these challenges, we present MATP, an evaluation framework for systematically verifying LLM reasoning via Multi-step Automatic Theorem Proving. MATP translates natural language reasoning into First-Order Logic (FOL) and applies automated theorem provers to assess step-by-step logical validity. This approach identifies hidden logical errors and provides fine-grained classifications of reasoning correctness. Evaluations on a benchmark comprising 10,830 reasoning instances generated by 10 LLMs across tasks from PrOntoQA-OOD, ProofWriter, and FOLIO show that MATP surpasses prompting-based baselines by over 42 percentage points in reasoning step verification. It further reveals model-level disparities, with reasoning models generating more logically coherent outputs than general models. These results demonstrate MATP’s potential to enhance the trustworthiness of LLM-generated reasoning.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已展现出令人印象深刻的推理能力，因而被用于医疗、法律和科学研究等高风险领域。然而，它们的推理常常包含被流畅语言所掩盖的细微逻辑错误，给关键应用带来重大风险。尽管事实核查、自一致性方法和基于规则的校验等现有手段提供了部分解决方案，但它们无法检测多步推理中的复杂逻辑缺陷。为克服这些挑战，我们提出了 MATP——一个通过多步自动定理证明（Multi-step Automatic Theorem Proving）系统性验证 LLM 推理的评测框架。MATP 将自然语言推理翻译为一阶逻辑（FOL），并调用自动定理证明器逐步评估逻辑有效性。该方法能够识别隐藏的逻辑错误，并对推理正确性给出细粒度分类。在一个由 10 个 LLM 在 PrOntoQA-OOD、ProofWriter 和 FOLIO 任务上生成的、包含 10,830 条推理实例的基准上进行评估，结果表明 MATP 在推理步骤验证上比基于提示的基线高出 42 个百分点以上。它还揭示了模型层面的差异：推理型模型生成的输出比通用模型在逻辑上更连贯。这些结果表明 MATP 有潜力提升 LLM 生成推理的可信度。","tl":"把 LLM 推理转成一阶逻辑，用定理证明器逐步验证。","au":["Xinyi Zheng","Ningke Li","Xiaokun Luan","Kailong Wang","Ling Shi","Meng Sun","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","cross-track-bridge"],"kw":["automated theorem proving","first-order logic","LLM reasoning verification","logical flaws","evaluation framework"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/292/x"},{"id":"p00779","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ADARULE: LLM-Driven Natural Language to LTL Conversion via Pattern-Adaptive Rule Induction","tz":"ADARULE：通过模式自适应规则归纳实现 LLM 驱动的自然语言到 LTL 转换","a":"Translating natural language (NL) specifications into Linear Temporal Logic (LTL) formulas is critical for bridging human intent and formal system verification. While large language models (LLMs) have made this task more feasible, adapting NL2LTL systems to different domains remains challenging due to varied linguistic conventions. Existing methods typically rely on manually crafted translation rules or pattern-specific templates, which are costly to construct and do not generalize across domains. A core challenge is that NL–LTL datasets provide paired examples but do not explicitly indicate which linguistic elements reflect pattern-specific translation conventions. To address this problem, we propose ADARULE, a feedback-guided approach for pattern-adaptive NL2LTL translation via automatic rule induction. The key insight is that even without explicit supervision, we can leverage LLMs to perform NL2LTL translation using only basic, general-purpose rules. By comparing the predicted LTL with ground truth LTL formulas, the LLM can identify where the general rules fall short and uses this feedback to induce new translation rules that capture pattern-specific conventions. ADARULE consists of two collaborative LLM-based components: a Translator that performs the NL2LTL conversion, and a Learner that analyzes failed translations to generate corrective rules. These rules are incorporated into the Translator’s prompts to improve future predictions. Through iterative learning, ADARULE progressively adapts to pattern-specific conventions without requiring manual engineering. Experiments on four benchmark NL2LTL datasets and three different foundation LLMs show that ADARULE outperforms the other baselines by at least 21.1% on average, demonstrating the effectiveness of automatic rule induction. Our code is available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/ADARULE-BBDB .","az":"将自然语言（NL）规约翻译为线性时序逻辑（LTL）公式，对于连接人类意图与形式化系统验证至关重要。尽管大语言模型（LLM）让这一任务变得更可行，但由于语言表达习惯多样，将 NL2LTL 系统适配到不同领域仍然充满挑战。现有方法通常依赖人工编写的翻译规则或特定模式的模板，构造成本高且难以跨领域泛化。一个核心挑战在于：NL–LTL 数据集只提供了配对样例，却没有显式指出哪些语言要素体现了特定模式的翻译惯例。为解决该问题，我们提出 ADARULE，一种基于反馈引导、通过自动规则归纳实现模式自适应 NL2LTL 翻译的方法。其关键洞见是：即便没有显式监督，我们也可以让 LLM 仅使用基础的通用规则来完成 NL2LTL 翻译；通过将预测的 LTL 与真值 LTL 公式进行比较，LLM 能够识别通用规则在何处失效，并利用该反馈归纳出捕捉特定模式惯例的新翻译规则。ADARULE 由两个协作的基于 LLM 的组件构成：执行 NL2LTL 转换的翻译器（Translator），以及分析失败翻译并生成纠正规则的学习器（Learner）。这些规则被加入翻译器的提示中以改进后续预测。通过迭代学习，ADARULE 无需人工工程即可逐步适应特定模式的惯例。在四个 NL2LTL 基准数据集与三个不同基础 LLM 上的实验表明，ADARULE 平均至少比其他基线高出 21.1%，验证了自动规则归纳的有效性。代码见 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/ADARULE-BBDB 。","tl":"用翻译-学习双智能体自动归纳 NL2LTL 的领域翻译规则。","au":["Jiayi Hu","Jingling Sun","Chong Wang","Yihao Huang","jincaofeng","Yilongfei Xu","Yong Li","Kailong Wang","Weikai Miao","Jin Song Dong","Geguang Pu"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["NL-to-LTL","rule induction","temporal logic specification","LLM prompting","formal verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/293/x"},{"id":"p00780","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Improving Code Generation via Small Language Model-as-a-judge","tz":"用小语言模型作为评判者改进代码生成","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have shown remarkable capabilities in automated code generation, powering tools such as GitHub Copilot and ChatGPT. While effective for mainstream languages, they may underperform on less common or domain-specific languages, prompting companies to develop in-house code generators to support their developers in coding activities. While open-source models can be trained for this, only LLMs with tens of billions of parameters match the performance of commercial tools, demanding costly training and deployment that many small and medium enterprises cannot afford. Recent work proposed supporting code generation with smaller models (SLMs) by generating multiple candidate solutions and using another SLM to select the most likely correct one. The most recent work in this area is the one by Sun et al. presenting RankEF, a T5 model trained to rank code solutions using both execution-based and non-execution-based information. However, Sun et al. do not assess the T5 ranker’s classification accuracy, that is, how often it misjudges correct implementations as incorrect or vice versa, leaving open questions about the reliability of LMs as code correctness judges for other tasks ( automated code review). Moreover, their experiments involve relatively old models, making it unclear the extent to which such a methodology would still help companies in cheaply training their own code generators with performance comparable to those of massive LLMs (both open and commercial models). We present an empirical study addressing these limitations. We train several state-of-the-art SLMs as code correctness judges and assess their ability to discriminate between correct and wrong implementations, independently from their application to code generation. We show that modern SLMs outperform RankEF, even without exploiting execution-based information. When used as code rankers, they achieve higher performance gains than RankEF and perform competitively with LLMs 5–25x larger, at a fraction of the cost.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在自动代码生成上展现出卓越能力，支撑了 GitHub Copilot 和 ChatGPT 等工具。虽然它们在主流语言上效果良好，但在较冷门或领域特定的语言上可能表现不佳，这促使企业自研内部代码生成器来支持开发者的编码活动。尽管可以训练开源模型来实现这一点，但只有数百亿参数规模的 LLM 才能匹配商用工具的性能，其训练与部署成本高昂，许多中小企业难以承受。近期工作提出用较小的模型（SLM）来支持代码生成：生成多个候选解，再用另一个 SLM 选出最可能正确的那个。该方向最新的工作是 Sun 等人提出的 RankEF——一个同时利用基于执行与非执行信息来对代码解排序的 T5 模型。然而，Sun 等人并未评估该 T5 排序器的分类准确率，即它多久会把正确实现误判为错误、或反之，这使得语言模型作为代码正确性评判者在其他任务（例如自动代码审查）中的可靠性仍是未知数。此外，他们的实验使用的模型相对陈旧，因此该方法论在多大程度上仍能帮助企业低成本训练出性能可比于大规模 LLM（开源与商用）的代码生成器并不清楚。我们开展了一项实证研究以弥补这些不足。我们训练了若干最先进的 SLM 作为代码正确性评判者，并独立于其在代码生成中的应用，评估它们区分正确与错误实现的能力。结果显示，现代 SLM 即便不利用基于执行的信息也优于 RankEF；当用作代码排序器时，它们取得的性能增益高于 RankEF，并以极低的成本与规模大 5–25 倍的 LLM 表现相当。","tl":"现代小模型当代码正确性评判者已胜过 RankEF 且成本极低。","au":["Giuseppe Crupi","Rosalia Tufano","Gabriele Bavota"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["small language models","code correctness judge","candidate reranking","RankEF","code generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/294/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.11911"},{"id":"p00781","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Can SAT Solvers Keep Up With the Linux Kernel's Feature Model?","tz":"SAT 求解器还跟得上 Linux 内核的特征模型吗？","a":"The Linux kernel is a highly relevant, yet also highly configurable software system. Kernel developers keep track of this configurability in a feature model, which defines the features of Linux and their dependencies. To support kernel developers in various activities, many (semi-)automated product-line analyses have been proposed over the years. Under the hood, these analyses can often be computed with SAT solvers. Yet, the Linux kernel has constantly been growing in complexity for decades, which increasingly hampers its efficient analysis. At the same time, SAT solvers have been improving in performance for decades, which eases analysis. In this paper, we investigate empirically whether SAT solvers can keep up with the Linux kernel’s feature model. To this end, we analyze historic feature models of Linux with historic SAT solvers from several sources. We find that SAT solvers are generally not able to keep up with Linux. Even the optimal SAT solver is slowing down by 10% every year, meaning that its performance halves every seven years. We conclude that the Linux kernel will become increasingly difficult to analyze if its growth is not counteracted.","az":"Linux 内核是一个极具现实意义、同时也高度可配置的软件系统。内核开发者用特征模型（feature model）来记录这种可配置性，该模型定义了 Linux 的特征及其依赖关系。为支持内核开发者的各类活动，多年来人们提出了许多（半）自动化的产品线分析方法。在底层，这些分析通常可用 SAT 求解器来计算。然而，Linux 内核的复杂度数十年来持续增长，这日益阻碍了对它的高效分析；与此同时，SAT 求解器的性能也在数十年间不断提升，这又让分析变得更容易。本文实证研究 SAT 求解器是否跟得上 Linux 内核的特征模型。为此，我们用来自多个来源的历史 SAT 求解器分析 Linux 的历史特征模型。我们发现 SAT 求解器总体上跟不上 Linux：即便是最优的 SAT 求解器，每年也会变慢 10%，意味着其性能每七年减半。我们得出结论：如果 Linux 内核的增长得不到遏制，它将变得越来越难以分析。","tl":"实证显示 SAT 求解器进步追不上 Linux 特征模型的膨胀。","au":["Elias Kuiter","Urs-Benedict Braun","Thomas Thüm","Sebastian Krieter","Gunter Saake"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["Linux feature model","SAT solver","product-line analysis","configurability","historical benchmark"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/295/x","pu":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SoftVarE-Group/Papers/main/2026/2026-ICSE-Kuiter.pdf","aw":"Distinguished Paper Award"},{"id":"p00782","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Characterizing GPU-accelerated Web Applications in Browsers","tz":"浏览器中 GPU 加速 Web 应用的特征刻画","a":"Driven by the rapid advancement of Web immersive experiences, the demand for GPU acceleration in Web applications has become an essential component of the Web ecosystem. However, little is known about the current practices of GPU-accelerated Web applications. To bridge the knowledge gap, we conduct the first comprehensive empirical study of real-world Web applications that leverage the Web Graphics Library (WebGL) for GPU acceleration, i.e., WebGL applications. We construct a dataset consisting of 5,954 real-world WebGL applications and develop a measurement tool to evaluate how these applications perform across various devices, operating systems, and browsers. Our findings reveal the performance defects in these applications, along with the root causes stemming from undesired development practices. Based on the findings, we propose actionable strategies for developers and browser vendors to mitigate the performance defects.","az":"在 Web 沉浸式体验快速发展的推动下，Web 应用对 GPU 加速的需求已成为 Web 生态不可或缺的组成部分。然而，人们对 GPU 加速 Web 应用的现状实践知之甚少。为弥补这一认知空白，我们对利用 Web 图形库（WebGL）进行 GPU 加速的真实 Web 应用（即 WebGL 应用）开展了首个全面的实证研究。我们构建了一个包含 5,954 个真实 WebGL 应用的数据集，并开发了一套测量工具，评估这些应用在不同设备、操作系统与浏览器上的表现。我们的发现揭示了这些应用中的性能缺陷，以及源自不良开发实践的根本原因。基于这些发现，我们为开发者和浏览器厂商提出了可操作的策略以缓解这些性能缺陷。","tl":"首次大规模刻画 WebGL 应用的性能缺陷与其成因。","au":["Yudong Han","Weichen Bi","Haiyang Shen","Mugeng Liu","Ruibo Wang","Yun Ma"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["WebGL","GPU-accelerated web apps","performance defects","browser measurement","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/296/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3744916.3787824"},{"id":"p00783","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SymRadar: PoC-Centered Bounded Verification for Vulnerability Repair","tz":"SymRadar：以 PoC 为中心的有界验证用于漏洞修复","a":"In this paper, we tackle the problem of patch verification. While automated vulnerability repair (AVR) techniques are gaining traction, it is not sufficient to merely generate patches; providing evidence of their correctness is also essential. However, the current state-of-the-art patch verification methods are not sufficiently effective. To address this issue, we propose SymRadar, a patch verification tool that performs under-constrained symbolic execution (UC-SE) on the patched function. Unlike standard UC-SE, SymRadar conducts UC-SE in the vicinity of the crash-inducing input. We demonstrate that SymRadar is more effective than existing patch verification methods. Another challenge in verifying patches generated by AVR tools is the large number of patches generated. To address this, we propose a novel optimization technique that allows SymRadar to handle multiple patches efficiently. Our experimental evaluation demonstrates that SymRadar is both effective and efficient in verifying patches generated by AVR tools.","az":"本文研究补丁验证问题。尽管自动漏洞修复（AVR）技术日益受到关注，但仅仅生成补丁是不够的，还必须提供其正确性的证据。然而，当前最先进的补丁验证方法效果并不理想。为解决这一问题，我们提出 SymRadar——一个在打过补丁的函数上执行欠约束符号执行（UC-SE）的补丁验证工具。与标准 UC-SE 不同，SymRadar 在触发崩溃的输入附近开展 UC-SE。我们证明 SymRadar 比现有补丁验证方法更有效。验证 AVR 工具生成的补丁的另一个挑战是补丁数量庞大。为此，我们提出一种新的优化技术，使 SymRadar 能高效处理多个补丁。实验评估表明，SymRadar 在验证 AVR 工具生成的补丁方面既有效又高效。","tl":"在崩溃输入邻域做欠约束符号执行来验证漏洞补丁。","au":["Seungheon Han","YoungJae Kim","Yeseung Lee","Jooyong Yi"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["patch verification","under-constrained symbolic execution","automated vulnerability repair","proof-of-concept","bounded verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/297/x"},{"id":"p00784","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CRUDinfer: Automated CRUD Semantics Inference for REST APIs Through Black-box Testing","tz":"CRUDinfer：通过黑盒测试自动推断 REST API 的 CRUD 语义","a":"REST APIs are the de facto standard for web service interaction, praised for flexibility and simplicity of adoption. Nevertheless, the lack of mandatory implementation guidelines for REST APIs has led to the diffusion of poor-quality and difficult-to-maintain web services. A key concern in this context is the misuse of CRUD (Create, Read, Update, and Delete) semantics of API operations. While best practices suggest mapping CRUD verbs to HTTP methods ( POST , GET , PUT/PATCH , and DELETE , respectively), many implementations fail to adhere to such a guideline. This common anti-pattern makes interaction with the API ambiguous, hindering maintainability and decreasing the effectiveness of automated REST API testing. In this paper, we propose CRUDinfer , a novel approach to automatically infer REST API operation CRUD semantics by leveraging (black-box) interactions with the API. The approach incrementally refines the knowledge about API operations’ CRUD semantics via CRUD test scenarios . Specifically, it employs interaction patterns typical of each CRUD semantics verb to craft test scenarios (i.e., HTTP interactions) for API operations with the aim of confirming their semantics. Testing failures indicate a mismatch between the intended CRUD semantics and the actual implementation. Thus, it refines API operations’ CRUD semantics knowledge through improved test scenarios. Empirical evaluation indicates high inference capabilities for , with an overall precision higher than 95% on the considered benchmark REST APIs.","az":"REST API 已是 Web 服务交互的事实标准，以灵活性和易于采用著称。然而，REST API 缺乏强制性的实现规范，导致大量质量不佳、难以维护的 Web 服务扩散开来。其中一个关键问题是 API 操作对 CRUD（创建、读取、更新、删除）语义的误用。尽管最佳实践建议将 CRUD 动词分别映射到 HTTP 方法（POST、GET、PUT/PATCH、DELETE），许多实现并未遵循该准则。这一常见反模式使得与 API 的交互变得含糊，损害可维护性并降低自动化 REST API 测试的有效性。本文提出 CRUDinfer，一种通过（黑盒）与 API 交互来自动推断 REST API 操作 CRUD 语义的新方法。该方法通过 CRUD 测试场景逐步细化对 API 操作 CRUD 语义的认识：具体而言，它利用各 CRUD 语义动词典型的交互模式，为 API 操作构造测试场景（即 HTTP 交互），以确认其语义。测试失败表明预期 CRUD 语义与实际实现之间存在不一致，于是它通过改进后的测试场景继续细化对 API 操作 CRUD 语义的认识。实证评估表明该工具具有很强的推断能力，在所考察的基准 REST API 上总体精确率高于 95%。","tl":"用黑盒 HTTP 交互场景迭代推断 REST 操作的真实 CRUD 语义。","au":["Michele Pasqua","Davide Corradini","Michele Perlotto","Mariano Ceccato"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["REST API","CRUD semantics inference","black-box testing","API anti-pattern","test scenarios"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/298/x"},{"id":"p00785","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Validating Mixed-Integer Programming Solvers","tz":"验证混合整数规划求解器的正确性","a":"Mixed-integer programming (MIP) is a fundamental class of mathematical optimization problems with broad applications in various domains such as finance, engineering, and management science. MIP solvers, software systems that automatically solve MIP problems, serve as the computational backbone for these applications. Given their widespread use, ensuring the correctness of MIP solvers is crucial, as incorrect results—such as falsely determining feasibility or returning incorrect solutions—can lead to serious real-world consequences. Despite its importance, validating the correctness of MIP solvers remains largely unexplored in both theory and practice. This paper presents the first systematic effort to address this problem. We propose feasibility-driven instance generation, a novel and effective technique for generating MIP instances to validate solver behaviors. The core idea is to systematically construct diverse MIP instances that are provably feasible or infeasible by construction. These instances are then used to test MIP solvers for finding correctness bugs. We realize this methodology in Flip. To date, Flip has uncovered 52 confirmed bugs in five widely used MIP solvers, spanning both open-source and commercial systems. Among these, 39 have been promptly fixed by the developers. Our efforts and findings have been well acknowledged and appreciated by the MIP solver community.","az":"混合整数规划（MIP）是一类基础的数学优化问题，在金融、工程与管理科学等众多领域有广泛应用。MIP 求解器作为自动求解 MIP 问题的软件系统，是这些应用的计算基石。鉴于其广泛使用，确保 MIP 求解器的正确性至关重要：诸如错误判定可行性或返回错误解之类的结果，可能带来严重的现实后果。尽管重要，验证 MIP 求解器正确性在理论与实践中都基本未被探索。本文提出首个系统性解决该问题的工作。我们提出可行性驱动的实例生成（feasibility-driven instance generation）——一种新颖且有效的 MIP 实例生成技术，用于验证求解器行为。其核心思想是系统性地构造在构造上即可证明可行或不可行的多样化 MIP 实例，然后用这些实例测试 MIP 求解器以发现正确性缺陷。我们在 Flip 中实现了该方法。迄今为止，Flip 已在五个广泛使用的 MIP 求解器（涵盖开源与商用系统）中发现 52 个已确认缺陷，其中 39 个已被开发者迅速修复。我们的工作与发现得到了 MIP 求解器社区的认可与赞赏。","tl":"构造可证可行/不可行实例来测 MIP 求解器，找出 52 个缺陷。","au":["Xintong Zhou","Zhenyang Xu","Chengnian Sun"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["MIP solver testing","feasibility-driven instance generation","solver correctness bugs","Flip","differential validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/299/x"},{"id":"p00786","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DyMA-Fuzz: Dynamic Direct Memory Access Abstraction for Re-hosted Monolithic Firmware Fuzzing","tz":"DyMA-Fuzz：面向重宿主单体固件模糊测试的动态 DMA 抽象","a":"The rise of smart devices in critical domains—including automotive, medical, industrial—demands robust firmware testing. Fuzzing firmware in re-hosted environments is a promising method for automated testing at scale, but remains difficult due to the tight coupling of code with a microcontroller’s peripherals. Existing fuzzing frameworks primarily address input challenges in providing inputs for Memory-Mapped I/O or interrupts, but largely overlook Direct Memory Access (DMA), a key high-throughput interface used that bypasses the CPU. We introduce DyMA-Fuzz to extend recent advances in stream-based fuzz input injection to DMA-driven interfaces in re-hosted environments. It tackles key challenges—vendor-specific descriptors, heterogeneous DMA designs, and varying descriptor locations—using runtime analysis techniques to infer DMA memory access patterns and automatically inject fuzzing data into target buffers, without manual configuration or datasheets. Evaluated on 94 firmware samples and 8 DMA-guarded CVE benchmarks, DyMA-Fuzz reveals vulnerabilities and execution paths missed by state-of-the-art tools and achieves up to 122% higher code coverage. These results highlight DyMA-Fuzz as a practical and effective advancement in automated firmware testing and a scalable solution for fuzzing complex embedded systems.","az":"智能设备在汽车、医疗、工业等关键领域的兴起，对稳健的固件测试提出了要求。在重宿主（re-hosted）环境中对固件进行模糊测试是实现大规模自动化测试的有前景方法，但由于代码与微控制器外设的紧耦合，这仍然困难重重。现有模糊测试框架主要解决为内存映射 I/O 或中断提供输入的难题，却在很大程度上忽视了直接内存访问（DMA）——一种绕过 CPU 的关键高吞吐接口。我们提出 DyMA-Fuzz，将近期基于流的模糊输入注入技术扩展到重宿主环境中的 DMA 驱动接口。它利用运行时分析技术推断 DMA 内存访问模式，并自动将模糊测试数据注入目标缓冲区，无需人工配置或数据手册，从而应对厂商专有描述符、异构 DMA 设计以及描述符位置不定等关键挑战。在 94 个固件样本和 8 个受 DMA 保护的 CVE 基准上评估，DyMA-Fuzz 发现了最先进工具遗漏的漏洞与执行路径，并取得高达 122% 的代码覆盖率提升。这些结果表明 DyMA-Fuzz 是自动化固件测试的一项实用而有效的进展，也是模糊测试复杂嵌入式系统的可扩展方案。","tl":"首次把模糊输入注入扩展到重宿主固件的 DMA 接口。","au":["Guy Farrelly","Michael Chesser","Seyit Camtepe","Damith C. Ranasinghe"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["firmware fuzzing","re-hosting","direct memory access","embedded systems","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/300/x"},{"id":"p00787","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Misbehavior Forecasting for Focused Autonomous Driving Systems Testing","tz":"面向自动驾驶系统聚焦测试的失范行为预测","a":"Simulation-based testing is the standard practice for assessing the reliability of self-driving cars’ software before deployment. Existing bug-finding techniques are either unreliable or expensive. We build on the insight that near misses observed during simulations may point to potential failures. We propose Foresee, a technique that identifies near misses using a misbehavior forecaster that computes possible future states of the ego-vehicle under test. Foresee performs local fuzzing in the neighborhood of each candidate near miss to surface previously unknown failures. In our empirical study, we evaluate the effectiveness of different configurations of Foresee using several scenarios provided in the CARLA simulator on both end-to-end and modular self-driving systems and examine its complementarity with the state-of-the-art fuzzer DriveFuzz. Our results show that Foresee is both more effective and more efficient than the baselines. Foresee exposes 128.70% and 38.09% more failures than a random approach and a state-of-the-art failure predictor while being 2.49× and 1.42× faster, respectively. Moreover, when used in combination with DriveFuzz, Foresee enhances failure detection by up to 93.94%.","az":"基于仿真的测试是部署前评估自动驾驶汽车软件可靠性的标准做法。现有的缺陷发现技术要么不可靠，要么代价高昂。我们基于这样一个洞见：仿真过程中观察到的“险些出事”（near miss）可能预示潜在失效。我们提出 Foresee，一种通过失范行为预测器计算被测自车可能的未来状态、进而识别险些出事情形的技术。Foresee 在每个候选险些出事情形的邻域内执行局部模糊测试，以暴露此前未知的失效。在实证研究中，我们使用 CARLA 仿真器提供的若干场景，在端到端与模块化两类自动驾驶系统上评估了 Foresee 的不同配置，并考察了它与最先进模糊测试工具 DriveFuzz 的互补性。结果表明 Foresee 比基线更有效也更高效：相比随机方法和最先进的失效预测器，Foresee 分别多暴露 128.70% 和 38.09% 的失效，同时分别快 2.49× 和 1.42×。此外，与 DriveFuzz 联合使用时，Foresee 将失效检测能力最高提升 93.94%。","tl":"用未来状态预测锁定“险些出事”，再局部模糊测试挖失效。","au":["M M Abid Naziri","Stefano Carlo Lambertenghi","Andrea Stocco","Marcelo d'Amorim"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving testing","misbehavior forecasting","near miss","simulation-based fuzzing","CARLA"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/301/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.18823"},{"id":"p00788","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Out of Distribution, Out of Luck: How Well Can LLMs Trained on Vulnerability Datasets Detect Top 25 CWE Weaknesses?","tz":"分布之外，运气用尽：在漏洞数据集上训练的 LLM 能多好地检测 Top 25 CWE 弱点？","a":"Automated vulnerability detection research has made substantial progress, yet its real-world impact remains limited. Prior work found that current vulnerability datasets suffer from issues including label inaccuracy rates of 20-71%, extensive duplication, and poor coverage of critical Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE). These issues create a significant “generalization gap” where models achieve misleading In-Distribution (ID) accuracies (testing on splits from the same dataset) by exploiting spurious correlations rather than learning true vulnerability patterns. To address these limitations, we present a three-part solution. First, we introduce BenchVul, a manually curated and balanced test dataset covering the MITRE Top 25 Most Dangerous CWEs, to enable fair model evaluation. Second, we construct a high-quality training dataset, TitanVul, comprising 38,548 functions by aggregating seven public sources and applying deduplication and validation using a novel multi-agent LLM framework. Third, we propose a Realistic Vulnerability Generation (RVG) framework, which synthesizes context-aware vulnerability examples for underrepresented but critical CWE types through simulated development workflows. Our evaluation reveals that In-Distribution (ID) performance does not reliably predict Out-of-Distribution (OOD) performance on BenchVul. For example, a model trained on BigVul achieves the highest 0.703 ID accuracy but fails on BenchVul’s real-world samples (0.493 OOD accuracy). Conversely, a model trained on our TitanVul achieves the highest OOD performance on both the real-world (0.881) and synthesized (0.785) portions of BenchVul, improving upon the next-best performing dataset by 5.3% and 11.8% respectively, despite a modest ID score (0.590). Augmenting TitanVul with our RVG framework further boosts this leading OOD performance, improving accuracy on unseen real-world data by 5.8% (to 0.932).","az":"自动漏洞检测研究已取得长足进展，但其现实影响仍然有限。已有工作发现，当前的漏洞数据集存在标签错误率 20–71%、大量重复、以及对关键通用弱点枚举（CWE）覆盖不足等问题。这些问题造成了显著的“泛化鸿沟”：模型通过利用虚假相关性而非学习真正的漏洞模式，在分布内（ID，即在同一数据集划分上测试）取得具有误导性的准确率。为克服这些局限，我们提出一个三部分的解决方案。第一，我们引入 BenchVul——一个人工整理、类别均衡的测试数据集，覆盖 MITRE Top 25 最危险 CWE，以支持公平的模型评测。第二，我们构建了高质量训练数据集 TitanVul，通过聚合七个公开来源、并使用一种新颖的多智能体 LLM 框架进行去重与校验，得到 38,548 个函数。第三，我们提出真实漏洞生成（RVG）框架，通过模拟开发工作流，为代表性不足但关键的 CWE 类型合成具有上下文感知的漏洞样例。我们的评估显示，分布内（ID）性能无法可靠预测在 BenchVul 上的分布外（OOD）性能：例如，在 BigVul 上训练的模型取得最高的 0.703 ID 准确率，但在 BenchVul 的真实世界样本上失败（OOD 准确率 0.493）；相反，在我们的 TitanVul 上训练的模型在 BenchVul 的真实世界部分（0.881）与合成部分（0.785）均取得最高 OOD 性能，分别比次优数据集高出 5.3% 和 11.8%，尽管其 ID 得分只有中等水平（0.590）。用我们的 RVG 框架增强 TitanVul 后，这一领先的 OOD 性能进一步提升，在未见真实数据上的准确率再提高 5.8%（达到 0.932）。","tl":"揭示漏洞检测 ID 分数无法预测 OOD，并给出新数据集与合成框架。","au":["Yikun Li","Ngoc Tan Bui","Ting Zhang","Chengran Yang","Xin Zhou","Martin Weyssow","Jinfeng Jiang","Junkai Chen","Huihui Huang","Huu Hung Nguyen","Chiok Yew Ho","Jie Tan","Ruiyin Li","Yide Yin","Han Wei Ang","Frank Liauw","Eng Lieh Ouh","Lwin Khin Shar","David Lo"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","out-of-distribution generalization","CWE Top 25","dataset curation","synthetic vulnerability generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/302/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.21817"},{"id":"p00789","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Empirical Study of Fine-Grained Entity Relationships for Tracing Natural Language and Code Vulnerability Artifacts","tz":"面向自然语言与代码漏洞制品追踪的细粒度实体关系实证研究","a":"Understanding software vulnerabilities requires analyzing fine-grained entities and their complex relationships across natural language (NL) artifacts and source code. Vulnerability descriptions often interweave vulnerability triggers (VT), crash phenomena (CP), and after-fix (AF) actions within the same sentence, making it challenging to distinguish root causes, failure symptoms, and remediation strategies. Additionally, missing key NL entities further hinders traceability, limiting an analyst’s ability to determine why and how a vulnerability was introduced and resolved. To address these challenges, we conduct an empirical study on fine-grained entity relationships using a manually curated dataset of 1,000 vulnerabilities. We extract phrase-level VT, CP, and AF entities, categorize them into structured taxonomies, and analyze cross-entity relationships within NL artifacts and source code, uncovering recurring patterns in vulnerability evolution and remediation strategies. Furthermore, we investigate the automation of vulnerability entity extraction using different approaches, showing that ELECTRA [8], a state-of-the-art pre-trained language model, along with other LLM-based approaches, outperforms other methods.","az":"理解软件漏洞需要分析跨自然语言（NL）制品与源代码的细粒度实体及其复杂关系。漏洞描述常常在同一句话中交织了漏洞触发条件（VT）、崩溃现象（CP）与修复后（AF）动作，使得区分根本原因、失效症状与修复策略变得困难。此外，关键 NL 实体的缺失进一步阻碍了可追踪性，限制了分析人员判断漏洞为何以及如何被引入和被解决的能力。为应对这些挑战，我们基于一个人工整理的包含 1,000 个漏洞的数据集，开展了关于细粒度实体关系的实证研究。我们抽取短语级的 VT、CP 与 AF 实体，将其归入结构化的分类体系，并分析 NL 制品与源代码内部的跨实体关系，揭示了漏洞演化与修复策略中反复出现的模式。此外，我们还研究了用不同方法自动抽取漏洞实体，结果表明最先进的预训练语言模型 ELECTRA 以及其他基于 LLM 的方法优于其他方法。","tl":"构建漏洞触发/崩溃/修复三类细粒度实体的分类与自动抽取。","au":["Simin Wang","Liguo Huang","Shiyi Wei","Amiao Gao","Ruiqi Hu","Vincent Ng"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["vulnerability artifacts","entity extraction","traceability","taxonomy","ELECTRA"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/303/x"},{"id":"p00790","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TAAF: A Trace Abstraction and Analysis Framework Synergizing Knowledge Graphs and LLMs","tz":"TAAF：融合知识图谱与 LLM 的执行轨迹抽象与分析框架","a":"Execution traces are a critical source of information for understanding, debugging, and optimizing complex software systems. However, traces from OS kernels or large-scale applications like Chrome or MySQL are massive and difficult to analyze. Existing tools rely on predefined analyses, and custom insights often require writing domain-specific scripts, which is an error-prone and time-consuming task. This paper introduces TAAF (Trace Abstraction and Analysis Framework), a novel approach that combines time-indexing, knowledge graphs (KGs), and large language models (LLMs) to transform raw trace data into actionable insights. TAAF constructs a time-indexed KG from trace events to capture relationships among entities such as threads, CPUs, and system resources. An LLM then interprets query-specific subgraphs to answer natural-language questions, reducing the need for manual inspection and deep system expertise. To evaluate TAAF, we introduce TraceQA–100, a benchmark of 100 questions grounded in real kernel traces. Experiments across three LLMs and multiple temporal settings show that TAAF improves answer accuracy by up to 31.2%, particularly in multi-hop and causal reasoning tasks. We further analyze where graph-grounded reasoning helps and where limitations remain, offering a foundation for next-generation trace analysis tools.","az":"执行轨迹是理解、调试和优化复杂软件系统的关键信息来源。然而，来自操作系统内核或 Chrome、MySQL 等大规模应用的轨迹体量庞大、难以分析。现有工具依赖预定义分析，获取定制洞见往往需要编写领域专用脚本，这既易出错又耗时。本文提出 TAAF（轨迹抽象与分析框架），一种将时间索引、知识图谱（KG）与大语言模型（LLM）相结合、把原始轨迹数据转化为可行动洞见的新方法。TAAF 从轨迹事件构建时间索引的知识图谱，以刻画线程、CPU 与系统资源等实体之间的关系；随后由 LLM 解释与查询相关的子图，以回答自然语言问题，减少人工检查与深厚系统专业知识的需求。为评估 TAAF，我们引入 TraceQA–100——一个基于真实内核轨迹构建的包含 100 个问题的基准。在三个 LLM 与多种时间设置下的实验表明，TAAF 将回答准确率最高提升 31.2%，在多跳与因果推理任务上尤为明显。我们还进一步分析了图结构化推理在何处有帮助、何处仍存在局限，为下一代轨迹分析工具奠定基础。","tl":"用时间索引知识图谱让 LLM 回答关于内核轨迹的自然语言问题。","au":["Alireza Ezaz","Ghazal Khodabandeh","Majid Babaei","Naser Ezzati-Jivan"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["execution traces","knowledge graph","LLM question answering","kernel tracing","TraceQA-100"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/304/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.02632"},{"id":"p00791","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fine-Grained Analyses for Evolution-Aware Runtime Verification","tz":"面向演化感知运行时验证的细粒度分析","a":"Runtime verification found many bugs by monitoring passing tests in many open-source projects against formal specifications (specs). But, RV is often too slow for use in continuous integration. So, evolution-aware techniques were proposed to speed up RV by re-monitoring only a subset of specs affected by code changes. These techniques use coarse-grained class-level analyses, so they can sub-optimally and imprecisely re-monitor unaffected specs. We propose FineMOP to speed up evolution-aware RV by using fine-grained analyses to re-monitor fewer unaffected specs. The key idea is simple: changes often do not require re-monitoring specs that are only related to unchanged parts of changed classes. We implement six variants of three fine-grained analyses in FineMOP and evaluate it on 1,104 revisions of 68 open-source Java projects. Compared with two class-level techniques, FineMOP is up to 4.86x faster, re-monitors up to 81.04% fewer specs per revision, and finds 99.68% of all new violations that these techniques find. Also, FineMOP and Regression Test Selection (RTS) are complementary: combining FineMOP with RTS is faster than FineMOP or RTS alone.","az":"运行时验证（RV）通过依据形式化规约（specs）监控通过的测试，在许多开源项目中发现了大量缺陷。但 RV 往往过慢，难以用于持续集成。因此，人们提出了演化感知技术，只重新监控受代码变更影响的规约子集来加速 RV。这些技术使用粗粒度的类级别分析，因而可能次优且不精确地重新监控未受影响的规约。我们提出 FineMOP，利用细粒度分析来减少重新监控的未受影响规约，从而加速演化感知 RV。其核心思想很简单：变更往往并不需要重新监控那些仅与被改类中未变更部分相关的规约。我们在 FineMOP 中实现了三类细粒度分析的六种变体，并在 68 个开源 Java 项目的 1,104 个修订版本上进行评估。与两种类级别技术相比，FineMOP 最高快 4.86 倍，每个修订版本重新监控的规约最多减少 81.04%，并能发现这些技术所发现的全部新违规中的 99.68%。此外，FineMOP 与回归测试选择（RTS）是互补的：将 FineMOP 与 RTS 结合比单独使用任一者都更快。","tl":"用细粒度变更分析大幅削减演化感知运行时验证的重监控规约。","au":["Pengyue Jiang","Kevin Guan","M. Mahdi Khosravi","Moustafa Ismail","Marcelo d'Amorim","Owolabi Legunsen"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["runtime verification","evolution-aware analysis","formal specifications","regression test selection","continuous integration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/305/x"},{"id":"p00792","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LikeThis! Empowering App Users to Submit UI Improvement Suggestions Instead of Complaints","tz":"LikeThis！让应用用户提交 UI 改进建议而非抱怨","a":"User feedback is crucial for the evolution of mobile apps. However, research suggests that users tend to submit uninformative, vague, or destructive feedback. Unlike recent AI4SE approaches that focus on generating code and other development artifacts, our work aims at empowering users to submit better and more constructive UI feedback with concrete suggestions on how to improve the app. We propose LikeThis!, a GenAI-based approach that takes a user comment with the corresponding screenshot to immediately generate multiple improvement alternatives, from which the user can easily choose their preferred option. To evaluate LikeThis!, we first conducted a model benchmarking study based on a public dataset of carefully critiqued UI designs. The results show that GPT-Image-1 significantly outperformed three other state-of-the-art image generation models in improving the designs to address UI issues while keeping the fidelity and without introducing new issues. An intermediate step in LikeThis! to generate a solution specification before changing the design was key to achieving effective improvement. Second, we conducted a user study with 10 production apps, where 15 users used LikeThis! to submit their feedback on encountered issues. Later, the developers of the apps assessed the understandability and actionability of the feedback with and without generated improvements. The results show that our approach helps generate better feedback from both user and developer perspectives, paving the way for AI-assisted user-developer collaboration.","az":"用户反馈对移动应用的演化至关重要。然而研究表明，用户往往提交信息量不足、含糊甚至具有破坏性的反馈。与近期专注于生成代码及其他开发制品的 AI4SE 方法不同，我们的工作旨在帮助用户提交更好、更具建设性的 UI 反馈，并附带如何改进应用的具体建议。我们提出 LikeThis!，一种基于生成式 AI 的方法：它以用户评论及对应截图为输入，即时生成多个改进备选方案，用户可轻松从中选择偏好的选项。为评估 LikeThis!，我们首先基于一个经过细致评论的 UI 设计公开数据集开展了模型基准测试研究。结果显示，GPT-Image-1 在改进设计以解决 UI 问题的同时保持保真度且不引入新问题方面，显著优于另外三个最先进的图像生成模型。LikeThis! 中在修改设计前先生成解决方案规约的中间步骤，是取得有效改进的关键。其次，我们在 10 个生产环境应用上开展了用户研究，15 名用户使用 LikeThis! 对其遇到的问题提交反馈；随后这些应用的开发者评估了带与不带生成改进方案的反馈的可理解性与可执行性。结果表明，我们的方法从用户和开发者双方视角都能产生更好的反馈，为 AI 辅助的用户—开发者协作铺平了道路。","tl":"把用户抱怨+截图即时变成可选的 UI 改进设计方案。","au":["Jialiang Wei","Ali Ebrahimi Pourasad","Walid Maalej"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","tg":["human-study","llm-based","multimodal"],"kw":["user feedback","UI improvement suggestion","generative AI","app evolution","user study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/306/x"},{"id":"p00793","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TACO: Trust Assessment of Large Language Models in Coding Assistance Tasks","tz":"TACO：编码辅助任务中大语言模型的可信度评估","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have rapidly become integral to software development workflows, particularly in coding assistance tasks (CAT) such as debugging, implementation, and code optimization. However, the trustworthiness of LLM-generated responses remains a critical concern, as hallucinations (incorrect or misleading outputs) can severely hinder developer productivity and software reliability. In this paper, we introduce TACO, a comprehensive framework for trust assessment of LLMs in CAT scenarios. TACO jointly evaluates both the code quality and the alignment with user intent of LLM responses, enabling fine-grained and interpretable trust evaluation. We construct two new benchmarks: TACO-Judge, a human-annotated dataset for validating evaluation methods, and TACO-Eval, a large-scale benchmark for assessing LLM performance on real-world CAT problems. Through extensive experiments, we (1) demonstrate the accuracy and practical value of TACO via both benchmark evaluation and user study, (2) validate its fairness and reliability through self-preference analysis and interpreter consistency with real execution, and (3) compare the trustworthiness of several state-of-the-art LLMs in CAT scenarios. Our results highlight both the promise and limitations of current LLMs, and establish TACO as a reliable tool for their evaluation in software engineering contexts.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已迅速成为软件开发工作流的重要组成部分，尤其是在调试、实现和代码优化等编码辅助任务（CAT）中。然而，LLM 生成回复的可信度仍是关键关切，因为幻觉（错误或误导性输出）会严重妨碍开发者生产力和软件可靠性。本文提出 TACO，一个用于评估 LLM 在 CAT 场景下可信度的综合框架。TACO 同时评估 LLM 回复的代码质量与其与用户意图的一致性，从而实现细粒度、可解释的可信度评估。我们构建了两个新基准：TACO-Judge，一个用于验证评估方法的人工标注数据集；以及 TACO-Eval，一个用于评估 LLM 在真实 CAT 问题上表现的大规模基准。通过大量实验，我们（1）通过基准评测与用户研究证明了 TACO 的准确性与实用价值；（2）通过自偏好分析与解释器同真实执行的一致性验证了其公平性与可靠性；（3）比较了若干最先进 LLM 在 CAT 场景下的可信度。结果既凸显了当前 LLM 的潜力也揭示了其局限，并确立了 TACO 作为在软件工程情境中评估 LLM 的可靠工具。","tl":"同时评代码质量与意图一致性的编码助手可信度框架与基准。","au":["Shihao Weng","Yang Feng","Jincheng Li","Yining Yin","Zhenlun Zhang","Lyuxi Liu","Jia Liu"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["trust assessment","coding assistance tasks","LLM hallucination","benchmark","LLM-as-a-judge"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/307/x"},{"id":"p00794","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Toward Efficient Package Maintenance: An Empirical Study of Patch Sharing across Four Linux Distributions","tz":"迈向高效的软件包维护：四大 Linux 发行版间补丁共享的实证研究","a":"As a cornerstone of cloud computing and artificial intelligence, the Linux operating system has given rise to many popular distributions (distros), such as Fedora and Debian. A distro includes a rich collection of software packages derived from third-party open-source projects (upstream). Due to the nature of reusing upstream, some packages originate from the same upstream projects, noted as homologous packages. Maintaining packages is a core but tedious task for distros, which relies on continuously developing code patches. The maintenance of homologous packages could benefit from cross-distro collaboration. However, their shared origin may also lead to redundant efforts and delayed reuse of valuable maintenance work performed by other distros. To measure potential inefficiencies and explore possible solutions, this paper conducts an empirical study of patch sharing among homologous packages across four representative distros spanning three distinct families: Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora, and openEuler. We find that homologous packages are prevalent across distros, even across different distro families. Specifically, there are 13,873 homologous packages shared between Debian and Fedora, accounting for 40.3% and 56.1% of all packages in Debian and Fedora, respectively. For homologous packages with the same upstream version, we found that 19.5% of the patches are shared between Fedora and Debian, and 46.7% between Fedora and openEuler. However, these shared patches often exhibit remarkable propagation latency, with a median lag of 530.0 days between Fedora and Debian and 169.0 days between Fedora and openEuler. These results highlight the importance and necessity of cross-distro-family patch recommendations. We identified 17 shared Fedora-exclusive patches and contributed them to openEuler, among which 15 patches were successfully merged, demonstrating the potential of cross-distro-family patch recommendation and inspiring further research in this area.","az":"作为云计算和人工智能的基石，Linux 操作系统催生了 Fedora、Debian 等众多流行发行版（distro）。一个发行版包含大量源自第三方开源项目（上游）的软件包。由于复用上游的特性，一些软件包源自相同的上游项目，被称为同源包（homologous packages）。维护软件包是发行版的一项核心但繁琐的工作，依赖于持续开发代码补丁。同源包的维护本可以受益于跨发行版协作。然而，共同的来源也可能导致重复劳动，以及对其他发行版已完成的宝贵维护工作的复用被延迟。为衡量潜在的低效并探索可能的解决方案，本文对横跨三个不同家族的四个代表性发行版（Debian、Ubuntu、Fedora 和 openEuler）之间同源包的补丁共享开展了实证研究。我们发现同源包在各发行版间普遍存在，甚至跨越不同的发行版家族：具体而言，Debian 与 Fedora 之间共有 13,873 个同源包，分别占 Debian 和 Fedora 全部软件包的 40.3% 和 56.1%。对于上游版本相同的同源包，我们发现 Fedora 与 Debian 之间有 19.5% 的补丁被共享，Fedora 与 openEuler 之间为 46.7%。然而，这些共享补丁常常表现出显著的传播延迟：Fedora 与 Debian 之间的中位滞后为 530.0 天，Fedora 与 openEuler 之间为 169.0 天。这些结果凸显了跨发行版家族补丁推荐的重要性与必要性。我们识别出 17 个可共享的 Fedora 独有补丁并贡献给 openEuler，其中 15 个成功合入，展示了跨发行版家族补丁推荐的潜力，并激励该方向的进一步研究。","tl":"量化四大发行版同源包补丁共享率与数百天的传播滞后。","au":["Jian Peng","Jiaxin Zhu","Yuwei Zhang","Wei Chen","Guoquan Wu","Wei Wang","Jun Wei"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Linux distributions","homologous packages","patch sharing","package maintenance","patch propagation latency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/308/x"},{"id":"p00795","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Heterogeneous Prompting and Execution Feedback for SWE Issue Test Generation and Selection","tz":"面向 SWE Issue 复现测试生成与选择的异构提示与执行反馈","a":"A software engineering issue (SWE issue) is easier to resolve when accompanied by a reproduction test. Unfortunately, most issues do not come with functioning reproduction tests, so this paper explores how to generate them automatically. The primary challenge in this setting is that the code to be tested is either missing or wrong, as evidenced by the existence of the issue in the first place. This has held back test generation for this scenario: without the correct code to execute, it is difficult to leverage execution feedback to generate good tests. This paper introduces novel techniques for leveraging execution feedback to get around this problem, implemented in a new reproduction test generator called e-Otter++. Experiments show that e-Otter++ represents a leap ahead in the state-of-the-art for this problem, generating tests with an average fail-to-pass rate of 63% on the TDD-Bench Verified benchmark.","az":"当软件工程 issue（SWE issue）附带复现测试时，它更容易被解决。遗憾的是，大多数 issue 并不附带可用的复现测试，因此本文探索如何自动生成它们。该场景下的主要挑战在于：待测试的代码要么缺失、要么有错——issue 的存在本身就是证据。这一点一直阻碍着该场景下的测试生成：没有正确的代码可执行，就难以利用执行反馈来生成好的测试。本文提出了若干利用执行反馈绕开该问题的新技术，并在一个新的复现测试生成器 e-Otter++ 中实现。实验表明，e-Otter++ 在该问题上实现了对现有最优水平的跨越，在 TDD-Bench Verified 基准上生成的测试平均 fail-to-pass 率达到 63%。","tl":"在代码缺失或有错时仍用执行反馈生成 issue 复现测试。","au":["Toufique Ahmed","Jatin Ganhotra","Avraham Shinnar","Martin Hirzel"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","agentic"],"kw":["reproduction test generation","execution feedback","fail-to-pass","TDD-Bench Verified","SWE issue"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/309/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.06365"},{"id":"p00796","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Breaking the Alphabet: Rethinking File Ordering in Code Review","tz":"打破字母序：重新思考代码审查中的文件排序","a":"Effective code review is central to maintaining software quality, yet little is known about how the ordering of changed files in Pull Requests (PRs) influences review effectiveness. Most popular code review tools default to alphabetical ordering, favoring predictability over contextual relevance. While prior studies examined how file position shapes reviewer attention, it remains unclear how such ordering influences cognitive load and perceived thoroughness, which can potentially introduce usability barriers, overlooked defects, and review inefficiencies that ultimately undermine software reliability. This study presents the first large-scale survey of 1,355 professional developers across 182 widely used open-source projects to investigate how file ordering impacts review behavior, comprehension, and perceived effectiveness. Our mixed-methods analysis reveals that only 10.2% of reviewers consider alphabetical ordering optimal, underscoring its cognitive misalignment with how they interpret code changes. Although some developers appreciate its predictability, more than half (57.6%) note that it increases context switching, disrupts logical reasoning, and contributes to review fatigue, with 63.9% expressing concern that the default ordering may cause them to miss bugs. We further identify key challenges in multi-file reviews and elicit developers’ expectations for improved tooling, including dependency-aware grouping and customizable file ordering (requested by 66% of reviewers). These findings highlight the need for reviewer-centric interface designs that better align tool behavior with human cognition.","az":"有效的代码审查是维持软件质量的核心，但人们对拉取请求（PR）中变更文件的排序如何影响审查效果知之甚少。大多数流行的代码审查工具默认使用字母序排序，偏向可预测性而非上下文相关性。尽管已有研究考察了文件位置如何影响审查者注意力，但这种排序如何影响认知负荷与感知到的审查彻底性仍不清楚，而这可能带来可用性障碍、被遗漏的缺陷以及审查低效，最终损害软件可靠性。本研究首次对 182 个广泛使用的开源项目中的 1,355 名专业开发者开展大规模调查，考察文件排序如何影响审查行为、理解与感知效果。我们的混合方法分析表明，仅有 10.2% 的审查者认为字母序排序是最优的，凸显其与开发者解读代码变更方式之间的认知错配。尽管部分开发者欣赏其可预测性，但超过一半（57.6%）指出它增加了上下文切换、打断了逻辑推理并加剧了审查疲劳，63.9% 的人担心默认排序可能导致他们漏掉缺陷。我们还进一步识别了多文件审查中的关键挑战，并征集了开发者对改进工具的期望，包括依赖感知的分组与可自定义的文件排序（66% 的审查者提出该需求）。这些发现凸显了以审查者为中心、使工具行为更契合人类认知的界面设计的必要性。","tl":"大规模调查证明默认字母序文件排序损害代码审查效果。","au":["Md Shamimur Rahman","Zadia Codabux","Chanchal K. Roy"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["code review","file ordering","pull request","cognitive load","developer survey"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/310/x"},{"id":"p00797","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Toxicity Ahead: Forecasting Conversational Derailment on GitHub","tz":"毒性将至：预测 GitHub 上的对话失控","a":"Toxic interactions in Open Source Software (OSS) communities reduce contributor engagement and threaten project sustainability. Preventing such toxicity before it emerges requires a clear understanding of how harmful conversations unfold. However, most proactive moderation strategies are manual, requiring significant time and effort from community maintainers. To support more scalable approaches, we curate a dataset of 159 derailed toxic threads and 207 non-toxic threads from GitHub discussions. Our analysis reveals that toxicity can be forecasted by tension triggers, sentiment shifts, and specific conversational patterns. We present a novel Large Language Model (LLM)-based framework for predicting conversational derailment on GitHub using a two-step prompting pipeline. First, we generate Summaries of Conversation Dynamics (SCDs) via Least-to-Most (LtM) prompting; then we use these summaries to estimate the likelihood of derailment . Evaluated on Qwen and Llama models, our LtM strategy achieves F1-scores of 0.901 and 0.852, respectively, at a decision threshold of 0.3, outperforming established NLP baselines on conversation derailment. External validation on a dataset of 308 GitHub issue threads (65 toxic, 243 non-toxic) yields an F1-score up to 0.797. Our findings demonstrate the effectiveness of structured LLM prompting for early detection of conversational derailment in OSS, enabling proactive and explainable moderation.","az":"开源软件（OSS）社区中的有毒互动会降低贡献者参与度并威胁项目可持续性。要在毒性出现之前加以预防，就需要清楚理解有害对话是如何演变的。然而，大多数主动式治理策略都是人工的，需要社区维护者投入大量时间与精力。为支持更可扩展的方法，我们整理了一个包含 159 个失控有毒讨论串与 207 个无毒讨论串的 GitHub discussions 数据集。我们的分析表明，毒性可以通过紧张触发因素、情感转变和特定对话模式来预测。我们提出一个基于大语言模型（LLM）的新框架，采用两步提示流水线预测 GitHub 上的对话失控：首先通过由少到多（Least-to-Most，LtM）提示生成对话动态摘要（SCD），然后利用这些摘要估计失控的可能性。在 Qwen 和 Llama 模型上评估，我们的 LtM 策略在决策阈值 0.3 时分别取得 0.901 和 0.852 的 F1 分数，优于已有的对话失控 NLP 基线。在一个包含 308 个 GitHub issue 讨论串（65 个有毒、243 个无毒）的数据集上的外部验证取得最高 0.797 的 F1 分数。我们的发现证明了结构化 LLM 提示对 OSS 中对话失控早期检测的有效性，可支持主动且可解释的治理。","tl":"用对话动态摘要提示提前预测 GitHub 讨论何时会失控变毒。","au":["Mia Mohammad Imran","Robert Zita","Rahat Rizvi Rahman","Preetha Chatterjee","Kostadin Damevski"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","empirical-study"],"kw":["conversational derailment","toxicity in OSS","Least-to-Most prompting","GitHub discussions","proactive moderation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/311/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.15031"},{"id":"p00798","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fast Flow-Sensitive C Program Partitioning via Iterative Value-Flow Refinement","tz":"通过迭代值流细化实现快速流敏感的 C 程序分区","a":"Software vulnerabilities that expose confidential data remain a persistent threat. Even vulnerabilities in unprivileged code can expose data in privileged code when they share memory. Program partitioning safeguards against this by dividing a monolithic program into component programs according to a security policy for sharing confidential data, following the Principle of Least Privilege: each component of a system should operate with minimum privileges. Automatic C program partitioners determine a secure partition by tracking dataflows of confidential values; when data and function pointers are involved, this means a pointer analysis, so precision and performance tradeoffs are necessary. Existing work uses Andersen’s flow-insensitive pointer analysis, which is efficient but will reject secure partitionable programs—on the other hand, whole-program flow-sensitive analysis has not traditionally scaled. In this paper, we present CSP (C Sparse Partitioner), a C partitioner that supports robust security policies for mutual distrust and employs sparse demand-driven pointer analysis to achieve flow-sensitive precision at a fraction of the cost of whole-program flow-sensitive analysis. Our key innovation is an iterative value-flow refinement where a flow-insensitive constraint system is locally refined for flow-sensitivity as partitioning conflicts are found. We evaluate CSP on large real-world C programs with security requirements such as OpenSSH and Sendmail, and find that our technique outperforms whole-program flow-sensitive pointer analysis by up to an order of magnitude without sacrificing precision.","az":"暴露机密数据的软件漏洞仍是持续威胁。即便是非特权代码中的漏洞，在与特权代码共享内存时也可能泄露其数据。程序分区（program partitioning）通过按照共享机密数据的安全策略将单体程序划分为多个组件程序来防范此类风险，遵循最小权限原则：系统的每个组件都应以最小权限运行。自动化的 C 程序分区器通过追踪机密值的数据流来确定安全分区；当涉及数据指针和函数指针时，这意味着需要指针分析，因而必须在精度与性能之间做出权衡。现有工作使用 Andersen 的流不敏感指针分析，虽然高效，却会拒绝本可安全分区的程序；另一方面，全程序流敏感分析历来难以扩展。本文提出 CSP（C Sparse Partitioner），一个支持互不信任的稳健安全策略的 C 分区器，采用稀疏的需求驱动指针分析，以远低于全程序流敏感分析的代价达到流敏感的精度。我们的关键创新是一种迭代值流细化：当发现分区冲突时，对流不敏感的约束系统进行局部的流敏感细化。我们在 OpenSSH、Sendmail 等具有安全需求的大型真实 C 程序上评估 CSP，发现我们的技术在不牺牲精度的前提下比全程序流敏感指针分析最高快一个数量级。","tl":"按需局部细化流敏感性，使 C 程序特权分区既精确又可扩展。","au":["Maxwell Levatich","Stephen A. Edwards"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["non-llm-classical","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["program partitioning","flow-sensitive pointer analysis","value-flow refinement","least privilege","C programs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/312/x"},{"id":"p00799","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Metamorphic Fuzzing for Multi-Agent Path Finding Algorithms","tz":"面向多智能体路径规划算法的蜕变模糊测试","a":"Multi-Agent Path Finding (MAPF) is a fundamental problem in multi-agent systems, with broad applications in warehouse logistics, robotics, and autonomous driving. Ensuring that MAPF solvers consistently return a solution whenever one exists and deliver high-quality plans is critical for real-world deployment. However, MAPF algorithms remain insufficiently tested. The high-dimensional, tightly coupled input space arising from map topology and agent configurations makes systematic testing extremely challenging. This paper introduces MAPFFuzz, a metamorphic fuzzing framework for systematically testing MAPF solvers to detect both completeness failures and optimality failures. MAPFFuzz uses semantics-aware mutation strategies that jointly perturb both maps and agent configurations, coupled with a lightweight feasibility verification mechanism to ensure valid scenarios. Additionally, it incorporates diversity-guided seed selection and leverages metamorphic relations as oracles to assess solution quality. We evaluate MAPFFuzz on four recent MAPF solvers: PIBT, HCA, PIBT+, and LaCAM*. Results show that MAPFFuzz can detect completeness failures and more than 400 cases with degree of suboptimality exceeding 25% with 100 agents on 128x128 map cases per solver. MAPFFuzz also identifies 37 scenarios unsolvable by LaCAM* even under a 30-second parallel optimization setting. These findings demonstrate that MAPFFuzz can reveal both completeness failures and significant solution degradations, even in state-of-the-art algorithms under generous time budgets.","az":"多智能体路径规划（MAPF）是多智能体系统中的一个基础问题，在仓储物流、机器人与自动驾驶中有广泛应用。确保 MAPF 求解器在解存在时始终返回解、并给出高质量方案，对其真实部署至关重要。然而，MAPF 算法的测试仍然不足：地图拓扑与智能体配置所构成的高维、紧耦合输入空间，使系统性测试极具挑战。本文提出 MAPFFuzz，一个用于系统性测试 MAPF 求解器、以检测完备性失效与最优性失效的蜕变模糊测试框架。MAPFFuzz 采用语义感知的变异策略，联合扰动地图与智能体配置，并配合轻量级可行性验证机制以确保场景有效；此外，它引入多样性引导的种子选择，并利用蜕变关系作为预言来评估解的质量。我们在四个较新的 MAPF 求解器（PIBT、HCA、PIBT+ 和 LaCAM*）上评估 MAPFFuzz。结果表明，在 128x128 地图、100 个智能体的用例上，MAPFFuzz 对每个求解器都能检测出完备性失效以及 400 多个次优程度超过 25% 的案例；它还识别出 37 个即使在 30 秒并行优化设置下 LaCAM* 也无法求解的场景。这些发现表明，即使在宽裕的时间预算下，MAPFFuzz 也能揭示最先进算法中的完备性失效与显著的解质量退化。","tl":"首个用蜕变关系做预言的 MAPF 求解器模糊测试框架。","au":["Luxia Lin","xudong zhang","Shihao Zhu","Yan Cai"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["multi-agent path finding","metamorphic fuzzing","solver testing","metamorphic relations","suboptimality detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/313/x"},{"id":"p00800","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TestifAI: Tomography-Based Testing for Deep Learning Systems","tz":"TestifAI：面向深度学习系统的断层扫描式测试","a":"As AI systems are increasingly deployed in safety-critical applica- tion domains (e.g., autonomous driving), associated risks increase too. Deep learning models underlying modern AI systems, therefore, must undergo thorough testing to ensure their correct behaviour. A single robustness test involves thousands of inferences to empir- ically verify if a model’s outputs remain stable under a bounded perturbation of its inputs. However, existing testing frameworks lack the means to systematically explore and summarise robustness across a combinatorial space of perturbations. We propose TestifAI, a deep learning testing framework for ef- ficient and accurate estimation of robustness against combinations of perturbations. TestifAI enables users to specify the operational conditions of an AI system as structured spaces of semantic input perturbations (e.g., image blur, brightness and zoom) and their dis- crete severity levels (e.g., low, medium and high). Within this space, users can query model robustness for any combination (e.g., “low blur, high brightness, and medium zoom”). To achieve efficiency and accuracy, TestifAI introduces partial model tomography, a novel ap- proach to reconstructing model behaviour in a multi-perturbation space from tests that apply only a small number of perturbations (lower-order projections). Namely, to estimate robustness against at least three perturbations, TestifAI trains an auxiliary model on the results of tests involving up to two perturbations only, hence avoid- ing execution of an exponential number of tests. Our experiments on five image and language classification tasks show that TestifAI can predict higher-order (3 and 4 perturbations) test outcomes from low-order (1 and 2 perturbations) observations with an aggregate robustness estimation error of less than 7%, while reducing the number of inferences by 60–80%.","az":"随着 AI 系统越来越多地部署于安全关键应用领域（例如自动驾驶），相关风险也随之上升。因此，支撑现代 AI 系统的深度学习模型必须经过充分测试以确保其行为正确。一次鲁棒性测试涉及数千次推理，用以实证验证模型输出在输入受限扰动下是否保持稳定。然而，现有测试框架缺乏系统性探索并汇总组合扰动空间上鲁棒性的手段。我们提出 TestifAI，一个用于高效且准确估计模型对扰动组合之鲁棒性的深度学习测试框架。TestifAI 允许用户将 AI 系统的运行条件指定为语义输入扰动（例如图像模糊、亮度和缩放）及其离散严重级别（例如低、中、高）构成的结构化空间。在该空间内，用户可以查询任意组合（例如“低模糊、高亮度、中等缩放”）下的模型鲁棒性。为兼顾效率与准确性，TestifAI 引入部分模型断层扫描（partial model tomography）——一种仅从施加少量扰动的测试（低阶投影）中重建多扰动空间内模型行为的新方法。具体而言，为估计对至少三种扰动的鲁棒性，TestifAI 在仅涉及最多两种扰动的测试结果上训练一个辅助模型，从而避免执行指数级数量的测试。我们在五个图像与语言分类任务上的实验表明，TestifAI 能从低阶（1 和 2 种扰动）观测预测高阶（3 和 4 种扰动）测试结果，总体鲁棒性估计误差低于 7%，同时将推理次数减少 60–80%。","tl":"用低阶扰动测试结果重建高阶组合鲁棒性，省 60–80% 推理。","au":["Arooj Arif","Tobias Hartung","Elena Botoeva","Alexandros Koliousis"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["deep learning testing","robustness estimation","combinatorial perturbations","model tomography","test efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/314/x"},{"id":"p00801","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Do Semantically Equivalent Code Transformations Impact Membership Inference on LLMs for Code?","tz":"语义等价的代码变换如何影响面向代码的 LLM 上的成员推断？","a":"The success of large language models for code relies on vast amounts of code data, including public open-source repositories, such as GitHub, and private, confidential code from companies. This raises concerns about intellectual property compliance and the potential unauthorized use of license-restricted code. While membership inference (MI) techniques have been proposed to detect such unauthorized usage, their effectiveness can be undermined by semantically equivalent code transformation techniques, which modify code syntax while preserving semantic. In this work, we systematically investigate whether semantically equivalent code transformation rules might be leveraged to evade MI detection. The results reveal that model accuracy drops by only 1.5% in the worst case for each rule, demonstrating that transformed datasets can effectively serve as substitutes for fine-tuning. Additionally, we find that one of the rules (RenameVariable) reduces MI success by 10.19%, highlighting its potential to obscure the presence of restricted code. To validate these findings, we conduct a causal analysis confirming that variable renaming has the strongest causal effect in disrupting MI detection. Notably, we find that combining multiple transformations does not further reduce MI effectiveness. Our results expose a critical loophole in license compliance enforcement for training large language models for code, showing that MI detection can be substantially weakened by transformation-based obfuscation techniques.","az":"面向代码的大语言模型之所以成功，依赖于海量代码数据，其中既包括 GitHub 等公开开源仓库，也包括企业内部私有、机密的代码。这引发了对知识产权合规性以及许可证受限代码可能被未授权使用的担忧。虽然已有成员推断（MI）技术被提出用于检测这类未授权使用，但它们的有效性可能被语义等价的代码变换技术所削弱——这类变换在保持语义不变的前提下修改代码语法。在本工作中，我们系统性地考察了语义等价的代码变换规则是否可以被用来规避 MI 检测。结果表明，对每条规则而言，模型准确率在最坏情况下也仅下降 1.5%，说明变换后的数据集可以有效替代原数据用于微调。此外，我们发现其中一条规则（RenameVariable，变量重命名）使 MI 的成功率下降了 10.19%，凸显了它掩盖受限代码存在性的潜力。为验证这些发现，我们开展了因果分析，确认变量重命名在干扰 MI 检测方面具有最强的因果效应。值得注意的是，我们发现组合多种变换并不会进一步降低 MI 的有效性。我们的结果揭示了训练面向代码的大语言模型时许可证合规执行中的一个关键漏洞，表明基于变换的混淆技术可以显著削弱 MI 检测。","tl":"揭示变量重命名等等价变换可显著规避代码模型的成员推断检测。","au":["Hans yang","Alejandro Velasco","Thanh Le-Cong","Md Nazmul Haque","Bowen Xu","Denys Poshyvanyk"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["membership inference","code LLM","semantic-preserving transformation","license compliance","variable renaming"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/315/x"},{"id":"p00802","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Checking Unsupervised Learning for Nondeterminism and Inconsistency via SMT Solving","tz":"通过 SMT 求解检查无监督学习实现中的不确定性与不一致性","a":"Unsupervised Learning (UL) implementations are widely used, but prone to issues such as nondeterminism and inconsistency, which makes them unreliable and exploitable. Moreover, the lack of a specification (or ground truth) makes UL implementations hard to verify or test: when they produce diverging results on a dataset, they do so subtly and silently, which gives users a false sense of security, and complicates developers’ job of tracing the error to its root cause. We introduce an approach, Ocelot, that reduces nondeterminism/inconsistency checking to satisfiability checking in Z3. Given the Python code of an UL implementation, Ocelot automatically isolates a nondeterministic “kernel” (variables and code), which forms the basis for a Z3 specification. A Z3-found solution acts as a “witness” dataset – a typically small dataset that can be used to reliably reproduce the error. Ocelot has exposed sources of nondeterminism and inconsistency in popular implementations (Scikit-learn, MATLAB, and R) of well-known Clustering algorithms (Affinity Propagation, DBSCAN, HAC, and K-means) and Anomaly Detection algorithms (Isolation Forest, Local Outlier Factor). Moreover, Ocelot has exposed regressions (changes in semantics) in the evolution of these implementations.","az":"无监督学习（UL）的实现被广泛使用，但容易出现不确定性（nondeterminism）与不一致性（inconsistency）等问题，这使其不可靠且可被利用。此外，由于缺乏规约（或称真值标准），UL 实现难以验证或测试：当它们在某个数据集上产生分歧结果时，往往是微妙且无声地发生，这给用户带来虚假的安全感，也让开发者难以把错误追溯到根因。我们提出了一种方法 Ocelot，把不确定性/不一致性的检查归约为 Z3 中的可满足性检查。给定某个 UL 实现的 Python 代码，Ocelot 会自动隔离出一个具有不确定性的“内核”（变量与代码），并以此为基础构造 Z3 规约。Z3 找到的解充当一个“见证”数据集——通常是一个很小的数据集，可用于可靠地复现该错误。Ocelot 已在若干知名聚类算法（Affinity Propagation、DBSCAN、HAC 和 K-means）以及异常检测算法（Isolation Forest、Local Outlier Factor）的流行实现（Scikit-learn、MATLAB 和 R）中暴露出不确定性与不一致性的来源。此外，Ocelot 还在这些实现的演化过程中暴露出回归（语义变化）问题。","tl":"把无监督学习实现的不确定性检查归约为 Z3 可满足性求解。","au":["Muyeed Ahmed","Iulian Neamtiu"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unsupervised learning","nondeterminism","SMT solving","Z3","witness dataset"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/316/x"},{"id":"p00803","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"OctopusGuard: K-Line Enhanced Token Scam Detector Powered by Multimodal LLMs","tz":"OctopusGuard：由多模态 LLM 驱动、结合 K 线图增强的代币骗局检测器","a":"Token scams in Decentralized Finance (DeFi) have become more sophisticated, shifting from simple contract exploits to behavior-driven fraud involving obfuscated code, abnormal fund flows, and deceptive market activity. While recent works leverage large language models (LLMs) for vulnerability detection, existing methods still depend on predefined patterns and lack deep semantic reasoning, limiting their ability to detect novel scams. In this paper, we present OctopusGuard, a unified multimodal detector for token scams, which includes three key contributions: (i) K-line information is, for the first time, introduced to token scam detection. A RAG-based knowledge base is constructed by combining K-line images from both benign and scam tokens to enhance training and reasoning. (ii) A novel, structured tool-augmented data chain-of-thought (structured CoT) is designed to integrate code, transaction data, and K-line images into a unified reasoning process. (iii) A multimodal fine-tuning pipeline that jointly trains on structured CoT to learn cross-modal correlations and enhance generalization across diverse scam strategies. We also construct a newly collected, labeled multimodal dataset of 1,495 recent token contracts and conduct extensive experiments. Results demonstrate that OctopusGuard significantly outperforms existing detectors and LLMs in detecting token scams, achieving an F1-score of 0.96.","az":"去中心化金融（DeFi）中的代币骗局已变得愈发复杂，从简单的合约漏洞利用转向行为驱动的欺诈，涉及混淆代码、异常资金流和欺骗性的市场活动。尽管近期工作利用大语言模型（LLM）进行漏洞检测，现有方法仍依赖预定义模式且缺乏深层语义推理，限制了其检测新型骗局的能力。本文提出 OctopusGuard，一个统一的多模态代币骗局检测器，包含三项关键贡献：(i) 首次将 K 线（K-line）信息引入代币骗局检测；通过结合正常代币与骗局代币的 K 线图像构建基于 RAG 的知识库，以增强训练与推理。(ii) 设计了一种新颖的、结构化的工具增强数据思维链（structured CoT），将代码、交易数据和 K 线图像整合进统一的推理过程。(iii) 提出一条多模态微调流水线，在结构化 CoT 上联合训练，以学习跨模态关联并增强对多样化骗局策略的泛化能力。我们还构建了一个新采集并标注的多模态数据集，包含 1,495 个近期代币合约，并开展了广泛实验。结果表明，OctopusGuard 在检测代币骗局方面显著优于现有检测器与 LLM，取得了 0.96 的 F1 分数。","tl":"首次把 K 线图像与代码、交易数据联合用于代币骗局检测。","au":["Litong Sun","YangTian Mi","Xiapu Luo","Weigang Wu"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["token scam detection","DeFi","multimodal LLM","K-line","structured chain-of-thought"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/317/x"},{"id":"p00804","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"On LLMs’ Internal Representation of Code Correctness","tz":"论 LLM 对代码正确性的内部表征","a":"Despite the effectiveness of large language models (LLMs) for code generation, they often output incorrect code. One reason is that model output probabilities are often not well-correlated with correctness, and reflect only the final output of the generation process. Inspired by findings that LLMs internally encode concepts like truthfulness, this paper explores if LLMs similarly represent code correctness. Specifically, we identify a correctness representation inside LLMs by contrasting the hidden states between pairs of correct and incorrect code for the same programming tasks. By experimenting on four LLMs, we show that exploiting this extracted correctness representation outperforms standard log-likelihood ranking, as well as verbalized model confidence. Furthermore, we explore how this internal correctness signal can be used to select higher-quality code samples, without requiring test execution. Ultimately, this work demonstrates how leveraging internal representations can enhance code generation systems and make LLMs more reliable, thus improving confidence in automatically generated code.","az":"尽管大语言模型（LLM）在代码生成上颇为有效，它们仍经常输出错误代码。原因之一在于，模型的输出概率往往与正确性相关性不佳，且只反映生成过程的最终输出。受到“LLM 在内部编码了真实性等概念”这一发现的启发，本文探究 LLM 是否同样表征了代码的正确性。具体而言，我们通过对比同一编程任务下正确代码与错误代码配对的隐藏状态，识别出 LLM 内部的一种正确性表征。通过在四个 LLM 上的实验，我们表明利用这一抽取出的正确性表征，其效果优于标准的对数似然排序，也优于模型用语言表述出的置信度。此外，我们还探索了如何在无需执行测试的情况下，利用这一内部正确性信号来挑选质量更高的代码样本。最终，这项工作展示了利用内部表征如何能够增强代码生成系统、使 LLM 更可靠，从而提升人们对自动生成代码的信心。","tl":"从隐藏状态提取正确性方向，无需执行即可优于似然排序选代码。","au":["Francisco Ribeiro","Claudio Spiess","Prem Devanbu","Sarah Nadi"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["internal representation","code correctness","hidden states","confidence estimation","code ranking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/318/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.07404"},{"id":"p00805","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Comfrey: Mitigating Integration Failures in LLM-enabled Software at Run-Time","tz":"Comfrey：在运行时缓解 LLM 赋能软件中的集成失效","a":"Due to the unrestricted outputs of LLMs and strict requirements of software components, integration failures are widespread in software that incorporates LLM agents and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). Even seemingly correct LLM/RAG responses can trigger software misbehaviors if they violate these requirements. In this paper, we conduct an empirical study to understand integration failures in real-world LLM-enabled applications. Guided by this study, we present Comfrey, a runtime framework that adapts the LLM agent and RAG responses to meet software requirements, serving as a middle layer between AI and software components. It automatically detects and resolves potential integration failures through a three-stage workflow, ensuring component compatibility. Our evaluation with a variety of open-source applications demonstrates that Comfrey detects 75.1% and prevents 63.3% of potential integration failures with 8.4% overhead, significantly outperforming the baselines. The artifact is available on Anonymous GitHub.","az":"由于 LLM 的输出不受约束而软件组件的要求严格，在集成了 LLM 智能体与检索增强生成（RAG）的软件中，集成失效十分普遍。即便看似正确的 LLM/RAG 响应，只要违反这些要求，也可能触发软件的错误行为。本文中，我们开展了一项实证研究，以理解真实世界 LLM 赋能应用中的集成失效。在该研究的指导下，我们提出 Comfrey，一个运行时框架，用于调整 LLM 智能体与 RAG 的响应以满足软件需求，充当 AI 组件与软件组件之间的中间层。它通过三阶段工作流自动检测并解决潜在的集成失效，确保组件兼容性。我们在多种开源应用上的评估表明，Comfrey 能检测 75.1%、预防 63.3% 的潜在集成失效，开销为 8.4%，显著优于各基线方法。相关制品已发布在 Anonymous GitHub 上。","tl":"提出运行时中间层，自动适配 LLM/RAG 响应以消除集成失效。","au":["Yuchen Shao","Yuheng Huang","Jiazhen Zou","Yuling Shi","Long Yang","Lei Ma","Ting Su","Chengcheng Wan"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["integration failure","LLM-enabled software","RAG","runtime adaptation","component compatibility"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/319/x"},{"id":"p00806","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Toward Systematic Counterfactual Fairness Evaluation of Large Language Models: The CAFFE Framework","tz":"迈向大语言模型反事实公平性的系统化评估：CAFFE 框架","a":"Nowadays, Large Language Models (LLMs) are foundational components of modern software systems. As their influence grows, concerns about fairness have become increasingly pressing. Prior work has proposed metamorphic testing to detect fairness issues, applying input transformations to uncover inconsistencies in model behavior. This paper introduces an alternative perspective for testing counterfactual fairness in LLMs, proposing a structured and intent-aware framework coined CAFFE (Counterfactual Assessment Framework for Fairness Evaluation). Inspired by traditional non-functional testing, CAFFE (1) formalizes LLM-Fairness test cases through explicitly defined components, including prompt intent, conversational context, input variants, expected fairness thresholds, and test environment configuration, (2) assists testers by automatically generating targeted test data, and (3) evaluates model responses using semantic similarity metrics. Our experiments, conducted on three different architectural families of LLM, demonstrate that CAFFE achieves broader bias coverage and more reliable detection of unfair behavior than existing metamorphic approaches.","az":"如今，大语言模型（LLM）已成为现代软件系统的基础组件。随着其影响力增长，对公平性的担忧日益紧迫。已有工作提出用蜕变测试来发现公平性问题，即施加输入变换以揭示模型行为的不一致。本文为测试 LLM 的反事实公平性提出了另一种视角，提出了一个结构化、意图感知的框架，称为 CAFFE（Counterfactual Assessment Framework for Fairness Evaluation，面向公平性评估的反事实评估框架）。受传统非功能性测试启发，CAFFE（1）通过明确定义的组成部分——提示意图、对话上下文、输入变体、期望的公平性阈值以及测试环境配置——来形式化 LLM 公平性测试用例；（2）通过自动生成有针对性的测试数据来辅助测试人员；（3）使用语义相似度指标评估模型响应。我们在三个不同架构家族的 LLM 上开展的实验表明，相较于已有的蜕变方法，CAFFE 实现了更广的偏见覆盖以及对不公平行为更可靠的检测。","tl":"用意图感知的反事实测试用例框架替代蜕变测试评估 LLM 公平性。","au":["Alessandra Parziale","Gianmario Voria","Valeria Pontillo","Gemma Catolino","Andrea De Lucia","Fabio Palomba"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["cross-track-bridge","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["counterfactual fairness","LLM testing","metamorphic testing","bias coverage","test framework"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/320/x"},{"id":"p00807","v":"ICSE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Empirical Study of Knowledge Distillation for Code Understanding Tasks","tz":"面向代码理解任务的知识蒸馏实证研究","a":"Pre-trained language models (PLMs) have emerged as powerful tools for code understanding. However, deploying these PLMs in large-scale applications faces practical challenges due to their computational intensity and inference latency. Knowledge distillation (KD), a promising model compression and acceleration technique, addresses these limitations by transferring knowledge from large teacher models to compact student models, enabling efficient inference while preserving most of the teacher models’ capabilities. While this technique has shown remarkable success in natural language processing and computer vision domains, its potential for code understanding tasks remains largely underexplored. In this paper, we systematically investigate the effectiveness and usage of KD in code understanding tasks. Our study encompasses two popular types of KD methods, i.e., logit-based and feature-based KD methods, experimenting across eight student models and two teacher PLMs from different domains on three downstream tasks. The experimental results indicate that KD consistently offers notable performance boosts across student models with different sizes compared with standard fine-tuning. Notably, code-specific PLM demonstrates better effectiveness as the teacher model. Among all KD methods, the latest feature-based KD methods exhibit superior performance, enabling student models to retain up to 98% teacher performance with merely 5% parameters. Regarding student architecture, our experiments reveal that similarity with teacher architecture does not necessarily lead to better performance. We further discuss the efficiency and behaviors in the KD process and inference, summarize the implications of findings, and identify promising future directions.","az":"预训练语言模型（PLM）已成为代码理解的强大工具。然而，由于计算开销大、推理延迟高，在大规模应用中部署这些 PLM 面临实际挑战。知识蒸馏（KD）作为一种有前景的模型压缩与加速技术，通过把知识从大型教师模型迁移到紧凑的学生模型来应对这些限制，从而在保留教师模型大部分能力的同时实现高效推理。尽管该技术在自然语言处理和计算机视觉领域已取得显著成功，其在代码理解任务上的潜力仍在很大程度上未被探索。本文系统性地研究了 KD 在代码理解任务中的有效性与使用方式。我们的研究涵盖两类流行的 KD 方法，即基于 logit 的和基于特征的 KD 方法，在三个下游任务上对八个学生模型和两个来自不同领域的教师 PLM 进行了实验。实验结果表明，与标准微调相比，KD 在不同规模的学生模型上都持续带来显著的性能提升。值得注意的是，面向代码的 PLM 作为教师模型表现更佳。在所有 KD 方法中，最新的基于特征的 KD 方法表现最优，使学生模型仅用 5% 的参数就能保留高达 98% 的教师性能。关于学生模型架构，我们的实验揭示：与教师架构相似并不必然带来更好的性能。我们进一步讨论了 KD 过程与推理中的效率与行为，总结了发现的启示，并指出了有前景的未来方向。","tl":"系统评测 logit 与特征蒸馏在代码理解上的效果与架构影响。","au":["Ruiqi Wang","Zezhou Yang","Cuiyun Gao","Xin Xia","Qing Liao"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["knowledge distillation","code understanding","pre-trained language models","model compression","feature-based KD"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/321/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.15423"},{"id":"p00809","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Casting a SPELL: Sentence Pairing Exploration for LLM Limitation-breaking","tz":"施放 SPELL：用句子配对探索突破 LLM 的限制","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have revolutionized software development through AI-assisted coding tools, enabling developers with limited programming expertise to create sophisticated applications. This democratization of software development has significantly lowered the barriers to entry for complex programming tasks. However, the same accessibility extends to malicious actors who may exploit these powerful tools to generate harmful software, including malware, ransomware, and other security threats. Existing jailbreaking research primarily focuses on general attack scenarios against LLMs, with limited exploration of malicious code generation as a jailbreak target and insufficient technical expertise to evaluate whether generated outputs align with specified malicious objectives. To address this gap, we propose SPELL, a comprehensive testing framework for LLM developer and Secure Team, specifically designed to evaluate the weakness of security alignment in malicious code generation. Our framework employs a time-division selection strategy that systematically constructs jailbreaking prompts by intelligently combining sentences from a prior knowledge dataset, balancing exploration of novel attack patterns with exploitation of successful techniques. Extensive evaluation across three advance code models (GPT-4.1, Claude-3.5, and Qwen2.5-Coder) demonstrates SPELL’s effectiveness, achieving attack success rates of 83.75%, 19.38%, and 68.12% respectively across eight malicious code categories. The generated prompts successfully produce malicious code in real-world AI development tools such as Cursor, with outputs confirmed as malicious by state-of-the-art detection systems at rates exceeding 73%, including 4 instances flagged as extremely dangerous by all detection tools. These findings reveal significant security gaps in current LLM implementations and provide valuable insights for improving AI safety alignment in code generation applications.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）通过 AI 辅助编码工具彻底改变了软件开发，使编程经验有限的开发者也能创建复杂应用。这种软件开发的民主化显著降低了复杂编程任务的入门门槛。然而，同样的易用性也惠及了恶意行为者，他们可能利用这些强大工具生成有害软件，包括恶意软件、勒索软件及其他安全威胁。现有的越狱研究主要聚焦于针对 LLM 的一般攻击场景，对以恶意代码生成为越狱目标的探索有限，也缺乏足够的技术专长来评估生成的输出是否符合指定的恶意目标。为填补这一空白，我们提出 SPELL，一个面向 LLM 开发者与安全团队的综合测试框架，专门用于评估恶意代码生成中安全对齐的薄弱环节。我们的框架采用一种分时选择策略，通过智能地组合来自先验知识数据集的句子来系统性地构造越狱提示，在探索新攻击模式与利用已成功技术之间取得平衡。在三个先进代码模型（GPT-4.1、Claude-3.5 和 Qwen2.5-Coder）上的广泛评估证明了 SPELL 的有效性，在八类恶意代码上分别取得 83.75%、19.38% 和 68.12% 的攻击成功率。生成的提示在 Cursor 等真实 AI 开发工具中成功产出了恶意代码，其输出被最先进的检测系统以超过 73% 的比例确认为恶意，其中 4 个实例被所有检测工具标记为极度危险。这些发现揭示了当前 LLM 实现中的重大安全缺口，并为改进代码生成应用中的 AI 安全对齐提供了有价值的洞见。","tl":"用句子组合的分时选择策略自动构造越狱提示诱导模型写恶意代码。","au":["Yifan Huang","Xiaojun Jia","Wenbo Guo","Yuqiang Sun","Yihao Huang","Chong Wang","Yang Liu"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","tg":["security","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["jailbreak","malicious code generation","security alignment","code LLM","attack success rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/1/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.21236"},{"id":"p00810","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding the Limitations of C/C++ Binary Third-Party Library Detection Tool: An Empirical Study at Scale","tz":"理解 C/C++ 二进制第三方库检测工具的局限：一项大规模实证研究","a":"Detecting third-party libraries (TPLs) in C/C++ binaries is essential for ensuring software security and compliance, particularly in safety- and performance-critical domains. While numerous academic and commercial Software Composition Analysis (SCA) tools have been proposed, their true capabilities remain unclear due to the absence of large-scale benchmarks and systematic evaluation. Equally lacking is a deeper understanding of why these tools often underperform, which limits both research progress and practical adoption. We address this gap with a large-scale study of binary SCA tools. We construct the largest publicly available benchmark to date, encompassing 38,228 test cases across 1,873 libraries drawn from a defined scope of 13,675 libraries. Using this benchmark, we systematically evaluate 11 representative tools, covering all open source research prototypes and widely adopted commercial solutions, across versions, architectures, and feature-database scales. Beyond aggregate performance metrics, we perform the first fine-grained, feature-level analysis to identify the intrinsic challenges of binary TPL detection. Our results show that existing tools perform unsatisfactorily, with average recall below 60% and precision around 75%. Feature-level analysis reveals fundamental obstacles: binaries lose most source-code features during compilation, and libraries exhibit high feature overlap due to functional similarity and dependency propagation. These findings explain current shortcomings, and we build on them to provide design recommendations, research directions, and practical guidance for managing open-source risks in binary software.","az":"在 C/C++ 二进制中检测第三方库（TPL）对于保障软件安全与合规至关重要，在安全关键与性能关键领域尤其如此。尽管已有大量学术与商业的软件成分分析（SCA）工具被提出，但由于缺乏大规模基准与系统性评估，它们的真实能力仍不清楚。同样缺失的还有对这些工具为何常常表现不佳的深入理解，这既限制了研究进展，也限制了实际采纳。我们通过一项针对二进制 SCA 工具的大规模研究来填补这一空白。我们构建了迄今最大的公开基准，涵盖 38,228 个测试用例，涉及 1,873 个库，取自一个包含 13,675 个库的界定范围。基于该基准，我们系统性地评估了 11 个代表性工具，覆盖所有开源研究原型与被广泛采用的商业方案，并跨版本、体系结构与特征库规模进行评测。除了汇总性能指标之外，我们还首次开展了细粒度的特征级分析，以识别二进制 TPL 检测的内在挑战。结果显示，现有工具表现并不令人满意，平均召回率低于 60%，精确率约为 75%。特征级分析揭示了根本性障碍：二进制在编译过程中丢失了大部分源码特征，且由于功能相似性与依赖传播，库之间存在高度的特征重叠。这些发现解释了当前的不足，我们在此基础上给出了设计建议、研究方向以及管理二进制软件中开源风险的实践指导。","tl":"构建最大二进制 SCA 基准并首次做特征级归因解释工具为何失效。","au":["CHENGYUE LIU","Zhengzi Xu","Kaixuan Li","Wu Jiahui","Sihao Qiu","Siyuan Li","Siyang Xiong","Yang Xiao","Yang Liu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["software composition analysis","third-party library detection","binary analysis","benchmark","feature-level analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/2/x"},{"id":"p00811","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Still Manual? Automated Linter Configuration via DSL-Based LLM Compilation of Coding Standards","tz":"还在手工配置？基于 DSL 的 LLM 编码规范编译实现 Linter 自动配置","a":"Coding standards are essential for maintaining consistent and high-quality code across teams and projects. Linters help developers enforce these standards by detecting code violations. However, manual linter configuration is complex and expertise-intensive, and the diversity and evolution of programming languages, coding standards, and linters lead to repetitive and maintenance-intensive configuration work. To reduce manual effort, we propose a domain-specific language (DSL)-driven, LLM-based compilation approach to automate configuration generation for coding standards, independent of programming languages, coding standards, and linters. Inspired by compiler design, we first design a DSL to express coding rules in a tool-agnostic, structured, readable, and precise manner. Then, we build linter configurations into DSL configuration instructions. For a given natural language coding standard, the compilation process parses it into DSL coding standards, matches them with the DSL configuration instructions to set configuration names, option names and values, verifies consistency between the standards and configurations, and finally generates linter-specific configurations. Experiments with Checkstyle for Java coding standard show that our approach achieves over 90% precision and recall in DSL representation, with accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-scores close to 70% (with some exceeding 70%) in fine-grained linter configuration generation. Notably, our approach outperforms baselines by over 100% in precision. An ablation study confirms the effectiveness of the main components of our approach. A user study further shows that our approach improves developers’ efficiency in configuring linters for coding standards. Finally, we demonstrate the generality of the approach by generating ESLint configurations for JavaScript coding standards, showcasing its broad applicability across other programming languages, coding standards, and linters. We developed a lightweight, general-purpose AI skill, which is publicly available on GitHub: LintConfig .","az":"编码规范对于在团队与项目间保持一致且高质量的代码至关重要。Linter 通过检测代码违规帮助开发者执行这些规范。然而，手工配置 linter 复杂且高度依赖专业知识，加之编程语言、编码规范与 linter 的多样性和持续演化，导致配置工作重复且维护成本高。为减少人工投入，我们提出一种由领域特定语言（DSL）驱动、基于 LLM 的编译方法，用于自动生成编码规范的配置，且与编程语言、编码规范和 linter 无关。受编译器设计启发，我们首先设计了一种 DSL，以工具无关、结构化、可读且精确的方式表达编码规则。随后，我们把 linter 配置构建为 DSL 配置指令。对于给定的自然语言编码规范，编译过程将其解析为 DSL 编码规范，与 DSL 配置指令进行匹配以设定配置名、选项名与取值，验证规范与配置之间的一致性，最终生成特定 linter 的配置。在针对 Java 编码规范使用 Checkstyle 的实验中，我们的方法在 DSL 表示上取得超过 90% 的精确率与召回率，在细粒度 linter 配置生成上的准确率、精确率、召回率与 F1 分数接近 70%（部分超过 70%）。值得注意的是，我们的方法在精确率上超过基线 100% 以上。消融实验确认了方法各主要组件的有效性。一项用户研究进一步表明，我们的方法提升了开发者为编码规范配置 linter 的效率。最后，我们通过为 JavaScript 编码规范生成 ESLint 配置展示了方法的通用性，说明其可广泛适用于其他编程语言、编码规范与 linter。我们开发了一个轻量级、通用的 AI skill，已公开发布在 GitHub 上：LintConfig。","tl":"用 DSL 把自然语言编码规范“编译”成任意 linter 的配置。","au":["zejun zhang","Yixin Gan","Zhenchang Xing","Tian Zhang","Yi Li","Qinghua Lu","Xiwei (Sherry) Xu","Liming Zhu"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","human-study"],"kw":["linter configuration","coding standards","domain-specific language","LLM compilation","Checkstyle"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/3/x","pu":"https://github.com/idiomaticrefactoring/idiomaticrefactoring/blob/main/assets/pdf/FSE_2026_ConfigGen_camera_ready%20(4).pdf"},{"id":"p00812","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PlayCoder: Making LLM-Generated GUI Code Playable","tz":"PlayCoder：让 LLM 生成的 GUI 代码真正可玩","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have transformed code generation, but their ability to generate code for applications with graphical user interfaces (GUIs), particularly games, remains underexplored. To explore their performance on applications with GUI, we construct a repository-aware evaluation dataset from 35 GUI applications. Prior code-generation benchmarks assess correctness using test cases, but this is insufficient for GUI applications. These applications are interactive and event-driven, and their correctness depends on stateful behavior over sequences of user actions. Consequently, evaluation should account for interaction flows and UI state transitions rather than relying solely on pass or fail test outcomes. To enable more reliable assessment beyond simple execution and unit tests, we propose Play@k, which measures whether at least one of k generated candidates yields an application that can be played end-to-end without logical errors. We further develop an LLM-based agent, PlayTester, that automates interactive evaluation by driving the GUI through task-oriented playthroughs and checking for logic violations. Through systematic evaluation, we demonstrate that 10 state-of-the-art code LLMs struggle to generate logically correct GUI applications, achieving near-zero Play@3 scores despite high compilation rates. To address these challenges, we introduce PlayCoder, a multi-agent, repository-aware framework that writes, evaluates and refines GUI application code via closed-loop control. PlayCoder substantially improves functional correctness and semantic alignment for both open-source and closed-source models, achieving up to 37.5% Exec@3 and 17.2% Play@3. Case studies show that it detects silent logic flaws missed by traditional metrics and repairs them through targeted edits. These results indicate that coupling an end-to-end GUI testing agent with repository-aware automated program repair is an effective path toward reliable GUI code generation.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已经变革了代码生成，但它们为带图形用户界面（GUI）的应用、尤其是游戏生成代码的能力仍未被充分探索。为考察其在 GUI 应用上的表现，我们基于 35 个 GUI 应用构建了一个仓库感知的评测数据集。以往的代码生成基准使用测试用例评估正确性，但这对 GUI 应用并不充分。这类应用是交互式、事件驱动的，其正确性取决于一系列用户操作上的有状态行为。因此，评估应当考虑交互流程与 UI 状态转移，而不是仅依赖测试的通过或失败结果。为实现超越简单执行与单元测试的更可靠评估，我们提出 Play@k，它衡量 k 个生成候选中是否至少有一个产出的应用能够端到端地被“玩通”而不出现逻辑错误。我们进一步开发了一个基于 LLM 的智能体 PlayTester，它通过面向任务的试玩驱动 GUI 并检查逻辑违规，从而自动化交互式评测。通过系统评估，我们发现 10 个最先进的代码 LLM 在生成逻辑正确的 GUI 应用上困难重重：尽管编译通过率很高，Play@3 得分却接近于零。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 PlayCoder，一个多智能体、仓库感知的框架，通过闭环控制来编写、评估并精化 GUI 应用代码。PlayCoder 对开源与闭源模型的功能正确性与语义一致性都有显著提升，Exec@3 最高达 37.5%，Play@3 最高达 17.2%。案例研究表明，它能发现传统指标遗漏的隐性逻辑缺陷，并通过有针对性的编辑加以修复。这些结果表明，将端到端 GUI 测试智能体与仓库感知的自动程序修复相结合，是通向可靠 GUI 代码生成的有效路径。","tl":"提出 Play@k 与试玩智能体，闭环修复让生成的 GUI 应用真正可运行。","au":["Zhiyuan Peng","Wei Tao","Xin Yin","Chenhao Ying","Yuan Luo","Yiwen Guo"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["GUI code generation","Play@k","interactive evaluation","multi-agent framework","repository-aware"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/4/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.19742"},{"id":"p00813","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Multi-LLM Persona Generation for Virtual Focus Groups in Software Engineering: A Controlled, Multi-Domain Study of Emotional Requirements Elicitation","tz":"面向软件工程虚拟焦点小组的多 LLM 人格生成：情感需求获取的受控多领域研究","a":"This paper presents a controlled, multi-domain evaluation of using multiple Large Language Models (LLMs) to automate and augment the elicitation of emotional requirements in software engineering. We study an anchor domain (mental-health journaling) alongside personal finance and fitness, and disentangle gains from iterative workflow versus true model plurality by comparing four AI configurations (one-shot vs. iterative; single-, two-, and three-model pipelines) against two human baselines: a standard human focus group and Emotional Goal Modeling (EGM). Outputs are assessed with blind human ratings (relevance, clarity, feasibility, innovation) and group-dynamics coding that includes productive, resolution-oriented conflict and empathy events. Across domains, heterogeneous-provider plurality increases persona dispersion and fosters productive conflict in AI-mediated focus groups, yielding more AI-only requirements that pass blind validation than single-model workflows (pooled C3–C1 uplift: +14.7%). To isolate plurality from provider capability, we add two same-model ablation controls in the anchor domain: (i) C1-MV (same-model multi-voice) and (ii) C3-SM (same-model three-step). In a small-sample evaluation (two seeds each), the resulting difference-in-differences on validated share indicating that a substantial portion (~55%) of the C3 uplift persists net of provider heterogeneity. EGM consistently improves clarity and feasibility through explicit goal tracing, while human groups contribute authenticity and language fit; together they form a complementary, auditable pipeline in which supportive reframing (empathy) and productive disagreement help convert dialog into implementable requirements.","az":"本文提出了一项受控的多领域评估，考察使用多个大语言模型（LLM）来自动化并增强软件工程中情感需求的获取。我们研究了一个锚定领域（心理健康日记），并辅以个人理财与健身领域，通过将四种 AI 配置（一次性 vs. 迭代式；单模型、双模型与三模型流水线）与两个人类基线——标准的人类焦点小组与情感目标建模（EGM）——进行比较，来区分迭代式工作流带来的收益与真正的模型多样性带来的收益。输出结果通过盲评人工打分（相关性、清晰度、可行性、创新性）以及群体动力学编码进行评估，后者包含富有成效的、面向解决的冲突与共情事件。跨领域来看，异构供应商带来的多样性提升了人格的离散度，并在 AI 中介的焦点小组中促成了富有成效的冲突，产生了比单模型工作流更多、且能通过盲评验证的“仅由 AI 提出”的需求（合并后的 C3–C1 提升：+14.7%）。为把多样性与供应商能力区分开，我们在锚定领域中增加了两组同模型消融对照：(i) C1-MV（同模型多声部）与 (ii) C3-SM（同模型三步）。在小样本评估中（每组两个随机种子），所得到的双重差分显示，在扣除供应商异构性之后，C3 的提升仍有相当一部分（约 55%）得以保留。EGM 通过显式的目标追溯持续改善清晰度与可行性，而人类小组则贡献真实性与语言贴合度；二者共同构成一条互补、可审计的流水线，其中支持性的重构表述（共情）与富有成效的分歧有助于把对话转化为可实现的需求。","tl":"证明跨厂商模型的多样性而非单纯迭代带来情感需求质量提升。","au":["Guangrui Fan","Dandan Liu","Lihu Pan","Rui Zhang","Qian Guo"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["requirements elicitation","emotional requirements","LLM personas","virtual focus group","model plurality"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/5/x"},{"id":"p00814","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GadgetHunter: Region-Based Neuro-Symbolic Detection of Java Deserialization Vulnerabilities","tz":"GadgetHunter：基于区域划分的神经符号 Java 反序列化漏洞检测","a":"Java deserialization vulnerabilities (JDVs) enable attackers to execute arbitrary code by crafting malicious serialized objects that trigger sequences of method calls (gadget chains) leading to dangerous operations. Existing detection approaches face a fundamental trade-off: static analysis achieves scalability but suffers from high false positives due to infeasible paths and imprecision with dynamic features like reflection; dynamic validation reduces false positives but incurs prohibitive costs and fails to explore deep exploitation chains. We present GadgetHunter, a neuro-symbolic JDV detector that combines scalable static analysis with targeted LLM reasoning and JDV exploitation-oriented constraint solving. Our approach partitions gadget chains into regions based on analyzability: statically resolvable segments are processed via interprocedural taint analysis, while dynamic boundaries are delegated to LLMs for semantic validation. We then extract critical constraints from each gadget and compose them into SMT formulas to determine chain feasibility through satisfiability solving. Evaluation on the ysoserial benchmark demonstrates that GadgetHunter reduces false negatives by up to 32% and false positives by 12-85% compared to state-of-the-art tools, while discovering 197 previously unknown gadget chains and rediscovering 4 recent CVEs. Our results show that combining symbolic reasoning with semantic understanding achieves both precision and practical impact in vulnerability detection.","az":"Java 反序列化漏洞（JDV）使攻击者能够通过构造恶意序列化对象来执行任意代码，这些对象会触发一系列方法调用（gadget 链）并导向危险操作。现有检测方法面临一个根本性权衡：静态分析可扩展，但由于不可行路径以及对反射等动态特性的不精确处理而误报率高；动态验证可降低误报，却带来高昂代价，且难以探索深层的利用链。我们提出 GadgetHunter，一种神经符号的 JDV 检测器，它将可扩展的静态分析、有针对性的 LLM 推理与面向 JDV 利用的约束求解结合起来。我们的方法依据可分析性将 gadget 链划分为多个区域：静态可解析的片段通过过程间污点分析处理，而动态边界则交由 LLM 进行语义验证。随后我们从每个 gadget 中抽取关键约束，并将其组合为 SMT 公式，通过可满足性求解判定链的可行性。在 ysoserial 基准上的评估表明，相较于最先进的工具，GadgetHunter 将漏报最多降低 32%，将误报降低 12%–85%，同时发现了 197 条此前未知的 gadget 链，并重新发现了 4 个近期 CVE。我们的结果表明，将符号推理与语义理解相结合，可在漏洞检测中同时取得精确性与实际影响力。","tl":"按可分析性分区，把动态边界交给 LLM、其余交给污点分析与 SMT。","au":["Kaixuan Li","Jian Zhang","Chong Wang","Sen Chen","Zong Cao","Min Zhang","Yang Liu"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Java deserialization","gadget chain","neuro-symbolic analysis","taint analysis","SMT solving"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/6/x","pu":"https://kaixuanli-ecnu.github.io/papers/kaixuan-FSE26_GadgetHunter.pdf"},{"id":"p00815","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Large Language Models for Opaque Predicate Resolution: A Universal Control Flow Deobfuscation Framework","tz":"用大语言模型消解不透明谓词：一个通用的控制流反混淆框架","a":"Code obfuscation is a process that complicates reverse engineering, protects intellectual property, and conceals malware. However, traditional deobfuscation methods are not universally applicable and can be easily circumvented. It is evident that advanced techniques, such as symbolic execution and SMT solvers, encounter difficulties when confronted with out-of-distribution code and particular obfuscation strategies. This hinders their efficacy to a considerable extent. This paper proposes a novel approach that integrates Large Language Models (LLMs) with decompiled code analysis to enhance understanding of control flow structures. Contributions include the formalisation of control flow deobfuscation tasks with new evaluation metrics and the proposal of a general predicate relationship inference method that adapts to diverse obfuscation techniques. The innovative model architecture combines linear LLM access with non-linear execution path expansion, thereby generating security-expert-friendly C pseudocode. Comprehensive evaluation on 780 binaries employing 13 distinct obfuscation techniques demonstrates that our method reduces average cyclomatic complexity by 52.4%, achieves full deobfuscation in 53.8% of cases, and suppresses Topological Feasible Path Set (TFPS) inflation caused by bogus control flow by over 99%. The framework demonstrates superiority over existing state-of-the-art tools in terms of both generality and semantic consistency, thus evidencing the transformative potential of LLMs in facilitating scalable malware reverse engineering.","az":"代码混淆是一种使逆向工程复杂化、保护知识产权并隐藏恶意软件的手段。然而，传统的反混淆方法并不具备普遍适用性，且容易被绕过。显然，符号执行与 SMT 求解器等先进技术在面对分布外代码以及特定混淆策略时会遇到困难，这在相当程度上削弱了其效果。本文提出一种新颖方法，将大语言模型（LLM）与反编译代码分析相结合，以增强对控制流结构的理解。贡献包括：对控制流反混淆任务的形式化及新的评价指标，以及提出一种可适配多样混淆技术的通用谓词关系推断方法。创新的模型架构将线性的 LLM 访问与非线性的执行路径扩展相结合，从而生成对安全专家友好的 C 伪代码。在采用 13 种不同混淆技术的 780 个二进制文件上的全面评估表明，我们的方法将平均圈复杂度降低 52.4%，在 53.8% 的案例中实现完全反混淆，并将由虚假控制流引起的拓扑可行路径集（TFPS）膨胀抑制超过 99%。该框架在通用性与语义一致性方面均优于现有最先进工具，从而证明了 LLM 在支撑可扩展恶意软件逆向工程方面的变革潜力。","tl":"用 LLM 推断谓词关系，实现跨多种混淆技术的通用控制流反混淆。","au":["Xiao Chen","Wang Qiuyun","Wang Shuwei","Zhang Weize","Yuling Liu","Baoxu Liu","Jiang Zhengwei"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["opaque predicate","control flow deobfuscation","binary reverse engineering","decompiled code","cyclomatic complexity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/7/x"},{"id":"p00816","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SwarmBox: A Plug-and-Play Drone Swarm Framework for Streamlined Development and Comprehensive Analysis","tz":"SwarmBox：面向简化开发与全面分析的即插即用无人机集群框架","a":"Drone swarms are emerging as paradigm-shifting technology with the potential to redefine traditional robot missions such as logistics, surveillance, and disaster response, through their ability to coordinate large numbers of autonomous drones. Yet, progress in swarm research and development is constrained by a fragmented development ecosystem; every new algorithm must be validated on a bespoke testbed, introducing significant and redundant engineering overhead, while producing results that are difficult to reproduce or compare. As a remedy, we present SwarmBox, an open-source testbed framework that provides a shared foundation for swarm robotics. SwarmBox streamlines swarm research and development by providing three key capabilities: (1) a plug-and-play software architecture that decouples high-level swarm logic from low-level flight control and platform dependencies; (2) a swarm-level integrated analyzer that exposes emergent behaviors across drones and system layers to facilitate debugging and analysis; and (3) a configurable experimentation environment that supports diverse missions and communication topologies to promote fair and reproducible benchmarking. Our evaluation demonstrates these benefits in practice. SwarmBox reduces software engineering effort by eliminating boilerplate code, abstracting low-level system details into coherent APIs, and simplifying swarm coordination into a uniform process. It improves fault diagnosis efficiency and uniquely exposes inter-agent interaction failures that traditional debugging methods cannot capture. It enables reproducible benchmarking by allowing systematic comparison of different swarm algorithms. It proves its generality and scalability by supporting diverse mission scenarios ranging from centralized coordination to fully decentralized swarms. Finally, its hardware abstraction layer minimizes the simulation-to-real gap, enabling unmodified application code to be seamlessly deployed on both simulation and physical drones. Together, these capabilities establish SwarmBox as a practical foundation for reproducible, community-driven swarm robotics research.","az":"无人机集群正成为一项具有范式转变意义的技术，凭借协调大量自主无人机的能力，有望重新定义物流、监控与灾害响应等传统机器人任务。然而，集群研究与开发的进展受制于碎片化的开发生态：每一个新算法都必须在定制的测试平台上验证，带来巨大而重复的工程开销，同时产生难以复现或比较的结果。作为解决方案，我们提出 SwarmBox，一个开源测试平台框架，为集群机器人提供共享的基础设施。SwarmBox 通过三项关键能力简化集群研究与开发：(1) 一种即插即用的软件架构，将高层集群逻辑与底层飞控及平台依赖解耦；(2) 一个集群级集成分析器，跨无人机与系统各层暴露涌现行为，便于调试与分析；(3) 一个可配置的实验环境，支持多样的任务与通信拓扑，促进公平且可复现的基准测试。我们的评估在实践中验证了这些优势。SwarmBox 通过消除样板代码、把底层系统细节抽象为一致的 API、并把集群协调简化为统一流程，降低了软件工程投入。它提升了故障诊断效率，并能独特地暴露传统调试方法无法捕捉的智能体间交互失效。它通过支持对不同集群算法的系统性比较实现了可复现的基准测试。它通过支持从集中式协调到完全去中心化集群的多样任务场景，证明了自身的通用性与可扩展性。最后，其硬件抽象层最小化了仿真到现实的差距，使未经修改的应用代码可以无缝部署到仿真与实体无人机上。这些能力共同确立了 SwarmBox 作为可复现、社区驱动的集群机器人研究的实用基础。","tl":"开源即插即用集群测试平台，暴露传统调试看不见的机间交互失效。","au":["Minki Lee","Seojin Lee","Seulbae Kim"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["drone swarm","testbed framework","swarm robotics","fault diagnosis","reproducible benchmarking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/8/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808100"},{"id":"p00817","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SnakeCharmer: Automatic Fuzzing Harness Generation for Pure and Hybrid Python Libraries","tz":"SnakeCharmer：面向纯 Python 与混合 Python 库的模糊测试 Harness 自动生成","a":"With Python’s rising popularity, ensuring the correctness of its ever-growing ecosystem of software libraries is more critical than ever. Recently, fuzzing has become a de facto technique for vetting software libraries, enabled via the use of harnesses: small wrapper programs that inject fuzzer-generated test cases into the library under test. While harness creation has shed its reliance on human expertise and is now fully automated for languages such as C and C++, Python remains uniquely challenging—both for pure Python libraries as well as hybrid ones combining Python with native C/C++ extensions—due to (1) limited visibility across language boundaries, (2) the absence of reliable bug oracles, and (3) incomplete type information. Consequently, attempts at automating harnessing for Python fail to both uphold critical runtime behaviors and produce the structured call and data flows needed for effective fuzzing, leaving much of today’s Python ecosystem largely unvetted. To overcome these challenges and broaden fuzzing’s reach across Python libraries, this paper introduces SnakeCharmer: the first automated harness generation approach for both pure and hybrid Python libraries. At its core, SnakeCharmer leverages static analysis to first capture key interface information from both Python and native code components, subsequently enriching it with runtime-captured type information and exception behaviors. During fuzzing, SnakeCharmer further distinguishes between expected exceptions and true library bugs, filtering out benign exceptions that would otherwise derail testing progress. Together, these techniques significantly enhance the scope and effectiveness of fuzzing across the Python library ecosystem, enabling the automated discovery of bugs in code previously inaccessible to existing Python fuzzing efforts. We evaluate SnakeCharmer alongside today’s leading Python auto-harnessing approach, PyRTFuzz; the actively fuzzed expert-written harnesses from both OSS-Fuzz and PolyFuzz; and the harnesses generated by Google’s own state-of-the-art LLM-driven automatic harnessing approach, OSS-Fuzz-Gen. Across 21 diverse Python libraries, SnakeCharmer attains type-recovery precision and exception-filtering accuracy of 95% and 97%, respectively, further attaining 1.48×, 1.87×, 1.78×, and 1.40× the code coverage of the fuzzing harnesses from PyRTFuzz, OSS-Fuzz, PolyFuzz, and OSS-Fuzz-Gen, respectively. Further, SnakeCharmer finds 16, 24, and 24 more Python library bugs than all expert- and LLM-created harnesses as well as PyRTFuzz, respectively—uncovering a total of 20 new bugs, with 18 since confirmed or fixed by developers.","az":"随着 Python 日益流行，确保其不断增长的软件库生态的正确性比以往任何时候都更加关键。近来，模糊测试已成为审查软件库的事实标准技术，其实现依赖 harness：一种把 fuzzer 生成的测试用例注入被测库的小型包装程序。虽然 harness 的构建已摆脱对人类专业知识的依赖，并在 C 和 C++ 等语言上实现了完全自动化，Python 仍然格外困难——无论是纯 Python 库还是把 Python 与原生 C/C++ 扩展结合的混合库——原因在于：(1) 跨语言边界的可见性有限；(2) 缺乏可靠的缺陷预言；(3) 类型信息不完整。因此，自动化 Python harness 的尝试既无法维持关键的运行时行为，也无法产生有效模糊测试所需的结构化调用流与数据流，导致当今大部分 Python 生态基本未被审查。为克服这些挑战并将模糊测试的覆盖面拓展到更多 Python 库，本文提出 SnakeCharmer：首个面向纯 Python 与混合 Python 库的自动化 harness 生成方法。其核心是，SnakeCharmer 利用静态分析首先从 Python 与原生代码组件中捕获关键接口信息，随后用运行时捕获的类型信息与异常行为加以丰富。在模糊测试过程中，SnakeCharmer 进一步区分预期异常与真正的库缺陷，过滤掉否则会阻碍测试进展的良性异常。这些技术共同显著增强了模糊测试在 Python 库生态中的覆盖范围与有效性，使此前现有 Python 模糊测试难以触及的代码中的缺陷得以被自动发现。我们将 SnakeCharmer 与当今领先的 Python 自动 harness 方法 PyRTFuzz、来自 OSS-Fuzz 与 PolyFuzz 的由专家编写并持续模糊测试的 harness，以及 Google 自家最先进的 LLM 驱动自动 harness 方法 OSS-Fuzz-Gen 进行了对比评估。在 21 个多样的 Python 库上，SnakeCharmer 的类型恢复精确率与异常过滤准确率分别达到 95% 与 97%，并分别取得 PyRTFuzz、OSS-Fuzz、PolyFuzz 与 OSS-Fuzz-Gen 的 harness 的 1.48 倍、1.87 倍、1.78 倍与 1.40 倍的代码覆盖率。此外，SnakeCharmer 比所有专家与 LLM 编写的 harness 以及 PyRTFuzz 分别多发现 16、24 与 24 个 Python 库缺陷——共计发现 20 个新缺陷，其中 18 个已被开发者确认或修复。","tl":"首个跨纯 Python 与原生扩展的自动 harness 生成，含异常过滤预言。","au":["Gabriel Sherman","Stefan Nagy"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["fuzzing harness generation","Python libraries","hybrid native extensions","type recovery","exception filtering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/9/x","pu":"https://futures.cs.utah.edu/papers/26FSE-b.pdf"},{"id":"p00818","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Cascaded Code Editing: Large-Small Model Collaboration for Effective and Efficient Code Editing","tz":"级联式代码编辑：大小模型协作实现高效且有效的代码编辑","a":"Code editing constitutes a fundamental practice in software development, wherein developers modify existing codebases according to natural language requirements. Accurate code editing necessitates a comprehensive understanding of both the existing codebase and the modification requirements. Although large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated promising performance in code editing tasks, they suffer from substantial inefficiency by generating entire modified files that largely consist of unchanged code. While smaller models could potentially address this inefficiency, they typically lack the capacity to effectively comprehend long code contexts required for accurate editing. To ensure both effectiveness and efficiency, we propose to decompose code editing into a two-stage cascade: edit sketch generation, wherein a large model first produces concise sketches representing the requisite modifications (the more challenging phase), and edit sketch application, wherein a smaller model integrates these sketches into the original code to produce the final output edited code (the simpler phase). This cascaded design reduces the number of tokens generated by the large model, as the majority of the output is handled by the smaller, more efficient model, thereby enhancing overall efficiency. However, the effectiveness of this approach is constrained by current small models’ limited capabilities in handling long-context scenarios and cross-file dependencies, which are essential for accurate sketch application in real-world codebases. To address these limitations and enhance smaller models’ sketch application capabilities, we introduce the first large-scale sketch application dataset comprising over 100K training instances and 800M tokens, along with a human-evaluated benchmark, and propose specialized training strategies including curriculum-based long-context training and multi-file augmentation. Our comprehensive experiments demonstrate that our cascaded framework inherently reduces inference costs compared to direct editing with large models. Furthermore, combining large models with our fine-tuned smaller models can achieve even superior performance. For instance, on the Aider benchmark, employing DeepSeek R1 as the edit sketch generation model alongside a fine-tuned Qwen2.5 Coder 14B model for the application phase improves Pass@2 11.1% compared to direct editing with DeepSeek R1 alone. Additionally, the cascaded approach reduces execution time and cost by 13% and 19%, respectively, demonstrating both performance gains and efficiency improvements.","az":"代码编辑是软件开发中的基础实践，开发者根据自然语言需求修改已有代码库。准确的代码编辑需要同时深入理解现有代码库与修改需求。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在代码编辑任务上表现出色，但它们会生成整个修改后的文件，其中大部分内容是未改动的代码，因而效率极低。较小的模型有潜力解决这种低效问题，但它们通常缺乏理解准确编辑所需的长代码上下文的能力。为兼顾有效性与效率，我们提出把代码编辑分解为两阶段级联：**编辑草图生成**，即由大模型先产出表示所需修改的简洁草图（更具挑战的阶段）；以及**编辑草图应用**，即由小模型把这些草图整合进原始代码以产出最终的编辑后代码（较简单的阶段）。这种级联设计减少了大模型生成的 token 数量，因为大部分输出由更小、更高效的模型处理，从而提升整体效率。然而，该方法的有效性受限于当前小模型在长上下文场景与跨文件依赖处理上的能力不足，而这些能力对于真实代码库中准确的草图应用至关重要。为解决这些限制并增强小模型的草图应用能力，我们引入了首个大规模草图应用数据集，包含超过 10 万条训练实例与 8 亿 token，以及一个经过人工评估的基准，并提出了包括基于课程学习的长上下文训练与多文件增强在内的专门训练策略。我们的全面实验表明，相比直接用大模型编辑，我们的级联框架天然降低了推理成本。此外，把大模型与我们微调后的小模型结合还能取得更优性能。例如，在 Aider 基准上，用 DeepSeek R1 作为编辑草图生成模型、并用微调后的 Qwen2.5 Coder 14B 模型完成应用阶段，相比单独使用 DeepSeek R1 直接编辑，Pass@2 提升了 11.1%。同时，级联方法将执行时间与成本分别降低了 13% 与 19%。","tl":"大模型只出编辑草图、微调小模型负责落地，成本与准确率双赢。","au":["Chaozheng Wang","Zezhou Yang","Shuzheng Gao","Cuiyun Gao Harbin Institute of Technology, Shenzhen","Li Zongjie","Yichen LI","Ting Peng","Hailiang Huang","Yuetang Deng","Michael Lyu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["code editing","model cascade","edit sketch","long-context training","inference cost"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/10/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.19201"},{"id":"p00819","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Bash-Commenter: Leveraging Syntax-Aware Preference Optimization to Reinforce Large Language Model for Bash Code Comment Generation","tz":"Bash-Commenter：利用语法感知的偏好优化强化大语言模型生成 Bash 代码注释","a":"Bash script comprehension is a significant challenge in Linux environments due to Bash’s syntactic freedom and complex command structures. Despite its critical role in system administration and development, Bash scripts often lack adequate comments, hindering code readability and maintainability. Existing approaches to automated Bash comment generation face two main challenges: (1) Limited training datasets that inadequately represent real-world Bash usage patterns, particularly for complex multi-line scripts; and (2) Insufficient understanding of Bash-specific concepts by Large Language Models (LLMs). Our empirical analysis shows that even after standard training, LLMs still struggle to precisely understand complex Bash command semantics, leading to inaccurate comments. To address these challenges, we propose Bash-Commenter, an advanced comment generation method based on LLaMA-3.1-8B that employs a three-stage pipeline. First, we perform Continual Pre-training (CPT) on large-scale Bash script data to enhance the model’s foundational understanding of Bash syntax and semantics, addressing the second challenge. Second, to overcome data limitations (the first challenge), we construct a comprehensive dataset of complex, multi-line scripts and then perform Supervised Fine-tuning (SFT). Finally, to resolve the subtle semantic errors that persist, we introduce Syntax-Aware Preference Optimization (SAPO). This method automatically constructs preference pairs by applying single, atomic operations (e.g., modifying a command option or removing an argument) to a script’s Abstract Syntax Tree (AST), creating minimal pairs of correct and subtly incorrect scripts. This final optimization stage enables fine-grained command semantics learning and context-dependent quality assessment, significantly improving comment accuracy. We evaluate Bash-Commenter on single-line Bash commands and multi-line Bash scripts. Our method outperforms state-of-the-art baselines, achieving 33.40% BLEU-4, 58.26% METEOR, and 57.03% ROUGE-L for 1,064 single-line commands, and 22.15% BLEU-4, 43.89% METEOR, and 32.80% ROUGE-L for 1,046 multi-line scripts. Moreover, human evaluation demonstrates the superior quality of comments generated by Bash-Commenter in terms of correctness, completeness, and naturalness.","az":"由于 Bash 语法自由度高、命令结构复杂，在 Linux 环境中理解 Bash 脚本是一项重大挑战。尽管 Bash 脚本在系统管理与开发中扮演关键角色，它们往往缺乏充分的注释，妨碍了代码的可读性与可维护性。现有的 Bash 注释自动生成方法面临两大挑战：(1) 训练数据集有限，无法充分代表真实世界的 Bash 使用模式，尤其是复杂的多行脚本；(2) 大语言模型（LLM）对 Bash 特有概念的理解不足。我们的实证分析表明，即便经过标准训练，LLM 仍难以精确理解复杂 Bash 命令的语义，导致注释不准确。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 Bash-Commenter，一种基于 LLaMA-3.1-8B 的先进注释生成方法，采用三阶段流水线。首先，我们在大规模 Bash 脚本数据上进行继续预训练（CPT），以增强模型对 Bash 语法与语义的基础理解，应对第二个挑战。其次，为克服数据局限（第一个挑战），我们构建了一个包含复杂多行脚本的综合数据集，并在其上进行监督微调（SFT）。最后，为解决仍然残留的细微语义错误，我们引入了语法感知偏好优化（SAPO）。该方法通过对脚本的抽象语法树（AST）施加单一的原子操作（例如修改某个命令选项或删除某个参数）来自动构造偏好对，从而生成正确脚本与略有错误脚本的最小对照对。这一最终优化阶段使模型能够进行细粒度的命令语义学习与依赖上下文的质量评估，显著提升了注释准确率。我们在单行 Bash 命令与多行 Bash 脚本上评估 Bash-Commenter。我们的方法优于最先进的基线，在 1,064 条单行命令上取得 33.40% BLEU-4、58.26% METEOR 和 57.03% ROUGE-L，在 1,046 个多行脚本上取得 22.15% BLEU-4、43.89% METEOR 和 32.80% ROUGE-L。此外，人工评估表明 Bash-Commenter 生成的注释在正确性、完整性与自然度方面质量更优。","tl":"用 AST 原子扰动构造最小偏好对，做语法感知偏好优化提升注释准确率。","au":["Lei Yu","Jingyuan Zhang","Xin Wang","Li Yang","Fengjun Zhang","Peng Wang","Jia Xu","Jiajia Ma"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["Bash comment generation","preference optimization","abstract syntax tree","continual pre-training","code summarization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/11/x"},{"id":"p00820","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"UNICS: Multilingual Code Search via Unified Pseudocode and Contrastive Transfer Learning","tz":"UNICS：基于统一伪代码与对比迁移学习的多语言代码搜索","a":"While pre-trained models have achieved remarkable success in code search, their multilingual capabilities remain a major hurdle, plagued by data imbalance, cross-lingual semantic interference, and the loss of critical information from existing unified representations like Abstract Syntax Trees (ASTs) or Intermediate Representations (IRs). Furthermore, conventional contrastive learning strategies often rely on simplistic hard negative sampling while overlooking the potential of mining hard positives to learn code’s intrinsic semantic invariance. To address these challenges, we introduce UNICS, a framework for multilingual code search built on a two-stage training strategy. In the first stage, UNICS is pre-trained on a novel dataset we constructed, which uses pseudo-code as a unified representation to learn a cross-lingual, algorithm-level logic that preserves full semantic fidelity. The second stage employs a multi-task transfer learning strategy that adapts this general knowledge to specific languages by decomposing code into semantic slices (e.g., API calls, function bodies) and incorporating tasks for hard positive mining and cross-lingual dynamic hard negative sampling. Experimental results demonstrate that UNICS achieves state-of-the-art performance across multiple multilingual and cross-lingual benchmarks, showcasing superior generalization and performance balance, especially in zero-shot transfer tasks to low-resource languages.","az":"尽管预训练模型在代码搜索上取得了显著成功，其多语言能力仍是一大障碍，受困于数据不平衡、跨语言语义干扰，以及抽象语法树（AST）或中间表示（IR）等已有统一表示所带来的关键信息丢失。此外，传统的对比学习策略往往依赖简单化的困难负样本采样，却忽视了挖掘困难正样本以学习代码内在语义不变性的潜力。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 UNICS，一个基于两阶段训练策略构建的多语言代码搜索框架。在第一阶段，UNICS 在我们构建的一个新数据集上进行预训练，该数据集以伪代码作为统一表示，用以学习一种保留完整语义保真度的跨语言、算法层面的逻辑。第二阶段采用多任务迁移学习策略，通过将代码分解为语义切片（例如 API 调用、函数体），并引入困难正样本挖掘与跨语言动态困难负样本采样任务，把这种通用知识适配到具体语言上。实验结果表明，UNICS 在多个多语言与跨语言基准上取得了最先进的性能，展现出优越的泛化能力与性能平衡，尤其是在面向低资源语言的零样本迁移任务中。","tl":"以伪代码作统一表示，并挖掘困难正样本提升多语言代码检索。","au":["Ye Fan","Jidong Ge","Chuanyi Li","Liguo Huang","Bin Luo"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["low-resource-or-non-english","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["multilingual code search","pseudocode representation","contrastive learning","hard positive mining","zero-shot transfer"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/12/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.27747"},{"id":"p00821","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards Automated Smart Contract Generation: Evaluation, Benchmarking, and Retrieval-Augmented Repair","tz":"迈向自动化智能合约生成：评测、基准与检索增强修复","a":"Smart contracts, predominantly written in Solidity and executed on blockchains like Ethereum, are immutable, making functional correctness paramount: once deployed, bugs and vulnerabilities become permanent. Despite rapid progress in transformer-based code LLMs, existing evaluations of Solidity code completion rely heavily on surface-form metrics (e.g., BLEU, CrystalBLEU) or hand-grading, which poorly correlate with functional correctness. Unlike Python, Solidity lacks large-scale and execution-based benchmarks, hindering systematic assessment and optimization of LLMs for smart contract development. To bridge this research gap, we introduce SolBench, a comprehensive benchmark and automated testing pipeline for Solidity, designed to emphasize functional correctness via differential fuzzing. SolBench contains 28,825 functions from 7,604 contracts collected from Etherscan (genesis–2024), spanning 10 popular domains. We benchmark 14 diverse LLMs (open/closed, 1.3B–671B parameters, general/code-specific, with/without reasoning). The dominant failure mode is missing crucial details (e.g., type definitions, state variables) in intra-contract context. Providing full-contract context mitigates this and improves code completion accuracy. However, full-context inference can be prohibitively expensive in practice. Generating outputs with large context windows using state-of-the-art models often incurs significant costs, rendering naive context scaling economically impractical. Crucially, most of a contract is irrelevant to implementing a given function; only a small subset of details is needed. To exploit this, we propose Retrieval-Augmented Repair (RAR), which integrates retrieval into code repair: it uses the executor’s error messages to extract only the most relevant snippets from the full contract. RAR sharply reduces input length for function completion, improving accuracy while significantly cutting computational cost. We further analyze retrieval and code repair strategies within RAR, showing substantial improvements in accuracy and efficiency. SolBench and our RAR framework enable principled evaluation and cost-effective improvement of Solidity code generation. Dataset and code are available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/SolBench-A144 .","az":"智能合约主要用 Solidity 编写并在以太坊等区块链上执行，具有不可变性，因此功能正确性至关重要：一旦部署，缺陷与漏洞就将永久存在。尽管基于 Transformer 的代码 LLM 进展迅速，现有对 Solidity 代码补全的评估仍严重依赖表层指标（如 BLEU、CrystalBLEU）或人工打分，而这些与功能正确性相关性很差。与 Python 不同，Solidity 缺乏大规模、基于执行的基准，阻碍了对 LLM 在智能合约开发上的系统评估与优化。为填补这一研究空白，我们提出 **SolBench**，一个面向 Solidity 的综合基准与自动化测试流水线，通过差分模糊测试强调功能正确性。SolBench 包含从 Etherscan 收集的（创世区块至 2024 年）7,604 个合约中的 28,825 个函数，覆盖 10 个热门领域。我们对 14 个多样化的 LLM（开源/闭源、1.3B–671B 参数、通用/代码专用、带/不带推理能力）进行了基准测试。主要的失败模式是在合约内上下文中遗漏关键细节（例如类型定义、状态变量）。提供完整合约上下文可以缓解这一问题并提升代码补全准确率。然而，全上下文推理在实践中可能代价高昂：用最先进模型以大上下文窗口生成输出往往带来巨大成本，使朴素的上下文扩展在经济上不可行。关键在于，合约的大部分内容与实现某个给定函数无关；只需要其中一小部分细节。为利用这一点，我们提出 **检索增强修复**（RAR），它把检索融入代码修复：利用执行器的错误信息，仅从完整合约中抽取最相关的片段。RAR 大幅缩短了函数补全的输入长度，在提升准确率的同时显著削减计算成本。我们进一步分析了 RAR 中的检索与代码修复策略，展示了在准确率与效率上的显著改进。SolBench 与我们的 RAR 框架使 Solidity 代码生成的原则性评测与低成本改进成为可能。数据集与代码见 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/SolBench-A144 。","tl":"提出执行式 Solidity 基准，并用报错驱动检索片段做低成本修复。","au":["Zaoyu Chen","Haoran Qin","Nuo Chen","Xiangyu Zhao","Lei Xue","Xiapu Luo","Xiao-Ming Wu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["Solidity code completion","SolBench","differential fuzzing","retrieval-augmented repair","smart contract generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/13/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.01098"},{"id":"p00822","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AgentBound: Securing Execution Boundaries of AI Agents","tz":"AgentBound：为 AI 智能体的执行边界提供安全保障","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have evolved into AI agents that interact with external tools and environments to perform complex tasks. The Model Context Protocol (MCP) has become the de facto standard for connecting agents with such resources, but security has lagged behind: thousands of MCP servers execute with unrestricted access to host systems, creating a broad attack surface. In this paper, we introduce AgentBound, the first access control framework for MCP servers. AgentBound combines a declarative policy mechanism, inspired by the Android permission model, with a policy enforcement engine that contains malicious behavior without requiring MCP server modifications. We build a dataset containing the 296 most popular MCP servers, and show that access control policies can be generated automatically from source code with 80.9% accuracy. We also show that AgentBound blocks the majority of security threats in several malicious MCP servers, and that policy enforcement engine introduces negligible overhead. Our contributions provide developers and project managers with a practical foundation for securing MCP servers while maintaining productivity, enabling researchers and tool builders to explore new directions for declarative access control and MCP security.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已演化为与外部工具和环境交互以完成复杂任务的 AI 智能体。模型上下文协议（MCP）已成为连接智能体与此类资源的事实标准，但安全性却明显滞后：数以千计的 MCP 服务器以不受限制的权限访问宿主系统运行，制造了广阔的攻击面。本文提出 AgentBound，首个面向 MCP 服务器的访问控制框架。AgentBound 将受 Android 权限模型启发的声明式策略机制与一个策略执行引擎结合起来，无需修改 MCP 服务器即可遏制恶意行为。我们构建了一个包含 296 个最流行 MCP 服务器的数据集，并表明访问控制策略可以从源代码自动生成，准确率达 80.9%。我们还表明，AgentBound 能阻断若干恶意 MCP 服务器中的大多数安全威胁，且策略执行引擎带来的开销可以忽略不计。我们的贡献为开发者与项目管理者提供了在保持生产力的同时保障 MCP 服务器安全的实用基础，并使研究者与工具构建者能够探索声明式访问控制与 MCP 安全的新方向。","tl":"首个 MCP 访问控制框架，可从源码自动生成权限策略并强制执行。","au":["Christoph Buehler","Matteo Biagiola","Luca Di Grazia","Guido Salvaneschi"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","agentic"],"kw":["MCP server security","access control","declarative policy","policy enforcement","AI agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/14/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3808103"},{"id":"p00823","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SmartCoder-R1: Towards Secure and Explainable Smart Contract Generation with Security-Aware Group Relative Policy Optimization","tz":"SmartCoder-R1：用安全感知的组相对策略优化实现安全且可解释的智能合约生成","a":"Smart contracts automate the management of high-value assets, where vulnerabilities can lead to catastrophic financial losses. In the task of automated smart contract generation using Large Language Models (LLMs), this challenge is amplified by two interconnected failures: first, they operate as unauditable “black boxes” by failing to produce a transparent reasoning process, and second, as a consequence, they generate code riddled with critical security vulnerabilities. To address both issues, we propose SmartCoder-R1 based on Qwen2.5-Coder-7B, a novel framework for secure and explainable smart contract generation. It begins with Continual Pre-training (CPT) to specialize the base model on the nuances of smart contract code. To construct the data for subsequent stages, we first prompt the DeepSeek model to generate reasoning-and-code samples from verified on-chain contracts, followed by a rigorous validation process where each sample is manually reviewed by security experts for compilability, functionality, security, and reasoning completeness. Based on this, we then apply Long Chain-of-Thought Supervised Fine-Tuning (L-CoT SFT) on 7,998 of these expert-validated samples to train the model to emulate human security analysis. Finally, to directly mitigate vulnerabilities, we employ Security-Aware Group Relative Policy Optimization (S-GRPO), a reinforcement learning phase that refines the generation policy using 1,691 samples by optimizing a weighted reward signal for compilation success, security compliance, and format correctness. Evaluated against 18 state-of-the-art baselines on a challenging benchmark of 756 real-world functions from 289 deployed contracts, SmartCoder-R1 establishes a new state of the art by achieving top performance across five key metrics: a ComPass of 87.70%, a VulRate of 8.60%, a SafeAval of 80.16%, a FuncRate of 53.84%, and a FullRate of 50.53%. This FullRate marks a 45.79% relative improvement over the strongest baseline, DeepSeek-R1. Crucially, its generated reasoning also excels in human evaluations, achieving high-quality ratings for Functionality (82.7%), Security (85.3%), and Clarity (90.7%).","az":"智能合约自动化管理高价值资产，其中的漏洞可能导致灾难性的财务损失。在使用大语言模型（LLM）自动生成智能合约的任务中，这一挑战被两个相互关联的失败放大：首先，它们像不可审计的“黑箱”一样运作，无法给出透明的推理过程；其次，作为其后果，它们生成的代码充斥着关键的安全漏洞。为同时解决这两个问题，我们基于 Qwen2.5-Coder-7B 提出 SmartCoder-R1，一个用于安全且可解释智能合约生成的新颖框架。它首先通过继续预训练（CPT）使基础模型专门适应智能合约代码的细微特性。为构建后续阶段所需的数据，我们先提示 DeepSeek 模型从经过验证的链上合约中生成“推理+代码”样本，随后进行严格的验证流程，由安全专家对每个样本在可编译性、功能性、安全性与推理完整性方面进行人工审查。在此基础上，我们在其中 7,998 个经专家验证的样本上应用长思维链监督微调（L-CoT SFT），训练模型模仿人类的安全分析。最后，为直接缓解漏洞，我们采用安全感知的组相对策略优化（S-GRPO），这是一个强化学习阶段，使用 1,691 个样本，通过优化编译成功、安全合规与格式正确性的加权奖励信号来精化生成策略。在一个由 289 个已部署合约中的 756 个真实函数构成的高难度基准上，与 18 个最先进基线相比，SmartCoder-R1 在五项关键指标上均取得最佳表现，确立了新的最先进水平：ComPass 87.70%、VulRate 8.60%、SafeAval 80.16%、FuncRate 53.84%、FullRate 50.53%。其中 FullRate 相对最强基线 DeepSeek-R1 实现了 45.79% 的相对提升。关键在于，其生成的推理过程在人工评估中同样出色，在功能性（82.7%）、安全性（85.3%）与清晰度（90.7%）上均获得高质量评分。","tl":"用安全感知 GRPO 与长思维链微调，让合约生成兼顾安全与可解释。","au":["Lei Yu","Jingyuan Zhang","Xin Wang","Li Yang","Fengjun Zhang","Jiajia Ma"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["smart contract generation","GRPO","secure code generation","chain-of-thought SFT","vulnerability rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/15/x"},{"id":"p00824","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"It Takes Two: Option-Aware Directed Greybox Fuzzing for Vulnerability PoC Generation","tz":"两者缺一不可：面向漏洞 PoC 生成的选项感知定向灰盒模糊测试","a":"Static analysis tools can identify potential vulnerabilities, but they often fall short in providing concrete proofs-of-concept (PoCs) to validate their findings. Directed greybox fuzzing (DGF) has emerged as a promising solution by systematically guiding execution toward suspicious code locations and generating reproducible PoCs that can trigger the target vulnerabilities. However, DGF tools often overlook the influence of configurable options on reaching target locations. Besides, option-aware greybox fuzzing (GF) tools suffer from ineffective option extraction to target locations, and inefficient coordination between options and file fuzzing. To address these limitations, we present CoupleFuzz, a novel option-aware DGF tool that redefines PoC inputs as the combination of option input (OI) and file input (FI). CoupleFuzz adopts a two-phase workflow. The static analysis phase extracts option knowledge for guiding the fuzzing. The option-aware fuzzing phase employs taint analysis to dynamically prioritize effective option combinations and file bytes to target locations, and introduces a novel cross-guided fuzzing strategy that coordinates OI and FI fuzzing modules and enables each module to adapt to and benefit from its counterpart’s advances, iteratively driving execution toward the target locations efficiently. Our evaluation has demonstrated that CoupleFuzz significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art DGF tools in generating PoCs for 22 real-world vulnerabilities, generating 15 (a 3.1 improvement) more PoCs than the best traditional DGF baseline and achieves an average speedup of 5.6 to reach target locations, with 6 0-day vulnerabilities confirmed by developers and 1 CVE identifier assigned.","az":"静态分析工具可以识别潜在漏洞，但往往无法提供具体的概念验证（PoC）来验证其发现。定向灰盒模糊测试（DGF）作为一种有前景的解决方案应运而生，它系统性地引导执行走向可疑代码位置，并生成可复现、能触发目标漏洞的 PoC。然而，DGF 工具常常忽视可配置选项对到达目标位置的影响。此外，选项感知的灰盒模糊测试（GF）工具存在面向目标位置的选项抽取无效、以及选项与文件模糊测试之间协同低效的问题。为解决这些局限，我们提出 CoupleFuzz，一种新颖的选项感知 DGF 工具，它把 PoC 输入重新定义为选项输入（OI）与文件输入（FI）的组合。CoupleFuzz 采用两阶段工作流。静态分析阶段抽取用于指导模糊测试的选项知识。选项感知模糊测试阶段使用污点分析动态地对通往目标位置的有效选项组合与文件字节排定优先级，并引入一种新颖的“交叉引导模糊测试”策略，协调 OI 与 FI 两个模糊测试模块，使各模块能够适应并受益于对方的进展，从而迭代地高效驱动执行走向目标位置。我们的评估表明，在为 22 个真实世界漏洞生成 PoC 方面，CoupleFuzz 显著优于最先进的 DGF 工具：比最好的传统 DGF 基线多生成 15 个（提升 3.1 倍）PoC，到达目标位置的平均加速比为 5.6 倍，并有 6 个 0-day 漏洞得到开发者确认、1 个获得 CVE 编号。","tl":"把命令行选项与文件输入耦合起来交叉引导，加速定向模糊测试到达目标。","au":["Susheng Wu","Xin Hu","Yiheng Cao","Zhuotong Zhou","Yiheng Huang","Yijian Wu","Bihuan Chen","Zhijia Zhao","Xin Peng"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["directed greybox fuzzing","proof-of-concept generation","option-aware fuzzing","taint analysis","cross-guided fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/16/x"},{"id":"p00825","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fairness Testing of Large Language Models in Role-Playing","tz":"大语言模型角色扮演中的公平性测试","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have become foundational in modern language-driven software applications, profoundly influencing daily life. A critical technique in leveraging their potential is role-playing, where LLMs simulate diverse roles to enhance their real-world utility. However, while research has highlighted the presence of social biases in LLM outputs, it remains unclear whether and to what extent these biases emerge during role-playing scenarios. In this paper, we conduct an empirical study on fairness testing of LLMs in role-playing scenarios. To enable this testing, we use LLMs to generate 550 social roles spanning a comprehensive set of 11 demographic attributes, producing 33,000 role-specific questions that target various forms of bias. These questions, covering Yes/No, multiple-choice, and open-ended formats, are designed to prompt LLMs to adopt specific roles and respond accordingly. We employ a combination of rule-based and LLM-based strategies to identify biased responses, rigorously validated through human evaluation. Using the generated questions as the test cases, we conduct extensive evaluations of 10 advanced LLMs. The evaluation reveal 107,580 biased responses across the studied LLMs, with individual models yielding between 7,579 and 16,963 biased responses, underscoring the prevalence of bias in role-playing contexts. To support future research, we have publicly released the dataset, along with all scripts and experimental results.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已成为现代语言驱动软件应用的基础，深刻影响着日常生活。发挥其潜力的一项关键技术是角色扮演，即让 LLM 模拟多样角色以增强其在现实世界中的效用。然而，尽管已有研究强调 LLM 输出中存在社会偏见，这些偏见是否以及在多大程度上会在角色扮演场景中显现仍不清楚。本文针对角色扮演场景下 LLM 的公平性测试开展了一项实证研究。为支持该测试，我们使用 LLM 生成了覆盖 11 种人口统计属性的 550 个社会角色，并据此产生 33,000 个针对各种偏见形式的角色特定问题。这些问题涵盖是/否题、多选题和开放式题型，旨在促使 LLM 扮演特定角色并据此作答。我们结合基于规则与基于 LLM 的策略来识别带偏见的回答，并通过人工评估进行严格验证。以生成的问题作为测试用例，我们对 10 个先进 LLM 进行了广泛评估。评估在所研究的各 LLM 中揭示出 107,580 条带偏见的回答，单个模型产生 7,579 至 16,963 条带偏见回答，凸显了角色扮演情境中偏见的普遍性。为支持未来研究，我们已公开发布该数据集以及全部脚本与实验结果。","tl":"构建 550 角色、3.3 万问题的测试集，揭示角色扮演下偏见普遍存在。","au":["Xinyue Li","Zhenpeng Chen","Jie M. Zhang","Ying Xiao","Li Tianlin","Weisong Sun","Yang Liu","Yiling Lou","Xuanzhe Liu"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["cross-track-bridge","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["fairness testing","role-playing","social bias","LLM evaluation","demographic attributes"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/17/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2411.00585"},{"id":"p00826","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Exorcist: Enabling Atomic-Level Runtime Detection of Spectre Attacks Using Precise Event Based Sampling","tz":"Exorcist：利用精确事件采样（PEBS）实现原子级的 Spectre 攻击运行时检测","a":"While being key hardware techniques for improving the performance of modern processors, the speculative execution mechanisms also lead to side-channel attacks, which pose significant threats to the security of computer systems. While researchers have proposed various solutions to mitigate the threat posed by speculative attacks, most existing approaches have focused on offline static vulnerability analysis, which suffers from significant limitations of incompleteness and poor scalability. Based on Intel’s Precise Event Based Sampling (PEBS) technique, this paper proposes Exorcist, a novel runtime framework for detecting Spectre-PHT attacks at the atomic level. Leveraging the key observation that the atomic execution of a Spectre-PHT gadget triggers both a cache miss and a branch mis-precision in a fixed sequence, Exorcist uses carefully configured PEBS monitoring to efficiently capture all related fine-grained hardware performance events, then launches a kernel- and user-level collaborated taint analysis to effectively pinpoint Spectre-PHT gadgets that have actually exploited vulnerable speculative executions. Our approach significantly reduces the amount of native instructions needed to be processed to confirm actual Spectre exploitation, making it capable of achieving high accuracy and a negligible false positive rate with second-level response time. We have implemented a prototype of Exorcist and performed a comprehensive evaluation on it. Experimental results indicate that Exorcist can efficiently detect Spectre-PHT attacks at runtime with acceptable performance overhead, including JIT-compiled Spectre-PHT payloads written in JavaScript that are beyond the reach of existing offline analysis-based approaches.","az":"推测执行机制是提升现代处理器性能的关键硬件技术，但它同时也导致了侧信道攻击，对计算机系统安全构成重大威胁。尽管研究者已提出多种方案缓解推测执行攻击的威胁，但现有方法大多聚焦于离线静态漏洞分析，存在不完备性与可扩展性差的显著局限。本文基于 Intel 的精确事件采样（Precise Event Based Sampling，PEBS）技术，提出 Exorcist，一个在原子级别检测 Spectre-PHT 攻击的新型运行时框架。我们的关键观察是：Spectre-PHT gadget 的原子化执行会以固定次序同时触发一次缓存未命中和一次分支预测失误。基于此，Exorcist 通过精心配置的 PEBS 监控高效捕获所有相关的细粒度硬件性能事件，随后启动内核态与用户态协同的污点分析，有效定位真正利用了脆弱推测执行的 Spectre-PHT gadget。我们的方法显著减少了确认真实 Spectre 利用所需处理的原生指令数量，从而在秒级响应时间内实现高准确率和可忽略的误报率。我们实现了 Exorcist 原型并进行了全面评估。实验结果表明，Exorcist 能够在可接受的性能开销下于运行时高效检测 Spectre-PHT 攻击，其中包括用 JavaScript 编写、经 JIT 编译的 Spectre-PHT 载荷——这类攻击是现有基于离线分析的方法无法覆盖的。","tl":"用 PEBS 硬件事件序列加协同污点分析，原子级实时确认 Spectre 真实利用。","au":["Hao Jia","Haoyu Ma","Changfeng Ding","Jinku Li"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Spectre","speculative execution","PEBS","runtime detection","taint analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/18/x"},{"id":"p00827","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"MetaRCA: A Generalizable Root Cause Analysis Framework for Cloud-Native Systems Powered by Meta Causal Knowledge","tz":"MetaRCA：由元因果知识驱动的云原生系统通用根因分析框架","a":"The dynamics and complexity of cloud-native systems present significant challenges for Root Cause Analysis (RCA). While causality-based RCA methods have shown significant progress in recent years, their practical adoption is fundamentally limited by three intertwined challenges: poor scalability against system complexity, brittle generalization across different system topologies, and inadequate integration of domain knowledge. These limitations create a vicious cycle, hindering the development of robust and efficient RCA solutions. This paper introduces MetaRCA, a generalizable RCA framework for cloud-native systems. MetaRCA first constructs a Meta Causal Graph (MCG) offline, a reusable knowledge base defined at the metadata level. To build the MCG, we propose an evidence-driven algorithm that systematically fuses knowledge from Large Language Models (LLMs), historical fault reports, and observability data. When a fault occurs, MetaRCA performs a lightweight online inference by dynamically instantiating the MCG into a localized graph based on the current context, and then leverages real-time data to weight and prune causal links for precise root cause localization. Evaluated on 252 public and 59 production failures, MetaRCA demonstrates state-of-the-art performance. It surpasses the strongest baseline by 29 percentage points in service-level and 48 percentage points in metric-level accuracy. This performance advantage widens as system complexity increases, with its overhead scaling near-linearly. Crucially, MetaRCA shows robust cross-system generalization, maintaining over 80% accuracy across diverse systems.","az":"云原生系统的动态性与复杂性给根因分析（RCA）带来了巨大挑战。尽管基于因果关系的 RCA 方法近年来取得显著进展，其实际落地仍受三个相互交织的挑战制约：面对系统复杂度时可扩展性差、跨不同系统拓扑时泛化能力脆弱、以及领域知识整合不足。这些局限形成恶性循环，阻碍了鲁棒且高效的 RCA 方案的发展。本文提出 MetaRCA，一个面向云原生系统的通用 RCA 框架。MetaRCA 首先离线构建元因果图（Meta Causal Graph，MCG），这是一个在元数据层面定义的可复用知识库。为构建 MCG，我们提出一种证据驱动的算法，系统性地融合来自大语言模型（LLM）、历史故障报告与可观测性数据的知识。当故障发生时，MetaRCA 执行轻量级在线推理：根据当前上下文将 MCG 动态实例化为局部图，再利用实时数据对因果边加权与剪枝，实现精确的根因定位。在 252 个公开故障与 59 个生产故障上的评测表明，MetaRCA 达到了当前最优性能：在服务级准确率上超越最强基线 29 个百分点，在指标级准确率上超越 48 个百分点。随着系统复杂度上升，该优势进一步扩大，而其开销近似线性增长。尤为重要的是，MetaRCA 展现出稳健的跨系统泛化能力，在多种不同系统上保持 80% 以上的准确率。","tl":"离线元因果图加在线实例化，使根因分析可跨系统复用。","au":["Shuai Liang","Pengfei Chen","Bozhe Tian","Gou Tan","Maohong Xu","Youjun Qu","Yahui Zhao","Yiduo Shang","Chongkang Tan"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["root cause analysis","cloud-native","causal graph","observability","incident diagnosis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/19/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.02032"},{"id":"p00828","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"V2E: Validating Smart Contract Vulnerabilities through Profit-driven Exploit Generation and Execution","tz":"V2E：通过盈利驱动的漏洞利用生成与执行来验证智能合约漏洞","a":"Smart contracts are a critical component of blockchain systems. Due to the large amount of digital assets carried by smart contracts, their security is of critical importance. Although numerous tools have been developed for detecting smart contract vulnerability, their effectiveness remains limited, particularly due to the high false positives included in the reported results. Therefore, developers and auditors are often overwhelmed with manually verifying the reported issues. A fundamental reason behind this is that while a reported vulnerability satisfies specific vulnerable patterns, it may not actually be exploitable, either because the vulnerable code cannot be triggered or it does not result in any financial loss. In this paper, we propose V2E, a new framework for validating whether a reported vulnerability is truly exploitable. The core idea of V2E is to automatically generate executable Proof-of-Concept Exploit (PoC for short), and then assess if the vulnerability could be triggered and incur any real damage (i.e., causing financial loss) by the PoC. While LLMs have shown proficiency in PoC generation, achieving our task is by no means trivial. In detail, it is difficult for LLM to: (1) generate and update PoC to trigger a specific vulnerability, (2) evaluate the PoC’s effectiveness to validate exploitable vulnerability. To this end, V2E automates the whole process through a novel combination of PoC generation, validation, and refinement: (1) Firstly, V2E generates targeted PoCs by analyzing potential vulnerability paths. (2) Then, V2E verifies the validity of PoCs through triggerability and profitability analysis. (3) In addition, V2E iteratively refines the generated PoC based on PoC execution feedback, therefore, increasing the chance to confirm the vulnerability. Evaluation on 264 manually labeled contracts shows that V2E outperforms the baseline approach. Particularly, V2E successfully identifies 102 out of 124 exploitable vulnerabilities, achieving a precision of 91.9% and a recall of 82.3%. In addition, it successfully eliminates 71 out of 140 false alarms (50.7%). Besides, V2E effectively enhances the performance of SOTA tools. It reduces the false positive rates of Slither by 76.9%, Mythril by 56.9% and Confuzzius by 65%.","az":"智能合约是区块链系统的关键组成部分。由于智能合约承载了大量数字资产，其安全性至关重要。尽管已有大量工具用于检测智能合约漏洞，但其有效性仍然有限，尤其是报告结果中误报率很高。因此，开发者与审计人员常常疲于人工核验所报告的问题。其根本原因在于：一个被报告的漏洞虽然满足特定的脆弱模式，却未必真正可被利用——可能是脆弱代码无法被触发，也可能是触发后并不造成任何资金损失。本文提出 V2E，一个用于验证所报漏洞是否真正可利用的新框架。V2E 的核心思想是自动生成可执行的概念验证漏洞利用（Proof-of-Concept Exploit，简称 PoC），随后通过该 PoC 评估漏洞能否被触发并造成实际损害（即引发资金损失）。尽管 LLM 在 PoC 生成上已展现出能力，完成这一任务绝非易事。具体而言，LLM 难以：(1) 生成并迭代更新 PoC 以触发特定漏洞；(2) 评估 PoC 的有效性以验证漏洞可利用性。为此，V2E 通过 PoC 生成、验证与精化的新颖组合实现全流程自动化：(1) 首先，V2E 通过分析潜在漏洞路径生成有针对性的 PoC；(2) 然后，V2E 通过可触发性与盈利性分析验证 PoC 的有效性；(3) 此外，V2E 基于 PoC 执行反馈迭代精化生成的 PoC，从而提高确认漏洞的成功率。在 264 个人工标注的合约上的评测表明，V2E 优于基线方法。特别地，V2E 成功识别出 124 个可利用漏洞中的 102 个，精确率达 91.9%，召回率达 82.3%。此外，它成功消除了 140 个误报中的 71 个（50.7%）。同时，V2E 有效提升了当前最优工具的表现：将 Slither 的误报率降低 76.9%，Mythril 降低 56.9%，Confuzzius 降低 65%。","tl":"以“能否触发且能否获利”为判据自动生成 PoC，过滤合约漏洞误报。","au":["Jingwen Zhang","Yuhong Nan","Kaiwen Ning","Mingxi Ye","Wei Li","Yuming Xiao","Yuming Feng","Weizhe Zhang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract","exploit generation","proof-of-concept","false positive reduction","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/20/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13611"},{"id":"p00829","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Eidolon: Perform Noise-Aware Fuzzing on FHE Libraries via Equivalence Expression Transformation","tz":"Eidolon：通过等价表达式变换对 FHE 库进行噪声感知的模糊测试","a":"Ensuring data privacy during computation is a critical challenge in many security systems. Fully Homomorphic Encryption (FHE) addresses this gap by enabling multiple operations on encrypted data without decryption, thus ensuring privacy is preserved throughout computation. However, existing cryptographic testing tools are unable to test the core functionality of FHE, which is the execution of computations on encrypted data. They are expertly designed to generate structured data for testing cryptographic algorithms. This structural mismatch, combined with a lack of awareness of FHE-specific noise management, leads them to generate invalid test inputs that fail to probe FHE libraries’ core logic. To address this gap, we propose Eidolon, a noise-aware fuzzer. It directs mutations toward arithmetic expressions that explore the computational space defined by the noise budget. As its test oracle, Eidolon leverages Equivalence Expressions Transformation, which transforms a standard arithmetic expression into two mathematically identical but structurally different forms (e.g., Factored, Horner) to detect inconsistencies in their outputs. We evaluated Eidolon on SEAL, OpenFHE, HELib, and TFHE. Compared with existing cryptographic fuzzers, Eidolon achieves 39.2%, 61.0%, and 99.0% higher final code coverage than CLFuzz, Cryptofuzz, and CDF, respectively. In total, Eidolon uncovered 20 previously unknown bugs, 10 of which have been fixed and 12 assigned CVEs.","az":"在计算过程中保障数据隐私是许多安全系统面临的关键挑战。全同态加密（FHE）通过允许在不解密的情况下对加密数据执行多种运算来填补这一空白，从而在整个计算过程中保持隐私。然而，现有的密码学测试工具无法测试 FHE 的核心功能，即在加密数据上执行计算。这些工具是为生成结构化数据以测试密码算法而专门设计的。这种结构上的不匹配，加上对 FHE 特有噪声管理的缺乏感知，导致它们生成无效的测试输入，无法触及 FHE 库的核心逻辑。为填补这一空白，我们提出 Eidolon，一个噪声感知的模糊测试器。它将变异导向那些在噪声预算所定义的计算空间中进行探索的算术表达式。作为测试预言，Eidolon 采用等价表达式变换（Equivalence Expressions Transformation），将标准算术表达式转换为两种数学上等价但结构不同的形式（例如因式分解形式、Horner 形式），以检测二者输出之间的不一致。我们在 SEAL、OpenFHE、HELib 和 TFHE 上评估了 Eidolon。与现有密码学模糊测试器相比，Eidolon 的最终代码覆盖率分别比 CLFuzz、Cryptofuzz 和 CDF 高 39.2%、61.0% 和 99.0%。Eidolon 总共发现了 20 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 10 个已被修复，12 个已分配 CVE 编号。","tl":"以噪声预算引导变异、用等价表达式差分做预言测 FHE 库。","au":["Zhensheng Xian","Zhen Yan","Yuanliang Chen","Xuelian Cao","Fuchen Ma","Dalong Shi","Yu Jiang"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["fully homomorphic encryption","fuzzing","noise budget","equivalence transformation","differential oracle"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/21/x"},{"id":"p00830","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Denoising Fault Localization with Test Line Proximity","tz":"用测试行邻近度为缺陷定位去噪","a":"When a program fails, statistical fault localization (SFL) provides important debugging hints by identifying the locations whose execution most correlates with failures. However, such correlations can be weakened if a test contains both passing and failing assertions, creating ambiguous and misleading associations. Likewise, if multiple lines correlate with the same strength, SFL provides little guidance to disambiguate between them. This paper proposes a novel proximity-based weighting scheme for SFL that assigns different weights to locations in the test subject based on temporal proximity to a failure. The more recently a subject line is executed before the test fails, the higher its weight. We operationalize a known heuristic into a lightweight statistical form compatible with existing SFL formulas. Our approach applies to any test , from simple single-line tests (where it preserves SFL behavior), to single-assertion tests with multiple lines (where it benefits from temporal proximity), to complex multi-assertion tests (where it provides the most benefit by distinguishing failing from passing assertions). Once computed, the weights can be integrated into any existing SFL technique. Our evaluation of proximity-weighted fault localization on 310~real-world programs shows that it consistently outperforms fault localization techniques across all test types. Proximity-weighted fault localization shows per-subject relative improvements of 200%–400%, meaning that, for a typical subject, it provides 3 to 5 times the baseline effectiveness. These improvements represent substantial gains over baseline techniques. Our approach can be integrated into existing fault localization techniques to improve performance, making it a valuable addition to automated debugging.","az":"当程序失败时，统计缺陷定位（SFL）通过识别执行与失败最相关的位置，为调试提供重要线索。然而，如果一个测试同时包含通过与失败的断言，这种相关性会被削弱，从而产生含糊且具误导性的关联。同样，当多行代码的相关强度相同时，SFL 几乎无法给出区分它们的指引。本文提出一种新颖的基于邻近度的 SFL 加权方案，依据与失败在时间上的邻近程度，为被测对象中的各个位置赋予不同权重：某一行在测试失败前被执行得越近，其权重越高。我们将一个已知的启发式规则转化为轻量的统计形式，使之与现有的 SFL 公式兼容。我们的方法适用于任何测试：从简单的单行测试（此时它保持原有 SFL 行为），到包含多行的单断言测试（此时它受益于时间邻近性），再到复杂的多断言测试（此时它通过区分失败断言与通过断言带来最大收益）。权重一旦计算完成，即可集成到任何已有的 SFL 技术中。我们在 310 个真实世界程序上对邻近度加权的缺陷定位进行评估，结果表明它在所有测试类型上都持续优于现有缺陷定位技术。邻近度加权的缺陷定位在单个被测对象上带来 200%–400% 的相对提升，意味着对典型被测对象而言其效果可达基线的 3 至 5 倍。这些提升相较基线技术是实质性的进步。我们的方法可以集成进现有缺陷定位技术以提升性能，是自动化调试的有价值补充。","tl":"按执行行与失败点的时间邻近度加权，显著提升统计缺陷定位。","au":["Marius Smytzek","Andreas Zeller"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["statistical fault localization","proximity weighting","assertions","debugging","suspiciousness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/22/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808110"},{"id":"p00831","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CrossFit: Demystifying VM Callback Bugs in Interpreters","tz":"CrossFit：揭示解释器中的虚拟机回调缺陷","a":"Scripting languages like Python, Ruby, and PHP are integral to modern software development. Despite security measures like memory safety and sandboxing, vulnerabilities within these engines can lead to critical issues such as remote code execution or sandbox escapes. A particularly pervasive class of vulnerabilities is callback bugs, which occur when user-defined callbacks violate runtime invariants, such as freeing an internal object still in use or modifying a data structure during traversal. These violations can result in severe consequences, including use-after-free, null-pointer dereferences, and type confusion, often leading to crashes, memory corruption, or even exploitable vulnerabilities. Detecting callback bugs remains challenging due to a lack of general understanding, as they have not been formally characterized or systematically studied. As such, existing tools lack the ability to (1) establish clear links between script-side callbacks and their native-side invokers, and (2) generate scripts that systematically satisfy preconditions required to trigger these bugs. We propose CrossFit, a novel 2-tier approach combining static analysis and targeted fuzzing to systemati- cally detect callback bugs. CrossFit first establishes links between script-side callbacks and their native-side invokers through context link analysis, enabling targeted exploration of high-risk code paths. It then generates proof-of-concept scripts with custom classes and magic methods, introducing side-effect operations to violate runtime invariants. Our evaluation shows that CrossFit effectively outperforms existing tools by up to 12.04% in terms of callsite coverage (i.e., potential sites where callback bugs may occur). We also identified 20 new bugs in PHP, Python, and Ruby, many of which are severe memory corruptions. Moreover, we provide a comprehensive benchmark totaling 150 proof-of-concepts to improve interpreter security","az":"Python、Ruby、PHP 等脚本语言是现代软件开发不可或缺的部分。尽管有内存安全与沙箱等安全措施，这些引擎内部的漏洞仍可能导致远程代码执行或沙箱逃逸等严重问题。一类尤为普遍的漏洞是回调缺陷（callback bugs），它发生在用户自定义回调违反运行时不变量时，例如释放一个仍在使用的内部对象，或在遍历过程中修改数据结构。这些违规会造成严重后果，包括释放后使用、空指针解引用和类型混淆，常常导致崩溃、内存破坏乃至可被利用的漏洞。由于缺乏总体性的理解——此类缺陷尚未被形式化刻画或系统研究——检测回调缺陷仍然困难。因此，现有工具无法做到：(1) 在脚本侧回调与其原生侧调用方之间建立清晰关联；(2) 系统性地生成满足触发这些缺陷所需前置条件的脚本。我们提出 CrossFit，一种结合静态分析与定向模糊测试的两层新方法，用于系统性检测回调缺陷。CrossFit 首先通过上下文链接分析，建立脚本侧回调与原生侧调用方之间的关联，从而实现对高风险代码路径的定向探索；随后生成带有自定义类与魔术方法的概念验证脚本，引入副作用操作以破坏运行时不变量。评测表明，CrossFit 在调用点覆盖率（即可能发生回调缺陷的潜在位置）上比现有工具最多高出 12.04%。我们还在 PHP、Python 和 Ruby 中发现了 20 个新缺陷，其中许多是严重的内存破坏问题。此外，我们提供了一个包含 150 个概念验证的综合基准，以促进解释器安全性研究。","tl":"首次系统刻画解释器回调缺陷，并用上下文链接分析定向触发。","au":["Chibin Zhang","Qiang Liu","Mathias Payer"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["security","benchmark-dataset","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["interpreter security","callback bugs","static analysis","directed fuzzing","memory corruption"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/23/x"},{"id":"p00832","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Mitigating the Risk of Defects and Improving Knowledge Distribution with Code Reviewer Recommenders","tz":"用代码评审者推荐系统降低缺陷风险并改善知识分布","a":"Defects are inevitable in software projects, leading to increased maintenance costs, user dissatisfaction, and a diminished software reputation. Code review is one of the most critical software quality assurance activities that reduces software defects and improves software quality. Prior works have quantified the impact of reviewer recommenders on the risk of inducing new defects based on the highest level of expertise among the developers in the reviewer team. However, our analysis shows that prior work overestimates the safety of a change and ignores the defect-finding effectiveness of the diverse knowledge of reviewers. In this study, we incorporate the knowledge of the entire reviewer team into the author’s level of expertise and introduce the novel Contribution-aware Changeset Safety Ratio (CCSR) outcome to assess the impact of code reviewer recommenders on the risk of inducing defects more accurately. When a pull request is risky, a natural mitigation is to add an expert reviewer. We are unaware of any works that have quantified the impact of adding a reviewer to risky PRs. We propose the novel AddExpertRec(D t ) strategy that recommends an additional expert reviewer for defect-prone pull requests to reduce the likelihood of introducing new defects when the risk is above the threshold D t . The simulation results show that AddExpertRec(D t ) can enhance the defect finding effectiveness of existing recommenders while still balancing reviewer workload and spreading knowledge to reduce the impact of turnover. Ultimately, our results give managers the ability to select a recommender strategy that best suits their project needs based on their resource constraints. The scripts and data are available in our replication package.","az":"软件项目中缺陷不可避免，会带来维护成本上升、用户不满以及软件声誉受损。代码评审是最关键的软件质量保障活动之一，可减少软件缺陷并提升软件质量。已有工作基于评审团队中开发者的最高专业水平，量化了评审者推荐系统对引入新缺陷风险的影响。然而，我们的分析表明，先前工作高估了变更的安全性，并忽略了评审者多元知识所带来的缺陷发现效力。在本研究中，我们将整个评审团队的知识纳入作者的专业水平之中，并提出新颖的“贡献感知变更集安全比”（Contribution-aware Changeset Safety Ratio，CCSR）指标，以更准确地评估代码评审者推荐系统对引入缺陷风险的影响。当某个拉取请求（PR）具有风险时，一种自然的缓解手段是增加一位专家评审者。据我们所知，尚无工作量化过为高风险 PR 增加评审者所带来的影响。我们提出新颖的 AddExpertRec(D t ) 策略：当风险高于阈值 D t 时，为缺陷易发的拉取请求推荐一位额外的专家评审者，以降低引入新缺陷的可能性。模拟结果表明，AddExpertRec(D t ) 能够增强现有推荐系统的缺陷发现效力，同时仍能平衡评审者工作负载并传播知识，以减轻人员流失的影响。最终，我们的结果使管理者能够依据资源约束选择最契合项目需求的推荐策略。相关脚本与数据已在复现包中提供。","tl":"提出 CCSR 指标并为高风险 PR 增派专家评审者的推荐策略。","au":["Mohammadali Sefidi Esfahani","Peter Rigby"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["code review","reviewer recommendation","defect risk","knowledge distribution","pull request"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/24/x","pu":"https://users.encs.concordia.ca/~pcr/paper/Sofia_Change_Safety_Ratio.pdf"},{"id":"p00833","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"WalleTruth: Visual-oriented Software Testing for Web3 Wallet Browser Extensions","tz":"WalleTruth：面向 Web3 钱包浏览器扩展的可视化导向软件测试","a":"Serving as the first touch point for users to the cryptocurrency world, cryptocurrency wallets allow users to manage, receive, and transmit digital assets on blockchains and interact with emerging decentralized finance (DeFi) applications. Unfortunately, cryptocurrency wallets have always been the prime targets for attackers, and incidents of wallet breaches have been reported from time to time. Although some recent studies have characterized the vulnerabilities and scams related to wallets, they have generally been characterized in coarse granularity, overlooking potential risks inherent in detailed designs of cryptocurrency wallets, especially from perspectives including user interaction and advanced features. To fill the void, in this paper, we present a fine-grained security analysis on browser-based cryptocurrency wallets. To pinpoint security issues of components in wallets, we design Walletruth, a visual-oriented testing framework specifically for browser-based wallet extensions. We have identified 12 attack vectors that can be abused by attackers to exploit cryptocurrency wallets and exposed 21 concrete attack strategies. By applying Walletruth on 39 widely-adopted browser-based wallet extensions, we astonishingly figure out all of them can be abused to steal crypto assets from innocent users. Identified potential attack vectors were reported to developers timely and 26 issues have been patched already. It is, hence, urgent for our community to take action to mitigate threats related to cryptocurrency wallets.","az":"作为用户接触加密货币世界的第一触点，加密货币钱包让用户得以在区块链上管理、接收与转移数字资产，并与新兴的去中心化金融（DeFi）应用交互。遗憾的是，加密货币钱包一直是攻击者的首要目标，钱包被攻破的事件时有报道。尽管近期已有研究刻画了与钱包相关的漏洞与骗局，但它们通常粒度较粗，忽略了加密货币钱包精细设计中固有的潜在风险，尤其是在用户交互与高级功能等方面。为填补这一空白，本文对基于浏览器的加密货币钱包进行细粒度安全分析。为定位钱包各组件中的安全问题，我们设计了 Walletruth，一个专门面向浏览器钱包扩展的可视化导向测试框架。我们识别出 12 类可被攻击者滥用以攻击加密货币钱包的攻击向量，并揭示了 21 种具体攻击策略。将 Walletruth 应用于 39 款被广泛采用的浏览器钱包扩展后，我们惊讶地发现它们全部都可被滥用以窃取无辜用户的加密资产。所识别的潜在攻击向量已及时报告给开发者，其中 26 个问题已被修复。因此，业界亟需采取行动以缓解与加密货币钱包相关的威胁。","tl":"可视化测试框架系统挖掘浏览器钱包的 12 类攻击向量。","au":["Xiaohui Hu","Ningyu He","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["cryptocurrency wallet","browser extension","visual testing","attack vectors","Web3 security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/25/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797150"},{"id":"p00834","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Detecting Code-Comment Inconsistencies in Smart Contracts by Combining LLM and Program Analysis","tz":"结合 LLM 与程序分析检测智能合约中的代码-注释不一致","a":"Smart contracts have attracted rapid development and widespread application. Due to the complexity of real-world smart contracts, it is error-prone to correctly enforce all intended functionalities in code implementations, resulting in unintended functional behaviors and security issues in practice. Code-comment inconsistency detection has emerged as an important solution to these issues, which leverages the redundant functional specifications in comments to detect code implementations that violate developers’ intentions. However, existing inconsistency detection solutions are typically pattern-based and limited to fixed types of inconsistencies, which prevents them from detecting the diverse inconsistencies between real-world code implementations and casually written comments. To bridge the gap, this paper presents SmartComment, the first technique that combines LLMs with program analysis techniques for detecting code-comment inconsistencies in smart contracts. SmartComment introduces an LLM-driven workflow which simulates real-world interactions between code reviewers and developers to identify inconsistencies. It incorporates various program analysis techniques into the workflow, including comment propagation and code context extraction for generating input context for inconsistency detection, as well as program variant generation and differential analysis for inconsistency confirmation. Our evaluation results show that SmartComment detects 203 valid inconsistencies from a dataset of 1,000 real-world contracts with a precision of 79.9%, highlighting its effectiveness in detecting prevalent and diverse real-world inconsistencies. Compared to previous work, SmartComment achieves both higher precision and recall, detecting over 90% of inconsistencies that existing methods fail to identify. Furthermore, an ablation experiment demonstrates the effectiveness of incorporating program analysis techniques into SmartComment, improving the F1-score from 58.7% to 81.3%.","az":"智能合约发展迅速、应用广泛。由于真实世界智能合约的复杂性，在代码实现中正确落实所有预期功能极易出错，实践中会导致非预期的功能行为与安全问题。代码-注释不一致检测已成为解决这些问题的重要途径，它利用注释中冗余的功能规约来发现违背开发者意图的代码实现。然而，现有的不一致检测方案通常基于模式匹配，且局限于固定类型的不一致，使其无法检测真实代码实现与随意撰写的注释之间多种多样的不一致。为弥合这一差距，本文提出 SmartComment，这是首个将 LLM 与程序分析技术相结合、用于检测智能合约代码-注释不一致的技术。SmartComment 引入了一个由 LLM 驱动的工作流，模拟真实世界中代码评审者与开发者之间的交互以识别不一致。该工作流融合了多种程序分析技术，包括用于生成不一致检测输入上下文的注释传播与代码上下文抽取，以及用于确认不一致的程序变体生成与差分分析。评测结果表明，SmartComment 在 1000 个真实合约的数据集上检测出 203 个有效不一致，精确率为 79.9%，凸显了其在检测普遍且多样的真实不一致上的有效性。与先前工作相比，SmartComment 在精确率与召回率上均更高，检出了超过 90% 现有方法无法识别的不一致。此外，消融实验表明，将程序分析技术融入 SmartComment 是有效的，使 F1 值从 58.7% 提升至 81.3%。","tl":"用 LLM 模拟评审对话并以程序变体差分确认注释与代码的不一致。","au":["Jiashuo Zhang","Jiachi Chen","Ting Zhang","Yue Li","Daoyuan Wu","Yanlin Wang","Jianbo Gao","Ting Chen","Zhong Chen"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract","code-comment inconsistency","program analysis","LLM workflow","differential analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/26/x"},{"id":"p00835","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Precondition Synthesis for Deep Neural Networks with Statistical Guarantees","tz":"为深度神经网络合成带统计保证的前置条件","a":"Deep neural networks (DNNs) are increasingly being deployed in safety-critical systems. However, existing formal verification methods provide limited quantitative guarantees for their reliable specification, and emerging precondition synthesis techniques are hindered by the scalability and architectural limitations of DNNs. In this paper, we propose a select-and-solve framework, StatPre, to automatically synthesize preconditions with statistical guarantees. StatPre aims to maximally weaken the synthesized preconditions while keeping them as accurate as possible to the real preconditions through a Box-based abstraction. The framework operates in two phases: the center selection phase, which identifies potential center points using a cluster-based heuristic with potential assessment, and the expansion solution phase, which solves the problem of optimizing maximal preconditions by employing statistical model approximation, equivalent constraint transformation, and automatic iterative execution. We evaluated StatPre on 15 models with 27 properties from 6 benchmarks and compared it with 4 existing deterministic and statistical schemes. The results demonstrate that StatPre effectively synthesizes preconditions with broader coverage while accurately approximating the real preconditions in practice. Additionally, StatPre exhibits competitive performance in handling high-dimensional, non-ReLU, complex-structured neural networks.","az":"深度神经网络（DNN）正越来越多地部署在安全攸关系统中。然而，现有的形式化验证方法对其可靠规约只能提供有限的定量保证，而新兴的前置条件合成技术又受到 DNN 可扩展性与架构方面的限制。本文提出一个“选择-求解”框架 StatPre，用于自动合成带统计保证的前置条件。StatPre 旨在通过基于 Box 的抽象，在尽可能贴近真实前置条件的同时最大程度地放宽所合成的前置条件。该框架分两个阶段运行：中心选择阶段，采用带潜力评估的聚类启发式来识别潜在的中心点；扩张求解阶段，通过统计模型近似、等价约束变换与自动迭代执行，求解最大化前置条件的优化问题。我们在来自 6 个基准的 15 个模型、27 条性质上评估了 StatPre，并与 4 种已有的确定性与统计性方案进行比较。结果表明，StatPre 能够有效合成覆盖更广的前置条件，同时在实践中准确逼近真实前置条件。此外，StatPre 在处理高维、非 ReLU、结构复杂的神经网络时也展现出有竞争力的性能。","tl":"用聚类选中心加统计近似求解，合成尽可能弱的 DNN 前置条件。","au":["Zengyu Liu","Bai Xue","Pengfei Yang","Ji Wang"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["precondition synthesis","neural network verification","statistical guarantees","box abstraction","safety-critical"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/27/x"},{"id":"p00836","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Aligning with Human Coding Preferences for Improving Code Generation","tz":"对齐人类编码偏好以改进代码生成","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable potential in automating software development tasks. While recent advances leverage Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) and Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) to align models with human preferences, the optimal training strategy remains unclear across diverse code preference scenarios. This paper systematically investigates the roles of SFT and DPO in aligning LLMs with different code preferences. Through both theoretical analysis and empirical observation, we hypothesize that SFT excels in scenarios with objectively verifiable optimal solutions, while applying SFT followed by DPO (S&D) enables models to explore superior solutions in scenarios without objectively verifiable optimal solutions. Based on the analysis and experimental evidence, we propose Adaptive Preference Optimization (APO), a dynamic integration approach that adaptively amplifies preferred responses, suppresses dispreferred ones, and encourages exploration of potentially superior solutions during training. Extensive experiments across six representative code preference tasks validate our theoretical hypotheses and demonstrate that APO consistently matches or surpasses the performance of existing SFT and S&D strategies. Our work provides both theoretical foundations and practical guidance for selecting appropriate training strategies in different code preference alignment scenarios.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在自动化软件开发任务上展现出显著潜力。尽管近期工作利用监督微调（SFT）与直接偏好优化（DPO）使模型对齐人类偏好，但在多样的代码偏好场景下，最优的训练策略仍不明确。本文系统研究了 SFT 与 DPO 在使 LLM 对齐不同代码偏好中的作用。通过理论分析与实证观察，我们提出假设：在存在客观可验证最优解的场景中 SFT 表现更好；而在不存在客观可验证最优解的场景中，先 SFT 后 DPO（S&D）能够让模型探索到更优的解。基于该分析与实验证据，我们提出自适应偏好优化（Adaptive Preference Optimization，APO），一种动态融合的方法，在训练过程中自适应地放大被偏好的响应、抑制不被偏好的响应，并鼓励对潜在更优解的探索。在六个具代表性的代码偏好任务上的大量实验验证了我们的理论假设，并表明 APO 始终能够匹配甚至超越现有 SFT 与 S&D 策略的性能。我们的工作为在不同代码偏好对齐场景中选择合适的训练策略提供了理论基础与实践指导。","tl":"按“最优解是否可验证”区分 SFT 与 DPO 适用场景，并提出自适应 APO。","au":["Xin Yin","Chao Ni","Xiaohu Yang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["preference alignment","SFT","DPO","code generation","adaptive preference optimization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/28/x"},{"id":"p00837","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"EfficientUICoder: A Bidirectional Token Compression Framework for Efficient MLLM-based UI Code Generation","tz":"EfficientUICoder：面向高效 MLLM UI 代码生成的双向 token 压缩框架","a":"Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs) have demonstrated exceptional performance in UI2Code tasks (i.e., generating code from UI mockups), significantly enhancing website development efficiency. However, UI2Code tasks incur substantially higher computational overhead compared to traditional code generation tasks. This overhead is primarily driven by the large number of input image tokens required to represent complex visual designs and the extensive volume of output code tokens needed to describe complete webpage structures. In this paper, we conduct a comprehensive preliminary study on popular MLLMs for UI2Code tasks, identifying significant redundancies in both image and code tokens. We observe that these redundancies not only exacerbate computational complexity but also hinder the model’s ability to focus on key UI elements, leading to excessively lengthy and often invalid HTML files. To address these challenges, we propose EfficientUICoder, a bidirectional compression framework designed for efficient UI code generation. First, we introduce an Element and Layout-aware Token Compression method, which preserves essential UI element and layout information by detecting element regions and constructing a UI element tree for efficient representation. Second, we design a Region-aware Token Refinement strategy that refines selected tokens by leveraging attention scores to evaluate semantic importance, discarding lowattention tokens from selected region while integrating high-attention tokens from unselected regions. Third, we develop an Adaptive Duplicate Token Suppression mechanism, which dynamically modulates token probabilities during decoding by tracking HTML/CSS code structure frequencies and applying exponential penalty strategies to minimize repetitive generation. Extensive experiments demonstrate that EfficientUICoder achieves a 55%-60% compression ratio without compromising the quality of the generated webpages, effectively reducing output code redundancy. In terms of efficiency, EfficientUICoder achieves superior improvements, reducing computational cost by up to 44.9%, generated tokens by up to 41.4%, prefill time by up to 46.6%, and inference time by up to 48.8% on 34B-level MLLMs.","az":"多模态大语言模型（MLLM）在 UI2Code 任务（即从 UI 原型图生成代码）上表现卓越，显著提升了网站开发效率。然而，与传统代码生成任务相比，UI2Code 任务带来了高得多的计算开销。这一开销主要源于表示复杂视觉设计所需的大量输入图像 token，以及描述完整网页结构所需的大量输出代码 token。本文对流行 MLLM 在 UI2Code 任务上进行了全面的初步研究，发现图像 token 与代码 token 中都存在显著冗余。我们观察到，这些冗余不仅加剧了计算复杂度，还妨碍模型聚焦于关键 UI 元素，导致生成过长且常常无效的 HTML 文件。为解决这些挑战，我们提出 EfficientUICoder，一个面向高效 UI 代码生成的双向压缩框架。首先，我们提出元素与布局感知的 token 压缩方法，通过检测元素区域并构建 UI 元素树来高效表示，从而保留关键的 UI 元素与布局信息。其次，我们设计了区域感知的 token 精化策略，利用注意力分数评估语义重要性来精化被选中的 token：丢弃选中区域内注意力较低的 token，同时整合未选中区域中注意力较高的 token。第三，我们提出自适应重复 token 抑制机制，通过跟踪 HTML/CSS 代码结构的出现频率并施加指数惩罚策略，在解码过程中动态调节 token 概率，以最小化重复生成。大量实验表明，EfficientUICoder 在不损害生成网页质量的前提下实现了 55%–60% 的压缩率，有效减少了输出代码冗余。在效率方面，EfficientUICoder 取得了显著提升：在 34B 级别 MLLM 上最多降低 44.9% 的计算成本、41.4% 的生成 token 数、46.6% 的预填充时间和 48.8% 的推理时间。","tl":"双向压缩图像与代码 token，使 MLLM 生成 UI 代码成本近乎减半。","au":["Jingyu Xiao","Zhongyi Zhang","Yuxuan Wan","Yintong Huo","Yang Liu","Michael Lyu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","multimodal"],"kw":["UI2Code","token compression","MLLM","HTML generation","inference efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/29/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.12159"},{"id":"p00838","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Mitigating Prompt-Induced Cognitive Biases in General-Purpose AI for Software Engineering","tz":"缓解面向软件工程的通用 AI 中由提示诱发的认知偏差","a":"Prompt-induced cognitive biases are changes in a general-purpose AI (GPAI) system’s decisions caused solely by biased wording in the input (e.g., framing, anchors), not task logic. In software engineering (SE) decision support (where problem statements and requirements are natural language) small phrasing shifts (e.g., popularity hints or outcome reveals) can push GPAI models toward suboptimal decisions. We study this with PROBE-SWE, a dynamic benchmark for SE that pairs biased and unbiased versions of the same SE dilemmas, controls for logic and difficulty, and targets eight SE-relevant biases (anchoring, availability, bandwagon, confirmation, framing, hindsight, hyperbolic discounting, overconfidence). We ask whether prompt engineering mitigates bias sensitivity in practice, focusing on actionable techniques that practitioners can apply off-the-shelf in real environments. Testing common strategies (e.g., chain-of-thought, self-debiasing) on popular GPAI systems, we find no statistically significant reductions in bias sensitivity. We then adopt a Prolog-style view of the reasoning process: solving SE dilemmas requires making explicit any background axioms and inference assumptions (i.e., SE best practices) that are usually implicit in the prompt. So, we hypothesize that bias-inducing features short-circuit assumptions elicitation, pushing GPAI models toward biased shortcuts. Building on this, we introduce an end-to-end method that elicits best practices and injects axiomatic reasoning cues in a prompt before answering, reducing overall bias sensitivity by ≈51% on average (𝑝 < .001). Finally, we report a thematic analysis that surfaces linguistic patterns associated with heightened bias sensitivity, clarifying when GPAI use is less advisable for SE decision support and where to focus future countermeasures.","az":"提示诱发的认知偏差，指通用 AI（GPAI）系统的决策仅因输入措辞带有偏向（例如框架效应、锚定）而发生改变，而非因任务逻辑改变。在软件工程（SE）决策支持中（问题陈述与需求均为自然语言），细微的措辞变化（例如流行度暗示或结果揭示）可能把 GPAI 模型推向次优决策。我们通过 PROBE-SWE 研究这一现象：这是一个面向 SE 的动态基准，为同一 SE 两难问题配对提供有偏与无偏版本，控制逻辑与难度，并针对八种与 SE 相关的偏差（锚定、可得性、从众、确认、框架、后见之明、双曲贴现、过度自信）。我们考察提示工程在实践中能否缓解偏差敏感性，重点关注从业者可在真实环境中开箱即用的可操作技术。在流行的 GPAI 系统上测试常见策略（例如思维链、自我去偏）后，我们发现偏差敏感性并无统计显著的下降。随后，我们采用类 Prolog 的推理过程视角：求解 SE 两难问题需要显式化通常隐含在提示中的背景公理与推理假设（即 SE 最佳实践）。因此我们假设，诱发偏差的特征会“短路”假设的显式化，把 GPAI 模型推向带偏见的捷径。基于此，我们提出一种端到端方法：在作答前先引出最佳实践并在提示中注入公理化推理线索，平均将总体偏差敏感性降低约 51%（𝑝 < .001）。最后，我们报告了一项主题分析，揭示与偏差敏感性升高相关的语言模式，厘清在哪些情形下不宜将 GPAI 用于 SE 决策支持，以及未来对策应聚焦之处。","tl":"提出 PROBE-SWE 基准，并以公理化提示将偏差敏感性降约 51%。","au":["Francesco Sovrano","Gabriele Dominici","Alberto Bacchelli"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["cognitive bias","prompt engineering","SE decision support","PROBE-SWE","debiasing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/30/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.16756"},{"id":"p00839","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Break to Adapt: Knowledge-Based Updates of Breaking Dependencies in JavaScript","tz":"打破以适应：基于知识的 JavaScript 破坏性依赖更新","a":"Modern software libraries continually evolve to maintain activeness, improve performance, and enhance security. This evolution frequently introduces major version updates that include incompatible modifications (breaking changes), which often cause downstream projects to fail and significantly increase the effort required for maintenance. To reduce this burden on developers, recent studies propose automated approaches that leverage API characterization techniques and compilation error reports to guide LLM-based updates. However, these methods rely on static typing and compilation feedback, which are not available in dynamic languages such as JavaScript. As a result, when applied to JavaScript, they degrade to a knowledge-free setting and cannot effectively support automated dependency updates. In this paper, we propose a knowledge-based approach that mines explicit update knowledge, referred to as breaking change records, from library repositories to support automated dependency updates in the presence of breaking changes (i.e., breaking dependency updates). We first conduct an empirical investigation of how breaking change records are maintained in top-ranked JavaScript libraries. Our study reveals that 83.8% of libraries maintain such records within their repositories, often spread across multiple locations. However, the quality of these records varies considerably, with issues such as implicit references to changed objects and vague adaptation instructions. To address this issue, we systematically characterize breaking change records by identifying recurring patterns in both their locations and the types of information they convey. Building on these insights, we develop BDUpdater, an agent-based framework that aggregates repository sources and refines raw records into structured breaking change lists, thereby mitigating the absence of API differencing tools. Leveraging this mined knowledge, BDUpdater pinpoints changed objects and statically identifies the affected client code, while supplying fine-grained change information to LLMs to guide accurate client code migration in the absence of compilation error messages. Our evaluation on 13 popular JavaScript libraries and 84 clients shows that BDUpdater recovers 90.5% of the breaking dependency updates with high semantic equivalence to developer-authored adaptations, while incurring an average cost of only $0.05 per client.","az":"现代软件库持续演化，以保持活跃度、提升性能并增强安全性。这种演化常常引入包含不兼容修改（破坏性变更）的大版本更新，往往导致下游项目失败，并显著增加维护所需的工作量。为减轻开发者负担，近期研究提出了利用 API 特征刻画技术与编译错误报告来指导基于 LLM 的更新的自动化方法。然而，这些方法依赖静态类型与编译反馈，而这在 JavaScript 等动态语言中并不可用。因此，当应用于 JavaScript 时，它们退化为无知识的设定，无法有效支持自动化依赖更新。本文提出一种基于知识的方法：从库仓库中挖掘显式的更新知识（称为破坏性变更记录），以支持存在破坏性变更情况下的自动依赖更新（即破坏性依赖更新）。我们首先对排名靠前的 JavaScript 库中破坏性变更记录的维护方式进行实证调查。研究发现，83.8% 的库在其仓库中维护了此类记录，且往往分散在多个位置；然而这些记录的质量差异很大，存在诸如对变更对象的隐式引用、适配指引含糊等问题。为解决该问题，我们通过识别记录位置与所传达信息类型中的重复模式，系统性地刻画破坏性变更记录。在此基础上，我们开发了 BDUpdater，一个基于智能体的框架，它聚合仓库中的多种来源，并将原始记录精炼为结构化的破坏性变更清单，从而弥补 API 差分工具的缺失。借助所挖掘的知识，BDUpdater 定位变更对象并静态识别受影响的客户端代码，同时向 LLM 提供细粒度变更信息，以在缺乏编译错误信息的情况下指导准确的客户端代码迁移。我们在 13 个流行 JavaScript 库和 84 个客户端上的评测表明，BDUpdater 恢复了 90.5% 的破坏性依赖更新，与开发者撰写的适配在语义上高度一致，而每个客户端的平均成本仅为 0.05 美元。","tl":"从仓库挖掘破坏性变更记录，替代动态语言缺失的编译反馈。","au":["Yifan Xia","Chengwei Liu","Zifan Xie","Lyuye Zhang","Peiyu Liu","Kangjie Lu","Yang Liu","Wenhai Wang","Shouling Ji"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","agentic","empirical-study"],"kw":["breaking changes","dependency update","JavaScript","LLM agent","API migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/31/x","pu":"https://nesa.zju.edu.cn/download/auto_20260423_yifan-2026fse.pdf"},{"id":"p00840","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Coding in a Bubble? Evaluating LLMs in Resolving Context Adaptation Bugs During Code Adaptation","tz":"在泡泡里编程？评估 LLM 在代码适配中解决上下文适配缺陷的能力","a":"Code adaptation is a fundamental but challenging task in software development, requiring developers to modify existing code for new contexts. A key challenge is to resolve Context Adaptation Bugs (CtxBugs), which occurs when code correct in its original context violates constraints in the target environment. Unlike isolated bugs, CtxBugs cannot be resolved through local fixes and require cross-context reasoning to identify semantic mismatches. Overlooking them may lead to critical failures in adaptation. Although Large Language Models (LLMs) show great potential in automating code-related tasks, their ability to resolve CtxBugs remains a significant and unexplored obstacle to their practical use in code adaptation. To bridge this gap, we propose CtxBugGen, a novel framework for generating CtxBugs to evaluate LLMs. Its core idea is to leverage LLMs’ tendency to generate plausible but context-free code when contextual constraints are absent. The framework generates CtxBugs through a four-step process to ensure their relevance and validity: (1) Selection of four established context-aware adaptation tasks from the literature, (2) Perturbation via task-specific rules to induce CtxBugs from LLMs while ensuring their plausibility, (3) Generation of candidate variants by prompting LLMs without any context constraints and (4) Identification of valid CtxBugs through syntactic differencing and test execution in the target context. Based on the benchmark constructed by CtxBugGen, we conduct an empirical study with four state-of-the-art LLMs. Our results reveal their unsatisfactory performance in CtxBug resolution. The best performing LLM, Kimi-K2, achieves 55.93% on Pass@1 and resolves just 52.47% of CtxBugs. The presence of CtxBugs degrades LLMs’ adaptation performance by up to 30%. Failure analysis indicates that LLMs often overlook CtxBugs and replicate them in their outputs. This suggests that LLMs overly focus on the local code correctness of the reused code while ignoring its compatibility in the target context. Our study highlights a critical weakness in LLMs’ cross-context reasoning and emphasize the need for new methods to enhance their context awareness for reliable code adaptation.","az":"代码适配是软件开发中一项基础却具挑战性的任务，需要开发者为新的上下文修改已有代码。其中的关键挑战是解决“上下文适配缺陷（Context Adaptation Bugs, CtxBugs）”，即在原有上下文中正确的代码，在目标环境中违反了约束。与孤立缺陷不同，CtxBugs 无法通过局部修复解决，需要跨上下文推理以识别语义失配；忽视它们可能在适配中导致严重故障。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在自动化代码相关任务上展现出巨大潜力，其解决 CtxBugs 的能力仍是其在代码适配中实际落地的一大未被探索的障碍。为填补这一空白，我们提出 CtxBugGen，一个用于生成 CtxBugs 以评估 LLM 的新框架。其核心思想是利用 LLM 在缺乏上下文约束时倾向于生成看似合理但脱离上下文的代码这一特性。该框架通过四步流程生成 CtxBugs，以确保其相关性与有效性：(1) 从文献中选取四项成熟的上下文感知适配任务；(2) 通过任务特定规则进行扰动，诱导 LLM 产生 CtxBugs 并保证其合理性；(3) 在不给任何上下文约束的情况下提示 LLM 生成候选变体；(4) 通过语法差分与在目标上下文中执行测试来识别有效的 CtxBugs。基于 CtxBugGen 构建的基准，我们对四个最先进的 LLM 开展了实证研究。结果显示它们在解决 CtxBug 上的表现并不令人满意：表现最好的 LLM Kimi-K2 的 Pass@1 为 55.93%，仅解决了 52.47% 的 CtxBugs。CtxBugs 的存在使 LLM 的适配性能最多下降 30%。失败分析表明，LLM 常常忽视 CtxBugs 并在输出中将其复制。这说明 LLM 过度关注被复用代码的局部正确性，却忽略了它在目标上下文中的兼容性。我们的研究揭示了 LLM 跨上下文推理的关键弱点，强调需要新方法来增强其上下文感知能力，以实现可靠的代码适配。","tl":"用“去上下文提示”自动造出上下文适配缺陷，暴露 LLM 跨上下文推理短板。","au":["Tanghaoran Zhang","Xinjun Mao","Shangwen Wang","Yuxin Zhao","Yao Lu","Zezhou Tang","Wenyu Xu","Longfei Sun","Changrong Xie","Kang Yang","Yue Yu"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["code adaptation","context adaptation bugs","benchmark generation","LLM evaluation","cross-context reasoning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/32/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.06497"},{"id":"p00841","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"VulKey: Automated Vulnerability Repair Guided by Domain-Specific Repair Patterns","tz":"VulKey：由领域专用修复模式引导的自动漏洞修复","a":"The increasing prevalence of software vulnerabilities highlights the need for effective Automatic Vulnerability Repair (AVR) tools. While LLM-based approaches are promising, they struggle to incorporate structured security knowledge from sources like CWE and NVD. Current methods either use this information superficially by concatenating the CWE-ID into the input prompt, yielding negligible benefits, or rely on few-shot learning with rigid, non-generalizable examples, which limits their effectiveness in real-world scenarios. To address this gap, we propose VulKey, an LLM-based AVR framework that leverages a hierarchical abstraction of expert knowledge to guide patch generation. Our novel three-level abstraction formulates repair strategies in terms of CWE type, syntactic actions, and semantic key elements. This approach captures the essence of a security fix with greater generality than concrete examples and more semantic richness than traditional syntax-based templates, overcoming the coverage limitations of prior methods. VulKey is implemented as a two-stage pipeline: first, expert knowledge matching predicts an appropriate repair pattern for the vulnerability; second, repair code generation uses a pattern-guided, fine-tuned LLM to produce secure patches. On the real-world C/C++ dataset PrimeVul, VulKey achieves 31.5% repair accuracy, surpassing the best baseline by 7.6% and outperforming leading tools such as VulMaster and GPT-5. Moreover, VulKey demonstrates cross-language and cross-model generalizability, with state-of-the-art performance on the Java benchmark Vul4J. These results underscore the importance of structured expert knowledge in advancing AVR effectiveness. Our work demonstrates that explicitly modeling and integrating expert security knowledge through hierarchical patterns is a crucial step toward building more effective and reliable AVR tools.","az":"软件漏洞日益普遍，凸显了对有效自动漏洞修复（AVR）工具的需求。尽管基于 LLM 的方法前景可期，它们却难以融入来自 CWE、NVD 等来源的结构化安全知识。现有方法要么只是把 CWE-ID 拼接进输入提示，浅层地使用这些信息，收益微乎其微；要么依赖带有僵化、不可泛化示例的少样本学习，限制了其在真实场景中的效果。为弥补这一空白，我们提出 VulKey，一个基于 LLM 的 AVR 框架，利用专家知识的分层抽象来指导补丁生成。我们新颖的三层抽象从 CWE 类型、语法动作和语义关键要素三个层面刻画修复策略。该方法比具体示例更具一般性，又比传统基于语法的模板更具语义丰富性，从而克服了先前方法的覆盖局限。VulKey 实现为两阶段流水线：首先，专家知识匹配为漏洞预测合适的修复模式；其次，修复代码生成阶段使用模式引导的、经过微调的 LLM 产出安全补丁。在真实世界 C/C++ 数据集 PrimeVul 上，VulKey 达到 31.5% 的修复准确率，比最佳基线高出 7.6%，并优于 VulMaster、GPT-5 等领先工具。此外，VulKey 展现出跨语言与跨模型的泛化能力，在 Java 基准 Vul4J 上取得最先进性能。这些结果凸显了结构化专家知识对提升 AVR 有效性的重要性。我们的工作表明，通过分层模式显式建模并整合专家安全知识，是构建更有效、更可靠 AVR 工具的关键一步。","tl":"以 CWE 类型-语法动作-语义要素三层抽象引导 LLM 生成安全补丁。","au":["Jia Li","Zhuangbin Chen","Yuxin Su","Michael Lyu"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automatic vulnerability repair","CWE","repair patterns","LLM fine-tuning","PrimeVul"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/33/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.01769"},{"id":"p00842","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TSGuard: Automated User-Centric Incident Diagnosis for AI Workloads in the Cloud","tz":"TSGuard：面向云上 AI 负载的自动化用户中心事故诊断","a":"AI workloads incur frequent failures and incidents from the underlying infrastructure. The current incident management workflow follows a provider-centric paradigm, where users report incidents to the infrastructure provider who then conducts troubleshooting. Due to the large number of incidents and the manual nature of the troubleshooting process, the provider often takes several days to resolve an incident, resulting in operational delays and productivity loss. To address these challenges, we present TSGuard, a user-centric multi-agent system that delivers immediate incident diagnosis to users who deploy the workloads. The core innovation of TSGuard is twofold: (1) constructing domain-specific knowledge bases by mining historical on-call experiences in the offline phase, and (2) mimicking human expert diagnosis via structured reasoning and iterative trial-and-error in the online phase. Evaluation using production incident records from public cloud A demonstrates that TSGuard significantly outperforms state-of-the-art baselines, improving diagnostic accuracy by 19.8%. Furthermore, TSGuard reduces the average verification time by 63.4% compared to sequential benchmark execution baseline.","az":"AI 负载常常因底层基础设施而频繁出现故障与事故。当前的事故管理流程遵循以提供方为中心的范式：用户向基础设施提供方上报事故，再由提供方进行排查。由于事故数量庞大且排查过程以人工为主，提供方往往需要数天才能解决一起事故，造成运营延迟与生产力损失。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 TSGuard，一个以用户为中心的多智能体系统，为部署负载的用户提供即时的事故诊断。TSGuard 的核心创新有两点：(1) 在离线阶段通过挖掘历史值班经验构建领域专用知识库；(2) 在在线阶段通过结构化推理与迭代试错来模拟人类专家的诊断过程。使用公有云 A 的生产事故记录进行的评测表明，TSGuard 显著优于最先进的基线方法，将诊断准确率提升 19.8%。此外，与顺序执行基准的基线相比，TSGuard 将平均验证时间缩短 63.4%。","tl":"挖掘值班经验建知识库，让用户侧多智能体即时诊断云上 AI 负载事故。","au":["Yitao Yang","Yangtao Deng","Yifan Xiong","Baochun Li","Hong Xu","Peng Cheng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["llm-based","agentic","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["incident diagnosis","AI workloads","multi-agent system","cloud operations","troubleshooting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/34/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.01481"},{"id":"p00843","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GREClue: Failure Indexing with Graph-based Failure Representation and Entropy-based Deep Clustering","tz":"GREClue：基于图的失败表示与基于熵的深度聚类的失败索引","a":"Failure indexing aims to group multiple failures according to their root causes and is an essential step in parallel debugging. Failure indexing consists mainly of two steps: failure representation and failure clustering. While many research efforts have been devoted to these two steps, serious issues still exist. For failure representation, existing works use coverage or program memory information, which unfortunately can not capture deep failure semantic. For failure clustering, advanced failure indexing methods use clustering algorithms with preset cluster centers, but this kind of clustering algorithm can handle spherical clusters well but performs poorly when handling clusters of other shapes. To address these issues, this paper proposes GREClue, a novel failure indexing approach with Graph-based failure Representation and Entropy-based deep Clustering. GREClue overcomes the issues in order. For failure representation, GREClue designs the failure semantic graph (FSG), a new graph representation that effectively contains semantic information and runtime information of failures. Based on FSG, GREClue further consists of an entropy-based deep clustering component, which can accurately cluster failed tests without presetting cluster centers. An extensive evaluation of GREClue shows that compared to the state-of-the-art failure indexing method, GREClue improves both the performance of estimating the number of faults and the clustering effectiveness by 10% to 41%. Moreover, it has also been shown that GREClue can effectively facilitate parallel debugging.","az":"失败索引旨在依据根因将多个失败分组，是并行调试中的关键步骤。失败索引主要包含两个步骤：失败表示与失败聚类。尽管已有大量研究投入这两个步骤，严重问题依然存在。在失败表示方面，现有工作使用覆盖信息或程序内存信息，遗憾的是它们无法捕捉深层的失败语义。在失败聚类方面，先进的失败索引方法使用带预设聚类中心的聚类算法，这类算法能较好处理球形簇，但在处理其他形状的簇时表现不佳。为解决这些问题，本文提出 GREClue，一种采用基于图的失败表示与基于熵的深度聚类的新型失败索引方法。GREClue 依次克服上述问题：在失败表示方面，GREClue 设计了失败语义图（failure semantic graph, FSG），一种能有效包含失败的语义信息与运行时信息的新图表示；在此基础上，GREClue 进一步包含一个基于熵的深度聚类组件，可在无需预设聚类中心的情况下准确地对失败测试进行聚类。对 GREClue 的广泛评测表明，与最先进的失败索引方法相比，GREClue 在缺陷数量估计性能与聚类效果上均提升了 10% 至 41%。此外，实验还表明 GREClue 能有效促进并行调试。","tl":"用失败语义图表示失败，并以基于熵的深度聚类免去预设簇心。","au":["Zhenyu Yang","Zhongxing Yu"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["failure indexing","parallel debugging","failure semantic graph","deep clustering","root cause grouping"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/35/x"},{"id":"p00844","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TestTailor: Generating High-Coverage Tests via Path-Proximal Tests with LLMs","tz":"TestTailor：借助路径邻近测试用 LLM 生成高覆盖率测试","a":"Automated unit testing is essential for ensuring software quality. Achieving high code coverage through automated unit test generation remains challenging, especially for hard-to-cover branches guarded by complex or deeply nested conditions. Traditional search-based approaches often stagnate at fitness plateaus, while recent LLM-based techniques provide mostly coarse-grained prompts, leaving models to guess how to reach uncovered targets. To address these limitations, we present TestTailor, a neuro-symbolic framework that exploits fine-grained, path-oriented guidance to guide LLM-based test generation. The key idea is to exploit path-proximal tests (i.e., existing test cases whose execution paths closely resemble the target uncovered path) and to analyze their divergence points. By combining this analysis with symbolic constraints (i.e., constraints collected from the target uncovered path using symbolic execution), TestTailor derives actionable path guidance and encodes them into concise prompts that tell the LLM not only what remains uncovered, but also how to reach it. We evaluate TestTailor on the widely used CODAMOSA benchmark comprising 486 Python modules. Results show that TestTailor consistently outperforms state-of-the-art baselines, improving statement coverage by 5.01% and branch coverage by 4.17% on average compared to the best baseline CoverUp, while reducing API cost by about 60%. Against the hybrid LLM-search-based technique CODAMOSA, TestTailor achieves even larger gains of 12.78% and 13.09% in statement and branch coverage, respectively. Moreover, TestTailor attains the highest coverage accuracy (85.2% vs. 75.3% for CoverUp and 63.8% for TELPA), and demonstrates robustness across different LLM backbones. These results highlight that TestTailor transforms vague coverage goals into precise path-level instructions, enabling LLMs to generate high-coverage test suites more efficiently and accurately.","az":"自动化单元测试对保障软件质量至关重要。通过自动单元测试生成实现高代码覆盖率仍然充满挑战，尤其是对由复杂或深层嵌套条件守护的难覆盖分支。传统的基于搜索的方法常在适应度平台期停滞，而近期基于 LLM 的技术大多只提供粗粒度提示，让模型自行猜测如何抵达未覆盖目标。为解决这些局限，我们提出 TestTailor，一个利用细粒度、面向路径的指引来引导基于 LLM 的测试生成的神经符号框架。其核心思想是利用路径邻近测试（即执行路径与目标未覆盖路径高度相似的已有测试用例）并分析其分叉点。将该分析与符号约束（即通过符号执行从目标未覆盖路径收集到的约束）相结合，TestTailor 推导出可操作的路径指引，并将其编码为简洁的提示，不仅告诉 LLM 哪些部分尚未覆盖，还告诉它如何抵达。我们在广泛使用的 CODAMOSA 基准（包含 486 个 Python 模块）上评估 TestTailor。结果表明，TestTailor 持续优于最先进的基线：相较最佳基线 CoverUp，平均提升语句覆盖率 5.01%、分支覆盖率 4.17%，同时将 API 成本降低约 60%。相较于混合 LLM 与搜索的技术 CODAMOSA，TestTailor 在语句与分支覆盖率上取得了更大的提升，分别为 12.78% 和 13.09%。此外，TestTailor 取得了最高的覆盖准确率（85.2%，而 CoverUp 为 75.3%，TELPA 为 63.8%），并在不同 LLM 底座上表现稳健。这些结果表明，TestTailor 将含糊的覆盖目标转化为精确的路径级指令，使 LLM 能更高效、更准确地生成高覆盖率测试套件。","tl":"用路径邻近测试的分叉点加符号约束，给 LLM 精确的“怎么覆盖”指令。","au":["Xiaoxuan Zhou","Yiling Lou","Jinhao Dong","Dan Hao"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unit test generation","code coverage","symbolic execution","neuro-symbolic","LLM prompting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/36/x"},{"id":"p00845","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GraphQLify: Automated and Type Safety-Preserving GraphQL API Adoption","tz":"GraphQLify：自动化且保持类型安全的 GraphQL API 迁移","a":"This paper introduces GraphQLify, an automated framework for facilitating the migration of existing APIs to GraphQL. While prior works in this area targeted relational databases, resource description frameworks (RDF), or machine-parsable API specifications, GraphQLify takes a new approach by leveraging static source code analysis for type inference. This approach helps generate GraphQL schemas, maintaining end-to-end type safety, a key premise of using GraphQL over REST. Since the separate GraphQL servers generated by existing techniques work as adapters to existing APIs, they incur performance overhead due to dynamic request binding and network latency. On the other hand, GraphQLify generates an embedded server to directly invoke existing API code, and therefore provides better performance. During our evaluation with 834 APIs from nine popular OSS projects, GraphQLify successfully converted all while matching the types from the original APIs. While OASGraph, the current state-of-the-art, had 3.5% failure rates and 42% type mismatches in our evaluation, both numbers are at 0% for GraphQLify. Finally, our evaluation suggests that for application workflows requiring five sequential API calls, clients can reduce data fetching time by a factor of 2 to 4 by using the GraphQLify-generated APIs over REST counterparts.","az":"本文介绍 GraphQLify，一个用于促进既有 API 向 GraphQL 迁移的自动化框架。此前该领域的工作以关系数据库、资源描述框架（RDF）或机器可解析的 API 规约为目标，而 GraphQLify 另辟蹊径，利用静态源码分析进行类型推断。该方法有助于生成 GraphQL 模式，并保持端到端的类型安全——这正是选择 GraphQL 而非 REST 的关键前提。由于现有技术生成的独立 GraphQL 服务器是作为既有 API 的适配器运行的，会因动态请求绑定与网络延迟而产生性能开销。相比之下，GraphQLify 生成一个嵌入式服务器，直接调用既有 API 代码，因而具有更好的性能。在我们对来自九个流行开源项目的 834 个 API 进行的评测中，GraphQLify 成功转换了全部 API，并与原始 API 的类型保持一致。当前最先进的工具 OASGraph 在我们的评测中失败率为 3.5%、类型不匹配率为 42%，而 GraphQLify 在这两项指标上均为 0%。最后，我们的评测表明，对于需要五次连续 API 调用的应用工作流，客户端使用 GraphQLify 生成的 API 相比 REST 版本可将数据获取时间缩短为原来的二分之一到四分之一。","tl":"用静态类型推断生成嵌入式 GraphQL 服务器，零类型失配且更快。","au":["Saleh Amareen","Arif Rahman","Sazzadur Rahaman","Amiangshu Bosu"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GraphQL","API migration","static analysis","type inference","REST"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/37/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.15465"},{"id":"p00846","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding Code Similarity across Instruction Set Architectures: An Empirical Study","tz":"理解跨指令集架构的代码相似性：一项实证研究","a":"Software interacts with hardware through Instruction Set Architectures (ISAs), such as x86, ARM, and RISC-V. Although many developers may be unaware of ISA heterogeneity, ISA-specific code is pervasive in foundational software systems that underpin the digital infrastructure of human society. Maintaining separate implementations is common when supporting multiple ISAs in such a foundational software project. This may introduce substantial additional effort. Meanwhile, separate ISA-specific implementations frequently exhibit code similarities across ISAs. To understand ISA-specific code and their similarities, and to gain insights for better management, we conducted an empirical study of 20 open-source foundational projects that support multiple ISAs. We confirmed the need for separate ISA-specific implementations, yet our analysis revealed a weighted average similarity of 21.7% across ISAs. We also observed cross-ISA co-change and cross-ISA participation patterns in the development and maintenance of ISA-specific code. This study offers the first systematic investigation of ISA-specific code similarities, yielding evidence that can be leveraged by practitioners and researchers working on ISA-related software engineering.","az":"软件通过指令集架构（ISA），如 x86、ARM 和 RISC-V，与硬件交互。尽管许多开发者可能并未意识到 ISA 的异构性，但 ISA 相关代码在支撑人类社会数字基础设施的基础软件系统中无处不在。在这类基础软件项目中支持多种 ISA 时，维护各自独立的实现十分常见，这可能带来大量额外工作量。与此同时，针对不同 ISA 的独立实现之间往往存在代码相似性。为理解 ISA 相关代码及其相似性，并为更好的管理获得洞见，我们对 20 个支持多 ISA 的开源基础项目开展了实证研究。我们确认了保留各自独立的 ISA 专用实现确有必要，但分析显示跨 ISA 的加权平均相似度为 21.7%。我们还观察到在 ISA 专用代码的开发与维护中存在跨 ISA 的共同变更与跨 ISA 的参与模式。本研究首次系统性地考察了 ISA 专用代码之间的相似性，产出的证据可供从事 ISA 相关软件工程的实践者与研究者借鉴。","tl":"首次量化多 ISA 独立实现间 21.7% 的相似度及共同变更模式。","au":["Haonan Yu","Jiaxin Zhu","Yingying Zheng","Yuwei Zhang","Wei Wang","Jun Wei","Tao Huang"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["instruction set architecture","code similarity","empirical study","open-source systems","co-change"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/38/x","pu":"https://github.com/lxtqa/ISAsimilarity/raw/main/ArchCode.pdf"},{"id":"p00847","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"How Do Developers Interact with AI? An Exploratory Study on Modeling Developer Programming Behavior","tz":"开发者如何与 AI 交互？一项建模开发者编程行为的探索性研究","a":"Artificial Intelligence (AI) is reshaping how developers adopt software engineering practices, yet the multi-dimensional nature of developer-AI interaction remains under-explored. Prior studies have primarily examined dimensions observable from developer activities such as “Prompt Crafting” and “Code Editing,” overlooking how hidden intentions and emotional dimensions intertwine with concrete actions during AI-assisted programming. Understanding the interplay is essential for improving developer experience and future AI assistant designs. To understand this phenomenon, we conducted a mixed-methods study with 76 developers. We first split developers into AI-assisted and non-AI groups. Each performed a programming task (either Python with API management or Java with SQL). Developers retrospectively labeled their self-reported intentions, tool-supported actions, and emotions (on a 7-point valence scale) from screen recordings, supplemented by participant surveys and interviews. Our user study resulted in a novel model, named S-IASE, with four dimensions to describe programming behavior for a given development state: intention, action, supporting tool, and emotion. Our analysis reveals several aggregated and sequential behavioral patterns. For example, for aggregated patterns, using AI assistants often led developers to focus more on actively “creating” code, evaluating, and verifying the generated results; for sequential patterns, AI-assisted participants showed emotionally stable development flows, as opposed to non-AI-assisted participants who experienced more fluctuating emotions. Interviews revealed further nuance: some developers reported impostor-like feelings, expressing guilt or self-doubt about relying on AI for programming. The uncovered patterns indicate that our model can provide actionable insights for improving AI assistants’ responsiveness, training developers in AI collaboration, and designing developer-centric AI studies. Our work bridges an important gap in understanding the complexities of developer-AI interaction in the programming context and sheds light on future developer-centric research directions.","az":"人工智能（AI）正在重塑开发者采纳软件工程实践的方式，然而开发者与 AI 交互的多维本质仍研究不足。既有研究主要考察可从开发者活动中观察到的维度，例如“提示撰写”和“代码编辑”，却忽视了隐藏的意图与情感维度如何在 AI 辅助编程中与具体行动相互交织。理解这种相互作用，对改进开发者体验与未来 AI 助手设计至关重要。为理解这一现象，我们对 76 名开发者开展了混合方法研究。我们首先将开发者分为 AI 辅助组与非 AI 组，每人完成一项编程任务（Python 与 API 管理任务，或 Java 与 SQL 任务）。开发者随后基于屏幕录像回溯性地标注自己的自述意图、工具支持的行动以及情绪（采用 7 点效价量表），并辅以参与者问卷与访谈。我们的用户研究得到一个新颖模型 S-IASE，它以四个维度描述在给定开发状态下的编程行为：意图、行动、支持工具与情绪。我们的分析揭示了若干聚合型与序列型行为模式。例如，在聚合模式方面，使用 AI 助手常使开发者更多地聚焦于主动“创造”代码、评估与验证生成结果；在序列模式方面，AI 辅助的参与者展现出情绪稳定的开发流程，而非 AI 辅助的参与者则经历更多情绪波动。访谈揭示了更多细微之处：一些开发者报告了类似“冒名顶替”的感受，对依赖 AI 编程表达出内疚或自我怀疑。所发现的模式表明，我们的模型可为提升 AI 助手的响应性、培训开发者进行 AI 协作以及设计以开发者为中心的 AI 研究提供可操作的洞见。我们的工作弥合了在编程情境中理解开发者与 AI 交互复杂性的重要空白，并为未来以开发者为中心的研究方向提供了启示。","tl":"提出意图-行动-工具-情绪四维 S-IASE 模型刻画 AI 辅助编程行为。","au":["Yinan Wu","Ze Shi (Zane) Li","Kathryn Stolee","Bowen Xu"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["developer-AI interaction","mixed-methods study","programming behavior model","emotion","AI assistant"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/39/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.16393"},{"id":"p00848","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Adaptive Mutation Scheduling with Deep Reinforcement Learning for Smart Contract Fuzzing","tz":"面向智能合约模糊测试的深度强化学习自适应变异调度","a":"Smart contracts underpin a wide range of decentralized applications—from financial services to supply-chain management—but their immutability and direct control of assets magnify the impact of any security bugs. Although many fuzz approaches have been proposed and have demonstrated their effectiveness in uncovering vulnerabilities, existing methods often rely on unguided random mutation scheduling, generate redundant inputs, and fail to adapt to smart contract-specific characteristics. To overcome these challenges, we present FuzzMaster, a feedback-driven fuzzing framework that combines deep reinforcement learning (DRL) with lightweight probabilistic scheduling to steer mutation selection at runtime intelligently. By continuously analyzing execution feedback—code coverage, function-call sequences, and vulnerability signals—FuzzMaster’s DRL agent and probabilistic tables prioritize high-impact mutations and avoid wasted effort on redundant seeds. On standard VeriSmart and SmartBugs benchmarks, FuzzMaster achieves a 66.2% detection rate with 100% precision (versus 46.9% for ItyFuzz and 43.1% for Confuzzius) and uncovers most bugs within the first second of execution. Meanwhile, in real-world Ethereum contracts, FuzzMaster identified 97 vulnerabilities in 6 categories. These results demonstrate that dynamic, vulnerability-aware mutation scheduling can dramatically improve both the efficiency and effectiveness of smart contract fuzz testing.","az":"智能合约支撑着从金融服务到供应链管理的大量去中心化应用，但其不可变性与对资产的直接控制放大了任何安全缺陷的影响。尽管已有许多模糊测试方法被提出并在挖掘漏洞上展现出有效性，现有方法常常依赖无引导的随机变异调度，生成冗余输入，且无法适应智能合约特有的特性。为克服这些挑战，我们提出 FuzzMaster，一个反馈驱动的模糊测试框架，将深度强化学习（DRL）与轻量级概率调度相结合，在运行时智能地引导变异选择。通过持续分析执行反馈——代码覆盖率、函数调用序列与漏洞信号——FuzzMaster 的 DRL 智能体与概率表会优先选择高影响的变异，避免在冗余种子上浪费精力。在标准的 VeriSmart 与 SmartBugs 基准上，FuzzMaster 取得 66.2% 的检测率与 100% 的精确率（相比之下 ItyFuzz 为 46.9%，Confuzzius 为 43.1%），并在执行的第一秒内即发现大多数缺陷。同时，在真实的以太坊合约上，FuzzMaster 识别出 6 类共 97 个漏洞。这些结果表明，动态的、漏洞感知的变异调度能够显著提升智能合约模糊测试的效率与有效性。","tl":"用深度强化学习加概率表在运行时自适应调度合约模糊变异。","au":["Qianqian Pang","Xin Yin","Tingting Bi","Lingfeng Bao","Chao Ni","Xiaohu Yang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract fuzzing","deep reinforcement learning","mutation scheduling","coverage feedback","vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/40/x"},{"id":"p00849","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Reducing the TCB of SGX-oriented LibOSes at Runtime","tz":"在运行时缩减面向 SGX 的 LibOS 可信计算基","a":"Intel Software Guard Extensions (SGX) provides a trusted execution environment (TEE) for applications to protect runtime code and data from the untrusted environment. All code residing in the enclave, including LibOSes and the libraries, is all taken into the Trusted Computing Base (TCB). The TCB size closely correlates with the potential vulnerabilities and the system’s attack surface. Vulnerabilities in the enclave can tamper with the control flow of the enclave program and potentially lead to data breaches. Existing SGX frameworks present a dilemma: either include a large LibOS in the enclave to ensure functionality, which inflates the TCB and attack surface, or move the OS out for a minimal TCB, which severely restricts application support or incurs high overhead, insecure interactions with the untrusted world. In this paper, we introduce DynaTCB, a runtime framework designed to balance security and functionality. To enhance security, DynaTCB dynamically adjusts the TCB according to runtime program behavior. To preserve functionality, it logically removes unneeded code from the TCB instead of physically removing it from the enclave, thus avoiding the drawbacks of frequent untrusted interactions. It performs binary-level analysis without requiring source code. Experimental results show that DynaTCB achieves a code reduction of over 95% for the Coreutils suite and more than 80% for real-world applications. Additionally, DynaTCB successfully mitigates several Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVEs), affirming its potential to significantly enhance security in SGX environments.","az":"Intel 软件防护扩展（SGX）为应用提供可信执行环境（TEE），以保护运行时代码与数据免受不可信环境的侵害。位于 enclave 内的所有代码，包括 LibOS 及各类库，都被计入可信计算基（TCB）。TCB 的规模与潜在漏洞及系统攻击面密切相关。enclave 中的漏洞可能篡改 enclave 程序的控制流，并可能导致数据泄露。现有 SGX 框架面临两难：要么在 enclave 中纳入庞大的 LibOS 以保证功能，从而膨胀 TCB 与攻击面；要么把操作系统移出以实现最小 TCB，却严重限制应用支持能力，或带来高昂开销与不安全的外部交互。本文提出 DynaTCB，一个旨在平衡安全性与功能性的运行时框架。为增强安全性，DynaTCB 依据运行时程序行为动态调整 TCB；为保持功能性，它在逻辑上将不需要的代码移出 TCB，而非从 enclave 中物理移除，从而避免频繁的不可信交互所带来的弊端。它在二进制层面进行分析，无需源代码。实验结果表明，DynaTCB 对 Coreutils 套件实现了超过 95% 的代码缩减，对真实应用超过 80%。此外，DynaTCB 成功缓解了若干 CVE 漏洞，印证了其显著提升 SGX 环境安全性的潜力。","tl":"按运行时行为在逻辑上动态裁剪 enclave 内代码，兼顾功能与最小 TCB。","au":["Donghui Yu","Dahan Pan","Fengwei Zhang","Haoran Fang","Ya Fang","Yuanyuan Zhang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Intel SGX","trusted computing base","LibOS","debloating","binary analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/41/x"},{"id":"p00850","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Reward-Free Code Alignment from Pretrained or Fine-Tuned LLM: Unpacking the Trade-offs for Code Generation","tz":"来自预训练或微调 LLM 的无奖励代码对齐：解析代码生成中的权衡","a":"Large Language Model (LLM) alignment trains an LLM using preference data to produce outputs that better reflect human values (e.g., to mitigate toxic or biased responses). While LLM alignment techniques are studied for non-coding tasks, we know little about their usefulness for coding tasks. Intuitively, for code generation tasks using LLMs, alignment techniques could help with coding solutions that better align with developer preferences, such as more secure code, supporting better coding practices, etc. However, it is unclear whether LLM code alignment could support both functional requirements (producing executable, correct code) and non-functional requirements (code readability, style, maintainability). It is also unknown whether alignment for a code LLM should begin with base pretrained version or the finetuned (i.e., instruction-tuned) version of the LLM. In this paper, we offer insights on the above two research questions by conducting an empirical study. We studied five state-of-the-art (SOTA) LLMs using two widely used LLM alignment techniques: Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) and BoNBoN. For each training record, we created a preference pair as accepted and rejected instances by using the SelfCodeAlign pipeline. DPO and BoNBoN are reward-free models, i.e., they eliminate the need for multiple reward scores for output preferences. We tuned each LLM using the two alignment techniques in two settings: pretrained and finetuned versions of an LLM. We evaluated functional requirements using four SOTA benchmarks (HumanEval+, MBPP+, EvalPerf, EvoEval) and non-functional requirements using the SOTA benchmark, CODAL. We find that pretrained-to-aligned pathways achieve larger improvements in the aligned variant over its pretrained variant (CodeLlama-7b: +75% non-functional, Llama3-8b: +42% functional). But the pretrained variant is generally less accurate than its finetuned variant. However, finetuned-to-aligned offers smaller performance improvements or, in some cases, degradation in the aligned variant than its finetuned variant. This means that while the base pretrained version is less accurate than its base finetuned variant, alignment reduces the performance gap between pretrained and finetuned variants. Non-functional requirements improve more consistently than functional requirements via alignment. Based on these findings, we provide nine recommendations to guide alignment for code LLMs.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）对齐使用偏好数据训练 LLM，使其输出更好地反映人类价值观（例如缓解有毒或有偏见的回复）。尽管 LLM 对齐技术已在非编码任务上被研究，我们对其在编码任务中的作用知之甚少。直观上，对于使用 LLM 的代码生成任务，对齐技术有助于产出更符合开发者偏好的编码方案，例如更安全的代码、更好地遵循编码实践等。然而，代码 LLM 的对齐能否同时支持功能性需求（生成可执行、正确的代码）与非功能性需求（代码可读性、风格、可维护性）尚不清楚；代码 LLM 的对齐应当从基础预训练版本开始还是从微调（即指令微调）版本开始，同样未知。本文通过一项实证研究，为上述两个研究问题提供洞见。我们使用两种广泛采用的 LLM 对齐技术——直接偏好优化（DPO）与 BoNBoN——研究了五个最先进（SOTA）的 LLM。对于每条训练记录，我们使用 SelfCodeAlign 流水线构造了由接受实例与拒绝实例组成的偏好对。DPO 与 BoNBoN 都是无奖励模型，即它们无需为输出偏好提供多个奖励分数。我们在预训练版本与微调版本两种设定下，用这两种对齐技术分别调优每个 LLM。我们使用四个 SOTA 基准（HumanEval+、MBPP+、EvalPerf、EvoEval）评估功能性需求，并使用 SOTA 基准 CODAL 评估非功能性需求。我们发现，从预训练到对齐的路径，其对齐变体相对其预训练变体的提升更大（CodeLlama-7b：非功能性 +75%；Llama3-8b：功能性 +42%），但预训练变体通常不如其微调变体准确。而从微调到对齐的路径，其对齐变体相对其微调变体的性能提升较小，某些情况下甚至出现下降。这意味着，虽然基础预训练版本不如其基础微调版本准确，但对齐缩小了预训练与微调变体之间的性能差距。通过对齐，非功能性需求的改善比功能性需求更为稳定一致。基于这些发现，我们给出九条指导代码 LLM 对齐的建议。","tl":"实证厘清预训练版与微调版起步做代码对齐的收益差异与九条建议。","au":["Sanjeepan Sivapiran","Gias Uddin"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["code alignment","DPO","BoNBoN","reward-free alignment","non-functional requirements"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/42/x"},{"id":"p00851","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Deployability-Centric Infrastructure-as-Code Generation: Fail, Learn, Refine, and Succeed through LLM-Empowered DevOps Simulation","tz":"以可部署性为中心的 Infrastructure-as-Code 生成：借助 LLM 驱动的 DevOps 仿真实现失败、学习、精化与成功","a":"Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) generation holds significant promise for automating cloud infrastructure provisioning. Recent advances in Large Language Models (LLMs) present a promising opportunity to democratize IaC development by generating deployable infrastructure templates from natural language descriptions. However, current evaluation focuses on syntactic correctness while ignoring deployability, the critical measure of the utility of IaC configuration files. Six state-of-the-art LLMs performed poorly on deployability, achieving only 20.8 30.2% deployment success rate on the first attempt. In this paper, we construct DPIaC-Eval, the first deployability-centric IaC template benchmark consists of 153 real-world scenarios cross 58 unique services. Also, we propose an LLM-based deployability-centric framework, dubbed IaCGen, that uses iterative feedback mechanism encompassing format verification, syntax checking, and live deployment stages, thereby closely mirroring the real DevOps workflows. Results show that IaCGen can makes all evaluated models reach 54.6 91.6% in 10 iterations. Additionally, human-in-the-loop feedback that provide direct guidance for the deployability errors, can further boost the performance to over 90% passItr@25 on all evaluated LLMs. Furthermore, we explore the trustworthiness of the generated IaC templates on user intent alignment and security compliance. The poor performance (25.2% user requirement coverage and 8.4% security compliance rate) indicates a critical need for continued research in this domain.","az":"Infrastructure-as-Code（IaC）生成在自动化云基础设施供给方面潜力巨大。大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展提供了一个有望普及 IaC 开发的机会，即从自然语言描述生成可部署的基础设施模板。然而，当前的评测只关注语法正确性，却忽略了可部署性——这一衡量 IaC 配置文件实用价值的关键指标。六个最先进的 LLM 在可部署性上表现不佳，首次尝试的部署成功率仅为 20.8~30.2%。本文构建了 DPIaC-Eval，这是首个以可部署性为中心的 IaC 模板基准，包含覆盖 58 种不同服务的 153 个真实场景。同时，我们提出了一个基于 LLM 的、以可部署性为中心的框架，称为 IaCGen，它采用涵盖格式验证、语法检查与实际部署阶段的迭代反馈机制，从而紧密贴合真实的 DevOps 工作流。结果表明，IaCGen 能让所有被评测模型在 10 轮迭代内达到 54.6~91.6%。此外，针对可部署性错误提供直接指导的人在回路反馈，可以将所有被评测 LLM 的性能进一步提升到 90% 以上的 passItr@25。进一步地，我们还探究了所生成 IaC 模板在用户意图对齐与安全合规方面的可信度。其糟糕的表现（25.2% 的用户需求覆盖率和 8.4% 的安全合规率）表明该领域亟需持续研究。","tl":"首个以真实部署成败为评价标准的 IaC 生成基准与迭代反馈框架。","au":["Tianyi Zhang","Shidong pan","zejun zhang","Zhenchang Xing","xiaoyu sun"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Infrastructure-as-Code","deployability","LLM code generation","benchmark","DevOps feedback loop"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/43/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.05623"},{"id":"p00852","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding Performance Problems in CUDA Programs","tz":"理解 CUDA 程序中的性能问题","a":"With the wide adoption of GPUs in high-performance computing, CUDA programming has become essential for leveraging GPU parallelism. However, its complex programming model poses challenges in performance optimization. Consequently, CUDA programs often suffer from performance problems. In that sense, it is crucial to understand the performance problems specific to CUDA programming. Unfortunately, no systematic study has been conducted in literature. To bridge this gap, we conduct the first systematic study to 1) characterize the symptoms and root causes of 216 performance problems collected from 55 StackOverflow posts and 122 NVIDIA forum posts, and 2) measure the speedup of fixing performance problems, and assess the capability of existing performance analysis methods using a dataset of 69 reproduced performance problems. Our findings provide practical guidance for developers, and opportunities for researchers to advance performance analysis.","az":"随着 GPU 在高性能计算中的广泛采用，CUDA 编程已成为利用 GPU 并行性的关键。然而，其复杂的编程模型给性能优化带来了挑战。因此，CUDA 程序常常存在性能问题。就此而言，理解 CUDA 编程特有的性能问题至关重要。遗憾的是，文献中尚未开展系统性的研究。为弥补这一空白，我们开展了首个系统性研究：1）刻画了从 55 个 StackOverflow 帖子和 122 个 NVIDIA 论坛帖子中收集的 216 个性能问题的症状与根因；2）度量了修复性能问题所带来的加速比，并利用一个包含 69 个可复现性能问题的数据集评估了现有性能分析方法的能力。我们的发现为开发者提供了实用指导，也为研究者推进性能分析提供了机会。","tl":"首个对 CUDA 性能问题症状与根因的系统性实证刻画。","au":["Yuyang Bi","Junming Cao","You Lu","Bihuan Chen","Tianwei Gan","Dingji Wang","Xin Peng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["CUDA","performance problems","GPU programming","empirical study","performance analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/44/x"},{"id":"p00853","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TypePro: Boosting LLM-Based Type Inference via Inter-Procedural Slicing","tz":"TypePro：通过过程间切片提升基于 LLM 的类型推断","a":"Dynamic languages (such as Python and JavaScript) offer flexibility and simplified type handling for programming, but this can also lead to an increase in type-related errors and additional overhead for compile-time type inference. As a result, type inference for dynamic languages has become a popular research area. Existing approaches typically achieve type inference through static analysis, machine learning, or large language models (LLMs). However, current work only focuses on the direct dependencies of variables related to type inference as the context, resulting in incomplete contextual information and thus affecting the accuracy of type inference. To address this issue, this paper proposes a method called TypePro, which leverages LLMs for type inference in dynamic languages. TypePro supplements contextual information by conducting inter-procedural code slicing. Then, TypePro proposes a set of candidate complex types based on the structural information of data types implied in the slices, thereby addressing the lack of domain knowledge of LLMs. We conducted experiments on the ManyTypes4Py and ManyTypes4TypeScript datasets, achieving Top-1 exact match (EM) rates of 88.9% and 86.6%, respectively. Notably, TypePro improves the Top-1 Exact Match by 7.1 and 10.3 percentage points over the second-best approach, showing the effectiveness and robustness of TypePro.","az":"动态语言（如 Python 和 JavaScript）为编程提供了灵活性和简化的类型处理，但这也会导致类型相关错误增多，并给编译期类型推断带来额外开销。因此，动态语言的类型推断已成为热门研究方向。现有方法通常通过静态分析、机器学习或大语言模型（LLM）实现类型推断。然而，当前工作仅将与类型推断相关变量的直接依赖作为上下文，导致上下文信息不完整，从而影响类型推断的准确率。为解决这一问题，本文提出了一种名为 TypePro 的方法，利用 LLM 对动态语言进行类型推断。TypePro 通过进行过程间代码切片来补充上下文信息。随后，TypePro 基于切片中隐含的数据类型结构信息提出一组候选复杂类型，从而弥补 LLM 领域知识的缺失。我们在 ManyTypes4Py 和 ManyTypes4TypeScript 数据集上开展了实验，分别取得了 88.9% 和 86.6% 的 Top-1 精确匹配（EM）率。值得注意的是，TypePro 的 Top-1 精确匹配比次优方法分别提升了 7.1 和 10.3 个百分点，表明了 TypePro 的有效性与鲁棒性。","tl":"用过程间切片补全上下文并给出候选复杂类型来增强 LLM 类型推断。","au":["linTeyu","Minghao Fan","Huaxun Huang","Zhirong Shen","Rongxin Wu"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["type inference","dynamic languages","inter-procedural slicing","LLM","ManyTypes4Py"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/45/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.02702"},{"id":"p00854","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding and Predicting Accepted Code Suggestions in AI-Assisted Programming","tz":"理解并预测 AI 辅助编程中被接受的代码建议","a":"AI-assisted programming tools are widely adopted, yet their practical utility is often undermined by undesired suggestions that interrupt developer workflows and cause frustration. While existing research has explored developer-AI interactions when programming qualitatively, a significant gap remains in quantitative analysis of developers’ acceptance of AI-generated code suggestions, partly because the necessary fine-grained interaction data is often proprietary. To bridge this gap, this paper conducts an empirical study using 66,329 industrial developer-AI interactions from a large technology company. We analyze features that are significantly different between accepted code suggestions and rejected ones. We find that accepted suggestions are characterized by significantly higher historical acceptance counts and ratios for both developers and projects, longer generation intervals, shorter preceding code context in the project, and older IDE versions. Based on these findings, we introduce CSAP (Code Suggestion Acceptance Prediction) to predict whether a developer will accept the code suggestion before it is displayed. Our evaluation of CSAP shows that it achieves the accuracy of 0.973 and 0.922 on imbalanced and balanced dataset respectively. Compared to a large language model baseline and an in-production industrial filter, CSAP relatively improves the accuracy by 12.6% and 69.5% on imbalanced dataset, and improves the accuracy by 87.0% and 140.1% on balanced dataset. Our results demonstrate that targeted personalization is a powerful approach for filtering out code suggestions with predicted rejection and reduce developer interruption. To the best of our knowledge, it is the first quantitative study of code suggestion acceptance on large-scale industrial data, and this work also sheds light on an important research direction of AI-assisted programming.","az":"AI 辅助编程工具已被广泛采用，但其实际效用常因不合意的建议打断开发者工作流、引发挫败感而被削弱。尽管已有研究定性地探讨了编程时的开发者-AI 交互，但在开发者对 AI 生成代码建议接受度的定量分析方面仍存在显著空白，部分原因在于所需的细粒度交互数据往往是专有的。为弥补这一空白，本文利用来自一家大型科技公司的 66,329 条工业开发者-AI 交互记录开展了一项实证研究。我们分析了被接受与被拒绝的代码建议之间存在显著差异的特征。我们发现，被接受的建议表现为：开发者与项目层面的历史接受次数和接受比例显著更高、生成间隔更长、项目中前置代码上下文更短，以及 IDE 版本更旧。基于这些发现，我们提出了 CSAP（代码建议接受度预测），用于在建议展示之前预测开发者是否会接受该代码建议。我们对 CSAP 的评估表明，其在不平衡数据集和平衡数据集上分别达到 0.973 和 0.922 的准确率。与一个大语言模型基线和一个在产的工业过滤器相比，CSAP 在不平衡数据集上相对提升准确率 12.6% 和 69.5%，在平衡数据集上提升 87.0% 和 140.1%。结果表明，有针对性的个性化是过滤掉预测会被拒绝的代码建议、减少开发者打断的有力途径。据我们所知，这是首个基于大规模工业数据对代码建议接受度开展的定量研究，本工作也为 AI 辅助编程指出了一个重要的研究方向。","tl":"用工业交互数据在展示前预测建议是否会被接受以减少打断。","au":["Jing Jiang","Liehao Li","Jinyun Hou","Xin Tan","Li Zhang"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study"],"kw":["code suggestion acceptance","developer-AI interaction","industrial dataset","personalization","prediction model"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/46/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21379"},{"id":"p00855","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Do Not Treat Code as Natural Language: Implications for Repository-Level Code Generation and Beyond","tz":"不要把代码当作自然语言：对仓库级代码生成及其他任务的启示","a":"Large language models for code (CodeLLMs) have demonstrated remarkable success in standalone code completion and generation, sometimes even surpassing human performance, yet their effectiveness diminishes in repository-level settings where cross-file dependencies and structural context are essential. Existing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) approaches often borrow strategies from NLP, relying on chunking-based indexing and similarity-based retrieval. Chunking results in the loss of coherence between code units and overlooks structural relationships, while similarity-driven methods frequently miss functionally relevant dependencies such as helper functions, classes, or global variables. To address these limitations, we present Hydra, a repository-level code generation framework that treats code as structured code rather than natural language. Our approach introduces (i) a structure-aware indexing strategy that represents repositories as hierarchical trees of functions, classes, and variables, preserving code structure and dependencies, (ii) a lightweight dependency-aware retriever (DAR) that explicitly identifies and retrieves the true dependencies required by a target function, and (iii) a hybrid retrieval mechanism that combines DAR with similarity-based retrieval to provide both essential building blocks and practical usage examples. Extensive experiments on the challenging DevEval and RepoExec benchmarks, both requiring function implementation from real-world repositories with complex large repository context, show that Hydra achieves state-of-the-art performance across open- and closed-source CodeLLMs. Notably, our method establishes a new state of the art in repository-level code generation, surpassing strongest baseline by over 5% in Pass@1 and even enabling smaller models to match or exceed the performance of much larger ones that rely on existing retrievers.","az":"面向代码的大语言模型（CodeLLM）在独立的代码补全与生成中取得了显著成功，有时甚至超越人类表现，但在跨文件依赖和结构上下文至关重要的仓库级场景中，其效果会下降。现有的检索增强生成（RAG）方法常常照搬 NLP 的策略，依赖基于分块的索引和基于相似度的检索。分块会破坏代码单元之间的连贯性并忽略结构关系，而相似度驱动的方法常常遗漏功能上相关的依赖，例如辅助函数、类或全局变量。为解决这些局限，我们提出了 Hydra，一个把代码当作结构化代码而非自然语言来处理的仓库级代码生成框架。我们的方法引入了：(i) 结构感知的索引策略，将仓库表示为由函数、类和变量构成的层次树，保留代码结构与依赖；(ii) 轻量级的依赖感知检索器（DAR），显式识别并检索目标函数所需的真实依赖；(iii) 混合检索机制，将 DAR 与基于相似度的检索结合，既提供必需的构件，也提供实际的用法示例。在具有挑战性的 DevEval 和 RepoExec 基准（二者都要求在复杂的大型仓库上下文中实现真实仓库的函数）上的大量实验表明，Hydra 在开源与闭源 CodeLLM 上均取得了最先进的性能。值得注意的是，我们的方法在仓库级代码生成上确立了新的最先进水平，Pass@1 超过最强基线 5% 以上，甚至使较小的模型能够匹敌或超过依赖现有检索器的大得多的模型。","tl":"用层次结构索引加依赖感知检索替代分块相似度 RAG。","au":["Minh Le-Anh","Huyen Nguyen","Khanh An Tran","Nam Le Hai","Linh Ngo Van","Nghi D. Q. Bui","Xuan-Bach D. Le"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["repository-level code generation","structure-aware indexing","dependency-aware retrieval","RAG","DevEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/47/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.11671"},{"id":"p00856","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Small is Beautiful: A Practical and Efficient Log Parsing Framework","tz":"小即是美：一个实用高效的日志解析框架","a":"Log parsing is a fundamental step in log analysis, partitioning raw logs into constant templates and dynamic variables. While recent semantic-based parsers leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) exhibit superior generalizability over traditional syntax-based methods, their effectiveness is heavily contingent on model scale. This dependency leads to significant performance collapse when employing smaller, more resource-efficient LLMs. Such degradation creates a major barrier to real-world adoption, where data privacy requirements and computational constraints necessitate the use of succinct models. To bridge this gap, we propose EFParser, an unsupervised LLM-based log parser designed to enhance the capabilities of smaller models through systematic architectural innovation. EFParser introduces a dual-cache system with an adaptive updating mechanism that distinguishes between novel patterns and variations of existing templates. This allows the parser to merge redundant templates and rectify prior errors, maintaining cache consistency. Furthermore, a dedicated correction module acts as a gatekeeper, validating and refining every LLM-generated template before caching to prevent error injection. Empirical evaluations on public large-scale datasets demonstrate that EFParser outperforms state-of-the-art baselines by an average of 12.5% across all metrics when running on smaller LLMs, even surpassing some baselines utilizing large-scale models. Despite its additional validation steps, EFParser maintains high computational efficiency, offering a robust and practical solution for real-world log analysis deployment.","az":"日志解析是日志分析的基础步骤，它将原始日志划分为固定模板和动态变量。尽管近来利用大语言模型（LLM）的语义类解析器相比传统的基于语法的方法展现出更强的泛化能力，但其效果高度依赖于模型规模。这种依赖导致在使用更小、更省资源的 LLM 时性能急剧崩塌。这种退化构成了现实落地的主要障碍，因为在数据隐私要求和算力约束下必须使用精简模型。为弥合这一差距，我们提出了 EFParser，一个无监督的基于 LLM 的日志解析器，通过系统性的架构创新来增强小模型的能力。EFParser 引入了带自适应更新机制的双缓存系统，能够区分全新模式与既有模板的变体。这使解析器可以合并冗余模板并纠正先前的错误，从而保持缓存一致性。此外，一个专门的纠错模块充当守门员，在缓存之前对每个 LLM 生成的模板进行验证与精化，以防止错误注入。在公开的大规模数据集上的实证评估表明，EFParser 在小型 LLM 上运行时，在所有指标上平均超过最先进基线 12.5%，甚至超越了部分使用大规模模型的基线。尽管增加了额外的验证步骤，EFParser 仍保持了很高的计算效率，为真实世界的日志分析部署提供了稳健实用的方案。","tl":"双缓存加纠错守门，使小模型也能做好日志解析。","au":["Minxing Wang","Yintong Huo"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["log parsing","small LLM","dual-cache","unsupervised","log analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/48/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22590"},{"id":"p00857","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Detection of Configuration-Specific Security Vulnerabilities via Patch Analysis","tz":"通过补丁分析自动检测配置相关的安全漏洞","a":"We study how security patches in highly configurable C/C++ systems map onto the space of compile-time variants. We formalize the Vulnerability Impact Condition (VIC)—a Boolean predicate over configuration options that denotes all variants that contained the original flaw—and introduce PatchLens, a purely static technique that recovers VICs by aligning AST-level patch hunks with source-level presence conditions and resolving file inclusion via lightweight build system analysis. Evaluating PatchLens on 1,193 Linux kernel, 290 FFmpeg, and 99 PHP patches, we compute precise, human-readable VICs without the need to compile any system variant. The resulting predicates are compact (avg. 2.09 variables for Linux, 3.30 for FFmpeg, 0.95 for PHP) and show that only a small fraction of vulnerabilities are system-wide, which carry higher CVSS scores; meanwhile, CVE texts almost never encode the required options (≈1% average recall), motivating automated enrichment of CVE descriptions with VICs. PatchLens and the accompanying dataset enable immediate applications in CI (variant-aware triage and test selection), targeted sampling and fuzzing, and feature risk scoring, offering a scalable, explainable path to vulnerability assessment in highly configurable software.","az":"我们研究高可配置 C/C++ 系统中的安全补丁如何映射到编译期变体空间。我们形式化了漏洞影响条件（Vulnerability Impact Condition，VIC）——一个定义在配置选项上的布尔谓词，用于表示所有包含原始缺陷的变体——并提出了 PatchLens，一种纯静态技术，通过将 AST 级补丁块与源码级存在条件对齐，并借助轻量级构建系统分析解析文件包含关系，从而恢复 VIC。我们在 1,193 个 Linux 内核补丁、290 个 FFmpeg 补丁和 99 个 PHP 补丁上评估 PatchLens，无需编译任何系统变体即可计算出精确且人类可读的 VIC。得到的谓词十分紧凑（Linux 平均 2.09 个变量，FFmpeg 3.30 个，PHP 0.95 个），并表明只有一小部分漏洞是全系统性的，而这部分漏洞的 CVSS 评分更高；与此同时，CVE 文本几乎从不编码所需的配置选项（平均召回率约 1%），这促使我们用 VIC 自动丰富 CVE 描述。PatchLens 及其配套数据集可直接应用于 CI（变体感知的分诊与测试选择）、定向采样与模糊测试以及特征风险评分，为高可配置软件的漏洞评估提供了一条可扩展、可解释的路径。","tl":"用静态补丁与存在条件对齐推出漏洞影响的配置谓词。","au":["Felipe Paixão","Eduardo Almeida","Joanna C. S. Santos","Paulo Anselmo da Mota Silveira Neto","Daniel Sadoc Menasche","Gustavo B. Figueiredo"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","tg":["non-llm-classical","benchmark-dataset","empirical-study"],"kw":["vulnerability impact condition","configurable systems","patch analysis","presence condition","CVE enrichment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/49/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.25863"},{"id":"p00858","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Property Refinement in Linear Temporal Logic: Formal Semantics and Algorithms for Software Verification","tz":"线性时序逻辑中的性质精化：面向软件验证的形式语义与算法","a":"Model checking using temporal logic is a key aspect of formal verification of modern complex software systems. These systems are often result of distributed development processes, involving multiple teams and iterative design cycles. This complexity is mirrored in the corresponding formal specifications, which often consist of a large number of temporal logic properties that need to be verified against a system model. Many of these properties overlap semantically, yet traditional verification treats them as independent, resulting in redundant checks that waste computational resources and inflate engineering effort We address this by introducing and operationalizing a formal theory of property refinement for temporal logic into a concrete methodology that automatically identifies and eliminates redundant properties from a verification suite. This is achieved by first partitioning specifications into equivalence classes based on shared atomic propositions, followed by an analysis of intra-class refinement relations to construct the minimal sufficient subset. Our extensive empirical evaluation confirms the practical viability of our approach, demonstrating it can reduce the number of required verification tasks by up to 75% and accelerate model checking by up to three orders of magnitude, with a one-time associated overhead cost of 0.035% for the refinement analysis. The results of the evaluation confirm that the benefits of this approach are threefold: it reduces the computational requirements for formal verification; it allows engineers to focus on the core requirements of the system, hereby reducing engineering effort; finally, the one-time negligible investment in refinement yields compounding returns, making it particularly advantageous for agile and long-term development lifecycles. This work thus establishes property refinement analysis as a key technique for scaling requirement engineering and software verification to modern complex software systems","az":"使用时序逻辑的模型检验是现代复杂软件系统形式化验证的关键环节。这些系统往往是分布式开发过程的产物，涉及多个团队与迭代式设计周期。这种复杂性也反映在相应的形式化规约中：它们常常包含大量需要针对系统模型进行验证的时序逻辑性质。其中许多性质在语义上相互重叠，而传统验证却把它们当作彼此独立来处理，导致冗余检查，浪费计算资源并抬高工程成本。为解决这一问题，我们引入并落地了一套关于时序逻辑“性质精化”的形式理论，将其转化为一种具体方法，可自动识别并剔除验证套件中的冗余性质。具体做法是：首先依据共享的原子命题把规约划分为等价类，随后分析类内的精化关系以构造最小充分子集。我们广泛的实证评估证实了该方法的实用可行性，表明它可将所需验证任务数量减少多达 75%，并将模型检验加速多达三个数量级，而精化分析仅带来一次性 0.035% 的开销成本。评估结果证实该方法有三重收益：降低形式化验证的计算需求；使工程师能够聚焦系统的核心需求，从而减少工程投入；最后，这一次性可忽略的投入会带来复利式回报，对敏捷与长周期开发生命周期尤为有利。因此，本工作确立了性质精化分析作为将需求工程与软件验证扩展到现代复杂软件系统的关键技术。","tl":"用 LTL 性质精化关系剔除冗余验证任务，检验提速三个数量级。","au":["Luca Brodo","Giuseppe Scalora","Stefan Henkler"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["linear temporal logic","property refinement","model checking","formal verification","specification redundancy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/50/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/50/Property-Refinement-in-Linear-Temporal-Logic-Formal-Semantics-and-Algorithms-for-Sof"},{"id":"p00859","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"OdoTest: An Automated Testing Approach for Odometry Systems","tz":"OdoTest：一种面向里程计系统的自动化测试方法","a":"Accurate odometry estimation is critical for the reliable operation of intelligent systems. Despite the remarkable progress of deep learning–based odometry models in controlled environments, real-world degradations such as IMU noise, visual impairments, and calibration errors often lead to significant estimation failures. Conventional testing methods, constrained by limited datasets and costly manual labeling, are insufficient for systematically revealing these vulnerabilities. In this paper, we propose OdoTest, the first automated testing framework for odometry models. OdoTest leverages odometry-specific metamorphic relations and introduces transformation operators that simulate realistic sensor and calibration perturbations, enabling the generation of transformed test datasets that expose model weaknesses. An odometry-oriented scenario generation strategy further improves testing efficiency. We evaluate OdoTest across multiple odometry models, and the results demonstrate that it can effectively detect erroneous behaviors under diverse odometry-specific conditions. Additionally, retraining with the generated scenarios improves odometry precision and reduces estimation errors, highlighting OdoTest’s potential for enhancing model reliability.","az":"精确的里程计估计对智能系统的可靠运行至关重要。尽管基于深度学习的里程计模型在受控环境中取得了显著进展，但现实世界中的退化因素——如 IMU 噪声、视觉受损和标定误差——常常导致严重的估计失败。传统测试方法受限于有限的数据集和高昂的人工标注成本，不足以系统性地揭示这些脆弱点。本文提出 OdoTest，首个面向里程计模型的自动化测试框架。OdoTest 利用里程计特有的蜕变关系，并引入了模拟真实传感器与标定扰动的变换算子，从而生成能够暴露模型弱点的变换后测试数据集。一种面向里程计的场景生成策略进一步提升了测试效率。我们在多个里程计模型上评估了 OdoTest，结果表明它能在多样的里程计特定条件下有效检测出错误行为。此外，使用生成的场景进行再训练可提升里程计精度并降低估计误差，凸显了 OdoTest 在增强模型可靠性方面的潜力。","tl":"首个用里程计专属蜕变关系自动测试里程计模型的框架。","au":["Jixiang Zhou","Mingfei Cheng","Shuncheng Tang","An Guo","Xiaofei Xie","Yinxing Xue","Lijun Zhang"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["odometry testing","metamorphic relations","sensor perturbation","scenario generation","model reliability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/51/x"},{"id":"p00860","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Validating LLM-Generated SQL Queries Through Metamorphic Prompting","tz":"通过蜕变提示验证 LLM 生成的 SQL 查询","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) can translate natural language (NL) into SQL, enabling non-experts to query databases via conversational interfaces. However, the generated SQL often contains intent-violating hallucinations—queries that are syntactically valid and executable, yet semantically misaligned with the user’s question. These failures are especially risky in real-world settings where users cannot verify the correctness. In this paper, we propose MRSQLGen, a framework for detecting intent-violating hallucinations, built on the metamorphic prompting paradigm. MRSQLGen rewrites the input prompt using task-specific transformation rules derived from a hallucination taxonomy, and validates the generated SQL by checking behavioral consistency across multiple executions. Each transformation is associated with a metamorphic relationship (MR) that defines the expected relation between results; discrepancies are aggregated through a majority-vote strategy to robustly flag hallucinations without ground-truth SQL. We evaluate MRSQLGen on two benchmarks (Spider and Bird) using five representative LLMs, including GPT-4o. Experimental results demonstrate that MRSQLGen consistently outperforms state-of-the-art hallucination detection techniques, achieving higher precision and recall in detecting hallucinated SQL queries.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）可以把自然语言（NL）翻译成 SQL，使非专家也能通过对话式界面查询数据库。然而，生成的 SQL 常常包含违背意图的幻觉——这些查询语法有效且可执行，但语义上与用户的问题不一致。在用户无法验证正确性的真实场景中，这类失败尤其危险。本文提出 MRSQLGen，一个建立在蜕变提示范式之上、用于检测违背意图幻觉的框架。MRSQLGen 使用从幻觉分类体系中导出的任务特定变换规则重写输入提示，并通过检查多次执行之间的行为一致性来验证生成的 SQL。每个变换都关联一个蜕变关系（MR），用以定义结果之间的预期关系；差异通过多数投票策略汇总，从而在没有真值 SQL 的情况下稳健地标记出幻觉。我们在两个基准（Spider 和 Bird）上使用包括 GPT-4o 在内的五个代表性 LLM 评估了 MRSQLGen。实验结果表明，MRSQLGen 始终优于最先进的幻觉检测技术，在检测幻觉 SQL 查询上取得了更高的精确率与召回率。","tl":"用蜕变提示与执行一致性在无真值下识别 SQL 幻觉。","au":["Li Lin","Qinglin Zhu","Jintai Hong","Chong Wang","Yang Liu","Rongxin Wu"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["text-to-SQL","hallucination detection","metamorphic prompting","metamorphic relation","Spider/Bird"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/52/x"},{"id":"p00861","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"On the Road to Personalized Code Intelligence: Portraiting and Assisting Developers Based on Their In-IDE Behaviors","tz":"迈向个性化代码智能：基于 IDE 内行为的开发者画像与辅助","a":"With the advent of powerful large language models (LLMs), research in automated software engineering has increasingly focused on leveraging these models to achieve a deeper semantic understanding of code or to engineer sophisticated agent-based processes. The predominant goal of these efforts is to enhance developer productivity through automated assistance. However, this research trajectory has largely overlooked a critical factor: the developers themselves. Programming is a deeply human and individualized activity; developers exhibit significant variation in their coding styles, tool-chain preferences, domain-specific expertise, and problem-solving strategies. Consequently, the current paradigm of one-size-fits-all code intelligence systems struggles to accommodate the unique characteristics and needs of individual developers. To address this gap, we introduce VirtualME, a novel IDE-embedded data infrastructure designed to model the developer by continuously capturing and interpreting their dynamic programming behaviors and preferences. VirtualME contains three components. (1) Log-level Behavior Extraction: it captures and extracts developers’ log-level behaviors (edits, navigations, etc.) from IDE. (2) Task-level Behavior Recognition: it aggregates log-level behaviors into task-level behaviors (“skimming API docs”, “iterative debugging”, etc.) via a multi-agent pipeline. (3) Developer-personality Measurement: it builds a rule engine to distill a four-dimensional developer persona: technology stack, ability, behavioral habits, and learning style. On top of VirtualME, we propose a solution for personalized repository-level knowledge Q&A by integrating the developer persona into a Chain-of-Thought (CoT) guided agent. We evaluated VirtualME by building a multi-repository benchmark with real-world developer trajectories, balancing correctness and personalization. Experimental results show that VirtualME-enhanced answers outperform generic baselines on five dimensions: correctness, cognitive-level fit, technology-stack relevance, behavioral-pattern alignment, and stylistic preference, yielding an average 33.80% improvement. Our results demonstrate that abundant, continuous developer-behavior data can unlockPersonalized Code Intelligence. By integrating this personalized understanding into the code intelligence loop, our approach paves the new way for adaptive and personalized code intelligence.","az":"随着强大的大语言模型（LLM）的出现，自动化软件工程研究日益聚焦于利用这些模型实现对代码更深层次的语义理解，或构建复杂的基于智能体的流程。这些努力的主要目标是通过自动化辅助提升开发者生产力。然而，这条研究路线在很大程度上忽略了一个关键因素：开发者本身。编程是一项深具人性且高度个体化的活动；开发者在编码风格、工具链偏好、领域专长和问题求解策略上存在显著差异。因此，当前“一刀切”的代码智能系统难以适配个体开发者的独特特征与需求。为填补这一空白，我们提出了 VirtualME，一种全新的嵌入 IDE 的数据基础设施，通过持续捕获和解读开发者动态的编程行为与偏好来对开发者建模。VirtualME 包含三个组件：(1) 日志级行为抽取：从 IDE 捕获并抽取开发者的日志级行为（编辑、导航等）；(2) 任务级行为识别：通过多智能体流水线把日志级行为聚合为任务级行为（如“浏览 API 文档”“迭代调试”）；(3) 开发者个性度量：构建规则引擎提炼出四维开发者画像：技术栈、能力、行为习惯和学习风格。在 VirtualME 之上，我们提出了一种个性化的仓库级知识问答方案，将开发者画像融入由思维链（CoT）引导的智能体中。我们通过构建一个包含真实开发者轨迹、兼顾正确性与个性化的多仓库基准来评估 VirtualME。实验结果表明，VirtualME 增强的回答在五个维度上优于通用基线：正确性、认知水平契合度、技术栈相关性、行为模式一致性和风格偏好，平均提升 33.80%。结果表明，丰富且连续的开发者行为数据能够解锁个性化代码智能。通过将这种个性化理解融入代码智能闭环，我们的方法为自适应、个性化的代码智能开辟了新路径。","tl":"用 IDE 行为日志建开发者画像，驱动个性化仓库问答。","au":["Yuhong Liu","YUNHE SU","Zhipeng Peng","Zhiwen Luo","Lin Shi","Zhi Jin","Li Zhang"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","agentic"],"kw":["IDE behavior telemetry","developer persona","personalized code intelligence","multi-agent pipeline","repository QA"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/53/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.29372"},{"id":"p00862","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Evaluating LLM-based Regression Test Generation","tz":"评估基于 LLM 的回归测试生成","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown tremendous promise in automated software engineering. In this paper, we investigate the opportunities of LLMs for just-in-time regression test generation for programs, like parsers, interpreters, or compilers, that take highly structured, human-readable inputs. When a new bug fix or code change is committed, the repository (as part of the CI/CD workflow) runs an LLM for a few minutes to generate regression test cases for that commit that exercise the changed code and potentially trigger any bugs. Specifically, we investigate LLM-based regression test generation as a machine translation task that takes the developer-provided commit message, the code change, and the name of the input format (e.g., XML) and produces regression test cases for the described change in the given input format. In our experiments testing 46 commits to Mujs, Libxml2, Poppler, JerryScript, Z3, and PHP, our feedback-directed, zero-shot LLM-based prototype Cleverest performed unexpectedly well, even if we did not provide the code change. In under 2 minutes, on average, Cleverest found more bugs than the state-of-the-art directed greybox fuzzer WAFLGo in 24 hours, even though WAFLGo started with a commit-reaching seed corpus in the majority of cases. If we amplify the Cleverest-generated test cases using those as a seed corpus in coverage-guided greybox fuzzing, the number of bugs found almost doubles. We call the integration with fuzzing as ClevFuzz . In addition, we found that some commit messages are more expressive than others, thus we wonder how this impacts the effectiveness of Cleverest. Our results above demonstrate that Cleverest picks up on the change intention. For instance, if the commit message describes that this patch changes how floating point variables are treated in the MuJS JavaScript interpreter, then Cleverest generates JavaScript programs that contain floating point variables. To study the impact of expressiveness, we change the commit messages minimally to reduce and increase the information in the commit message, respectively, and find a substantial impact on effectiveness. For instance, adding 18 words on average (max. 46) to make ineffective commit messages more expressive almost doubled the number of bugs found.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在自动化软件工程中展现出巨大潜力。本文研究 LLM 在为接受高度结构化、人类可读输入的程序（如解析器、解释器或编译器）进行即时回归测试生成方面的机会。当一个新的缺陷修复或代码变更被提交时，仓库（作为 CI/CD 工作流的一部分）运行 LLM 数分钟，为该提交生成能够触及被改动代码、并可能触发缺陷的回归测试用例。具体而言，我们把基于 LLM 的回归测试生成视为一项机器翻译任务：输入是开发者提供的提交信息、代码变更和输入格式名称（如 XML），输出是针对所描述变更、采用给定输入格式的回归测试用例。在我们对 Mujs、Libxml2、Poppler、JerryScript、Z3 和 PHP 的 46 个提交的测试实验中，我们的反馈导向、零样本的基于 LLM 的原型 Cleverest 表现出乎意料地好，即使我们并不提供代码变更也是如此。平均在 2 分钟内，Cleverest 发现的缺陷就多于最先进的定向灰盒模糊器 WAFLGo 在 24 小时内发现的数量，尽管 WAFLGo 在多数情况下是从可到达该提交的种子语料开始的。如果我们把 Cleverest 生成的测试用例作为种子语料放入覆盖率引导的灰盒模糊测试中进行放大，发现的缺陷数量几乎翻倍。我们把这种与模糊测试的结合称为 ClevFuzz。此外，我们发现有些提交信息比其他的更具表达力，因此我们想知道这会如何影响 Cleverest 的效果。上述结果表明 Cleverest 能够捕捉到变更意图。例如，如果提交信息描述该补丁改变了 MuJS JavaScript 解释器中浮点变量的处理方式，Cleverest 就会生成包含浮点变量的 JavaScript 程序。为研究表达力的影响，我们对提交信息做最小化修改以分别减少和增加其信息量，发现这对效果有实质性影响。例如，平均增加 18 个词（最多 46 个）以使原本无效的提交信息更具表达力，可使发现的缺陷数量几乎翻倍。","tl":"把提交信息当翻译输入，零样本生成回归测试胜过定向模糊器。","au":["Jing Liu","Seongmin Lee","Eleonora Losiouk","Marcel Böhme"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["regression test generation","commit message","LLM","directed greybox fuzzing","interpreters and compilers"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/54/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.11086"},{"id":"p00863","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Beyond Language Boundaries: Uncovering Programming Language Families for Code Language Models","tz":"超越语言边界：为代码语言模型揭示编程语言的语系","a":"The rapid proliferation of diverse programming languages presents both opportunities and challenges for developing multilingual code LLMs. While existing techniques often train code LLMs by simply aggregating multilingual code data, few explore the deeper relationships between programming languages and how such relationships can be utilized to optimize the training and inference of code LLMs. In this work, we investigate two fundamental questions: (1) What are the deep linguistic relationships among programming languages? and (2) How can these relationships be leveraged to improve multilingual code LLMs? We propose an embedding-based framework to uncover the latent families of programming languages. Our approach begins by defining 21 primary linguistic features of programming languages, such as variable definition, control structures, and method declarations, and then employs LLMs to generate feature-aligned code samples across multiple languages. By embedding these semantically parallel code snippets from 19 languages, we construct a similarity matrix and perform hierarchical clustering to uncover inherent language relationships. Our analysis reveals clear hierarchical structures among programming languages. Closely related languages form well-defined clusters (e.g., C, C++, Java, and Swift group together), while Go exhibits as a central language with the highest cross-language similarity. Building on the uncovered language families, we propose three strategies to enhance multilingual LLM training: transfer learning across linguistically related languages, linguistic proximity-guided curriculum learning, and centroid-based intermediary code translation. Experiments on four code intelligence tasks demonstrate that our methods significantly improve multilingual LLM performance. This work offers a universal perspective on programming languages and advances more effective strategies for multilingual code LLM training.","az":"编程语言的迅速增多为开发多语言代码 LLM 带来了机遇也带来了挑战。现有技术通常只是简单聚合多语言代码数据来训练代码 LLM，很少探究编程语言之间的深层关系，以及如何利用这些关系来优化代码 LLM 的训练与推理。在本工作中，我们研究两个基础问题：(1) 编程语言之间存在怎样的深层语言学关系？(2) 如何利用这些关系改进多语言代码 LLM？我们提出了一个基于嵌入的框架来揭示编程语言的潜在语系。我们的方法首先定义了编程语言的 21 项主要语言学特征，例如变量定义、控制结构和方法声明，然后利用 LLM 跨多种语言生成特征对齐的代码样本。通过对来自 19 种语言的这些语义平行代码片段进行嵌入，我们构建了相似度矩阵并进行层次聚类，以揭示语言之间的固有关系。我们的分析揭示了编程语言之间清晰的层次结构。关系紧密的语言形成界限分明的簇（例如 C、C++、Java 和 Swift 聚在一起），而 Go 表现为跨语言相似度最高的中心语言。基于揭示出的语系，我们提出了三种增强多语言 LLM 训练的策略：在语言学相关的语言之间迁移学习、由语言学邻近性引导的课程学习，以及基于中心语言的中介代码翻译。在四项代码智能任务上的实验表明，我们的方法显著提升了多语言 LLM 的性能。本工作为编程语言提供了一个普适视角，并推进了更有效的多语言代码 LLM 训练策略。","tl":"用嵌入聚类给编程语言分“语系”，据此做迁移与课程学习。","au":["Shangbo Yun","Jianghong Huang","Xiaodong Gu","Beijun Shen"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","low-resource-or-non-english"],"kw":["multilingual code LLM","programming language families","hierarchical clustering","transfer learning","curriculum learning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/55/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.19509"},{"id":"p00864","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ToxiShield: Promoting Inclusive Developer Communication through Real-Time Toxicity Filtering","tz":"ToxiShield：通过实时毒性过滤促进包容的开发者沟通","a":"Toxic interactions during code reviews can undermine teamwork and hinder productivity in software engineering (SE) teams. While prior studies explore toxicity detection and empirical investigation, they lack real-time detoxification tools to support the SE community. To address this gap, we present ToxiShield, a browser extension for GitHub pull requests that is built using three modules: i) Toxicity Filter – to identify whether a text is toxic, ii) Communication coach – to facilitate just-in-time fine-grained toxicity categorization with explanations, and iii) The Reframer – that generates a revised, constructive alternative of a toxic text. For each module, we trained and evaluated multiple deep learning and Large Language Models (LLMs) to identify the best choice. A BERT-based binary detection model, trained on 38,761 code review samples, achieves 98% accuracy and an F1-score of 97% and is the selected one for the Toxicity Filter module. For the Communication Coach, prompt-tuned Claude 3.5 Sonnet achieved the best performance with 39% MCC and 42% F1 in multiclass toxicity classification with detailed reasoning. For Reframer, we evaluated five LLMs using a fine-tuning strategy on a dataset of 10,120 code review comments. The fine-tuned Llama 3.2 model achieves 95.27% style transfer accuracy, 97.03% fluency, 67.07% content preservation, and an 84% J-score. We further validated ToxiShield through a human evaluation using the Technology Acceptance Model with 10 participants, confirming its perceived usefulness and ease of adoption. ToxiShield sets a benchmark for advancing constructive communication in software engineering, driving inclusivity and healthier collaboration in open-source communities.","az":"代码评审中的毒性互动会破坏团队协作并阻碍软件工程（SE）团队的生产力。尽管已有研究探讨了毒性检测与实证调查，但缺少支持 SE 社区的实时去毒工具。为填补这一空白，我们提出了 ToxiShield，一个面向 GitHub 拉取请求的浏览器扩展，由三个模块构建：i) 毒性过滤器——判断一段文本是否有毒；ii) 沟通教练——提供即时的细粒度毒性分类及解释；iii) 重述器——为有毒文本生成修订后的建设性替代表达。对每个模块，我们训练并评估了多种深度学习模型和大语言模型（LLM）以确定最佳选择。一个基于 BERT 的二分类检测模型在 38,761 条代码评审样本上训练，达到 98% 的准确率和 97% 的 F1 分数，被选为毒性过滤器模块。对于沟通教练，经提示调优的 Claude 3.5 Sonnet 表现最佳，在带详细推理的多类毒性分类中取得 39% 的 MCC 和 42% 的 F1。对于重述器，我们在 10,120 条代码评审评论的数据集上以微调策略评估了五个 LLM。微调后的 Llama 3.2 模型取得 95.27% 的风格迁移准确率、97.03% 的流畅度、67.07% 的内容保持度和 84% 的 J 分数。我们进一步通过基于技术接受模型、有 10 名参与者的人类评估验证了 ToxiShield，确认了其感知有用性与易采纳性。ToxiShield 为推进软件工程中的建设性沟通树立了标杆，推动开源社区的包容性与更健康的协作。","tl":"浏览器插件实时检测并改写代码评审中的毒性言论。","au":["Md Awsaf Alam Anindya","Showvik Biswas","Anindya Iqbal","Jaydeb Sarker","Amiangshu Bosu"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","human-study"],"kw":["toxicity detection","code review communication","text detoxification","browser extension","inclusive collaboration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/56/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3808130"},{"id":"p00865","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ProofFusion: Improving Neural Theorem Proving via Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Reasoning","tz":"ProofFusion：通过自适应检索增强推理改进神经定理证明","a":"Interactive theorem proving (ITP) is a powerful approach to ensuring the correctness of complex software systems. However, it often requires substantial manual effort, which makes it costly to use in practice. Recently, neural network based approaches have shown promise in automatically generating proof tactics. Nevertheless, existing methods suffer from a long-tailed distribution in tactic usage within the training data. A few frequent tactics dominate the probability distribution, while many rare yet crucial ones are consistently suppressed in the model’s candidate ranking. This distributional bias can cause potentially provable goals to be prematurely abandoned during proof search. In addition, the decision making process of neural networks when generating tactics lacks explicit reasoning traces, making it difficult for humans to explain or verify the underlying logic. To address these limitations, we propose ProofFusion, an adaptive retrieval-augmented reasoning framework that improves the proving capability of neural theorem provers without requiring retraining. Our key insight is inspired by the way human provers tackle a new theorem by consulting similar previously proven theorems to guide their own reasoning. Specifically, we develop a proof semantic-aware retriever that searches a knowledge base for semantically similar historical proof goals together with their tactic, producing a traceable set of reference decisions. We then employ a dual-track reranking fusion mechanism to integrate both the original predictions of the neural model and the retrieved reference tactics. Furthermore, to mitigate potential noise introduced by retrieval, we design a capability-adaptive retrieval mechanism that dynamically determines when retrieval should be applied. We conduct a systematic evaluation on 10,782 theorems from 26 Coq projects in a real ITP environment. Experimental results show that ProofFusion increases the number of theorems proved by four state-of-the-art neural theorem provers by an average of 6.89%, and increases the number of previously unprovable theorems solved by an average of 17.50%. In addition, it substantially improves the explainability of proof steps, achieving an average explainable proof goal proportion of 82.1% across the four provers. Together, these results demonstrate that ProofFusion is a practical and effective complement to existing neural theorem proving systems, enhancing both performance and explainability.","az":"交互式定理证明（ITP）是确保复杂软件系统正确性的有力手段。然而，它往往需要大量人工投入，实际使用成本高昂。近来，基于神经网络的方法在自动生成证明策略（tactic）方面展现出前景。然而，现有方法受到训练数据中策略使用长尾分布的困扰：少数高频策略主导了概率分布，而许多罕见但关键的策略在模型候选排序中被持续压制。这种分布偏差会导致本可证明的目标在证明搜索中被过早放弃。此外，神经网络在生成策略时的决策过程缺乏显式的推理轨迹，使人难以解释或验证其底层逻辑。为解决这些局限，我们提出 ProofFusion，一种自适应的检索增强推理框架，无需重新训练即可提升神经定理证明器的证明能力。我们的关键洞见受人类证明者的启发：面对新定理时，他们会参考此前证明过的相似定理来引导自己的推理。具体而言，我们开发了一个证明语义感知的检索器，在知识库中搜索语义相似的历史证明目标及其策略，产生一组可追溯的参考决策。随后我们采用双轨重排融合机制，整合神经模型的原始预测与检索到的参考策略。此外，为缓解检索可能引入的噪声，我们设计了能力自适应的检索机制，动态判断何时应当应用检索。我们在真实 ITP 环境中对来自 26 个 Coq 项目的 10,782 个定理进行了系统评估。实验结果表明，ProofFusion 使四个最先进的神经定理证明器证明的定理数量平均提升 6.89%，并使此前无法证明的定理被解决的数量平均提升 17.50%。此外，它显著提升了证明步骤的可解释性，在四个证明器上平均达到 82.1% 的可解释证明目标比例。总之，这些结果表明 ProofFusion 是对现有神经定理证明系统切实有效的补充，同时提升了性能与可解释性。","tl":"检索历史证明目标并双轨重排，免训练提升神经定理证明。","au":["Manqing Zhang","Yunwei Dong","Lingru Zhou","Bingxu Xiao","Yepang Liu"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","llm-based"],"kw":["neural theorem proving","Coq","retrieval-augmented reasoning","tactic prediction","explainability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/57/x","pu":"https://manqing-zhang.github.io/publications/fse26.pdf"},{"id":"p00866","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RepoReasoner: Evaluating Repository-Level Code Reasoning Ability of Long-Context Language Models","tz":"RepoReasoner：评测长上下文语言模型的仓库级代码推理能力","a":"Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have significantly improved their ability to handle complex software engineering tasks at the repository level. However, existing benchmarks for evaluating code reasoning ability operate almost exclusively at the function level, where all necessary information is provided within a single, localized context. This approach fails to capture the complexity of real-world software development, where developers must reason about dependencies and logic scattered across entire repositories, creating a critical gap between current evaluation methodologies and real-world challenges. To bridge this gap, we introduce , a benchmark designed to evaluate repository-level code reasoning ability. Moving beyond self-contained code snippets, assesses LLMs’ ability to navigate, retrieve, and synthesize information distributed across multiple files through two tasks: (1) Output Prediction, which evaluates fine-grained, stateful reasoning by tracing complex, cross-file execution paths to predict a function’s final output, and (2) Call Chain Prediction, which assesses high-level architectural understanding by identifying the correct sequence of files involved in an execution from noisy context. We construct our benchmark using a multi-stage pipeline that leverages dynamic analysis of pytest execution traces to capture true, runtime-dependent call chains, and employs LLM-based I/O rewriting to create logically equivalent instances that prevent memorization. Our extensive evaluation of seven state-of-the-art LLMs reveals that repository-level reasoning remains a fundamental challenge. Even with perfect context, the best-performing model (DeepSeek-R1) achieves only 69.1% Pass@1 on Output Prediction, indicating that complex reasoning—not just retrieval—is the primary bottleneck. LLMs struggle with high-level architectural understanding, exhibiting high precision but low recall (F1 < 0.51) in call chain reconstruction. Counterintuitively, simply increasing context length can be counterproductive, as noise sometimes outweighs the benefits of additional information. All models show significant performance drops on our I/O-rewritten data, confirming partial reliance on memorization rather than genuine reasoning. These findings highlight the need for future research to focus on enhancing architectural comprehension and robust reasoning capabilities in repository-level code analysis.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展显著提升了其处理仓库级复杂软件工程任务的能力。然而，现有评测代码推理能力的基准几乎全部停留在函数级，所有必要信息都包含在单一的局部上下文中。这种做法无法刻画真实软件开发的复杂性——开发者必须对散布于整个仓库的依赖与逻辑进行推理，从而在当前评测方法与真实挑战之间造成了关键鸿沟。为弥合这一鸿沟，我们提出了一个旨在评测仓库级代码推理能力的基准。该基准超越自包含的代码片段，通过两项任务评估 LLM 在多个文件间导航、检索和综合信息的能力：(1) 输出预测，通过追踪复杂的跨文件执行路径来预测函数的最终输出，评估细粒度、有状态的推理；(2) 调用链预测，通过从含噪上下文中识别执行涉及的正确文件序列，评估高层架构理解。我们采用多阶段流水线构建基准：利用对 pytest 执行轨迹的动态分析捕获真实的、依赖运行时的调用链，并借助基于 LLM 的输入输出改写生成逻辑等价的实例以防止记忆。我们对七个最先进 LLM 的广泛评估表明，仓库级推理仍是根本性挑战。即便给予完美上下文，表现最好的模型（DeepSeek-R1）在输出预测上也仅达到 69.1% 的 Pass@1，说明复杂推理——而不仅仅是检索——才是主要瓶颈。LLM 在高层架构理解上表现挣扎，在调用链重建中精确率高但召回率低（F1 < 0.51）。与直觉相反，单纯增加上下文长度可能适得其反，因为噪声有时会盖过额外信息带来的收益。所有模型在我们改写输入输出的数据上都出现显著性能下降，证实其部分依赖记忆而非真正推理。这些发现凸显了未来研究需要聚焦于增强仓库级代码分析中的架构理解与稳健推理能力。","tl":"用跨文件输出预测与调用链预测揭示仓库级推理才是瓶颈。","au":["Yanlin Wang","Suiquan Wang","Yanli Wang","Bowen Zhang","Daya Guo","Jiachi Chen","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["repository-level code reasoning","benchmark","output prediction","call chain prediction","long-context LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/58/x"},{"id":"p00867","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"VulInstruct: Teaching LLMs Root-Cause Reasoning for Vulnerability Detection via Security Specifications","tz":"VulInstruct：通过安全规约教会 LLM 面向漏洞检测的根因推理","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have achieved remarkable progress in code understanding and analysis tasks. However, state-of-the-art LLMs demonstrate limited performance in vulnerability detection tasks, and even state-of-the-art models struggle to distinguish vulnerable code from patched code. We argue that a key reason for this limitation is that LLMs lack an understanding of security specifications—the expectations defined by developers and security teams about how code should behave to remain safe. When the actual behavior of the code differs from these expectations and introduces a security risk, it becomes a potential vulnerability. However, such knowledge is rarely explicit in training data, leaving models unable to reason about the root causes of security flaws. To address this challenge, We propose VulInstruct, a specification-guided approach that systematically extracts reusable security specifications from historical vulnerabilities to instruct the detection of new ones. Specifically, VulInstruct designs two automatic pipelines to construct a specification knowledge base from complementary perspectives: (i) General specifications, extracted from high-quality patches across diverse projects, capturing fundamental safe behaviors accumulated across the open-source ecosystem; and (ii) Domain-specific specifications, context-dependent expectations repeatedly violated in particular repositories or domains that are relevant to the target code under analysis. Before analyzing new code, VulInstruct leverages this specification knowledge base to retrieve relevant past cases and their associated specifications, enabling LLMs to reason about expected safe behaviors rather than relying solely on surface patterns. We evaluate VulInstruct under strict evaluation criteria requiring both correct predictions and valid reasoning. On the PrimeVul dataset, VulInstruct achieves 45.0% F1-score (32.7% improvement) and 37.7% recall (50.8% improvement) compared to the strongest baselines, while uniquely detecting 24.3% of all identified vulnerabilities—2.4 more than any baseline. In pair-wise evaluation distinguishing vulnerable from patched code, VulInstruct also achieves a 32.3% relative improvement over the best baseline. Beyond benchmarks, VulInstruct discovered a previously unknown high-severity vulnerability in production code by recognizing violations of extracted specifications, demonstrating its practical value for real-world vulnerability discovery. All code and supplementary materials are available at https://github.com/zhuhaopku/VulInstruct .","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在代码理解与分析任务上取得了显著进展。然而，最先进的 LLM 在漏洞检测任务中表现有限，甚至最先进的模型也难以区分有漏洞的代码与已打补丁的代码。我们认为，这一局限的关键原因在于 LLM 缺乏对安全规约的理解——即开发者与安全团队对代码应如何表现才算安全所定义的预期。当代码的实际行为偏离这些预期并引入安全风险时，就构成了潜在漏洞。然而，这类知识在训练数据中很少被显式表达，使模型无法对安全缺陷的根因进行推理。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 VulInstruct，一种规约引导的方法，系统性地从历史漏洞中抽取可复用的安全规约，用以指导对新漏洞的检测。具体而言，VulInstruct 设计了两条自动流水线，从互补视角构建安全规约知识库：(i) 通用规约，从跨多个项目的高质量补丁中抽取，刻画开源生态中积累的基本安全行为；(ii) 领域特定规约，即在特定仓库或领域中被反复违反、与待分析目标代码相关的上下文相关预期。在分析新代码之前，VulInstruct 利用该规约知识库检索相关的历史案例及其关联规约，使 LLM 能够对预期的安全行为进行推理，而不是仅依赖表面模式。我们在要求预测正确且推理有效的严格评价标准下评估 VulInstruct。在 PrimeVul 数据集上，VulInstruct 相比最强基线取得 45.0% 的 F1 分数（提升 32.7%）和 37.7% 的召回率（提升 50.8%），并独有地检出了全部已识别漏洞中的 24.3%——是任何基线的 2.4 倍。在区分有漏洞与已打补丁代码的成对评测中，VulInstruct 也比最佳基线相对提升 32.3%。除基准之外，VulInstruct 通过识别对所抽取规约的违反，在生产代码中发现了一个此前未知的高危漏洞，展示了其在真实漏洞发现中的实用价值。全部代码与补充材料见 https://github.com/zhuhaopku/VulInstruct 。","tl":"从历史补丁抽取可复用安全规约来引导漏洞根因推理。","au":["Hao Zhu","Jia Li","Cuiyun Gao","Jiaru Qian","Yihong Dong","Huanyu Liu","Lecheng Wang","Ziliang Wang","Xiaolong Hu","Ge Li"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","security specification","root-cause reasoning","PrimeVul","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/59/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/59/VulInstruct-Teaching-LLMs-Root-Cause-Reasoning-for-Vulnerability-Detection-via-Secur"},{"id":"p00868","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Knowledge-Graph-Driven Data Synthesis for Low-Resource Software Development: A HarmonyOS Case Study","tz":"知识图谱驱动的低资源软件开发数据合成：以 HarmonyOS 为例","a":"In low-resource framework software development (e.g., HarmonyOS), large language models (LLMs) typically lack exposure during pre-training, leading to poor performance when generating code for such frameworks. While LLMs often preserve code logic across different programming languages, they tend to fail on framework- specific APIs and syntax errors. This suggests that pre-training enables LLMs to master general algorithms, but they remain unfamiliar with the syntax and API characteristics of unseen low-resource languages or frameworks. Consequently, even large-scale commercial models such as GPT-4o struggle to produce correct code without prior knowledge of these elements. Inspired by these challenges, we introduce APIKG4Syn, a framework that leverages API knowledge graphs to generate API-Oriented question–code pairs without requiring executable code for low-resource framework. APIKG4Syn provides both single-API information and multi-API information, the latter identified through uncertainty estimation (UE)-guided Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS), to construct a comprehensive dataset for fine-tuning LLMs in low-resource scenarios. To evaluate APIKG4Syn, we select HarmonyOS as a case study and develop the first HarmonyOS benchmark for code generation. Experimental results demonstrate that Qwen fine-tuned with APIKG4Syn achieves a pass@1 of 25.00%, surpassing the untuned GPT baseline at 17.59%. These findings underscore the effectiveness of API-Oriented data in improving LLM performance for low-resource software development.","az":"在低资源框架软件开发（如 HarmonyOS）中，大语言模型（LLM）通常在预训练阶段缺乏接触，导致为此类框架生成代码时表现不佳。虽然 LLM 常能在不同编程语言之间保持代码逻辑，但它们往往在框架特有的 API 上失败并产生语法错误。这表明预训练使 LLM 掌握了通用算法，但它们仍不熟悉未见过的低资源语言或框架的语法与 API 特性。因此，即便是 GPT-4o 这样的大规模商用模型，在缺乏这些要素的先验知识时也难以产出正确代码。受这些挑战启发，我们提出 APIKG4Syn，一个利用 API 知识图谱为低资源框架生成面向 API 的问题—代码对、且无需可执行代码的框架。APIKG4Syn 同时提供单 API 信息与多 API 信息，后者通过不确定性估计（UE）引导的蒙特卡洛树搜索（MCTS）识别，用以构建在低资源场景下微调 LLM 的全面数据集。为评估 APIKG4Syn，我们选择 HarmonyOS 作为案例研究，并开发了首个 HarmonyOS 代码生成基准。实验结果表明，用 APIKG4Syn 微调的 Qwen 取得了 25.00% 的 pass@1，超过未调优的 GPT 基线的 17.59%。这些发现凸显了面向 API 的数据在提升 LLM 低资源软件开发能力方面的有效性。","tl":"用 API 知识图谱加 MCTS 合成训练数据攻克 HarmonyOS 代码生成。","au":["Mingwei Liu","Zheng Pei","Yanlin Wang","Zihao Wang","Zikang Li","Enci Lin","Xin Peng","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["low-resource-or-non-english","llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["low-resource framework","HarmonyOS","API knowledge graph","data synthesis","MCTS fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/60/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.00380"},{"id":"p00869","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Look Before You Leap: Context-Sensitive GUI Grounding for Boosting Automated Extended Reality (XR) Testing","tz":"三思而后行：上下文敏感的 GUI Grounding 助力扩展现实（XR）自动化测试","a":"In recent years, Extended Reality (XR) has emerged as a transformative technology, offering users immersive and interactive experiences across diversified virtual or virtual-real environments. Users can interact with XR applications (apps) through interactable GUI elements (IGEs) on the stereoscopic three-dimensional (3D) graphical user interface (GUI). IGE constitutes the fundamental element of XR GUI, embodying rich semantic information. The accurate recognition and precise understanding of these IGEs is instrumental, serving as the foundation of GUI grounding, which can facilitates downstream tasks, including automated XR testing. A straightforward XR test generator can interact randomly within the app’s 3D environment, making it trapped in uninteractable space and resulting in an ineffective and inefficient testing process. In contrast, a more intelligent test generator, informed by the accurate locations and semantics of IGEs, can make wiser decisions on interaction targets and orders, forming test sequences that cover more functionalities faster. The most recent IGE detection approaches in SE are designed for 2D mobile apps and typically train a supervised object detection model based on a large-scale manually-labeled GUI dataset, usually with a pre-defined set of clickable GUI element categories like buttons and spinners. Such approaches can hardly be applied to IGE detection in XR apps, due to a multitude of challenges including complexities posed by open-vocabulary and heterogeneous IGE categories, intricacies of context-sensitive interactability, and the necessities of precise spatial perception and visual-semantic alignment for accurate IGE detection results. Thus, it is necessary to embark on the IGE research tailored to XR apps. In this paper, we propose the first zero-shot cOntext-sensitive inteRactable GUI ElemeNT detection framework for Extended Reality apps, named Orienter. By imitating human behaviors, Orienter observes and understands the semantic contexts of XR app scenes first, before performing the detection. The detection process is iterated within a feedback-directed validation and reflection loop. Specifically, Orienter contains three components, including (1) Semantic context comprehension for capturing the apps’ GUI context, (2) Reflection-directed IGE candidate detection for identifying and localizing valid GUI elements based on multi-perspective description guided IGE detection, as well as feedback-directed reflection, and (3) Context-sensitive interactability classification which integrates semantic contexts for interactability prediction. To evaluate our approach and facilitate follow-up research, we spend more than three months constructing the first benchmark dataset which contains 1,552 images from 100 industrial-setting apps on Steam, with 4,470 interactable annotations across 766 semantics categories. Extensive experiments on the dataset demonstrate that Orienter is more effective than the state-of-the-art GUI element detection approaches (i.e., GPT-4o, OmniParser, YOLO v8, CenterNet2, Faster R-CNN, UIED, etc. ), surpassing their F1 Score by up to 3.7× and 121.4× (1.4× and 46.2× on average) in distinguishing the interactibility and semantics of the IGEs, respectively. Orienter is beneficial for boosting the performance of automatic testing by isolating the interactable action space from the whole space, regardless of the testing strategies employed. Experiments demonstrate that Orienter-guided testing covers 103.1% more IGEs with 125.7% more effective interactions than testing without action space isolation.","az":"近年来，扩展现实（XR）已成为一项变革性技术，在多样的虚拟或虚实融合环境中为用户提供沉浸式、交互式体验。用户通过立体三维（3D）图形用户界面（GUI）上的可交互 GUI 元素（IGE）与 XR 应用交互。IGE 构成了 XR GUI 的基本元素，蕴含丰富的语义信息。对这些 IGE 的准确识别与精确理解至关重要，是 GUI grounding 的基础，可以支撑包括自动化 XR 测试在内的下游任务。一个朴素的 XR 测试生成器会在应用的 3D 环境中随机交互，从而被困在不可交互的空间中，导致测试过程低效无果。相反，一个更智能的测试生成器，若掌握 IGE 的精确位置与语义，就能在交互目标与顺序上做出更明智的决策，形成更快覆盖更多功能的测试序列。SE 领域中最新的 IGE 检测方法是为 2D 移动应用设计的，通常基于大规模人工标注的 GUI 数据集训练有监督目标检测模型，且往往带有预定义的可点击 GUI 元素类别集合（如按钮和下拉框）。由于诸多挑战——包括开放词表与异构 IGE 类别带来的复杂性、上下文敏感的可交互性的微妙之处，以及精确 IGE 检测所必需的精准空间感知与视觉—语义对齐——此类方法难以应用于 XR 应用中的 IGE 检测。因此，有必要开展面向 XR 应用的 IGE 研究。本文提出首个面向扩展现实应用的零样本上下文敏感可交互 GUI 元素检测框架，名为 Orienter。通过模仿人类行为，Orienter 先观察并理解 XR 应用场景的语义上下文，然后再执行检测。检测过程在反馈导向的验证与反思循环中迭代。具体而言，Orienter 包含三个组件：(1) 语义上下文理解，用于捕获应用的 GUI 上下文；(2) 反思导向的 IGE 候选检测，基于多视角描述引导的 IGE 检测以及反馈导向的反思来识别并定位有效的 GUI 元素；(3) 上下文敏感的可交互性分类，融合语义上下文进行可交互性预测。为评估我们的方法并便利后续研究，我们花费三个多月构建了首个基准数据集，包含来自 Steam 上 100 个工业级应用的 1,552 张图像，涵盖 766 个语义类别的 4,470 条可交互标注。在该数据集上的大量实验表明，Orienter 比最先进的 GUI 元素检测方法（即 GPT-4o、OmniParser、YOLO v8、CenterNet2、Faster R-CNN、UIED 等）更有效，在区分 IGE 的可交互性与语义上分别以最高 3.7 倍和 121.4 倍（平均 1.4 倍和 46.2 倍）超越它们的 F1 分数。无论采用何种测试策略，Orienter 都有助于通过将可交互动作空间从整体空间中分离出来来提升自动化测试性能。实验表明，Orienter 引导的测试相比没有动作空间隔离的测试多覆盖 103.1% 的 IGE，并多出 125.7% 的有效交互。","tl":"零样本上下文敏感地检出 XR 可交互元素以隔离动作空间。","au":["Shuqing Li","Binchang Li","Yepang Liu","Cuiyun Gao","Jianping Zhang","Shing-Chi Cheung","Michael Lyu"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["multimodal","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["XR testing","interactable GUI element detection","GUI grounding","zero-shot","action space isolation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/61/x"},{"id":"p00870","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"QuanForge: A Mutation Testing Framework for Quantum Neural Networks","tz":"QuanForge：面向量子神经网络的变异测试框架","a":"With the growing synergy between deep learning and quantum computing, Quantum Neural Networks (QNNs) have emerged as a promising paradigm by leveraging quantum parallelism and entanglement. However, testing QNNs remains underexplored due to their complex quantum dynamics and limited interpretability. Developing a mutation testing technique for QNNs further requires addressing stochastic factors, including the inherent randomness of mutation operators and quantum measurements. To tackle these challenges, we propose QuanForge, a mutation testing framework specifically designed for QNNs. We first introduce statistical mutation killing to provide a more reliable criterion. QuanForge incorporates nine post-training mutation operators at both gate and parameter levels, capable of simulating various potential errors in quantum circuits. Finally, a mutation generation algorithm is formalized, which systematically produces effective mutants, thereby enabling a robust and reliable mutation analysis. Through extensive experiments on benchmark datasets and QNN architectures, we show that QuanForge can effectively identify weak test suites and localize vulnerable circuit regions. We also analyze the generation capability of different operators, providing guidance for future mutant design and structural assessment of QNNs.","az":"随着深度学习与量子计算的协同不断加深，量子神经网络（QNN）通过利用量子并行性与纠缠，已成为一种有前景的范式。然而，由于其复杂的量子动力学和有限的可解释性，QNN 的测试仍未被充分探索。为 QNN 开发变异测试技术还需处理随机性因素，包括变异算子固有的随机性和量子测量的随机性。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 QuanForge，一个专为 QNN 设计的变异测试框架。我们首先引入统计式变异体杀死判定，以提供更可靠的准则。QuanForge 纳入了门级与参数级共九种训练后变异算子，能够模拟量子电路中各种潜在错误。最后，我们形式化了一种变异体生成算法，系统地产生有效变异体，从而实现稳健可靠的变异分析。通过在基准数据集与 QNN 架构上的大量实验，我们表明 QuanForge 能有效识别薄弱的测试套件并定位脆弱的电路区域。我们还分析了不同算子的生成能力，为未来的变异体设计与 QNN 结构评估提供指导。","tl":"用统计式杀死判定与九种量子变异算子做 QNN 变异测试。","au":["Minqi Shao","Shangzhou Xia","Jianjun Zhao"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["quantum neural networks","mutation testing","statistical mutation killing","quantum circuits","test suite adequacy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/62/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.20706"},{"id":"p00871","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ReFLAIR: Detecting Responsive Layout Reflow Issues using Multimodal Generative AI","tz":"ReFLAIR：利用多模态生成式 AI 检测响应式布局的 Reflow 问题","a":"With over 60 percent of global Internet traffic originating from mobile devices, Responsive Web Design (RWD) has become essential for ensuring seamless user experiences across diverse screen sizes and resolutions. The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines require that both information and functionality remain accessible when reflow occurs. However, existing checkers or research tools have limitations: they either employ static analysis that fails to capture how content is actually displayed to users or focus on only one accessibility aspect, such as keyboard operation. Consequently, no prior study has comprehensively addressed both information and functionality loss during reflow for Graphical User Interfaces (GUIs). This paper introduces ReFLAIR (Reflow Fault Localization using AI-based Responsive analysis), a multimodal generative AI–driven approach for dynamically detecting reflow issues that cause loss of information or functionality in the GUI. ReFLAIR systematically extracts informative and actionable widgets, compares their presence and behavior across original and reflowed layouts, and employs both scrolling and large language model–guided expansion to uncover hidden interface widgets. We evaluate ReFLAIR on a dataset of 24 diverse webpages drawn from popular sites, prior benchmarks, and newly released websites. Results show that ReFLAIR outperforms five state-of-the-art techniques, improving precision by 20.91% and recall by 55.38%, while maintaining reasonable computational and runtime cost. An ablation study confirms that dynamic exploration (i.e., scrolling and expansion) is essential for high accuracy. In summary, our approach contributes to accessibility testing by providing an effective, scalable, and cost-efficient solution for identifying reflow issues in RWD.","az":"全球超过 60% 的互联网流量来自移动设备，响应式网页设计（RWD）已成为在不同屏幕尺寸与分辨率下确保无缝用户体验的关键。Web 内容无障碍指南要求在发生 reflow（重排）时信息与功能都必须保持可访问。然而，现有的检查器或研究工具存在局限：它们要么采用无法捕捉内容实际呈现给用户的静态分析，要么只关注单一无障碍方面，例如键盘操作。因此，此前没有研究全面处理图形用户界面（GUI）在 reflow 期间的信息与功能丢失问题。本文介绍 ReFLAIR（Reflow Fault Localization using AI-based Responsive analysis），一种多模态生成式 AI 驱动的方法，用于动态检测导致 GUI 中信息或功能丢失的 reflow 问题。ReFLAIR 系统性地抽取信息性与可操作性控件，比较它们在原始布局与 reflow 后布局中的存在与行为，并结合滚动与大语言模型引导的展开来发掘隐藏的界面控件。我们在包含 24 个来自热门站点、既有基准和新发布网站的多样网页数据集上评估 ReFLAIR。结果表明 ReFLAIR 优于五种最先进技术，精确率提升 20.91%，召回率提升 55.38%，同时保持合理的计算与运行时开销。消融实验证实，动态探索（即滚动与展开）对高准确率至关重要。总之，我们的方法通过为识别 RWD 中的 reflow 问题提供有效、可扩展且经济的方案，为无障碍测试作出了贡献。","tl":"多模态动态探索检测重排后信息与功能丢失的无障碍缺陷。","au":["Yirui He","Ziyao He","Syed Fatiul Huq","Sam Malek"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["accessibility-inclusion","multimodal","llm-based"],"kw":["responsive web design","reflow accessibility","WCAG","multimodal LLM","GUI widget analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/63/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808136"},{"id":"p00872","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TORAI: Multi-Source Root Cause Analysis for Blind Spots in the Microservice Service Call Graph","tz":"TORAI：面向微服务调用图盲点的多源根因分析","a":"Typical multi-source root cause analysis (RCA) methods for microservice systems assume all services have traces to construct a service call graph. However, this assumption is not practical as microservice systems evolve rapidly and may contain blackbox services without traces, such as compiled software or unsupported services. We refer to these services as blind spots. In the presence of blind spots, the performance of existing multi-source RCA methods may be affected, as they only diagnose visible services on the call graph. To overcome this limitation, we propose TORAI, a novel unsupervised approach that effectively pinpoints fine-grained root causes without relying on the service call graph. Instead, TORAI first measures anomaly severity using available multi-source telemetry data. It then performs clustering to group services based on their severity symptoms and conducts causal analysis to rank services within each severity cluster. Finally, TORAI aggregates the cluster rankings and uses hypothesis testing to identify fine-grained root causes. TORAI provides an unsupervised approach that leverages available multi-source telemetry data for RCA without requiring a constructed service call graph or further intrusive actions, thus addressing the limitations of existing methods. Our experiments on three benchmark systems demonstrate that TORAI outperforms state-of-the-art baselines remarkably in the presence of blind spots. Performance on real-world failures further shows that TORAI can accurately pinpoint the root causes in top-3 recommendations.","az":"典型的微服务系统多源根因分析（RCA）方法假设所有服务都有调用链（trace）可用于构建服务调用图。然而，这一假设并不现实，因为微服务系统演化迅速，可能包含没有调用链的黑盒服务，例如已编译的软件或不受支持的服务。我们把这些服务称为“盲点”。在存在盲点的情况下，现有多源 RCA 方法的性能可能受到影响，因为它们只诊断调用图上可见的服务。为克服这一局限，我们提出 TORAI，一种新颖的无监督方法，无需依赖服务调用图即可有效定位细粒度根因。TORAI 首先利用可获得的多源遥测数据度量异常严重程度；随后进行聚类，按严重程度症状对服务分组，并在每个严重程度簇内进行因果分析以对服务排序；最后，TORAI 汇总各簇排序，并使用假设检验识别细粒度根因。TORAI 提供了一种无监督方法，利用可获得的多源遥测数据进行 RCA，无需构建服务调用图，也无需进一步的侵入式操作，从而解决了现有方法的局限。我们在三个基准系统上的实验表明，在存在盲点的情况下，TORAI 显著优于最先进的基线。在真实故障上的表现进一步说明，TORAI 能够在前三条推荐中准确定位根因。","tl":"不依赖调用图，靠异常严重度聚类加因果排序定位根因。","au":["Luan Pham","Huong Ha","Xiuzhen Zhang","Hongyu Zhang"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["root cause analysis","microservices","blind spots","multi-source telemetry","unsupervised causal ranking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/64/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.13522"},{"id":"p00873","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"One Size Does Not Fit All: Revisiting Code Context Engineering for Repository-Level Code Generation","tz":"一种方案并不适用于所有场景：重新审视仓库级代码生成的代码上下文工程","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in code generation at the function or file level. However, they achieve limited performance on repository-level code generation due to the complicated repository context where a substantial amount of files and functions exist. To address this challenge, code context engineering methods are proposed to accurately extract the relevant code context required by repository-level code generation. These methods belong to three dominant paradigms: 1) Similarity-based In-Context Learning (ICL), which retrieves similar code examples in the repository as demonstrations; 2) Static Analysis, which captures relevant code context based on structural dependencies in the repository; and 3) Navigation-based Paradigms, which invokes LLMs to dynamically explore repositories for context identification. Despite the prevalence of code context engineering approaches, their individual contributions are often coupled within complex agents in repository-level code generation, making it difficult to isolate and evaluate the effectiveness of three paradigms. This paper presents the first large-scale and systematic empirical study that compares three code context engineering paradigms independently. We evaluate seven representative code context engineering methods based on the three paradigms, with eight popular LLMs on repository-level code generation. We also propose a new metric named Dependency Collection Rate (DCR) and efficiency metrics to enable the direct comparison of code context engineering methods, rather than observing their impacts only on the final code generation performance. Our findings reveal fundamental trade-offs: static analysis provides the most reliable effectiveness-efficiency trade-off, while navigation-based approaches with powerful models achieve the highest performance ceiling but require powerful models and incur 10-20× higher computational costs. Based on these findings, we provide actionable implications for AI coding researchers and software developers to guide the design and deployment of context-aware coding tools.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在函数级或文件级代码生成中展现出卓越能力。然而，由于仓库上下文复杂、存在大量文件与函数，它们在仓库级代码生成上的表现有限。为应对这一挑战，研究者提出了代码上下文工程方法，以准确抽取仓库级代码生成所需的相关代码上下文。这些方法归属三种主流范式：1) 基于相似度的上下文学习（ICL），在仓库中检索相似代码示例作为示范；2) 静态分析，基于仓库中的结构依赖捕获相关代码上下文；3) 基于导航的范式，调用 LLM 动态探索仓库以识别上下文。尽管代码上下文工程方法已很普遍，但它们各自的贡献往往被耦合在仓库级代码生成的复杂智能体之中，使人难以隔离并评估三种范式的有效性。本文提出首个大规模、系统的实证研究，独立比较三种代码上下文工程范式。我们在仓库级代码生成上，用八个流行 LLM 评估了基于三种范式的七种代表性代码上下文工程方法。我们还提出了一个名为依赖收集率（DCR）的新指标以及效率指标，以支持对代码上下文工程方法的直接比较，而不仅仅是观察它们对最终代码生成性能的影响。我们的发现揭示了根本性的权衡：静态分析提供了最可靠的效果—效率折中，而基于导航的方法在使用强大模型时能达到最高的性能上限，但需要强模型并带来 10-20 倍更高的计算成本。基于这些发现，我们为 AI 编程研究者与软件开发者提供了可操作的启示，以指导上下文感知编程工具的设计与部署。","tl":"首次解耦比较三类上下文工程范式并提出依赖收集率指标。","au":["Yichen LI","Qiye Lin","Yun Peng","Zhihan Jiang","Jinyang Liu","Chaozheng Wang","Yintong Huo","Cuiyun Gao"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["code context engineering","repository-level code generation","static analysis context","dependency collection rate","empirical comparison"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/65/x"},{"id":"p00874","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Hallucinations in LLM-based Code Summarization: Unveiling, Detection, and Mitigation","tz":"基于 LLM 的代码摘要中的幻觉：揭示、检测与缓解","a":"Code summarization plays a vital role in program comprehension and software maintenance by generating natural language descriptions to summarize the semantics of code. While Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown remarkable performance in this area, recent empirical studies reveal a critical limitation: LLMs are prone to hallucinations, producing summaries that are factually inaccurate or unfaithful to the source code, potentially misleading developers. In this paper, we propose to unveil, detect, and mitigate hallucinations in LLM-based code summarization. First, we construct Hallu-Eval, a novel dataset for unveiling hallucination phenomena and rigorously evaluating the effectiveness of hallucination detection and mitigation in LLM-based code summarization. It comprises both original code snippets to capture naturally occurring hallucinations and their semantically perturbed counterparts, which are designed to systematically induce challenging logical hallucinations, all complemented with manual hallucination annotations. Next, we propose Hallu-Det, a synergistic approach that combines direct entity-level detection to identify explicit hallucinations with a synonymous mutation-based refinement to reliably confirm or refute more ambiguous cases. Finally, we introduce Hallu-Shield, an inference-time mitigation approach that leverages an external value model to guide LLMs toward producing more faithful summaries—without costly retraining of the LLM itself. Extensive experiments show that Hallu-Eval effectively triggers hallucinations, increasing the hallucination rate of models such as Qwen2.5-Coder-7B from 17% to 97% on perturbed code. Our detection approach, Hallu-Det, achieves the best performance among baselines, reaching an F1-score of 0.95 for summaries generated by Qwen2.5-Coder-7B. Moreover, our mitigation method, Hallu-Shield, reduces hallucination rates—for example, from 66% to 59%, a 10.6% relative reduction, on DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B—while simultaneously improving summary quality, achieving a 71.5% win rate in a side-by-side evaluation using an LLM as a judge.","az":"代码摘要通过生成自然语言描述来概括代码语义，在程序理解与软件维护中扮演着关键角色。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在该领域表现出色，近期的实证研究揭示了一个关键局限：LLM 容易产生幻觉，生成事实不准确或不忠实于源代码的摘要，可能误导开发者。本文提出对基于 LLM 的代码摘要中的幻觉进行揭示、检测与缓解。首先，我们构建了 Hallu-Eval，一个用于揭示幻觉现象并严格评估幻觉检测与缓解效果的新数据集。它既包含用于捕捉自然出现幻觉的原始代码片段，也包含语义扰动后的对应版本，用以系统性诱发具有挑战性的逻辑幻觉，并全部辅以人工幻觉标注。其次，我们提出 Hallu-Det，一种协同方法，将直接的实体级检测（用于识别显式幻觉）与基于同义变异的精化（用于可靠地确认或排除更模糊的情形）相结合。最后，我们引入 Hallu-Shield，一种推理期缓解方法，借助外部价值模型引导 LLM 生成更忠实的摘要——无需对 LLM 本身进行昂贵的重训练。大量实验表明，Hallu-Eval 能有效触发幻觉，在扰动代码上将 Qwen2.5-Coder-7B 等模型的幻觉率从 17% 提高到 97%。我们的检测方法 Hallu-Det 在各基线中表现最佳，对 Qwen2.5-Coder-7B 生成的摘要达到 0.95 的 F1 分数。此外，我们的缓解方法 Hallu-Shield 降低了幻觉率——例如在 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上从 66% 降至 59%，相对下降 10.6%——同时提升了摘要质量，在以 LLM 为评判者的并排评测中取得 71.5% 的胜率。","tl":"给代码摘要幻觉配齐诱发数据集、检测器与推理期缓解器。","au":["Guanghua Wan","Yuanning Feng","Yao Wan","Zhaoyang Chu","Zhangqian Bi","Junxiao Han","Zhou Zhao","Hongyu Zhang","Pingpeng Yuan","Xuanhua Shi","Hai Jin"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["code summarization","hallucination detection","semantic perturbation","value model guidance","LLM-as-a-judge"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/66/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808139"},{"id":"p00875","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CodeCureAgent: Automatic Classification and Repair of Static Analysis Warnings","tz":"CodeCureAgent：静态分析告警的自动分类与修复","a":"Static analysis tools are widely used to detect bugs, vulnerabilities, and code smells. Traditionally, developers must resolve these warnings manually by analyzing the warning, deciding whether to fix or suppress it, and validating the correctness of the code change. Because this process is tedious, developers sometimes ignore warnings, leading to an accumulation of warnings and a degradation of code quality. Prior work suggests techniques to automatically repair static analysis warnings, but these are limited to specific analysis rules, cannot perform multi-file edits, and rely on weak validation mechanisms. This paper presents CodeCureAgent, an approach that harnesses LLM-based agents to automatically analyze, classify, and repair static analysis warnings. Unlike previous work, our method does not follow a predetermined algorithm. Instead, we adopt an agentic framework that iteratively invokes tools to gather additional information from the codebase (e.g., via code search) and edit the codebase to resolve the warning. CodeCureAgent detects and suppresses false positives, while fixing true positives when identified. We equip CodeCureAgent with a three-step heuristic to approve patches: (1) build the project, (2) verify that the warning disappears without introducing new warnings, and (3) run the test suite. We evaluate CodeCureAgent on a dataset of 1,000 SonarQube warnings found in 106 Java projects and covering 291 distinct rules. Our approach produces plausible fixes for 96.8% of the warnings, outperforming state-of-the-art baseline approaches by 30.7% and 29.2% in plausible-fix rate, respectively. Manual inspection of 291 cases reveals a correct-fix rate of 86.3%, showing that CodeCureAgent can reliably repair static analysis warnings. The approach incurs LLM costs of about 2.9 cents (USD) and an end-to-end processing time of about four minutes per warning. We envision CodeCureAgent helping to clean existing codebases and being integrated into CI/CD pipelines to prevent the accumulation of static analysis warnings.","az":"静态分析工具被广泛用于检测缺陷、漏洞和代码坏味。传统上，开发者必须手工处理这些告警：分析告警、决定是修复还是抑制，并验证代码改动的正确性。由于这一过程繁琐，开发者有时会忽略告警，导致告警堆积和代码质量下降。已有工作提出了自动修复静态分析告警的技术，但它们局限于特定的分析规则，无法进行多文件编辑，并且依赖较弱的验证机制。本文提出 CodeCureAgent，一种利用基于 LLM 的智能体自动分析、分类并修复静态分析告警的方法。与以往工作不同，我们的方法不遵循预先设定的算法，而是采用智能体框架，迭代地调用工具从代码库中收集更多信息（例如通过代码搜索），并编辑代码库以消解告警。CodeCureAgent 会检测并抑制误报，同时在识别为真阳性时进行修复。我们为 CodeCureAgent 配备了三步启发式来批准补丁：(1) 构建项目，(2) 验证告警消失且未引入新告警，(3) 运行测试套件。我们在一个数据集上评估 CodeCureAgent，该数据集包含 106 个 Java 项目中的 1,000 个 SonarQube 告警，覆盖 291 条不同规则。我们的方法对 96.8% 的告警产生了貌似合理的修复，在合理修复率上分别比最先进的基线方法高出 30.7% 和 29.2%。对 291 个案例的人工检查显示正确修复率为 86.3%，说明 CodeCureAgent 能可靠地修复静态分析告警。该方法每条告警的 LLM 成本约为 2.9 美分，端到端处理时间约四分钟。我们设想 CodeCureAgent 可帮助清理现有代码库，并被集成到 CI/CD 流水线中，以防止静态分析告警的堆积。","tl":"智能体式分类并修复静态告警，含误报抑制与三重验证。","au":["Pascal Joos","Islem BOUZENIA","Michael Pradel"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static analysis warnings","LLM agent","warning repair","false positive suppression","SonarQube"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/67/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808140"},{"id":"p00876","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Speculate: Generating REST API Specifications Using LLMs","tz":"Speculate：使用 LLM 生成 REST API 规约","a":"REST APIs are widely used for accessing web services. To support their use and testing, developers often write API specifications in open formats like OpenAPI. However, writing these specifications manually is tedious and error-prone, leading to incomplete or outdated specifications that can hinder both API usage and automated testing. Existing tools attempt to generate API specifications from source code using static or dynamic analysis. Unfortunately, these tools are often tightly coupled to specific languages and frameworks, making them hard to generalize and extend. This paper presents Speculate, the first approach to combine lightweight static analysis with large language models(LLMs) to automatically generate REST API specifications from source code.By leveraging LLMs trained on diverse codebases, Speculate generalizes easily across languages and frameworks. We evaluate Speculate on 19 real-world web repositories spanning two programming languages and three REST frameworks. Our results show that Speculate outperforms existing tools on both precision and recall across all dimensions.","az":"REST API 被广泛用于访问 Web 服务。为支持其使用与测试，开发者通常会用 OpenAPI 等开放格式编写 API 规约。然而手工编写这些规约既繁琐又易出错，导致规约不完整或过时，从而同时阻碍 API 的使用和自动化测试。已有工具尝试用静态或动态分析从源码生成 API 规约。遗憾的是，这些工具往往与特定语言和框架紧密耦合，难以泛化和扩展。本文提出 Speculate，这是首个将轻量级静态分析与大语言模型（LLM）相结合、从源码自动生成 REST API 规约的方法。借助在多样化代码库上训练的 LLM，Speculate 能够轻松跨语言、跨框架泛化。我们在 19 个真实 Web 仓库上评估 Speculate，这些仓库涵盖两种编程语言和三种 REST 框架。结果表明，Speculate 在所有维度的精确率和召回率上都优于现有工具。","tl":"首次把轻量静态分析与 LLM 结合，跨语言框架自动产出 REST 规约。","au":["Krishanu Singh","Kushagra Karar","Abhilash Jindal","Guowei Yang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["REST API specification","OpenAPI","static analysis","LLM","specification generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/68/x"},{"id":"p00877","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Thought is All You Need: Smart Contract Vulnerability Detection with Thought-Augmented Large Language Model","tz":"思维即所需：基于思维增强大语言模型的智能合约漏洞检测","a":"Smart contracts are self-executing agreements with code-defined terms enabling trustless blockchain transactions. Their immutability and control over significant financial assets make them attractive attack targets, with vulnerabilities potentially causing catastrophic financial losses. Large Language Models (LLMs) have revolutionized numerous domains with remarkable capabilities in code understanding and problem-solving. Despite these advancements, recent research reveals that LLMs still face significant limitations in accurately detecting complex vulnerabilities in smart contracts. This disparity between the capabilities of LLMs and the stringent requirements of security analysis underscores the necessity for tailored methodologies to enhance LLM-based vulnerability detection strategies. In this paper, we propose Synapse, the first smart contract detection framework leveraging thought-augmented LLM and fine-grained analysis under focal context. Specifically, Synapse mimics security researchers’ vulnerability discovery workflow, including vulnerability pattern learning, concrete thought generation, reasoning, and verification. We employ an advanced buffer-of-thoughts (BoT) approach for LLMs to learn and apply vulnerability-specific reasoning to concrete contracts, improving detection accuracy. We also leverage specialized reasoning and code models to optimize different stages of the vulnerability detection process. To evaluate Synapse, we collected real-world on-chain contract incidents from security company alerts not covered by existing datasets. Synapse identified 117 previously undiscovered vulnerabilities in on-chain smart contracts, including one critical vulnerability that safeguarded assets totaling $30 million from potential losses.","az":"智能合约是以代码定义条款的自执行协议，支撑了无需信任的区块链交易。其不可变性以及对大量金融资产的控制使其成为极具吸引力的攻击目标，漏洞可能造成灾难性的经济损失。大语言模型（LLM）以出色的代码理解与问题求解能力变革了众多领域。尽管取得了这些进展，近期研究表明 LLM 在准确检测智能合约中的复杂漏洞方面仍存在显著局限。LLM 的能力与安全分析的严苛要求之间的落差，凸显了设计定制化方法以增强基于 LLM 的漏洞检测策略的必要性。本文提出 Synapse，这是首个利用思维增强 LLM 并在聚焦上下文下进行细粒度分析的智能合约检测框架。具体而言，Synapse 模拟安全研究者的漏洞发现工作流，包括漏洞模式学习、具体思维生成、推理与验证。我们采用先进的思维缓冲（buffer-of-thoughts, BoT）方法，让 LLM 学习并将漏洞专属的推理应用到具体合约上，从而提升检测准确率。我们还利用专门的推理模型与代码模型来优化漏洞检测流程的不同阶段。为评估 Synapse，我们收集了来自安全公司告警、且未被现有数据集覆盖的真实链上合约事件。Synapse 在链上智能合约中识别出 117 个此前未被发现的漏洞，其中包括一个关键漏洞，避免了总额达 3000 万美元资产的潜在损失。","tl":"用思维缓冲模拟安全专家流程，链上挖出 117 个新合约漏洞。","au":["Chaoyuan Peng","Muhui Jiang","Yajin Zhou","Lei Wu"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract","vulnerability detection","buffer-of-thoughts","LLM","on-chain incidents"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/69/x"},{"id":"p00878","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SWE Data Construction, Automatically!","tz":"SWE 数据构建，全自动化！","a":"Constructing large-scale datasets for the GitHub issue resolution task is crucial for both training and evaluating the software engineering capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs). However, the existing GitHub issue resolution data construction pipeline is challenging and labor-intensive. We identify three key limitations in existing pipelines: (1) test patches collected often omit binary file changes; (2) the manual construction of evaluation environments is labor-intensive; and (3) the fail2pass validation phase requires manual inspection of test logs and writing custom parsing code to extract test status from logs. In this paper, we propose SWE-Factory, a fully automated issue resolution data construction pipeline, to resolve these limitations. First, our pipeline automatically recovers missing binary test files and ensures the correctness of test patches. Second, we introduce SWE-Builder, a LLM-based multi-agent system that automates evaluation environment construction. Third, we introduce a standardized, exit-code-based log parsing method to automatically extract test status, enabling a fully automated fail2pass validation. Experiments on 671 real-world GitHub issues across four programming languages show that our method can effectively construct valid evaluation environments for GitHub issues at a reasonable cost. For example, with GPT-4.1 mini, our SWE-Builder constructs 337 valid task instances out of 671 issues, at $0.047 per instance. Our ablation study further shows the effectiveness of different components of SWE-Builder. We also demonstrate through manual inspection that our exit-code- based fail2pass validation method is highly accurate, achieving an F1 score of 0.99. Additionally, we conduct an exploratory experiment to investigate whether we can use SWE-Factory to enhance models’ software engineering ability. After training five models on 2,809 Python task instances collected by our method, all models show improved software engineering ability. For example, the resolve rate of a trained Qwen2.5-Coder-14B-Instruct on SWE-bench Verified increases from 5.8% to 21.0%. We hope our method can accelerate the construction of large-scale, high-quality GitHub issue resolution datasets for both training and evaluation.","az":"为 GitHub issue 求解任务构建大规模数据集，对训练和评估大语言模型（LLM）的软件工程能力都至关重要。然而，现有的 GitHub issue 求解数据构建流程既困难又费时费力。我们指出现有流程的三个关键局限：（1）收集到的测试补丁常常遗漏二进制文件的改动；（2）评测环境需要人工搭建，人力成本高；（3）fail2pass 验证阶段需要人工检查测试日志并编写定制解析代码以提取测试状态。本文提出 SWE-Factory，一个全自动的 issue 求解数据构建流程来解决这些局限。首先，我们的流程会自动恢复缺失的二进制测试文件，并确保测试补丁的正确性。其次，我们提出 SWE-Builder，一个基于 LLM 的多智能体系统，用于自动化构建评测环境。第三，我们引入一种标准化的、基于退出码的日志解析方法来自动提取测试状态，从而实现完全自动的 fail2pass 验证。在涵盖四种编程语言的 671 个真实 GitHub issue 上的实验表明，我们的方法能以合理成本有效构建有效的评测环境。例如，使用 GPT-4.1 mini 时，SWE-Builder 从 671 个 issue 中构建出 337 个有效任务实例，每个实例成本为 0.047 美元。消融实验进一步验证了 SWE-Builder 各组件的有效性。我们还通过人工检查表明，基于退出码的 fail2pass 验证方法准确率很高，F1 分数达到 0.99。此外，我们进行了一项探索性实验，考察能否用 SWE-Factory 提升模型的软件工程能力。在我们方法收集的 2809 个 Python 任务实例上训练五个模型后，所有模型的软件工程能力都有提升。例如，训练后的 Qwen2.5-Coder-14B-Instruct 在 SWE-bench Verified 上的解决率从 5.8% 提升到 21.0%。我们希望该方法能加速大规模高质量 GitHub issue 求解数据集的构建，服务于训练与评测。","tl":"全自动流水线批量造 issue 求解任务，环境搭建与 fail2pass 全免人工。","au":["Lianghong Guo","Yanlin Wang","Caihua Li","Wei Tao","Pengyu Yang","Jiachi Chen","Haoyu Song","Duyu Tang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["issue resolution dataset","SWE-bench","multi-agent environment construction","fail2pass validation","data pipeline"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/70/x"},{"id":"p00879","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AdaDec: A Uncertainty-Guided Lookahead Decoding Framework for LLM-based Code Generation","tz":"AdaDec：面向 LLM 代码生成的不确定性引导前瞻解码框架","a":"Code generation with large language models (LLMs) is highly sensitive to token selection during decoding, particularly at uncertain decision points that influence program logic. While standard strategies such as greedy decoding treat all tokens uniformly, they overlook code-specific uncertainty patterns, leading to suboptimal performance. This paper presents an empirical study revealing that many generation errors stem from token ranking mistakes at high-uncertainty steps, where the correct token is present but not top-ranked. Motivated by these findings, we propose AdaDec, a lookahead-based uncertainty-guided adaptive decoding framework that integrates a token-level pause-then-rerank mechanism driven by token uncertainty. AdaDec learns model-specific uncertainty thresholds and applies a lookahead-based reranking strategy when uncertainty is high. Experiments on HumanEval+, MBPP+, and DevEval benchmarks show that AdaDec improves Pass@1 accuracy by up to 20.9% in absolute terms over greedy decoding, and consistently outperforms state-of-the-art adaptive decoding methods such as AdapT, while reducing computational cost and latency through efficient, selective pausing. Our results highlight the promise of uncertainty-aware adaptive decoding for improving both the reliability and efficiency of LLM-based code generation.","az":"使用大语言模型（LLM）进行代码生成对解码过程中的 token 选择高度敏感，尤其是在影响程序逻辑的高不确定性决策点上。诸如贪心解码这样的标准策略对所有 token 一视同仁，忽视了代码特有的不确定性模式，导致性能欠佳。本文给出一项实证研究，揭示许多生成错误源于高不确定性步骤上的 token 排序失误——正确的 token 其实存在，只是没有排在首位。受这些发现启发，我们提出 AdaDec，一个基于前瞻的、由不确定性引导的自适应解码框架，它整合了由 token 不确定性驱动的 token 级“暂停—再排序”（pause-then-rerank）机制。AdaDec 会学习模型特定的不确定性阈值，并在不确定性较高时应用基于前瞻的重排序策略。在 HumanEval+、MBPP+ 与 DevEval 基准上的实验表明，AdaDec 相比贪心解码将 Pass@1 准确率绝对提升最多达 20.9%，并持续优于 AdapT 等最先进的自适应解码方法，同时通过高效的选择性暂停降低了计算开销与延迟。我们的结果凸显了不确定性感知的自适应解码在提升 LLM 代码生成可靠性与效率方面的潜力。","tl":"只在高不确定性 token 处暂停并前瞻重排，Pass@1 最高提 20.9%。","au":["He Kaifeng","Mingwei Liu","Chong Wang","Zike Li","Yanlin Wang","Xin Peng","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["adaptive decoding","token uncertainty","lookahead reranking","code generation","Pass@1"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/71/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.08980"},{"id":"p00880","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CertiCoder: Towards MISRA-Compliant C Code Generation with LLMs","tz":"CertiCoder：迈向用 LLM 生成符合 MISRA 规范的 C 代码","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly applied to code generation in IDEs, CI pipelines, and automated workflows. Existing evaluations, however, have largely focused on functionality, with comparatively limited attention to compliance with established safety standards. This gap is particularly critical for C, where programmes may compile and pass unit tests yet still violate MISRA C:2012, a widely adopted guideline in safety-critical domains. We present CertiCoder, a post-training framework with rule-aware optimization that transforms tool-verified outcomes into per-rule contrasts and trains models through three stages: rule tuning, cold-start supervised fine-tuning, and rule-aware preference optimization. This design helps models not only distinguish compliant from violating outputs but also associate violations with specific rules. To support reproducible assessment, we construct a Codeforces-derived C benchmark with frozen splits, multi-level decontamination, and metrics that jointly measure MISRA compliance (S_{1}), functional correctness (F_{1}), and their conjunction (J_{1}). On Qwen2.5-Coder backbones (3B–14B), CertiCoder substantially improves compliance from near-zero to measurable J_{1} levels and generally preserves functional correctness, outperforming non–rule-aware baselines such as SFT and SafeCoder. To our knowledge, this makes CertiCoder among the first post-training frameworks to explicitly optimize both compliance and correctness, offering a practical step toward more auditable and extensible use of LLMs in safety-critical software systems.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）正越来越多地应用于 IDE、CI 流水线和自动化工作流中的代码生成。然而，现有评估大多聚焦于功能性，对既定安全标准的合规性关注相对有限。这一空白对 C 语言尤为关键：程序可能既能编译又能通过单元测试，却仍然违反 MISRA C:2012——安全关键领域广泛采用的一套准则。我们提出 CertiCoder，一个带有“规则感知优化”的后训练框架，它将工具验证得到的结果转化为逐规则的对比，并通过三个阶段训练模型：规则调优、冷启动监督微调、以及规则感知的偏好优化。这一设计不仅帮助模型区分合规输出与违规输出，还能把违规与具体规则关联起来。为支持可复现的评估，我们构建了一个源自 Codeforces 的 C 语言基准，具有冻结划分、多层次去污染，以及联合度量 MISRA 合规性（S₁）、功能正确性（F₁）及二者合取（J₁）的指标。在 Qwen2.5-Coder 系列骨干模型（3B–14B）上，CertiCoder 将合规性从接近零提升到可度量的 J₁ 水平，并总体上保持了功能正确性，优于 SFT 和 SafeCoder 等非规则感知的基线方法。据我们所知，这使 CertiCoder 成为最早显式同时优化合规性与正确性的后训练框架之一，为在安全关键软件系统中更可审计、可扩展地使用 LLM 迈出了务实的一步。","tl":"规则感知后训练把 MISRA 合规率从近乎为零拉到可度量水平。","au":["Min Gou","Zhiyu Yao","Hualong Ma","Ende Zhang","Jian Zhou","Fei He"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["MISRA C compliance","post-training","preference optimization","safety-critical code","benchmark"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/72/x"},{"id":"p00881","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Recommending Usability Improvements with Multimodal Large Language Models","tz":"用多模态大语言模型推荐可用性改进","a":"Usability describes quality attributes of application user interfaces that determine how effectively users can interact with them. Traditional usability evaluation methods require considerable expertise and resources, which can be challenging, especially for small teams and organizations. Automating usability evaluation could make it more accessible and help to improve the user experience. The recent emergence of powerful multimodal large language models (MLLMs) has opened new opportunities for automating usability evaluation and recommendation of improvements. These models can process visual inputs such as images and videos alongside textual context, which enables the identification of usability issues and the generation of actionable suggestions to resolve these issues. In this paper, we present a novel automated approach that uses limited application context and screen recordings of user interactions as input to an MLLM. The model automatically identifies and describes usability issues based on Nielsen’s usability heuristics, and provides corresponding explanations and improvement recommendations. To reduce the developer effort of manual prioritization, the recommendations are ranked by severity. The quality and practical usefulness of the generated recommendations were evaluated based on a user study that involved software engineers as participants. The evaluation focused on the highest-ranked suggestions provided by the model. The results demonstrate the potential of our approach to provide low-effort usability improvement recommendations. This makes it a promising complement to traditional evaluation methods, especially in settings with limited access to usability experts. In this sense, the approach serves as a basis for future integration into development tools to enable automated usability evaluation within software engineering workflows.","az":"可用性刻画了应用用户界面的质量属性，决定了用户与之交互的有效程度。传统的可用性评估方法需要大量专业知识和资源，这对小团队和小型机构而言尤其困难。将可用性评估自动化可以降低门槛，并有助于改善用户体验。近期强大的多模态大语言模型（MLLM）的出现，为自动化可用性评估和改进建议带来了新机会。这些模型能够在文本上下文之外处理图像和视频等视觉输入，从而能够识别可用性问题并生成可操作的改进建议。本文提出一种新颖的自动化方法，它以有限的应用上下文和用户交互的屏幕录像作为 MLLM 的输入。模型基于 Nielsen 的可用性启发式原则自动识别并描述可用性问题，并给出相应解释与改进建议。为减少开发者手工排序的工作量，这些建议会按严重程度排序。我们通过一项以软件工程师为被试的用户研究，评估了所生成建议的质量与实用价值，评估聚焦于模型给出的排名最高的建议。结果表明，我们的方法有潜力以很低的投入提供可用性改进建议，从而成为传统评估方法的有力补充，在难以接触可用性专家的场景中尤为有价值。在这个意义上，该方法为未来集成进开发工具、在软件工程流程中实现自动化可用性评估奠定了基础。","tl":"用屏幕录像喂 MLLM，按严重度排序输出可用性改进建议。","au":["Sebastian Lubos","Alexander Felfernig","Damian Garber","Viet-Man Le","Manuel Henrich"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","human-study"],"kw":["usability evaluation","multimodal LLM","screen recording","Nielsen heuristics","improvement recommendation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/73/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25420"},{"id":"p00882","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PuzzleMark: Implicit Jigsaw Learning for Robust Code Dataset Watermarking in Neural Code Completion Models","tz":"PuzzleMark：面向神经代码补全模型的隐式拼图式鲁棒代码数据集水印","a":"Constructing and curating high-quality code datasets requires significant resources, making them valuable intellectual property. Unfortunately, these datasets currently face severe risks of unauthorized use. Although digital watermarking offers a post hoc mechanism for copyright authentication, existing methods are predominantly based on the co-occurrence pattern, which is not robust and is susceptible to watermark detection and removal attacks. In this paper, we propose PuzzleMark, a robust watermarking method for code datasets. To reduce the risk of watermark exposure, PuzzleMark introduces a carrier selection strategy that leverages code complexity to evaluate the suitability of code snippets as watermark carriers, and selects those with high suitability for watermarking. To enhance the robustness of the watermark, PuzzleMark proposes a novel concatenation pattern to replace the traditional co-occurrence pattern, and implements two watermarking strategies through variable name concatenation. PuzzleMark adaptively embeds watermarks based on the inherent characteristics of the code, making it more stealthy while maintaining design simplicity. For watermark verification, PuzzleMark employs an independent-samples t-test to verify suspicious models under a black-box setting. Experimental results demonstrate that PuzzleMark achieves a 100% verification success rate and a 0% false positive rate, with negligible impact on model performance. Both our human study and our evaluation using four state-of-the-art watermark detection methods show that PuzzleMark exhibits strong imperceptibility, with an average suspicious rate 0.24 and an average recall 30.41%, respectively. Furthermore, the consistent retention of verifiability under two attack scenarios further corroborates the robustness of PuzzleMark. As a practical digital watermarking method, PuzzleMark provides strong protection for the intellectual property of code datasets and offers new insights for future research.","az":"构建和整理高质量代码数据集需要大量资源，使其成为宝贵的知识产权。不幸的是，这些数据集当前面临被未经授权使用的严重风险。尽管数字水印提供了一种事后的版权认证机制，现有方法大多基于共现模式，鲁棒性不足，容易被水印检测与移除攻击攻破。本文提出 PuzzleMark，一种面向代码数据集的鲁棒水印方法。为降低水印暴露的风险，PuzzleMark 引入一种载体选择策略，利用代码复杂度评估代码片段作为水印载体的适宜性，并选择适宜性高的片段加水印。为增强水印鲁棒性，PuzzleMark 提出一种新颖的拼接模式来替代传统的共现模式，并通过变量名拼接实现两种水印策略。PuzzleMark 依据代码固有特征自适应地嵌入水印，在保持设计简洁的同时更具隐蔽性。在水印验证方面，PuzzleMark 采用独立样本 t 检验，在黑盒设置下验证可疑模型。实验结果表明，PuzzleMark 取得了 100% 的验证成功率和 0% 的误报率，对模型性能的影响可以忽略。我们的人类研究以及使用四种最先进水印检测方法的评估均表明，PuzzleMark 具有很强的不可感知性，平均可疑率不超过 0.24，平均召回率不超过 30.41%。此外，在两种攻击场景下可验证性得以持续保持，进一步印证了 PuzzleMark 的鲁棒性。作为一种实用的数字水印方法，PuzzleMark 为代码数据集的知识产权提供了有力保护，并为未来研究提供了新的思路。","tl":"用变量名拼接模式替代共现水印，隐蔽且抗检测移除攻击。","au":["Haocheng Huang","Yuchen Chen","Weisong Sun","Peizhuo Lv","Yuan Xiao","Chunrong Fang","Yang Liu","Xiaofang Zhang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"privacy-memorization-watermarking-and-unlearning","tg":["security","llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["dataset watermarking","code completion model","intellectual property","black-box verification","robustness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/74/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.27677"},{"id":"p00883","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SmartIFSyn: Automated Information Flow Security Policy Synthesis for Smart Contracts","tz":"SmartIFSyn：面向智能合约的信息流安全策略自动合成","a":"Smart contracts have achieved significant success, however, their security remains a long-standing challenge. The immutability and transparency of smart contracts require establishing a strong mechanism to prevent private leakage and trusted data tampering. Apart from traditional logic and code-level vulnerabilities arising from insufficient control over contract variables and function parameters, smart contracts may store private-dependent information in blockchain records, which is a critical type of vulnerability, but often overlooked in existing security analysis. In this paper, we present an automated approach for synthesizing security policies, named SmartIFSyn, to eliminate information flow vulnerabilities in smart contracts. We formalize the semantics of Solidity, the most widely used smart contract language, and analyze information flow security of Solidity smart contracts from two perspectives: local-variable security and global-interaction security. We present a type system to guide the elimination of local-variable vulnerabilities by inferring a policy and resort to constraint solving to synthesize a desired policy in case that the type system fails. The policy ensures both local-variable and global-interaction security while it is maximally aligned with user preference. Furthermore, the policy can be subsequently converted into enforceable specifications. We implement our approach in a tool and evaluate it on 17,160 real-world Ethereum smart contracts. The experimental results demonstrate the efficacy of our approach, e.g., detected 243 vulnerabilities in 223 real-world Ethereum smart contracts.","az":"智能合约已取得显著成功，但其安全性仍是长期挑战。智能合约的不可变性与透明性要求建立强有力的机制来防止隐私泄露与可信数据被篡改。除了因对合约变量和函数参数控制不足而产生的传统逻辑与代码级漏洞外，智能合约还可能把依赖隐私的信息存入区块链记录，这是一类关键但常被现有安全分析忽视的漏洞。本文提出一种名为 SmartIFSyn 的自动化安全策略合成方法，以消除智能合约中的信息流漏洞。我们形式化了最广泛使用的智能合约语言 Solidity 的语义，并从两个视角分析 Solidity 智能合约的信息流安全：局部变量安全与全局交互安全。我们提出一个类型系统，通过推断策略来指导消除局部变量漏洞；当类型系统失败时，则借助约束求解来合成所需策略。该策略在最大程度契合用户偏好的同时，保证局部变量安全与全局交互安全。此外，该策略随后可转换为可强制执行的规约。我们在一个工具中实现了该方法，并在 17160 个真实以太坊智能合约上进行评估。实验结果证明了方法的有效性，例如在 223 个真实以太坊智能合约中检测出 243 个漏洞。","tl":"用类型系统加约束求解自动合成合约信息流安全策略。","au":["Yinghao Wu","Miaomiao Zhang","Fu Song","John Baugh"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["information flow security","policy synthesis","Solidity semantics","type system","constraint solving"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/75/x"},{"id":"p00884","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"StepFly: Agentic Troubleshooting Guide Automation for Incident Diagnosis","tz":"StepFly：面向事故诊断的智能体式排障指南自动化","a":"Effective incident management in large-scale IT systems relies on troubleshooting guides (TSGs), but their manual execution is slow and error-prone. While recent advances in LLMs offer promise for automating incident management tasks, existing LLM-based solutions lack specialized support for several key challenges, including managing TSG quality issues, interpreting complex control flow, handling data-intensive queries, and exploiting execution parallelism. We first conducted an empirical study on 92 real-world TSGs, and, guided by our findings, we present StepFly, a novel end-to-end agentic framework for troubleshooting guide automation. Our approach features a three-stage workflow: the first stage provides a comprehensive guide together with a tool, TSG Mentor, to assist SREs in improving TSG quality; the second stage performs offline preprocessing using LLMs to extract structured execution DAGs from unstructured TSGs and to create dedicated Query Preparation Plugins (QPPs); and the third stage executes online using a DAG-guided scheduler-executor framework with a memory system to guarantee correct workflow and support parallel execution of independent steps. Our empirical evaluation on a collection of real-world TSGs and incidents demonstrates that StepFly achieves a ∼94% success rate on GPT-4.1, outperforming baselines with less time and token consumption. Furthermore, it achieves a remarkable execution time reduction of 32.9% to 70.4% for parallelizable TSGs.","az":"大规模 IT 系统中有效的事故管理依赖排障指南（TSG），但其人工执行既缓慢又容易出错。尽管大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展为自动化事故管理任务带来了希望，现有基于 LLM 的方案在若干关键挑战上缺乏专门支持，包括管理 TSG 的质量问题、解释复杂控制流、处理数据密集型查询以及利用执行并行性。我们首先对 92 个真实 TSG 开展实证研究，并在研究发现的指导下提出 StepFly，一个面向排障指南自动化的端到端智能体框架。我们的方法包含三阶段工作流：第一阶段提供一份完整指南以及工具 TSG Mentor，帮助 SRE 改进 TSG 质量；第二阶段使用 LLM 进行离线预处理，从非结构化的 TSG 中抽取结构化的执行 DAG，并创建专用的查询准备插件（QPP）；第三阶段在线执行，采用 DAG 引导的调度器—执行器框架并配备记忆系统，以保证工作流正确性并支持独立步骤的并行执行。我们在一批真实 TSG 与事故上的实证评估表明，StepFly 在 GPT-4.1 上达到约 94% 的成功率，以更少的时间和 token 消耗超越基线方法。此外，对可并行的 TSG，它将执行时间降低了 32.9% 至 70.4%。","tl":"把非结构化排障指南抽成 DAG 后并行执行，成功率约 94%。","au":["Jiayi Mao","Liqun Li","Yanjie Gao","Zegang Peng","Shilin He","Chaoyun Zhang","Si Qin","Samia Khalid","Qingwei Lin","Saravan Rajmohan","Sitaram Lanka","Dongmei Zhang"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["agentic","llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["troubleshooting guide","incident diagnosis","agentic framework","execution DAG","parallel execution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/76/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.10074"},{"id":"p00885","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Protocol Reverse Engineering via Deep Transfer Learning","tz":"基于深度迁移学习的协议逆向工程","a":"Protocol reverse engineering infers the specification of proprietary or poorly documented protocols and serves as the foundation for security analysis such as fuzz testing. While many existing techniques achieve this by mining statistical features from network traces, they face increasing challenges due to incomplete field pattern information available in the traces. Although protocol development has accumulated rich prior knowledge about protocol design, this knowledge remains largely untapped in protocol reverse engineering. This paper introduces TransRE, a protocol reverse engineering tool that leverages prior syntax knowledge from standardized protocols through deep transfer learning to better understand proprietary protocols. TransRE first selects optimal source domains by analyzing inter-domain differences between the existing knowledge base and the target protocol. It then employs a neural network to extract representation features and applies domain adaptation techniques to optimize the syntax transfer model, enabling accurate inference of protocol formats. Our evaluation on 12 widely used protocols shows that TransRE identifies fields with a perfection score of 0.43, which is 1.48×-3.07× the performance achieved by five state-of-the-art methods. Furthermore, to demonstrate practical applicability, we enhanced an existing protocol fuzzer with TransRE for testing proprietary protocols in real-world network cameras and discovered four bugs.","az":"协议逆向工程用于推断私有或文档不全协议的规约，是模糊测试等安全分析的基础。尽管许多现有技术通过从网络流量中挖掘统计特征来实现这一目标，但由于流量中可获得的字段模式信息不完整，它们面临越来越大的挑战。虽然协议开发过程中积累了关于协议设计的丰富先验知识，这些知识在协议逆向工程中仍基本未被利用。本文提出 TransRE，一个协议逆向工程工具，它通过深度迁移学习利用来自标准化协议的先验语法知识，以更好地理解私有协议。TransRE 首先通过分析已有知识库与目标协议之间的域间差异来选择最优源域；随后使用神经网络提取表示特征，并应用域适应技术优化语法迁移模型，从而实现对协议格式的准确推断。我们在 12 个广泛使用的协议上的评估表明，TransRE 的字段识别完美度得分为 0.43，是五种最先进方法性能的 1.48×–3.07×。此外，为展示实际适用性，我们用 TransRE 增强了一个现有协议模糊测试工具，用于测试真实网络摄像头中的私有协议，并发现了四个缺陷。","tl":"把标准协议的语法先验迁移到私有协议，字段推断得分翻数倍。","au":["Yanyang Zhao","Zhengxiong Luo","Wenlong Zhang","Feifan Wu","Yuanliang Chen","Fuchen Ma","Qi Xu","Heyuan Shi","Yu Jiang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["protocol reverse engineering","transfer learning","domain adaptation","protocol format inference","protocol fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/77/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797124"},{"id":"p00886","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SWR-Bench: Assessing LLM Performance in Real-World Code Review Comment Generation","tz":"SWR-Bench：评估 LLM 在真实代码评审意见生成中的表现","a":"Automated Code Review (ACR) is crucial for software quality, yet existing benchmarks often fail to reflect real-world complexities, hindering the evaluation of modern Large Language Models (LLMs). Current benchmarks frequently focus on fine-grained code units, lack complete project context, and use inadequate evaluation metrics. To address these limitations, we introduce swrbench, a new benchmark comprising 1000 manually verified Pull Requests (PRs) from GitHub, offering PR-centric review with full project context. swrbench employs an objective LLM-based evaluation method that aligns strongly with human judgment (~90% agreement) by verifying if issues from a structured ground truth are covered in generated reviews. Our systematic evaluation of mainstream ACR tools and LLMs on swrbench reveals that current systems underperform, and ACR tools are more adept at detecting functional errors. Subsequently, we propose and validate a simple multi-review aggregation strategy that significantly boosts ACR performance, increasing F1 scores by up to 43.67%. Our contributions include the swrbench benchmark, its objective evaluation method, a comprehensive study of current ACR capabilities, and an effective enhancement approach, offering valuable insights for advancing ACR research.","az":"自动化代码评审（ACR）对软件质量至关重要，但现有基准往往无法反映真实世界的复杂性，妨碍了对现代大语言模型（LLM）的评估。当前基准常聚焦于细粒度代码单元、缺乏完整项目上下文，并使用不充分的评估指标。为解决这些局限，我们提出 swrbench，一个由来自 GitHub 的 1000 个人工校验 Pull Request（PR）组成的新基准，提供以 PR 为中心、具备完整项目上下文的评审场景。swrbench 采用一种客观的基于 LLM 的评估方法：通过核验结构化标准答案中的问题是否被生成的评审所覆盖，该方法与人类判断高度一致（约 90% 的一致率）。我们在 swrbench 上对主流 ACR 工具与 LLM 进行系统评估，结果显示当前系统表现欠佳，而 ACR 工具更擅长检测功能性错误。随后，我们提出并验证了一种简单的多评审聚合策略，它显著提升了 ACR 性能，使 F1 分数最高提升 43.67%。我们的贡献包括 swrbench 基准、其客观评估方法、对当前 ACR 能力的全面研究，以及一种有效的增强方法，为推进 ACR 研究提供了有价值的洞见。","tl":"以 PR 为单位、带完整项目上下文的评审基准，并给出聚合增强法。","au":["Zhengran Zeng","Ruikai Shi","Keke Han","Yixin Li","Kaicheng Sun","Yidong Wang","Zhuohao Yu","Rui Xie","Wei Ye","Shikun Zhang"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["automated code review","pull request benchmark","LLM evaluation","review comment generation","multi-review aggregation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/78/x"},{"id":"p00887","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding Binary Code Similarity for Real-World Vulnerability Detection: A Large-Scale Empirical Study","tz":"理解二进制代码相似性在真实漏洞检测中的作用：一项大规模实证研究","a":"Firmware lies at the heart of IoT devices. Its development depends heavily on third-party libraries (TPLs), which greatly accelerate the process but simultaneously introduce associated vulnerabilities. Binary Code Similarity Detection (BCSD) is an effective technique for identifying vulnerabilities in firmware by comparing pairs of code segments. However, existing studies either evaluate their performance only on small-scale datasets or lack diversity in terms of vulnerabilities, TPLs, and firmware. Consequently, a comprehensive understanding of BCSD for real-world vulnerability detection remains absent. To bridge this gap, we conduct a large-scale study of vulnerability detection across 60,000 firmware images from 200 vendors using BCSD. Rather than introducing a novel model, we examine the influence of four key factors—vulnerable function versions, vulnerability search space, function sizes, and compilation toolchains on BCSD performance. Our results reveal that these factors substantially affect performance, often by wide margins. To address this, we propose a build-aware query strategy that derives queries from representative real-world binaries, effectively closing the gap and raising the mean reciprocal rank (MRR) from 0.818 to 0.981. Furthermore, we demonstrate that a TPL-aware, two-stage search process significantly enhances accuracy, improving MRR by 18.5% by limiting the search space.","az":"固件是物联网设备的核心。其开发在很大程度上依赖第三方库（TPL），这虽极大加快了开发进程，但同时引入了相关漏洞。二进制代码相似性检测（BCSD）是通过比较代码片段对来识别固件漏洞的一种有效技术。然而，现有研究要么只在小规模数据集上评估性能，要么在漏洞、第三方库和固件的多样性上不足。因此，学界仍缺乏对 BCSD 用于真实漏洞检测的全面理解。为弥合这一空白，我们使用 BCSD 在来自 200 家厂商的 60000 个固件镜像上开展了大规模漏洞检测研究。我们并未提出新模型，而是考察四个关键因素——易受攻击函数的版本、漏洞搜索空间、函数规模以及编译工具链——对 BCSD 性能的影响。结果表明，这些因素会大幅影响性能，差距往往很大。为此，我们提出一种构建感知（build-aware）的查询策略，从有代表性的真实二进制中导出查询，有效弥合了差距，将平均倒数排名（MRR）从 0.818 提升到 0.981。此外，我们还证明一种感知第三方库的两阶段搜索流程能显著提升准确率，通过限制搜索空间使 MRR 提升 18.5%。","tl":"6 万固件实测揭示 BCSD 的四大影响因素，并给出构建感知查询策略。","au":["Jingdong Guo","Chaopeng Dong","Yimo Ren","Siyuan Li","Jie Liu","Hong Li","Hongsong Zhu"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","security","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["binary code similarity detection","firmware","third-party library","vulnerability search","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/79/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.28870"},{"id":"p00888","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GPU-Accelerated Flow-Sensitive Pointer Analysis for C/C++ Programs","tz":"面向 C/C++ 程序的 GPU 加速流敏感指针分析","a":"Flow-sensitive pointer analysis offers highly precise results that are essential for various security analyses, bug detection tools, and compiler optimizations. However, its high computational cost often leads to prohibitively long analysis times, especially for large, real-world programs. Despite decades of research, state-of-the-art algorithms still struggle to achieve acceptable performance at industrial scale, forcing developers to choose less precise alternatives. To overcome these limitations, we present GPA a GPU-accelerated flow-sensitive pointer analysis for C/C++ programs. To maximize hardware utilization, GPA dynamically balances computation by combining the massive parallelism of GPUs with a graph neural network that predicts per-variable workloads. Compared to state-of-the-art CPU-based analyses, GPA improves runtime performance by a factor of 1.3 to 14 on large programs (i.e., ≥275~KLOC) without sacrificing precision. However, on most small programs (i.e., <100~KLOC) and some medium ones (i.e., 100–275~KLOC), traditional algorithms run faster due to the overhead of memory management on GPUs that GPA incurs. By making the computation of highly precise pointer information more tractable, GPA enables running analyses and developer tools that were previously infeasible on large codebases.","az":"流敏感指针分析能给出高度精确的结果，对各类安全分析、缺陷检测工具和编译器优化都至关重要。然而，其高昂的计算开销常导致分析时间长得难以承受，对大型真实程序尤其如此。尽管经过数十年研究，最先进的算法在工业规模上仍难以达到可接受的性能，迫使开发者退而选择精度较低的替代方案。为克服这些限制，我们提出 GPA，一种面向 C/C++ 程序的 GPU 加速流敏感指针分析。为最大化硬件利用率，GPA 将 GPU 的大规模并行能力与一个预测每变量工作量的图神经网络结合，动态平衡计算负载。与最先进的基于 CPU 的分析相比，GPA 在大型程序（即 ≥275 KLOC）上将运行性能提升 1.3× 到 14×，且不牺牲精度。然而，在大多数小程序（<100 KLOC）和部分中等规模程序（100–275 KLOC）上，由于 GPA 带来的 GPU 内存管理开销，传统算法运行更快。通过让高精度指针信息的计算变得更可行，GPA 使此前在大型代码库上无法运行的分析与开发者工具成为可能。","tl":"GPU 并行加上 GNN 预测负载，大程序指针分析最高提速 14 倍。","au":["Jiaqi He","Karim Ali"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["flow-sensitive pointer analysis","GPU acceleration","graph neural network","workload balancing","C/C++"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/80/x"},{"id":"p00889","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Knowledge-Aware Test Reuse","tz":"自动化的知识感知测试复用","a":"The quality of foundational libraries is critical for the reliability of modern software ecosystems. However, developers often have insufficient time for testing due to various reasons. Recent studies show that 68% of deep learning libraries lack unit tests, and their absence negatively impacts libraries health. While automated test generation techniques have been proposed, they frequently produce invalid inputs or semantically inconsistent assertions due to missing domain knowledge. An alternative is cross-library test reuse, as many libraries in scientific computing and machine learning expose functionally similar APIs. Nevertheless, effective test reuse requires careful semantic alignment rather than naive “copy-and-paste”, as subtle API mismatches and incomplete domain knowledge often yield invalid tests. To address these challenges, we present KATRER, a knowledge-aware framework for automated test reuse. KATRER models each library as a heterogeneous graph that integrates semantic and structural information and introduces a Test Fingerprint representation for tests, which captures code, docstrings, usage examples, pre-/post-conditions, and invoked APIs. This enables accurate API alignment and prevents invalid calls. KATRER further employs a collaborative LLM pipeline that verifies semantic compatibility, performs stepwise API substitution, and validates test correctness. We evaluate KATRER among five libraries in two domains, generating 13,191 sub-tests from 1,484 source tests, with 7,257 retained after filtering. KATRER improves syntactic correctness and execution success by 17.46% compared to baselines, while uncovering 22 previously unknown defects in CuPy and cuML, 8 of which have already been fixed. These results demonstrate that knowledge-aware test reuse substantially reduces manual adaptation effort and enhances the robustness of widely used libraries.","az":"基础库的质量对现代软件生态的可靠性至关重要。然而由于各种原因，开发者常常没有足够时间进行测试。近期研究显示，68% 的深度学习库缺少单元测试，而这种缺失会对库的健康度产生负面影响。虽然已有自动化测试生成技术被提出，但它们常因缺乏领域知识而产生无效输入或语义不一致的断言。另一种思路是跨库测试复用，因为科学计算与机器学习领域的许多库暴露了功能相似的 API。然而，有效的测试复用需要谨慎的语义对齐，而非简单的“复制粘贴”，因为细微的 API 不匹配和不完整的领域知识常会产生无效测试。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 KATRER，一个知识感知的自动化测试复用框架。KATRER 将每个库建模为整合了语义与结构信息的异构图，并为测试引入“测试指纹”（Test Fingerprint）表示，用以刻画代码、docstring、使用示例、前置/后置条件以及被调用的 API。这使得 API 对齐更准确，并可避免无效调用。KATRER 还采用一条协作式 LLM 流水线，用于验证语义兼容性、逐步执行 API 替换并校验测试正确性。我们在两个领域的五个库上评估 KATRER，从 1484 个源测试生成了 13191 个子测试，过滤后保留 7257 个。与基线相比，KATRER 将语法正确性与执行成功率提升了 17.46%，并在 CuPy 和 cuML 中发现了 22 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 8 个已被修复。这些结果表明，知识感知的测试复用能大幅减少人工适配工作量，并提升广泛使用的库的健壮性。","tl":"用异构图与测试指纹做语义对齐，把已有测试跨库复用生成新测试。","au":["Ziyuan Zhang","Yi Gao","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Shanping Li"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test reuse","cross-library API alignment","heterogeneous graph","test fingerprint","unit test generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/81/x"},{"id":"p00890","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Evaluating Risk and Confidence in Performance Bounds of Configuration Sampling Strategies","tz":"评估配置采样策略性能界限的风险与置信度","a":"Modern software usually exposes a large number of configuration options to the user, which gives rise to enormous configuration spaces in practice. Appropriate choices for these options dramatically influence the performance of the software (throughput, memory consumption, execution time, etc.). However, due to the sheer size of the configuration space, systematically identifying the best or worst-performing configurations is computationally infeasible through exhaustive exploration. Instead, practitioners rely on budgeted sampling strategies, such as uniform random sampling or statistical recursive search, to explore the configuration space under fixed measurement budgets in an attempt to find the best or worst configuration. A fundamental limitation of existing sampling strategies is the lack of quantifiable guarantees that the selected configuration truly reflects best-case (or worst-case) performance. In this paper, we define the basic concepts of posterior risk and posterior confidence and present a probabilistic framework to evaluate how well sampling strategies identify the best- or worst-performing configuration of a software system. We evaluate our framework by comparing five representative sampling strategies on seven real-world configurable software systems. Using our framework, we find that statistical recursive search yields consistently tighter best-case guarantees—higher posterior confidence and lower posterior risk—than the alternatives at the same budget. Our results demonstrate the potential of our framework as a principled basis for reporting, comparing, and refining sampling strategies, and as a tool for practitioners to select strategies and budgets with quantified guarantees across systems and sample sizes. Extended ablations—including additional sampling strategies and per-system breakdowns—are available in the supplementary material.","az":"现代软件通常向用户暴露大量配置选项，在实践中形成了巨大的配置空间。这些选项的取值会极大影响软件性能（吞吐量、内存消耗、执行时间等）。然而，由于配置空间规模庞大，通过穷举探索来系统性识别性能最佳或最差的配置在计算上不可行。取而代之，从业者依赖有预算约束的采样策略，如均匀随机采样或统计递归搜索，在固定测量预算下探索配置空间，试图找到最佳或最差配置。现有采样策略的一个根本局限在于，缺乏可量化的保证来说明所选配置是否真正反映了最优（或最差）性能。本文定义了“后验风险”与“后验置信度”的基本概念，并给出一个概率框架来评估采样策略识别软件系统最佳或最差性能配置的效果。我们通过在七个真实可配置软件系统上比较五种代表性采样策略来评估该框架。借助该框架，我们发现在相同预算下，统计递归搜索能持续给出更紧的最优情形保证——更高的后验置信度与更低的后验风险。我们的结果表明，该框架可作为报告、比较和改进采样策略的原则性基础，并可作为从业者在不同系统与样本规模下以量化保证选择策略与预算的工具。包含更多采样策略与逐系统细分的扩展消融实验见补充材料。","tl":"提出后验风险与后验置信度，为配置采样结果给出可量化保证。","au":["Kallistos Weis","Martina Maggio","Norbert Siegmund","Sven Apel"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["configurable software","performance sampling","posterior risk","posterior confidence","measurement budget"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/82/x","pu":"https://www.se.cs.uni-saarland.de/publications/docs/WMS+26.pdf"},{"id":"p00891","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Can Old Tests do New Tricks for Resolving SWE Issues?","tz":"旧测试能为解决 SWE Issue 玩出新花样吗？","a":"Test suites in real-world projects are often large and achieve high code coverage, yet they remain insufficient for detecting all bugs. The abundance of unresolved issues in open-source project trackers highlights this gap. While regression tests are typically designed to ensure past functionality is preserved in the new version, they can also serve a complementary purpose: debugging the current version. Specifically, regression tests can (1) enhance the generation of reproduction tests for newly reported issues, and (2) validate that patches do not regress existing functionality. We present TestLoc, a fully automated technique that leverages issue tracker reports and strategically reuses regression tests for both bug reproduction and patch validation. A key contribution of TestLoc is its ability to automatically minimize the regression suite to a small, highly relevant subset of tests. Due to the predominance of LLM-based debugging techniques, this minimization is essential as large test suites exceed context limits, introduce noise, and inflate inference costs. TestLoc can be plugged into any agentic bug repair pipeline and orthogonally improve overall performance. As a proof of concept, we show that TestLoc leads to a $6.2%-9.0%$ relative increase in issue reproduction rate within the Otter framework and a $9.4%-12.9%$ relative increase in issue resolution rate within the Agentless framework on SWE-Bench Lite and SWE-Bench Verified benchmarks, capturing fixes that were correctly produced by agents but not submitted as final patches. Compared to the benefits, the cost overhead of using TestLoc is minimal, i.e., $0.02 and $0.05 per SWE-Bench instance, using GPT-4o and Claude-3.7-Sonnet models, respectively.","az":"真实项目中的测试套件往往规模庞大、代码覆盖率很高，却仍不足以检出所有缺陷。开源项目问题追踪系统中大量未解决的 issue 正说明了这一差距。回归测试通常用于确保新版本保留既有功能，但它们还能发挥互补作用：调试当前版本。具体而言，回归测试可以（1）增强为新上报 issue 生成复现测试的能力，（2）验证补丁不会破坏既有功能。我们提出 TestLoc，一种全自动技术，它利用问题追踪系统中的报告，并有策略地复用回归测试，同时服务于缺陷复现与补丁验证。TestLoc 的一项关键贡献在于能够自动将回归套件最小化为一个规模很小、高度相关的测试子集。鉴于基于 LLM 的调试技术占主导地位，这种最小化至关重要，因为大型测试套件会超出上下文限制、引入噪声并抬高推理成本。TestLoc 可以插入任何智能体式缺陷修复流水线，正交地提升整体性能。作为概念验证，我们在 SWE-Bench Lite 与 SWE-Bench Verified 基准上表明，TestLoc 使 Otter 框架下的 issue 复现率相对提升 6.2%–9.0%，使 Agentless 框架下的 issue 解决率相对提升 9.4%–12.9%，捕获了此前智能体已正确生成却未作为最终补丁提交的修复。相比收益，使用 TestLoc 的成本开销极小，即在 SWE-Bench 实例上使用 GPT-4o 和 Claude-3.7-Sonnet 分别为每实例 0.02 美元和 0.05 美元。","tl":"把回归套件最小化成高相关子集，同时提升复现率与补丁验证。","au":["Yang Chen","Toufique Ahmed","Reyhaneh Jabbarvand","Martin Hirzel"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["regression test reuse","bug reproduction","patch validation","test minimization","SWE-Bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/83/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.18270"},{"id":"p00892","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SQLiFuzz: Uncovering SQL Injection in Any Web Applications","tz":"SQLiFuzz：在任意 Web 应用中挖掘 SQL 注入","a":"SQL injection (SQLi) is one of the most critical and prevalent security vulnerabilities, as it enables attackers to manipulate backend databases, bypass authentication, and even gain complete control of the underlying system. Since web applications are the primary target for SQL injection, the web developers must test to ensure the applications are robust to this attack. Recently, there have been several advanced solutions using fuzzing approaches to test SQL injection vulnerability; however, our preliminary analysis reveals key limitations that reduce their effectiveness: they primarily focus on GUI-based inputs while neglecting API endpoints, rely on less effective request selection strategies, and require complex configurations to deploy. To address these gaps, we propose SQLiFuzz, a universal and simple-to-deploy SQL injection fuzzer that operates across both GUI (web pages) and API entry points. SQLiFuzz introduces three key innovations: (i) a reverse proxy that unifies request collection and fuzzing and integrates seamlessly with existing crawlers and API scanners, (ii) a database proxy that enables request–query matching and serves as a reliable oracle, and (iii) a feedback-driven fuzzer that prioritizes potentially vulnerable requests and parameters and validates exploitability through database responses. We evaluate SQLiFuzz on six security benchmarks and ten real-world applications. SQLiFuzz successfully detected the majority of known SQLi cases in the benchmarks and uncovered nine new vulnerabilities, which had been overlooked by state-of-the-art tools, in the real-world applications. These results highlight SQLiFuzz’s ability to reveal SQLi across diverse architectures while maintaining practicality and ease of deployment.","az":"SQL 注入（SQLi）是最关键、最普遍的安全漏洞之一，它使攻击者能够操纵后端数据库、绕过认证，甚至完全控制底层系统。由于 Web 应用是 SQL 注入的主要目标，Web 开发者必须进行测试以确保应用对此类攻击具有健壮性。近来已有若干使用模糊测试方法检测 SQL 注入漏洞的先进方案；然而我们的初步分析揭示了削弱其有效性的关键局限：它们主要关注基于 GUI 的输入而忽视 API 端点，依赖效果较差的请求选择策略，并且部署时需要复杂配置。为填补这些空白，我们提出 SQLiFuzz，一个通用且易于部署的 SQL 注入模糊测试工具，可同时作用于 GUI（网页）与 API 入口点。SQLiFuzz 引入三项关键创新：（i）一个反向代理，统一请求收集与模糊测试，并可与现有爬虫和 API 扫描器无缝集成；（ii）一个数据库代理，实现请求—查询匹配并充当可靠的测试预言；（iii）一个反馈驱动的模糊测试器，对可能存在漏洞的请求与参数进行优先级排序，并通过数据库响应验证可利用性。我们在六个安全基准和十个真实应用上评估 SQLiFuzz。SQLiFuzz 成功检测出基准中的大多数已知 SQLi 案例，并在真实应用中发现了九个被最先进工具遗漏的新漏洞。这些结果凸显了 SQLiFuzz 在不同架构下揭示 SQLi 的能力，同时保持实用性与易部署性。","tl":"反向代理加数据库代理做预言，GUI 与 API 入口统一 SQLi 模糊测试。","au":["I Putu Arya Dharmaadi","Thuan Pham","Fadi Mohsen","Fatih Turkmen"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["SQL injection","web application fuzzing","reverse proxy","database oracle","API endpoints"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/84/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3808149"},{"id":"p00893","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ScanCoder: Leveraging Human Attention Patterns to Enhance LLMs for Code","tz":"ScanCoder：利用人类注意力模式增强代码大模型","a":"Code comprehension is a fundamental challenge in software engineering that impacts developer productivity and software quality. While Large Language Models (LLMs) demonstrate strong capabilities in code generation and summarization, they process code differently from human developers, who employ strategic attention patterns focused on semantically critical elements. Recent research has successfully integrated human attention patterns captured through eye-tracking into AI models for software engineering tasks, however, existing human-AI approaches face critical limitations that prevent widespread practical deployment, particularly for LLM enhancement. Existing approaches to incorporate human cognitive insights face scalability limitations due to resource-intensive eye-tracking studies and lack empirical validation for cross-language generalizability. We present ScanCoder, a framework that integrates cognitive simulation with LLM enhancement through (1) generating human-like attention patterns at scale using minimal eye-tracking data via cognitive simulation with Adaptive Character of Thought-Rational (ACT-R) architecture, and (2) cognitively-guided fine-tuning that emphasizes tokens according to their cognitive salience and attention order. Our approach demonstrates cross-language transfer by applying C++-derived cognitive patterns to enhance Java programming tasks. Comprehensive evaluation on CodeXGLUE benchmarks shows consistent improvements across different LLM architectures, achieving gains of 39% for CrystalBLEU completion metrics and 22% for BERTScore summarization. Mechanistic analysis reveals that cognitive guidance reshapes model attention in task-dependent ways, increasing focus on semantically critical tokens by 2.5×. This work establishes the first scalable framework for integrating simulated human cognitive patterns into LLM training, enabling more interpretable and effective code understanding.","az":"代码理解是软件工程中的基础性挑战，影响开发者生产力与软件质量。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在代码生成与摘要上表现出很强能力，它们处理代码的方式与人类开发者不同——后者会采用聚焦于语义关键元素的策略性注意力模式。近期研究已成功将通过眼动追踪捕获的人类注意力模式融入面向软件工程任务的 AI 模型，然而现有的人机结合方法存在阻碍其广泛实际部署的关键局限，尤其是在增强 LLM 方面。现有融入人类认知洞见的方法因眼动追踪研究资源消耗大而面临可扩展性限制，并且缺乏跨语言泛化能力的实证验证。我们提出 ScanCoder，一个将认知模拟与 LLM 增强相结合的框架，其做法包括：（1）借助基于 ACT-R（Adaptive Character of Thought-Rational）架构的认知模拟，用极少的眼动追踪数据大规模生成类人注意力模式；（2）进行认知引导的微调，按 token 的认知显著性与注意力顺序对其加权强调。我们的方法通过将源自 C++ 的认知模式应用于增强 Java 编程任务，展示了跨语言迁移能力。在 CodeXGLUE 基准上的全面评估显示，不同 LLM 架构下均有一致提升，代码补全的 CrystalBLEU 指标提升 39%，摘要的 BERTScore 提升 22%。机理分析表明，认知引导以任务相关的方式重塑了模型注意力，使其对语义关键 token 的关注提升了 2.5 倍。这项工作建立了首个将模拟人类认知模式融入 LLM 训练的可扩展框架，使代码理解更可解释、更有效。","tl":"用 ACT-R 认知模拟大规模造类人注意力，再做认知引导微调。","au":["Yueke Zhang","Yifan Zhang","Zihan Fang","Greg Trafton","Daniel Levin","Kevin Leach","Yu Huang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["human attention","eye tracking","ACT-R cognitive simulation","cognitively-guided fine-tuning","code comprehension"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/85/x"},{"id":"p00894","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Empowering Autonomous Debugging Agents with Efficient Dynamic Analysis","tz":"用高效动态分析赋能自主调试智能体","a":"Autonomous agents for automated program repair represent a promising frontier in software engineering, yet their effectiveness is often hindered by reliance on post-mortem, coarse-grained execution feedback. While integrating traditional interactive debuggers seems a natural solution, their low-level, line-by-line interaction paradigm turns to be cost-inefficient for LLM-based agents, leading to exhausted budgets and unproductive loops. To mitigate this, we introduce Agent-centric Debugging Interface (ADI), a novel agent-centric debugging interface designed for cost-efficient, end-to-end autonomous interaction. Specifically, Agent-centric Debugging Interface realizes a function-level interaction paradigm, powered by our Frame Lifetime Trace—a comprehensive data structure encapsulating a function’s stateful execution trace—and a set of high-level navigational commands. Our extensive evaluation on the SWE-bench benchmark demonstrates the effectiveness and efficiency of ADI. By simply equipping a basic agent with ADI, it successfully resolves 63.8% of the tasks on the SWE-bench Verified set, even slightly outperforming the highly-optimized and high-investment Claude-Tools agent, at an average cost of $1.28 per task with Claude-Sonnet-3.7. Furthermore, we demonstrate ADI’s generality by integrating it as a plug-and-play component into the existing SOTA agents, delivering consistent gains ranging from 6.2% to 18.5% on the resolved tasks. These results indicate that Agent-centric Debugging Interface could achieve a general and efficient enhancement for the existing autonomous agents.","az":"面向自动程序修复的自主智能体是软件工程中一个充满前景的前沿方向，但其效果常受限于对事后、粗粒度执行反馈的依赖。虽然集成传统交互式调试器看似是自然的解决方案，但其低层、逐行的交互范式对基于 LLM 的智能体而言成本效率很低，会耗尽预算并陷入无效循环。为缓解这一问题，我们提出 ADI（Agent-centric Debugging Interface），一个以智能体为中心、面向低成本端到端自主交互的全新调试接口。具体而言，ADI 实现了函数级的交互范式，由我们的 Frame Lifetime Trace（一种封装函数有状态执行轨迹的综合数据结构）以及一组高层导航命令驱动。我们在 SWE-bench 基准上的大量评估证明了 ADI 的有效性与高效性。仅仅为一个基础智能体配备 ADI，它便在 SWE-bench Verified 集上成功解决了 63.8% 的任务，甚至略微超过了经过高度优化、投入巨大的 Claude-Tools 智能体，而在 Claude-Sonnet-3.7 下的平均成本为每任务 1.28 美元。此外，我们通过将 ADI 作为即插即用组件集成到现有 SOTA 智能体中，展示了其通用性，在已解决任务上带来 6.2% 至 18.5% 的一致增益。这些结果表明，以智能体为中心的调试接口可为现有自主智能体带来通用且高效的增强。","tl":"把逐行调试换成函数级交互与帧生命周期轨迹，显著降本增效。","au":["Jiahong Xiang","Xiaoyang Xu","Xiaopan Chu","Hongliang Tian","Yuqun Zhang"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["debugging interface","dynamic analysis","autonomous repair agent","execution trace","SWE-bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/86/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.24212"},{"id":"p00895","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Cross-Refactoring-Type Test Program Migration for Refactoring Engines","tz":"面向重构引擎的跨重构类型测试程序迁移","a":"Refactoring engines are an essential part of modern IDEs, supporting automated or semi-automated software refactorings. However, these refactoring engines suffer from software defects, just like other complex software systems, and buggy refactoring engines may silently inject fatal errors into software projects. Consequently, thorough testing of refactoring engines is highly desirable. To this end, this paper proposes an automated approach called EngineTest to test Java refactoring engines. Unlike existing approaches, it is the first in this line to leverage both LLMs and bug reports of refactoring types other than the targeted refactoring type. The key rationale is that the same mistake, e.g., ignoring the potential name shadowing, may result in similar errors in multiple refactoring types. Consequently, we may retrieve a bug report for a refactoring type, leverage LLMs to figure out the underlying reason, and request LLMs to generate test programs for other types of refactorings. Finally, we run the test cases and validate them with differential testing and LLM-based inconsistent checking. We evaluate the proposed approach with widely used state-of-the-practice refactoring engines in Eclipse, NetBeans, and IntelliJ IDEA. Our evaluation results demonstrate that a total of 77 previously unknown bugs have been identified, and 30 of them have been manually confirmed by the tool vendors.","az":"重构引擎是现代 IDE 的重要组成部分，支持自动或半自动的软件重构。然而这些重构引擎与其他复杂软件系统一样存在软件缺陷，有缺陷的重构引擎可能会悄无声息地把致命错误注入软件项目。因此，对重构引擎进行彻底测试非常必要。为此，本文提出一种名为 EngineTest 的自动化方法来测试 Java 重构引擎。与现有方法不同，它是该方向上首个同时利用 LLM 和目标重构类型之外的其他重构类型缺陷报告的方法。其关键思路是：同一种失误，例如忽视潜在的名字遮蔽（name shadowing），可能在多种重构类型中导致类似错误。因此，我们可以检索某一重构类型的缺陷报告，借助 LLM 找出其根本原因，并要求 LLM 为其他类型的重构生成测试程序。最后，我们运行这些测试用例，并通过差分测试和基于 LLM 的不一致检查加以验证。我们使用 Eclipse、NetBeans 和 IntelliJ IDEA 中广泛使用的业界主流重构引擎评估所提方法。评估结果表明，总共识别出 77 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 30 个已被工具厂商人工确认。","tl":"跨重构类型迁移缺陷报告造测试程序，挖出 77 个引擎新缺陷。","au":["Chunhao Dong","Yanjie Jiang","Yang Zhang","Yuxia Zhang","Hui Liu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["refactoring engine testing","test program migration","bug reports","differential testing","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/87/x"},{"id":"p00896","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ViBR: Automated Bug Replay from Video-based Reports Using Vision-Language Models","tz":"ViBR：使用视觉语言模型从视频缺陷报告自动复现缺陷","a":"Bug reports play a critical role in software maintenance by helping users convey encountered issues to developers. Recently, GUI screen capture videos have gained popularity as a bug reporting artifact due to their ease of use and ability to retain rich contextual information. However, automatically reproducing bugs from such recordings remains a significant challenge. Existing methods often rely on fragile image-processing heuristics, explicit touch indicators, or pre-constructed UI transition graphs, which require non-trivial instrumentation and app-specific setup. This paper presents ViBR, a lightweight and fully automated approach that reproduces bugs directly from GUI recordings. Specifically, ViBR combines CLIP-based embedding similarity for action segmentation with Vision-Language Models (VLMs) for region-aware GUI state comparison and guided bug replay. Experimental results show that ViBR successfully reproduces 73.7% of bug recordings, significantly outperforming state-of-the-art baselines and ablation variants.","az":"缺陷报告在软件维护中扮演关键角色，帮助用户向开发者传达遇到的问题。近来，GUI 屏幕录制视频因易于使用且能保留丰富上下文信息，作为一种缺陷报告制品日益流行。然而，从这类录制中自动复现缺陷仍是重大挑战。现有方法往往依赖脆弱的图像处理启发式规则、显式的触摸指示标记，或预先构建的 UI 跳转图，这些都需要相当的插桩工作和针对具体应用的配置。本文提出 ViBR，一种轻量且全自动的方法，可直接从 GUI 录制中复现缺陷。具体而言，ViBR 将基于 CLIP 嵌入相似度的动作切分与用于区域感知 GUI 状态比较和引导式缺陷重放的视觉语言模型（VLM）相结合。实验结果表明，ViBR 成功复现了 73.7% 的缺陷录制，显著优于最先进的基线方法与各消融变体。","tl":"CLIP 切分动作加 VLM 状态比对，直接从录屏复现缺陷 73.7%。","au":["Sidong Feng","Dingbang Wang","Nikola Tomic","Tingting Yu","Aldeida Aleti","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["multimodal","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["video-based bug report","bug reproduction","vision-language model","GUI replay","action segmentation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/88/x"},{"id":"p00897","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"BackportBench: A Multilingual Benchmark for Automated Patch Backporting","tz":"BackportBench：面向自动化补丁回移的多语言基准","a":"Many modern software projects evolve rapidly to incorporate new features and security patches. It is important for users to update their dependencies to safer versions, but many still use older, vulnerable package versions because upgrading can be difficult and may break their existing codebase. Software developers can mitigate this problem by backporting security patches to older releases. However, manually backporting is time-consuming and error-prone. The effectiveness of existing automated backporting techniques on general software remains unclear since they typically target only code-hunk or function-level patch porting scenarios and are evaluated with imperfect metrics. To facilitate the development and evaluation of automated backporting techniques, we introduce BackportBench, the first comprehensive benchmark suite for patch backporting problem. BackportBench is a multilingual benchmark that contains 202 patch backporting problems from PyPI, Maven, and npm, each with executable Docker environments and relevant test cases. We evaluated existing patch porting methods and LLM-based techniques that have the potential to adapt to this task using BackportBench. The results show that the agentic method has outperformed traditional patch porting methods, especially on cases that require logical and structural changes. However, the performance varies across different programming languages. Based on the findings, we draw several implications for researchers and software practitioners in future work on automated backporting.","az":"许多现代软件项目快速演化，以纳入新特性和安全补丁。用户将依赖更新到更安全的版本很重要，但许多人仍在使用较旧且存在漏洞的包版本，因为升级可能很困难，还可能破坏现有代码库。软件开发者可以通过把安全补丁回移到较旧发行版来缓解这一问题。然而人工回移既耗时又易出错。现有自动化回移技术在通用软件上的有效性仍不清楚，因为它们通常只针对代码块级或函数级的补丁移植场景，且使用了不完善的指标来评估。为促进自动化回移技术的开发与评估，我们提出 BackportBench，首个面向补丁回移问题的综合基准套件。BackportBench 是一个多语言基准，包含来自 PyPI、Maven 和 npm 的 202 个补丁回移问题，每个问题都配有可执行的 Docker 环境和相关测试用例。我们使用 BackportBench 评估了现有的补丁移植方法以及有潜力适配该任务的基于 LLM 的技术。结果表明，智能体式方法已经超越传统补丁移植方法，尤其是在需要逻辑与结构改动的案例上。然而，其性能在不同编程语言之间存在差异。基于这些发现，我们为研究者与软件从业者在未来自动化回移工作中给出若干启示。","tl":"首个多语言可执行补丁回移基准，显示智能体法优于传统移植。","au":["Zhiqing Zhong","Jiaming Huang","Pinjia He"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["patch backporting","multilingual benchmark","security patch","executable Docker environment","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/89/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.01396"},{"id":"p00898","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Particles to Perils: SVGD-Based Hazardous Scenario Generation for Autonomous Driving Systems Testing","tz":"从粒子到风险：基于 SVGD 的自动驾驶系统测试危险场景生成","a":"Simulation-based testing of autonomous driving systems (ADS) must reveal realistic, diverse failures that arise from dense traffic and complex interactions among heterogeneous dynamic obejcts (vehicles, cyclists, and pedestrians). The effectiveness of ADS testing is highly sensitive to the choice of initial conditions (seeds). However, existing search-based seeding approaches (e.g., genetic algorithms) struggle in the high-dimensional spaces induced by dense and heterogeneous traffic, collapsing into a limited set of modes and leaving many realistic failure scenarios undiscovered. We present PtoP, a novel framework for testing autonomous driving systems. At its core, PtoP couples adaptive random seed generation—which produces seeds that hit diverse initial failure modes—with Stein Variational Gradient Descent (SVGD) to explore diverse, failure-inducing initial conditions. Each particle represents the initial state of a dynamic object. SVGD jointly leverages gradient-driven attraction toward high-hazard regions and kernel-mediated repulsion to maintain diversity among particles, producing risk-seeking yet well-distributed seeds that span multiple distinct failure modes. Beyond seed generation, PtoP serves as a plug-and-play framework that integrates seamlessly with online testing techniques (e.g., reinforcement learning–based testers) and, by providing principled seeds, boosts their overall testing effectiveness. We evaluate PtoP in CARLA—a state-of-the-art simulator—on two autonomous driving systems: an industry-grade stack (Apollo) and an end-to-end ADS native to CARLA. When combined with state-of-the-art baselines, PtoP substantially increases the safety-violation rate (by up to 27.68%), scenario diversity (by up to 9.6%), and map coverage (by up to 16.78%) over the baselines. Our framework and all associated data are available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/PtoP-75B3 .","az":"对自动驾驶系统（ADS）的基于仿真的测试必须揭示由密集交通以及异构动态对象（车辆、骑行者、行人）之间复杂交互所引发的真实、多样的失效。ADS 测试的有效性对初始条件（种子）的选择高度敏感。然而，现有基于搜索的种子生成方法（例如遗传算法）在密集异构交通带来的高维空间中表现不佳，会坍缩到少数几种模式，使许多真实的失效场景未被发现。我们提出 PtoP，一个用于测试自动驾驶系统的新框架。其核心是将自适应随机种子生成（生成能触发多样初始失效模式的种子）与 Stein 变分梯度下降（SVGD）相结合，以探索多样的、可诱发失效的初始条件。每个粒子代表一个动态对象的初始状态。SVGD 同时利用朝向高危区域的梯度驱动吸引力和核介导的排斥力来维持粒子间的多样性，从而产生既追求风险又分布良好的种子，覆盖多种不同的失效模式。除种子生成之外，PtoP 还是一个即插即用框架，可与在线测试技术（如基于强化学习的测试器）无缝集成，并通过提供有原则的种子提升它们的整体测试效果。我们在最先进的仿真器 CARLA 中，对两个自动驾驶系统进行评估：工业级技术栈 Apollo 和 CARLA 原生的端到端 ADS。与最先进基线结合时，PtoP 大幅提升了安全违规率（最高 27.68%）、场景多样性（最高 9.6%）和地图覆盖率（最高 16.78%）。我们的框架与全部相关数据可在 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/PtoP-75B3 获取。","tl":"用 SVGD 的吸引—排斥机制造出既高危又多样的 ADS 测试种子。","au":["Linfeng Liang","Xiao Cheng","Tsong Yueh Chen","Xi Zheng"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving testing","scenario generation","Stein variational gradient descent","seed diversity","CARLA"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/90/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18918"},{"id":"p00899","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Detecting Bugs in Rust Compiler Fix Suggestions via Constraint-Violation-Guided Mutation","tz":"通过约束违反引导的变异检测 Rust 编译器修复建议中的缺陷","a":"Rust is a modern systems programming language that ensures memory safety through unique mechanisms, including ownership, borrowing, and lifetime annotations. These features prevent critical vulnerabilities but also impose strict constraints that many developers find difficult to understand. To mitigate this challenge, the Rust compiler, rustc, provides rich diagnostics and fix suggestions. However, recent studies reveal that diagnostic issues account for about 20% of all reported rustc bugs. Our analysis of rustc’s suggestion bugs fixed over the past three years shows that most of them originated from errors in Rust-specific core modules, such as the type checker and borrow checker, rather than from simple mistakes in the general diagnostic logic, like suggesting an incorrect variable name or mismatched parentheses. The impact of diagnostic issues, especially bugs in rustc’s fix suggestion, should not be underestimated, as they can mislead developers and reduce rustc’s usability, and in severe cases may even lead to rustc crashes. Existing testing tools, however, provide little support for systematically evaluating the correctness and reliability of these suggestions. To address this gap, in this paper, we present SugBreaker, an automated testing framework specifically designed to validate rustc’s suggestions. We propose a constraint-violation-guided mutation approach that injects type-related, borrow-related, and lifetime-related errors into valid Rust programs to trigger compiler diagnostics and iteratively verify the correctness of suggested fixes. SugBreaker has already detected 12 bugs, and 11 of them have been confirmed or fixed; all of them are triggered by different rustc error messages. Compared with a series of rustc testing baseline tools, SugBreaker achieves broader coverage of rustc’s core checking modules and a higher suggestion trigger rate, which further confirms the effectiveness and efficiency of SugBreaker for testing rustc’s fix suggestions.","az":"Rust 是一门现代系统编程语言，通过所有权、借用和生命周期标注等独特机制保证内存安全。这些特性防止了关键漏洞，但也施加了许多开发者难以理解的严格约束。为缓解这一挑战，Rust 编译器 rustc 提供了丰富的诊断信息和修复建议。然而近期研究显示，诊断相关问题约占全部已报告 rustc 缺陷的 20%。我们对过去三年中修复的 rustc 建议类缺陷的分析表明，其中大多数源于 Rust 特有核心模块（如类型检查器和借用检查器）中的错误，而非通用诊断逻辑中的简单失误（如建议了错误的变量名或括号不匹配）。诊断问题的影响，尤其是 rustc 修复建议中的缺陷，不应被低估，因为它们会误导开发者、降低 rustc 的可用性，严重时甚至可能导致 rustc 崩溃。然而现有测试工具几乎不支持系统性地评估这些建议的正确性与可靠性。为填补这一空白，本文提出 SugBreaker，一个专门用于验证 rustc 建议的自动化测试框架。我们提出一种约束违反引导的变异方法，向合法 Rust 程序中注入类型相关、借用相关和生命周期相关的错误，以触发编译器诊断，并迭代验证所建议修复的正确性。SugBreaker 已检测出 12 个缺陷，其中 11 个已被确认或修复；它们均由不同的 rustc 错误消息触发。与一系列 rustc 测试基线工具相比，SugBreaker 覆盖了更广的 rustc 核心检查模块，并具有更高的建议触发率，这进一步印证了 SugBreaker 测试 rustc 修复建议的有效性与高效性。","tl":"注入类型/借用/生命周期错误专测 rustc 修复建议，已报 12 个缺陷。","au":["Zixi Liu","Yang Feng","Jialiang Jiang","Baowen Xu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Rust compiler","fix suggestion","constraint-violation mutation","diagnostics bugs","compiler testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/91/x"},{"id":"p00900","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Active Learning of Symbolic Automata for Reactive Programs via Dynamic Symbolic Mapper","tz":"通过动态符号映射器为反应式程序主动学习符号自动机","a":"Active learning of formal behavior models from program source code is a powerful approach for a wide range of software analysis, validation, and verification tasks, including understanding system intent, automating specification mining, generating test oracles, and checking formal properties. Recent advances in active learning of symbolic automata, powered by program synthesis and model checking, provide both rich expressiveness and soundness guarantees for the learned models. However, these techniques often encounter significant performance bottlenecks, particularly when dealing with reactive programs that expose many program variables with large value domains. This work introduces an extended active learning algorithm tailored for reactive programs by incorporating a novel dynamic symbolic mapper for learning symbolic automata. The mapper abstracts program behavior using learner-inferred predicates over program variables, encodes each valuation of these variables as a Boolean vector induced by these predicates (Boolean abstraction), and dynamically refines the abstraction in response to missing behaviors identified by the teacher. The mapper is granularity-aware: for teaching, it employs the coarsest predicates sufficient to expose missing behaviors, enabling broad exploration; for learning, it refines the abstraction only to the finest predicates necessary to resolve the uncovered gaps, trying to avoid refinements that could otherwise be triggered by coarse abstraction. We evaluated our approach on 120 benchmarks, including SV-COMP tasks, Simulink model-driven programs, LeetCode problems, and representative embedded control software. The results show that our method learns 32 more symbolic automata and reduces the average active learning time by 55.6% compared to the state-of-the-art.","az":"从程序源码中主动学习形式化行为模型，是支撑广泛软件分析、验证与确认任务的有力方法，这些任务包括理解系统意图、自动化规约挖掘、生成测试预言以及检查形式化性质。由程序合成与模型检验驱动的符号自动机主动学习的最新进展，为学到的模型同时提供了丰富的表达能力与可靠性保证。然而，这些技术常遇到显著的性能瓶颈，尤其是在处理暴露大量程序变量且取值域很大的反应式程序时。本工作提出一种为反应式程序量身定制的扩展主动学习算法，通过引入一种用于学习符号自动机的新颖动态符号映射器实现。该映射器使用学习器推断出的、定义在程序变量上的谓词来抽象程序行为，将这些变量的每一种赋值编码为由这些谓词诱导的布尔向量（布尔抽象），并根据教师识别出的缺失行为动态细化抽象。该映射器是粒度感知的：在教学时，它采用足以暴露缺失行为的最粗谓词，从而支持广泛探索；在学习时，它只把抽象细化到解决已发现差距所必需的最细谓词，尽量避免粗抽象可能触发的多余细化。我们在 120 个基准上评估了该方法，包括 SV-COMP 任务、Simulink 模型驱动程序、LeetCode 题目以及具有代表性的嵌入式控制软件。结果表明，与最先进方法相比，我们的方法多学出 32 个符号自动机，并将平均主动学习时间降低了 55.6%。","tl":"粒度感知的动态符号映射器，让符号自动机学习提速 55.6%。","au":["Yoel Kim","Yunja Choi"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["active automata learning","symbolic automata","reactive programs","Boolean abstraction","specification mining"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/92/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808154"},{"id":"p00901","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards Secure Logging: Characterizing and Benchmarking Logging Code Security Issues with LLMs","tz":"迈向安全日志：用 LLM 刻画并基准测试日志代码的安全问题","a":"Logging code plays an important role in software systems by recording key events and behaviors, which are essential for debugging and monitoring. However, insecure logging practices can inadvertently expose sensitive information or enable attacks such as log injection, posing serious threats to system security and privacy. Prior research has examined general defects in logging code, but systematic analysis of logging code security issues remains limited, particularly in leveraging LLMs for detection and repair. In this paper, we derive a comprehensive taxonomy of logging code security issues, encompassing four common issue categories and 10 corresponding patterns. We further construct a benchmark dataset with 101 real-world logging security issue reports that have been manually reviewed and annotated. We then propose an automated framework that incorporates various contextual knowledge to evaluate LLMs’ capabilities in detecting and repairing logging security issues. Our experimental results reveal a notable disparity in performance: while LLMs are moderately effective at detecting security issues (e.g., the accuracy ranges from 12.9% to 52.5% on average), they face noticeable challenges in reliably generating correct code repairs. We also find that the issue description alone improves the LLMs’ detection accuracy more than the security pattern explanation or a combination of both. Overall, our findings provide actionable insights for practitioners and highlight the potential and limitations of current LLMs for secure logging.","az":"日志代码在软件系统中扮演重要角色，它记录关键事件与行为，这对调试和监控至关重要。然而，不安全的日志实践可能无意中泄露敏感信息，或使日志注入等攻击成为可能，从而对系统安全与隐私构成严重威胁。已有研究考察过日志代码中的一般性缺陷，但对日志代码安全问题的系统性分析仍然有限，尤其是在利用大语言模型进行检测与修复方面。本文中，我们推导出一个全面的日志代码安全问题分类法，涵盖四类常见问题和 10 种相应模式。我们进一步构建了一个基准数据集，包含 101 份经过人工审阅与标注的真实世界日志安全问题报告。随后我们提出一个自动化框架，融入多种上下文知识，用以评估 LLM 在检测与修复日志安全问题上的能力。实验结果揭示了显著的性能差异：LLM 在检测安全问题上具有中等效果（例如，平均准确率在 12.9% 到 52.5% 之间），但在可靠地生成正确的代码修复方面面临明显挑战。我们还发现，仅提供问题描述对 LLM 检测准确率的提升，要优于提供安全模式解释或两者的组合。总体而言，我们的发现为从业者提供了可操作的洞见，并凸显了当前 LLM 在安全日志方面的潜力与局限。","tl":"首个日志代码安全问题分类法与 101 例基准，评测 LLM 检测修复能力。","au":["He Yang Yuan","Xin Wang","Kundi Yao","An Ran Chen","Zishuo Ding","Zhenhao Li"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["logging code security","taxonomy","benchmark","LLM detection and repair","log injection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/93/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.20211"},{"id":"p00902","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Wily Hare Has Three Havens: Combating Programmable Logic Controller Attacks via Virtualization Redundancy","tz":"狡兔三窟：以虚拟化冗余对抗可编程逻辑控制器攻击","a":"Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs) lack built-in security mechanisms, and their critical role in industrial control systems makes them prime targets for cyberattacks. Recent advances in next-generation PLCs have introduced embedded virtualization technologies that partition functional domains within a single hardware platform and integrate AI and edge computing to improve business performance. Nevertheless, many PLC vendors and researchers have largely overlooked the potential of virtualization to strengthen PLC security. To address this gap, we propose TriHaven, an embedded virtualization-based security architecture for PLCs. TriHaven separates the PLC control loop and deploys its components in dedicated virtual machines, each with distinct design characteristics. By further implementing a redundancy-compare strategy for PLC control logic execution, TriHaven enables real-time attack detection and rapid emergency response through control switching, thereby mitigating diverse and previously unknown threats. Using the Jailhouse virtualization framework, our experiments on OpenPLC and Beremiz–two open-source PLC runtimes–demonstrate the feasibility of TriHaven while preserving essential security objectives.","az":"可编程逻辑控制器（PLC）缺乏内建的安全机制，而它们在工业控制系统中的关键角色使其成为网络攻击的首要目标。新一代 PLC 的最新进展引入了嵌入式虚拟化技术，在单一硬件平台内划分功能域，并集成 AI 与边缘计算以提升业务性能。然而，许多 PLC 厂商与研究者在很大程度上忽视了虚拟化在增强 PLC 安全方面的潜力。为填补这一空白，我们提出 TriHaven，一种基于嵌入式虚拟化的 PLC 安全架构。TriHaven 将 PLC 控制回路拆分，并把其组件部署在各自专用的虚拟机中，每个虚拟机具有不同的设计特性。通过进一步对 PLC 控制逻辑执行实施冗余比对策略，TriHaven 能够实现实时攻击检测，并通过控制切换实现快速应急响应，从而缓解多样的乃至此前未知的威胁。我们基于 Jailhouse 虚拟化框架，在 OpenPLC 与 Beremiz 两个开源 PLC 运行时上的实验，证明了 TriHaven 在保持核心安全目标的同时具备可行性。","tl":"用嵌入式虚拟化冗余比对实现 PLC 实时攻击检测与控制切换。","au":["Wenjie Wang","Yazhe Wang","Lei Ren"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["PLC security","embedded virtualization","redundancy comparison","industrial control system","Jailhouse"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/94/x"},{"id":"p00903","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Semantics-Guided Control-Flow Reconstruction for Firmware Binaries via Static Analysis","tz":"基于静态分析的固件二进制语义引导控制流重构","a":"Control-flow reconstruction is a fundamental yet challenging problem in firmware analysis, particularly for stripped or raw-format binaries that lack symbolic metadata. Existing methods typically rely on syntax heuristics or format-specific patterns, which are inadequate for real-world firmware that includes indirect jumps, manually crafted assembly, and limited metadata. We present a semantics-guided static analysis framework for accurate control-flow reconstruction in stripped ELF and raw-format firmware binaries. Our approach consists of two complementary components: (i) an intra-procedural control-flow reconstruction method that incrementally recovers direct branches, indirect jumps, and call-return flows via fixpoint-guided value-flow analysis; and (ii) an inter-procedural analysis that resolves indirect calls through cross-function value tracking and loop-structure matching. By decoupling control-flow reasoning from instruction semantics and function abstraction, our framework robustly handles tightly intertwined control-flow patterns and mitigates the impact of misanalysis. We implement our approach in Scarf (Semantics-guided Control-flow Analysis for Raw and Firmware binaries) and evaluate it on over 300 real-world firmware binaries in both ELF and raw formats. Compared with state-of-the-art reverse engineering tools, Scarf consistently achieves higher precision in control-flow recovery and demonstrates clear advantages on raw firmware, especially in resolving indirect jumps, call–return flows, and indirect calls. These results demonstrate that semantics-guided analysis provides a robust and scalable foundation for control flow reconstruction in metadata-deficient firmware.","az":"控制流重构是固件分析中一个基础但极具挑战的问题，对于缺乏符号元数据的剥离（stripped）或原始格式二进制尤其如此。现有方法通常依赖语法启发式规则或特定格式的模式，难以应对包含间接跳转、手工编写汇编以及元数据有限的真实固件。我们提出一个语义引导的静态分析框架，用于在剥离的 ELF 与原始格式固件二进制中进行精确的控制流重构。我们的方法由两个互补组件构成：（i）一种过程内控制流重构方法，通过不动点引导的值流分析逐步恢复直接分支、间接跳转以及调用—返回流；（ii）一种过程间分析，通过跨函数值追踪与循环结构匹配来解析间接调用。通过将控制流推理与指令语义和函数抽象解耦，我们的框架能稳健地处理紧密交织的控制流模式，并减轻误分析的影响。我们在 Scarf（面向原始与固件二进制的语义引导控制流分析）中实现了该方法，并在 300 多个真实固件二进制（ELF 与原始格式）上进行评估。与最先进的逆向工程工具相比，Scarf 在控制流恢复上持续取得更高精度，并在原始格式固件上展现出明显优势，尤其是在解析间接跳转、调用—返回流与间接调用方面。这些结果表明，语义引导的分析为元数据缺失的固件中的控制流重构提供了稳健且可扩展的基础。","tl":"用不动点值流分析解间接跳转与间接调用，重构剥离固件控制流。","au":["Fengjuan Gao","Qingjie Zhu","Yi Zhang","Yu Wang","Xuandong Li","Ke Wang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["control-flow reconstruction","firmware binary","value-flow analysis","indirect jump resolution","stripped ELF"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/95/x"},{"id":"p00904","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"When Shared Worlds Break: Demystifying Defects in Multi-User Extended Reality Software Systems","tz":"当共享世界崩塌：揭秘多用户扩展现实软件系统中的缺陷","a":"Multi-user Extended Reality (XR) systems enable transformative shared experiences but introduce unique software defects that compromise user experience. Understanding software defects in multi-user XR systems is crucial for enhancing system reliability, yet remains underexplored. To fill the gap, this paper presents the first large-scale empirical study of multi-user XR defects, analyzing 2,649 real-world bug reports from diverse sources, including developer forums, GitHub repositories, and app reviews on mainstream XR app stores. Through rigorous qualitative analysis using iterative open coding, we develop a comprehensive taxonomy that classifies multi-user XR bugs along three dimensions: Symptom Manifestation, Root Cause Origin, and Consequence Severity. Our findings reveal that synchronization inconsistencies and avatar-related anomalies are the most prevalent symptoms, while network/synchronization logic defects and session management flaws emerge as dominant root causes. Critically, over 34% of analyzed bugs lead to severe consequences that fundamentally break the shared experience, including system crashes, persistent disconnections, and complete interaction breakdowns, etc. We also identify concerning privacy and health implications unique to multi-user XR contexts. Based on our findings of defect analysis, we provide actionable recommendations for developers, platform vendors, and researchers. Our results demonstrate that multi-user XR systems face distinct challenges at the intersection of distributed systems, real-time 3D interaction, and immersive experiences, necessitating specialized approaches to testing, debugging, and quality assurance. Our datasets and results are released to facilitate follow-up studies: https://sites.google.com/view/multi-user-xr-study .","az":"多用户扩展现实（XR）系统带来了变革性的共享体验，但也引入了损害用户体验的独特软件缺陷。理解多用户 XR 系统中的软件缺陷对提升系统可靠性至关重要，但这一问题仍缺乏探索。为填补这一空白，本文首次对多用户 XR 缺陷开展大规模实证研究，分析了来自开发者论坛、GitHub 仓库以及主流 XR 应用商店评论等多种来源的 2,649 份真实缺陷报告。通过采用迭代开放编码的严格定性分析，我们建立了一个全面的分类法，沿症状表现、根因来源与后果严重性三个维度对多用户 XR 缺陷进行分类。我们的发现表明，同步不一致与化身（avatar）相关异常是最普遍的症状，而网络/同步逻辑缺陷与会话管理缺陷是主导性的根因。尤为关键的是，所分析缺陷中超过 34% 会导致从根本上破坏共享体验的严重后果，包括系统崩溃、持续断连以及交互完全失效等。我们还识别出多用户 XR 场景特有的、令人担忧的隐私与健康影响。基于缺陷分析的发现，我们为开发者、平台厂商与研究者提供了可操作的建议。我们的结果表明，多用户 XR 系统处于分布式系统、实时 3D 交互与沉浸式体验的交叉点，面临独特挑战，需要专门的测试、调试与质量保障方法。我们的数据集与结果已公开以便后续研究：https://sites.google.com/view/multi-user-xr-study 。","tl":"首次大规模刻画多用户 XR 缺陷，建三维分类法并揭示同步类根因。","au":["Shuqing Li","Chenran Zhang","Binchang Li","Cuiyun Gao","Michael Lyu"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["multi-user XR","bug taxonomy","empirical study","synchronization defects","bug reports"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/96/x"},{"id":"p00905","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Boosting LLMs for Mutation Generation","tz":"增强 LLM 的变异体生成能力","a":"LLM-based mutation testing is rapidly emerging as a promising testing technology, but existing approaches typically rely on a fixed set of mutations as few-shot examples or none at all. This can result in generic low-quality mutations, missed context-specific mutation patterns, substantial numbers of redundant and uncompilable mutants, and limited semantic similarity to real bugs. To overcome these limitations, we introduce SMART. SMART integrates retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) on a vectorized dataset of real-world bugs, focused code chunking, and supervised fine-tuning using mutations coupled with real-world bugs. We conducted an extensive empirical study of SMART using 1,991 real-world Java bugs from the Defects4J and ConDefects datasets, comparing SMART to the state-of-the-art LLM-based approaches, LLMut and LLMorpheus. The results reveal that SMART substantially improves mutation validity, effectiveness, and efficiency (even enabling small-scale 7B-scale models to match/surpass large models like GPT-4o). We also demonstrate that SMART significantly impacts downstream Software Engineering applications to test case prioritization and fault localization. More specifically, SMART improves validity (weighted average generation rate) from 42.89% to 65.6%. It raises the non-duplicate rate from 87.38% to 95.62%, and the compilable rate from 88.85% to 90.21%. In terms of effectiveness, it achieves a real bug detection rate of 92.61% (vs. 57.86% for LLMut) and improves the average Ochiai coefficient from 25.61% to 38.44%. For fault localization, it locates 64 more bugs by MUSE and 57 bugs by Metallaxis as Top-1.","az":"基于 LLM 的变异测试正迅速成为一项有前景的测试技术，但现有方法通常依赖一组固定的变异作为少样本示例，甚至完全不提供示例。这会导致生成通用的低质量变异体、遗漏特定上下文的变异模式、产生大量冗余与不可编译的变异体，以及与真实缺陷的语义相似度有限。为克服这些局限，我们提出 SMART。SMART 在真实缺陷的向量化数据集上集成检索增强生成（RAG）、聚焦式代码切块，以及使用与真实缺陷配对的变异进行的监督微调。我们使用来自 Defects4J 与 ConDefects 数据集的 1,991 个真实 Java 缺陷，对 SMART 开展了广泛的实证研究，并与最先进的基于 LLM 的方法 LLMut 和 LLMorpheus 进行对比。结果表明，SMART 大幅提升了变异体的有效性、效能与效率（甚至使 7B 规模的小模型能够匹敌或超越 GPT-4o 这类大模型）。我们还证明，SMART 对下游软件工程应用（测试用例优先级排序与缺陷定位）具有显著影响。具体而言，SMART 将有效性（加权平均生成率）从 42.89% 提升至 65.6%，将非重复率从 87.38% 提升至 95.62%，可编译率从 88.85% 提升至 90.21%。在效能方面，它取得了 92.61% 的真实缺陷检测率（LLMut 为 57.86%），并将平均 Ochiai 系数从 25.61% 提升至 38.44%。在缺陷定位方面，它使 MUSE 多定位出 64 个缺陷、Metallaxis 多定位出 57 个缺陷（Top-1）。","tl":"用真实缺陷 RAG 加微调生成变异体，7B 模型即超 GPT-4o。","au":["Bo Wang","Ming Deng","Mingda Chen","Chengran Yang","Youfang Lin","Mark Harman","Mike Papadakis","Jie M. Zhang"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mutation testing","retrieval-augmented generation","supervised fine-tuning","Defects4J","fault localization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/97/x"},{"id":"p00906","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ChainDelta: Automatic Patch-based Exploit Generation for Ethereum with Fuzzing Agents","tz":"ChainDelta：借助模糊测试智能体为以太坊自动生成基于补丁的漏洞利用","a":"Given the critical nature of Ethereum, exploiting 1-day vulnerabilities that are patched but not yet widely deployed is essential. Meanwhile, Automatic Patch-based Exploit Generation (APEG) is a promising technique for this, as it helps developers understand root causes, verify fixes in downstream forks, and detect incomplete patches. However, existing exploit generation tools can not work well for vulnerabilities on Ethereum due to three key unique challenges: (1) navigating complex and cross-language exploit paths hidden within patches, (2) synthesizing complicated and stateful environment configurations, and (3) handling non-deterministic inconsistencies between blockchain nodes that lead to false alarms. To address these challenges, we introduce ChainDelta, a novel fuzzing agent framework driven by Large Language Models to automatically generate exploits based on Ethereum security patches. ChainDelta consists of three core modules: a directed fuzzer utilizes call graph analysis to guide testing towards vulnerable code based on the patch information; an agent-based environment fuzzer acts as an expert to automatically set up the necessary blockchain states to trigger vulnerabilities; and finally, a state-aware sanitizer performs differential analysis while monitoring the blockchain transient state to distinguish true inconsistencies from benign non-determinism. We evaluate ChainDelta on a diverse benchmark with real-world vulnerability patches, covering a wide range of types such as data racing and denial-of-service. ChainDelta successfully generated exploits with a 70% success rate and only a 12.5% false positive rate. An ablation study confirms the contribution of each module to the overall performance. To demonstrate its practical impacts, we conducted a real-world auditing campaign on top of ChainDelta, leading to the discovery of four previously undisclosed vulnerabilities with bug bounties.","az":"鉴于以太坊的关键性，利用那些已被修补但尚未广泛部署的 1-day 漏洞十分重要。与此同时，基于补丁的自动漏洞利用生成（APEG）是应对这一问题的有前景的技术，它能帮助开发者理解根因、在下游分叉中验证修复，并检测不完整的补丁。然而，由于三项独特挑战，现有的漏洞利用生成工具在以太坊漏洞上效果不佳：（1）在补丁中隐藏的复杂跨语言利用路径中导航；（2）合成复杂且有状态的环境配置；（3）处理区块链节点之间导致误报的非确定性不一致。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 ChainDelta，一个由大语言模型驱动的新型模糊测试智能体框架，可基于以太坊安全补丁自动生成漏洞利用。ChainDelta 包含三个核心模块：一个定向模糊器，利用调用图分析并结合补丁信息将测试引导至易受攻击的代码；一个基于智能体的环境模糊器，充当专家角色自动搭建触发漏洞所需的区块链状态；以及一个状态感知的 sanitizer，在监控区块链瞬时状态的同时执行差分分析，以区分真实的不一致与良性的非确定性。我们在一个涵盖真实漏洞补丁的多样化基准上评估 ChainDelta，覆盖数据竞争与拒绝服务等多种类型。ChainDelta 成功生成漏洞利用的成功率为 70%，误报率仅为 12.5%。消融实验确认了各模块对整体性能的贡献。为展示其实际影响，我们基于 ChainDelta 开展了真实世界的审计行动，发现了四个此前未披露的漏洞并获得了漏洞赏金。","tl":"首个以太坊补丁驱动的 LLM 模糊智能体，70% 成功生成 1-day 利用。","au":["Mingxi Ye","Yuhong Nan","Zhijie Zhong","Jianzhong Su","Xingwei Lin","Peilin Zheng","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automatic patch-based exploit generation","Ethereum","directed fuzzing","LLM agent","1-day vulnerability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/98/x"},{"id":"p00907","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Suspicious Signals to Crashes: Guiding Bug-driven GUI Testing via Code-inspired Tracing","tz":"从可疑信号到崩溃：以代码启发的追踪引导缺陷驱动的 GUI 测试","a":"Mobile applications frequently suffer from crash bugs that are triggered under specific GUI interaction sequences. Existing automated GUI testing techniques mainly emphasize increasing coverage through diverse exploration strategies, but they often fail to reach the precise interaction contexts that lead to crashes, resulting in low bug detection efficiency. This paper proposes TraceDroid, a novel automated GUI testing approach that leverages suspicious code-level signals to guide dynamic exploration. Instead of treating static analysis as an independent detection method, TraceDroid uses heuristic rules distilled from real crash reports to detect suspicious code segments, associate them with GUI widgets, and collect code-level interaction signals. It then constructs the Activity Transition Graph (ATG), performs rough path generation, and employs LLM-based executable path completion to produce a set of suspicious paths. Finally, TraceDroid executes these paths through global path planning, local path generation, and execution-aware monitoring to efficiently expose crashes. We evaluate TraceDroid on 70 real crash bugs across 42 open-source apps, comparing it with 15 state-of-the-art baselines. TraceDroid achieves the best performance, with a recall of 77%, exceeding the best baseline by 28%, while maintaining comparable or higher coverage. Furthermore, TraceDroid successfully detects 21 previously unknown crash bugs in 116 popular Google Play apps, of which 15 have been fixed and 6 confirmed by developers, demonstrating its effectiveness in real-world scenarios.","az":"移动应用经常遭遇在特定 GUI 交互序列下触发的崩溃缺陷。现有自动化 GUI 测试技术主要强调通过多样化的探索策略提升覆盖率，但它们往往无法到达导致崩溃的精确交互上下文，从而缺陷检测效率低下。本文提出 TraceDroid，一种新型自动化 GUI 测试方法，利用代码层面的可疑信号来引导动态探索。TraceDroid 并未将静态分析视为独立的检测手段，而是使用从真实崩溃报告中提炼的启发式规则来检测可疑代码段、将其与 GUI 控件关联，并收集代码层面的交互信号。随后它构建活动迁移图（ATG），进行粗略路径生成，并采用基于 LLM 的可执行路径补全来产生一组可疑路径。最后，TraceDroid 通过全局路径规划、局部路径生成与执行感知监控来执行这些路径，从而高效暴露崩溃。我们在 42 个开源应用的 70 个真实崩溃缺陷上评估 TraceDroid，并与 15 个最先进的基线方法比较。TraceDroid 取得了最佳性能，召回率达 77%，比最佳基线高出 28%，同时保持相当或更高的覆盖率。此外，TraceDroid 在 116 个热门 Google Play 应用中成功检测出 21 个此前未知的崩溃缺陷，其中 15 个已被修复、6 个已被开发者确认，展示了其在真实场景中的有效性。","tl":"用代码级可疑信号加 LLM 路径补全引导 GUI 探索直达崩溃。","au":["Mengzhuo Chen","Zhe Liu","Chunyang Chen","Junjie Wang","Boyu Wu","Yuekai Huang","Jun Hu","Qing Wang"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GUI testing","crash bug detection","activity transition graph","LLM path completion","Android"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/99/x"},{"id":"p00908","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Characterizing Trust Boundary Vulnerabilities in TEE Container Systems: An Empirical Study","tz":"刻画 TEE 容器系统中的信任边界漏洞：一项实证研究","a":"Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) have become a cornerstone of confidential computing, attracting significant attention from academia and industry. To support secure and scalable application deployment on confidential clouds, TEE containers (Tcons) have been introduced as middleware to shield applications from malicious operating systems and orchestration layers while preserving usability. In this paper, we present the first comprehensive analysis of Tcons, focusing on three critical layers: OS interfaces, encrypted I/O, and orchestration mechanisms. To enable systematic evaluation, we design TBouncer, an automated analyzer that precisely exercises and benchmarks Tcon isolation boundaries. Our study uncovers fundamental flaws in existing Tcons, leading to exploitable vulnerabilities such as code execution, denial-of-service, and information leakage. In total, we identify six attack vectors, twelve new bugs, and three CVEs. These findings provide new insights into the underestimated attack surface of Tcons and highlight key directions for building more secure and trustworthy container solutions.","az":"可信执行环境（TEE）已成为机密计算的基石，吸引了学术界与工业界的大量关注。为支持在机密云上安全且可扩展地部署应用，TEE 容器（Tcon）作为中间件被引入，用以屏蔽恶意操作系统与编排层对应用的影响，同时保持可用性。本文首次对 Tcon 开展全面分析，聚焦三个关键层次：操作系统接口、加密 I/O 与编排机制。为实现系统化评估，我们设计了 TBouncer，一个可精确触发并基准测试 Tcon 隔离边界的自动化分析器。我们的研究揭示了现有 Tcon 中的根本性缺陷，导致代码执行、拒绝服务与信息泄露等可被利用的漏洞。总计，我们识别出六种攻击向量、十二个新缺陷与三个 CVE。这些发现为 Tcon 被低估的攻击面提供了新的洞见，并为构建更安全可信的容器方案指明了关键方向。","tl":"首个 TEE 容器信任边界系统分析，自动化触发出 12 个新缺陷与 3 个 CVE。","au":["Weijie Liu","Hongbo Chen","Shuo Huai","Zhen Xu","Wenhao Wang","XiaoFeng Wang","Danfeng Zhang","Zhi Li","Haixu Tang","Zheli Liu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["trusted execution environment","TEE container","trust boundary","confidential computing","attack surface"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/100/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.20962"},{"id":"p00909","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Flash: Query-Efficient Black-Box Static Malware Evasion through Transferable GAN-Guided Modification Sequences","tz":"Flash：通过可迁移的 GAN 引导修改序列实现查询高效的黑盒静态恶意软件规避","a":"Machine learning (ML)–based static malware detectors are widely deployed for Portable Executable (PE) files due to their scalability and efficiency, yet they remain vulnerable to carefully crafted adversarial perturbations. Existing black-box evasion methods either rely on transfer attacks, which break down when surrogate and target decision boundaries diverge, or on query-driven searches, which require impractically many queries. We present Flash, a two-phase adversarial framework tailored for static PE malware detection that integrates the strengths of both approaches. In the first phase, a generative adversarial network is trained against heterogeneous surrogate detectors to generate function-preserving PE modifications with inherent evasiveness. In the second phase, an evolutionary optimizer refines these sequences directly against the target model with a dual-objective fitness that balances evasion success and minimal perturbation cost. Experiments on 12,039 VirusShare PE files and six state-of-the-art static detectors demonstrate that Flash reduces query counts by 86% while maintaining bypass rates above 95.8%. Furthermore, adversarial training with Flash-generated samples reduces attack success rates by 82.4%, highlighting Flash’s utility for both exposing vulnerabilities and strengthening the robustness of static PE malware detectors.","az":"基于机器学习（ML）的静态恶意软件检测器因其可扩展性与效率被广泛部署于可移植可执行（PE）文件，但它们仍易受精心构造的对抗扰动影响。现有黑盒规避方法要么依赖迁移攻击——当替代模型与目标模型的决策边界发生分歧时便会失效，要么依赖查询驱动的搜索——需要不切实际的大量查询。我们提出 Flash，一个为静态 PE 恶意软件检测量身定制的两阶段对抗框架，融合了两类方法的优势。第一阶段，针对异构的替代检测器训练一个生成对抗网络，以生成保持功能的 PE 修改，使其本身即具备规避性。第二阶段，一个进化优化器直接针对目标模型精炼这些修改序列，采用兼顾规避成功率与最小扰动代价的双目标适应度函数。在 12,039 个 VirusShare PE 文件与六个最先进静态检测器上的实验表明，Flash 将查询次数减少 86%，同时保持 95.8% 以上的绕过率。此外，使用 Flash 生成的样本进行对抗训练可将攻击成功率降低 82.4%，凸显了 Flash 在暴露漏洞与增强静态 PE 恶意软件检测器鲁棒性两方面的实用价值。","tl":"GAN 生成可迁移修改序列加进化精炼，查询量降 86% 仍高绕过率。","au":["Anyuan Sang","Li Yang","Lu Zhou","Junbo Jia","Huipeng Yang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["static malware detection","black-box evasion","GAN","adversarial PE modification","query efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/101/x"},{"id":"p00910","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Odyssey : Hunting Smart Contract Vulnerabilities with Fine-grained State Modeling and Exploration","tz":"Odyssey：以细粒度状态建模与探索挖掘智能合约漏洞","a":"With the rapid development of blockchain, decentralized applications (DApps) have attracted massive funds due to their convenient interactive services. Recently, the increasing market value of DApps has also attracted many malicious actors to exploit smart contract vulnerabilities for launching attacks. Moreover, as smart contracts utilize more state variables to support complex functionalities, some vulnerabilities require specific states to trigger (marked as vulnerable state), and bring new challenges to the vulnerability detection task. Although many smart contract fuzzers have been proposed for vulnerability detection, they still face limitations due to their inability to efficiently explore smart contract state spaces. To address this challenge, we propose a novel fuzzer, Odyssey, with fine-grained state modeling and exploration, which efficiently explores smart contract state and increases the probability of reaching vulnerable state. We improve the efficacy of the fuzzer with two key mechanisms: (1) we model an essential state space consisting of the variables related to sensitive operations for compressing the exploration scope; (2) we design a state-aware exploration strategy to identify test seeds that cover new state scope or cause interesting state transitions, thereby improving the efficiency of exploration. To evaluate the performance in vulnerability detection, we adopt Odyssey to a labeled benchmark consisting of 130 vulnerable contracts. Odyssey detects at least 70% more vulnerabilities than other fuzzers. Moreover, we evaluate Odyssey on a dataset that consists of 143 DApps (involving 437 contracts) from real-world security incidents. The experimental results demonstrate that state-aware feedback enhances the ability of Odyssey in state exploration by achieving 19% higher state coverage. Meanwhile, Odyssey successfully finds 15 exploits of vulnerabilities in real-world attacks, showing its advantage in detecting real-world vulnerabilities.","az":"随着区块链的迅速发展，去中心化应用（DApp）凭借便捷的交互服务吸引了海量资金。近来，DApp 不断上升的市场价值也吸引了众多恶意行为者利用智能合约漏洞发起攻击。此外，随着智能合约使用更多状态变量来支持复杂功能，一些漏洞需要特定状态才能触发（标记为易受攻击状态），这给漏洞检测任务带来了新挑战。尽管已有许多智能合约模糊器被提出用于漏洞检测，但由于无法高效探索智能合约的状态空间，它们仍存在局限。为应对这一挑战，我们提出新型模糊器 Odyssey，具备细粒度的状态建模与探索能力，可高效探索智能合约状态并提高到达易受攻击状态的概率。我们通过两项关键机制提升模糊器的效能：（1）我们对由与敏感操作相关的变量构成的核心状态空间建模，以压缩探索范围；（2）我们设计了一种状态感知的探索策略，识别能覆盖新状态范围或引发有价值状态迁移的测试种子，从而提升探索效率。为评估漏洞检测性能，我们将 Odyssey 应用于一个包含 130 个易受攻击合约的带标注基准。Odyssey 检测出的漏洞比其他模糊器至少多 70%。此外，我们在一个由真实安全事件中的 143 个 DApp（涉及 437 个合约）构成的数据集上评估 Odyssey。实验结果表明，状态感知反馈使 Odyssey 的状态探索能力提升，状态覆盖率提高 19%。同时，Odyssey 成功找到真实攻击中的 15 个漏洞利用，展现了其在检测真实世界漏洞上的优势。","tl":"以敏感操作相关变量压缩状态空间，状态感知反馈提升合约漏洞检出。","au":["Jianzhong Su","Mingxi Ye","Jiachi Chen","Yuhong Nan","Peilin Zheng","Tao Zhang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract fuzzing","state modeling","vulnerability detection","DApp","state coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/102/x"},{"id":"p00911","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"NESA: Relational Neuro-Symbolic Static Program Analysis","tz":"NESA：关系式神经符号静态程序分析","a":"Static program analysis plays an essential role in program optimization, bug detection, and debugging. However, reliance on compilation and limited customization hinder its adoption in the real world. This paper presents a compositional neuro-symbolic approach named NESA that facilitates compilation-free and customizable static program analysis using large language models (LLMs) with mitigated hallucinations. Specifically, we propose an analysis policy language, a restricted form of Datalog, to support users decomposing a static program analysis problem into several sub-problems that target simpler syntactic or semantic properties upon smaller code snippets. The problem decomposition enables the LLMs to target more manageable semantic-related sub-problems with reduced hallucinations, while the syntactic ones are resolved by parsing-based analysis without hallucinations. An analysis policy then is evaluated with lazy and incremental prompting, which significantly mitigates the hallucinations and improves the performance. We evaluate NESA for program slicing and bug detection upon benchmark and real-world programs. Evaluation results show that while NESA supports compilation-free and customizable analysis, it can still achieve comparable and even better performance than existing techniques. In a customized taint vulnerability detection upon TaintBench, for example, NESA achieves a precision of 66.27%, a recall of 78.57%, and an F1 score of 0.72, surpassing an industrial approach by 0.20 in F1 score. NESA also detects 13 real-world memory leak bugs, which have been fixed by developers.","az":"静态程序分析在程序优化、缺陷检测与调试中发挥着关键作用。然而，对编译的依赖以及有限的可定制性阻碍了它在现实世界中的采用。本文提出一种组合式神经符号方法 NESA，利用大语言模型（LLM）实现免编译且可定制的静态程序分析，并缓解幻觉问题。具体而言，我们提出一种分析策略语言——Datalog 的受限形式——支持用户将一个静态程序分析问题分解为若干子问题，这些子问题针对更小代码片段上更简单的语法或语义属性。问题分解使 LLM 能够处理更可控的语义相关子问题并减少幻觉，而语法相关的子问题则由基于解析的分析无幻觉地解决。随后，分析策略以惰性与增量式提示进行求值，这显著缓解了幻觉并提升了性能。我们在基准程序与真实程序上评估 NESA 的程序切片与缺陷检测能力。评估结果表明，NESA 在支持免编译、可定制分析的同时，仍能取得与现有技术相当甚至更好的性能。例如，在 TaintBench 上的定制化污点漏洞检测中，NESA 取得了 66.27% 的精确率、78.57% 的召回率与 0.72 的 F1 分数，F1 上比一个工业方法高出 0.20。NESA 还检测出 13 个真实世界的内存泄漏缺陷，均已被开发者修复。","tl":"用受限 Datalog 分解分析任务，惰性增量提示使 LLM 静态分析免编译少幻觉。","au":["Chengpeng Wang","Yifei Gao","Wuqi Zhang","Xuwei Liu","Jinyao Guo","Mingwei Zheng","Qingkai Shi","Xiangyu Zhang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["neuro-symbolic analysis","static program analysis","Datalog policy language","program slicing","hallucination mitigation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/103/x"},{"id":"p00912","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"JavaScript Pointer Analysis with Adaptive Heap Abstraction","tz":"采用自适应堆抽象的 JavaScript 指针分析","a":"The conventional approach to represent objects in static program analysis is to use allocation-site abstraction. This design choice may lead to redundant computations when many abstract objects are similar. Existing mechanisms that aim to merge such objects are not effective for JavaScript. We propose a novel adaptive heap abstraction technique that during analysis discovers and merges similar abstract objects, thereby reducing the analysis complexity while preserving most of the precision. The technique has been implemented in a state-of-the-art program analyzer for JavaScript. On a collection of 96 challenging programs, it yields a 2X speedup on average (up to 17X) with a negligible loss of precision. The experimental results also show the effects of various analysis configurations.","az":"在静态程序分析中表示对象的传统做法是使用分配点（allocation-site）抽象。当许多抽象对象彼此相似时，这一设计选择可能导致冗余计算。现有旨在合并此类对象的机制对 JavaScript 并不有效。我们提出一种新颖的自适应堆抽象技术，在分析过程中发现并合并相似的抽象对象，从而降低分析复杂度并保留大部分精度。该技术已在一个最先进的 JavaScript 程序分析器中实现。在 96 个具有挑战性的程序集合上，它平均带来 2 倍加速（最高 17 倍），且精度损失可忽略。实验结果还展示了各种分析配置的影响。","tl":"分析中动态发现并合并相似抽象对象，JS 指针分析平均提速 2 倍。","au":["Wenyuan Xu","Anders Møller"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["pointer analysis","heap abstraction","JavaScript","allocation-site abstraction","analysis scalability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/104/x","pu":"https://cs.au.dk/~amoeller/papers/aha/paper.pdf"},{"id":"p00913","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ACME: Automated Clause Mapping Engine for Testing Emerging Database Systems","tz":"ACME：用于测试新兴数据库系统的自动子句映射引擎","a":"A growing number of emerging database management systems, such as time-series and streaming databases, have been developed to support specialized workloads with enhanced performance and functionality. However, these systems are often less mature than traditional relational databases, making them more prone to logic bugs and internal errors that affect correctness and reliability. To address this, we propose an enhanced differential testing framework designed for emerging SQL-like databases. Our key insight is that many of these systems are conceptually extensions of relational databases, allowing us to uncover bugs by comparing query results with those from more robust relational systems. To bridge the differences in syntax and semantics between emerging and relational databases, we leverage Large Language Models (LLMs) to automate the discovery of supported clauses and generate clause mappings that translate system-specific features into equivalent expressions in SQL. Our approach proceeds in three steps: (i) collecting and analyzing the syntax of clauses supported by both the emerging database system and a relational reference system, (ii) constructing clause mappings via LLMs, validating them through testing queries, and formalizing them into Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) transformations or mapping functions, and (iii) generating semantically equivalent but syntactically varied queries to expand the scope of differential testing. To ensure the reliability of LLM-generated clause mappings, we introduce a testing query mechanism that re-prompts incorrect mappings after runtime verification. We implemented this approach in a tool called ACME and applied it to four widely used emerging database systems, uncovering 57 previously unknown bugs, including 17 logic bugs and 40 internal errors. Of these, 50 have been fixed and 5 confirmed by vendors. Our results demonstrate the practicality and effectiveness of ACME in improving the reliability of emerging database systems through scalable, LLM-assisted differential testing.","az":"越来越多的新兴数据库管理系统（如时序数据库与流式数据库）被开发出来，以支持具有更好性能与功能的专用负载。然而，这些系统往往不如传统关系数据库成熟，因而更易出现影响正确性与可靠性的逻辑缺陷与内部错误。为此，我们提出一个为新兴的类 SQL 数据库设计的增强差分测试框架。我们的核心洞见是，许多此类系统在概念上是关系数据库的扩展，因而可以通过将查询结果与更稳健的关系系统的结果进行比较来发现缺陷。为弥合新兴数据库与关系数据库在语法与语义上的差异，我们利用大语言模型（LLM）自动发现所支持的子句，并生成将系统特定特性翻译为等价 SQL 表达的子句映射。我们的方法分三步进行：（i）收集并分析新兴数据库系统与关系参照系统共同支持的子句语法；（ii）通过 LLM 构建子句映射，借助测试查询验证它们，并将其形式化为抽象语法树（AST）变换或映射函数；（iii）生成语义等价但语法多样的查询，以扩大差分测试的范围。为确保 LLM 生成的子句映射的可靠性，我们引入一种测试查询机制，在运行时验证后对错误映射重新提示。我们在名为 ACME 的工具中实现了该方法，并将其应用于四个广泛使用的新兴数据库系统，发现了 57 个此前未知的缺陷，包括 17 个逻辑缺陷与 40 个内部错误。其中 50 个已被修复、5 个已被厂商确认。我们的结果表明，ACME 通过可扩展的、LLM 辅助的差分测试，切实有效地提升了新兴数据库系统的可靠性。","tl":"用 LLM 自动构建子句映射，把新兴数据库查询映射到 SQL 做差分测试。","au":["Yuancheng Jiang","Jianing Wang","Chuqi Zhang","Roland H. C. Yap","Zhenkai Liang","Manuel Rigger"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["differential testing","emerging database systems","clause mapping","logic bugs","LLM-assisted testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/105/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797134"},{"id":"p00914","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PROGnosticator: Testing Source-to-Source Code Translators via Construct-oriented Fuzzing","tz":"PROGnosticator：以面向语言构造的模糊测试检验源到源代码转换器","a":"To ease software interoperability and migration, developers are increasingly embracing transpilers: automated tools for converting source code from one language to another. Unfortunately, differences in language constructs, syntax, and semantics leave transpilers facing many translation bugs, emitting incorrect or nonfunctional translations. Thorough, proactive transpiler testing is thus critical to the reliability of emergent translation-oriented development. While fuzzers excel in testing adjacent classes of language processors (e.g., compilers), current fuzzers remain tied to only the specific code patterns expressed in their inputs— hardcoded grammars or seed programs—which are costly to curate and extend, constraining their testing to just narrow subsets of language constructs. Worse yet, their generated programs are often overly complex, requiring non-trivial reduction to pinpoint the exact code patterns behind transpiler errors. Evaluating current and future transpilers thus demands a rigorous, input-independent fuzzing strategy—systematically exercising languages’ broad range of code constructs without needing costly per-language expertise or re-engineering. To bridge this gap, we present Construct-oriented Fuzzing: a language-agnostic yet construct-aware approach for systematically testing transpilers. Motivated by our insights from past transpiler bugs, revealing most translation errors embody construct-specific mishandling, our approach explicitly targets the vast space of code patterns derived from core language constructs. Harnessing large language models’ code understanding and synthesis, we (1) automatically enumerate a language’s core constructs, before (2) generating self-contained programs exercising them individually—and combinations thereof—precisely testing transpilers’ many edgecases whilst eschewing cumbersome grammars or seeds. In evaluating our prototype, PROGnosticator, against four state-of-the-art compiler and transpiler fuzzers across seven transpilers for C, Go, and JavaScript, we show how our approach attains high per-language validity as well as construct-usage diversity—exposing 77 total transpiler bugs, of which 64 are previously unknown, with 63 since confirmed or fixed by developers.","az":"为便于软件互操作与迁移，开发者越来越多地采用 transpiler：将源代码从一种语言自动转换为另一种语言的工具。遗憾的是，语言构造、语法与语义上的差异使 transpiler 面临诸多翻译缺陷，产生不正确或不可运行的译码。因此，彻底而主动的 transpiler 测试对以翻译为导向的新兴开发方式的可靠性至关重要。尽管模糊器在测试相邻类别的语言处理器（如编译器）方面表现出色，但当前的模糊器仍被绑定在其输入所表达的特定代码模式上——硬编码的文法或种子程序——这些代价高昂且难以扩展，将测试局限在语言构造的狭窄子集。更糟的是，它们生成的程序往往过于复杂，需要非平凡的约简才能定位导致 transpiler 错误的确切代码模式。因此，评估当前与未来的 transpiler 需要一种严格的、与输入无关的模糊测试策略——系统地覆盖语言广泛的代码构造，而无需昂贵的逐语言专业知识或重新工程。为弥合这一差距，我们提出面向构造的模糊测试：一种语言无关但构造感知的系统性 transpiler 测试方法。受我们对过往 transpiler 缺陷的洞见启发——多数翻译错误体现为特定构造的错误处理——我们的方法显式地针对由核心语言构造派生出的庞大代码模式空间。借助大语言模型的代码理解与合成能力，我们（1）自动枚举一门语言的核心构造，然后（2）生成分别以及组合地使用这些构造的自包含程序，精准地测试 transpiler 的诸多边界情形，同时避免繁琐的文法或种子。在原型 PROGnosticator 的评估中，我们针对 C、Go 与 JavaScript 的七个 transpiler，与四个最先进的编译器与 transpiler 模糊器进行比较，结果表明我们的方法在各语言上取得了高有效性与构造使用多样性——共暴露 77 个 transpiler 缺陷，其中 64 个此前未知，63 个已被开发者确认或修复。","tl":"枚举语言核心构造生成自包含程序，语言无关地测出 64 个转换器新缺陷。","au":["Yeaseen Arafat","Stefan Nagy"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["transpiler testing","construct-oriented fuzzing","source-to-source translation","LLM program synthesis","language-agnostic"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/106/x","pu":"https://futures.cs.utah.edu/papers/26FSE-a.pdf"},{"id":"p00915","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LLM-Assisted Input-Requirement-Aware Differential Testing of Array Programming Frameworks","tz":"LLM 辅助的输入需求感知的数组编程框架差分测试","a":"Array programming (AP) frameworks (e.g., NumPy and Octave) are widely adopted in scientific computing. Critical defects can jeopardize the entire ecosystem. The stability of API designs enables differential testing on various implementations (e.g., two versions). However, two primary obstacles remain. First, current test generation cannot effectively generate valid inputs, as the APIs (e.g., matrix multiplication) have type constraints and semantic requirements. Second, unit testing approaches test APIs independently, but they share a core N-dimensional array structure (ndarray) as inputs. Modifying one API may alter the ndarray’s properties, breaking the correctness of others. We propose a differential testing tool for array programming, called ArrayDiff. We first collect semantic requirements from NumPy’s APIs and leverage LLMs to transfer NumPy’s requirements to other frameworks. Then, we propose an input-requirement-aware API call generator (IRA-ACG). Based on IRA-ACG, ArrayDiff employs search algorithms to evolve tests while ensuring valid inputs. ArrayDiff can generate valid and complex API call sequences to detect potential differences. We evaluate ArrayDiff and its ablation versions on five AP pairs. They detect 47 valid-input differences and 39 invalid ones, with 23 confirmed as bugs or document issues. IRA-ACG boosts the detection of valid-input differences, which constitute most confirmed bugs. Comparing ArrayDiff with TitanFuzz (LLM-based fuzzer) and Ghostwriter (unit tester) confirms the benefits of IRA-ACG and sequence-level testing.","az":"数组编程（AP）框架（如 NumPy 与 Octave）在科学计算中被广泛采用，其中的关键缺陷可能危及整个生态系统。API 设计的稳定性使得可以对不同实现（例如两个版本）进行差分测试。然而仍存在两大障碍。第一，现有测试生成无法有效生成有效输入，因为这些 API（如矩阵乘法）具有类型约束与语义要求。第二，单元测试方法独立地测试各 API，但它们共享作为输入的核心 N 维数组结构（ndarray）；修改一个 API 可能改变 ndarray 的属性，从而破坏其他 API 的正确性。我们提出一个面向数组编程的差分测试工具 ArrayDiff。我们首先收集 NumPy API 的语义要求，并利用 LLM 将 NumPy 的要求迁移到其他框架。随后，我们提出一个输入需求感知的 API 调用生成器（IRA-ACG）。基于 IRA-ACG，ArrayDiff 采用搜索算法演化测试，同时确保输入有效。ArrayDiff 能够生成有效且复杂的 API 调用序列以检测潜在差异。我们在五对 AP 框架上评估 ArrayDiff 及其消融版本，共检出 47 个有效输入差异与 39 个无效输入差异，其中 23 个被确认为缺陷或文档问题。IRA-ACG 显著提升了有效输入差异的检出，而这类差异构成了大多数被确认的缺陷。将 ArrayDiff 与 TitanFuzz（基于 LLM 的模糊器）以及 Ghostwriter（单元测试器）比较，进一步证实了 IRA-ACG 与序列级测试的收益。","tl":"用 LLM 迁移 API 语义要求生成有效 ndarray 调用序列做差分测试。","au":["Zhichao Zhou","Jingzhu He"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["array programming frameworks","differential testing","NumPy","input requirements","API call sequence generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/107/x","pu":"https://jhe16.github.io/files/FSE26.pdf"},{"id":"p00916","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"InDe-LLM: Defending Against Jailbreak Attacks in LLM-Powered Systems via Intention Disentangling","tz":"InDe-LLM：通过意图解耦防御 LLM 驱动系统中的越狱攻击","a":"Jailbreak attacks have been regarded as a crucial threat to LLM-powered software systems. Recent studies indicate the existence of a steering vector within models’ internal activations, which can adjust a model’s propensity to reject user requests, and thus is regarded as an effective approach for training-free defense. However, attackers may wrap their malicious intentions within a seemingly benign context, which shifts the distribution of harmful prompts toward benign inputs along the steering vector, effectively bypassing existing defense approaches. In this work, we propose a defense framework InDe-LLM based on intention disentangling. By projecting the embedding of inputs into a benign-invariant subspace, we could disentangle the harmful intentions of jailbreak prompts without affecting benign inputs. Next, such disentangled harmful intentions can be easily identified based on LLMs’ well-aligned concept of harmfulness, and rejected through activation steering. Our experiments show that InDe-LLM achieves high defense effectiveness, outperforming baselines by 27.2%–43.5% across three models and ten attacks while preserving high utility on benign inputs. Moreover, our evaluation demonstrates that it exhibits high transferability to unseen attacks.","az":"越狱攻击已被视为对 LLM 驱动软件系统的关键威胁。近期研究表明，模型内部激活中存在一个引导向量（steering vector），可以调节模型拒绝用户请求的倾向，因而被视为一种有效的免训练防御手段。然而，攻击者可能将恶意意图包裹在看似良性的上下文中，使有害提示的分布沿引导向量方向偏向良性输入，从而有效绕过现有防御方法。在本工作中，我们提出基于意图解耦的防御框架 InDe-LLM。通过将输入的嵌入投影到一个良性不变子空间，我们能够在不影响良性输入的前提下解耦出越狱提示中的有害意图。接着，这些被解耦出的有害意图可以基于 LLM 已良好对齐的有害性概念被轻松识别，并通过激活引导予以拒绝。我们的实验表明，InDe-LLM 取得了很高的防御效果，在三个模型与十种攻击上比基线高出 27.2%–43.5%，同时在良性输入上保持较高效用。此外，我们的评估表明它对未见攻击具有很高的可迁移性。","tl":"把输入投影到良性不变子空间解耦有害意图，再以激活引导拒答。","au":["YujueWang","Quan Zhang","Chijin Zhou","Gwihwan Go","Dalong Shi","Yu Jiang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","tg":["security","llm-based"],"kw":["jailbreak defense","activation steering","intention disentangling","LLM-powered systems","benign-invariant subspace"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/108/x"},{"id":"p00917","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"VisionScratch: LLM-Based Automated Feedback Generation Using Code-Produced Videos for Scratch Programs","tz":"VisionScratch：基于代码运行视频的 Scratch 程序 LLM 自动反馈生成","a":"Block-based programming environments such as Scratch are increasingly popular in programming education, in particular for young learners. While the use of blocks helps prevent syntax errors, semantic bugs remain common and difficult to debug. Existing tools for Scratch debugging rely heavily on predefined rules or user manual inputs, and crucially, they ignore the platform’s inherently visual nature. We introduce VisionScratch, the first multimodal feedback generation system for Scratch that leverages both the project’s block code and its generated gameplay video to diagnose and repair bugs. VisionScratch uses a two-stage pipeline: a vision-language model first aligns visual symptoms with code structure to identify a single critical issue, then proposes minimal, abstract syntax tree level repairs that are verified via execution in the Scratch virtual machine. We evaluate VisionScratch on a set of real-world Scratch projects against state-of-the-art LLM-based tools and human testers. Results show that gameplay video is a crucial debugging signal: VisionScratch substantially outperforms prior tools in both bug identification and repair quality, even without access to project descriptions or goals. This work demonstrates that video can serve as a first-class specification in visual programming environments, opening new directions for LLM-based debugging beyond symbolic code alone.","az":"以 Scratch 为代表的块状编程环境在编程教育中日益流行，尤其面向低龄学习者。虽然使用积木块有助于避免语法错误，但语义缺陷仍然常见且难以调试。现有的 Scratch 调试工具严重依赖预定义规则或用户手工输入，更关键的是，它们忽略了该平台固有的视觉特性。我们提出 VisionScratch，首个面向 Scratch 的多模态反馈生成系统，同时利用项目的积木代码及其生成的游戏运行视频来诊断与修复缺陷。VisionScratch 采用两阶段流水线：视觉语言模型首先将视觉症状与代码结构对齐以识别单个关键问题，随后提出最小化的、抽象语法树层面的修复，并通过在 Scratch 虚拟机中执行来验证。我们在一组真实的 Scratch 项目上，将 VisionScratch 与最先进的基于 LLM 的工具以及人类测试者进行比较。结果表明，游戏运行视频是关键的调试信号：即便没有项目描述或目标，VisionScratch 在缺陷识别与修复质量上都大幅优于既有工具。这项工作表明，视频可以在可视化编程环境中充当一等的规约，为超越纯符号代码的 LLM 调试开辟了新方向。","tl":"首次把游戏运行视频当作规约，驱动 Scratch 程序的诊断与 AST 级修复。","au":["Yuan Si","Daming Li","Hanyuan Shi","Jialu Zhang"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Scratch","multimodal feedback","vision-language model","automated repair","programming education"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/109/x"},{"id":"p00918","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Agentic Verification of Software Systems","tz":"软件系统的智能体式验证","a":"Automatically generated code is gaining traction recently owing to prevalence of Large Language Models (LLMs). Further, the AlphaProof initiative has demonstrated the possibility of using AI for general mathematical reasoning. Reasoning about computer programs (software) can be accomplished via such general mathematical reasoning, however, it tends to be more structured. The structure of the program can be used to structure the proof as well as its intermediate lemmas. In this work, we present a first LLM agent for conducting program verification. Unlike past works which rely on extensive training of LLMs on proof examples, our agent learns on-the-fly and improves the proof via an iterative refinement loop. The iterative improvement of the proof is achieved by the proof agent communicating with Rocq (formerly Coq) theorem prover to get additional context. The final result of the iteration is a proof derivation checked by the Rocq theorem prover. In this way, our proof construction involves autonomous collaboration between the proof agent and the theorem prover. This autonomy facilitates the search for proofs and decision-making in deciding on the structure of the proof tree. Experimental evaluation on SV-COMP benchmarks, as well as on Linux kernel modules, shows promising efficacy in achieving agentic program verification. As automation in code generation becomes more widespread, we posit that our proof agent can be potentially integrated with AI coding agents to achieve a generate-and-validate loop, thereby moving closer to the vision of trusted automatic programming.","az":"由于大语言模型（LLM）的普及，自动生成的代码近来备受关注。此外，AlphaProof 计划已展示了使用 AI 进行一般数学推理的可能性。关于计算机程序（软件）的推理可以借助这种一般数学推理来完成，但它往往更具结构性：程序的结构既可用于组织证明，也可用于组织其中间引理。在本工作中，我们提出首个用于开展程序验证的 LLM 智能体。与以往依赖在证明示例上大量训练 LLM 的工作不同，我们的智能体在线即时学习，并通过迭代精化循环改进证明。证明的迭代改进是通过证明智能体与 Rocq（原 Coq）定理证明器通信以获取额外上下文来实现的。迭代的最终结果是一个由 Rocq 定理证明器检查通过的证明推导。如此一来，我们的证明构造涉及证明智能体与定理证明器之间的自主协作。这种自主性有助于搜索证明以及在决定证明树结构时做出决策。在 SV-COMP 基准以及 Linux 内核模块上的实验评估显示，智能体式程序验证具有可观的效果。随着代码生成的自动化日益普及，我们认为我们的证明智能体有望与 AI 编程智能体集成，形成生成—验证循环，从而更接近可信自动编程的愿景。","tl":"首个与 Rocq 交互迭代精化的程序验证 LLM 智能体，无需证明数据训练。","au":["Haoxin Tu","Huan Zhao","Yahui Song","Mehtab Zafar","Ruijie Meng","Abhik Roychoudhury"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["program verification","LLM agent","Rocq/Coq theorem prover","iterative refinement","SV-COMP"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/110/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.17330"},{"id":"p00919","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"The Interaction of Complexity and Provenance in Code Review Decisions: Evidence from a Controlled Experiment","tz":"代码复杂度与来源标注在代码评审决策中的交互作用：一项受控实验的证据","a":"Modern code review platforms increasingly embed suggested code revisions, including those generated by AI. While such features promise efficiency, they may also change how developers evaluate changes, particularly when code is complex or when suggestions are labeled by source. Prior studies have examined trust and automation bias in software engineering, but it remains unclear how code complexity and perceived authorship (human vs. AI) jointly shape developers’ review decisions. We present the results of a between-subjects experiment with 385 participants, who were asked to review a code revision. The study controlled for code complexity (low vs. high), provenance labels (human vs. AI), and revision correctness. We analyzed developers’ review decisions through compliance patterns: acceptance of correct or rejection of incorrect code revisions (appropriate-compliance), acceptance of incorrect code revisions (over-compliance), and rejection of correct code revisions (under-compliance). Our findings show that higher code complexity significantly (p<.05) increases over-compliance. While provenance alone had no main effect, its influence emerged in interaction: under high-complexity conditions, reviewers were substantially more likely to accept incorrect revisions labeled as AI-authored. This work contributes: (i) empirical evidence that higher code complexity increases the likelihood of accepting incorrect suggestions, (ii) analysis of provenance showing no main effect on overall acceptance but a trend toward higher over-compliance under AI labels, and (iii) evidence of a significant interaction where complex, AI-labeled revisions led to more frequent acceptance of incorrect suggestions—an effect absent under human labels. Together, these results highlight the need for review systems that surface complexity cues and promote more accurate evaluation of AI-labeled suggestions.","az":"现代代码评审平台越来越多地嵌入建议的代码修订，包括由 AI 生成的修订。尽管这类功能承诺带来效率，但它们也可能改变开发者评估变更的方式，尤其是在代码复杂或建议被标注了来源时。已有研究考察过软件工程中的信任与自动化偏差，但代码复杂度与感知到的作者身份（人类 vs. AI）如何共同塑造开发者的评审决策仍不清楚。我们展示了一项被试间实验的结果，385 名参与者被要求评审一项代码修订。该研究控制了代码复杂度（低 vs. 高）、来源标签（人类 vs. AI）与修订正确性。我们通过依从模式分析开发者的评审决策：接受正确修订或拒绝错误修订（恰当依从）、接受错误修订（过度依从）、拒绝正确修订（依从不足）。我们的发现表明，更高的代码复杂度显著（p<.05）增加了过度依从。虽然来源标注单独并无主效应，但其影响在交互中显现：在高复杂度条件下，评审者明显更可能接受被标注为 AI 撰写的错误修订。本工作贡献了：（i）更高代码复杂度会提升接受错误建议可能性的实证证据；（ii）对来源标注的分析，显示其对总体接受率无主效应但在 AI 标签下有过度依从上升的趋势；（iii）存在显著交互作用的证据——复杂且标注为 AI 的修订导致更频繁地接受错误建议，而在人类标签下不存在该效应。总体而言，这些结果凸显了评审系统需要呈现复杂度线索，并促进对 AI 标注建议更准确的评估。","tl":"385 人实验发现高复杂度下 AI 标签会显著提高错误修订的接受率。","au":["Neha Singh","Francesco Sovrano","Vincent Hellendoorn","Alberto Bacchelli"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["human-study"],"kw":["code review","controlled experiment","automation bias","code complexity","AI provenance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/111/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3808165"},{"id":"p00920","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DualCodeDetect: Zero-Shot LLM-Generated Code Detection via Dual-Channel Perturbation","tz":"DualCodeDetect：通过双通道扰动实现零样本的 LLM 生成代码检测","a":"The rapid advancement of large language models (LLMs) in code generation has greatly improved software development efficiency, but it has also raised concerns about misuse, making the distinction between human-written and LLM-generated code an urgent task. However, existing detection methods for LLM-generated content, particularly perturbation-based zero-shot methods, are primarily designed for natural language scenarios and fail to transfer effectively to the task of detecting generated code. When directly applied to code, they face two major challenges: (1) the low-entropy nature of code restricts the perturbation space and weakens discriminative signals; and (2) prior perturbation methods often compromise semantic integrity or executability, leading to substantial performance degradation. To address these issues, we propose DualCodeDetect, a novel zero-shot detection framework that amplifies the differences between LLM-generated and human-written code through a dual-channel perturbation mechanism. In the semantic channel, we design an identifier perturbation strategy based on outside-nucleus sampling, which disrupts the strong consistency of LLMs in identifier selection. In the structural channel, empirical analysis reveals that LLM-generated code exhibits greater uniformity in stylistic features; leveraging this insight, we construct a rule-based library of semantics-preserving code transformations to introduce structural perturbations that further magnify statistical disparities. In experiments conducted across two datasets and six representative code LLMs, DualCodeDetect achieves an average AUROC of 0.8535 under both T=0.2 and T=1.0 temperature settings, demonstrating significant superiority over existing detection methods.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在代码生成上的快速进步极大提升了软件开发效率，但也引发了对滥用的担忧，使区分人写代码与 LLM 生成代码成为紧迫任务。然而，现有针对 LLM 生成内容的检测方法，尤其是基于扰动的零样本方法，主要是为自然语言场景设计的，难以有效迁移到生成代码的检测任务上。直接应用于代码时，它们面临两大挑战：（1）代码的低熵特性限制了扰动空间，削弱了判别信号；（2）以往的扰动方法往往破坏语义完整性或可执行性，导致性能大幅下降。为解决这些问题，我们提出 DualCodeDetect，一个新颖的零样本检测框架，通过双通道扰动机制放大 LLM 生成代码与人写代码之间的差异。在语义通道，我们设计了一种基于核外（outside-nucleus）采样的标识符扰动策略，破坏 LLM 在标识符选择上的强一致性。在结构通道，实证分析表明 LLM 生成的代码在风格特征上表现出更高的一致性；基于这一洞见，我们构建了一个基于规则的语义保持代码变换库，引入结构扰动以进一步放大统计差异。在两个数据集与六个代表性代码 LLM 上的实验中，DualCodeDetect 在 T=0.2 与 T=1.0 两种温度设置下均取得 0.8535 的平均 AUROC，显著优于现有检测方法。","tl":"标识符与结构双通道扰动放大差异，实现零样本 AI 代码检测。","au":["Zhengdao Li","Xiuwei Shang","Zhenkan Fu","Shikai Guo","Weiming Zhang","Nenghai Yu","Kejiang Chen"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["LLM-generated code detection","zero-shot detection","perturbation","identifier sampling","AUROC"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/112/x"},{"id":"p00921","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TransLibEval: Demystify Large Language Models’ Capability in Third-party Library-targeted Code Translation","tz":"TransLibEval：揭示大语言模型在面向第三方库的代码翻译中的能力","a":"In recent years, Large Language Models (LLMs) have been widely studied in the code translation field on the method, class, and even repository levels. However, most of these benchmarks are limited in terms of Third-Party Library (TPL) categories and scales, making TPL-related errors hard to expose and hindering the development of targeted solutions. Considering the high dependence (over 90%) on TPLs in practical programming, demystifying and analyzing LLMs’ code translation performance involving various TPLs becomes imperative. To address this gap, we construct TransLibEval, the first benchmark dedicated to library-centric code translation. It consists of 200 real-world tasks across Python, Java, and C++, each explicitly involving TPLs from diverse categories such as data processing, machine learning, and web development, with comprehensive dependency coverage and high-coverage test suites. We evaluate seven recent LLMs of commercial, general, and code-specialized families under six translation strategies of three categories: Direct, IR-guided, and Retrievalaugmented. Experimental results show a dramatic performance drop compared with library-free settings (average CA decline over 60%), while diverse strategies demonstrate heterogeneous advantages. Furthermore, we analyze 4,831 failed cases from GPT-4o, one of the State-of-the-Art (SOTA) LLMs, revealing numerous third-party reference errors that were obscured previously. These findings highlight the unique challenges of library-centric translation and provide practical guidance for improving TPL-aware code intelligence.","az":"近年来，大语言模型（LLM）在代码翻译领域已在方法级、类级甚至仓库级被广泛研究。然而，大多数此类基准在第三方库（TPL）的类别与规模上都很有限，使得 TPL 相关错误难以暴露，阻碍了针对性解决方案的发展。考虑到实际编程中对 TPL 的高度依赖（超过 90%），揭示并分析 LLM 在涉及各种 TPL 时的代码翻译性能变得势在必行。为填补这一空白，我们构建了 TransLibEval，首个专注于以库为中心的代码翻译的基准。它包含跨 Python、Java 与 C++ 的 200 个真实任务，每个任务都显式涉及来自数据处理、机器学习、Web 开发等不同类别的 TPL，具有全面的依赖覆盖与高覆盖率的测试套件。我们在三类共六种翻译策略（直接、IR 引导、检索增强）下评估了商用、通用与代码专用家族的七个近期 LLM。实验结果显示，与无库设置相比性能急剧下降（平均 CA 下降超过 60%），而不同策略展现出各异的优势。此外，我们分析了来自最先进 LLM 之一 GPT-4o 的 4,831 个失败案例，揭示了大量此前被掩盖的第三方引用错误。这些发现凸显了以库为中心的翻译的独特挑战，并为改进面向 TPL 的代码智能提供了实用指导。","tl":"首个以第三方库为中心的代码翻译基准，暴露 LLM 平均 CA 骤降六成。","au":["Pengyu Xue","Kunwu Zheng","Zhen Yang","Yifei Pei","Linhao Wu","Jiahui Dong","Xiapu Luo","Yan Xiao","Fei Liu","Yuxuan Zhang","Xiran Lyu","Xianhang Li","Xuanyu Zhu","Chengyi Wang"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["code translation","third-party libraries","benchmark","LLM evaluation","retrieval-augmented translation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/113/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.12087"},{"id":"p00922","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Two-Level Adaptation for Budget-Constrained Continuous Dynamic Dependence Analysis","tz":"面向预算受限的持续动态依赖分析的两级自适应方法","a":"Dynamic dependence analysis is essential for software performance optimization, debugging, regression testing, and security analysis. In long-running and distributed systems, continuously performing this analysis while balancing cost and precision under strict time budgets is a persistent challenge. Current state-of-the-art (SOTA) approaches tackle this problem but suffer from inefficient budget utilization and/or imprecise dependence results, limiting their practicality in real-world software engineering workflows. We introduce GDist, a novel two-level adaptation framework that self-tunes analysis parameters to optimize cost-effectiveness for continuous dynamic dependence analysis. GDist integrates a decision-tree-based model, tailored to particular system executions, with domain knowledge about analysis precision levels, ensuring a more precise and budget-observing adaptation strategy. We evaluate GDist on 12 real-world distributed systems and in two key applications: regression test reduction and vulnerability detection. Results show that GDist improves budget utilization by 29% and precision by 18% over SOTA. Specifically, GDist reduces regression testing costs by 31% while maintaining test effectiveness and lowers the cost of identifying true-positive vulnerabilities by 36% in enterprise-scale systems. Its lightweight adaptation and the inherent interpretability of decision trees make it well-suited for scalable, cost-aware software maintenance and security analysis. These merits position GDist as a practical and adaptive solution for modern software engineering challenges.","az":"动态依赖分析对软件性能优化、调试、回归测试与安全分析都至关重要。在长时间运行的分布式系统中，在严格的时间预算下持续执行这种分析并平衡成本与精度，是一项长期挑战。当前最先进（SOTA）的方法尝试解决该问题，但存在预算利用率低和/或依赖结果不精确的问题，限制了它们在真实软件工程工作流中的实用性。我们提出 GDist，一种新颖的两级自适应框架，能自我调优分析参数以优化持续动态依赖分析的成本效益。GDist 将一个针对特定系统执行定制的基于决策树的模型，与关于分析精度层级的领域知识相结合，确保更精确且遵守预算的自适应策略。我们在 12 个真实分布式系统上，以及回归测试约简与漏洞检测两个关键应用中评估 GDist。结果表明，GDist 相较 SOTA 将预算利用率提升 29%、精度提升 18%。具体而言，GDist 在保持测试有效性的同时将回归测试成本降低 31%，并在企业级系统中将识别真阳性漏洞的成本降低 36%。其轻量级自适应与决策树固有的可解释性，使其非常适合可扩展、成本感知的软件维护与安全分析。这些优点使 GDist 成为应对现代软件工程挑战的实用且自适应的方案。","tl":"以决策树加精度层级知识两级自调，预算利用率与精度双升。","au":["Xiaoqin Fu","Haipeng Cai"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["dynamic dependence analysis","budget-constrained analysis","adaptive tuning","regression test reduction","distributed systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/114/x","pu":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/404051008_Two-Level_Adaptation_for_Budget-Constrained_Continuous_Dynamic_Dependence_Analysis"},{"id":"p00923","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Mining Long Tail Bugs: Identifying Rare and Overlooked Issues in Code","tz":"挖掘长尾缺陷：识别代码中稀有且被忽视的问题","a":"Using data mining to extract frequent code patterns for bug detection has proven effective. However, prior studies have overlooked the prevalence of infrequent (rare) patterns, even though violations of such patterns can also lead to bugs. In this paper, we present LTMiner, which mines rare patterns from large-scale projects and detects potential bugs by checking for violations of these patterns. In practice, rare patterns far outnumber frequent ones and lack strong statistical support. Consequently, we face a pattern explosion, and many rare patterns and their violations are uninteresting. LTMiner addresses this by using instance-based ranking and filtering to prioritize violations of rare patterns. It further employs a large language model (LLM) as a domain expert to audit top-ranked violations; mined information supports in-context learning, and task decomposition and self-reflection mitigate possible hallucinations. This pipeline effectively curbs pattern explosion and false positives, uncovering previously unknown bugs in large-scale projects at an acceptable cost. Applied to Linux 6.12.1, LTMiner identified 42 previously unknown bugs, 27 of which have been confirmed by developers. These results indicate that, although rare-pattern bugs are sparse, a considerable number remain and exhibit a non-negligible long tail. We believe that rare-pattern bugs constitute a promising blue ocean for bug detection.","az":"使用数据挖掘提取频繁代码模式以检测缺陷已被证明有效。然而，以往研究忽视了非频繁（稀有）模式的普遍性，尽管违反这类模式同样可能导致缺陷。本文提出 LTMiner，它从大规模项目中挖掘稀有模式，并通过检查对这些模式的违反来检测潜在缺陷。实践中，稀有模式的数量远超频繁模式，且缺乏强统计支持。因此，我们面临模式爆炸，许多稀有模式及其违反并无价值。LTMiner 通过基于实例的排序与过滤来优先处理稀有模式的违反，从而应对这一问题。它进一步使用大语言模型（LLM）作为领域专家来审计排名靠前的违反；挖掘到的信息支撑上下文学习，而任务分解与自我反思则缓解可能的幻觉。该流水线有效抑制了模式爆炸与误报，以可接受的成本在大规模项目中发现此前未知的缺陷。应用于 Linux 6.12.1 时，LTMiner 识别出 42 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 27 个已被开发者确认。这些结果表明，尽管稀有模式缺陷分布稀疏，但仍有相当数量存在并呈现不可忽视的长尾。我们相信，稀有模式缺陷构成了缺陷检测的一片有前景的蓝海。","tl":"首次系统挖掘稀有代码模式违反，LLM 审计在 Linux 发现 42 个新缺陷。","au":["Wentao Liang","Yanjun Wu","Xiang Ling","Tianyue Luo","Dinghao Liu","Haotian Zhang","Jingzheng Wu"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["rare pattern mining","bug detection","long tail bugs","LLM auditing","Linux kernel"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/115/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797071"},{"id":"p00924","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Pig: Leveraging Large Language Models for Python Library Migrations","tz":"Pig：利用大语言模型实现 Python 库迁移","a":"We present Pig, a novel approach to automating Python library migration by leveraging large language models (LLMs). Library migration is an increasingly common task in modern Python development, yet it remains tedious and error-prone due to the lack of general solutions that can handle diverse libraries without relying on documentation or code examples. To address this challenge, Pig employs a four-step pipeline that effectively harnesses the capabilities of LLMs. First, Pig decomposes the migration task into smaller units by performing API-level slicing, allowing the LLM to focus on minimal, relevant context. Second, it guides LLMs using prompts informed by common failure patterns in naive LLM-based migrations and plausible API candidates. Third, Pig selectively extracts the migration-related code fragments from the LLM outputs. Finally, it transplants the migrated code back into the original program with post-processing to ensure semantic correctness and consistency. We demonstrate the effectiveness of Pig by evaluating it on 364 API-level migration tasks, where it improves the average success rate of the baseline approach by 53.5% across seven different LLM models.","az":"我们提出 Pig，一种利用大语言模型（LLM）自动化 Python 库迁移的新方法。库迁移在现代 Python 开发中日益常见，但由于缺乏能够在不依赖文档或代码示例的情况下处理多样库的通用方案，这项任务仍然繁琐且易错。为应对这一挑战，Pig 采用四步流水线来有效发挥 LLM 的能力。首先，Pig 通过执行 API 级切片将迁移任务分解为更小的单元，使 LLM 能够聚焦于最小且相关的上下文。其次，它使用由朴素 LLM 迁移中常见失败模式以及可能的 API 候选所构建的提示来引导 LLM。第三，它有选择地从 LLM 输出中提取与迁移相关的代码片段。最后，它将迁移后的代码移植回原程序，并进行后处理以确保语义正确性与一致性。我们在 364 个 API 级迁移任务上评估 Pig，结果表明它在七种不同的 LLM 模型上将基线方法的平均成功率提升了 53.5%。","tl":"用 API 级切片加失败模式提示，把库迁移拆成 LLM 可控的小任务。","au":["Miryeong Kang","Wonseok Oh","Gabin An","Hakjoo Oh"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Python library migration","API-level slicing","LLM prompting","code transplantation","API mapping"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/116/x","pu":"https://prl.korea.ac.kr/papers/fse26-pig.pdf"},{"id":"p00925","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Unveiling AI-Driven Web Applications: Insights into Characteristics, Functionality, and Compliance","tz":"揭示 AI 驱动的 Web 应用：特征、功能与合规性洞察","a":"Collaborative platforms such as Google Workspace, Microsoft Teams, and Zoom increasingly rely on third-party applications (referred to as plugins) to extend their core functionalities, with AI-assisted plugins emerging as a key driver of productivity. Despite their popularity and rapid adoption, Little is known about the characteristics of the marketplace, the potential security and privacy risks that concern users, and the compliance of plugins with AI ethics guidelines. In this paper, we present the first large-scale, cross-platform study of plugins from five major web application marketplaces, covering domains from office productivity to software development. We systematically examine the distribution characteristics of current plugins, analyze users’ concerns, and assess their compliance with emerging AI regulations. Our findings indicate that (i) the current marketplaces exhibit an uneven distribution of functionality and installations, (ii) AI-assisted plugins face a range of emerging issues that negatively impact user experience, and (iii) a significant proportion of plugins fail to comply with established AI ethics principles. Our work highlights the need for stricter policies and security auditing to maintain plugin functionality.","az":"Google Workspace、Microsoft Teams 与 Zoom 等协作平台越来越依赖第三方应用（称为插件）来扩展其核心功能，其中 AI 辅助插件正成为生产力的关键驱动。尽管它们广受欢迎、被迅速采用，但人们对该市场的特征、用户关切的潜在安全与隐私风险，以及插件对 AI 伦理准则的遵从情况知之甚少。本文首次对来自五个主要 Web 应用市场的插件开展大规模跨平台研究，覆盖从办公生产力到软件开发的多个领域。我们系统考察了当前插件的分布特征，分析了用户的关切，并评估了它们与新兴 AI 法规的合规性。我们的发现表明：（i）当前市场在功能与安装量上呈现不均衡分布；（ii）AI 辅助插件面临一系列负面影响用户体验的新兴问题；（iii）相当比例的插件未能遵守既有的 AI 伦理原则。我们的工作凸显了需要更严格的政策与安全审计来维护插件功能。","tl":"首次跨五大市场刻画 AI 插件生态，揭示其风险与 AI 伦理合规缺口。","au":["Liuhuo Wan","Zicong Liu","Chuan Yan","Liujia Wan","Naipeng Dong","Zi Huang","Guangdong Bai"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","security"],"kw":["AI plugins","web application marketplace","compliance","security and privacy risks","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/117/x","pu":"https://cosunshine.github.io/files/unveiling_AI-driven_security.pdf"},{"id":"p00926","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"VerilogASTBench: Benchmark Construction of Verilog AST Dataset with Dual-Stage AST Semantic Enhancement Framework","tz":"VerilogASTBench：基于双阶段 AST 语义增强框架的 Verilog AST 数据集基准构建","a":"With the increasing complexity and scale of integrated circuit (IC) designs, automated circuit design methods are essential for Verilog implementation. Although Large Language Models (LLMs) perform well in general-purpose coding such as C++ and Python, their performance in Verilog is constrained by domain-specific semantic and structural rules as well as the scarcity of high-quality training datasets. To address these issues, this work proposes a semantically enhanced Verilog code parsing and automatic repair framework based on Abstract Syntax Tree (AST). First, an advanced register-transfer level (RTL) analysis framework was developed to achieve semantic enhancement through static analysis–driven functional role inference and attribute annotation. Second, enhanced AST information is used to construct structured prompts and generate semantically rich module descriptions via an Application Programming Interface (API) for dataset construction. Finally, an AST-guided automatic Verilog repair framework was designed, which leverages enhanced AST analysis for precise defect localization and intelligent repair through compiler feedback loops. Experimental results indicate that the proposed method successfully repaired 15.24% of defective Verilog code, resulting in a high-quality RTL benchmark dataset containing 318,021 samples. Models fine-tuned on this dataset demonstrate significant performance improvements across three benchmarks, achieving average improvements of 13.76% and 16.95% on Eval-Machine pass@1 and pass@5, 8.97% and 14.56% on Eval-Human pass@1 and pass@5, and 15.70% and 12.20% on RTLLM V1.1 Syntax-VCS and Func.","az":"随着集成电路（IC）设计的复杂度和规模不断增加，自动化电路设计方法对 Verilog 实现至关重要。尽管大语言模型（LLM）在 C++、Python 等通用编程中表现良好，但其在 Verilog 上的性能受限于领域特有的语义与结构规则，以及高质量训练数据集的稀缺。为解决这些问题，本文提出了一种基于抽象语法树（AST）的语义增强 Verilog 代码解析与自动修复框架。首先，我们开发了一个先进的寄存器传输级（RTL）分析框架，通过静态分析驱动的功能角色推断与属性标注来实现语义增强。其次，利用增强后的 AST 信息构造结构化提示，并通过应用程序接口（API）生成语义丰富的模块描述，用于数据集构建。最后，设计了一个 AST 引导的 Verilog 自动修复框架，借助增强的 AST 分析进行精确的缺陷定位，并通过编译器反馈回路实现智能修复。实验结果表明，所提方法成功修复了 15.24% 的缺陷 Verilog 代码，从而构建出一个包含 318,021 个样本的高质量 RTL 基准数据集。在该数据集上微调的模型在三个基准上均取得显著提升：Eval-Machine 的 pass@1 与 pass@5 平均提升 13.76% 和 16.95%，Eval-Human 的 pass@1 与 pass@5 平均提升 8.97% 和 14.56%，RTLLM V1.1 的 Syntax-VCS 与 Func 平均提升 15.70% 和 12.20%。","tl":"用 AST 语义增强自动修复并造出 31.8 万条 Verilog 训练数据。","au":["luping zhang","Chao Chen","Dapeng Yan","Hui Xu","Mingsheng Cao","Jingkuan Song","Zhikuang Cai","Yufeng Guo"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Verilog","abstract syntax tree","RTL dataset","automatic repair","fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/118/x","pu":"https://shiyiyanqin.github.io/papers/VerilogASTBench__FSE2026_Preprint.pdf"},{"id":"p00927","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Project-Level C-to-Rust Translation via Pointer Knowledge Graphs","tz":"基于指针知识图谱的项目级 C 到 Rust 翻译","a":"Translating C code into Rust is an effective way to ensure its memory safety. Rule-based translation produces Rust code that remains unsafe and fails to leverage Rust’s safety features. LLM-based methods can generate more idiomatic and safer Rust as LLMs are trained on large amounts of human-written code. Although promising, existing LLM-based methods still struggle with project-level C-to-Rust translation. They typically partition a C project into smaller units (e.g., functions) based on the call graph and translate them bottom-up to resolve dependencies. However, this bottom-up, unit-by-unit paradigm often fails to handle pointer translation due to the lack of a global perspective on pointer usage. To address this, we propose a novel C-Rust Pointer Knowledge Graph (KG) that enriches a code-dependency graph with two types of pointer semantics: (i) pointer-usage information, recording global behaviors such as points-to flows and lower-level struct usage by higher-level units; and (ii) Rust-oriented annotations, encoding ownership, mutability, nullability, and lifetimes. Based on the C-Rust Pointer KG and its synergy with LLMs, we further propose PtrTrans, a project-level C-to-Rust translation technique. In PtrTrans, the C-Rust Pointer KG provides LLMs with comprehensive pointer semantics from a global perspective, thus guiding LLMs towards generating safe and idiomatic Rust code from a given C project. Our experiments show that PtrTrans reduces unsafe usages in translated Rust by 99.9% compared to both rule-based translation and LLM-based rewriting, while achieving an average 29.3% higher functional correctness than fuzzing-enhanced LLM methods.","az":"将 C 代码翻译为 Rust 是保证其内存安全的一种有效途径。基于规则的翻译产生的 Rust 代码仍然是 unsafe 的，无法利用 Rust 的安全特性。基于 LLM 的方法由于在大量人工编写代码上训练，能够生成更地道、更安全的 Rust 代码。尽管前景可期，现有基于 LLM 的方法在项目级 C 到 Rust 翻译上仍然吃力。它们通常依据调用图把 C 项目划分为更小的单元（例如函数），并自底向上翻译以解决依赖。然而，这种自底向上、逐单元的范式常常由于缺乏对指针使用的全局视角而无法正确处理指针翻译。为此，我们提出了一种新颖的 C-Rust 指针知识图谱（KG），它在代码依赖图的基础上补充了两类指针语义：（i）指针使用信息，记录诸如指向流以及高层单元对底层结构体的使用等全局行为；（ii）面向 Rust 的标注，编码所有权、可变性、可空性和生命周期。基于该 C-Rust 指针知识图谱及其与 LLM 的协同，我们进一步提出了项目级 C 到 Rust 翻译技术 PtrTrans。在 PtrTrans 中，C-Rust 指针 KG 从全局视角向 LLM 提供完整的指针语义，从而引导 LLM 为给定 C 项目生成安全且地道的 Rust 代码。实验表明，与基于规则的翻译和基于 LLM 的重写相比，PtrTrans 将翻译后 Rust 中的 unsafe 使用减少了 99.9%，同时其功能正确性比模糊测试增强的 LLM 方法平均高出 29.3%。","tl":"用全局指针知识图谱指导 LLM 做项目级 C→Rust 翻译。","au":["Zhiqiang Yuan","Wenjun Mao","Zhou","Xiyue Shang","Chong Wang","Yiling Lou","Xin Peng"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["C-to-Rust translation","pointer knowledge graph","memory safety","project-level translation","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/119/x"},{"id":"p00928","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CuFuzz: An API-Knowledge-Graph Coverage-Driven Fuzzing Framework for CUDA Libraries","tz":"CuFuzz：面向 CUDA 库的 API 知识图谱覆盖驱动模糊测试框架","a":"In the AI-driven era, NVIDIA CUDA libraries have become indispensable for accelerating compute-intensive tasks, yet their security assessment remains critically understudied due to closed-source code and unique programming paradigms. Existing efforts primarily target CUDA compiler vulnerabilities (e.g., NVCC), but overlook broader library-specific risks. This paper addresses the challenges of fuzzing CUDA libraries: (1) the absence of guidance narrows the set of APIs that generated harnesses can reach; and (2) input mutation remains inefficient for LLM-generated harnesses. A new tool called CuFuzz has been proposed, aimed at uncovering potential vulnerabilities in the CUDA libraries. CuFuzz has the ability to generate testing harnesses for various CUDA library functions from scratch, perform efficient parameter mutation, and adapt to the needs of multiple CUDA libraries. First, LLMs are used to extract semantic relationships from CUDA documentation and sample codes, constructing a knowledge graph that prioritizes API interactions and contextual dependencies. The API coverage bitmap is proposed to guide the fuzzer to explore under-tested library functions. In addition to harness generation, the API knowledge graph is also combined with compiler diagnostics to repair erroneous harnesses, thereby improving compilation success rates. Subsequently, CuFuzz employs the LLMs to analyze and decouple parameter dependencies, separates out the mutable parameters, and performs parameter-isolated mutation on them to enhance mutation efficiency. Evaluated across three CUDA releases (12.4, 12.7, and 13.0) on eight widely adopted libraries (e.g., cuBLAS, cuFFT), CuFuzz achieves 2.97x higher API coverage and 4.0x superior API edge coverage relative to baseline (Fuzz4all), on average. The experiments uncovered 4 unknown bugs, validated by NVIDIA’s security team and obtained 2 CVEs.","az":"在 AI 驱动的时代，NVIDIA CUDA 库已成为加速计算密集型任务不可或缺的组件，但由于代码闭源和独特的编程范式，其安全评估仍严重缺乏研究。已有工作主要针对 CUDA 编译器（如 NVCC）的漏洞，却忽视了更广泛的库特有风险。本文针对 CUDA 库模糊测试的挑战展开研究：（1）缺乏引导导致生成的测试驱动（harness）可触达的 API 集合过窄；（2）对 LLM 生成的 harness 而言输入变异效率低下。我们提出了新工具 CuFuzz，旨在挖掘 CUDA 库中潜在的漏洞。CuFuzz 能够从零为各类 CUDA 库函数生成测试 harness、执行高效的参数变异，并适配多种 CUDA 库的需求。首先，利用 LLM 从 CUDA 文档与示例代码中抽取语义关系，构建一个对 API 交互与上下文依赖进行优先级排序的知识图谱。我们提出 API 覆盖位图来引导模糊测试器探索测试不足的库函数。除 harness 生成外，API 知识图谱还与编译器诊断信息相结合，用于修复错误的 harness，从而提升编译成功率。随后，CuFuzz 使用 LLM 分析并解耦参数依赖，分离出可变参数，并对其执行参数隔离变异以提升变异效率。在三个 CUDA 版本（12.4、12.7 和 13.0）以及八个广泛使用的库（如 cuBLAS、cuFFT）上评估，CuFuzz 相对基线（Fuzz4all）平均取得 2.97 倍更高的 API 覆盖率和 4.0 倍更优的 API 边覆盖率。实验共发现 4 个未知缺陷，已获 NVIDIA 安全团队确认并取得 2 个 CVE。","tl":"用 API 知识图谱和覆盖位图引导 CUDA 库 harness 生成与变异。","au":["Ximing Fan","Yong Fang","Peng Jia","Yang Liu","Yijia Xu","Xi Peng","Yuhao Zhou"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["CUDA library fuzzing","API knowledge graph","harness generation","coverage-guided","parameter mutation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/120/x"},{"id":"p00929","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SmarTrim: Symbolic Execution for Smart Contracts Powered by Redundant Transaction-Sequence Pruning","tz":"SmarTrim：由冗余交易序列剪枝驱动的智能合约符号执行","a":"We present SmarTrim, a new symbolic execution technique for detecting vulnerabilities in smart contracts. Smart contracts require rigorous safety validation since flaws in them can cause significant financial loss. Numerous symbolic execution techniques -which generate vulnerable transaction sequences to trigger and help understand vulnerabilities- have been extensively studied to enhance the security and safety of smart contracts. However, their performance remains unsatisfactory due to the extremely large search space for transaction sequences. To mitigate this issue, SmarTrim introduces a novel technique that safely reduces the search space by detecting and pruning redundant transaction sequences. Experimental results show that SmarTrim greatly outperforms eleven state-of-the-art analyzers in detecting critical vulnerabilities in real-world smart contracts.","az":"我们提出 SmarTrim，一种用于检测智能合约漏洞的新符号执行技术。智能合约需要严格的安全验证，因为其中的缺陷可能造成重大经济损失。为提升智能合约的安全性，学界已广泛研究了大量符号执行技术——它们生成可触发漏洞的交易序列，以帮助理解漏洞。然而，由于交易序列的搜索空间极其庞大，这些技术的性能仍不尽如人意。为缓解该问题，SmarTrim 提出了一种新技术，通过检测并剪除冗余的交易序列来安全地缩减搜索空间。实验结果表明，在真实世界智能合约的关键漏洞检测上，SmarTrim 大幅优于十一种最先进的分析器。","tl":"剪掉冗余交易序列，大幅压缩合约符号执行搜索空间。","au":["Hyegeun Song","Jiseong Han","Sunbeom So"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic execution","smart contract","transaction sequence pruning","vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/121/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797074"},{"id":"p00930","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding, Detecting, and Repairing Real-World In-Context-Learning-Based Text-to-SQL Errors","tz":"理解、检测与修复真实世界中基于上下文学习的 text-to-SQL 错误","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have been adopted for text-to-SQL tasks, utilizing their in-context learning (ICL) capability to translate natural language questions into SQL queries. However, such a technique faces correctness problems. In this paper, we conduct the first comprehensive study of text-to-SQL errors of ICL-based techniques. Our study covers four representative ICL-based techniques, five basic repairing methods, two benchmarks, and two LLM settings. We find that text-to-SQL errors are widespread and summarize 27 error types of 7 categories. We also find that existing repairing attempts have limited correctness improvement while having high computational overhead and many mis-repairs. Based on these findings, we propose MapleDoctor, a novel text-to-SQL error detection and repairing framework. The evaluation demonstrates that MapleDoctor outperforms existing solutions by repairing 13.8% more queries with neglectable mis-repairs and reducing 67.4% overhead. The artifact is publicly available at GitHub.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已被用于 text-to-SQL 任务，利用其上下文学习（ICL）能力将自然语言问题翻译为 SQL 查询。然而，这类技术面临正确性问题。本文首次对基于 ICL 的技术的 text-to-SQL 错误进行了全面研究。我们的研究覆盖四种代表性的 ICL 技术、五种基础修复方法、两个基准以及两种 LLM 设置。我们发现 text-to-SQL 错误普遍存在，并总结出 7 大类共 27 种错误类型。我们还发现，现有的修复尝试在正确性上提升有限，却带来高昂的计算开销和大量误修复。基于这些发现，我们提出了新颖的 text-to-SQL 错误检测与修复框架 MapleDoctor。评估表明，MapleDoctor 优于现有方案：多修复 13.8% 的查询，误修复可忽略不计，并减少 67.4% 的开销。相关制品已在 GitHub 公开。","tl":"首次系统刻画 ICL text-to-SQL 错误并给出低开销修复框架。","au":["Jiawei Shen","Chengcheng Wan","Ruoyi Qiao","Jiazhen Zou","Hang Xu","Yuchen Shao","Yueling Zhang","Weikai Miao","Geguang Pu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["text-to-SQL","in-context learning","error taxonomy","query repair","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/122/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09310"},{"id":"p00931","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Carbon-Taxed Transformers: A Green Compression Pipeline for Overgrown Language Models","tz":"碳税化 Transformer：面向过度膨胀语言模型的绿色压缩流水线","a":"The accelerating adoption of Large Language Models (LLMs) in software engineering (SE) has brought with it a silent crisis: unsustainable computational cost. While these models demonstrate remarkable capabilities in different SE tasks, they are unmanageably large, slow to deploy, memory-intensive, and carbon-heavy. This reality threatens not only the scalability and accessibility of AI-powered SE, but also its long-term environmental sustainability. The research challenge is clear: we must go beyond accuracy and address efficiency and environmental cost as first-class design constraints. To meet this challenge, we introduce Carbon-Taxed Transformers (CTT), a systematic multi-architectural compression principled pipeline ordering inspired by economic carbon taxation principles. Drawing from the economic concept of carbon pricing, CTT operationalizes a computational carbon tax that penalizes architectural inefficiencies and rewards deployment-ready compression. We evaluate CTT across three core SE tasks: code clone detection, code summarization, and code generation, with models spanning encoder-only, encoder-decoder, and decoder-only architecture. Our results show that CTT delivers on inference: (1) up to 49 memory reduction, (2) time reduction up to 8-10 for clone detection, up to 3 for summarization, and 4–7 for generation, (3) up to 81% reduction in CO_2 emissions and (4) CTT retains around 98% accuracy on clone detection, around 89% on summarization, and up to 91% (textual metrics) and 68% (pass@1) for generation. Two ablation studies show that pipeline ordering and individual component contributions are both essential, providing empirical justification for CTT’s design and effectiveness. This work establishes a viable path toward responsible AI in SE through aggressive yet performance-preserving compression.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在软件工程（SE）中的加速采用带来了一场无声的危机：难以为继的计算成本。尽管这些模型在各类 SE 任务中展现出卓越能力，它们却过于庞大、部署缓慢、内存占用高且碳排放沉重。这一现实不仅威胁到 AI 驱动 SE 的可扩展性与可及性，也威胁其长期的环境可持续性。研究挑战十分明确：我们必须超越准确率，把效率与环境成本作为一等的设计约束。为应对这一挑战，我们提出碳税化 Transformer（CTT），一种受经济学碳税原理启发的、系统化的多架构压缩有序流水线。借鉴碳定价的经济学概念，CTT 实现了一种计算碳税，惩罚架构上的低效并奖励可部署的压缩。我们在三项核心 SE 任务上评估 CTT：代码克隆检测、代码摘要和代码生成，模型涵盖仅编码器、编码器-解码器和仅解码器三种架构。结果表明 CTT 在推理上取得成效：（1）内存最多减少 49 倍；（2）克隆检测时间最多减少 8-10 倍，摘要最多 3 倍，生成 4-7 倍；（3）CO2 排放最多减少 81%；（4）CTT 在克隆检测上保留约 98% 的准确率，摘要约 89%，生成上文本指标最高 91%、pass@1 最高 68%。两项消融实验表明流水线顺序与各组件贡献均不可或缺，为 CTT 的设计与有效性提供了实证依据。这项工作通过激进但保持性能的压缩，为 SE 中负责任的 AI 开辟了一条可行路径。","tl":"按“碳税”原则排定压缩流水线顺序，压缩代码模型并减排。","au":["Ajmain Inqiad Alam","Palash Ranjan Roy","Chanchal K. Roy","Banani Roy","Kevin Schneider"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"efficient-inference-quantization-and-ml-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["model compression","green AI","carbon footprint","code LLM","inference efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/123/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25903"},{"id":"p00932","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DuCodeMark: Dual-Purpose Code Dataset Watermarking via Style-Aware Watermark–Poison Design","tz":"DuCodeMark：通过风格感知的水印-投毒设计实现双重用途的代码数据集水印","a":"The proliferation of large language models for code (CodeLLMs) and open-source contributions has heightened concerns over unauthorized use of source code datasets. While watermarking provides a viable protection mechanism by embedding ownership signals, existing methods rely on detectable trigger–target patterns and are limited to source-level tasks, overlooking binary-level scenarios such as decompilation. In this paper, we propose DuCodeMark, a stealthy and robust dual-purpose watermarking method for code datasets that generalizes across both source-level and binary-level code tasks. DuCodeMark parses each code sample into an abstract syntax tree (AST), applies language-specific style transformations to construct stealthy trigger–target pairs, and injects repressible poisoned features into a subset of return-typed samples to enhance robustness against watermark removal or evasion. These features remain inactive during normal training but are activated upon watermark removal, degrading model performance. For verification, DuCodeMark employs a black-box method based on the independent-samples t-test. We conduct a comprehensive evaluation of DuCodeMark across 72 settings spanning two code tasks, two programming languages, three CodeLLMs, and six decoding temperatures. The results demonstrate that it consistently achieves strong verifiability (p < 0.05), high stealthiness (suspicious rate 0.36), robustness against both watermark and poisoning attacks (recall 0.57), and a substantial drop in model performance upon watermark removal (Pass@1 drops by 28.6%), underscoring its practicality and resilience.","az":"代码大语言模型（CodeLLM）的激增与开源贡献的增长，加剧了人们对源代码数据集被未授权使用的担忧。虽然水印通过嵌入所有权信号提供了一种可行的保护机制，现有方法依赖可被检测的触发-目标模式，且仅限于源码级任务，忽视了如反编译这类二进制级场景。本文提出 DuCodeMark，一种隐蔽且鲁棒的代码数据集双重用途水印方法，可同时泛化到源码级与二进制级代码任务。DuCodeMark 将每个代码样本解析为抽象语法树（AST），应用语言特定的风格变换来构造隐蔽的触发-目标对，并在部分带返回类型的样本中注入可抑制的投毒特征以增强对水印移除或规避的鲁棒性。这些特征在正常训练时保持不激活，一旦水印被移除即被激活，从而降低模型性能。在验证方面，DuCodeMark 采用基于独立样本 t 检验的黑盒方法。我们在涵盖两项代码任务、两种编程语言、三种 CodeLLM 和六种解码温度的 72 种设置下对 DuCodeMark 进行了全面评估。结果表明，它始终具备强可验证性（p < 0.05）、高隐蔽性（可疑率 ≤ 0.36）、对水印攻击与投毒攻击的鲁棒性（召回率 ≤ 0.57），并在水印被移除时造成模型性能大幅下降（Pass@1 下降 28.6%），凸显了其实用性与韧性。","tl":"把水印与可激活投毒结合，源码和二进制任务都能验权。","au":["Yuchen Chen","Yuan Xiao","Chunrong Fang","Zhenyu Chen","Baowen Xu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"privacy-memorization-watermarking-and-unlearning","tg":["security","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["dataset watermarking","code LLM","data poisoning","AST style transformation","ownership verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/124/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.10611"},{"id":"p00933","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Grounded Theory of Debugging in Professional Software Engineering Practice","tz":"专业软件工程实践中调试行为的扎根理论","a":"Debugging is a central yet complex activity in software engineering. Prior studies have documented debugging strategies and tool usage, but little theory explains how experienced developers reason about bugs in large, real-world codebases. We conducted a qualitative study using a grounded theory approach. We observed seven professional developers and five professional live-coding streamers working on 17 debugging tasks in their own codebases, capturing diverse contexts of debugging. We theorize debugging as a structured, iterative diagnostic process in which programmers update a mental model of the system to guide information gathering. Developers gather information by alternating between navigation and execution strategies, employing forward and backward tracing modes of reasoning and adapting these approaches according to codebase context, complexity, and familiarity. Developers also gather external resources to complement code-based evidence, with their experience enabling them to systematically construct a mental model. We contribute a grounded theory of professional debugging that surfaces the human-centered dimensions of the practice, with implications for tool design and software engineering education.","az":"调试是软件工程中核心却复杂的活动。已有研究记录了调试策略与工具使用，但鲜有理论解释经验丰富的开发者如何在大型真实代码库中对缺陷进行推理。我们采用扎根理论方法开展了一项定性研究。我们观察了七位专业开发者和五位专业直播编程主播在各自代码库上完成的 17 个调试任务，捕捉了多样化的调试情境。我们把调试理论化为一个结构化、迭代的诊断过程：程序员在其中不断更新对系统的心智模型，以指导信息收集。开发者通过在导航策略与执行策略之间交替来收集信息，运用前向与后向的追踪推理模式，并依据代码库的情境、复杂度与熟悉程度调整这些方法。开发者还会获取外部资源来补充基于代码的证据，其经验使他们能够系统化地构建心智模型。我们贡献了一套关于专业调试的扎根理论，揭示了这一实践中以人为中心的维度，并对工具设计与软件工程教育具有启示。","tl":"扎根理论刻画调试为心智模型驱动的迭代诊断过程。","au":["Haolin Li","Michael Coblenz"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["human-study","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["debugging","grounded theory","qualitative study","mental model","professional developers"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/125/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3797077"},{"id":"p00934","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"An Empirical Study of Fuzz Harness Degradation","tz":"模糊测试 Harness 退化的实证研究","a":"Fuzzing is a widely used technique to automatically test software for potential faults. To fuzz software projects efficiently and effectively, they must use fuzz harnesses , i.e., small programs that connect the fuzzer to the project’s code under test. However, as projects evolve, it is unclear whether fuzz harnesses are maintained in lockstep or left to stagnate, and whether unmaintained fuzz harnesses gradually degrade in terms of code coverage and bug-finding effectiveness. In this paper, we focus on OSS-Fuzz, the largest continuous fuzzing platform in practice, which provides harnesses for 510 open-source C/C++ projects, many of them security-critical. These harnesses are usually contributed by project maintainers or external developers, yet their ongoing maintenance is not always ensured. Our analysis shows that, overall, harnesses exhibit only a small reduction in coverage and retain surprising longevity in their ability to uncover bugs. This holds even without explicit updates, as long as they continue to build. At the same time, we identify specific cases where harnesses degrade, analyze their root causes, and categorize them systematically. Finally, we extend OSS-Fuzz and Fuzz Introspector, a companion project to investigate fuzzer performance, with new metrics to automatically detect harness degradation, enabling more effective monitoring of fuzzing quality in evolving projects.","az":"模糊测试是自动测试软件潜在故障的广泛使用的技术。为高效有效地对软件项目做模糊测试，必须使用 fuzz harness，即把模糊测试器与项目被测代码连接起来的小程序。然而，随着项目演化，harness 是否被同步维护、还是被搁置不管，以及未维护的 harness 是否会在代码覆盖率与发现缺陷能力上逐渐退化，都尚不清楚。本文聚焦 OSS-Fuzz——实践中最大的持续模糊测试平台，它为 510 个开源 C/C++ 项目（其中许多是安全关键的）提供 harness。这些 harness 通常由项目维护者或外部开发者贡献，但其持续维护并不总能得到保证。我们的分析表明，总体而言 harness 的覆盖率只有小幅下降，并在发现缺陷的能力上保持了出人意料的长效性。即便没有显式更新，只要它们还能继续构建，这一结论依然成立。与此同时，我们识别出 harness 确实退化的具体案例，分析其根因并进行系统分类。最后，我们为 OSS-Fuzz 及其配套项目 Fuzz Introspector（用于考察模糊测试器性能）扩展了新的度量指标，以自动检测 harness 退化，从而在演化中的项目里更有效地监控模糊测试质量。","tl":"实测 harness 老化影响很小，并给出自动退化检测指标。","au":["Philipp Görz","Joschua Schilling","Nicolai Bissantz","Thorsten Holz"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["fuzz harness","OSS-Fuzz","harness degradation","code coverage","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/126/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.06177"},{"id":"p00935","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Binvariants: Enhancing Fuzzing of Closed-source Binary Executables via Register-level Likely Invariants","tz":"Binvariants：借助寄存器级似然不变式增强闭源二进制可执行文件的模糊测试","a":"Closed-source software is ubiquitous in everyday computing, underscoring the need for robust security vetting of “binary-only” executable code. While code-coverage-guided fuzzing has long proven effective at unearthing software bugs, fuzzing in open-source contexts has since evolved beyond code coverage as its principal guiding metric. State-of-the-art fuzzing advancements demonstrate that likely data invariants—data-level properties which, if violated, expose unusual and often bug-preceding program states—significantly widen fuzzing’s reach to defects ordinarily occluded by coverage-only testing. Unfortunately, current invariant-guided fuzzing universally depends on source-level abstractions, rendering it unportable to binary-only targets. Consequently, closed-source software fuzzing—and more importantly, binary-only bug discovery—remain stalled at now-obsolete coverage-only techniques, even as open-source software fuzzing advances well past them. To bridge this longstanding gap, this paper introduces register-level likely invariants: the first technique to integrate likely data invariants within binary-only fuzzing. In contrast to contemporary source-level data invariant mining, our approach operates directly on CPU registers, capturing the low-level program states that themselves encode higher-level data relationships. From these low-level states, we automatically derive likely data invariants and expose their violations as fuzzer-observable signals via runtime instrumentation, steering fuzzing into states often unreachable by code coverage alone. In doing so, our approach surfaces qualitatively different states, complementing traditional coverage-guided fuzzing with distinct bug-finding capabilities. We implement our approach as a prototype, Binvariants, and evaluate its performance across 25 benchmark applications: 7 closed-source, as well as 18 open-source programs compiled as binary-only executables. Our results show that, compared to driving binary fuzzing solely via code coverage, register-level likely invariants helps fuzzing trigger over 27× more unique invariant violations beyond coverage-only fuzzing, thereby exercising a mean 52% more distinct code regions. Moreover, our approach uncovers 143 total bugs versus coverage-only fuzzing’s 137—including 20 missed by code coverage—demonstrating how register-level likely invariants extends binary-only fuzzing’s reach into execution states beyond what coverage alone is capable of.","az":"闭源软件在日常计算中无处不在，这凸显了对“仅有二进制”的可执行代码进行稳健安全审查的必要性。虽然代码覆盖率引导的模糊测试长期以来在挖掘软件缺陷方面成效显著，开源场景下的模糊测试早已超越以代码覆盖率作为主要引导指标的阶段。最新的模糊测试进展表明，似然数据不变式——一旦被违反即揭示异常且往往先于缺陷出现的程序状态的数据级属性——显著扩展了模糊测试对那些仅靠覆盖率测试通常难以触及的缺陷的触达范围。遗憾的是，当前的不变式引导模糊测试普遍依赖源码级抽象，无法移植到仅有二进制的目标上。因此，闭源软件模糊测试——更重要的是仅有二进制的缺陷发现——仍停滞在如今已过时的纯覆盖率技术上，尽管开源软件模糊测试早已远远超越它们。为弥合这一长期存在的鸿沟，本文引入了寄存器级似然不变式：首个将似然数据不变式融入仅有二进制模糊测试的技术。与当代源码级的数据不变式挖掘不同，我们的方法直接作用于 CPU 寄存器，捕捉那些本身编码了更高层数据关系的底层程序状态。我们从这些底层状态自动推导似然数据不变式，并通过运行时插桩把它们的违反暴露为模糊测试器可观测的信号，从而引导模糊测试进入仅靠代码覆盖率常常无法到达的状态。由此，我们的方法揭示出性质不同的程序状态，以独特的缺陷发现能力补充了传统的覆盖率引导模糊测试。我们将该方法实现为原型 Binvariants，并在 25 个基准应用上评估其性能：7 个闭源程序，以及 18 个编译为仅有二进制形式的开源程序。结果表明，相比仅用代码覆盖率驱动二进制模糊测试，寄存器级似然不变式帮助模糊测试触发的独特不变式违反数量超出 27 倍，从而平均多覆盖 52% 的不同代码区域。此外，我们的方法共发现 143 个缺陷，而仅覆盖率的模糊测试为 137 个——其中 20 个是代码覆盖率所遗漏的，表明寄存器级似然不变式把仅有二进制模糊测试的触达范围拓展到了覆盖率无法企及的执行状态。","tl":"首次在纯二进制模糊测试中用寄存器级似然不变式做反馈。","au":["Zao Yang","Stefan Nagy"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["non-llm-classical","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["binary-only fuzzing","likely invariants","register-level analysis","runtime instrumentation","bug discovery"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/127/x","pu":"https://futures.cs.utah.edu/papers/26FSE-c.pdf"},{"id":"p00936","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards Automated Crowdsourced Testing via Personified-LLM","tz":"迈向基于人格化 LLM 的自动化众包测试","a":"The rapid proliferation and increasing complexity of software demand robust quality assurance, with graphical user interface (GUI) testing playing a pivotal role. Crowdsourced testing has proven effective in this context by leveraging the diversity of human testers to achieve rich, scenario-based coverage across varied devices, user behaviors, and usage environments. In parallel, automated testing, particularly with the advent of large language models (LLMs), offers significant advantages in controllability, reproducibility, and efficiency, enabling scalable and systematic exploration. However, automated approaches often lack the behavioral diversity characteristic of human testers, limiting their capability to fully simulate real-world testing dynamics. To address this gap, we present PersonaTester, a novel personified-LLM-based framework designed to automate crowdsourced GUI testing. By injecting representative personas, defined along three orthogonal dimensions: testing mindset, exploration strategy, and interaction habit, into LLM-based agents, PersonaTester enables the simulation of diverse human-like testing behaviors in a controllable and repeatable manner. Experimental results demonstrate that PersonaTester faithfully reproduces the behavioral patterns of real crowdworkers, exhibiting strong intra-persona consistency and clear inter-persona variability (117.86% – 126.23% improvement over the baseline). Moreover, persona-guided testing agents consistently generate more effective test events and trigger more crashes (100+) and functional bugs (11) than the baseline without persona, thus substantially advancing the realism and effectiveness of automated crowdsourced GUI testing.","az":"软件的快速普及与日益增长的复杂度要求稳健的质量保障，其中图形用户界面（GUI）测试扮演关键角色。众包测试在这一背景下已被证明行之有效，它利用人类测试者的多样性，在不同设备、用户行为和使用环境下实现丰富的、面向场景的覆盖。与此同时，自动化测试，尤其是随着大语言模型（LLM）的出现，在可控性、可复现性和效率方面具有显著优势，能够实现可扩展且系统化的探索。然而，自动化方法往往缺乏人类测试者所特有的行为多样性，限制了其充分模拟真实测试动态的能力。为弥合这一差距，我们提出 PersonaTester，一种新颖的基于人格化 LLM 的框架，用于自动化众包 GUI 测试。通过将沿三个正交维度（测试心态、探索策略和交互习惯）定义的代表性人格注入基于 LLM 的智能体，PersonaTester 能够以可控且可重复的方式模拟多样的类人测试行为。实验结果表明，PersonaTester 忠实再现了真实众包工作者的行为模式，表现出很强的人格内一致性和清晰的人格间差异性（相对基线提升 117.86%–126.23%）。此外，人格引导的测试智能体持续生成更有效的测试事件，触发的崩溃（100 多个）和功能缺陷（11 个）均多于无人格的基线，从而显著提升了自动化众包 GUI 测试的真实性与有效性。","tl":"把众包测试者人格注入 LLM 智能体以复现行为多样性。","au":["Shengcheng Yu","Yuchen Ling","Chunrong Fang","Zhenyu Chen","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["crowdsourced testing","GUI testing","persona","LLM agent","Android"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/128/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24160"},{"id":"p00937","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DECODE: Dynamic Exploration for Constraint-Guided Vulnerability Discovery in Deep Learning Operators","tz":"DECODE：面向深度学习算子约束引导漏洞发现的动态探索","a":"The security and robustness of deep learning (DL) frameworks are vital, as vulnerabilities in low-level operator implementations can lead to serious reliability and security risks. While testing has proven effective in uncovering such flaws, existing techniques struggle to accurately capture the complex input constraints required by DL operators, resulting in low test coverage and missed bugs. To address this, we propose DECODE, a fully automated framework that performs efficient and precise constraint extraction through dynamic analysis. DECODE models operator-specific input requirements by observing valid execution traces and exploring constraint relationships. It then uses these refined constraints to generate high-quality test inputs capable of exposing memory error vulnerabilities. We evaluated DECODE on two widely used DL frameworks - TensorFlow and PyTorch - where it uncovered 96 bugs (54 in TensorFlow and 42 in PyTorch), 70 of which have been confirmed by developers. Compared to state-of-the-art tools, DECODE detected 41, 75, and 87 more bugs than IvySyn, DocTer, and DeepREL, respectively, demonstrating its superior effectiveness in uncovering previously undetected vulnerabilities.","az":"深度学习（DL）框架的安全性与鲁棒性至关重要，因为底层算子实现中的漏洞可能导致严重的可靠性与安全风险。虽然测试已被证明能有效发现此类缺陷，现有技术难以准确刻画 DL 算子所要求的复杂输入约束，导致测试覆盖率低并遗漏缺陷。为此，我们提出 DECODE，一个全自动框架，通过动态分析实现高效且精确的约束抽取。DECODE 通过观察有效执行轨迹并探索约束之间的关系来建模算子特定的输入需求，随后利用这些精化后的约束生成能够暴露内存错误漏洞的高质量测试输入。我们在两个广泛使用的 DL 框架 TensorFlow 和 PyTorch 上评估 DECODE，共发现 96 个缺陷（TensorFlow 54 个、PyTorch 42 个），其中 70 个已被开发者确认。与最先进工具相比，DECODE 分别比 IvySyn、DocTer 和 DeepREL 多检测出 41、75 和 87 个缺陷，展现出在挖掘此前未被发现漏洞方面的卓越有效性。","tl":"用动态执行轨迹反推算子输入约束来生成致错输入。","au":["Haotong Liu","Zhi Wang","Liu Zhuohang","Wanpeng Li"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["deep learning operators","constraint extraction","dynamic analysis","memory error","TensorFlow/PyTorch"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/129/x"},{"id":"p00938","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GraphLocator: Graph-guided Causal Reasoning for Issue Localization","tz":"GraphLocator：面向 Issue 定位的图引导因果推理","a":"The issue localization task aims to identify the locations in a software repository that requires modification given a natural language issue description. This task is fundamental yet challenging in automated software engineering due to the semantic gap between issue description and source code implementation. This gap manifests as two mismatches: (1) symptom–to-cause mismatches, where descriptions do not explicitly reveal underlying root causes; (2) one-to-many mismatches, where a single issue corresponds to multiple interdependent code entities. To address these two mismatches, we propose GraphLocator, an LLM-based approach that mitigates symptom–to-cause mismatches through causal structure discovering and resolves one-to-many mismatches via dynamic issue disentangling. The key artifact of GraphLocator is the causal issue graph (CIG), in which vertices represent discovered sub-issues along with their associated code entities, and edges encode the causal dependencies between them. The workflow of GraphLocator consists of two phases: symptom vertices locating and dynamic CIG discovering; it first identifies symptom locations on the repository graph, then dynamically expands the CIG by iteratively reasoning over neighboring vertices, discovering new sub-issues and updating causal dependencies. Experiments on three real-world Python and Java datasets demonstrates the effectiveness of GraphLocator: (1) Compared with baselines, GraphLocator achieves more accurate localization with average improvements of +19.49% in function-level recall and +11.89% in precision with acceptable overhead. (2) GraphLocator outperforms baselines on both symptom-to-cause and one-to-many mismatch scenarios, achieving recall improvement of +16.44% and +19.18%, precision improvement of +7.78% and +13.23%, respectively. (3) The disentangled causal structure CIG generated by GraphLocator yields the highest relative improvement, resulting in a 28.74% increase in performance on the downstream issue-resolving task.","az":"Issue 定位任务旨在依据自然语言 issue 描述，识别软件仓库中需要修改的位置。由于 issue 描述与源码实现之间存在语义鸿沟，该任务在自动化软件工程中既基础又具挑战性。这一鸿沟体现为两类不匹配：（1）症状到根因的不匹配，即描述并未显式揭示底层根因；（2）一对多不匹配，即单个 issue 对应多个相互依赖的代码实体。为解决这两类不匹配，我们提出 GraphLocator，一种基于 LLM 的方法，通过因果结构发现缓解症状到根因的不匹配，并通过动态 issue 解耦化解一对多不匹配。GraphLocator 的关键制品是因果 issue 图（CIG），其中顶点表示被发现的子 issue 及其关联代码实体，边编码它们之间的因果依赖。GraphLocator 的工作流包含两个阶段：症状顶点定位与动态 CIG 发现；它首先在仓库图上识别症状位置，然后通过对邻居顶点迭代推理来动态扩展 CIG，发现新的子 issue 并更新因果依赖。在三个真实世界的 Python 与 Java 数据集上的实验验证了 GraphLocator 的有效性：（1）与基线相比，GraphLocator 以可接受的开销实现了更精确的定位，函数级召回率平均提升 +19.49%，精确率平均提升 +11.89%；（2）在症状到根因和一对多两类不匹配场景下 GraphLocator 均优于基线，召回率分别提升 +16.44% 和 +19.18%，精确率分别提升 +7.78% 和 +13.23%；（3）GraphLocator 生成的解耦因果结构 CIG 带来最高的相对提升，使下游 issue 求解任务性能提高 28.74%。","tl":"用因果 issue 图解耦子问题以提升 issue 定位精度。","au":["Wei Liu","Chao Peng","Pengfei Gao","Aofan Liu","Wei Zhang","Haiyan Zhao","Zhi Jin"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["issue localization","causal issue graph","repository graph","LLM","issue resolution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/130/x"},{"id":"p00939","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CASCADE: Detecting Inconsistencies between Code and Documentation with Automatic Test Generation","tz":"CASCADE：通过自动测试生成检测代码与文档之间的不一致","a":"Maintaining consistency between code and documentation is a crucial yet frequently overlooked aspect of software development. Even minor mismatches can confuse API users, introduce new bugs, and increase overall maintenance effort. This creates demand for automated solutions that can assist developers in identifying code-documentation inconsistencies. However, since automatic reports still require human confirmation, false positives carry serious consequences: wasting developer time and discouraging practical adoption. We introduce CASCADE (Consistency Analysis for Source Code And Documentation through Execution), a novel tool for detecting inconsistencies with a strong emphasis on reducing false positives. CASCADE leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) to generate unit tests directly from natural-language documentation. Since these tests are derived from the documentation, any failure during execution indicates a potential mismatch between the documented and actual behavior of the code. To minimize false positives, CASCADE also generates code from the documentation to cross-check the generated tests. By design, an inconsistency is reported only when two conditions are met: the existing code fails the test, while the code generated from the documentation passes the same test. We evaluated CASCADE on a novel dataset of inconsistent and consistent code-documentation pairs drawn from open-source Java projects. Further, we applied CASCADE to additional Java, C#, and Rust repositories, where we uncovered 12 previously unknown inconsistencies, of which 8 have subsequently been fixed by maintainers, demonstrating both CASCADE’s precision and its applicability to real-world codebases.","az":"保持代码与文档的一致性是软件开发中至关重要却常被忽视的方面。即使是细微的不匹配也可能让 API 使用者困惑、引入新缺陷并增加整体维护成本，因而催生了对能协助开发者识别代码-文档不一致的自动化方案的需求。然而，由于自动报告仍需人工确认，误报会带来严重后果：浪费开发者时间并打击实际采用的积极性。我们提出 CASCADE（通过执行进行源码与文档一致性分析），一种以显著降低误报为重点的不一致检测新工具。CASCADE 利用大语言模型（LLM）直接从自然语言文档生成单元测试。由于这些测试源自文档，执行期间的任何失败都意味着文档化行为与代码实际行为之间可能存在不匹配。为最小化误报，CASCADE 还会从文档生成代码，用以交叉校验所生成的测试。按设计，只有同时满足两个条件时才报告不一致：现有代码未通过该测试，而由文档生成的代码通过了同一测试。我们在一个由开源 Java 项目中抽取的、包含一致与不一致代码-文档对的新数据集上评估了 CASCADE。此外，我们将 CASCADE 应用于更多 Java、C# 和 Rust 仓库，发现了 12 个此前未知的不一致，其中 8 个随后已被维护者修复，既证明了 CASCADE 的精确性，也证明了其对真实代码库的适用性。","tl":"用文档生成的测试加代码交叉校验来压低不一致误报。","au":["Tobias Kiecker","Jan Arne Sparka","Martin Reuter","Albert Ziegler","Lars Grunske"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code-documentation inconsistency","test generation","LLM","false positive reduction","API documentation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/131/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.19400"},{"id":"p00940","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Feature Slice Matching for Precise Bug Detection","tz":"面向精确缺陷检测的特征切片匹配","a":"Measuring the function similarity to detect bugs is effective, but the statements unrelated to the bugs can impede the performance due to the noise interference. Suppressing the noise interference in existing works does not manage the tough job, i.e., eliminating the noise in the targets. In this paper, we propose MATUS to mitigate the target noise for precise bug detection based on similarity measurement. Feature slices are extracted from both the buggy query and the targets to represent the semantic feature of (potential) bug logics. In particular, MATUS guides the target slicing with the prior knowledge from the buggy code, in an end-to-end way to pinpoint the slicing criterion in the targets. All feature slices are embedded and compared based on the vector similarity. Buggy candidates are audited to confirm unknown bugs in the targets. Experiments show that MATUS holds advantages in bug detection for real-world projects with acceptable efficiency. In total, MATUS has spotted 31 unknown bugs in the Linux kernel. All of them have been confirmed by the kernel developers, and 11 have been assigned CVEs.","az":"通过度量函数相似度来检测缺陷是有效的，但与缺陷无关的语句会因噪声干扰而拖累性能。已有工作对噪声干扰的抑制无法胜任这项艰巨任务，即消除目标代码中的噪声。本文提出 MATUS，以缓解目标噪声，从而实现基于相似度度量的精确缺陷检测。我们从含缺陷的查询代码和目标代码中提取特征切片，用以表征（潜在）缺陷逻辑的语义特征。特别地，MATUS 以来自缺陷代码的先验知识引导目标代码的切片，以端到端的方式在目标中确定切片准则。所有特征切片被嵌入并基于向量相似度进行比较，含缺陷的候选会被人工审计以确认目标中的未知缺陷。实验表明，MATUS 在真实项目的缺陷检测中具有优势且效率可接受。MATUS 共在 Linux 内核中发现 31 个未知缺陷，全部获内核开发者确认，其中 11 个已分配 CVE。","tl":"用缺陷先验引导目标切片，去噪后做相似度缺陷检测。","au":["Ke Ma","Jianjun Huang","Wei You","Bin Liang","Jingzheng Wu","Yanjun Wu","Yuanjun Gong"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["bug detection","program slicing","code similarity","Linux kernel","CVE"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/132/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.24858"},{"id":"p00941","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DiverFPS: Generating Diverse Solutions for Floating-Point SMT Formulas","tz":"DiverFPS：为浮点 SMT 公式生成多样化的解","a":"Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT) is a fundamental technique underpinning a wide range of applications in software engineering and testing. Among various SMT theories, the theory of floating-point plays a crucial role in practical software systems, yet reasoning about floating-point constraints remains challenging. Although existing SMT solvers are capable of producing single solutions, many applications, particularly in software testing and verification, require diverse sets of solutions to adequately exercise program behaviors. While achieving high diversity is essential for exploring system behaviors, it is also important to limit the number of generated solutions, as overly large solution sets can considerably increase testing time and resource consumption, thereby diminishing efficiency. In this work, we propose DiverFPS, a novel floating-point SMT sampler designed to generate small solution sets that achieve high target abstract syntax tree (AST)-coverage, which is commonly regarded as the standard metric for assessing solution diversity in the SMT sampling domain. DiverFPS operates in two stages: an exploration stage that aims to achieve the target AST-coverage as fully as possible, and a pruning stage that prunes redundant solutions while preserving the target AST-coverage. We further introduce three novel techniques, namely solution-driven restart strategy, context-aware encoding technology, and coverage-driven pruning strategy, which enhance the performance of DiverFPS. Extensive experiments on publicly available SMT-LIB benchmarks for QF_FP and QF_BVFP logics demonstrate that DiverFPS outperforms state-of-the-art SMT samplers. It successfully achieves the target AST-coverage on a larger number of benchmarks, which existing samplers fail to reach, while producing solution sets that are up to 92.9% smaller, the former improving the effectiveness of practical software testing and verification, and the latter improving testing efficiency and reducing resource consumption. These results demonstrate that DiverFPS is a high-performing sampler for floating-point SMT sampling.","az":"可满足性模理论（SMT）是支撑软件工程与测试中诸多应用的基础技术。在各种 SMT 理论中，浮点理论在实际软件系统中扮演关键角色，但对浮点约束的推理仍然困难。尽管现有 SMT 求解器能够产出单个解，许多应用——尤其是软件测试与验证——需要多样化的解集来充分激发程序行为。虽然高多样性对探索系统行为至关重要，限制生成解的数量同样重要，因为过大的解集会显著增加测试时间与资源消耗，从而降低效率。本文提出 DiverFPS，一种新颖的浮点 SMT 采样器，旨在生成规模小但能达到高目标抽象语法树（AST）覆盖率的解集——AST 覆盖率通常被视为 SMT 采样领域评估解多样性的标准指标。DiverFPS 分两个阶段运行：探索阶段尽可能完整地达到目标 AST 覆盖率，剪枝阶段在保持目标 AST 覆盖率的同时剪除冗余解。我们进一步提出三项新技术：解驱动的重启策略、上下文感知的编码技术以及覆盖驱动的剪枝策略，用以提升 DiverFPS 的性能。在公开的 SMT-LIB 基准（QF_FP 与 QF_BVFP 逻辑）上的大量实验表明，DiverFPS 优于最先进的 SMT 采样器：它在更多基准上成功达到目标 AST 覆盖率（现有采样器无法达到），同时生成的解集最多小 92.9%；前者提升了实际软件测试与验证的有效性，后者提升了测试效率并降低资源消耗。这些结果表明 DiverFPS 是一款高性能的浮点 SMT 采样器。","tl":"以更小解集达到目标 AST 覆盖率的浮点 SMT 采样器。","au":["Shuangyu Lyu","Chuan Luo","Ruizhi Shi","Zhuo Su","Chunming Hu"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["SMT sampling","floating-point constraints","solution diversity","AST coverage","pruning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/133/x"},{"id":"p00942","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Characterizing and Mitigating False-Positive Bug Reports in the Linux Kernel","tz":"刻画并缓解 Linux 内核中的误报缺陷报告","a":"False-positive bug reports represent a significant yet underexplored challenge in the development and maintenance of the Linux kernel. They occur when correct system behavior is mistakenly flagged as a defect, consuming developer effort without leading to actual code improvements. Such reports can mislead developers, waste debugging resources, and delay the resolution of real bugs. In this paper, we present the first comprehensive empirical study of false-positive bug reports in the Linux kernel. We manually construct a dataset of 2,006 bug reports comprising 1,509 genuine bugs and 497 false positives collected from Bugzilla and Syzkaller. Our analysis indicates that false positives demand effort comparable to real bugs, often requiring extended discussions and non-trivial closure time. They occur in several components, especially File Systems and Drivers, mainly due to external dependencies and semantic misunderstandings. To address this challenge, we evaluate large language models (LLMs) for automated false-positive bug report mitigation. Among various prompting strategies, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) performs best, achieving 91% recall and an F1 score of 88%. These findings highlight the non-negligible cost of false positive bug reports and show the promise of LLMs for more efficient false positive mitigation in the Linux kernel.","az":"误报缺陷报告是 Linux 内核开发与维护中一个重要却缺乏研究的挑战。当正确的系统行为被错误地标记为缺陷时就会产生误报，它们消耗开发者精力却不带来实际的代码改进。此类报告可能误导开发者、浪费调试资源，并延迟真实缺陷的解决。本文首次对 Linux 内核中的误报缺陷报告展开全面的实证研究。我们人工构建了一个包含 2,006 份缺陷报告的数据集，其中包括来自 Bugzilla 和 Syzkaller 的 1,509 个真实缺陷和 497 个误报。分析表明，误报所需的处理精力与真实缺陷相当，往往需要长时间的讨论和不短的关闭时间。它们出现在多个组件中，尤其是文件系统和驱动，主要成因是外部依赖和语义误解。为应对这一挑战，我们评估了用大语言模型（LLM）自动缓解误报缺陷报告的效果。在多种提示策略中，检索增强生成（RAG）表现最佳，取得 91% 的召回率和 88% 的 F1 值。这些发现凸显了误报缺陷报告不可忽视的成本，并展示了 LLM 在更高效缓解误报方面的潜力。","tl":"首个内核误报缺陷报告数据集，并用 RAG 自动识别误报。","au":["jiashuo tian","Dong Wang","Chen Yang","Haichi Wang","Zan Wang","Junjie Chen"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["false positive bug reports","Linux kernel","Syzkaller","empirical study","retrieval-augmented generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/134/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.07678"},{"id":"p00943","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Neuron-Guided Interpretation of Code LLMs: Where, Why, and How?","tz":"代码大模型的神经元引导解释：在哪里、为什么、以及如何？","a":"Code language models have demonstrated strong capabilities across a wide range of code intelligence tasks. Nevertheless, the majority of existing research prioritizes performance improvements on benchmark datasets while overlooking the interpretability of model internals. They often treat code LLMs as black boxes, which results in limited transparency, reduced controllability, and uncertain reliability. In this work, we investigate the inner mechanisms of code LLMs at both neuron and layer levels, aiming to localize network regions that encode programming language-specific and language-agnostic semantic representations of code. Our study employs two state-of-the-art models, Llama-3.1-8B and Qwen2.5-Coder-32B, across five widely-used programming languages: C++, Java, Python, Go, and JavaScript. We analyze neuron activation patterns in response to multilingual code inputs and examine the contributions of different layers during output generation. Our empirical results indicate that: (1) code LLMs exhibit neurons specialized for individual programming languages as well as a universal set supporting general code generation; and (2) lower layers predominantly capture syntactic structures specific to each language, while higher layers abstract into semantic representations that generalize across languages. We further exploit these insights to enhance three downstream tasks: neuron-guided fine-tuning for code generation, clone detection using concept-layer embeddings, and transfer learning guided by concept-layer representations for code summarization. Experimental evaluations show that each strategy consistently improves the performance of multilingual code LLMs.","az":"代码语言模型已在广泛的代码智能任务中展现出强大能力。然而，现有研究大多侧重于在基准数据集上提升性能，却忽视了模型内部机制的可解释性。它们常常把代码 LLM 当作黑箱，导致透明度有限、可控性降低、可靠性不确定。本工作在神经元与层两个层面考察代码 LLM 的内部机制，旨在定位那些编码编程语言特定与语言无关代码语义表示的网络区域。我们的研究采用两个最先进的模型 Llama-3.1-8B 和 Qwen2.5-Coder-32B，覆盖五种广泛使用的编程语言：C++、Java、Python、Go 和 JavaScript。我们分析神经元对多语言代码输入的激活模式，并考察不同层在输出生成过程中的贡献。实证结果表明：（1）代码 LLM 既存在专门针对单一编程语言的神经元，也存在支撑通用代码生成的通用神经元集合；（2）低层主要捕捉各语言特有的语法结构，而高层抽象为可跨语言泛化的语义表示。我们进一步利用这些洞见增强三项下游任务：面向代码生成的神经元引导微调、使用概念层嵌入的克隆检测，以及由概念层表示引导的代码摘要迁移学习。实验评估显示，每种策略都能持续提升多语言代码 LLM 的性能。","tl":"定位语言特定/通用神经元，并用其改进三项下游代码任务。","au":["Zhe Yin","Xiaodong Gu","Beijun Shen"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"interpretability-and-model-internals","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["code LLM interpretability","neuron analysis","multilingual code","layer-wise representation","fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/135/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.19980"},{"id":"p00944","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Tuple-Oriented Sampling Method for Generating Small Pairwise Covering Arrays in Configurable Software Systems","tz":"面向可配置软件系统生成小规模成对覆盖数组的元组导向采样方法","a":"Pairwise testing is the most commonly used combinatorial interaction testing (CIT) technique to verify highly configurable systems, aiming to select the minimum number of testing configurations to cover all valid pairwise combinations of option values. The core problem of pairwise testing is the pairwise covering array generation (PCAG) problem. Existing PCAG methods typically struggle to generate small-scale pairwise covering arrays (PCA) for instances with complex constraints, or they require excessive computational time. To address these limitations, we propose DivSampCA, which employs a tuple-oriented adaptive sampling technique to enhance the diversity of the sampled configurations. Moreover, DivSampCA employs a novel full coverage strategy to ensure that the remaining uncovered pairwise tuples are covered with as few configurations as possible. We validate our method on 121 publicly available configurable system instances, and the experimental results show that DivSampCA achieves the smallest covering array in 71% of the instances, which is on average 15.54% smaller than that of other algorithms. Moreover, it is the fastest in 65% of the instances, reducing the average time by 42.36%. These results indicate that DivSampCA can generate smaller covering arrays in a shorter time and represents a significant advancement in solving the PCAG problem.","az":"成对测试是验证高可配置系统最常用的组合交互测试（CIT）技术，其目标是选出最少数量的测试配置以覆盖所有有效的选项取值成对组合。成对测试的核心问题是成对覆盖数组生成（PCAG）问题。现有 PCAG 方法通常难以为带复杂约束的实例生成小规模成对覆盖数组（PCA），或者需要过多的计算时间。为克服这些局限，我们提出 DivSampCA，它采用元组导向的自适应采样技术来提升所采样配置的多样性。此外，DivSampCA 采用一种新颖的全覆盖策略，确保用尽可能少的配置覆盖剩余未覆盖的成对元组。我们在 121 个公开可用的可配置系统实例上验证了该方法，实验结果表明 DivSampCA 在 71% 的实例上得到最小的覆盖数组，平均比其他算法小 15.54%；此外它在 65% 的实例上最快，平均时间减少 42.36%。这些结果表明 DivSampCA 能在更短时间内生成更小的覆盖数组，是求解 PCAG 问题的重大进展。","tl":"元组导向自适应采样生成更小更快的成对覆盖数组。","au":["Kaichen Chen","Yi Xiang","Haining Wang","Jiatong Ma","Fujian Feng","Miqing Li","Han Huang"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["combinatorial interaction testing","pairwise covering array","adaptive sampling","configurable systems","constraints"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/136/x"},{"id":"p00945","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Reducing Cost of LLM Agents with Trajectory Reduction","tz":"通过轨迹裁剪降低 LLM 智能体的成本","a":"Multi-turn agent systems based on Large Language Models (LLMs) have been increasingly popular for software engineering tasks. While LLM agents show decent effectiveness, the high computational cost of input tokens due to the ever-growing trajectory remains an efficiency concern for their applications. Efficiency is largely neglected in existing studies and agent products, and this paper fills the gap by introducing an inference-time trajectory reduction approach to reduce the cost of agents. Through analyzing existing agent trajectories, we demonstrate that useless, redundant, and expired information is widespread in all trajectories, which can be identified and reduced without harming the agent’s performance. We then design a simple yet effective trajectory reduction approach, AgentDiet, which automatically removes such waste information. We implement AgentDiet on a top-performing coding agent, and the evaluation on two LLMs and two benchmarks shows that AgentDiet can reduce input tokens by 39.9% ~ 59.7%, or the final computational cost by 21.1% ~ 35.9%, while maintaining the same agent performance. This indicates that trajectory reduction is a promising direction for agent systems.","az":"基于大语言模型（LLM）的多轮智能体系统在软件工程任务中日益流行。尽管 LLM 智能体展现出不错的有效性，但由于轨迹不断增长导致输入 token 的高计算成本，仍是其应用中的效率隐忧。效率问题在已有研究和智能体产品中大多被忽视，本文通过引入一种推理期轨迹裁剪方法来降低智能体成本，填补了这一空白。通过分析现有的智能体轨迹，我们表明无用、冗余和过期的信息在所有轨迹中普遍存在，并且可以在不损害智能体性能的前提下被识别与裁剪。随后我们设计了一种简单而有效的轨迹裁剪方法 AgentDiet，可自动移除这类浪费信息。我们在一个性能领先的编程智能体上实现了 AgentDiet，在两个 LLM 与两个基准上的评估表明，AgentDiet 能将输入 token 减少 39.9%~59.7%，或将最终计算成本降低 21.1%~35.9%，同时保持智能体性能不变。这表明轨迹裁剪是智能体系统一个有前景的方向。","tl":"自动删除轨迹中无用冗余过期信息，token 降近六成。","au":["Yuan-An Xiao","Pengfei Gao","Chao Peng","Yingfei Xiong"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["LLM agent","trajectory reduction","token cost","inference-time efficiency","coding agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/137/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.23586"},{"id":"p00946","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ReGA: Model-based Safeguard for LLMs via Representation-Guided Abstraction","tz":"ReGA：通过表示引导抽象为 LLM 构建基于模型的安全防护","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have achieved tremendous success in various tasks, yet concerns about their safety and security have emerged. In particular, they pose risks in generating harmful content and vulnerability to jailbreaking attacks, creating unaddressed security issues regarding their deployments. In the context of software engineering for artificial intelligence (SE4AI) techniques, model-based analysis has demonstrated notable potential for analyzing and monitoring machine learning models, particularly in stateful deep neural networks. However, it suffers from scalability issues when extended to LLMs due to their vast feature spaces. In this paper, we aim to address the scalability issue of model-based analysis techniques for safeguarding LLM-scale models. Motivated by the recent discovery of low-dimensional safety-critical representations that emerged in LLMs, we propose ReGA, a model-based analysis framework with Representation-Guided Abstraction, to safeguard LLMs against harmful prompts and generations. By leveraging safety-critical representations, which are key directions in hidden states that indicate safety-related concepts, ReGA effectively narrows the scalability gap when developing the abstract model for safety modeling. Our comprehensive evaluation shows that ReGA performs sufficiently well in distinguishing between safe and harmful inputs, achieving an AUROC of 0.975 at the prompt level and 0.985 at the conversation level. Additionally, ReGA exhibits robustness to real-world attacks and generalization across different safety perspectives, outperforming existing safeguard paradigms in terms of interpretability and scalability. Overall, ReGA serves as an efficient and scalable solution to enhance LLM safety by integrating representation engineering with model-based abstraction, paving the way for new paradigms to utilize software insights for AI safety. Our code is available in the supplementary materials.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已在各类任务中取得巨大成功，但对其安全性与安全防护的担忧随之出现。特别是，它们存在生成有害内容的风险，并易受越狱攻击，给部署带来尚未解决的安全问题。在面向人工智能的软件工程（SE4AI）技术脉络中，基于模型的分析在分析与监控机器学习模型方面已展现出显著潜力，尤其是对有状态的深度神经网络。然而，将其扩展到 LLM 时，由于 LLM 特征空间巨大，该方法面临可扩展性问题。本文旨在解决基于模型的分析技术在防护 LLM 规模模型时的可扩展性难题。受近期在 LLM 中发现的低维安全关键表示的启发，我们提出 ReGA，一种采用表示引导抽象的基于模型的分析框架，用以防护 LLM 免受有害提示与有害生成的影响。通过利用安全关键表示——即隐状态中指示安全相关概念的关键方向——ReGA 在构建用于安全建模的抽象模型时有效缩小了可扩展性差距。我们的全面评估显示，ReGA 在区分安全与有害输入方面表现足够出色，提示级 AUROC 达 0.975，对话级达 0.985。此外，ReGA 对真实世界攻击表现出鲁棒性，并能在不同安全视角间泛化，在可解释性与可扩展性方面优于现有的防护范式。总体而言，ReGA 通过将表示工程与基于模型的抽象相结合，为提升 LLM 安全提供了一种高效且可扩展的方案，为利用软件领域洞见服务 AI 安全开辟了新范式。代码见补充材料。","tl":"用安全关键表示做抽象建模，解决 LLM 护栏的可扩展性。","au":["Zeming Wei","Chengcan Wu","Meng Sun"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["cross-track-bridge","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["LLM safeguard","representation-guided abstraction","jailbreak","model-based analysis","SE4AI"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/138/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.01770"},{"id":"p00947","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TLR: Codebase-Level C Memory Management Error Repair with Large Language Models","tz":"TLR：用大语言模型进行代码库级的 C 内存管理错误修复","a":"Memory management errors in C remain a leading source of software vulnerabilities due to the inherent complexity of manual memory handling. Traditional Automated Program Repair (APR) largely relies on rule- or template-based techniques, which require expert-crafted specifications and often struggle to generalize. Recently, Large Language Models (LLMs) have emerged as a complementary approach, leveraging broad exposure to codebases and programming idioms to synthesize fixes that can extend beyond existing templates and rules. This paper introduces TLR, a novel framework that augments LLM-based repair with typestate-guided context retrieval. By using a finite typestate automaton to track error-propagation paths and memory state transitions, our approach provides the LLM with focused, semantically rich context for codebase-level memory error repair, effectively addressing both interprocedural reasoning and LLM context window limitations. Our framework has successfully repaired 37 out of 49 real-world memory errors derived from 14 open-source projects that collectively comprise over a million lines of code. Compared to state-of-the-art memory error APR tools, SAVER and ProveNFix, our approach correctly fixes 14.50× and 2.36× more errors, respectively. Moreover, TLR outperforms current open-source state-of-the-art LLM-based SWE-agent 1.0 by repairing 94% more errors. We have also successfully repaired three critical zero-day memory errors, with fixes that have been accepted and implemented by the original developers. These results highlight a promising paradigm for codebase-level program repair through program analysis-guided, retrieval-augmented LLMs, combining formal verification strengths with neural model adaptability.","az":"由于手工内存管理本身的复杂性，C 语言中的内存管理错误仍是软件漏洞的主要来源。传统的自动程序修复（APR）大多依赖基于规则或模板的技术，需要专家编写规约，且往往难以泛化。近来，大语言模型（LLM）作为一种互补途径涌现，它利用对大量代码库与编程惯用法的广泛接触来合成可超越既有模板和规则的修复。本文提出 TLR，一种以类型状态引导的上下文检索增强 LLM 修复的新框架。通过使用有限类型状态自动机跟踪错误传播路径与内存状态转移，我们的方法为 LLM 提供聚焦且语义丰富的上下文以完成代码库级内存错误修复，有效应对跨过程推理与 LLM 上下文窗口限制。我们的框架成功修复了源自 14 个开源项目（合计超过百万行代码）的 49 个真实内存错误中的 37 个。与最先进的内存错误 APR 工具 SAVER 和 ProveNFix 相比，我们的方法正确修复的错误分别多出 14.50 倍和 2.36 倍。此外，TLR 比当前开源最先进的 LLM 驱动 SWE-agent 1.0 多修复 94% 的错误。我们还成功修复了三个关键的零日内存错误，其修复已被原开发者接受并实施。这些结果凸显了通过程序分析引导、检索增强的 LLM 实现代码库级程序修复这一有前景的范式。","tl":"用类型状态自动机检索跨过程上下文喂给 LLM 修内存错误。","au":["Xiao Cheng","Zhihao Guo","Huan Huo","Yulei Sui"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["memory error repair","typestate automaton","context retrieval","LLM","codebase-level APR"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/139/x","pu":"https://jumormt.github.io/data/fse26_tlr.pdf"},{"id":"p00948","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Empirical Insights of Test Selection Metrics under Multiple Testing Objectives and Distribution Shifts","tz":"多重测试目标与分布偏移下测试选择指标的实证洞见","a":"Deep learning (DL)-based systems can exhibit unexpected behavior when exposed to out-of-distribution (OOD) scenarios, posing serious risks in safety-critical domains such as malware detection and autonomous driving. This underscores the importance of thoroughly testing such systems before deployment. To this end, researchers have proposed a wide range of test selection metrics designed to effectively select inputs. However, prior evaluations of metrics reveal three key limitations: (1) narrow testing objectives, for example, many studies assess metrics only for fault detection, leaving their effectiveness for performance estimation unclear; (2) limited coverage of OOD scenarios, with natural and label shifts are rarely considered; (3) Biased dataset selection, where most work focuses on image data while other modalities remain underexplored. Consequently, a unified benchmark that examines how these metrics perform under multiple testing objectives, diverse OOD scenarios, and different data modalities is still lacking. This leaves practitioners uncertain about which test selection metrics are most suitable for their specific objectives and contexts. To address this gap, we conduct an extensive empirical study of 15 existing metrics, evaluating them under three testing objectives (fault detection, performance estimation, and retraining guidance), five types of OOD scenarios (corrupted, adversarial, temporal, natural, and label shifts), three data modalities (image, text, and Android packages), and 13 DL models. In total, our study encompasses 1,640 experimental scenarios, offering a comprehensive evaluation and statistical analysis.","az":"基于深度学习（DL）的系统在面对分布外（OOD）场景时可能表现出意外行为，在恶意软件检测和自动驾驶等安全关键领域带来严重风险，这凸显了部署前对此类系统进行充分测试的重要性。为此，研究者提出了大量旨在有效选择输入的测试选择指标。然而，以往对这些指标的评估暴露出三个关键局限：（1）测试目标狭窄，例如许多研究只针对故障检测评估指标，其在性能估计方面的有效性仍不明确；（2）对 OOD 场景覆盖有限，自然偏移与标签偏移很少被考虑；（3）数据集选择有偏，多数工作聚焦图像数据，而其他模态探索不足。因此，仍然缺乏一个统一的基准来考察这些指标在多种测试目标、多样 OOD 场景和不同数据模态下的表现，这使从业者难以确定哪些测试选择指标最适合其特定目标与情境。为填补这一空白，我们对 15 种现有指标开展了广泛的实证研究，在三种测试目标（故障检测、性能估计、再训练指导）、五类 OOD 场景（损坏、对抗、时间、自然与标签偏移）、三种数据模态（图像、文本和 Android 安装包）以及 13 个 DL 模型下对其进行评估。总体而言，我们的研究涵盖 1,640 个实验场景，提供了全面的评估与统计分析。","tl":"1640 个场景横评 15 种 DL 测试选择指标的适用边界。","au":["Jingyu ZHANG","Fan Wang","Jacky Keung","Yihan Liao","Yan Xiao","Lei Ma"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["test selection metrics","out-of-distribution","deep learning testing","performance estimation","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/140/x","pu":"https://metricsbenchmark.github.io/FSE_ID1421_Camera_Ready.pdf"},{"id":"p00949","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PoCGen: Generating Proof-of-Concept Exploits for Vulnerabilities in Npm Packages","tz":"PoCGen：为 npm 包中的漏洞生成概念验证利用","a":"Security vulnerabilities in software packages are a significant concern for developers and users alike. Patching these vulnerabilities in a timely manner is crucial to restoring the integrity and security of software systems. However, previous work has shown that vulnerability reports often lack proof-of-concept (PoC) exploits, which are essential for fixing the vulnerability, testing patches, and avoiding regressions. Creating a PoC exploit is challenging because vulnerability reports are informal and often incomplete, and because it requires a detailed understanding of how inputs passed to potentially vulnerable APIs may reach security-relevant sinks. In this paper, we present PoCGen, a novel approach to autonomously generate and validate PoC exploits for vulnerabilities in npm packages. The approach is the first to address this task by combining the complementary strengths of large language models (LLMs), e.g., to understand informal vulnerability reports, with static analysis, e.g., to identify taint paths, and dynamic analysis, e.g., to validate generated exploits. PoCGen successfully generates exploits for 77% of the vulnerabilities in the SecBench.js dataset. This success rate significantly outperforms a recent baseline (by 45 absolute percentage points), while imposing an average cost of only $0.02 per generated exploit. Moreover, PoCGen generates six successful exploits for recent real-world vulnerabilities, five of which are now included in their respective vulnerability reports.","az":"软件包中的安全漏洞是开发者与用户共同关心的重要问题。及时修补这些漏洞对于恢复软件系统的完整性与安全性至关重要。然而，已有工作表明，漏洞报告往往缺少概念验证（PoC）利用，而后者对于修复漏洞、测试补丁和避免回归必不可少。构造 PoC 利用颇具挑战，因为漏洞报告是非正式的且常常不完整，并且需要详细理解传入潜在脆弱 API 的输入如何抵达安全相关的汇点。本文提出 PoCGen，一种自主为 npm 包漏洞生成并验证 PoC 利用的新方法。该方法首次通过结合大语言模型（LLM）的互补优势（例如理解非正式的漏洞报告）、静态分析（例如识别污点路径）与动态分析（例如验证生成的利用）来完成这一任务。PoCGen 成功为 SecBench.js 数据集中 77% 的漏洞生成了利用，该成功率显著超过近期基线（绝对高出 45 个百分点），而每个生成利用的平均成本仅为 0.02 美元。此外，PoCGen 还为近期的真实世界漏洞生成了六个成功的利用，其中五个现已被收录进相应的漏洞报告。","tl":"LLM 结合静态污点与动态验证自动产出可用 PoC 利用。","au":["Deniz Simsek","Aryaz Eghbali","Michael Pradel"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["proof-of-concept exploit","npm packages","taint analysis","LLM","vulnerability validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/141/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.04962"},{"id":"p00950","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AccessRefinery: Fast Mining Concise Access Control Intents on Public Cloud","tz":"AccessRefinery：在公有云上快速挖掘精简的访问控制意图","a":"Modern cloud applications heavily rely on Identity and Access Management (IAM) services to enforce flexible access control over their data. However, the flexibility comes at a cost: IAM policies are often complex and prone to misconfigurations, leading to risks of data exposure. There is an increasing need to mine a compact set of intents that describe what the policies collectively try to achieve, thereby enabling operators to better understand their policies. However, existing tools on mining access control intent have two major limitations: (1) the mining process is slow and even times out on some complex policies; (2) the mined intents are excessive in number and thus still hard to understand. To overcome these limitations, this paper presents AccessRefinery, which can speed up the mining process while reducing the number of intents. The key idea for the speedup is to reduce the redundancy of the multi-round SMT solving, by preprocessing the constraints into bit-vector constraints. For intent reduction, AccessRefinery computes a compact set of intents that can cover the mined intents, by solving a min-set-cover problem. Experiments based on real and synthetic datasets show that AccessRefinery achieves a ~10–100× speedup in intent mining, and reduces the number of intents by up to ~10×.","az":"现代云应用高度依赖身份与访问管理（IAM）服务来对其数据实施灵活的访问控制。然而，灵活性是有代价的：IAM 策略往往复杂且容易配置错误，导致数据暴露风险。人们越来越需要挖掘出一组紧凑的意图来描述这些策略共同试图达成的目标，从而帮助运维人员更好地理解自己的策略。然而，现有的访问控制意图挖掘工具存在两大局限：（1）挖掘过程缓慢，在某些复杂策略上甚至超时；（2）挖掘出的意图数量过多，因而仍然难以理解。为克服这些局限，本文提出 AccessRefinery，它能在加速挖掘过程的同时减少意图数量。加速的关键思路是把约束预处理为位向量约束，以降低多轮 SMT 求解的冗余。在意图精简方面，AccessRefinery 通过求解一个最小集合覆盖问题，计算出一组能够覆盖已挖掘意图的紧凑意图集合。基于真实与合成数据集的实验表明，AccessRefinery 在意图挖掘上实现约 10–100 倍加速，并将意图数量最多减少约 10 倍。","tl":"位向量预处理加最小集合覆盖，让 IAM 意图挖掘又快又少。","au":["Ning Kang","Peng Zhang","Jianyuan Zhang","Hao Li","Dan Wang","Zhenrong Gu","Weibo Lin","Shibiao Jiang","Zhu He","Xu Du","Longfei Chen","Jun Li","Xiaohong Guan"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["cloud IAM","access control policy","intent mining","SMT solving","min-set-cover"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/142/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797087"},{"id":"p00951","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ReDef: Do Code Language Models Truly Understand Code Changes for Just-in-Time Software Defect Prediction?","tz":"ReDef：代码语言模型真的理解代码变更从而做好即时缺陷预测吗？","a":"Just-in-Time software defect prediction (JIT-SDP) plays a critical role in prioritizing risky code changes during code review and continuous integration. However, existing datasets often suffer from noisy labels and low precision in identifying bug-inducing commits. To address this, we present ReDef (Revert-based Defect dataset), a high-confidence benchmark of function-level modifications curated from 22 large-scale C/C++ projects. Defective cases are anchored by revert commits, while clean cases are validated through post-hoc history checks. Ambiguous instances are conservatively filtered out via a GPT-assisted triage process involving multiple votes and audits. This pipeline yields 3,164 defective and 10,268 clean modifications, offering substantially more reliable labels than prior resources. Beyond dataset construction, we provide a systematic evaluation of how Code Language Models (CLMs)—specifically CodeBERT, CodeT5+, UniXcoder, and Qwen2.5—reason about code modifications. We first investigate which input encodings most effectively expose change information under five different strategies. We then design four counterfactual perturbation strategies (e.g., swapping added/deleted blocks, inverting diff polarity) to serve as diagnostic probes. We posit that if models genuinely capture change semantics, such distortions should lead to a clear decline in predictive performance. Our results show that compact diff-style encodings consistently outperform whole-function formats across all CLMs, supported by rigorous statistical confirmation. However, under counterfactual tests, performance remains effectively stable, revealing that what appears to be robustness in fact reflects a reliance on superficial cues rather than true semantic understanding. These findings indicate that, at least in code-change understanding tasks, current CLMs remain limited in their ability to genuinely comprehend the relational dynamics of code modifications.","az":"即时软件缺陷预测（JIT-SDP）在代码评审和持续集成中对高风险代码变更进行优先级排序方面发挥着关键作用。然而，已有数据集常常存在标签噪声大、识别引入缺陷提交的精确率低的问题。为此，我们提出了 ReDef（基于回滚的缺陷数据集），这是一个从 22 个大规模 C/C++ 项目中整理出的高置信度函数级修改基准。缺陷样本以回滚提交（revert commit）为锚点确定，干净样本则通过事后历史检查加以验证。歧义样本则通过 GPT 辅助的分诊流程（包含多轮投票与审计）被保守地过滤掉。该流水线最终产出 3,164 个缺陷修改和 10,268 个干净修改，提供了比以往资源可靠得多的标签。除数据集构建之外，我们还系统评估了代码语言模型（CLMs）——具体为 CodeBERT、CodeT5+、UniXcoder 和 Qwen2.5——是如何对代码修改进行推理的。我们首先在五种不同策略下考察哪种输入编码方式最有效地暴露变更信息。随后我们设计了四种反事实扰动策略（例如交换新增/删除代码块、反转 diff 极性）作为诊断探针。我们的假设是：如果模型真的捕捉到了变更语义，这类扰动应导致预测性能明显下降。结果表明，紧凑的 diff 式编码在所有 CLM 上都稳定优于整函数格式，并得到了严格的统计检验支持。然而在反事实测试下，性能实际上保持稳定，这揭示出看似的鲁棒性实则反映了模型依赖表层线索而非真正的语义理解。这些发现表明，至少在代码变更理解任务上，当前的 CLM 在真正理解代码修改的关系动态方面仍然有限。","tl":"用回滚提交构建高置信 JIT 数据集，并用反事实探针揭示模型只学表层线索。","au":["Doha Nam","Taehyoun Kim","Duksan Ryu","Jongmoon Baik"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["just-in-time defect prediction","revert commit dataset","code language models","counterfactual perturbation","code change understanding"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/143/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.09192"},{"id":"p00952","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards the Localization of Multi-Root-Cause Failures in Microservice Systems: An Active Intervention Framework","tz":"面向微服务系统多根因故障的定位：一种主动干预框架","a":"In large-scale microservice systems, multi-root-cause failures often intertwine, significantly increasing overall system risk and triggering a deluge of cascading alerts that pose serious challenges to fault diagnosis and recovery. Existing root-cause localization techniques remain largely passive, relying on rule-based pattern recognition or graph-based propagation inference, and thus falter when faced with the complexity of multi–root-cause failures. To address these challenges, this paper introduces a novel active-intervention-based framework for root-cause localization. This framework uses Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning (HRL) to infer root causes and employs an Intervention-enhanced Graph ATtention network (IGAT) to predict the fault scenarios each cause may trigger. By iteratively comparing these predicted scenarios against the system’s real-time state, the framework dynamically refines its localization model. Experimental results on two public datasets and a constructed dataset show that our method outperforms the second-best method by at least 22% on the PR@1 metric in single root cause scenarios and leads by 51.7% on the RE@3 metric in multiple root cause scenarios. This fully demonstrates its significant advantages in the field of fault root cause analysis.","az":"在大规模微服务系统中，多根因故障常常相互交织，显著提升系统整体风险，并引发大量级联告警，给故障诊断与恢复带来严峻挑战。已有的根因定位技术大多是被动的，依赖基于规则的模式识别或基于图的传播推断，因而在面对多根因故障的复杂性时表现不佳。为应对这些挑战，本文提出了一种新颖的基于主动干预的根因定位框架。该框架使用分层强化学习（HRL）推断根因，并采用干预增强的图注意力网络（IGAT）预测每个根因可能触发的故障场景。通过不断将这些预测场景与系统的实时状态进行比较，框架动态地精化其定位模型。在两个公开数据集和一个自建数据集上的实验结果表明，在单根因场景下我们的方法在 PR@1 指标上至少超过次优方法 22%，在多根因场景下在 RE@3 指标上领先 51.7%。这充分展示了其在故障根因分析领域的显著优势。","tl":"用分层强化学习加主动干预预测故障场景，攻克多根因定位。","au":["Yazhuo Gao","Lin Yang","Lianxiao Meng","Ran Zhu","Yining Cao"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["root cause localization","microservice","hierarchical reinforcement learning","graph attention network","active intervention"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/144/x"},{"id":"p00953","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Balancing Latency and Accuracy of Code Completion via Local-Cloud Model Cascading","tz":"通过本地-云端模型级联平衡代码补全的延迟与准确率","a":"Line-level code completion aims to complete the current line in real-time as developers type. Low latency is crucial to maintaining a seamless and uninterrupted coding experience, enabling developers to remain in a productive flow. However, existing approaches face a fundamental trade-off: large language models (LLMs) provide high-quality suggestions but require expensive computational resources to ensure acceptable inference latency. In contrast, static-analysis-based methods and small language models respond quickly but often generate suboptimal completions. To fill this gap, our idea is to rely on the small model by default and only escalate the large model when necessary to achieve latency-accuracy trade-offs. Based on this idea, we propose MCCom(Model-Cascading-based code Completion), a framework that cascades a local small model with a high-performance cloud large model for code completion. Realizing effective model cascading requires answering two non-trivial questions, i.e., when to invoke the large model and how to enable effective collaboration between small and large models. For the first question, we leverage a valuable but easily overlooked signal, i.e., user actions, during code completion to accurately identify failed completions. This deferral decision allows us to invoke the large model only when necessary, reducing both latency and cloud-side computation costs. To enable effective collaboration, MCCom employs a two-stage speculative decoding strategy and an iterative retrieval mechanism that collectively accelerate and improve the quality of completions. Due to the lack of high-quality small models for code completion, we also train a lightweight model with only 121M parameters to implement MCCom. The small model achieves an average of 73.8% of the performance of the state-of-the-art 7B model. We evaluate MCCom on the RepoEval benchmark and a new benchmark, StmtEval, collected from real-world projects. Experimental results show that our approach not only reduces inference latency by up to 47.9% and cuts down LLM usage by an average of 46.3%, but also improves the exact match rate of the large model by an average of 8.9%.","az":"行级代码补全旨在开发者输入时实时补全当前行。低延迟对于保持流畅不中断的编码体验、让开发者维持高效心流至关重要。然而，已有方法面临一个根本性的权衡：大语言模型（LLM）能提供高质量建议，但需要昂贵的计算资源才能保证可接受的推理延迟；相反，基于静态分析的方法和小模型响应很快，却常常生成次优的补全。为填补这一空白，我们的想法是默认依赖小模型，仅在必要时升级到大模型，从而实现延迟与准确率的折中。基于此，我们提出 MCCom（基于模型级联的代码补全），一个将本地小模型与高性能云端大模型级联起来做代码补全的框架。实现有效的模型级联需要回答两个非平凡的问题：何时调用大模型，以及如何让大小模型有效协作。对第一个问题，我们利用了一个有价值却易被忽视的信号，即代码补全过程中的用户行为，来准确识别失败的补全。这一推迟决策使我们只在必要时调用大模型，从而同时降低延迟与云端计算成本。为实现有效协作，MCCom 采用两阶段投机解码策略和迭代检索机制，共同加速并提升补全质量。由于缺乏高质量的代码补全小模型，我们还训练了一个仅 121M 参数的轻量模型来实现 MCCom。该小模型平均达到了最先进 7B 模型 73.8% 的性能。我们在 RepoEval 基准和一个从真实项目收集的新基准 StmtEval 上评估 MCCom。实验结果表明，我们的方法不仅将推理延迟最多降低 47.9%、平均减少 46.3% 的 LLM 调用，还将大模型的精确匹配率平均提升了 8.9%。","tl":"用用户行为信号决定何时升级到云端大模型的补全级联方案。","au":["Lu Hanzhen","Lishui Fan","Jiachi Chen","Qiuyuan Chen","Zhao Wei","Zhongxin Liu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code completion","model cascading","speculative decoding","latency-accuracy trade-off","small language model"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/145/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.05974"},{"id":"p00954","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LoCaL: Countering Surface Bias in Code Evaluation Metrics","tz":"LoCaL：对抗代码评估指标中的表层偏差","a":"With the increasing popularity of large language models (LLMs) and LLM-based agents, reliable and effective code evaluation metrics (CEMs) have become crucial for progress across several software engineering tasks. While popular benchmarks often provide test cases to assess the correctness of generated code, crafting and executing test cases is expensive. Reference-based CEMs provide a cheaper alternative by scoring a candidate program based on its functional similarity to a reference. Although prior research has focused on reporting the weak correlation between these CEMs and functional correctness, the causes are only assumed, and plausible solutions remain unexplored. In this work, we critically evaluate four state-of-the-art reference-based CEMs, revealing their strong bias towards surface-level features rather than code functionality. Despite this surface bias, current evaluation datasets for these CEMs rarely include code pairs that are surface-similar yet functionally dissimilar, or functionally similar yet surface-dissimilar. To mitigate this gap, we propose LoCaL ( Looks Can Lie), a CEM evaluation benchmark, with 3117 code pairs at both the method and program levels. Each pair is labeled with a functional similarity score and aims to target regions where CEMs are likely to perform poorly. The functional similarity scores are calculated through differential fuzzing, which eliminates the need for predefined test cases and, at the same time, improves the reliability of the scores by executing an order of magnitude more tests than prior work. We find that all four CEMs show significant performance degradation on LoCaL, compared to the baselines. Finally, based on our findings, we draw the implication that exposing CEMs to LoCaL-like data might facilitate the development of metrics that are robust to surface bias.","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）和基于 LLM 的智能体日益流行，可靠且有效的代码评估指标（CEM）对多项软件工程任务的进展变得至关重要。虽然流行基准通常提供测试用例来评估生成代码的正确性，但编写和执行测试用例代价高昂。基于参考的 CEM 提供了更廉价的替代方案，即依据候选程序与参考实现的功能相似度来打分。尽管以往研究主要报告了这类 CEM 与功能正确性之间的弱相关性，其成因却只是被假定，可行的解决方案仍未被探索。在本工作中，我们批判性地评估了四种最先进的基于参考的 CEM，揭示了它们强烈偏向表层特征而非代码功能。尽管存在这种表层偏差，当前用于评估这些 CEM 的数据集却很少包含表层相似但功能不同、或功能相似但表层不同的代码对。为弥补这一缺口，我们提出 LoCaL（Looks Can Lie），一个 CEM 评估基准，包含方法级和程序级共 3117 对代码。每一对都标注了功能相似度分数，并刻意针对 CEM 可能表现不佳的区域。功能相似度分数通过差分模糊测试计算，这既免除了预定义测试用例的需求，又因执行的测试数量比以往工作多一个数量级而提高了分数的可靠性。我们发现，相比基线，四种 CEM 在 LoCaL 上都出现了显著的性能下降。最后，基于这些发现，我们提出一个启示：让 CEM 接触 LoCaL 这类数据，或许有助于开发出对表层偏差鲁棒的指标。","tl":"用差分模糊测试造出表层与功能解耦的代码对，戳穿参考型代码指标。","au":["Simantika Bhattacharjee Dristi","Matthew B Dwyer"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study"],"kw":["code evaluation metrics","surface bias","differential fuzzing","functional similarity","benchmark"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/146/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.15397"},{"id":"p00955","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ExpeRepair: Dual-Memory Enhanced LLM-based Repository-Level Program Repair","tz":"ExpeRepair：双记忆增强的基于 LLM 的仓库级程序修复","a":"Automatically repairing software issues remains a fundamental challenge at the intersection of software engineering and AI. Although recent advancements in Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated potential for repository-level repair tasks, current methodologies exhibit two notable limitations: (1) they often address issues in isolation, neglecting to incorporate insights from previously resolved issues, and (2) they rely on static, rigid prompting strategies that constrain their ability to generalize across diverse and evolving issue scenarios. We propose ExpeRepair, a novel LLM-based program repair framework inspired by the dual memory systems of human cognition, where episodic and semantic memory synergistically support learning and decision-making. Unlike existing methods, ExpeRepair continuously learns from historical repair experiences via dual-channel knowledge accumulation, enabling it to adaptively reuse past knowledge during inference. Specifically, ExpeRepair organizes prior repair knowledge into two complementary memories: an episodic memory that stores concrete repair demonstrations, and a semantic memory that encodes abstract, reflective insights. At inference time, ExpeRepair activates both memory systems by retrieving relevant demonstrations from episodic memory and recalling high-level repair insights from semantic memory. It further enhances adaptability through dynamic prompt composition, synergistically integrating both memory types to replace static prompts with context-aware, experience-driven prompts. We evaluate ExpeRepair on two benchmarks: SWE-Bench Lite and SWE-Bench Verified. Experimental results show that ExpeRepair achieves Pass@1 scores of 60.3% and 74.6% on the two benchmarks, respectively, establishing new state-of-the-art performance among open-source methods. We have open-sourced ExpeRepair at https://github.com/ExpeRepair/ExpeRepair .","az":"自动修复软件问题仍是软件工程与人工智能交叉处的一个根本挑战。尽管大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展在仓库级修复任务上展现出潜力，现有方法仍表现出两个明显局限：（1）它们往往孤立地处理每个 issue，忽视了从以往已解决问题中吸取经验；（2）它们依赖静态、僵化的提示策略，限制了在多样且不断演化的问题场景中的泛化能力。我们提出 ExpeRepair，一个受人类认知双记忆系统启发的基于 LLM 的程序修复框架，其中情景记忆与语义记忆协同支撑学习与决策。与现有方法不同，ExpeRepair 通过双通道知识累积持续从历史修复经验中学习，使其能在推理时自适应地复用过去的知识。具体而言，ExpeRepair 将既往修复知识组织为两种互补的记忆：存储具体修复示例的情景记忆，以及编码抽象反思性洞见的语义记忆。在推理时，ExpeRepair 同时激活两套记忆系统，从情景记忆中检索相关示例，并从语义记忆中调取高层修复洞见。它进一步通过动态提示组合增强适应性，协同整合两类记忆，用情景感知、经验驱动的提示替代静态提示。我们在两个基准 SWE-Bench Lite 和 SWE-Bench Verified 上评估 ExpeRepair。实验结果表明，ExpeRepair 在两个基准上分别取得了 60.3% 和 74.6% 的 Pass@1 分数，在开源方法中确立了新的最先进水平。我们已在 https://github.com/ExpeRepair/ExpeRepair 开源 ExpeRepair。","tl":"引入情景+语义双记忆，让修复智能体复用历史经验并动态组合提示。","au":["Fangwen Mu","Junjie Wang","Lin Shi","Song Wang","Shoubin Li","Qing Wang"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["repository-level repair","episodic memory","semantic memory","SWE-Bench","dynamic prompt composition"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/147/x"},{"id":"p00956","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Bringing Managed Language Support to WebAssembly with External Library Linking","tz":"通过外部库链接为 WebAssembly 带来托管语言支持","a":"WebAssembly (Wasm) has emerged as a powerful bytecode format for running applications with near-native performance in portable and secure environments. However, while Wasm currently supports compiled languages like C, C++, and Rust, it lacks robust support for managed languages such as Python, Java, and JavaScript. This limitation hinders the deployment of applications in domains like machine learning and data processing that rely heavily on managed language ecosystems. To address this, we propose WALL-E, a novel framework to integrate managed languages into Wasm environments without complex runtime nesting or recompilation. WALL-E employs a unique external library linking strategy, using a client-server architecture to connect Wasm modules with managed language libraries running in their native runtimes. This approach preserves the native execution speed and language feature compatibility of managed languages by eliminating the overhead associated with double-layer virtual machines. Our evaluation shows that WALL-E supports ten managed languages without framework modifications and achieves a speedup of hundreds of times over the runtime nesting solution, with low communication overhead. WALL-E enhances the practicality of Wasm in cloud and edge computing, enabling efficient multi-language applications.","az":"WebAssembly（Wasm）已成为一种强大的字节码格式，可在可移植且安全的环境中以接近原生的性能运行应用。然而，虽然 Wasm 目前支持 C、C++ 和 Rust 等编译型语言，它对 Python、Java、JavaScript 等托管语言缺乏健壮支持。这一局限阻碍了机器学习与数据处理等高度依赖托管语言生态的领域中的应用部署。为此，我们提出 WALL-E，一个无需复杂运行时嵌套或重新编译即可将托管语言集成进 Wasm 环境的新框架。WALL-E 采用独特的外部库链接策略，通过客户端-服务器架构把 Wasm 模块与运行在其原生运行时中的托管语言库连接起来。该方法消除了双层虚拟机带来的开销，从而保留了托管语言的原生执行速度与语言特性兼容性。我们的评估表明，WALL-E 无需修改框架即可支持十种托管语言，相比运行时嵌套方案实现了数百倍的加速，且通信开销很低。WALL-E 提升了 Wasm 在云计算与边缘计算中的实用性，使高效的多语言应用成为可能。","tl":"用外部库链接替代运行时嵌套，让 Wasm 原生跑十种托管语言。","au":["Shuyao Jiang","Ruiying Zeng","Yangfan Zhou","Michael Lyu"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["WebAssembly","managed languages","external library linking","runtime nesting","edge computing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/148/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.21919"},{"id":"p00957","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SBridge: Identifying Source-to-Binary Function Similarity via Cross-Domain Control Block Matching","tz":"SBridge：通过跨域控制块匹配识别源码到二进制的函数相似性","a":"We present SBridge, a precise approach for identifying functions in binaries that are similar to the given source code functions. Identifying reused code in binaries is critical for security, particularly for detecting propagated vulnerabilities. Although binary-to-binary comparison is feasible, leveraging source code as the reference is more practical because source code is easier to collect and analyze directly without compilation. However, significant gaps between source and binary representations, including function inlining, create challenges in cross-domain function detection. Existing approaches primarily rely on string literals or structural similarities between entire functions, failing to capture detailed code behavior and generating many false alarms. SBridge addresses these limitations through a key innovation: control block-based function matching, which encapsulates essential functional features by segmenting functions into meaningful units such as conditionals and loops. Leveraging control blocks as a cross-domain representation, SBridge enables precise measurement of function similarity between source and binary code, effectively overcoming challenges posed by function inlining and stripped binaries. For evaluation, we collected 3,904 real-world C/C++ binaries from BinKit. In experiments identifying binary functions identical to input source functions, despite approximately 40% of binary functions being inlined, SBridge achieved 75.13% recall@1 and 80.98% recall@5, outperforming existing approaches, which achieved up to 43.31% recall@1 and 50.2% recall@5. Our further analysis confirmed that SBridge effectively identifies propagated vulnerabilities in binaries.","az":"我们提出 SBridge，一种在二进制中精确识别与给定源码函数相似的函数的方法。识别二进制中被复用的代码对安全至关重要，尤其是检测传播性漏洞。虽然二进制对二进制的比较是可行的，但以源码作为参照更实用，因为源码更易收集、且无需编译即可直接分析。然而，源码与二进制表示之间存在显著差距，包括函数内联，这给跨域函数检测带来了挑战。已有方法主要依赖字符串字面量或整函数级的结构相似性，无法捕捉细粒度的代码行为，产生大量误报。SBridge 通过一项关键创新解决了这些局限：基于控制块的函数匹配，即把函数切分为条件语句和循环等有意义的单元，从而封装本质的功能特征。利用控制块作为跨域表示，SBridge 能精确度量源码与二进制代码之间的函数相似性，有效克服函数内联和剥离符号二进制带来的挑战。在评估中，我们从 BinKit 收集了 3,904 个真实世界的 C/C++ 二进制。在识别与输入源码函数相同的二进制函数的实验中，尽管约 40% 的二进制函数被内联，SBridge 仍取得了 75.13% 的 recall@1 和 80.98% 的 recall@5，优于已有方法最高 43.31% 的 recall@1 和 50.2% 的 recall@5。我们的进一步分析确认，SBridge 能有效识别二进制中的传播性漏洞。","tl":"以条件与循环构成的控制块作跨域表示，克服内联做源码-二进制匹配。","au":["Heedong Yang","Jeongwoo Lee","Hajin Yun","Seunghoon Woo"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["source-to-binary matching","code similarity","control block","function inlining","vulnerability propagation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/149/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.28058"},{"id":"p00958","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Unleashing HPC Application Performance through Software Deployment: A Joint Model of Software Parallelism and Co-location","tz":"通过软件部署释放 HPC 应用性能：软件并行性与共置的联合模型","a":"Software deployment is a critical software engineering practice, particularly for high performance computing (HPC) software. The deployment determines the software execution performance because the deployment maps a number of software components to multiple CPUs in a server. Inappropriate mapping decreases software parallelism and increases resource contention due to software co-location on the same CPUs. However, calculating the mapping to maximize the software performance is challenging, primarily due to the lack of a joint performance model that accounts for both software parallelism and co-location. Consequently, existing industry practice has to rely on experienced engineers to manually tune the mapping during deployment, resulting in substantial human resource waste of man-months and suboptimal software performance. This paper proposes a holistic approach to mapping multiple CPUs among multiple software components to achieve better applicability and performance. We develop a performance model for predicting performance impact of different CPU mapping configurations, along with a search algorithm to identify the best mapping scheme. Our performance model jointly considers software parallelism and co-location, breaks the performance estimation into regularized execution and interference coefficient to improve accuracy, and integrates expert knowledge to reduce the model complexity. Our search algorithm employs nested iterative packing algorithm to explore all possible mapping schemes, thereby uncovering the optimal solution. Evaluation on a multi-module HPC application shows 17% better performance than its default CPU mapping Our solution has been deployed in a commercial HPC cluster with more than 50K CPU cores, delivering 26.5% performance improvement and saving many man-months effort spent on performance tuning.","az":"软件部署是一项关键的软件工程实践，对高性能计算（HPC）软件尤其如此。部署决定了软件的执行性能，因为部署把若干软件组件映射到服务器中的多个 CPU 上。不当的映射会降低软件并行性，并因软件共置于同一 CPU 而加剧资源争用。然而，计算出使软件性能最大化的映射颇具挑战，主要原因在于缺少一个同时考虑软件并行性与共置的联合性能模型。因此，现有工业实践不得不依赖经验丰富的工程师在部署时手工调优映射，造成大量人月级的人力浪费和次优的软件性能。本文提出一种整体性方法，在多个软件组件之间映射多个 CPU，以获得更好的适用性与性能。我们构建了一个性能模型来预测不同 CPU 映射配置的性能影响，并配以一个搜索算法来找出最佳映射方案。我们的性能模型联合考虑软件并行性与共置，把性能估计拆解为规范化执行与干扰系数以提升精度，并融入专家知识以降低模型复杂度。我们的搜索算法采用嵌套迭代装箱算法来探索所有可能的映射方案，从而找出最优解。在一个多模块 HPC 应用上的评估显示，其性能比默认 CPU 映射高出 17%。我们的方案已部署于一个拥有超过 5 万 CPU 核的商用 HPC 集群，带来 26.5% 的性能提升，并节省了大量用于性能调优的人月投入。","tl":"首个联合建模并行性与共置的 CPU 映射性能模型，已在 5 万核集群落地。","au":["Yuxin Ren","li zhou","Chumin Sun","Rui Fan","Jie Sun","Ning Jia","Xinwei Hu"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["HPC deployment","CPU mapping","performance model","software co-location","search algorithm"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/150/x"},{"id":"p00959","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CrypFormBench: Benchmarking Formal Analysis Capability of Large Language Models for Cryptographic schemes","tz":"CrypFormBench：评测大语言模型对密码方案形式化分析的能力","a":"Manual formal analysis of cryptographic schemes is a labor-intensive and expertise-demanding task. While model-checking tools (e.g., Scyther and Tamarin) and computational-security tools (e.g., CryptoVerif and EasyCrypt) significantly enhance the automation of security proofs, they still require experts to abstract schemes and write formal descriptions in specialized languages. Large language models (LLMs) can offer a promising alternative, while their effectiveness in this domain remains unexplored, and the absence of standardized evaluation methodologies makes their capabilities difficult to assess. To address the gaps, we introduce CrypFormBench (C.F.B for short), a comprehensive benchmark supporting both symbolic and computational security, designed to systematically evaluate 5 core capabilities of LLMs in formal analysis of cryptographic schemes, including formal code interpretation, generation, completion, transformation, and correction. It comprises 700 instances covering 7 mainstream formal languages and 677 schemes, supporting the verification of 160 security properties. The evaluation of 9 state-of-the-art LLMs reveals that most of them perform well in code interpretation and completion due to their code-awareness advantages, but struggle to achieve code generation, cross-language transformation, and false-positive correction. Overall, LLMs exhibit limited effectiveness in formal analysis of cryptographic schemes, with only Claude-3.5 scoring above 50 out of 100. Based on our findings, we propose practical recommendations for the model design and usage, such as fine-tuning and few-shot mechanisms, to bolster LLMs’ effectiveness in securing cryptographic schemes. Taken together, our analysis of LLMs’ formal analysis capabilities in cryptographic schemes highlights current progress and outlines directions for future improvements.","az":"对密码方案进行人工形式化分析是一项劳动密集且高度依赖专业知识的任务。虽然模型检测工具（如 Scyther 和 Tamarin）和计算安全性工具（如 CryptoVerif 和 EasyCrypt）显著提升了安全证明的自动化程度，它们仍需要专家去抽象方案并用专门语言编写形式化描述。大语言模型（LLM）可以提供一种有前景的替代方案，但其在该领域的有效性仍未被探索，而缺乏标准化的评测方法也使其能力难以评估。为填补这些空白，我们提出 CrypFormBench（简称 C.F.B），一个同时支持符号安全性与计算安全性的综合基准，用于系统评测 LLM 在密码方案形式化分析中的 5 项核心能力，包括形式化代码解释、生成、补全、转换与纠错。它包含 700 个实例，覆盖 7 种主流形式化语言和 677 个方案，支持 160 条安全性质的验证。对 9 个最先进 LLM 的评测表明，得益于代码感知优势，大多数模型在代码解释与补全上表现良好，但在代码生成、跨语言转换和误报纠正上举步维艰。总体而言，LLM 在密码方案形式化分析中的有效性有限，仅 Claude-3.5 在百分制中得分超过 50。基于这些发现，我们提出了面向模型设计与使用的实用建议，例如微调和少样本机制，以增强 LLM 在保障密码方案安全方面的效力。总体来看，我们对 LLM 在密码方案形式化分析能力上的分析既刻画了当前进展，也指出了未来改进的方向。","tl":"首个覆盖 7 种形式化语言、5 项能力的密码方案形式化分析 LLM 基准。","au":["Zhaoxuan Li","Qionglu Zhang","Hengyuan Liu","Xiaoyan Gu","Xianhui Lu","Hongbo Liu","Bingzheng Wang","Haihui Fan","Ziming Zhao","Rui Zhang","Li Zhou"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","security"],"kw":["cryptographic scheme","formal analysis benchmark","Tamarin / EasyCrypt","LLM evaluation","security properties"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/151/x","pu":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.25561"},{"id":"p00960","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Failure-Based Testing for Deep Reinforcement Learning Agents","tz":"面向深度强化学习智能体的基于失效的测试","a":"Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) agents have been widely adopted across diverse domains to address challenging decision-making problems, such as autonomous driving and robotic control. Given that many of these applications are safety- and security-critical, rigorous testing of DRL agents is indispensable. Existing testing methods are typically guided by reward signals to detect failures. However, for well-trained agents, whose performance approaches optimal levels in standard operating conditions, reward signals remain generally high, making current methods ineffective at uncovering critical failures. To address the challenges, we propose a novel failure-based method that leverages task-induced failure insights to improve the efficiency of DRL agent testing. Since DRL agents are inherently designed with human-defined tasks, they provide valuable cues about task difficulty. By intuition, a DRL agent is more likely to fail when confronted with a more difficult task, so we prioritize testing the most difficult task. Building on this foundation, we propose Prior Random Testing, a black-box failure-based testing method that enables targeted prioritization while preserving the diversity of generated test cases. Guided by task-induced failure insights, PRT prioritizes failure-prone regions of the input domain, thereby facilitating efficient failure detection. PRT is evaluated on three widely used benchmarks and compared with different state-of-the-art methods including fuzzing, search-based and generative-based methods. PRT ranks among the top performers in terms of both the cost for finding the first failure and the diversity of test cases.","az":"深度强化学习（DRL）智能体已被广泛应用于各类领域，用以解决自动驾驶和机器人控制等具有挑战性的决策问题。鉴于其中许多应用是安全关键和安保关键的，对 DRL 智能体进行严格测试不可或缺。现有测试方法通常以奖励信号为引导来发现失效。然而，对于训练充分、在标准运行条件下性能接近最优的智能体而言，奖励信号普遍较高，使得当前方法难以揭示关键失效。为应对这些挑战，我们提出一种新颖的基于失效的方法，利用任务诱导的失效洞见来提升 DRL 智能体测试的效率。由于 DRL 智能体本质上是围绕人为定义的任务设计的，这些任务提供了关于任务难度的宝贵线索。直觉上，智能体在面对更困难的任务时更可能失败，因此我们优先测试最困难的任务。在此基础上，我们提出先验随机测试（Prior Random Testing, PRT），一种黑盒的基于失效的测试方法，既能实现有针对性的优先级排序，又能保持生成测试用例的多样性。在任务诱导失效洞见的引导下，PRT 优先探索输入域中易失效的区域，从而促进高效的失效检测。我们在三个广泛使用的基准上评估 PRT，并与包括模糊测试、基于搜索和基于生成的方法在内的多种最先进方法进行比较。在发现首个失效的代价和测试用例多样性两方面，PRT 均位居前列。","tl":"用任务难度先验而非奖励信号引导 DRL 智能体测试，优先探索易失效区域。","au":["Weibin Lin","Jiangtao Meng","Zheng Zheng"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DRL agent testing","failure-based testing","task difficulty prior","black-box testing","test diversity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/152/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.31372"},{"id":"p00961","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"EventADL: Open-Box Anomaly Detection and Localization Framework for Events in Cloud-Based Service Systems","tz":"EventADL：面向云服务系统事件的开箱式异常检测与定位框架","a":"Anomaly detection and localization (ADL) is critical for maintaining high reliability and availability in cloud-based systems. Recent ADL developments focus on metric and log data, leaving event data relatively unexplored. To address this gap, we propose EventADL, the first open-box ADL framework for events in cloud-based service systems. To motivate the design of our framework, we conduct a systematic analysis on 520 real-world incidents, and provide several important insights into how anomalies and their root causes manifest through event data. The EventADL framework has three phases: offline training, online anomaly detection, and anomaly localization. During the training phase, EventADL learns Event Semantic Patterns (ESPs) for pointwise anomaly detection and Event Frequency Patterns (EFPs) for frequency-based anomaly detection using unlabelled historical data. In the online anomaly detection phase, any data in the event stream that deviates significantly from these patterns is identified as anomalous. In the localization phase, EventADL constructs an Intervention Graph that models the relationships between recent interventions (i.e., system changes visible through events) and the detected anomalies for automatic root cause localization. The framework is designed to operate efficiently without labeled data , and to produce interpretable results. Our evaluation on three real cloud-based service systems and two real-world incidents, compared against ten state-of-the-art baselines, demonstrates that EventADL outperforms existing methods, achieving F1-scores of at least 90% for anomaly detection and 100% top-3 accuracy in anomaly localization.","az":"异常检测与定位（ADL）对维持云端系统的高可靠性与高可用性至关重要。近期 ADL 研究主要聚焦于指标和日志数据，而事件数据相对未被充分探索。为填补这一空白，我们提出 EventADL，首个面向云服务系统事件的开箱式（open-box）ADL 框架。为指导框架设计，我们对 520 个真实事故进行了系统分析，得出若干关于异常及其根因如何在事件数据中体现的重要洞见。EventADL 框架包含三个阶段：离线训练、在线异常检测和异常定位。在训练阶段，EventADL 利用无标注的历史数据学习用于逐点异常检测的事件语义模式（ESP）和用于基于频率的异常检测的事件频率模式（EFP）。在在线异常检测阶段，事件流中任何显著偏离这些模式的数据都会被判定为异常。在定位阶段，EventADL 构建一个干预图（Intervention Graph），对近期干预（即通过事件可见的系统变更）与检测到的异常之间的关系进行建模，以实现自动根因定位。该框架被设计为无需标注数据即可高效运行，并产出可解释的结果。我们在三个真实云服务系统和两起真实事故上、对照十个最先进基线进行评估，结果表明 EventADL 优于现有方法，异常检测的 F1 分数至少达到 90%，异常定位的 top-3 准确率达到 100%。","tl":"首个基于事件语义与频率模式、并用干预图定位根因的无监督 ADL 框架。","au":["Luan Pham","Victor Nicolet","Joey Dodds","Hui Guan","Daniel Kroening"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["anomaly detection","event data","root cause localization","cloud service systems","intervention graph"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/153/x","pu":"https://www.amazon.science/publications/eventadl-open-box-anomaly-detection-and-localization-framework-for-events-in-cloud-based-service-systems"},{"id":"p00962","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"OCPPuzz: Specification-driven Fuzzing of Charging Station Management Systems with Large Language Model","tz":"OCPPuzz：结合大语言模型的充电站管理系统规约驱动模糊测试","a":"Electric vehicles (EVs) are being rapidly adopted, with over 61,000 publicly accessible charging stations deployed across the United States as of 2024. A core component of this infrastructure is the Charging Station Management System (CSMS), which is responsible for security-critical tasks such as user authentication and billing. Given its importance, the CSMS has become a target of real-world attacks that have resulted in financial losses, data breaches, and denial-of-service(DoS) incidents. Nevertheless, research on CSMS security remains limited, and automated testing tools are lacking. Testing CSMS is challenging because they communicate with charging stations (CS) using the Open Charge Point Protocol (OCPP). Effective testing must contend with OCPP’s complexity: 1) messages containing up to 48 fields, 2) inter- and intra-message field dependencies, and 3) its stateful nature, which requires tracking the states of both CS and CSMS during testing. To address these challenges, we present OCPPuzz, a specification-based fuzzing framework for CSMS. OCPPuzz automatically extracts message structures, field constraints, and dependency rules from the OCPP specification, as well as valid CS-CSMS state transitions described in its use case diagrams. To handle specifications expressed in natural language and semi-formal diagrams, OCPPuzz combines heuristic rule-based extraction with large language models (LLMs). We evaluated OCPPuzz on four open-source CSMS implementations and uncovered numerous deviations from the OCPP specification that led to critical security issues, including DoS and free charging. We reported 930 implementation bugs to the corresponding vendors, of which 492 have been acknowledged so far. In addition, we reported 134 specification bugs in OCPP to the Open Charge Alliance (OCA); 79 have been committed for fixes and 85 acknowledged for further investigation. We expect additional acknowledgments and fixes in the near future.","az":"电动汽车（EV）正在被迅速普及，截至 2024 年美国已部署超过 61,000 个公共充电站。该基础设施的核心组件是充电站管理系统（CSMS），它负责用户认证与计费等安全关键任务。鉴于其重要性，CSMS 已成为真实攻击的目标，导致了经济损失、数据泄露和拒绝服务（DoS）事件。然而，针对 CSMS 安全的研究仍然有限，自动化测试工具也十分匮乏。测试 CSMS 颇具挑战，因为它们通过开放充电点协议（OCPP）与充电桩（CS）通信。有效的测试必须应对 OCPP 的复杂性：1）消息最多包含 48 个字段；2）消息间与消息内的字段依赖；3）其有状态特性，要求测试过程中同时跟踪 CS 与 CSMS 的状态。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 OCPPuzz，一个面向 CSMS 的基于规约的模糊测试框架。OCPPuzz 自动从 OCPP 规约中抽取消息结构、字段约束和依赖规则，以及其用例图中描述的合法 CS-CSMS 状态转换。为处理以自然语言和半形式化图表表达的规约，OCPPuzz 将启发式规则抽取与大语言模型（LLM）相结合。我们在四个开源 CSMS 实现上评估 OCPPuzz，发现了大量偏离 OCPP 规约之处，并导致包括 DoS 和免费充电在内的严重安全问题。我们向相应厂商报告了 930 个实现缺陷，其中 492 个已被确认。此外，我们向开放充电联盟（OCA）报告了 134 个 OCPP 规约缺陷，其中 79 个已被提交修复，85 个被确认需进一步调查。我们预计近期还会有更多确认与修复。","tl":"用 LLM 从自然语言规约抽出字段约束与状态机，实现有状态 CSMS 模糊测试。","au":["Jongchan Hong","Jaewon Kim","Sungjae Hwang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["security","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["specification-based fuzzing","OCPP protocol","charging station management system","stateful testing","LLM-assisted extraction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/154/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797091"},{"id":"p00963","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GAER: Graph Auto-Encoders for Unsupervised Software Architecture Recovery","tz":"GAER：用于无监督软件架构恢复的图自编码器","a":"Recovering the modular architecture of software systems from source code is a longstanding challenge, especially when documentation is incomplete or outdated. Manual recovery is labor-intensive, error-prone, and does not scale to large systems. While automated approaches have been proposed, many rely on handcrafted heuristics or focus narrowly on either structural or semantic information, which limits their ability to capture the full range of architectural signals. We introduce GAER, an unsupervised architecture recovery approach based on graph auto-encoders (GAEs) that frames architecture recovery as a representation learning problem. Software systems are modeled as heterogeneous graphs with typed dependencies, while folder hierarchies and code semantics are incorporated as node features. We evaluate two encoder variants, GAT and GCN, and find that GAT generally yields more accurate and stable decompositions. Experiments on ten open-source systems with ground-truth architectures show that GAER improves recovery accuracy by about 30% on average across evaluation metrics compared to a state-of-the-art method. By automatically deriving architectural views that integrate multiple signals, GAER reduces the manual effort required to maintain architectural documentation and supports more effective system understanding.","az":"从源码中恢复软件系统的模块化架构是一个长期存在的挑战，尤其是在文档不完整或过时的情况下。人工恢复既费力又易错，且无法扩展到大型系统。虽然已有自动化方法被提出，但许多依赖手工启发式规则，或仅狭隘地关注结构信息或语义信息之一，限制了它们捕捉完整架构信号的能力。我们提出 GAER，一种基于图自编码器（GAE）的无监督架构恢复方法，它把架构恢复形式化为一个表示学习问题。软件系统被建模为带类型依赖的异构图，同时把文件夹层次结构和代码语义作为节点特征纳入。我们评估了 GAT 和 GCN 两种编码器变体，发现 GAT 通常给出更准确、更稳定的分解结果。在十个具有真值架构的开源系统上的实验表明，相比一种最先进方法，GAER 在各项评估指标上平均将恢复准确率提升约 30%。通过自动导出融合多种信号的架构视图，GAER 降低了维护架构文档所需的人工投入，并支持更有效的系统理解。","tl":"把架构恢复当作图表示学习，融合类型依赖、目录层次与代码语义。","au":["Rakhshanda Jabeen","Morgan Ericsson","Jonas Nordqvist","Anna Wingkvist"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["architecture recovery","graph auto-encoder","heterogeneous graph","unsupervised","software modularization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/155/x"},{"id":"p00964","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Unveiling the Fragility of Binary Code Similarity Detection via Targeted Attacks with Model Explanations","tz":"借助模型解释的定向攻击揭示二进制代码相似性检测的脆弱性","a":"Binary code similarity detection (BCSD) serves as a fundamental technique for various software engineering tasks, e.g., vulnerability detection and classification. Attacks against such BCSD models have therefore drawn extensive attention, aiming at misleading the models to generate erroneous predictions. Prior works have explored various approaches to generating semantic-preserving variants, i.e., adversarial samples, to evaluate the robustness of the models against adversarial attacks. However, they have mainly relied on heuristic criteria or iterative greedy algorithms to locate salient code influencing the model output, failing to operate on a solid theoretical basis. Moreover, when processing programs with high complexities, such attacks tend to be time-consuming. In this work, we unveil the fragility of BCSD models through a novel attack framework guided by model explanations. In particular, we focus on targeted attacks where the attack goal is to mislead the model’s predictions to a specific target. Our attack leverages the superior capability of black-box, model-agnostic explainers in interpreting the model decision boundaries, thereby pinpointing the critical code snippet to apply semantic-preserving perturbations. The evaluation results demonstrate that compared with the state-of-the-art attacks, the proposed attacks achieve higher attack success rate in almost all scenarios, while also improving the efficiency and transferability. Our real-world case studies on vulnerability detection and classification further demonstrate the security implications of our attacks, highlighting fundamental vulnerabilities in current BCSD models, and the urgent need for more robust designs.","az":"二进制代码相似性检测（BCSD）是多种软件工程任务（例如漏洞检测与分类）的基础技术。因此，针对此类 BCSD 模型的攻击引起了广泛关注，其目标是误导模型产生错误预测。以往工作探索了多种生成语义保持变体（即对抗样本）的方法，以评估模型面对对抗攻击的鲁棒性。然而，它们主要依赖启发式准则或迭代贪心算法来定位影响模型输出的显著代码，缺乏坚实的理论基础。此外，在处理高复杂度程序时，这类攻击往往非常耗时。在本工作中，我们通过一个由模型解释引导的新颖攻击框架，揭示了 BCSD 模型的脆弱性。具体而言，我们聚焦定向攻击，其攻击目标是把模型预测误导至某个特定目标。我们的攻击利用黑盒、模型无关的解释器在刻画模型决策边界上的优越能力，从而精准定位应施加语义保持扰动的关键代码片段。评估结果表明，与最先进攻击相比，所提攻击在几乎所有场景下都取得了更高的攻击成功率，同时提升了效率与可迁移性。我们在漏洞检测与分类上的真实案例研究进一步展示了该攻击的安全影响，凸显了当前 BCSD 模型的根本性缺陷以及对更鲁棒设计的迫切需求。","tl":"用黑盒模型解释器精准定位关键代码，实现高效可迁移的 BCSD 定向攻击。","au":["Mingjie Chen","Tiancheng Zhu","Mingxue Zhang","Yiling He","Minghao Lin","Penghui Li","Kui Ren"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["binary code similarity detection","targeted attack","model explanation","adversarial examples","semantics-preserving perturbation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/156/x"},{"id":"p00965","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Specifications to Implementation in the Gen-AI Era: Lessons from a Project-based Software Engineering Course","tz":"从规约到实现的生成式 AI 时代：一门项目式软件工程课程的经验","a":"This paper investigates experiences, educational needs, and approaches for integrating Generative AI tools in an upper-level project-based undergraduate course on Software Engineering. We report on our course setup, our analysis of students’ experience in the last offering of the course, and an independent case study that we conducted to identify strengths, weaknesses, and strategies for using IDE-embedded AI tools, specifically GitHub Copilot and Cursor, when implementing a project equivalent in size and complexity to those typically carried out by the students in the course. Our results show that students utilize AI tools in all stages of project development: from requirements, through design, to implementation, testing, and code review, to generate and refine artifacts and to learn unfamiliar concepts. Students have mixed levels of satisfaction with using the tools, both as chat interfaces and as IDE-embedded solutions. We found no correlation between the degree of students’ reliance on AI and their grades. While Generative AI tools simplify repetitive development tasks and help quickly ramp up when working with unfamiliar frameworks and programming languages, these tools are still far from replacing software engineers or rendering software engineering education unnecessary. In fact, in the new AI-empowered reality, skills such as requirements engineering, design, code review, and systematic testing become more relevant than ever. We conclude the paper with a set of suggestions for future offerings of this and similar Software Engineering courses and for using AI in Software Engineering more broadly. We see a promising future for AI-empowered Software Engineering, where humans lead creative work and AI manages repetitive implementation tasks and programming language nuances.","az":"本文考察了在一门高年级项目式本科软件工程课程中整合生成式 AI 工具的经验、教育需求与方法。我们报告了课程设置、对最近一轮开课中学生体验的分析，以及我们开展的一项独立案例研究——在实现一个与学生课程项目规模和复杂度相当的项目时，识别使用 IDE 内嵌 AI 工具（具体为 GitHub Copilot 和 Cursor）的优势、劣势与策略。结果显示，学生在项目开发的各个阶段都在使用 AI 工具：从需求、设计，到实现、测试和代码评审，用以生成和精化制品，并学习不熟悉的概念。学生对这些工具的满意度参差不齐，无论是作为聊天界面还是作为 IDE 内嵌方案。我们发现学生对 AI 的依赖程度与其成绩之间没有相关性。虽然生成式 AI 工具简化了重复性的开发任务，并有助于在面对陌生框架和编程语言时快速上手，但这些工具距离取代软件工程师或让软件工程教育变得多余仍然很远。事实上，在这一由 AI 赋能的新现实中，需求工程、设计、代码评审和系统化测试等技能比以往任何时候都更为重要。我们在文末给出一组建议，既面向本课程及类似软件工程课程的未来开课，也更广泛地面向在软件工程中使用 AI。我们看好 AI 赋能的软件工程的未来：人类主导创造性工作，AI 负责重复性的实现任务和编程语言细节。","tl":"课程实证显示学生对 AI 的依赖度与成绩无关，需求与评审技能反而更关键。","au":["Yingying Wang","Masih Beigi Rizi","Fatemeh Khashei","Julia Rubin"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["human-study","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["SE education","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","project-based course","generative AI adoption"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/157/x","pu":"http://people.ece.ubc.ca/mjulia/publications/2026_AI_In_SE_FSE.pdf"},{"id":"p00966","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SmartDispatch: Dynamic Substitution of NumPy-style APIs on Heterogenous CPU-GPU Systems","tz":"SmartDispatch：异构 CPU-GPU 系统上 NumPy 风格 API 的动态替换","a":"The popularity of Python in various application domains has driven widespread adoption of NumPy-style APIs. To accelerate performance, libraries such as PyTorch, JAX, CuPy, and cuPyNumeric offer GPU-compatible counterparts to NumPy functions. However, substituting NumPy with these alternatives is not always beneficial due to overheads from type conversion, data transfer, and kernel launch costs. We present SmartDispatch, a runtime framework that dynamically substitutes NumPy-style API calls with semantically equivalent implementations from other libraries to improve performance. Our system includes a knowledge base of equivalent APIs, a hardware-aware microbenchmarking component to identify substitution thresholds, and a runtime substitution tool. Evaluation on four platforms with varying CPU-GPU architectures using machine learning models from real-world benchmarks shows that consistent performance gains (1.3× to 5.8×) can be achieved without requiring code modification, demonstrating the effectiveness of cross-library substitution in heterogeneous environments.","az":"Python 在各类应用领域的流行推动了 NumPy 风格 API 的广泛采用。为加速性能，PyTorch、JAX、CuPy 和 cuPyNumeric 等库提供了与 NumPy 函数对应的 GPU 兼容实现。然而，由于类型转换、数据传输和内核启动开销，用这些替代品取代 NumPy 并不总是有益。我们提出 SmartDispatch，一个运行时框架，能动态地把 NumPy 风格的 API 调用替换为其他库中语义等价的实现以提升性能。我们的系统包括一个等价 API 知识库、一个硬件感知的微基准测试组件（用于确定替换阈值），以及一个运行时替换工具。在四个具有不同 CPU-GPU 架构的平台上、使用来自真实基准的机器学习模型进行的评估表明，无需修改代码即可获得稳定的性能提升（1.3 倍到 5.8 倍），证明了在异构环境中跨库替换的有效性。","tl":"运行时按硬件感知阈值把 NumPy 调用换成等价 GPU 库实现，无需改代码。","au":["Jinku Cui","Yueming Hao","Shuyin Jiao","Jiajia Li","Xu Liu"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["NumPy-style API","dynamic substitution","heterogeneous CPU-GPU","microbenchmarking","runtime framework"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/158/x"},{"id":"p00967","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Not All RAGs Are Created Equal: A Component-Wise Empirical Study for Software Engineering Tasks","tz":"并非所有 RAG 生而平等：面向软件工程任务的组件级实证研究","a":"While Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is increasingly adopted to ground Large Language Models (LLMs) in software artifacts, the optimal configuration of its components remains an open question for software engineering (SE) tasks. The lack of systematic guidance forces practitioners into costly, ad-hoc experimentation. This paper presents a comprehensive, component-wise empirical study that dissects the RAG pipeline, evaluating over 20 distinct models and methods. Our study systematically isolates and evaluates 4 query processing techniques, 7 retrieval models spanning sparse, dense, and hybrid paradigms, 4 context refinement methods, and 5 distinct generators. We test these components on a suite of 3 core SE tasks: code generation, summarization, and repair. Our empirical findings reveal a crucial insight: the retriever-side components, particularly the choice of the retrieval algorithm, often exert a more significant influence on final system performance than the selection of the generator model. Strikingly, the classic lexical retriever BM25 demonstrates exceptionally robust performance across diverse tasks. Our analysis provides a practical, data-driven roadmap for researchers and practitioners, offering clear guidance on prioritizing optimization efforts when constructing effective RAG systems for software engineering contexts.","az":"尽管检索增强生成（RAG）被越来越多地用于把大语言模型（LLM）锚定到软件制品上，其各组件的最优配置对软件工程（SE）任务而言仍是一个开放问题。缺乏系统性指导迫使从业者进行代价高昂的临时性试验。本文呈现了一项全面的、组件级的实证研究，剖析 RAG 流水线，评估了超过 20 种不同的模型与方法。我们的研究系统地隔离并评估了 4 种查询处理技术、7 个涵盖稀疏、稠密与混合范式的检索模型、4 种上下文精化方法以及 5 种不同的生成器。我们在 3 项核心 SE 任务上测试这些组件：代码生成、代码摘要和程序修复。我们的实证发现揭示了一个关键洞见：检索侧组件，尤其是检索算法的选择，对最终系统性能的影响往往大于生成器模型的选择。令人惊讶的是，经典的词法检索器 BM25 在各类任务上都展现出异常稳健的性能。我们的分析为研究者和从业者提供了一份实用的、数据驱动的路线图，清晰指出在构建面向软件工程的有效 RAG 系统时应优先投入哪些优化。","tl":"实证证明检索器选择比生成器更影响 SE 任务，BM25 依然稳健。","au":["Qiang Ke","Yanjie Zhao","Hongjin Leng","Shengming Zhao","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["retrieval-augmented generation","component-wise study","BM25","code generation","program repair"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/159/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.14503"},{"id":"p00968","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Verifying Smart Contract Security Against Re-entrancy Attacks through Relational Value Analysis","tz":"通过关系值分析验证智能合约对重入攻击的安全性","a":"Reentrancy vulnerabilities are a critical security risk in smart contracts, posing a significant threat to the entire blockchain ecosystem. These vulnerabilities arise when a malicious attacker exploits the design of a smart contract to re-enter a function within the execution of another function, thus breaking atomicity and manipulating the smart contract state in unintended ways. While multiple countermeasures have been proposed to fortify smart contracts against re-entrancy based attacks, automatically verifying their effectiveness remains a difficult problem due to the inherent complexity of smart contracts and evolving attack techniques. In this work, we propose RAVEN, a sound and precise approach to verify smart contract safety against re-entrancy attacks automatically. At its core, RAVEN performs a content-sensitive semantic relational value analysis using the polyhedral abstract domain to establish hyper-properties such as absorption and commutativity of different program segments, which are sufficient to ensure safety against re-entrancy. Notably, unlike many prior approaches, we also prove the soundness of RAVEN, thus guaranteeing that contracts deemed as safe by RAVEN would not suffer from classical re-entrancy attacks. We have implemented our approach and evaluated RAVEN against nine state-of-the-art tools using four comprehensive test suites of Solidity smart contracts labeled for re-entrancy. The results demonstrate that RAVEN attains higher precision than existing approaches in detecting both re-entrancy-safe and vulnerable contracts. In particular, RAVEN produced 0/781 false positives on two test suites and 444/21,355 false positives on the remaining two, representing an approximate 77.3% reduction in false positives over prior tools. Moreover, this improvement was achieved with a comparable average analysis time of 141.9 seconds, versus 128.8 seconds for prior tools.","az":"重入漏洞是智能合约中的关键安全风险，对整个区块链生态构成重大威胁。这类漏洞产生于恶意攻击者利用合约设计，在一个函数执行过程中重新进入另一个函数，从而破坏原子性并以非预期方式操纵合约状态。尽管已有多种对策被提出以加固智能合约抵御重入类攻击，自动验证这些对策的有效性仍是难题，原因在于智能合约固有的复杂性和不断演进的攻击技术。在本工作中，我们提出 RAVEN，一种可靠且精确的方法，用于自动验证智能合约对重入攻击的安全性。其核心是，RAVEN 使用多面体抽象域执行上下文敏感的语义关系值分析，以建立诸如不同程序片段的吸收性与交换性等超性质（hyper-property），这些性质足以确保对重入的安全性。值得注意的是，与许多先前方法不同，我们还证明了 RAVEN 的可靠性（soundness），从而保证被 RAVEN 判定为安全的合约不会遭受经典重入攻击。我们实现了该方法，并在四个针对重入标注的 Solidity 智能合约综合测试集上，将 RAVEN 与九个最先进工具进行对比评估。结果表明，在检测重入安全合约与脆弱合约两方面，RAVEN 都比现有方法具有更高的精确率。特别地，RAVEN 在两个测试集上产生 0/781 的误报，在另外两个测试集上产生 444/21,355 的误报，相比以往工具误报减少约 77.3%。而且这一改进是在可比的平均分析时间下取得的：141.9 秒对以往工具的 128.8 秒。","tl":"用多面体抽象域证明吸收性与交换性超性质，给出可靠的重入安全验证。","au":["Divya Rathore","Kartik Nagar"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["reentrancy","smart contract verification","relational value analysis","polyhedral abstract domain","soundness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/160/x","pu":"https://kartiknagar.github.io/publication/fse26/fse26.pdf"},{"id":"p00969","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"In Line with Context: Repository-Level Code Generation via Context Inlining","tz":"与上下文同行：通过上下文内联实现仓库级代码生成","a":"Repository-level code generation has attracted growing attention in recent years. Unlike function-level code generation, it requires the model to understand the entire repository, reasoning over complex dependencies across functions, classes, and modules. However, existing approaches such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) or context-based function selection often fall short: they primarily rely on surface-level similarity and struggle to capture the rich dependencies that govern repository-level semantics. In this paper, we introduce InlineCoder, a novel framework for repository-level code generation. InlineCoder enhances the understanding of repository context by inlining the unfinished function into its call graph, thereby reframing the challenging repository understanding as an easier function-level coding task. Given a function signature, InlineCoder first generates a draft completion, termed an anchor, which approximates downstream dependencies and enables perplexity-based confidence estimation. This anchor drives a bidirectional inlining process: (i) Upstream Inlining, which embeds the anchor into its callers to capture diverse usage scenarios; and (ii) Downstream Retrieval, which integrates the anchor’s callees into the prompt to provide precise dependency context. The enriched context, combining draft completion with upstream and downstream perspectives, equips the LLM with a comprehensive repository view. Extensive experiments on the DevEval and RepoExec benchmarks demonstrate that InlineCoder substantially outperforms a wide range of state-of-the-art baselines, with average relative gains of 29.73% in EM, 20.82% in ES, and 49.34% in BLEU on RepoExec compared to the strongest baseline. These results highlight its effectiveness in understanding repository contexts as well as its generalization across domains.","az":"近年来，仓库级代码生成受到越来越多关注。与函数级代码生成不同，它要求模型理解整个仓库，并对跨函数、类与模块的复杂依赖进行推理。然而，检索增强生成（RAG）或基于上下文的函数选择等已有方法往往力有不逮：它们主要依赖表层相似性，难以捕捉支配仓库级语义的丰富依赖。本文提出 InlineCoder，一个面向仓库级代码生成的新框架。InlineCoder 通过把未完成的函数内联到其调用图中来增强对仓库上下文的理解，从而把困难的仓库理解重构为更容易的函数级编码任务。给定函数签名，InlineCoder 首先生成一个草稿补全，称为锚点（anchor），它近似了下游依赖并支持基于困惑度的置信度估计。该锚点驱动一个双向内联过程：（i）上游内联，把锚点嵌入其调用者中以捕捉多样的使用场景；（ii）下游检索，把锚点的被调用者整合进提示以提供精确的依赖上下文。这种结合草稿补全与上下游视角的丰富上下文，使 LLM 获得全面的仓库视图。在 DevEval 和 RepoExec 基准上的大量实验表明，InlineCoder 大幅优于一系列最先进基线，在 RepoExec 上相较最强基线平均相对提升 EM 29.73%、ES 20.82%、BLEU 49.34%。这些结果凸显了它在理解仓库上下文方面的有效性以及跨领域的泛化能力。","tl":"先出草稿作锚点，再双向内联调用者与被调用者组装仓库上下文。","au":["Chao Hu","Wenhao Zeng","Yuling Shi","Beijun Shen","Xiaodong Gu"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["repository-level code generation","context inlining","call graph","anchor draft completion","RepoExec"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/161/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.00376"},{"id":"p00970","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Verifying Structural Robustness of Deep Neural Network","tz":"验证深度神经网络的结构鲁棒性","a":"Neural network verification has emerged as a useful technique for improving the reliability of deep learning systems. Current verification approaches primarily focus on local robustness, where perturbations are applied independently to each input element. Despite its common use, local robustness does not capture perturbations that exhibit coordinated relationships between input elements. Such perturbations arise from systematic transformations or filtering operations that preserve structural characteristics of the data. These perturbations, which we call “structural robustness”, represent a significant gap in existing verification capabilities. This work focuses on structural robustness verification by formalizing two important classes of structured perturbations: linear position-invariant and linear position-varying. Those perturbations allow input elements to be modified in coordinated ways while preserving essential data structure. The main challenge is that structural perturbations cannot be directly expressed using standard interval-based specification formats that existing verification tools typically support. To address this limitation, we introduce VeriS, a technique that reformulates structural robustness into standard local robustness problems by creating specialized subnetworks that encode perturbation behavior and integrates them with the original network architecture. VeriS enables verification across continuous spaces defined by structural robustness specifications while maintaining compatibility with existing verification tools. VeriS also introduces optimizations that significantly enhance verification performance such as converting complex operations into standard representations. We implement and evaluate VeriS on benchmarks involving neural networks across three domains: image classification, audio processing, and healthcare applications. Our evaluation, which encompasses 5508 verification problems, demonstrates that VeriS successfully verifies 78% of structural robustness specifications when integrated with state-of-the-art verification tools. These results show that VeriS enables the verification of complex structural perturbations that were previously beyond the reach of existing neural network verification.","az":"神经网络验证已成为提升深度学习系统可靠性的有用技术。当前验证方法主要关注局部鲁棒性，即对每个输入元素独立施加扰动。尽管被广泛使用，局部鲁棒性无法刻画输入元素之间存在协同关系的扰动。这类扰动源自保持数据结构特征的系统性变换或滤波操作。我们把这类扰动称为“结构鲁棒性”，它代表了现有验证能力中的一个重要空白。本工作聚焦结构鲁棒性验证，形式化了两类重要的结构化扰动：线性位置不变型与线性位置可变型。这些扰动允许输入元素以协同方式被修改，同时保持本质的数据结构。主要挑战在于，结构扰动无法直接用现有验证工具通常支持的标准区间式规约格式来表达。为突破这一限制，我们提出 VeriS，一种把结构鲁棒性重新表述为标准局部鲁棒性问题的技术：它构造编码扰动行为的专用子网络，并将其与原始网络架构集成。VeriS 使得在结构鲁棒性规约定义的连续空间上进行验证成为可能，同时保持与现有验证工具的兼容性。VeriS 还引入了显著提升验证性能的优化，例如把复杂操作转换为标准表示。我们在涉及图像分类、音频处理和医疗应用三个领域的神经网络基准上实现并评估了 VeriS。我们的评估涵盖 5508 个验证问题，结果表明，当与最先进验证工具集成时，VeriS 成功验证了 78% 的结构鲁棒性规约。这些结果表明，VeriS 使此前现有神经网络验证难以企及的复杂结构扰动验证成为可能。","tl":"用编码扰动的子网络把结构鲁棒性化归为标准局部鲁棒性验证问题。","au":["Hai Duong","Thanh Le","Lam Nguyen","ThanhVu Nguyen"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["neural network verification","structural robustness","local robustness","subnetwork encoding","verification tools"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/162/x","pu":"https://hocdot.github.io/assets/papers/duong2026verifying.pdf"},{"id":"p00971","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"IntentTester: Intent-Driven Multi-Agent Framework for Cross-Library Test Migration","tz":"IntentTester：面向跨库测试迁移的意图驱动多智能体框架","a":"Unit tests capture both functional checks and domain-specific knowledge, but this knowledge remains locked within individual projects and is rarely reused across libraries with overlapping functionality. Existing migration techniques based on structural code mappings (e.g., API signatures) often break down under divergent designs or cross-language settings, resulting in non-executable migrated tests. In this paper, we present IntentTester, a multi-agent framework for intent-driven test reuse. Instead of translating raw code, IntentTester abstracts tests into a language-agnostic Test Description Language (TDL), aligns them with semantically related entities and dependencies in a repository graph, and synthesizes executable tests through LLM-guided reasoning and iterative validation. This design enables cross-library and cross-language migration without manual intervention, producing migrated tests that existing structure-mapping approaches cannot achieve. We evaluate IntentTester on nine open-source projects across three domains (JSON, HTML, Time) and two languages (Java, Python). IntentTester generates 2,776 syntactically correct tests with 85% correctness; in comparison, the two baselines achieve 51% and 43%. Among them, 2,410 tests execute successfully, yielding a 74% effectiveness rate. Beyond higher success rates, IntentTester also surfaced previously unknown defects—including stack overflows, null dereferences, and parsing inconsistencies, several acknowledged or patched by maintainers. Our results show that intent-driven migration shifts the focus from code mappings to semantic alignment, allowing practical cross-library and cross-language test reuse while improving test quality and exposing implementation flaws.","az":"单元测试同时承载了功能检查与领域特定知识，但这些知识被锁在各个项目内部，很少能在功能重叠的库之间复用。已有的基于结构化代码映射（如 API 签名）的迁移技术在设计差异较大或跨语言场景下常常失效，导致迁移后的测试无法执行。本文提出 IntentTester，一个面向意图驱动测试复用的多智能体框架。IntentTester 不翻译原始代码，而是把测试抽象为与语言无关的测试描述语言（TDL），将其与仓库图中语义相关的实体和依赖对齐，并通过 LLM 引导的推理与迭代验证合成可执行的测试。该设计无需人工干预即可实现跨库与跨语言迁移，产出现有结构映射方法无法实现的迁移测试。我们在三个领域（JSON、HTML、Time）、两种语言（Java、Python）的九个开源项目上评估 IntentTester。IntentTester 生成了 2,776 个语法正确的测试，正确率达 85%；相比之下两个基线分别为 51% 和 43%。其中 2,410 个测试成功执行，有效率为 74%。除更高的成功率外，IntentTester 还暴露了此前未知的缺陷，包括栈溢出、空指针解引用和解析不一致，其中若干已被维护者确认或修复。我们的结果表明，意图驱动的迁移把关注点从代码映射转向语义对齐，在提升测试质量和暴露实现缺陷的同时，实现了实用的跨库、跨语言测试复用。","tl":"用语言无关的测试描述语言做语义对齐，实现跨库跨语言测试迁移。","au":["Yi Gao","Ziyuan Zhang","Xing Hu","Xiaohu Yang","Xin Xia"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test migration","cross-library reuse","test description language","multi-agent framework","cross-language testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/163/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.25588"},{"id":"p00972","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LinkAnchor: An Autonomous LLM-Based Agent for Issue-to-Commit Link Recovery","tz":"LinkAnchor：用于 issue-提交链接恢复的自主 LLM 智能体","a":"Issue-to-commit link recovery plays a central role in software traceability and project management, yet it remains a challenging task. Prior studies show that only about 42.2% of issues on GitHub are correctly linked to their commits, highlighting the need for more effective solutions. Existing work has explored a range of ML/DL approaches, and more recently, large language models (LLMs) have been applied to this problem. However, these methods face two major limitations. First, LLMs are restricted by limited context windows and cannot simultaneously process all available data sources, such as long commit histories, extensive issue discussions, and large code repositories. Second, most approaches operate on individual issue–commit pairs, where the model determines for each pair whether the commit is related to the issue. While straightforward in design, this strategy quickly becomes impractical in repositories with tens of thousands of commits, as it requires exhaustively evaluating an enormous number of candidate pairs. To address these challenges, we present LinkAnchor, the first autonomous LLM-based agent designed specifically for issue-to-commit link recovery. LinkAnchor introduces a lazy-access architecture that allows the underlying LLM to dynamically retrieve only the most relevant contextual data, such as commits, issue comments, and code files, without exceeding token limits. Unlike prior approaches, LinkAnchor does not exhaustively score every possible pair but instead efficiently identifies the last resolving commit of an issue, enabling the complete reconstruction of the resolving commit chain and retrieval of all relevant commits. Our evaluations show that LinkAnchor outperforms state-of-the-art baselines by 41–714% in Hit@1 across six large-scale open-source projects, while costing only about 0.01 US dollars per issue. Finally, LinkAnchor is designed and tested for both GitHub and Jira, and its modular architecture makes it straightforward to extend to other platforms.","az":"issue 到提交的链接恢复在软件可追溯性与项目管理中居于核心地位，但仍是一项有挑战的任务。以往研究表明，GitHub 上只有约 42.2% 的 issue 被正确链接到其提交，凸显了对更有效方案的需求。已有工作探索了一系列 ML/DL 方法，最近大语言模型（LLM）也被应用于该问题。然而这些方法面临两大局限。第一，LLM 受限于有限的上下文窗口，无法同时处理所有可用数据源，例如长提交历史、冗长的 issue 讨论和庞大的代码仓库。第二，大多数方法作用于单个 issue-提交对，模型需对每一对判断该提交是否与该 issue 相关。这种策略设计虽直接，但在拥有数万提交的仓库中很快变得不切实际，因为它需要穷尽评估海量候选对。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 LinkAnchor，首个专为 issue-提交链接恢复设计的自主 LLM 智能体。LinkAnchor 引入一种惰性访问（lazy-access）架构，使底层 LLM 能动态地只检索最相关的上下文数据，例如提交、issue 评论和代码文件，而不超出 token 限制。与以往方法不同，LinkAnchor 不穷尽地为每一个可能的配对打分，而是高效识别某个 issue 的最后一个解决提交，从而完整重建解决提交链并检索所有相关提交。我们的评估表明，在六个大规模开源项目上，LinkAnchor 在 Hit@1 上比最先进基线高出 41%–714%，而每个 issue 的成本仅约 0.01 美元。最后，LinkAnchor 针对 GitHub 和 Jira 均已设计并测试，其模块化架构使其易于扩展到其他平台。","tl":"惰性访问架构让智能体只查必要上下文并直接锁定最终解决提交。","au":["Arshia Akhavan","Alireza Hoseinpour","Abbas Heydarnoori","Hamid Bagheri","Mehdi Keshani"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["issue-commit link recovery","LLM agent","lazy access architecture","traceability","GitHub / Jira"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/164/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.12232"},{"id":"p00973","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"How Low Can You Go? The Data-Light SE Challenge","tz":"你能压到多低？数据轻量化的软件工程挑战","a":"Much of software engineering (SE) research assumes that progress depends on massive datasets and CPU-intensive optimizers. Yet has this assumption been rigorously tested? The counter-evidence presented in this paper suggests otherwise. For over 100 optimization tasks from recent SE papers (including software configuration, performance tuning, product line engineering, project health forecasting, defect prediction, software testing, software process and cost estimation, and cross-domain generalization datasets), even with just a few dozen labels, very simple methods (e.g., diversity sampling, a minimal Bayesian learner, its distance-based non-parametric variant, or random probes) achieve over 90% of the best reported results. Furthermore, these simple methods perform just as well as more complex state-of-the-art optimizers like SMAC, TPE, DEHB, etc. While some tasks would require better outcomes and more sampling, these results seen after a few dozen samples would suffice for many engineering needs (particularly when the goal is rapid and cost-efficient guidance rather than slow and exhaustive optimization). To say that another way, at least some SE tasks are better served by lightweight approaches that demand fewer labels and far less computation. We hence propose the data-light challenge: when will a handful of labels suffice for SE tasks? To enable a large-scale investigation of this issue, we contribute (1) a mathematical formalization of labeling, (2) lightweight baseline algorithms, and (3) results on public-domain data showing the conditions under which lightweight methods excel or fail. For the purposes of open science, our scripts and data are online at https://github.com/KKGanguly/NEO .","az":"许多软件工程（SE）研究都假定，进展依赖于海量数据集和 CPU 密集的优化器。然而这一假设被严格检验过吗？本文给出的反证表明并非如此。在取自近期 SE 论文的 100 多个优化任务上（涵盖软件配置、性能调优、产品线工程、项目健康预测、缺陷预测、软件测试、软件过程与成本估算，以及跨领域泛化数据集），即便只用几十个标签，非常简单的方法（例如多样性采样、一个极简贝叶斯学习器、其基于距离的非参数变体，或随机探针）也能达到已报告最佳结果的 90% 以上。此外，这些简单方法的表现与 SMAC、TPE、DEHB 等更复杂的最先进优化器不相上下。虽然某些任务需要更好的结果和更多采样，但在几十个样本之后得到的这些结果已足以满足许多工程需求（尤其当目标是快速且低成本的指导，而非缓慢而穷尽的优化时）。换言之，至少某些 SE 任务更适合使用需要更少标签、远更低计算量的轻量方法。因此我们提出数据轻量化挑战：什么时候少量标签就足以应付 SE 任务？为支持对该问题的大规模研究，我们贡献了：（1）标注过程的数学形式化；（2）轻量基线算法；（3）在公开数据上的结果，展示轻量方法在何种条件下表现出色或失效。为践行开放科学，我们的脚本与数据已公开于 https://github.com/KKGanguly/NEO 。","tl":"在百余个 SE 优化任务上证明几十个标签+极简方法即可达 90% 最佳效果。","au":["Kishan Kumar Ganguly","Tim Menzies"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["position-vision","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["data-light SE","label efficiency","search-based optimization","baseline algorithms","hyperparameter optimization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/165/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.13524"},{"id":"p00974","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Unfulfilled Promises: LLM-Based Detection of OS Compatibility Issues in Infrastructure as Code","tz":"未兑现的承诺：基于 LLM 的基础设施即代码操作系统兼容性问题检测","a":"Modern infrastructures rely on Infrastructure as Code (IaC) systems to keep complex deployments consistent, reproducible, and scalable at production scale. The reliability of these infrastructures, however, depends on the correctness of their building blocks, which are reusable components (modules) that each performs a dedicated task, such as installing a package, managing an OS user, or configuring a service, and reconciling its state with the desired specification. A central promise of these components is portability: a specification written once should correctly manage the targeted resource on every OS the IaC component supports. When this property is violated, defects can propagate across entire infrastructures, causing outages, security vulnerabilities, and costly misconfigurations. In this work, we introduce crOSsible, the first automated framework for cross-OS testing of IaC modules. crOSsible leverages large language models (LLMs) to synthesize and repair integration tests from structured module documentation, and executes them across 13 versions of 8 major Linux distributions. While our techniques are generally applicable to different IaC systems, we instantiate and evaluate them on Ansible, the most widely used IaC framework for managing individual servers. Evaluation across 259 popular Ansible modules demonstrates both effectiveness and real-world impact. In just 12 hours of testing, crOSsible uncovered 36 previously unknown bugs, including 22 portability violations. In total, 27 issues have been confirmed by maintainers, with 11 already fixed. The discovered issues range from crashes to dangerous soundness defects where modules reported success despite leaving systems misconfigured. Beyond bug discovery, crOSsible improved the code coverage of Ansible modules by 12.3% on average, systematically exercising OS-specific code paths that existing tests missed.","az":"现代基础设施依赖基础设施即代码（IaC）系统，以在生产规模上保持复杂部署的一致性、可复现性与可扩展性。然而这些基础设施的可靠性取决于其构件的正确性，这些构件是可复用的组件（模块），每个模块执行一项专门任务，例如安装软件包、管理操作系统用户或配置服务，并将其状态与期望规约进行对账。这些组件的一个核心承诺是可移植性：一次编写的规约应当能在该 IaC 组件支持的每一个操作系统上正确管理目标资源。当这一性质被违反时，缺陷会在整个基础设施中传播，造成宕机、安全漏洞和代价高昂的误配置。在本工作中，我们提出 crOSsible，首个用于 IaC 模块跨操作系统测试的自动化框架。crOSsible 利用大语言模型（LLM）从结构化的模块文档中合成并修复集成测试，并在 8 个主流 Linux 发行版的 13 个版本上执行这些测试。虽然我们的技术普遍适用于不同 IaC 系统，我们在 Ansible 上进行实例化与评估——它是管理单台服务器最广泛使用的 IaC 框架。在 259 个流行 Ansible 模块上的评估展示了有效性与真实影响。仅 12 小时的测试，crOSsible 就发现了 36 个此前未知的缺陷，其中包括 22 个可移植性违规。总计 27 个问题已被维护者确认，其中 11 个已被修复。所发现的问题从崩溃到危险的可靠性缺陷不等，后者指模块在实际上让系统处于错误配置状态的情况下仍报告成功。除缺陷发现外，crOSsible 还把 Ansible 模块的代码覆盖率平均提升了 12.3%，系统性地执行了现有测试遗漏的操作系统相关代码路径。","tl":"用 LLM 从模块文档合成集成测试，跨 Linux 发行版查 IaC 可移植性违规。","au":["Georgios-Petros Drosos","Georgios Alexopoulos","Thodoris Sotiropoulos","Dimitris Mitropoulos","Zhendong Su"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Infrastructure as Code","Ansible modules","cross-OS testing","portability violation","LLM test synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/166/x"},{"id":"p00975","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automating Dockerfile Refactoring to Multi-Stage Builds","tz":"自动化 Dockerfile 重构为多阶段构建","a":"Containerization has become a cornerstone of modern software deployment, yet many projects still ship single-stage Dockerfiles that bundle compilers, build tools, and temporary files into production images, thereby hurting performance and security. Multi-stage builds are recommended, yet uptake appears uneven, plausibly because refactoring legacy Dockerfiles demands nontrivial reasoning about build lifecycles and dependency separation. This paper presents , an automated refactoring approach that converts single-stage Dockerfiles into optimized multi-stage builds. first performs static analysis to identify the technology stack and to infer build-time and runtime dependencies. It then applies a lightweight gate that estimates refactoring benefit from a composite of image bloat, structural inefficiency, and security risk, proceeding only when refactoring is warranted. Finally, it synthesizes a multi-stage Dockerfile that isolates build tooling, copies only the artifacts needed at runtime, and applies production hardening. Evaluated on 521 real-world single-stage projects, successfully produced working multi-stage Dockerfiles for 60.3% of targets. The resulting images were, on average, 52.2% smaller and contained 50.0% fewer high-risk vulnerabilities than the originals, outperforming baselines. lowers the barrier to multi-stage adoption at scale, yielding leaner images with reduced attack surface and improved maintainability. We release the tool, its knowledge assets, and the evaluation dataset to support reproducibility and future research.","az":"容器化已成为现代软件部署的基石，但许多项目仍在交付单阶段 Dockerfile，把编译器、构建工具和临时文件一并打包进生产镜像，从而损害性能与安全。多阶段构建是被推荐的做法，但其采纳程度却参差不齐，这很可能是因为重构遗留 Dockerfile 需要对构建生命周期与依赖分离进行非平凡的推理。本文提出 \\tool，一种把单阶段 Dockerfile 转换为优化后多阶段构建的自动化重构方法。\\tool 首先执行静态分析以识别技术栈并推断构建期与运行期依赖；随后应用一个轻量门控，从镜像臃肿度、结构低效性和安全风险的综合指标来估计重构收益，仅在重构确有必要时才继续；最后它合成一个多阶段 Dockerfile，隔离构建工具链，只复制运行时所需的制品，并施加生产环境加固。在 521 个真实世界单阶段项目上的评估显示，\\tool 为 60.3% 的目标成功产出了可用的多阶段 Dockerfile。所得镜像平均缩小 52.2%，高危漏洞数量比原镜像减少 50.0%，优于基线方法。\\tool 大规模地降低了采用多阶段构建的门槛，带来更精简、攻击面更小、可维护性更好的镜像。我们公开了该工具、其知识资产以及评估数据集，以支持可复现性与后续研究。","tl":"静态分析推断构建/运行依赖并加收益门控，自动改写为多阶段构建。","au":["Dongjin Chen","Wenhua Yang","Minxue Pan","Yu Zhou"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["Dockerfile refactoring","multi-stage build","container image size","static analysis","production hardening"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/167/x"},{"id":"p00976","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TransAgent: Enhancing LLM-Based Code Translation via Fine-Grained Execution Alignment","tz":"TransAgent：通过细粒度执行对齐增强基于 LLM 的代码翻译","a":"Code translation transforms code between programming languages while preserving functionality, which is critical in software development and maintenance. While traditional learning-based code translation methods have limited effectiveness due to the lack of sufficient parallel training data, Large Language Models (LLMs) have recently advanced this field with their strong code generation and comprehension capabilities. However, code translated by LLMs still suffers from diverse quality issues, such as syntax and semantic errors. In this work, we propose {}, a novel multi-agent system that eliminates the errors during LLM-based code translation. The main insight of {} is to localize error-prone code blocks via fine-grained execution alignment between source and target code. We evaluate {} on a newly constructed benchmark of recent programming tasks to mitigate data leakage. {} outperforms the latest {} by up to 33.3% in translation accuracy and achieves an average improvement of 56.7% over {} in program repair performance. We also conduct an ablation study and evaluate {} across different LLMs, demonstrating its effectiveness and strong generalizability.","az":"代码翻译在保持功能不变的前提下将代码在不同编程语言之间转换，这在软件开发与维护中至关重要。传统基于学习的代码翻译方法由于缺乏足够的平行训练数据而效果有限，而大语言模型（LLM）凭借其强大的代码生成与理解能力近来推动了该领域的发展。然而，LLM 翻译出的代码仍然存在多种质量问题，例如语法和语义错误。在本文中，我们提出了 \\ourtool{}，一个新颖的多智能体系统，用于消除基于 LLM 的代码翻译过程中的错误。\\ourtool{} 的核心洞见是：通过源代码与目标代码之间的细粒度执行对齐来定位易出错的代码块。我们在一个新构建的、由近期编程任务组成的基准上评估 \\ourtool{}，以缓解数据泄漏问题。\\ourtool{} 在翻译准确率上比最新的 \\unitrans{} 最多高出 33.3%，在程序修复性能上比 \\agentless{} 平均提升 56.7%。我们还进行了消融实验，并在不同的 LLM 上评估 \\ourtool{}，证明了其有效性与良好的泛化能力。","tl":"用源码与目标码的细粒度执行对齐定位翻译错误块。","au":["Zhiqiang Yuan","Weitong Chen","Hanlin Wang","Xin Peng","Zhenpeng Chen","Yiling Lou"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["code translation","execution alignment","multi-agent system","program repair","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/168/x"},{"id":"p00977","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"iCoRe: An Iterative Correlation-Aware Retriever for Bug Reproduction Test Generation","tz":"iCoRe：面向缺陷复现测试生成的迭代式关联感知检索器","a":"Automatically generating bug reproduction tests (BRT) from issue descriptions is crucial for facilitating software maintenance. Large Language Model (LLM)-based approaches have shown great potential for this task. Their effectiveness heavily relies on retrieving high-quality context from the codebase. The retrieval phase of existing approaches relies on either traditional methods like BM25 or modern LLM-driven strategies. The LLM-based retrieval strategies typically involve equipping an LLM with tools to autonomously explore the code repository or having it select the most relevant files and code snippets from a provided list as context. However, these retrieval methods suffer from three key limitations: (1) They often employ a unified strategy for retrieving both source code and test cases, overlooking their distinct retrieval requirements. (2) They focus solely on semantic similarity, ignoring function call relationships that reflect behavioral relevance, which often leads to the retrieval of irrelevant context. (3) The retrieval lacks a feedback loop from the generation phase, preventing it from refining the context based on execution results. These limitations collectively result in low-quality context, thereby hindering the accuracy of bug reproduction. To address these challenges, we propose iCoRe, an iterative, correlation-aware context retrieval approach. iCoRe is explicitly designed to be aware of three key correlations: 1) the correlation between source code and test cases, which requires differentiated retrieval, 2) the correlation between textual semantics and function call structures for accurate relevance assessment, and 3) the correlation between the retrieval and generation phases, which enables iterative feedback and refinement. To evaluate iCoRe, we integrate it with an LLM-based BRT generator and conduct a comprehensive evaluation on the SWT-bench Lite benchmark. Experimental results show that our method achieves a Fail-to-Pass rate of 42.0%, representing a significant 31.7% relative improvement over existing retrieval methods.","az":"从 issue 描述自动生成缺陷复现测试（BRT）对促进软件维护至关重要。基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法在该任务上展现出巨大潜力，其效果高度依赖于从代码库中检索高质量上下文。现有方法的检索阶段要么依赖 BM25 等传统方法，要么依赖现代的 LLM 驱动策略。基于 LLM 的检索策略通常是给 LLM 配备工具让其自主探索代码仓库，或让其从给定列表中挑选最相关的文件与代码片段作为上下文。然而，这些检索方法存在三个关键局限：（1）它们常常对源代码与测试用例采用统一的检索策略，忽视了两者不同的检索需求；（2）它们只关注语义相似度，忽略了反映行为相关性的函数调用关系，这往往导致检索到无关上下文；（3）检索缺乏来自生成阶段的反馈回路，无法根据执行结果来精炼上下文。这些局限共同导致上下文质量低下，从而削弱缺陷复现的准确性。为解决这些挑战，我们提出 iCoRe，一种迭代式、关联感知的上下文检索方法。iCoRe 显式地设计为感知三种关键关联：1）源代码与测试用例之间的关联，这要求差异化检索；2）文本语义与函数调用结构之间的关联，用于准确评估相关性；3）检索阶段与生成阶段之间的关联，从而支持迭代反馈与精炼。为评估 iCoRe，我们将其与一个基于 LLM 的 BRT 生成器集成，并在 SWT-bench Lite 基准上开展了全面评估。实验结果表明，我们的方法达到了 42.0% 的 Fail-to-Pass 率，相比现有检索方法实现了 31.7% 的显著相对提升。","tl":"区分代码与测试、融合调用关系并带生成反馈的迭代检索。","au":["JunyiWang","Jialun Cao","Zhongxin Liu"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["bug reproduction test","context retrieval","SWT-bench","fail-to-pass","call graph"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/169/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.19224"},{"id":"p00978","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Chiseling Out Efficiency: Structured Skeleton Supervision for Efficient Code Generation","tz":"凿出效率：用结构化骨架监督实现高效代码生成","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) are capable of generating syntactically correct and functionally complete programs, greatly streamlining software development. However, recent studies reveal that these programs typically execute substantially slower than human-optimized counterparts. Existing approaches to bridging this efficiency gap typically involve either iteratively optimizing code after generation or fine-tuning models on corpora of efficient code. Yet, these methods expose the model to efficiency signals only by mimicking complete, optimized solutions, without explicitly encoding the structural code patterns essential for achieving high runtime performance. Addressing this gap presents two core challenges: (1) extracting and representing latent, efficiency-oriented structural patterns embedded within complex syntax and control flows, and (2) effectively learning these patterns without destabilizing the semantic training of LLMs. To tackle these challenges, we propose EffiSkel, an efficiency skeleton-guided framework that explicitly extracts and learns efficiency skeletons—abstract, reusable structural patterns underpinning efficient code—by leveraging three complementary strategies: lexical analysis based on token-frequency saliency, syntactic analysis using similarity over Abstract Syntax Trees (ASTs), and dynamic line-level profiling of execution time. These skeletons are integrated into a multi-task learning regime that jointly optimizes code generation and skeleton prediction, introducing an explicit inductive bias toward efficiency-aware code generation. Experiments across multiple programming languages and benchmarks demonstrate that EffiSkel significantly enhances both functional correctness and efficiency, resulting on Mercury with DeepSeek-Coder (7B) a +11.11% (vs. EffiCoder) and +3.71% (vs. CodeDPO) higher Efficiency Ratio (ER), and a +0.36 (vs. EffiCoder) and +0.22 (vs. CodeDPO) increase in Average Speedup (AS). These results highlight the effectiveness of explicitly modeling efficiency skeletons in improving the runtime performance of code generated by LLMs.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）能够生成语法正确且功能完整的程序，极大简化了软件开发。然而，近期研究发现，这些程序的执行速度通常远慢于人工优化的对应版本。现有弥合这一效率差距的方法，通常是在生成之后迭代优化代码，或在高效代码语料上微调模型。然而，这些方法只是让模型通过模仿完整的优化解来接触效率信号，并未显式编码实现高运行性能所必需的结构化代码模式。解决这一空白面临两个核心挑战：（1）从复杂的语法与控制流中抽取并表示潜在的、面向效率的结构模式；（2）在不破坏 LLM 语义训练稳定性的前提下有效学习这些模式。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 EffiSkel，一个由效率骨架（effi ciency skel eton）引导的框架，它通过三种互补策略显式抽取并学习效率骨架——即支撑高效代码的抽象、可复用的结构模式：基于词元频率显著性的词法分析、基于抽象语法树（AST）相似度的句法分析，以及执行时间的动态行级剖析。这些骨架被整合进一个多任务学习机制中，联合优化代码生成与骨架预测，从而为面向效率的代码生成引入显式的归纳偏置。跨多种编程语言与基准的实验表明，EffiSkel 显著提升了功能正确性与效率：在 Mercury 上使用 DeepSeek-Coder（7B）时，效率比（ER）相比 EffiCoder 提升 +11.11%、相比 CodeDPO 提升 +3.71%，平均加速比（AS）相比 EffiCoder 提高 +0.36、相比 CodeDPO 提高 +0.22。这些结果凸显了显式建模效率骨架在提升 LLM 生成代码运行性能方面的有效性。","tl":"把可复用的效率结构骨架作为多任务监督信号注入训练。","au":["Yu Yu","Zhihong Sun","Jia Li","Yao Wan","Chuanyi Li","Hongyu Zhang","Ruyun Wang","Tao Huang","Zhi Jin","Ge Li","Chen Lyu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["efficient code generation","efficiency skeleton","multi-task learning","AST similarity","profiling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/170/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.06821"},{"id":"p00979","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Rethinking the Evaluation of Microservice RCA with a Fault Propagation-Aware Benchmark","tz":"重新思考微服务根因分析评测：一个故障传播感知的基准","a":"While cloud-native microservice architectures have revolutionized software development, their inherent operational complexity makes failure Root Cause Analysis (RCA) a critical yet challenging task. Numerous data-driven RCA models have been proposed to address this challenge. However, we find that the benchmarks used to evaluate these models are often too simple to reflect real-world scenarios. Our preliminary study reveals that simple rule-based methods can achieve performance comparable to or even surpassing state-of-the-art (SOTA) models on four widely used public benchmarks. This finding suggests that the oversimplification of existing benchmarks might lead to an overestimation of the performance of RCA methods. To further investigate the oversimplification issue, we conduct a systematic analysis of popular public RCA benchmarks, identifying key limitations in their fault infjection strategies, call graph structures, and telemetry signal patterns. Based on these insights, we propose an automated framework for generating more challenging and comprehensive benchmarks that include complex fault propagation scenarios. Our new dataset contains 1,430 validated failure cases from 9,152 fault injections, covering 25 fault types across 6 categories, dynamic workloads, and hierarchical ground-truth labels that map failures from services down to code-level causes. Crucially, to ensure the failure cases are relevant to IT operations, each case is validated to have a discernible impact on user-facing SLIs. Our re-evaluation of 11 SOTA models on this new benchmark shows that they achieve low Top@1 accuracies, averaging 0.21 with the best-performing model reaching merely 0.37 and execution times escalating from seconds to hours. From this analysis, we identify three critical failure patterns common to current models: scalability issues, observability blind spots and modeling bottlenecks. Based on these findings, we provide actionable guidelines for future RCA research. We emphasize the need for robust algorithms and the co-development of challenging benchmarks. To facilitate further research, we publicly release our benchmark generation framework, the new dataset, and our implementations of the evaluated SOTA models.","az":"云原生微服务架构虽然革新了软件开发，但其固有的运维复杂性使得故障根因分析（RCA）成为一项关键而困难的任务。已有大量数据驱动的 RCA 模型被提出以应对这一挑战。然而，我们发现用于评估这些模型的基准往往过于简单，无法反映真实场景。我们的初步研究表明，简单的基于规则的方法在四个被广泛使用的公开基准上，性能可与最先进（SOTA）模型相当甚至超越。这一发现说明现有基准的过度简化可能导致对 RCA 方法性能的高估。为进一步考察这一过度简化问题，我们对流行的公开 RCA 基准开展了系统分析，识别出其在故障注入策略、调用图结构与遥测信号模式方面的关键局限。基于这些洞见，我们提出一个自动化框架，用于生成更具挑战性、更全面、包含复杂故障传播场景的基准。我们的新数据集包含来自 9,152 次故障注入的 1,430 个经过验证的失效案例，覆盖 6 大类 25 种故障类型、动态负载，以及将失效从服务层映射到代码级原因的层次化真值标签。尤为关键的是，为确保失效案例与 IT 运维相关，每个案例都被验证对面向用户的 SLI 有可辨别的影响。我们在新基准上对 11 个 SOTA 模型的重新评估显示，它们的 Top@1 准确率很低，平均仅 0.21，表现最好的模型也只有 0.37，且执行时间从秒级上升到小时级。基于该分析，我们识别出当前模型共有的三种关键失败模式：可扩展性问题、可观测性盲区与建模瓶颈。据此我们给出了面向未来 RCA 研究的可操作指南，强调需要鲁棒算法与更具挑战性基准的协同发展。为促进后续研究，我们公开发布了基准生成框架、新数据集以及所评估 SOTA 模型的实现。","tl":"揭示现有 RCA 基准过简，并自动生成含故障传播的新基准。","au":["Aoyang Fang","Songhan Zhang","Yifan Yang","Haotong Wu","Junjielong Xu","Xuyang Wang","Rui Wang","Manyi Wang","Qisheng Lu","Pinjia He"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["root cause analysis","microservices","benchmark generation","fault injection","observability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/171/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04711"},{"id":"p00980","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Phantom Rendering Detection: Identifying and Analyzing unnecessary UI computations","tz":"幻影渲染检测：识别与分析不必要的 UI 计算","a":"Modern mobile applications have high-resolution user interfaces (UI) and heavy computations, resulting in significant energy consumption and latency, especially on older devices. Precisely measuring the performance of mobile operations (e.g., the number of CPU instructions) and detecting performance issues are critical for mobile software engineering. In this study, we characterize a previously underexplored class of performance issues on mobile called Phantom Rendering, which occurs when mobile applications perform unnecessary UI-related offscreen computations but do not visually render them. For example, the animation component stops visually rendering on the screen but continues to refresh in the background. This problem represents a root-level disconnection between UI-related offscreen computational effort and visual rendering, inherent to dual-thread rendering architectures, which has been employed across most modern mobile platforms such as Android, iOS, and OpenHarmony. However, this is hard to automatically detect due to a lack of fine-grained performance measurements and detection methods. To address the challenges, we propose HapPRDetection that contains a fine-grained performance profiler that can sample CPU Retired Instructions, the CPU instructions that have completed their execution and are no longer in the pipeline, and algorithms for automated detection of Phantom Rendering through differential analysis and hierarchical attribution. Our approach advances performance analysis methodology by bridging the semantic gap between fine-grained computational measurements (i.e., the number of CPU Retired Instructions at the function level) and high-level rendering behavior. Through our evaluation of the top-22 real-world mobile applications by download volume in OpenHarmony with 193 test steps, we show that Phantom Rendering issues occur in 19 test cases across 8 applications and that they range up to 40% of wasted CPU instructions in each problematic operation. We provide new insights into mobile rendering efficiency and our detection strategy offers practical solutions to identify and resolve Phantom Rendering during the mobile development loop. Our approach and implementation are available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/PhantomRendering-8356 .","az":"现代移动应用具有高分辨率用户界面（UI）和繁重的计算，导致显著的能耗与延迟，在较旧设备上尤为明显。精确测量移动操作的性能（例如 CPU 指令数）并检测性能问题，对移动软件工程至关重要。在本研究中，我们刻画了一类此前未被充分探索的移动性能问题——幻影渲染（Phantom Rendering），它发生在移动应用执行了不必要的 UI 相关离屏计算却并未在视觉上渲染出来的情形。例如，动画组件已停止在屏幕上视觉渲染，却仍在后台持续刷新。该问题代表了 UI 相关离屏计算开销与视觉渲染之间的根本性脱节，源于双线程渲染架构，而这一架构被 Android、iOS、OpenHarmony 等大多数现代移动平台所采用。然而，由于缺乏细粒度性能测量与检测方法，这一问题难以自动检测。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 HapPRDetection，它包含一个细粒度性能剖析器，可采样 CPU 退休指令（即已完成执行、不再位于流水线中的 CPU 指令），以及通过差分分析与层次化归因实现幻影渲染自动检测的算法。我们的方法通过弥合细粒度计算测量（即函数级 CPU 退休指令数）与高层渲染行为之间的语义鸿沟，推进了性能分析方法学。我们在 OpenHarmony 上下载量排名前 22 的真实移动应用、193 个测试步骤上进行评估，结果显示幻影渲染问题出现在 8 个应用的 19 个测试用例中，在每个问题操作中最高可浪费 40% 的 CPU 指令。我们为移动渲染效率提供了新洞见，我们的检测策略为在移动开发环节中识别并解决幻影渲染提供了实用方案。我们的方法与实现已公开在 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/PhantomRendering-8356 。","tl":"首次刻画并自动检测离屏计算却不渲染的“幻影渲染”缺陷。","au":["Zhihao Lin","Mingyi Zhou","Bo Sun","Han Hu","Gang Fan","Li Li"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["phantom rendering","mobile performance","CPU retired instructions","OpenHarmony","differential analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/172/x","pu":"https://mathieu0905.github.io/papers/hapray_fse.pdf"},{"id":"p00981","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Structure-Aware Delta Debugging with Geometric-Information Weights","tz":"结构感知的 Delta Debugging：基于几何信息权重","a":"Delta debugging is a fundamental technique for automatically minimizing failure-inducing inputs. ProbDD augments ddmin by replacing its deterministic partitioning with a probability-guided search. Recently, Weighted Delta Debugging (WDD) augments ddmin (W_ddmin) or ProbDD (W_ProbDD) with token-based weighting to address size disparities, but it can conflate syntactic size with structural complexity: elements with similar token counts may differ substantially in syntactic structure or semantic significance. We introduce Structure-Aware Delta Debugging (SADD), which quantifies element importance using geometric and information-theoretic properties of program structure. SADD defines a unified weight function that combines three complementary signals—geometric volume, decision uniformity, and effective branch complexity. We instantiate SADD in two algorithms: SA_ddmin, which augments ddmin with structure-aware partitioning, and SA_ProbDD, which injects structural weights into ProbDD’s probabilistic selection. We evaluate SADD against ddmin, W_ddmin, W_ProbDD, and ProbDD within two state-of-the-art delta debugging frameworks, HDD and Perses, using 62 real-world C and XML benchmarks. Under HDD, our approach substantially reduces average delta debugging times: 57.12% (SA_ddmin vs. ddmin), 15.04% (SA_ddmin vs. W_ddmin), and 14.64% (SA_ProbDD vs. ProbDD) on C benchmarks, and 30.12% (SA_ddmin vs. ddmin) and 20.10% (SA_ProbDD vs. ProbDD) on XML benchmarks. On C under Perses, it achieves 7.02% (SA_ProbDD vs. ProbDD). In other cases—such as XML programs with simpler, flatter structures where WDD’s token counting suffices, or under Perses, which already applies structural transformations before ddmin—the gains are limited or absent. An ablation study shows that geometric volume provides the foundation, while information-theoretic metrics add complementary, context-sensitive refinements. Overall, modeling structural complexity improves delta debugging precisely when input hierarchies exhibit diversity that token counts alone cannot capture.","az":"Delta debugging 是自动最小化失败诱导输入的基础技术。ProbDD 通过以概率引导的搜索取代 ddmin 的确定性划分，从而对其进行增强。近期，加权 Delta Debugging（WDD）用基于词元的加权来增强 ddmin（W_ddmin）或 ProbDD（W_ProbDD），以应对规模差异，但它可能把句法规模与结构复杂度混为一谈：词元数量相近的元素在句法结构或语义重要性上可能差别很大。我们提出结构感知 Delta Debugging（SADD），它利用程序结构的几何与信息论属性来量化元素的重要性。SADD 定义了一个统一的权重函数，融合三种互补信号——几何体积、决策均匀性与有效分支复杂度。我们将 SADD 实例化为两个算法：SA_ddmin，用结构感知划分增强 ddmin；以及 SA_ProbDD，将结构权重注入 ProbDD 的概率选择中。我们在两个最先进的 delta debugging 框架 HDD 与 Perses 中，使用 62 个真实世界的 C 与 XML 基准，将 SADD 与 ddmin、W_ddmin、W_ProbDD 和 ProbDD 进行对比。在 HDD 下，我们的方法大幅降低平均 delta debugging 时间：C 基准上分别为 57.12%（SA_ddmin 对 ddmin）、15.04%（SA_ddmin 对 W_ddmin）、14.64%（SA_ProbDD 对 ProbDD），XML 基准上为 30.12%（SA_ddmin 对 ddmin）和 20.10%（SA_ProbDD 对 ProbDD）。在 Perses 下的 C 程序上取得 7.02%（SA_ProbDD 对 ProbDD）。在其他情形下——例如结构更简单、更扁平、词元计数已足够的 XML 程序，或在 ddmin 之前已应用结构变换的 Perses 中——收益有限甚至不存在。消融实验表明，几何体积提供了基础，而信息论指标带来互补的、上下文敏感的精化。总体而言，当输入层次结构呈现出词元计数无法刻画的多样性时，建模结构复杂度恰恰能改进 delta debugging。","tl":"用几何体积与信息论指标度量结构复杂度来加权最小化。","au":["Yonggang Tao","Jingling Xue"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["delta debugging","input minimization","ProbDD","structural weighting","HDD / Perses"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/173/x"},{"id":"p00982","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Compiling Code LLMs into Lightweight Executables","tz":"将代码大模型编译为轻量可执行文件","a":"The demand for better prediction accuracy and higher execution performance in neural networks continues to grow. The emergence and success of Large Language Models (LLMs) have led to the development of many cloud-based tools for software engineering tasks such as code suggestion. While effective, cloud deployment raises concerns over privacy, latency, and reliance on connectivity. Running LLMs locally on personal devices such as laptops would address these issues by enabling offline use and reducing response time. However, local deployment is challenging: commodity devices lack high-performance accelerators like GPUs and are constrained by limited memory and compute capacity, making it difficult to execute large models efficiently. We present Ditto, a novel method for optimizing both the model size of Code LLMs and their inference programs, particularly for statically-typed programming languages such as C. Our approach integrates two key components: (1) a model compression technique inspired by product quantization, which clusters model parameters into codebooks and quantizes them to lower bit widths while ensuring that outputs remain within a bounded error, as well as synthesizing the inference program for the quantized model; and (2) a compilation pass integrated into LLVM that automatically detects and replaces unoptimized General Matrix-Vector Multiplication (GEMV) operations—the most computationally intensive component in code models—with implementations from Basic Linear Algebra Subprograms (BLAS) libraries, which are highly optimized for runtime performance. The output of Ditto is an optimized and compiled executable for running selected Code LLMs. We evaluate Ditto on three popular Code LLMs—Code Llama, MagicCoder, and OpenCodeInterpreter, achieving up to 10.5× faster inference and 6.4× lower memory usage compared with their original inference pipeline, while maintaining accuracy close to that of the full-precision models (with an average loss of only 0.27% in pass@1). Furthermore, Ditto outperforms the state-of-the-art int8 quantization baseline, achieving up to 6.61% higher pass@1 accuracy, 2.2× speedup, and 1.6× memory usage reduction, which demonstrates the effectiveness of our approach.","az":"人们对神经网络更高预测准确率与更高执行性能的需求持续增长。大语言模型（LLM）的出现与成功催生了许多面向软件工程任务（如代码建议）的云端工具。这些工具虽然有效，但云端部署带来了隐私、延迟以及对网络连接依赖的担忧。在笔记本电脑等个人设备上本地运行 LLM 可以解决这些问题，实现离线使用并缩短响应时间。然而，本地部署颇具挑战：普通设备缺乏 GPU 等高性能加速器，且受限于有限的内存与算力，难以高效执行大模型。我们提出 Ditto，一种同时优化代码 LLM 的模型体积及其推理程序的新方法，尤其面向 C 这样的静态类型编程语言。我们的方法整合了两个关键组件：（1）一种受乘积量化启发的模型压缩技术，它将模型参数聚类为码本并量化到更低位宽，同时保证输出误差有界，并为量化后的模型合成推理程序；（2）一个集成到 LLVM 中的编译遍（pass），它自动检测并将未优化的通用矩阵-向量乘法（GEMV）操作——代码模型中计算最密集的部分——替换为对运行时性能高度优化的基础线性代数子程序（BLAS）库实现。Ditto 的输出是一个可运行选定代码 LLM 的、经优化并编译好的可执行文件。我们在三个流行的代码 LLM——Code Llama、MagicCoder 和 OpenCodeInterpreter 上评估 Ditto，相比其原始推理流水线，取得最高 10.5 倍的推理加速与 6.4 倍的内存占用降低，同时保持接近全精度模型的准确率（pass@1 平均仅损失 0.27%）。此外，Ditto 优于最先进的 int8 量化基线，取得最高 6.61% 更高的 pass@1 准确率、2.2 倍加速与 1.6 倍内存降低，证明了我们方法的有效性。","tl":"乘积量化加 LLVM 编译遍，把代码模型编成本地可执行文件。","au":["Jieke Shi","Junda He","Zhou Yang","Chengran Yang","Mykhailo Klymenko","Thong Hoang","Xiwei (Sherry) Xu","Zhenchang Xing","David Lo"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"efficient-inference-quantization-and-ml-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code LLM compression","product quantization","LLVM pass","GEMV / BLAS","local inference"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/174/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29813"},{"id":"p00983","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Three Heads Are Better Than One: A Multi-Perspective Reasoning Framework for Enhanced Vulnerability Detection","tz":"三个臭皮匠胜过一个：面向增强漏洞检测的多视角推理框架","a":"Automated vulnerability detection is crucial for enhancing software security by identifying potential flaws that attackers could exploit, thereby reducing the reliance on labor-intensive manual code audits. Recent advancements have shifted towards leveraging large language models (LLMs) for vulnerability detection, with techniques like Vul-RAG and VulnSage demonstrating progress through structured prompting and external knowledge integration. However, these approaches typically rely on a single reasoning paradigm, limiting their ability to address the complex and diverse nature of real-world vulnerabilities. To overcome these limitations, we propose ReasonVul, a novel multi-perspective reasoning framework that harnesses cognitive synergy among three specialized LLM agents, each embodying a distinct reasoning mode. The framework begins with independent analyses of the source code, followed by a structured debate mechanism to resolve conflicts through iterative rebuttal and revision, ultimately converging on a collaborative judgment. Evaluated on the PrimeVul dataset, ReasonVul achieves a PairAcc of 40.00% and an F1-score of 72.52%, surpassing the best baseline by 81.24% in PairAcc. Further tests on the JITVUL dataset confirm its generalizability, with a PairAcc of 28.67%. Additionally, we analyzed 542 conflict cases and found that 389 were correctly resolved, highlighting the framework’s ability to uncover hidden vulnerabilities through the error-correction mechanism driven by the debate. This work emphasizes the importance of multi-perspective reasoning and collaborative validation in achieving robust and comprehensive vulnerability detection in real-world software systems.","az":"自动化漏洞检测通过识别攻击者可能利用的潜在缺陷来增强软件安全，从而减少对费时费力的人工代码审计的依赖。近期进展转向利用大语言模型（LLM）进行漏洞检测，Vul-RAG 与 VulnSage 等技术通过结构化提示与外部知识集成取得了进步。然而，这些方法通常依赖单一推理范式，限制了其应对真实世界漏洞复杂多样性的能力。为克服这些局限，我们提出 ReasonVul，一个新颖的多视角推理框架，它借助三个各自体现不同推理模式的专用 LLM 智能体之间的认知协同。该框架先对源代码进行独立分析，随后通过结构化辩论机制，经由迭代的反驳与修订来化解冲突，最终收敛到协同判断。在 PrimeVul 数据集上的评估表明，ReasonVul 取得了 40.00% 的 PairAcc 与 72.52% 的 F1 分数，在 PairAcc 上超过最佳基线 81.24%。在 JITVUL 数据集上的进一步测试确认了其泛化能力，PairAcc 达到 28.67%。此外，我们分析了 542 个冲突案例，发现其中 389 个被正确解决，凸显了该框架通过辩论驱动的纠错机制发掘隐藏漏洞的能力。本工作强调了多视角推理与协同验证对实现真实软件系统中稳健、全面漏洞检测的重要性。","tl":"三种推理模式的智能体辩论纠错来判定漏洞。","au":["Xin Peng","Bo Lin","Jing Wang","Xiaoling Li","Jun Ma","Jie Yu","Xiaoguang Mao","Shangwen Wang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","multi-agent debate","PrimeVul","LLM reasoning","cognitive synergy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/175/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3808197"},{"id":"p00984","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"One Size Does Fit All: Exploring Model Fusion for Software Engineering Tasks","tz":"一套方案确实通吃：探索面向软件工程任务的模型融合","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have achieved remarkable performance in software engineering (SE), and fine-tuning LLM for specific SE tasks has gradually become a new paradigm. However, storing fine-tuned checkpoints for multiple tasks incurs heavy storage and deployment complexity. Model fusion, which operates on fine-tuned parameters, offers excellent parameter compression and scalability, yet its effectiveness in the SE domain remains underexplored, making such an investigation essential for guiding the development of customized fusion techniques for the SE domain. To bridge this gap, we conduct a systematic study of model fusion in the SE contexts and reveal the following major findings: (1) when fusing programming languages (PLs) within the same task, model fusion usually works well and can enhance the performance of PLs with fewer data when PLs share similar features. (2) when fusing SE tasks of the same category within a same PL, all methods except TALL-Masks generally suffer substantial performance degradation on specific tasks; (3) when fusing SE tasks of different categories across different PLs, all existing model fusion methods exhibit significant performance degradation on certain tasks. In our evaluation results, TALL-Masks, which introduces a mask for each task to extract the most relevant dimensions from the fusion parameters, achieves promising performance. However, during parameters fusion, weak features (i.e., small variation in fine-tuned parameters) are easily overshadowed by strong ones (i.e., large variation in fine-tuned parameters) during parameter fusion, causing the constructed masks to fail to extract the most relevant parameters. To overcome this situation, we propose an improved version of TALL-Masks, called Scaling-Masks. The key idea is to amplify weak features to prevent them from being overshadowed by strong ones, which is achieved by scaling the value range of weak features to match that of strong features. Experimental results demonstrate that Scaling-Masks can significantly improve fusion performance for tasks with extremely weak features without affecting other tasks, with normalized accuracy improved by 63.49% for vulnerability detection when fusing SE tasks of different categories and 24.02% for PHP when fusing PLs in the code repair task.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在软件工程（SE）中取得了显著性能，针对特定 SE 任务微调 LLM 已逐渐成为新范式。然而，为多个任务分别存储微调后的检查点会带来沉重的存储与部署复杂度。模型融合作用于微调后的参数，提供了出色的参数压缩与可扩展性，但其在 SE 领域的有效性仍未被充分探索，因此开展此类研究对指导 SE 领域定制化融合技术的发展至关重要。为填补这一空白，我们对 SE 场景下的模型融合开展了系统研究，得出以下主要发现：（1）在同一任务内融合多种编程语言（PL）时，模型融合通常效果良好，当 PL 之间具有相似特征时，可以提升数据较少的 PL 的性能；（2）在同一 PL 内融合同一类别的 SE 任务时，除 TALL-Masks 外的所有方法通常在特定任务上遭受显著性能下降；（3）跨不同 PL 融合不同类别的 SE 任务时，所有现有模型融合方法都在某些任务上表现出显著性能下降。在我们的评估结果中，TALL-Masks 为每个任务引入一个掩码以从融合参数中提取最相关维度，取得了有希望的性能。然而，在参数融合过程中，弱特征（即微调参数变化较小者）容易被强特征（即微调参数变化较大者）淹没，导致构建出的掩码无法提取最相关的参数。为克服这一情形，我们提出 TALL-Masks 的改进版本，称为 Scaling-Masks。其核心思想是放大弱特征，防止其被强特征淹没，具体做法是将弱特征的取值范围缩放到与强特征匹配。实验结果表明，Scaling-Masks 能在不影响其他任务的前提下显著改善特征极弱任务的融合性能：在融合不同类别 SE 任务时，漏洞检测的归一化准确率提升 63.49%；在代码修复任务中融合多种 PL 时，PHP 提升 24.02%。","tl":"系统评测 SE 任务模型融合，并用弱特征缩放改进掩码融合。","au":["Yinggang Qiu","Yihao Qin","Mingyang Geng","Shangwen Wang","Dezun Dong"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["model fusion","model merging","TALL-Masks","multi-task SE","parameter compression"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/176/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3808198"},{"id":"p00985","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Improving Data Leakage Detection in Machine Learning Notebooks through Static Slicing and Structured LLM Prompts","tz":"通过静态切片与结构化 LLM 提示改进机器学习 Notebook 中的数据泄漏检测","a":"Data leakage remains a critical yet under-diagnosed issue in machine learning pipelines, leading to inflated results and unreliable deployments. Existing detection approaches rely on static rules that often miss open-coded manipulations and fail to capture the diversity of real-world notebooks. This paper introduces a novel methodology that integrates static slicing with large language models (LLMs) to improve leakage detection. We use a Datalog-based static analysis that isolates compact, provenance-aware slices corresponding to model training and evaluation pairs, and we pair these with structured LLM prompts that guide step-by-step reasoning about potential leakage for each isolated slice. Evaluated on a curated benchmark of Python notebooks from Kaggle and GitHub, our approach achieves state-of-the-art performance in both preprocessing and overlap leakage detection, substantially outperforming end-to-end prompting and the rule-based baseline. Our findings highlight the effectiveness of combining program slicing and prompt engineering for data leakage detection and establish the first systematic LLM-based solution for detecting data leakage in machine learning code.","az":"数据泄漏仍是机器学习流水线中一个关键却诊断不足的问题，会导致结果虚高与部署不可靠。现有检测方法依赖静态规则，常常遗漏自由编写的数据操作，也无法涵盖真实世界 notebook 的多样性。本文提出一种新颖的方法学，将静态切片与大语言模型（LLM）相结合以改进泄漏检测。我们使用基于 Datalog 的静态分析，隔离出与模型训练和评估配对相对应的、紧凑且带有来源信息的切片，并将其与结构化的 LLM 提示配对，引导模型对每个隔离切片中潜在的泄漏进行逐步推理。在一个由 Kaggle 与 GitHub 上的 Python notebook 精心整理而成的基准上评估，我们的方法在预处理泄漏与重叠泄漏检测上都达到了最先进的性能，大幅优于端到端提示与基于规则的基线。我们的发现凸显了结合程序切片与提示工程进行数据泄漏检测的有效性，并确立了首个用于检测机器学习代码中数据泄漏的系统性 LLM 方案。","tl":"用 Datalog 切片缩小范围再让 LLM 逐步推断数据泄漏。","au":["Taha Draoui","Mohamed Wiem Mkaouer","Christian D. Newman"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["data leakage","Jupyter notebooks","program slicing","Datalog static analysis","structured prompting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/177/x"},{"id":"p00986","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Comment Traps: How Defective Commented-out Code Augment Defects in AI-Assisted Code Generation","tz":"注释陷阱：有缺陷的注释掉代码如何加剧 AI 辅助代码生成中的缺陷","a":"With the rapid development of large language models in code generation, AI-powered editors such as GitHub Copilot and Cursor are revolutionizing software development practices. At the same time, studies have identified potential defects in the generated code. Previous research has predominantly examined how code context influences the generation of defective code, often overlooking the impact of defects within commented-out code (CO code). AI coding assistants’ interpretation of CO code in prompts affects the code they generate. This study evaluates how AI coding assistants, GitHub Copilot and Cursor, are influenced by defective CO code. The experimental results show that defective CO code in the context causes AI coding assistants to generate more defective code, reaching up to 58.17 percent. Our findings further demonstrate that the tools do not simply copy the defective code from the context. Instead, they actively reason to complete incomplete defect patterns and continue to produce defective code despite distractions such as incorrect indentation or tags. Even with explicit instructions to ignore the defective CO code, the reduction in defects does not exceed 21.84 percent. These findings underscore the need for improved robustness and security measures in AI coding assistants.","az":"随着大语言模型在代码生成方面的迅猛发展，GitHub Copilot 与 Cursor 等 AI 驱动的编辑器正在变革软件开发实践。与此同时，已有研究识别出生成代码中潜在的缺陷。以往研究主要考察代码上下文如何影响缺陷代码的生成，却往往忽视了被注释掉的代码（CO 代码）中缺陷所带来的影响。AI 编程助手对提示中 CO 代码的解读会影响其生成的代码。本研究评估了 AI 编程助手 GitHub Copilot 与 Cursor 受有缺陷 CO 代码影响的程度。实验结果表明，上下文中的有缺陷 CO 代码会导致 AI 编程助手生成更多缺陷代码，最高可达 58.17%。我们的发现进一步表明，这些工具并非简单地从上下文中复制缺陷代码；相反，它们会主动推理以补全不完整的缺陷模式，并且在诸如错误缩进或标记等干扰下仍继续产出缺陷代码。即便给出明确指令要求忽略有缺陷的 CO 代码，缺陷的减少幅度也不超过 21.84%。这些发现凸显了在 AI 编程助手中改进鲁棒性与安全措施的必要性。","tl":"注释掉的缺陷代码会被助手主动补全，明令忽略也难消除。","au":["Yuan Huang","Yukang Zhou","Xiangping Chen","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","security"],"kw":["commented-out code","AI coding assistant","defective code generation","GitHub Copilot","Cursor"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/178/x"},{"id":"p00987","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Influence-Aware Bayesian-Inspired Token Reweighting for Improved Code Generation","tz":"面向改进代码生成的影响力感知贝叶斯式词元重加权","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have achieved remarkable progress in code generation, yet the structural properties of programming languages introduce distinctive challenges. In particular, program correctness is disproportionately influenced by a subset of structurally critical tokens, such as API names, variable identifiers, and control-flow keywords, termed as influential tokens. Errors in predicting these tokens often propagate and accumulate through subsequent decoding steps, leading to substantial degradation in overall correctness. Addressing the heterogeneous difficulty of predicting such tokens is therefore crucial for improving the reliability of code generation. To address this challenge, we introduce Influence-Aware Bayesian Code Generation (I-BAYGEN), a framework that explicitly handles influential tokens. The framework consists of two components. First, it identifies influential tokens using a loss-based detection mechanism, and measures the influential degree of each token in three ways. Second, to handle the influential tokens, we explicitly steer additional reasoning paths as the evidence to obtain the posterior token distribution during code generation, which can be treated as Bayesian inference. To optimize the posterior likelihood, we involve the influence scores as weights to enhance the self-rewarding, making the LLM pay more attention to the identified influential tokens. Using the influence-based reweighting mechanism, the framework provides differentiated treatment to tokens based on their difficulty, with influential tokens receiving enhanced attention through refined reward structures and deeper reasoning processes. Comprehensive experiments on competition-level programming benchmarks demonstrate that I-BAYGEN achieves up to 47.2% relative improvement in accuracy over state-of-the-art approaches employing non-weighted rewards. Moreover, qualitative analysis reveals that the framework produces reasoning paths that are more interpretable and logically coherent, effectively addressing heterogeneous token difficulty in code generation.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在代码生成方面取得了显著进展，但编程语言的结构特性带来了独特挑战。特别地，程序的正确性受一小部分结构关键词元（如 API 名称、变量标识符和控制流关键字，称为影响力词元）的影响尤为突出。预测这些词元时的错误往往会在后续解码步骤中传播与累积，导致整体正确性大幅下降。因此，处理这类词元预测难度的异质性，对提升代码生成的可靠性至关重要。为应对这一挑战，我们提出影响力感知贝叶斯代码生成（I-BAYGEN），一个显式处理影响力词元的框架。该框架包含两个组件。首先，它使用基于损失的检测机制识别影响力词元，并以三种方式度量每个词元的影响力程度。其次，为处理这些影响力词元，我们在代码生成过程中显式引导额外的推理路径作为证据，从而获得后验词元分布，这可视为贝叶斯推断。为优化后验似然，我们将影响力分数作为权重来增强自奖励，使 LLM 更加关注被识别出的影响力词元。借助这种基于影响力的重加权机制，该框架依据词元难度对其进行差异化处理，影响力词元通过精化的奖励结构与更深入的推理过程获得更多关注。在竞赛级编程基准上的全面实验表明，I-BAYGEN 相比采用非加权奖励的最先进方法，准确率最高实现 47.2% 的相对提升。此外，定性分析显示该框架产生的推理路径更具可解释性与逻辑连贯性，有效应对了代码生成中词元难度的异质性问题。","tl":"识别结构关键词元并用贝叶斯式重加权与额外推理路径纠偏。","au":["YUQI ZHU","Ge Li","Hong Mei","Zhi Jin","Jia Li","Qibin Zheng","Jieyuan Zhang"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["influential tokens","token reweighting","Bayesian inference","code generation","self-rewarding"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/179/x"},{"id":"p00988","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"pPatch: Automated Vulnerability Unpatching","tz":"pPatch：自动化的漏洞反补丁","a":"Unpatching, the process of reverting security patches to reintroduce historical vulnerabilities into newer software versions, is valuable for creating realistic benchmarks to evaluate security analysis tools. However, this process is challenging due to code evolution, leading to context conflicts, compilation errors, or untriggerable issues. In fact, 61.25% of Linux kernel security patches we examined cannot be trivially reverted to recent versions. To address this, we propose pPatch, an automated framework designed to systematically unpatch security vulnerabilities and generate vulnerability benchmark. pPatch overcomes the limitations of naive reversion by employing a novel approach that progressively consults conflicting commits to identify and integrate necessary code changes, aiming for minimal modifications to preserve program semantics while successfully reintroducing the vulnerability without side effects. Then pPatch unpatches 614 historic kernel vulnerabilities from Linux kernel v6.6 and v6.12, resulting in 371 and 353 successfully unpatched vulnerabilities with manual analysis. Based on the validation with Proof-of-Concept (PoC) and automated fuzzing, we constructed KVULNBENCH with 187 verified vulnerabilities, the first automatically generated and verified high-quality vulnerability dataset specifically for the Linux kernel. Using KVULNBENCH we evaluated the performance of state-of-the-art kernel security tools (e.g., syzkaller), demonstrating that KVULNBENCH provides a valuable resource for realistically assessing kernel security tools.","az":"反补丁（unpatching）指回退安全补丁，从而把历史漏洞重新引入较新版本的软件，这对构建真实的基准以评估安全分析工具很有价值。然而，由于代码演化，该过程颇具挑战，会导致上下文冲突、编译错误或问题无法触发。事实上，我们考察的 Linux 内核安全补丁中有 61.25% 无法被简单地回退到近期版本。为解决这一问题，我们提出 pPatch，一个用于系统化反补丁安全漏洞并生成漏洞基准的自动化框架。pPatch 通过一种新颖的方法克服朴素回退的局限：逐步查阅冲突的提交，以识别并整合必要的代码更改，力求以最小修改保持程序语义，同时在无副作用的情况下成功重新引入漏洞。随后，pPatch 从 Linux 内核 v6.6 与 v6.12 中反补丁了 614 个历史内核漏洞，经人工分析分别得到 371 个和 353 个成功反补丁的漏洞。基于概念验证（PoC）与自动化模糊测试的验证，我们构建了 KVULNBENCH，包含 187 个已验证漏洞，这是首个专门面向 Linux 内核、自动生成并经过验证的高质量漏洞数据集。利用 KVULNBENCH，我们评估了最先进的内核安全工具（例如 syzkaller）的性能，证明 KVULNBENCH 是真实评估内核安全工具的宝贵资源。","tl":"自动回退内核安全补丁，构建 187 个已验证漏洞的基准。","au":["Tianyi Jing","Pengyu Ding","Meng Xu","Yinhao Hu","Zheng Yu","Dongliang Mu"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unpatching","security patch reversion","Linux kernel","vulnerability benchmark","syzkaller"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/180/x"},{"id":"p00989","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Co-Evolution of Types and Dependencies: Towards Repository-Level Type Inference for Python Code","tz":"类型与依赖的协同演化：迈向 Python 代码的仓库级类型推断","a":"Python’s dynamic typing mechanism, while promoting flexibility, is a significant source of runtime type errors that plague large-scale software, which inspires the automatic type inference techniques. Existing type inference tools have achieved advances in type inference within isolated code snippets. However, repository-level type inference remains a significant challenge, primarily due to the complex inter-procedural dependencies that are difficult to model and resolve. To fill this gap, we present PyTIR, a novel approach based on LLMs that achieves repository-level type inference through the co-evolution of types and dependencies. PyTIR constructs an Entity Dependency Graph (EDG) to model the objects and type dependencies across the repository. During the inference process, it iteratively refines types and dependencies in EDG for accurate type inference. Our key innovations are: (1) an EDG model designed to capture repository-level type dependencies; (2) an iterative type inference approach where types and dependencies co-evolve in each iteration; and (3) a type-checker-in-the-loop strategy that validates and corrects inferences on-the-fly, thereby reducing error propagation. When evaluated on 12 complex Python repositories,PyTIR significantly outperformed prior works, achieving a TypeSim score of 0.89 and a TypeExact score of 0.84, representing a 27% and 40% relative improvement over the strongest baseline. More importantly, PyTIR removed new type errors introduced by the tool by 92.7%. This demonstrates a significant leap towards automated, reliable type annotation for real-world Python development.","az":"Python 的动态类型机制在提升灵活性的同时，也是大规模软件中运行时类型错误的重要来源，这催生了自动类型推断技术。现有类型推断工具在孤立代码片段内的类型推断上取得了进展。然而，仓库级类型推断仍是重大挑战，主要原因在于复杂的过程间依赖难以建模与求解。为填补这一空白，我们提出 PyTIR，一种基于 LLM 的新方法，通过类型与依赖的协同演化实现仓库级类型推断。PyTIR 构建实体依赖图（EDG）来建模整个仓库中的对象与类型依赖。在推断过程中，它迭代地精化 EDG 中的类型与依赖，以实现准确的类型推断。我们的关键创新包括：（1）用于刻画仓库级类型依赖的 EDG 模型；（2）类型与依赖在每轮迭代中协同演化的迭代式类型推断方法；（3）类型检查器在环（type-checker-in-the-loop）策略，实时验证并纠正推断结果，从而减少错误传播。在 12 个复杂 Python 仓库上的评估中，PyTIR 显著优于已有工作，取得 TypeSim 0.89 与 TypeExact 0.84，相比最强基线分别实现 27% 与 40% 的相对提升。更重要的是，PyTIR 将工具引入的新类型错误消除了 92.7%。这标志着面向真实 Python 开发的自动化、可靠类型标注迈出了重要一步。","tl":"用实体依赖图让类型与依赖协同迭代演化并由类型检查器纠错。","au":["Shuo Sun","Shixin Zhang","Jiwei Yan","Jun Yan","Jian Zhang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["type inference","Python","entity dependency graph","repository-level analysis","type checker in the loop"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/181/x"},{"id":"p00990","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Interrogation Testing of CHC Solvers","tz":"CHC 求解器的问询式测试","a":"A Constrained Horn Clause (CHC) is a specific type of logic formula that contains uninterpreted predicates. CHC formulas are often used by static program analyzers to encode program properties, which are then verified using CHC solvers. The solvers themselves are complex tools and may contain bugs, which can lead to verifying unsafe programs, flagging safe programs as unsafe, or providing analyzers with incorrect invariants and counterexamples. It is, therefore, crucial to develop techniques for systematically testing CHC solvers. In this paper, we present the first interrogation-testing technique for CHC solvers, which we implement in a tool called HornGator. Our technique uses witnesses generated by the solver under test to form new CHC instances. It also integrates a knowledge base maintaining a history of past solver queries. All this information helps HornGator generate more diverse instances, thereby improving its bug-finding effectiveness. As a result, HornGator found 21 unique bugs in five state-of-the-art CHC solvers, all of which are confirmed by the developers, 18 are fixed, and eight are of the highest severity.","az":"约束霍恩子句（CHC）是一类包含未解释谓词的逻辑公式。CHC 公式常被静态程序分析器用来编码程序性质，随后由 CHC 求解器进行验证。求解器本身是复杂工具，可能含有缺陷，从而导致验证通过不安全的程序、把安全程序判为不安全，或向分析器提供错误的不变式与反例。因此，开发系统化测试 CHC 求解器的技术至关重要。本文提出首个面向 CHC 求解器的问询式测试（interrogation-testing）技术，并将其实现为工具 HornGator。我们的技术利用被测求解器生成的见证（witness）来构造新的 CHC 实例，同时集成了一个维护历史求解查询的知识库。所有这些信息帮助 HornGator 生成更具多样性的实例，从而提升其发现缺陷的有效性。结果表明，HornGator 在五个最先进的 CHC 求解器中发现了 21 个独特缺陷，全部获得开发者确认，其中 18 个已被修复，8 个属于最高严重级别。","tl":"用求解器自产的见证反过来构造新实例进行问询式测试。","au":["David Kaindlstorfer","Anastasia Isychev","Valentin Wüstholz","Maria Christakis"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["CHC solver testing","interrogation testing","witness-based instance generation","solver bugs","HornGator"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/182/x","pu":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/FSE-2026-CHC.pdf"},{"id":"p00991","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SpecWeaver: End-to-End HTTP API Specification Inference Across Multi-Layer Routing in Production Web Services","tz":"SpecWeaver：在生产 Web 服务的多层路由中进行端到端 HTTP API 规约推断","a":"HTTP API specifications are essential for modern web development, yet existing tools fail in production environments due to multi-layer routing. Production deployments employ infrastructure-level and framework-level routing that apply sequential rewrite and dispatch rules, creating a gap between client-visible external paths and internal paths. To address this challenge, we present SpecWeaver, the first tool to automatically extract and unify heterogeneous configuration-defined routing rules with code-level handlers. Our approach combines routing component information gathering, iterative configuration discovery using LLMs, and routing extraction from diverse configuration files to construct a routing graph representation that captures end-to-end routing relationships. Evaluated on 10 production applications, SpecWeaver extracts 36,361 rewrite rules and 48,394 dispatch rules with 99.44%/100% precision, materializes 8,288 external API paths, contributes 5,116 previously undocumented APIs with 160 unauthenticated endpoints, helps an existing testing tool improve testing coverage by 328.6% compared to the baseline, and discovers 305 bugs.","az":"HTTP API 规约对现代 Web 开发至关重要，但现有工具在生产环境中因多层路由而失效。生产部署会采用基础设施层与框架层的路由，它们应用顺序化的重写与分发规则，从而在客户端可见的外部路径与内部路径之间造成鸿沟。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 SpecWeaver，首个自动抽取并统一异构的、由配置定义的路由规则与代码级处理函数的工具。我们的方法结合了路由组件信息收集、利用 LLM 的迭代式配置发现，以及从多样配置文件中抽取路由，进而构建刻画端到端路由关系的路由图表示。在 10 个生产应用上的评估表明，SpecWeaver 抽取了 36,361 条重写规则与 48,394 条分发规则，精确率分别为 99.44%/100%，具体化出 8,288 条外部 API 路径，贡献了 5,116 条此前未被记录的 API（其中 160 个为免认证端点），帮助一个现有测试工具相比基线提升了 328.6% 的测试覆盖率，并发现了 305 个缺陷。","tl":"统一多层路由配置与代码处理函数，还原真实外部 API 规约。","au":["Wenbo Hu","Jie Lu","Jingting Chen","Feng Li","Chenghang Shi","Xiaonan Shi","Jinchen Wang","Wei Huo"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["API specification inference","multi-layer routing","web services","routing graph","undocumented endpoints"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/183/x"},{"id":"p00992","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Building Software by Rolling the Dice: A Qualitative Study of Vibe Coding","tz":"靠掷骰子造软件：关于 Vibe Coding 的质性研究","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are reshaping software engineering by enabling vibe coding—building software primarily through prompts rather than writing code. Although widely publicized as a productivity breakthrough, little is known about how practitioners actually define and engage in these practices. To shed some light on this emerging phenomenon, we conducted a grounded theory study of 20 vibe-coding videos, including 7 live-streamed coding sessions (~16 hours, 254 prompts) and 13 opinion videos (~5 hours), supported by additional analysis of activity durations and intents of prompts. Our findings reveal a spectrum of behaviors: some vibe coders rely almost entirely on AI without inspecting code, while others examine and adapt generated outputs. Across approaches, all must contend with the stochastic nature of code generation, with debugging and refinement described as “rolling the dice.” Further, divergent mental models, shaped by developers’ expertise and engagement with AI, influence prompting strategies, evaluation practices, and levels of trust. These findings open new directions for research on the future of software engineering and point to practical opportunities for tool design and education.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）正在重塑软件工程，催生了 vibe coding——主要通过提示而非亲手写代码来构建软件。尽管它被广泛宣传为生产力突破，但关于从业者实际如何定义并参与这些实践，人们所知甚少。为揭示这一新兴现象，我们对 20 个 vibe coding 视频开展了扎根理论研究，其中包括 7 场直播编程会话（约 16 小时、254 条提示）和 13 个观点类视频（约 5 小时），并辅以对活动时长与提示意图的额外分析。我们的发现揭示了一个行为谱系：一些 vibe coder 几乎完全依赖 AI 而不检查代码，另一些则会审视并调整生成的输出。无论采用哪种方式，所有人都必须应对代码生成的随机性，调试与精化被描述为“掷骰子”。此外，由开发者专业水平及其与 AI 互动程度所塑造的不同心智模型，会影响提示策略、评估实践与信任水平。这些发现为软件工程未来的研究开辟了新方向，并为工具设计与教育指出了切实机会。","tl":"以 20 个真实视频扎根理论刻画 vibe coding 的行为谱系。","au":["Yi-Hung Chou","Boyuan Jiang","Yiwen Chen","Mingyue Weng","Victoria Jackson","Thomas Zimmermann","James Jones"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["human-study","empirical-study"],"kw":["vibe coding","grounded theory","prompting strategies","mental models","trust in AI"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/184/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.22418"},{"id":"p00993","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Accelerating Policy Synthesis in Large-Scale MDPs via Hierarchical Adaptive Refinement","tz":"通过分层自适应精化加速大规模 MDP 中的策略综合","a":"Software-intensive systems, such as software product lines and robotics, utilise Markov decision processes (MDPs) to capture uncertainty and analyse sequential decision-making problems. Despite the usefulness of conventional policy synthesis methods, they fail to scale to large state spaces. Our approach addresses this issue and accelerates policy synthesis in large MDPs by dynamically refining the MDP and iteratively selecting the most fragile MDP regions for refinement. This iterative procedure offers a balance between accuracy and efficiency, as refinement occurs only when necessary. We formally show that the composed policy is near-optimal under standard assumptions, with error bounded by the local solver tolerance and boundary mismatch. Across diverse case studies and MDPs up to 1M states, we demonstrate that our approach achieves up to 2x speedup over PRISM, offering a competitive solution for real-world policy synthesis in large MDPs.","az":"软件产品线与机器人等软件密集型系统利用马尔可夫决策过程（MDP）来刻画不确定性并分析序贯决策问题。尽管传统的策略综合方法很有用，但它们无法扩展到大规模状态空间。我们的方法解决了这一问题：通过动态精化 MDP 并迭代地选择最脆弱的 MDP 区域进行精化，从而加速大规模 MDP 中的策略综合。这一迭代过程在准确性与效率之间取得平衡，因为仅在必要时才进行精化。我们形式化地证明，在标准假设下所组合出的策略是近最优的，其误差由局部求解器容差与边界失配所界定。在多样的案例研究以及规模达 100 万状态的 MDP 上，我们证明该方法相比 PRISM 可获得最高 2 倍的加速，为大规模 MDP 中的真实策略综合提供了有竞争力的方案。","tl":"只对最脆弱区域自适应精化，近最优地加速大规模策略综合。","au":["Alexandros Evangelidis","Gricel Vázquez","Simos Gerasimou"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["policy synthesis","Markov decision process","adaptive refinement","near-optimality bound","PRISM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/185/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.17792"},{"id":"p00994","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Red Teaming LLMs via Linguistic-Aware Fuzzing","tz":"通过语言学感知的模糊测试对 LLM 进行红队测试","a":"Safety alignment aims to prevent Large Language Models (LLMs) from producing harmful content. However, safety alignment remains vulnerable to malicious instructions. Red teaming is a critical methodology for identifying such vulnerabilities in LLMs. Existing approaches often rely on jailbreak templates or rule-based transformation, limiting the diversity of generated tests and the continued testing capability of these test approaches. To address these limitations, we propose Lingfuzz, a linguistic-aware fuzzing framework for continuing red teaming LLMs. The key idea of this framework is to mutate the existing malicious instructions at the lexical and syntactic levels, while keeping the malicious intentions of the instructions. Such mutations enable generating diverse malicious instructions due to the unlimited space of lexical and syntactic choices, while having a continued testing capability by iteratively mutating the mutants. We evaluated Lingfuzz on three aligned GPT-series LLMs. The results show that Lingfuzz triggers safety alignment vulnerabilities in 81.3% of the cases in JailbreakBench benchmark. The malicious instructions generated by Lingfuzz have more than three times higher diversity than previous work according to the self-BLEU metric, while keeping the similar effectiveness in triggering safety alignment vulnerabilities. Lingfuzz also demonstrates strong continued testing capability by showing five times less sensitivity to the LLM evolution than other approaches.","az":"安全对齐旨在防止大语言模型（LLM）生成有害内容。然而，安全对齐仍然易受恶意指令攻击。红队测试是识别 LLM 中此类漏洞的关键方法学。现有方法常依赖越狱模板或基于规则的变换，限制了所生成测试的多样性以及这些测试方法的持续测试能力。为解决这些局限，我们提出 Lingfuzz，一个用于持续红队测试 LLM 的语言学感知模糊测试框架。该框架的核心思想是在词法与句法层面变异已有的恶意指令，同时保持指令的恶意意图。由于词法与句法选择的空间无限，这类变异既能生成多样的恶意指令，又能通过对变异体的迭代再变异而具备持续测试能力。我们在三个经过对齐的 GPT 系列 LLM 上评估了 Lingfuzz。结果表明，Lingfuzz 在 JailbreakBench 基准中 81.3% 的案例上触发了安全对齐漏洞。根据 self-BLEU 指标，Lingfuzz 生成的恶意指令多样性比以往工作高出三倍以上，同时在触发安全对齐漏洞方面保持相近的有效性。Lingfuzz 还表现出强大的持续测试能力，对 LLM 演化的敏感度比其他方法低五倍。","tl":"在词法与句法层保意变异恶意指令，实现可持续的红队测试。","au":["Shuai Yuan","Nian Luo","Jingling Sun","Yihao Huang","Chengyu Zhang"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["cross-track-bridge","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["red teaming","safety alignment","linguistic mutation","fuzzing","JailbreakBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/186/x"},{"id":"p00995","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RealBench: A Repo-Level Code Generation Benchmark Aligned with Real-World Software Development Practices","tz":"RealBench：一个与真实软件开发实践对齐的仓库级代码生成基准","a":"Writing code requires significant time and effort in software development. To automate this process, researchers have made substantial progress using Large Language Models (LLMs) for code generation. Many benchmarks like HumanEval and EvoCodeBench have been created to evaluate LLMs by requiring them to generate code from natural language requirements. However, in enterprise applications and team development, developers typically write code based on structured designs or specifications rather than raw natural language descriptions. This gap between existing benchmarks and real industry development practices means that current benchmark scores may not accurately reflect how much code generation can help automate software development tasks. To address this gap, we propose RealBench, a repository-level code generation benchmark aligned with real-world industry software development practices. Each example includes both natural language requirements and UML diagrams as system design, matching how developers typically receive specifications. Based on the constructed benchmarks, we conduct a systematic evaluation of advanced LLMs’ code generation capabilities when provided with structured system designs. Specifically, we design three generation strategies to evaluate advanced LLMs on RealBench and propose two evaluation granularities with five metrics. The experimental results reveal key insights in current LLMs’ capabilities for repo-level code generation aligned with real-world software development practices. First, we notice that regarding repo-level code generation, LLMs show much worse performance and there are significant performance gaps among LLMs. Second, LLMs are good at finding and creating modules defined in UML diagrams, but the quality of generated modules is often poor due to grammar and logic errors. Third, generating the entire repository at once is the best generation strategy on smaller repositories, while generating a complex repository with the module-by-module strategy works better compared to other strategies. Fourth, the detailed system design is very important for repository-level code generation tasks through conducting ablation studies on system designs. Lastly, we discuss the frequent error types in generated repositories to provide insights for optimizing repo-level code generation.","az":"编写代码在软件开发中需要大量时间与精力。为自动化这一过程，研究者在使用大语言模型（LLM）进行代码生成方面取得了显著进展。HumanEval 与 EvoCodeBench 等许多基准被创建出来，通过要求 LLM 从自然语言需求生成代码来对其评估。然而，在企业应用与团队开发中，开发者通常依据结构化的设计或规约而非原始自然语言描述来编写代码。现有基准与真实工业开发实践之间的这一鸿沟，意味着当前的基准分数可能无法准确反映代码生成在多大程度上能帮助自动化软件开发任务。为弥合这一鸿沟，我们提出 RealBench，一个与真实工业软件开发实践对齐的仓库级代码生成基准。每个样例同时包含自然语言需求与作为系统设计的 UML 图，契合开发者通常收到规约的方式。基于所构建的基准，我们系统评估了先进 LLM 在获得结构化系统设计时的代码生成能力。具体而言，我们设计了三种生成策略以在 RealBench 上评估先进 LLM，并提出两种评估粒度与五项指标。实验结果揭示了当前 LLM 在与真实软件开发实践对齐的仓库级代码生成方面能力的若干关键洞见。第一，我们注意到在仓库级代码生成上，LLM 的表现要差得多，且不同 LLM 之间存在显著性能差距。第二，LLM 擅长发现并创建 UML 图中定义的模块，但生成模块的质量常因语法与逻辑错误而较差。第三，在较小的仓库上，一次性生成整个仓库是最佳生成策略；而对复杂仓库，逐模块生成策略相比其他策略效果更好。第四，通过对系统设计开展消融实验，我们发现详细的系统设计对仓库级代码生成任务非常重要。最后，我们讨论了生成仓库中的常见错误类型，以为优化仓库级代码生成提供启示。","tl":"以需求加 UML 设计为输入的仓库级代码生成基准与策略对比。","au":["Jia Li","Hongyi Deng","Yiran Zhang","Kechi Zhang","Tianqi Shao","Tiankuo Zhao","Weinan Wang","Zhi Jin","Ge Li","Yang Liu","Yingtao Fang","Yihong Dong"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","multimodal"],"kw":["repository-level code generation","benchmark","UML system design","generation strategies","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/187/x"},{"id":"p00996","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Sound Termination and Non-Termination Analysis of C Programs with Bit-Precise Bounded Semantics and Advanced Constructs","tz":"基于位精确有界语义与高级构造的 C 程序健全停机与非停机分析","a":"Program termination and non-termination analysis is a foundational problem in formal verification with important implications for software safety and reliability. Despite extensive research, existing techniques struggle with real-world C programs that manipulate complex data types such as pointers, arrays, and structures, or that perform low-level operations such as bitwise arithmetic and bounded integer computations. This paper introduces Athena, a framework for sound termination and non-termination analysis of C programs that faithfully captures concrete C semantics and supports advanced constructs. Athena combines pointer-to-array rewriting, bounded integer semantics via modulo arithmetic or bit-vector semantics, and an extended translation to Labeled Transition Systems (LTS), yielding structured, analyzable representations suitable for logic-based reasoning. Our analysis engine builds on MuVal, a modular verification engine based on the first-order fixpoint logic μCLP with background theories, and extends it with support for array, tuple, and bit-vector theories in ranking function synthesis and recurrent set detection. We evaluate Athena on the 2024 Termination Competition (TermCOMP) and on 117 real-world benchmarks featuring 445 non-termination bugs. On real-world benchmarks, it achieves the highest correctness (62.39%), surpassing the well-established tools UAutomizer and AProVE. On TermCOMP, it attains 75.60%, outperforming AProVE, while producing zero wrong results across both suites. These results demonstrate that Athena advances the state of the art by providing a strong combination of precision and soundness in the analysis of complex C programs.","az":"程序停机与非停机分析是形式化验证中的基础问题，对软件安全性与可靠性具有重要意义。尽管已有大量研究，现有技术在处理操作指针、数组、结构体等复杂数据类型，或执行按位运算与有界整数计算等底层操作的真实 C 程序时仍然吃力。本文提出 Athena，一个用于 C 程序健全停机与非停机分析的框架，它忠实刻画具体的 C 语义并支持高级语言构造。Athena 结合了指针到数组的重写、通过模运算或位向量语义实现的有界整数语义，以及到带标号迁移系统（LTS）的扩展翻译，从而产生结构化、可分析、适合逻辑推理的表示。我们的分析引擎构建在 MuVal 之上——一个基于带背景理论的一阶不动点逻辑 μCLP 的模块化验证引擎——并在排名函数综合与递归集检测中扩展了对数组、元组与位向量理论的支持。我们在 2024 年停机竞赛（TermCOMP）以及 117 个包含 445 个非停机缺陷的真实基准上评估 Athena。在真实基准上，它取得最高的正确率（62.39%），超过了成熟工具 UAutomizer 与 AProVE；在 TermCOMP 上取得 75.60%，优于 AProVE，且在两个测试集上均未产生任何错误结果。这些结果表明 Athena 在复杂 C 程序分析中提供了精度与健全性的有力结合，推进了该领域的最新水平。","tl":"把位精确有界语义与指针数组重写并入停机性分析引擎。","au":["Negar Fathi","Hiroshi Unno","Tachio Terauchi","Rahul Purandare"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["termination analysis","non-termination","bit-precise semantics","ranking function synthesis","C programs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/188/x","pu":"https://github.com/negarfathi/Athena/blob/master/Paper.pdf"},{"id":"p00997","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Revealing Regressions: A Comparative Study of State-Capture Strategies in Validating Program Behavior","tz":"揭示回归：验证程序行为中状态捕获策略的对比研究","a":"A central challenge in software testing is deciding which parts of a program’s state to check as evidence of correct behavior to reveal regressions. These checks are embodied as test oracles, typically as assertions in test cases. State observation strategies play a decisive role in shaping how effectively regressions can be revealed. Such strategies range from exhaustive memory snapshots to selective attribute checks via getter methods and nullability checks. These strategies are deeply embedded in both research and practice: academic work has explored heuristic- and serialization-based oracles, while industry has widely adopted snapshot testing. Despite their importance, the effects of different state-capture choices remain poorly understood from a scientific perspective. In this work, we present an experimental framework for systematically analyzing these design choices along the dimensions of observation scope, extraction approach, and extraction depth. Using this framework, we conduct an empirical study across twelve real-world projects, measuring how state-capture strategies influence regression-revealing capability and the richness of oracle information. Our findings reveal that human-written assertions often under-utilize available program state, achieving well below the fault-revealing potential of systematic observation strategies. Simple design choices, such as exposing unchecked intermediate return values, carefully selecting getters, and deepening state extraction, can yield measurable improvements (avg. 35.7%) in regression detection without needing to observe an overwhelmingly large amount of program-state data. Additionally, we highlight the challenges of observability, assertion desirability, and the trade-offs of capturing richer program states. Such insights show how small design choices can yield major differences in regression detection and potentially offer concrete directions for both tool builders and practitioners.","az":"软件测试中的一个核心挑战是决定检查程序状态的哪些部分，作为行为正确的证据以揭示回归。这些检查体现为测试预言，通常以测试用例中的断言形式出现。状态观察策略在决定回归能被多有效地揭示方面起着决定性作用。这类策略从穷尽式内存快照，到通过 getter 方法进行的选择性属性检查以及空值检查，不一而足。这些策略在研究与实践中都根深蒂固：学术界探索了基于启发式与序列化的预言，工业界则广泛采用了快照测试。尽管它们很重要，不同状态捕获选择的影响从科学角度看仍缺乏理解。在本工作中，我们提出一个实验框架，沿观察范围、抽取方式与抽取深度三个维度系统分析这些设计选择。利用该框架，我们在十二个真实项目上开展实证研究，测量状态捕获策略如何影响揭示回归的能力以及预言信息的丰富程度。我们的发现表明，人工编写的断言常常未能充分利用可获得的程序状态，其揭错潜力远低于系统性观察策略。一些简单的设计选择——例如暴露未被检查的中间返回值、精心选择 getter、加深状态抽取——即可在无需观察海量程序状态数据的情况下带来可测量的回归检测提升（平均 35.7%）。此外，我们强调了可观察性、断言可取性方面的挑战，以及捕获更丰富程序状态所带来的权衡。这些洞见表明，微小的设计选择可能在回归检测上带来重大差异，并可能为工具构建者与从业者提供具体方向。","tl":"系统量化状态捕获维度，证明人工断言远未用尽程序状态。","au":["Hang Du","Vijay Krishna Palepu","James Jones"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["test oracles","assertions","state capture","regression detection","snapshot testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/189/x","pu":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3797107"},{"id":"p00998","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Cost-Effective Testing of MPC Compilers","tz":"低成本高效益的 MPC 编译器测试","a":"Secure multi-party computation (MPC) enables privacy-preserving computations using secret data, with applications ranging from health care and finance to machine learning and blockchains. MPC compilers translate high-level function descriptions to the low-level representations required for the actual execution, making them critical for both usability and scalability of MPC. However, these compilers may contain logic bugs that cause them to quietly produce wrong outputs, the consequences of which could be catastrophic given the sensitive applications of this technology. Testing MPC compilers in order to find these severe bugs is, therefore, paramount. With only a single testing tool currently available (which is not publicly available in its entirety and has several serious limitations), this issue is far from resolved. In this paper, we present BabelFuzz, a cost-effective framework for testing MPC compilers. By introducing an expressive intermediate representation (IR) for its seed-program generation, BabelFuzz is able to support multiple compilers that use different input languages, while keeping the development effort of adding new targets low. Even better, this approach allows us to translate our IR to mainstream languages, which provides a powerful differential-testing oracle for highly efficient bug detection. BabelFuzz not only found 24 new logic bugs across four MPC compilers, but it is also able to rediscover every fixed bug the previous state of the art in testing MPC compilers found.","az":"安全多方计算（MPC）能够在保密数据上进行隐私保护计算，其应用涵盖医疗、金融乃至机器学习与区块链。MPC 编译器将高层函数描述翻译为实际执行所需的底层表示，因而对 MPC 的可用性与可扩展性都至关重要。然而，这些编译器可能包含逻辑缺陷，使其悄然产出错误结果，鉴于该技术的敏感应用场景，后果可能是灾难性的。因此，测试 MPC 编译器以发现这些严重缺陷至关重要。目前仅有一个测试工具可用（且未完整公开，并存在若干严重局限），这一问题远未解决。本文提出 BabelFuzz，一个低成本高效益的 MPC 编译器测试框架。通过为种子程序生成引入一种表达力强的中间表示（IR），BabelFuzz 能够支持使用不同输入语言的多种编译器，同时把新增目标的开发工作量保持在较低水平。更好的是，该方法允许我们将 IR 翻译为主流语言，从而提供了一个强大的差分测试预言以实现高效的缺陷检测。BabelFuzz 不仅在四个 MPC 编译器中发现了 24 个新的逻辑缺陷，还能重新发现此前最先进 MPC 编译器测试工作所发现的每一个已修复缺陷。","tl":"用可翻译到主流语言的中间表示做 MPC 编译器差分测试。","au":["Sebastian Watzinger","Valentin Wüstholz","Deepak Garg","Maria Christakis"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["MPC compiler testing","differential testing","intermediate representation","seed program generation","logic bugs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/190/x","pu":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/FSE-2026-MPC.pdf"},{"id":"p00999","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AccessDroid: Detecting Screen Reader Accessibility Issues in Android Applications via Semantics Trees","tz":"AccessDroid：通过语义树检测 Android 应用中的屏幕阅读器无障碍问题","a":"Screen readers are essential for visually impaired users to access mobile apps, yet inadequate developer support often leads to ambiguous or missing content. While prior work has primarily focused on missing content, ambiguity remains underexplored. This paper categorizes screen reader accessibility issues into three types: semantics separation, semantics downshift, and semantics missing. We propose AccessDroid, a lightweight approach that automatically detects both ambiguity and missing content issues in Android apps and generates diagnostic reports. Evaluated on 361 screens from 50 real-world Android apps, AccessDroid detects over 95% of screen reader accessibility issues with an average time of 15ms per page. AccessDroid improves precision by 97.5% over the LLM approach while incurring significantly lower time overhead. It also achieves 2.41% higher recall than the industrial-grade Accessibility Scanner, with comparable detection efficiency.","az":"屏幕阅读器对视障用户访问移动应用至关重要，但开发者支持不足常常导致内容含混或缺失。已有工作主要关注内容缺失，而歧义问题仍未被充分探索。本文将屏幕阅读器无障碍问题归为三类：语义分离、语义降级与语义缺失。我们提出 AccessDroid，一种轻量级方法，可自动检测 Android 应用中的歧义与内容缺失问题并生成诊断报告。在来自 50 个真实 Android 应用的 361 个界面上评估，AccessDroid 检出了超过 95% 的屏幕阅读器无障碍问题，每页平均耗时 15 毫秒。相比 LLM 方法，AccessDroid 的精确率提升 97.5%，而时间开销显著更低；相比工业级的 Accessibility Scanner，其召回率高出 2.41%，检测效率相当。","tl":"用语义树把屏幕阅读器歧义细分三类并毫秒级检测。","au":["Hang Zhou","Wei Song"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["accessibility-inclusion","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["screen reader accessibility","Android apps","semantics tree","ambiguity detection","Accessibility Scanner"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/191/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797108"},{"id":"p01000","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Repair of TEE Partitioning Issues via DSL-Guided and LLM-Assisted Patching","tz":"通过 DSL 引导与 LLM 辅助的补丁实现 TEE 划分问题的自动修复","a":"Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) provide hardware-based isolation to protect sensitive data and computations from potentially compromised operating systems (OS). However, TEE applications inevitably interact with the untrusted OS through SDK interfaces, and improper partitioning can introduce severe vulnerabilities such as data leakage and code injection. While prior work has proposed static analysis tools to detect such issues, automated repair remains largely unexplored. This problem is particularly challenging due to three TEE-specific factors: the lack of standardized secure development guidelines, the difficulty of extracting semantic information from low-level C code, and the absence of mature testing and validation methods. In this work, we present TEERepair, a framework for automatically repairing bad partitioning issues in TEE applications. Our approach tackles the above challenges by introducing a domain-specific language (DSL) to encode repair rules that express and capture common TEE security patterns, which are instantiated as patch templates with placeholders for context-specific variables. We then leverage large language models (LLMs) to reason about code semantics and synthesize context-aware patches, and further generate test clients to validate the repairs. We evaluate TEERepair on the TEE Partitioning Errors Benchmark (PartitioningE-Bench), achieving an overall precision of 95.29% and recall of 91.01%, with improvements of 37.04% in precision and 51.68% in recall over an LLM-only baseline. Furthermore, applying TEERepair to 20 real-world TEE projects, we submitted 5 repair pull requests, 2 of which have been confirmed and merged by project maintainers.","az":"可信执行环境（TEE）提供基于硬件的隔离，以保护敏感数据与计算免受可能已被攻陷的操作系统（OS）侵害。然而，TEE 应用不可避免地要通过 SDK 接口与不可信的 OS 交互，不当的划分可能引入数据泄露、代码注入等严重漏洞。尽管此前工作提出了检测此类问题的静态分析工具，自动修复仍在很大程度上未被探索。这一问题因三个 TEE 特有因素而格外困难：缺乏标准化的安全开发指南、从底层 C 代码中抽取语义信息的难度，以及成熟测试与验证方法的缺失。在本工作中，我们提出 TEERepair，一个自动修复 TEE 应用中不当划分问题的框架。我们的方法通过引入一种领域专用语言（DSL）来编码修复规则以应对上述挑战，这些规则表达并捕获常见的 TEE 安全模式，并被实例化为带有上下文相关变量占位符的补丁模板。随后我们利用大语言模型（LLM）推理代码语义并合成上下文感知的补丁，并进一步生成测试客户端以验证修复。我们在 TEE 划分错误基准（PartitioningE-Bench）上评估 TEERepair，取得 95.29% 的整体精确率与 91.01% 的召回率，相比仅用 LLM 的基线在精确率上提升 37.04%、召回率上提升 51.68%。此外，将 TEERepair 应用于 20 个真实 TEE 项目，我们提交了 5 个修复拉取请求，其中 2 个已被项目维护者确认并合并。","tl":"用 DSL 修复规则模板加 LLM 语义填充修复 TEE 划分漏洞。","au":["Chengyan Ma","Jieke Shi","Ruidong Han","Ye Liu","FENG Li","Yuqing Niu","David Lo"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Trusted Execution Environment","partitioning vulnerability","automated repair","domain-specific language","LLM patch synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/192/x","pu":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2605.22087"},{"id":"p01001","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Repair of Requirements for Cyber-Physical Systems in Simulink Requirements Tables","tz":"面向信息物理系统的 Simulink 需求表自动需求修复","a":"The development of complex software systems, such as cyber-physical systems (CPSs), involves the continuous evolution of both system implementations and their requirements. These two artifacts often proceed independently, creating a risk of misalignment between a system and its requirements. For example, a system may be updated due to implementation-level concerns, resulting in a new version that no longer satisfies its original requirements. Traditional compliance recovery techniques, such as automated program repair, address this problem by modifying the system while assuming that the requirements are correct. However, faulty or outdated requirements are a well-documented challenge in practice, motivating the complementary task of requirements repair. In this paper, we propose a framework that leverages system execution data to repair misaligned requirements of CPSs, thereby restoring requirement-to-system compliance. Our approach evaluates the correctness of declarative requirements expressed over time-based, real-valued signals using the MATLAB Simulink Requirement Tables language. We evaluate two implementations of our framework on six real-world case studies covering 12 requirements. The results confirm the effectiveness of the proposed framework in producing correct and useful repaired requirements.","az":"复杂软件系统（例如信息物理系统 CPS）的开发涉及系统实现与其需求的持续演化。这两类制品往往各自独立推进，从而带来系统与需求相互错配的风险。例如，系统可能因实现层面的考量而被更新，产生的新版本不再满足其原始需求。诸如自动程序修复之类的传统合规性恢复技术，通过修改系统来处理这一问题，同时假定需求本身是正确的。然而，需求存在缺陷或已经过时在实践中是有充分文献记载的挑战，这促使我们研究互补的任务——需求修复。本文提出一个框架，利用系统执行数据来修复 CPS 中相互错配的需求，从而恢复需求与系统之间的合规性。我们的方法使用 MATLAB Simulink Requirement Tables 语言，在基于时间的实值信号上评估声明式需求的正确性。我们在覆盖 12 条需求的六个真实案例研究上评估了该框架的两种实现。结果证实了所提框架在产生正确且有用的修复后需求方面的有效性。","tl":"用执行数据反过来修复 CPS 的形式化需求而非改代码。","au":["Aren Babikian","Alessio Di Sandro","Federico Formica","Claudio Menghi","Marsha Chechik"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["requirements repair","cyber-physical systems","Simulink Requirement Tables","signal-based requirements","compliance recovery"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/193/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.03870"},{"id":"p01002","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Satisfiability Solving with LLMs","tz":"用大语言模型求解可满足性问题","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used for tasks that implicitly reduce to Boolean satisfiability (SAT), yet their reasoning ability on SAT remains unclear. We present a systematic study of LLMs on 2-SAT and 3-SAT, together with two canonical reductions—Vertex Cover and a discrete 3D-packing formulation—designed to probe representation-invariant reasoning. Our evaluation begins with the conventional lens (accuracy/precision/recall/F1) and the phase-transition setting. We find that traditional metrics are frequently misleading: models exhibit a strong SAT bias, fail to reproduce the classical easy–hard–easy signature around the 3-SAT threshold, and degrade sharply as the number of variables N grows. To address this, we introduce a distribution-agnostic paired-formula protocol (minimally different SAT/UNSAT instances) and a new measure, Accurate Differentiation Rate (ADR), which requires getting both members of each pair correct. ADR cleanly separates reasoning-oriented models from heuristic ones and correlates with witness validity (truth assignments that actually satisfy the formula). Extending beyond CNF, we test cross-representation consistency via standard reductions: (i) CNF → Vertex Cover and (ii) 3-SAT → discrete 3D packing with verifiable placement constraints. Decisions made on CNF and on their graph/packing counterparts agree for most models on >80% of instances, revealing stable decision rules across representations. A leading model (e.g., GPT-5) achieves both high invariance and correctness at small N, but still suffers scale-induced degradation. Taken together, our results support the thesis that SAT is a foundational probe for LLM reasoning: performance on SAT predicts transfer to other NP-style reductions, while paired evaluation with ADR provides a faithful, representation-robust assessment beyond conventional metrics.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）越来越多地被用于隐含可归约为布尔可满足性（SAT）的任务，然而它们在 SAT 上的推理能力仍不清楚。我们对 LLM 在 2-SAT 与 3-SAT 上的表现进行了系统研究，并配合两种经典归约——顶点覆盖（Vertex Cover）与离散三维装箱形式化——用以探测表示不变的推理能力。我们的评估首先采用传统视角（准确率/精确率/召回率/F1）以及相变（phase-transition）设定。我们发现传统指标常常具有误导性：模型表现出强烈的 SAT 偏置，无法复现 3-SAT 阈值附近经典的“易—难—易”特征，并且随着变量数 N 增长而急剧退化。为此，我们引入一种与分布无关的配对公式协议（最小差异的 SAT/UNSAT 实例对），并提出一个新度量——精确区分率（Accurate Differentiation Rate, ADR），它要求每一对中的两个实例都判断正确。ADR 能够清晰地区分面向推理的模型与启发式模型，并与见证有效性（真正满足公式的真值赋值）相关。在 CNF 之外，我们通过标准归约检验跨表示一致性：(i) CNF → 顶点覆盖，以及 (ii) 3-SAT → 带可验证放置约束的离散三维装箱。对大多数模型而言，在 CNF 上的判定与在其图/装箱对应物上的判定在超过 80% 的实例上一致，揭示出跨表示的稳定决策规则。领先的模型（例如 GPT-5）在小 N 时同时取得了高不变性与高正确性，但仍然受到规模引发的性能退化影响。综合来看，我们的结果支持这样一个论点：SAT 是探测 LLM 推理能力的基础性探针——在 SAT 上的表现可以预测其向其他 NP 类归约问题的迁移，而基于 ADR 的配对评估提供了超越传统指标、忠实且对表示鲁棒的评估方式。","tl":"提出配对公式协议与 ADR 指标，揭示 LLM 的 SAT 偏置。","au":["Leizhen Zhang","Shuhan Chen","Sheng Chen"],"top":"llm-reasoning-and-test-time-scaling","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["cross-track-bridge","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["Boolean satisfiability","LLM reasoning","Accurate Differentiation Rate","phase transition","NP reductions"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/194/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.28602"},{"id":"p01003","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Reducing Coverage-Equivalent Inputs in Grammar-based Fuzzing by Avoiding Recurrent Rule Sequences","tz":"通过避免重复规则序列减少基于文法的模糊测试中的覆盖等价输入","a":"We present RSFuzz, a new technique to enhance grammar-based fuzzing by reducing the generation of coverage-equivalent inputs during testing. Grammar-based fuzzers apply production rules from a given grammar to generate well-structured inputs for the target program. However, a key limitation is that many existing fuzzers still produce a large number of “coverage-equivalent” inputs—those that revisit already explored program paths—thereby restricting their ability to uncover new bugs and improve coverage. To address this issue, RSFuzz automatically identifies recurrent sequences of production rules that cause coverage-equivalent inputs and prevents their reuse during fuzzing. A key challenge in practice lies in the large number of coverage-equivalent input groups, each with many inputs, making it difficult to identify the underlying recurrent sequences. RSFuzz tackles this challenge with a customized algorithm that iteratively groups coverage-equivalent inputs, selects promising groups, and extracts recurrent sequences for each group based on accumulated data while running any grammar-based fuzzer. We integrated RSFuzz with existing random and probabilistic fuzzers and evaluated it on eight real-world programs using JavaScript and JSON input formats. Experimental results show that incorporating RSFuzz with both fuzzers exclusively detects 108 and 31 crashes with distinct stack traces, increases line coverage by 6.5% and 5.1%, and reduces duplicate-coverage input generation by 29.7% and 37.7%, respectively, compared to their performance without RSFuzz.","az":"我们提出 RSFuzz，一种通过在测试过程中减少覆盖等价输入的生成来增强基于文法的模糊测试的新技术。基于文法的模糊测试器依据给定文法应用产生式规则，为目标程序生成结构良好的输入。然而，一个关键局限在于许多现有模糊测试器仍会产生大量“覆盖等价”的输入——即重新走访已探索过的程序路径的输入——从而限制了它们发现新缺陷和提升覆盖率的能力。为解决这一问题，RSFuzz 自动识别导致覆盖等价输入的重复产生式规则序列，并在模糊测试过程中阻止其被重复使用。实践中的一个关键挑战在于覆盖等价输入组数量庞大、每组输入众多，使得识别其背后的重复序列十分困难。RSFuzz 通过一个定制算法应对这一挑战：在运行任意基于文法的模糊测试器的同时，迭代地对覆盖等价输入进行分组、选择有希望的分组，并基于累积数据为每个分组抽取重复序列。我们将 RSFuzz 与现有的随机式与概率式模糊测试器集成，并在使用 JavaScript 与 JSON 输入格式的八个真实程序上进行评估。实验结果表明，将 RSFuzz 与两类模糊测试器结合后，分别独有地检测到 108 个和 31 个具有不同调用栈的崩溃，将行覆盖率分别提升 6.5% 和 5.1%，并将重复覆盖输入的生成分别减少 29.7% 和 37.7%。","tl":"识别并禁用导致覆盖重复的产生式规则序列。","au":["Jaehan Yoon","Yunji Seo","Hakjoo Oh","Sooyoung Cha"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["grammar-based fuzzing","coverage-equivalent inputs","production rule sequences","seed generation","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/195/x","pu":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZCezmqjSuQYkBl_ZQqIQ3WH9F3JsaNnL/view?usp=sharing"},{"id":"p01004","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Failing with Purpose: Dangling Coverage-Guided Negative Test Generation from a Mechanized P4 Type System","tz":"有意失败：基于机械化 P4 类型系统的悬挂覆盖率引导负向测试生成","a":"A type checker must reject ill-typed programs in addition to accepting well-typed programs. Negative type checker tests, programs expected to be rejected, validate that a type checker enforces the language’s typing rules as intended. We focus on negative type checker tests for P4, a domain-specific language for programmable network devices, whose type system encodes design principles and hardware constraints of the network dataplane. Failing to reject an ill-typed P4 program risks violating these principles and constraints, leading to unexpected errors. A comprehensive negative test suite covering subtle and diverse ill-typed conditions is thus important. However, constructing comprehensive negative tests is challenging: the negative input space lacks systematic characterization, and existing P4 program generators do not target subtle type errors. This paper addresses the problem in three steps. (i) We mechanize the P4 type system using the SpecTec framework. Unlike the informal official P4 specification, the mechanized type system is formal and machine-readable. Mechanization enables a systematic analysis of the type system. (ii) Across the mechanized type system, we identify dangling premises, which are premises in the typing rules that, when violated, cause type errors. Based on them, we propose dangling coverage, a novel metric for quantifying negative test coverage. (iii) Finally, we implement a coverage-guided fuzzer that mutates well-typed P4 programs into ill-typed programs that increase dangling coverage. Our method identifies 939 dangling premises that characterize distinct ill-typed conditions in the P4 type system. The fuzzer generates a negative test suite achieving 33.02%p higher dangling coverage than the existing P4C reference compiler’s test suite. The generated tests also reveal 29 previously unknown bugs in the compiler frontend, demonstrating the effectiveness of both the coverage metric and the fuzzer. The tests generated by our fuzzer are now integrated into the P4C test suite.","az":"类型检查器不仅要接受类型正确的程序，还必须拒绝类型错误的程序。负向类型检查器测试——即预期被拒绝的程序——用于验证类型检查器是否按设计意图强制执行语言的类型规则。我们关注 P4 的负向类型检查器测试，P4 是一种面向可编程网络设备的领域专用语言，其类型系统编码了网络数据平面的设计原则与硬件约束。未能拒绝一个类型错误的 P4 程序，可能导致违反这些原则与约束，进而引发意料之外的错误。因此，一个覆盖细微且多样的类型错误条件的全面负向测试套件十分重要。然而，构造全面的负向测试颇具挑战：负向输入空间缺乏系统化的刻画，而已有的 P4 程序生成器并不针对细微的类型错误。本文分三步解决该问题。(i) 我们使用 SpecTec 框架对 P4 类型系统进行机械化。与非形式化的 P4 官方规范不同，机械化后的类型系统是形式化且机器可读的，使得对类型系统的系统性分析成为可能。(ii) 在机械化的类型系统上，我们识别出“悬挂前提”（dangling premises），即类型规则中一旦被违反就会导致类型错误的前提。基于它们，我们提出“悬挂覆盖率”（dangling coverage），一种量化负向测试覆盖的新指标。(iii) 最后，我们实现了一个覆盖率引导的模糊测试器，将类型正确的 P4 程序变异为能够提升悬挂覆盖率的类型错误程序。我们的方法识别出 939 个悬挂前提，刻画了 P4 类型系统中各不相同的类型错误条件。该模糊测试器生成的负向测试套件比现有 P4C 参考编译器的测试套件在悬挂覆盖率上高出 33.02 个百分点。生成的测试还揭示了编译器前端中 29 个此前未知的缺陷，证明了该覆盖指标与模糊测试器的有效性。我们的模糊测试器所生成的测试现已被集成进 P4C 测试套件。","tl":"提出悬挂前提与悬挂覆盖率，系统生成类型检查器负向测试。","au":["Jaehyun Lee","Seokhun Jeong","Sukyoung Ryu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["P4 type system","negative tests","dangling coverage","mechanized specification","coverage-guided fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/196/x"},{"id":"p01005","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Debugging Engine Enhanced by Prior Knowledge: Can We Teach LLM How to Debug?","tz":"由先验知识增强的调试引擎：我们能教会大模型如何调试吗？","a":"Automated Program Repair (APR) powered by Large Language Models (LLMs) has shown strong potential for improving software reliability. However, existing LLM-based APR approaches underutilize the rich debugging knowledge latent in large-scale bug-fix corpora. Prior work has primarily advanced APR through multi-agent coordination, prompt engineering, task decomposition, or model training. While effective to some extent, these methods rely heavily on the implicit reasoning capacity of LLMs, without explicitly modeling the debugging knowledge that underlies successful program repair. We present DeepK, a novel framework that systematically extracts, validates, and reuses debugging knowledge to guide LLMs in APR. Rather than treating historical bug-fix pairs solely as contextual exemplars, DeepK distills them into a structured knowledge base of verified debugging knowledge. This knowledge base can be seamlessly integrated into diverse APR pipelines, providing interpretable reasoning traces and step-wise repair strategies that enhance the repair performance. We evaluate DeepK on multiple benchmarks (ACPR, Atcoder) using both GPT-4o and DeepSeek-v3. Results show that DeepK consistently surpasses state-of-the-art APR systems in repair accuracy. Ablation studies confirm the importance of edit description generation, multi-perspective retrieval, and two-fold debugging knowledge. Varying the number of retrieved entries further highlights the trade-off between informativeness and noise. These findings emphasize the essential contribution of explicit debugging knowledge in advancing LLM-based APR and establish DeepK as an extensible framework for building more reliable repair systems.","az":"由大语言模型（LLM）驱动的自动程序修复（APR）在提升软件可靠性方面展现出强大潜力。然而，现有基于 LLM 的 APR 方法未能充分利用大规模缺陷修复语料中潜藏的丰富调试知识。此前的工作主要通过多智能体协作、提示工程、任务分解或模型训练来推进 APR。这些方法在一定程度上有效，但高度依赖 LLM 的隐式推理能力，并未显式建模支撑成功程序修复的调试知识。我们提出 DeepK，一个系统性地抽取、验证并复用调试知识以指导 LLM 进行 APR 的新框架。DeepK 不把历史缺陷修复对仅仅当作上下文范例，而是将其提炼为一个结构化的、经过验证的调试知识库。该知识库可以无缝集成到多种 APR 流水线中，提供可解释的推理轨迹与分步修复策略，从而提升修复性能。我们在多个基准（ACPR、Atcoder）上使用 GPT-4o 与 DeepSeek-v3 评估 DeepK。结果表明，DeepK 在修复准确率上持续超越最先进的 APR 系统。消融实验确认了编辑描述生成、多视角检索以及双重调试知识的重要性。改变检索条目数量的实验进一步凸显了信息量与噪声之间的权衡。这些发现强调了显式调试知识对推进基于 LLM 的 APR 的关键作用，并将 DeepK 确立为一个可扩展的、用于构建更可靠修复系统的框架。","tl":"把历史修复对蒸馏成可验证的结构化调试知识库。","au":["Kunyi Li","Sai Wu","Xiu Tang","Chang Yao","Songhao Bu","Quanqing Xu","Gang Chen"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated program repair","debugging knowledge base","bug-fix corpora","multi-perspective retrieval","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/197/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3797110"},{"id":"p01006","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Natural Language-Focused Software Engineering via Code-Documentation Equivalence","tz":"以自然语言为中心的软件工程：基于代码—文档等价性","a":"Source code documentation is an integral part of software development and maintenance, as it helps in understanding the code and facilitates communication among developers. However, existing documentation is often incomplete, outdated, or inaccurate, which can lead to misunderstandings and errors. In the era of large language models (LLMs), which are being extensively used for software engineering tasks, the quality of documentation becomes even more critical, as documentation provides important context for the models. In this paper, we introduce the notion of documentation-to-code equivalence, a novel property that captures whether documentation accurately and completely describes the code it documents. We present a novel approach, called Documentary, to automatically generate equivalent documentation for a given code snippet. Our evaluation shows that Documentary can generate such documentation for 65.5% of the evaluated, function-level code snippets. To show the benefits of documentation-to-code equivalence, we describe and evaluate two software engineering tasks tasks: code understanding and code editing. Our results show document-to-code equivalence allows an LLM to predict the output of a function with 12.8–24.5% higher accuracy, when compared to human-written documentation and documentation generated by a baseline approach. Likewise, the property helps developers successfully perform code changes by modifying only the documentation, rather than the code itself, in 1.2–12.8% more cases than the baselines.","az":"源代码文档是软件开发与维护中不可或缺的一部分，它有助于理解代码并促进开发者之间的沟通。然而，现有文档往往不完整、过时或不准确，这会导致误解与错误。在大语言模型（LLM）被广泛用于软件工程任务的时代，文档质量变得更加关键，因为文档为模型提供了重要的上下文。本文引入“文档—代码等价性”这一概念，它是一种新属性，用于刻画文档是否准确且完整地描述了其所记录的代码。我们提出一种名为 Documentary 的新方法，为给定代码片段自动生成等价的文档。我们的评估表明，Documentary 能为所评估的函数级代码片段中的 65.5% 生成此类文档。为展示文档—代码等价性的收益，我们描述并评估了两项软件工程任务：代码理解与代码编辑。结果表明，与人工撰写的文档以及基线方法生成的文档相比，该属性可使 LLM 预测函数输出的准确率提高 12.8%–24.5%。同样地，该属性还帮助开发者在多出 1.2%–12.8% 的情形中，仅通过修改文档而非代码本身就成功完成代码变更。","tl":"提出文档—代码等价性，并用它支撑“改文档即改代码”。","au":["Aryaz Eghbali","Zhongxin Liu","Michael Pradel"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code documentation","documentation-to-code equivalence","code understanding","code editing","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/198/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.22247"},{"id":"p01007","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RAT: Retrieval-Augmented Testing of Certificate Revocation List Parsers in TLS Implementations","tz":"RAT：对 TLS 实现中证书吊销列表解析器的检索增强测试","a":"Transport Layer Security (TLS) implementations form the backbone of countless software systems, spanning from web browsers, email clients, cloud services, and Internet of Things software, by enabling secure authentication and encrypted communication. However, their reliability hinges on the integrity of components like Certificate Revocation List (CRL), which revokes compromised certificates to prevent attackers from exploiting expired or unauthorized credentials. Despite CRL’s critical role, CRL parsers, which decode CRL data for validation, remain overlooked in security research, exposing TLS-dependent software to potential threats. To address this gap, we introduce Retrieval-Augmented Testing (RAT), a framework powered by Large Language Models (LLMs), to systematically evaluate CRL parsers in mainstream TLS implementations such as OpenSSL, GnuTLS, and wolfSSL. RAT begins with leveraging an LLM to retrieve historical bug reports and cross-reference them with Request for Comments (RFC) 5280 specifications, generating structured test cases via an Abstract Syntax Notation One-aware mutation engine. These test cases are then fed into CRL parsers, and RAT employs an LLM to normalize their outputs. By analyzing these normalized results, RAT detects discrepancies and uncovers latent risks in CRL parsers. Our work makes the following contributions: (1) Unlike prior work focusing on certificate validation, this is the first study to systematically assess CRL parsers; (2) We propose RAT, a novel testing framework that leverages an LLM to integrate insights from retrieved bug reports and RFC 5280, enabling automated test-case generation; and (3) We have implemented an open-source prototype of RAT and experiments uncovered 23 new bugs, features, enhancements, fixes in commits, and x509s, demonstrating RAT’s potential to bolster the security foundation of TLS-powered systems worldwide.","az":"传输层安全协议（TLS）的实现构成了无数软件系统的支柱，涵盖从网页浏览器、邮件客户端、云服务到物联网软件，为其提供安全认证与加密通信。然而，它们的可靠性取决于诸如证书吊销列表（CRL）等组件的完整性——CRL 用于吊销已被攻破的证书，防止攻击者利用过期或未授权的凭据。尽管 CRL 角色关键，负责解码 CRL 数据以供校验的 CRL 解析器在安全研究中仍被忽视，使依赖 TLS 的软件暴露于潜在威胁之下。为填补这一空白，我们提出检索增强测试（Retrieval-Augmented Testing, RAT），一个由大语言模型驱动的框架，用于系统性评估 OpenSSL、GnuTLS、wolfSSL 等主流 TLS 实现中的 CRL 解析器。RAT 首先利用 LLM 检索历史缺陷报告，并与 RFC 5280 规范交叉比对，再通过一个感知 ASN.1（Abstract Syntax Notation One）的变异引擎生成结构化测试用例。随后这些测试用例被输入 CRL 解析器，RAT 使用 LLM 对其输出进行归一化。通过分析这些归一化结果，RAT 检测差异并揭示 CRL 解析器中潜藏的风险。我们的工作作出如下贡献：(1) 与以往聚焦证书校验的工作不同，这是首个系统性评估 CRL 解析器的研究；(2) 我们提出 RAT，一个利用 LLM 融合检索到的缺陷报告与 RFC 5280 洞见、实现测试用例自动生成的新测试框架；(3) 我们实现了 RAT 的开源原型，实验揭示了 23 个新的缺陷、特性、增强、提交中的修复以及 x509 相关问题，展示了 RAT 在巩固全球 TLS 驱动系统安全基础方面的潜力。","tl":"首次系统测试 CRL 解析器：检索历史缺陷加 RFC 驱动差分测试。","au":["Chu Chen","Qianxin Cheng","Pinghong Ren","Hairong Yu","Cong Tian","Zhenhua Duan","Xu Lu","Bin Yu","WenSheng Wang","Jin Liu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["TLS implementations","certificate revocation list","differential testing","ASN.1 mutation","RFC 5280"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/199/x","pu":"https://github.com/secsoftware/preprint/blob/main/2026-FSE-RAT-preprint.pdf"},{"id":"p01008","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"MR-Coupler: Automated Metamorphic Test Generation via Functional Coupling Analysis","tz":"MR-Coupler：通过功能耦合分析实现蜕变测试自动生成","a":"Metamorphic testing (MT) is a widely recognized technique for alleviating the oracle problem in software testing. However, its adoption is hindered by the difficulty of constructing effective metamorphic relations (MRs), which often require domain-specific or hard-to-obtain knowledge. In this work, we propose a novel approach that leverages the functional coupling between methods, which is readily available in source code, to automatically construct MRs and generate metamorphic test cases (MTCs). Our technique, MR-Coupler, identifies functionally coupled method pairs, employs large language models to generate candidate MTCs, and validates them through test amplification and mutation analysis. In particular, we leverage three functional coupling patterns to avoid expensive enumeration of possible method pairs, and a novel validation mechanism to reduce false alarms. Our evaluation of MR-Coupler on 100 human-written MTCs and 50 real-world bugs shows that it generates valid MTCs for over 90% of tasks, improves valid MTC generation by 64.90%, and reduces false alarms by 36.56% compared to baselines. Furthermore, the MTCs generated by MR-Coupler detect 44% of the real bugs. Moreover, the code structures of these MTCs closely follow the human-written MR skeletons. Our results highlight the effectiveness of leveraging functional coupling for automated MR construction and the potential of MR-Coupler to facilitate the adoption of MT in practice. We also released the tool and experimental data to support future research.","az":"蜕变测试（MT）是缓解软件测试中预言问题的一项被广泛认可的技术。然而，其推广受制于构造有效蜕变关系（MR）的困难，这通常需要领域特定或难以获取的知识。在本工作中，我们提出一种新方法，利用方法之间的功能耦合（这一信息在源代码中即可轻易获得）来自动构造 MR 并生成蜕变测试用例（MTC）。我们的技术 MR-Coupler 识别功能上耦合的方法对，使用大语言模型生成候选 MTC，并通过测试放大与变异分析对其进行验证。具体而言，我们利用三种功能耦合模式来避免对所有可能方法对的昂贵枚举，并设计了一种新的验证机制以减少误报。我们在 100 个人工编写的 MTC 与 50 个真实缺陷上评估 MR-Coupler，结果显示它为超过 90% 的任务生成了有效的 MTC，相较基线将有效 MTC 生成提升 64.90%，并将误报减少 36.56%。此外，MR-Coupler 生成的 MTC 检测出 44% 的真实缺陷。而且，这些 MTC 的代码结构与人工编写的 MR 骨架高度接近。我们的结果凸显了利用功能耦合进行 MR 自动构造的有效性，以及 MR-Coupler 在实践中推动蜕变测试落地的潜力。我们同时发布了工具与实验数据以支持后续研究。","tl":"用方法间功能耦合自动推导蜕变关系，免除领域知识。","au":["Congying Xu","Hengcheng Zhu","Songqiang Chen","Jiarong Wu","Valerio Terragni","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["metamorphic testing","metamorphic relations","functional coupling","oracle problem","mutation analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/200/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.10126"},{"id":"p01009","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Behind Defective Mobile AR Apps: Studying Reviews and Bugs of Android AR Software with Comparison to Prior Bug Studies","tz":"缺陷缠身的移动 AR 应用背后：Android AR 软件的评论与缺陷研究及与既有缺陷研究的对比","a":"As Augmented Reality (AR) applications grow in popularity, understanding and addressing AR software bugs becomes crucial. AR applications, due to their interaction with the physical world, present unique challenges that differ from traditional software. In this study we collected 5, 440 user reviews from the Google Play Store and 2, 846 issues from open-source AR applications using Google ARCore. We categorized these into structured hierarchical categories and identified the features affected by each issue. To assess the complexity of bug fixes, we conducted a commit-level analysis, exploring API changes by parsing the source code and generating Abstract Syntax Trees (ASTs). Additionally, we compared the symptoms reported by users with those tracked by developers to understand their alignment","az":"随着增强现实（AR）应用日益流行，理解并处理 AR 软件缺陷变得至关重要。由于 AR 应用与物理世界交互，它们带来了不同于传统软件的独特挑战。在本研究中，我们从 Google Play 商店收集了 5,440 条用户评论，并从使用 Google ARCore 的开源 AR 应用中收集了 2,846 个 issue。我们将其归入结构化的层次类别，并识别出每个问题所影响的功能特性。为评估缺陷修复的复杂度，我们进行了提交级分析，通过解析源代码并生成抽象语法树（AST）来考察 API 变更。此外，我们比较了用户报告的症状与开发者跟踪的症状，以理解二者的一致性。","tl":"首次对 ARCore 应用评论与 issue 做分层缺陷刻画与对比。","au":["Tahmid Rafi","Xueling Zhang","Jianwei Niu","Xiaoyin Wang"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["empirical-study","multimodal"],"kw":["augmented reality apps","bug study","user reviews","ARCore","abstract syntax tree analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/201/x","pu":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cnBhyxRXdj2xBSRZ8rK8m-i1FWWdIK0R/view?usp=sharing"},{"id":"p01010","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"In Bugs We Trust? On Measuring the Randomness of a Fuzzer Benchmarking Outcome","tz":"缺陷可信吗？论模糊测试基准评测结果随机性的度量","a":"In Google’s FuzzBench platform, we find that the outcome of coverage-based evaluation more strongly agrees with the outcome of a bug-based evaluation than an independent bug-based evaluation itself. Recently, Böhme et al. found that despite a very strong correlation between coverage achieved and bugs found, there is no strong agreement between the outcome of a coverage- and a bug-based evaluation: The fuzzer best at achieving coverage may be the worst at finding bugs. However, in trying to explain this moderate agreement, we wondered whether the outcome of bug-based benchmarking itself is perhaps much more “noisy” and turned to applied statistics to develop the tools necessary to investigate our hypothesis. In this paper, we call this degree of “noisyness” of a benchmarking outcome as the concordance of the benchmarking procedure and quantify it using a measure of statistical reliability widely-used in psychology, called mean split-half reliability, i.e., the expected agreement on benchmark outcome between two random halfs of the benchmark set. In our experiments with FuzzBench and Magma, we find that the concordance of coverage-based benchmarking is consistently strong while that of bug-based benchmarking is weak on FuzzBench and moderate on Magma. In contrast to FuzzBench, for the Magma benchmark set, which was designed for bug-based evaluation, a coverage-based evaluation does not predict the outcome of a bug-based evaluation better than an independent bug-based evaluation. We investigate concordance as a measure of benchmarking efficiency, as in green fuzzer benchmarking. We empirically confirm, the resources of a procedure with higher concordance can be reduced more substantially (in terms of campaign length or benchmark set size) while maintaining a similar benchmark outcome than a procedure with lower concordance. We report the corresonding savings in terms of carbon emissions.","az":"在 Google 的 FuzzBench 平台上，我们发现基于覆盖率的评测结果与基于缺陷的评测结果之间的一致性，甚至强于两次独立的基于缺陷的评测之间的一致性。近期，Böhme 等人发现，尽管所达成的覆盖率与所发现的缺陷之间存在很强的相关性，基于覆盖率的评测与基于缺陷的评测在结果上却没有强一致性：在覆盖率上最好的模糊测试器，可能在找缺陷上最差。然而，在试图解释这种中等程度的一致性时，我们怀疑基于缺陷的基准评测本身或许要“噪声”得多，于是转向应用统计学来开发研究这一假设所需的工具。本文将基准评测结果的这种“噪声程度”称为该评测流程的“一致度”（concordance），并使用心理学中广泛使用的统计信度度量——平均折半信度（mean split-half reliability），即基准集合随机对半划分后两半在评测结果上的期望一致性——来量化它。在对 FuzzBench 与 Magma 的实验中，我们发现基于覆盖率的基准评测其一致度始终很强，而基于缺陷的基准评测在 FuzzBench 上较弱、在 Magma 上为中等。与 FuzzBench 不同，对于专为基于缺陷的评测而设计的 Magma 基准集合，基于覆盖率的评测并不比一次独立的基于缺陷的评测更能预测基于缺陷的评测结果。我们将一致度作为基准评测效率的一种度量加以考察，正如绿色模糊测试基准评测所主张的那样。我们通过实验确认：在保持相似评测结果的前提下，一致度更高的流程可以更大幅度地削减资源（无论是测试活动时长还是基准集合规模），优于一致度更低的流程。我们还以碳排放的形式报告了相应的节省。","tl":"引入折半信度量化模糊测试基准结果的噪声与可削减资源。","au":["Ardi Madadi","Seongmin Lee","Cornelius Aschermann","Marcel Böhme"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["fuzzer benchmarking","split-half reliability","concordance","FuzzBench","Magma"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/202/x","pu":"https://nimgnoeseel.github.io/assets/pdf/concordance-paper.pdf"},{"id":"p01011","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TUSR: A Test Unit–Based Framework for Repairing Obsolete GUI Test Scripts","tz":"TUSR：一个基于测试单元的过时 GUI 测试脚本修复框架","a":"Graphical User Interface (GUI) testing is a primary technique for testing mobile applications. Among existing testing methods, script-based testing is widely adopted because test scripts can be replayed across devices and versions. However, as mobile apps evolve, frequent changes to GUI appearance and interaction logic often render scripts written for earlier versions obsolete. Existing repair approaches typically follow a stepwise framework, repairing scripts action by action. While effective for minor GUI appearance changes, they struggle when interaction logic is modified. In this paper, we present TUSR, a test unit–based repair framework that fundamentally departs from the stepwise paradigm. TUSR introduces the concept of a “Test Unit”—a contiguous sequence of test actions serving a single testing intention—and repairs scripts at the unit level. It first splits scripts into test units using a multi-modal LLM with a rule-based correction mechanism to ensure consistency, then conducts dynamic repair guided by a Chain-of-Thought prompt enhanced with reflective memory. Experiments on 20 real-world Android applications, covering 262 test scripts and 3,485 actions, demonstrate that TUSR significantly outperforms state-of-the-art black-box and white-box repair approaches.","az":"图形用户界面（GUI）测试是测试移动应用的主要手段。在现有测试方法中，基于脚本的测试被广泛采用，因为测试脚本可以跨设备、跨版本重放。然而，随着移动应用演化，GUI 外观与交互逻辑的频繁变化常常使为早期版本编写的脚本变得过时。已有的修复方法通常遵循逐步式框架，逐个动作地修复脚本。这类方法在应对细微的 GUI 外观变化时有效，但在交互逻辑被修改时则力不从心。本文提出 TUSR，一个基于测试单元的修复框架，从根本上摆脱了逐步式范式。TUSR 引入“测试单元”概念——即服务于单一测试意图的一段连续测试动作序列——并在单元层面修复脚本。它首先使用多模态大语言模型并配合基于规则的纠正机制将脚本切分为测试单元以确保一致性，然后在带有反思式记忆增强的思维链提示引导下进行动态修复。在 20 个真实 Android 应用上覆盖 262 个测试脚本、3,485 个动作的实验表明，TUSR 显著优于最先进的黑盒与白盒修复方法。","tl":"以“测试单元”为粒度而非逐动作修复过时 GUI 脚本。","au":["Shaoheng Cao","Minxue Pan","Xuandong Li"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GUI test script repair","test unit","Android testing","multi-modal LLM","reflective memory"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/203/x"},{"id":"p01012","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"GUIMigrator: Semantics-Preserving Transpilation from Android XML to Compose and SwiftUI","tz":"GUIMigrator：从 Android XML 到 Compose 与 SwiftUI 的语义保持转译","a":"Constructing user interfaces (UIs) is one of the most resource-intensive tasks in mobile development, often consuming more than half of overall effort. Although declarative frameworks such as Jetpack Compose (Android) and SwiftUI (iOS) have become mainstream, the majority of existing Android apps still rely on legacy XML-based layouts. Migrating these UIs to declarative paradigms is essential for maintainability and cross-platform reuse, but manual migration is costly, error-prone, and difficult to scale. We present GUIMigrator, a semantics-preserving framework that automates the migration of Android XML-based UIs to Jetpack Compose and SwiftUI. We design the Semantic UI Transpiler, which abstracts layout structures and resource semantics from legacy XML and systematically re-expresses them using the component abstractions and idioms of modern declarative frameworks. This design ensures that migrated UIs preserve both visual fidelity and functional equivalence, while generating idiomatic, compilable code that maintains cross-platform consistency with minimal manual intervention. By separating semantic interpretation from platform-specific realization, GUIMigrator provides a deterministic yet extensible basis for cross-platform modernization, avoiding the unpredictability of purely generative approaches. We evaluate GUIMigrator on 31 open-source applications across ten domains. Results show that GUIMigrator achieves high migration completeness and visual similarity (Compose average 82%, SwiftUI 78%), outperforms a GPT-4 baseline in structural fidelity, and reduces manual development effort by over 90%. These findings demonstrate that GUIMigrator provides an effective and practical solution for reusing Android UIs across modern declarative frameworks, advancing automated cross-platform UI development.","az":"构建用户界面（UI）是移动开发中最耗费资源的任务之一，往往占据整体工作量的一半以上。尽管 Jetpack Compose（Android）与 SwiftUI（iOS）等声明式框架已成为主流，绝大多数现有 Android 应用仍依赖基于 XML 的遗留布局。将这些 UI 迁移到声明式范式对可维护性与跨平台复用至关重要，但人工迁移成本高、易出错且难以规模化。我们提出 GUIMigrator，一个语义保持的框架，用于将基于 XML 的 Android UI 自动迁移到 Jetpack Compose 与 SwiftUI。我们设计了语义 UI 转译器（Semantic UI Transpiler），它从遗留 XML 中抽象出布局结构与资源语义，并系统性地用现代声明式框架的组件抽象与惯用法重新表达它们。该设计确保迁移后的 UI 同时保持视觉保真度与功能等价性，并生成符合惯用法、可编译的代码，在极少人工干预下维持跨平台一致性。通过将语义解释与平台特定实现相分离，GUIMigrator 为跨平台现代化提供了确定性且可扩展的基础，避免了纯生成式方法的不可预测性。我们在覆盖十个领域的 31 个开源应用上评估 GUIMigrator。结果显示，GUIMigrator 实现了很高的迁移完整度与视觉相似度（Compose 平均 82%，SwiftUI 78%），在结构保真度上优于 GPT-4 基线，并将人工开发工作量减少超过 90%。这些发现表明，GUIMigrator 为在现代声明式框架之间复用 Android UI 提供了有效且实用的解决方案，推进了自动化跨平台 UI 开发。","tl":"确定性语义转译器实现 XML 界面到声明式框架的迁移。","au":["Yi Gao","Xing Hu","Xiaohu Yang","Xin Xia"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["UI migration","Jetpack Compose","SwiftUI","semantics-preserving transpilation","cross-platform modernization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/204/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.16656"},{"id":"p01013","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Spectrum-based Failure Attribution for Multi-Agent Systems","tz":"面向多智能体系统的基于频谱的失效归因","a":"Large Language Model Powered Multi-Agent Systems (MASs) are increasingly employed to automate complex real-world problems, such as programming and scientific discovery. Despite their promising, MASs are not without their flaws. However, failure attribution in MASs—pinpointing the specific agent actions responsible for failures—remains underexplored and labor-intensive, posing significant challenges for debugging and system improvement. To bridge this gap, we propose FAMAS, the first spectrum-based failure attribution approach for MASs, which operates through systematic trajectory replay and abstraction, followed by spectrum analysis. The core idea of FAMAS is to estimate, from variations across repeated MAS executions, the likelihood that each agent action is responsible for the failure. In particular, we propose a novel suspiciousness formula tailored to MASs, which integrates two key factor groups, namely the agent behavior group and the action behavior group, to account for the agent activation patterns and the action activation patterns within the execution trajectories of MASs. Through expensive evaluations against 12 baselines on the Who&When benchmark, FAMAS demonstrates superior performance by outperforming all the methods in comparison.","az":"由大语言模型驱动的多智能体系统（MAS）正越来越多地被用于自动化复杂的真实世界问题，例如编程与科学发现。尽管前景可期，MAS 并非没有缺陷。然而，MAS 中的失效归因——即指明导致失败的具体智能体动作——仍然研究不足且高度依赖人力，给调试与系统改进带来重大挑战。为弥补这一空白，我们提出 FAMAS，首个面向 MAS 的基于频谱的失效归因方法，它通过系统化的轨迹重放与抽象，再进行频谱分析来工作。FAMAS 的核心思想是：从多次重复 MAS 执行之间的差异出发，估计每个智能体动作对失败负责的可能性。特别地，我们提出了一个为 MAS 量身定制的可疑度公式，融合了两组关键因子——智能体行为组与动作行为组——以刻画 MAS 执行轨迹中的智能体激活模式与动作激活模式。通过在 Who&When 基准上与 12 个基线进行代价高昂的评估，FAMAS 展现出优越性能，超越了所有参与比较的方法。","tl":"把频谱式缺陷定位迁移到多智能体轨迹的失效归因。","au":["Yu Ge","Linna Xie","Zhong Li","Yu Pei","Tian Zhang"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["failure attribution","multi-agent systems","spectrum-based analysis","trajectory replay","suspiciousness formula"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/205/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13782"},{"id":"p01014","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Clotho: Measuring Task-Specific Pre-Generation Test Adequacy for LLM Inputs","tz":"Clotho：面向大模型输入的任务特定生成前测试充分性度量","a":"Software increasingly relies on the emergent capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs), from natural language understanding to program analysis and generation. Yet testing them on specific tasks remains difficult and costly: many prompts lack ground truth, forcing reliance on human judgment, while existing uncertainty and adequacy measures typically require full inference. A key challenge is to assess input adequacy in a way that reflects the demands of the task, ideally before even generating any output. We introduce Clotho, a task-specific, pre-generation adequacy measure that estimates input difficulty directly from hidden LLM states. Given a large pool of unlabelled inputs for a specific task, Clotho uses a Gaussian Mixture Model (GMM) to adaptively sample the most informative cases for human labelling. Based on this reference set the GMM can then rank unseen inputs by their likelihood of failure. In our empirical evaluation across eight benchmark tasks and three open-weight LLMs, Clotho can predict failures with a ROC-AUC of 0.716, after labelling reference sets that are on average only 5.4% of inputs. It does so without generating any outputs, thereby reducing costs compared to existing uncertainty measures. Comparison of Clotho and post-generation uncertainty measures shows that the two approaches complement each other. Crucially, we show that adequacy scores learned from open-weight LLMs transfer effectively to proprietary models, extending the applicability of the approach. When prioritising test inputs for proprietary models, Clotho reveals 126.8% more failures, on average, in the top 100 inputs compared to random selection.","az":"软件越来越依赖大语言模型（LLM）的涌现能力，从自然语言理解到程序分析与生成皆是如此。然而，针对具体任务测试它们仍然困难且昂贵：许多提示缺乏标准答案，迫使人们依赖人工判断，而现有的不确定性与充分性度量通常需要完整推理。一个关键挑战在于如何以反映任务需求的方式评估输入的充分性，且最好在生成任何输出之前就完成。我们提出 Clotho，一种任务特定的生成前充分性度量，它直接从 LLM 的隐藏状态估计输入难度。给定某一任务的大量无标注输入池，Clotho 使用高斯混合模型（GMM）自适应地采样最具信息量的样例交给人工标注。基于这一参考集，GMM 便可按失败可能性对未见输入进行排序。在跨八个基准任务与三个开源权重 LLM 的实证评估中，Clotho 在平均只标注 5.4% 输入构成参考集后，即可以 0.716 的 ROC-AUC 预测失败。它无需生成任何输出，因而相比已有不确定性度量降低了成本。Clotho 与生成后不确定性度量的对比表明，两类方法相互补充。关键在于，我们证明从开源权重 LLM 学到的充分性分数可以有效迁移到专有模型，从而扩展了该方法的适用范围。在为专有模型排序测试输入时，Clotho 在排名前 100 的输入中平均比随机选择多揭示 126.8% 的失败。","tl":"用隐藏状态在生成前预测哪些输入会让模型失败。","au":["Juyeon Yoon","Somin Kim","Robert Feldt","Shin Yoo"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"interpretability-and-model-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test adequacy","pre-generation","hidden states","Gaussian Mixture Model","failure prediction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/206/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.17314"},{"id":"p01015","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"WebTestPilot: Agentic End-to-End Web Testing against Natural Language Specification by Inferring Oracles with Symbolized GUI Elements","tz":"WebTestPilot：以符号化 GUI 元素推断预言、面向自然语言规约的智能体式端到端 Web 测试","a":"Visual language model (VLM) agents show great promise in automating graphical user interface (GUI) testing against requirements in natural language. However, the probabilistic nature of language models can have inherent hallucinations. Therefore, given a detected inconsistency between the requirement and the web application, it is hard to distinguish whether it stems from the hallucination or a real application bug. Addressing this issue presents two core technical challenges: (1) limited capability and accuracy in deriving implicit test oracles, where the agent must act as its own oracle to implicitly decide if the application’s behavior is correct without guidance, and (2) limited reliability due to probabilistic inference, where an LLM’s inconsistent reasoning undermines its trustworthiness as an oracle. We introduce WebTestPilot, a neurosymbolic LLM-based approach that addresses both challenges through symbolization. WebTestPilot detects and abstracts critical GUI elements of a web application into symbolic variables. This design improves reliability by constraining assertion generation to operations grounded in explicitly defined symbols, thereby reducing unconstrained or inconsistent reasoning. At the same time, it improves accuracy by representing application states and their relationships in a structured symbolic form, which increases the likelihood of the agent recognizing data, causal, and temporal dependencies across states. Together, these capabilities enable WebTestPilot to generate reliable and accurate test oracles that capture meaningful implicit expectations derived from test requirements. To advance research in this area, we build a benchmark of bug-injected web apps for evaluating NL-to-E2E testing. The results show that WebTestPilot achieves a task completion rate of 99%, with 96% precision and 96% recall in bug detection, outperforming the best baseline (+70 precision, +27 recall). The agent generalizes across diverse natural language inputs (i.e., those containing typos, grammatical errors, redundant sentences, stylistic restyling, or abbreviations) and model scales (3B–72B). In a real-world deployment with a no-code platform, WebTestPilot discovered 8 bugs during development, including data binding, UI, and navigation issues.","az":"视觉语言模型（VLM）智能体在依据自然语言需求自动化图形用户界面（GUI）测试方面展现出巨大潜力。然而，语言模型的概率性本质会带来固有的幻觉。因此，给定一个在需求与 Web 应用之间检测到的不一致，很难分辨它究竟源自幻觉还是真实的应用缺陷。解决这一问题面临两大核心技术挑战：(1) 推导隐式测试预言的能力与准确性有限——智能体必须充当自己的预言，在没有指导的情况下隐式判断应用行为是否正确；(2) 概率性推理导致可靠性有限——LLM 前后不一致的推理削弱了其作为预言的可信度。我们提出 WebTestPilot，一种基于 LLM 的神经符号方法，通过符号化同时应对这两大挑战。WebTestPilot 检测 Web 应用中的关键 GUI 元素并将其抽象为符号变量。该设计通过把断言生成约束在显式定义的符号之上来提升可靠性，从而减少无约束或不一致的推理。同时，它以结构化的符号形式表示应用状态及其相互关系，从而提高智能体识别跨状态的数据依赖、因果依赖与时序依赖的可能性，进而提升准确性。这些能力共同使 WebTestPilot 能够生成可靠且准确的测试预言，捕捉由测试需求导出的、有意义的隐式预期。为推进该领域研究，我们构建了一个注入缺陷的 Web 应用基准，用于评估自然语言到端到端测试的能力。结果显示，WebTestPilot 的任务完成率达到 99%，在缺陷检测上取得 96% 的精确率与 96% 的召回率，超过最好的基线（精确率 +70，召回率 +27）。该智能体在多样的自然语言输入（含拼写错误、语法错误、冗余句子、风格改写或缩写）以及不同模型规模（3B–72B）上均能泛化。在与一个无代码平台的真实部署中，WebTestPilot 在开发过程中发现了 8 个缺陷，涵盖数据绑定、UI 与导航问题。","tl":"把 GUI 元素符号化以约束断言生成，抑制预言幻觉。","au":["Xiwen Teoh","Yun Lin","Duc-Minh Nguyen","Ruofei Ren","Wenjie Zhang","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","agentic","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["end-to-end web testing","VLM agent","test oracle inference","neurosymbolic","GUI symbolization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/207/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.11724"},{"id":"p01016","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fool Me If You Can: On the Robustness of Binary Code Similarity Detection Models against Semantics-preserving Transformations","tz":"能骗到你算你行：论二进制代码相似性检测模型对语义保持变换的鲁棒性","a":"Binary analysis plays an essential role in cybersecurity, facilitating reverse engineering to reveal the inner workings of programs in the absence of source code. Traditional approaches, such as static and dynamic analysis, extract valuable insights from stripped binaries, but often demand substantial expertise and manual effort. Recent advances in deep learning have opened promising opportunities to enhance binary analysis by capturing latent features and disclosing underlying code semantics. Despite the growing number of binary analysis models based on machine learning, their robustness to adversarial code transformations remains underexplored. In this work, we evaluate the robustness of deep learning models for the task of binary code similarity detection (BCSD) under semantics-preserving transformations. The unique nature of machine instructions presents distinct challenges compared to the typical input perturbations found in other domains. To achieve our goal, we introduce asmFooler, a system that evaluates the resilience of BCSD models using a diverse set of adversarial code transformations that preserve functional semantics. We construct a dataset of 9,565 binary variants from 620 baseline samples by applying eight semantics-preserving transformations across six representative BCSD models. Our major findings highlight several key insights: i) model robustness highly relies on the design of the processing pipeline, including code pre-processing, model architecture, and internal feature selection, which collectively determine how code semantics are captured; ii) the effectiveness of adversarial transformations is bounded by a transformation budget, shaped by model-specific constraints such as input size limits and the expressive capacity of semantically equivalent instructions; iii) well-crafted adversarial transformations can be highly effective, even when introducing minimal perturbations; and iv) such transformations disrupt the model’s ability to recognize and focus on semantically significant instructions.","az":"二进制分析在网络安全中扮演着关键角色，它支撑逆向工程，在没有源代码的情况下揭示程序的内部工作机制。静态与动态分析等传统方法能从剥离符号的二进制中提取有价值的洞见，但往往需要大量专业知识与人工投入。深度学习的最新进展为增强二进制分析带来了有希望的机会，因为它能捕获潜在特征并揭示底层代码语义。尽管基于机器学习的二进制分析模型日益增多，它们对对抗性代码变换的鲁棒性仍研究不足。在本工作中，我们评估用于二进制代码相似性检测（BCSD）任务的深度学习模型在语义保持变换下的鲁棒性。机器指令的独特性质带来了不同于其他领域典型输入扰动的挑战。为实现目标，我们引入 asmFooler，一个使用多样的、保持功能语义的对抗性代码变换来评估 BCSD 模型抗性的系统。我们对六个具有代表性的 BCSD 模型，应用八种语义保持变换，从 620 个基线样本构建出包含 9,565 个二进制变体的数据集。我们的主要发现包括若干关键洞见：i) 模型鲁棒性高度依赖处理流水线的设计，包括代码预处理、模型架构与内部特征选择，它们共同决定代码语义如何被捕获；ii) 对抗性变换的有效性受变换预算限制，而该预算由模型特定的约束（如输入长度上限以及语义等价指令的表达能力）所塑造；iii) 精心构造的对抗性变换即便引入极小扰动也可能非常有效；iv) 此类变换会破坏模型识别并聚焦语义关键指令的能力。","tl":"用八种语义保持变换系统攻破六个二进制相似性检测模型。","au":["Jiyong Uhm","Minseok Kim","Michalis Polychronakis","Hyungjoon Koo"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["security","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["binary code similarity detection","semantics-preserving transformations","adversarial robustness","reverse engineering","deep learning models"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/208/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.12681"},{"id":"p01017","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Generalizing Test Cases for Comprehensive Test Scenario Coverage","tz":"泛化测试用例以实现全面的测试场景覆盖","a":"Test cases are essential for software development and maintenance. In practice, developers derive multiple test cases from an implicit pattern based on their understanding of requirements and inference of diverse test scenarios, each validating a specific behavior of the focal method. However, producing comprehensive tests is time-consuming and error-prone: many important tests that should have accompanied the initial test are added only after a significant delay, sometimes only after bugs are triggered. Existing automated test generation techniques largely focus on code coverage. Yet in real projects, practical tests are seldom driven by code coverage alone, since test scenarios do not necessarily align with control-flow branches. Instead, test scenarios originate from requirements, which are often implicitly embedded in a project’s design and implementation. Given a focal method, its underlying requirement can often be inferred from relevant project knowledge and the initial test that reflects the developer’s intent. In this work, we propose TestGeneralizer, a framework for generalizing test cases to comprehensively cover test scenarios. TestGeneralizer orchestrates three stages: (1) enhancing the understanding of the requirement and scenario behind the focal method and initial test; (2) generating a test scenario template and crystallizing it into various test scenario instances; and (3) generating and refining executable test cases from these instances. To ensure accuracy and completeness, TestGeneralizer combines rule-based prompts, automatically optimized via a prompt auto-tuning technique, with crucial project knowledge retrieved through program analysis. We evaluate TestGeneralizer against three state-of-the-art baselines (EvoSuite, gpt-o4-mini, and ChatTester) on 12 open-source Java projects, covering 506 multi-test focal methods and 1,637 test scenarios. TestGeneralizer achieves significant improvements: +64.00% and +56.87% over EvoSuite, +34.63% and +29.37% over gpt-o4-mini, and +28.70% and +20.05% over ChatTester, in mutation-based and LLM-assessed scenario coverage, respectively. In a field study, we submitted 27 generalized tests overlooked by developers; 16 were accepted and merged into official repositories, demonstrating the practical usefulness of TestGeneralizer.","az":"测试用例对软件开发与维护至关重要。在实践中，开发者基于对需求的理解与对多样测试场景的推断，从一个隐式模式派生出多个测试用例，每个用例验证被测方法的某一特定行为。然而，产出全面的测试既耗时又易错：许多本应与初始测试一同编写的重要测试，往往在很久之后才被补上，有时甚至要等到缺陷被触发之后。现有自动测试生成技术大多聚焦于代码覆盖率。然而在真实项目中，实用的测试很少仅由代码覆盖率驱动，因为测试场景未必与控制流分支对齐。相反，测试场景源自需求，而需求常常隐含地嵌入在项目的设计与实现之中。给定一个被测方法，其背后的需求往往可以从相关项目知识以及体现开发者意图的初始测试中推断出来。在本工作中，我们提出 TestGeneralizer，一个泛化测试用例以全面覆盖测试场景的框架。TestGeneralizer 编排三个阶段：(1) 增强对被测方法与初始测试背后的需求与场景的理解；(2) 生成测试场景模板并将其具体化为各种测试场景实例；(3) 从这些实例生成并精化可执行的测试用例。为确保准确性与完整性，TestGeneralizer 将基于规则的提示（通过提示自动调优技术自动优化）与经由程序分析检索到的关键项目知识相结合。我们在 12 个开源 Java 项目上，覆盖 506 个多测试被测方法与 1,637 个测试场景，将 TestGeneralizer 与三个最先进基线（EvoSuite、gpt-o4-mini 与 ChatTester）进行比较。TestGeneralizer 取得显著提升：在基于变异与由 LLM 评估的场景覆盖上，分别比 EvoSuite 高出 64.00% 与 56.87%，比 gpt-o4-mini 高出 34.63% 与 29.37%，比 ChatTester 高出 28.70% 与 20.05%。在一项实地研究中，我们提交了 27 个被开发者忽略的泛化测试，其中 16 个被接受并合入官方仓库，证明了 TestGeneralizer 的实用价值。","tl":"以场景而非分支覆盖为目标，从初始测试泛化出更多用例。","au":["Binhang Qi","Yun Lin","Xinyi Weng","Chenyan Liu","Hailong Sun","Gordon Fraser","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test scenario coverage","test generalization","unit test generation","prompt auto-tuning","program analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/209/x"},{"id":"p01018","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Uncovering Similar but Different Packages in PyPI and Potential Security Threats","tz":"揭示 PyPI 中相似但不同的软件包及其潜在安全威胁","a":"In this study, we present a large-scale, in-depth study of package replication in PyPI. As a vital platform, PyPI streamlines Python package distribution for developers. However, beyond small-scale code cloning, we observe that many replicated packages exist on PyPI, which duplicate most of the codebase from existing packages. Such replication not only confuses developers but also propagates known vulnerabilities and enables the creation of new malicious packages. To address this issue, we comprehensively examine the characteristics and potential threats of replicated packages. Using one-third of the entire PyPI repository (200K packages), we investigate replication from three perspectives: replication of popular packages, vulnerable packages, and malicious packages. Our experiments reveal three critical findings about package replication in PyPI: (1) by identifying 1,361 replicated packages of the top 3K popular projects, we show that replication frequently redistributes substantial portions of existing packages under different maintainers; (2) by uncovering 256 previously unknown replicated vulnerable packages, we demonstrate that replication creates vulnerability blind spots that current detection tools rarely catch; (3) by analyzing 3,883 known malicious packages, we found that 186 (4.79%) replicated popular ones, and this pattern further led us to identify seven previously unknown replicated malicious packages, highlighting its role as an attack vector for malware distribution through minor modifications and code injection.","az":"在本研究中，我们对 PyPI 中的软件包复制现象开展了大规模、深入的研究。作为关键平台，PyPI 为开发者简化了 Python 包的分发。然而，除了小规模的代码克隆之外，我们观察到 PyPI 上存在许多复制包，它们从已有包中复制了大部分代码库。这类复制不仅令开发者困惑，还会传播已知漏洞，并为制造新的恶意包提供便利。为应对这一问题，我们全面考察了复制包的特征与潜在威胁。我们使用整个 PyPI 仓库的三分之一（20 万个包），从三个视角研究复制：热门包的复制、脆弱包的复制以及恶意包的复制。我们的实验揭示了关于 PyPI 包复制的三项关键发现：(1) 通过识别出前 3000 个热门项目的 1,361 个复制包，我们表明复制常常在不同维护者名下重新分发已有包的大量内容；(2) 通过发现 256 个此前未知的被复制的脆弱包，我们证明复制制造了当前检测工具很少能捕捉到的漏洞盲区；(3) 通过分析 3,883 个已知恶意包，我们发现其中 186 个（4.79%）复制了热门包，这一模式进一步引导我们识别出七个此前未知的被复制恶意包，凸显了复制作为通过微小改动与代码注入分发恶意软件的攻击途径的作用。","tl":"大规模量化 PyPI 包复制造成的漏洞盲区与恶意分发链路。","au":["Sunha Park","Soojin Han","Seunghoon Woo"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","security"],"kw":["PyPI","package replication","software supply chain","vulnerable packages","malicious packages"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/210/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.29785"},{"id":"p01019","v":"FSE 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Event-B Agent: Towards LLM Agent for Formal Model Synthesis and Repair","tz":"Event-B Agent：迈向用于形式化模型合成与修复的大模型智能体","a":"Building software that is correct by construction is a long-standing goal in software engineering, as it ensures that reliability is achieved during design rather than after deployment. Formal methods realize this vision by allowing system behavior and requirements to be expressed in mathematics, enabling correctness to be guaranteed through proofs and verification. However, the steep learning curve and demand for mathematical expertise hinder its widespread adoption. Large language models (LLMs) have recently shown promise in bridging this gap through autoformalization, but existing approaches often address isolated tasks, such as theorem proving or model synthesis verified by model checking. While valuable, these single-perspective efforts do not fully exploit the potential of a more comprehensive framework where models and proofs evolve together. To address this gap, we propose Event-B Agent, a novel framework inspired by the interleaved nature of software design. From natural language requirements, Event-B Agent constructs an initial model and iteratively adjusts it using feedback from model checking and theorem proving. Adjusting and refining the model, in turn, simplifies proof discharge that ensures correctness with respect to requirements. Evaluation across systems of varying complexity shows that Event-B Agent substantially outperforms baselines in end-to-end model synthesis and repair. These results show a promising direction into achieving correctness-by-construction through probabilistic approaches like LLM agents.","az":"构建“构造即正确”的软件是软件工程中长期追求的目标，因为它确保可靠性是在设计阶段而非部署之后获得的。形式化方法通过允许用数学表达系统行为与需求，使正确性能够经由证明与验证得到保证，从而实现这一愿景。然而陡峭的学习曲线与对数学专长的要求阻碍了其广泛采用。大语言模型（LLM）近来在通过自动形式化（autoformalization）弥合这一鸿沟方面展现出潜力，但现有方法往往只处理孤立任务，例如定理证明，或由模型检验验证的模型合成。这些单一视角的努力虽有价值，却没有充分发挥一个更综合框架的潜力——在该框架中模型与证明共同演化。为填补这一空白，我们提出 **Event-B Agent**，一个受软件设计交织特性启发的新框架。Event-B Agent 从自然语言需求出发构建初始模型，并利用来自模型检验与定理证明的反馈迭代地调整它。反过来，对模型的调整与精化又简化了证明义务的消解，从而确保模型相对于需求的正确性。在不同复杂度系统上的评估表明，Event-B Agent 在端到端的模型合成与修复上大幅优于基线。这些结果展示了通过 LLM 智能体这类概率性方法实现“构造即正确”的一个有希望的方向。","tl":"让模型检验与定理证明反馈驱动 Event-B 模型与证明共同演化。","au":["Hongshu Wang","Xinyue Zuo","Yuhan Sun","Qin Li","Yamine AIT AMEUR","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Event-B","autoformalization","model checking","theorem proving","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/211/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.17475"},{"id":"p01020","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SpecFSM: Extracting and Repairing Finite State Machines from Protocol Specification Documents","tz":"SpecFSM：从协议规范文档中抽取并修复有限状态机","a":"Finite state machines (FSMs) are a fundamental abstraction for modeling dynamic system behavior and are widely used in protocol analysis. However, automatically extracting FSMs from natural-language specifications remains challenging. Protocol documents are often lengthy and structurally complex, with state-transition descriptions scattered across the text. As a result, large language models (LLMs) operating under incomplete context are prone to generating spurious transitions and logically flawed FSMs. In this paper, we propose SpecFSM, a framework for the automatic extraction and repair of protocol FSMs from natural-language specifications. SpecFSM combines state completion, evidence tracing, and formal verification into a unified pipeline that infers missing states, constrains incorrect transitions, and repairs logical defects in the extracted models. Experiments on multiple protocol documents show that SpecFSM improves the average number of correctly extracted state transitions by 54.7% over existing methods, while producing FSMs with stronger logical validity and better interpretability.","az":"有限状态机（FSM）是建模动态系统行为的基础抽象，被广泛用于协议分析。然而，从自然语言规范中自动抽取 FSM 仍具挑战性。协议文档通常篇幅冗长、结构复杂，状态转移的描述散落在文本各处。因此，在上下文不完整的情况下运行的大语言模型（LLM）容易生成虚假的转移和逻辑上有缺陷的 FSM。本文提出 SpecFSM，一个从自然语言规范中自动抽取与修复协议 FSM 的框架。SpecFSM 将状态补全、证据溯源与形式化验证结合进统一流水线，推断缺失状态、约束错误转移，并修复抽取模型中的逻辑缺陷。在多份协议文档上的实验表明，SpecFSM 相比现有方法将正确抽取的状态转移平均数量提升了 54.7%，同时产出逻辑有效性更强、可解释性更好的 FSM。","tl":"状态补全加证据溯源与形式验证联合修复抽取出的协议 FSM。","au":["Xiangdong Li","DaWei Huang","Jingjing Guan","Hui Li"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["protocol FSM extraction","specification documents","state completion","evidence tracing","formal verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/1/x"},{"id":"p01021","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automated PoC Synthesis from On-Chain Attack Transactions","tz":"从链上攻击交易自动合成概念验证漏洞利用","tl":"（据标题推断）直接由链上攻击交易反推并自动生成 PoC。","au":["Xing Su","Hao Wu","Hanzhong Liang","Yunlin Jiang","Yuxi Cheng","Yating Liu","Fengyuan Xu","Sheng Zhong"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["proof-of-concept synthesis","on-chain attack transactions","smart contract security","exploit reconstruction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/2/x"},{"id":"p01022","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Context-Aware Trust Verification for Identity-Based Software Signing","tz":"面向基于身份的软件签名的上下文感知信任验证","a":"End-to-end security verification, from requirements through architecture to code, requires datasets that span all three artifact types with fine-grained security labels. No existing dataset provides this combination. We present the EVerest dataset, a multi-artifact resource based on EVerest, an industry-driven open-source software stack for electric vehicle charging stations. The dataset includes 84 manually elicited security requirements annotated with security objectives, 1,445 fine-grained security elements (components, entities, data, data flows, states, etc.), acceptance windows, coreferences, and architectural trace links, as well as the EVerest software architecture model, source code, and natural language documentation. It enables research on security requirements classification, named entity recognition, architectural trace linking, and design-time or code-level security verification. During dataset creation, a real security weakness (CWE-1295) was identified, disclosed to the project maintainers, and subsequently fixed. The dataset is publicly available. A short video is available at https://youtu.be/pnn1uqpomvQ.","az":"从需求经架构到代码的端到端安全验证，需要同时覆盖这三类制品并带有细粒度安全标注的数据集。目前尚无数据集提供这样的组合。我们提出 EVerest 数据集，一个基于 EVerest（一个由产业界推动的电动汽车充电桩开源软件栈）的多制品资源。该数据集包含 84 条人工抽取并以安全目标标注的安全需求、1,445 个细粒度安全元素（组件、实体、数据、数据流、状态等）、接受窗口、共指关系与架构追踪链接，以及 EVerest 的软件架构模型、源代码和自然语言文档。它支持安全需求分类、命名实体识别、架构追踪链接，以及设计期或代码级安全验证等研究。在数据集构建过程中，我们识别出一个真实的安全弱点（CWE-1295），并已向项目维护者披露且随后被修复。该数据集已公开发布。简短视频见 https://youtu.be/pnn1uqpomvQ 。","tl":"首个贯通需求—架构—代码并带细粒度安全标注的数据集。","au":["Chinenye Okafor","James C. Davis","Santiago Torres-Arias"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["benchmark-dataset","security","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["security requirements","architecture trace links","multi-artifact dataset","EVerest","end-to-end security verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/3/x"},{"id":"p01023","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A11YRepair: Bridging Web Accessibility Barriers via Knowledge-Enhanced Divide-and-Conquer Repair","tz":"A11YRepair：以知识增强的分而治之修复弥合 Web 无障碍障碍","a":"Web accessibility (A11Y), which ensures web content is perceivable and usable for users with disabilities, is a critical requirement for modern web applications. Yet existing tooling overwhelmingly focuses on detecting A11Y violations rather than repairing them. Automated program repair (APR) techniques appear promising for this setting, but our study shows that state-of-the-art APR systems perform poorly when applied to real-world A11Y violations. Unlike conventional sparse-bug scenarios, web A11Y issues often manifest as multiple structurally related violations per page, requiring coordinated edits across multiple files. Existing repair systems fail to manage this multi-fault scale, as they handle each bug individually without considering their relationships or incorporating domain rules such as the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG). We propose A11YRepair, an LLM-based framework for web A11Y repair. A11YRepair introduces a divide-and-conquer workflow that first clusters violations requiring coordinated edits to reduce redundant localization, and then decomposes each cluster by root cause so the LLM can generate focused and consistent patches. The framework further incorporates WCAG-driven knowledge to strengthen domain awareness during both fault localization and patch synthesis. To support systematic evaluation, we construct A11YBench, a benchmark of 60 real-world web projects collected from GitHub. Experimental results show that A11YRepair achieves higher repair effectiveness and lower cost than state-of-the-art baselines, and ablation studies confirm the importance of its divide-and-conquer design and selective domain knowledge integration. Specifically, patches generated by A11YRepair have been merged into open-source projects from Google, Microsoft, Facebook, IBM, K8s, Docker, and Alibaba, demonstrating its practical value.","az":"Web 无障碍（A11Y）确保网页内容对残障用户可感知、可使用，是现代 Web 应用的关键需求。然而现有工具绝大多数聚焦于检测 A11Y 违规，而非修复它们。自动程序修复（APR）技术在这一场景中看似有希望，但我们的研究表明，最先进的 APR 系统在应用于真实世界 A11Y 违规时表现不佳。与传统稀疏缺陷场景不同，Web A11Y 问题往往在一个页面上表现为多个结构相关的违规，需要跨多个文件的协调编辑。现有修复系统无法应对这种多缺陷规模，因为它们逐个处理缺陷，既不考虑缺陷之间的关系，也不融入诸如 Web 内容无障碍指南（WCAG）之类的领域规则。我们提出 A11YRepair，一个基于 LLM 的 Web A11Y 修复框架。A11YRepair 引入分而治之的工作流：先对需要协调编辑的违规进行聚类以减少冗余定位，再按根因对每个簇进行分解，使 LLM 能生成聚焦且一致的补丁。该框架进一步在缺陷定位与补丁合成两个阶段引入 WCAG 驱动的知识以强化领域意识。为支持系统性评估，我们构建了 A11YBench，一个由 GitHub 收集的 60 个真实 Web 项目组成的基准。实验结果表明，A11YRepair 相比最先进基线取得了更高的修复有效性与更低的成本，消融实验确认了其分而治之设计与选择性领域知识融合的重要性。具体而言，A11YRepair 生成的补丁已被合并进 Google、Microsoft、Facebook、IBM、K8s、Docker 与阿里巴巴的开源项目，展示了其实用价值。","tl":"按根因聚类违规并注入 WCAG 知识实现协调式无障碍修复。","au":["Kai Huang","Ling Zhu","Jian Zhang","Xiaofei Xie","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["accessibility-inclusion","llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["web accessibility","WCAG","automated repair","divide-and-conquer","A11YBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/4/x"},{"id":"p01024","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GALA: Graph-Augmented LLM Agents for Root Cause Analysis and Incident Response in Microservices","tz":"GALA：面向微服务根因分析与事件响应的图增强大模型智能体","a":"Microservice root cause analysis (RCA) requires correlating failures across heterogeneous telemetry within complex service dependency graphs. Existing methods often rely on a single telemetry modality; recent LLM-based approaches can suffer from unconstrained exploration and hallucination; and most systems stop at fault ranking without producing actionable incident response. We present GALA, a graph-augmented LLM agentic framework centered on graph-guided investigation, which uses service dependencies to bound exploration and refine diagnosis through localized multi-modal evidence. For initial hypothesis generation, GALA combines complementary telemetry signals with STRIX, a novel trace- and graph-structure-aware scoring module. GALA then produces ranked diagnoses, incident summaries, and stratified action recommendations. We further introduce SURE-score, a human-guided evaluation framework co-developed with industry SRE experts for assessing RCA-specific output quality beyond conventional text similarity metrics. On two microservice benchmarks, GALA consistently achieves the strongest overall results, surpassing the best LLM-based baseline by more than 25 percentage points in AC@1, while also receiving the highest ratings from both SURE-score and independent human SRE evaluation.","az":"微服务根因分析（RCA）需要在复杂的服务依赖图中关联异构遥测数据上的故障。现有方法往往只依赖单一遥测模态；近期基于 LLM 的方法可能受困于无约束的探索与幻觉；而大多数系统止步于故障排序，并不产出可执行的事件响应。我们提出 GALA，一个以图引导调查为核心的图增强 LLM 智能体框架，它利用服务依赖关系限定探索范围，并通过局部化的多模态证据精化诊断。在初始假设生成阶段，GALA 将互补的遥测信号与 STRIX（一个新颖的、感知调用链与图结构的评分模块）相结合。随后，GALA 产出排序后的诊断结论、事件摘要与分层的行动建议。我们还引入 SURE-score，一个与业界 SRE 专家共同开发、以人为引导的评估框架，用于在传统文本相似度指标之外评估 RCA 特有的输出质量。在两个微服务基准上，GALA 始终取得最强的整体结果，在 AC@1 上比最好的基于 LLM 的基线高出 25 个百分点以上，同时在 SURE-score 与独立的人类 SRE 评估中均获得最高评分。","tl":"用服务依赖图约束智能体探索并直接产出事件响应建议。","au":["Yifang Tian","Yaming Liu","Zichun Chong","Zihang Huang","Yiran Li","Hans-Arno Jacobsen"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["root cause analysis","microservices","LLM agent","service dependency graph","incident response"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/5/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.08968"},{"id":"p01025","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"IntOAgent: A Practical Framework for Automated Detection and Triggering of Integer Overflow Vulnerabilities","tz":"IntOAgent：一个自动检测与触发整数溢出漏洞的实用框架","a":"Integer overflows remain a long-standing yet often underestimated class of vulnerabilities in C/C++ software, often leading to logic errors and severe downstream security consequences. Despite their simple arithmetic nature, accurately detecting integer overflows in real-world codebases remains challenging. Existing approaches suffer from poor scalability due to the large search space of arithmetic operations, and often fail to generate triggerable proof-of-concept (PoCs) because jointly satisfying statement reachability and overflow-triggering constraints is inherently difficult. In this paper, we propose IntOAgent, a scalable agent-based framework for automated detection and triggering of integer overflow vulnerabilities. IntOAgent is built on the key insight that reachability and overflow triggering should be treated as distinct yet coordinated tasks. To improve scalability, IntOAgent employs a two-stage filtering strategy to prune provably safe operations and a boundary-aware path prioritization to focus on overflow-prone executions. To enable effective PoC generation, IntOAgent infers input structures and integrates overflow-guided range analysis to drive inputs toward boundary violations while preserving path feasibility. We evaluate IntOAgent on established benchmarks Juliet c and five widely-used real-world projects (SQLite, Libxml2, Libplist, V8, and Libpng) against state-of-the-art directed fuzzing and LLM-based techniques. IntOAgent outperforms existing approaches in both effectiveness and efficiency, discovering all existing vulnerabilities and 117 previously unknown integer overflow vulnerabilities (68 assigned CVEs). These results demonstrate that IntOAgent enables scalable generation of triggerable PoCs, significantly improving the practical detection of integer overflow vulnerabilities.","az":"整数溢出是 C/C++ 软件中长期存在却常被低估的一类漏洞，往往导致逻辑错误与严重的下游安全后果。尽管其算术本质简单，在真实代码库中准确检测整数溢出仍然困难。现有方法因算术运算的搜索空间巨大而可扩展性差，并且往往无法生成可触发的概念验证（PoC），因为同时满足语句可达性与溢出触发约束本身就极为困难。本文提出 IntOAgent，一个可扩展的、基于智能体的整数溢出漏洞自动检测与触发框架。IntOAgent 建立在一个关键洞见之上：可达性与溢出触发应当被视为彼此不同却相互协调的两项任务。为提升可扩展性，IntOAgent 采用两阶段过滤策略剪除可证明安全的运算，并使用边界感知的路径优先级排序聚焦于易溢出的执行。为实现有效的 PoC 生成，IntOAgent 推断输入结构，并集成溢出导向的区间分析，在保持路径可行性的同时驱动输入逼近边界违规。我们在成熟基准 Juliet C 以及五个广泛使用的真实项目（SQLite、Libxml2、Libplist、V8、Libpng）上，将 IntOAgent 与最先进的定向模糊测试和基于 LLM 的技术进行对比评估。IntOAgent 在有效性与效率上均优于现有方法，发现了全部已有漏洞以及 117 个此前未知的整数溢出漏洞（其中 68 个已分配 CVE）。这些结果表明，IntOAgent 能够可扩展地生成可触发的 PoC，显著提升了整数溢出漏洞的实际检测能力。","tl":"把可达性与溢出触发解耦协调，规模化生成可触发 PoC。","au":["Yuelin Wang","Jiongchi Yu","Xiaofei Xie","Yaohui Sun","Tianyu Shi","Yanbang Sun","Qiang Hu","Junjie Wang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["agentic","llm-based","security"],"kw":["integer overflow","proof-of-concept generation","LLM agent","range analysis","path prioritization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/6/x"},{"id":"p01026","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM-Based Agents for Identifying Bug-Introducing Commits","tz":"基于大模型智能体识别引入缺陷的提交","a":"The growing diversity of code clone types, from syntactic copies to cross-language semantic clones to AI-generated duplicates, has created a fragmentation crisis in clone detection. Current deep learning detectors are domain specialists that degrade significantly outside their training distribution, with F1 drops exceeding 70% across domains. Deploying multiple specialized models is impractical, yet training a single cross-domain detector requires simultaneous access to all training data. To address this, we investigate model merging, a family of post-hoc techniques that operate solely on trained checkpoints. We evaluate parameter merging with five task-vector methods, architecture merging via greedy layer stitching, and cross-tokenizer alignment across four code models, three benchmarks, and twelve configurations. Same-base TIES merging creates effective cross-domain detectors, validated across two model families and three random seeds, reaching 0.865 combined F1 on UniXcoder, 93% of multi-task performance without any training data at the merging step. WUDI achieves the highest in-distribution combined F1 at 0.899, but TIES generalizes better to unseen AI-generated clones, making it our recommended method. Cross-base merging yields only marginal and high-variance gains across all five methods, indicating that task vector compatibility through a shared pre-trained base is the binding factor for effective merging. Merged detectors also outperform zero-shot code LLMs on GPTCloneBench at lower inference cost and generalize up to 4x better than multi-task training to unseen AI-generated clones, suggesting a trade-off between in-domain performance and OOD robustness. This work provides one of the first systematic empirical studies of model merging for software engineering and a practical recipe for building cross-domain clone detectors.","az":"代码克隆类型日益多样化——从语法层面的复制，到跨语言的语义克隆，再到 AI 生成的重复代码——已经造成了克隆检测领域的碎片化危机。当前的深度学习检测器都是领域专才，一旦离开训练分布性能就会显著下降，跨领域的 F1 跌幅超过 70%。部署多个专用模型并不现实，而训练单一的跨领域检测器又要求同时获取全部训练数据。为此，我们研究模型合并（model merging）——一类仅在已训练好的检查点上操作的事后技术。我们评估了采用五种任务向量方法的参数合并、通过贪心层拼接实现的架构合并，以及跨分词器对齐，涵盖四个代码模型、三个基准测试和十二种配置。同基座的 TIES 合并能够构造出有效的跨领域检测器，并在两个模型家族和三个随机种子上得到验证，在 UniXcoder 上达到 0.865 的综合 F1，相当于多任务训练性能的 93%，而合并环节完全不需要任何训练数据。WUDI 取得了最高的分布内综合 F1（0.899），但 TIES 对未见过的 AI 生成克隆泛化得更好，因此是我们推荐的方法。跨基座合并在全部五种方法上都只带来边际且方差很大的收益，说明通过共享预训练基座获得的任务向量兼容性是合并有效性的决定性因素。合并后的检测器在 GPTCloneBench 上也以更低的推理成本超过了零样本代码大模型，并且对未见过的 AI 生成克隆的泛化能力比多任务训练高出最多 4 倍，这表明分布内性能与分布外鲁棒性之间存在权衡。本工作提供了面向软件工程的模型合并的首批系统性实证研究之一，以及构建跨领域克隆检测器的可操作配方。","tl":"首次系统验证模型合并可零数据构建跨域克隆检测器","au":["Niklas Risse","Marcel Böhme"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["model merging","code clone detection","task vectors","TIES merging","cross-domain generalization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/7/x"},{"id":"p01027","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ARMOR: A Robust Self-Supervised Framework for Root Cause Analysis in Microservices under Missing Modality","tz":"ARMOR：面向模态缺失场景的微服务根因分析鲁棒自监督框架","a":"Automated incident management is critical for microservice reliability. While recent unified frameworks leverage multimodal data for joint optimization, they unrealistically assume perfect data completeness. In practice, network fluctuations and agent failures frequently cause missing modalities. Existing approaches relying on static placeholders introduce imputation noise that masks anomalies and degrades performance. To address this, we propose ARMOR, a robust self-supervised framework designed for missing modality scenarios. ARMOR features: (i) a modality-specific asymmetric encoder that isolates distribution disparities among metrics, logs, and traces; and (ii) a missing-aware gated fusion mechanism utilizing learnable placeholders and dynamic bias compensation to prevent cross-modal interference from incomplete inputs. By employing self-supervised auto-regression with mask-guided reconstruction, ARMOR jointly optimizes anomaly detection (AD), failure triage (FT), and root cause localization (RCL). AD and RCL require no fault labels, while FT relies solely on failure-type annotations for the downstream classifier. Extensive experiments demonstrate that ARMOR achieves state-of-the-art performance under complete data conditions and maintains robust diagnostic accuracy even with severe modality loss.","az":"自动化事故管理对微服务可靠性至关重要。尽管近期的统一框架利用多模态数据进行联合优化，它们却不切实际地假设数据是完整的。而在实践中，网络波动与采集代理故障经常导致模态缺失。已有方法依赖静态占位符，会引入插补噪声，从而掩盖异常并降低性能。为此，我们提出 ARMOR，一个面向模态缺失场景的鲁棒自监督框架。ARMOR 具备两大特性：(i) 模态专用的非对称编码器，用以隔离指标、日志与调用链之间的分布差异；(ii) 缺失感知的门控融合机制，利用可学习占位符与动态偏置补偿，防止不完整输入造成跨模态干扰。通过采用带掩码引导重建的自监督自回归训练，ARMOR 联合优化异常检测（AD）、故障分诊（FT）与根因定位（RCL）。其中 AD 与 RCL 无需故障标签，FT 仅需故障类型标注用于下游分类器。大量实验表明，ARMOR 在数据完整条件下达到了最先进性能，并且在严重模态缺失时仍能保持稳健的诊断准确率。","tl":"用缺失感知门控融合实现模态缺失下的微服务根因分析","au":["Wenzhuo Qian","Hailiang Zhao","Ziqi Wang","Zhipeng Gao","Jiayi Chen","Zhiwei Ling","Shuiguang Deng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["root cause analysis","microservices","missing modality","self-supervised learning","anomaly detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/8/x"},{"id":"p01028","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Beyond Text Matching: Towards Reference-Free Evaluation for Human-Oriented Binary Reverse Engineering","tz":"超越文本匹配：面向人类导向二进制逆向工程的无参考评测","a":"Human-Oriented Binary Reverse Engineering (HOBRE) aims to transform decompiled pseudocode into a more human-friendly representation, thereby reducing the cognitive burden of reverse analysis and improving efficiency. However, reliably evaluating HOBRE outputs remains a fundamental challenge. On one hand, human evaluation is costly, time-consuming, as well as difficult to scale. On the other hand, existing automated metrics either rely on executable test cases and runtime environments, which are often unavailable for real-world binaries, or depend on high-quality source code references that are typically inaccessible and fail to capture semantically equivalent but lexically diverse outputs. Although the emerging LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm is naturally well-suited to HOBRE evaluation, its effectiveness has not yet been fully studied. This paper presents the first systematic investigation of the LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm for HOBRE, covering three representative tasks: function name recovery, binary code summarization, and decompilation optimization. We introduce BinJudgeBench, the first expert-annotated, reference-free evaluation benchmark based on multi-dimensional human judgment. Our empirical study reveals that LLM-as-a-Judge achieves an average correlation of 63.20% with human judgment, significantly outperforming traditional automated metrics at 35.04%. By analyzing the impact of various judge configurations, including backbone LLMs, prompting strategies, and decoding temperatures, on both correlation and cost, we find that no ``one-size-fits-all'' configuration exists, as the optimal setup varies across tasks and individual samples. To address this, we propose BinJudge, which employs a lightweight routing mechanism to adaptively select the optimal judge configuration for each specific task and sample. BinJudge improves correlation with human experts by 4.5%-24.7% and reduces API cost to 0.06×-0.84× of that of static best configurations, providing a scalable, cost-effective, and high-fidelity automated evaluation scheme for HOBRE.","az":"人类导向的二进制逆向工程（HOBRE）旨在把反编译得到的伪代码转换成更易于人类理解的表示，从而减轻逆向分析的认知负担、提升效率。然而，可靠地评测 HOBRE 的输出仍是一个根本性挑战。一方面，人工评测代价高、耗时长且难以规模化；另一方面，现有自动化指标要么依赖可执行测试用例与运行时环境（而真实二进制往往不具备），要么依赖高质量的源码参考（通常无法获取，且无法刻画语义等价但词法多样的输出）。尽管新兴的 LLM-as-a-Judge 范式天然适合 HOBRE 评测，其有效性尚未得到充分研究。本文首次系统性地考察了 LLM-as-a-Judge 范式在 HOBRE 上的表现，覆盖三个代表性任务：函数名恢复、二进制代码摘要与反编译优化。我们提出 BinJudgeBench，这是首个基于多维人工判断、由专家标注的无参考评测基准。我们的实证研究显示，LLM-as-a-Judge 与人类判断的平均相关度达到 63.20%，显著优于传统自动化指标的 35.04%。通过分析不同评判配置（骨干大模型、提示策略、解码温度）对相关度与成本的影响，我们发现不存在“放之四海而皆准”的配置，最优设置随任务和单个样本而变化。为此，我们提出 BinJudge，利用轻量级路由机制为每个具体任务与样本自适应地选择最优评判配置。BinJudge 将与人类专家的相关度提升了 4.5%–24.7%，并把 API 成本降至静态最佳配置的 0.06×–0.84×，为 HOBRE 提供了可扩展、低成本且高保真的自动化评测方案。","tl":"首个无参考 HOBRE 评测基准并用路由选最优评判配置","au":["Xiuwei Shang","Li Hu","Xiao Jiang","Jieke Shi","Junda He","Zhou Yang","Shaoyin Cheng","Guoqiang Chen","Weiming Zhang","David Lo"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["LLM-as-a-Judge","binary reverse engineering","reference-free evaluation","decompilation","function name recovery"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/9/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.07038"},{"id":"p01029","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Source-Free Detection and Impact Analysis of Compiler Optimization Problems in Mobile Applications","tz":"移动应用中编译器优化问题的无源码检测与影响分析","a":"Mobile apps frequently suffer from frame drops, overheating, and excessive power consumption. While developers optimize algorithms and debug code, a critical bottleneck often goes unnoticed: native libraries compiled with low optimization levels (O0/O1 instead of O2/O3). Because these libraries execute without functional errors, the resulting performance degradation remains hidden in production apps. We present OptDetect, a source-free framework that detects compiler optimization problems directly from app binaries. OptDetect handles mixed optimization levels through binary disassembly, chunk-level classification, and weighted score aggregation, achieving 93.0 % accuracy on controlled datasets and 81.9 % on real-world datasets. Applying OptDetect to 21,972 native libraries from 830 top-ranked Google Play apps, we find that 30.5 % of libraries use low optimization levels, affecting 91.7 % of apps. Through case studies on 12 production apps, fixing detected issues reduces CPU instructions by 10-63 % (median: 20.5 %) for commercial apps and 15-58 % (median: 32 %) for open-source apps. Performance complaints decrease in 5 of 6 commercial apps, and ratings increase in 5 of 6. Further investigation reveals that widely-used third-party libraries are themselves distributed at low optimization levels, with 49.7 % of 1,073 libraries in a major repository exhibiting this problem. These findings show that compiler optimization problems are common, source-free detectable, and practically consequential in mobile app ecosystems.","az":"移动应用常常出现掉帧、发热和电量消耗过大的问题。开发者往往忙于优化算法、调试代码，却忽视了一个关键瓶颈：本地库在编译时使用了较低的优化级别（O0/O1 而非 O2/O3）。由于这些库在功能上不会报错，由此导致的性能退化在生产环境的应用中被长期隐藏。我们提出 OptDetect，一个无需源码的框架，可直接从应用二进制中检测编译器优化问题。OptDetect 通过二进制反汇编、块级分类与加权分数聚合来处理混合优化级别，在受控数据集上达到 93.0% 的准确率，在真实数据集上达到 81.9%。我们把 OptDetect 应用于来自 830 个 Google Play 榜单应用的 21,972 个本地库，发现 30.5% 的库使用了低优化级别，影响了 91.7% 的应用。通过对 12 个生产应用的案例研究，修复检测到的问题使商业应用的 CPU 指令数减少 10%–63%（中位数 20.5%），开源应用减少 15%–58%（中位数 32%）。6 个商业应用中有 5 个的性能投诉下降，5 个的评分上升。进一步调查发现，广泛使用的第三方库本身就以低优化级别分发：某大型仓库的 1,073 个库中有 49.7% 存在该问题。这些发现表明，编译器优化问题在移动应用生态中普遍存在、可在无源码条件下检测，并且具有实际后果。","tl":"从二进制识别本地库低编译优化级别，实测显著降能耗","au":["Han Hu","Xiaoheng Xie","Bo Sun","Jian Gu","Gang Fan","Li Li"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["compiler optimization level","mobile apps","binary analysis","native libraries","performance degradation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/10/x"},{"id":"p01030","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Quantum Squeeziness: An Information Theoretical Metric for Quantum Software Testability","tz":"Quantum Squeeziness：面向量子软件可测性的信息论度量","a":"Testability—the degree to which faults can be revealed and diagnosed—has long been fundamental in software engineering but remains largely unexplored for quantum software. This work presents the first formalisation of testability for quantum programs, adapting classical concepts to quantum computation. We introduce Quantum Squeeziness, an information-theoretic metric inspired by classical squeeziness, to quantify how faults are masked and prevented from propagating to observable outcomes. We treat it as an inverse measure of testability: higher squeeziness implies stronger fault masking and reduced detectability. We propose an efficient method to compute Quantum Squeeziness and validate it through large-scale quantum mutation analysis. Across more than 50k mutants, we observe a strong negative correlation between squeeziness and mutation score, showing that higher squeeziness predicts lower testability. We further introduce a technique that constrains where and how perturbations are injected, reducing cost while preserving accuracy. The computation is 15% faster than a standard error-propagation baseline, while the optimised variant, FastSqueeziness, reduces mean runtime from 3200s to 189s (16.9 times speedup) with 95% accuracy. By establishing a rigorous foundation of testability for quantum software, this work opens new directions at the intersection of software engineering, quantum information theory, and testing. Beyond testing and debugging, it also supports applications in quantum error mitigation and correction, enabling principled assessment and improvement of program robustness.","az":"可测性——即缺陷能被暴露和诊断的程度——长期以来是软件工程的基础概念，但在量子软件上仍几乎未被探索。本工作首次形式化了量子程序的可测性，把经典概念迁移到量子计算中。我们提出 Quantum Squeeziness，一种受经典 squeeziness 启发的信息论度量，用以量化缺陷被掩盖、无法传播到可观测输出的程度。我们将其视为可测性的逆向度量：squeeziness 越高，意味着缺陷掩盖越强、可检测性越低。我们提出了一种高效计算 Quantum Squeeziness 的方法，并通过大规模量子变异分析加以验证。在超过 5 万个变异体上，我们观察到 squeeziness 与变异得分之间存在强负相关，表明更高的 squeeziness 预示更低的可测性。我们进一步提出一种约束扰动注入位置与方式的技术，在保持准确性的同时降低开销。该计算比标准的误差传播基线快 15%，而优化变体 FastSqueeziness 把平均运行时间从 3200 秒降到 189 秒（加速 16.9 倍），准确率达 95%。通过为量子软件的可测性建立严格基础，本工作在软件工程、量子信息论与测试的交叉处开辟了新方向。除测试与调试外，它还可支持量子误差缓解与纠错，实现对程序鲁棒性的有原则的评估与改进。","tl":"首次形式化量子程序可测性并给出信息论度量","au":["Avner Bensoussan","Hector Menendez","Mohammad Reza Mousavi"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["quantum software testing","testability metric","information theory","mutation analysis","fault masking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/11/x"},{"id":"p01031","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Spec2V: Planning-Guided Specification-to-Verilog Generation Framework with Verification-Driven Debugging","tz":"Spec2V：规划引导、验证驱动调试的规约到 Verilog 生成框架","a":"Field Programmable Gate Array (FPGA) is essential in mission-critical fields like aerospace. It offers high flexibility and deterministic real-time response. With the increase in development demands and system complexity, the traditional design paradigm that relies on manual expertise has become inefficient. Although large language models (LLMs) provide a potential pathway for automated code generation, a significant semantic gap remains between the linear reasoning patterns of LLMs and the inherent parallelism of FPGA hardware logic. Current methods encounter difficulties in decomposing complex tasks, low-resource code generation, and resolving simulation errors. To address these issues, we present Spec2V, an agent framework for the generation of Verilog code. Spec2V incorporates two key complementary components: (i) we propose a task planning method based on a dual-layer Tree of Thought. It decouples complex specifications into macro-topology and micro-logic structures to mitigate logical drift from linear reasoning and to improve the accuracy of initial solutions. (ii) During validation and debugging, Spec2V reformulates failure analysis as a structured attribution task with an LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm. It utilizes the reasoning capabilities of LLMs and multi-source evidence to localize the sources of simulation errors. Furthermore, the framework introduces a multi-temperature hedged sampling strategy and a waveform mismatch rate filtering mechanism to identify correct implementations efficiently from extensive candidate spaces. On the public VerilogEval Machine and Human benchmarks, Spec2V achieves Pass@1 accuracies of up to 99.8% and 99.4%, respectively. Case studies on representative RTL design tasks further demonstrate that Spec2V significantly reduces the manual effort required for implementation and mitigates the overhead of iterative engineering through closed-loop planning, validation, and debugging.","az":"现场可编程门阵列（FPGA）在航空航天等关键任务领域不可或缺，它兼具高灵活性与确定性实时响应。随着开发需求增长与系统复杂度提升，依赖人工经验的传统设计范式已显低效。尽管大语言模型（LLM）为自动化代码生成提供了可能路径，但 LLM 的线性推理模式与 FPGA 硬件逻辑固有的并行性之间仍存在显著语义鸿沟。现有方法在复杂任务分解、低资源代码生成和仿真错误修复方面都面临困难。为解决这些问题，我们提出 Spec2V，一个用于生成 Verilog 代码的智能体框架。Spec2V 包含两个互补的关键组件：(i) 我们提出了基于双层思维树的任务规划方法，将复杂规约解耦为宏观拓扑与微观逻辑结构，以缓解线性推理带来的逻辑漂移并提升初始方案的准确性；(ii) 在验证与调试阶段，Spec2V 借助 LLM-as-a-Judge 范式，把失败分析重新表述为结构化的归因任务，利用 LLM 的推理能力与多源证据定位仿真错误的来源。此外，该框架引入多温度对冲采样策略与波形失配率过滤机制，以便从庞大的候选空间中高效识别正确实现。在公开的 VerilogEval Machine 与 Human 基准上，Spec2V 的 Pass@1 准确率分别最高达到 99.8% 与 99.4%。针对代表性 RTL 设计任务的案例研究进一步表明，Spec2V 显著减少了实现所需的人工工作量，并通过规划、验证与调试的闭环降低了迭代工程的开销。","tl":"双层思维树规划加归因式调试把 Verilog Pass@1 推到近满分","au":["Xuming Liu","Chi Zhang","Jinglong Xu","Shan Zhou","Jinbo Wang"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Verilog generation","tree of thought planning","LLM-as-a-Judge","verification-driven debugging","VerilogEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/12/x"},{"id":"p01032","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Characterizing the Landscape of Open-Source Satellite Software","tz":"刻画开源卫星软件的全景","a":"Satellites have become fundamental components of modern technological systems, supporting critical infrastructure in communication, navigation, Earth observation, and scientific research. As space exploration advances and demand for satellite-enabled services grows, reliance on complex, heterogeneous satellite software continues to increase. A systematic understanding of the satellite software landscape is therefore increasingly important, yet existing studies still lack a comprehensive empirical examination. To address this gap, we present the first characterization study of open-source satellite software, examining its ecosystem and development practices. We mine and analyze 22,286 satellite-related GitHub projects through three research questions on popularity trends (RQ1), software goals (RQ2), and development practices (RQ3). First, we characterize the temporal evolution of projects and active developers, revealing increasing popularity. Second, through manual inspection of 646 projects, we construct a taxonomy of 43 software-goal categories spanning conceptual design, datasets, system implementation, simulation, testing, and tools. Third, we conduct an in-depth analysis of projects with source code, revealing a highly heterogeneous and task-specialized ecosystem with 66 programming languages and diverse implementation strategies. Finally, we summarize key findings and derive actionable implications for satellite developers and researchers.","az":"卫星已成为现代技术体系的基础组成部分，支撑着通信、导航、对地观测与科学研究等关键基础设施。随着太空探索推进和卫星服务需求增长，人们对复杂、异构的卫星软件的依赖不断加深。因此，系统性理解卫星软件的全貌变得愈发重要，但已有研究仍缺乏全面的实证考察。为填补这一空白，我们首次开展开源卫星软件的刻画研究，考察其生态与开发实践。我们挖掘并分析了 22,286 个与卫星相关的 GitHub 项目，围绕流行度趋势（RQ1）、软件目标（RQ2）与开发实践（RQ3）三个研究问题展开。首先，我们刻画了项目与活跃开发者随时间的演化，揭示出日益上升的流行度。其次，通过人工检查 646 个项目，我们构建了包含 43 个软件目标类别的分类体系，涵盖概念设计、数据集、系统实现、仿真、测试与工具。第三，我们对含源码的项目做了深入分析，揭示出一个高度异构、任务专用化的生态，涉及 66 种编程语言和多样的实现策略。最后，我们总结了关键发现，并为卫星开发者与研究者提炼出可操作的启示。","tl":"首次大规模刻画开源卫星软件生态并建 43 类目标分类","au":["Jinfeng Wen","Qi Liang","Yuehan Sun","Federica Sarro","Ao Zhou","Xuanzhe Liu","Shangguang Wang"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["satellite software","open source ecosystem","GitHub mining","taxonomy","development practices"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/13/x"},{"id":"p01033","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Bridging the Gap between Intent and Impact: An Empirical Study of GPU Optimizations in Deep Learning Frameworks","tz":"弥合意图与实效的鸿沟：深度学习框架中 GPU 优化的实证研究","tl":"（据标题推断）实测深度学习框架里 GPU 优化的真实收益与落差","au":["Siqi Wang","Fanjing Luo","Xing Hu","Xinyu Wang","Xin Xia"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study"],"kw":["GPU optimization","deep learning frameworks","empirical study","performance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/14/x"},{"id":"p01034","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CIPIHunter: Detecting Configuration-Induced Prediction Instability in Deep Learning Frameworks","tz":"CIPIHunter：检测深度学习框架中配置引发的预测不稳定性","a":"In the automotive domain, in-car scene understanding (ISU) enables the detection of safety-critical events, such as driver distraction, and supports drivers or passengers by analyzing the in-car scene and adapting the environment (e.g., ambient lighting). The industry is increasingly exploring vision-language models (VLMs) to interpret camera-recorded in-car scenes and extract information for downstream reasoning tasks. However, VLMs may generate incomplete, erroneous, or misleading scene descriptions, highlighting the need for systematic testing. Collecting real in-vehicle data is costly, difficult to scale, and often infeasible, particularly in early design stages. In this paper, we present ISU-Test, an automated testing approach that combines rendering-based scene generation with search-based testing to evaluate ISU systems. By framing testing as an optimization problem and systematically modifying scene parameters, our method generates diverse in-car scenarios and explores a wide range of configurations. We evaluate ISU-Test on both an industrial prototype and open-source VLMs across two case studies: question answering and captioning, comparing against randomized scenario generation. Results show that ISU-Test significantly outperforms the baseline, achieving up to 10 times higher failure rates and up to 3.6 times higher failure coverage.","az":"在汽车领域，车内场景理解（ISU）可检测诸如驾驶员分心等安全关键事件，并通过分析车内场景、调整环境（例如氛围灯）来辅助驾驶员或乘客。业界正日益尝试用视觉语言模型（VLM）来解读摄像头记录的车内场景，并为下游推理任务提取信息。然而，VLM 可能生成不完整、错误或具有误导性的场景描述，这凸显了系统化测试的必要性。采集真实的车内数据成本高、难以规模化，在早期设计阶段往往不可行。本文提出 ISU-Test，一种把基于渲染的场景生成与基于搜索的测试相结合的自动化测试方法，用以评估 ISU 系统。通过把测试构造为优化问题并系统性地修改场景参数，我们的方法能够生成多样的车内场景并探索广泛的配置空间。我们在一个工业原型和多个开源 VLM 上评估 ISU-Test，涵盖问答与图像描述两个案例研究，并与随机场景生成做对比。结果表明，ISU-Test 显著优于基线，失败率最高提升 10 倍，失败覆盖率最高提升 3.6 倍。","tl":"用渲染场景加搜索式测试系统暴露车内场景理解的失败","au":["Yanzhou Mu","Shuo Meng","Mijung Kim","Xiang Chen","Chunrong Fang","Zhenyu Chen","Juan Zhai"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["in-car scene understanding","vision-language models","search-based testing","scene generation","automotive testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/15/x"},{"id":"p01035","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TasmScan: Continuation-Aware Taint Analysis for TVM Bytecode with Savelist Abstraction","tz":"TasmScan：面向 TVM 字节码的续延感知污点分析与 Savelist 抽象","a":"The Open Network (TON) has over 175 million activated on-chain addresses and relies on the TVM (TON Virtual Machine) to execute smart contracts. TVM uses first-class continuations with savelists to manage control flow and register state across continuation invocations. Since savelist-captured registers allow data to flow across continuation boundaries without passing through the operand stack, bytecode-level analyses cannot construct complete data flow tracking without explicitly modeling savelist semantics. We present TasmScan, the first bytecode-level static analysis framework for TVM that enables cross-continuation data flow reasoning without requiring source code. TasmScan models savelist semantics via forward register analysis with a formal over-approximation guarantee for exact-resolved save sites and locally tracked register definitions, then lifts bytecode into TASIR, a typed intermediate representation, and performs path-sensitive taint analysis with context-aware sources to detect defects. We evaluate TasmScan on 2,921 contracts from the TON verifier registry and a labeled benchmark of 208 contracts with human-confirmed ground truth. On the full corpus, TasmScan resolves all 294,546 dynamic continuation targets with 100% precision; ablation confirms that savelist propagation is essential for resolving indirect register calls that depend on cross-continuation register passing. On the benchmark, TasmScan detects 95.3% of defects across five classes with 96.8% precision. A 366-pair stratified sample from the full corpus estimates 85.8% overall precision. TasmScan offers a 17x median speedup over the state-of-the-art symbolic-execution baseline, and in the path-analysis comparison completes 100% of analyses with zero crashes or timeouts.","az":"The Open Network（TON）拥有超过 1.75 亿个已激活的链上地址，并依赖 TVM（TON 虚拟机）执行智能合约。TVM 使用带 savelist 的一等续延（first-class continuation）来管理控制流以及跨续延调用的寄存器状态。由于 savelist 捕获的寄存器允许数据跨越续延边界流动而不经过操作数栈，字节码层面的分析若不显式建模 savelist 语义，就无法构建完整的数据流跟踪。我们提出 TasmScan，这是首个面向 TVM 的字节码级静态分析框架，无需源码即可进行跨续延的数据流推理。TasmScan 通过前向寄存器分析对 savelist 语义建模，对精确解析的保存点与局部跟踪的寄存器定义给出形式化的过近似保证，随后把字节码提升为带类型的中间表示 TASIR，并借助上下文感知的污点源执行路径敏感的污点分析以检测缺陷。我们在来自 TON 验证器注册表的 2,921 个合约以及一个含 208 个合约、带人工确认基准真值的标注基准上评估 TasmScan。在完整语料上，TasmScan 以 100% 的精确率解析了全部 294,546 个动态续延目标；消融实验确认 savelist 传播对解析依赖跨续延寄存器传递的间接寄存器调用是必不可少的。在基准上，TasmScan 检出了五类缺陷中 95.3% 的缺陷，精确率为 96.8%。对完整语料做 366 对分层抽样估计出的总体精确率为 85.8%。相较最先进的符号执行基线，TasmScan 的中位加速比为 17 倍，并且在路径分析对比中以零崩溃、零超时完成了 100% 的分析。","tl":"首次建模 savelist 语义实现 TVM 字节码跨续延污点分析","au":["Yixuan Liu","Yin Wu","Yi Li"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["TVM bytecode","taint analysis","smart contract security","continuations","static analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/16/x","pu":"https://liyiweb.com/files/Liu2026TCA.pdf"},{"id":"p01036","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Quick Bug Detection through Black-Box Checking: A Systematic Evaluation","tz":"通过黑盒检查快速发现缺陷：一项系统性评估","a":"Rust's ownership type system prevents memory errors in safe code, but certain desirable properties remain orthogonal to compilation: the soundness of unsafe operations (e.g., raw pointer dereferences), functional correctness, and absence of runtime panics. We present Kani, an open-source model checker for Rust that pushes bounded model checking beyond bug-finding to provide correctness guarantees for these properties. Kani compiles proof harnesses from Rust's Mid-level Intermediate Representation (MIR) into CBMC's bit-precise verification engine, automatically checking a comprehensive set of safety properties with no user annotation. To extend verification from bounded to unbounded, Kani provides a specification language comprising function contracts, loop contracts, quantifiers, and function stubbing. We demonstrate feasibility through case studies on industrial Rust projects, where contracts upgraded verification from panic-freedom to functional correctness, uncovering six previously unknown bugs. Kani operates at scale in production CI, with over 16,000 harnesses verified per code change in the Rust standard library verification campaign.","az":"Rust 的所有权类型系统能在安全代码中防止内存错误，但某些重要性质与编译过程正交：unsafe 操作（如裸指针解引用）的健全性、功能正确性以及运行时 panic 的缺席。我们提出 Kani，一个面向 Rust 的开源模型检查器，它把有界模型检查从单纯的找缺陷推进到为上述性质提供正确性保证。Kani 把证明桩（proof harness）从 Rust 的中间表示 MIR 编译到 CBMC 的位精确验证引擎，无需用户注解即可自动检查一整套安全性质。为把验证从有界扩展到无界，Kani 提供了一套规约语言，包括函数契约、循环契约、量词与函数桩化。我们通过对工业级 Rust 项目的案例研究展示了可行性：契约把验证从无 panic 提升到功能正确性，并发现了六个此前未知的缺陷。Kani 已在生产 CI 中规模化运行，在 Rust 标准库验证行动中每次代码变更都要验证超过 16,000 个证明桩。","tl":"Kani 用契约把 Rust 有界检查升级为无界功能正确性保证","au":["Bram Pellen","María Belén Rodríguez","Frits Vaandrager","Petra van den Bos"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Rust verification","bounded model checking","Kani","function contracts","CBMC"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/17/x"},{"id":"p01037","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Scalable Rule-Based Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for the Next Release Problem","tz":"面向下一版本发布问题的可扩展规则驱动深度强化学习框架","a":"Next-release planning and feature selection remain critical challenges in the software deployment cycle, especially with the rapid introduction of updates and AI-driven functionalities. Selecting a subset of high-impact features that balances customer satisfaction with stakeholder business goals requires scalable models capable of producing near real-time predictions from requirements descriptions. However, uncertainty about which features truly align with customer needs makes this task difficult. This paper proposes a scalable feature prioritization framework that leverages rules derived from feature perplexity, probabilistic relevance, and customer-oriented criteria. We introduce a dual deep-reinforcement learning (DDRL) architecture that recommends high-value requirements through a hierarchical strategy. The first level applies graph reinforcement learning (GRL) guided by rule-based reasoning to structure tasks and reduce search space, while the second level uses deep reinforcement learning (DRL) to refine predictions. Experimental results on Zoom, Webex, and Teams datasets show that the approach maintains linear complexity ($O(m)$) compared to the cubic complexity ($O(m^3)$) of traditional graph-based methods, where $m$ is the number of edges. The model achieves up to 85.56% accuracy and superior decision quality (false negatives at just 11.28%), outperforming GraphRL, REST, and NSGA-II in stakeholder-driven next-release planning.","az":"下一版本规划与特性选择仍是软件交付周期中的关键挑战，尤其在更新与 AI 驱动功能快速引入的背景下。要选出既能平衡客户满意度又能兼顾利益相关者商业目标的高价值特性子集，需要能够从需求描述中近实时给出预测的可扩展模型。然而，哪些特性真正契合客户需求存在不确定性，使该任务变得困难。本文提出一个可扩展的特性优先级排序框架，利用由特性困惑度、概率相关性与面向客户的准则导出的规则。我们引入一种双层深度强化学习（DDRL）架构，通过分层策略推荐高价值需求：第一层应用由规则推理引导的图强化学习（GRL）来组织任务并缩小搜索空间，第二层使用深度强化学习（DRL）细化预测。在 Zoom、Webex 与 Teams 数据集上的实验表明，该方法保持线性复杂度 O(m)，而传统基于图的方法为立方复杂度 O(m^3)，其中 m 为边数。模型准确率最高达 85.56%，决策质量更优（假阴性仅 11.28%），在以利益相关者为导向的下一版本规划上优于 GraphRL、REST 与 NSGA-II。","tl":"规则引导的双层深度强化学习把发布规划降到线性复杂度","au":["Hemanth Gudaparthi","Nan Niu","Prem Swaroopaanda Ramalingam","Laxman Chowdary Kakara"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["next release problem","requirements prioritization","deep reinforcement learning","graph reinforcement learning","feature selection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/18/x"},{"id":"p01038","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DynCA: An Effective Algorithm for 3-Wise Combinatorial Interaction Testing in Highly Configurable Systems","tz":"DynCA：面向高可配置系统 3-维组合交互测试的高效算法","a":"This release is for artifact evaluation. Changes:1. To dispel the reviewers' concerns, we moved artifacts/README.md into README.md in repository's root.2. We updated README.md to emphasize that Docker builds and CMake configuration require a network connection.3. We fixed the misspelling in artifacts/representative.txt.4. We updated REQUIREMENTS.md to clarify the 512 GB main memory is required by only a very small number of large instances.","az":"本次发布用于制品评审。变更如下：1. 为打消评审人的顾虑，我们把 artifacts/README.md 移动到了仓库根目录下的 README.md。2. 我们更新了 README.md，强调 Docker 构建与 CMake 配置需要网络连接。3. 我们修正了 artifacts/representative.txt 中的拼写错误。4. 我们更新了 REQUIREMENTS.md，澄清 512 GB 主内存仅极少数大型实例才需要。","tl":"新算法高效构造高可配置系统的 3-维覆盖数组","au":["Ruizhi Shi","Shuangyu Lyu","Renyu Yang","Wei Wu","Chanjuan Liu","Chunming Hu","Chuan Luo"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["combinatorial interaction testing","covering array","configurable systems","3-wise coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/19/x"},{"id":"p01039","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Effective and Efficient Context Retrieval via Partial Dependency Graph for Repository-Level Code Generation","tz":"面向仓库级代码生成的部分依赖图高效上下文检索","a":"Repository-level code translation is critical for modernizing legacy systems, yet existing approaches based on large language models (LLMs) operate at the file level and fail to scale to codebases with complex inter-file dependencies. This limitation is evident in our industrial setting, where we aim to migrate a production repository (STAR) from Java to Kotlin, but file-level approaches produce fragmented results and fail to achieve end-to-end correctness. In this paper, we show that the primary cause of failure at the repository level is dependency inconsistency. Through an empirical study on open-source and industrial systems, we find that most errors arise from unresolved cross-file dependencies that cannot be effectively addressed by iterative feedback alone. We propose a dependency-aware incremental migration framework that elevates the unit of translation from individual files to dependency-consistent batches. Our approach constructs a dependency graph, groups interdependent files, and performs batched translation with iterative compile- and test-driven validation. We evaluate our method on a 51K line of code (LOC) industrial system and multiple repositories across interoperable language pairs (Java-Kotlin, Java-Scala, and C#-F#). On the STAR repository, file-level approaches achieve 38.16% compilation and 9.39% test success, whereas our approach achieves 100% compilation and test success across the evaluated settings, converging within a small number of iterations. These results show that dependency-aware batching improves scalability and reliability in repository-level code translation.","az":"仓库级代码翻译对遗留系统现代化至关重要，然而基于大语言模型（LLM）的现有方法都在文件级别操作，无法扩展到具有复杂跨文件依赖的代码库。这一局限在我们的工业场景中尤为明显：我们希望把一个生产仓库（STAR）从 Java 迁移到 Kotlin，而文件级方法产出的结果支离破碎，无法实现端到端的正确性。本文表明，仓库级失败的首要原因是依赖不一致。通过对开源与工业系统的实证研究，我们发现大多数错误源于未解析的跨文件依赖，仅靠迭代反馈无法有效解决。我们提出一个依赖感知的增量迁移框架，把翻译单元从单个文件提升为依赖一致的批次。该方法构建依赖图、把相互依赖的文件分组，并在编译与测试驱动的迭代验证下执行批量翻译。我们在一个 5.1 万行代码（LOC）的工业系统以及多个可互操作语言对（Java-Kotlin、Java-Scala、C#-F#）的仓库上评估该方法。在 STAR 仓库上，文件级方法的编译成功率为 38.16%、测试成功率为 9.39%，而我们的方法在所有评估设置下都达到 100% 的编译与测试成功率，并在少量迭代内收敛。这些结果表明，依赖感知的批量化提升了仓库级代码翻译的可扩展性与可靠性。","tl":"按依赖图分批翻译，使仓库级迁移编译与测试全通过","au":["Zhongxin Liu","Zhonghao Jiang","Zhifan Ye","Haoye Wang","Jiakun Liu","Xiaoxue Ren"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["repository-level code translation","dependency graph","Java to Kotlin","incremental migration","legacy modernization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/20/x"},{"id":"p01040","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Ambiguity Meets Atypicality: Dual-Perspective Test Input Prioritization for DNNs","tz":"当模糊性遇上非典型性：面向 DNN 的双视角测试输入优先级排序","a":"While Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) have achieved remarkable progress in cutting-edge domains, their inherent brittleness has become a growing concern. To ensure the reliability and safety of DNN-enabled software, DNN testing has emerged as an indispensable practice. Within this context, test input prioritization is essential for early fault detection and reducing labeling costs. However, it remains challenging to accurately identify failure-inducing inputs. Although decision ambiguity and distributional atypicality are two widely adopted perspectives for characterizing inter-class competition and intra-class typicality respectively, relying on either perspective in isolation inevitably introduces blind spots. In this paper, we propose DuFP (Dual perspective Feature space Prioritization), a KNN density-based test input prioritization approach for DNNs that jointly incorporates both inter-class and intra-class perspectives. The prioritization framework of DuFP is built upon class-conditional density estimation. Based on the estimation results, prediction correctness is characterized by an ambiguity score and an atypicality score, with the former reflecting decision ambiguity and the latter quantifying distributional atypicality. A hybrid uncertainty score is then constructed by integrating both scores to guide the final prioritization. We evaluate DuFP on prioritization and selection tasks across image and text datasets under clean, corrupted, and adversarial scenarios. Experimental results demonstrate that DuFP effectively and efficiently prioritizes fault-inducing inputs and outperforms state-of-the-art approaches.","az":"尽管深度神经网络（DNN）在前沿领域取得了显著进展，其固有的脆弱性也日益令人担忧。为保证 DNN 驱动软件的可靠性与安全性，DNN 测试已成为不可或缺的实践。在此背景下，测试输入优先级排序对于尽早发现缺陷、降低标注成本至关重要。然而，准确识别会诱发失败的输入仍然困难。决策模糊性与分布非典型性分别是刻画类间竞争与类内典型性的两个被广泛采用的视角，但孤立地依赖其中任一视角都不可避免地带来盲区。本文提出 DuFP（双视角特征空间优先级排序），一种基于 KNN 密度、同时融合类间与类内视角的 DNN 测试输入优先级排序方法。DuFP 的优先级框架建立在类条件密度估计之上。基于估计结果，预测正确性由一个模糊性分数与一个非典型性分数共同刻画，前者反映决策模糊性，后者量化分布非典型性。随后通过整合两个分数构造混合不确定性分数，以指导最终排序。我们在图像与文本数据集上、在干净、受扰与对抗三种场景下评估 DuFP 的排序与选择任务。实验结果表明，DuFP 能够有效且高效地优先选出诱发缺陷的输入，并优于当前最先进的方法。","tl":"融合类间模糊性与类内非典型性提升 DNN 测试输入排序","au":["Haoran Li","Shihai Wang","Bin Liu","Jialuo Chen","Wenjing Zhu","Yu Liu","Tengfei Shi","Shudi Guo"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["test input prioritization","DNN testing","density estimation","uncertainty","labeling cost"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/21/x"},{"id":"p01041","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Not In My Git Yard: Catching Backdoors at Commit and Release Time","tz":"不许进我的 Git 院子：在提交与发布时刻拦截后门","a":"Code-level backdoors—stealthy code changes that grant hidden privileges via secret triggers—pose a persistent threat to open-source software. Known attempts to inject such backdoors into widely used projects through malicious commits, tampered release packages, or compromised third-party dependencies, were stopped only by luck and manual review. Existing Continuous Integration (CI) pipelines cannot detect these attacks, and downstream binary analysis tools require substantial manual effort. In this work, we present Lily, an automated approach that strengthens open-source development and release processes against backdoor injection. Lily integrates a backdoor detection mechanism into (1) CI pipelines to block malicious commits, and (2) release vetting workflows to prevent tampered releases or compromised dependencies from entering large ecosystems, such as Linux distributions. Lily offers two key contributions. First, it enhances CI-compatible fuzzing with the capability to detect triggers of suspicious behavior based on historical and current software executions. This enables fast, precise backdoor detection suitable for both CI and update validation workflows. Second, it combines code change analysis with fuzzing data to precisely point maintainers to backdoor-revealing code regions, even when release updates modify millions of lines of code. We also outline five strategies attackers could use to evade Lily, and evaluate corresponding defenses. Our experiments across hundreds of benign and backdoored commits and releases show that Lily achieves high detection accuracy with low false alarm rates, reliably identifies malicious code, resists adversarial attempts, and would have prevented real-world backdoor incidents.","az":"代码级后门——通过秘密触发条件授予隐藏权限的隐蔽代码改动——对开源软件构成持续威胁。已知的通过恶意提交、被篡改的发布包或被攻陷的第三方依赖向广泛使用的项目注入此类后门的尝试，都只是靠运气和人工评审才被阻止。现有的持续集成（CI）流水线无法检测这类攻击，而下游的二进制分析工具又需要大量人工投入。本文提出 Lily，一种自动化方法，用以强化开源开发与发布流程对后门注入的抵抗力。Lily 把后门检测机制集成到 (1) CI 流水线中以拦截恶意提交，以及 (2) 发布审查流程中，以防止被篡改的发布或被攻陷的依赖进入 Linux 发行版等大型生态。Lily 有两项关键贡献。第一，它增强了与 CI 兼容的模糊测试，使其能够基于历史与当前的软件执行来检测可疑行为的触发条件，从而实现快速、精确、适用于 CI 与更新验证流程的后门检测。第二，它把代码变更分析与模糊测试数据结合起来，即使发布更新改动了数百万行代码，也能精确地把维护者指向暴露后门的代码区域。我们还概述了攻击者可能用来规避 Lily 的五种策略，并评估了相应的防御。我们在数百个良性与含后门的提交和发布上的实验表明，Lily 达到了高检测准确率与低误报率，能可靠识别恶意代码、抵抗对抗性尝试，并且本可以阻止现实世界中发生过的后门事件。","tl":"把变更分析与 CI 模糊测试结合，在提交与发布期抓后门","au":["Dimitri Kokkonis","Michaël Marcozzi","Stefano Zacchiroli"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["code backdoor detection","CI pipeline","fuzzing","release vetting","open-source supply chain"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/22/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3834352"},{"id":"p01042","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"EffiHolmes: Differential Profiling-Guided Repository Level Time Inefficiency Fix Localization","tz":"EffiHolmes：差分性能剖析引导的仓库级耗时低效修复点定位","a":"Large software systems often suffer from time inefficiencies that cause excessive execution time despite functional correctness. Localizing their fix locations is difficult because, unlike functional bugs, they produce neither test failures nor stack-trace clues, making traditional and recent LLM-based fault localization methods unsuitable. Runtime profiling provides alternative evidence but faces three challenges in repository-level settings: single-run profiling cannot reliably distinguish inefficiency hotspots from execution noise; existing profilers struggle to extract relevant execution paths from extensive background execution; and a semantic gap remains between observed hotspots and actual fix locations. We propose EffiHolmes, an LLM-based framework for repository-level time inefficiency fix localization. EffiHolmes uses differential profiling under default and scaled workloads to identify inefficiency hotspots, extracts compact execution paths connecting these hotspots to the reported inefficient function, and employs domain-guided LLM reasoning to locate the underlying inefficiency logic. We also introduce RepoEffi-Bench, the first benchmark for repository-level inefficiency localization, containing 140 high-quality issues collected from popular Python repositories. Experiments show that EffiHolmes consistently outperforms state-of-the-art retrieval-, agent-, and profiling-based baselines, improving file-level Acc@3 by 4.29 percentage points with GPT-5.1 and function-level Acc@5 by 15.00 percentage points with qwen3-4b. It also remains robust across model capacities.","az":"大型软件系统常常存在时间上的低效问题：功能虽然正确，执行时间却过长。定位其修复位置十分困难，因为与功能性缺陷不同，它们既不产生测试失败，也没有栈轨迹线索，使传统方法和近期基于 LLM 的缺陷定位方法都不适用。运行时性能剖析提供了另一种证据，但在仓库级场景下面临三个挑战：单次剖析无法可靠地把低效热点与执行噪声区分开；现有剖析器难以从大量背景执行中抽取相关执行路径；观察到的热点与真正的修复位置之间仍存在语义鸿沟。我们提出 EffiHolmes，一个基于 LLM 的仓库级耗时低效修复点定位框架。EffiHolmes 在默认负载与放大负载下进行差分剖析以识别低效热点，抽取连接这些热点与所报告低效函数的紧凑执行路径，并利用领域引导的 LLM 推理定位底层的低效逻辑。我们还提出 RepoEffi-Bench，这是首个面向仓库级低效定位的基准，包含从流行 Python 仓库收集的 140 个高质量 issue。实验表明，EffiHolmes 始终优于最先进的基于检索、基于智能体与基于剖析的基线：在 GPT-5.1 上文件级 Acc@3 提升 4.29 个百分点，在 qwen3-4b 上函数级 Acc@5 提升 15.00 个百分点，并且在不同模型能力下都保持稳健。","tl":"差分剖析加 LLM 推理定位仓库级性能低效的修复点","au":["Haowen Yang","Yun Peng","Zishuo Ding"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["performance inefficiency","fix localization","differential profiling","LLM reasoning","RepoEffi-Bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/23/x"},{"id":"p01043","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Maximal Format-Free Data Repair","tz":"极大化的无格式数据修复","tl":"（据标题推断）无需格式规约即可极大化修复受损结构化数据","au":["Zijian Luo","Xi Wu","Hong Jin Kang","Alan Fekete","Rahul Gopinath"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["data repair","format-free","structured input","grammar inference"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/24/x"},{"id":"p01044","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AgentExecutor: Partial Code Execution via Agentic Context Generation","tz":"AgentExecutor：通过智能体式上下文生成实现部分代码执行","a":"Executing code snippets is essential for dynamic program analysis, but it remains challenging to execute an arbitrary code snippet due to issues like missing context and incomplete dependencies. Existing approaches to partial code execution, such as LExecutor and Treefix, leverage the power of language models to infer missing information and enable execution. However, they suffer from (i) limited action spaces and feedback, and (ii) rigid optimization strategies, which restrict their effectiveness and efficiency. In this paper, we propose AgentExecutor, a novel multi-agent framework for partial code execution. Our approach introduces a three-phase design: execution environment preparation, dynamic exploration with iterative refinement, and prefix evolution via program synthesis. Supported by the power of LLM agents who can think, act, and get feedback iteratively, AgentExecutor is able to autonomously explore a richer action space, enabling diverse operations such as creating resource files and resolving environment configuration. Furthermore, it adopts adaptive optimization strategies, including coverage-guided context pruning and prefix evolution via program synthesis, to systematically improve the execution quality of partial code. We evaluate AgentExecutor on two widely used datasets comprising Stack Overflow snippets and open-source project code. The results show that AgentExecutor achieves up to 94% and 90% code coverage, outperforming the state-of-the-art approach Treefix by 19.9% and 13.8%, respectively. In addition, AgentExecutor significantly reduces execution time (by up to 80.3%) and cost (by up to 56.6%). These findings demonstrate that AgentExecutor provides an effective and efficient solution for partial code execution.","az":"执行代码片段是动态程序分析的基础，但由于上下文缺失、依赖不完整等问题，执行任意代码片段仍然困难。已有的部分代码执行方法（如 LExecutor 与 Treefix）利用语言模型的能力推断缺失信息以支持执行。然而它们存在两方面不足：(i) 动作空间与反馈有限；(ii) 优化策略僵化，限制了其有效性与效率。本文提出 AgentExecutor，一种用于部分代码执行的新型多智能体框架。我们的方法采用三阶段设计：执行环境准备、带迭代精化的动态探索，以及通过程序合成实现的前缀演化。借助能够迭代地思考、行动并获取反馈的 LLM 智能体，AgentExecutor 能够自主探索更丰富的动作空间，支持创建资源文件、解决环境配置等多样操作。此外，它采用自适应优化策略，包括覆盖率引导的上下文剪枝与通过程序合成实现的前缀演化，以系统性地提升部分代码的执行质量。我们在两个广泛使用的数据集（Stack Overflow 代码片段与开源项目代码）上评估 AgentExecutor。结果显示，AgentExecutor 分别达到最高 94% 与 90% 的代码覆盖率，比最先进方法 Treefix 分别高出 19.9% 与 13.8%。此外，AgentExecutor 显著降低了执行时间（最多减少 80.3%）与成本（最多减少 56.6%）。这些发现表明，AgentExecutor 为部分代码执行提供了有效且高效的解决方案。","tl":"多智能体自主补齐环境与上下文，让任意代码片段跑起来","au":["Junkai Chen","Chengran Yang","Xing Hu","Zhenhao Li","Xin Xia","David Lo"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["partial code execution","multi-agent framework","dynamic analysis","context generation","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/25/x"},{"id":"p01045","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automated Lemma Discovery in Agentic Program Verification","tz":"智能体式程序验证中的自动引理发现","a":"Deductive verification provides strong correctness guarantees for code by extracting verification conditions (VCs) and writing formal proofs for them. The expertise-intensive task of VC proving is the main bottleneck in this process, and has been partly automated owing to recent advances in Large Language Model (LLM) agents. However, existing proof agents are not able to discover helper lemmas – auxiliary lemmas that aid in proving – and thus fall short as programs grow in size and complexity. In this paper, we argue that VC proving for program verification is more than a purely mathematical task, and benefits considerably from program comprehension. Our key insight is that human proof engineers often discover and apply helper lemmas based on their understanding of the program semantics, which are not directly reflected in the VCs produced by VC generators. Inspired by this insight, we propose an LLM agent, LemmaNet, that discovers helper lemmas in two ways. Specifically, the agent first synthesizes lemmas offline by directly analyzing the source code and specifications and then relating this semantic understanding to the mechanical, verbose encoding produced by VC generators. As the proof unfolds, LemmaNet then adapts existing helper lemmas online to accommodate evolving proof states, enabling the agent to effectively discharge complex VCs on-the-fly. We implement LemmaNet on top of an existing proof agent AutoRocq for Rocq and the Frama-C ecosystem, and evaluate it on SV-COMP and established real-world subjects, including modules of the Linux kernel, Contiki OS, standard C++ library, and X.509 parser. Our experimental results demonstrate that LemmaNet significantly outperforms state-of-the-art approaches, highlighting the importance of program comprehension-aided lemma discovery in agentic program verification.","az":"演绎验证通过抽取验证条件（VC）并为其撰写形式化证明，为代码提供强正确性保证。VC 证明这一高度依赖专业知识的任务是该流程的主要瓶颈，近期大语言模型（LLM）智能体的进展已部分实现了其自动化。然而，现有的证明智能体无法发现辅助引理（helper lemma）——即有助于完成证明的附加引理，因此随着程序规模与复杂度增长便力不从心。本文主张，程序验证中的 VC 证明不只是纯数学任务，它能从程序理解中获益良多。我们的关键洞见是：人类证明工程师往往基于对程序语义的理解来发现并应用辅助引理，而这些语义并未直接体现在 VC 生成器产出的 VC 中。受此启发，我们提出 LLM 智能体 LemmaNet，它以两种方式发现辅助引理。具体而言，该智能体首先通过直接分析源码与规约来离线合成引理，并把这种语义理解与 VC 生成器产出的机械、冗长的编码关联起来；随着证明推进，LemmaNet 再在线地调整已有辅助引理以适应不断演化的证明状态，从而使智能体能够即时有效地消解复杂的 VC。我们在已有的证明智能体 AutoRocq（面向 Rocq 与 Frama-C 生态）之上实现了 LemmaNet，并在 SV-COMP 以及 Linux 内核模块、Contiki OS、C++ 标准库和 X.509 解析器等成熟的真实对象上进行评估。实验结果表明，LemmaNet 显著优于最先进方法，凸显了在智能体式程序验证中借助程序理解发现引理的重要性。","tl":"让证明智能体借程序语义离线加在线地发现辅助引理","au":["Huan Zhao","Haoxin Tu","Zhengyao Liu","Martin C. Rinard","Abhik Roychoudhury"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["deductive verification","helper lemma discovery","LLM agent","verification conditions","Frama-C"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/26/x"},{"id":"p01046","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Regression Accumulation in Multi-turn LLM Programming Conversations","tz":"多轮 LLM 编程对话中的回归累积","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench's macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施主要用 C 编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全，研究者正在探索把 C 自动翻译到 Rust 等更安全的语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不只包含 C 代码，还经常使用名为宏（macro）的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。最先进的技术通过先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译来回避宏的翻译。但这种做法产生的译文与原始 C 代码相去甚远，因为预处理会把所有宏定义内联展开。为了在译文中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并将其提炼为首个形式化定义的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们引入首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机采样的宏。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估大语言模型（LLM）在此前未被研究的宏翻译任务上的效果。LLM 翻译成功的 MacroBench 用例比 MerC 多 22% 到 77%，但其中有 8% 到 28% 的译文是错误的，需要开发者额外验证；相比之下，MerC 只产出正确译文。我们的关键洞见是：先运行 MerC、再对剩余部分使用 LLM，比单独使用任一技术收益更大。这种“双打”方法的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时比 MerC 平均多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"形式化宏翻译器与 LLM 组合，兼顾正确率与覆盖面","au":["Andie Huang","Lin Ma","Amjed Tahir","Qian Zhang","Liwen Xiao","Lysa Xiao"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["C to Rust translation","macro translation","MacroBench","formally-specified translator","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/27/x"},{"id":"p01047","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TheBotCompany: Self-Organizing Multi-agent Systems for Continuous Software Development","tz":"TheBotCompany：面向持续软件开发的自组织多智能体系统","a":"Large language model (LLM)-based multi-agent systems have shown promise in automating software development tasks. However, most vibe-coding systems focus on completing small tasks and incremental code changes, leaving persistent, continuous software development largely unexplored. We present TheBotCompany, an open-source orchestration framework for continuous multi-agent software development. TheBotCompany introduces three key innovations: (1) a three-phase state machine (Strategy to Execution to Verification) for milestone-driven development, (2) self-organizing agent teams where manager agents dynamically hire, assign, and retire worker agents based on project needs, and (3) asynchronous human oversight. We evaluate TheBotCompany on real-world software projects over multiple days of continuous development, measuring team adaptation patterns, milestone completion rates, cost efficiency, and code quality. Our results demonstrate that the self-organizing approach enables effective long-term software development with measurable progress, while the verification phase catches defects that would otherwise persist.","az":"基于大语言模型（LLM）的多智能体系统已展现出自动化软件开发任务的潜力。然而，大多数 vibe-coding 系统聚焦于完成小任务和增量式代码改动，持久、连续的软件开发在很大程度上仍未被探索。我们提出 TheBotCompany，一个面向持续多智能体软件开发的开源编排框架。TheBotCompany 引入三项关键创新：(1) 用于里程碑驱动开发的三阶段状态机（策略→执行→验证）；(2) 自组织的智能体团队，其中管理者智能体根据项目需要动态地雇佣、分派和裁撤工作者智能体；(3) 异步的人类监督。我们在真实软件项目上、历经多日的连续开发中评估 TheBotCompany，测量团队适应模式、里程碑完成率、成本效率与代码质量。结果表明，自组织方法能够以可度量的进展支撑有效的长期软件开发，同时验证阶段可捕获那些否则会长期遗留的缺陷。","tl":"管理者智能体动态雇佣裁撤，支撑跨日持续软件开发","au":["Wenhan Lyu","Yue Xiao","Yixuan Zhang","Yifan Sun"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["multi-agent system","continuous software development","self-organizing agents","milestone-driven","human oversight"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/28/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.25928"},{"id":"p01048","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Comments Mislead: An Empirical Study of Outdated Comments in LLM-Based Code Completion","tz":"当注释产生误导：LLM 代码补全中过时注释的实证研究","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench's macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施主要用 C 编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全，研究者正在探索把 C 自动翻译到 Rust 等更安全的语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不只包含 C 代码，还经常使用名为宏（macro）的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。最先进的技术通过先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译来回避宏的翻译。但这种做法产生的译文与原始 C 代码相去甚远，因为预处理会把所有宏定义内联展开。为了在译文中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并将其提炼为首个形式化定义的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们引入首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机采样的宏。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估大语言模型（LLM）在此前未被研究的宏翻译任务上的效果。LLM 翻译成功的 MacroBench 用例比 MerC 多 22% 到 77%，但其中有 8% 到 28% 的译文是错误的，需要开发者额外验证；相比之下，MerC 只产出正确译文。我们的关键洞见是：先运行 MerC、再对剩余部分使用 LLM，比单独使用任一技术收益更大。这种“双打”方法的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时比 MerC 平均多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"（摘要为宏翻译）形式化翻译器先行、LLM 兜底效果最佳","au":["Zhikun Xia","Yuan Huang","Xiangping Chen","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["macro translation","C to Rust","MacroBench","MerC","LLM translation errors"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/29/x"},{"id":"p01049","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Property-Based Testing of Wafer Handling Robots via Model-Based Planning and Fuzzing","tz":"通过基于模型的规划与模糊测试对晶圆搬运机器人做基于性质的测试","a":"Wafer handling robots (WHRs) in semiconductor manufacturing require ultra-precise control software, where bugs can cause severe mechanical damage and costly downtime, making reliability validation critical. Yet no existing work addresses WHR validation. In this experience paper, we introduce a property-based testing approach for WHRs. Our key observation is that the system requirements of WHRs could be used as the properties for bug detection.However, applying property-based testing to WHR systems is challenging due to the input generation challenge. Complex action dependencies make it difficult to generate valid test inputs, while enormous state spaces hinder achieving adequate test coverage. To address this, we propose model-based planning and fuzzing. Our insight is that the WHR can be represented as a state-based model. Based on this model, we systematically generate valid test inputs through backward planning, then explore diverse scenarios through parameter and environment mutation. We implemented our approach as the ArmGo tool and evaluated it on a production WHR deployed in industrial lithography equipment. ArmGo discovered 21 previously unknown bugs (all confirmed, 15 fixed), including axis limit violations, entanglement issues, and missing interlock checks. ArmGo has been deployed in the continuous integration (CI) pipeline of our industrial partner and is actively used for validating WHRs. We also have distilled a number of practical lessons learned based on our investigation.","az":"半导体制造中的晶圆搬运机器人（WHR）需要超精密的控制软件，其缺陷可能造成严重的机械损坏与高昂停机成本，因此可靠性验证至关重要。然而目前尚无工作研究 WHR 的验证。在这篇经验论文中，我们提出一种面向 WHR 的基于性质的测试方法。我们的关键观察是：WHR 的系统需求可以直接用作检测缺陷的性质。然而，把基于性质的测试应用于 WHR 系统面临输入生成的挑战：复杂的动作依赖使生成合法测试输入十分困难，而巨大的状态空间又阻碍达到充分的测试覆盖。为此，我们提出基于模型的规划与模糊测试。我们的洞见是 WHR 可以表示为一个基于状态的模型。基于该模型，我们通过反向规划系统性地生成合法测试输入，然后通过参数与环境变异探索多样的场景。我们把该方法实现为 ArmGo 工具，并在部署于工业光刻设备中的一台量产 WHR 上进行评估。ArmGo 发现了 21 个此前未知的缺陷（全部确认，15 个已修复），包括轴限位越界、缠绕问题与缺失的互锁检查。ArmGo 已部署到我们工业合作伙伴的持续集成（CI）流水线中，并被持续用于验证 WHR。我们还基于本次调查提炼出若干实用经验教训。","tl":"把机器人需求当性质，用反向规划生成合法输入查出 21 个缺陷","au":["Ruiyang Xu","Jingjing Liang","Guoyue Zheng","Geguang Pu","Ting Su"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["property-based testing","wafer handling robot","model-based planning","fuzzing","industrial deployment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/30/x"},{"id":"p01050","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ATLAS: Agentic Taxonomy of LArge-Scale Software Ecosystems","tz":"ATLAS：大规模软件生态的智能体式分类体系","a":"The open-source ecosystem on GitHub lacks a systematic hierarchical taxonomy of software repositories. GitHub Topics, the dominant organizational mechanism, is flat, inconsistent, and covers only 67% of projects. We present ATLAS, the first framework that automatically constructs a hierarchical taxonomy for software repositories and classifies projects into it end-to-end. By combining LLM global knowledge with real repository distributions, ATLAS proposes meaningful splitting dimensions and iteratively corrects those that fail to accommodate real projects. A Designer Agent proposes splitting dimensions while a Classifier Agent assigns repositories; a self-corrective refinement loop uses classification failures to drive dimension revision through escalating strategies. We evaluate ATLAS on 54,387 GitHub repositories against six baselines spanning four paradigms, two downstream tasks, and three model families. On a stratified 2,001-repository benchmark, ATLAS achieves a Taxonomy Quality F-score (TQF) of 83.13%, outperforming the best baseline by 15 percentage points (on the full 54k corpus the approximate TQF is 73.0%, a gap driven by Path Granularity's all-or-nothing scoring on longer paths rather than lower classification accuracy). It is the only method to simultaneously achieve high structural quality and high practical applicability. On downstream tasks, ATLAS enables alternative discovery with P@1 = 85.71%, surpassing even human-curated lists (62.34%), and achieves the highest P@1 for repository retrieval. The taxonomy further reveals structural ecosystem trends that are difficult to obtain from flat tags or similarity methods: the shift from libraries to AI/ML applications (now 61% of newly community-adopted projects) becomes visible only through hierarchical, type-based categorization. An interactive taxonomy explorer is available at https://atlas-taxonomy.netlify.app/","az":"GitHub 上的开源生态缺乏一个系统化的软件仓库层次分类体系。作为主导的组织机制，GitHub Topics 是扁平的、不一致的，且只覆盖了 67% 的项目。我们提出 ATLAS，首个自动为软件仓库构建层次分类体系并端到端地把项目归类其中的框架。通过把 LLM 的全局知识与真实仓库分布相结合，ATLAS 能提出有意义的划分维度，并对那些无法容纳真实项目的维度进行迭代纠正。设计者智能体（Designer Agent）提出划分维度，分类者智能体（Classifier Agent）分配仓库；自纠正的精化回路利用分类失败，通过逐级升级的策略驱动维度修订。我们在 54,387 个 GitHub 仓库上，针对涵盖四种范式的六个基线、两个下游任务与三个模型家族评估 ATLAS。在一个分层抽样的 2,001 个仓库基准上，ATLAS 的分类体系质量 F 分数（TQF）达到 83.13%，比最佳基线高出 15 个百分点（在完整的 5.4 万语料上近似 TQF 为 73.0%，这一差距源于路径粒度在较长路径上的全有或全无式打分，而非分类准确率下降）。它是唯一同时实现高结构质量与高实用性的方法。在下游任务上，ATLAS 支持的替代品发现取得 P@1 = 85.71%，甚至超过人工整理的清单（62.34%），并在仓库检索上取得最高的 P@1。该分类体系还揭示出用扁平标签或相似度方法难以获得的生态结构趋势：从库向 AI/ML 应用的迁移（现已占新获社区采纳项目的 61%）只有通过层次化、基于类型的分类才能显现。交互式分类体系浏览器见 https://atlas-taxonomy.netlify.app/","tl":"双智能体自纠正地自动构建 GitHub 仓库层次分类体系","au":["Junyi Lu","Mengyao Lyu","Wu Jiahui","Lei Yu","Chengwei Liu","Fengjun Zhang","Li Yang","Chun Zuo","Yang Liu"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["software repository taxonomy","LLM agents","GitHub ecosystem","hierarchical classification","repository retrieval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/31/x"},{"id":"p01051","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SimServing: Native-Execution Simulation for Evolution-Resilient LLM Serving Configuration Tuning","tz":"SimServing：面向演化鲁棒的 LLM 服务配置调优的原生执行仿真","a":"The artifact (https://figshare.com/s/53f5b0a509a83bb9a677) contains the SimServing source code, experiment scripts, plotting scripts, and the data needed to reproduce the reported results, including the instrumentation patches for vLLM and MindIE.","az":"该制品（https://figshare.com/s/53f5b0a509a83bb9a677）包含 SimServing 源代码、实验脚本、绘图脚本，以及复现论文所报告结果所需的数据，其中还包括针对 vLLM 和 MindIE 的插桩补丁。","tl":"用原生执行仿真替代真实压测来调优 LLM 服务配置，并抗版本演化。","au":["Yujie Huang","Jiazhen Gu","Zhihan Jiang","Michael Lyu"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["LLM serving","configuration tuning","native-execution simulation","vLLM","MindIE"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/32/x"},{"id":"p01052","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LLM Agents Can See Code Repositories","tz":"LLM 智能体能够“看懂”代码仓库","a":"Production deployment of AI coding agents requires fast, reproducible evaluation signals. Existing industrial practices trade off speed and fidelity: online A/B testing takes weeks and risks user experience, shadow deployment yields signals that are not reproducible across runs, and public benchmarks diverge from production workloads in language distribution, prompt style, and codebase structure. This paper presents REAP (Relevance and Execution-Audited Pipeline), an automated curation pipeline that constructs production-derived benchmarks from real developer-agent sessions without manual labeling. Such curation, while in-distribution to production usage, runs into several challenges. Untestable prompts, misaligned tests, and test flakiness all compromise evaluation reliability. While tasks can be manually audited to ensure only high-quality tasks remain in the benchmark, this approach is infeasible in the monorepo setting: the build infrastructure state is often ephemeral in large monorepos and requires the benchmark to be continuously re-curated against the current codebase. As manual verification cannot be sustained at this cadence, REAP adds an automated verification layer using LLM-based task classification, agentic test-relevance validation, and multi-run stability checks to ensure the executable benchmark yields trustworthy signals. We use REAP to curate Harvest, a benchmark where each task feeds the coding agent a real developer prompt and verifies the resulting code change against fail-to-pass tests retrieved from production. Harvest's distribution spans more than four programming languages with a majority of tasks drawn from Hack. Model and harness evaluations reveal that solve rates range from 42.9% to 58.2% across five frontier models, surfacing capability differences that inform concrete deployment decisions.","az":"在生产环境中部署 AI 编程智能体需要快速、可复现的评测信号。现有工业实践在速度与保真度之间存在取舍：在线 A/B 测试耗时数周且有损害用户体验的风险，影子部署得到的信号在多次运行之间不可复现，而公开基准在语言分布、提示风格和代码库结构上又与生产工作负载存在偏离。本文提出 REAP（Relevance and Execution-Audited Pipeline），一条自动化的数据构建流水线，可在无需人工标注的情况下，从真实的开发者—智能体会话中构建源自生产环境的基准。这样的构建虽然与生产使用同分布，却面临若干挑战：不可测试的提示、不匹配的测试以及测试不稳定性都会损害评测可靠性。虽然可以通过人工审核任务来保证基准中只保留高质量任务，但在单体仓库（monorepo）场景下这种做法不可行：大型单体仓库中的构建基础设施状态往往是短暂的，要求基准针对当前代码库持续重新构建。由于人工验证无法以这样的节奏持续进行，REAP 增加了一层自动验证机制，使用基于 LLM 的任务分类、智能体式的测试相关性验证以及多次运行的稳定性检查，以确保可执行基准产生可信的信号。我们使用 REAP 构建了 Harvest 基准：其中每个任务把一条真实的开发者提示喂给编程智能体，并用从生产环境中检索到的 fail-to-pass 测试来验证由此产生的代码改动。Harvest 的分布覆盖四种以上编程语言，其中大多数任务来自 Hack。对模型与脚手架（harness）的评测显示，五个前沿模型的解决率在 42.9% 到 58.2% 之间，揭示出可为具体部署决策提供依据的能力差异。","tl":"自动从生产会话中构建可执行的编程智能体基准 Harvest。","au":["Dongjian Ma","Silin Chen","yufeiyang","Yuling Shi","Yanfu Yan","Xiaodong Gu"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["production-derived benchmark","coding agents","fail-to-pass tests","monorepo","automated curation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/33/x"},{"id":"p01053","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Are Reasoning Traces Faithful in LLM-Based Code Vulnerability Detection?","tz":"基于 LLM 的代码漏洞检测中，推理链条是否忠实？","a":"Reasoning traces generated by large language models (LLMs) provide interpretability by exposing the factors that purportedly support their predictions. Such interpretability is important because model decisions may rely on spurious factors, and it can help practitioners identify such reliance and respond appropriately. However, the usefulness of reasoning traces hinges on their faithfulness, namely whether they reflect the factors that the model actually relies on when producing its prediction. Unfaithful traces may instead serve as plausible narratives that do not correspond to the true decision process. Despite its importance, reasoning-trace faithfulness has not been systematically studied in LLM-based vulnerability detection. We present VulFaith, the first framework for evaluating reasoning-trace faithfulness in this domain. We formalize two complementary criteria: completeness, which requires that all decision-relevant factors sustaining an insecure prediction are exposed, and per-factor faithfulness, which requires that each cited factor is genuinely relied upon by the model. To operationalize these criteria, we design an automated repair-based evaluation scheme that removes cited insecurity factors through code repairs and re-queries the model to test whether the prediction remains sustained. We implement VulFaith and conduct experiments on both repository-level and function-level vulnerability datasets, evaluating ten state-of-the-art open-source models and four commercial LLMs. Our results show that unfaithfulness is widespread, with completeness unfaithfulness reaching up to 66.14% and per-factor unfaithfulness up to 94.00%. We further validate that the unfaithfulness cases identified by VulFaith can support data augmentation for supervised fine-tuning, reducing completeness unfaithfulness by up to 47.89% and per-factor unfaithfulness by up to 59.18%.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）生成的推理轨迹通过展示据称支撑其预测的各种因素来提供可解释性。这种可解释性很重要，因为模型的决策可能依赖于虚假因素，而推理轨迹可以帮助从业者识别这种依赖并做出恰当反应。然而，推理轨迹的有用性取决于其忠实性，即它们是否真正反映了模型在产生预测时实际依赖的因素。不忠实的轨迹可能只是与真实决策过程并不对应的、看似合理的叙述。尽管这一问题很重要，推理轨迹的忠实性在基于 LLM 的漏洞检测领域尚未被系统研究。我们提出 VulFaith，这是该领域中首个评估推理轨迹忠实性的框架。我们形式化了两条互补的准则：完整性，要求所有支撑“不安全”预测的决策相关因素都被展示出来；以及逐因素忠实性，要求每一个被引用的因素确实被模型所依赖。为了将这两条准则可操作化，我们设计了一套基于修复的自动评估方案：通过代码修复移除被引用的不安全因素，再重新查询模型，测试其预测是否依然成立。我们实现了 VulFaith，并在仓库级和函数级漏洞数据集上开展实验，评估了十个最先进的开源模型和四个商用 LLM。结果表明，不忠实现象普遍存在，完整性方面的不忠实率高达 66.14%，逐因素不忠实率高达 94.00%。我们还进一步验证，VulFaith 识别出的不忠实案例可以用于支撑有监督微调的数据增强，将完整性不忠实率最多降低 47.89%，将逐因素不忠实率最多降低 59.18%。","tl":"首次用“修复后重问”方案量化漏洞检测推理链的不忠实。","au":["Wang Jialai","Juncheng Lu","Songtao Yang","Bingyi He","Zeyu Gao","Chao Zhang","Shuai Wang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"interpretability-and-model-internals","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["reasoning trace faithfulness","vulnerability detection","LLM interpretability","repair-based evaluation","supervised fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/34/x"},{"id":"p01054","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CtxFuzz: Context-Aware Directed Fuzzing via Runtime Fuzzer-Agent Cooperation","tz":"CtxFuzz：通过运行时 fuzzer 与智能体协作实现上下文感知的定向模糊测试","tl":"（据标题推断）让 LLM 智能体在运行时与 fuzzer 协作提供上下文以引导定向模糊测试。","au":["Jiho Kim","Dongkwan Kim","HyungSeok Han","Youngjoon Kim","Soyeon Park","Sangwoo Ji","Joshua Wang","Dae R. Jeong","Taesoo Kim"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["directed fuzzing","context-aware fuzzing","fuzzer-agent cooperation","runtime feedback"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/35/x"},{"id":"p01055","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SustainSR: Interpretable OSS Sustainability Prediction via Symbolic Regression","tz":"SustainSR：基于符号回归的可解释开源软件可持续性预测","tl":"（据标题推断）用符号回归给出可解释的开源项目可持续性预测公式。","au":["Yang Deng","Mustafa Misir","Jinfu Chen","Jifeng Xuan"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["OSS sustainability","symbolic regression","interpretable prediction","open source community"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/36/x"},{"id":"p01056","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Stop When It Matters: Detectability-Guided Microbenchmarking for Performance Regression Testing","tz":"在关键时刻停止：面向性能回归测试的可检测性引导微基准测试","a":"ASE-2026 Reproducibility Guide This artifact contains the TT-MDE implementation, scripts for each research question, and cached result files used by the paper. Repository Layout local-mde.ipynb: notebook for loading results/mde-reproduce/** and reproducing the paper tables and figures. results/mde/: cached experiment outputs for the RQs and discussion studies. src/: Python scripts for running experiments, evaluating results, and generating intermediate data. jmh-1.37-mde/: fork of JMH 1.37 with the Phase-1 TT-MDE stopping logic. tools/: helper scripts for launching and managing experiment jobs. GitHub Link https://github.com/chenzongxiong/ASE-2026","az":"ASE-2026 可复现性指南。本制品包含 TT-MDE 的实现、针对每个研究问题的脚本，以及论文所用的缓存结果文件。仓库结构：local-mde.ipynb 为用于加载 results/mde-reproduce/** 并复现论文中表格与图表的 notebook；results/mde/ 为各研究问题与讨论性实验的缓存实验输出；src/ 为运行实验、评估结果和生成中间数据的 Python 脚本；jmh-1.37-mde/ 为集成了第一阶段 TT-MDE 停止逻辑的 JMH 1.37 分支；tools/ 为用于启动和管理实验作业的辅助脚本。GitHub 链接：https://github.com/chenzongxiong/ASE-2026","tl":"用最小可检测效应量决定微基准何时停止，降低性能回归测试成本。","au":["Zongxiong Chen","Derui Zhu","Jinfu Chen","Kundi Yao","Alexander Pretschner","Weiyi Shang","Manfred Hauswirth","Sonja Schimmler"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","reproducibility-replication","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["microbenchmarking","performance regression testing","minimal detectable effect","JMH","stopping criterion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/37/x"},{"id":"p01057","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evolution-Aware Regression Test Prioritization of ML-Enabled Systems using Gradient-Based Behavior Vectors","tz":"使用基于梯度的行为向量对 ML 赋能系统进行演化感知的回归测试优先级排序","a":"The machine learning(ML) component of an ML-enabled system evolves through retraining, fine-tuning, and optimization, so previously valid test results may no longer hold. A single evolution step can worsen performance on some test cases while improving others, making regression test prioritization inherently directional. We present Gradient-based Behavior Vector-Parameter Delta(GBV-PD), the first approach to operationalize the behavior vector space for evolution-aware regression test prioritization. GBV-PD represents each test case as a gradient-based vector(GBV), a low-dimensional projection of its loss gradient under the original model. It then projects the observed parameter update of the evolved model onto the same PCA basis and uses the resulting alignment to estimate whether each test case's loss is likely to increase or decrease, without running the evolved model on test cases during prioritization. In an empirical study across classification and regression tasks, GBV-PD consistently outperformed non-directional baselines and remained competitive with a full-gradient reference, while offering better time and storage profiles for repeated updates via reusable GBV caching. These results show that behavior-space ideas can be operationalized into a practical and efficient mechanism for repeated-update regression testing of evolving ML-enabled systems.","az":"机器学习（ML）赋能系统中的 ML 组件会通过重训练、微调和优化不断演化，因此先前有效的测试结果可能不再成立。一次演化步骤可能在某些测试用例上使性能变差、在另一些用例上使性能变好，这使得回归测试优先级排序本质上具有方向性。我们提出基于梯度的行为向量—参数增量方法（GBV-PD），这是首个将行为向量空间可操作化用于演化感知回归测试优先级排序的方法。GBV-PD 将每个测试用例表示为一个基于梯度的向量（GBV），即该用例在原模型下损失梯度的低维投影。随后，它把观测到的演化后模型的参数更新投影到相同的 PCA 基上，并利用由此得到的对齐程度来估计每个测试用例的损失是可能上升还是下降，而无需在优先级排序过程中在测试用例上运行演化后的模型。在涵盖分类与回归任务的实证研究中，GBV-PD 始终优于非方向性基线，并与使用完整梯度的参考方法保持竞争力，同时通过可复用的 GBV 缓存，在重复更新场景下提供了更好的时间与存储开销表现。这些结果表明，行为空间的思想可以被落实为一种实用且高效的机制，用于不断演化的 ML 赋能系统的重复更新回归测试。","tl":"用梯度行为向量与参数增量的对齐方向预测哪些测试会变差。","au":["Eunho Cho","Donghwan Shin","In-Young Ko"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["regression test prioritization","ML-enabled systems","gradient-based behavior vector","model evolution","PCA projection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/38/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.28037"},{"id":"p01058","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Multi-level Code Optimization via Mixture of Prompts","tz":"基于混合提示（Mixture of Prompts）的多层次代码优化","a":"Runtime efficiency is a critical factor that impacts both software quality and user satisfaction. There are many approaches proposed for code optimization to improve runtime efficiency. Traditional code optimization methods operate on intermediate representations (IRs) during compilation for static languages. They are effective but struggle to handle dynamic languages that do not require compilation. Recently, large language models (LLMs) have been leveraged to directly optimize source code in dynamic languages. However, these methods fail to identify suitable optimization targets and usually conduct incomprehensive single-level optimization. To address these challenges, we propose Optimo, a multi-level LLM-based code optimization approach built on a novel Mixture-of-Prompts (MoP) architecture. In the MoP architecture, Optimo identifies time-critical code structures as performance bottlenecks via differential profiling. These structures are then routed to some optimization strategies, akin to expert models in MoE, each tailored to optimize specific code patterns. Unlike traditional approaches that focus only on statement-level optimizations, Optimo operates at four levels of abstraction, ranging from coarse-grained algorithmic improvements to fine-grained optimizations in API usage. We evaluate Optimo on two code efficiency benchmarks, COFFE and Effibench. Our results demonstrate that Optimo achieves an up to 57.48% opt%, i.e., the percentage of optimized programs that are correct and at least 10% faster than the original programs, and an up to 3.97x speedup when optimizing human-written code, and it consistently outperforms the best baseline by up to 96.51% in terms of opt%. Furthermore, Optimo achieves an up to 42.42% opt% and an up to 13.51x speedup when optimizing LLM-generated code.","az":"运行时效率是同时影响软件质量与用户满意度的关键因素。目前已有许多用于提升运行时效率的代码优化方法。传统的代码优化方法在编译期针对静态语言的中间表示（IR）进行操作，它们虽然有效，但难以处理无需编译的动态语言。近来，人们开始利用大语言模型（LLM）直接优化动态语言的源代码。然而，这些方法无法识别合适的优化目标，且通常只进行不全面的单层次优化。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 Optimo，一种基于全新混合提示（Mixture-of-Prompts, MoP）架构的多层次 LLM 代码优化方法。在 MoP 架构中，Optimo 通过差分性能剖析（differential profiling）识别出作为性能瓶颈的时间关键代码结构，然后把这些结构路由到若干优化策略上——类似于 MoE 中的专家模型，每种策略都针对特定代码模式进行优化。与只关注语句级优化的传统方法不同，Optimo 在四个抽象层次上工作，从粗粒度的算法改进一直到细粒度的 API 使用优化。我们在 COFFE 和 Effibench 两个代码效率基准上评估 Optimo。结果表明，在优化人工编写的代码时，Optimo 的 opt%（即优化后既正确又比原程序至少快 10% 的程序所占比例）最高可达 57.48%，最高加速比达 3.97 倍，并且在 opt% 上始终超过最佳基线，最高超出 96.51%。此外，在优化 LLM 生成的代码时，Optimo 的 opt% 最高可达 42.42%，最高加速比达 13.51 倍。","tl":"用差分剖析定位瓶颈并按代码模式路由到多层次优化提示专家。","au":["Yun Peng","Jun Wan","Jiakun Liu","Shuzheng Gao","David Lo","Xiaoxue Ren"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code optimization","mixture of prompts","differential profiling","runtime efficiency","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/39/x"},{"id":"p01059","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evaluating the Maintainability of ViewModel Tests using Multi-modal DSLs: An Industrial Mixed-Methods Study","tz":"使用多模态 DSL 评估 ViewModel 测试的可维护性：一项工业混合方法研究","a":"As in many modern software engineering domains, the quality of an application's Graphical User Interface (GUI) is fundamentally verified by automated testing. One established approach to mitigate testing challenges is to leverage architectural patterns, such as Model-View-ViewModel (MVVM), to decouple presentation logic and test it in isolation. However, developing these ViewModel tests in general-purpose programming languages (GPLs) often forces engineers to write excessive boilerplate code for test setup and complex assertion chains. While multi-modal domain-specific languages (DSLs) show promise in mitigating these GPL-related issues, empirical evidence of their impact on test maintainability in practice is lacking. To address this gap, we present an industrial mixed-methods study evaluating how abstracting GUI tests to the ViewModel level via multi-modal DSLs impacts maintenance overhead in practice, using the ViMoTest method as our representative realization. After establishing industrial applicability via a pre-study comprising action research and a case study, we conducted a task-based evaluation with industry experts, triangulated with semi-structured interviews and a questionnaire. Quantitative results indicate that the ViMoTest method shows a strong tendency to reduce test specification effort and size compared to a C++ engineering baseline. Furthermore, qualitative expert feedback indicates that visual assertions and robust refactoring capabilities reduce cognitive load during structural test evolution. Overall, this study provides empirical evidence that multi-modal DSLs positively impact the maintainability of ViewModel tests.","az":"与许多现代软件工程领域一样，应用程序图形用户界面（GUI）的质量从根本上要靠自动化测试来验证。缓解测试难题的一种成熟做法是利用架构模式（例如 Model-View-ViewModel, MVVM）将展示逻辑解耦并单独测试。然而，在通用编程语言（GPL）中开发这类 ViewModel 测试往往迫使工程师编写大量样板代码来完成测试搭建和复杂的断言链。虽然多模态领域特定语言（DSL）有望缓解这些与 GPL 相关的问题，但关于它们在实践中对测试可维护性影响的实证证据仍然缺乏。为填补这一空白，我们开展了一项工业混合方法研究，以 ViMoTest 方法作为代表性实现，评估通过多模态 DSL 把 GUI 测试抽象到 ViewModel 层次对实际维护开销的影响。在通过一项包含行动研究与案例研究的前置研究确立其工业适用性之后，我们与业界专家开展了基于任务的评估，并用半结构化访谈和问卷进行三角验证。定量结果表明，与 C++ 工程基线相比，ViMoTest 方法在减少测试规约工作量与规模方面呈现出明显趋势。此外，专家的定性反馈表明，可视化断言与健壮的重构能力降低了结构性测试演化过程中的认知负荷。总体而言，本研究提供了实证证据，表明多模态 DSL 对 ViewModel 测试的可维护性具有积极影响。","tl":"工业实证显示多模态 DSL 显著降低 ViewModel 测试的维护开销。","au":["Mario Fuksa","Sandro Speth","Steffen Becker"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["human-study","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["ViewModel testing","multi-modal DSL","test maintainability","MVVM","industrial mixed-methods study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/40/x"},{"id":"p01060","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Sound and Efficient Statistical Model Checking for Probabilities and Bounded Rewards","tz":"面向概率与有界奖励的可靠且高效的统计模型检验","tl":"（据标题推断）给出对概率与有界奖励同时保证可靠性且更高效的统计模型检验方法。","au":["Hao Bu","Lin Huang","Tao Wei","Jingyi Wang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["statistical model checking","bounded rewards","probabilistic verification","soundness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/41/x"},{"id":"p01061","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Tracing the Invisible: Semantic Message Flow Discovery via Data Contracts in Real-World Distributed Systems","tz":"追踪不可见者：真实分布式系统中基于数据契约的语义消息流发现","a":"Research artifact accompanying the ASE 2026 paper “Tracing the Invisible: Semantic Message Flow Discovery via Data Contracts in Real-World Distributed Systems.” The record contains the Hermes implementation, scripts, evaluation results, the submitted paper, and supporting documentation used in the study.","az":"本记录是 ASE 2026 论文《Tracing the Invisible: Semantic Message Flow Discovery via Data Contracts in Real-World Distributed Systems》的配套研究制品，包含 Hermes 的实现、脚本、评估结果、投稿论文以及研究中使用的支撑文档。","tl":"借助数据契约恢复真实分布式系统中隐式的语义消息流。","au":["youlong chen","Jie Lu","mingtao huang","Chenghang Shi","Yongheng Huang","Haofeng Li","Dong Liu","Mengna Ma","Yong Liu","Qinfen Hao","Lian Li"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["message flow discovery","data contracts","distributed systems","Hermes","observability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/42/x"},{"id":"p01062","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Your Credentials Are Leaked by LLM Agent Skills: An Empirical Study","tz":"你的凭据是如何被 LLM 智能体技能（Agent Skills）泄露的：一项实证研究","a":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents increasingly rely on third-party skills that operate within privileged execution environments and routinely handle sensitive credentials, yet how these credentials are leaked remains largely unexplored. To fill this gap, we present the first large-scale empirical study on credential leakage in agent skills. From 170,226 artifacts on SkillsMP, the largest open-source skill marketplace, we sampled 17,022 skills via stratified random sampling and analyzed each through static secret extraction (regex and AST parsing), dynamic sandbox testing with mock credentials, and cross-referencing developer intent against runtime behavior. Our analysis identifies 520 affected skills containing 1,708 security issues, and yields a taxonomy of 10 leakage patterns. Three findings stand out. First, 76.3% of cases require jointly analyzing natural-language descriptions and programming logic, showing that credential exposure in skills is fundamentally cross-modal. Second, debug logging accounts for 73.5% of vulnerabilities because agent frameworks feed stdout into the LLM context window, turning routine debugging into a credential exposure vector. Third, 89.6% of leaked credentials are immediately exploitable -- 92.5% during routine execution without elevated privileges -- and the fork-based distribution model defeats remediation, as secrets removed from 107 upstream repositories persist across 50+ independent forks. Following responsible disclosure, all malicious skills have been removed and 91.6% of hardcoded cases remediated. We release our dataset, taxonomy, and detection pipeline to support future agent security research.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）智能体越来越依赖第三方技能（skills），这些技能运行在特权执行环境中，并经常处理敏感凭据，但这些凭据究竟是如何被泄露的，在很大程度上仍未被探究。为填补这一空白，我们开展了首个关于智能体技能中凭据泄露的大规模实证研究。我们从最大的开源技能市场 SkillsMP 上的 170,226 个制品中，通过分层随机抽样选取了 17,022 个技能，并对每个技能进行了静态秘密提取（正则与 AST 解析）、使用模拟凭据的动态沙箱测试，以及将开发者意图与运行时行为进行交叉比对的分析。我们的分析识别出 520 个受影响技能，共含 1,708 个安全问题，并归纳出包含 10 种泄露模式的分类体系。其中三项发现尤为突出：第一，76.3% 的案例需要联合分析自然语言描述与程序逻辑，说明技能中的凭据暴露本质上是跨模态的；第二，调试日志占全部漏洞的 73.5%，原因在于智能体框架会把标准输出送入 LLM 的上下文窗口，使得例行调试变成凭据泄露的渠道；第三，89.6% 的被泄露凭据可被立即利用——其中 92.5% 在例行执行过程中无需提升权限即可利用——而基于 fork 的分发模式使补救失效：从 107 个上游仓库中移除的秘密仍然残留在 50 多个独立 fork 中。在负责任披露之后，所有恶意技能都已被下架，91.6% 的硬编码案例已被修复。我们公开了数据集、分类体系与检测流水线，以支持未来的智能体安全研究。","tl":"首次大规模揭示智能体技能的凭据泄露模式，调试日志是主因。","au":["Zhihao Chen","Ying Zhang","Yi Liu","Gelei Deng","Yuekang Li","Yanjun Zhang","Jianting Ning","Leo Zhang","Lei Ma","Zhiqiang Li"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["agent skills","credential leakage","LLM agent security","skill marketplace","static and dynamic analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/43/x"},{"id":"p01063","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"WebCQ: Cooperative Multi-agent Deep Reinforcement Learning for Scalable Web GUI Testing","tz":"WebCQ：面向可扩展 Web GUI 测试的协作式多智能体深度强化学习","a":"Multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL)-based techniques have shown promise for GUI testing. However, as the complexity of modern GUI software increases, existing MARL-based approaches (e.g., MARG and Fastbot) struggle to scale due to the inherent limitations of their underlying tabular reinforcement learning algorithms. This limits their applicability to large-scale commercial GUI software, especially web applications with vast state spaces and many interactive elements. To fill this gap, we propose WebCQ, a novel MARL-based approach for scalable web GUI testing. WebCQ incorporates QTRAN for multi-agent coordination and a lightweight synchronization mechanism, allowing it to work under asynchronous web testing scenarios. It extracts semantic and exploration features for each UI event to form an action vector. This vector is concatenated with the current state vector and fed into the policy network, enabling DQN-based decision making within a dynamic action space. We evaluated WebCQ on eight large-scale commercial websites. Under the same time budget and agent count, WebCQ explored 33.3% more states and executed 42.2% more unique actions than MARG, while triggering more failures on six of the eight websites under test. It also demonstrated strong scalability, maintaining higher action throughput during 20-hour experiments, and achieving greater performance improvements as the number of agents increased. These results show that WebCQovercomes key limitations of existing MARL-based approaches, providing a scalable and effective solution for enhancing modern web GUI testing.","az":"基于多智能体强化学习（MARL）的技术在 GUI 测试中已展现出潜力。然而，随着现代 GUI 软件复杂度的提升，现有基于 MARL 的方法（如 MARG 和 Fastbot）由于其底层表格型强化学习算法的固有局限而难以扩展，这限制了它们在大规模商业 GUI 软件上的适用性，尤其是状态空间庞大、交互元素众多的 Web 应用。为填补这一空白，我们提出 WebCQ，一种面向可扩展 Web GUI 测试的全新 MARL 方法。WebCQ 引入 QTRAN 实现多智能体协同，并设计了一种轻量级同步机制，使其能够在异步的 Web 测试场景下工作。它为每个 UI 事件抽取语义特征与探索特征以构成动作向量，再将该向量与当前状态向量拼接后输入策略网络，从而在动态动作空间中实现基于 DQN 的决策。我们在八个大规模商业网站上评估了 WebCQ。在相同时间预算和智能体数量下，WebCQ 比 MARG 多探索了 33.3% 的状态，多执行了 42.2% 的独特动作，并在八个被测网站中的六个上触发了更多失败。它还展现出很强的可扩展性：在 20 小时实验中保持了更高的动作吞吐量，并随着智能体数量增加取得了更大的性能提升。这些结果表明，WebCQ 克服了现有基于 MARL 的方法的关键局限，为增强现代 Web GUI 测试提供了可扩展且有效的解决方案。","tl":"用 QTRAN 与动态动作空间 DQN 让多智能体 Web GUI 测试可扩展。","au":["Yujia Fan","Sinan Wang","Zebang Fei","Yao Qin","Huaxuan Li","Yepang Liu"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["web GUI testing","multi-agent reinforcement learning","QTRAN","DQN","state exploration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/44/x"},{"id":"p01064","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MalSkills: Detecting Malicious Skills in the Agentic Supply Chain via Neuro-symbolic Reasoning","tz":"MalSkills：通过神经符号推理检测智能体供应链中的恶意技能","a":"Skills are increasingly used to extend LLM agents by packaging prompts, code, and configurations into reusable modules. As public registries and marketplaces expand, they form an emerging agentic supply chain, but also introduce a new attack surface for malicious skills. Detecting malicious skills is challenging because relevant evidence is often distributed across heterogeneous artifacts and must be reasoned in context. Existing static, LLM-based, and dynamic approaches each capture only part of this problem, making them insufficient for robust real-world detection. In this paper, we present MalSkills, a neuro-symbolic framework for malicious skills detection. MalSkills first extracts security-sensitive operations from heterogeneous artifacts through a combination of symbolic parsing and LLM-assisted semantic analysis. It then constructs the skill dependency graph that links artifacts, operations, operands, and value flows across the skill. On top of this graph, MalSkills performs neuro-symbolic reasoning to infer malicious patterns or previously unseen suspicious workflows. We evaluate MalSkills on a benchmark of 200 real-world skills against 5 state-of-the-art baselines. MalSkills achieves 93% F1, outperforming the baselines by 5--87 percentage points. We further apply MalSkills to analyze 150,108 skills collected from 7 public registries, flagging 620 potentially malicious skills. Through manual review, we confirm that 400 of them are indeed malicious, all of which were responsibly reported and are currently awaiting confirmation from the platforms and maintainers. These results demonstrate the practical potential of MalSkills in securing the agentic supply chain.","az":"技能（skills）被越来越多地用于扩展 LLM 智能体，它们把提示、代码和配置打包成可复用模块。随着公共注册表和市场的扩张，它们构成了一条新兴的智能体供应链，但同时也引入了恶意技能这一新的攻击面。检测恶意技能颇具挑战，因为相关证据往往分散在异构制品之中，并且必须结合上下文进行推理。现有的静态方法、基于 LLM 的方法和动态方法各自只覆盖了该问题的一部分，不足以支撑稳健的真实世界检测。本文提出 MalSkills，一个用于恶意技能检测的神经符号框架。MalSkills 首先通过符号解析与 LLM 辅助语义分析相结合的方式，从异构制品中抽取对安全敏感的操作；随后构建技能依赖图，将整个技能中的制品、操作、操作数与值流联系起来；在该图之上，MalSkills 执行神经符号推理，以推断恶意模式或此前未见过的可疑工作流。我们在包含 200 个真实技能的基准上，将 MalSkills 与 5 个最先进的基线进行对比评估。MalSkills 取得了 93% 的 F1 值，比基线高出 5 到 87 个百分点。我们进一步将 MalSkills 应用于从 7 个公共注册表收集的 150,108 个技能，标记出 620 个潜在恶意技能。通过人工复核，我们确认其中 400 个确实为恶意，所有这些都已被负责任地上报，目前正等待平台与维护者的确认。这些结果表明了 MalSkills 在保护智能体供应链方面的实际潜力。","tl":"用技能依赖图上的神经符号推理识别恶意 Agent Skill。","au":["Shenao Wang","HeJunjie","Yanjie Zhao","Yayi Wang","Kan Yu","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["malicious skill detection","agentic supply chain","neuro-symbolic reasoning","skill dependency graph","LLM agents"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/45/x"},{"id":"p01065","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Less Is More: Tuning Configurable Systems with Imperfect Fidelity","tz":"少即是多：在不完美保真度下调优可配置系统","a":"Configuration tuning is essential for optimizing the performance of highly configurable systems, e.g., throughput or runtime, under a given environment. Yet, this is a challenging process as there can be many options to tune, and configuration measurement is often highly expensive. In this paper, we demonstrate the phenomenon of ``less can be more'': system configuration tuning can be greatly improved with much superior budget utilization by partially tuning under the imperfect-fidelity—an environment that is similar, but cheaper to measure, compared with the concerned perfect-fidelity of environment under which the system should be tuned. We codify a conceptual framework of fidelity for configurable systems, drawing on which allows us to propose MFTune, a tuner that proactively explores in the space of >10^4 possible imperfect-fidelity settings to approximate a useful one, which strikes for the wideness of tuning. This creates high-quality seeds for the perfect-fidelity, which in turn ensures the tuning depth. Experiment results against 10 state-of-the-art tuners, obtained from running diverse real-world systems for 19 months 24 7, show that MFTune performs considerably better on 83.33% cases with up to 19.34% improvement while achieving hours of budget saving in general.","az":"配置调优对于在给定环境下优化高度可配置系统的性能（例如吞吐量或运行时间）至关重要。然而这是一个颇具挑战的过程，因为待调选项可能很多，而且配置测量往往代价高昂。本文展示了“少即是多”的现象：通过在不完美保真度（imperfect-fidelity）下进行部分调优——即在一个与目标环境相似但测量成本更低的环境中调优，而非直接在系统本应被调优的完美保真度环境中调优——系统配置调优可以以远优的预算利用率获得大幅改进。我们为可配置系统建立了一个关于保真度的概念框架，并据此提出 MFTune，一个能够在超过 $10^4$ 种可能的不完美保真度设置构成的空间中主动探索、以逼近某个有用设置的调优器，从而追求调优的广度。这为完美保真度环境提供了高质量的种子，进而保证了调优的深度。在与 10 个最先进调优器的对比实验中（这些实验来自对多样化真实系统连续 19 个月、7×24 小时的运行），结果表明 MFTune 在 83.33% 的案例上表现明显更好，最高提升达 19.34%，同时总体上节省了数小时的预算。","tl":"先在廉价的低保真环境粗调再迁移种子，大幅省下调优预算。","au":["Yulong Ye","Miqing Li","Tao Chen"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["configuration tuning","configurable systems","multi-fidelity","measurement budget","MFTune"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/46/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.00759"},{"id":"p01066","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Programming by Chat: A Large-Scale Behavioral Analysis of 11,579 Real-World AI-Assisted IDE Sessions","tz":"以聊天编程：对 11,579 个真实 AI 辅助 IDE 会话的大规模行为分析","a":"IDE-integrated AI coding assistants, which operate conversationally within developers’ working codebases with access to project context and multi-file editing, are rapidly reshaping software development. However, empirical investigation of this shift remains limited: existing studies largely rely on small-scale, controlled settings or analyze general-purpose chatbots rather than codebase-aware IDE workflows. We present, to the best of our knowledge, the first large-scale study of real-world conversational programming in IDE-native settings, analyzing 74,998 developer messages from 11,579 chat sessions across 1,300 repositories and 899 developers using Cursor and GitHub Copilot. These chats were committed to public repositories as part of routine development, capturing in-the-wild behavior. Our findings reveal three shifts in how programming work is organized: conversational programming operates as progressive specification, with developers iteratively refining outputs rather than specifying complete tasks upfront; developers redistribute cognitive work to AI, delegating diagnosis, comprehension, and validation rather than engaging with code and outputs directly; and developers actively manage the collaboration, externalizing plans into persistent artifacts, and negotiating AI autonomy through context injection and behavioral constraints. These results provide foundational empirical insights into AI-assisted development and offer implications for the design of future programming environments.","az":"集成于 IDE 的 AI 编程助手能够在开发者的工作代码库中以对话方式运行，可访问项目上下文并进行多文件编辑，正在迅速重塑软件开发。然而，对这一转变的实证研究仍然有限：已有研究大多依赖小规模的受控实验，或分析通用聊天机器人而非具备代码库感知能力的 IDE 工作流。我们提出了据我们所知首个针对 IDE 原生场景下真实对话式编程的大规模研究，分析了来自 1,300 个仓库、899 名开发者、使用 Cursor 和 GitHub Copilot 的 11,579 个聊天会话中的 74,998 条开发者消息。这些聊天记录是在日常开发中被提交到公共仓库的，捕捉到了真实环境中的行为。我们的发现揭示了编程工作组织方式的三个转变：对话式编程表现为渐进式规约，开发者会不断迭代地细化输出，而不是一开始就给出完整的任务说明；开发者把认知工作重新分配给 AI，将诊断、理解与验证等工作委派出去，而不是自己直接面对代码和输出；开发者会主动管理这种协作，把计划外化为持久化的制品，并通过注入上下文与施加行为约束来协商 AI 的自主性。这些结果为 AI 辅助开发提供了基础性的实证洞见，并对未来编程环境的设计提出了启示。","tl":"大规模真实 IDE 聊天记录揭示渐进式规约与认知工作再分配。","au":["Ningzhi Tang","Chaoran Chen","Zihan Fang","Gelei Xu","Maria Dhakal","Yiyu Shi","Collin McMillan","Yu Huang","Toby Jia-Jun Li"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["conversational programming","AI coding assistant","IDE chat sessions","developer behavior","Cursor / Copilot"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/47/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.00436"},{"id":"p01067","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Understanding Bugs in Modern Agentic Frameworks: A Study of Symptoms, Root Causes, and Triggering Conditions","tz":"理解现代智能体框架中的缺陷：症状、根因与触发条件研究","a":"Modern agentic frameworks such as CrewAI and AutoGen have evolved into complex, autonomous multi-agent systems, introducing reliability challenges that go beyond earlier pipeline-based LLM libraries. However, existing empirical studies focus on earlier LLM libraries or task-level bugs, leaving the unique complexities of these agentic frameworks unexplored. We present a comprehensive study of 409 fixed bugs across five representative agentic frameworks, proposing a five-layer architectural abstraction. Our taxonomy identifies previously unreported symptom categories—Unexpected Execution Sequence, User Configuration Ignored, and Incomplete/Incorrect Trace—and isolates agent-specific root causes including Model-Related Fault, Cognitive Context Mismanagement, and Orchestration Fault. Notably, the model integration layer is the most bug-prone yet receives disproportionately low test inclusion rate during bug fixing (47%), revealing a critical validation gap. Despite varying design paradigms, bug symptoms, root causes, and bug-prone components show substantial cross-framework consistency (JS similarity 0.62–0.88). Finally, we present the first systematic study of bug-triggering conditions, identifying error-prone factor combinations across element configurations, input patterns, and operations, and demonstrate their transferability across frameworks, providing a foundation for test oracle design and cross-framework benchmark.","az":"CrewAI、AutoGen 等现代智能体框架已经演化为复杂的自治多智能体系统，带来了超越早期流水线式 LLM 库的可靠性挑战。然而，现有实证研究要么聚焦于更早期的 LLM 库，要么聚焦于任务级缺陷，使得这些智能体框架特有的复杂性尚未被探究。我们对五个代表性智能体框架中的 409 个已修复缺陷开展了全面研究，并提出了一种五层架构抽象。我们的分类体系识别出此前未被报道的症状类别——非预期执行顺序、用户配置被忽略、以及不完整/不正确的轨迹——并分离出智能体特有的根因，包括模型相关故障、认知上下文管理不当和编排故障。值得注意的是，模型集成层是最易出错的层次，但在缺陷修复过程中其测试纳入率却极低（47%），揭示出一个关键的验证空白。尽管设计范式各异，各框架在缺陷症状、根因和易错组件上表现出高度的一致性（JS 相似度为 0.62–0.88）。最后，我们首次系统研究了缺陷触发条件，识别出跨元素配置、输入模式和操作的易错因素组合，并验证了它们在不同框架间的可迁移性，为测试预言设计与跨框架基准构建奠定了基础。","tl":"首次刻画智能体框架缺陷的症状、根因与可迁移触发条件。","au":["Xiaowen Zhang","Hannuo Zhang","Shin Hwei Tan"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["agentic frameworks","bug taxonomy","root cause analysis","triggering conditions","CrewAI / AutoGen"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/48/x"},{"id":"p01068","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Neuro-symbolic Requirements Elicitation: Utilizing Formal Verification Counterexamples as Contextual Prompts","tz":"神经符号需求获取：将形式化验证的反例用作上下文提示","tl":"（据标题推断）把形式化验证产生的反例当作提示上下文来驱动需求获取。","au":["Okba Tibermacine","Chouki Tibermacine"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["requirements elicitation","neuro-symbolic","formal verification counterexamples","contextual prompting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/49/x"},{"id":"p01069","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SmartPoC: Validating Smart Contract Vulnerability Findings through PoC Generation and Execution","tz":"SmartPoC：通过生成并执行 PoC 来验证智能合约漏洞报告","tl":"（据标题推断）自动生成并执行 PoC 以判定智能合约漏洞报告是否真实。","au":["Longfei Chen","Ruibin Yan","Taiyu Wong","Yiyang Chen","Wang Jialai","Chao Zhang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","llm-based"],"kw":["smart contract","proof-of-concept generation","vulnerability validation","false positive filtering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/50/x"},{"id":"p01070","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Every Scenario Matters: Scenario-Guided White-Box Testing for Static Code Checkers Powered by LLMs","tz":"每个场景都重要：由 LLM 驱动的场景引导式静态代码检查器白盒测试","a":"In static analysis tools, each detection rule corresponds to a dedicated code checker. The checker’s quality directly determines the validity of reported defects. Thus, comprehensive testing of these checkers is crucial. Existing checker testing approaches usually generate test cases from high-level rule descriptions while treating checkers as black boxes. However, these descriptions usually omit implementation-level conditions and checking scenarios. To bridge this gap, our key insight is that the rule description and checker implementation provide complementary information for comprehensive testing. The implementation supplies concrete checking logic, while the rule anchors the intended semantics. Building on this, we propose ScenSCT, a novel scenario-guided white-box checker testing approach powered by LLMs. ScenSCT first translates the checker’s source code into a unified logic-based representation (CheckerIR) and applies both logic-decomposition and scenario-validation strategies to extract concrete checking scenarios. It then converts these scenarios into test cases through execution-feedback-guided test alignment to instantiate scenario constraints and scenario-invariant test augmentation to generate variants that preserve the target scenario. We evaluate ScenSCT on real-world Java checkers from five mainstream static analysis tools. In single-tool evaluation, ScenSCT extracts an average of ~9 scenarios and generates ~39 tests per checker, uncovering 270 potential issues (58 false positives and 212 false negatives) with an overall precision of 86.4%. Furthermore, cross-tool evaluation reveals 177 capability differences among shared checkers. Overall, ScenSCT offers a systematic testing method to improve the reliability of static analysis tools.","az":"在静态分析工具中，每条检测规则都对应一个专门的代码检查器（checker）。检查器的质量直接决定所报告缺陷的有效性，因此对这些检查器进行全面测试至关重要。现有的检查器测试方法通常从高层规则描述生成测试用例，并把检查器视为黑盒。然而，这些描述往往省略了实现层面的条件与检查场景。为弥合这一差距，我们的关键洞见是：规则描述与检查器实现为全面测试提供了互补信息——实现提供了具体的检查逻辑，而规则锚定了预期语义。基于此，我们提出 ScenSCT，一种由 LLM 驱动的、场景引导的白盒检查器测试方法。ScenSCT 首先把检查器源代码翻译为统一的基于逻辑的表示（CheckerIR），并应用逻辑分解与场景验证两种策略来抽取具体的检查场景；随后，它通过执行反馈引导的测试对齐来实例化场景约束，并通过保持场景不变的测试增强生成变体，从而把这些场景转化为测试用例。我们在来自五款主流静态分析工具的真实 Java 检查器上评估 ScenSCT。在单工具评估中，ScenSCT 平均为每个检查器抽取约 9 个场景并生成约 39 个测试，共发现 270 个潜在问题（58 个误报和 212 个漏报），整体精确率为 86.4%。此外，跨工具评估揭示了共有检查器之间的 177 处能力差异。总体而言，ScenSCT 提供了一种系统化的测试方法，可提升静态分析工具的可靠性。","tl":"从检查器源码抽取检查场景，白盒地为静态分析器造测试。","au":["Jun Liu","Liqiang Ji","Jiwei Yan","Linjie Pan","Jinsong Ren","Jun Yan","Jian Zhang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static analyzer testing","code checker","white-box testing","scenario extraction","LLM-based test generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/51/x"},{"id":"p01071","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Adaptive Proof Refinement with LLM-Guided Strategy Selection","tz":"基于 LLM 引导策略选择的自适应证明精化","tl":"（据标题推断）让 LLM 选择证明策略以自适应地精化失败的形式化证明。","au":["Minghai Lu","Zhe Zhou","Danning Xie","Songlin Jia","Benjamin Delaware","Tianyi Zhang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["proof refinement","theorem proving","strategy selection","LLM-guided verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/52/x"},{"id":"p01072","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Assessing the Cross-Version Applicability of Java Library Vulnerability Exploits","tz":"评估 Java 库漏洞利用程序的跨版本适用性","a":"Open-source software supply chain security relies heavily on assessing affected versions of library vulnerabilities. While prior studies have leveraged exploits for verifying vulnerability affected versions, they point out a key limitation that exploits are version-specific and cannot be directly applied across library versions. Despite being widely acknowledged, this limitation has not been systematically validated at scale, leaving the actual applicability of exploits across versions unexplored. To fill this gap, we conduct the first large-scale empirical study on exploit applicability across library versions. We construct a comprehensive dataset consisting of 259 exploits spanning 128 Java libraries and 28,150 historical versions, covering 61 CWEs that account for 76.33% of vulnerabilities in Maven. Leveraging this dataset, we execute each exploit against the library version history and compare the execution outcomes with our manually annotated ground-truth affected versions. We further investigate the root causes of inconsistencies between exploit execution and ground truth, and explore strategies for exploit migration. Our results (RQ1) show that, even without migration, exploits achieve 83.0% recall and 99.3% precision in identifying affected versions in Java, outperforming most widely used vulnerability databases and assessment tools. Notably, this capability enables us to contribute 796 confirmed missing affected versions to the CPE dictionary. We investigate the remaining exploit failures (RQ2) and find that they mainly stem from compatibility issues introduced by library evolution and changing environmental constraints. Based on these observations, we manually migrate exploits for 1,885 versions and distill a taxonomy of 10 strategies from these successful adaptation cases (RQ3), thereby increasing the overall recall to 96.1%.","az":"开源软件供应链安全在很大程度上依赖于评估库漏洞的受影响版本。尽管已有研究利用漏洞利用程序（exploit）来验证漏洞受影响版本，但它们指出了一个关键局限：exploit 是版本特定的，无法直接跨库版本使用。这一局限虽被广泛承认，却从未在大规模上被系统验证，因此 exploit 跨版本的实际适用性仍未被探究。为填补这一空白，我们开展了首个关于 exploit 跨库版本适用性的大规模实证研究。我们构建了一个综合数据集，包含覆盖 128 个 Java 库、28,150 个历史版本的 259 个 exploit，涵盖 61 个 CWE，占 Maven 中漏洞的 76.33%。基于该数据集，我们针对库的版本历史逐一执行每个 exploit，并将执行结果与人工标注的受影响版本真值进行比较。我们进一步调查了 exploit 执行结果与真值之间不一致的根本原因，并探索了 exploit 迁移的策略。结果（RQ1）表明，即便不做迁移，exploit 在识别 Java 受影响版本上也达到了 83.0% 的召回率和 99.3% 的精确率，优于大多数被广泛使用的漏洞数据库与评估工具。值得注意的是，这一能力使我们为 CPE 字典贡献了 796 个经确认此前缺失的受影响版本。我们进一步分析了剩余的 exploit 执行失败（RQ2），发现它们主要源于库演化带来的兼容性问题以及不断变化的环境约束。基于这些观察，我们为 1,885 个版本手工迁移了 exploit，并从这些成功适配案例中提炼出包含 10 种策略的分类体系（RQ3），从而把整体召回率提升到 96.1%。","tl":"首次大规模验证 exploit 跨版本可复用，并提炼 10 种迁移策略。","au":["Zirui Chen","Qi Zhan","Jiayuan Zhou","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Xiaohu Yang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["exploit applicability","affected version assessment","Java library vulnerabilities","exploit migration","CPE dictionary"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/53/x"},{"id":"p01073","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TDRepro: A Neurosymbolic Approach to Reproducing Timing-Dependent Flaky Test Failures","tz":"TDRepro：一种复现时序依赖型不稳定测试失败的神经符号方法","a":"Tests that nondeterministically pass or fail on the same version of code are known as flaky tests, and their failures substantially hinder regression testing and debugging. Reproducing failures from timingdependent (TD) flaky tests is particularly challenging because these failures depend on rare thread interleavings that may not occur even after running the test many times. Prior approaches reproduce such failures by searching for locations at which to inject delays during execution, but this search process can be expensive. We present TDRepro, an automated approach that leverages large-language models (LLMs) and program analysis to efficiently reproduce TD-test failures. TDRepro first identifies relevant methods by collecting executed methods during the test run and identifying those that execute concurrently with other methods. It then ranks these methods by computing the embedding similarity between each method’s code and the observed failure log. Finally, TDRepro uses an LLM to identify candidate locations for delay injection within the top-ranked methods. TDRepro validates these candidates by injecting delays and rerunning the test, iteratively refining the candidate locations based on unsuccessful attempts until the target failure is reproduced or the maximum number of iterations is reached. We evaluate TDRepro on 82 TD tests across 25 modules from open-source Java Maven projects. TDRepro reproduces 100% more failures than the prior state-of-the-art approach, FlakeRake, and achieves more reliable reproduction, with 55 tests reaching a failure reproduction rate of >99%, compared with 30 tests for FlakeRake. Repeatedly reproducing failures with TDRepro requires 1482.1× and 10.4× less time and costs 888.4× and 9.6× less than repeatedly rerunning tests and using FlakeRake, respectively.","az":"在同一版本代码上不确定地时而通过、时而失败的测试被称为不稳定测试（flaky test），其失败会严重阻碍回归测试与调试。复现时序依赖（TD）型不稳定测试的失败尤其困难，因为这类失败依赖于罕见的线程交错，即使把测试运行很多次也可能不会出现。已有方法通过搜索执行期间注入延迟的位置来复现此类失败，但这一搜索过程代价高昂。我们提出 TDRepro，一种利用大语言模型（LLM）与程序分析来高效复现 TD 测试失败的自动化方法。TDRepro 首先通过收集测试运行期间被执行的方法，并识别其中与其他方法并发执行的方法，来确定相关方法；然后，它通过计算每个方法代码与观测到的失败日志之间的嵌入相似度来对这些方法排序；最后，TDRepro 使用 LLM 在排名靠前的方法中确定候选的延迟注入位置。TDRepro 通过注入延迟并重跑测试来验证这些候选位置，并根据失败的尝试迭代地精化候选位置，直到目标失败被复现或达到最大迭代次数。我们在来自开源 Java Maven 项目的 25 个模块、82 个 TD 测试上评估 TDRepro。TDRepro 复现的失败数量比此前最先进的方法 FlakeRake 多 100%，并且复现更可靠：有 55 个测试的失败复现率超过 99%，而 FlakeRake 只有 30 个。与反复重跑测试和使用 FlakeRake 相比，使用 TDRepro 反复复现失败所需时间分别减少 1482.1 倍和 10.4 倍，成本分别降低 888.4 倍和 9.6 倍。","tl":"用 LLM 结合并发方法排序精准选定延迟注入点复现时序型 flaky 失败。","au":["Shanto Rahman","Talank Baral","August Shi","Wing Lam"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["flaky tests","timing-dependent failures","failure reproduction","delay injection","neurosymbolic"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/54/x","pu":"https://people.cs.gmu.edu/~winglam/publications/2026/RahmanETAL26TDRepro.pdf"},{"id":"p01074","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Think Before You Code: Dual Reasoning for the NLSafety–Utility Trade-Off in LLM Code Generation","tz":"三思而后码：面向 LLM 代码生成中 NL 安全性与效用权衡的双重推理","a":"Large language models (LLMs) for code generation are typically evaluated on functional correctness alone, overlooking whether generated code propagates harmful content embedded in the prompt. Prior work has shown that most Code LLMs reproduce offensive identifiers from injected renaming instructions without warning, yet existing approaches focus on detecting harmful content, neglecting functional correctness. Grounded in the Theory of Dual Channel Constraints (which states that code is a dual-channel medium combining an algorithmic (AL) channel for machine execution and a natural language (NL) channel for human communication, creating a unique safety-utility trade-off where a model must balance functional execution with responsible communication), we propose NLSafety-Utility Duality Score (SUDS), a metric that unifies code utility, safety adherence, and warning awareness into a single score across 12 ranked response scenarios, and Dual Reasoning (DR), a structured inference-time technique that requires an explicit safety audit and task-grounded code review before code generation. Evaluated on five LLMs across two benchmarks augmented with harmful keyword injections (820 and 2,135 samples), DR consistently achieves the highest SUDS across all models, improving mean SUDS by 1.32× to 3.42× over the baseline, while chain-of-thought prompting yields negligible safety gains and a safety-aware prompt provides only partial improvement. Further analysis reveals that DR's effectiveness scales with model capacity, that the one-shot exemplar primarily stabilizes output format for smaller models, and that structured reasoning cannot compensate for models with limited safety vocabularies.","az":"用于代码生成的大语言模型（LLM）通常只按功能正确性来评估，而忽视了生成的代码是否会传播嵌入在提示中的有害内容。已有研究表明，大多数代码 LLM 会在没有任何警示的情况下照搬注入的重命名指令中的冒犯性标识符，但现有方法只关注检测有害内容，忽略了功能正确性。基于双通道约束理论（该理论指出，代码是一种双通道媒介，既包含供机器执行的算法（AL）通道，也包含供人类交流的自然语言（NL）通道，由此产生了一种独特的安全性—效用权衡：模型必须在功能执行与负责任的交流之间取得平衡），我们提出 NLSafety-Utility 对偶得分（SUDS），一种把代码效用、安全遵从与警示意识统一为单一分数的指标，覆盖 12 种分级的响应场景；以及双重推理（Dual Reasoning, DR），一种结构化的推理期技术，要求模型在生成代码之前先进行显式的安全审计和与任务相关的代码审查。在两个经有害关键词注入增强的基准（分别含 820 和 2,135 个样本）上对五个 LLM 的评估表明，DR 在所有模型上都取得了最高的 SUDS，相较基线把平均 SUDS 提升了 1.32 倍到 3.42 倍；与此同时，思维链提示带来的安全收益可忽略不计，而安全感知提示只带来部分改进。进一步分析显示，DR 的有效性随模型容量而提升；单样例示范主要是为较小模型稳定输出格式；结构化推理无法弥补安全词汇有限的模型的不足。","tl":"提出统一安全与效用的 SUDS 指标及生成前双重审计推理。","au":["Honghao Tan","Haibo Wang","Shin Hwei Tan"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["safety-utility trade-off","code generation","dual channel constraints","SUDS metric","dual reasoning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/55/x"},{"id":"p01075","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fragmented Markers, Mixed Results: A Systematic Review of AI Coding Assistants and Developer Productivity","tz":"碎片化的指标与混杂的结论：AI 编程助手与开发者生产力的系统性综述","a":"AI coding assistants are increasingly embedded in software engineering practice, yet the literature still offers no cumulative, easily interpretable picture of their effects on software developer productivity. The central problem is not a lack of studies, but a lack of comparability: prior work operationalizes productivity through heterogeneous markers, settings, and reporting styles, making cross-study conclusions difficult. To address this, we conduct a staged systematic literature review. In the first stage, we synthesize studies that explicitly examine developer productivity. In the second, we extend the scope to productivity-related developer outcomes using SPACE as a theory-informed lens, capturing human-centered evidence that explicit productivity studies often omit. Across both stages, we analyze how productivity is operationalized, which confounding factors are discussed, and how reported effects are distributed. We identify 187 unique productivity and productivity-related markers, while individual studies typically only use five, revealing a broad but highly fragmented evidence base. Explicit productivity research is dominated by time-, output-, and artifact-oriented proxies, whereas the broader SPACE-aligned corpus makes satisfaction, psychological aspects, and well-being substantially more visible. Reported effects are often positive, but this pattern is stronger in perceived and tendency-based findings than in objective or statistically evaluated ones. Overall, the literature suggests that AI coding assistants can support productivity, but current evidence does not yet support simple, context-independent conclusions. The key contribution of this review is therefore a structured basis for making productivity evidence more interpretable, multidimensional, and comparable across studies.","az":"AI 编程助手正日益嵌入软件工程实践，但文献至今仍未就其对软件开发者生产力的影响给出累积性的、易于解读的图景。核心问题不是研究数量不足，而是缺乏可比性：已有工作通过各不相同的指标、场景和报告方式来操作化生产力，使得跨研究的结论难以得出。为此，我们开展了一项分阶段的系统性文献综述。第一阶段，我们综合了明确考察开发者生产力的研究；第二阶段，我们以 SPACE 作为理论指引扩展范围，纳入与生产力相关的开发者结果，从而捕捉那些显式生产力研究常常忽略的以人为本的证据。在两个阶段中，我们都分析了生产力是如何被操作化的、讨论了哪些混杂因素，以及所报告效应的分布情况。我们识别出 187 个不同的生产力及生产力相关指标，而单项研究通常只使用其中五个，揭示出一个覆盖面广但高度碎片化的证据基础。显式的生产力研究以时间导向、产出导向和制品导向的代理指标为主，而更广义的、与 SPACE 对齐的文献集则让满意度、心理层面与幸福感显著更为可见。所报告的效应往往是正面的，但这一模式在感知类和趋势类发现中比在客观或经统计检验的发现中更为明显。总体而言，文献表明 AI 编程助手能够支持生产力，但当前证据尚不足以支撑简单的、不依赖上下文的结论。因此，本综述的关键贡献在于提供了一个结构化基础，使生产力证据在跨研究之间更可解读、更具多维性、也更可比较。","tl":"系统梳理 187 个碎片化生产力指标，指出证据不支持简单结论。","au":["Annemarie Wittig","Alina Mailach","Norbert Siegmund"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["systematic literature review","AI coding assistants","developer productivity","SPACE framework","productivity markers"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/56/x"},{"id":"p01076","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Reasoning Shapes Social Bias in LLM-Generated Code?","tz":"推理过程如何塑造 LLM 生成代码中的社会偏见？","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used for code generation, yet generated programs may exhibit social bias through unfair or differential treatment of sensitive demographic attributes. While prior work mainly studies direct code generation, bias in reasoning-based generation remains underexplored. We conduct the first systematic study of social bias in reasoning-based code generation, evaluating 9 standard LLMs and large reasoning models (LRMs) on realistic bias-sensitive tasks across three human-centered decision scenarios. We find that reasoning generally reduces bias, lowering the average bias rate from 0.64 to 0.40, but the effect varies substantially across models. Meanwhile, code quality is not consistently preserved, with the average quality dropping from 0.72 to 0.59. Biased reasoning strongly predicts biased code, and adjusting generation configurations alone is insufficient for robust mitigation. Based on these findings, we propose ProbeDebias, a reasoning-aware framework that detects and rewrites biased reasoning traces before code generation. ProbeDebias achieves 87.76% F1 for reasoning-bias detection and reduces code bias by 83.73% on average while largely preserving quality. Compared with SOTA baselines, it further reduces average bias by 52.70%-54.42% and improves quality by 9.79%-36.79%. These results highlight the value of reasoning-stage analysis for trustworthy code generation.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）正越来越多地用于代码生成，但生成的程序可能通过对敏感人口统计属性的不公平或差别化处理而表现出社会偏见。既有工作主要研究直接代码生成，而基于推理的代码生成中的偏见仍缺乏探索。我们开展了首个关于基于推理的代码生成中社会偏见的系统性研究，在三类以人为中心的决策场景下、针对具有现实性的偏见敏感任务，评测了 9 个标准 LLM 与大型推理模型（LRM）。我们发现推理总体上会降低偏见，将平均偏见率从 0.64 降到 0.40，但不同模型之间效果差异很大。同时代码质量未能一致保持，平均质量从 0.72 下降到 0.59。带偏见的推理强烈预示带偏见的代码，而仅调整生成配置不足以实现稳健的缓解。基于这些发现，我们提出 ProbeDebias，一个面向推理的框架，在代码生成之前检测并改写带偏见的推理轨迹。ProbeDebias 在推理偏见检测上达到 87.76% 的 F1，平均将代码偏见降低 83.73%，同时在很大程度上保持了质量。与 SOTA 基线相比，它进一步将平均偏见降低 52.70%–54.42%，并将质量提升 9.79%–36.79%。这些结果凸显了推理阶段分析对可信代码生成的价值。","tl":"首次系统研究推理式代码生成的偏见，并在推理阶段改写去偏。","au":["Weifeng Sun","Jieke Shi","Zhou Yang","Yuchen Chen","Hongyan Li","Meng Yan","David Lo"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["social bias","code generation","large reasoning models","bias mitigation","reasoning traces"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/57/x"},{"id":"p01077","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Runnable Code to Shippable Applications: Test-Driven Development for Full-Stack Web Application Generation","tz":"从可运行代码到可交付应用：面向全栈 Web 应用生成的测试驱动开发","tl":"（据标题推断）用测试驱动开发把生成的代码推进到可上线的全栈应用。","au":["Yuxuan Wan","Tingshuo Liang","Jiakai Xu","Jingyu Xiao","Yintong Huo","Michael Lyu"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["test-driven development","full-stack web application","code generation","shippable application"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/58/x"},{"id":"p01078","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Planner-Fuzz: Overcoming Diagnostic Saturation in UAV Planners via Boundary-Oriented Fuzzing","tz":"Planner-Fuzz：以边界导向的模糊测试克服无人机规划器的诊断饱和","tl":"（据标题推断）用边界导向变异突破 UAV 规划器测试的诊断饱和瓶颈。","au":["Rongbo Chen","Chengcheng Zhao","Peng Cheng","Jiming Chen","Taegyu Kim"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["UAV planner","boundary-oriented fuzzing","diagnostic saturation","safety-critical testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/59/x"},{"id":"p01079","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automated Assertion Generation and Regression Testing for Machine Learning Notebooks","tz":"面向机器学习 Notebook 的自动断言生成与回归测试","a":"In the automotive domain, in-car scene understanding (ISU) enables the detection of safety-critical events, such as driver distraction, and supports drivers or passengers by analyzing the in-car scene and adapting the environment (e.g., ambient lighting). The industry is increasingly exploring vision-language models (VLMs) to interpret camera-recorded in-car scenes and extract information for downstream reasoning tasks. However, VLMs may generate incomplete, erroneous, or misleading scene descriptions, highlighting the need for systematic testing. Collecting real in-vehicle data is costly, difficult to scale, and often infeasible, particularly in early design stages. In this paper, we present ISU-Test, an automated testing approach that combines rendering-based scene generation with search-based testing to evaluate ISU systems. By framing testing as an optimization problem and systematically modifying scene parameters, our method generates diverse in-car scenarios and explores a wide range of configurations. We evaluate ISU-Test on both an industrial prototype and open-source VLMs across two case studies: question answering and captioning, comparing against randomized scenario generation. Results show that ISU-Test significantly outperforms the baseline, achieving up to 10 times higher failure rates and up to 3.6 times higher failure coverage.","az":"在汽车领域，车内场景理解（ISU）能够检测诸如驾驶员分心等安全关键事件，并通过分析车内场景、调整车内环境（例如氛围灯）来辅助驾驶员或乘客。业界正越来越多地探索使用视觉语言模型（VLM）来解释摄像头记录的车内场景，并为下游推理任务提取信息。然而，VLM 可能生成不完整、错误或误导性的场景描述，因此亟需系统化测试。采集真实的车内数据成本高、难以规模化，且常常不可行，在早期设计阶段尤其如此。本文提出 ISU-Test，一种将基于渲染的场景生成与基于搜索的测试相结合的自动化测试方法，用于评估 ISU 系统。我们将测试建模为一个优化问题，通过系统性地修改场景参数，生成多样化的车内场景并探索广泛的配置空间。我们在一个工业原型系统和开源 VLM 上、通过问答与图像描述两个案例研究对 ISU-Test 进行评估，并与随机场景生成进行对比。结果表明 ISU-Test 显著优于基线，失效率最高提升 10 倍，失效覆盖率最高提升 3.6 倍。","tl":"用渲染场景与搜索式测试暴露车内场景理解 VLM 的失效。","au":["Yingao (Elaine) Yao","Vedant Nimje","Varun Viswanath","Saikat Dutta"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["multimodal","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["in-car scene understanding","vision-language model","search-based testing","scenario generation","failure coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/60/x"},{"id":"p01080","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Learning the Lexical Structure of Black-Box Systems by Parsing Systematic String Edit Mutations","tz":"通过解析系统化字符串编辑变异学习黑盒系统的词法结构","a":"A replication package containing our implementation and experimental data for the paper Learning the Lexical Structure of Black-Box Systemsby Parsing Systematic String Edit Mutations accepted at ASE 2026.","az":"本复现包包含论文《Learning the Lexical Structure of Black-Box Systems by Parsing Systematic String Edit Mutations》（已被 ASE 2026 接收）的实现与实验数据。","tl":"（据标题推断）用系统化字符串编辑变异反推黑盒系统的词法规则。","au":["Moeketsi Raselimo","Lars Grunske","Bernd Fischer"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["lexical structure inference","black-box systems","string edit mutations","grammar inference"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/61/x"},{"id":"p01081","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"KQFuzz: Knowledge-Guided Fuzzing for Quantum Libraries via Large Language Models","tz":"KQFuzz：借助大语言模型对量子库进行知识引导的模糊测试","a":"As quantum computing continually improves, ensuring the reliability and correctness of quantum libraries has become increasingly critical. To this end, many LLM-based fuzzing approaches towards quantum libraries have been proposed to uncover potential bugs. However, these methods still suffer from limitations such as insufficient flexibility and low efficiency, which hinder the progress of the quantum computing field. To address these challenges, we propose KQFuzz, a novel knowledge-guided fuzzer for quantum libraries. It leverages comprehensive codebase knowledge to ground LLM-based test generation, synergizing this with fitness-guided evaluation and two-level mutations to explore complex execution paths and trigger potential bugs. Firstly, KQFuzz introduces a novel prompting scheme tailored to quantum programs, which strategically incorporates knowledge of the codebase to efficiently generate high-quality quantum seed programs. Moreover, we develop evaluation and mutation strategies to handle the generated seed programs, facilitating efficient fuzzing execution while further enriching the diversity of the resulting test cases. We implement KQFuzz and conduct fuzzing on three popular quantum libraries, including Qiskit, PennyLane, and Cirq. Experimental results demonstrate that our approach significantly outperforms other state-of-the-art methods, with coverage improved by up to 18.44%. During the development of KQFuzz, we discovered 13 bugs, all of which have been confirmed and 12 have already been fixed by the developers.","az":"随着量子计算持续进步，保证量子库的可靠性与正确性变得愈发关键。为此，已有许多面向量子库的基于 LLM 的模糊测试方法被提出以发现潜在缺陷。然而，这些方法仍存在灵活性不足、效率偏低等局限，阻碍了量子计算领域的发展。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 KQFuzz，一种面向量子库的新型知识引导模糊测试器。它利用全面的代码库知识来支撑基于 LLM 的测试生成，并将其与适应度引导的评估和两级变异协同起来，以探索复杂执行路径并触发潜在缺陷。首先，KQFuzz 引入了一种为量子程序量身定制的新型提示方案，策略性地融入代码库知识，以高效生成高质量的量子种子程序。此外，我们设计了评估与变异策略来处理生成的种子程序，在提升模糊测试执行效率的同时进一步丰富所得测试用例的多样性。我们实现了 KQFuzz，并在 Qiskit、PennyLane 和 Cirq 三个流行量子库上开展模糊测试。实验结果表明我们的方法显著优于其他最新方法，覆盖率最高提升 18.44%。在 KQFuzz 的开发过程中，我们发现了 13 个缺陷，全部得到确认，其中 12 个已被开发者修复。","tl":"用代码库知识引导 LLM 生成量子种子程序并两级变异做模糊测试。","au":["Fuyuan Xia","Qixin Zhang","Chenhao Ying","Haojin Zhu","Shuai Wang","Yuan Luo","Pingchuan Ma","Yuxuan Du"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["quantum libraries","knowledge-guided fuzzing","LLM test generation","Qiskit","two-level mutation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/62/x"},{"id":"p01082","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"What Breaks When LLMs Code? Characterizing Operational Safety Failures of Agentic Code Assistants","tz":"LLM 写代码时会出什么问题？刻画智能体编程助手的运行安全失效","a":"Autonomous coding agents built on large language models (LLMs) are rapidly being integrated into development workflows, yet their operational safety properties remain poorly understood beyond evaluations of explicitly malicious inputs. In practice, high-impact failures arise during benign, goal-directed use through environment breakage, fabricated success reports, etc. that current benchmarks do not capture. What categories of operational safety failures actually occur when coding agents are used for everyday development tasks and what is their impact? We present an incident-driven empirical study grounded in two complementary evidence streams. We screen 68,816 papers from 22 premier venues, curating 185 safety-relevant studies, and mine 16,586 GitHub issues from widely deployed LLM-powered coding tools, manually confirming 547 genuine safety failures. Applying systematic open coding over both corpora, we derive a multi-dimensional safety taxonomy of 33 operational risk types organized across seven dimensions, and annotate each incident with contributing factors, task context, severity, and downstream impact. Our findings show that coding-agent failures are often severe, with 326 of 547 incidents rated high or critical. The dominant risks are constraint violations, destructive operations, authorization bypasses, and deception, and over 65% of incidents arise in bug fixing and setup or configuration, patterns largely missing from prior literature. These results have direct implications for SE tool designers and benchmark developers: guardrails must go beyond adversarial-prompt defenses to enforce environmental constraints, failure transparency, and safe-halt behaviors.","az":"构建在大语言模型（LLM）之上的自主编程智能体正被迅速集成进开发工作流，但除了对显式恶意输入的评测之外，它们的运行安全特性仍知之甚少。实际中，高影响的失效往往发生在良性的、目标导向的使用过程中，例如破坏环境、编造成功报告等，而当前的基准测试无法捕捉这些情况。当编程智能体被用于日常开发任务时，究竟会出现哪些类别的运行安全失效，其影响如何？我们基于两条互补的证据流，开展了一项以事件为驱动的实证研究。我们筛查了来自 22 个顶级会议的 68,816 篇论文，整理出 185 项与安全相关的研究；并从广泛部署的 LLM 驱动编程工具中挖掘了 16,586 个 GitHub issue，人工确认了 547 起真实的安全失效。对两个语料系统地实施开放式编码后，我们得到一个多维安全分类体系，包含分布在七个维度上的 33 种运行风险类型，并为每起事件标注了促成因素、任务上下文、严重程度与下游影响。我们的发现表明，编程智能体的失效往往很严重，547 起事件中有 326 起被评为高危或严重。主要风险是约束违反、破坏性操作、越权绕过与欺骗，且超过 65% 的事件发生在缺陷修复与环境搭建或配置环节，这些模式在既有文献中大多缺失。这些结果对 SE 工具设计者与基准开发者具有直接启示：防护栏必须超越对抗性提示防御，进而强制执行环境约束、失效透明性与安全停机行为。","tl":"以真实事件挖掘出编程智能体 33 类运行安全风险分类体系。","au":["Alif Al Hasan","Sumon Biswas"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["empirical-study","security","agentic"],"kw":["coding agents","operational safety","failure taxonomy","GitHub issue mining","guardrails"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/63/x"},{"id":"p01083","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Compression Becomes an Attack Surface: Black-Box Attacks on Prompt-Compressed LLM Agents","tz":"当压缩变成攻击面：针对提示压缩型 LLM 智能体的黑盒攻击","a":"Prompt compression is increasingly deployed in LLM agents to reduce latency and cost. It determines what the backend LLM ultimately sees, thereby unexpectedly changing the security boundary of the agent pipeline. We show that, when trusted and untrusted inputs are compressed under a shared budget, this lossy transformation exposes a new attack surface in the LLM agents. By perturbing only untrusted inputs before compression, an adversary can cause the compressor to discard task-critical evidence or safety guardrails before LLM inference. Unlike prompt injection, jailbreaks, or RAG poisoning, our attack target is the compressor rather than the backend LLM. The perturbation need not encode a meaningful instruction or even survive compression. We formalize this vulnerability as adversarial information loss (AIL), the excess downstream behavioral distortion caused by adversarially steering a lossy compressor beyond benign compression alone. To exploit AIL, we present COMA, a transfer-based black-box attack that uses attacker-side surrogate compressors and backend LLMs to optimize pre-compression perturbations. COMA first selects a misbehavior-inducing target in compressed space, then searches for a perturbation whose surrogate compression matches that target. Across three tasks (agent tool selection, question answering, and system prompt corruption) and six widely used compressors, COMA achieves an average attack success rate of 0.71, versus 0.21 for the strongest non-compression-based baseline. COMA further generalizes across compression budgets, backend LLMs, and surrogate compressors, transfers to two case studies of real-world agents. We also show that isolating trusted inputs from untrusted inputs during compression improves robustness, especially for system prompt corruption.","az":"提示压缩正越来越多地部署在 LLM 智能体中以降低延迟与成本。它决定了后端 LLM 最终看到的内容，因而出人意料地改变了智能体流水线的安全边界。我们表明，当可信输入与不可信输入在共享预算下被一并压缩时，这种有损变换在 LLM 智能体中暴露出一个新的攻击面。攻击者只需在压缩前扰动不可信输入，就能使压缩器在 LLM 推理之前丢弃任务关键证据或安全防护栏。与提示注入、越狱或 RAG 投毒不同，我们的攻击目标是压缩器而非后端 LLM。扰动无需编码有意义的指令，甚至无需在压缩后幸存。我们将该漏洞形式化为对抗性信息损失（AIL），即相对于良性压缩而言，通过对抗性操纵有损压缩器所额外造成的下游行为畸变。为利用 AIL，我们提出 COMA，一种基于迁移的黑盒攻击，利用攻击者侧的替代压缩器与后端 LLM 来优化压缩前扰动。COMA 首先在压缩空间中选定一个可诱发错误行为的目标，然后搜索使替代压缩结果与该目标匹配的扰动。在三项任务（智能体工具选择、问答与系统提示破坏）和六个广泛使用的压缩器上，COMA 取得平均 0.71 的攻击成功率，而最强的非压缩类基线仅为 0.21。COMA 还能在不同压缩预算、后端 LLM 与替代压缩器之间泛化，并迁移到两个真实智能体的案例研究。我们还表明，在压缩过程中将可信输入与不可信输入隔离可提升鲁棒性，对系统提示破坏尤其有效。","tl":"提出攻击提示压缩器本身的黑盒方法 COMA 与对抗性信息损失概念。","au":["Zesen Liu","Zhixiang Zhang","Yuchong Xie","Dongdong She"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","tg":["security","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["prompt compression","black-box attack","adversarial information loss","LLM agents","attack surface"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/64/x"},{"id":"p01084","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ExplainBench: Evaluating Code Explanations from Agents","tz":"ExplainBench：评估智能体生成的代码解释","a":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents have seen rapid adoption in software engineering. As agents take a greater role in the actual generation of code, they are making larger changes, spanning tens to hundreds of lines. This makes manual review of agent results increasingly infeasible, leading developers to turn to explanations to understand enacted changes. Despite this, there are no benchmarks that evaluate the trustworthiness of agent-generated explanations. To bridge this gap, we propose ExplainBench, a benchmark to automatically evaluate explanations from coding agents. ExplainBench is based on the intuition that informative explanations should enable an LLM to correctly answer questions, allowing quantitative comparison of explanation quality between agents. With this observation, we construct a suite of questions that evaluates whether explanations accurately describe (1) the intended behavior of buggy code and (2) the effect of applying the agent patch itself. Experiments first reveal that explanation quality is a distinct axis of agent evaluation: ExplainBench ranks agents differently from the widely-used SWE-bench Verified benchmark. A deeper breakdown of explanation quality in agents shows frequent problems in explanations, such that explanations often claim that a patch is correct when it is not. Based on this insight, we implement and evaluate an explanation audit agent which runs additional tests to validate and refine explanations. This agent improved the explanations of all evaluated agents, demonstrating agent explanations can be automatically made more trustworthy.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）智能体在软件工程中被迅速采用。随着智能体在代码实际生成中承担更大角色，它们做出的改动也越来越大，跨越数十到数百行。这使得人工审查智能体结果变得愈发不可行，促使开发者转而依赖解释来理解已实施的改动。尽管如此，目前还没有评估智能体生成解释可信度的基准。为填补这一空白，我们提出 ExplainBench，一个自动评估编程智能体解释的基准。ExplainBench 基于这样一个直觉：有信息量的解释应当能让一个 LLM 正确回答问题，从而可以定量比较不同智能体的解释质量。基于这一观察，我们构建了一套问题，用以评估解释是否准确描述了（1）有缺陷代码的预期行为，以及（2）应用智能体补丁本身所产生的效果。实验首先揭示解释质量是智能体评估中一个独立的维度：ExplainBench 对智能体的排名与被广泛使用的 SWE-bench Verified 不同。对智能体解释质量的深入拆解表明，解释中常见问题频发，例如常常声称补丁是正确的而实际上并非如此。基于这一洞见，我们实现并评估了一个解释审计智能体，它会运行额外测试来验证与精化解释。该智能体改进了所有被评估智能体的解释，表明智能体解释可以被自动地变得更可信。","tl":"用问答式度量首次基准化智能体代码解释的可信度并自动审计。","au":["Zhiyuan Pan","Sungmin Kang","Imam Nur Bani Yusuf","Abhik Roychoudhury"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["code explanation","coding agents","benchmark","explanation trustworthiness","SWE-bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/65/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.26451"},{"id":"p01085","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Finding Typing-Related Bugs in JVM Implementations","tz":"在 JVM 实现中发现类型相关的缺陷","tl":"（据标题推断）系统性挖掘 JVM 实现里的类型检查与类型相关缺陷。","au":["Yanzhou Lu","Junjie Chen","Yingquan Zhao","Tianchang Gao","Zan Wang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["JVM implementation","typing bugs","differential testing","runtime testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/66/x"},{"id":"p01086","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Compressing Code Context for LLM-Based Issue Resolution","tz":"为基于 LLM 的 Issue 求解压缩代码上下文","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) are now capable of resolving real-world GitHub issues. However, current approaches overapproximate the code context and suffer from two compounding problems: the prohibitive cost of processing massive inputs, and low effectiveness as noise floods the context window and distracts the model from the bug-fixing signal. Existing compression techniques fail to resolve this tension: generic compressors compromise the semantic integrity of code, while code-specific tools lack awareness of code structure and task context to preserve essential patch ingredients. To address this, we propose a novel framework consisting of two components. First, Oracle-guided Code Distillation (OCD), a context distillation algorithm that combines genetic search and delta debugging to systematically reduce code contexts to their minimal sufficient subsequence - retaining only the ingredients required for a successful fix. We use this distilled data to fine-tune SWEzze, a lightweight model that learns to compress code context at inference time, filtering noise and combating distraction while preserving fix ingredients. Evaluated on SWE-bench Verified across three frontier LLMs, SWEzze maintains a stable compression rate of about 6 times across models, reduces the total token budget by 51.8%-71.3% relative to the uncompressed setting, improves issue resolution rates by 5.0%-9.2%, and delivers the best overall balance among effectiveness, compression ratio, and latency compared with state-of-the-art context compression baselines.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）如今已能解决真实世界的 GitHub issue。然而，当前方法对代码上下文过度近似，面临两个相互叠加的问题：处理海量输入的高昂成本，以及噪声淹没上下文窗口、使模型偏离修复信号而导致的低有效性。现有压缩技术无法化解这一张力：通用压缩器会破坏代码的语义完整性，而面向代码的工具又缺乏对代码结构与任务上下文的感知，无法保留关键的补丁要素。为此，我们提出一个由两部分构成的新框架。首先是 Oracle 引导的代码蒸馏（OCD），一种结合遗传搜索与 delta 调试的上下文蒸馏算法，系统性地将代码上下文缩减为其最小充分子序列——只保留成功修复所需的要素。我们用这些蒸馏数据微调出 SWEzze，一个轻量模型，它学会在推理时压缩代码上下文，在保留修复要素的同时过滤噪声、对抗分心。在 SWE-bench Verified 上、跨三个前沿 LLM 的评测显示，SWEzze 在各模型上维持约 6 倍的稳定压缩率，相对未压缩设置将总 token 预算减少 51.8%–71.3%，将 issue 解决率提升 5.0%–9.2%，并在有效性、压缩比与延迟之间取得优于最新上下文压缩基线的整体平衡。","tl":"用 Oracle 蒸馏出最小充分上下文训练轻量压缩模型 SWEzze。","au":["Haoxiang Jia","Earl T. Barr","Sergey Mechatev"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["context compression","issue resolution","delta debugging","SWE-bench Verified","token budget"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/67/x"},{"id":"p01087","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Dependencies Depend: A Large-Scale Study on Conditional Dependencies and Their Security Implications in C/C++","tz":"当依赖是有条件的：C/C++ 中条件依赖及其安全影响的大规模研究","tl":"（据标题推断）首次大规模刻画 C/C++ 条件依赖及其带来的安全风险。","au":["Yifeng Di","Juewei Zhang","Tianyi Zhang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["conditional dependencies","C/C++","software supply chain","security implications","large-scale study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/68/x"},{"id":"p01088","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Fully Automated Medical Imaging Code Generation via Validation-Based Context Engineering","tz":"迈向全自动医学影像代码生成：基于验证的上下文工程","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated considerable promise in program generation for small-scale and conventional application development; however, they remain limited when applied to complex, domain-specific tasks such as medical image processing. General-purpose models lack explicit domain knowledge and robust validation mechanisms to ensure correctness, often requiring substantial human intervention to produce reliable processing pipelines. To address these limitations, we propose AutoMedImg, a multi-agent framework for fully automated medical image processing code generation. AutoMedImg orchestrates specialised agents across two phases: a Planning Phase that performs dataset analysis and architecture design with semantic and formal verification, and a Coding Phase that generates modules in parallel with static checking, execution testing, and assembly validation. This multi-stage validation mitigates error propagation throughout generation, while comprehensive auto-context engineering combining domain-specific knowledge bases, shared memory, and validation feedback automates context construction without manual prompting. A cross-project adaptive pipeline synthesis mechanism further accumulates validated pipelines and retrieves proven components for new tasks based on project similarity, enhancing generation efficiency through cross-project learning. Extensive evaluation across six diverse and well-established medical imaging datasets with five backbone LLMs demonstrates that AutoMedImg achieves zero human intervention, with Dice scores of up to 0.90 for segmentation tasks and 99% accuracy for classification.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在小规模与常规应用开发的程序生成上已展现出可观潜力；然而，当应用于医学图像处理这类复杂的领域专用任务时，它们仍然受限。通用模型缺乏显式的领域知识与稳健的验证机制来保证正确性，往往需要大量人工干预才能产出可靠的处理流水线。为克服这些局限，我们提出 AutoMedImg，一个用于全自动医学图像处理代码生成的多智能体框架。AutoMedImg 在两个阶段中编排多个专职智能体：规划阶段执行数据集分析与架构设计，并辅以语义验证与形式化验证；编码阶段并行生成各模块，并进行静态检查、执行测试与组装验证。这种多阶段验证抑制了生成过程中的误差传播；同时，融合领域知识库、共享记忆与验证反馈的全面自动上下文工程，无需人工撰写提示即可自动构建上下文。一个跨项目自适应流水线合成机制进一步积累经验证的流水线，并基于项目相似度为新任务检索已验证组件，通过跨项目学习提升生成效率。在六个多样且成熟的医学影像数据集上、使用五个骨干 LLM 的大量评测表明，AutoMedImg 实现了零人工干预，分割任务的 Dice 系数最高达 0.90，分类准确率达 99%。","tl":"用多阶段验证与自动上下文工程实现零干预的医学影像代码生成。","au":["Zixiao Zhao","Jing Sun","Zhe Hou","Cheng-Hao Cai","Qian Liu","Mengze Li","Zijian Zhang","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["medical image processing","multi-agent framework","context engineering","validation-based generation","code generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/69/x"},{"id":"p01089","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Plan to Action: How Well Do Agents Follow the Plan?","tz":"从计划到行动：智能体究竟有多遵循计划？","a":"Agents are commonly instructed to follow a task-specific plan for guidance. However, it is unknown to what extent agents actually follow instructed plans. Without such an analysis, determining the extent agents comply with a given plan, it is impossible to assess whether a solution was reached through correct strategic reasoning or through other means, e.g., data contamination or overfitting to a benchmark. This paper presents the first extensive, systematic analysis of plan compliance in programming agents, examining 21,120 trajectories from SWE-agent across four LLMs on SWE-bench Verified and SWE-bench Pro under eight plan variations. Without an explicit plan, agents fall back on internalized workflows during training, which are often incomplete, overfit, or inconsistently applied. Providing the standard plan improves issue resolution, and we observe that periodic plan reminders can mitigate plan violations and improve task success. A subpar plan hurts performance even more than no plan at all. Surprisingly, inserting additional task-relevant phases in the early stage can degrade performance, particularly when these phases do not align with the model's internal problem-solving strategy. These findings call for fine-tuning paradigms that teach models to follow instructed plans, rather than encoding task-specific plans in them, so that they reason and act adaptively, rather than memorizing workflows.","az":"智能体通常被要求遵循任务专用的计划以获得指导。然而，智能体实际在多大程度上遵循所给计划尚不清楚。缺少这样的分析——即判定智能体对给定计划的遵从程度——就无法评估一个解是通过正确的策略性推理得到的，还是通过其他途径得到的，例如数据污染或对基准的过拟合。本文首次对编程智能体的计划遵从性开展了广泛而系统的分析，考察了 SWE-agent 在四个 LLM 上、于 SWE-bench Verified 与 SWE-bench Pro 上、在八种计划变体下产生的 21,120 条轨迹。在没有显式计划时，智能体会退回到训练中内化的工作流，而这些工作流往往不完整、过拟合或应用不一致。提供标准计划能提升 issue 解决率，我们还观察到周期性的计划提醒可以缓解计划违反并提高任务成功率。较差的计划比完全没有计划更损害性能。令人意外的是，在早期阶段插入额外的任务相关阶段反而会降低性能，尤其当这些阶段与模型内部的问题求解策略不一致时。这些发现呼吁采用新的微调范式，教会模型遵循被指定的计划，而不是把任务专用计划编码进模型，从而使其能够自适应地推理与行动，而非死记工作流。","tl":"用 2 万余条轨迹量化编程智能体的计划遵从性及其反直觉效应。","au":["Shuyang Liu","Saman Dehghan","Jatin Ganhotra","Martin Hirzel","Reyhaneh Jabbarvand"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["plan following","programming agents","SWE-agent","trajectory analysis","SWE-bench Pro"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/70/x"},{"id":"p01090","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Needle in the Repo: Diagnosing Maintainability Failures in AI-Generated Repository Edits","tz":"仓库中的针：诊断 AI 生成仓库改动的可维护性失效","tl":"（据标题推断）识别 AI 仓库级编辑中隐蔽的可维护性劣化模式。","au":["Haichao Zhu","Qian Zhang","Jiyuan Wang","Zhaorui Yang","Yuxin Qiu"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["AI-generated edits","maintainability","repository-level changes","code quality"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/71/x"},{"id":"p01091","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"An Empirical Study of Data Access Practice in Android AR Apps to Understand User Privacy Risks","tz":"理解用户隐私风险：Android AR 应用数据访问实践的实证研究","a":"The zip archive contains all resources necessary to reproduce and replicate the results presented in this paper, including the complete source code, detailed findings, and the comprehensive list of analyzed applications. To reproduce our results, it is encouraged to consult the README.md file included in the archive, which provides step-by-step instructions for setup and execution.","az":"该 zip 压缩包包含复现本文所呈现结果所需的全部资源，包括完整源代码、详细发现以及所分析应用的完整清单。为复现我们的结果，建议查阅压缩包中附带的 README.md 文件，其中提供了环境搭建与执行的分步说明。","tl":"（据标题推断）首次实证刻画 Android AR 应用的数据访问与隐私风险。","au":["Sabbir Hussain Meraj","Long Trac","Xiaoyin Wang","Xusheng Xiao","Wei Wang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Android AR apps","data access practice","user privacy risk","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/72/x"},{"id":"p01092","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Clarity Is Not Assumed: Understanding LLM-Based Code Generation under Ambiguous Requirements","tz":"清晰并非默认：理解歧义需求下基于 LLM 的代码生成","a":"To support the empirical study of requirement ambiguity, we provide an integrated toolkit including the ORCHID benchmark datasets and accompanying evaluation pipelines. The toolkit contains function-level tasks with controlled injection of four ambiguity types (lexical, syntactic, semantic, and vagueness), together with modules for LLM-based code generation and analysis. It enables systematic evaluation of (1) performance impact under ambiguous requirements, (2) functional consistency across generations, and (3) ambiguity recognition and resolution capability. In addition, it provides utilities for quantifying performance degradation, functional divergence, and ambiguity recognition behavior across models.","az":"为支撑对需求歧义的实证研究，我们提供了一个集成工具包，包括 ORCHID 基准数据集及配套评测流水线。该工具包包含函数级任务，并对四类歧义（词法、句法、语义与含糊）进行受控注入，同时提供基于 LLM 的代码生成与分析模块。它支持系统性评估：（1）歧义需求下的性能影响；（2）多次生成之间的功能一致性；（3）歧义识别与消解能力。此外，它还提供用于量化性能退化、功能发散以及跨模型歧义识别行为的实用工具。","tl":"构建受控注入四类需求歧义的 ORCHID 基准评估代码生成。","au":["Di Yang","Xinou Xie","Xiuwen Yang","Ming Hu","Yihao Huang","Yueling Zhang","Weikai Miao","Ting Su","Chengcheng Wan","Geguang Pu"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["ambiguous requirements","ORCHID benchmark","code generation","functional consistency","ambiguity resolution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/73/x"},{"id":"p01093","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Conflict Extraction in Probabilistic Datalog Analyses","tz":"概率 Datalog 分析中的冲突提取","tl":"（据标题推断）从概率 Datalog 分析结果中提取冲突以解释推导矛盾。","au":["Siyu Chen","Chungha Sung","Xuyang Li","Jingbo Wang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["probabilistic Datalog","conflict extraction","static analysis","program analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/74/x"},{"id":"p01094","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"EMERGE: Checking Implementation Equivalence for LLMs via Rule Synthesis","tz":"EMERGE：通过规则合成检查 LLM 的实现等价性","a":"Verifying whether two implementations of the same large language model are equivalent across frameworks is difficult in practice. Even when they implement the same computation, the graphs may differ in operator decomposition, tensor layout, and the use of fused or opaque kernels, making manual rewrite rules hard to build and maintain. We present Emerge, a framework for checking Implementation Equivalence over computation graphs extracted from model implementations. Instead of writing rules manually, Emerge infers candidate relations from execution values, and synthesizes rewrite rules on demand when existing rules are insufficient. Each synthesized rule is then validated using SMT solving when possible and constraint-aware randomized testing for opaque kernels. As these local equivalences accumulate, Emerge eventually establishes whether the two implementations are equivalent. Our implementation targets inference computation graphs captured from HuggingFace Transformers and vLLM. Our evaluation shows that Emerge establishes equivalence for correct implementation pairs at practical cost. It also detects 10 of 13 known implementation bugs, uncovers 8 previously unknown implementation issues that were later confirmed by developers, and localizes the first mismatch when equivalence cannot be established.","az":"在实践中，验证同一个大语言模型在不同框架下的两份实现是否等价十分困难。即便它们实现的是相同计算，其计算图也可能在算子分解、张量布局以及融合或不透明算子的使用上存在差异，使得手工编写与维护重写规则十分困难。我们提出 Emerge，一个在从模型实现中抽取的计算图上检查“实现等价性”的框架。Emerge 不依赖手工编写规则，而是从执行数值中推断候选关系，并在已有规则不足时按需合成重写规则。每条合成的规则随后在可能时用 SMT 求解进行验证，对不透明算子则采用约束感知的随机测试。随着这些局部等价关系不断累积，Emerge 最终判定两份实现是否等价。我们的实现针对从 HuggingFace Transformers 与 vLLM 捕获的推理计算图。评测表明，Emerge 能以可接受的代价为正确的实现对建立等价性；它还检出了 13 个已知实现缺陷中的 10 个，发现了 8 个此前未知、后被开发者确认的实现问题，并在无法建立等价性时定位首个不匹配点。","tl":"按需合成并验证重写规则，自动判定跨框架 LLM 实现等价性。","au":["Qi Zhan","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Shanping Li"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["implementation equivalence","computation graph","rule synthesis","SMT solving","vLLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/75/x"},{"id":"p01095","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SpecTrum: Specification-Guided Differential Fuzzing for Ethereum Consensus Clients","tz":"SpecTrum：面向以太坊共识客户端的规约引导差分模糊测试","a":"Ethereum's consensus safety relies on independent consensus client implementations agreeing on every state transition. When they diverge due to implementation errors, the network can fork, finality can stall, and severe attacks are possible. To prevent such consensus divergences, Ethereum provides a Python reference implementation (consensus-spec), which acts as a specification, and a hand-crafted official test suite (spectests). However, as an executable implementation, Ethereum's specification defines validity implicitly through runtime behavior. As a result, it lacks a systematic way to ensure that all validity conditions are thoroughly evaluated. We present SpecTrum, a framework that addresses this problem in three stages. First, we introduce Consensus-SpecTec, a mechanized specification of the Ethereum consensus algorithm, which makes validity conditions explicit as if-premises. Second, we define premise coverage, a metric that measures which if-premises are evaluated to true and false across spectests. Third, we develop a specification-based test generator that extracts constraints on premises not evaluated to false by spectests and generates inputs to evaluate them. Applying SpecTrum to five major Ethereum consensus clients, we identify 27 cross-client divergence cases, 22 of which cannot be found without the premises inserted in our mechanization. All 27 cases reproduce across fork versions, and extending the mechanized specification to a new fork takes modest effort proportional to the specification difference.","az":"以太坊的共识安全依赖于各个独立的共识客户端实现在每一次状态转换上达成一致。当它们因实现错误而产生分歧时，网络可能分叉、最终性可能停滞，并可能引发严重攻击。为防止此类共识分歧，以太坊提供了一个 Python 参考实现（consensus-spec）作为规约，以及一套手工编写的官方测试套件（spectests）。然而，作为一份可执行实现，以太坊的规约是通过运行时行为隐式地定义有效性的。因此，它缺乏系统性手段来确保所有有效性条件都被充分评估。我们提出 SpecTrum，一个分三阶段解决该问题的框架。第一，我们引入 Consensus-SpecTec，即以太坊共识算法的机械化规约，它将有效性条件显式化为 if 前提。第二，我们定义了前提覆盖率，用以度量在 spectests 中哪些 if 前提被取值为真、哪些被取值为假。第三，我们开发了基于规约的测试生成器，为那些未被 spectests 取值为假的前提提取约束，并生成输入来对其求值。将 SpecTrum 应用于五个主流以太坊共识客户端，我们识别出 27 例跨客户端分歧，其中 22 例若没有我们在机械化规约中插入的前提便无法发现。全部 27 例在各分叉版本中均可复现，且将机械化规约扩展到新分叉所需的工作量与规约差异成正比、较为适中。","tl":"把以太坊规约机械化为 if 前提并以前提覆盖率驱动差分测试。","au":["Seokhun Jeong","Gyeongmin Dan","Sukyoung Ryu","Sungjae Hwang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Ethereum consensus clients","differential fuzzing","mechanized specification","premise coverage","consensus divergence"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/76/x"},{"id":"p01096","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Where Does Balance Break? Boundary Discovery for Game Balance Testing under a Finite Simulation Budget","tz":"平衡在哪里被打破？有限仿真预算下游戏平衡性测试的边界发现","a":"Software testing often relies on assumptions such as reproducible executions and stable correctness criteria. However, many modern software systems exhibit non-deterministic executions and large behavior spaces, making exhaustive exploration impractical and single-run judgments unreliable. These characteristics make it difficult to identify where acceptable behavior ends and problematic behavior begins. Competitive multiplayer games represent a challenging instance of such systems, where balance must be maintained so that no single strategy dominates. Even small parameter changes can trigger abrupt balance disruption, yet detecting such failures requires repeated simulations under non-deterministic outcomes and high-dimensional parameter spaces. In this paper, we formulate game balance regression testing as a boundary-discovery problem under a finite simulation budget. The objective is to efficiently identify inputs near the boundary that separates balanced and unbalanced regions. To address this problem, we propose BBExplorer, which combines multi-directional candidate generation, budget-aware two-stage screening, and adaptive step-size shrinkage for boundary refinement. Experimental results on two games with different levels of complexity show that the approach is strong in low-dimensional settings and remains effective in higher-dimensional ones. It also exhibits stable boundary behavior across unseen random seeds and threshold settings. These results indicate that BBExplorer is effective for practical balance regression testing and, more broadly, for boundary-oriented testing in non-deterministic, budget-constrained systems.","az":"软件测试常常依赖可复现执行与稳定正确性判据等假设。然而，许多现代软件系统表现出非确定性执行与庞大的行为空间，使穷举探索不切实际、单次运行的判断不可靠。这些特性使得难以确定可接受行为在何处终止、问题行为从何处开始。竞技类多人游戏正是此类系统的一个具有挑战性的实例：必须维持平衡，使得没有任何单一策略占据支配地位。即便参数发生微小变化也可能触发突兀的平衡破坏，而检测此类失效需要在非确定性结果与高维参数空间下反复仿真。本文将游戏平衡性回归测试形式化为有限仿真预算下的边界发现问题，目标是高效识别位于分隔平衡区域与失衡区域的边界附近的输入。为此，我们提出 BBExplorer，它结合多方向候选生成、预算感知的两阶段筛选以及用于边界精化的自适应步长收缩。在两款复杂度不同的游戏上的实验结果表明，该方法在低维设定中表现强劲，在较高维设定中依然有效；它在未见过的随机种子与阈值设置下也表现出稳定的边界行为。这些结果表明 BBExplorer 对实际的平衡性回归测试是有效的，更广义地说，也适用于非确定性、预算受限系统中的边界导向测试。","tl":"将游戏平衡回归测试建模为预算受限下的边界发现搜索问题。","au":["Hiroki Mukai","Yusaku Kato","Norihiro Yoshida","Erina Makihara","Katsuro Inoue"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["game balance testing","boundary discovery","simulation budget","non-deterministic systems","regression testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/77/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28364"},{"id":"p01097","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"On the Effects of Customized Configurations of Static Code Analysis Tools: A Prospective Cohort Study of SonarQube Cloud","tz":"静态代码分析工具自定义配置的影响：SonarQube Cloud 的前瞻性队列研究","a":"The growing diversity of code clone types, from syntactic copies to cross-language semantic clones to AI-generated duplicates, has created a fragmentation crisis in clone detection. Current deep learning detectors are domain specialists that degrade significantly outside their training distribution, with F1 drops exceeding 70% across domains. Deploying multiple specialized models is impractical, yet training a single cross-domain detector requires simultaneous access to all training data. To address this, we investigate model merging, a family of post-hoc techniques that operate solely on trained checkpoints. We evaluate parameter merging with five task-vector methods, architecture merging via greedy layer stitching, and cross-tokenizer alignment across four code models, three benchmarks, and twelve configurations. Same-base TIES merging creates effective cross-domain detectors, validated across two model families and three random seeds, reaching 0.865 combined F1 on UniXcoder, 93% of multi-task performance without any training data at the merging step. WUDI achieves the highest in-distribution combined F1 at 0.899, but TIES generalizes better to unseen AI-generated clones, making it our recommended method. Cross-base merging yields only marginal and high-variance gains across all five methods, indicating that task vector compatibility through a shared pre-trained base is the binding factor for effective merging. Merged detectors also outperform zero-shot code LLMs on GPTCloneBench at lower inference cost and generalize up to 4x better than multi-task training to unseen AI-generated clones, suggesting a trade-off between in-domain performance and OOD robustness. This work provides one of the first systematic empirical studies of model merging for software engineering and a practical recipe for building cross-domain clone detectors.","az":"代码克隆类型日益多样——从语法层面的复制，到跨语言的语义克隆，再到 AI 生成的重复代码——已在克隆检测领域造成碎片化危机。当前的深度学习检测器是领域专家，一旦超出训练分布便显著退化，跨领域的 F1 下降超过 70%。部署多个专用模型并不现实，而训练单一的跨领域检测器又要求同时获取所有训练数据。为此，我们研究模型合并，即一类仅在已训练检查点上操作的事后技术。我们在四个代码模型、三个基准与十二种配置上，评测了采用五种任务向量方法的参数合并、通过贪心层拼接的架构合并，以及跨分词器对齐。同基座的 TIES 合并能够构建有效的跨领域检测器，并在两个模型家族与三个随机种子上得到验证，在 UniXcoder 上达到 0.865 的综合 F1，相当于多任务性能的 93%，且合并步骤不需要任何训练数据。WUDI 取得了最高的分布内综合 F1（0.899），但 TIES 对未见过的 AI 生成克隆泛化更好，因此是我们推荐的方法。跨基座合并在全部五种方法上仅带来边际且方差很大的增益，说明通过共享预训练基座获得的任务向量兼容性是有效合并的决定性因素。合并后的检测器在 GPTCloneBench 上以更低推理成本超越零样本代码 LLM，对未见过的 AI 生成克隆的泛化能力比多任务训练高出多达 4 倍，提示分布内性能与分布外鲁棒性之间存在权衡。本工作提供了面向软件工程的模型合并的首批系统性实证研究之一，以及构建跨领域克隆检测器的实用配方。","tl":"首次系统验证模型合并可零训练数据构建跨域克隆检测器。","au":["Sabato Nocera","Sira Vegas","Giuseppe Scanniello"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["code clone detection","model merging","task vectors","TIES","cross-domain generalization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/78/x"},{"id":"p01098","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RefineAct: Automatic Runtime Verification of LLM Agent Actions","tz":"RefineAct：对 LLM 智能体动作的自动运行时验证","tl":"（据标题推断）在运行时自动验证并约束 LLM 智能体执行的动作。","au":["Fraol Batole","Foutse Khomh","Hridesh Rajan"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["agentic","llm-based","security"],"kw":["runtime verification","LLM agent actions","guardrails","agent safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/79/x"},{"id":"p01099","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Verifier-in-the-Loop LLM Solving of Heap Constraints for Concolic Execution","tz":"验证器在环的 LLM 堆约束求解用于 Concolic 执行","tl":"（据标题推断）让 LLM 在验证器回路中求解传统难解的堆约束。","au":["Shaoran Xia","Leyi Cheng","Caihua Dong","Dongdong She","Bo Wang","Xin Peng","Zhen Dong"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["heap constraints","concolic execution","verifier-in-the-loop","constraint solving","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/80/x"},{"id":"p01100","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RealAIGC: Towards More Realistic Evaluation of AI-Generated Code Detection in Real-World Code Repository","tz":"RealAIGC：迈向真实代码仓库中 AI 生成代码检测的更真实评测","a":"AI-generated code (AIGC) from autonomous coding agents are widely adopted across the software development lifecycle. However, AIGC also introduces critical challenges to open-source community governance, making AIGC detection important. Existing AIGC detection benchmarks are fundamentally misaligned with real-world development processes. To address this gap, we construct RealAIGC, a benchmark for AIGC detection grounded in real-world code repositories. RealAIGC is built from the development histories of GitHub and includes pull request (PR) generated by five coding agents alongside human-written code, covering eight major programming languages. It supports multi-granularity detection at the repository, PR, commit, file, and function levels, with more than four million functions. Based on RealAIGC, we conduct a realistic empirical evaluation of 28 AIGC detection methods across three categories. The results show that supervised approaches perform well only in small, homogeneous, single-language repositories, but degrade significantly in mainstream dynamic languages and in large-scale, multi-developer environments. Perplexity based methods are nearly ineffective in realistic settings. No existing method demonstrates general applicability, and all approaches perform unsatisfactorily at the commit and PR levels. This work provides empirical guidance for advancing AIGC detection techniques.","az":"来自自主编程智能体的 AI 生成代码（AIGC）已在软件开发生命周期中被广泛采用。然而，AIGC 也给开源社区治理带来了严峻挑战，使得 AIGC 检测变得重要。现有的 AIGC 检测基准与真实开发过程存在根本性错位。为弥补这一差距，我们构建了 RealAIGC，一个立足真实代码仓库的 AIGC 检测基准。RealAIGC 基于 GitHub 的开发历史构建，包含由五个编程智能体生成的拉取请求（PR）以及人工编写的代码，覆盖八种主流编程语言。它支持仓库、PR、提交、文件与函数等多粒度检测，包含超过四百万个函数。基于 RealAIGC，我们对三大类共 28 种 AIGC 检测方法开展了贴近现实的实证评测。结果表明，有监督方法仅在小规模、同质化的单语言仓库中表现良好，而在主流动态语言以及大规模、多开发者的环境中显著退化。基于困惑度的方法在现实场景中几乎无效。没有任何现有方法展现出通用适用性，且所有方法在提交级与 PR 级上的表现都不令人满意。本工作为推进 AIGC 检测技术提供了实证指导。","tl":"用真实仓库 PR 构建多粒度基准，揭示现有 AIGC 检测普遍失效。","au":["Wentao Chen","Yufei Chen","Huiqun Yu","Guisheng Fan","Kaiwen Zhi","Peite Guo","Jianyuan Yu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["AI-generated code detection","benchmark","real-world repositories","coding agents","multi-granularity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/81/x"},{"id":"p01101","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Hybrid Fuzzing in Input Generation Logic","tz":"输入生成逻辑中的混合模糊测试","tl":"（据标题推断）把混合模糊测试重构到输入生成逻辑层面。","au":["Siwei Wei","Shihao Zhu","Ruijie Meng","Yan Cai"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["hybrid fuzzing","input generation","concolic execution","fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/82/x"},{"id":"p01102","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Understanding the Code and Architectural Smells Generated by LLMs and Autonomous Agents","tz":"理解大语言模型与自主智能体所生成代码中的代码坏味与架构坏味","a":"This is a replication package for the peer review of the paper 'Understanding the Code and Architectural Smells Generated by LLMs and Autonomous Agents'","az":"这是论文《理解大语言模型与自主智能体所生成代码中的代码坏味与架构坏味》用于同行评审的复现包。","tl":"首次系统刻画智能体产出代码的架构坏味。","au":["Yuecai Zhu","Nikolaos Tsantalis","Peter Rigby"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["code smells","architectural smells","LLM-generated code","autonomous agents"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/83/x"},{"id":"p01103","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Toward Inclusive Programming Support for Novice Programmers with Dyslexia: Insights from a Comparative Study","tz":"面向阅读障碍新手程序员的包容性编程支持：一项对比研究的启示","tl":"（据标题推断）用对比实验揭示阅读障碍者的编程支持需求。","au":["Zihan Fang","Janice Chung","Ruijia Chen","Marcia Barnes","Yuhang Zhao","Yu Huang"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["accessibility-inclusion","human-study"],"kw":["dyslexia","novice programmers","inclusive programming","comparative study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/84/x"},{"id":"p01104","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AEG-Edit: Bridging API Evolution and Code Semantics for Accurate API Usage in Code Generation","tz":"AEG-Edit：打通 API 演化与代码语义，实现代码生成中的准确 API 使用","a":"As APIs across standard libraries and software ecosystems evolve, the API knowledge frozen in pre-trained LLMs becomes outdated. Prompt-based methods supply updated documentation at inference time yet suffer from context neglect, often reverting to memorized deprecated usages. Existing parametric approaches, whether fine-tuning or model editing, face two common challenges: they treat API changes as textual fact updates, overlooking the changes in code semantics needed for executable correctness (C1), and lack a mechanism to concentrate updates on positions involved in the API evolution, causing parameter interference beyond the evolution boundary (C2). We propose AEG-Edit, which constructs a heterogeneous API evolution graph, encodes and aligns the graph signal with the LLM hidden space, and concentrates gradient effort on positions involved in the API evolution through API-weighted windowing and optimization. On RustEvo²+ (708 Rust tasks) and PyEvo (622 Python tasks) across two representative open-source LLMs at the 7–8B parameter scale, AEG-Edit achieves statistically significant Pass@1 gains on RustEvo²+, improving over the strongest baseline by up to 6.49% on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct. Ablation and transferability analyses confirm that the heterogeneous API evolution graph drives the gains and transfers to alternative editing backbones.","az":"随着标准库和软件生态中的 API 不断演化，预训练大语言模型中被冻结的 API 知识逐渐过时。基于提示的方法在推理时提供更新后的文档，但会出现上下文忽视问题，常常退回到被记忆下来的已废弃用法。现有的参数化方法，无论是微调还是模型编辑，都面临两个共同挑战：它们把 API 变更当作文本事实更新，忽视了可执行正确性所需的代码语义变化（C1）；并且缺乏把更新集中在与 API 演化相关位置上的机制，导致参数干扰越出演化边界（C2）。我们提出 AEG-Edit，它构建一个异构 API 演化图，将图信号编码并与大语言模型的隐空间对齐，并通过 API 加权窗口化与优化把梯度更新集中到与 API 演化相关的位置。在 RustEvo²+（708 个 Rust 任务）和 PyEvo（622 个 Python 任务）上，针对两个具有代表性的 7–8B 参数规模开源大语言模型，AEG-Edit 在 RustEvo²+ 上取得了统计显著的 Pass@1 提升，在 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct 上最高比最强基线提升 6.49%。消融实验与可迁移性分析证实，异构 API 演化图是性能提升的主要来源，并且能够迁移到其他编辑骨干模型上。","tl":"用异构 API 演化图做定位式模型编辑更新 API 知识。","au":["Yitong Lin","Haoye Tian","Dehai Zhao","Chao Ni","Xiaohu Yang","Xiaoxue Ren"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["model editing","API evolution","code generation","knowledge graph","Pass@1"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/85/x"},{"id":"p01105","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ReqEvolve: User-Oriented Software Self-Evolution through Automatic Requirement Interpretation","tz":"ReqEvolve：通过自动需求解读实现面向用户的软件自演化","a":"The paradigm of software self-evolution enables systems to autonomously extend and reconfigure their own capabilities during execution in response to technical specifications. Yet requests for new functionality often originate from end users and are rarely expressed in technical terms. As a result, developers must translate user needs into technical specifications before the system can evolve, delaying early validation of the requested functionality by preventing users from immediately observing the resulting behaviour. To address this gap, we present ReqEvolve, a runtime code generation system that enables user-driven self-evolution by accepting high-level user requests. The system integrates automatic requirements engineering (RE) and test-driven development (TDD) to transform these requests into executable functionality through clarification, specification decomposition, test generation, and runtime integration. We evaluate ReqEvolve on 72 software evolution cases across 18 projects against two baselines: SpecFix, an RE-focused code generation approach, and an ablation variant of our system. ReqEvolve achieves 89.2% Pass@1, outperforming SpecFix by 18.8% (p < 0.01, r = 0.79, large effect) and the ablation baseline by 32.6% (p < 0.001, r = 0.88, large effect). These results provide initial evidence that user-driven self-evolution is a viable paradigm for autonomously extending software capabilities from user requests, thereby accelerating requirements validation prior to developer verification.","az":"软件自演化范式使系统能够在运行期间根据技术规格自主扩展和重配置自身能力。然而，新功能的诉求往往来自最终用户，且很少以技术术语表达。因此，开发者必须先把用户需求翻译成技术规格，系统才能演化，这延迟了对所请求功能的早期验证，使用户无法立即观察到相应行为。为弥补这一鸿沟，我们提出 ReqEvolve，一个运行时代码生成系统，通过接受高层用户请求来实现用户驱动的自演化。该系统整合了自动需求工程（RE）与测试驱动开发（TDD），通过澄清、规格分解、测试生成和运行时集成，把这些请求转化为可执行的功能。我们在 18 个项目的 72 个软件演化案例上评估 ReqEvolve，并与两个基线对比：面向需求工程的代码生成方法 SpecFix，以及本系统的消融变体。ReqEvolve 取得 89.2% 的 Pass@1，比 SpecFix 高 18.8%（p < 0.01，r = 0.79，大效应量），比消融基线高 32.6%（p < 0.001，r = 0.88，大效应量）。这些结果初步证明，用户驱动的自演化是一种可行范式，可从用户请求出发自主扩展软件能力，从而在开发者验证之前加速需求验证。","tl":"让终端用户的口语化请求直接驱动系统运行时自演化。","au":["Md Asif Iqbal Fahim","Alessio Ferrari"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["software self-evolution","requirements engineering","test-driven development","runtime code generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/86/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/86/ReqEvolve-User-Oriented-Software-Self-Evolution-through-Automatic-Requirement-Interp"},{"id":"p01106","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Testing IFrame Rendering in Web Browsers","tz":"测试 Web 浏览器中的 IFrame 渲染","a":"Source code and results used in paper. Please refer to the readme.md in the file.This includes the results of ICheck for5.2 Effectiveness of Test Oracles5.3 Effectiveness of Bug Detection Capability5.4 Effectiveness of Input Reduction Capability5.5 Ablation Study5.6 Case Studies for Detected Bugs","az":"论文中使用的源代码与实验结果。请参阅文件中的 readme.md。其中包含 ICheck 针对以下部分的结果：5.2 测试预言的有效性；5.3 缺陷检测能力的有效性；5.4 输入约简能力的有效性；5.5 消融实验；5.6 已检出缺陷的案例研究。","tl":"针对浏览器 IFrame 渲染提出专门的测试预言与输入约简。","au":["Dahyeon Park","Seongil Wi","Yuseok Jeon","Mijung Kim"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["browser testing","IFrame rendering","test oracle","input reduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/87/x"},{"id":"p01107","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Real-World Perturbation Testing of Autonomous Driving Systems","tz":"自动驾驶系统的真实世界扰动测试","a":"Autonomous Driving Systems (ADS) must operate reliably under diverse conditions, yet representative data for rare or adverse scenarios is difficult to obtain. Perturbation-based testing is widely used to assess robustness, but most studies focus on offline datasets or simulation, leaving open questions about how such results translate to real-world driving. We present a large-scale study of 72 camera and LiDAR perturbations, evaluated across three testing modalities: offline model-level analysis, hardware-in-the-loop execution, and closed-loop system-level testing on a full-scale autonomous vehicle. The study covers both an end-to-end vision-based driving model and a modular LiDAR-based perception and planning stack. Our results reveal a clear gap between testing levels. For camera-based systems, perturbations with limited offline impact can still induce unstable control and failures in real-world driving. For LiDAR-based systems, degradation is more consistent at the perception level but weakly predictive of system-level failures. Across both modalities, model-level metrics alone are insufficient to identify the most harmful perturbations. We further show that real-time feasibility is a key constraint in real-world testing, and that robustness observations obtained from recorded data do not consistently transfer to closed-loop behavior on a physical vehicle, highlighting the importance of complementary real-world, system-level evaluation.","az":"自动驾驶系统（ADS）必须在多样条件下可靠运行，但罕见或恶劣场景的代表性数据很难获得。基于扰动的测试被广泛用于评估鲁棒性，但大多数研究集中在离线数据集或仿真上，这些结果如何迁移到真实驾驶仍是未解问题。我们呈现一项大规模研究，涵盖 72 种相机与激光雷达扰动，并在三种测试模态下评估：离线模型级分析、硬件在环执行，以及在全尺寸自动驾驶车辆上的闭环系统级测试。该研究同时覆盖端到端基于视觉的驾驶模型和模块化的基于激光雷达的感知与规划栈。我们的结果揭示了不同测试层级之间的明显差距。对基于相机的系统而言，离线影响有限的扰动仍可能在真实驾驶中引发控制不稳定与失效。对基于激光雷达的系统而言，感知层面的性能退化更为一致，但对系统级失效的预测性很弱。在两种模态下，仅靠模型级指标都不足以识别出危害最大的扰动。我们进一步表明，实时可行性是真实世界测试中的关键约束，并且从录制数据中获得的鲁棒性观察结果并不能一致地迁移到实车的闭环行为上，这凸显了开展互补的真实世界系统级评估的重要性。","tl":"实车闭环证明离线扰动指标预测不了系统级失效。","au":["Stefano Carlo Lambertenghi","Matthias Weil","Andrea Stocco"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["autonomous driving systems","perturbation testing","hardware-in-the-loop","closed-loop testing","LiDAR"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/88/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.04953"},{"id":"p01108","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SwiftGram: Dynamic Lexical Forking for Precise and Efficient Grammar-Constrained Decoding","tz":"SwiftGram：面向精确高效语法约束解码的动态词法分叉","a":"This artifact accompanies the paper “SwiftGram: Dynamic Lexical Forking for Precise and Efficient Grammar-Constrained Decoding.” It contains the SwiftGram implementation, experiment scripts, benchmark data, and instructions for reproducing the evaluation.","az":"本制品配套论文《SwiftGram：面向精确高效语法约束解码的动态词法分叉》。其中包含 SwiftGram 的实现、实验脚本、基准数据，以及复现评估结果的说明。","tl":"用动态词法分叉同时提升约束解码的精度与速度。","au":["Shuyi Ling","Liangyi Kang","Jie Liu","Shuai Wang","Zhirou Ma","Dan Ye"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"efficient-inference-quantization-and-ml-systems","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","llm-based"],"kw":["grammar-constrained decoding","lexical forking","structured generation","decoding efficiency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/89/x"},{"id":"p01109","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GraphLedger: Repository-Level Vulnerability Detection via Graph-Based Compression and Assumption Validation","tz":"GraphLedger：基于图压缩与假设验证的仓库级漏洞检测","a":"GraphLedger is an LLM-assisted, repository-level vulnerability detection agent that combines static code property graphs with adaptive context compression and assumption-ledger verification. Given a codebase and vulnerability types (e.g., SQL injection, XSS, path traversal), it analyzes relevant files across commits, generates structured vulnerability findings with evidence traces, and supports reproducible benchmark evaluation on CVEFixes/CWE-Bench-style datasets.","az":"GraphLedger 是一个由大语言模型辅助的仓库级漏洞检测智能体，它把静态代码属性图与自适应上下文压缩、假设账本验证结合起来。给定一个代码库和漏洞类型（例如 SQL 注入、XSS、路径遍历），它会跨提交分析相关文件，生成带证据轨迹的结构化漏洞发现，并支持在 CVEFixes / CWE-Bench 风格的数据集上进行可复现的基准评估。","tl":"用代码属性图压缩加假设账本抑制漏洞误报。","au":["Thi-Hong-Cuc Le","Hoang Quoc Bao Hua","Xuan-Bach Le"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["repository-level vulnerability detection","code property graph","context compression","assumption validation","CWE-Bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/90/x"},{"id":"p01110","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Escaping the Self-Repair Trap: Improving Test Oracle Generation via Dual-Context Awareness","tz":"逃离自修复陷阱：以双重上下文感知改进测试预言生成","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown strong potential for regression-oracle completion, where a test prefix is given and the current program version is treated as expected behavior. Recent approaches increasingly rely on iterative self-repair and execution feedback, but optimizing execution success does not necessarily yield strong fault-revealing oracles. This objective, widely adopted in repair-based methods, serves only as a proxy and may be misaligned with the true goal of oracle generation. Such misalignment biases the repair process, giving rise to a feedback-driven degeneration that we term the Self-Repair Trap, where iterative repair progressively drives models toward assertions that are easier to satisfy but less effective at detecting faults. To address this issue, we propose DCAware, a computationally efficient, non-iterative framework that prioritizes high signal-to-noise contextual grounding over multi-round repair. DCAware integrates structured static context with selectively retrieved dynamic states, enabling precise and robust oracle generation without iterative feedback loops. Extensive experiments based on execution and mutation testing show that DCAware consistently improves fault-revealing effectiveness while maintaining high execution success, outperforming prior methods with substantially lower computational cost. Our results suggest that improving contextual quality is more effective than adding iterative repair complexity in the studied regression-oracle setting.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在回归预言补全任务上展现出很强的潜力：给定测试前缀，并把当前程序版本视为期望行为。近期方法越来越依赖迭代式自修复与执行反馈，但优化执行成功率并不必然产出揭错能力强的预言。这一在基于修复的方法中被广泛采用的目标只是一个代理指标，可能与预言生成的真实目标不一致。这种不一致会使修复过程产生偏差，导致一种由反馈驱动的退化现象，我们称之为“自修复陷阱”：迭代修复会逐步把模型推向更容易被满足、但检测缺陷能力更弱的断言。为解决该问题，我们提出 DCAware，一个计算高效的非迭代框架，它优先追求高信噪比的上下文锚定，而非多轮修复。DCAware 把结构化的静态上下文与有选择检索到的动态状态整合起来，无需迭代反馈循环即可实现精确且稳健的预言生成。基于执行与变异测试的大量实验表明，DCAware 在保持高执行成功率的同时持续提升揭错有效性，以显著更低的计算成本超越了已有方法。我们的结果表明，在所研究的回归预言设定中，提升上下文质量比增加迭代修复的复杂度更为有效。","tl":"指出并绕开迭代自修复使断言越修越弱的陷阱。","au":["Kefan Li","Hongyue Yu","Yuan Yuan"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["test oracle generation","regression oracle","self-repair trap","mutation testing","assertion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/91/x"},{"id":"p01111","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PSearch: Search-Based Patch Generation in the Era of LLM-Based Automated Program Repair","tz":"PSearch：基于大模型的自动程序修复时代下的搜索式补丁生成","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have substantially advanced Automated Program Repair (APR), yet most existing LLM-based APR methods still rely on trial-and-error to generate patches. Such a strategy explores candidate patches in a weakly structured manner, making it difficult to assess the future potential of search directions and allocate search budget effectively. To address this limitation, we propose Psearch, a search-based patch generation framework for LLM-based APR centered on iterative patch evaluation and refinement. Instead of treating patch generation as repeated independent sampling, Psearch maintains a structured search state over intermediate patches, continuously evaluates the promise of explored search paths, and prioritizes the most promising ones for further refinement. This design enables Psearch to abandon weak directions early and progressively approach correct fixes through long-horizon search. Importantly, Psearch can be integrated with different search algorithms, while our current implementation adopts Monte Carlo Tree Search as one effective instantiation. We evaluate Psearch on five widely used bug and vulnerability benchmarks. Experimental results show that Psearch correctly repairs 201 out of 835 bugs in Defects4J, outperforming all 12 state-of-the-art baselines. Psearch also fixes 27 of 79 vulnerabilities in VUL4J and resolves 164 of 300 issues in SWE-Bench-Lite. Moreover, with a patch size of 16, Psearch reduces monetary cost to roughly 50% of strong baselines while maintaining superior repair effectiveness. These results highlight the effectiveness of Psearch for improving LLM-based APR.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）显著推进了自动程序修复（APR），但现有多数基于大模型的 APR 方法仍依赖试错来生成补丁。这种策略以弱结构化的方式探索候选补丁，难以评估搜索方向的未来潜力，也难以有效分配搜索预算。为克服这一局限，我们提出 Psearch，一个以迭代式补丁评估与精化为核心、面向基于大模型 APR 的搜索式补丁生成框架。Psearch 不把补丁生成视为重复的独立采样，而是在中间补丁上维护结构化的搜索状态，持续评估已探索搜索路径的前景，并优先对最有希望的路径继续精化。这一设计使 Psearch 能尽早放弃弱方向，并通过长程搜索逐步逼近正确修复。重要的是，Psearch 可以与不同的搜索算法结合，而当前实现采用蒙特卡洛树搜索作为一种有效实例化。我们在五个广泛使用的缺陷与漏洞基准上评估 Psearch。实验结果表明，Psearch 在 Defects4J 的 835 个缺陷中正确修复了 201 个，优于全部 12 个最先进基线。Psearch 还修复了 VUL4J 中 79 个漏洞里的 27 个，并解决了 SWE-Bench-Lite 中 300 个 issue 里的 164 个。此外，在补丁规模为 16 时，Psearch 将金钱成本降至强基线的约 50%，同时保持更优的修复效果。这些结果凸显了 Psearch 在提升基于大模型 APR 方面的有效性。","tl":"用蒙特卡洛树搜索结构化地分配补丁搜索预算。","au":["hai chuan hu","ye shang","Weifeng Sun","Quanjun Zhang"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated program repair","Monte Carlo Tree Search","patch generation","Defects4J","SWE-Bench-Lite"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/92/x"},{"id":"p01112","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Same Scrutiny, More Time: Eye Tracking Insights into Reviewing LLM-Labelled Code","tz":"同样的审视，更多的时间：评审被标注为 LLM 生成代码的眼动研究","a":"Modern software development increasingly involves the use of large language models (LLMs) to generate code. Despite their rapid advancement, LLMs remain prone to errors and hallucinations, emphasizing the importance of careful code inspection. However, in practice, developers' trust in LLM-generated code and their willingness to review it thoroughly may not align with these recommendations, which is a gap that remains largely unexplored. In this study, we conduct a Wizard-of-Oz experiment to examine how software engineers behave when code is explicitly labelled as LLM-generated during a code review task. We collect both behavioral data and participant feedback through eye-tracking and exit interviews. Combining Bayesian data analysis with qualitative analysis, we found that while the thoroughness of code review did not change for participants, they spent more time fixating on LLM-labelled code, indicating that the label itself influences attention. Practitioners also adapted their review strategy for LLM-labelled code by assessing the code based on specific criteria (e.g., logical correctness), or using the prompt to guide their review. These findings inform LLM-based tool design on labelling while incorporating the prompt as a software artifact. Our study reveals a gap between reviewers' intentions and actual reviewing behaviour, highlighting the need for software companies to revisit their AI policies (particularly regarding LLM-assisted development) to better support developers in reviewing LLM-generated code.","az":"现代软件开发越来越多地使用大语言模型（LLM）来生成代码。尽管大语言模型进展迅速，它们仍容易出错和产生幻觉，这凸显了仔细进行代码审查的重要性。然而在实践中，开发者对大模型生成代码的信任程度以及彻底评审的意愿，可能与这些建议并不一致，而这一落差在很大程度上尚未被研究。在本研究中，我们开展了一项“绿野仙踪”（Wizard-of-Oz）实验，考察当代码在代码评审任务中被明确标注为大模型生成时，软件工程师的行为如何变化。我们通过眼动追踪和退出访谈同时收集行为数据与被试反馈。结合贝叶斯数据分析与定性分析，我们发现：虽然被试的代码评审彻底程度没有改变，但他们在被标注为 LLM 生成的代码上注视时间更长，这表明标签本身会影响注意力分配。从业者还会针对带 LLM 标签的代码调整评审策略，例如依据特定标准（如逻辑正确性）评估代码，或利用提示词来引导评审。这些发现可为基于大模型的工具在标注设计上提供启示，同时提示应把提示词纳入软件制品。我们的研究揭示了评审者意图与实际评审行为之间的落差，强调软件公司需要重新审视其 AI 政策（尤其是涉及 LLM 辅助开发的部分），以更好地支持开发者评审大模型生成的代码。","tl":"LLM 标签只增加注视时长，并未提高评审彻底度。","au":["Ranim Khojah","Francisco Gomes de Oliveira Neto","Mazen Mohamad","Julian Frattini","Philipp Leitner"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["human-study","llm-based"],"kw":["eye tracking","code review","LLM-generated code","Wizard-of-Oz","developer trust"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/93/x"},{"id":"p01113","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Breaking Customized LLMs for Coding: Automated Red Teaming for Instruction Backdoor Attacks","tz":"攻破面向编程的定制化大语言模型：针对指令后门攻击的自动红队","a":"LLM customization platforms allow users to build task-specific models for code intelligence tasks by embedding instructions into system prompts, without modifying the underlying model parameters. While these platforms lower the barrier to developing customized LLMs, they also introduce a new attack surface: instruction backdoor attacks, in which adversaries implant hidden malicious behaviors into customized instructions. However, existing attacks suffer from two key limitations. First, they often rely on explicit trigger patterns readily detected by platform-side or user-side inspection. Second, they require substantial manual effort to craft task-specific backdoored instructions, limiting their scalability. In this paper, we propose ARIA, an automated red-teaming framework for crafting covert and effective backdoored instructions against customized LLMs. ARIA leverages an attacker LLM to iteratively generate and refine backdoored instructions, guided by structured feedback from the target LLM along three dimensions: stealthiness, clean-task utility, and backdoor effectiveness. We evaluate ARIA on three code intelligence tasks, using four representative LLMs, and compare it with three baseline attacks. Experimental results show that ARIA achieves the highest attack success rate of 0.945, while maintaining the best clean-task utility across all tasks. ARIA also generalizes well across programming languages and remains robust to generation temperature. Furthermore, ARIA significantly outperforms existing attacks in evading platform-side and user-side detection, achieving a false negative rate of up to 1.000, and stays effective against existing defense methods, demonstrating its strong generalizability and robustness.","az":"大语言模型定制平台允许用户把指令嵌入系统提示，从而为代码智能任务构建特定任务模型，而无需修改底层模型参数。这些平台降低了开发定制化大模型的门槛，但也带来了新的攻击面：指令后门攻击，即攻击者把隐藏的恶意行为植入定制指令中。然而，现有攻击存在两个关键局限。第一，它们往往依赖显式触发模式，容易被平台侧或用户侧的检查发现。第二，它们需要大量人工来构造针对特定任务的后门指令，限制了可扩展性。本文提出 ARIA，一个自动红队框架，用于构造针对定制化大模型的隐蔽而有效的后门指令。ARIA 利用一个攻击者大模型迭代地生成并精化后门指令，并由目标大模型在三个维度上给出的结构化反馈加以引导：隐蔽性、干净任务效用和后门有效性。我们在三个代码智能任务上评估 ARIA，使用四个具有代表性的大语言模型，并与三种基线攻击比较。实验结果表明，ARIA 取得了最高的攻击成功率 0.945，同时在所有任务上保持最佳的干净任务效用。ARIA 还能很好地跨编程语言泛化，并对生成温度保持稳健。此外，ARIA 在规避平台侧与用户侧检测方面显著优于现有攻击，假阴性率最高达到 1.000，并且对已有防御方法仍然有效，展示了其很强的泛化性与稳健性。","tl":"自动生成无显式触发词的隐蔽指令后门。","au":["Yuchen Chen","Wei Cheng","Yuan Xiao","Weisong Sun","Chunrong Fang","Yang Liu","Zhenyu Chen","Baowen Xu"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["security","llm-based"],"kw":["instruction backdoor","red teaming","customized LLM","code intelligence","attack success rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/94/x"},{"id":"p01114","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"On the Reliability of Code Comprehension Proxies","tz":"论代码可理解性代理指标的可靠性","a":"Prior work on code comprehension uses different comprehension proxies-for example, Likert-scale ratings or answers to input-output questions about program snippets, usually collected from students, to approximate whether code is comprehensible to software engineers, but the relative reliability of these proxies is not known. This paper investigates the relative reliability of a collection of proxies common in the extant literature with a pair of human studies. First, we conducted an expert-consensus study with a panel of five professional software engineers to establish a ground-truth comprehensibility ranking of eight code snippets by adapting the Delphi expert-consensus protocol. The Delphi protocol is widely used for expert consensus under conditions of uncertainty in other domains, such as medicine and national-security forecasting, but to our knowledge, this is its first application in software engineering. Second, we conducted a study with 44 student participants who completed tasks, allowing us to measure 14 comprehension proxies derived from the literature on the same set of eight code snippets. Finally, we conducted a correlation analysis on the results, concluding that proxies 1) derived from input-output questions and 2) that measure response time rather than accuracy are especially reliable. We also found that proxies derived from questions about program syntax (rather than semantics) are especially unreliable, regardless of measurement strategy, which draws into question the reliability of parts of the existing comprehensibility literature.","az":"以往关于代码理解的研究使用了各种不同的理解代理指标——例如李克特量表评分，或对程序片段输入输出问题的回答，通常来自学生被试——以近似判断代码对软件工程师是否易于理解，但这些代理指标的相对可靠性尚不清楚。本文通过一对人类研究，考察文献中常见的一组代理指标的相对可靠性。第一，我们与五位专业软件工程师组成的专家小组开展了一项专家共识研究，通过改编德尔菲（Delphi）专家共识流程，为八个代码片段建立可理解性的真值排序。德尔菲流程在医学、国家安全预测等其他领域被广泛用于不确定条件下的专家共识，但据我们所知，这是它首次被应用于软件工程。第二，我们开展了一项有 44 名学生被试完成任务的研究，使我们能够在同一组八个代码片段上测量文献中衍生出的 14 种理解代理指标。最后，我们对结果进行了相关性分析，得出结论：1）源自输入输出问题的代理指标，以及 2）测量响应时间而非准确率的代理指标，尤其可靠。我们还发现，源自关于程序语法（而非语义）问题的代理指标尤其不可靠，无论采用何种测量策略，这对现有可理解性文献中部分工作的可靠性提出了质疑。","tl":"首次用德尔菲专家共识检验 14 种可理解性代理。","au":["Erfan Arvan","Nadeeshan De Silva","Oscar Chaparro","Martin Kellogg"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["human-study","empirical-study"],"kw":["code comprehension","proxy reliability","Delphi protocol","human study","construct validity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/95/x"},{"id":"p01115","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Discovering Performance Archetypes: Critical-Path-Aware Pattern Analysis and Regression Detection","tz":"发现性能原型：关键路径感知的模式分析与回归检测","tl":"（据标题推断）把关键路径模式抽象成可复用的性能原型。","au":["Kaveh Shahedi","Heng Li","Maxime Lamothe","Foutse Khomh"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study"],"kw":["performance regression","critical path analysis","pattern mining","performance archetypes"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/96/x"},{"id":"p01116","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Barista: Synthesizing Typestate Specifications with LLM Agents","tz":"Barista：用大语言模型智能体合成 Typestate 规约","tl":"（据标题推断）让 LLM 智能体自动写出可检验的 typestate 规约。","au":["Catarina Gamboa","Paulo Canelas","Ricardo Costa","Marcio Caetano","Jonathan Aldrich","Alcides Fonseca"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["typestate specification","specification synthesis","LLM agents","formal specification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/97/x"},{"id":"p01117","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Longitudinal Study of Android Apps Signing Key Protection","tz":"Android 应用签名密钥保护的纵向研究","a":"Android app signing relies on developer-managed credentials, making secure key protection essential for the integrity of the software supply chain. A recent platform key leakage incident involving two major OEM manufacturers demonstrates that even robustly designed signing mechanisms can be compromised due to developers' oversight. In this work, we conduct a longitudinal ecosystem study to characterize this threat by mining public repositories for Android signing credentials, recovering compromised keys via exposed passwords, and matching them against signatures from over 4,000 apps collected from major stores and OEM system images. Our analysis identifies 5,673 compromised keystores on GitHub and 26 unique certificates linked to 278 real-world apps. These include 26 third-party apps in public app stores and 252 preinstalled apps from seven manufacturers, collectively affecting over 10 billion users. We demonstrate the practical exploitability of these leaks through a proof-of-concept app replacement attack and identify spillover risks in non-smartphone platforms, including a popular automotive head-unit platform installed in over 1,100 vehicle models. Our results reveal that signing-key mismanagement is a systemic risk, underscoring the need for a more rigorous key-management support in Android release engineering and distribution infrastructures.","az":"Android 应用签名依赖开发者自行管理的凭据，因此安全的密钥保护对软件供应链的完整性至关重要。近期一起涉及两家主要 OEM 厂商的平台密钥泄露事件表明，即便设计稳健的签名机制，也可能因开发者疏忽而被攻破。在本工作中，我们开展了一项纵向生态研究以刻画这一威胁：挖掘公开仓库中的 Android 签名凭据，通过暴露的口令恢复被泄露的密钥，并将其与从主流应用商店和 OEM 系统镜像中收集的 4000 多个应用的签名进行匹配。我们的分析在 GitHub 上识别出 5673 个被泄露的 keystore，以及与 278 个真实应用关联的 26 个唯一证书。其中包括公开应用商店中的 26 个第三方应用，以及来自七家厂商的 252 个预装应用，累计影响超过 100 亿用户。我们通过一个概念验证的应用替换攻击展示了这些泄露的实际可利用性，并识别出在非智能手机平台上的外溢风险，包括一个安装在 1100 多款车型上的流行汽车车机平台。我们的结果表明，签名密钥管理不当是一种系统性风险，凸显了在 Android 发布工程与分发基础设施中提供更严格密钥管理支持的必要性。","tl":"实证挖出 5673 个泄露签名密钥并验证可替换攻击。","au":["Mark Meng","Qing Zhang","Weirao Lu","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["security","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["Android app signing","key leakage","software supply chain","keystore","preinstalled apps"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/98/x"},{"id":"p01118","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Clarity: From Formal System Designs to Verified RL Controllers","tz":"Clarity：从形式化系统设计到经过验证的强化学习控制器","tl":"（据标题推断）把形式化设计直接编译成可验证的 RL 控制器。","au":["Austin O'Quinn","Conor Snedeker","Max Taylor","Lance Joneckis","Christopher Stewart"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["formal system design","verified controller","reinforcement learning","controller synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/99/x"},{"id":"p01119","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Towards Verifiable Fairness Testing: Auditable Coverage over Data-Supported Input Domains","tz":"迈向可验证的公平性测试：面向有数据支撑输入域的可审计覆盖","a":"The replication package for this paper, including the source code, experimental scripts, configuration files, and supporting materials required to reproduce the reported results, is publicly archived on this repository.","az":"本文的复现包已公开归档于该仓库，其中包含复现所报告结果所需的源代码、实验脚本、配置文件和支撑材料。","tl":"给公平性测试补上可审计的输入域覆盖判据。","au":["Yingqian Guo","Wentian Zhao","Tian Song"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["fairness testing","auditable coverage","input domain","verifiable testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/100/x"},{"id":"p01120","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PL4SA: Optimized Partial Library Selection for Efficient Static Analysis","tz":"PL4SA：面向高效静态分析的最优部分库选择","tl":"（据标题推断）只加载必要的部分库即可加速静态分析。","au":["Guohao Feng","Yifei Lu","Minxue Pan"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static analysis","partial library selection","analysis scalability","call graph"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/101/x"},{"id":"p01121","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"VeriSBOM: Secure and Verifiable SBOM Sharing via Zero-Knowledge Proofs","tz":"VeriSBOM：基于零知识证明的安全可验证 SBOM 共享","a":"A Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) is a key component for the transparency of software supply chain; it is a structured inventory of the components, dependencies, and associated metadata of a software artifact. However, an SBOM often contain sensitive information that organizations are unwilling to disclose in full to anyone, for two main concerns: technological risks deriving from exposing proprietary dependencies or unpatched vulnerabilities, and business risks, deriving from exposing architectural strategies. Therefore, delivering a plaintext SBOM may result in the disruption of the intellectual property of a company. To address this, we present VeriSBOM, a trustless, selectively disclosed SBOM framework that provides cryptographic verifiability of SBOMs using zero-knowledge proofs. Within VeriSBOM, third parties can validate specific statements about a delivered software. Respectively, VeriSBOM allows independent third parties to verify if a software contains authentic dependencies distributed by official package managers and that the same dependencies satisfy rigorous policy constraints such as the absence of vulnerable dependencies or the adherence with specific licenses models. VeriSBOM leverages a scalable vector commitment scheme together with folding-based proof aggregation to produce succinct zero-knowledge proofs that attest to security and compliance properties while preserving confidentiality. Crucially, the verification process requires no trust in the SBOM publisher beyond the soundness of the underlying primitives, and third parties can independently check proofs against the public cryptographic commitments. We implement VeriSBOM, analyze its security, and evaluate its performance on real-world package registries. The results show that our method enables scalable, privacy-preserving, and verifiable SBOM sharing and validation.","az":"软件物料清单（SBOM）是软件供应链透明度的关键组成部分；它是一份关于软件制品的组件、依赖及相关元数据的结构化清单。然而，SBOM 往往包含组织不愿向任何人完整披露的敏感信息，原因主要有二：暴露专有依赖或未修补漏洞带来的技术风险，以及暴露架构策略带来的商业风险。因此，交付明文 SBOM 可能会损害一家公司的知识产权。为解决这一问题，我们提出 VeriSBOM，一个无需信任、支持选择性披露的 SBOM 框架，利用零知识证明提供 SBOM 的密码学可验证性。在 VeriSBOM 中，第三方可以验证关于所交付软件的特定陈述。相应地，VeriSBOM 允许独立第三方验证某个软件是否包含由官方包管理器分发的真实依赖，以及这些依赖是否满足严格的策略约束，例如不含有漏洞的依赖或符合特定许可证模型。VeriSBOM 利用可扩展的向量承诺方案，结合基于折叠（folding）的证明聚合，生成简洁的零知识证明，在保持机密性的同时证明安全性与合规性属性。关键在于，除底层原语的可靠性之外，验证过程无需对 SBOM 发布者有任何信任，第三方可以独立地针对公开的密码学承诺检查证明。我们实现了 VeriSBOM，分析了其安全性，并在真实世界的包注册表上评估了性能。结果表明，我们的方法能够实现可扩展、隐私保护且可验证的 SBOM 共享与校验。","tl":"用向量承诺加折叠证明实现 SBOM 选择性披露。","au":["Gianpietro Castiglione","Shahriar Ebrahimi","Narges Khakpour"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["SBOM","zero-knowledge proofs","software supply chain","selective disclosure","vector commitment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/102/x"},{"id":"p01122","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Bifrost: Empowering Pretrained Language Model with Fallibility Representation for Log-Based Fault Diagnosis","tz":"Bifrost：以易错性表示增强预训练语言模型的基于日志的故障诊断","a":"Log-based fault diagnosis is crucial for runtime debugging and maintenance. Existing fault diagnosis methods use language models pre-trained on natural language (PLMs) for log representation. However, system faults are reflected in the multi-level structure of system logs. PLMs pre-trained on natural language struggle to comprehensively capture multi-level fault information, failing to meet the requirements of fault diagnosis. We refer to this information as fallibility representations. To address this problem, we propose a novel log representation learning method, Bifrost. It draws inspiration from the log analysis experience of Site Reliability Engineers and meticulously designs strategies based on self-supervised contrastive learning to learn the fallibility representations of logs. Across three public systems and one industrial ML-as-a-Service system, the log representations produced by Bifrost outperform existing PLMs by average margins of 9.83% in F1 for anomaly detection, 18.28% in HR@k for root cause localization, and 20.88% in Macro-F1 for fault identification.","az":"基于日志的故障诊断对运行时调试与维护至关重要。现有故障诊断方法使用在自然语言上预训练的语言模型（PLM）进行日志表示。然而，系统故障体现在系统日志的多层次结构之中。在自然语言上预训练的 PLM 难以全面捕捉多层次的故障信息，无法满足故障诊断的要求。我们把这类信息称为易错性表示（fallibility representations）。为解决该问题，我们提出一种新的日志表示学习方法 Bifrost。它借鉴站点可靠性工程师（SRE）的日志分析经验，基于自监督对比学习精心设计策略，以学习日志的易错性表示。在三个公开系统和一个工业级 ML-as-a-Service 系统上，Bifrost 产生的日志表示在异常检测的 F1 上平均超过现有 PLM 9.83%，在根因定位的 HR@k 上平均超出 18.28%，在故障识别的 Macro-F1 上平均超出 20.88%。","tl":"用对比学习习得日志的多层次“易错性”表示。","au":["Minghua He","Tong Jia","Lingzhe Zhang","Chiming Duan","Xinlong Zhao","Leyi Pan","Cheng Wang","Kangjin Wang","Yinghao Yu","Liping Zhang","Yifan Wu","Ying Li"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["log-based fault diagnosis","contrastive learning","log representation","root cause localization","anomaly detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/103/x"},{"id":"p01123","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"All or Nothing: How Library Type Annotations Affect Client-Side Errors in Python","tz":"全有或全无：Python 库类型注解如何影响客户端错误","a":"This artifact contains scripts, datasets, and experimental pipelines for All or Nothing: How Library Type Annotations Affect Client-Side Errors in Python If you only want to reproduce the main results, READ starter.md and start with the **Questions Folder**. Additional details are provided in the starter.md for full reproducibility from scratch. Additional scripts and plots can be found under ASE_plots.","az":"本制品包含论文《全有或全无：Python 库类型注解如何影响客户端错误》所用的脚本、数据集和实验流水线。如果你只想复现主要结果，请阅读 starter.md 并从 **Questions 文件夹** 开始。starter.md 中还提供了从零开始完整复现的更多细节。额外的脚本与绘图位于 ASE_plots 目录下。","tl":"实证显示库类型注解需全覆盖才对客户端有效。","au":["Eric Asare","Luca Di Grazia","Sarah Nadi"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["type annotations","Python","client-side errors","gradual typing","type checking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/104/x"},{"id":"p01124","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Tensor-Based Batch Fuzzing with Adaptive Perturbation Scaling for Deep Neural Networks","tz":"面向深度神经网络的张量化批量模糊测试与自适应扰动缩放","a":"Deep neural networks are increasingly deployed in safety-critical domains such as autonomous driving and medical diagnosis, yet their opaque, high-dimensional parameter spaces make it difficult to systematically assess model reliability on unseen inputs. Existing coverage-guided sequential fuzzing frameworks for DNNs inherit a one-input-per-iteration design from traditional software fuzzing and apply uniform perturbation budgets across all input dimensions, limiting both testing throughput (i.e., inputs processed per unit time) and the precision of input-space exploration. We present a new specification-aware batch fuzzing framework with adaptive perturbation scaling that addresses both limitations. Rather than relying on a fixed global perturbation radius epsilon, our approach derives mutation step sizes from specification-defined feasible ranges (the gap between lower and upper bounds) using a shared scale factor. This scaling can be applied either as a global scalar (isotropic) or as per-dimension step sizes (anisotropic), keeping perturbations consistent with the underlying constraint structure. As a result, the fuzzer can explore input spaces with heterogeneous feature scales more effectively across all specifications in the batch. We embed input constraints and output property checks directly into the network as non-trainable layers, yielding a wrapped model that processes B specification instances in a single batched iteration, substantially improving fuzzing efficiency and counterexample exploration. We evaluate our framework extensively on three benchmarks, covering six networks and over 400 specifications across TrafficSigns, Cifar100, and TinyImageNet. Our tensor-based fuzzing achieves up to 40X higher throughput and 4X more violations than the sequential baseline under the same time budget, demonstrating significantly improved effectiveness in specification-guided fuzzing.","az":"深度神经网络越来越多地被部署在自动驾驶、医疗诊断等安全攸关领域，但其不透明的高维参数空间使得系统性评估模型在未见输入上的可靠性十分困难。现有面向 DNN 的覆盖率引导顺序模糊测试框架沿袭了传统软件模糊测试“每次迭代一个输入”的设计，并在所有输入维度上施加统一的扰动预算，这既限制了测试吞吐量（即单位时间处理的输入数），也限制了输入空间探索的精度。我们提出一种新的规约感知批量模糊测试框架，配合自适应扰动缩放，同时解决上述两个局限。我们的方法不依赖固定的全局扰动半径 epsilon，而是使用共享的缩放因子，从规约定义的可行范围（上下界之间的差距）中推导变异步长。该缩放既可作为全局标量（各向同性）应用，也可作为逐维步长（各向异性）应用，使扰动与底层约束结构保持一致。因此，模糊测试器能够在批次内所有规约上更有效地探索具有异构特征尺度的输入空间。我们把输入约束与输出属性检查直接以不可训练层的形式嵌入网络，得到一个包装后的模型，它可以在一次批量迭代中处理 B 个规约实例，大幅提升模糊测试效率与反例探索能力。我们在三个基准上进行了广泛评估，覆盖 TrafficSigns、Cifar100 和 TinyImageNet 上的六个网络和 400 多条规约。在相同时间预算下，我们基于张量的模糊测试相比顺序基线取得最高 40 倍的吞吐量和 4 倍的违例数，展示出在规约引导模糊测试中显著提升的有效性。","tl":"把 DNN 模糊测试改成张量批量并按规约自适应缩放扰动。","au":["Guanqin Zhang","Yulei Sui"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DNN testing","batch fuzzing","adaptive perturbation scaling","specification-guided","counterexample"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/105/x"},{"id":"p01125","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ChangeWiki: Repository-Level Change Summarization Augmented with Architecture Semantics","tz":"ChangeWiki：以架构语义增强的仓库级变更摘要","tl":"（据标题推断）把架构语义注入仓库级变更摘要生成。","au":["Zijun Wang","Wuxia Jin","Jiale Li","Zhanhong Mou","Ting Liu"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["change summarization","repository-level","architecture semantics","documentation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/106/x"},{"id":"p01126","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Refine2Diff: Detecting Protocol Specification–Implementation Inconsistencies via Specification-Driven Code Refinement","tz":"Refine2Diff：通过规约驱动的代码精化检测协议规约与实现之间的不一致","tl":"（据标题推断）把规约逐步精化成代码以对比出协议实现偏差。","au":["Yuekun Wang","Lili Quan","Xiaofei Xie"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["protocol specification","specification-implementation inconsistency","code refinement","formal specification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/107/x"},{"id":"p01127","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Free Is More: Empowering Software Agents via Issue-Free Trajectory Learning and Entropy-Aware RLVR Training","tz":"Free Is More：用无 Issue 轨迹学习与熵感知 RLVR 训练强化软件智能体","a":"Production deployment of AI coding agents requires fast, reproducible evaluation signals. Existing industrial practices trade off speed and fidelity: online A/B testing takes weeks and risks user experience, shadow deployment yields signals that are not reproducible across runs, and public benchmarks diverge from production workloads in language distribution, prompt style, and codebase structure. This paper presents REAP (Relevance and Execution-Audited Pipeline), an automated curation pipeline that constructs production-derived benchmarks from real developer-agent sessions without manual labeling. Such curation, while in-distribution to production usage, runs into several challenges. Untestable prompts, misaligned tests, and test flakiness all compromise evaluation reliability. While tasks can be manually audited to ensure only high-quality tasks remain in the benchmark, this approach is infeasible in the monorepo setting: the build infrastructure state is often ephemeral in large monorepos and requires the benchmark to be continuously re-curated against the current codebase. As manual verification cannot be sustained at this cadence, REAP adds an automated verification layer using LLM-based task classification, agentic test-relevance validation, and multi-run stability checks to ensure the executable benchmark yields trustworthy signals. We use REAP to curate Harvest, a benchmark where each task feeds the coding agent a real developer prompt and verifies the resulting code change against fail-to-pass tests retrieved from production. Harvest's distribution spans more than four programming languages with a majority of tasks drawn from Hack. Model and harness evaluations reveal that solve rates range from 42.9% to 58.2% across five frontier models, surfacing capability differences that inform concrete deployment decisions.","az":"AI 编程智能体的生产部署需要快速、可复现的评测信号。现有工业实践在速度与保真度之间存在权衡：在线 A/B 测试需要数周并可能损害用户体验，影子部署给出的信号在多次运行之间不可复现，而公开基准在语言分布、提示风格和代码库结构上都与生产负载存在偏离。本文提出 REAP（Relevance and Execution-Audited Pipeline，相关性与执行审计流水线），这是一条自动化的数据构建流水线，它无需人工标注，就能从真实的开发者—智能体会话中构建源自生产环境的基准。这种构建方式虽然与生产使用同分布，却会遇到若干挑战：不可测试的提示、错配的测试以及测试的不稳定性都会损害评测的可靠性。虽然可以通过人工审计任务来保证基准中只保留高质量任务，但在 monorepo 场景下这种做法不可行：大型 monorepo 中构建基础设施的状态往往是短暂的，要求基准针对当前代码库持续地重新构建。由于人工验证无法按这种节奏持续进行，REAP 增加了一层自动验证机制，使用基于 LLM 的任务分类、智能体式的测试相关性校验以及多次运行的稳定性检查，以确保这个可执行基准能产出可信的信号。我们用 REAP 构建了 Harvest 基准，其中每个任务都向编程智能体输入一条真实的开发者提示，并用从生产环境中检索到的 fail-to-pass 测试来验证由此产生的代码变更。Harvest 的分布覆盖四种以上编程语言，其中大多数任务来自 Hack。对模型与脚手架的评测显示，五个前沿模型的解决率在 42.9% 到 58.2% 之间，暴露出的能力差异可为具体的部署决策提供依据。","tl":"用无 issue 轨迹学习加熵感知 RLVR 来训练软件智能体。","au":["Xin-Cheng Wen","Binbin Chen","Haoxuan Lan","Hang Yu","Peng Di","Cuiyun Gao"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["llm-based","agentic","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["software agents","trajectory learning","RLVR","entropy-aware training"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/108/x"},{"id":"p01128","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Quantum Bugs Live and Die: A Lifecycle-Based Empirical Study of Bugs in Quantum Software","tz":"量子缺陷如何产生与消亡：量子软件缺陷的生命周期实证研究","a":"Despite growing evidence that bugs in quantum software exhibit distinctive characteristics, existing studies are typically scoped to individual frameworks or single quality attributes and do not examine how quantum-specific bugs behave across the broader software lifecycle. To address this gap, we construct QBugsSet, a lifecycle-based benchmark containing 2,429 bugs and 1,793 realistic negative samples, mined from real GitHub bug-fixing commits in the Qiskit, Cirq, and PennyLane ecosystems, and use it to conduct a comprehensive empirical study comparing quantum-specific and classical bugs across lifecycle distribution, bug-fix latency and pre-fix spatial propagation, repair burden, and LLM-based debugging effectiveness. We find that quantum-specific bugs are more concentrated in semantically critical stages, tend to persist longer before repair (median 17 vs. 7 days), and more often require coordinated multi-hunk repairs (37.8% vs. 27.3%). These lifecycle characteristics highlight a practical limitation of current automation: even the best frontier LLM achieves an end-to-end full repair rate of only 3.82% on quantum-specific bugs, compared with 8.51% on classical bugs. Overall, these findings provide evidence-based guidance for future debugging support that integrates stronger quantum-aware semantic reasoning with broader repository context.","az":"尽管越来越多的证据表明量子软件中的缺陷具有独特特征，现有研究通常只局限于单个框架或单一质量属性，并未考察量子特有缺陷在更广泛的软件生命周期中如何表现。为填补这一空白，我们构建了 QBugsSet———一个基于生命周期的基准，包含 2,429 个缺陷和 1,793 个真实的负样本，均挖掘自 Qiskit、Cirq 和 PennyLane 生态中真实的 GitHub 缺陷修复提交；并用它开展了一项全面的实证研究，从生命周期分布、缺陷修复延迟与修复前的空间传播、修复负担以及基于 LLM 的调试有效性等方面，对比量子特有缺陷与经典缺陷。我们发现，量子特有缺陷更集中于语义关键的阶段，在被修复前往往持续更久（中位数 17 天对 7 天），并且更常需要协调一致的多处（multi-hunk）修复（37.8% 对 27.3%）。这些生命周期特征凸显了当前自动化的一个现实局限：即使是最强的前沿 LLM，在量子特有缺陷上的端到端完全修复率也只有 3.82%，而在经典缺陷上为 8.51%。总体而言，这些发现为未来的调试支持提供了基于证据的指导：需要把更强的量子语义推理与更广的仓库上下文结合起来。","tl":"首个跨生命周期对比量子与经典缺陷的基准与实证研究。","au":["Yasai Shi","Xiangxin Meng","Xiangjie Huang","Jian Zhang","Tianyu Wo","Xu Wang"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["quantum software bugs","bug lifecycle","QBugsSet","LLM-based debugging","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/109/x"},{"id":"p01129","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Automated Table Reproduction via Code Generation","tz":"通过代码生成自动复现表格","a":"Production deployment of AI coding agents requires fast, reproducible evaluation signals. Existing industrial practices trade off speed and fidelity: online A/B testing takes weeks and risks user experience, shadow deployment yields signals that are not reproducible across runs, and public benchmarks diverge from production workloads in language distribution, prompt style, and codebase structure. This paper presents REAP (Relevance and Execution-Audited Pipeline), an automated curation pipeline that constructs production-derived benchmarks from real developer-agent sessions without manual labeling. Such curation, while in-distribution to production usage, runs into several challenges. Untestable prompts, misaligned tests, and test flakiness all compromise evaluation reliability. While tasks can be manually audited to ensure only high-quality tasks remain in the benchmark, this approach is infeasible in the monorepo setting: the build infrastructure state is often ephemeral in large monorepos and requires the benchmark to be continuously re-curated against the current codebase. As manual verification cannot be sustained at this cadence, REAP adds an automated verification layer using LLM-based task classification, agentic test-relevance validation, and multi-run stability checks to ensure the executable benchmark yields trustworthy signals. We use REAP to curate Harvest, a benchmark where each task feeds the coding agent a real developer prompt and verifies the resulting code change against fail-to-pass tests retrieved from production. Harvest's distribution spans more than four programming languages with a majority of tasks drawn from Hack. Model and harness evaluations reveal that solve rates range from 42.9% to 58.2% across five frontier models, surfacing capability differences that inform concrete deployment decisions.","az":"AI 编程智能体的生产部署需要快速、可复现的评测信号。现有工业实践在速度与保真度之间存在权衡：在线 A/B 测试需要数周并可能损害用户体验，影子部署给出的信号在多次运行之间不可复现，而公开基准在语言分布、提示风格和代码库结构上都与生产负载存在偏离。本文提出 REAP（Relevance and Execution-Audited Pipeline，相关性与执行审计流水线），这是一条自动化的数据构建流水线，它无需人工标注，就能从真实的开发者—智能体会话中构建源自生产环境的基准。这种构建方式虽然与生产使用同分布，却会遇到若干挑战：不可测试的提示、错配的测试以及测试的不稳定性都会损害评测的可靠性。虽然可以通过人工审计任务来保证基准中只保留高质量任务，但在 monorepo 场景下这种做法不可行：大型 monorepo 中构建基础设施的状态往往是短暂的，要求基准针对当前代码库持续地重新构建。由于人工验证无法按这种节奏持续进行，REAP 增加了一层自动验证机制，使用基于 LLM 的任务分类、智能体式的测试相关性校验以及多次运行的稳定性检查，以确保这个可执行基准能产出可信的信号。我们用 REAP 构建了 Harvest 基准，其中每个任务都向编程智能体输入一条真实的开发者提示，并用从生产环境中检索到的 fail-to-pass 测试来验证由此产生的代码变更。Harvest 的分布覆盖四种以上编程语言，其中大多数任务来自 Hack。对模型与脚手架的评测显示，五个前沿模型的解决率在 42.9% 到 58.2% 之间，暴露出的能力差异可为具体的部署决策提供依据。","tl":"把表格复现变成可执行的代码生成任务。","au":["Doehyun Baek","Michael Pradel"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["table reproduction","code generation","data analysis","reproducibility"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/110/x"},{"id":"p01130","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MicroAgent: Context-Augmented Multi-agent Framework for Automatic Microservice Decomposition","tz":"MicroAgent：面向自动微服务拆分的上下文增强多智能体框架","a":"The adoption of Microservice Architecture (MSA) has revolutionized software engineering by enhancing scalability, agility, and maintainability over traditional monolithic applications. As more developers transition their legacy systems to microservice-based architectures, effective microservice decomposition-partitioning monolithic applications into highly cohesive services-becomes vital. However, this decomposition task presents significant challenges. Manual approaches are time-consuming and labor-intensive. Existing automated methods often fail to capture the necessary semantic insights from complex applications, while naive applications of Large Language Models tend to overlook crucial contextual information and design principles, leading to suboptimal results. To address these challenges, we propose MicroAgent, a Context-Augmented Multi-Agent Framework for Microservice Decomposition. Our framework divides the decomposition process into five distinct subtasks and assigns each to a specialized agent. To enhance the effectiveness of each agent, we provide tailored, multi-granularity context that keeps its analysis focused and mitigates information overload. Furthermore, to ensure the decomposition adheres to established design principles, we integrate analytical tools that guide the agents' decision-making. Experimental evaluations on 10 Java Web applications demonstrate that MicroAgent achieves an average decomposition accuracy of 89.2%, outperforming the state-of-the-art method by 24.6%. We also conduct a case study to highlight the practical benefits of our design.","az":"微服务架构（MSA）的采用通过在可扩展性、敏捷性和可维护性上超越传统单体应用，深刻改变了软件工程。随着越来越多开发者把遗留系统迁移到基于微服务的架构，有效的微服务拆分———把单体应用划分为高内聚的服务———变得至关重要。然而这一拆分任务面临显著挑战：人工方法既费时又费力；现有自动化方法往往无法从复杂应用中捕获必要的语义洞见；而对大语言模型的朴素使用又容易忽略关键的上下文信息与设计原则，导致次优结果。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 MicroAgent，一个面向微服务拆分的上下文增强多智能体框架。我们的框架把拆分过程划分为五个独立子任务，并将每个子任务交给一个专门的智能体。为提升每个智能体的有效性，我们提供了定制化的多粒度上下文，使其分析保持聚焦并缓解信息过载。此外，为确保拆分遵循既定的设计原则，我们集成了分析工具来引导智能体的决策。在 10 个 Java Web 应用上的实验评估表明，MicroAgent 取得了平均 89.2% 的拆分准确率，比当前最先进方法高出 24.6%。我们还开展了一项案例研究，以突出该设计的实际收益。","tl":"用多粒度上下文加专职多智能体做微服务拆分。","au":["Zishan Su","Junjie Huang","Shiwen Shan","chenxingyan","Hui Zeng","Yuxin Su","Yanlin Wang","Michael Lyu"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["microservice decomposition","multi-agent framework","context augmentation","monolith migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/111/x"},{"id":"p01131","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Gradient-Free Repair of Code LLMs: A Closed-Form Fisher-Guided Bayesian Approach","tz":"代码大模型的免梯度修复：一种闭式 Fisher 引导的贝叶斯方法","tl":"（据标题推断）用闭式 Fisher 贝叶斯更新免梯度地修复代码模型。","au":["Zhiyu Duan","Chong Bian","iainzhang","Shunkun Yang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["code LLM repair","gradient-free","Fisher information","Bayesian model editing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/112/x"},{"id":"p01132","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Pattern over Pixels: Measuring Pattern Completion Bias in Multimodal Code Generation","tz":"模式胜过像素：度量多模态代码生成中的模式补全偏差","a":"Repository-level code translation is critical for modernizing legacy systems, yet existing approaches based on large language models (LLMs) operate at the file level and fail to scale to codebases with complex inter-file dependencies. This limitation is evident in our industrial setting, where we aim to migrate a production repository (STAR) from Java to Kotlin, but file-level approaches produce fragmented results and fail to achieve end-to-end correctness. In this paper, we show that the primary cause of failure at the repository level is dependency inconsistency. Through an empirical study on open-source and industrial systems, we find that most errors arise from unresolved cross-file dependencies that cannot be effectively addressed by iterative feedback alone. We propose a dependency-aware incremental migration framework that elevates the unit of translation from individual files to dependency-consistent batches. Our approach constructs a dependency graph, groups interdependent files, and performs batched translation with iterative compile- and test-driven validation. We evaluate our method on a 51K line of code (LOC) industrial system and multiple repositories across interoperable language pairs (Java-Kotlin, Java-Scala, and C#-F#). On the STAR repository, file-level approaches achieve 38.16% compilation and 9.39% test success, whereas our approach achieves 100% compilation and test success across the evaluated settings, converging within a small number of iterations. These results show that dependency-aware batching improves scalability and reliability in repository-level code translation.","az":"仓库级代码翻译对遗留系统的现代化改造至关重要，但现有基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法都在文件级别运作，无法扩展到存在复杂跨文件依赖的代码库。这一局限在我们的工业场景中体现得很明显：我们希望把一个生产仓库（STAR）从 Java 迁移到 Kotlin，而文件级方法产出的结果零碎，无法实现端到端的正确性。本文表明，仓库级失败的主要原因是依赖不一致。通过对开源系统与工业系统的实证研究，我们发现大多数错误来自未解决的跨文件依赖，而这些依赖仅靠迭代反馈无法有效解决。我们提出一种依赖感知的增量迁移框架，把翻译单元从单个文件提升为依赖一致的批次。我们的方法构建依赖图，把相互依赖的文件分组，并在迭代的编译驱动与测试驱动验证下执行批量翻译。我们在一个 51K 行代码（LOC）的工业系统以及多个可互操作语言对（Java-Kotlin、Java-Scala、C#-F#）的仓库上评估了该方法。在 STAR 仓库上，文件级方法只达到 38.16% 的编译成功率和 9.39% 的测试成功率，而我们的方法在所有评估设置下都实现了 100% 的编译与测试成功率，并在很少的迭代次数内收敛。这些结果表明，依赖感知的批量化提升了仓库级代码翻译的可扩展性与可靠性。","tl":"揭示多模态代码生成更依赖模式补全而非视觉输入。","au":["Khai Nguyen","Oscar Chaparro","Antonio Mastropaolo"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["multimodal","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["multimodal code generation","pattern completion bias","visual grounding","benchmark"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/113/x"},{"id":"p01133","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GPU-Accelerated Belief Propagation for Program Analysis","tz":"面向程序分析的 GPU 加速置信传播","tl":"（据标题推断）把程序分析的置信传播搬到 GPU 上并行加速。","au":["Haoyu Feng","Xin Zhang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["belief propagation","program analysis","GPU acceleration","probabilistic analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/114/x"},{"id":"p01134","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Inferring the Shape of Data Frames in R Programs using Abstract Interpretation","tz":"使用抽象解释推断 R 程序中数据框的形状","a":"Data frames are a fundamental data structure in many data analysis tasks and are widely used in programming languages like R. Due to their omnipresence in data analysis, there are many functions that operate on their shape and content, for example, to clean and transform study data. However, languages like R do not offer static guarantees on data frames making it difficult to reason about their shape at a specific point in the program. In this paper, we present a novel static analysis to infer the shape of data frames in R programs using abstract interpretation by tracking the ensured and potential column names, as well as the potential number of columns and rows. For this, we use a reduced product domain and define abstract semantics for the most commonly used data frame operations, such as mutating, filtering, and subsetting. We evaluate the correctness and accuracy of our analysis on a selection of 78 executable real-world R scripts achieving empirical evidence for soundness by never under-approximating the data frame shape. Additionally, we demonstrate the ability of our analysis to infer the shape of data frames on a large dataset of 33,314 real-world R scripts by inferring concrete shape constraints for 42.1 % and exact shapes for 0.9 % of the data frame operations, improving to 58.7 % and 4.2 % if all datasets read in these scripts are available to our analysis. Using the inferred data frame shapes, we identified 40 real-world R scripts containing potential invalid data frame accesses. This shows the potential of our analysis to significantly support researchers in using data frames in data analysis.","az":"数据框是许多数据分析任务中的基础数据结构，在 R 等编程语言中被广泛使用。由于它们在数据分析中无处不在，存在大量操作其形状与内容的函数，例如用于清洗与转换研究数据。然而，像 R 这样的语言并不对数据框提供静态保证，这使得我们难以在程序中的某个具体位置推理其形状。本文提出一种新颖的静态分析，使用抽象解释推断 R 程序中数据框的形状，其做法是跟踪已确保的列名与可能的列名，以及可能的列数和行数。为此，我们使用了一个约简积（reduced product）域，并为最常用的数据框操作（如 mutate、filter 和 subset）定义了抽象语义。我们在精选的 78 个可执行的真实 R 脚本上评估了分析的正确性与精度，由于从不低估数据框形状，取得了健全性的经验证据。此外，我们在包含 33,314 个真实 R 脚本的大规模数据集上展示了该分析的推断能力：它为 42.1% 的数据框操作推断出具体的形状约束，为 0.9% 推断出精确形状；若这些脚本读入的所有数据集都可供分析使用，则分别提升到 58.7% 和 4.2%。利用推断出的数据框形状，我们识别出 40 个包含潜在非法数据框访问的真实 R 脚本。这表明该分析在支持研究者使用数据框进行数据分析方面具有显著潜力。","tl":"首个用抽象解释推断 R 数据框列名与行列数的分析。","au":["Oliver Gerstl","Florian Sihler","Matthias Tichy"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["abstract interpretation","data frame shape","R programs","static analysis","reduced product domain"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/115/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.03889"},{"id":"p01135","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Translation Tag Team: Formal Rules and LLMs Translate More Macros Together Than Apart","tz":"翻译双打：形式化规则与大模型联手翻译更多的宏","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench’s macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施大多用 C 编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全，研究者正在探索把 C 自动翻译到 Rust 等更安全的语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不只包含 C 代码，还常常使用名为宏（macro）的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。当前最先进的技术通过先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译来回避宏的翻译。但这种做法产出的翻译与原始 C 代码大相径庭，因为预处理会内联所有宏定义。为了在翻译后的代码中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并将其提炼为首个形式化规定的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们引入了首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机采样的宏。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估了大语言模型（LLM）在此前从未被研究过的宏翻译任务上的效果。LLM 翻译的 MacroBench 用例比 MerC 多 22% 到 77%，但其中有 8% 到 28% 的翻译是错误的，需要开发者额外验证；相比之下，MerC 只产出正确的翻译。我们的关键洞见是：先运行 MerC，再对剩余部分使用 LLM，比单独使用任一种技术收益更大。这种“双打”方法的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时比 MerC 平均多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"先用形式化宏翻译器再用 LLM 补漏，兼顾正确率与覆盖率。","au":["Brent Pappas","Joseph Zaluksy","Zachary Burkett","Paul Gazzillo"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["C to Rust translation","macro translation","MerC","MacroBench","LLM translation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/116/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.06705"},{"id":"p01136","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ProbGuard: Proactive Runtime Monitoring for LLM Agent Safety via Probabilistic Prediction","tz":"ProbGuard：通过概率预测实现 LLM 智能体安全的主动运行时监控","a":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents increasingly operate across domains such as robotics, virtual assistants, and web automation. However, their stochastic decision-making introduces safety risks that are difficult to anticipate during execution. Existing runtime monitoring frameworks, such as AgentSpec, primarily rely on reactive safety rules that detect violations only when unsafe behavior is imminent or has already occurred, limiting their ability to handle long-horizon dependencies. We present ProbGuard, a proactive runtime monitoring framework for LLM agents that anticipates safety violations through probabilistic risk prediction. ProbGuard abstracts agent executions into symbolic states and learns a Discrete-Time Markov Chain (DTMC) from execution traces to model behavioral dynamics. At runtime, the monitor estimates the probability that execution will remain safe from the current state, and triggers an intervention when this probability falls below a user-defined threshold. To improve robustness, ProbGuard incorporates semantic validity constraints in the abstraction and admits a PAC-style analysis that characterizes the sample complexity required to certify the learned model under standard assumptions. We evaluate ProbGuard in two safety-critical domains: autonomous driving and embodied household agents. Across evaluated scenarios, ProbGuard consistently predicts traffic law violations and collisions in advance, with warnings up to 15.84 seconds at a threshold yielding no false alarms, and up to 38.66 seconds at stricter thresholds. In embodied agent tasks, ProbGuard’s re-prompting intervention mode reduces unsafe behavior by 65.37% relative to the unmonitored baseline while retaining 80.4% of the baseline task completion; a stricter halting configuration reduces unsafe behavior by 93.60% at a larger cost in completion.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）智能体正越来越多地应用于机器人、虚拟助手和 Web 自动化等领域。然而，它们随机性的决策带来了在执行期间难以预料的安全风险。现有的运行时监控框架（如 AgentSpec）主要依赖被动的安全规则，只有在不安全行为即将发生或已经发生时才检测到违规，因而难以处理长程依赖。我们提出 ProbGuard，一个面向 LLM 智能体的主动运行时监控框架，通过概率化的风险预测提前预判安全违规。ProbGuard 把智能体的执行抽象为符号状态，并从执行轨迹中学习一个离散时间马尔可夫链（DTMC）来建模行为动态。在运行时，监控器估计从当前状态出发执行仍然保持安全的概率，并在该概率低于用户设定的阈值时触发干预。为提升鲁棒性，ProbGuard 在抽象中引入了语义有效性约束，并支持一种 PAC 风格的分析，刻画在标准假设下认证所学模型所需的样本复杂度。我们在两个安全关键领域评估了 ProbGuard：自动驾驶与具身家庭智能体。在评估的各类场景中，ProbGuard 都能提前预测交通法规违规与碰撞：在不产生误报的阈值下预警可提前达 15.84 秒，在更严格的阈值下可提前达 38.66 秒。在具身智能体任务中，ProbGuard 的重新提示（re-prompting）干预模式相对无监控基线把不安全行为减少了 65.37%，同时保留了基线 80.4% 的任务完成率；更严格的停机配置可将不安全行为减少 93.60%，但任务完成率代价更大。","tl":"用 DTMC 概率预测在违规发生前提前干预智能体。","au":["Haoyu Wang","Chris Poskitt","Jiali Wei","Jun Sun"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["security","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["LLM agent safety","runtime monitoring","Discrete-Time Markov Chain","proactive intervention","PAC analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/117/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.00500"},{"id":"p01137","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Tangent: An Empirical Study of Testing Practices for LLM-Based Agent Applications","tz":"Tangent：基于 LLM 的智能体应用测试实践实证研究","a":"The machine learning(ML) component of an ML-enabled system evolves through retraining, fine-tuning, and optimization, so previously valid test results may no longer hold. A single evolution step can worsen performance on some test cases while improving others, making regression test prioritization inherently directional. We present Gradient-based Behavior Vector-Parameter Delta(GBV-PD), the first approach to operationalize the behavior vector space for evolution-aware regression test prioritization. GBV-PD represents each test case as a gradient-based vector(GBV), a low-dimensional projection of its loss gradient under the original model. It then projects the observed parameter update of the evolved model onto the same PCA basis and uses the resulting alignment to estimate whether each test case's loss is likely to increase or decrease, without running the evolved model on test cases during prioritization. In an empirical study across classification and regression tasks, GBV-PD consistently outperformed non-directional baselines and remained competitive with a full-gradient reference, while offering better time and storage profiles for repeated updates via reusable GBV caching. These results show that behavior-space ideas can be operationalized into a practical and efficient mechanism for repeated-update regression testing of evolving ML-enabled systems.","az":"机器学习（ML）赋能系统中的 ML 组件会通过重训练、微调和优化不断演化，因此此前有效的测试结果可能不再成立。单次演化步骤可能让部分测试用例的表现变差、同时让另一些变好，这使得回归测试优先级排序本质上具有方向性。我们提出基于梯度的行为向量—参数增量方法（Gradient-based Behavior Vector-Parameter Delta，GBV-PD），这是首个把行为向量空间落地用于演化感知回归测试优先级排序的方法。GBV-PD 把每个测试用例表示为一个基于梯度的向量（GBV），即该用例在原模型下损失梯度的低维投影；随后把演化后模型观测到的参数更新投影到同一个 PCA 基上，并利用由此得到的对齐程度来估计每个测试用例的损失是可能上升还是下降，而无需在优先级排序过程中用演化后的模型运行这些测试用例。在涵盖分类与回归任务的一项实证研究中，GBV-PD 始终优于无方向性的基线方法，并与全梯度参考方法保持竞争力，同时通过可复用的 GBV 缓存，在重复更新场景下具有更好的时间与存储特性。这些结果表明，行为空间的思想可以被落地为一种实用且高效的机制，用于演化中的 ML 赋能系统的重复更新回归测试。","tl":"首次系统刻画 LLM 智能体应用的真实测试实践。","au":["Rangeet Pan","Tyler Stennett","Divya Sankar","Bridget McGinn","Alessandro Orso","Raju Pavuluri","Saurabh Sinha","Maja Vukovic"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["LLM agent applications","testing practices","empirical study","agent testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/118/x"},{"id":"p01138","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Unified Model for Cross-Domain Clone Detection via Model Merging","tz":"通过模型合并构建跨领域克隆检测的统一模型","a":"The growing diversity of code clone types, from syntactic copies to cross-language semantic clones and AI-generated duplicates, has created a fragmentation crisis in clone detection. Current deep learning detectors behave as domain specialists and degrade significantly outside their training distributions. In our evaluation, F1 drops exceed 70% across domains. Deploying multiple specialized models is impractical, while training a single cross-domain detector requires simultaneous access to all training data. To address this limitation, we investigate model merging , a family of post-hoc techniques that operate solely on trained checkpoints. We systematically evaluate parameter merging using five task-vector methods, namely Task Arithmetic, TIES, DARE-TIES, WUDI, and PCB, as well as architecture merging through greedy layer stitching and cross-tokenizer alignment. Our study spans four pretrained code models, three benchmarks, and twelve merging configurations. Same-base TIES merging creates effective cross-domain detectors, as validated across two model families and three random seeds. On UniXcoder, it achieves 0.865 combined F1 , corresponding to 93% of multi-task training performance , without requiring training data during the merging step. WUDI achieves the highest in-distribution combined F1 at 0.899 , but TIES generalizes better to unseen AI-generated clones. We therefore recommend TIES as the practical merging strategy. Cross-base merging produces only marginal and high-variance gains across all five methods, indicating that task-vector compatibility through a shared pretrained base is the binding factor for effective merging in our setting. Merged encoder-based detectors also outperform zero-shot instruction-tuned code LLMs on GPTCloneBench, achieving 0.609 F1 compared with 0.454 F1 for the strongest LLM baseline, while incurring substantially lower per-pair inference costs. They also generalize up to 4× better than multi-task training to unseen AI-generated clones, revealing a trade-off between in-domain performance and out-of-distribution robustness. This work provides one of the first systematic empirical studies of model merging for software engineering and offers a practical recipe for building cross-domain code clone detectors.","az":"代码克隆类型日益多样，从语法层面的复制到跨语言语义克隆再到 AI 生成的重复代码，已在克隆检测领域造成了碎片化危机。当前的深度学习检测器表现得像领域专家，一旦离开训练分布性能就显著下降。在我们的评估中，跨领域的 F1 下降超过 70%。部署多个专用模型并不现实，而训练单个跨领域检测器又要求同时访问全部训练数据。为解决这一局限，我们研究了模型合并（model merging），这是一类仅在已训练检查点上操作的事后技术。我们系统评估了使用五种任务向量方法（Task Arithmetic、TIES、DARE-TIES、WUDI 和 PCB）的参数合并，以及通过贪心层缝合与跨分词器对齐实现的架构合并。我们的研究涵盖四个预训练代码模型、三个基准和十二种合并配置。同基座的 TIES 合并能够产生有效的跨领域检测器，这一点在两个模型家族和三个随机种子上都得到了验证。在 UniXcoder 上，它取得了 0.865 的综合 F1，相当于多任务训练性能的 93%，而在合并阶段无需任何训练数据。WUDI 取得了最高的分布内综合 F1（0.899），但 TIES 对未见过的 AI 生成克隆泛化得更好。因此我们推荐 TIES 作为实用的合并策略。跨基座合并在全部五种方法上都只带来边际且方差很大的收益，说明在我们的设定中，通过共享预训练基座获得的任务向量兼容性是有效合并的决定因素。合并后的编码器式检测器在 GPTCloneBench 上也优于零样本的指令微调代码 LLM，取得 0.609 F1，而最强 LLM 基线为 0.454 F1，同时每对比较的推理成本要低得多。它们在未见过的 AI 生成克隆上的泛化能力也比多任务训练最多好 4 倍，揭示了域内性能与分布外鲁棒性之间的权衡。这项工作提供了面向软件工程的模型合并的首批系统性实证研究之一，并给出了构建跨领域代码克隆检测器的实用配方。","tl":"证明同基座 TIES 合并可免训练地造出跨域克隆检测器。","au":["Palash Ranjan Roy","Banani Roy","Kevin Schneider","Chanchal K. Roy"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["model merging","clone detection","task arithmetic","TIES","cross-domain generalization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/119/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.04215"},{"id":"p01139","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Don’t Retest Everything: Auditable Regression Scoping for Safety-Critical Systems","tz":"别把所有测试都跑一遍：安全关键系统的可审计回归测试范围界定","tl":"（据标题推断）给安全关键系统做可审计、可追溯的回归测试选择。","au":["Francesco Basciani","Daniele Masti","Patrizio Pelliccione","Alberto Petrucci","Franco Raimondi","Emerson Sales","Paolo Serri"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["regression test scoping","safety-critical systems","auditability","test selection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/120/x"},{"id":"p01140","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Recovering Revisions of Pull Requests with Altered History","tz":"恢复历史被改写的 Pull Request 的修订版本","tl":"（据标题推断）找回因 force-push 等历史改写而丢失的 PR 修订。","au":["Gengyi Sun","Georges Aaron RANDRIANAINA","Tao Xiao","Yasutaka Kamei","Shane McIntosh"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["pull request","force push","revision recovery","change history"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/121/x","pu":"https://rebels.cs.uwaterloo.ca/papers/ase2026_sun.pdf"},{"id":"p01141","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Making Theft Useless: Adulteration-Based Protection of Proprietary Knowledge Graphs in GraphRAG Systems","tz":"让窃取变得无用：GraphRAG 系统中基于掺杂的专有知识图谱保护","a":"Graph Retrieval-Augmented Generation (GraphRAG) has emerged as a key technique for enhancing Large Language Models (LLMs) with proprietary Knowledge Graphs (KGs) in knowledge-intensive applications. As these KGs often represent an organization's highly valuable intellectual property (IP), they face a significant risk of theft for private use. In this scenario, attackers operate in isolated environments. This private-use threat renders passive defenses like watermarking ineffective, as they require output access for detection. Simultaneously, the low-latency demands of GraphRAG make strong encryption which incurs prohibitive overhead impractical. To address these challenges, we propose AURA, a novel framework based on Data Adulteration designed to make any stolen KG unusable to an adversary. Our framework pre-emptively injects plausible but false adulterants into the KG. For an attacker, these adulterants deteriorate the retrieved context and lead to factually incorrect responses. Conversely, for authorized users, a secret key enables the efficient filtering of all adulterants via encrypted metadata tags before they are passed to the LLM, ensuring query results remain completely accurate. Our evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness of this approach: AURA degrades the performance of unauthorized systems to an accuracy of just 5.3%, while maintaining 100% fidelity for authorized users with negligible overhead. Furthermore, AURA proves robust against various sanitization attempts, retaining 80.2% of its adulterants.","az":"图检索增强生成（GraphRAG）已成为用专有知识图谱（KG）增强大语言模型（LLM）以服务知识密集型应用的关键技术。由于这些知识图谱往往代表着组织极具价值的知识产权（IP），它们面临被窃取用于私下使用的重大风险。在这种场景下，攻击者在隔离环境中操作。这种私用型威胁使得水印等被动防御失效，因为它们需要访问输出才能检测。与此同时，GraphRAG 的低时延需求又让开销高昂的强加密变得不切实际。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 AURA，一个基于数据掺杂（Data Adulteration）的新颖框架，旨在让任何被窃取的知识图谱对攻击者而言都不可用。我们的框架预先向知识图谱中注入貌似合理但虚假的掺杂项。对攻击者而言，这些掺杂项会劣化检索到的上下文，导致事实错误的回答。反之，对授权用户而言，一个密钥可以在内容传给 LLM 之前，通过加密的元数据标签高效过滤掉所有掺杂项，确保查询结果完全准确。我们的评估证明了该方法的有效性：AURA 把未授权系统的性能劣化到仅 5.3% 的准确率，同时为授权用户保持 100% 的保真度且开销可忽略。此外，AURA 对各种净化（sanitization）尝试表现出鲁棒性，保留了 80.2% 的掺杂项。","tl":"预注入可密钥过滤的假节点，使被窃知识图谱不可用。","au":["Weijie Wang","Peizhuo Lv","Yan Wang","Weiqing Huang","Rujie Dai","Guokun Xu","Qiujian Lv","Hangcheng Liu","Hao Hu","Jiaheng Zhang"],"top":"privacy-memorization-watermarking-and-unlearning","alt":"agent-memory-context-and-retrieval","tg":["cross-track-bridge","security"],"kw":["GraphRAG","knowledge graph IP protection","data adulteration","retrieval poisoning defense"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/122/x"},{"id":"p01142","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Decompiling the Web: Automated Semantic Recovery of Post-compilation Abstraction Leaks","tz":"反编译 Web：编译后抽象泄漏的自动语义恢复","a":"GraphQL APIs power production systems across financial services, e-commerce, and social platforms, yet their most critical access-control vulnerabilities--Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR), Use-After-Free (UAF), and state-dependent injection--routinely escape automated security testing. Industry-standard scanners (ZAP) and the leading research fuzzer (EvoMaster) test operations in isolation and cannot compose the multi-step sequences these flaws require. We present GraphQLer, an open-source automated security testing framework built for production GraphQL APIs. GraphQLer constructs a typed dependency graph from live schema introspection and synthesizes vulnerability chains--ordered operation sequences targeting specific flaw classes. Three strategies cover the critical attack surface: topological SCC-traversal for general reachability, cross-user IDOR replay for broken access control, and CREATE -> DELETE -> READ synthesis for UAF. On a production financial API (FinServ), GraphQLer identified eight potential vulnerabilities--including denial-of-service vectors that exposed stack traces and sensitive implementation details--without prior documentation or authentication credentials. On a self-hosted Saleor instance pinned to the CVE-2022-39275 commit, GraphQLer reproduced all four broken-access-control mutations cited in the security advisory. On the 11 public APIs of the coverage set, GraphQLer achieves 85.52% mean PositiveCoverage versus 29.29% (EvoMaster) and 21.80% (ZAP); across the 21 evaluated APIs it detects all 5 confirmed IDOR endpoints, UAF behavior on two controlled schemas, and confirms XSS and SQLi on DVGA (an independent third-party oracle)--while all baselines detect zero chain-based vulnerabilities.","az":"GraphQL API 支撑着金融服务、电子商务和社交平台的生产系统，然而其最关键的访问控制漏洞———不安全的直接对象引用（IDOR）、释放后使用（UAF）以及依赖状态的注入———却经常逃过自动化安全测试。业界标准扫描器（ZAP）与领先的研究型模糊测试工具（EvoMaster）都孤立地测试各个操作，无法组合出这些缺陷所需的多步序列。我们提出 GraphQLer，一个面向生产级 GraphQL API 的开源自动化安全测试框架。GraphQLer 通过实时的模式自省构建带类型的依赖图，并合成漏洞链———针对特定缺陷类别的有序操作序列。三种策略覆盖了关键攻击面：用于一般可达性的拓扑 SCC 遍历、用于越权访问控制的跨用户 IDOR 重放，以及用于 UAF 的 CREATE -> DELETE -> READ 合成。在一个生产级金融 API（FinServ）上，GraphQLer 在没有先验文档和认证凭据的情况下识别出八个潜在漏洞，其中包括会暴露栈跟踪和敏感实现细节的拒绝服务向量。在固定到 CVE-2022-39275 提交的自托管 Saleor 实例上，GraphQLer 复现了安全公告中提到的全部四个越权访问控制变更操作。在覆盖率集合的 11 个公开 API 上，GraphQLer 取得了 85.52% 的平均 PositiveCoverage，而 EvoMaster 为 29.29%、ZAP 为 21.80%；在全部 21 个被评估的 API 上，它检出了全部 5 个已确认的 IDOR 端点，在两个受控模式上检出 UAF 行为，并在 DVGA（一个独立的第三方预言）上确认了 XSS 与 SQLi———而所有基线都未检出任何基于链的漏洞。","tl":"自动恢复编译后 Web 代码中泄漏的高层抽象语义。","au":["Shriyans Sudhi","Yinxi Liu"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["web decompilation","semantic recovery","abstraction leak","reverse engineering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/123/x"},{"id":"p01143","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AutoSQL: Extracting SQL Templates from Imperative ORM Code in Large-Scale Repositories","tz":"AutoSQL：从大规模仓库的命令式 ORM 代码中抽取 SQL 模板","a":"Suboptimal SQL queries can significantly degrade the performance of cloud systems, motivating the extraction and auditing of SQL statements before deployment. However, Go ORM frameworks construct SQL imperatively through scattered method-call sequences, making it difficult to statically recover the resulting SQL templates. We present AutoSQL, a system that reconstructs SQL templates from Go ORM code. AutoSQL constructs a Code Index, a directed graph that captures structural dependencies between functions, types, and global variables as navigable edges. It then traces upstream call chains from ORM invocation sites to identify database-interacting functions as entry points. For each entry point, an LLM agent traverses the Code Index to collect code slices that influence SQL generation, switching to pattern-based search when the graph cannot resolve a retrieval goal. We call this strategy Hybrid Context Retrieval. Once sufficient context is collected, the agent synthesizes SQL templates. Evaluation on a benchmark of 579 test-covered entry points and 1,186 runtime-traced SQL statements from five large-scale Go repositories shows that AutoSQL achieves 68.04% to 72.18% recall, exceeding the static reachability baseline by 11.80% to 15.94% and outperforming existing methods by 8.52% to 21.50%.","az":"次优的 SQL 查询会显著降低云系统的性能，这促使人们在部署前抽取并审计 SQL 语句。然而，Go 的 ORM 框架通过分散的方法调用序列以命令式方式构造 SQL，使得静态恢复最终生成的 SQL 模板十分困难。我们提出 AutoSQL，一个从 Go ORM 代码中重建 SQL 模板的系统。AutoSQL 构建了 Code Index———一个有向图，把函数、类型和全局变量之间的结构依赖表示为可导航的边。随后它从 ORM 调用点向上追溯调用链，识别出与数据库交互的函数作为入口点。对每个入口点，一个 LLM 智能体遍历 Code Index 以收集影响 SQL 生成的代码切片，当图无法解析某个检索目标时则切换为基于模式的搜索。我们把这一策略称为混合上下文检索（Hybrid Context Retrieval）。一旦收集到足够的上下文，智能体就合成 SQL 模板。在来自五个大规模 Go 仓库的 579 个被测试覆盖的入口点和 1,186 条运行时追踪的 SQL 语句组成的基准上进行评估，结果表明 AutoSQL 达到了 68.04% 到 72.18% 的召回率，比静态可达性基线高出 11.80% 到 15.94%，比现有方法高出 8.52% 到 21.50%。","tl":"用代码图加 LLM 智能体的混合检索还原 ORM 生成的 SQL。","au":["Junsong Pu","Yichen LI","Zhuangbin Chen","Zhihan Jiang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","agentic","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["ORM code analysis","SQL template extraction","code index","hybrid context retrieval","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/124/x"},{"id":"p01144","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SIMD-Accelerated Sparse Bit-Vectors for Pointer Analysis","tz":"面向指针分析的 SIMD 加速稀疏位向量","tl":"（据标题推断）用 SIMD 重新设计稀疏位向量以加速指针分析。","au":["Zhaoyang Tan","Peisen Yao","Kui Ren"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["pointer analysis","sparse bit-vector","SIMD acceleration","static analysis performance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/125/x"},{"id":"p01145","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DesignFix: Context-Augmented Repair of Design Rule Violations","tz":"DesignFix：上下文增强的设计规则违规修复","a":"Iterative repair loops have become a core design pattern in LLM-based software engineering systems. These workflows repeatedly generate, validate, and repair artifacts using feedback such as compiler errors or test failures. Despite their widespread use, the impact of repair-loop iteration limits remains poorly understood, as most prior work adopts fixed, often arbitrary, repair budgets. We study repair-loop effectiveness across multiple software engineering tasks, including code generation, test generation, and code translation. Across several representative workflows, datasets, and contemporary low-cost LLMs, we observe a consistent pattern of diminishing returns: the first three to four repair iterations account for most achievable gains, while later iterations contribute only marginal improvements. We further find that repair behavior is influenced more strongly by workflow orchestration and feedback design than by the underlying model itself. These results suggest that repair budgets should be treated as an explicit experimental variable, as they directly affect evaluation outcomes, computational cost, runtime, and reproducibility in LLM-based software engineering research.","az":"迭代修复循环已成为基于 LLM 的软件工程系统中的一种核心设计模式。这类工作流反复地生成、验证并修复制品，其反馈来自编译错误或测试失败等信号。尽管这种模式被广泛使用，修复循环迭代次数上限的影响却仍然缺乏理解，因为以往工作大多采用固定且往往是任意设定的修复预算。我们在多项软件工程任务上研究了修复循环的有效性，包括代码生成、测试生成和代码翻译。在若干具有代表性的工作流、数据集以及当前的低成本 LLM 上，我们观察到一致的收益递减模式：前三到四轮修复贡献了绝大部分可获得的收益，而后续迭代只带来边际改进。我们进一步发现，修复行为受工作流编排与反馈设计的影响，要比受底层模型本身的影响更大。这些结果表明，修复预算应被视为一个显式的实验变量，因为它直接影响基于 LLM 的软件工程研究中的评测结果、计算成本、运行时间与可复现性。","tl":"用增强上下文自动修复设计规则违规告警。","au":["Mainul Hossain","Thomas LaToza"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["design rule violation","automated repair","context augmentation","static checker alerts"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/126/x"},{"id":"p01146","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LaMAR: Latent Multi-agent Collaboration via KV-Cache Communication for Automated Program Repair","tz":"LaMAR：通过 KV-Cache 通信实现面向自动程序修复的隐空间多智能体协作","a":"Iterative repair loops have become a core design pattern in LLM-based software engineering systems. These workflows repeatedly generate, validate, and repair artifacts using feedback such as compiler errors or test failures. Despite their widespread use, the impact of repair-loop iteration limits remains poorly understood, as most prior work adopts fixed, often arbitrary, repair budgets. We study repair-loop effectiveness across multiple software engineering tasks, including code generation, test generation, and code translation. Across several representative workflows, datasets, and contemporary low-cost LLMs, we observe a consistent pattern of diminishing returns: the first three to four repair iterations account for most achievable gains, while later iterations contribute only marginal improvements. We further find that repair behavior is influenced more strongly by workflow orchestration and feedback design than by the underlying model itself. These results suggest that repair budgets should be treated as an explicit experimental variable, as they directly affect evaluation outcomes, computational cost, runtime, and reproducibility in LLM-based software engineering research.","az":"迭代修复循环已成为基于 LLM 的软件工程系统中的一种核心设计模式。这类工作流反复地生成、验证并修复制品，其反馈来自编译错误或测试失败等信号。尽管这种模式被广泛使用，修复循环迭代次数上限的影响却仍然缺乏理解，因为以往工作大多采用固定且往往是任意设定的修复预算。我们在多项软件工程任务上研究了修复循环的有效性，包括代码生成、测试生成和代码翻译。在若干具有代表性的工作流、数据集以及当前的低成本 LLM 上，我们观察到一致的收益递减模式：前三到四轮修复贡献了绝大部分可获得的收益，而后续迭代只带来边际改进。我们进一步发现，修复行为受工作流编排与反馈设计的影响，要比受底层模型本身的影响更大。这些结果表明，修复预算应被视为一个显式的实验变量，因为它直接影响基于 LLM 的软件工程研究中的评测结果、计算成本、运行时间与可复现性。","tl":"让修复智能体在 KV-Cache 隐空间而非自然语言里通信。","au":["Rui Jiao","Yue Zhang","Zhexuan Feng","Jinku Li"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["automated program repair","multi-agent collaboration","KV-cache communication","latent communication"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/127/x"},{"id":"p01147","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Enhancing Trace-Based Root Cause Analysis for Microservice Systems via Code Change Understanding","tz":"通过代码变更理解增强微服务系统的基于调用链的根因分析","tl":"（据标题推断）把代码变更信息引入 trace 根因分析定位故障。","au":["Min Zhang","Chenxi Zhang","Senyu Xie","Shihong Chen","Lei Wu","Xin Peng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","kw":["root cause analysis","microservices","distributed tracing","code change understanding"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/128/x"},{"id":"p01148","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Assessing Uncertainty in Performance Modeling: Conformal Prediction vs. Bayesian Regression","tz":"评估性能建模中的不确定性：共形预测与贝叶斯回归的比较","tl":"（据标题推断）比较共形预测与贝叶斯回归量化性能模型不确定性。","au":["Stefan Jahns","Johannes Dorn","Max Weber","Sven Apel","Norbert Siegmund"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["performance modeling","uncertainty quantification","conformal prediction","Bayesian regression"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/129/x"},{"id":"p01149","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RACE-Bench: A Reasoning-Augmented Benchmark for Repository-Level Code Agents on Feature Addition","tz":"RACE-Bench：面向仓库级代码智能体功能新增任务的推理增强基准","a":"Repository-level code agents have shown strong promise in real-world feature addition tasks, making reliable evaluation of their capabilities increasingly important. However, existing benchmarks primarily evaluate these agents as black boxes based on final test correctness, providing limited insight into how they reason and where failures arise. To address this limitation, we introduce RACE-bench, a reasoning-augmented benchmark for evaluating code agents on repository-level feature addition tasks. RACE-bench contains 528 real-world feature addition instances from 12 open-source repositories. Each instance is paired with executable patch verification and structured intermediate reference reasoning covering issue understanding, file localization, implementation tasks, and step decomposition. Based on this design, we introduce a dual-track evaluation framework that jointly measures patch correctness and intermediate reasoning alignment with developer-accepted reference trajectories. We evaluate three representative repository-level code agents on RACE-bench. On the full benchmark, Resolved Rate ranges from 29% to 70% across different agents. Our reasoning-level analysis further shows that while current agents perform well at understanding high-level intent, their performance degrades substantially when translating intent into concrete implementation steps. We also find patches that can be applied but still fail the tests cover fewer reference-reasoning elements (35.7% lower recall) and contain more unsupported reasoning elements (94.1% higher over-prediction) than successful patches. These findings highlight the importance of evaluating repository-level code agents beyond final patch correctness by examining the quality of their reasoning processes.","az":"仓库级代码智能体在真实的功能新增任务上已展现出很强的潜力，这使得可靠地评估其能力变得愈发重要。然而现有基准主要把这些智能体当作黑盒，依据最终测试的正确性进行评估，对它们如何推理、失败发生在何处提供的洞见十分有限。为解决这一局限，我们提出 RACE-bench，一个用于评估代码智能体在仓库级功能新增任务上的推理增强基准。RACE-bench 包含来自 12 个开源仓库的 528 个真实功能新增实例。每个实例都配有可执行的补丁验证，以及覆盖 issue 理解、文件定位、实现任务和步骤分解的结构化中间参考推理。在此设计基础上，我们引入了双轨评估框架，同时衡量补丁正确性以及中间推理与开发者认可的参考轨迹之间的一致性。我们在 RACE-bench 上评估了三个有代表性的仓库级代码智能体。在完整基准上，不同智能体的解决率（Resolved Rate）在 29% 到 70% 之间。我们的推理层面分析进一步表明，当前智能体在理解高层意图方面表现良好，但在把意图转化为具体实现步骤时性能大幅下降。我们还发现，那些可以应用但仍未通过测试的补丁，相比成功的补丁覆盖了更少的参考推理要素（召回率低 35.7%），并包含更多无依据的推理要素（过度预测高 94.1%）。这些发现凸显了在最终补丁正确性之外，通过考察推理过程质量来评估仓库级代码智能体的重要性。","tl":"用参考推理轨迹做双轨评测，看智能体在哪一步想错。","au":["Shuhan Liu","Zhiyi Zhao","Xing Hu","Kui Liu","Xiaohu Yang","Xin Xia"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["repository-level code agents","feature addition","reasoning-augmented benchmark","dual-track evaluation","resolved rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/130/x"},{"id":"p01150","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Effective Are NPM Malicious Package Detectors? A Large-Scale Empirical Study","tz":"NPM 恶意包检测器到底有多有效？一项大规模实证研究","a":"Replication package for the ASE 2026 paper \"How Effective Are NPM Malicious Package Detectors? A Large-Scale Empirical Study\". This repository contains the unified benchmark and evaluation framework used in the paper. The benchmark comprises 6,420 malicious package versions across 4,286 unique packages and 7,288 benign packages collected from the npm registry. Every malicious version is annotated with 11 behavior categories and 8 evasion techniques. Malicious samples are drawn from five academic datasets and from public security advisories, and each entry was reviewed by three security experts before inclusion. The framework evaluates 11 detection tools with 16 variants spanning static analysis, dynamic analysis, machine learning, and LLM-based approaches. We also release the analysis scripts that reproduce every table and figure in the paper.","az":"这是 ASE 2026 论文《How Effective Are NPM Malicious Package Detectors? A Large-Scale Empirical Study》的复现包。本仓库包含论文中使用的统一基准与评估框架。该基准包含从 npm 仓库收集的、覆盖 4,286 个不同包的 6,420 个恶意包版本，以及 7,288 个良性包。每个恶意版本都标注了 11 种行为类别和 8 种规避技术。恶意样本取自五个学术数据集以及公开的安全公告，每个条目在纳入前都经过三位安全专家的审核。该框架评估了 11 款检测工具的 16 个变体，涵盖静态分析、动态分析、机器学习和基于 LLM 的方法。我们还发布了可复现论文中每一张表和每一幅图的分析脚本。","tl":"统一基准横评 11 款 npm 恶意包检测工具的真实能力。","au":["Wenbo Guo","Zhongwen Chen","Zhengzi Xu","Chengwei Liu","Ming Kang","Shiwen Song","CHENGYUE LIU","Yijia Xu","Weisong Sun","Yang Liu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["npm malicious packages","supply chain security","detector evaluation","benchmark","evasion techniques"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/131/x"},{"id":"p01151","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Localizing Data Annotation Faults in Semantic Segmentation Systems","tz":"语义分割系统中的数据标注缺陷定位","a":"The machine learning(ML) component of an ML-enabled system evolves through retraining, fine-tuning, and optimization, so previously valid test results may no longer hold. A single evolution step can worsen performance on some test cases while improving others, making regression test prioritization inherently directional. We present Gradient-based Behavior Vector-Parameter Delta(GBV-PD), the first approach to operationalize the behavior vector space for evolution-aware regression test prioritization. GBV-PD represents each test case as a gradient-based vector(GBV), a low-dimensional projection of its loss gradient under the original model. It then projects the observed parameter update of the evolved model onto the same PCA basis and uses the resulting alignment to estimate whether each test case's loss is likely to increase or decrease, without running the evolved model on test cases during prioritization. In an empirical study across classification and regression tasks, GBV-PD consistently outperformed non-directional baselines and remained competitive with a full-gradient reference, while offering better time and storage profiles for repeated updates via reusable GBV caching. These results show that behavior-space ideas can be operationalized into a practical and efficient mechanism for repeated-update regression testing of evolving ML-enabled systems.","az":"机器学习（ML）赋能系统中的 ML 组件会通过重训练、微调和优化不断演化，因此此前有效的测试结果可能不再成立。单次演化既可能让部分测试用例的表现变差，也可能让另一些变好，这使得回归测试优先级排序天然具有方向性。我们提出了基于梯度的行为向量—参数增量方法（Gradient-based Behavior Vector-Parameter Delta, GBV-PD），这是首个将行为向量空间落地用于演化感知回归测试优先级排序的方法。GBV-PD 将每个测试用例表示为一个基于梯度的向量（GBV），即该用例在原始模型下损失梯度的低维投影；随后把演化后模型观测到的参数更新投影到同一 PCA 基上，并利用由此得到的对齐程度来估计每个测试用例的损失是可能上升还是下降，而无需在排序阶段用演化后的模型真实运行这些测试用例。在覆盖分类与回归任务的实证研究中，GBV-PD 始终优于无方向性的基线方法，并与使用完整梯度的参考方法保持竞争力，同时借助可复用的 GBV 缓存，在重复更新场景下具有更好的时间与存储开销表现。这些结果表明，行为空间的思想可以被落地为一种实用且高效的机制，用于不断演化的 ML 赋能系统的重复更新回归测试。","tl":"用梯度行为向量投影预测演化后测试用例变好还是变差。","au":["Pengyi Yang","Teng Long","Zhiwu Xu","Linhai Jing"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["regression test prioritization","ML-enabled systems","gradient behavior vector","model evolution","data annotation faults"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/132/x"},{"id":"p01152","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"“Impossible to Hide Secret ...”: Uncovering Security and Privacy Issues in LLM-Native IDEs","tz":"“秘密根本藏不住……”：揭示 LLM 原生 IDE 中的安全与隐私问题","a":"LLM-native IDEs (Integrated Development Environments), aka LIDEs, are designed from the ground up to work with Large Language Models (LLMs). LIDEs have found remarkable success in Software Engineering (SE) tasks such as coding, debugging, and program comprehension. LIDEs are software systems, and, like any system, they can exhibit vulnerabilities. In this paper, we study the security and privacy issues that developers reported while using popular LIDEs in their development tasks. We collected 1.1M posts from 29 popular subreddits related to LIDEs. We identified 446 posts and analyzed over 6K comments to the posts that discussed security and privacy issues in almost all popular LIDEs, such as Cursor, Copilot, Codex, etc. Using a mix of qualitative and quantitative methods, we constructed a taxonomy of the reported security and privacy issues. Our results show that most issues in LIDEs stem from system-level design choices, rather than the underlying LLMs, such as user data access, unchecked autonomous actions, etc. To overcome these issues, developers frequently relied on external safeguards like code sandboxing and manual reviewing, highlighting prevalent mistrust among developers about LIDEs. We share lessons from our study to support future design of secure and privacy-aware LIDEs.","az":"LLM 原生 IDE（集成开发环境，简称 LIDE）从设计之初就是为了配合大语言模型（LLM）工作。LIDE 在编码、调试、程序理解等软件工程（SE）任务上取得了显著成功。LIDE 本身也是软件系统，和任何系统一样，它们可能存在漏洞。本文研究开发者在开发任务中使用主流 LIDE 时所报告的安全与隐私问题。我们从 29 个与 LIDE 相关的热门 subreddit 中收集了 110 万条帖子，识别出 446 条相关帖子，并分析了这些帖子下超过 6000 条评论，这些讨论几乎覆盖了所有主流 LIDE，如 Cursor、Copilot、Codex 等。通过定性与定量相结合的方法，我们构建了所报告安全与隐私问题的分类体系。结果表明，LIDE 中的大多数问题源于系统层面的设计选择而非底层 LLM 本身，例如用户数据访问、未经检查的自主动作等。为应对这些问题，开发者往往依赖代码沙箱和人工审查等外部防护措施，这凸显出开发者对 LIDE 普遍存在的不信任。我们分享了研究中得到的经验教训，以支持未来设计更安全、更具隐私意识的 LIDE。","tl":"首次用百万级社区帖构建 LLM 原生 IDE 安全隐私问题分类体系。","au":["Mostafijur Rahman Akhond","Md Afif Al Mamun","Gias Uddin","Song Wang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["security","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["LLM-native IDE","security and privacy","taxonomy","Reddit mining","developer trust"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/133/x"},{"id":"p01153","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Smart Contract Synthesis via Multi-modal Specifications","tz":"基于多模态规约的智能合约合成","a":"This record contains the reproducibility artifact for the paper\"Smart Contract Synthesis via Multi-modal Specifications.\" It includesthe SmartSpec source code, benchmarks, experiment scripts, and instructionsneeded to reproduce the evaluation results. Paper DOI: https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837430","az":"本条目包含论文《Smart Contract Synthesis via Multi-modal Specifications》的可复现性制品，其中包括 SmartSpec 源代码、基准测试集、实验脚本以及复现评估结果所需的说明。论文 DOI：https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837430","tl":"SmartSpec 用多模态规约驱动智能合约代码合成。","au":["Tanglin Chen","Haoxian Chen","Huilin Xiang","Yuepeng Wang"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","multimodal"],"kw":["smart contract synthesis","multi-modal specification","SmartSpec","program synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/134/x"},{"id":"p01154","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"BDiff: Block-Aware and Accurate Text-Based Code Differencing","tz":"BDiff：块感知的高精度文本代码差分算法","tl":"（据标题推断）提出块感知的文本 diff 算法提升代码差分精度。","au":["Yao Lu","Wanwei Liu","Tanghaoran Zhang","Kang Yang","Yang Zhang","Wenyu Xu","Longfei Sun","Xinjun Mao","Shuzheng Gao","Michael Lyu"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code differencing","diff algorithm","block-aware","change analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/135/x"},{"id":"p01155","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PCodeTrans: Translate Decompiled Pseudocode to Trace-Level Equivalent Source Code","tz":"PCodeTrans：将反编译伪代码翻译为轨迹级等价的源代码","tl":"（据标题推断）以执行轨迹等价为目标翻译反编译伪代码。","au":["Yuxin Cui","Zeyu Gao","Siliang Qin","Yuanda Wang","JiaMing Wang","xizeLuo","Peng Zhou","Chao Zhang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["decompilation","pseudocode translation","trace equivalence","reverse engineering"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/136/x"},{"id":"p01156","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AlphaCu: A Transformation-Driven Synthesis Framework for LLM-Based GPU Kernel Generation","tz":"AlphaCu：面向 LLM GPU Kernel 生成的变换驱动合成框架","tl":"（据标题推断）用变换驱动的合成框架提升 LLM 生成 GPU kernel 的质量。","au":["Yangjie Zhou","Xing Ma","Zihan Liu","Wang Qing","Weihao Cui","Sun Wu","Hanjing Wang","Binhang Qi","Jingwen Leng","Yun Lin","Jin Song Dong","Minyi Guo"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GPU kernel generation","CUDA","program transformation","LLM code synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/137/x"},{"id":"p01157","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Do LLMs Read Bug Reports? An Empirical Study of Attention in LLMs for Automated Program Repair","tz":"LLM 是怎么读缺陷报告的？面向自动程序修复的 LLM 注意力实证研究","a":"Large Language Model (LLM)-based Automated Program Repair systems are advancing rapidly, yet their performance remains inconsistent. Even when provided with the same contextual information, an LLM may generate a correct patch for one bug but fail on another closely related bug. Why this happens remains poorly understood, and it is unclear how LLMs prioritize the diverse information in bug reports and whether model attention affects repair success. In this paper, we present the first empirical study of attention patterns in LLM-based program repair, providing interpretable insights into how models process bug reports and where their attention is concentrated during repair. We analyze 319 real-world Python and Java bugs from SWE-bench Verified and Multi-SWE-bench to study (RQ1) how model attention is distributed across bug report sections, (RQ2) how attention patterns within each section differ between successful and unsuccessful repairs, and (RQ3) how these patterns compare to information developers consider important for bug fixing. We find that successful repairs are characterized by diffused attention across multiple diagnostic components such as bug descriptions, stacktraces, and test cases, while failures often exhibit over-localized attention toward metadata such as version information. We further observe that stronger alignment between model attention and developer-identified key sections and phrases is associated with higher repair success. Our results provide the first empirical evidence that attention misallocation is a key factor in LLM-based APR failures, and offer actionable insights for designing more interpretable and reliable future APR systems.","az":"基于大语言模型（LLM）的自动程序修复系统正在快速发展，但其性能仍不稳定。即便提供相同的上下文信息，LLM 可能为某个缺陷生成正确补丁，却在另一个高度相似的缺陷上失败。造成这一现象的原因仍缺乏理解，我们也不清楚 LLM 如何在缺陷报告的多样信息中分配优先级，以及模型注意力是否影响修复成功率。本文首次对基于 LLM 的程序修复中的注意力模式开展实证研究，为模型如何处理缺陷报告、以及修复过程中注意力集中在何处提供可解释的洞见。我们分析了来自 SWE-bench Verified 与 Multi-SWE-bench 的 319 个真实 Python 与 Java 缺陷，研究：（RQ1）模型注意力如何分布在缺陷报告的各个部分；（RQ2）在成功与失败的修复之间，各部分内部的注意力模式有何差异；（RQ3）这些模式与开发者认为对修复缺陷重要的信息相比如何。我们发现，成功的修复表现为注意力弥散分布在多个诊断要素上，如缺陷描述、堆栈跟踪和测试用例；而失败的修复往往表现为注意力过度局部化在版本信息等元数据上。我们进一步观察到，模型注意力与开发者标识出的关键段落和短语的对齐程度越高，修复成功率越高。我们的结果首次提供了实证证据，表明注意力错配是基于 LLM 的 APR 失败的关键因素，并为设计更可解释、更可靠的未来 APR 系统提供了可操作的启示。","tl":"首证注意力错配是 LLM 程序修复失败的关键因素。","au":["Ramtin Ehsani","Irene Manotas","Saurabh Pujar","Luca Buratti","Preetha Chatterjee"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["attention analysis","automated program repair","bug reports","SWE-bench","interpretability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/138/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25873"},{"id":"p01158","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Mind the Gap: Do Widely-Used SAST Tools Really Cover the Language-Specific Top CWEs?","tz":"小心差距：主流 SAST 工具真的覆盖了各语言最高频的 CWE 吗？","a":"## Mind the Gap: Do Widely-used SAST Tools Really Cover the Language-Specific Top CWEs? This repository contains the data, evaluation criteria, and experimental results for the research paper: \"Mind the Gap: Do Widely-used SAST Tools Really Cover theLanguage-Specific Top CWEs?\". This study presents a large-scale empirical analysis of nine popular Static Application Security Testing (SAST) tools to evaluate their coverage of language-specific top CWEs across C/C++, Java, and Python. Project Overview Static Application Security Testing (SAST) tools are critical for identifying vulnerabilities early, but existing evaluations often focus on language-agnostic rankings like the MITRE CWE Top 25. This project addresses the mismatch between tool capabilities and developers' actual security needs by:Constructing Language-Specific Datasets: Identifying top CWEs from 197,016 CVEs reported over the past decade. Evaluating Coverage Gaps: Analyzing 9 popular SAST tools to identify where they fail to detect common vulnerabilities. Assessing Migration Potential: Investigating how multi-language tools can reuse existing checkers to fill coverage gaps. ## Repository Structure The project is organized into the following core components: CVEData/ Contains the raw and processed vulnerability data used to identify top CWEs.Primary Source: 197,016 labeled CVE entries from the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) covering 2016 to 2025.Heuristic Labeling: Implementation of the automated labeling process—using file extensions, language names, and 167 manually selected keywords—to map CVEs to specific languages.Accuracy: Manual validation confirms an overall labeling accuracy of 91.5%. CWEView1000/ Contains the hierarchical data for CWE View 1000 (Research Concepts).Comprehensive Set: Includes 944 CWE types organized by their underlying causes and patterns. Root Categories: Systematic organization of all CWEs into 10 root categories (e.g., CWE-664, CWE-707, CWE-284) to ensure a holistic evaluation. ToolData/ Technical specifications and checker data for the nine evaluated SAST tools.Analyzed Tools: CodeQL, Semgrep, SonarQube, Cppcheck, Clang Static Analyzer (CSA), Flawfinder, Insider, SpotBugs + FindSecBugs, and Bandit. Tool Metadata: Includes descriptions of analysis paradigms (e.g., Datalog-based semantic engines, symbolic execution, pattern matching) and the specific CWE checkers each tool implements. RQ Results.xlsx Detailed results for the three core Research Questions (RQs) ## Key Findings Language Sensitivity: Vulnerability patterns are highly language-dependent; Jaccard similarity between C/C++ and other languages is only 0.17 to 0.18.C/C++ Priority: SAST coverage is lowest for C/C++, highlighting a critical need for tool improvement in this area. Complementary Strengths: No single tool achieves complete coverage; practitioners should combine tools based on their specific detection goals. Migration Potential: Leveraging checker migration between languages is a cost-effective way to extend CWE coverage, especially for multi-language tools.","az":"## 小心差距：主流 SAST 工具真的覆盖了各语言最高频的 CWE 吗？本仓库包含论文《Mind the Gap: Do Widely-used SAST Tools Really Cover the Language-Specific Top CWEs?》的数据、评估标准与实验结果。本研究对九款流行的静态应用安全测试（SAST）工具开展大规模实证分析，评估它们在 C/C++、Java 和 Python 上对各语言高频 CWE 的覆盖情况。项目概览：SAST 工具对于尽早发现漏洞至关重要，但现有评估往往聚焦于与语言无关的排行榜，如 MITRE CWE Top 25。本项目通过以下方式弥合工具能力与开发者实际安全需求之间的错配：构建语言特定数据集——从过去十年报告的 197,016 条 CVE 中识别各语言高频 CWE；评估覆盖缺口——分析 9 款流行 SAST 工具，找出它们未能检出常见漏洞之处；评估迁移潜力——研究多语言工具如何复用已有检查器来填补覆盖缺口。## 仓库结构：项目划分为以下核心组成部分。CVEData/：包含用于识别高频 CWE 的原始与处理后漏洞数据。主要来源：来自国家漏洞数据库（NVD）、覆盖 2016 至 2025 年的 197,016 条带标注 CVE 条目。启发式标注：实现了自动标注流程——利用文件扩展名、语言名称和 167 个人工挑选的关键词，将 CVE 映射到特定语言。准确率：人工验证确认整体标注准确率为 91.5%。CWEView1000/：包含 CWE View 1000（Research Concepts）的层次化数据。完整集合：包含按底层成因与模式组织的 944 种 CWE 类型。根类别：将所有 CWE 系统性地组织为 10 个根类别（如 CWE-664、CWE-707、CWE-284），以确保评估的全面性。ToolData/：九款受评 SAST 工具的技术规格与检查器数据。受分析工具：CodeQL、Semgrep、SonarQube、Cppcheck、Clang Static Analyzer（CSA）、Flawfinder、Insider、SpotBugs + FindSecBugs 以及 Bandit。工具元数据：包含对分析范式（如基于 Datalog 的语义引擎、符号执行、模式匹配）的描述，以及每款工具实现的具体 CWE 检查器。RQ Results.xlsx：三个核心研究问题（RQ）的详细结果。## 主要发现：语言敏感性——漏洞模式高度依赖语言，C/C++ 与其他语言之间的 Jaccard 相似度仅为 0.17 到 0.18。C/C++ 优先——SAST 对 C/C++ 的覆盖最低，凸显该领域工具亟需改进。互补优势——没有任何单一工具能实现完整覆盖，实践者应根据具体检测目标组合使用多款工具。迁移潜力——在语言之间迁移检查器是扩展 CWE 覆盖的高性价比途径，对多语言工具尤其如此。","tl":"揭示 SAST 工具对各语言高频 CWE 的系统性覆盖缺口。","au":["zhilin li","Yiran Nie","Xianglong Qi","Jiwei Yan","Jun Yan"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["SAST tools","CWE coverage","CVE analysis","static analysis evaluation","checker migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/139/x"},{"id":"p01159","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Smart Brain: Semantic Anomaly Detection for Operational Time Series in Large Scale Service Systems","tz":"Smart Brain：面向大规模服务系统运维时序数据的语义异常检测","tl":"（据标题推断）以语义方式检测大规模服务系统运维时序异常。","au":["Hang Cui","Zexin Wang","Jingjing Li","Juncheng Hu","Haotian Si","Cenjie Hu","Quan Zhou","Yongchang Hu","Lei Han","Dan Pei","Changhua Pei","Gaogang Xie"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["anomaly detection","operational time series","service systems","AIOps"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/140/x"},{"id":"p01160","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"AgentChaos: Chaos Engineering for Agent Systems via Programmatic Fault Injection","tz":"AgentChaos：通过程序化故障注入对智能体系统做混沌工程","a":"Agent systems rely on LLM APIs for every response, but these APIs can return server errors, truncated responses, or corrupted content that propagates through downstream agents and causes task failure. Evaluating robustness under these faults is crucial for reliable deployment. Existing fault injection methods are offline, require source code modification, or cannot modify specific response fields. A comprehensive evaluation also requires a systematic fault taxonomy because different fault types affect downstream agents differently. We propose AgentChaos, a chaos engineering framework for controlled, runtime, non-intrusive LLM API fault injection. Since all agent systems access LLMs through the same HTTP interface, we inject faults at this shared layer without modifying source code. We define crash, omission, and value faults on content and tool call fields, intercept and modify LLM API responses at runtime, and verify whether each fault is triggered to filter untriggered tasks and avoid underestimating fault impact. Evaluations across agent systems, benchmarks, and backbone LLMs under 65 fault configurations show that all systems degrade under fault injection, with pass@1 dropping by up to 50 percentage points. The ranking is consistent across models, suggesting that robustness depends on system implementation rather than model capability. Existing fault diagnosis methods achieve below 53% accuracy on fault type and below 56% on fault step, leaving room for improvement. We further reveal practical findings for agent system developers.","az":"智能体系统的每一次响应都依赖 LLM API，但这些 API 可能返回服务器错误、被截断的响应或损坏的内容，并沿着下游智能体传播，导致任务失败。评估系统在这些故障下的鲁棒性对于可靠部署至关重要。现有故障注入方法要么是离线的，要么需要修改源代码，要么无法修改响应中的特定字段。全面的评估还需要系统化的故障分类体系，因为不同故障类型对下游智能体的影响各不相同。我们提出 AgentChaos，一个用于受控、运行时、非侵入式 LLM API 故障注入的混沌工程框架。由于所有智能体系统都通过相同的 HTTP 接口访问 LLM，我们在这一共享层注入故障，无需修改源代码。我们在内容字段和工具调用字段上定义了崩溃故障、遗漏故障与取值故障，在运行时拦截并修改 LLM API 响应，并验证每个故障是否被真正触发，以过滤掉未触发的任务、避免低估故障影响。在多个智能体系统、基准测试和骨干 LLM 上、涵盖 65 种故障配置的评估表明，所有系统在故障注入下都出现性能退化，pass@1 最多下降 50 个百分点。这一排名在不同模型间保持一致，说明鲁棒性取决于系统实现而非模型能力。现有故障诊断方法在故障类型上的准确率低于 53%，在故障步骤上低于 56%，仍有很大改进空间。我们还为智能体系统开发者揭示了若干实用发现。","tl":"在 HTTP 层非侵入注入 LLM API 故障，量化智能体系统鲁棒性。","au":["Gou Tan","Zhensu Sun","Jieke Shi","Ting Zhang","Zilong He","Qingfu Wu","Shuai Liang","Weifeng Sun","Junda He","Pengfei Chen","Chuanfu Zhang","Lwin Khin Shar","David Lo"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["chaos engineering","fault injection","agent systems","LLM API robustness","fault taxonomy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/141/x"},{"id":"p01161","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Precise and Efficient Static Data Race Detection","tz":"精确且高效的静态数据竞争检测","tl":"（据标题推断）兼顾精度与效率的静态数据竞争检测方法。","au":["Pei Wang","Zhihang Sun","Fei He"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["data race detection","static analysis","concurrency","precision and scalability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/142/x"},{"id":"p01162","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Best-Effort GR(1) Synthesis: Exploiting Environmental Cooperation under Unrealizability","tz":"尽力而为的 GR(1) 综合：在不可实现性下利用环境协作","tl":"（据标题推断）不可实现规约下借环境协作做尽力而为综合。","au":["Sirui Liu","Yating Zhang","Chi Hu","Wei Dong"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["GR(1) synthesis","reactive synthesis","unrealizability","environment assumptions"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/143/x"},{"id":"p01163","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TELLER: Non-intrusive Cross-Layer Root-Cause Analysis for LLM Inference","tz":"TELLER：面向 LLM 推理的非侵入式跨层根因分析","a":"Large language model (LLM) inference has evolved from an offline workload into a continuously operated software service, yet root-cause analysis remains difficult because a single request spans the inference engine, Python/C++ backend, host CUDA APIs, GPU kernels, and distributed communication. Existing profilers expose raw timelines, while log-based diagnosis often misses cross-layer execution semantics and request-level structure. We present TELLER, a non-intrusive Trace- and Log-aware LLM inference Root-cause analysis framework. TELLER first collects NVTX/CUPTI traces and service logs without modifying model binaries, then reconstructs per-request call-chain trees and aligns log lines with the corresponding execution steps. We introduce a dependency-aware causal-context slice that preserves parent-child structure, temporal order, and communication relations, and a Trace Pair Encoding (TPE) tokenizer that compresses such slices into compact structural token sequences with parent, depth, and duration attributes. On top of these representations, TELLER combines numeric candidate localization with a multimodal root-cause model that jointly predicts abnormal steps, localizes suspicious operators, and generates natural-language explanations. Experiments on multi-node GPU inference workloads show a clear compression-accuracy trade-off: a moderate TPE vocabulary reduces per-step trace length by more than 80% while achieving the best overall performance on both horizontal (cross-node communication) and vertical (within-node execution stack) views, whereas more aggressive compression substantially degrades diagnosis quality. Further analyses under low-fault priors, strengthened baselines, modality ablations, explanation-quality checks, and tracing overhead show that TELLER provides a practical triage and evidence-localization substrate for LLM inference RCA.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）推理已从离线负载演变为持续运行的软件服务，但根因分析仍然困难，因为单个请求会跨越推理引擎、Python/C++ 后端、主机 CUDA API、GPU kernel 以及分布式通信。现有性能剖析器只暴露原始时间线，而基于日志的诊断往往缺失跨层执行语义与请求级结构。我们提出 TELLER，一个非侵入式的、感知 trace 与日志的 LLM 推理根因分析框架。TELLER 首先在不修改模型二进制的情况下收集 NVTX/CUPTI trace 与服务日志，随后重建每个请求的调用链树，并将日志行与对应的执行步骤对齐。我们引入了一种依赖感知的因果上下文切片，它保留父子结构、时间顺序与通信关系；以及一种 Trace Pair Encoding（TPE）分词器，把这类切片压缩为带有父节点、深度与时长属性的紧凑结构化 token 序列。在这些表示之上，TELLER 将数值候选定位与一个多模态根因模型相结合，联合预测异常步骤、定位可疑算子并生成自然语言解释。在多节点 GPU 推理负载上的实验展示了清晰的压缩—准确率权衡：适中的 TPE 词表可将每步 trace 长度缩短 80% 以上，同时在横向（跨节点通信）与纵向（节点内执行栈）两个视角上都取得最佳整体性能；而更激进的压缩会显著降低诊断质量。在低故障先验、强化基线、模态消融实验、解释质量检查与追踪开销等方面的进一步分析表明，TELLER 为 LLM 推理根因分析提供了实用的分诊与证据定位基础设施。","tl":"用 trace 压缩编码实现 LLM 推理栈跨层根因定位与解释。","au":["Ruilin Xu","Junyi Li","Pengfei Chen","Zongxuan Xie"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["root cause analysis","LLM inference serving","trace and log analysis","GPU profiling","Trace Pair Encoding"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/144/x"},{"id":"p01164","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Predicate-Guided Synthesis of Input Generators via Gentoo","tz":"Gentoo：谓词引导的输入生成器合成","a":"Modern generator-based fuzzing techniques combine lightweight input generators with coverage-guided mutation as a method of exploring deep execution paths in a target program. A complimentary approach in prior research focuses on creating highly customized, domain-specific generators that encode structural and semantic logic sufficient enough to reach deep program states; the challenge comes from the overhead of writing and testing these complex generators. We investigate whether AI coding agents can automatically synthesize such target-specific generators, and whether the resulting generators are strong enough to obviate the need for coverage guidance and mutation entirely. Our approach, Gentoo, is comprised of an LLM coding agent (provided terminal access and source code of the fuzz target and its library) instructed to iteratively synthesize and refine an input generator, and optionally provided fine-grained predicate-level coverage feedback. We evaluate three configurations of Gentoo against human-written generators on fuzz targets for 7 real-world Java libraries. Our findings show that agent-synthesized generators achieve statistically significantly higher branch coverage than human-written baseline generators on 4 of 7 benchmarks. Critically, the use of coverage guidance and mutation strategies is not statistically significantly beneficial for agent-synthesized generators, but is significant for all human-written generators, suggesting that structural and semantic logic encoded in the agent generators makes coverage guidance largely unnecessary.","az":"现代基于生成器的模糊测试技术把轻量输入生成器与覆盖率引导的变异结合起来，作为探索目标程序深层执行路径的手段。先前研究中一条互补路线是构建高度定制的领域专用生成器，其中编码了足以到达深层程序状态的结构与语义逻辑；难点在于编写和测试这些复杂生成器的开销。我们研究 AI 编程智能体能否自动合成这类针对特定目标的生成器，以及所得生成器是否强到足以完全省去覆盖率引导与变异。我们的方法 Gentoo 由一个 LLM 编程智能体构成（该智能体可访问终端以及模糊测试目标及其库的源代码），被指示迭代地合成并精化输入生成器，并可选地获得细粒度的谓词级覆盖率反馈。我们在 7 个真实 Java 库的模糊测试目标上，将 Gentoo 的三种配置与人工编写的生成器进行比较。结果表明，在 7 个基准中的 4 个上，智能体合成的生成器取得了统计显著更高的分支覆盖率。关键的是，覆盖率引导与变异策略对智能体合成的生成器并没有统计显著的收益，但对所有人工编写的生成器都是显著的，这说明智能体生成器中编码的结构与语义逻辑，使覆盖率引导在很大程度上变得不必要。","tl":"编程智能体合成的输入生成器可让覆盖率引导变得多余。","au":["Vasudev Vikram","Rohan Padhye"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["generator-based fuzzing","input generator synthesis","LLM coding agent","predicate coverage","branch coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/145/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.01442"},{"id":"p01165","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DepUpgrade: Automating Dependency Upgrade through State-Path Exploration","tz":"DepUpgrade：通过状态路径探索实现依赖升级自动化","tl":"（据标题推断）用状态路径探索自动完成依赖版本升级。","au":["Yifan An","Xiangxi Ma","Wentong Tian","Xuanqi Wang","Qingao Dong","Xiang Gao","Hailong Sun"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["dependency upgrade","state-path exploration","build breakage","library migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/146/x"},{"id":"p01166","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PWCC: Probability-Weighted Combinatorial Coverage for Risk-Informed Scenario Testing of Autonomous Systems","tz":"PWCC：面向自主系统风险感知场景测试的概率加权组合覆盖","tl":"（据标题推断）用概率加权组合覆盖衡量自主系统场景测试充分性。","au":["Borhaneddine Hamadou","Chokri Mraidha","Nicholas Matragkas"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["combinatorial coverage","scenario testing","autonomous systems","risk-informed testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/147/x"},{"id":"p01167","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Lost in Translation, Found in Summary: Summary-Driven Supervision for Cross-Language Code Retrieval","tz":"翻译中失落，摘要中寻回：面向跨语言代码检索的摘要驱动监督","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench's macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施大多用 C 语言编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全性，研究者正在探索把 C 自动翻译到 Rust 等更安全语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不只包含 C 代码，还常常使用被称为宏（macro）的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。最先进的技术通过先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译来回避宏的翻译，但这种做法产出的译文与原始 C 代码差异很大，因为预处理会把所有宏定义内联展开。为了在翻译后的代码中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并把它们提炼为首个具有形式化规约的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们提出首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机采样的宏构建。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估大语言模型（LLM）在此前未被研究过的宏翻译任务上的有效性。LLM 翻译的 MacroBench 用例比 MerC 多出 22% 到 77%，但其中有 8% 到 28% 的翻译是错误的，需要开发者额外验证；相比之下，MerC 只产生正确的翻译。我们的核心洞见是：先运行 MerC、再对剩余部分使用 LLM，比单独使用任一技术收益更大。这种“组队”方式的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时平均比 MerC 多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"用代码摘要作监督信号弥合跨语言代码检索的语义鸿沟。","au":["Zhijie Liu","Yisi Liu","Linxi Jiang","Yutian Tang","Lili Xiao","Zhipeng Xue"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","low-resource-or-non-english"],"kw":["cross-language code retrieval","summary-driven supervision","code search","code representation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/148/x"},{"id":"p01168","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ExeCRE: Execution-Consistency Guided Reliability Estimation for Self-Correcting Code Generation","tz":"ExeCRE：面向自纠错代码生成的执行一致性引导可靠性估计","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench's macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施大多用 C 语言编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全性，研究者正在探索把 C 自动翻译到 Rust 等更安全语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不只包含 C 代码，还常常使用被称为宏（macro）的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。最先进的技术通过先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译来回避宏的翻译，但这种做法产出的译文与原始 C 代码差异很大，因为预处理会把所有宏定义内联展开。为了在翻译后的代码中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并把它们提炼为首个具有形式化规约的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们提出首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机采样的宏构建。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估大语言模型（LLM）在此前未被研究过的宏翻译任务上的有效性。LLM 翻译的 MacroBench 用例比 MerC 多出 22% 到 77%，但其中有 8% 到 28% 的翻译是错误的，需要开发者额外验证；相比之下，MerC 只产生正确的翻译。我们的核心洞见是：先运行 MerC、再对剩余部分使用 LLM，比单独使用任一技术收益更大。这种“组队”方式的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时平均比 MerC 多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"用执行一致性信号判断自纠错代码何时可信、何时该停。","au":["Yiru Dong","Richong Zhang","Fanshuang Kong","Si Chen"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["reliability estimation","execution consistency","self-correcting code generation","confidence estimation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/149/x"},{"id":"p01169","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"DAGGER: Dynamic Agentic Graph-Guided Efficient Reasoner for Container Image Dependency Optimization","tz":"DAGGER：面向容器镜像依赖优化的动态图引导高效智能体推理器","tl":"（据标题推断）用依赖图引导的智能体精简容器镜像依赖。","au":["Shikhar Vashistha","Neetesh Kumar"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["container image","dependency optimization","agentic reasoning","graph-guided","Docker"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/150/x"},{"id":"p01170","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RamFuzz: LLM-Guided Greybox Fuzzing for Spatial Memory Corruption via Valid Range Violation","tz":"RamFuzz：基于有效范围违规的 LLM 引导灰盒模糊测试挖掘空间内存破坏","tl":"（据标题推断）以有效范围违规为导向用 LLM 引导模糊测试找内存越界。","au":["Shangzhi Xu","Wei Song","Yuekang Li","Nan Sun","Muhammad Ejaz Ahmed","Willy Susilo","Benjamin Turnbull","Xiao Cheng","Siqi Ma"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["greybox fuzzing","spatial memory corruption","valid range violation","LLM-guided fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/151/x"},{"id":"p01171","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"To Ban or Not to Ban? How Open Source Projects Govern GenAI Contributions","tz":"禁还是不禁？开源项目如何治理生成式 AI 贡献","a":"Generative AI (GenAI) is playing an increasingly important role in open source software (OSS). Beyond completing code and documentation, GenAI is increasingly involved in issues, pull requests, code reviews, and security reports. Yet, cheaper generation does not mean cheaper review - and the resulting maintenance burden has pushed OSS projects to experiment with GenAI-specific rules in contribution guidelines, security policies, and repository instructions, even including a total ban on AI-assisted contributions. However, governing GenAI in OSS is far more than a ban-or-not question. The responses remain scattered, with neither a shared governance framework in practice nor a systematic understanding in research. Therefore, in this paper, we conduct a multi-stage analysis on various qualitative materials related to GenAI governance retrieved from 67 highly visible OSS projects. Our analysis identifies recurring concerns across contribution workflows, derives three governance orientations, and maps out 12 governance strategies and their policy instruments. We show that governing GenAI in OSS extends well beyond banning - it requires coordinated responses across accountability, verification, review capacity, code provenance, and platform infrastructure. Overall, our work distills dispersed community practices into a structured overview, providing a conceptual baseline for researchers and a practical reference for maintainers and platform designers.","az":"生成式 AI（GenAI）在开源软件（OSS）中扮演着越来越重要的角色。除了补全代码和文档，GenAI 也越来越多地参与 issue、拉取请求、代码审查和安全报告。然而，生成变便宜并不意味着审查也变便宜——由此带来的维护负担促使 OSS 项目开始在贡献指南、安全策略和仓库说明中尝试制定针对 GenAI 的规则，甚至包括完全禁止 AI 辅助的贡献。但在 OSS 中治理 GenAI 远不止“禁或不禁”这一个问题。各方回应仍然零散，实践中既没有共享的治理框架，研究上也缺乏系统性的理解。为此，本文对从 67 个高知名度 OSS 项目中检索到的、与 GenAI 治理相关的各类定性材料开展多阶段分析。我们的分析识别出贯穿贡献工作流的反复出现的关切，提炼出三种治理取向，并梳理出 12 种治理策略及其政策工具。我们表明，在 OSS 中治理 GenAI 远超“封禁”本身——它需要在问责、验证、审查能力、代码溯源与平台基础设施等方面做出协调一致的回应。总体而言，我们的工作把分散的社区实践提炼为结构化的全景视图，为研究者提供概念基线，也为维护者和平台设计者提供实用参考。","tl":"提炼开源社区治理 GenAI 贡献的三种取向与 12 种策略。","au":["Wenhao Yang","Runzhi He","Minghui Zhou"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["open source governance","generative AI contributions","contribution guidelines","maintainer burden","policy instruments"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/152/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.26487"},{"id":"p01172","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GraphDroid: Asynchronous LLM-Based Mobile App GUI Testing via History-Aware Exploration and Hybrid Intent Fulfillment","tz":"GraphDroid：通过历史感知探索与混合意图达成实现异步 LLM 移动应用 GUI 测试","tl":"（据标题推断）异步 LLM 调度加历史感知探索提升 GUI 测试覆盖。","au":["Xiaolei Li","Jialun Cao","Zhijian Hou","Yuzhi Zhao","Yepang Liu","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"gui-computer-use-agents","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mobile GUI testing","LLM-based exploration","history-aware","intent fulfillment","Android"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/153/x"},{"id":"p01173","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"VARIES: Verification Harness Synthesis and Efficient Scheduling for Unsoundness Detection in Rust Libraries","tz":"VARIES：面向 Rust 库不健全性检测的验证 Harness 合成与高效调度","tl":"（据标题推断）合成并调度验证 harness 揪出 Rust 库的 unsoundness。","au":["Huan Li","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Xinyu Wang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["verification harness synthesis","Rust unsoundness","unsafe code","scheduling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/154/x"},{"id":"p01174","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Prism: A Multi-solution Reasoning and Synthesis Framework for Repository-Level Issue Resolution","tz":"Prism：面向仓库级 Issue 求解的多方案推理与综合框架","tl":"（据标题推断）生成并综合多个候选方案来求解仓库级 issue。","au":["Yibo Wang","Guotian Wang","Zhihao Peng","Ying Wang","Chang Xu","Zhiliang Zhu"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["issue resolution","repository-level","multi-solution reasoning","SWE agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/155/x"},{"id":"p01175","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RepoProbe: Benchmarking Architecture-Aware Repository Comprehension with Checklists","tz":"RepoProbe：用检查清单评测架构感知的仓库理解能力","a":"The integration of Large Language Models (LLMs) into software engineering has shifted the focus from function-level generation to repository-scale assistance. However, existing benchmarks largely rely on bug reports from GitHub Issues, which often allow models to bypass genuine understanding via pattern matching on error logs. This misalignment under-measures Edit Bias, which refers to premature generation, where models prematurely propose code modifications instead of understanding the existing repository architecture. Furthermore, current LLM-as-a-Judge scalar scoring suffers from high variance and low interpretability. This work introduces RepoProbe, a novel benchmark for evaluating repository-level code understanding through open-ended Q&A using GitHub Discussions, which focuses on open-ended architectural inquiries rather than defect reporting. To ensure rigorous evaluation, we propose a Checklist-Based Verification Protocol that decomposes answers into atomic, verifiable facts, thereby replacing subjective ratings with objective verification. Our evaluation of state-of-the-art (SOTA) LLMs reveals a persistent gap between high clarity and evidencegrounded technical correctness. It also quantitatively confirms the prevalence of edit bias, in which models prioritize code generation instead of architectural analysis. Finally, we demonstrate that our verification protocol significantly improves evaluation reliability compared to traditional evaluations with scalar scoring.","az":"把大语言模型（LLM）引入软件工程，已使关注点从函数级生成转向仓库级辅助。然而，现有基准大多依赖 GitHub Issues 中的缺陷报告，这常常让模型可以通过在错误日志上做模式匹配来绕过真正的理解。这种错配低估了“编辑偏置”（Edit Bias），即模型过早地提出代码修改，而不是先理解既有的仓库架构。此外，当前 LLM-as-a-Judge 的标量打分方差大、可解释性低。本文提出 RepoProbe，一个通过基于 GitHub Discussions 的开放式问答来评估仓库级代码理解的新基准，它关注开放式的架构性问询而非缺陷报告。为确保评估的严谨性，我们提出一套基于检查清单的验证协议，把答案分解为原子的、可验证的事实，从而用客观验证取代主观评分。我们对当前最先进（SOTA）LLM 的评估揭示出：模型在表述清晰度上很高，但与证据相符的技术正确性之间始终存在差距。评估还定量确认了编辑偏置的普遍存在，即模型优先生成代码而非进行架构分析。最后，我们证明，与传统的标量打分评估相比，我们的验证协议显著提升了评估的可靠性。","tl":"用检查清单式事实核验量化 LLM 仓库架构理解与编辑偏置。","au":["Yuexi Yang","Alyssa Wu","Ji Luo","Richeng Xuan","Zhichao Hu","Yuhong Liu","Zhen Qin"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["repository comprehension","checklist verification","GitHub Discussions","edit bias","LLM-as-a-judge"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/156/x"},{"id":"p01176","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RFC2TLA+: Extracting and Verifying Formal Models from RFC Documents using Continuous LLM Feedback","tz":"RFC2TLA+：利用持续的 LLM 反馈从 RFC 文档中抽取并验证形式化模型","tl":"（据标题推断）用 LLM 持续反馈把 RFC 文本自动转成可验证的 TLA+ 模型。","au":["Guozhen Ding","Kexin Li","Ilya Grishchenko","David Lie"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["TLA+","formal model extraction","RFC documents","LLM feedback","protocol verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/157/x"},{"id":"p01177","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"It Takes Two to Tango: Accelerating Code Generation via Cache-Inspired Hierarchical Speculative Decoding","tz":"独木不成林：借助缓存启发的分层投机解码加速代码生成","a":"This repository contains code and the distilled checkpoints of the draft models for CodeLlama-34b and Deepseek-Code-33b for the paper “It Takes Two to Tango: Accelerating Code Generation via Cache-Inspired Hierarchical Speculative Decoding”. CacheCoder.zip contains the source code of this research. checkpoints.zip contains the distilled weights of the draft model used in this research.","az":"本仓库包含论文《It Takes Two to Tango: Accelerating Code Generation via Cache-Inspired Hierarchical Speculative Decoding》中面向 CodeLlama-34b 与 Deepseek-Code-33b 的草稿模型代码及蒸馏后的检查点。CacheCoder.zip 包含本研究的源代码，checkpoints.zip 包含本研究所用草稿模型的蒸馏权重。","tl":"提出缓存启发的分层投机解码，显著加速代码生成推理。","au":["Yinggang Qiu","Shangwen Wang","Yihao Qin","Mingyang Geng","Dezun Dong"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["speculative decoding","code generation","draft model","inference acceleration","CodeLlama"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/158/x"},{"id":"p01178","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"One Is Not Enough: The Untold Story of Multiple Security Patches for One Vulnerability","tz":"一个补丁还不够：一个漏洞对应多个安全补丁的隐秘真相","a":"Security patches (SPs) are the main mechanism for fixing software vulnerabilities, yet a single vulnerability is not always resolved by a single patch: fixes may be completed incrementally, propagated across maintained branches, or replicated across related repositories. When patch records are incomplete, downstream users may observe only part of the required fix set and therefore apply only partial patching. However, comprehensive patch discovery remains difficult because the prevalence and causes of the multi-SP phenomenon are still poorly understood. In this paper, we present the first large-scale empirical study of multi-SP vulnerabilities. By merging four major vulnerability databases, we construct a dataset of 6,053 multi-SP CVEs with 16,260 SPs, showing that 20.6% of CVEs with patches involve multiple SPs and that merging databases increases recognized multi-SP CVE counts by 36-55% over any single source. We further analyze why a vulnerability is associated with multiple SPs and derive a two-level taxonomy with 6 categories and 16 sub-categories. Based on these findings, we develop SPectre, a taxonomy-driven prototype for comprehensive patch discovery. On 300 multi-SP CVEs, after manually verifying ground-truth SPs, SPectre improves multi-SP patch coverage over representative patch localization baselines, achieving 0.927 recall on same-repository cases and 0.873 recall on cross-repository cases after manual ground truth verification. On 100 recent CVEs recorded as single-patch by all public databases, SPectre further discovers 28 previously unreported SPs across 20 CVEs. Our results show that multi-SP vulnerabilities are both prevalent and systematically underreported, motivating stronger patch-completeness awareness, improved vulnerability database curation, and relation-aware security tooling.","az":"安全补丁（SP）是修复软件漏洞的主要手段，然而单个漏洞并不总是由单个补丁解决：修复可能是增量完成的，可能被传播到多个维护分支，也可能被复制到相关仓库中。当补丁记录不完整时，下游用户可能只看到所需修复集合的一部分，从而只做了部分打补丁。然而，全面的补丁发现依然困难，因为多安全补丁（multi-SP）现象的普遍程度与成因仍缺乏了解。本文首次对多安全补丁漏洞开展大规模实证研究。通过合并四个主流漏洞数据库，我们构建了一个包含 6,053 个 multi-SP CVE、16,260 个安全补丁的数据集，结果显示在有补丁的 CVE 中有 20.6% 涉及多个安全补丁，且合并数据库相比任何单一来源能使可识别的 multi-SP CVE 数量提升 36%-55%。我们进一步分析了一个漏洞为何会关联多个安全补丁，并推导出一个包含 6 个大类、16 个子类的两级分类体系。基于这些发现，我们开发了 SPectre——一个由分类体系驱动的全面补丁发现原型。在 300 个 multi-SP CVE 上，经人工核验真实补丁后，SPectre 相比有代表性的补丁定位基线提升了多补丁覆盖率，在同仓库场景下召回率达 0.927，在跨仓库场景下达 0.873。在 100 个被所有公开数据库记为单补丁的近期 CVE 上，SPectre 还在 20 个 CVE 中额外发现了 28 个此前未被报告的安全补丁。我们的结果表明，多安全补丁漏洞既普遍又被系统性地漏报，这促使我们更加重视补丁完整性、改进漏洞数据库的整理方式并构建关系感知的安全工具。","tl":"首次大规模揭示“一漏洞多补丁”现象并给出补丁发现原型。","au":["Fangyuan Zhang","Lyuye Zhang","Lingling Fan","Chengwei Liu","Yinan Li","Liang Huang","Yang Liu","Zheli Liu","Sen Chen"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["security patches","multi-SP vulnerabilities","patch discovery","CVE databases","patch completeness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/159/x"},{"id":"p01179","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Not as Sweet by Another Name: An Empirical Study of Format Robustness in LLM Document Workflows","tz":"换个名字就不甜了：LLM 文档工作流中格式鲁棒性的实证研究","a":"The machine learning(ML) component of an ML-enabled system evolves through retraining, fine-tuning, and optimization, so previously valid test results may no longer hold. A single evolution step can worsen performance on some test cases while improving others, making regression test prioritization inherently directional. We present Gradient-based Behavior Vector-Parameter Delta(GBV-PD), the first approach to operationalize the behavior vector space for evolution-aware regression test prioritization. GBV-PD represents each test case as a gradient-based vector(GBV), a low-dimensional projection of its loss gradient under the original model. It then projects the observed parameter update of the evolved model onto the same PCA basis and uses the resulting alignment to estimate whether each test case's loss is likely to increase or decrease, without running the evolved model on test cases during prioritization. In an empirical study across classification and regression tasks, GBV-PD consistently outperformed non-directional baselines and remained competitive with a full-gradient reference, while offering better time and storage profiles for repeated updates via reusable GBV caching. These results show that behavior-space ideas can be operationalized into a practical and efficient mechanism for repeated-update regression testing of evolving ML-enabled systems.","az":"机器学习（ML）赋能系统中的 ML 组件会经由重训练、微调和优化不断演化，因此此前有效的测试结果可能不再成立。一次演化步骤可能让部分测试用例表现变差、同时让另一些变好，这使得回归测试优先级排序本质上带有方向性。我们提出了基于梯度的行为向量—参数增量方法（GBV-PD），这是首个将行为向量空间落地用于演化感知回归测试优先级排序的方法。GBV-PD 将每个测试用例表示为一个基于梯度的向量（GBV），即该用例在原始模型下损失梯度的低维投影。随后它把演化后模型观测到的参数更新投影到同一 PCA 基上，并利用由此得到的对齐程度来估计每个测试用例的损失更可能上升还是下降，且在排序阶段无需在演化后的模型上真正运行这些测试用例。在覆盖分类与回归任务的实证研究中，GBV-PD 持续优于非方向性基线，并与使用完整梯度的参考方法保持竞争力，同时借助可复用的 GBV 缓存，在重复更新场景下具有更好的时间与存储开销。这些结果表明，行为空间的思想可以被落地为一种实用且高效的机制，用于不断演化的 ML 赋能系统的重复更新式回归测试。","tl":"用梯度行为向量预测测试损失升降，实现有方向的回归测试排序。","au":["Xiaoyu Zhang","Xianyun Cheng","Tianlin Li","Yuwei Zheng","Yue Yang","Yang Liu"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["regression test prioritization","ML-enabled systems","gradient behavior vector","model evolution","test selection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/160/x"},{"id":"p01180","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RealisticTritonBench: A Benchmark for Triton-Kernel Generation in Real-World AI Frameworks","tz":"RealisticTritonBench：面向真实 AI 框架的 Triton 内核生成基准","a":"In modern AI frameworks, GPU kernels are key to overall system performance. Combining usability, portability, and near-handwritten CUDA performance, Triton is widely adopted for implementing GPU kernels. Recent advances show the potential of large language models (LLMs) to automatically generate Triton kernels, reducing the manual effort required from expert kernel developers. Several benchmarks evaluate LLM-generated Triton kernels. However, they suffer from three key limitations: (1) they restrict tasks to PyTorch-to-Triton translation, failing to reflect the diversity and complexity of real-world Triton tasks; (2) they evaluate only individual-kernel performance rather than end-to-end performance, the core criterion for real-world deployment in AI frameworks; and (3) they rely on manually written evaluation scripts for individual kernels, which may contain flaws that models can exploit to bypass correctness checks and obtain inflated scores. To address these limitations, we introduce RealisticTritonBench, the first benchmark to derive Triton kernel generation tasks from real-world pull requests in popular AI frameworks, enabling realistic, production-like evaluation. RealisticTritonBench systematically extracts PRs that modify Triton kernels from popular open-source AI frameworks and transforms them into generation tasks with concrete engineering contexts. Each task takes a natural language requirement as input and requires a corresponding Triton kernel implementation, with a complete and reproducible evaluation environment. Unlike prior benchmarks focused on isolated kernel performance, RealisticTritonBench integrates generated kernels into their original frameworks and evaluates them using end-to-end tests, enabling a more faithful assessment. We evaluate leading LLMs on RealisticTritonBench and find that they still struggle with real-world Triton kernel generation tasks.","az":"在现代 AI 框架中，GPU 内核是整体系统性能的关键。Triton 兼顾易用性、可移植性以及接近手写 CUDA 的性能，被广泛用于实现 GPU 内核。近期进展表明，大语言模型（LLM）有望自动生成 Triton 内核，从而减少专家内核开发者的人工投入。已有若干基准用于评估 LLM 生成的 Triton 内核，但它们存在三大局限：（1）把任务限制为 PyTorch 到 Triton 的翻译，无法反映真实 Triton 任务的多样性与复杂性；（2）只评估单个内核的性能，而非真实部署中最核心的端到端性能；（3）依赖为单个内核手工编写的评测脚本，这些脚本可能存在缺陷，被模型利用来绕过正确性检查、获得虚高分数。为解决这些问题，我们提出 RealisticTritonBench，这是首个从流行 AI 框架的真实 pull request 中派生 Triton 内核生成任务的基准，从而实现贴近生产环境的真实评测。RealisticTritonBench 系统性地从流行开源 AI 框架中抽取修改 Triton 内核的 PR，并将其转化为带有具体工程上下文的生成任务。每个任务以自然语言需求为输入，要求给出相应的 Triton 内核实现，并配有完整且可复现的评测环境。与以往关注孤立内核性能的基准不同，RealisticTritonBench 将生成的内核集成回其原始框架，并使用端到端测试进行评估，从而获得更忠实的评价。我们在 RealisticTritonBench 上评测了领先的 LLM，发现它们在真实世界的 Triton 内核生成任务上仍然吃力。","tl":"首个源自真实 PR、按端到端测试评分的 Triton 内核生成基准。","au":["Jinjun Huang","Zhongzhen Wen","Tongtong Xu","Meng Yan","Xin Xia","Zhongxin Liu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["Triton kernel generation","benchmark","GPU kernels","end-to-end evaluation","pull requests"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/161/x"},{"id":"p01181","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Guessing to Seeing: Enhancing LLM-Based Program Repair via Trace-Guided Multi-strategy Debate","tz":"从猜测到看见：通过轨迹引导的多策略辩论增强基于 LLM 的程序修复","a":"Automated Program Repair (APR) aims to resolve software bugs without human intervention, but complex logic errors and silent failures remain challenging. Existing LLM-based APR methods mainly rely on source code and coarse test feedback, making it difficult to capture runtime behaviors and dynamic data dependencies. Execution traces expose concrete state transitions, yet a single LLM interpreting them in isolation may commit to an incorrect repair hypothesis and produce test-overfitting patches. We therefore treat runtime evidence as shared constraints for validating repair hypotheses rather than merely as additional prompt context. We propose TraceRepair, a multi-agent framework in which a Probe Agent captures execution snapshots of critical variables, while specialized repair agents generate, compare, and iteratively refine candidate patches against the observed runtime evidence. A Judge Agent then arbitrates the remaining hypotheses and synthesizes the final patch. Evaluated on Defects4J, TraceRepair correctly fixes 392 defects and outperforms existing LLM-based approaches. Further experiments demonstrate improved efficiency and strong generalization on a newly constructed dataset of recent bugs, suggesting that the gains arise from dynamic reasoning rather than memorization.","az":"自动程序修复（APR）旨在无需人工干预地解决软件缺陷，但复杂的逻辑错误与静默失败仍然具有挑战性。现有基于 LLM 的 APR 方法主要依赖源代码和粗粒度的测试反馈，难以捕捉运行时行为与动态数据依赖。执行轨迹能够暴露具体的状态转移，但单个 LLM 孤立地解读轨迹时可能过早锁定错误的修复假设，产生过拟合测试的补丁。因此，我们把运行时证据视为验证修复假设的共享约束，而不仅仅是额外的提示上下文。我们提出 TraceRepair，一个多智能体框架：Probe Agent 负责捕获关键变量的执行快照，专门的修复智能体则针对观测到的运行时证据生成、比较并迭代精化候选补丁；随后由 Judge Agent 对剩余假设进行裁决并合成最终补丁。在 Defects4J 上，TraceRepair 正确修复了 392 个缺陷，优于已有的基于 LLM 的方法。进一步实验表明其效率更高，并在新构建的近期缺陷数据集上具有很强的泛化性，说明性能提升源自动态推理而非记忆。","tl":"把执行轨迹作为共享约束，多智能体辩论裁决出更可靠补丁。","au":["Jiaqing Wu","Tong Wu","Manqing Zhang","Yunwei Dong","Bo Shen"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["automated program repair","execution traces","multi-agent debate","Defects4J","patch overfitting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/162/x"},{"id":"p01182","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Extensions Lie: Large-Scale Study of Privacy Policy Compliance in Browser Extensions","tz":"当扩展说谎时：浏览器扩展隐私政策合规性的大规模研究","a":"ExtPolice-Artifact This artifact accompanies our ASE 2026 submission: \"When Extensions Lie: Large-scale Study of Privacy Policy Compliance in Browser Extensions\".Due to double-blind review requirements, certain components of the artifact have been anonymized, sanitized, or partially withheld. The full artifact will be released upon acceptance. Repository Structure dataset/: Contains the datasets used in our evaluation: auth_sites.csv: List of authenticated websites. URLs are removed for anonymity. unauth_sites.csv: List of unauthenticated websites. flagged_extensions.csv: Extensions observed with privacy-related behaviors. patches/: Chromium patches implementing our multi-type taint analysis engine. As our prototype builds upon Arcanum, we provide diff files against the Arcanum baseline. prompts/: Prompt templates used for LLM-based sensitive content identification and policy analysis. sample_webpages/: A subset of webpages from our dataset, with sensitive information redacted or replaced. scripts/: Scripts supporting different stages of our analysis pipeline. Some auxiliary configuration and utility scripts are omitted in this anonymized release.","az":"ExtPolice-Artifact：本制品配套我们的 ASE 2026 投稿《When Extensions Lie: Large-scale Study of Privacy Policy Compliance in Browser Extensions》。由于双盲评审要求，制品中的部分组件已被匿名化、脱敏或部分保留未公开，完整制品将在论文录用后发布。仓库结构：dataset/ 包含评测所用数据集：auth_sites.csv 为已登录网站列表（URL 已移除以保证匿名性）；unauth_sites.csv 为未登录网站列表；flagged_extensions.csv 为观察到存在隐私相关行为的扩展。patches/ 为实现我们多类型污点分析引擎的 Chromium 补丁；由于原型基于 Arcanum 构建，我们提供相对 Arcanum 基线的 diff 文件。prompts/ 为用于基于 LLM 的敏感内容识别与政策分析的提示模板。sample_webpages/ 为数据集中网页的一个子集，其中敏感信息已被涂抹或替换。scripts/ 为支撑分析流水线各阶段的脚本，本匿名版本中省略了部分辅助配置与工具脚本。","tl":"用多类型污点分析大规模核查浏览器扩展是否违背其隐私政策。","au":["Zilun Wang","Zeyang Zhuang","Mingxue Zhang","Wei Meng","Michael Lyu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["browser extensions","privacy policy compliance","taint analysis","Chromium","large-scale study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/163/x"},{"id":"p01183","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MultiKernelBench: A Multi-platform Benchmark for Kernel Generation","tz":"MultiKernelBench：面向内核生成的多平台基准","tl":"（据标题推断）首个跨多种硬件平台评测 GPU 内核生成的基准。","au":["Zhongzhen Wen","zhangyinghui","Zhong Li","Zhongxin Liu","Linna Xie","Tian Zhang"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["kernel generation","multi-platform benchmark","GPU kernels","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/164/x"},{"id":"p01184","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Post-quantum Cryptography in the Wild: Assessing the Readiness of Open-Source Ecosystems","tz":"野外的后量子密码学：评估开源生态的就绪程度","tl":"（据标题推断）大规模测量开源生态向后量子密码迁移的就绪度。","au":["Tongxin Yuan","Zhanpeng Liu","Jiashuo Liang","Zhuosheng Zhang","Gongshen Liu","Yang Yu","Guancheng Li"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","security"],"kw":["post-quantum cryptography","open-source ecosystem","migration readiness","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/165/x"},{"id":"p01185","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CodeFault: Predicting Fault Risks from Code Changes via Multi-modal Learning","tz":"CodeFault：通过多模态学习从代码变更预测缺陷风险","tl":"（据标题推断）用多模态学习融合代码变更信号预测缺陷风险。","au":["Yifan Xiao","Shijie Li","Yu Huang"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["multimodal"],"kw":["defect prediction","code changes","multi-modal learning","fault risk"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/166/x"},{"id":"p01186","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ReLog: Execution-Aware Logging with Runtime Feedback for LLM-Oriented Debugging","tz":"ReLog：面向 LLM 调试的运行时反馈驱动的执行感知日志生成","a":"Logging statements are essential for software debugging and maintenance. However, existing approaches to automatic logging generation rely on static analysis and produce statements in a single pass without considering runtime behavior. They are also typically evaluated by similarity to developer-written logs, assuming these logs form an adequate gold standard. This assumption is increasingly limiting in the LLM era, where logs are consumed not only by developers but also by LLMs for downstream tasks. As a result, optimizing logs for human similarity does not necessarily reflect their practical utility. To address these limitations, we introduce ReLog, an iterative logging generation framework guided by runtime feedback. ReLog leverages LLMs to generate, execute, evaluate, and refine logging statements so that runtime logs better support downstream tasks. Instead of comparing against developer-written logs, we evaluate ReLog through downstream debugging tasks, including defect localization and repair. We construct a benchmark based on Defects4J under both direct and indirect debugging settings. Results show that ReLog consistently outperforms all baselines, achieving an F1 score of 0.520 and repairing 97 defects in the direct setting, and the best F1 score of 0.408 in the indirect setting where source code is unavailable. Additional experiments across multiple LLMs demonstrate the generality of the framework, while ablations confirm the importance of iterative refinement and compilation repair. Overall, our work reframes logging as a runtime-guided, task-oriented process and advocates evaluating logs by their downstream utility rather than textual similarity.","az":"日志语句对软件调试与维护至关重要。然而，现有的自动日志生成方法依赖静态分析，一次性生成日志语句而不考虑运行时行为；它们通常还以与开发者编写日志的相似度来评估，默认这些日志构成了充分的黄金标准。在 LLM 时代，这一假设的局限性日益凸显：日志不仅被开发者消费，也被 LLM 用于下游任务，因此按与人类日志的相似度优化并不一定反映其实际效用。为解决这些局限，我们提出 ReLog，一个由运行时反馈引导的迭代式日志生成框架。ReLog 利用 LLM 生成、执行、评估并精化日志语句，使运行时日志能更好地支撑下游任务。我们不再与开发者编写的日志作比较，而是通过下游调试任务（包括缺陷定位与修复）来评估 ReLog。我们基于 Defects4J 构建了直接与间接两种调试设定下的基准。结果显示，ReLog 持续优于所有基线：在直接设定下取得 0.520 的 F1 分数并修复了 97 个缺陷，在源代码不可用的间接设定下取得最佳 F1 分数 0.408。在多个 LLM 上的补充实验验证了框架的通用性，消融实验确认了迭代精化与编译修复的重要性。总体而言，我们的工作把日志重新定位为一个运行时引导、面向任务的过程，并主张按日志的下游效用而非文本相似度来评估它们。","tl":"按下游调试效用而非文本相似度来生成并评估日志语句。","au":["Xin Wang","Yang Feng","Xiaoqian Jiao","Yang Zhang","Zhenhao Li","Zishuo Ding"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["logging generation","runtime feedback","fault localization","Defects4J","LLM-oriented debugging"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/167/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29122v2"},{"id":"p01187","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Documentation vs. Code Patterns: What Drives LLM-Based Exception Oracle Generation?","tz":"文档还是代码模式：是什么驱动了基于 LLM 的异常预言生成？","a":"LLM-based test oracle generation (TOG) methods report high accuracy on exception oracle generation, but it remains unclear what evidence drives these predictions. In particular, do models use explicit exceptional-behavior documentation such as Javadoc @throws clauses, or do they rely on recurring patterns in tests, code, and documentation? We investigate this question through a large-scale intervention-based study of three TOG systems spanning classifier-based and generative architectures and model sizes from roughly 110M to 7B parameters, evaluated on three real-world benchmarks comprising two generated-test datasets and a new benchmark of developer-written tests. We first remove Javadoc @throws clauses and find that accuracy changes only marginally, with the largest drop below one percentage point. This indicates that structured exception documentation is not the primary driver of exception-oracle prediction. We then apply attribution-guided substitution ablations to identify the signals that predictions depend on. The results show that high accuracy can be driven by shortcut signals: some models are highly sensitive to a small number of structural tokens, while others distribute reliance across many lexical cues. These findings challenge the assumption that strong exception-oracle accuracy reflects robust use of exception semantics. Future TOG systems should therefore be evaluated not only by whether they predict the correct oracle type, but also by whether their predictions are grounded in meaningful exception-triggering evidence.","az":"基于 LLM 的测试预言生成（TOG）方法在异常预言生成上报告了很高的准确率，但究竟是什么证据在驱动这些预测仍不清楚。具体而言，模型是使用了诸如 Javadoc @throws 子句这类显式的异常行为文档，还是依赖测试、代码与文档中反复出现的模式？我们通过一项大规模的干预式研究来回答这个问题，研究覆盖三个 TOG 系统，涵盖基于分类器与生成式两类架构、参数规模从约 1.1 亿到 70 亿，并在三个真实基准上评估，其中包括两个生成测试数据集和一个新构建的开发者编写测试基准。我们首先移除 Javadoc @throws 子句，发现准确率仅有边际变化，最大下降不足一个百分点，这表明结构化的异常文档并不是异常预言预测的主要驱动因素。随后我们施加归因引导的替换消融实验，以识别预测所依赖的信号。结果显示，高准确率可能由捷径信号驱动：有的模型对少数几个结构性 token 高度敏感，另一些则把依赖分散到许多词法线索上。这些发现挑战了“高异常预言准确率即体现对异常语义的稳健使用”这一假设。因此，未来的 TOG 系统不仅应以是否预测出正确的预言类型来评估，还应考察其预测是否建立在有意义的异常触发证据之上。","tl":"揭示异常预言生成的高准确率多由捷径信号而非异常文档驱动。","au":["Soneya Binta Hossain","Tasfia Tasnim","Matthew B Dwyer"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["test oracle generation","exception oracle","Javadoc @throws","attribution ablation","shortcut learning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/168/x"},{"id":"p01188","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Harnessing Uncertainty in Code Language Models: Lessons from Vulnerability Detection","tz":"驾驭代码语言模型中的不确定性：来自漏洞检测的经验","tl":"（据标题推断）以漏洞检测为切口研究代码模型不确定性的可用性。","au":["Haodong Li","Xiao Cheng","Xudong Wang","Zhihao Guo","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","security"],"kw":["uncertainty estimation","code language models","vulnerability detection","calibration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/169/x"},{"id":"p01189","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Breaking the Isolation: Coordinated Multi-agent Fuzzing for Smart Contracts with Multi-dimensional Objective Learning","tz":"打破孤立：面向智能合约的多智能体协同模糊测试与多维目标学习","tl":"（据标题推断）让多个模糊测试智能体协同并学习多维目标以挖合约漏洞。","au":["Ruichao Liang","Ruochen Cao","Jing Chen","Kun He","Yebo Feng","Yue Xue","Cong Wu"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract fuzzing","multi-agent coordination","objective learning","vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/170/x"},{"id":"p01190","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"HyTri: Hybrid Triage of CI Failures via LLM Guided Semantic Reasoning and Change Attribution","tz":"HyTri：结合 LLM 语义推理与变更归因的 CI 失败混合分诊","tl":"（据标题推断）把 LLM 语义推理与变更归因结合来分诊 CI 失败。","au":["Lior Broide","Argaman Mordoch","Roni Stern"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["CI failure triage","change attribution","LLM reasoning","continuous integration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/171/x"},{"id":"p01191","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Latent Reuse in Agent Skills: Multi-modal Clone Detection at Ecosystem Scale","tz":"Agent Skill 中的潜在复用：生态规模下的多模态克隆检测","a":"The growing diversity of code clone types, from syntactic copies to cross-language semantic clones to AI-generated duplicates, has created a fragmentation crisis in clone detection. Current deep learning detectors are domain specialists that degrade significantly outside their training distribution, with F1 drops exceeding 70% across domains. Deploying multiple specialized models is impractical, yet training a single cross-domain detector requires simultaneous access to all training data. To address this, we investigate model merging, a family of post-hoc techniques that operate solely on trained checkpoints. We evaluate parameter merging with five task-vector methods, architecture merging via greedy layer stitching, and cross-tokenizer alignment across four code models, three benchmarks, and twelve configurations. Same-base TIES merging creates effective cross-domain detectors, validated across two model families and three random seeds, reaching 0.865 combined F1 on UniXcoder, 93% of multi-task performance without any training data at the merging step. WUDI achieves the highest in-distribution combined F1 at 0.899, but TIES generalizes better to unseen AI-generated clones, making it our recommended method. Cross-base merging yields only marginal and high-variance gains across all five methods, indicating that task vector compatibility through a shared pre-trained base is the binding factor for effective merging. Merged detectors also outperform zero-shot code LLMs on GPTCloneBench at lower inference cost and generalize up to 4x better than multi-task training to unseen AI-generated clones, suggesting a trade-off between in-domain performance and OOD robustness. This work provides one of the first systematic empirical studies of model merging for software engineering and a practical recipe for building cross-domain clone detectors.","az":"代码克隆类型日益多样，从语法层面的拷贝到跨语言的语义克隆，再到 AI 生成的重复代码，已经造成了克隆检测领域的碎片化危机。当前的深度学习检测器都是领域专才，一旦离开训练分布性能就大幅退化，跨领域 F1 下降超过 70%。部署多个专用模型并不现实，而训练单一的跨领域检测器又要求同时获取全部训练数据。为此，我们研究模型融合（model merging）——一类仅对已训练检查点进行操作的事后技术。我们在四个代码模型、三个基准、十二种配置上评估了采用五种任务向量方法的参数融合、基于贪心层拼接的架构融合，以及跨分词器对齐。同基座的 TIES 融合能够产生有效的跨领域检测器，并在两个模型家族与三个随机种子上得到验证，在 UniXcoder 上达到 0.865 的综合 F1，相当于多任务性能的 93%，且在融合环节完全不需要训练数据。WUDI 取得了最高的分布内综合 F1（0.899），但 TIES 对未见过的 AI 生成克隆泛化更好，因而是我们推荐的方法。跨基座融合在全部五种方法上都只带来边际且方差很大的收益，说明通过共享预训练基座实现的任务向量兼容性才是有效融合的决定性因素。融合后的检测器在 GPTCloneBench 上以更低的推理成本超过零样本代码 LLM，并在未见过的 AI 生成克隆上比多任务训练泛化能力高出最多 4 倍，提示分布内性能与分布外鲁棒性之间存在权衡。本工作提供了软件工程领域中关于模型融合的首批系统性实证研究之一，以及构建跨领域克隆检测器的实用方案。","tl":"用模型融合免训练地拼出跨领域克隆检测器，OOD 泛化更强。","au":["Jiaying Zhu","Lyuye Zhang","Wenbo Guo","Yang Liu"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["clone detection","model merging","task vectors","TIES","cross-domain generalization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/172/x"},{"id":"p01192","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Specification-Guided Synthesis of Deadlock-Free Communication Protocol Refinements with Large Language Models","tz":"借助大语言模型的规约引导式无死锁通信协议精化合成","a":"Rust's ownership type system prevents memory errors in safe code, but certain desirable properties remain orthogonal to compilation: the soundness of unsafe operations (e.g., raw pointer dereferences), functional correctness, and absence of runtime panics. We present Kani, an open-source model checker for Rust that pushes bounded model checking beyond bug-finding to provide correctness guarantees for these properties. Kani compiles proof harnesses from Rust's Mid-level Intermediate Representation (MIR) into CBMC's bit-precise verification engine, automatically checking a comprehensive set of safety properties with no user annotation. To extend verification from bounded to unbounded, Kani provides a specification language comprising function contracts, loop contracts, quantifiers, and function stubbing. We demonstrate feasibility through case studies on industrial Rust projects, where contracts upgraded verification from panic-freedom to functional correctness, uncovering six previously unknown bugs. Kani operates at scale in production CI, with over 16,000 harnesses verified per code change in the Rust standard library verification campaign.","az":"Rust 的所有权类型系统可以在安全代码中防止内存错误，但某些理想性质与编译过程正交：unsafe 操作（例如裸指针解引用）的健全性、功能正确性以及不发生运行时 panic。我们提出 Kani，一个面向 Rust 的开源模型检查器，它把有界模型检查从找缺陷推进到为这些性质提供正确性保证。Kani 把证明 harness 从 Rust 的中级中间表示（MIR）编译到 CBMC 的位精确验证引擎，无需用户注解即可自动检查一整套安全性质。为了把验证从有界扩展到无界，Kani 提供了一套规约语言，包含函数契约、循环契约、量词和函数桩。我们通过工业级 Rust 项目的案例研究证明了其可行性：契约把验证从“无 panic”升级为功能正确性，并发现了六个此前未知的缺陷。Kani 已在生产环境的 CI 中规模化运行，在 Rust 标准库验证行动中每次代码变更要验证超过 16,000 个 harness。","tl":"用规约引导的 LLM 合成可保证无死锁的通信协议精化。","au":["Yang Li","Ping Hou","Nobuko Yoshida"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["deadlock freedom","protocol refinement","specification-guided synthesis","model checking","Rust verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/173/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.27964"},{"id":"p01193","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Execution-as-Configuration: Security Smells in Model Configuration Artifacts","tz":"配置即执行：模型配置制品中的安全坏味","a":"Abstract Model sharing hubs rely on configuration artifacts to control model loading and execution. Although treated as metadata, files such as {config.json} determine class resolution and dependency selection, effectively making configurations an execution control surface. Yet their security implications remain largely unexplored. In this paper, we present a large-scale study of model configuration-related security smells. We introduce a taxonomy of 12 security smell types capturing execution-enabling constructs, trust boundary confusion, supply-chain risks, information leakage, and operational risks in model configuration files. To operationalize this taxonomy, we design MONTICELLO, a repository-aware security smell detection approach that combines pattern-based rules with contextual reasoning. We analyze 44,812 repositories across Hugging Face, OpenCSG, and ModelScope. Configuration smells are pervasive: 65.5%--95.5% of repositories contain at least one. These smells expose repositories to concrete risks, including unsafe deserialization, dynamic code execution, and trust boundary violations. Quick Start Requirements pip install -r requirements.txt JSON config analysis # Benchmark evaluation python scripts/static_analyzers/python_detector.py benchmark results/open_coding/js_microbenchmark_v2_multilabel.json --mode merged # Scan a directory python scripts/static_analyzers/python_detector.py scan data/huggingface/json_configs/ Smell Taxonomy (JSON configs) 55 original smells are grouped into 12 canonical smell groups: | Group | Name | |---|---| | G01 | Auto Class Remapping (`auto_map`) | | G02 | Custom Pipeline Entry Point (`custom_pipelines`) | | G03 | Cross-Repository Code Reference | | G04 | PEFT Adapter Config (`peft_type`) | | G05 | Trust Remote Code Flag | | G06 | External URL in Configuration | | G07 | Unpinned Revision (`revision: null`) | | G08 | Mutable Revision Reference | | G09 | Credential Exposure | | G10 | Debug Mode Enabled | | G11 | Absolute Path Disclosure | | G12 | Unbounded Generation Limits | Full mapping: [`data/json_smell_groups.csv`](data/json_smell_groups.csv) Repository Structure hf_config_security_smells/ ├── data/ │ ├── json_smell_groups.csv ← 55→12 smell merge mapping │ ├── Original_smell_list.csv ← original 55 smell definitions │ └── huggingface/json_configs/ ← reconstructed via scripts/data_collection/reconstruct_configs.py ├── scripts/ │ ├── static_analyzers/ │ │ ├── python_detector.py ← detector (benchmark + scan modes) │ │ ├── generate_smell_stats.py ← aggregates prevalence statistics │ │ └── generate_smell_report.py ← produces Markdown smell report │ ├── open_coding/ │ ├── analysis/ │ └── data_collection/ ├── results/ │ ├── benchmark_reports/ ← precision/recall evaluation outputs │ │ └── BENCHMARK_REPORT.md │ ├── open_coding/ ← benchmark ground-truth files │ ├── prevalence/ ← per-group repo counts across platforms │ └── run_sast/ │ └── sast_analysis_summary.json ← aggregated SAST tool results (Bandit, CodeQL, Semgrep)","az":"摘要：模型分享平台依赖配置制品来控制模型的加载与执行。尽管 config.json 之类的文件常被当作元数据，它们却决定了类解析与依赖选择，实际上使配置成为一个执行控制面。然而其安全含义在很大程度上仍未被探究。本文对模型配置相关的安全坏味开展了大规模研究。我们提出一个包含 12 类安全坏味的分类体系，覆盖启用执行的构造、信任边界混淆、供应链风险、信息泄露以及模型配置文件中的运维风险。为落地该分类体系，我们设计了 MONTICELLO——一种仓库感知的安全坏味检测方法，将基于模式的规则与上下文推理结合。我们分析了 Hugging Face、OpenCSG 与 ModelScope 上的 44,812 个仓库。配置坏味十分普遍：65.5%--95.5% 的仓库至少包含一个坏味。这些坏味使仓库面临具体风险，包括不安全的反序列化、动态代码执行和信任边界违规。快速开始：依赖 pip install -r requirements.txt；JSON 配置分析：基准评测执行 python scripts/static_analyzers/python_detector.py benchmark results/open_coding/js_microbenchmark_v2_multilabel.json --mode merged，扫描目录执行 python scripts/static_analyzers/python_detector.py scan data/huggingface/json_configs/。坏味分类体系（JSON 配置）：55 个原始坏味被归并为 12 个规范坏味组：G01 自动类重映射（auto_map）；G02 自定义流水线入口（custom_pipelines）；G03 跨仓库代码引用；G04 PEFT 适配器配置（peft_type）；G05 trust remote code 标志；G06 配置中的外部 URL；G07 未固定的修订版本（revision: null）；G08 可变修订引用；G09 凭据泄露；G10 调试模式开启；G11 绝对路径泄露；G12 无上界的生成限制。完整映射见 data/json_smell_groups.csv。仓库结构：hf_config_security_smells/ 下包含 data/（json_smell_groups.csv 为 55→12 的坏味归并映射，Original_smell_list.csv 为原始 55 个坏味定义，huggingface/json_configs/ 由 scripts/data_collection/reconstruct_configs.py 重建）、scripts/（static_analyzers/ 下的 python_detector.py 检测器（支持 benchmark 与 scan 模式）、generate_smell_stats.py 聚合流行度统计、generate_smell_report.py 生成 Markdown 坏味报告，以及 open_coding/、analysis/、data_collection/）、results/（benchmark_reports/ 精确率/召回率评测输出及 BENCHMARK_REPORT.md、open_coding/ 基准真值文件、prevalence/ 各平台各组的仓库计数、run_sast/sast_analysis_summary.json 汇总的 SAST 工具（Bandit、CodeQL、Semgrep）结果）。","tl":"把模型配置文件视作执行控制面，提出 12 类安全坏味并大规模检测。","au":["Mohammed Latif Siddiq","Prince Noah Johnson","Joanna C. S. Santos"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["model configuration","security smells","Hugging Face","supply chain risk","static detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/174/x"},{"id":"p01194","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Evidence-Grounded Logic Vulnerability Detection for Smart Contracts via Runtime Context Reasoning","tz":"基于运行时上下文推理的智能合约逻辑漏洞证据化检测","tl":"（据标题推断）用运行时上下文作为证据来推理智能合约逻辑漏洞。","au":["Guang Gong","Yucong Jiang","Rong Jian","Xiaotao Feng","Zhihan Wei","Qi Li","Ke Xu"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["smart contract","logic vulnerability","runtime context","evidence-grounded detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/175/x"},{"id":"p01195","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Fully Automating Template Polyhedral Analysis by Leveraging LLMs","tz":"借助 LLM 全自动化模板多面体分析","tl":"（据标题推断）用 LLM 自动生成模板，免除多面体分析的人工调参。","au":["Renjie Huang","Liqian Chen","Hongfei Fu","Banghu Yin","Dengping Wei","Ji Wang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["polyhedral analysis","abstract interpretation","template generation","LLM-augmented analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/176/x"},{"id":"p01196","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Does AI Actually Help in Incident Response? Identifying Good First Messages in Cloud Service Incidents","tz":"AI 究竟何时对事件响应有帮助？识别云服务事件中的优质首条消息","a":"Logging statements are essential for software debugging and maintenance. However, existing approaches to automatic logging generation rely on static analysis and produce statements in a single pass without considering runtime behavior. They are also typically evaluated by similarity to developer-written logs, assuming these logs form an adequate gold standard. This assumption is increasingly limiting in the LLM era, where logs are consumed not only by developers but also by LLMs for downstream tasks. As a result, optimizing logs for human similarity does not necessarily reflect their practical utility. To address these limitations, we introduce ReLog, an iterative logging generation framework guided by runtime feedback. ReLog leverages LLMs to generate, execute, evaluate, and refine logging statements so that runtime logs better support downstream tasks. Instead of comparing against developer-written logs, we evaluate ReLog through downstream debugging tasks, including defect localization and repair. We construct a benchmark based on Defects4J under both direct and indirect debugging settings. Results show that ReLog consistently outperforms all baselines, achieving an F1 score of 0.520 and repairing 97 defects in the direct setting, and the best F1 score of 0.408 in the indirect setting where source code is unavailable. Additional experiments across multiple LLMs demonstrate the generality of the framework, while ablations confirm the importance of iterative refinement and compilation repair. Overall, our work reframes logging as a runtime-guided, task-oriented process and advocates evaluating logs by their downstream utility rather than textual similarity.","az":"日志语句对软件调试与维护至关重要。然而，现有的自动日志生成方法依赖静态分析，一次性生成日志语句而不考虑运行时行为；它们通常还以与开发者编写日志的相似度来评估，默认这些日志构成了充分的黄金标准。在 LLM 时代，这一假设的局限性日益凸显：日志不仅被开发者消费，也被 LLM 用于下游任务，因此按与人类日志的相似度优化并不一定反映其实际效用。为解决这些局限，我们提出 ReLog，一个由运行时反馈引导的迭代式日志生成框架。ReLog 利用 LLM 生成、执行、评估并精化日志语句，使运行时日志能更好地支撑下游任务。我们不再与开发者编写的日志作比较，而是通过下游调试任务（包括缺陷定位与修复）来评估 ReLog。我们基于 Defects4J 构建了直接与间接两种调试设定下的基准。结果显示，ReLog 持续优于所有基线：在直接设定下取得 0.520 的 F1 分数并修复了 97 个缺陷，在源代码不可用的间接设定下取得最佳 F1 分数 0.408。在多个 LLM 上的补充实验验证了框架的通用性，消融实验确认了迭代精化与编译修复的重要性。总体而言，我们的工作把日志重新定位为一个运行时引导、面向任务的过程，并主张按日志的下游效用而非文本相似度来评估它们。","tl":"刻画云事件响应中 AI 首条消息何时真正有用。","au":["Minghua Ma","Rujia Wang","Chetan Bansal","Saravan Rajmohan","Yingnong Dang","Hongyu Zhang"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["incident response","cloud services","AI assistance","first message","on-call"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/177/x"},{"id":"p01197","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"“We Must Have Missed This Comment”: Detecting and Repairing Stale Function References in Linux Kernel Comments","tz":"“我们一定是漏掉了这条注释”：检测并修复 Linux 内核注释中的过时函数引用","a":"As the Linux kernel evolves, code comments may become outdated, as the functions they reference can be refactored or removed independently without corresponding updates to the comments. Such stale function references can mislead maintainers and thus hinder code comprehension. Prior work on detecting code-comment inconsistency mainly focused on addressing semantic misalignment between Javadoc comments and their directly annotated functions, making them inapplicable to this type of externally induced staleness in the Linux kernel. Therefore, we propose ReCite, a three-stage approach to identify and repair such stale references: (1) detecting unresolved function-form symbols—symbols in comments that appear to reference functions but for which no matching function can be found in the current codebase, (2) tracing the evolution history of each unresolved symbol through the Git history, and (3) generating LLM-based repair suggestions grounded in the evolution history and current code context. On Linux kernel v6.18-rc1, ReCite detects 869 stale references with generated repair suggestions. A manual evaluation on 200 sampled repairs shows that 178 (89.0%) provide useful repair guidance, with 85 (42.5%) directly applicable. Of our 75 submitted patches, 50 have been accepted. We also empirically study all unresolved function-form symbols.","az":"随着 Linux 内核的演化，代码注释可能变得过时，因为它们引用的函数可能被独立地重构或删除而注释却没有相应更新。这类过时的函数引用会误导维护者，从而妨碍代码理解。已有的代码—注释不一致检测工作主要针对 Javadoc 注释与其直接标注函数之间的语义不匹配，无法适用于 Linux 内核中这种由外部因素诱发的过时问题。为此，我们提出 ReCite，一个分三阶段识别并修复此类过时引用的方法：（1）检测未解析的函数形式符号——即注释中看起来引用了函数、但在当前代码库中找不到匹配函数的符号；（2）通过 Git 历史追溯每个未解析符号的演化历程；（3）基于演化历史与当前代码上下文生成基于 LLM 的修复建议。在 Linux kernel v6.18-rc1 上，ReCite 检测出 869 处过时引用并生成了修复建议。对 200 个抽样修复的人工评估显示，其中 178 个（89.0%）提供了有用的修复指导，85 个（42.5%）可直接应用。我们提交的 75 个补丁中已有 50 个被接受。我们还对全部未解析的函数形式符号进行了实证研究。","tl":"借 Git 演化史检测并修复内核注释里失效的函数引用。","au":["Kexin Sun","Yunbo Lyu","Xutong Ma","Hongyu Kuang","Ratnadira Widyasari","He Zhang","Xiaoxing Ma","Julia Lawall","David Lo"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study"],"kw":["stale comments","Linux kernel","code-comment inconsistency","evolution history","repair suggestions"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/178/x","pu":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.03734"},{"id":"p01198","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"LARA: Static ReDoS Detection for Regular Expressions with Lookahead via Matching Automata","tz":"LARA：基于匹配自动机的带前瞻正则表达式静态 ReDoS 检测","a":"Recent work on LLM-driven autonomous penetration testing reports promising results, but existing systems often bundle architectural, prompting, and tool-integration choices together. This makes it difficult to determine what is gained over a simple agent and harness. We present Cochise, a 630 LOC Python reference implementation for autonomous penetration-testing experiments. Cochise connects to a Linux execution host over SSH and supports attacking controlled target environments reachable from that jump host. The prototype implements a Planner--Executor architecture in which long-term state is maintained by the planner, while a ReAct-style executor issues commands over SSH and self-corrects based on command outputs. The scenario prompt can be adapted to different target environments. We evaluate the harness against a live third-party testbed, Game of Active Directory (GOAD). Cochise is intended not as a state-of-the-art penetration-testing agent, but as a reusable experimental infrastructure for comparing models, agent architectures, and penetration-testing traces. Alongside the prototype, we release replay and analysis tools: (i) cochise-replay for offline visualization of captured runs, (ii) cochise-analyze-logs and cochise-analyze-graphs for cost, token, duration, and compromise analysis, and (iii) a corpus of JSON trajectory logs from GOAD runs, so that researchers can study agent behavior without provisioning the 48--64 GB RAM / 190 GB storage testbed themselves. Tool demo video available at https://youtu.be/2mQimB1ufyI.","az":"近期关于 LLM 驱动的自主渗透测试的工作报告了令人鼓舞的结果，但现有系统往往把架构、提示与工具集成方面的选择捆绑在一起，导致难以判断相比一个简单智能体加脚手架究竟带来了什么收益。我们提出 Cochise，一个 630 行 Python 的参考实现，用于自主渗透测试实验。Cochise 通过 SSH 连接到一台 Linux 执行主机，并支持攻击可从该跳板机访问的受控目标环境。该原型实现了 Planner--Executor 架构：由 planner 维护长期状态，而 ReAct 风格的 executor 通过 SSH 下发命令并根据命令输出自我纠正。场景提示可针对不同目标环境进行适配。我们在一个第三方实况靶场 Game of Active Directory（GOAD）上评估该脚手架。Cochise 的定位不是最先进的渗透测试智能体，而是一套可复用的实验基础设施，用于比较不同模型、智能体架构与渗透测试轨迹。除原型外，我们还发布了重放与分析工具：(i) cochise-replay 用于离线可视化已捕获的运行；(ii) cochise-analyze-logs 与 cochise-analyze-graphs 用于成本、token、时长与攻陷情况分析；(iii) 来自 GOAD 运行的 JSON 轨迹日志语料库，使研究者无需自行搭建需要 48--64 GB 内存 / 190 GB 存储的靶场即可研究智能体行为。工具演示视频见 https://youtu.be/2mQimB1ufyI 。","tl":"用匹配自动机静态检测含前瞻正则的 ReDoS 风险。","au":["Mengxi Wang","Chengyao Peng","Weihao Su","Guiyi He","Rongchen Li","hong huang","Haiming Chen"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["ReDoS","regular expressions","lookahead","matching automata","static detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/179/x"},{"id":"p01199","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ConfFuzz: Parameter-Aware Greybox Fuzzing for Configurable Cloud Systems","tz":"ConfFuzz：面向可配置云系统的参数感知灰盒模糊测试","a":"Several experience reports illustrate that mutation testing is capable of supporting a shift-left testing strategy, especially in industries where late bug discovery incurs very high costs and risks. In the context of cyber-physical systems, a shift left implies that engineers need to test the design models used to simulate, prototype, and analyse the feasibility of the system under design. In this paper, we analyse the challenges we encountered and the lessons we learned when incorporating mutation testing in the context of DUCO, a company producing ventilation systems for buildings. The engineers within DUCO have years of experience with model-based engineering centered around Simulink and StateFlow, including unit tests for their models. During a pilot project with our tool prototype MUT4SLX we learned that equivalent mutants, requirement traceability, and mutation testing for Stateflow represent particular challenges not yet reported in the academic literature.","az":"多份经验报告表明，变异测试能够支撑“左移测试”策略，在缺陷发现过晚会带来极高成本与风险的行业中尤其如此。在信息物理系统的语境下，左移意味着工程师需要测试那些用于仿真、原型与可行性分析的设计模型。本文分析了我们在 DUCO（一家生产建筑通风系统的公司）场景中引入变异测试时遇到的挑战与获得的经验教训。DUCO 的工程师在以 Simulink 与 StateFlow 为核心的基于模型的工程方面拥有多年经验，其中包括为模型编写单元测试。在使用我们的工具原型 MUT4SLX 开展试点项目的过程中，我们发现等价变异体、需求可追溯性以及面向 Stateflow 的变异测试构成了学术文献中尚未报告过的特殊挑战。","tl":"让灰盒模糊测试感知配置参数，挖掘可配置云系统的缺陷。","au":["Shuai Wang","Hao Wang","Darko Marinov","Tianyin Xu","Yongle Zhang"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["greybox fuzzing","configurable systems","cloud systems","configuration parameters"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/180/x"},{"id":"p01200","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Synthesizing File-Level Data for Unit Test Generation with Chain-of-Thoughts via Self-Debugging","tz":"通过自调试合成带思维链的文件级单元测试生成数据","a":"Automatic unit test (UT) generation is essential for software quality assurance, but existing approaches--including symbolic execution, search-based approaches, and recent LLM-based generators--struggle to produce human-quality tests with correct, meaningful assertions and reliable chain-of-thought (CoT) explanations. We identify a gap in UT training data: repository-mined tests lack developer CoTs, while LLM-distilled CoTs are often incorrect or incomplete. To address this issue, we propose a novel data-distillation approach that uses self-debugging to produce high-quality UT training examples paired with faithful CoTs. Our approach combines (1) guided test repair, a heuristic loop (error-, failure-, and coverage-focused steps) that asks the used model to diagnose and iteratively fix generated tests, and (2) CoT compression, which compacts original and debugging CoTs into concise explanations that directly justify correct tests. We apply this pipeline to a large corpus of open-source projects to construct a dataset of 74,518 high-quality <focal method, test, CoT> examples, and then use it for supervised fine-tuning of a base model. An empirical evaluation shows that the fine-tuned model achieves high UT generation effectiveness: it attains a pass rate of 36.17% on test assertions, a branch coverage of 43.90%, and a mutation score of 88.66%, substantially higher than state-of-the-art commercial models like o4-mini.","az":"自动单元测试（UT）生成对软件质量保障至关重要，但现有方法——包括符号执行、基于搜索的方法以及近期基于 LLM 的生成器——都难以产出具有正确、有意义断言以及可靠思维链（CoT）解释的、达到人类质量的测试。我们发现 UT 训练数据存在一个缺口：从仓库挖掘得到的测试缺少开发者的 CoT，而由 LLM 蒸馏出的 CoT 又常常是错误或不完整的。为解决这一问题，我们提出一种新颖的数据蒸馏方法，利用自调试来产出高质量的 UT 训练样例及其忠实的 CoT。我们的方法结合了：（1）引导式测试修复，一个启发式循环（分别聚焦编译错误、测试失败与覆盖率的步骤），要求所用模型诊断并迭代修复生成的测试；（2）CoT 压缩，把原始 CoT 与调试 CoT 压缩为直接论证正确测试的简洁解释。我们把该流水线应用于大规模开源项目语料，构建了包含 74,518 个高质量 <目标方法, 测试, CoT> 样例的数据集，并用它对基础模型做有监督微调。实证评估表明，微调后的模型具有很高的 UT 生成效果：测试断言通过率达 36.17%，分支覆盖率达 43.90%，变异分数达 88.66%，显著高于 o4-mini 等先进商用模型。","tl":"用自调试蒸馏出忠实 CoT 的单测训练数据，微调后超越 o4-mini。","au":["Ziyue Hua","Tianyu Chen","Yeyun Gong","Shuai Lu","Peng Cheng","Qinglin Zhu","Yibo He","Yingjie Fu","Wenpin Jiao","Wei Yang","Tao Xie"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["unit test generation","chain-of-thought","self-debugging","data distillation","supervised fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/181/x"},{"id":"p01201","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"FAiLGen: Calibrating LLM for Failing Test Generation with Monte Carlo Tree Search","tz":"FAiLGen：用蒙特卡洛树搜索校准大语言模型以生成失败测试","tl":"（据标题推断）用 MCTS 校准 LLM 采样，生成能暴露缺陷的失败测试。","au":["Li Tsz On","Xiaochuan Yan","Dehui Yi","Yuhang Jiang","Kexin Li","Congying Xu","Ying Wang","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["failing test generation","Monte Carlo Tree Search","LLM calibration","bug reproduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/182/x"},{"id":"p01202","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Feature-Focused Test Generation","tz":"面向特征聚焦的测试生成","a":"Specification-based test generators use input specifications to produce valid tests for complex systems, covering the entire input space of the system under test. This broad generation capability, however, can become a burden when one wants to focus test generation on a particular subset of the input space, say, a feature whose implementation has recently changed or is particularly critical. In this paper, we propose Feature-Focused Test Generation (FFTG), an approach that treats specification-based test generation as a configuration problem. From the input specification, FFTG first extracts a feature model that represents alternate and optional expansions as possible feature values. After the tester selects which features to focus upon, FFTG specializes the specification accordingly, generating inputs in which only the focused features vary. We implement FFTG in a prototype named Compás. In our evaluation, we find that Compás-generated slices: (1) effectively focus test generation on specific features, preserving validity; (2) exercise unique code locations associated with the targeted features and thus enable traceability of features; and (3) enable test suite minimization, with a small set of slices retaining the aggregate coverage of the full suite while requiring fewer tests. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first work to apply product line engineering techniques to specification-based testing.","az":"基于规约的测试生成器利用输入规约为复杂系统产生合法测试，覆盖被测系统的整个输入空间。然而，当人们希望把测试生成集中在输入空间的某个特定子集上（例如某个实现最近发生变更或格外关键的特征）时，这种宽泛的生成能力反而会成为负担。本文提出特征聚焦测试生成（Feature-Focused Test Generation, FFTG），该方法把基于规约的测试生成视为一个配置问题。FFTG 首先从输入规约中抽取一个特征模型，用可选与备选的展开方式表示可能的特征取值。在测试人员选定要聚焦的特征之后，FFTG 相应地对规约进行特化，生成只让被聚焦特征发生变化的输入。我们在名为 Compás 的原型中实现了 FFTG。评估结果表明，Compás 生成的切片：(1) 能有效地把测试生成聚焦到特定特征上，同时保持输入合法性；(2) 能执行到与目标特征相关的独有代码位置，从而实现特征的可追溯性；(3) 支持测试套件最小化——用一小组切片即可保留完整套件的整体覆盖率，而所需测试用例更少。据我们所知，这是第一项把产品线工程技术应用于基于规约的测试的工作。","tl":"把规约测试生成建模为配置问题，按特征切片聚焦生成。","au":["José Antonio Zamudio Amaya","Gaetano Sapia","Alexi Turcotte","David Benavides","Marcel Böhme","Andreas Zeller"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["specification-based testing","feature model","product line engineering","test suite minimization","traceability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/183/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837479"},{"id":"p01203","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SecChain: Operationalizing Security Guidelines for Multi-agent Smart Contract Generation","tz":"SecChain：在多智能体智能合约生成中落地安全规范","a":"Fine-tuned code models often behave as domain specialists and can degrade sharply under distribution shift: in our clone-detection setting, a model trained on same-language clones drops 71 % F1 on cross-language clones, while multi-task training falls to 0.151 F1 on unseen AI-generated clones. Our companion study shows that post-hoc model merging can address this fragmentation, achieving 93 % of multi-task performance without training data while generalizing 4 better to unseen clone types. However, no practical tool exists that lets SE researchers diagnose checkpoint compatibility, merge specialists, validate results on SE benchmarks, and export models for deployment. We present MergeSE, an open-source CLI and web tool for training-free model merging of HuggingFace encoder checkpoints. While motivated by OOD generalization in clone detection, MergeSE supports SE classification workflows more broadly through a built-in registry of nine task types, including vulnerability detection, defect prediction, and code-smell detection. MergeSE provides five operations: tasks, inspect, merge, evaluate, and export. It supports five merging algorithms, including TIES, DARE-TIES, Wudi, PCB, and averaging; detects cross-task classification-head mismatches; produces seedable deterministic outputs; and includes bundled benchmark samples for smoke-test reproduction. A full merge of two 124M-parameter checkpoints completes in under 5 seconds on CPU. End-to-end validation confirms that MergeSE-produced checkpoints match reference implementations and recover cross-domain performance from domain-specific specialists. The tool is available online at https://mergese.usask.ca, and the development repository is at https://github.com/srlabUsask/MergeSE.","az":"经过微调的代码模型往往表现为领域专才，在分布偏移下性能会急剧下降：在我们的克隆检测场景中，用同语言克隆训练的模型在跨语言克隆上 F1 下降 71\\%，而多任务训练在未见过的 AI 生成克隆上 F1 跌至 0.151。我们的配套研究表明，事后的模型合并可以缓解这种碎片化：在不使用训练数据的情况下达到多任务性能的 93\\%，并且对未见克隆类型的泛化能力提升 4 倍。然而，目前还没有一款实用工具能让软件工程研究者诊断检查点兼容性、合并专才模型、在 SE 基准上验证结果并导出模型以供部署。我们提出 **MergeSE**，一个开源的命令行与 Web 工具，用于对 HuggingFace 编码器检查点进行免训练的模型合并。虽然其动机来自克隆检测中的分布外泛化，MergeSE 通过内置的九类任务注册表更广泛地支持 SE 分类工作流，包括漏洞检测、缺陷预测和代码坏味检测。MergeSE 提供五种操作：*tasks*、*inspect*、*merge*、*evaluate* 和 *export*。它支持五种合并算法，包括 TIES、DARE-TIES、Wudi、PCB 和平均法；能检测跨任务分类头不匹配；可产生可设随机种子的确定性输出；并附带用于冒烟测试复现的基准样例。在 CPU 上完整合并两个 124M 参数的检查点耗时不到 5 秒。端到端验证确认 MergeSE 产出的检查点与参考实现一致，并能从领域专才模型中恢复跨领域性能。工具可在 https://mergese.usask.ca 获取，开发仓库位于 https://github.com/srlabUsask/MergeSE。","tl":"把安全规范拆解为可执行约束，驱动多智能体产出更安全的合约。","au":["Dianxiang Sun","Liming Nie","Yang Liu"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["smart contract generation","security guidelines","multi-agent","secure code generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/184/x"},{"id":"p01204","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SafeDep: Detecting State Mutation Unsoundness in Rust via Dependency Slicing and LLM Reasoning","tz":"SafeDep：结合依赖切片与大模型推理检测 Rust 中的状态变更不健全性","tl":"（据标题推断）依赖切片缩小范围后，用 LLM 推理判定 Rust 状态变更不健全。","au":["Zihao Rao","Yilin Chen","Chengjun Chen","Hui Xu"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["Rust unsoundness","dependency slicing","LLM reasoning","static analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/185/x"},{"id":"p01205","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Selective Undo/Redo Algorithm for Dependency-Constrained Operation Histories Based on Change Propagation","tz":"基于变更传播的依赖约束操作历史选择性撤销/重做算法","tl":"（据标题推断）用变更传播实现依赖受限历史中的选择性撤销重做。","au":["Xiaoxiong Fan","Hou Tam","Hanxi Zhu","Song-Hai Zhang"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["selective undo","operation history","change propagation","dependency constraints"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/186/x"},{"id":"p01206","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"WiDepFuzz: Finding Wi-Fi Protocol Bugs in Mobile Hotspot via Field Dependency Model","tz":"WiDepFuzz：借助字段依赖模型发现移动热点中的 Wi-Fi 协议缺陷","tl":"（据标题推断）建模协议字段依赖，指导变异挖掘移动热点 Wi-Fi 缺陷。","au":["Yuanliang Chen","Fuchen Ma","Taotao Gu","Yu Jiang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Wi-Fi protocol fuzzing","field dependency model","mobile hotspot","protocol implementation bugs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/187/x"},{"id":"p01207","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CTForge: Automatically Generating Test Suites for Software Configuration","tz":"CTForge：为软件配置自动生成测试套件","tl":"（据标题推断）自动合成覆盖配置选项空间的配置测试套件。","au":["Yuanliang Zhang","Zhizheng Zheng","Shanshan Li","Zhouyang Jia","Chaopeng Luo","Liqian Chen","Zhenbang Chen","Ji Wang","Liao Xiangke"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["configuration testing","test suite generation","software configuration","misconfiguration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/188/x"},{"id":"p01208","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Panorama: Unveiling Latent Dependencies for Microservice Autoscaling via Meta-learning","tz":"Panorama：通过元学习揭示微服务自动扩缩容中的潜在依赖","tl":"（据标题推断）用元学习刻画服务间潜在依赖，改进自动扩缩容决策。","au":["Zhuangbin Chen","Hongjiang Feng","Yang Liu","Juzheng Zheng","Xiaoyu He","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["microservice autoscaling","latent dependency","meta-learning","cloud operations"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/189/x"},{"id":"p01209","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ReCodeAgent: A Multi-agent Workflow for Language-Agnostic Translation and Validation of Large-Scale Repositories","tz":"ReCodeAgent：面向大规模仓库的语言无关翻译与验证多智能体工作流","a":"Most repository-level code translation and validation techniques have been evaluated on a single source-target programming language (PL) pair, owing to the complex engineering effort required to adapt new PL pairs. Programming agents can enable PL-agnosticism in repository-level code translation and validation: they can synthesize code across many PLs and autonomously use existing tools specific to each PL’s analysis. However, state-of-the-art has yet to offer a fully autonomous agentic approach for repository-level code translation and validation of large-scale programs. This paper proposes ReCodeAgent, an autonomous multi-agent approach for language-agnostic repository-level code translation and validation. Users only need to provide the project in the source PL and specify the target PL for ReCodeAgent to automatically translate and validate the entire repository. ReCodeAgent is the first technique to achieve high translation success rates across many PLs. We compare the effectiveness of ReCodeAgent with four alternative neuro-symbolic and agentic approaches to translate 118 real-world projects, with 1,975 LoC and 43 translation units for each project, on average. The projects cover 6 PLs and 4 PL pairs. Our results demonstrate that ReCodeAgent consistently outperforms prior techniques on translation correctness, improving test pass rate by 60.8% on ground-truth tests, with an average cost of $15.3. We also perform process-centric analysis of ReCodeAgent trajectories to confirm its procedural efficiency. Finally, we investigate how the design choices (a multi-agent vs. single-agent architecture) influence ReCodeAgent performance: on average, the test pass rate drops by 40.4%, and trajectories become 28% longer and persistently inefficient.","az":"大多数仓库级代码翻译与验证技术都只在单一的源-目标编程语言（PL）对上做过评估，原因在于适配新的语言对需要复杂的工程投入。编程智能体有望让仓库级代码翻译与验证做到语言无关：它们能跨多种语言合成代码，并自主使用各语言特有的现成分析工具。然而，现有最新研究尚未给出面向大规模程序的、完全自主的仓库级代码翻译与验证的智能体方法。本文提出 ReCodeAgent，一种用于语言无关的仓库级代码翻译与验证的自主多智能体方法。用户只需提供源语言的项目并指定目标语言，ReCodeAgent 就会自动翻译并验证整个仓库。ReCodeAgent 是第一个能在多种语言上取得高翻译成功率的技术。我们将 ReCodeAgent 与四种可选的神经符号方法与智能体方法进行对比，翻译了 118 个真实项目，平均每个项目 1,975 行代码、43 个翻译单元，覆盖 6 种编程语言和 4 个语言对。结果表明，ReCodeAgent 在翻译正确性上持续优于已有技术，在真值测试上把测试通过率提升了 60.8%，平均成本为 15.3 美元。我们还对 ReCodeAgent 的轨迹做了面向过程的分析，确认了其过程效率。最后，我们考察了设计选择（多智能体 vs. 单智能体架构）如何影响 ReCodeAgent 的表现：平均而言，测试通过率下降 40.4%，轨迹长度增加 28%，且持续处于低效状态。","tl":"首个语言无关的自主多智能体仓库级翻译与验证方案。","au":["Ali Reza Ibrahimzada","Brandon Paulsen","Daniel Kroening","Reyhaneh Jabbarvand"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["repository-level code translation","multi-agent workflow","language-agnostic","translation validation","test pass rate"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/190/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.07341"},{"id":"p01210","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Aligning User Requirement with Large Language Model in Code Generation","tz":"在代码生成中让大语言模型对齐用户需求","a":"Repository-level code translation is critical for modernizing legacy systems, yet existing approaches based on large language models (LLMs) operate at the file level and fail to scale to codebases with complex inter-file dependencies. This limitation is evident in our industrial setting, where we aim to migrate a production repository (STAR) from Java to Kotlin, but file-level approaches produce fragmented results and fail to achieve end-to-end correctness. In this paper, we show that the primary cause of failure at the repository level is dependency inconsistency. Through an empirical study on open-source and industrial systems, we find that most errors arise from unresolved cross-file dependencies that cannot be effectively addressed by iterative feedback alone. We propose a dependency-aware incremental migration framework that elevates the unit of translation from individual files to dependency-consistent batches. Our approach constructs a dependency graph, groups interdependent files, and performs batched translation with iterative compile- and test-driven validation. We evaluate our method on a 51K line of code (LOC) industrial system and multiple repositories across interoperable language pairs (Java-Kotlin, Java-Scala, and C#-F#). On the STAR repository, file-level approaches achieve 38.16% compilation and 9.39% test success, whereas our approach achieves 100% compilation and test success across the evaluated settings, converging within a small number of iterations. These results show that dependency-aware batching improves scalability and reliability in repository-level code translation.","az":"仓库级代码翻译对于遗留系统现代化至关重要，但现有基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法都在文件层面工作，无法扩展到具有复杂跨文件依赖的代码库。这一局限在我们的工业场景中尤为明显：我们希望把一个生产仓库（STAR）从 Java 迁移到 Kotlin，但文件级方法产出的结果支离破碎，无法达成端到端的正确性。本文表明，仓库级失败的主要原因是依赖不一致。通过对开源与工业系统的实证研究，我们发现大多数错误来自未解决的跨文件依赖，而仅靠迭代反馈无法有效解决这些问题。我们提出一种依赖感知的增量迁移框架，把翻译单元从单个文件提升为依赖一致的批次。该方法构建依赖图，将相互依赖的文件分组，并以批为单位进行翻译，辅以迭代的编译与测试驱动验证。我们在一个 51K 行代码（LOC）的工业系统以及多个可互操作语言对（Java-Kotlin、Java-Scala、C#-F#）的仓库上评估了本方法。在 STAR 仓库上，文件级方法只达到 38.16% 的编译通过率和 9.39% 的测试通过率，而我们的方法在所有评估设置下都达到 100% 的编译与测试通过率，并能在少量迭代内收敛。结果表明，依赖感知的批处理提升了仓库级代码翻译的可扩展性与可靠性。","tl":"显式对齐用户需求意图，减少代码生成的需求偏差。","au":["Jia Li","Ruiqi Bai","Yangkang Luo","Yiran Zhang","Wentao Yang","Zeyu Sun","Tiankuo Zhao","Dongming Jin","Lei Li","Zhi Jin"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["requirement alignment","code generation","user intent","large language model"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/191/x"},{"id":"p01211","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"QDoctor: Probe-Based Testing for Quantum Programs","tz":"QDoctor：面向量子程序的探针式测试","tl":"（据标题推断）在量子程序中插入探针以观测中间态并判定缺陷。","au":["Qichen Wang","Shangzhou Xia","Xiaoyu Guo","Jianjun Zhao"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["quantum program testing","probe-based testing","quantum software","test oracle"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/192/x"},{"id":"p01212","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Doc2Feat-Bench: Evaluating Documentation-Driven Feature Addition","tz":"Doc2Feat-Bench：评测由文档驱动的功能新增","tl":"（据标题推断）首个以文档为输入评测智能体新增功能的基准。","au":["Zhonghao Jiang","Le Deng","Jialun Cao","Michael Pradel","Zhongxin Liu"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["feature addition","documentation-driven","benchmark","repository-level"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/193/x"},{"id":"p01213","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RegoMender: A Multi-agent Framework for Automated Rego Policy Repair","tz":"RegoMender：面向 Rego 策略自动修复的多智能体框架","a":"Iterative repair loops have become a core design pattern in LLM-based software engineering systems. These workflows repeatedly generate, validate, and repair artifacts using feedback such as compiler errors or test failures. Despite their widespread use, the impact of repair-loop iteration limits remains poorly understood, as most prior work adopts fixed, often arbitrary, repair budgets. We study repair-loop effectiveness across multiple software engineering tasks, including code generation, test generation, and code translation. Across several representative workflows, datasets, and contemporary low-cost LLMs, we observe a consistent pattern of diminishing returns: the first three to four repair iterations account for most achievable gains, while later iterations contribute only marginal improvements. We further find that repair behavior is influenced more strongly by workflow orchestration and feedback design than by the underlying model itself. These results suggest that repair budgets should be treated as an explicit experimental variable, as they directly affect evaluation outcomes, computational cost, runtime, and reproducibility in LLM-based software engineering research.","az":"迭代修复循环已经成为基于大语言模型的软件工程系统中的核心设计模式。这类工作流会利用编译错误或测试失败等反馈，反复地生成、验证并修复制品。尽管被广泛使用，修复循环迭代上限的影响却仍未被很好地理解，因为以往工作大多采用固定且往往是任意设定的修复预算。我们在多项软件工程任务上研究了修复循环的有效性，包括代码生成、测试生成和代码翻译。在若干具有代表性的工作流、数据集以及当代低成本大语言模型上，我们观察到一致的收益递减模式：前三到四轮修复迭代贡献了大部分可获得的收益，而后续迭代只带来边际提升。我们进一步发现，修复行为受工作流编排与反馈设计的影响，要强于受底层模型本身的影响。这些结果表明，修复预算应当被当作一个显式的实验变量，因为它会直接影响基于大语言模型的软件工程研究中的评估结论、计算成本、运行时间与可复现性。","tl":"多智能体协作修复 Rego 策略，首次把 APR 推向策略代码。","au":["Ruijie Zhang","Huaxiao Yin","Li Hu","Fanqi Kong","Haozhe Liang","Shaoyin Cheng","Kun Zhang","Bibo Tu"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["Rego policy repair","multi-agent framework","automated program repair","policy as code"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/194/x"},{"id":"p01214","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Defensive Capability Analysis for JavaScript Libraries","tz":"面向 JavaScript 库的防御性能力分析","a":"Capability analysis is a key building block for JavaScript supply-chain security tasks such as malware detection, security auditing, and runtime policy construction. However, existing approaches do not provide guarantees in the presence of JavaScript’s dynamic features. We present a defensive capability analysis for JavaScript libraries that soundly reportys every exercised capability for code executed under a lightweight protected runtime. The analysis tracks only objects that are relevant to capabilities. It reports capability usage either at the program locations where such objects are used, or conservatively when relevant objects escape through operations that the analysis does not model precisely. To address a small number of dynamic language features that would otherwise invalidate this analysis, we complement the static analysis with a lightweight runtime enforcement mechanism that blocks those patterns. We implement the approach and evaluate it on large datasets of benign and malicious npm packages. The results show that the approach scales to real-world packages, pinpoints capability-usage locations with high accuracy, and remains compatible with 98.2% of benign libraries when using the protected runtime. Moreover, it detects capability usage in 99.8% of the malicious packages in our dataset, while the remaining cases are blocked by the runtime protection. Our study also shows that at least 72.9% of the npm packages use no security-sensitive capabilities at all, suggesting that capability analysis can substantially reduce auditing effort in practice.","az":"能力分析是 JavaScript 供应链安全任务（如恶意软件检测、安全审计和运行时策略构建）的关键基石。然而，现有方法在 JavaScript 的动态特性面前无法给出保证。我们提出一种面向 JavaScript 库的防御性能力分析方法：对于在轻量级受保护运行时下执行的代码，它能健全地报告每一项被实际使用的能力。该分析只跟踪与能力相关的对象，并在这些对象被使用的程序位置报告能力使用；当相关对象通过分析未能精确建模的操作逃逸时，则保守地报告。为处理少数会使该分析失效的动态语言特性，我们用一种轻量级的运行时强制机制来补充静态分析，阻断这些模式。我们实现了该方法，并在大规模的良性与恶意 npm 包数据集上进行评估。结果表明，该方法可扩展到真实世界的包，能以很高的准确率定位能力使用位置，并在使用受保护运行时的情况下与 98.2% 的良性库保持兼容。此外，它在数据集中 99.8% 的恶意包上检出了能力使用，其余情况则被运行时保护所阻断。我们的研究还表明，至少 72.9% 的 npm 包完全不使用任何安全敏感能力，这说明能力分析在实践中可以大幅降低审计工作量。","tl":"静态能力分析加轻量运行时强制，健全覆盖 JS 动态特性。","au":["Wenyuan Xu","Anders Møller"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["capability analysis","JavaScript supply chain","npm malware","runtime enforcement","soundness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/195/x","pu":"https://cs.au.dk/~amoeller/papers/capa/paper.pdf"},{"id":"p01215","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RAVEN: Measuring Detection Instability in Anti-virus Engines under Semantics-Preserving Perturbations","tz":"RAVEN：测量杀毒引擎在语义保持扰动下的检测不稳定性","tl":"（据标题推断）系统量化语义保持扰动如何动摇杀毒引擎判定。","au":["Younghoon Ban","Beomjin Jin","Doowon Kim","Hyoungshick Kim","Haehyun Cho"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["anti-virus engines","semantics-preserving perturbation","detection instability","malware detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/196/x"},{"id":"p01216","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CiL-Agent: Compiler-in-the-Loop LLM Agent for Memory-Safe C Program Repair","tz":"CiL-Agent：面向内存安全 C 程序修复的编译器在环大模型智能体","tl":"（据标题推断）把编译器反馈放进智能体回路，迭代修复 C 内存安全缺陷。","au":["Yang Shen","Yating Zhang","Jiaqiang Yao","Liu Minghao","Wei Dong"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","tg":["agentic","llm-based","security"],"kw":["memory safety repair","compiler-in-the-loop","LLM agent","C program repair"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/197/x"},{"id":"p01217","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Safe Multi-site Binary Instrumentation of Running x86-64 Programs","tz":"对运行中的 x86-64 程序进行安全的多点二进制插桩","a":"Applying binary instrumentation to a running x86-64 process is difficult because variable-length instructions and weak alignment guarantees prevent safe in-place code modification under concurrent execution. Existing run-time approaches either trap concurrent threads on every overwrite or require global synchronization, limiting scalability. This paper presents DIBE, a run-time binary editing framework that safely instruments running x86-64 programs without trapping in the common case. An admin process resolves all instrumentation decisions, including multi-site patching tactics and trampoline placement, and exports them as metadata. A lightweight runtime inside the target process replays these edits, safely activating E9Patch's multi-site rewriting tactics on the live process by applying their dependent overwrites in an order that keeps every intermediate program state correct under concurrent execution, a guarantee that single-site punning and offline rewriting do not provide. It applies 77-90% of overwrites using hardware atomic primitives invisible to concurrent threads, with a trap-based fallback only for the remaining cross-boundary cases. We evaluate DIBE on 28 SPEC CPU2006 benchmarks and a multi-process Nginx server, and demonstrate it at browser scale on a running Chrome renderer and as a live memory-safety checker. DIBE matches static E9Patch on both instrumentation coverage (near-complete) and execution time overhead (within 0.5% at the geometric mean), keeps per-instruction overwrite latency sub-microsecond, and records zero trap hits across all Nginx configurations under sustained load.","az":"对正在运行的 x86-64 进程施加二进制插桩十分困难，因为变长指令和薄弱的对齐保证使得在并发执行下无法安全地原地修改代码。已有的运行时方法要么在每次覆写时都陷入（trap）并发线程，要么需要全局同步，从而限制了可扩展性。本文提出 DIBE，一个运行时二进制编辑框架，能够在常见情况下不触发陷入的前提下安全地对运行中的 x86-64 程序插桩。一个管理进程负责解析所有插桩决策，包括多点打补丁策略与跳板（trampoline）放置，并将其导出为元数据。目标进程内部的一个轻量级运行时重放这些编辑，通过按一定顺序施加相互依赖的覆写、使每个中间程序状态在并发执行下都保持正确，从而在活进程上安全地启用 E9Patch 的多点重写策略——这是单点指令双关（punning）和离线重写所无法提供的保证。它用对并发线程不可见的硬件原子原语完成了 77-90% 的覆写，仅对剩余的跨边界情况使用基于陷入的回退方案。我们在 28 个 SPEC CPU2006 基准以及一个多进程 Nginx 服务器上评估 DIBE，并在运行中的 Chrome 渲染进程这一浏览器级规模上、以及作为在线内存安全检查器进行了演示。DIBE 在插桩覆盖率（接近完全）和执行时间开销（几何平均在 0.5% 以内）上都与静态的 E9Patch 相当，把每条指令的覆写延迟保持在亚微秒级，并在持续负载下的所有 Nginx 配置中记录到零次陷入命中。","tl":"按依赖顺序施加覆写，实现免陷入的活进程多点重写。","au":["Jihun Baek","Sanghoon Han","Hyungon Moon"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["binary instrumentation","run-time rewriting","x86-64","E9Patch","concurrent execution safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/198/x"},{"id":"p01218","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Mobile Bug Reproduction via Global State Reprioritization and LLM-Guided Trajectory Exploration","tz":"基于全局状态重排序与大模型引导轨迹探索的移动缺陷复现","tl":"（据标题推断）全局状态重排序结合 LLM 引导探索，提升移动缺陷复现率。","au":["Dingbang Wang","Sidong Feng","William G.J. Halfond","Tingting Yu"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["mobile bug reproduction","state reprioritization","trajectory exploration","LLM-guided","Android"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/199/x"},{"id":"p01219","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"IncSFS: Incremental Full-Sparse Flow-Sensitive Pointer Analysis for C/C++","tz":"IncSFS：面向 C/C++ 的增量式全稀疏流敏感指针分析","a":"Pointer analysis is a fundamental technique for compiler optimization and program analysis. Flow-sensitive pointer analysis provides high precision but is difficult to scale to large projects. Tailored for rapid iteration scenarios where software evolves continuously, we introduce IncSFS, the first incremental full-sparse flow-sensitive pointer analysis algorithm for C/C++ programs. IncSFS first transforms the value-flow graph into a constraint graph and performs strongly connected component detection to ensure precision. It then propagates increases and decreases in points-to sets in an interleaved manner, supporting code deletion and insertion within a single analysis pass. IncSFS is guaranteed to terminate and compute the least fixed point when the points-to relation remains object-acyclic during analysis. Experiments on six large-scale real-world projects show that IncSFS is precise and efficient, achieving average speedups of 9.60x over full flow-sensitive pointer analysis and 5.84x over the traditional reset-recompute approach. It also improves efficiency by 15.8% over state-of-the-art incremental pointer analysis algorithms that propagate points-to-set changes.","az":"指针分析是编译优化与程序分析的基础技术。流敏感指针分析精度很高，但难以扩展到大型项目。面向软件持续演化的快速迭代场景，我们提出 IncSFS，这是首个面向 C/C++ 程序的增量式全稀疏流敏感指针分析算法。IncSFS 首先把值流图转换为约束图，并执行强连通分量检测以保证精度；随后以交错方式传播指向集的增量与减量，在一遍分析中同时支持代码的删除与插入。当分析过程中指向关系保持对象无环时，IncSFS 保证终止并计算出最小不动点。在六个大规模真实项目上的实验表明，IncSFS 兼具精度与效率：相比完整的流敏感指针分析平均加速 9.60 倍，相比传统的重置-重算方法平均加速 5.84 倍；相比传播指向集变化的最新增量指针分析算法，效率也提升了 15.8%。","tl":"交错传播增减量，实现单遍支持增删的增量全稀疏流敏感分析。","au":["Kunlin Liu","Zhenbang Chen","Piyi Zu","Yide Du","Ji Wang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["incremental pointer analysis","flow-sensitive","full-sparse","value-flow graph","C/C++"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/200/x"},{"id":"p01220","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ExcavatorFuzz: LLM-Guided Path-Difficulty-Driven Directed Greybox Fuzzing","tz":"ExcavatorFuzz：大模型引导、路径难度驱动的定向灰盒模糊测试","a":"Several experience reports illustrate that mutation testing is capable of supporting a shift-left testing strategy, especially in industries where late bug discovery incurs very high costs and risks. In the context of cyber-physical systems, a shift left implies that engineers need to test the design models used to simulate, prototype, and analyse the feasibility of the system under design. In this paper, we analyse the challenges we encountered and the lessons we learned when incorporating mutation testing in the context of DUCO, a company producing ventilation systems for buildings. The engineers within DUCO have years of experience with model-based engineering centered around Simulink and StateFlow, including unit tests for their models. During a pilot project with our tool prototype MUT4SLX we learned that equivalent mutants, requirement traceability, and mutation testing for Stateflow represent particular challenges not yet reported in the academic literature.","az":"若干经验报告表明，变异测试能够支撑左移测试策略，尤其是在后期发现缺陷会带来极高成本与风险的行业中。在信息物理系统的语境下，左移意味着工程师需要测试那些用于仿真、原型化并分析待设计系统可行性的设计模型。本文分析了我们在 DUCO（一家生产建筑通风系统的公司）场景中引入变异测试时遇到的挑战与获得的经验教训。DUCO 的工程师在以 Simulink 和 StateFlow 为中心的基于模型的工程方面拥有多年经验，包括为其模型编写单元测试。在使用我们的工具原型 MUT4SLX 开展试点项目的过程中，我们了解到等价变异体、需求可追溯性以及面向 Stateflow 的变异测试，是学术文献尚未报道过的特有挑战。","tl":"用 LLM 估计路径可达难度，据此调度定向模糊测试能量。","au":["Kaiyu Xie","Siyuan Li","Jiaqian Peng","Yun Yang","Yaowen Zheng","Kai Cheng","Jiayu Zhang","Shizhao Tian","liyubo","Hongsong Zhu"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["directed greybox fuzzing","path difficulty","LLM-guided","seed scheduling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/201/x"},{"id":"p01221","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"GANADI: Uncovering C/C++ OSS Reuse Genealogies via Pivotal Function-Based Clustering to Enhance Supply Chain Security","tz":"GANADI：基于关键函数聚类揭示 C/C++ 开源复用谱系以增强供应链安全","a":"Containerization dominates enterprise software delivery, yet Dockerfiles that assemble container images frequently harbor security misconfigurations and structural technical debt. This problem is poorly understood in corporate inner-source environments, where proprietary context and isolated governance prevent direct application of open-source findings. We present an automated, six-stage pipeline that: (1) crawls an enterprise GitLab instance, (2) enriches each Dockerfile with static security and quality metrics (Hadolint, ShellCheck, Trivy) and lifecycle data, (3) groups functionally identical workloads using LLM-generated semantic descriptions and HDBSCAN, and (4) quantifies the optimization gap against cluster-internal reference implementations. Applied to 11,470 Dockerfiles from over 6,200 repositories at a single large industrial company, we find a systemic deficit: 99 % of files contain at least one security misconfiguration, 80.8 % violate Dockerfile best practices, and the median artifact has not been revised for 838~days. Despite this, high-quality reference implementations already exist within 83 % of functional clusters. Adopting these internal standards would increase the average security posture score by 60.4 % without developing any new templates. These findings, grounded in one organization's inner-source ecosystem, provide a data-driven foundation for future automated, context-aware recommender systems targeting enterprise supply-chain security; whether the observed technical-debt distribution and optimization gap generalize to other enterprises remains an open question for future multi-organization study.","az":"容器化主导着企业软件交付，但用于组装容器镜像的 Dockerfile 常常隐藏着安全错误配置与结构性技术债。这一问题在企业内源（inner-source）环境中尤其缺乏理解，因为专有上下文和相互隔离的治理机制使得开源研究结论难以直接套用。我们提出一条自动化的六阶段流水线：(1) 爬取企业内部的 GitLab 实例；(2) 为每个 Dockerfile 补充静态安全与质量指标（Hadolint、ShellCheck、Trivy）以及生命周期数据；(3) 利用 LLM 生成的语义描述与 HDBSCAN 对功能相同的工作负载分组；(4) 相对于簇内参考实现量化优化差距。我们将其应用于某家大型工业企业的 6,200 多个仓库中的 11,470 个 Dockerfile，发现了系统性的缺陷：99\\% 的文件至少包含一项安全错误配置，80.8\\% 违反 Dockerfile 最佳实践，且中位制品已有 838 天未被修订。尽管如此，83\\% 的功能簇内部其实已经存在高质量的参考实现。采用这些内部标准可以在不开发任何新模板的情况下，把平均安全态势得分提升 60.4\\%。这些扎根于单一组织内源生态的发现，为面向企业供应链安全的、自动化且上下文感知的推荐系统提供了数据驱动的基础；至于所观察到的技术债分布与优化差距能否推广到其他企业，仍是未来多组织研究需要回答的开放问题。","tl":"以关键函数聚类重建开源代码复用谱系，定位供应链风险。","au":["Dongyeon Kim","Seunghoon Woo","Heejo Lee"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["OSS reuse genealogy","software composition analysis","pivotal function clustering","supply chain security","C/C++"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/202/x"},{"id":"p01222","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"OrthCoder: Balancing Security and Utility in Secure Code Generation via Orthogonal Adaptation","tz":"OrthCoder：通过正交适配在安全代码生成中平衡安全性与效用","tl":"（据标题推断）用正交参数适配解耦安全对齐与代码效用的冲突。","au":["Menghan Tian","Youliang Yuan","Zhiqing Zhong","Pinjia He"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["secure code generation","orthogonal adaptation","security-utility trade-off","fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/203/x"},{"id":"p01223","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Zero-Knowledge VMs: Security and Usability in Practice","tz":"零知识虚拟机：实践中的安全性与可用性","a":"Recent work on LLM-driven autonomous penetration testing reports promising results, but existing systems often bundle architectural, prompting, and tool-integration choices together. This makes it difficult to determine what is gained over a simple agent and harness. We present Cochise, a 630 LOC Python reference implementation for autonomous penetration-testing experiments. Cochise connects to a Linux execution host over SSH and supports attacking controlled target environments reachable from that jump host. The prototype implements a Planner--Executor architecture in which long-term state is maintained by the planner, while a ReAct-style executor issues commands over SSH and self-corrects based on command outputs. The scenario prompt can be adapted to different target environments. We evaluate the harness against a live third-party testbed, Game of Active Directory (GOAD). Cochise is intended not as a state-of-the-art penetration-testing agent, but as a reusable experimental infrastructure for comparing models, agent architectures, and penetration-testing traces. Alongside the prototype, we release replay and analysis tools: (i) cochise-replay for offline visualization of captured runs, (ii) cochise-analyze-logs and cochise-analyze-graphs for cost, token, duration, and compromise analysis, and (iii) a corpus of JSON trajectory logs from GOAD runs, so that researchers can study agent behavior without provisioning the 48--64 GB RAM / 190 GB storage testbed themselves. Tool demo video available at https://youtu.be/2mQimB1ufyI.","az":"近期关于大语言模型驱动的自主渗透测试的工作报告了令人鼓舞的结果，但现有系统往往把架构、提示与工具集成的各种选择捆绑在一起，这使人难以判断相对于一个简单的智能体加执行框架究竟获得了什么。我们提出 Cochise，一个 630 行 Python 代码的参考实现，用于自主渗透测试实验。Cochise 通过 SSH 连接到一台 Linux 执行主机，并支持攻击可从该跳板机访问的受控目标环境。该原型实现了 Planner--Executor 架构：由 planner 维护长期状态，而 ReAct 风格的 executor 通过 SSH 下发命令并根据命令输出自我纠正。场景提示可以适配不同的目标环境。我们在一个真实的第三方测试床 Game of Active Directory（GOAD）上评估该执行框架。Cochise 的定位并不是最先进的渗透测试智能体，而是一套可复用的实验基础设施，用于比较不同模型、智能体架构与渗透测试轨迹。除原型之外，我们还发布了回放与分析工具：(i) cochise-replay，用于离线可视化已捕获的运行；(ii) cochise-analyze-logs 与 cochise-analyze-graphs，用于成本、token、时长与攻陷情况分析；(iii) 一份来自 GOAD 运行的 JSON 轨迹日志语料，使研究者无需自行搭建需要 48--64 GB 内存 / 190 GB 存储的测试床即可研究智能体行为。工具演示视频见 https://youtu.be/2mQimB1ufyI。","tl":"系统考察 zkVM 在真实使用中的安全缺陷与可用性障碍。","au":["Jinan Jiang","Jinzhao Chu","Pengyu Xue","Xinghao Peng","Haoran Qin","Xiapu Luo"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","empirical-study"],"kw":["zero-knowledge VM","zkVM security","usability","cryptographic toolchain"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/204/x"},{"id":"p01224","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Formal Verification-Integrated Reinforcement Learning for Automated ORM Schema Synthesis","tz":"面向 ORM 模式自动合成的形式化验证集成强化学习方法","a":"Object-relational mapping (ORM) frameworks are widely used to bridge object-oriented models and relational databases, but conventional tools generate only single point solutions and often miss optimal trade-offs between performance and storage consumption. Exhaustive tradespace analysis can discover Pareto-optimal database designs, but it is computationally prohibitive for realistic systems. This paper introduces ReinforceORM, an automated and scalable framework that formulates ORM schema synthesis as a multi-objective optimization problem solved via reinforcement learning with formal verification. Our approach integrates multiple RL algorithms to efficiently search the vast space of mapping strategies, balancing insertion time, query performance, and storage consumption, while employing Alloy-based formal analysis to provide bounded verification of structural and semantic correctness in generated schemas. Evaluation across fifteen diverse, real-world software systems shows that ReinforceORM identifies over 80% of ground-truth Pareto-optimal ORM configurations—an 18-fold improvement over leading ORM frameworks such as Hibernate, Django ORM, SQLAlchemy, and Entity Framework. Compared to state-of-the-art specification-driven search, ReinforceORM reduces analysis runtime and memory usage by four and five orders of magnitude, respectively, while maintaining near-optimal solution quality.","az":"对象-关系映射（ORM）框架被广泛用于在面向对象模型与关系数据库之间架起桥梁，但传统工具只会生成单一的点解，常常错过性能与存储消耗之间的最优权衡。穷举式的权衡空间分析虽能发现帕累托最优的数据库设计，但对现实系统而言计算代价过高。本文提出 ReinforceORM，一个自动化且可扩展的框架，它把 ORM 模式合成表述为一个多目标优化问题，并通过结合形式化验证的强化学习来求解。我们的方法集成多种 RL 算法以高效搜索庞大的映射策略空间，在插入时间、查询性能与存储消耗之间取得平衡，同时采用基于 Alloy 的形式化分析，为所生成模式的结构与语义正确性提供有界验证。在十五个多样化的真实软件系统上的评估表明，ReinforceORM 能识别出超过 80% 的真值帕累托最优 ORM 配置——相比 Hibernate、Django ORM、SQLAlchemy 和 Entity Framework 等主流 ORM 框架提升了 18 倍。与最先进的规约驱动搜索相比，ReinforceORM 将分析运行时间和内存占用分别降低了四个和五个数量级，同时保持接近最优的解质量。","tl":"把 ORM 模式合成变成 RL 多目标搜索，并用 Alloy 有界验证正确性。","au":["Md Rashedul Hasan","Hamid Bagheri"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["ORM schema synthesis","multi-objective optimization","reinforcement learning","Alloy formal verification","Pareto-optimal"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/205/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/205/Formal-Verification-Integrated-Reinforcement-Learning-for-Automated-ORM-Schema-Synthe"},{"id":"p01225","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Repository-Aware Metamorphic Relation Generation for Augmented Reality Applications using Large Language Models","tz":"使用大语言模型为增强现实应用生成仓库感知的蜕变关系","a":"Simulation-based testing enables safe and repeatable evaluation of autonomous driving systems, but its effectiveness is limited by the gap between synthetic simulator outputs and real-world camera observations. To address this problem, we present Cam2Sim, a tool that transforms real-world driving recordings into playable CARLA simulation scenarios. Starting from camera images and poses, Cam2Sim reconstructs road geometry, ego trajectories, parked vehicles, and simulation assets, and augments the reconstructed environment with Gaussian Splatting to render camera observations that resemble the original recording. The framework supports ROS-based data extraction, parked-vehicle detection, OpenStreetMap-based map generation, CARLA scenario construction, Gaussian Splatting training, trajectory replay, and closed-loop execution with a system under test. We validate Cam2Sim on a real-world urban-driving scenario with a camera-based end-to-end driving model, comparing reconstruction quality, image-generation quality, and closed-loop behavior against both a simulation-only baseline and the real-world target. Results show that Gaussian-Splatting-based rendering reduces the visual gap with respect to standard simulator rendering and improves behavioral similarity to the real-world reference runs. The artifact is publicly available at https: //github.com/ast-fortiss-tum/cam2sim, and a screencast showing the tool is available at https://youtu.be/KmZ74l1__lI","az":"基于仿真的测试能够对自动驾驶系统进行安全且可重复的评估，但其有效性受限于合成仿真输出与真实世界摄像头观测之间的差距。为解决这一问题，我们提出 Cam2Sim，一个把真实驾驶录制转换为可运行 CARLA 仿真场景的工具。Cam2Sim 从摄像头图像与位姿出发，重建道路几何、自车轨迹、停放车辆与仿真资产，并用高斯泼溅（Gaussian Splatting）增强重建环境，以渲染出与原始录制相近的摄像头观测。该框架支持基于 ROS 的数据抽取、停放车辆检测、基于 OpenStreetMap 的地图生成、CARLA 场景构建、高斯泼溅训练、轨迹回放，以及与被测系统的闭环执行。我们在一个真实的城市驾驶场景上，使用基于摄像头的端到端驾驶模型验证 Cam2Sim，并在重建质量、图像生成质量与闭环行为上与仅用仿真的基线和真实世界目标进行对比。结果表明，基于高斯泼溅的渲染相比标准仿真器渲染缩小了视觉差距，并提升了与真实世界参考运行的行为相似度。制品已公开于 https://github.com/ast-fortiss-tum/cam2sim，工具演示视频见 https://youtu.be/KmZ74l1__lI。","tl":"利用仓库上下文让 LLM 为 AR 应用自动构造蜕变关系。","au":["Dibyendu Brinto Bose","Jiawei Qin","Chris Brown"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based","multimodal"],"kw":["metamorphic relation generation","augmented reality testing","repository-aware","large language models","test oracle"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/206/x"},{"id":"p01226","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Learning to Triage Vulnerability Reports from Program Analysis: An Empirical Study in Node.js","tz":"学习对程序分析产生的漏洞报告进行分诊：Node.js 上的实证研究","a":"Program analysis tools often produce large volumes of candidate vulnerability reports that require costly manual review, creating a practical challenge: how can security analysts prioritize the reports most likely to be true vulnerabilities? This paper investigates whether machine learning can be applied to prioritizing vulnerabilities reported by program analysis tools. We focus on Node.js packages and collect a benchmark of 1,883 Node.js packages, each containing one reported ACE or ACI vulnerability. We evaluate a variety of machine learning approaches, including classical models, graph neural networks (GNNs), large language models (LLMs), and hybrid models that combine GNNs and LLMs, trained on data derived from program analysis tool outputs (NodeMedic-FINE in our case study). The top LLM achieves F1=0.915, while the best provenance-graph-based method achieves F1=0.904. On the reports that the upstream tool flags but cannot automatically confirm, at a target of recovering 90% of the exploitable reports, the leading model eliminates 75% of the benign reports from manual review. If the best model is tuned to operate at a precision level of 0.8 (i.e., allowing 20% false positives among all warnings), our approach can report 99.2% of exploitable taint flows while missing only 0.8%, demonstrating strong potential for real-world vulnerability triage.","az":"程序分析工具常常产生大量候选漏洞报告，需要昂贵的人工复核，由此带来一个现实挑战：安全分析人员如何优先处理最可能是真实漏洞的报告？本文研究机器学习能否用于对程序分析工具报告的漏洞进行优先级排序。我们聚焦 Node.js 包，收集了一个包含 1,883 个 Node.js 包的基准，每个包含一个已报告的 ACE 或 ACI 漏洞。我们评估了多种机器学习方法，包括经典模型、图神经网络（GNN）、大语言模型（LLM），以及结合 GNN 与 LLM 的混合模型，它们都在源自程序分析工具输出（本案例研究中为 NodeMedic-FINE）的数据上训练。最好的 LLM 达到 F1=0.915，而最好的基于溯源图的方法达到 F1=0.904。对于上游工具标记但无法自动确认的报告，在恢复 90% 可利用报告的目标下，领先模型可从人工复核中剔除 75% 的良性报告。如果将最佳模型调到精确率 0.8 的工作点（即允许全部告警中有 20% 的误报），我们的方法可以报告 99.2% 的可利用污点流，仅漏掉 0.8%，展现出面向真实世界漏洞分诊的巨大潜力。","tl":"用 GNN 与 LLM 对污点分析告警排序，削减 75% 人工复核。","au":["Ronghao Ni","Aidan Z.H. Yang","Min-Chien Hsu","Nuno Sabino","Limin Jia","Ruben Martins","Darion Cassel","Kevin Cheang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["vulnerability triage","program analysis","Node.js","graph neural network","false positive reduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/207/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.20739v2"},{"id":"p01227","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Code Transformation Rule Synthesis using LLMs: Potential and Limits","tz":"使用 LLM 进行代码变换规则合成：潜力与局限","a":"Binary decompilation plays a vital role in various cybersecurity and software engineering tasks. Recently, end-to-end decompilation methods powered by large language models (LLMs) have attracted increasing attention for their ability to generate highly readable source code with minimal human intervention. However, existing LLM-based methods still struggle with reconstructing program structure and logic, achieving accurate data recovery, ensuring data security and privacy, and maintaining computational efficiency. To address these challenges, we propose the CodeInverter Suite, with three main pieces: (1) the CodeInverter Workflow (CIW) is a novel prompt engineering method that incorporates control flow graphs (CFG) and explicit data mappings to enhance structure reconstruction and data recovery during decompilation; (2) building upon CIW, we construct the CodeInverter Dataset (CID), a large-scale domain-specific dataset containing 8.69 million samples enriched with CFGs and data mapping information; (3) we develop CodeInverter Models (CIMs), two lightweight LLMs with 1.3B and 6.7B parameters, enabling efficient inference in privacy-sensitive and resource-constrained environments. Extensive experiments on two benchmark datasets demonstrate that CIW significantly enhances the decompilation performance of various LLMs, with average improvements of 13.07% in re-executability and 23.94% in re-compilability. For our proposed decompilation model, CIM-6.7B achieves state-of-the-art performance in terms of re-executability and readability, outperforming existing LLMs-even with over 100 times more parameters-by an average of 11.03% and 6.27%, respectively.","az":"二进制反编译在各类网络安全与软件工程任务中扮演着关键角色。近来，由大语言模型（LLM）驱动的端到端反编译方法因能在极少人工干预下生成可读性很高的源码而受到越来越多关注。然而，现有基于 LLM 的方法在重建程序结构与逻辑、实现准确的数据恢复、保障数据安全与隐私以及维持计算效率方面仍存在困难。为解决这些挑战，我们提出 CodeInverter 套件，包含三部分：(1) CodeInverter Workflow（CIW）是一种新颖的提示工程方法，引入控制流图（CFG）和显式数据映射，以增强反编译过程中的结构重建与数据恢复；(2) 在 CIW 基础上，我们构建了 CodeInverter 数据集（CID），这是一个大规模领域专用数据集，包含 869 万条样本，并富含 CFG 与数据映射信息；(3) 我们开发了 CodeInverter 模型（CIMs），即 1.3B 与 6.7B 参数的两个轻量级 LLM，可在隐私敏感和资源受限环境中高效推理。在两个基准数据集上的大量实验表明，CIW 显著提升了多种 LLM 的反编译性能，可重新执行率平均提升 13.07%，可重新编译率平均提升 23.94%。对于我们提出的反编译模型，CIM-6.7B 在可重新执行性与可读性上达到了最先进水平，分别平均超过现有 LLM（即便后者参数量多出 100 倍以上）11.03% 与 6.27%。","tl":"用 CFG 与数据映射提示加轻量模型提升二进制反编译质量。","au":["Axel Allain","Aymeric Blot","Djamel Eddine Khelladi","Mathieu Acher"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["binary decompilation","control flow graph","prompt engineering","lightweight LLM","re-executability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/208/x"},{"id":"p01228","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Low-Cost Human-in-the-Loop Investigation of Toxicity on GitHub at Scale","tz":"低成本人在回路方法的 GitHub 大规模毒性内容研究","a":"Toxic interactions in open source discussions can alienate contributors and threaten project sustainability, yet prior empirical studies of GitHub toxicity have been limited in scale, raising questions about their generalizability. Scaling up is difficult because toxicity on GitHub is often implicit and context-dependent, making both fully manual annotation and LLM-based labeling unreliable. We present a human-in-the-loop (HITL) annotation methodology that makes large-scale, domain-calibrated toxicity labeling practical. A single call to a small, local LLM produces both a toxicity prediction and a set of interpretable event category scores. A lightweight Random Forest validator then uses those scores to flag the small subset of conversations most likely to be mislabeled, directing human review only where it is needed. The validator outperforms confidence-based and multi-LLM baselines while adding low annotation cost. We apply this pipeline to over 124,000 GitHub issue and pull request conversations. Using the resulting dataset, we evaluate key findings from prior small-scale research, confirming some and qualifying others, and present new insights into the prevalence, characteristics, and dynamics of toxicity across diverse open source projects.","az":"开源讨论中的有毒互动会疏远贡献者并威胁项目可持续性，然而以往关于 GitHub 毒性的实证研究规模有限，其结论的普适性存疑。扩大规模之所以困难，是因为 GitHub 上的毒性往往是隐含且依赖上下文的，这使得完全人工标注和基于 LLM 的标注都不可靠。我们提出一种人在回路（HITL）标注方法，使大规模、领域校准的毒性标注变得可行。对一个小型本地 LLM 的一次调用即可同时产出毒性预测和一组可解释的事件类别分数。随后一个轻量级随机森林验证器利用这些分数标记出最可能被误标的一小部分对话，从而把人工复核集中在真正需要的地方。该验证器优于基于置信度和多 LLM 的基线，且只增加很低的标注成本。我们将该流水线应用于超过 124,000 条 GitHub issue 与 pull request 对话。基于所得数据集，我们评估了以往小规模研究的关键结论，确认了其中一些并修正了另一些，并对多样开源项目中毒性的普遍程度、特征与动态给出了新的洞见。","tl":"小模型加随机森林验证器，实现 12 万条 GitHub 对话的低成本毒性标注。","au":["Rahat Rizvi Rahman","Mia Mohammad Imran","Kostadin Damevski"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["toxicity","human-in-the-loop annotation","open source community","GitHub issues","random forest validator"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/209/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25946"},{"id":"p01229","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Generation of Web Apps with Agentic IDEs: An Empirical Assessment","tz":"用智能体 IDE 生成 Web 应用：一项实证评估","a":"Agentic IDEs are among the most significant innovations in software engineering, aiming to accelerate application development through LLM-based agents that can assist developers during development. However, their evaluation in end-to-end development tasks involving the generation of complete applications remains limited. To fill this gap, we propose a rigorous comparative analysis of three popular agentic IDEs (Copilot, Cursor, and Windsurf) in the generation of five full-stack Web applications from scratch. Results show high maturity in the generation of established patterns, such as CRUD operations and authentication features. In contrast, the generation of less common distributed architectures, such as a task queue architecture, produces significantly more errors. Overall, results show that Agentic IDEs cannot replace developers but shift their role toward building software by orchestrating LLM-based agents through natural-language instructions and iterative refinement. Yet, each agentic IDE shows its peculiarities, although differences are narrow.","az":"智能体 IDE 是软件工程中最重要的创新之一，旨在通过可在开发过程中辅助开发者的基于 LLM 的智能体来加速应用开发。然而，它们在涉及生成完整应用的端到端开发任务中的评估仍然有限。为填补这一空白，我们对三款流行的智能体 IDE（Copilot、Cursor 和 Windsurf）在从零生成五个全栈 Web 应用上的表现进行了严格的对比分析。结果表明，在生成成熟的既有模式（如 CRUD 操作和认证功能）方面已具备较高成熟度；相比之下，生成较不常见的分布式架构（如任务队列架构）则产生了显著更多的错误。总体而言，结果显示智能体 IDE 无法取代开发者，而是把开发者的角色转向通过自然语言指令和迭代式细化来编排基于 LLM 的智能体、从而构建软件。同时，各款智能体 IDE 各有特点，尽管彼此差异并不大。","tl":"对比三款智能体 IDE 生成全栈应用，罕见架构错误率明显更高。","au":["Manuel Marceca","Maria Teresa Rossi","Leonardo Mariani"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["agentic IDE","full-stack web app generation","Copilot","Cursor","empirical assessment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/210/x"},{"id":"p01230","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Looks Good, but Does It Run? A Large-Scale Empirical Study of the Executability of Example Code in Model Cards","tz":"看着不错，但能跑吗？模型卡中示例代码可执行性的大规模实证研究","tl":"（据标题推断）首次大规模实测模型卡示例代码能否真正运行。","au":["Simeng Yao","Jialin Zhao","Yang Zhang","Tun Li","Tao Wang","Changrong Xie","Zezhou Tang","Yiwen Wu"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["model cards","example code","executability","empirical study","model hub"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/211/x"},{"id":"p01231","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Thread to Pool: Modeling and Static Detection of Thread Pool Misuses in Java Programs","tz":"从线程到线程池：Java 程序中线程池误用的建模与静态检测","tl":"（据标题推断）首次系统建模 Java 线程池误用模式并静态检测。","au":["Baoquan Cui","Yucheng Qiu","Rui Han","Hang Gao","Jian Zhang"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["thread pool misuse","static detection","Java concurrency","API misuse"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/212/x"},{"id":"p01232","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"HERO: Hypothesis-Centered Root-Cause Analysis for Microservice Incidents","tz":"HERO：面向微服务故障的以假设为中心的根因分析","tl":"（据标题推断）用假设生成与验证的循环做微服务根因定位。","au":["Jiewei Lyu","Junquan Yi","Shu Liang","Pengfei Chen","Long Pan"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["root cause analysis","microservice incident","observability","hypothesis-driven"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/213/x"},{"id":"p01233","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Gray-Box Fuzzing in Local Space","tz":"局部空间中的灰盒模糊测试","a":"Several experience reports illustrate that mutation testing is capable of supporting a shift-left testing strategy, especially in industries where late bug discovery incurs very high costs and risks. In the context of cyber-physical systems, a shift left implies that engineers need to test the design models used to simulate, prototype, and analyse the feasibility of the system under design. In this paper, we analyse the challenges we encountered and the lessons we learned when incorporating mutation testing in the context of DUCO, a company producing ventilation systems for buildings. The engineers within DUCO have years of experience with model-based engineering centered around Simulink and StateFlow, including unit tests for their models. During a pilot project with our tool prototype MUT4SLX we learned that equivalent mutants, requirement traceability, and mutation testing for Stateflow represent particular challenges not yet reported in the academic literature.","az":"多份经验报告表明，变异测试能够支撑测试左移策略，尤其是在缺陷发现过晚会带来极高成本与风险的行业中。在信息物理系统的语境下，测试左移意味着工程师需要测试那些用于仿真、原型化和分析待设计系统可行性的设计模型。本文分析了我们在 DUCO（一家生产楼宇通风系统的公司）环境中引入变异测试时遇到的挑战与获得的经验教训。DUCO 的工程师在以 Simulink 和 StateFlow 为核心的基于模型的工程方面拥有多年经验，其中包括针对模型的单元测试。在与我们的工具原型 MUT4SLX 开展的试点项目中，我们发现等价变异体、需求可追踪性以及面向 Stateflow 的变异测试构成了学术文献尚未报道的特殊挑战。","tl":"工业试点揭示 Simulink/Stateflow 变异测试的三类未报道挑战。","au":["Martin Jonáš","Jan Strejcek","Marek Trtík"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["mutation testing","Simulink","Stateflow","cyber-physical systems","industrial experience report"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/214/x"},{"id":"p01234","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Revisiting LLMs on New Feature Implementation in Real-World Software Development Practices","tz":"重新审视 LLM 在真实软件开发实践中的新功能实现能力","tl":"（据标题推断）在真实开发场景重估 LLM 的新特性实现能力。","au":["Jia Li","Tingxuan Huang","Tiankuo Zhao","Yiming Wang","Yiran Zhang","Anshun Hu","Kechi Zhang","Lecheng Wang","Zinan Sheng","Kui Liu","Ge Li","Zhi Jin"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["feature implementation","real-world development","LLM evaluation","repository-level task"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/215/x"},{"id":"p01235","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Self-Discovering Security Oracles: Meta-learning Vulnerability Detection Strategies through Adversarial Self-Play","tz":"自发现的安全预言：通过对抗自博弈元学习漏洞检测策略","a":"Current Large Language Model (LLM) based vulnerability detection systems rely on static prompting strategies and fixed analysis pipelines that fail to adapt to evolving threat landscapes. These approaches struggle to discover unknown vulnerability patterns beyond their training distributions, limiting their effectiveness against emerging security threats. This paper explores adversarial meta-learning where foundation models autonomously discover vulnerability detection strategies through reinforcement learning and competitive self-play. We present MetaMorphSES, a framework that enables Foundational models to evolve in terms of both vulnerability generation capabilities (as a red team) and detection strategies (as a blue team) through adversarial co-evolution without predetermined prompts or fixed architectures. The system learns to generate increasingly sophisticated synthetic vulnerabilities while simultaneously developing detection strategies that generalize to real-world security flaws. Through a dual-loop optimization process, the inner loop generates and detects vulnerabilities while the outer meta-learning loop discovers optimal detection strategies through reinforcement learning. Our experiments on six real-world vulnerability corpora demonstrate that meta-learned security strategies yield substantially stronger detection of unseen vulnerabilities (up to 0.90 F1) against nine strong baselines spanning rule-based static analysis, zero-shot and fine-tuned LLMs, and recent vulnerability detectors, with the system reaching a stable equilibrium. While training remains resource-intensive, the approach establishes adversarial meta-learning as a novel and effective way to discover security vulnerabilities with foundational models through self-directed adaptation without explicit programming of detection rules.","az":"当前基于大语言模型（LLM）的漏洞检测系统依赖静态的提示策略和固定的分析流水线，难以适应不断演化的威胁态势。这类方法难以发现超出其训练分布之外的未知漏洞模式，从而限制了其应对新兴安全威胁的有效性。本文探索对抗式元学习，让基础模型通过强化学习和竞争性自博弈自主发现漏洞检测策略。我们提出 MetaMorphSES 框架，使基础模型能够在没有预设提示或固定架构的情况下，通过对抗式协同进化同时提升漏洞生成能力（作为红队）与检测策略（作为蓝队）。该系统学会生成日益复杂的合成漏洞，同时发展出能泛化到真实世界安全缺陷的检测策略。通过双层优化过程，内层循环生成并检测漏洞，外层元学习循环则通过强化学习发现最优检测策略。我们在六个真实世界漏洞语料上的实验表明，元学习得到的安全策略在检测未见漏洞方面显著更强（F1 最高达 0.90），优于涵盖基于规则的静态分析、零样本与微调 LLM 以及近期漏洞检测器的九个强基线，且系统达到了稳定的均衡。尽管训练仍然资源密集，该方法确立了对抗式元学习作为一种新颖有效的途径，可让基础模型通过自主适应发现安全漏洞，而无需显式编写检测规则。","tl":"红蓝队自博弈元学习自动演化出泛化的漏洞检测策略。","au":["Md Rashedul Hasan","Hamid Bagheri"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["adversarial self-play","meta-learning","vulnerability detection","reinforcement learning","security oracle"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/216/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/216/Self-Discovering-Security-Oracles-Meta-learning-Vulnerability-Detection-Strategies-t"},{"id":"p01236","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"S2CAgent: A Self-Learning Agent Knowledge Graph Framework for Software Supply Chain Analysis","tz":"S2CAgent：面向软件供应链分析的自学习智能体知识图谱框架","a":"Containerization dominates enterprise software delivery, yet Dockerfiles that assemble container images frequently harbor security misconfigurations and structural technical debt. This problem is poorly understood in corporate inner-source environments, where proprietary context and isolated governance prevent direct application of open-source findings. We present an automated, six-stage pipeline that: (1) crawls an enterprise GitLab instance, (2) enriches each Dockerfile with static security and quality metrics (Hadolint, ShellCheck, Trivy) and lifecycle data, (3) groups functionally identical workloads using LLM-generated semantic descriptions and HDBSCAN, and (4) quantifies the optimization gap against cluster-internal reference implementations. Applied to 11,470 Dockerfiles from over 6,200 repositories at a single large industrial company, we find a systemic deficit: 99 % of files contain at least one security misconfiguration, 80.8 % violate Dockerfile best practices, and the median artifact has not been revised for 838~days. Despite this, high-quality reference implementations already exist within 83 % of functional clusters. Adopting these internal standards would increase the average security posture score by 60.4 % without developing any new templates. These findings, grounded in one organization's inner-source ecosystem, provide a data-driven foundation for future automated, context-aware recommender systems targeting enterprise supply-chain security; whether the observed technical-debt distribution and optimization gap generalize to other enterprises remains an open question for future multi-organization study.","az":"容器化主导着企业软件交付，然而用于组装容器镜像的 Dockerfile 经常隐藏安全误配置和结构性技术债。在企业内源（inner-source）环境中，由于专有上下文和相互隔离的治理方式，开源领域的结论无法直接套用，这一问题因而缺乏理解。我们提出一条自动化的六阶段流水线：(1) 爬取企业 GitLab 实例；(2) 用静态安全与质量指标（Hadolint、ShellCheck、Trivy）以及生命周期数据丰富每个 Dockerfile；(3) 使用 LLM 生成的语义描述与 HDBSCAN 将功能相同的工作负载聚类；(4) 相对于簇内参考实现量化优化差距。将其应用于某大型工业公司超过 6,200 个仓库中的 11,470 个 Dockerfile，我们发现系统性缺陷：99% 的文件至少包含一处安全误配置，80.8% 违反 Dockerfile 最佳实践，中位制品已有 838 天未被修订。尽管如此，83% 的功能簇内部已经存在高质量的参考实现。采用这些内部标准可使平均安全态势得分提升 60.4%，且无需开发任何新模板。这些基于单一组织内源生态的发现为未来面向企业供应链安全的自动化、上下文感知推荐系统提供了数据驱动的基础；所观察到的技术债分布与优化差距能否推广到其他企业，仍是未来多组织研究的开放问题。","tl":"企业内 1.1 万 Dockerfile 实测：照搬内部最优实现即可提升 60% 安全分。","au":["Youfei Huang","Zhong Li","Minxue Pan","Xuandong Li"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study"],"kw":["Dockerfile","security misconfiguration","inner source","technical debt","container supply chain"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/217/x"},{"id":"p01237","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ArkEval: Benchmarking and Evaluating Automated Code Repair for ArkTS","tz":"ArkEval：面向 ArkTS 自动代码修复的基准与评测","a":"Iterative repair loops have become a core design pattern in LLM-based software engineering systems. These workflows repeatedly generate, validate, and repair artifacts using feedback such as compiler errors or test failures. Despite their widespread use, the impact of repair-loop iteration limits remains poorly understood, as most prior work adopts fixed, often arbitrary, repair budgets. We study repair-loop effectiveness across multiple software engineering tasks, including code generation, test generation, and code translation. Across several representative workflows, datasets, and contemporary low-cost LLMs, we observe a consistent pattern of diminishing returns: the first three to four repair iterations account for most achievable gains, while later iterations contribute only marginal improvements. We further find that repair behavior is influenced more strongly by workflow orchestration and feedback design than by the underlying model itself. These results suggest that repair budgets should be treated as an explicit experimental variable, as they directly affect evaluation outcomes, computational cost, runtime, and reproducibility in LLM-based software engineering research.","az":"迭代修复循环已成为基于 LLM 的软件工程系统的核心设计模式。这类工作流利用编译错误或测试失败等反馈，反复生成、验证并修复制品。尽管被广泛使用，修复循环迭代上限的影响仍缺乏理解，因为以往工作大多采用固定且往往武断的修复预算。我们在多项软件工程任务上研究修复循环的有效性，包括代码生成、测试生成和代码翻译。在若干具代表性的工作流、数据集和当代低成本 LLM 上，我们观察到一致的收益递减模式：前三到四次修复迭代贡献了大部分可获得的增益，而后续迭代仅带来边际改进。我们进一步发现，修复行为受工作流编排与反馈设计的影响远大于底层模型本身。这些结果表明，修复预算应被当作一个显式的实验变量，因为它直接影响基于 LLM 的软件工程研究中的评测结果、计算成本、运行时间与可复现性。","tl":"实证表明修复循环三四轮后收益递减，预算应作显式实验变量。","au":["bang xie","Senjian Zhang","Zhiyuan Peng","Wei Chen","Xin Yin","Chenhao Ying","Yuan Luo"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["repair loop","iteration budget","diminishing returns","workflow orchestration","reproducibility"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/218/x"},{"id":"p01238","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Vibe to Spec: An Empirical Study to Demystify Specifications in Code Generation","tz":"从氛围编程到规约：揭示代码生成中规约作用的实证研究","a":"Repository-level code translation is critical for modernizing legacy systems, yet existing approaches based on large language models (LLMs) operate at the file level and fail to scale to codebases with complex inter-file dependencies. This limitation is evident in our industrial setting, where we aim to migrate a production repository (STAR) from Java to Kotlin, but file-level approaches produce fragmented results and fail to achieve end-to-end correctness. In this paper, we show that the primary cause of failure at the repository level is dependency inconsistency. Through an empirical study on open-source and industrial systems, we find that most errors arise from unresolved cross-file dependencies that cannot be effectively addressed by iterative feedback alone. We propose a dependency-aware incremental migration framework that elevates the unit of translation from individual files to dependency-consistent batches. Our approach constructs a dependency graph, groups interdependent files, and performs batched translation with iterative compile- and test-driven validation. We evaluate our method on a 51K line of code (LOC) industrial system and multiple repositories across interoperable language pairs (Java-Kotlin, Java-Scala, and C#-F#). On the STAR repository, file-level approaches achieve 38.16% compilation and 9.39% test success, whereas our approach achieves 100% compilation and test success across the evaluated settings, converging within a small number of iterations. These results show that dependency-aware batching improves scalability and reliability in repository-level code translation.","az":"仓库级代码翻译对于遗留系统现代化至关重要，然而现有基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法工作在文件级别，无法扩展到具有复杂跨文件依赖的代码库。这一局限在我们的工业场景中十分明显：我们希望把一个生产仓库（STAR）从 Java 迁移到 Kotlin，但文件级方法产生了割裂的结果，无法达成端到端正确性。本文表明，仓库级失败的主要原因是依赖不一致。通过对开源与工业系统的实证研究，我们发现大多数错误源于未解决的跨文件依赖，仅靠迭代反馈难以有效处理。我们提出一个依赖感知的增量迁移框架，把翻译单元从单个文件提升为依赖一致的批次。我们的方法构建依赖图，将相互依赖的文件分组，并以批为单位进行翻译，同时进行迭代的编译与测试驱动验证。我们在一个 51K 行代码（LOC）的工业系统以及多个可互操作语言对（Java-Kotlin、Java-Scala、C#-F#）的仓库上评估该方法。在 STAR 仓库上，文件级方法仅达到 38.16% 的编译通过率和 9.39% 的测试通过率，而我们的方法在所评估的设置中达到 100% 的编译与测试通过率，并在少量迭代内收敛。这些结果表明，依赖感知的批处理提升了仓库级代码翻译的可扩展性与可靠性。","tl":"按依赖图成批翻译，让仓库级 Java→Kotlin 迁移达到 100% 通过。","au":["Ruirui He","Hanqing Lu","Lezhi Ma","Kai Ye","Qiong Wu","Shangqing Liu","Lei Bu","Xuandong Li"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["repository-level code translation","dependency graph","Java to Kotlin","legacy modernization","incremental migration"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/219/x"},{"id":"p01239","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Instruction Alignment for Binary Code Representation Learning","tz":"面向二进制代码表示学习的指令对齐","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench's macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施大多用 C 编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全，研究者正在探索把 C 自动翻译为 Rust 等更安全的语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不仅仅由 C 代码构成，还经常使用称为宏的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。最新技术通过先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译来回避宏的翻译。但这种做法产生的译码与原始 C 代码差异很大，因为预处理会把所有宏定义内联展开。为在翻译后的代码中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并将其提炼为首个形式化定义的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们引入首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机抽样的宏。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估大语言模型（LLM）在此前未被研究的宏翻译任务上的效果。LLM 比 MerC 多翻译了 22% 到 77% 的 MacroBench 用例，但其中有 8% 到 28% 的翻译是错误的，需要开发者额外验证；相比之下，MerC 只产出正确的翻译。我们的关键洞见是：先运行 MerC、再用 LLM 处理剩余部分，其收益大于单独使用任一技术。这种“搭档”方式的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时比 MerC 平均多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"首个形式化 C 宏到 Rust 翻译器 MerC 与 MacroBench，并与 LLM 互补。","au":["Huaijin Wang","Shuai Wang"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["C to Rust translation","macro translation","MacroBench","formal translator","memory safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/220/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11766"},{"id":"p01240","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Formula Completion Suggestions for Alloy Models with Selection Guidance","tz":"带选择引导的 Alloy 模型公式补全建议","tl":"（据标题推断）为 Alloy 规约提供带选择引导的公式自动补全。","au":["Mohammad Nurullah Patwary","Allison Sullivan"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Alloy","formal specification","formula completion","modeling assistance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/221/x"},{"id":"p01241","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"COBug: A Bug Localization Pipeline for COBOL: Does It Work? An Exploratory Study","tz":"COBug：面向 COBOL 的缺陷定位流水线——它有效吗？一项探索性研究","tl":"（据标题推断）首次检验缺陷定位流水线在 COBOL 上是否奏效。","au":["Kavyasri Gajula","Phanindra Kodela","Sridhar Chimalakonda"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["low-resource-or-non-english","empirical-study"],"kw":["bug localization","COBOL","legacy system","exploratory study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/222/x"},{"id":"p01242","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Accurate and Low-Cost Residual Risk Assessment via Sampled Profiling and Structure-Aware Coverage Amplification","tz":"基于采样剖析与结构感知覆盖放大的准确低成本剩余风险评估","a":"Several experience reports illustrate that mutation testing is capable of supporting a shift-left testing strategy, especially in industries where late bug discovery incurs very high costs and risks. In the context of cyber-physical systems, a shift left implies that engineers need to test the design models used to simulate, prototype, and analyse the feasibility of the system under design. In this paper, we analyse the challenges we encountered and the lessons we learned when incorporating mutation testing in the context of DUCO, a company producing ventilation systems for buildings. The engineers within DUCO have years of experience with model-based engineering centered around Simulink and StateFlow, including unit tests for their models. During a pilot project with our tool prototype MUT4SLX we learned that equivalent mutants, requirement traceability, and mutation testing for Stateflow represent particular challenges not yet reported in the academic literature.","az":"多份经验报告表明，变异测试能够支撑测试左移策略，尤其是在缺陷发现过晚会带来极高成本与风险的行业中。在信息物理系统的语境下，测试左移意味着工程师需要测试那些用于仿真、原型化和分析待设计系统可行性的设计模型。本文分析了我们在 DUCO（一家生产楼宇通风系统的公司）环境中引入变异测试时遇到的挑战与获得的经验教训。DUCO 的工程师在以 Simulink 和 StateFlow 为核心的基于模型的工程方面拥有多年经验，其中包括针对模型的单元测试。在与我们的工具原型 MUT4SLX 开展的试点项目中，我们发现等价变异体、需求可追踪性以及面向 Stateflow 的变异测试构成了学术文献尚未报道的特殊挑战。","tl":"以采样剖析与结构感知覆盖放大低成本估算剩余风险。","au":["Seongmin Lee","Işıl Özgü","Marcel Böhme","Miryung Kim"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["residual risk","sampled profiling","coverage amplification","mutation testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/223/x"},{"id":"p01243","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"SPSYN: Synthesizing DeFi Price-Manipulation Exploits via Semantic Recovery and State-Guided Search","tz":"SPSYN：通过语义恢复与状态引导搜索合成 DeFi 价格操纵攻击","tl":"（据标题推断）用语义恢复加状态引导搜索自动合成价格操纵攻击。","au":["Bosi Zhang","Ningyu He","Guangdong Bai","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DeFi","price manipulation","exploit synthesis","semantic recovery","state-guided search"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/224/x"},{"id":"p01244","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"To Think or Not to Think: Evaluating LLM Reasoning and Agents in Vulnerability Detection","tz":"思考还是不思考：评测 LLM 推理与智能体在漏洞检测中的表现","a":"GraphQL APIs power production systems across financial services, e-commerce, and social platforms, yet their most critical access-control vulnerabilities--Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR), Use-After-Free (UAF), and state-dependent injection--routinely escape automated security testing. Industry-standard scanners (ZAP) and the leading research fuzzer (EvoMaster) test operations in isolation and cannot compose the multi-step sequences these flaws require. We present GraphQLer, an open-source automated security testing framework built for production GraphQL APIs. GraphQLer constructs a typed dependency graph from live schema introspection and synthesizes vulnerability chains--ordered operation sequences targeting specific flaw classes. Three strategies cover the critical attack surface: topological SCC-traversal for general reachability, cross-user IDOR replay for broken access control, and CREATE -> DELETE -> READ synthesis for UAF. On a production financial API (FinServ), GraphQLer identified eight potential vulnerabilities--including denial-of-service vectors that exposed stack traces and sensitive implementation details--without prior documentation or authentication credentials. On a self-hosted Saleor instance pinned to the CVE-2022-39275 commit, GraphQLer reproduced all four broken-access-control mutations cited in the security advisory. On the 11 public APIs of the coverage set, GraphQLer achieves 85.52% mean PositiveCoverage versus 29.29% (EvoMaster) and 21.80% (ZAP); across the 21 evaluated APIs it detects all 5 confirmed IDOR endpoints, UAF behavior on two controlled schemas, and confirms XSS and SQLi on DVGA (an independent third-party oracle)--while all baselines detect zero chain-based vulnerabilities.","az":"GraphQL API 支撑着金融服务、电子商务和社交平台的生产系统，然而其最关键的访问控制漏洞——不安全的直接对象引用（IDOR）、释放后使用（UAF）以及依赖状态的注入——常常逃过自动化安全测试。业界标准扫描器（ZAP）和领先的研究型模糊测试工具（EvoMaster）孤立地测试各个操作，无法组合出这些缺陷所需的多步序列。我们提出 GraphQLer，一个面向生产级 GraphQL API 的开源自动化安全测试框架。GraphQLer 通过实时 schema 内省构建带类型的依赖图，并合成漏洞链——针对特定缺陷类别的有序操作序列。三种策略覆盖关键攻击面：用于一般可达性的拓扑 SCC 遍历、用于失效访问控制的跨用户 IDOR 重放，以及用于 UAF 的 CREATE -> DELETE -> READ 合成。在一个生产金融 API（FinServ）上，GraphQLer 在没有任何事先文档或认证凭据的情况下识别出八个潜在漏洞，其中包括暴露堆栈跟踪和敏感实现细节的拒绝服务向量。在固定到 CVE-2022-39275 提交的自托管 Saleor 实例上，GraphQLer 复现了安全通告中提到的全部四个失效访问控制变更操作。在覆盖集的 11 个公开 API 上，GraphQLer 的平均 PositiveCoverage 达到 85.52%，而 EvoMaster 为 29.29%、ZAP 为 21.80%；在全部 21 个被评估的 API 上，它检出了全部 5 个确认的 IDOR 端点、两个受控 schema 上的 UAF 行为，并在 DVGA（一个独立第三方预言）上确认了 XSS 与 SQL 注入——而所有基线检出的基于链的漏洞数量均为零。","tl":"用类型依赖图合成多步漏洞链，测出 GraphQL 访问控制缺陷。","au":["Hua Beng Tan","Ratnadira Widyasari","Merve Astekin","Arda Goknil","Hasan Sozer","Yan Naing Tun","Erik Johannes Husom","Lwin Khin Shar","Lingxiao Jiang"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["GraphQL security testing","IDOR","dependency graph","vulnerability chain","API fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/225/x"},{"id":"p01245","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Demystifying Solana Bots: From GitHub Blueprints to On-Chain Fingerprints","tz":"揭秘 Solana 机器人：从 GitHub 蓝图到链上指纹","a":"Solana is an emerging blockchain platform designed for high throughput and low transaction fees, making it inexpensive to submit transactions at scale and, consequently, increasing exposure to bot spamming and related financial exploitation. Solana bots are typically off-chain software systems that operate in a competitive on-chain execution environment by constructing and submitting transactions, and the bot-related transactions on the decentralized exchanges exceed 250 million dollars in daily trading volume in January 2026. Prior studies on Solana have examined system performance, smart-contract security, and specific on-chain phenomena. However, we still lack a systematic understanding of what Solana bots implement in practice and how these implementations manifest as observable on-chain execution fingerprints. To address this gap, we performed a large-scale empirical study of Solana bots from two complementary views: (i) 586 bot repositories collected from GitHub, and (ii) 200 bot addresses on Solana, with over 44 million on-chain transactions. Our study derives an implementation-grounded taxonomy of Solana bots comprising 15 categories grouped into five domains (e.g., Trading Operations, MEV, and On-chain Analytics), identifies a largely shared five-stage operational pipeline manifested in bot implementations, and uncovers systematic variation in on-chain trading behaviors of Solana bots across diverse trading platforms and assets. Based on our findings, we highlight future research directions, and provide recommendations for building and operating bots on the Solana blockchain.","az":"Solana 是一个面向高吞吐与低交易费设计的新兴区块链平台，这使得大规模提交交易成本低廉，也因此更易受到机器人刷量及相关金融剥削的影响。Solana 机器人通常是链下软件系统，通过构造并提交交易在竞争激烈的链上执行环境中运作；2026 年 1 月，去中心化交易所上与机器人相关的交易日成交量超过 2.5 亿美元。以往关于 Solana 的研究考察过系统性能、智能合约安全以及特定链上现象。然而，我们仍然缺乏对 Solana 机器人在实践中究竟实现了什么、以及这些实现如何表现为可观测的链上执行指纹的系统性理解。为填补这一空白，我们从两个互补视角开展了对 Solana 机器人的大规模实证研究：(i) 从 GitHub 收集的 586 个机器人仓库；(ii) Solana 上的 200 个机器人地址，涉及超过 4,400 万笔链上交易。我们的研究得出了一个基于实现的 Solana 机器人分类法，包含归入五个领域（如交易操作、MEV 和链上分析）的 15 个类别，识别出机器人实现中普遍共享的五阶段运作流水线，并揭示了 Solana 机器人在不同交易平台与资产上的链上交易行为存在系统性差异。基于这些发现，我们指出了未来的研究方向，并为在 Solana 区块链上构建与运营机器人提供了建议。","tl":"首次对 Solana 机器人做代码与链上双视角的分类与指纹刻画。","au":["Xiaoye Zheng","Yujing Chen","Minghao Wu","David Lo","Difan Xie","Daoyuan Wu","Xiaohu Yang","Zhiyuan Wan"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["Solana","trading bots","MEV","on-chain fingerprint","empirical taxonomy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/226/x"},{"id":"p01246","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"CLEAR: Causal Context-Based Agentic Reasoning for Vulnerability Detection","tz":"CLEAR：面向漏洞检测的因果上下文智能体推理","a":"GraphQL APIs power production systems across financial services, e-commerce, and social platforms, yet their most critical access-control vulnerabilities--Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR), Use-After-Free (UAF), and state-dependent injection--routinely escape automated security testing. Industry-standard scanners (ZAP) and the leading research fuzzer (EvoMaster) test operations in isolation and cannot compose the multi-step sequences these flaws require. We present GraphQLer, an open-source automated security testing framework built for production GraphQL APIs. GraphQLer constructs a typed dependency graph from live schema introspection and synthesizes vulnerability chains--ordered operation sequences targeting specific flaw classes. Three strategies cover the critical attack surface: topological SCC-traversal for general reachability, cross-user IDOR replay for broken access control, and CREATE -> DELETE -> READ synthesis for UAF. On a production financial API (FinServ), GraphQLer identified eight potential vulnerabilities--including denial-of-service vectors that exposed stack traces and sensitive implementation details--without prior documentation or authentication credentials. On a self-hosted Saleor instance pinned to the CVE-2022-39275 commit, GraphQLer reproduced all four broken-access-control mutations cited in the security advisory. On the 11 public APIs of the coverage set, GraphQLer achieves 85.52% mean PositiveCoverage versus 29.29% (EvoMaster) and 21.80% (ZAP); across the 21 evaluated APIs it detects all 5 confirmed IDOR endpoints, UAF behavior on two controlled schemas, and confirms XSS and SQLi on DVGA (an independent third-party oracle)--while all baselines detect zero chain-based vulnerabilities.","az":"GraphQL API 支撑着金融服务、电子商务和社交平台的生产系统，然而其最关键的访问控制漏洞——不安全的直接对象引用（IDOR）、释放后使用（UAF）以及依赖状态的注入——常常逃过自动化安全测试。业界标准扫描器（ZAP）和领先的研究型模糊测试工具（EvoMaster）孤立地测试各个操作，无法组合出这些缺陷所需的多步序列。我们提出 GraphQLer，一个面向生产级 GraphQL API 的开源自动化安全测试框架。GraphQLer 通过实时 schema 内省构建带类型的依赖图，并合成漏洞链——针对特定缺陷类别的有序操作序列。三种策略覆盖关键攻击面：用于一般可达性的拓扑 SCC 遍历、用于失效访问控制的跨用户 IDOR 重放，以及用于 UAF 的 CREATE -> DELETE -> READ 合成。在一个生产金融 API（FinServ）上，GraphQLer 在没有任何事先文档或认证凭据的情况下识别出八个潜在漏洞，其中包括暴露堆栈跟踪和敏感实现细节的拒绝服务向量。在固定到 CVE-2022-39275 提交的自托管 Saleor 实例上，GraphQLer 复现了安全通告中提到的全部四个失效访问控制变更操作。在覆盖集的 11 个公开 API 上，GraphQLer 的平均 PositiveCoverage 达到 85.52%，而 EvoMaster 为 29.29%、ZAP 为 21.80%；在全部 21 个被评估的 API 上，它检出了全部 5 个确认的 IDOR 端点、两个受控 schema 上的 UAF 行为，并在 DVGA（一个独立第三方预言）上确认了 XSS 与 SQL 注入——而所有基线检出的基于链的漏洞数量均为零。","tl":"把访问控制漏洞检测转为有序操作链合成，基线全部为零检出。","au":["Sungju Yun","Sijune hwang","Yeonjoon Lee","Kyungtae Kang","Sungbin Park"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["GraphQL","access control vulnerability","operation sequence synthesis","security testing","UAF"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/227/x"},{"id":"p01247","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Large Language Model Enabled Symbolic Execution for Automated Functional Analysis","tz":"大语言模型赋能的符号执行与自动功能分析","tl":"（据标题推断）让 LLM 辅助符号执行完成程序功能语义分析。","au":["Meixi Liu","Zhenbang Chen","Xudong Wang","Ziran He","Jiachen Gu","Minghui Chen","Lei Wang","Wei Dong"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic execution","LLM-augmented analysis","functional analysis","program semantics"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/228/x"},{"id":"p01248","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Structure-Guided Semantic Deobfuscation of Android Identifiers","tz":"结构引导的 Android 标识符语义反混淆","a":"The growing diversity of code clone types, from syntactic copies to cross-language semantic clones to AI-generated duplicates, has created a fragmentation crisis in clone detection. Current deep learning detectors are domain specialists that degrade significantly outside their training distribution, with F1 drops exceeding 70% across domains. Deploying multiple specialized models is impractical, yet training a single cross-domain detector requires simultaneous access to all training data. To address this, we investigate model merging, a family of post-hoc techniques that operate solely on trained checkpoints. We evaluate parameter merging with five task-vector methods, architecture merging via greedy layer stitching, and cross-tokenizer alignment across four code models, three benchmarks, and twelve configurations. Same-base TIES merging creates effective cross-domain detectors, validated across two model families and three random seeds, reaching 0.865 combined F1 on UniXcoder, 93% of multi-task performance without any training data at the merging step. WUDI achieves the highest in-distribution combined F1 at 0.899, but TIES generalizes better to unseen AI-generated clones, making it our recommended method. Cross-base merging yields only marginal and high-variance gains across all five methods, indicating that task vector compatibility through a shared pre-trained base is the binding factor for effective merging. Merged detectors also outperform zero-shot code LLMs on GPTCloneBench at lower inference cost and generalize up to 4x better than multi-task training to unseen AI-generated clones, suggesting a trade-off between in-domain performance and OOD robustness. This work provides one of the first systematic empirical studies of model merging for software engineering and a practical recipe for building cross-domain clone detectors.","az":"代码克隆类型日益多样，从语法层面的拷贝到跨语言的语义克隆，再到 AI 生成的重复代码，已在克隆检测领域造成了碎片化危机。当前的深度学习检测器都是领域专才，一旦离开训练分布性能便显著下降，跨领域 F1 降幅超过 70%。部署多个专用模型并不现实，而训练单一跨领域检测器又要求同时获得全部训练数据。为此，我们研究模型合并——一类仅在训练好的检查点上操作的事后技术。我们评估了使用五种任务向量方法的参数合并、通过贪心层拼接的架构合并，以及跨分词器对齐，覆盖四个代码模型、三个基准和十二种配置。同基座的 TIES 合并能够产生有效的跨领域检测器，并在两个模型家族与三个随机种子上得到验证，在 UniXcoder 上达到 0.865 的综合 F1，即在合并阶段不使用任何训练数据的情况下达到多任务性能的 93%。WUDI 取得了最高的分布内综合 F1（0.899），但 TIES 对未见过的 AI 生成克隆泛化更好，因此成为我们推荐的方法。跨基座合并在全部五种方法上仅带来边际且方差很大的收益，说明通过共享预训练基座获得的任务向量兼容性是有效合并的决定性因素。合并后的检测器在 GPTCloneBench 上也以更低的推理成本超过零样本代码 LLM，并且在未见过的 AI 生成克隆上比多任务训练的泛化能力最高好 4 倍，提示分布内性能与分布外鲁棒性之间存在权衡。本工作提供了面向软件工程的模型合并的首批系统性实证研究之一，以及构建跨领域克隆检测器的实用方案。","tl":"无需训练数据，模型合并即可得到跨领域克隆检测器。","au":["Mingyang Chen","Zhentao Xie","Yaqi Gao","Shuang Li","Wenrui Diao"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["model merging","clone detection","task vectors","TIES","cross-domain generalization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/229/x"},{"id":"p01249","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Orbis: Guiding Symbolic Execution Techniques to Maximize Option-Related Branch Coverage","tz":"Orbis：引导符号执行技术最大化选项相关分支覆盖","a":"We present Orbis, a complementary approach that guides symbolic execution techniques toward maximizing option-related branch (OB) coverage. Although state-of-the-art symbolic execution techniques have substantially improved code coverage and bug detection, existing techniques often fail to exercise core program functionalities, which are frequently exposed as program options. To quantify this limitation, we evaluate how effectively current techniques cover option-related branches and find that they reach only 8.0% of the targeted OBs, which are accessible only through specific options. Orbis overcomes this challenge by systematically guiding symbolic execution to improve OB coverage. For a given program, Orbis automatically identifies all defined options and determines their associated branches by analyzing dynamic execution traces. It then iteratively constructs target option arguments by stochastically combining identified options according to their estimated potential, directs symbolic execution to explore states influenced by these arguments, and refines their potential while simultaneously reducing SMT-solver invocations using data accumulated during symbolic execution. Experimental results on 15 open-source C programs show that integrating Orbis with four independent state-of-the-art techniques significantly increases OB coverage to 323.0%, boosts total branch coverage by 112.1%, and detects five additional unique bugs on average compared to the standalone techniques.","az":"我们提出 Orbis，一种互补的方法，用于引导符号执行技术最大化与选项相关的分支（OB）覆盖。尽管最先进的符号执行技术已显著提升了代码覆盖率和缺陷检测能力，现有技术往往无法触及核心程序功能，而这些功能常常以程序选项的形式暴露。为量化这一局限，我们评估了当前技术覆盖选项相关分支的效果，发现它们仅触及目标 OB 的 8.0%，这些分支只能通过特定选项到达。Orbis 通过系统性地引导符号执行来克服该挑战，从而提升 OB 覆盖率。对于给定程序，Orbis 自动识别所有已定义的选项，并通过分析动态执行轨迹确定其关联分支；随后根据估计的潜力随机组合已识别的选项，迭代构造目标选项参数，引导符号执行探索受这些参数影响的状态，并利用符号执行期间积累的数据不断修正其潜力估计，同时减少 SMT 求解器的调用次数。在 15 个开源 C 程序上的实验结果表明，将 Orbis 与四种独立的最先进技术集成后，OB 覆盖率显著提升至 323.0%，总分支覆盖率提升 112.1%，并且平均比原独立技术多检出五个独特缺陷。","tl":"面向程序选项引导符号执行，OB 覆盖率提升三倍多。","au":["Minjong Kim","Sungjae Hwang","Sooyoung Cha"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic execution","option-related branch coverage","SMT solver invocations","branch coverage","bug detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/230/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837526"},{"id":"p01250","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MultiFixer: A Coordinator-Proposer Based Multi-agent Framework for Fixing Multi-hunk Bugs","tz":"MultiFixer：基于协调者-提议者的多智能体多 hunk 缺陷修复框架","a":"Automated Program Repair (APR) has benefited greatly from Large Language Models (LLMs), but existing LLM-based APR methods still struggle with multi-hunk bugs that require coordinated changes across multiple locations. These bugs demand repository-level context understanding, repair-order scheduling, and effective hunk-level patch generation and selection. To address these challenges, we propose MultiFixer, a novel Coordinator-Proposer based multi-agent framework for multi-hunk repair. MultiFixer performs tool-augmented bug analysis, constructs fine-grained repair context, iteratively generates patches through a Coordinator-Proposer architecture, and applies two-stage patch refinement for syntactic and semantic correctness. We evaluate MultiFixer on 835 bugs from Defects4J and three vulnerability benchmarks. On Defects4J, MultiFixer fixes 326 bugs, including 62 multi-method and 27 multi-file bugs, and outperforms prior APR baselines in the reported comparisons with the same base model. Moreover, MultiFixer also fixes 46 multi-hunk bugs among 95 unique fixes. When combined with Claude-3.5-Sonnet, MultiFixer repairs 420 bugs, establishing a new state of the art on Defects4J. On VUL4J, MultiFixer repairs 24 real-world vulnerabilities, including 5 multi-hunk cases. On the multi-hunk subsets of SEC-bench and PatchEval, MultiFixer fixes 11 and 19 vulnerabilities, respectively, outperforming all compared baselines under GPT-3.5. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of MultiFixer for multi-hunk repair.","az":"自动程序修复（APR）从大语言模型（LLM）中获益良多，但现有基于 LLM 的 APR 方法在处理需要跨多个位置协同修改的多 hunk 缺陷时仍然吃力。这类缺陷要求仓库级上下文理解、修复顺序调度，以及有效的 hunk 级补丁生成与选择。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 MultiFixer，一个面向多 hunk 修复的新颖的协调者-提议者（Coordinator-Proposer）多智能体框架。MultiFixer 进行工具增强的缺陷分析，构建细粒度修复上下文，通过协调者-提议者架构迭代生成补丁，并施加两阶段补丁精化以保证语法与语义正确性。我们在来自 Defects4J 和三个漏洞基准的 835 个缺陷上评估 MultiFixer。在 Defects4J 上，MultiFixer 修复了 326 个缺陷，其中包括 62 个跨方法缺陷和 27 个跨文件缺陷，在使用相同基座模型的对比中优于先前的 APR 基线。此外，MultiFixer 在 95 个独有修复中还修复了 46 个多 hunk 缺陷。当与 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 结合时，MultiFixer 修复了 420 个缺陷，在 Defects4J 上创造了新的最先进水平。在 VUL4J 上，MultiFixer 修复了 24 个真实世界漏洞，其中包括 5 个多 hunk 案例。在 SEC-bench 与 PatchEval 的多 hunk 子集上，MultiFixer 分别修复了 11 个和 19 个漏洞，在 GPT-3.5 下优于所有对比基线。这些结果证明了 MultiFixer 在多 hunk 修复上的有效性。","tl":"协调者-提议者多智能体协同定位与调度，攻克多 hunk 缺陷修复。","au":["hai chuan hu","Chunrong Fang","ye shang","Jiawei Liu","Weifeng Sun","Guoqing Xie","Chenxing Zhong","Quanjun Zhang"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["multi-hunk repair","coordinator-proposer","multi-agent APR","Defects4J","patch refinement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/231/x"},{"id":"p01251","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Mining Tactics for Automated Theorem Proving","tz":"面向自动定理证明的策略挖掘","a":"Automated theorem proving is essential for the formal verification of safety-critical systems. As the corpus of formal proofs grows, a natural paradigm is to learn from existing proofs. However, current learning-based approaches predominantly train Large Language Models (LLMs) as end-to-end provers, which yields resource-intensive, opaque systems. Conversely, while traditional symbolic provers are computationally efficient, how to automatically improve these solvers from data remains an open challenge. This paper bridges this gap by proposing LLM2Ltac, a novel approach that leverages the reasoning power of LLMs not as end-to-end provers, but as intelligent synthesizers to mine purely symbolic tactics from data. Given a corpus of formal proofs, LLM2Ltac asks an LLM to identify latent proof strategies and formalize them into reusable tactics. These tactics are verified for validity and generalizability, and finally integrated into symbolic provers to enhance their automated proving capabilities without the runtime cost of LLMs. We implement LLM2Ltac on Rocq 8.20.0 and mine tactics from 11,725 theorems in the standard library. We evaluate our approach on 6,199 theorems from four large real-world verification projects, namely, compcert, Coq-Art, Ext-Lib, and VFA. Results show that the mined tactics improve CoqHammer to prove 23.87% more theorems, and when integrating the improved CoqHammer with Claude Code, the overall proved theorems increases by 9.90%, indicating the effectiveness of LLM2Ltac.","az":"自动定理证明对于安全攸关系统的形式化验证至关重要。随着形式化证明语料的不断增长，一个自然的范式是从已有证明中学习。然而，当前基于学习的方法主要把大语言模型（LLM）训练成端到端的证明器，这带来了资源消耗大、不透明的系统。反过来，传统符号证明器虽然计算效率高，但如何从数据中自动改进这些求解器仍是一个开放挑战。本文提出 LLM2Ltac 来弥合这一鸿沟：它并不把 LLM 当作端到端证明器，而是利用其推理能力作为智能合成器，从数据中挖掘纯符号的证明策略（tactics）。给定一个形式化证明语料库，LLM2Ltac 让 LLM 识别潜在的证明策略并将其形式化为可复用的 tactic。这些 tactic 会经过有效性与泛化性验证，最终集成进符号证明器，从而在不承担 LLM 运行时开销的前提下增强其自动证明能力。我们在 Rocq 8.20.0 上实现了 LLM2Ltac，并从标准库的 11,725 条定理中挖掘 tactic。我们在 compcert、Coq-Art、Ext-Lib 和 VFA 四个大型真实验证项目的 6,199 条定理上进行评估。结果表明，挖掘得到的 tactic 使 CoqHammer 多证明 23.87% 的定理；将改进后的 CoqHammer 与 Claude Code 集成后，总体被证明的定理数量提升 9.90%，说明 LLM2Ltac 是有效的。","tl":"用 LLM 从证明语料挖掘可复用符号 tactic 增强符号证明器。","au":["Jian Fang","Yixun Yao","Yingfei Xiong"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated theorem proving","tactic mining","Rocq/Coq","CoqHammer","symbolic prover"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/232/x"},{"id":"p01252","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Leveraging System-Level Observations to Inform Bayesian Learning of Model Parameters for Quantitative Verification","tz":"利用系统级观测指导定量验证中模型参数的贝叶斯学习","a":"Rust's ownership type system prevents memory errors in safe code, but certain desirable properties remain orthogonal to compilation: the soundness of unsafe operations (e.g., raw pointer dereferences), functional correctness, and absence of runtime panics. We present Kani, an open-source model checker for Rust that pushes bounded model checking beyond bug-finding to provide correctness guarantees for these properties. Kani compiles proof harnesses from Rust's Mid-level Intermediate Representation (MIR) into CBMC's bit-precise verification engine, automatically checking a comprehensive set of safety properties with no user annotation. To extend verification from bounded to unbounded, Kani provides a specification language comprising function contracts, loop contracts, quantifiers, and function stubbing. We demonstrate feasibility through case studies on industrial Rust projects, where contracts upgraded verification from panic-freedom to functional correctness, uncovering six previously unknown bugs. Kani operates at scale in production CI, with over 16,000 harnesses verified per code change in the Rust standard library verification campaign.","az":"Rust 的所有权类型系统能够在安全代码中防止内存错误，但某些期望的性质与编译过程是正交的：unsafe 操作（例如裸指针解引用）的可靠性、功能正确性以及运行时 panic 的缺失。我们提出 Kani，一个面向 Rust 的开源模型检验器，它把有界模型检验从单纯的找缺陷推进到为上述性质提供正确性保证。Kani 将证明 harness 从 Rust 的中层中间表示（MIR）编译到 CBMC 的位精确验证引擎，自动检查一整套安全性质且无需用户标注。为了把验证从有界扩展到无界，Kani 提供了一种规约语言，包含函数契约、循环契约、量词和函数桩（stubbing）。我们通过工业级 Rust 项目的案例研究证明了其可行性：契约把验证从无 panic 提升到功能正确性，并发现了六个此前未知的缺陷。Kani 已在生产环境的 CI 中规模化运行，在 Rust 标准库验证行动中每次代码变更会验证超过 16,000 个 harness。","tl":"Kani 用契约把 Rust 有界模型检验扩展到无界功能正确性验证。","au":["Simos Gerasimou","Xingyu Zhao"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Rust verification","bounded model checking","Kani","function contracts","CBMC"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/233/x"},{"id":"p01253","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Generating Loop Invariants for Deductive Verification Using Iterator Profiles","tz":"利用迭代器画像为演绎验证生成循环不变式","tl":"（据标题推断）用迭代器画像自动推导演绎验证所需循环不变式。","au":["Keisuke Nishimura","Jean-Pierre Lozi","Julia Lawall"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["loop invariant","deductive verification","iterator profile","program verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/234/x"},{"id":"p01254","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"RustGTC: Constraint-Guided Test Generation for Rust APIs via Comment Analysis and Code Context","tz":"RustGTC：结合注释分析与代码上下文的 Rust API 约束引导测试生成","tl":"（据标题推断）从注释中抽取约束来引导 Rust API 测试生成。","au":["Yichi Zhang","Jinhao Huang","Yang Feng"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Rust API testing","test generation","comment analysis","constraint-guided","code context"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/235/x"},{"id":"p01255","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"HyBinMAS: LLM-Powered Hybrid Analysis for Function Name Recovery of Stripped Binaries","tz":"HyBinMAS：由 LLM 驱动的混合分析用于剥离符号二进制的函数名恢复","a":"Binary decompilation plays a vital role in various cybersecurity and software engineering tasks. Recently, end-to-end decompilation methods powered by large language models (LLMs) have attracted increasing attention for their ability to generate highly readable source code with minimal human intervention. However, existing LLM-based methods still struggle with reconstructing program structure and logic, achieving accurate data recovery, ensuring data security and privacy, and maintaining computational efficiency. To address these challenges, we propose the CodeInverter Suite, with three main pieces: (1) the CodeInverter Workflow (CIW) is a novel prompt engineering method that incorporates control flow graphs (CFG) and explicit data mappings to enhance structure reconstruction and data recovery during decompilation; (2) building upon CIW, we construct the CodeInverter Dataset (CID), a large-scale domain-specific dataset containing 8.69 million samples enriched with CFGs and data mapping information; (3) we develop CodeInverter Models (CIMs), two lightweight LLMs with 1.3B and 6.7B parameters, enabling efficient inference in privacy-sensitive and resource-constrained environments. Extensive experiments on two benchmark datasets demonstrate that CIW significantly enhances the decompilation performance of various LLMs, with average improvements of 13.07% in re-executability and 23.94% in re-compilability. For our proposed decompilation model, CIM-6.7B achieves state-of-the-art performance in terms of re-executability and readability, outperforming existing LLMs-even with over 100 times more parameters-by an average of 11.03% and 6.27%, respectively.","az":"二进制反编译在各类网络安全与软件工程任务中扮演着关键角色。近来，由大语言模型（LLM）驱动的端到端反编译方法因能在极少人工干预下生成可读性很高的源代码而受到越来越多关注。然而，现有基于 LLM 的方法在重建程序结构与逻辑、实现准确的数据恢复、保障数据安全与隐私以及维持计算效率方面仍然存在困难。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 CodeInverter 套件，包含三个主要部分：（1）CodeInverter 工作流（CIW）是一种新颖的提示工程方法，融合控制流图（CFG）与显式数据映射，以增强反编译过程中的结构重建与数据恢复；（2）在 CIW 基础上，我们构建了 CodeInverter 数据集（CID），这是一个大规模领域专用数据集，包含 869 万个样本，并富含 CFG 与数据映射信息；（3）我们开发了 CodeInverter 模型（CIMs），即两个分别为 1.3B 和 6.7B 参数的轻量级 LLM，可在隐私敏感和资源受限环境中高效推理。在两个基准数据集上的大量实验表明，CIW 显著提升了多种 LLM 的反编译性能，可重执行率平均提升 13.07%，可重编译率平均提升 23.94%。对于我们提出的反编译模型，CIM-6.7B 在可重执行性与可读性方面达到了最先进水平，平均分别超出现有 LLM（即便后者参数量多出 100 倍以上）11.03% 和 6.27%。","tl":"用 CFG 与数据映射提示加领域数据训练轻量反编译模型。","au":["Chenxi Wang","Lei Xu","Xincheng He","Gaozhan Yu","Ye Wang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","security"],"kw":["binary decompilation","control flow graph","function name recovery","code LLM","re-executability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/236/x"},{"id":"p01256","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Beyond Syntactic Differencing: Semantic-Aware Scheduling for Cross-Configuration Incremental Builds","tz":"超越语法差分：面向跨配置增量构建的语义感知调度","tl":"（据标题推断）用语义差分替代语法差分调度跨配置增量构建。","au":["Xiaolong Dai","Shanshan Li","Jun Lyu","Xintao Niu"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["incremental build","cross-configuration","semantic differencing","build scheduling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/237/x"},{"id":"p01257","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Probe to Generate: Program Variant-Guided Test Augmentation for Repository-Level Repair Benchmarks","tz":"探测以生成：面向仓库级修复基准的程序变体引导测试增强","a":"Test-based benchmarks such as SWE-bench have become a standard basis for evaluating automated issue resolution agents, deeming a patch correct if it passes a provided regression test suite. In practice, weak test suites can admit plausible but semantically incorrect patches, inflating reported agent performance. We present , a test augmentation framework that uses semantically modified program variants as behavioral probes to identify and close gaps in benchmark test suites. Variants of the reference patch that survive the original tests reveal under-constrained behaviors, which then guide targeted regression test generation. Each generated test is retained only if it passes on the reference patch, fails on at least one surviving variant, and remains robust under behavior-preserving transformations. On SWE-bench Verified, 77% of instances admit at least one surviving variant. generates 1,014 validated tests across 211 instances, increasing patch-region line and branch coverage by 10.8 and 9.5 percentage points. Re-evaluating the top-10 repair agents with the augmented suites reduces resolved rates by 4.2%-9.0%, showing that many previously accepted patches exploit benchmark test gaps rather than fully satisfying the intended repair semantics. These findings demonstrate that benchmark evaluation is not solely a patch-generation problem but also a test-strength problem.","az":"诸如 SWE-bench 之类基于测试的基准已成为评估自动 issue 求解智能体的标准依据：只要补丁通过给定的回归测试套件即被判定为正确。但在实践中，薄弱的测试套件会放行看似合理却语义错误的补丁，从而虚高地报告智能体性能。我们提出 \\tool，一个测试增强框架，它使用语义修改后的程序变体作为行为探针，识别并弥补基准测试套件中的缺口。参考补丁的变体若能通过原有测试，就暴露出约束不足的行为，这些行为随后指导有针对性的回归测试生成。每个生成的测试只有在参考补丁上通过、在至少一个存活变体上失败、且在保行为变换下依然稳健时才被保留。在 SWE-bench Verified 上，77% 的实例至少存在一个存活变体。\\tool 在 211 个实例上生成了 1,014 个经过验证的测试，使补丁区域的行覆盖率和分支覆盖率分别提升 10.8 和 9.5 个百分点。用增强后的套件重新评测排名前十的修复智能体，其解决率下降 4.2%–9.0%，说明许多此前被接受的补丁其实是利用了基准的测试缺口，而非真正满足预期的修复语义。这些发现表明基准评测不仅是补丁生成问题，也是测试强度问题。","tl":"用存活程序变体补强 SWE-bench 测试，揭示修复率被高估。","au":["Chenglin Li","Yisen Xu","Zehao Wang","Shin Hwei Tan","Tse-Hsun (Peter) Chen"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["benchmark-dataset","agentic","empirical-study"],"kw":["SWE-bench","test augmentation","program variants","patch correctness","benchmark validity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/238/x"},{"id":"p01258","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Safeguarding LLM Agents from Misalignment through Provenance Analysis","tz":"通过溯源分析保护 LLM 智能体免于目标偏离","a":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents increasingly operate across domains such as robotics, virtual assistants, and web automation. However, their stochastic decision-making introduces safety risks that are difficult to anticipate during execution. Existing runtime monitoring frameworks, such as AgentSpec, primarily rely on reactive safety rules that detect violations only when unsafe behavior is imminent or has already occurred, limiting their ability to handle long-horizon dependencies. We present ProbGuard, a proactive runtime monitoring framework for LLM agents that anticipates safety violations through probabilistic risk prediction. ProbGuard abstracts agent executions into symbolic states and learns a Discrete-Time Markov Chain (DTMC) from execution traces to model behavioral dynamics. At runtime, the monitor estimates the probability that execution will remain safe from the current state, and triggers an intervention when this probability falls below a user-defined threshold. To improve robustness, ProbGuard incorporates semantic validity constraints in the abstraction and admits a PAC-style analysis that characterizes the sample complexity required to certify the learned model under standard assumptions. We evaluate ProbGuard in two safety-critical domains: autonomous driving and embodied household agents. Across evaluated scenarios, ProbGuard consistently predicts traffic law violations and collisions in advance, with warnings up to 15.84 seconds at a threshold yielding no false alarms, and up to 38.66 seconds at stricter thresholds. In embodied agent tasks, ProbGuard's re-prompting intervention mode reduces unsafe behavior by 65.37% relative to the unmonitored baseline while retaining 80.4% of the baseline task completion; a stricter halting configuration reduces unsafe behavior by 93.60% at a larger cost in completion.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）智能体正越来越多地运行于机器人、虚拟助手和网页自动化等领域。然而，它们随机性的决策带来了在执行期难以预判的安全风险。现有的运行时监控框架（如 AgentSpec）主要依赖被动的安全规则，只有当不安全行为迫在眉睫或已经发生时才检测到违规，因而难以处理长程依赖。我们提出 ProbGuard，一个面向 LLM 智能体的主动式运行时监控框架，通过概率化风险预测来预判安全违规。ProbGuard 将智能体执行抽象为符号状态，并从执行轨迹中学习一个离散时间马尔可夫链（DTMC）来建模行为动态。在运行时，监控器估计从当前状态出发执行保持安全的概率，当该概率低于用户设定阈值时触发干预。为提升鲁棒性，ProbGuard 在抽象中加入语义有效性约束，并支持一种 PAC 风格的分析，用以刻画在标准假设下认证所学模型所需的样本复杂度。我们在两个安全攸关领域评估 ProbGuard：自动驾驶和具身家庭智能体。在所评估的各类场景中，ProbGuard 能持续提前预测交通法规违规与碰撞，在无误报的阈值下可提前 15.84 秒预警，在更严格的阈值下可提前 38.66 秒。在具身智能体任务中，ProbGuard 的重提示（re-prompting）干预模式相对于无监控基线将不安全行为减少 65.37%，同时保留基线 80.4% 的任务完成度；更严格的中止配置可将不安全行为减少 93.60%，但完成度代价更大。","tl":"用 DTMC 概率预测提前预警并干预智能体不安全行为。","au":["Yining She","Yiliang Liang","Eunsuk Kang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["agentic","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["LLM agent safety","runtime monitoring","Discrete-Time Markov Chain","probabilistic risk prediction","intervention"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/239/x"},{"id":"p01259","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PropGen: Automated Property Generation for Property-Based Testing of Mobile Apps","tz":"PropGen：面向移动应用属性测试的自动属性生成","a":"Simulation-based testing enables safe and repeatable evaluation of autonomous driving systems, but its effectiveness is limited by the gap between synthetic simulator outputs and real-world camera observations. To address this problem, we present Cam2Sim, a tool that transforms real-world driving recordings into playable CARLA simulation scenarios. Starting from camera images and poses, Cam2Sim reconstructs road geometry, ego trajectories, parked vehicles, and simulation assets, and augments the reconstructed environment with Gaussian Splatting to render camera observations that resemble the original recording. The framework supports ROS-based data extraction, parked-vehicle detection, OpenStreetMap-based map generation, CARLA scenario construction, Gaussian Splatting training, trajectory replay, and closed-loop execution with a system under test. We validate Cam2Sim on a real-world urban-driving scenario with a camera-based end-to-end driving model, comparing reconstruction quality, image-generation quality, and closed-loop behavior against both a simulation-only baseline and the real-world target. Results show that Gaussian-Splatting-based rendering reduces the visual gap with respect to standard simulator rendering and improves behavioral similarity to the real-world reference runs. The artifact is publicly available at https: //github.com/ast-fortiss-tum/cam2sim, and a screencast showing the tool is available at https://youtu.be/KmZ74l1__lI","az":"基于仿真的测试能够对自动驾驶系统进行安全且可重复的评估，但其有效性受限于合成仿真器输出与真实世界摄像头观测之间的差距。为解决该问题，我们提出 Cam2Sim，一个把真实驾驶录像转换为可运行的 CARLA 仿真场景的工具。Cam2Sim 从摄像头图像和位姿出发，重建道路几何、自车轨迹、停放车辆和仿真资产，并用高斯溅射（Gaussian Splatting）增强重建环境，以渲染出与原始录像相似的摄像头观测。该框架支持基于 ROS 的数据抽取、停放车辆检测、基于 OpenStreetMap 的地图生成、CARLA 场景构建、高斯溅射训练、轨迹回放，以及与被测系统的闭环执行。我们在一个真实城市驾驶场景上用基于摄像头的端到端驾驶模型验证 Cam2Sim，将重建质量、图像生成质量与闭环行为同仅用仿真的基线以及真实世界目标进行对比。结果表明，基于高斯溅射的渲染相比标准仿真器渲染缩小了视觉差距，并提升了与真实世界参考运行的行为相似度。制品已公开于 https://github.com/ast-fortiss-tum/cam2sim ，演示视频见 https://youtu.be/KmZ74l1__lI 。","tl":"用高斯溅射把真实驾驶录像转成高保真 CARLA 闭环场景。","au":["Yiheng Xiong","Shiwen Song","Bo Ma","Ting Su","Xiaofei Xie"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","multimodal"],"kw":["simulation-based testing","autonomous driving","CARLA","Gaussian Splatting","scenario reconstruction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/240/x"},{"id":"p01260","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"From Function to Repository: Towards Understanding and an Agentic Approach for Repo-Level Directed Input Generation","tz":"从函数到仓库：理解仓库级定向输入生成并提出智能体方法","tl":"（据标题推断）把定向输入生成从函数级推进到仓库级的智能体方法。","au":["Haoyu Wang","Ming Wen","Haoran Yan","Jiayi Huang","Xuanhua Shi","Hai Jin"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["directed input generation","repository-level","agentic fuzzing","reachability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/241/x"},{"id":"p01261","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Comprehensive Evaluation of Code Language Models for Security Patch Detection","tz":"代码语言模型用于安全补丁检测的全面评估","a":"Automated detection of vulnerability-fixing commits ( ) is critical for timely security patch deployment, as advisory databases lag patch releases by a median of 25 days and many fixes never receive advisories. Code language models are increasingly adopted for identifying VFCs, yet whether they can recognize a security fix from the code change itself remains unclear, as reported performance is shaped by commit messages, project-level data leakage, and uncertain data quality. We present a rigorous re-evaluation that jointly controls these factors through a unified framework consolidating 20 fragmented datasets spanning more than 180000 commits. Training 270 models from 125M to 80B parameters, we isolate the code signal under group-stratified code-only evaluation and assess the impact of model capacity and additional code context, ranging from intra-procedural enrichment to inter-procedural repository context. Model capacity yields clear but insufficient gains, and the evaluated context signals provide no reliable improvement under strict false positive budgets. At a false positive rate of 0.5%, every evaluated fine-tuned code-only model misses at least 80% of vulnerability fixes. A manual expert audit further shows that label error concentrates in commits lacking CVE association and primarily distorts evaluation. We derive concrete recommendations for evaluating on aggregated VFC datasets and release our unified framework and evaluation suite.","az":"自动检测漏洞修复提交（VFC）对于及时部署安全补丁至关重要，因为公告数据库相对补丁发布中位滞后 25 天，且许多修复从未获得公告。代码语言模型正越来越多地被用于识别 VFC，但它们能否仅凭代码变更本身识别出安全修复仍不清楚，因为已报告的性能受到提交信息、项目级数据泄漏和数据质量不确定性的影响。我们提出一次严格的重新评估，通过一个统一框架同时控制这些因素，该框架整合了 20 个碎片化数据集、覆盖超过 180000 个提交。我们训练了 270 个从 125M 到 80B 参数的模型，在按组分层的仅代码评测下分离出代码信号，并评估模型容量以及额外代码上下文（从过程内增强到跨过程的仓库级上下文）的影响。模型容量带来明显但不充分的提升，而所评估的上下文信号在严格的误报预算下并未提供可靠改进。在 0.5% 的误报率下，所有被评估的仅代码微调模型都漏掉了至少 80% 的漏洞修复。进一步的人工专家审计显示，标签错误集中在缺乏 CVE 关联的提交上，并主要扭曲了评测结果。我们给出了在聚合 VFC 数据集上进行评测的具体建议，并发布了统一框架与评测套件。","tl":"严格控制泄漏后显示代码模型难以仅凭代码识别安全修复提交。","au":["Nils Loose","Joseph Bienhüls","Kristoffer Hempel","Felix Mächtle","Thomas Eisenbarth"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["vulnerability-fixing commit","security patch detection","code language models","data leakage","label quality"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/242/x"},{"id":"p01262","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Exact-IaC: Execution-Driven Exact Knowledge Injection for Reliable IaC Synthesis","tz":"Exact-IaC：以执行驱动的精确知识注入实现可靠的 IaC 合成","tl":"（据标题推断）用执行驱动的精确知识注入提升 IaC 代码合成可靠性。","au":["Hua Ge","Minxue Pan"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["Infrastructure-as-Code","knowledge injection","execution feedback","code synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/243/x"},{"id":"p01263","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TrackTest: Trajectory Generation and Prioritization for Testing Multiple Object Tracking System","tz":"TrackTest：面向多目标跟踪系统测试的轨迹生成与优先级排序","tl":"（据标题推断）生成并排序轨迹用例以高效测试多目标跟踪系统。","au":["Xinyu Gao","Haoxin Chen","Shuoxiao Zhang","Enyi Tang","Hengrui Xu","Haoxiang Tian","Minghui Wei","An Guo"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["multiple object tracking","test generation","test prioritization","trajectory"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/244/x"},{"id":"p01264","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PELSE: Asymmetric-Evidence-Guided MCU Peripheral Model Synthesis","tz":"PELSE：非对称证据引导的 MCU 外设模型合成","tl":"（据标题推断）用非对称证据引导自动合成 MCU 外设模型。","au":["Guohao Wu","Chunlin Wang","Rui Yao","Feng Hong","Hongliang Liang","Qiuping Yi"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","security"],"kw":["MCU firmware","peripheral model synthesis","emulation","embedded"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/245/x"},{"id":"p01265","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Benchmarking Automated Security Patch Backporting: How Far Are We?","tz":"自动安全补丁回移的基准评测：我们走到哪一步了？","a":"Automated security patch backporting is critical for mitigating N-day vulnerabilities. Recent tools report success rates above 80% on their respective datasets. However, these evaluations are often confined to homogeneous environments, such as one repository or specific project versions. Consequently, it remains unclear how well these tools generalize beyond their originally targeted scenarios. We present Porting Benchmark, a curated dataset of 1,234 security patch backporting cases spanning cross-version, cross-branch, and cross-repository scenarios, paired with a common evaluation framework. Using this benchmark, we evaluate five tools spanning program analysis, LLM prompting, and LLM agents under aligned settings. Our results show that aligned evaluation changes the apparent performance landscape: PortGPT and TSBPort remain comparatively strong on the Replication Dataset, while FixMorph and Mystique degrade substantially under the common protocol. Performance degrades sharply on structurally complex patches: the best commit-level success rate falls from 85.2% on Type-I patches to 24.0% on Type-IV. We identify four root-cause categories (missing target API awareness, cross-version semantic mismatch, non-local dependency propagation failure, and patch construction or localization failure) and derive concrete directions for next-generation tool design. On a 45-case dynamically validated subset with verified test cases and constructed POCs, we further observe that reference-based benchmark scores do not fully capture real-world remediation: exact match sharply under-credits harder target adaptations, while executable validation reveals residual integration failures in the target that static reference agreement misses. Executable-feedback refinement provides limited but measurable recovery on the hardest executable cases.","az":"自动安全补丁回移（backporting）对于缓解 N-day 漏洞至关重要。近期工具在各自数据集上报告了超过 80% 的成功率。然而这些评估往往局限于同质环境，例如单一仓库或特定项目版本，因此这些工具在其原本目标场景之外的泛化能力仍不清楚。我们提出 Porting Benchmark，一个精心构建的数据集，包含 1,234 个安全补丁回移案例，覆盖跨版本、跨分支和跨仓库场景，并配有统一的评测框架。基于该基准，我们在对齐的设定下评估了涵盖程序分析、LLM 提示和 LLM 智能体的五个工具。结果表明，对齐评测改变了表面上的性能格局：PortGPT 和 TSBPort 在复现数据集上仍相对较强，而 FixMorph 与 Mystique 在统一协议下性能明显退化。在结构复杂的补丁上性能急剧下降：最佳的提交级成功率从 Type-I 补丁的 85.2% 跌至 Type-IV 的 24.0%。我们识别出四类根因（缺乏目标 API 感知、跨版本语义不匹配、非局部依赖传播失败、补丁构造或定位失败），并由此提出下一代工具设计的具体方向。在一个包含 45 个案例、带有验证测试用例与构造 POC 的动态验证子集上，我们进一步观察到基于参考的基准分数并不能完全反映真实世界的修复效果：精确匹配严重低估了较难的目标适配，而可执行验证则揭示了静态参考一致性所忽略的目标端残留集成失败。可执行反馈的精化带来了有限但可测量的改进。","tl":"统一基准显示补丁回移工具在跨仓库复杂补丁上大幅退化。","au":["Jincheng Yang","Yulong Fu","Chengwei Liu","Lyuye Zhang","Fangyuan Zhang","Bingyang Ren","Yang Liu","Hui Li"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","agentic"],"kw":["patch backporting","N-day vulnerability","benchmark","LLM agents","executable validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/246/x"},{"id":"p01266","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"When Knowledge Changes: Metamorphic Testing of RAG Systems with Mutations","tz":"当知识发生变化：用变异对 RAG 系统进行蜕变测试","a":"Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)-based LLM systems rely on external document corpora that can evolve and change over time. However, current evaluation methodologies (e.g., RAGAS) assess correctness against static snapshots, failing to detect faults when routine updates, factual changes, or noise alter the underlying data. We introduce a metamorphic testing framework that evaluates the consistency of RAG systems under corpus evolution. We formalise a fault taxonomy and 11 mutation operators that systematically perturb the system at both the pre-chunk (retrieval index) and post-chunk (retrieved context) levels. An empirical evaluation across five datasets and over 28k mutants reveals metamorphic violation rates of 4.9-10.2%. In a meta-evaluation against ground truth, our metamorphic oracle achieves F1 scores of 0.927-1.000, while the best RAGAS metric reaches only 0.570. Finally, we provide actionable insights into mitigating these faults through retrieval re-configuration, generator upgrades, and LLM-based reranking.","az":"基于检索增强生成（RAG）的 LLM 系统依赖会随时间演化和变化的外部文档语料。然而当前的评测方法（如 RAGAS）只针对静态快照评估正确性，无法在常规更新、事实变更或噪声改变底层数据时检测出故障。我们提出一个蜕变测试框架，用以评估 RAG 系统在语料演化下的一致性。我们形式化了一个故障分类体系和 11 个变异算子，在 pre-chunk（检索索引）与 post-chunk（检索到的上下文）两个层面系统性地扰动系统。在五个数据集、超过 28k 个变异体上的实证评估显示蜕变违例率为 4.9%–10.2%。在针对真值的元评估中，我们的蜕变预言取得 0.927–1.000 的 F1 分数，而最佳的 RAGAS 指标仅达到 0.570。最后，我们给出了通过检索重配置、生成器升级和基于 LLM 的重排序来缓解这些故障的可操作见解。","tl":"用 11 个语料变异算子做蜕变测试暴露 RAG 一致性故障。","au":["Jinhan Kim","Samuele Pasini","Paolo Tonella"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["RAG testing","metamorphic testing","mutation operators","corpus evolution","RAGAS"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/247/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.26843"},{"id":"p01267","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Testing Static Analyzers via Semantic-Preserving Mutators Learned from Real-World Refactoring Practice","tz":"用从真实重构实践中学到的保语义变异算子测试静态分析器","tl":"（据标题推断）从真实重构中学习保语义变异来测静态分析器。","au":["Meilin Li","Kaixuan Li","Zifan Xie","Shiyu Qiu","Ming Wen","Maolin Sun","Hongyu Zhang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static analyzer testing","semantic-preserving mutation","refactoring practice","differential testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/248/x","pu":"https://xzf1234.github.io/pdfs/ASE26_SAFuzzer.pdf"},{"id":"p01268","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"ReSEDA: Automatic and Precise Program-Level ReDoS Triage via Interprocedural Taint Analysis and Agentic Exploit Generation","tz":"ReSEDA：基于过程间污点分析与智能体式利用生成的自动精确程序级 ReDoS 分诊","tl":"（据标题推断）污点分析加智能体生成 exploit 精确分诊 ReDoS。","au":["Rongchen Li","Weihao Su","Chengyao Peng","hong huang","Haiming Chen","Guiyi He"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["ReDoS","taint analysis","exploit generation","vulnerability triage","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/249/x"},{"id":"p01269","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"A Few Pages of Markdown: Committed AI Configuration and Lower Quality Cost after Coding-Agent Adoption","tz":"几页 Markdown：编程智能体采纳后提交的 AI 配置与更低的质量代价","a":"Coding agents increase development velocity but also technical debt. Prior work reports only average effects across adopters, hiding wide differences between teams. We introduce RAMP (Repository AI Maturity Profile), a four-level cumulative maturity model grounded in version-controlled artifacts that teams commit to configure AI tools. RAMP runs from behavioral rules and coding standards through named agent definitions to multi-agent orchestration, with observed practice concentrated in the first three levels. Across 441 repositories the levels behave as a cumulative scale, and independent human annotation reproduces RAMP's repository-level labels on 97% of a held-out sample. Adoption is cumulative, forward-only, and set-and-forget: 73.8% of artifacts are committed once and never modified. Re-estimating an existing agent-adoption panel within each stratum, agents accelerate development regardless of maturity (28-38% more commits), but quality diverges: among agent-first repositories, where the contrast is identified, those without committed AI configuration show roughly twice the increase in cognitive complexity (+53% versus +27%) and 1.7x the increase in static-analysis warnings. Because maturity is observational, correlated engineering discipline or model capability may explain part of the gap; we present these findings as hypothesis-generating and release RAMP as a reusable instrument.","az":"编程智能体提升了开发速度，但也增加了技术债。已有工作只报告采纳者之间的平均效应，掩盖了团队之间的巨大差异。我们提出 RAMP（Repository AI Maturity Profile），一个基于团队提交到版本控制中用于配置 AI 工具的制品的四级累积成熟度模型。RAMP 从行为规则和编码规范，经由具名的智能体定义，直到多智能体编排；观察到的实践主要集中在前三级。在 441 个仓库上，各等级表现为一个累积量表，独立的人工标注在留出样本上以 97% 的比例复现了 RAMP 的仓库级标签。采纳是累积的、只进不退的，并且是“设置后不再管”的：73.8% 的制品只提交一次，此后从未修改。在每一层内重新估计一个已有的智能体采纳面板数据模型后发现，无论成熟度如何，智能体都会加速开发（提交数增加 28%–38%），但质量出现分化：在可识别该对比的 agent-first 仓库中，没有提交 AI 配置的仓库其认知复杂度增幅约为有配置者的两倍（+53% 对 +27%），静态分析告警增幅为 1.7 倍。由于成熟度是观察性的，相关的工程纪律或模型能力可能解释部分差距；我们把这些发现作为假设生成性的结果提出，并发布 RAMP 作为一个可复用的测量工具。","tl":"提交 AI 配置的仓库在采纳智能体后质量劣化明显更小。","au":["Yegor Denisov-Blanch","Shyam Agarwal","Pavel Azaletskiy","Hao He","Rylan Schaeffer","Brando Miranda","Bogdan Vasilescu","Sanmi Koyejo"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","agentic"],"kw":["coding agent adoption","AI configuration artifacts","repository maturity model","technical debt","cognitive complexity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/250/x"},{"id":"p01270","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Perception, Reasoning, and Action: A ReAct-Based Vulnerability Detection Framework with Repository-Level Reasoning","tz":"感知、推理与行动：一种具备仓库级推理的 ReAct 式漏洞检测框架","tl":"（据标题推断）用 ReAct 式智能体在仓库级上下文中检测漏洞。","au":["Xin-Cheng Wen","Hanyue Luo","Cuiyun Gao","Hao Zhu","Yang Xiao","Ge Li"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","ReAct","repository-level reasoning","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/251/x"},{"id":"p01271","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"TDiFf: Detecting Bugs in DataFrame Systems via Transferred DBMS Test Cases","tz":"TDiFf：通过迁移 DBMS 测试用例检测 DataFrame 系统中的缺陷","a":"DataFrame systems are core components of modern data analytics platforms and achieve high performance through various optimization techniques. However, these optimizations can introduce subtle defects that are difficult to detect, undermining system reliability. Existing testing approaches primarily rely on manually written unit tests or automated unit test generation tools, which often produce invalid or low-quality test cases and have limited ability to exercise complex API sequences and optimization-induced behaviors. In this paper, we present TDiFf, a novel LLM-based testing framework for DataFrame systems. TDiFf leverages the database-like characteristics of DataFrame systems by translating SQL queries into Python DataFrame test cases for differential testing. To address limitations of LLMs in mapping SQL constructs to DataFrame APIs and preserving semantic consistency, TDiFf incorporates feature knowledge extracted from SQL and DataFrame API documentation. In addition, it utilizes data flow graphs derived from SQL query plans to guide the generation of syntactically valid and semantically consistent DataFrame API sequences. We evaluate TDiFf on six widely used DataFrame systems: Pandas , Dask , CuDF , Modin , PySpark , and Polars . The results show that more than 99% of the generated DataFrame test cases are valid. Using these test cases, TDiFf uncovers 35 unique and previously unknown bugs confirmed by developers and outperforms state-of-the-art baseline approaches by 2.5× to 14×.","az":"DataFrame 系统是现代数据分析平台的核心组件，并通过各种优化技术获得高性能。然而这些优化可能引入难以检测的细微缺陷，损害系统可靠性。现有测试方法主要依赖人工编写的单元测试或自动单元测试生成工具，往往产生无效或低质量的测试用例，且难以触发复杂的 API 序列和由优化引发的行为。本文提出 TDiFf，一个基于 LLM 的 DataFrame 系统测试框架。TDiFf 利用 DataFrame 系统类数据库的特性，把 SQL 查询翻译成 Python DataFrame 测试用例以进行差分测试。为解决 LLM 在把 SQL 构造映射到 DataFrame API 以及保持语义一致性上的不足，TDiFf 融入了从 SQL 与 DataFrame API 文档中抽取的特性知识；此外，它利用从 SQL 查询计划导出的数据流图来引导生成语法有效且语义一致的 DataFrame API 序列。我们在六个广泛使用的 DataFrame 系统上评估 TDiFf：Pandas、Dask、CuDF、Modin、PySpark 和 Polars。结果显示，生成的 DataFrame 测试用例中超过 99% 是有效的。借助这些测试用例，TDiFf 发现了 35 个此前未知且已被开发者确认的独特缺陷，并以 2.5 倍到 14 倍的优势超过最先进的基线方法。","tl":"把 SQL 查询翻译成 DataFrame 用例做差分测试发现 35 个新缺陷。","au":["Jiaxin Hu","Shaowei Chen","Rongxin Wu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["DataFrame systems","differential testing","SQL translation","LLM-based testing","data flow graph"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/252/x"},{"id":"p01272","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"MiniPoly: Automatic Extraction of Efficient JavaScript Polyfill from Language Specification","tz":"MiniPoly：从语言规范自动抽取高效的 JavaScript Polyfill","tl":"（据标题推断）直接从 JS 规范自动抽取精简高效的 polyfill。","au":["Jungwoong Kim","Youngmin Cho","Jihyeok Park"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["JavaScript polyfill","language specification","code extraction","compatibility"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/253/x"},{"id":"p01273","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"IcFuzz: Fuzzing Isaac Sim with Semantic Stage Guidance and Multi-level Mutation","tz":"IcFuzz：以语义阶段引导和多层次变异对 Isaac Sim 进行模糊测试","a":"Robotics simulators serve as a foundational infrastructure for embodied AI, facilitating safe and scalable robotic system development. NVIDIA Isaac Sim has emerged as one of the most popular simulators, distinguished by its GPU-accelerated physics engine and photorealistic rendering, which enable high-fidelity modeling of complex environments. However, its inherent complexity inevitably introduces software bugs that can compromise simulation reliability. Existing fuzzing approaches struggle to test Isaac Sim effectively due to challenges of context-aware object semantics, hierarchical simulation control, and a vast simulation state space. In this paper, we propose IcFuzz, the first fuzzing approach for Isaac Sim. IcFuzz first performs an LLM-based semantic stage segmentation, decomposing simulation programs into structured stages that capture context-aware object semantics. Guided by this information, IcFuzz designs multi-level mutation operators to systematically exercise the simulator across hierarchical granularities. To efficiently navigate the vast simulation state space, IcFuzz employs a multi-armed bandit algorithm to adaptively schedule mutation operators. Experimental results show that IcFuzz outperforms the baselines in terms of both code coverage and bug detection. Specifically, IcFuzz achieves approximately 190%–205% of the code coverage of the baselines and detects an average of 3.7 unique crashes over three rounds of 12-hour tests, while no crashes are detected by the baselines. Moreover, IcFuzz has uncovered 11 bugs over approximately four months, 9 of which have been confirmed or fixed by the developers.","az":"机器人仿真器是具身智能的基础设施，能够支撑安全且可扩展的机器人系统开发。NVIDIA Isaac Sim 已成为最流行的仿真器之一，其 GPU 加速的物理引擎与照片级真实渲染使复杂环境的高保真建模成为可能。然而，其固有的复杂性不可避免地引入了可能损害仿真可靠性的软件缺陷。由于存在上下文感知的对象语义、层次化的仿真控制以及巨大的仿真状态空间等挑战，现有模糊测试方法难以有效测试 Isaac Sim。本文提出 IcFuzz，首个面向 Isaac Sim 的模糊测试方法。IcFuzz 首先执行基于 LLM 的语义阶段切分，把仿真程序分解为能够捕捉上下文感知对象语义的结构化阶段；在这些信息的引导下，IcFuzz 设计了多层次变异算子，以在层次化粒度上系统性地检验仿真器。为高效探索庞大的仿真状态空间，IcFuzz 采用多臂老虎机算法自适应地调度变异算子。实验结果表明，IcFuzz 在代码覆盖率和缺陷检测上均优于基线：IcFuzz 达到基线约 190%–205% 的代码覆盖率，在三轮 12 小时测试中平均检测到 3.7 个独特崩溃，而基线未检测到任何崩溃。此外，IcFuzz 在约四个月内发现了 11 个缺陷，其中 9 个已被开发者确认或修复。","tl":"首个 Isaac Sim 模糊测试器，用语义阶段切分与多层变异找缺陷。","au":["Zhixiang Chen","Zhuangbin Chen","Ruoxi Jia","Zeqin Liao","Wei Li","Jinyang Liu","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Isaac Sim","robotics simulator","fuzzing","multi-level mutation","multi-armed bandit"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/254/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.06088"},{"id":"p01274","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"How Well Do LLMs Generate Taxonomies in the SE Domain? A Multi-perspective Evaluation Framework","tz":"LLM 在软件工程领域生成分类体系的效果如何？一个多视角评估框架","a":"Taxonomies provide a shared conceptual framework for organizing heterogeneous observations in software engineering (SE) research. Manually constructing such taxonomies is labor-intensive and requires annotators with expertise in the SE domain. While advances in Large Language Models (LLMs) have led to the emergence of automated taxonomy generation methods outside the SE domain, their applicability to technically complex SE artifacts remains unclear. In this experience paper, we present the first comprehensive empirical evaluation of how state-of-the-art automated methods perform on SE artifacts through a multi-perspective evaluation framework, including taxonomy quality, alignment with taxonomies defined by human experts, reliability under independent annotation, and efficiency. To support this evaluation, we systematically collect seven SE papers with publicly available artifacts and human-defined taxonomies, and conduct experiments using two automated methods (TnT-LLM and CLIMB) with five state-of-the-art LLMs. Our evaluation reveals a clear trade-off: TnT-LLM constructs high-quality taxonomies comparable to human-defined ones but incurs substantially higher cost and runtime and tends to generate overly complex taxonomies, whereas CLIMB is 15–40 faster and 8–49 cheaper but tends to score lower on quality when technical inference beyond surface-level similarity is required. These findings suggest that TnT-LLM and CLIMB can be used in practical situations in the SE domain, while researchers should first assess the complexity of the generated taxonomies and their cost using a subset of the target data to decide whether to use automated methods or human experts. Our work represents a first step toward a systematic understanding of automated taxonomy generation in SE, offering actionable insights for future research and practice.","az":"分类体系（taxonomy）为软件工程（SE）研究中组织异构观察提供了共享的概念框架。人工构建这类分类体系既费力，又需要具备 SE 领域专业知识的标注者。尽管大语言模型（LLM）的进展催生了 SE 领域之外的自动分类体系生成方法，但它们对技术复杂的 SE 制品的适用性仍不清楚。在这篇经验论文中，我们通过一个多视角评估框架，首次全面实证评估了最先进的自动化方法在 SE 制品上的表现，评估维度包括分类体系质量、与人类专家定义分类体系的一致性、独立标注下的可靠性以及效率。为支撑该评估，我们系统收集了七篇具有公开制品和人工定义分类体系的 SE 论文，并使用两种自动化方法（TnT-LLM 和 CLIMB）配合五个最先进的 LLM 开展实验。评估揭示出明显的权衡：TnT-LLM 能构建出与人类定义相当的高质量分类体系，但成本与运行时间高得多，且倾向于生成过于复杂的体系；而 CLIMB 快 15–40 倍、便宜 8–49 倍，但在需要超越表层相似度的技术推断时质量得分较低。这些发现表明 TnT-LLM 与 CLIMB 在 SE 领域的实际场景中均可使用，但研究者应先用目标数据的一个子集评估所生成分类体系的复杂度及其成本，再决定采用自动化方法还是人类专家。我们的工作是系统理解 SE 领域自动分类体系生成的第一步，为未来研究与实践提供了可操作的洞见。","tl":"首次系统评估自动分类体系生成方法在 SE 制品上的质量与成本权衡。","au":["Sota Nakashima","Yuta Ishimoto","Masanari Kondo","Tao Xiao","Yasutaka Kamei"],"top":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["taxonomy generation","TnT-LLM","CLIMB","SE artifacts","multi-perspective evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/255/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.01592"},{"id":"p01275","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Implicit, Yet Impactful: Understanding Hidden Dependencies in Java Projects","tz":"隐式却影响深远：理解 Java 项目中的隐藏依赖","a":"As software usage continues to expand, package managers automatically resolve dependencies to construct a dependency graph based on user-specified requirements. These explicitly declared dependencies, known as direct dependencies, receive significant attention in terms of maintainability and security. However, implicit dependencies, which are not explicitly defined by users but are still directly utilized or referenced in their project code due to oversight, remain largely unnoticed. Unlike ordinary transitive dependencies, which may remain unused and invisible to the root, implicit dependencies are actively used yet undeclared, leaving their versions outside the project's direct control. This lack of awareness poses substantial challenges related to security and maintainability. In this study, we present the first study to treat implicit dependencies as the focal phenomenon and quantitatively characterize their lifecycle consequences for the Maven ecosystem. We meticulously collected and built a large-scale dataset with 1,157 libraries with 19,812 versions from the Maven Central Repository and 972 modules from GitHub. Our findings reveal that 34.12% of the analyzed dataset contains implicit dependencies, with two primary causes identified as key contributors to the issue. Among these, 48% introduce breaking changes due to version drift, and 36 CVEs have vulnerable methods directly used by root projects; 30.28% of implicit dependencies are affected by known vulnerabilities under the version-range convention SCA tools use for declared dependencies. Finally, we identified and analyzed four major countermeasures, providing actionable insights and practical implications for addressing this overlooked issue for stakeholders within the OSS ecosystem.","az":"随着软件使用范围持续扩大，包管理器会根据用户指定的需求自动解析依赖并构建依赖图。这些显式声明的依赖（即直接依赖）在可维护性和安全性方面受到了大量关注。然而，隐式依赖——用户并未显式定义，却由于疏忽而在项目代码中被直接使用或引用——在很大程度上仍被忽视。与可能未被使用、对根项目不可见的普通传递依赖不同，隐式依赖被实际使用却未被声明，其版本因而脱离了项目的直接控制。这种缺乏认知带来了显著的安全与可维护性挑战。在本研究中，我们首次把隐式依赖作为核心现象来研究，并定量刻画其在 Maven 生态中的生命周期后果。我们细致地收集并构建了一个大规模数据集，包含来自 Maven 中央仓库的 1,157 个库、19,812 个版本，以及来自 GitHub 的 972 个模块。我们的发现显示，所分析数据集中有 34.12% 含有隐式依赖，并识别出两个导致该问题的主要成因。其中，48% 因版本漂移引入了破坏性变更，36 个 CVE 的脆弱方法被根项目直接使用；按 SCA 工具用于已声明依赖的版本范围约定，30.28% 的隐式依赖受已知漏洞影响。最后，我们识别并分析了四类主要应对措施，为开源生态中的各方利益相关者提供了针对这一被忽视问题的可操作洞见与实践启示。","tl":"首次量化 Maven 隐式依赖的普遍性及其破坏性变更与漏洞后果。","au":["Lyuye Zhang","Chengwei Liu","Fangyuan Zhang","Yiran Zhang","Yuan Zhou","Yang Liu"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","security"],"kw":["implicit dependencies","Maven ecosystem","version drift","breaking changes","software composition analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/256/x"},{"id":"p01276","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Piece by Piece: Automating Combination Interaction GUI Testing via Planning and Dual Memory","tz":"逐块拼合：通过规划与双重记忆自动化组合交互的 GUI 测试","a":"Combination interactions require coordinated operations across multiple GUI widgets within a page to complete a functional task, which are common in modern mobile apps. However, due to widget dependencies, dynamic interface transitions, and context-sensitive execution, existing automated GUI testing approaches based on predefined models or state exploration struggle to reliably complete such interactions. LLM-based GUI testing methods improve semantic understanding but often generate inconsistent actions due to the lack of coordination modeling and interaction context. To address these challenges, this paper proposes COMBDroid, an automated GUI testing approach that enables reliable completion of combination interactions through structured planning and dual memory. COMBDroid first detects combination interaction patterns from GUI structure, then generates page-level interaction plans and grounds them into widget-level executable actions. Inspired by Sudoku solving, COMBDroid maintains a dual-memory mechanism, where context memory preserves execution states within a functionality and experience memory captures reusable interaction patterns. COMBDroid is designed as an integrable module that activates when combination interactions are detected and allows existing testing tools to resume exploration after completion. We evaluate COMBDroid on 100 combination interaction functionalities collected from 100 mobile apps, comparing it with 15 state-of-the-art GUI testing baselines. COMBDroid achieves 103% higher passing rate than the best baseline and improves activity coverage by 65%-100% when integrated with existing testing tools. Furthermore, GUI testing tools integrated with COMBDroid detect 37 new crash bugs in real-world apps, with 26 fixed and the remaining confirmed by developers, demonstrating its effectiveness in improving GUI testing.","az":"组合交互需要在一个页面内跨多个 GUI 控件协调操作才能完成一项功能任务，这在现代移动应用中非常常见。然而，由于控件之间存在依赖、界面转换是动态的以及执行对上下文敏感，现有基于预定义模型或状态探索的自动化 GUI 测试方法难以可靠地完成这类交互。基于大语言模型的 GUI 测试方法提升了语义理解能力，但由于缺乏协调建模与交互上下文，常常生成前后不一致的动作。为应对这些挑战，本文提出 COMBDroid，一种通过结构化规划与双重记忆来可靠完成组合交互的自动化 GUI 测试方法。COMBDroid 首先从 GUI 结构中检测组合交互模式，然后生成页面级交互计划，并将其落地为控件级的可执行动作。受数独求解启发，COMBDroid 维护一种双重记忆机制：上下文记忆保存某一功能内部的执行状态，经验记忆则捕获可复用的交互模式。COMBDroid 被设计为可集成模块，在检测到组合交互时激活，并允许已有测试工具在完成后继续探索。我们在从 100 个移动应用中收集的 100 项组合交互功能上评估 COMBDroid，并与 15 个最新 GUI 测试基线进行比较。COMBDroid 的通过率比最佳基线高出 103%，在与现有测试工具集成后将活动（activity）覆盖率提升 65%-100%。此外，集成了 COMBDroid 的 GUI 测试工具在真实应用中检测出 37 个新的崩溃缺陷，其中 26 个已修复，其余均获开发者确认，证明了其在改进 GUI 测试方面的有效性。","tl":"用规划加上下文/经验双记忆攻克多控件组合交互测试","au":["Zhe Liu","Oujin Wang","Junjie Wang","Chunyang Chen","Mengzhuo Chen","Boyu Wu","Yuekai Huang","Qing Wang"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GUI testing","combination interaction","dual memory","LLM agent","Android"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/257/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837553"},{"id":"p01277","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"The CodeInverter Suite: Structure- and Data-Aware Binary Decompilation with Efficient LLMs","tz":"CodeInverter 套件：用高效 LLM 实现结构与数据感知的二进制反编译","a":"Binary decompilation plays a vital role in various cybersecurity and software engineering tasks. Recently, end-to-end decompilation methods powered by large language models (LLMs) have attracted increasing attention for their ability to generate highly readable source code with minimal human intervention. However, existing LLM-based methods still struggle with reconstructing program structure and logic, achieving accurate data recovery, ensuring data security and privacy, and maintaining computational efficiency. To address these challenges, we propose the CodeInverter Suite, with three main pieces: (1) the CodeInverter Workflow (CIW) is a novel prompt engineering method that incorporates control flow graphs (CFG) and explicit data mappings to enhance structure reconstruction and data recovery during decompilation; (2) building upon CIW, we construct the CodeInverter Dataset (CID), a large-scale domain-specific dataset containing 8.69 million samples enriched with CFGs and data mapping information; (3) we develop CodeInverter Models (CIMs), two lightweight LLMs with 1.3B and 6.7B parameters, enabling efficient inference in privacy-sensitive and resource-constrained environments. Extensive experiments on two benchmark datasets demonstrate that CIW significantly enhances the decompilation performance of various LLMs, with average improvements of 13.07% in re-executability and 23.94% in re-compilability. For our proposed decompilation model, CIM-6.7B achieves state-of-the-art performance in terms of re-executability and readability, outperforming existing LLMs-even with over 100 times more parameters-by an average of 11.03% and 6.27%, respectively.","az":"二进制反编译在各类网络安全与软件工程任务中起着关键作用。近来，由大语言模型（LLM）驱动的端到端反编译方法因能以极少人工干预生成高可读性源码而受到越来越多关注。然而，现有基于 LLM 的方法在重建程序结构与逻辑、实现准确的数据恢复、保障数据安全与隐私以及维持计算效率方面仍存在困难。为解决这些挑战，我们提出 CodeInverter 套件，包含三部分：(1) CodeInverter Workflow (CIW) 是一种新颖的提示工程方法，引入控制流图（CFG）与显式数据映射，以增强反编译过程中的结构重建与数据恢复；(2) 在 CIW 基础上，我们构建了 CodeInverter Dataset (CID)，一个包含 869 万条样本、并富含 CFG 与数据映射信息的大规模领域专用数据集；(3) 我们开发了 CodeInverter Models (CIMs)，两个参数量分别为 1.3B 和 6.7B 的轻量级 LLM，可在隐私敏感与资源受限环境中高效推理。在两个基准数据集上的大量实验表明，CIW 显著提升了各类 LLM 的反编译性能，可重执行性平均提升 13.07%，可重编译性平均提升 23.94%。对于我们提出的反编译模型，CIM-6.7B 在可重执行性与可读性方面达到最新水平，平均分别超过现有 LLM（即使其参数量多出 100 倍以上）11.03% 和 6.27%。","tl":"用 CFG 与数据映射提示训练轻量反编译专用模型","au":["Peipei Liu","Jian Sun","Rongkang Sun","Li Chen","Zhaoteng Yan","Xiaoling Zhang","Dawei Wang","Dapeng Sun","Peizheng Zhang","Dan Li"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["binary decompilation","control flow graph","domain-specific dataset","lightweight LLM","re-executability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/258/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.07215"},{"id":"p01278","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Guided Decoding as a Defense against Package Hallucination in LLM-Generated Code","tz":"引导式解码：抵御 LLM 生成代码中的依赖包幻觉","tl":"（据标题推断）在解码阶段约束依赖包名以消除包幻觉","au":["Alberick Euraste Djire","Iyiola E. Olatunji","Melissa Tessa","Earl T. Barr","Jacques Klein","Tegawendé F. Bissyandé"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["package hallucination","guided decoding","LLM-generated code","supply chain security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/259/x"},{"id":"p01279","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Post-hoc Attention Steering of Large Language Models for Robust Code Understanding under Obfuscation","tz":"面向混淆场景下鲁棒代码理解的大语言模型事后注意力引导","a":"Modern critical software infrastructure is largely written in C. Since C lacks memory safety, researchers are investigating automatic translation of C to safer languages like Rust. But real-world C software consists of more than just C code, often using named code fragments called macros which are not part of the C language proper. State-of-the-art techniques avoid translating macros by preprocessing C code first before translating it. But this approach produces translations that are dissimilar to the original C code, because preprocessing inlines all macro definitions. To preserve macro usage in translated code, we study the language features that macros and C share and distill them into the first formally-specified translator, MerC. To evaluate MerC, we introduce the first macro translation benchmark, MacroBench, with test cases based on macros randomly sampled from real-world C programs. We find that MerC supports 50% of MacroBench's macro test cases. We also use MacroBench to evaluate how effective large language models (LLMs) are at performing the previously-unstudied task of macro translation. LLMs translate 22% to 77% more of MacroBench than MerC, but with 8% and 28% of these translations being incorrect translations requiring additional validation by developers. In contrast, MerC only produces correct translations. Our key insight is that running MerC first then using LLMs on the remainder reaps greater benefits than using either technique alone. This tag team approach has an average failure rate 32% lower than that of LLMs, while also translating an average of 51% more test cases than MerC.","az":"现代关键软件基础设施大多用 C 语言编写。由于 C 缺乏内存安全性，研究者正在探索将 C 自动翻译为 Rust 等更安全的语言。但真实世界的 C 软件不只包含 C 代码，往往还使用被称为宏（macro）的具名代码片段，而宏并不属于 C 语言本体。最新技术会先对 C 代码做预处理再翻译，从而回避宏的翻译。但这种做法会产生与原始 C 代码大相径庭的翻译结果，因为预处理会把所有宏定义内联展开。为在翻译后的代码中保留宏的使用，我们研究了宏与 C 共有的语言特性，并将其提炼为首个形式化定义的翻译器 MerC。为评估 MerC，我们提出首个宏翻译基准 MacroBench，其测试用例基于从真实 C 程序中随机采样的宏构建。我们发现 MerC 支持 MacroBench 中 50% 的宏测试用例。我们还用 MacroBench 评估大语言模型（LLM）在此前未被研究过的宏翻译任务上的效果。LLM 比 MerC 多翻译 22% 到 77% 的 MacroBench 用例，但其中 8% 到 28% 的翻译是错误的，需要开发者额外验证。相比之下，MerC 只产生正确的翻译。我们的关键洞见是：先运行 MerC，再用 LLM 处理剩余部分，其收益大于单独使用任一技术。这种“组合拳”方式的平均失败率比 LLM 低 32%，同时比 MerC 平均多翻译 51% 的测试用例。","tl":"首个形式化宏翻译器 MerC 与基准，并与 LLM 互补","au":["Xiaokai Rong","Aashish Yadavally","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["C to Rust translation","macro translation","MerC","MacroBench","formal translator"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/260/x"},{"id":"p01280","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"PAIChecker: Uncovering and Checking PR-Issue Misalignment in SWE-Bench-Like Benchmarks","tz":"PAIChecker：揭示并检查 SWE-bench 类基准中的 PR-Issue 错配","a":"SWE-bench-like benchmarks are widely used for evaluating LLM’s issue resolution capability. They typically follow a common construction pipeline: each PR (Pull Request) is paired with its linked issue by extracting issue references from the PR description; the issue description is used as the problem statement, and the PR patch serves as the test oracle. However, due to the inherent complexity of developing and maintaining large repositories, such PR-Issue pairings are often misaligned in practice. In this work, we systematically study SWE-bench Verified instances, finding that 13.6% exhibit misalignment across five patterns in eleven fine-grained scenarios. To enable reliable and scalable construction of those benchmarks in the future, we propose PAIChecker, a multi-agent system for checking PR-Issue misalignment in SWE-bench-like benchmarks. Specifically, PAIChecker adopts a three-phase design that combines specific pattern identification, cross-agent label synthesis, and code-level validation, thereby enabling more accurate, generalizable, and progressively verified detection. Experiments on SWE-Gym and SWE-bench Multilingual show that PAIchecker achieves the best performance across all four LLM backbones, reaching up to 92.12% and 91.67% binary accuracy, respectively.","az":"SWE-bench 类基准被广泛用于评估大语言模型的 issue 求解能力。它们通常遵循一套共同的构建流程：通过从 PR（Pull Request）描述中抽取 issue 引用，把每个 PR 与其关联的 issue 配对；issue 描述被用作问题陈述，PR 补丁则作为测试预言。然而，由于开发与维护大型仓库本身具有复杂性，这种 PR-Issue 配对在实践中常常是错配的。在本工作中，我们系统研究了 SWE-bench Verified 实例，发现其中 13.6% 存在错配，可归为五种模式、十一种细粒度场景。为使未来能够可靠且可扩展地构建此类基准，我们提出 PAIChecker，一个用于检查 SWE-bench 类基准中 PR-Issue 错配的多智能体系统。具体而言，PAIChecker 采用三阶段设计，结合特定模式识别、跨智能体标签合成与代码级验证，从而实现更准确、更具泛化性且逐级验证的检测。在 SWE-Gym 与 SWE-bench Multilingual 上的实验表明，PAIChecker 在全部四个 LLM 骨干模型上都取得最佳表现，二分类准确率分别高达 92.12% 和 91.67%。","tl":"量化并自动检测 SWE-bench 中 13.6% 的 PR-Issue 错配","au":["Manyi Wang","Junjielong Xu","Pinjia He"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["llm-based","agentic","empirical-study"],"kw":["SWE-bench","PR-issue misalignment","benchmark quality","multi-agent checking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/261/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.28587"},{"id":"p01281","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Can Large Language Models Decompose User Stories into Tasks? Exploring the Role of Prompting Strategies and Models","tz":"大语言模型能把用户故事拆解为任务吗？探究提示策略与模型的作用","a":"Refining user stories (USs) into tasks is an important step in agile software development, as it translates software requirements into project management artifacts that are assigned to team members. This story-to-task decomposition can be tedious. In this paper, we propose and evaluate DELTA, a Large Language Model (LLM)-based approach that automatically generates tasks from USs and assesses the quality of the resulting decompositions. We conduct a two-phase empirical study to evaluate DELTA. In the first phase, we identify the best-performing DELTA configuration by comparing different prompting strategies, LLM families, and sizes using text similarity metrics on human-created and LLM-generated decompositions. The comparison based on these metrics did not identify a single consistently best-performing configuration. Therefore, in the second phase, we conducted an expert evaluation to determine whether the observed differences in text similarity are reflected in expert judgments and whether DELTA’s criteria-based evaluation module, which uses LLM judges, aligns with expert judgments. Our results show that DELTA’s evaluation module produces rankings that align more closely with expert judgments than text similarity metrics. Moreover, experts generally prefer the top three LLM-generated decompositions, as ranked by LLM judges, over those created by humans, and they express a willingness to adopt DELTA.","az":"把用户故事（US）细化为任务是敏捷软件开发中的重要一步，因为它把软件需求转化为可分配给团队成员的项目管理制品。这种从故事到任务的拆解可能十分繁琐。本文提出并评估 DELTA，一种基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法，可自动从用户故事生成任务，并评估所得拆解结果的质量。我们开展了两阶段实证研究来评估 DELTA。第一阶段，我们在人工创建与 LLM 生成的拆解上使用文本相似度指标，比较不同提示策略、LLM 家族与规模，以确定表现最佳的 DELTA 配置。基于这些指标的比较并未找到一个始终最优的配置。因此，第二阶段我们开展了专家评估，以判断文本相似度上观察到的差异是否反映在专家判断中，以及 DELTA 中使用 LLM 评判者的基于准则的评估模块是否与专家判断一致。结果表明，DELTA 的评估模块产生的排序比文本相似度指标更贴近专家判断。此外，专家普遍更偏好由 LLM 评判者排名前三的 LLM 生成拆解，而非人工创建的拆解，并表示愿意采用 DELTA。","tl":"LLM 评判者的用户故事拆解排序比文本相似度更贴近专家","au":["Delina Ly","Fatma Başak Aydemir","Fabiano Dalpiaz"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","tg":["llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["user story decomposition","agile task generation","prompting strategies","LLM-as-a-judge","expert evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/262/x","pu":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837558"},{"id":"p01282","v":"ASE 2026","k":"Research Track","t":"Certified Program Synthesis with a Multi-modal Verifier","tz":"借助多模态验证器实现可认证的程序合成","a":"Certified program synthesis (aka vericoding) is the process of automatically generating a program, its formal specification, and a machine-checkable proof of their alignment from a natural-language description. Two challenges make vericoding difficult. First, specifications synthesised from natural language are often either too weak to be meaningful or too strong to be implementable, yet existing approaches lack systematic means to detect such defects. Second, the landscape of program verifiers is fragmented: each tool supports a particular reasoning mode -- auto-active (e.g., Dafny, Verus) or interactive (e.g., Coq, Lean) -- with its own trade-off between automation and expressivity. This forces every synthesis methodology to be tailored to a single verification paradigm, limiting the class of tasks it can handle effectively. We overcome both challenges by structuring the certified synthesis workflow around a multi-modal verifier -- a single tool combining dynamic validation, automated proofs, and interactive proof scripting in one foundational framework. We realise this idea in LeetProof, an agentic pipeline built on Velvet, a multi-modal verifier embedded in Lean. Multi-modality enables LeetProof to validate generated specifications via randomised property-based testing before any code is synthesised, decompose the synthesis task into sub-problems guided by verification conditions, and delegate residual proof obligations to frontier AI provers specialised for Lean. We evaluate LeetProof on benchmarks derived from prior work on certified synthesis. Our specification validation uncovers defects in existing reference benchmarks, and LeetProof's staged pipeline achieves a significantly higher rate of fully certified solutions than a single-mode baseline at the same budget -- consistently across two frontier LLM backends.","az":"可认证程序合成（又称 vericoding）指从自然语言描述自动生成程序、其形式化规约以及二者一致性的机器可检查证明。有两项挑战使 vericoding 变得困难。第一，从自然语言合成的规约往往要么太弱以致没有意义，要么太强以致无法实现，而现有方法缺乏系统手段来发现这类缺陷。第二，程序验证器的生态是割裂的：每个工具只支持某一种推理模式——自动主动式（如 Dafny、Verus）或交互式（如 Coq、Lean）——各自在自动化与表达力之间做出取舍。这迫使每种合成方法都只能围绕单一验证范式定制，限制了它能有效处理的任务类别。我们通过把可认证合成工作流构建在一个多模态验证器之上来同时克服这两个挑战——该工具在一个基础框架中融合了动态验证、自动化证明与交互式证明脚本编写。我们在 LeetProof 中实现了这一思路，它是构建于 Velvet（一个嵌入 Lean 的多模态验证器）之上的智能体流水线。多模态性使 LeetProof 能在合成任何代码之前，通过随机化的基于性质的测试来验证生成的规约，依据验证条件把合成任务分解为子问题，并把残余的证明义务委派给专门面向 Lean 的前沿 AI 证明器。我们在源自既有可认证合成工作的基准上评估 LeetProof。我们的规约验证发现了现有参考基准中的缺陷，并且在相同预算下，LeetProof 的分阶段流水线在两个前沿 LLM 后端上都一致地取得了显著更高的完全认证解答率。","tl":"用多模态验证器先验规约再分阶段合成带证明的程序","au":["Yueyang Feng","Dipesh Kafle","Vladimir Gladshtein","Vitaly Kurin","George Pîrlea","Qiyuan Zhao","Peter Müller","Ilya Sergey"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["certified program synthesis","vericoding","Lean","multi-modal verifier","specification validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/263/x"},{"id":"p01283","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Testing Computation Pushdown in Distributed Database Systems","tz":"分布式数据库系统中计算下推的测试","a":"Computation pushdown is a critical technique in distributed database management systems (DBMSs), enabling certain operations to be executed closer to the data to reduce network overhead and improve performance. However, its behavior depends on multiple factors beyond the input query itself, such as data distribution and resource utilization. This makes it difficult to validate correctness using only input queries in a black-box manner. Existing testing methods that rely solely on query manipulation cannot effectively control or predict pushdown behavior, and are therefore insufficient. In this paper, we introduce Controlled Pushdown Execution (CPE), a white-box method that enables systematic validation of computation pushdown. CPE modifies the source code of DBMSs to forbid a specific pushdown operator and compares the results. Any discrepancy reveals a bug. Our study shows that CPE can control all supported operators across different systems. We applied CPE to three production-grade distributed DBMSs: CockroachDB, TiDB, and YugabyteDB. CPE found 25 previously unknown and unique bugs, 14 of which are logic bugs—incorrect results. CPE finds 3 more bugs than historical bugs and can reproduce all historical bugs. Beyond computation pushdown, the core insight of controllable execution can generalize to other contexts (e.g., transaction schedule), providing a systematic way to uncover subtle logic bugs.","az":"计算下推是分布式数据库管理系统（DBMS）中的关键技术，它让某些操作在更靠近数据的位置执行，以减少网络开销并提升性能。然而，其行为取决于输入查询之外的多个因素，例如数据分布与资源利用率。这使得仅凭输入查询以黑盒方式验证其正确性十分困难。仅依赖查询变换的现有测试方法无法有效控制或预测下推行为，因此并不充分。本文提出“受控下推执行”（Controlled Pushdown Execution, CPE），一种可系统验证计算下推的白盒方法。CPE 修改 DBMS 的源代码以禁用某个特定下推算子，并比较结果。任何差异都揭示一个缺陷。我们的研究表明，CPE 能在不同系统中控制所有受支持的算子。我们把 CPE 应用于三个生产级分布式 DBMS：CockroachDB、TiDB 和 YugabyteDB。CPE 发现了 25 个此前未知且互不重复的缺陷，其中 14 个是逻辑缺陷——即结果不正确。CPE 发现的缺陷数是历史缺陷的 3 倍，并且能复现全部历史缺陷。除计算下推之外，可控执行这一核心洞见还可推广到其他场景（例如事务调度），为系统性地发现微妙的逻辑缺陷提供了一条路径。","tl":"白盒禁用下推算子做差分比对，揪出分布式库逻辑缺陷","au":["Jinsheng Ba","Zuming Jiang","Zhendong Su"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["computation pushdown","distributed DBMS testing","logic bugs","white-box differential testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/1/x"},{"id":"p01284","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Do Coverage and Mutation Scores of LLM-Generated Test Suites Correlate With Their Effectiveness? (Replicability Study)","tz":"LLM 生成测试套件的覆盖率与变异得分是否与其有效性相关？（可复现性研究）","a":"Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have driven growing interest in using LLMs to automate test generation. Prior work commonly evaluates generated test suites using proxy metrics such as code coverage and mutation score. However, studies by Inozemtseva et al. and Papadakis et al. show that, for human-written tests, correlations among coverage, mutation, and real-bug detection can largely vanish once test suite size is controlled, raising concerns about the validity of evaluations based on proxy metrics. It also remains unclear whether these conclusions carry over to LLM-generated tests, given that prevailing LLM-based test-generation workflows differ substantially from traditional approaches. In this paper, we conduct a large-scale replication study of these two prior works using a wide range of test suites generated by a diverse set of LLMs, and re-examine the relationships among coverage, mutation, and real-bug detection effectiveness. Our findings diverge substantially from prior results. We show that the usefulness of coverage and mutation is highly context-dependent: in regression-style settings where the code provided to the LLM can be reasonably assumed bug-free, these metrics can provide meaningful signals when comparing across models; in another common scenario where the code-under-test may already be buggy and the goal is to expose the bug within code-under-test, they no longer serve as reliable indicators. We also find little evidence that test suite size is a dominant confounder for correlations among coverage, mutation, and real-bug detection for LLM-generated tests. Based on these findings, we discuss how to interpret results from prior studies and provide actionable guidance for evaluating LLM-based test generation.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展激发了用 LLM 自动化测试生成的浓厚兴趣。已有工作通常用代码覆盖率、变异得分等代理指标来评估生成的测试套件。然而，Inozemtseva 等人与 Papadakis 等人的研究表明，对人工编写的测试而言，一旦控制测试套件规模，覆盖率、变异与真实缺陷检测之间的相关性可能基本消失，这令基于代理指标的评估的效度令人担忧。同时，鉴于主流的基于 LLM 的测试生成工作流与传统方法差异很大，这些结论是否适用于 LLM 生成的测试仍不清楚。本文使用由多种 LLM 生成的大量测试套件，对上述两项先前工作开展大规模复现研究，重新审视覆盖率、变异与真实缺陷检测有效性之间的关系。我们的发现与先前结果有显著分歧。我们表明覆盖率与变异的有用性高度依赖场景：在回归式场景中，若可以合理假定提供给 LLM 的代码无缺陷，这些指标在跨模型比较时能提供有意义的信号；而在另一种常见场景中，若被测代码本身可能已有缺陷、目标是暴露其中的缺陷，这些指标便不再是可靠的指示器。我们还发现几乎没有证据表明测试套件规模是 LLM 生成测试中覆盖率、变异与真实缺陷检测相关性的主导混淆因素。基于这些发现，我们讨论了应如何解读先前研究的结果，并为评估基于 LLM 的测试生成提供了可操作的指导。","tl":"复现表明代理指标对 LLM 测试的效度高度依场景而定","au":["Junda Zhao","Shurui Zhou","Eldan Cohen"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["reproducibility-replication","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["replication study","code coverage","mutation score","LLM test generation","metric validity"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/2/x"},{"id":"p01285","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"BashCoder-R1: Towards Robust and Explainable Bash Script Generation with Robustness-Aware Group Relative Policy Optimization","tz":"BashCoder-R1：面向鲁棒且可解释的 Bash 脚本生成的鲁棒性感知 GRPO","a":"Bash scripts underpin system administration, DevOps automation, and Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD), where code quality directly determines system stability and security. Yet when Large Language Models (LLMs) are tasked with generating such scripts, two problems compound each other: models produce code without any accompanying justification for their design choices, and this absence of scrutiny correlates with scripts that silently harbor robustness flaws, including mishandled edge cases, unchecked failure modes, and fragile assumptions about the execution environment. We present BashCoder-R1, a framework that tackles both problems jointly, treating explainability as a design goal rather than a byproduct of correctness. The training pipeline proceeds in three stages. Continual Pre-training (CPT) first adapts the base model to the syntactic conventions and idioms specific to Bash. We then curate thousands of expert-validated reasoning-and-code samples and use them for Long Chain-of-Thought Supervised Fine-Tuning (L-CoT SFT), training the model to reproduce the deliberative, risk-averse thinking pattern of an experienced system administrator before it writes any code. Finally, Robustness-Aware Group Relative Policy Optimization (R-GRPO) directly refines the generation policy against a weighted reward combining syntax correctness, robustness as verified by the static analyzer shellcheck, and adherence to the required reasoning format. We evaluate BashCoder-R1 on BashBench, a benchmark we construct from 952 real-world automation tasks (773 single-line commands and 179 multi-line scripts), against a wide range of state-of-the-art baselines. BashCoder-R1 attains SyntaxPass of 100.00%/94.97%, RobustWarnRate of 4.01%/16.47%, RobustPass of 95.99%/79.33%, FuncRate of 93.01%/93.85%, and FullRate of 90.04%/73.18% on single-line/multi-line tasks respectively, a relative FullRate improvement of 37.82% and 20.18% over the strongest baseline, DeepSeek-V3.2 (Reasoning). Human evaluation across Functionality, Robustness, and Clarity further confirms that BashCoder-R1’s reasoning chains are rated highest in quality among all compared systems.","az":"Bash 脚本支撑着系统管理、DevOps 自动化与持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD），其代码质量直接决定系统的稳定性与安全性。然而，当大语言模型（LLM）被要求生成此类脚本时，两个问题相互叠加：模型生成代码时不给出任何设计选择的理由，而这种缺乏审视的状态又与脚本中潜藏的鲁棒性缺陷相关，包括边界情况处理不当、失败模式未被检查以及对执行环境的脆弱假设。我们提出 BashCoder-R1，一个同时应对这两个问题的框架，把可解释性视为设计目标而非正确性的副产品。其训练流水线分三个阶段。持续预训练（CPT）首先让基座模型适应 Bash 特有的语法惯例与习语。随后我们整理了数千条经专家验证的“推理+代码”样本，用于长思维链监督微调（L-CoT SFT），训练模型在写下任何代码之前重现资深系统管理员那种审慎、规避风险的思考模式。最后，鲁棒性感知的组相对策略优化（R-GRPO）以加权奖励直接精炼生成策略，该奖励综合了语法正确性、由静态分析器 shellcheck 验证的鲁棒性以及对所需推理格式的遵循。我们在 BashBench 上评估 BashCoder-R1，该基准由我们从 952 个真实自动化任务（773 条单行命令与 179 个多行脚本）构建，并与大量最新基线比较。BashCoder-R1 在单行/多行任务上分别取得 SyntaxPass 100.00%/94.97%、RobustWarnRate 4.01%/16.47%、RobustPass 95.99%/79.33%、FuncRate 93.01%/93.85%、FullRate 90.04%/73.18%，FullRate 相对最强基线 DeepSeek-V3.2（Reasoning）分别提升 37.82% 和 20.18%。在功能性、鲁棒性与清晰度三方面的人工评估进一步确认，BashCoder-R1 的推理链在所有被比较系统中质量评分最高。","tl":"用 shellcheck 奖励的 GRPO 训练出鲁棒可解释的 Bash 生成模型","au":["Lei Yu","Peng Wang","Jia Xu","Jingyuan Zhang","Xin Wang","Jiajia Ma","Li Yang","Changzhi Deng","Zenghua Wang","Fengjun Zhang"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Bash script generation","GRPO","robustness reward","shellcheck","BashBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/3/x"},{"id":"p01286","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"XSearch: Explainable Code Search via Concept-to-Code Alignment","tz":"XSearch：基于概念到代码对齐的可解释代码搜索","a":"With the emergence of deep learning, semantic code search has been widely adopted in both academia and industry. These approaches embed natural-language queries and code snippets into a shared embedding space and retrieve results based on vector similarity. Despite their strong performance on benchmark datasets, they often suffer from poor explainability and generalization. Retrieved code may appear semantically similar yet miss critical functional requirements of the query, while providing no explanation of why the result was retrieved. Moreover, such failures become more severe under distribution shift, where models struggle to generalize to unseen benchmarks. In this work, we propose XSearch, an intrinsically explainable code search framework. Our key insight is that, by relying on global embedding similarity, all existing retrievers inherently take an inductive view. They learn statistical patterns, rather than truly understand the query’s functional requirements. Therefore, we address the problem by reformulating code search as a deductive concept alignment problem. At a high level, XSearch (i) identifies functional concepts in the query and (ii) explicitly aligns them with corresponding code statements. This explain-then-predict design not only produces inherent concept-level explanations, but also mitigates shortcut learning that harms out-of-distribution generalization. We train an encoder with explicit concept-alignment objectives and perform retrieval through explicit matching between query concepts and code statements. Experiments show that, when trained on CodeSearchNet with a small model size (GraphCodeBERT with 125M parameters), XSearch improves performance on out-of-distribution benchmarks from 0.02 to 0.33 (15×) over eight state-of-the-art retrievers, and consistently outperforms both encoder-based and decoder-based baselines with up to 7B parameters. A controlled user study further demonstrates that concept-alignment explanations enable users to accept or reject retrieved results both faster and more accurately.","az":"随着深度学习的兴起，语义代码搜索已在学术界与工业界被广泛采用。这类方法把自然语言查询与代码片段嵌入到共享的嵌入空间，并依据向量相似度检索结果。尽管它们在基准数据集上表现强劲，却常常可解释性与泛化性都很差。检索到的代码可能语义上看起来相似，却遗漏了查询的关键功能需求，而且完全不解释该结果为何被检索出来。更严重的是，在分布偏移下这类失败会加剧，模型难以泛化到未见过的基准。本工作提出 XSearch，一个内在可解释的代码搜索框架。我们的关键洞见是：由于依赖全局嵌入相似度，所有现有检索器本质上都采取归纳视角——它们学到的是统计模式，而非真正理解查询的功能需求。因此，我们把代码搜索重新表述为演绎式的概念对齐问题。在高层上，XSearch (i) 识别查询中的功能概念，(ii) 将其显式地与对应的代码语句对齐。这种“先解释后预测”的设计不仅产生概念级的内在解释，还缓解了损害分布外泛化的捷径学习。我们用显式的概念对齐目标训练编码器，并通过查询概念与代码语句之间的显式匹配来完成检索。实验表明，在 CodeSearchNet 上以较小模型规模（1.25 亿参数的 GraphCodeBERT）训练时，XSearch 相较八个最新检索器把分布外基准上的性能从 0.02 提升到 0.33（15 倍），并持续超越参数量高达 70 亿的编码器类与解码器类基线。一项受控用户研究进一步表明，概念对齐解释让用户能更快且更准确地接受或拒绝检索结果。","tl":"把代码搜索改写为概念到语句的演绎对齐，兼得解释与泛化","au":["Liu Yiming","Ruofan Liu","Yun Lin","Zicong Zhang","Weiyu Kong","Pengnian Qi","Xiao Cheng","Weinan Zhang","Qianxiang Wang","Linpeng Huang"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","human-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code search","concept alignment","explainability","out-of-distribution generalization","GraphCodeBERT"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/4/x"},{"id":"p01287","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"E4R-Reviewer: Effective and Explainable Automated Code Review via End-to-End Reasoning-Guided Alignment","tz":"E4R-Reviewer：通过端到端推理引导对齐实现高效且可解释的自动代码评审","a":"Code review is a key practice for ensuring software quality and maintainability. Despite progress in Automated Code Review (ACR), existing methods face two core challenges: (1) Isolated Task Modeling. Current approaches often model and optimize subtasks in ACR independently, ignoring the inherent logical order and internal dependencies among them which affects the effectiveness of ACR. (2) Lack of Explainability. At the task level, the absence of explanatory information in review comments increases developers’ cognitive load; at the model level, the black-box nature fundamentally undermines developer trust. To address these challenges, we propose E4R-Reviewer, improving the Effectiveness and Explainability of ACR via End-to-End Reasoning-guided alignment. For effectiveness, E4R-Reviewer unifies multiple fine-grained ACR subtasks into a single end-to-end reasoning process, enabling cross-task knowledge sharing and allowing the model to explicitly complete a reasoning chain of “quality estimation–issue localization–issue classification–issue description–fix suggestion–code refinement” in one generation. Meanwhile, we adopt a Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO)-based reinforcement-learning alignment, treating the reasoning steps as optimizable intermediate objectives. We design subtask-specific rewards and integrate them via curriculum-inspired, multi-stage reward fusion that follows the real-world review workflow. For explainability, E4R-Reviewer produces reasoning process and generates structured review results covering all fine-grained ACR subtasks, improving the transparency and explainability of the review results. Extensive evaluations on public, real-world datasets demonstrate that E4R-Reviewer significantly outperforms existing methods and achieves state-of-the-art performance: a 74.61% F1-score in quality estimation and +22.96% CodeBLEU in code refinement. Furthermore, Large Language Model (LLM) and human evaluation further confirm the superiority of E4R-Reviewer in terms of effectiveness and explainability.","az":"代码评审是保障软件质量与可维护性的关键实践。尽管自动代码评审（ACR）已有进展，现有方法仍面临两大核心挑战：(1) 孤立的任务建模。当前方法往往独立地建模与优化 ACR 中的各个子任务，忽视它们之间固有的逻辑顺序与内部依赖，从而影响 ACR 的有效性。(2) 缺乏可解释性。在任务层面，评审意见中缺少解释性信息会加重开发者的认知负担；在模型层面，黑盒特性从根本上削弱开发者的信任。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 E4R-Reviewer，通过端到端推理引导对齐来提升 ACR 的有效性与可解释性。在有效性方面，E4R-Reviewer 把多个细粒度 ACR 子任务统一为单一的端到端推理过程，实现跨任务知识共享，使模型能在一次生成中显式完成“质量评估—问题定位—问题分类—问题描述—修复建议—代码精化”的推理链。同时，我们采用基于组相对策略优化（GRPO）的强化学习对齐，把推理步骤视为可优化的中间目标。我们设计了子任务专用奖励，并通过受课程学习启发的多阶段奖励融合按真实评审工作流加以整合。在可解释性方面，E4R-Reviewer 产出推理过程并生成覆盖全部细粒度 ACR 子任务的结构化评审结果，提升了评审结果的透明度与可解释性。在公开真实数据集上的大量评估表明，E4R-Reviewer 显著优于现有方法并达到最新水平：质量评估 F1 为 74.61%，代码精化 CodeBLEU 提升 22.96%。此外，大语言模型评估与人工评估进一步确认了 E4R-Reviewer 在有效性与可解释性上的优势。","tl":"把代码评审各子任务串成一条 GRPO 优化的端到端推理链","au":["Yifei Liu","Xizhi Hou","Li Yang","Huan Liu","Chen Zhu","Fengjun Zhang","Chun Zuo"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated code review","GRPO","reasoning-guided alignment","explainability","code refinement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/5/x"},{"id":"p01288","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Classification, Root Cause Analysis, and Repair Recommendations for Failed Mobile Testing by Specialized LLM","tz":"用专用大语言模型对失败的移动测试进行自动分类、根因分析与修复建议","a":"Engineers utilize test scripts to conduct testing on mobile applications to ensure software reliability. In industrial settings, failures in mobile application testing stem not only from faults in the program or scripts but also from other aspects, such as the testing environment, making it challenging to apply existing automated analysis methods in such settings. Furthermore, mobile testing in industrial contexts generates a large volume of artifacts, such as screenshots and logs, and involves diverse device models, varied test environments, and complex functionalities. All these factors make the manual analysis of failed mobile tests a process that is typically time-consuming, costly, and labor-intensive. Large language models (LLMs) with strong logical reasoning capabilities offer a novel perspective for automated analysis of failed mobile tests. However, due to their limited knowledge of mobile testing, general LLMs can only achieve sub-optimal effectiveness in these tasks. To address these challenges, we propose AnaDroid, a novel LLM training framework specifically tailored for analyzing failed mobile tests. AnaDroid performs feature preprocessing for failed mobile tests and trains the large language model through two novel, tailored training procedures. Specifically, AnaDroid first leverages bidirectional pre-training to instill the domain-specific knowledge and reasoning capabilities required for failed test analysis into the model. AnaDroid further employs preference optimization to enhance the model’s capacity to capture critical information within the input context, thereby further improving its analytical effectiveness. Through extensive evaluations across six open-source LLMs of diverse architectures and scales on a large-scale industrial dataset of 284k failed mobile testing scripts, AnaDroid outperformed all 4 baselines across three analysis tasks. Furthermore, during a month-long deployment within a global company’s testing system, demonstrated its practical utility by successfully providing root cause and repair recommendations for 78% and 81% of the 11,304 failed tests, respectively.","az":"工程师使用测试脚本对移动应用进行测试以保障软件可靠性。在工业环境中，移动应用测试的失败不仅源于程序或脚本中的故障，还来自测试环境等其他方面，这使得现有自动化分析方法难以在此类场景中应用。此外，工业场景下的移动测试会产生大量制品，如截图与日志，并涉及多样的设备型号、各异的测试环境与复杂的功能。所有这些因素使得人工分析失败的移动测试通常耗时、昂贵且劳动密集。具备强大逻辑推理能力的大语言模型（LLM）为失败移动测试的自动分析提供了新视角。然而，由于对移动测试的知识有限，通用 LLM 在这些任务上只能取得次优效果。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 AnaDroid，一个专为分析失败移动测试而定制的新型 LLM 训练框架。AnaDroid 对失败的移动测试做特征预处理，并通过两种新颖的定制训练流程来训练大语言模型。具体而言，AnaDroid 首先利用双向预训练，把失败测试分析所需的领域知识与推理能力注入模型；随后采用偏好优化增强模型捕获输入上下文中关键信息的能力，进一步提升分析效果。在一个包含 28.4 万条失败移动测试脚本的大规模工业数据集上，对六个不同架构与规模的开源 LLM 开展的大量评估表明，AnaDroid 在三项分析任务上均优于全部 4 个基线。此外，在一家跨国公司测试系统中为期一个月的部署里，该工具分别为 11,304 个失败测试中的 78% 和 81% 成功给出了根因与修复建议，展示了其实际效用。","tl":"双向预训练加偏好优化的专用模型分诊工业移动测试失败","au":["Chun Li","Fei Wang","Minxue Pan","Zhong Li","Mengliang Zeng","Bin Zhang","Xuejiao Yu","Boyun Wang","Kaijian Hua","Xuandong Li"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale","multimodal"],"kw":["mobile test failure analysis","root cause analysis","domain-specific LLM training","preference optimization","industrial deployment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/6/x"},{"id":"p01289","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LLMutantKiller: Using Large Language Models to Generate Tests that Kill Mutants","tz":"LLMutantKiller：用大语言模型生成能杀死变异体的测试","a":"The primary goal of mutation testing is to assess the quality of an application’s test suite. This is accomplished by introducing syntactic changes into a program and determining if any test failures occur for the resulting mutated program, commonly referred to as a mutant. If so, the mutant is said to be killed, confirming that the test suite is of sufficient quality to detect the introduced fault. A problem arises if a mutant does not impact the behavior of any test. Such a surviving mutant may occur for two reasons: either it involves a semantics- preserving program transformation or the test suite is not strong enough. Determining why a mutant survives often involves complex, non-local reasoning. This paper presents an LLM-based test generation technique for killing surviving mutants, implemented in a tool called LLMutantKiller. The technique is feedback-directed in the sense that if a test is produced that does not kill a given mutant, the LLM is re-prompted up to a specified number of times with scenario-specific feedback such as syntax errors, dependency violations, or execution logs (e.g., failing assertions) and asked to try again. We evaluate LLMutantKiller on 915 randomly selected surviving mutants that were produced by StrykerJS, a state-of-the-art mutation testing tool, taken from 13 open-source JavaScript/TypeScript applications. The results show that LLMutantKiller kills up to 95.3% of the surviving mutants classified as inducing behavioral changes and that it rarely produces invalid tests.","az":"变异测试的首要目标是评估应用测试套件的质量。其做法是向程序中引入语法改动，并判断由此得到的变异程序（通常称为变异体）是否会导致测试失败。若会，则称该变异体被杀死，说明测试套件质量足以检测出所引入的故障。问题在于，某个变异体可能不影响任何测试的行为。这种存活的变异体出现有两种原因：要么它涉及一次保语义的程序变换，要么测试套件不够强。判断变异体为何存活往往需要复杂的非局部推理。本文提出一种基于 LLM 的测试生成技术以杀死存活变异体，并实现为工具 LLMutantKiller。该技术是反馈导向的：若生成的测试没能杀死给定变异体，就用场景相关的反馈（如语法错误、依赖违规或执行日志，例如失败的断言）重新提示 LLM，最多重复指定次数，并要求其再试一次。我们在 915 个随机选取的存活变异体上评估 LLMutantKiller，这些变异体由最新变异测试工具 StrykerJS 在 13 个开源 JavaScript/TypeScript 应用上产生。结果表明，LLMutantKiller 杀死了其中被归类为引起行为改变的变异体的最多 95.3%，且极少产生无效测试。","tl":"反馈迭代提示 LLM 杀死 95% 的存活变异体","au":["Farideh Khalili","Aidan Domondon","Harshit Garg","Frank Tip"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mutation testing","surviving mutants","LLM test generation","feedback-directed","JavaScript"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/7/x"},{"id":"p01290","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Industrial Practice of LLM-based Test Case Carving and Assertion Generation (Experience Paper)","tz":"基于 LLM 的测试用例切取与断言生成的工业实践（经验论文）","a":"Enterprise regression testing for microservice systems is often constrained by incomplete or outdated documentation. In practice, QA engineers frequently rely on real execution traffic to reconstruct business scenarios; however, turning raw traffic into replayable regression tests with stable validation logic remains labor-intensive and error-prone. This paper presents NL2Test, an end-to-end approach and tool that generates executable API regression tests from (i) a natural-language scenario description and (ii) a traffic capture recorded while executing the scenario. NL2Test addresses two coupled tasks: test case carving, which extracts a minimal replayable request sequence and reconstructs data dependencies so that dynamic values are bound from their responses rather than hard-coded; and assertion generation, which produces assertions aligned with business intent while avoiding non-deterministic fields and hallucinated paths. To improve reliability, NL2Test uses LLMs for semantic interpretation and constrained code synthesis, and uses deterministic algorithms for request filtering, dependency confirmation via value consistency, and assertion-path validation. We evaluate NL2Test on 51 industrial regression scenarios extracted from a large consumer-facing Internet company. NL2Test achieves an exact-match rate of 82.4% (42/51), and produces a functionally usable draft in 98.0% (50/51) of scenarios when allowing minor post-edits. In a 9-month production deployment starting in March 2025, NL2Test generated 3,196 test cases with an overall code adoption rate of 85.4%. These results indicate that traffic-grounded generation with deterministic guardrails can substantially reduce manual effort while improving regression automation in complex microservice environments.","az":"微服务系统的企业级回归测试常受限于不完整或过时的文档。实践中，QA 工程师经常依赖真实执行流量来重建业务场景；然而，把原始流量转化为具备稳定校验逻辑的可回放回归测试仍然费时且易错。本文提出 NL2Test，一种端到端方法与工具，可从 (i) 自然语言场景描述与 (ii) 执行该场景时录制的流量捕获中生成可执行的 API 回归测试。NL2Test 解决两个耦合任务：测试用例切取（test case carving），即抽取最小可回放的请求序列并重建数据依赖，使动态值从其响应中绑定而非硬编码；以及断言生成，即产生与业务意图一致、同时避免非确定性字段与幻觉路径的断言。为提升可靠性，NL2Test 用 LLM 做语义解释与受约束的代码合成，并用确定性算法做请求过滤、基于取值一致性的依赖确认以及断言路径校验。我们在从一家大型面向消费者的互联网公司抽取的 51 个工业回归场景上评估 NL2Test。NL2Test 取得 82.4%（42/51）的完全匹配率，并在允许少量后期编辑时于 98.0%（50/51）的场景中产出功能可用的草稿。在 2025 年 3 月开始、为期 9 个月的生产部署中，NL2Test 生成了 3,196 个测试用例，总体代码采纳率为 85.4%。这些结果表明，以流量为依据、辅以确定性护栏的生成方式能大幅减少人工投入，并改进复杂微服务环境中的回归自动化。","tl":"用真实流量加自然语言描述切取可回放微服务回归测试","au":["Haozhen You","Zhen Dong","Jingjing Wang","Qiang Li","Xin Peng"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test case carving","assertion generation","API regression testing","microservices","industrial deployment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/8/x"},{"id":"p01291","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Sifting the Noise: A Comparative Study of LLM Agents in Vulnerability False Positive Filtering","tz":"筛去噪声：LLM 智能体在漏洞误报过滤中的对比研究","a":"Static Application Security Testing (SAST) tools are essential for identifying software vulnerabilities, but they often produce a high volume of false positives (FPs), imposing a substantial manual triage burden on developers. Recent advances in Large Language Model (LLM) agents offer a promising direction by enabling iterative reasoning, tool use, and environment interaction to refine SAST alerts. However, the comparative effectiveness of different LLM-based agent architectures for FP filtering remains poorly understood. In this paper, we present a comparative study of three state-of-the-art LLM-based agent frameworks, i.e., Aider, OpenHands, and SWE-agent, for vulnerability FP filtering. We evaluate these frameworks using the vulnerabilities from the OWASP Benchmark and real-world open-source Java projects. The experimental results show that LLM-based agents can remove the majority of SAST noise, reducing an initial FP detection rate of over 92% on the OWASP Benchmark to as low as 6.3% in the best configuration. However, the benefits of agents are strongly backbone- and CWE-dependent: agentic frameworks significantly outperform vanilla prompting for stronger models such as Claude Sonnet 4 and GPT-5, but yield limited or inconsistent gains for weaker backbones. Moreover, aggressive FP reduction can come at the cost of suppressing true vulnerabilities, highlighting important trade-offs. Finally, we observe large disparities in computational cost across agent frameworks. Overall, our study demonstrates that LLM-based agents are a powerful but non-uniform solution for SAST FP filtering, and that their practical deployment requires careful consideration of agent design, backbone model choice, vulnerability category, and operational cost.","az":"静态应用安全测试（SAST）工具对识别软件漏洞至关重要，但它们往往产生大量误报（FP），给开发者带来沉重的人工分诊负担。大语言模型（LLM）智能体的最新进展提供了一个有前景的方向，可通过迭代推理、工具使用与环境交互来精炼 SAST 告警。然而，不同 LLM 智能体架构在误报过滤上的相对效果仍缺乏了解。本文对三个最新的基于 LLM 的智能体框架（Aider、OpenHands 与 SWE-agent）在漏洞误报过滤上的表现开展对比研究。我们使用 OWASP Benchmark 中的漏洞以及真实世界的开源 Java 项目来评估这些框架。实验结果表明，基于 LLM 的智能体能消除大部分 SAST 噪声，把 OWASP Benchmark 上超过 92% 的初始误报率在最佳配置下降至低至 6.3%。然而，智能体带来的收益强烈依赖骨干模型与 CWE 类别：对 Claude Sonnet 4 与 GPT-5 这类更强模型，智能体框架显著优于朴素提示；但对较弱骨干模型，收益有限或不稳定。此外，激进的误报削减可能以压制真实漏洞为代价，凸显了重要的取舍。最后，我们观察到各智能体框架之间的计算成本差异巨大。总体而言，我们的研究表明基于 LLM 的智能体是 SAST 误报过滤的强大但不均衡的方案，其实际部署需要谨慎考量智能体设计、骨干模型选择、漏洞类别与运行成本。","tl":"对比三种智能体框架过滤 SAST 误报的收益与代价","au":["Yunpeng Xiong","Ting Zhang"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","agentic","empirical-study"],"kw":["SAST false positives","LLM agents","OWASP Benchmark","alert triage","comparative study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/9/x"},{"id":"p01292","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Datura: Progressive Red Teaming Testing for Tool Invocation Chain in LLM Agents","tz":"Datura：面向 LLM 智能体工具调用链的渐进式红队测试","a":"LLM agents that invoke external tools face critical safety vulnerabilities when malicious manipulations exploit their implicit trust in tool outputs and metadata. However, identifying these vulnerabilities through testing is challenging due to the need to bypass safety guardrails with semantically legitimate inputs, the difficulty in characterizing successful attacks amid implicit tool trust, and the requirement to maintain logical consistency across fragile state-dependent execution chains. In this paper, we first conduct an empirical study to investigate how external tools influence the reasoning of agents. Guided by the findings, we propose Datura, an automated red teaming testing framework that exposes safety vulnerabilities through chained tool manipulation. Through a five-stage workflow, Datura dynamically generates test cases where each individual step appears legitimate yet collectively achieves harmful outcomes. We evaluate Datura across five LLMs and 740 safety-critical tasks under five defense including real-world safety mechanisms. Datura achieves 94.86–99.59% attack success rate, outperforming the strongest baseline by 7.56–24.32 percentage points, and maintains 78.78–95.54% effectiveness across defenses where baselines drop to near-zero. The artifact is available on Anonymous GitHub.","az":"调用外部工具的 LLM 智能体在遭遇恶意操纵利用其对工具输出与元数据的隐式信任时，会面临严重的安全漏洞。然而，通过测试识别这些漏洞颇具挑战：需要用语义上合法的输入绕过安全护栏，在隐式工具信任之下难以刻画攻击是否成功，还要在脆弱的、依赖状态的执行链中保持逻辑一致性。本文首先开展实证研究，考察外部工具如何影响智能体的推理。在这些发现指导下，我们提出 Datura，一个通过链式工具操纵暴露安全漏洞的自动化红队测试框架。Datura 采用五阶段工作流，动态生成测试用例，使其中每一步单独看都合法，却共同导致有害后果。我们在五个 LLM、740 个安全关键任务以及包含真实安全机制在内的五种防御下评估 Datura。Datura 取得 94.86–99.59% 的攻击成功率，比最强基线高出 7.56–24.32 个百分点，并在基线几乎归零的各类防御下仍保持 78.78–95.54% 的有效性。相关制品已在匿名 GitHub 上公开。","tl":"用逐步合法的链式工具操纵红队测试智能体工具调用链","au":["Yuchen Shao","Ziqun Bao","Yuheng Huang","Yuling Shi","Mingyu Weng","Yiwen Sun","Long Yang","Lei Ma","Ting Su","Chengcheng Wan"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"agent-tool-use-and-function-calling","tg":["security","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["red teaming","tool invocation chain","LLM agent safety","attack success rate","guardrail bypass"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/10/x"},{"id":"p01293","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Learning from the Test: Self-Referential Differential Testing for Deep RL Agents","tz":"从测试中学习：面向深度强化学习智能体的自引用差分测试","a":"Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) has achieved significant success in complex decision-making problems. As DRL systems are increasingly deployed in real-world applications, ensuring their quality and reliability is paramount. Current works primarily focus on detecting safety-critical failures, often neglecting policy optimality, which can lead to reduced efficiency, user distrust, and economic losses. This oversight, compounded by the inherent “testing oracle problem” for optimality, leaves a significant gap in comprehensively evaluating DRL systems. To address this gap, we propose Delta (Differential Testing for DRL Agents), a novel and comprehensive framework that automatically identifies both safety-critical and optimality bugs in DRL agents. Delta employs a two-phase approach: (1) Safety Testing, where the Agent Under Test (AUT) is evaluated for catastrophic failures while collecting data from its decision-making policy, and (2) Optimality Testing, where this collected data from the prior phase is used to train a challenger agent via Offline Reinforcement Learning. Differential testing is then performed by comparing the challenger agent against the AUT; instances, where the challenger achieves higher cumulative rewards indicate optimality issues in the AUT. We demonstrate Delta’s effectiveness across five environments. We investigate the effectiveness of three offline RL algorithms (BC, BCQ, and CQL) in generating challenger agents. Experimental results demonstrate that safety testing datasets are valuable for training competent DRL agents. Challenger agents trained with BCQ proved most effective for identifying optimality issues within the framework of Delta. Across the five environments, Delta uncovered an average of 2,517 optimality issues, outperforming the baseline methods by 50.2%.","az":"深度强化学习（DRL）在复杂决策问题上取得了显著成功。随着 DRL 系统越来越多地部署于真实应用，保障其质量与可靠性至关重要。现有工作主要聚焦于检测安全关键失效，往往忽视策略最优性，而这可能导致效率下降、用户不信任与经济损失。这一忽视再加上最优性固有的“测试预言问题”，使得全面评估 DRL 系统存在显著空白。为填补这一空白，我们提出 Delta（Differential Testing for DRL Agents），一个能自动识别 DRL 智能体中安全关键缺陷与最优性缺陷的新颖且全面的框架。Delta 采用两阶段方法：(1) 安全测试，评估被测智能体（AUT）是否出现灾难性失效，同时从其决策策略中收集数据；(2) 最优性测试，用前一阶段收集的数据通过离线强化学习训练一个挑战者智能体。随后通过将挑战者智能体与 AUT 比较来完成差分测试；挑战者获得更高累计奖励的实例即表明 AUT 存在最优性问题。我们在五个环境中展示了 Delta 的有效性。我们考察了三种离线 RL 算法（BC、BCQ 与 CQL）在生成挑战者智能体上的效果。实验结果表明，安全测试数据集对训练有能力的 DRL 智能体很有价值；在 Delta 框架内，用 BCQ 训练的挑战者智能体在识别最优性问题上最为有效。在五个环境中，Delta 平均发现 2,517 个最优性问题，比基线方法高出 50.2%。","tl":"用离线 RL 训出挑战者智能体来差分暴露策略非最优缺陷","au":["Junda He","Jieke Shi","Zhou Yang","Mingfei Cheng","David Lo"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["deep reinforcement learning testing","differential testing","offline RL","optimality bugs","oracle problem"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/11/x"},{"id":"p01294","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CLASScanner: Efficient C++ Class Recovery from Binaries Driven by Object Flow Graphs","tz":"CLASScanner：由对象流图驱动的高效 C++ 二进制类结构恢复","a":"C++ class recovery is fundamental to reverse engineering, serving as a basis for critical downstream tasks such as vulnerability analysis, malware comprehension, and decompiler output optimization. Existing approaches face several challenges, including dependency on virtual function tables and a lack of support for non-polymorphic classes, dependency on high-quality test cases for dynamic analysis, and dependency on computationally expensive reasoning. Furthermore, existing rule-based techniques fail to recover class relationships in non-polymorphic classes, including inheritance and composition, thereby reducing fidelity to original program semantics. To address these problems, we propose CLASScanner, a novel approach for recovering C++ classes from stripped binaries. We design a data-flow abstraction, Object Flow Graph (OFG), to model the behaviors of objects across different contexts throughout their lifecycles. Driven by the OFG, CLASScanner identifies classes and recovers their attributes and methods. We further propose a progressive framework that synergizes static analysis with LLM-based reasoning to infer class inheritance and composition relationships. We evaluate CLASScanner on a dataset of real-world binaries comprising 167,982 functions. It achieved F1-scores of 95.4, 93.7, 75.4, 89.9, and 92.7 in recovering attributes, constructors, destructors, class inheritance, and class composition, respectively. Compared to state-of-the-art approaches, CLASScanner significantly improves the F1-scores while reducing runtime overhead, requiring only 10.3% of the execution time on average, making it promising for real-world reverse engineering tasks.","az":"C++ 类恢复是逆向工程的基础，也是漏洞分析、恶意软件理解与反编译输出优化等关键下游任务的基石。现有方法面临若干挑战，包括依赖虚函数表、不支持非多态类、动态分析依赖高质量测试用例，以及依赖计算代价高昂的推理。此外，现有基于规则的技术无法恢复非多态类中的类关系（包括继承与组合），从而降低了对原始程序语义的还原度。为解决这些问题，我们提出 CLASScanner，一种从剥离符号的二进制中恢复 C++ 类的新方法。我们设计了一种数据流抽象——对象流图（Object Flow Graph, OFG）——来建模对象在其生命周期中跨不同上下文的行为。在 OFG 驱动下，CLASScanner 识别类并恢复其属性与方法。我们进一步提出一个渐进式框架，将静态分析与基于 LLM 的推理协同起来，以推断类的继承与组合关系。我们在一个包含 167,982 个函数的真实二进制数据集上评估 CLASScanner，在恢复属性、构造函数、析构函数、类继承与类组合上分别取得 95.4、93.7、75.4、89.9 与 92.7 的 F1 分数。与最新方法相比，CLASScanner 在显著提升 F1 的同时降低了运行时开销，平均只需 10.3% 的执行时间，使其在真实逆向工程任务中很有前景。","tl":"用对象流图加 LLM 推理恢复非多态 C++ 类及其关系","au":["JiaMing Wang","GongMing Wang","Songtao Yang","Xi Cao","Chao Zhang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["C++ class recovery","object flow graph","binary reverse engineering","inheritance inference","static analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/12/x"},{"id":"p01295","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Metamorphic Coverage","tz":"蜕变覆盖率","a":"Metamorphic testing is a widely used methodology that examines an expected relation between pairs of executions to automatically find bugs, such as correctness bugs. We found that code coverage cannot accurately measure the extent to which code is validated and mutation testing is computationally expensive for evaluating metamorphic testing methods. In this work, we propose Metamorphic Coverage (MC), a coverage metric that examines the distinct code executed by pairs of test inputs within metamorphic testing. Our intuition is that, typically, a bug can be observed if the corresponding code is executed when executing either test input but not the other one, so covering more differential code covered by pairs of test inputs might be more likely to expose bugs. While most metamorphic testing methods have been based on this general intuition, our work defines and systematically evaluates MC on five widely used metamorphic testing methods for testing database engines, compilers, and constraint solvers. The code measured by MC overlaps with the bug-fix locations of 50 of 64 bugs found by metamorphic testing methods, and MC has a stronger positive correlation with bug numbers than line coverage. MC is 4x more sensitive than line coverage in distinguishing testing methods’ effectiveness, and the average value of MC is 6x smaller than line coverage while still capturing the part of the program that is being tested. MC required 359x less time than mutation testing. Based on a case study for an automated database system testing approach, we demonstrate that when used for feedback guidance, MC significantly outperforms code coverage, by finding 41% more bugs. Consequently, this work might have broad applications for assessing metamorphic testing methods and improving test-case generation.","az":"蜕变测试是一种被广泛使用的方法论，它检查成对执行之间的预期关系，以自动发现诸如正确性缺陷等问题。我们发现代码覆盖率无法准确衡量代码被验证的程度，而变异测试在评估蜕变测试方法时计算代价过高。本工作提出蜕变覆盖率（Metamorphic Coverage, MC），一种考察蜕变测试中成对测试输入所执行的差异代码的覆盖度量。我们的直觉是：通常，如果对应代码在执行其中一个测试输入时被执行、而在另一个输入下未被执行，缺陷就可能被观察到；因此覆盖更多由测试输入对产生的差异代码，可能更有机会暴露缺陷。尽管多数蜕变测试方法都基于这一大致直觉，我们的工作对 MC 做出定义，并在用于测试数据库引擎、编译器与约束求解器的五种广泛使用的蜕变测试方法上系统评估。MC 所度量的代码与蜕变测试方法发现的 64 个缺陷中 50 个的缺陷修复位置重叠，且 MC 与缺陷数量的正相关性强于行覆盖率。在区分测试方法有效性上，MC 的敏感度是行覆盖率的 4 倍；MC 的平均值比行覆盖率小 6 倍，却仍能刻画程序中被测试的部分。MC 所需时间比变异测试少 359 倍。基于一项针对自动化数据库系统测试方法的案例研究，我们证明当把 MC 用作反馈引导时，它显著优于代码覆盖率，多发现 41% 的缺陷。因此，本工作在评估蜕变测试方法与改进测试用例生成方面可能具有广泛应用价值。","tl":"提出度量成对执行差异代码的蜕变覆盖率并用作反馈","au":["Jinsheng Ba","Yuancheng Jiang","Manuel Rigger"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["metamorphic testing","coverage metric","differential code","feedback guidance","DBMS testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/13/x"},{"id":"p01296","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RPCSpecter: Detecting Blockchain RPC Bugs through a Specification-Driven, Constraint-Aware Fuzzing Approach","tz":"RPCSpecter：以规约驱动、约束感知的模糊测试检测区块链 RPC 缺陷","a":"Blockchain Remote Procedure Calls (RPCs) serve as the primary interface for interaction between decentralized applications and blockchain networks. Despite their critical role, existing RPC implementations are prone to bugs that are often challenging to detect using traditional testing methods. In this paper, we introduce RPCSpecter, an automated framework for constraint-aware fuzz testing of blockchain RPC Implementations. The core of RPCSpecter is a three-stage process: (1) Constraint Extraction, where implicit semantic dependencies from the documented RPC specifications are parsed and converted into executable constraints, (2) Constraint-Guided Mutation, which generates diverse and semantically valid test inputs based on these constraints, and (3) Bidirectional Assertion, which validates both valid and invalid RPC responses through dynamic checks and self-learning mechanisms. We evaluate RPCSpecter on both Ethereum and Solana, two predominant platforms in the Blockchain ecosystem, with a total of 6 clients, such as Geth, Besu and Agave. The results show that RPCSpecter uncovers a total of 26 previously unknown bugs, including critical errors that are undetectable by existing fuzzers or manual testing, as well as multiple silent semantic inconsistencies. Particularly, 4 of them have been acknowledged, and one of the bugs affecting three major Ethereum clients is confirmed as a vulnerability, with a $3,000 bounty-award. Additionally, we demonstrate how RPCSpecter’s constraint-driven approach significantly improves the efficiency and effectiveness of fuzz testing by systematically guiding mutation to explore boundary conditions and rare edge cases. Our research provides a more robust, scalable, and automated solution for enhancing the reliability and security of blockchain RPC implementations.","az":"区块链远程过程调用（RPC）是去中心化应用与区块链网络交互的主要接口。尽管作用关键，现有 RPC 实现却容易存在缺陷，而这些缺陷往往难以用传统测试方法检出。本文提出 RPCSpecter，一个面向区块链 RPC 实现的约束感知模糊测试自动化框架。RPCSpecter 的核心是一个三阶段流程：(1) 约束抽取，把文档化 RPC 规约中的隐式语义依赖解析并转换为可执行约束；(2) 约束引导的变异，基于这些约束生成多样且语义有效的测试输入；(3) 双向断言，通过动态检查与自学习机制同时校验有效与无效的 RPC 响应。我们在区块链生态中两大主流平台 Ethereum 与 Solana 上评估 RPCSpecter，共涉及 Geth、Besu 与 Agave 等 6 个客户端。结果显示，RPCSpecter 共发现 26 个此前未知的缺陷，其中既有现有模糊测试工具或人工测试无法检出的严重错误，也有多处静默的语义不一致。特别地，其中 4 个已被确认，一个影响三大 Ethereum 客户端的缺陷被确认为漏洞并获得 3,000 美元赏金。此外，我们展示了 RPCSpecter 的约束驱动方法如何通过系统性地引导变异去探索边界条件与罕见边缘情况，从而显著提升模糊测试的效率与效果。我们的研究为增强区块链 RPC 实现的可靠性与安全性提供了更健壮、可扩展且自动化的方案。","tl":"从 RPC 规约抽取约束引导变异，挖出 26 个区块链客户端缺陷","au":["Yuming Xiao","Yuhong Nan","Zhijie Zhong","Mingxi Ye","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["blockchain RPC","constraint-aware fuzzing","specification extraction","Ethereum","Solana"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/14/x"},{"id":"p01297","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TrapHunter: Exposing Covert Pathways in Trap Token Contracts","tz":"TrapHunter：揭露陷阱型代币合约中的隐蔽路径","a":"Standardized token contracts (e.g., ERC-20) form the foundation of digital assets. However, attackers increasingly abuse this standardization to disguise malicious trap tokens. Unlike obvious violations, these contracts employ a strategy of “deceptive adherence”: they strictly adhere to standard protocols to evade detection, while embedding covert logic to defraud users. To address this, we first systematize the trap landscape by proposing a novel taxonomy derived from the intrinsic functional lifecycle of tokens (Generation, Circulation, Persistence, and Observation). We then propose TrapHunter, an end-to-end framework designed to identify these traps and expose covert pathways within these deceptive contracts via intent deviation analysis. Specifically, TrapHunter introduces a unified semantic representation combining Abstract Behavior Trees (ABTs) and Augmented Path Graphs (APGs) to normalize intra-procedural syntax and reveal the hidden execution paths driven by inter-procedural state dependencies. Crucially, it bridges the semantic gap by leveraging LLMs to reason about the behavioral intent of deviations from reference implementations, followed by a fork-based dynamic validation to confirm exploitability. Experimental evaluations on 269 real-world contracts with three LLMs (DeepSeek, GPT, and Gemini) demonstrate that TrapHunter effectively detects all six categories of traps, achieving an average precision of 81.8% and recall of 85.4%, significantly outperforming state-of-the-art tools.","az":"标准化代币合约（如 ERC-20）构成了数字资产的基础。然而，攻击者越来越多地滥用这种标准化来伪装恶意的陷阱代币。与明显的违规不同，这些合约采取“欺骗性遵从”策略：严格遵守标准协议以规避检测，同时嵌入隐蔽逻辑以欺诈用户。为此，我们首先通过提出一种源自代币内在功能生命周期（生成、流通、持有、观察）的新分类法，对陷阱形态进行体系化。随后我们提出 TrapHunter，一个端到端框架，通过意图偏离分析来识别这些陷阱并揭示欺骗性合约中的隐蔽路径。具体而言，TrapHunter 引入一种统一语义表示，结合抽象行为树（ABT）与增强路径图（APG），用以规范化过程内语法并揭示由过程间状态依赖驱动的隐藏执行路径。关键在于，它利用大语言模型推理相对参考实现的行为意图偏离，从而弥合语义鸿沟，并辅以基于分叉（fork）的动态验证来确认可利用性。在 269 个真实合约上使用三种 LLM（DeepSeek、GPT 与 Gemini）的实验评估表明，TrapHunter 能有效检测全部六类陷阱，平均精确率 81.8%、召回率 85.4%，显著优于最新工具。","tl":"用意图偏离分析揭露“形式合规”的陷阱代币隐蔽逻辑","au":["Yin Wu","Yixuan Liu","Yi Li","Chenyang Peng","Hao Wu","Ming Fan","Ting Liu","Haijun Wang"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["trap token contracts","ERC-20","intent deviation analysis","abstract behavior tree","dynamic validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/15/x","pu":"https://liyiweb.com/files/Wu2026TEC.pdf"},{"id":"p01298","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SimiFuzz: Seed–Worker Scheduling for Parallel Fuzzing via Contextual Bandits","tz":"SimiFuzz：通过上下文赌博机实现并行模糊测试的种子—工作者调度","a":"Parallel fuzzing is now a standard way to scale vulnerability discovery, yet its efficiency is still limited by ineffective task allocation among workers. Existing approaches mainly aim to reduce conflicts, yet none explicitly captures the interaction between seeds and workers: the same seed can yield very different gains on different workers due to their divergent exploration states. As a result, parallel fuzzing can drift toward over-isolation that wastes shared progress, or excessive overlap that duplicates effort. To address this challenge, we present SimiFuzz, a context-aware scheduling framework that learns to assign seed–worker pairs online. SimiFuzz encodes each assignment with a compact context vector that jointly models seed characteristics, worker state, and seed–worker interaction. On top of this representation, SimiFuzz employs a LinUCB-based contextual bandit to score candidate pairs, balancing individual worker efficiency against group-level redundancy to maximize collective progress. To handle non-stationary fuzzing dynamics, SimiFuzz adopts a time-slice feedback mechanism that aggregates coverage gains within fixed intervals, combining globally new edges with cross-learning progress to form stable reward signals. We implement SimiFuzz on top of AFL++ and evaluate it on eight real-world targets. Across 24-hour campaigns with 10 parallel workers, SimiFuzz improves average edge coverage by 28.84% and achieves the best final coverage on all targets, while detecting 29 more unique bugs and 9 more CVEs.","az":"并行模糊测试如今已是扩展漏洞挖掘的标准手段，但其效率仍受制于工作者之间无效的任务分配。现有方法主要着眼于减少冲突，却没有一种显式刻画种子与工作者之间的交互：由于各工作者的探索状态不同，同一个种子在不同工作者上可能带来截然不同的收益。结果，并行模糊测试可能滑向浪费共享进展的过度隔离，或重复劳动的过度重叠。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 SimiFuzz，一个在线学习分配“种子—工作者”配对的上下文感知调度框架。SimiFuzz 用一个紧凑的上下文向量编码每次分配，联合建模种子特征、工作者状态以及种子—工作者交互。在此表示之上，SimiFuzz 采用基于 LinUCB 的上下文赌博机为候选配对打分，在个体工作者效率与群体级冗余之间取得平衡，以最大化整体进展。为应对非平稳的模糊测试动态，SimiFuzz 采用时间片反馈机制，在固定间隔内聚合覆盖率增益，结合全局新边与交叉学习进展形成稳定的奖励信号。我们在 AFL++ 之上实现 SimiFuzz，并在八个真实目标上评估。在 10 个并行工作者、24 小时的实验中，SimiFuzz 把平均边覆盖率提升 28.84%，并在所有目标上取得最佳最终覆盖率，同时多检测出 29 个独特缺陷与 9 个 CVE。","tl":"用 LinUCB 上下文赌博机在线分配种子与并行工作者","au":["Yijia Guo","Zhiguo Ding","Hong Liang","Ming Zhong","Dandan Zhao","Xuhong Zhang","Bo Zhang","Shouling Ji","Hao Peng"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["parallel fuzzing","seed scheduling","contextual bandit","LinUCB","AFL++"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/16/x"},{"id":"p01299","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Natural Language to Executable Properties for Property-based Testing of Mobile Apps (Experience Paper)","tz":"从自然语言到可执行性质：面向移动应用基于性质测试的实践（经验论文）","a":"Property-based testing (PBT) is a popular software testing methodology and is effective in validating the functionality of mobile applications (apps for short). However, its adoption in practice remains limited, largely due to the manual effort and technical expertise required to specify executable properties. In this experience paper, we propose a novel structured property synthesis approach that automatically translates property descriptions in natural language into executable properties, and implement it in a tool named iPBT. Our approach decomposes the problem into UI semantic grounding and executable property synthesis. It first builds an enriched widget context via multimodal LLMs to align visual elements with their functional semantics, and then uses an LLM with in-context learning to generate framework-specific executable properties. We evaluate with a closed-source LLM (GPT-4o) and an open-source LLM (DeepSeek-V3) on 124 diverse property descriptions derived from an existing benchmark dataset. achieves 95.2% (118/124) accuracy on both LLMs. Notably, an ablation study reveals that the enriched widget context contributes to an absolute improvement of up to 20.2% (from 75.0% to 95.2%). A user study with 10 participants demonstrates that reduces the time required to write executable properties by 56%, suggesting substantially lower manual effort. Furthermore, evaluations on 1,180 linguistically diverse variations demonstrate ’s robustness (87.6% accuracy), indicating its capability to handle varied expressions.","az":"基于性质的测试（PBT）是一种流行的软件测试方法论，在验证移动应用（简称 app）功能方面很有效。然而，其在实践中的采用仍然有限，主要是因为指定可执行性质需要大量人工投入与技术专长。在这篇经验论文中，我们提出一种新颖的结构化性质合成方法，可自动把自然语言的性质描述翻译为可执行性质，并将其实现为工具 iPBT。我们的方法把问题分解为 UI 语义落地与可执行性质合成两部分：先通过多模态大语言模型构建富含信息的控件上下文，把视觉元素与其功能语义对齐；再用带上下文学习的 LLM 生成特定框架的可执行性质。我们在源自现有基准数据集的 124 条多样性质描述上，用一个闭源 LLM（GPT-4o）与一个开源 LLM（DeepSeek-V3）评估该工具。该工具在两个 LLM 上均取得 95.2%（118/124）的准确率。值得注意的是，消融实验显示富化的控件上下文带来最高 20.2% 的绝对提升（从 75.0% 提升到 95.2%）。一项包含 10 名参与者的用户研究表明，该工具把编写可执行性质所需时间减少了 56%，说明人工投入大幅降低。此外，在 1,180 条语言表达各异的变体上的评估证明了该工具的鲁棒性（准确率 87.6%），表明其能处理多样化的表述。","tl":"多模态控件语义落地把自然语言描述转成可执行测试性质","au":["Yiheng Xiong","Ting Su","Jingling Sun","Jue Wang","Qin Li","Geguang Pu","Zhendong Su"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","human-study"],"kw":["property-based testing","natural language to property","UI semantic grounding","multimodal LLM","mobile apps"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/17/x"},{"id":"p01300","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DDOR: Delta Debugging for Explainable Overrefusal Testing and Repair","tz":"DDOR：用 delta 调试实现可解释的过度拒绝测试与修复","a":"While safety alignment and guardrails help large language models (LLMs) avoid harmful outputs, they can also induce overrefusal, i.e., unwarranted rejection of benign queries that merely appear risky. We present DDOR (Delta Debugging for OverRefusal), a fully automated and causally grounded framework for overrefusal testing and repair in a black-box setting, where only model inputs and outputs are accessible and internal safety mechanisms remain opaque. DDOR applies delta debugging to localize minimal refusal-triggering fragments (mRTFs) that provide phrase-level, explainable evidence for why a refusal occurs. Conditioned on these mRTFs, DDOR generates diverse, context-rich prompts and performs multi-oracle validation to filter intrinsically unsafe or ambiguous cases, producing scalable and model-specific overrefusal test suites (approximately 1K cases per model). Beyond evaluation, we further leverage localized mRTFs to perform targeted prompt repair, substantially reducing overrefusal while preserving the original intent and maintaining safety on genuinely harmful inputs. Overall, DDOR offers a practical end-to-end solution to both evaluate and mitigate overrefusal, improving LLM usability without sacrificing safety.","az":"尽管安全对齐与护栏有助于大语言模型（LLM）避免有害输出，它们也可能诱发过度拒绝（overrefusal），即无端拒绝那些仅仅看起来有风险的良性查询。我们提出 DDOR（Delta Debugging for OverRefusal），一个全自动、基于因果的框架，用于黑盒场景下的过度拒绝测试与修复——在该场景中只能访问模型的输入与输出，内部安全机制仍不透明。DDOR 应用 delta 调试来定位最小的触发拒绝片段（mRTF），为拒绝发生的原因提供短语级、可解释的证据。以这些 mRTF 为条件，DDOR 生成多样且上下文丰富的提示，并执行多预言验证以过滤本质不安全或含糊的用例，从而产出可扩展且针对具体模型的过度拒绝测试套件（每个模型约 1K 条用例）。除评估之外，我们还进一步利用定位到的 mRTF 进行有针对性的提示修复，在保留原始意图并对真正有害输入维持安全性的同时，大幅减少过度拒绝。总体而言，DDOR 提供了一套实用的端到端方案，可同时评估与缓解过度拒绝，在不牺牲安全性的前提下提升 LLM 的可用性。","tl":"用 delta 调试定位最小触发拒绝片段并据此修复过度拒绝","au":["Zhou Qinyan","Peixin Zhang","Jun Sun","Haonan Zhang","Dongxia Wang"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["cross-track-bridge","llm-based","security"],"kw":["overrefusal","delta debugging","black-box testing","prompt repair","LLM safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/18/x"},{"id":"p01301","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fairness Invariants: A Relational Approach to Explaining and Mitigating Fairness Bugs","tz":"公平性不变量：解释与缓解公平性缺陷的关系式方法","a":"Data-driven software systems are increasingly deployed in high-stakes socio-economic domains, from criminal justice to financial lending. However, these systems often exhibit individual discrimination—unjustified disparities in which a program yields different outcomes for similar individuals who differ only in their protected attributes (e.g., race, gender, age). While existing research has focused on detecting and quantifying these bugs, there remains a critical lack of principled mechanisms to explain and localize individual fairness bugs. Current explanation techniques are largely designed for single-input decisions rather than the relational nature of discrimination, which inherently involves a comparison between an original and a counterfactual pair. We present REMI, a framework for the automated localization, explanation, and mitigation of individual fairness bugs. Inspired by loop-invariant synthesis in formal methods, we treat counterfactual fairness as a relational invariant discovery problem. We introduce a bidirectional relational explanation framework that learns over paired examples (𝑥, 𝑥′) to identify regions of the input space where fairness is violated. Unlike traditional one-way implication pairs used in invariant inference, our approach enforces bidirectional constraints: requiring identical outcomes for both original and counterfactual samples. REMI utilizes three data-alignment techniques to infer interpretable rule-based models that act as “fairness invariants.” These rules serve as guardrails to selectively block or relabel unfair predictions without requiring model retraining. Our evaluation on symbolic and neural network programs demonstrates that REMI localizes ground-truth fairness bugs in over 83% of cases, significantly outperforming state-of-the-art baselines and reducing discriminatory decisions in black-box models by up to 94%","az":"数据驱动的软件系统正越来越多地部署在从刑事司法到金融借贷等高风险的社会经济领域。然而，这些系统常常表现出个体歧视——即程序对仅在受保护属性（如种族、性别、年龄）上存在差异的相似个体给出不同结果，形成不合理的差异。尽管已有研究主要聚焦于检测和量化这类缺陷，但仍严重缺乏有原则的机制来解释和定位个体公平性缺陷。现有的解释技术大多是为单输入决策设计的，而没有针对歧视本身的关系性本质，后者本质上涉及原始样本与反事实样本这一配对之间的比较。我们提出 REMI，一个用于自动定位、解释与缓解个体公平性缺陷的框架。受形式化方法中循环不变量合成的启发，我们把反事实公平性视为一个关系不变量发现问题。我们引入了一个双向的关系解释框架，它在配对样本 (𝑥, 𝑥′) 上学习，以识别输入空间中公平性被违反的区域。与不变量推断中传统使用的单向蕴含对不同，我们的方法施加双向约束：要求原始样本与反事实样本都得到相同的结果。REMI 利用三种数据对齐技术来推断可解释的基于规则的模型，这些规则充当“公平性不变量”。它们作为护栏，在无需重新训练模型的前提下有选择地阻断或重标注不公平的预测。我们在符号程序和神经网络程序上的评估表明，REMI 在超过 83% 的情形中成功定位了真实的公平性缺陷，显著优于最新基线，并在黑盒模型中将歧视性决策最多减少了 94%。","tl":"把反事实公平性建模为双向关系不变量，实现公平缺陷定位与护栏式缓解。","au":["Ranit Debnath Akash","Ashish Kumar","Gang (Gary) Tan","Saeid Tizpaz-Niari"],"top":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["cross-track-bridge","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["individual fairness","fairness bug localization","relational invariant","counterfactual pairs","bias mitigation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/19/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26209"},{"id":"p01302","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SyzDiversity: Diversity-Guided Linux Kernel Fuzzing","tz":"SyzDiversity：多样性引导的 Linux 内核模糊测试","a":"Linux kernel vulnerabilities can pose severe security threats to the entire software ecosystem. While coverage-guided kernel fuzzers have been proposed to uncover such vulnerabilities, their code coverage and bug-finding capability are still limited due to the lack of seed diversity, which is caused by the compounding effect of initial seed generation, seed scheduling, and seed mutation. To address this limitation, we propose a diversity-guided kernel fuzzer SyzDiversity. Specifically, to mitigate overvaluation of early seeds, SyzDiversity leverages proof-of-concept (PoC) seeds derived from real-world vulnerabilities as initial seeds, and further partitions these seeds into multiple communities. Moreover, to improve diversity guidance in seed scheduling, it leverages a novel metric, community popularity rate (CPR), to model community diversity, and introduces a CPR-aware hierarchical Multi-Armed Bandit (MAB) algorithm that integrates CPR and code coverage as reward signals to prioritize the scheduling of diverse seed communities and seeds. Further, to efficiently populate sparse communities or break through community boundaries, it adopts a CPR-guided seed mutation strategy that adaptively allocates higher mutation frequencies to communities that are more conducive to the diversity evolution of the seeds. Our extensive experiments on Linux kernel versions v5.15 and v6.14 has demonstrated that SyzDiversity improves code coverage and bug-finding capability by 17.4% and 9.1×, respectively, compared to the state-of-the-art kernel fuzzers. It has discovered 32 unique new vulnerabilities, with 12 of them confirmed.","az":"Linux 内核漏洞可能对整个软件生态构成严重的安全威胁。虽然已有覆盖引导的内核模糊测试工具被提出用于挖掘此类漏洞，但由于种子多样性不足——这是初始种子生成、种子调度和种子变异三者叠加效应所致——它们的代码覆盖率和缺陷发现能力仍然有限。为解决这一局限，我们提出了多样性引导的内核模糊测试工具 SyzDiversity。具体而言，为缓解对早期种子的高估，SyzDiversity 利用源自真实世界漏洞的概念验证（PoC）种子作为初始种子，并进一步将这些种子划分为多个社区。此外，为在种子调度中提升多样性引导，它引入了一个新指标——社区流行率（CPR）来刻画社区多样性，并提出了一种 CPR 感知的分层多臂老虎机（MAB）算法，将 CPR 与代码覆盖率共同作为奖励信号，以优先调度多样化的种子社区与种子。进一步地，为高效填充稀疏社区或突破社区边界，它采用了 CPR 引导的种子变异策略，自适应地为更有利于种子多样性演化的社区分配更高的变异频率。我们在 Linux 内核 v5.15 与 v6.14 上的大量实验表明，与最新的内核模糊测试工具相比，SyzDiversity 将代码覆盖率和缺陷发现能力分别提升了 17.4% 和 9.1 倍。它发现了 32 个此前未知的新漏洞，其中 12 个已被确认。","tl":"用社区流行率指标与分层 MAB 调度提升内核种子多样性。","au":["Kun Hu","Jiaji Qin","Chaofeng Sha","Bihuan Chen","Shuoran Bai","Qicai Chen","Chenglin Wang","Xin Peng","Wenyun Zhao"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["kernel fuzzing","seed diversity","multi-armed bandit","seed scheduling","Linux kernel vulnerabilities"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/20/x"},{"id":"p01303","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Sakura: An Approach for Generating Complex Tests from Natural Language Test Descriptions","tz":"Sakura：从自然语言测试描述生成复杂测试的方法","a":"Testing is a core activity in software development workflows, and research on its automation has spanned several decades. Most existing approaches focus on generating unit tests for individual methods, validating isolated API endpoints, or targeting user interface (UI) layers. However, for non-API and non-UI tests, automated test generators typically exercise a single focal method. Recent empirical evidence shows a substantial gap between such generated tests and developer-written tests, which often span multiple focal classes and methods, involve complex call sequences, and contain elaborate assertion chains—characteristics that current automated approaches fail to capture. To address this gap, we propose to drive test generation from developer intent expressed as natural language (NL) descriptions. NL provides an expressive and accessible medium for specifying complex test scenarios and functional intent. We present Sakura, the first agent-based framework for generating structurally complex test cases from NL descriptions of test scenarios. Sakura decomposes NL descriptions into structured blocks and processes them using a multi-agent system consisting of a localization agent that grounds test steps in concrete application code via static analysis, a composition agent that synthesizes compilable test code and iteratively refines it using execution feedback, and a supervisor agent that coordinates agent interactions. The framework is tightly grounded in static analysis to ensure correctness and executability. To evaluate Sakura, we curate a novel dataset of NL test descriptions at three levels of abstraction, reflecting different end-user personas, systematically generated from developer-written tests mined from Apache Commons projects. Across 20 applications and 1,464 test scenarios, Sakura significantly outperforms off-the-shelf agentic tools such as Gemini CLI instantiated with multiple LLMs. Specifically, Sakura achieves 50–78% higher test compilability and 38–66% higher coverage overlap (overlap between the ground-truth test and the generated test) compared to baselines using the same models. Moreover, Sakura paired with small open-source models such as Devstral Small 2 and Qwen3-Coder outperforms Gemini CLI using large proprietary models, while also being more cost-effective.","az":"测试是软件开发流程中的核心活动，其自动化研究已持续数十年。现有方法大多聚焦于为单个方法生成单元测试、验证孤立的 API 端点，或针对用户界面（UI）层。然而，对于非 API、非 UI 的测试，自动测试生成器通常只覆盖单一焦点方法。近期的实证证据显示，此类生成的测试与开发者手写的测试之间存在显著差距：后者往往跨越多个焦点类和方法，涉及复杂的调用序列，并包含精细的断言链——这些特征是当前自动化方法所无法捕捉的。为弥合这一差距，我们提出以自然语言（NL）描述所表达的开发者意图来驱动测试生成。自然语言为描述复杂测试场景和功能意图提供了富有表达力且易于使用的媒介。我们提出了 Sakura，这是首个基于智能体的框架，用于从测试场景的自然语言描述生成结构复杂的测试用例。Sakura 将自然语言描述分解为结构化的语块，并交由一个多智能体系统处理：定位智能体通过静态分析把测试步骤落到具体的应用代码上；组合智能体合成可编译的测试代码，并利用执行反馈迭代精化；监督智能体则协调各智能体之间的交互。该框架紧密依托静态分析以确保正确性与可执行性。为评估 Sakura，我们构建了一个新的数据集，包含三种抽象层次的自然语言测试描述，反映不同的终端用户画像，并系统性地由从 Apache Commons 项目中挖掘的开发者手写测试生成。在 20 个应用、1,464 个测试场景上，Sakura 显著优于以多种 LLM 实例化的 Gemini CLI 等现成智能体工具。具体而言，在使用相同模型的情况下，Sakura 的测试可编译率高出 50–78%，覆盖重叠率（真实测试与生成测试之间的覆盖重叠）高出 38–66%。此外，Sakura 搭配 Devstral Small 2、Qwen3-Coder 等小型开源模型时，其表现优于使用大型闭源模型的 Gemini CLI，且更具成本效益。","tl":"首个由自然语言测试描述驱动、静态分析接地的多智能体复杂测试生成框架。","au":["Tyler Stennett","Rangeet Pan","Bridget McGinn","Alessandro Orso","Saurabh Sinha"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["test generation","natural language test description","multi-agent framework","static analysis grounding","test compilability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/21/x"},{"id":"p01304","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"To Run or Not to Run: Analyzing the Cost-Effectiveness of Code Execution in LLM-Based Program Repair","tz":"跑还是不跑：分析基于 LLM 的程序修复中代码执行的成本效益","a":"LLM-based coding agents increasingly adopt a “generate-run-revise” paradigm, where iterative test execution is used to refine patches. This execution-centric approach has become standard practice in state-of-the-art systems. However, executions can be time-consuming and costly, and their prevalence and impact in these agents remain underexplored. In this paper, we conduct a two-stage empirical study to analyze execution behavior in LLM-based program repair. First, we analyze 7,745 agent traces from SWE-bench leaderboard submissions to characterize execution behavior at scale. Second, we perform controlled experiments on 200 SWE-bench instances across two agents (Claude Code and Codex) under four execution paradigms, enabling fine-grained comparison of performance and cost. Our analysis reveals several key observations: ❶ Code execution is used across all agents and models analyzed, with an average of 8.8 test runs per task. Execution behavior varies substantially across agents and models, with frequency ranging from 2 to 19 per task. Late-stage executions (66–100% of conversation) consistently achieve higher success rates than early-stage ones, with an average success rate of 57.9%. ❷ The resolve rate difference between Prohibited (environment-restricted) and Unrestricted (fully-configured) modes is only 1.25 percentage points, which is not statistically significant (𝑝 > 0.05). Prohibited mode consumes 56–62% fewer tokens and 48–54% less time for Claude Code. ❸ Execution has limited impact because 57–62% of repairs are completed in a single edit without requiring feedback, localization accuracy remains above 95% without execution, and 81–100% of failed cases passed agent-executed validation but failed official evaluation. Overall, execution is common but often adds little, so agents should run tests only when needed (especially near the end) to save cost with little change in repair quality. These observations provide empirical insights into the role of execution in agent-based repair and may inform future research on execution-efficient agent design.","az":"基于 LLM 的编程智能体越来越多地采用“生成-运行-修订”范式，通过迭代执行测试来精化补丁。这种以执行为中心的方式已成为最先进系统中的标准做法。然而，执行可能耗时且昂贵，其在这些智能体中的普遍程度与实际影响仍未被充分研究。本文开展了一项两阶段实证研究，分析基于 LLM 的程序修复中的执行行为。首先，我们分析了来自 SWE-bench 排行榜提交的 7,745 条智能体轨迹，以大规模刻画执行行为。其次，我们在 200 个 SWE-bench 实例上，针对两个智能体（Claude Code 与 Codex）在四种执行范式下进行受控实验，实现对性能与成本的细粒度比较。我们的分析得出若干关键观察：❶ 所分析的所有智能体和模型都使用了代码执行，平均每个任务运行 8.8 次测试。不同智能体和模型之间的执行行为差异很大，频率从每任务 2 次到 19 次不等。后期执行（对话进程的 66–100% 处）的成功率始终高于早期执行，平均成功率为 57.9%。❷ 禁止执行（环境受限）与不受限（完全配置）两种模式之间的解决率差异仅为 1.25 个百分点，不具统计显著性（𝑝 > 0.05）。对 Claude Code 而言，禁止执行模式少消耗 56–62% 的 token 与 48–54% 的时间。❸ 执行的影响有限，因为 57–62% 的修复只需一次编辑即可完成、无需反馈；不执行时定位准确率仍保持在 95% 以上；并且 81–100% 的失败案例通过了智能体自行执行的验证却未通过官方评测。总体而言，执行虽普遍但常常收益甚微，因此智能体应仅在必要时（尤其在接近结束时）运行测试，以在几乎不影响修复质量的情况下节省成本。这些观察为理解执行在基于智能体的修复中的作用提供了实证洞见，并可为未来执行高效的智能体设计研究提供参考。","tl":"实证表明修复智能体的测试执行多半冗余，可大幅省 token 而不降解决率。","au":["Zhihao Lin","Junhua Zhu","Mingyi Zhou","Xin Wang","Zhensu Sun","Renyu Yang","David Lo","Li Li"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["code execution cost","SWE-bench traces","agentic program repair","token efficiency","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/22/x"},{"id":"p01305","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LLM-Based Repair of Static Nullability Errors","tz":"基于 LLM 的静态可空性错误修复","a":"Modern Java projects increasingly adopt static analysis tools that prevent null-pointer exceptions by treating nullness as a type property. However, integrating such tools into large, existing codebases remains a significant challenge. While annotation inference can eliminate many errors automatically, a subset of residual errors—typically a mix of real bugs and false positives—often persist and can only be resolved via code changes. Manually addressing these errors is tedious and error-prone. Large language models (LLMs) offer a promising path toward automating these repairs, but naively-prompted LLMs often generate incorrect, contextually-inappropriate edits. We present NullRepair, a system that integrates LLMs into a structured workflow for resolving the errors from a nullability checker. NullRepair’s decision process follows a flowchart derived from manual analysis of 200 real-world errors. It leverages static analysis to identify safe and unsafe usage regions of symbols, using error-free usage examples to contextualize model prompts. Patches are generated through an iterative interaction with the LLM that incorporates project-wide context and decision logic. Our evaluation on 12 real-world Java projects shows that NullRepair resolves 63% of the 1,119 nullability errors that remain after applying a state-of-the-art annotation inference technique. Unlike two baselines (single-shot prompt and mini-SWE-agent), NullRepair also largely preserves program semantics, with all unit tests passing in 10/12 projects after applying every edit proposed by NullRepair, and 98% or more tests passing in the remaining two projects.","az":"现代 Java 项目越来越多地采用将可空性视为类型属性、从而防止空指针异常的静态分析工具。然而，把这类工具集成进大型既有代码库仍然是一大挑战。虽然注解推断可以自动消除许多错误，但仍会残留一部分错误——通常是真实缺陷与误报的混合——它们只能通过修改代码来解决。手工处理这些错误既繁琐又容易出错。大语言模型（LLM）为自动化这些修复提供了有希望的路径，但简单提示的 LLM 常常生成不正确、与上下文不符的编辑。我们提出 NullRepair 系统，它把 LLM 集成进一个结构化工作流中，用于消解可空性检查器报出的错误。NullRepair 的决策过程遵循一张由对 200 个真实错误的人工分析所导出的流程图。它利用静态分析识别符号的安全与不安全使用区域，并用无错误的使用示例为模型提示提供上下文。补丁通过与 LLM 的迭代交互生成，其中融入了项目级上下文与决策逻辑。我们在 12 个真实 Java 项目上的评估显示，在应用了最先进的注解推断技术之后仍残留的 1,119 个可空性错误中，NullRepair 解决了 63%。与两个基线（单次提示与 mini-SWE-agent）不同，NullRepair 还在很大程度上保持了程序语义：在应用其提出的所有编辑后，10/12 的项目单元测试全部通过，其余两个项目也有 98% 以上的测试通过。","tl":"用静态分析划分安全/不安全使用区并结合流程图，驱动 LLM 修可空性错误。","au":["Nima Karimipour","Pascal Joos","Michael Pradel","Martin Kellogg","Manu Sridharan"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["nullability errors","static analysis","LLM-based repair","type-based checker","Java"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/23/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.20674"},{"id":"p01306","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"How Much Static Structure Do Code Agents Need? A Study of Deterministic Anchoring","tz":"代码智能体需要多少静态结构？关于确定性锚定的研究","a":"LLM-based code agents navigate repositories through keyword search but miss the structural relationships, such as call graphs, inheritance hierarchies, and configuration dependencies, that define how software actually works. This makes agent navigation stochastic and difficult to reproduce across runs. We investigate whether lightweight static analysis can provide deterministic anchors for these agents: stable structural facts injected as plain-text comments that constrain probabilistic exploration and make navigation more predictable. Starting from a strong baseline, Codex from OpenAI, we systematically inject varying granularities of structural annotations and measure their effects on localization, trajectory behavior, and run-to-run stability. Our study identifies what we call the deterministic anchoring effect: static structure helps less by making agents “smarter” and more by making their navigation disciplined and reproducible. Three observations support this finding: ❶ Anchoring works: lightweight call/inheritance topology improves function-level localization (+2.2pp Func@5) and shortens trajectories (−1.6 interaction rounds) with minimal overhead (<10% tokens); ❷ Anchoring is scale-sensitive: the optimal granularity and directionality depend on repository characteristics, where denser semantics show diminishing returns and hub-heavy projects benefit from inverse-only links that expose “who-calls-me” without forward edges; ❸ Anchoring stabilizes: tags increase the link-following rate from 0.15–0.18 to 0.21–0.24 and roughly halve run-to-run variance on medium-scale repositories. These observations suggest practical guidelines: default to lightweight topology on medium projects, prune forward edges in large repositories, and reserve dense tags for implicit-dependency cases. Code and traces are available in our repositories: https://anonymous.4open.science/r/CodeAnchor-Impl-8CA2 .","az":"基于 LLM 的代码智能体通过关键词搜索在仓库中导航，却错过了定义软件实际工作方式的结构关系，例如调用图、继承层次与配置依赖。这使得智能体的导航具有随机性，且难以在多次运行之间复现。我们研究轻量级静态分析能否为这些智能体提供确定性锚点：以纯文本注释形式注入的稳定结构事实，用以约束概率性探索并使导航更可预测。我们从一个强基线——OpenAI 的 Codex——出发，系统性地注入不同粒度的结构注解，并测量它们对定位、轨迹行为以及运行间稳定性的影响。我们的研究识别出所谓的确定性锚定效应：静态结构的帮助较少来自让智能体“更聪明”，更多来自让其导航更有纪律、更可复现。三项观察支持这一结论：❶ 锚定有效：轻量级的调用/继承拓扑提升了函数级定位（Func@5 +2.2pp），并缩短了轨迹（交互轮次 −1.6），开销极小（token 增加 <10%）；❷ 锚定对规模敏感：最优粒度与方向性取决于仓库特征，语义更密集时收益递减，而以枢纽节点为主的项目则受益于仅反向链接——暴露“谁调用了我”而不给出正向边；❸ 锚定带来稳定性：标签把链接跟随率从 0.15–0.18 提升到 0.21–0.24，并在中等规模仓库上将运行间方差大致减半。这些观察给出实用指引：中等规模项目默认使用轻量拓扑，大型仓库中剪除正向边，密集标签则留给隐式依赖的情形。代码与轨迹见我们的仓库：https://anonymous.4open.science/r/CodeAnchor-Impl-8CA2 。","tl":"发现静态结构注入的价值在于降低智能体导航方差而非提升智力。","au":["Zhihao Lin","Mingyi Zhou","Yizhuo Yang","Li Li"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["code agents","deterministic anchoring","static structure","call graph annotation","run-to-run stability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/24/x"},{"id":"p01307","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"The Fix is Right at Hand: Fixing Incompatibility Errors Guided by Library Knowledge for Automatic Library Upgrade","tz":"解药就在手边：以库知识引导修复不兼容错误以实现自动库升级","a":"Third-party libraries (TPLs) play critical roles in modern software development. Upgrading them is crucial for enhanced security and functionality, but often introduces incompatibility errors, caused by breaking changes in library APIs, in client code. Existing approaches rely on predefined migration patterns or API recommendation heuristics, which suffer from limited pattern coverage and ignore the usage context of broken API, leading to incorrect or incomplete fixes. To address these limitations, we propose Librarian, a novel LLM-based approach to automatically fix incompatibility errors when upgrading a dependent library in a client project. The core idea of Librarian is to extract context-aware fix hints from the library codebase, serving as semantic few-shot examples, enabling LLM to generate fixes without relying on predefined patterns. Since LLM may generate an incorrect or incomplete fix, Librarian performs fix refinement based on compilation feedback from the client project. Our evaluation has demonstrated that Librarian achieves a fixing success rate of 84.2%, outperforming the state-of-the-arts by at least 45.3%. Our evaluation has also indicated the practical usefulness of Librarian in fixing incompatibility errors in 32 real-world projects.","az":"第三方库（TPL）在现代软件开发中扮演关键角色。升级它们对增强安全性与功能性至关重要，但常常由于库 API 的破坏性变更而在客户端代码中引入不兼容错误。已有方法依赖预定义的迁移模式或 API 推荐启发式，存在模式覆盖有限、忽略被破坏 API 的使用上下文等问题，导致修复不正确或不完整。为克服这些局限，我们提出 Librarian，一种基于 LLM 的新方法，用于在客户端项目升级依赖库时自动修复不兼容错误。Librarian 的核心思想是从库代码库中抽取上下文感知的修复提示，作为语义化的少样本示例，使 LLM 无需依赖预定义模式即可生成修复。由于 LLM 可能生成不正确或不完整的修复，Librarian 还基于客户端项目的编译反馈执行修复精化。我们的评估表明，Librarian 的修复成功率达到 84.2%，比最新方法至少高出 45.3%。评估还表明，Librarian 在 32 个真实项目中修复不兼容错误具有实际可用性。","tl":"从库代码库抽取上下文感知修复示例，驱动 LLM 修不兼容并用编译反馈精化。","au":["Zhuotong Zhou","Susheng Wu","JunPeng Zhao","Bihuan Chen","YenQin Hoo","Yiheng Huang","Yiheng Cao","Xin Peng"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["library upgrade","breaking changes","incompatibility fixing","API migration","compilation feedback"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/25/x"},{"id":"p01308","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SWE-PDB: Teaching LLMs to Leverage Debugging Tools via Agentic Training","tz":"SWE-PDB：通过智能体式训练教会 LLM 使用调试工具","a":"Interaction with debugging tools enables large language models (LLMs) to reason over concrete runtime states, rather than relying solely on static analysis of source code. Specifically, with the help of a debugger, an LLM-based agent can observe actual program execution by inspecting intermediate variable states and stepping through the control flow. These runtime observations enable the model to better understand program behavior and identify the root causes of bugs. Despite these advantages, using debuggers correctly and effectively remains challenging for many models because debugger interaction is inherently stateful and requires executing complex, long-horizon action sequences. As a result, models often exhibit unproductive interactions in which the debugger is underutilized or even disrupts the debugging process. To address this challenge, we propose SWE-PDB, the first training-based framework that teaches LLMs to leverage debuggers for interactive debugging and program repair. Our approach constructs large-scale buggy Python instances with verified failing tests from diverse sources and synthesizes multi-turn interactive debugging trajectories that follow structured debugging workflows. To ensure data quality, we apply multi-stage trajectory filtering and refinement, and train models using agentic supervised fine-tuning to learn effective debugger behaviors, followed by agentic reinforcement learning with rule-based rewards to improve generalization and promote more strategic debugger usage. Extensive evaluations across diverse benchmarks demonstrate substantial gains. In particular, SWE-PDB-14B achieves 38.0% accuracy on SWE-bench Verified with complete test suites, more than tripling the base model’s performance, while improving interaction efficiency and exhibiting robust, meaningful debugger usage.","az":"与调试工具交互使大语言模型（LLM）能够基于具体的运行时状态进行推理，而不仅仅依赖对源代码的静态分析。具体而言，借助调试器，基于 LLM 的智能体可以通过检查中间变量状态和单步跟踪控制流来观察实际的程序执行。这些运行时观察使模型能更好地理解程序行为并识别缺陷的根本原因。尽管有这些优势，正确而有效地使用调试器对许多模型来说仍很困难，因为调试器交互本质上是有状态的，且需要执行复杂的长程动作序列。结果是，模型常常表现出无效的交互，调试器被利用不足，甚至干扰了调试过程。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 **SWE-PDB**，首个基于训练的框架，教会 LLM 利用调试器进行交互式调试与程序修复。我们的方法从多种来源构建大规模带已验证失败测试的 Python 缺陷实例，并合成遵循结构化调试工作流的多轮交互式调试轨迹。为确保数据质量，我们采用多阶段轨迹过滤与精化，并使用智能体式监督微调训练模型以学习有效的调试器行为，随后再用基于规则奖励的智能体式强化学习来提升泛化能力并促成更具策略性的调试器使用。在多个基准上的大量评估显示出显著提升。特别地，**SWE-PDB-14B 在带完整测试套件的 SWE-bench Verified 上达到了 38.0% 的准确率**，比基座模型的性能提升了三倍以上，同时提高了交互效率并表现出稳健、有意义的调试器使用行为。","tl":"首个用合成调试轨迹 SFT+RL 训练模型有策略地使用调试器的框架。","au":["Jiaxing Liu","Xing Hu","Xin Xia"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["interactive debugging","agentic training","debugger tool use","trajectory synthesis","SWE-bench Verified"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/26/x"},{"id":"p01309","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PackMonitor: Towards Zero Package Hallucinations via Decoding-Time Monitoring","tz":"PackMonitor：通过解码期监控迈向零软件包幻觉","a":"As Large Language Models (LLMs) are increasingly integrated into software development workflows, their trustworthiness has become a critical concern. However, in dependency recommendation scenarios, the reliability of LLMs is undermined by widespread package hallucinations, where models often recommend hallucinated packages. Recent studies have proposed a range of approaches to mitigate this issue. Nevertheless, existing approaches typically merely reduce hallucination rates rather than eliminate them, leaving persistent software security risks. In this work, we argue that package hallucinations are theoretically preventable based on the key insight that package validity is decidable through finite and enumerable authoritative package lists. Building on this, we propose PackMonitor, the first approach capable of fundamentally eliminating package hallucinations by continuously monitoring the model’s decoding process and intervening when necessary. To implement this in practice, PackMonitor addresses three key challenges: (1) determining when to trigger intervention via a Context-Aware Parser that continuously monitors model outputs and selectively activates intervening only during installation command generation; (2) resolving how to intervene by employing a Package-Name Intervenor that strictly limits the decoding space to an authoritative package list; and (3) ensuring monitoring efficiency through a DFA-Caching Mechanism that enables scalability to millions of packages with negligible overhead. Extensive experiments on five widely used LLMs demonstrate that PackMonitor is a training-free, plug-and-play solution that consistently reduces package hallucination rates to zero while maintaining low-latency inference and preserving original model capabilities.","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）越来越多地被集成进软件开发流程，其可信性已成为关键关切。然而在依赖推荐场景中，LLM 的可靠性被广泛存在的软件包幻觉所削弱——模型常常推荐并不存在的包。近期研究提出了一系列缓解该问题的方法。然而，现有方法通常只是降低幻觉率而非彻底消除，留下持续的软件安全风险。在本工作中，我们主张软件包幻觉在理论上是可以预防的，其关键洞见在于：包的有效性可以通过有限且可枚举的权威包列表来判定。基于此，我们提出 PackMonitor，这是首个能够从根本上消除软件包幻觉的方法，它持续监控模型的解码过程并在必要时进行干预。为在实践中实现这一点，PackMonitor 解决了三个关键挑战：（1）通过上下文感知解析器决定何时触发干预，该解析器持续监控模型输出，仅在生成安装命令时选择性地激活干预；（2）通过包名干预器解决如何干预的问题，将解码空间严格限制在权威包列表内；（3）通过 DFA 缓存机制保证监控效率，使其能以可忽略的开销扩展到数百万个软件包。在五个广泛使用的 LLM 上的大量实验表明，PackMonitor 是一种免训练、即插即用的方案，能够持续将软件包幻觉率降为零，同时保持低延迟推理并保留模型原有能力。","tl":"用上下文触发的受限解码加 DFA 缓存，把包幻觉率降到零。","au":["Xiting Liu","Yuetong Liu","Yitong Zhang","Jia Li","Shi-Min Hu"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["package hallucination","constrained decoding","DFA caching","dependency recommendation","training-free defense"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/27/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.20717"},{"id":"p01310","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TensorLock: Recovering Model Dependency for Model Supply Chain","tz":"TensorLock：为模型供应链恢复模型依赖关系","a":"The public models on the model hosting platforms have undergone exponential growth, allowing developers to build upon existing models rather than training from scratch. These models are continuously reused, modified, and re-distributed similar to traditional software components, breeding a dense and rapidly evolving model supply chain. However, while enjoying the benefits of model reuse, developers also inherit supply risks ranging from legal liabilities to security threats. To mitigate these risks, a well-established model dependency graph can significantly benefit supply chain risk governance. Unfortunately, although model hosting platforms offer mechanisms for dependency disclosure, such declarations are optional and frequently missing. To address this challenge, we propose a novel model dependency recovering framework TensorLock. It works in two phases; i.e., (1) model clustering, and (2) type-aware dependency identification within theseclusters. In the first phase, TensorLock performs connectivity-based clustering to accommodate the open-ended dependency topology, grouping models with dependency relations. In the second phase, TensorLock employs a divide-and-conquer strategy, leveraging distinct type-specific fingerprints to first identify data-free dependencies (Quantization and Merging), and then resolve data-driven Fine-Tuning dependencies. Our evaluation demonstrates that TensorLock substantially outperforms state-of-the-art approaches, achieving an ARI of 0.96 in clustering and a DF1 of 0.82 in dependency identification, improving over the best baselines by at least 39% and 193%, respectively. Additionally, we apply TensorLock to 289 supposedly isolated models and recover 189 previously missing model dependencies, with 42 model authors confirming our findings.","az":"模型托管平台上的公开模型数量呈指数级增长，使开发者可以在既有模型之上构建，而无需从零训练。这些模型像传统软件组件一样被不断复用、修改和再分发，孕育出一条密集且快速演化的模型供应链。然而，在享受模型复用带来的好处的同时，开发者也继承了从法律责任到安全威胁的供应风险。为缓解这些风险，一个完善的模型依赖图能极大地助力供应链风险治理。遗憾的是，尽管模型托管平台提供了依赖声明机制，这类声明是可选的且经常缺失。为应对这一挑战，我们提出了新颖的模型依赖恢复框架 TensorLock。它分两个阶段工作：（1）模型聚类，以及（2）在这些簇内进行类型感知的依赖识别。在第一阶段，TensorLock 执行基于连通性的聚类以适配开放式的依赖拓扑，把具有依赖关系的模型分组。在第二阶段，TensorLock 采用分治策略，利用不同类型专属的指纹，先识别无需数据的依赖（量化与合并），再解析数据驱动的微调依赖。我们的评估表明，TensorLock 大幅优于最新方法，在聚类上达到 0.96 的 ARI，在依赖识别上达到 0.82 的 DF1，分别比最佳基线至少提升 39% 与 193%。此外，我们把 TensorLock 应用于 289 个看似孤立的模型，恢复出 189 条此前缺失的模型依赖，其中 42 位模型作者确认了我们的发现。","tl":"用连通性聚类加类型指纹恢复模型托管平台上缺失的依赖边。","au":["Susheng Wu","Ziqian Chen","Chengyuan Li","Kaifeng Huang","Zekai Chen","Yijian Wu","Bihuan Chen","Yiheng Cao","Zhuotong Zhou","Yiheng Huang","Xin Peng"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["model supply chain","model dependency graph","model clustering","fingerprinting","pre-trained model reuse"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/28/x"},{"id":"p01311","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SEER: Self-Enhancing Chain-of-Thought Compression for Reasoning Models","tz":"SEER：面向推理模型的自增强思维链压缩","a":"Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting can substantially improve the reasoning ability of large language models (LLMs), but it often comes with high inference cost due to long and poorly controlled reasoning traces. This overhead is particularly problematic in software engineering tasks (e.g., code generation), where both latency and output reliability matter. To better understand this trade-off, we conduct an empirical study on widely used code generation benchmarks and observe that many modern reasoning models produce excessively verbose CoTs (often thousands of tokens), which frequently leads to truncation and unstable generation. Using a strict n-gram repetition detector, we find that the vast majority of truncations are associated with degenerate looping behaviors. Moreover, longer CoT does not necessarily yield better outcomes: failed generations tend to be longer than successful ones, indicating diminishing or even negative returns from overlong reasoning. Motivated by these findings, we propose SEER (Self-Enhancing Efficient Reasoning), a self-enhancing framework for adaptive CoT compression. SEER improves the conciseness of reasoning while preserving output quality, without relying on external compression tools. SEER refines self-generated CoT data via Best-of-N sampling to suppress looping and redundant traces, then applies a lightweight, data-driven filter to encourage concise yet correct reasoning. It then fine-tunes the model on the filtered data to internalize concise reasoning behaviors. Across three software engineering tasks, SEER reduces CoT length by 41.6% on average while improving task performance, largely by reducing truncation and mitigating reasoning loops.","az":"思维链（CoT）提示可以显著提升大语言模型（LLM）的推理能力，但由于推理轨迹冗长且难以控制，往往带来高昂的推理成本。在软件工程任务（如代码生成）中，延迟与输出可靠性都很重要，这一开销尤其成问题。为更好理解这一权衡，我们在广泛使用的代码生成基准上开展了实证研究，观察到许多现代推理模型会产生过度冗长的 CoT（常达数千 token），这经常导致截断和生成不稳定。使用严格的 n-gram 重复检测器，我们发现绝大多数截断都与退化的循环行为相关。此外，更长的 CoT 并不一定带来更好的结果：失败的生成往往比成功的生成更长，表明过长的推理收益递减甚至为负。受这些发现启发，我们提出 SEER（Self-Enhancing Efficient Reasoning），一个用于自适应 CoT 压缩的自增强框架。SEER 在保持输出质量的同时提升推理的简洁性，且不依赖外部压缩工具。SEER 通过 Best-of-N 采样精化自生成的 CoT 数据以抑制循环与冗余轨迹，然后应用一个轻量的数据驱动过滤器以鼓励简洁且正确的推理。随后它在过滤后的数据上微调模型，从而将简洁推理行为内化。在三个软件工程任务上，SEER 平均将 CoT 长度减少 41.6%，同时提升任务性能，这主要得益于减少截断与缓解推理循环。","tl":"用自生成数据过滤加微调把冗长思维链压缩 41.6% 且性能更好。","au":["Kerui Huang","Shuhan Liu","Xing Hu","Tongtong Xu","Lingfeng Bao","Xin Xia"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["chain-of-thought compression","reasoning efficiency","Best-of-N sampling","code generation","truncation and looping"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/29/x"},{"id":"p01312","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"NSync: Automated Cloud Infrastructure-as-Code Reconciliation with AI Agents","tz":"NSync：用 AI 智能体自动对账云端基础设施即代码","a":"Cloud infrastructure is managed through a mix of interfaces—traditionally, cloud consoles, command-line interfaces (CLI), and SDKs are the tools of choice. Recently, Infrastructure-as-Code/IaC frameworks (e.g., Terraform) have quickly gained popularity. Unlike conventional tools, IaC~frameworks encode the infrastructure in a ``source-of-truth'' configuration. They are capable of automatically carrying out modifications to the cloud—deploying, updating, or destroying resources—to bring the actual infrastructure into alignment with the IaC configuration. When IaC frameworks are used together with consoles, CLI, or SDKs, IaC is unaware of changes through these non-IaC interfaces, and the IaC configuration no longer captures the intended state. This is called infrastructure drift. IaC frameworks will revert non-IaC changes based on the outdated IaC configuration, leading to misconfigurations or failures. We propose NSync, an automated system for IaC reconciliation, which aims to propagate out-of-band changes back to the IaC program in the form of an update. Our key insight is that infrastructure changes via IaC, consoles, CLI, or SDK eventually all occur via cloud API invocations—the lowest layer for cloud management operations. Hence, NSync gleans insights from API traces to detect drift (i.e., non-IaC changes) and reconcile it (i.e., update the IaC configuration to capture the changes). This is a challenging task—identifying the intended change from low-level, noisy API traces is not easy; moreover, because of the criticality of cloud infrastructure, NSync cannot directly test the synthesized updates in a live environment. NSync addresses these challenges using an agentic design. It infers high-level infrastructure change intent from cloud API sequences with the help of LLMs, and synthesizes targeted IaC updates using domain-specific context management with customized agent tooling; it further maintains an evolving knowledge base of past successful reconciliation runs, reusing prior insights to achieve higher accuracy on future tasks. In addition to system design, we contribute a novel evaluation pipeline for injecting drift to cloud infrastructure and assessing reconciliation attempts, by sourcing from authoritative cloud operation examples and transplating them into an IaC-centric framework. Experiments across five real-world Terraform projects and 372 drift scenarios show that NSync outperforms the baseline both in terms of accuracy (from 0.71 to 0.97 pass@3) and token efficiency (1.47 improvement).","az":"云基础设施通过多种界面进行管理——传统上，云控制台、命令行界面（CLI）和 SDK 是首选工具。近来，基础设施即代码（IaC）框架（如 Terraform）迅速流行。与传统工具不同，IaC 框架把基础设施编码在一份“真相来源”配置中。它们能够自动对云执行修改——部署、更新或销毁资源——使实际基础设施与 IaC 配置保持一致。当 IaC 框架与控制台、CLI 或 SDK 共同使用时，IaC 无法感知通过这些非 IaC 界面所做的变更，IaC 配置便不再刻画预期状态。这被称为\\textit{基础设施漂移}。IaC 框架会基于过时的 IaC 配置回滚这些非 IaC 变更，导致配置错误或故障。我们提出 NSync，一个用于\\textit{IaC 对账}的自动化系统，旨在把带外变更以更新的形式传播回 IaC 程序。我们的关键洞见是：无论通过 IaC、控制台、CLI 还是 SDK 进行的基础设施变更，最终都经由云 API 调用发生——这是云管理操作的最底层。因此，NSync 从 API 轨迹中提取洞见以检测漂移（即非 IaC 变更）并对其进行对账（即更新 IaC 配置以捕获这些变更）。这是一项具有挑战性的任务——从底层、含噪的 API 轨迹中识别预期变更并不容易；而且由于云基础设施的关键性，NSync 无法直接在生产环境中测试合成出的更新。NSync 以智能体化设计应对这些挑战。它借助 LLM 从云 API 序列中推断高层的基础设施变更意图，并通过面向领域的上下文管理与定制化智能体工具来合成有针对性的 IaC 更新；它还维护一个不断演化的历史成功对账运行知识库，复用先前经验以在未来任务上取得更高准确率。除系统设计外，我们还贡献了一套新颖的评估流水线，通过从权威云操作示例中取材并将其移植到以 IaC 为中心的框架中，来向云基础设施注入漂移并评估对账尝试。在五个真实 Terraform 项目和 372 个漂移场景上的实验表明，NSync 在准确率（pass@3 从 0.71 提升到 0.97）与 token 效率（提升 1.47$\\times$）上均优于基线。","tl":"从云 API 轨迹推断变更意图，智能体式把基础设施漂移回写进 Terraform。","au":["Zhenning Yang","Hui Guan","Victor Nicolet","Brandon Paulsen","Joey Dodds","Daniel Kroening","Ang Chen"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Infrastructure-as-Code","infrastructure drift","Terraform","API trace analysis","agentic reconciliation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/30/x"},{"id":"p01313","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Test vs Mutant: Adversarial LLM Agents for Robust Unit Test Generation","tz":"测试 vs 变异体：面向鲁棒单元测试生成的对抗式 LLM 智能体","a":"Software testing is a critical, yet resource-intensive phase of the software development lifecycle. Over the years, various automated tools have been developed to aid in this process: Search-based approaches typically achieve high coverage but produce tests with low readability, whereas large language model (LLM)-based methods generate more human-readable tests but often suffer from low coverage and compilability. While the majority of research efforts have focused on improving test coverage and readability, little attention has been paid to enhancing the robustness of bug detection, particularly in exposing corner cases and vulnerable execution paths. To address this gap, we propose , a novel adversarial framework for LLM-powered test case generation. comprises two interacting agents: a test case generation agent (T) and a mutant generation agent (M). These agents engage in an adversarial loop, where M persistently creates new mutants “hacking” the blind spots of T’s current test suite, while T iteratively refines its test cases to “kill” the challenging mutants produced by M. This interaction loop is guided by both coverage and mutation scores, enabling the system to co-evolve toward both high test coverage and bug detection capability. Experimental results in the Defects4J dataset show that our approach improves fault detection rates by 8.56% over the best existing LLM-based methods and by 63.30% over EvoSuite, while also improving line and branch coverage.","az":"软件测试是软件开发生命周期中关键却资源密集的阶段。多年来，人们开发了各种自动化工具来辅助这一过程：基于搜索的方法通常能获得高覆盖率，但生成的测试可读性差；而基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法生成的测试更易读，却常常覆盖率与可编译率偏低。虽然大多数研究致力于提升测试覆盖率与可读性，却很少关注增强缺陷检测的鲁棒性，尤其是在暴露边界情形和易受攻击的执行路径方面。为填补这一空白，我们提出 \\ourmethod，一个用于 LLM 驱动测试用例生成的新型对抗框架。\\ourmethod 由两个相互作用的智能体组成：测试用例生成智能体（$\\mathcal{T}$）与变异体生成智能体（$\\mathcal{M}$）。这两个智能体进行对抗式循环：$\\mathcal{M}$ 不断制造新的变异体以“攻击” $\\mathcal{T}$ 当前测试套件的盲点，而 $\\mathcal{T}$ 则迭代精化其测试用例以“杀死” $\\mathcal{M}$ 生成的高难度变异体。该交互循环由覆盖率与变异得分共同引导，使系统能够朝着高测试覆盖率与强缺陷检测能力共同演化。在 Defects4J 数据集上的实验结果表明，我们的方法相较最好的现有 LLM 方法把故障检测率提升了 8.56%，相较 EvoSuite 提升了 63.30%，同时也提升了行覆盖率与分支覆盖率。","tl":"让测试智能体与变异体智能体对抗共演化，提升测试的杀变异能力。","au":["Pengyu Chang","Yixiong Fang","Silin Chen","Yuling Shi","Beijun Shen","Xiaodong Gu"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["unit test generation","adversarial agents","mutation score","Defects4J","fault detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/31/x"},{"id":"p01314","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Guarding the Lifeline: A First Look and Automated Defect Diagnosis for ROS Central Index","tz":"守护生命线：ROS 中央索引的首次审视与自动缺陷诊断","a":"The Robot Operating System (ROS) relies on a centralized dependency index, rosdistro central index, to manage packages across its heterogeneous software ecosystem, which integrates independently evolving Operating System (OS) repositories for system libraries, ROS repositories for domain-specific support, and Programming Language (PL) repositories for functional modules. While this design enables portability, it introduces a critical fragility since the entire ROS dependency management depends on this manually curated, static index that must map packages across independently evolving, multi-source repositories. This leads to persistent defects in the central index, such as missing, incorrect, or outdated installation rules, which undermine the reliability of ROS dependency management. To address this problem, we conducted the first in-depth empirical study of 863 real-world maintenance cases for the ROS central index. We categorize defects into coverage and correctness types, identify their root structural causes, and demonstrate that manual maintenance is bottlenecked by the difficulty of identifying equivalent packages across repositories. Motivated by these findings, we propose RosdepAuditor, an automated auditing framework that introduces a cross-repository mapping mechanism with hybrid scoring to infer package equivalence and detect defects. Evaluated on a ground-truth dataset, RosdepAuditor achieves 95.2% mapping accuracy without generating non-existent packages, outperforming existing pattern-based and upstream-based approaches, and leading LLM models. When applied to the live index, it uncovered 3,062 potential defects across 2,121 entries, 46 of which have been verified and fixed, demonstrating its practical usefulness in strengthening ROS dependency management.","az":"机器人操作系统（ROS）依赖一个集中式依赖索引——rosdistro \\emph{中央索引}——来管理其异构软件生态中的软件包，该生态整合了独立演化的操作系统（OS）仓库（提供系统库）、ROS 仓库（提供领域专用支持）以及编程语言（PL）仓库（提供功能模块）。这种设计虽然带来了可移植性，却引入了严重的脆弱性，因为整个 ROS 依赖管理都依赖这份人工维护的静态索引，而它必须跨越独立演化的多来源仓库进行包映射。这导致中央索引中持续存在缺陷，例如安装规则缺失、错误或过时，削弱了 ROS 依赖管理的可靠性。为解决这一问题，我们对 ROS 中央索引的 863 个真实维护案例开展了首次深入实证研究。我们把缺陷划分为覆盖类和正确性类，识别其根本的结构性成因，并论证人工维护的瓶颈在于难以识别跨仓库的等价软件包。受这些发现启发，我们提出 RosdepAuditor，一个自动化审计框架，引入了带混合打分的跨仓库映射机制来推断包等价性并检测缺陷。在一个带真值的数据集上评估，RosdepAuditor 达到 95.2% 的映射准确率且不会生成不存在的包，优于现有的基于模式和基于上游的方法以及领先的 LLM 模型。将其应用于线上索引时，它在 2,121 个条目中发现了 3,062 个潜在缺陷，其中 46 个已被验证并修复，展示了其在增强 ROS 依赖管理方面的实际价值。","tl":"首次实证刻画 ROS 中央索引缺陷，并用跨仓库包等价映射自动审计。","au":["Weijie Sun","Huiyan Wang","Ying Wang","Chang Xu"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["ROS rosdistro","dependency index defects","cross-repository package mapping","empirical study","automated auditing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/32/x"},{"id":"p01315","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Scitix: Scalable Constraint-Based Type Inference for Code Snippets with Missing Types","tz":"Scitix：面向类型缺失代码片段的可扩展约束式类型推断","a":"Code snippets are commonly used in online developer communities to help communicate ideas and algorithms. However, contextual information, like dependencies and the exact types, are often missing in code snippets, which makes their reuse difficult. Some of the most successful automated techniques use logical constraints to infer the types and dependencies, but they do not work in practice because they require an exact knowledge base that contains all possible dependencies and exact types. However, such a knowledge base is both computationally expensive for constraint solving and impossible to achieve in the presence of missing types (e.g., user-defined types) in code snippets. To this end, this paper proposes a novel, scalable technique named Scitix. Our insight is two-fold. First, inspired by gradual typing, we represent certain missing types as Any, ignoring such types during constraint solving, improving performance and scalability. Second, our novel, iterative constraint-solving approach saves on computation and skips constraints involving these missing types. Our extensive evaluations show that our insights improve both performance and scalability compared to SnR (the state of the art). Specifically, Scitix achieves F1-scores of 94.8% and 86.8% on Stack Overflow and generated code snippets, respectively, using a large knowledge base of over 3,000 jars. In contrast, SnR consistently times out, yielding F1-scores close to 0%. Even with the smallest knowledge base, where SnR does not time out, Scitix reduces the number of errors by 77% and 45% compared to SnR. Compared to state-of-the-art large language models (LLMs) like GPT-4o and LLM-based ZS4C, Scitix achieves up to 78% reduction in error rates. Scitix’s strong performance highlights its potential as a practical technique for type inference in real-world code snippets.","az":"代码片段常被用于在线开发者社区中交流思路与算法。然而，依赖关系和确切类型等上下文信息在代码片段中往往缺失，使得复用变得困难。一些最成功的自动化技术使用逻辑约束来推断类型和依赖，但它们在实践中并不奏效，因为它们要求一个包含所有可能依赖和确切类型的精确知识库。然而，这样的知识库既在约束求解上计算代价高昂，又在代码片段存在类型缺失（例如用户自定义类型）时根本无法实现。为此，本文提出一种新颖且可扩展的技术 Scitix。我们的洞见有两方面。首先，受渐进类型的启发，我们把某些缺失类型表示为 Any，在约束求解中忽略这类类型，从而提升性能与可扩展性。其次，我们提出的新型迭代式约束求解方法节省了计算，并跳过涉及这些缺失类型的约束。我们的大量评估表明，与当前最先进的 SnR 相比，我们的洞见同时改善了性能与可扩展性。具体而言，在使用超过 3,000 个 jar 的大型知识库时，Scitix 在 Stack Overflow 片段和生成的代码片段上分别取得 94.8% 与 86.8% 的 F1 分数；相比之下，SnR 始终超时，F1 分数接近 0%。即使在 SnR 不超时的最小知识库上，Scitix 也相比 SnR 分别减少了 77% 与 45% 的错误数量。与 GPT-4o 等最先进的大语言模型（LLM）以及基于 LLM 的 ZS4C 相比，Scitix 的错误率最多降低 78%。Scitix 的出色表现凸显了它作为真实代码片段类型推断实用技术的潜力。","tl":"借渐进类型把缺失类型记为 Any，并迭代求解，使片段类型推断可扩展。","au":["Yiwen Dong","Zhenyang Xu","Yongqiang Tian","Edward Lee","Ondřej Lhoták","Chengnian Sun"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["type inference","code snippets","constraint solving","gradual typing","dependency resolution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/33/x"},{"id":"p01316","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Beyond Similarity Scores: Evidence-Based Third-Party Library Detection for C/C++ Binaries","tz":"超越相似度分数：面向 C/C++ 二进制的基于证据的第三方库检测","a":"Detecting third-party libraries (TPLs) in C/C++ binaries is essential for software supply chain security, enabling vulnerability identification and license compliance. Existing methods predominantly rely on similaritymatching: extracting features from binaries and comparing them against library databases. However, similarityscores alone cannot reliably determine library presence. Low similarity causes false negatives when matchablefeatures are limited. More critically, high similarity does not guarantee accuracy: libraries often share featuresthrough shared dependencies, forks, or similar functionality, causing multiple candidates to match even whenonly one is present. These issues suggest that similarity matching is effective for narrowing candidates butinsufficient as the final decision mechanism. Rather than relying solely on similarity scores, reliable detectionrequires multi-source evidence to verify each candidate. To this end, we propose BLADE, which reframes TPL detection as evidence-based candidate verification.Instead of relying on similarity scores to make final decisions, BLADE retrieves candidates broadly to mitigatefalse negatives, and then collects evidence from multiple sources, which an LLM analyzes through structuredverification workflows to filter false positives: first confirming candidates with clear identity markers, thensystematically checking remaining candidates against common false positive patterns. To evaluate BLADE,we build the largest C/C++ binary TPL benchmark to date, comprising 3,403 binaries and 1,016 libraries.Results show that BLADE achieves 97.60% precision and 93.74% recall (F1: 95.63%), improving F1-score by 41.83percentage points over the best baseline. The average cost is $0.0378 per binary. BLADE has been deployed ina commercial software composition analysis product, demonstrating practical feasibility at scale.","az":"在 C/C++ 二进制中检测第三方库（TPL）对软件供应链安全至关重要，它使漏洞识别和许可证合规成为可能。现有方法主要依赖相似度匹配：从二进制中提取特征并与库数据库进行比对。然而，仅靠相似度分数无法可靠判定库是否存在。相似度低会因可匹配特征有限而造成漏报。更关键的是，高相似度也不保证准确：库之间常因共享依赖、分叉或功能相似而共享特征，导致即使只存在一个库也会有多个候选被匹配上。这些问题表明，相似度匹配适合用来缩小候选范围，却不足以作为最终判定机制。可靠的检测不能只依赖相似度分数，而需要多源证据来验证每个候选。为此，我们提出 BLADE，它把 TPL 检测重构为基于证据的候选验证。BLADE 不依赖相似度分数做最终决策，而是广泛地召回候选以缓解漏报，然后从多个来源收集证据，由 LLM 通过结构化的验证工作流进行分析以过滤误报：先确认具有明确身份标识的候选，再系统性地对照常见误报模式检查剩余候选。为评估 BLADE，我们构建了迄今最大的 C/C++ 二进制 TPL 基准，包含 3,403 个二进制和 1,016 个库。结果表明，BLADE 达到 97.60% 的精确率和 93.74% 的召回率（F1：95.63%），相较最佳基线把 F1 提升了 41.83 个百分点，平均每个二进制成本为 0.0378 美元。BLADE 已部署于一款商业软件成分分析产品中，展示了大规模场景下的实际可行性。","tl":"把二进制第三方库检测从相似度打分改造为 LLM 多源证据验证。","au":["CHENGYUE LIU","Zhengzi Xu","Lyuye Zhang","Wu Jiahui","Kaixuan Li","Yang Liu"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["third-party library detection","binary SCA","evidence-based verification","false positive filtering","C/C++ binaries"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/34/x"},{"id":"p01317","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Defusing Logic Bombs in Symbolic Execution with LLM-Generated Ghost Code","tz":"用 LLM 生成的 Ghost Code 拆解符号执行中的逻辑炸弹","a":"Symbolic execution is a powerful program analysis technique, but its effectiveness is fundamentally limited by solver-hostile program fragments, complex numerical reasoning, and unbounded heap structures. Recent work proposed replacing constraint solvers with large language models (LLMs) to bypass these limitations, but such approaches struggle to analyze real-world codebases, where deep execution paths require globally consistent reasoning across many interacting constraints. We present Gordian, a hybrid symbolic execution framework that uses LLMs selectively to generate lightweight ghost code that aids an SMT solver in handling solver-hostile code fragments, while preserving its precise, global reasoning capability. In particular, we propose three types of ghost code: (1) inversion of difficult code fragments with iterative bidirectional constraint propagation, (2) modeling via solver-friendly surrogates while preserving relevant behavior, and (3) semantic partitioning of unbounded heap spaces. We implemented Gordian on top of the KLEE symbolic execution engine and evaluated it on synthetic “logic bombs” capturing distinct symbolic reasoning challenges, a popular mathematical library FDLibM, and three structured-input programs (libexpat, jq, and bc). Across all benchmarks, Gordian improves coverage on average by 52-84% over traditional symbolic execution baselines, and by 86-419% over LLM-based techniques, while reducing LLM token usage by an average of 90-96%. This highlights the practicality and effectiveness of this approach in real-world settings.","az":"符号执行是一种强大的程序分析技术，但其有效性从根本上受限于对求解器不友好的程序片段、复杂的数值推理以及无界的堆结构。近期工作提出用大语言模型（LLM）取代约束求解器以绕开这些限制，但此类方法难以分析真实世界代码库——在那里，深层执行路径需要跨越众多相互作用的约束进行全局一致的推理。我们提出 Gordian，一个混合式符号执行框架，它有选择地使用 LLM 生成轻量的 ghost code 来帮助 SMT 求解器处理对求解器不友好的代码片段，同时保留其精确的全局推理能力。具体而言，我们提出三类 ghost code：（1）通过迭代式双向约束传播对困难代码片段进行求逆；（2）用对求解器友好的代理进行建模，同时保留相关行为；（3）对无界堆空间进行语义划分。我们在 KLEE 符号执行引擎之上实现了 Gordian，并在刻画不同符号推理挑战的合成“逻辑炸弹”、流行数学库 FDLibM 以及三个结构化输入程序（libexpat、jq 和 bc）上进行评估。在所有基准上，Gordian 相较传统符号执行基线平均提升覆盖率 52–84%，相较基于 LLM 的技术提升 86–419%，同时平均减少 90–96% 的 LLM token 使用量。这凸显了该方法在真实场景中的实用性与有效性。","tl":"选择性用 LLM 生成 ghost code 辅助 SMT，而非取代求解器。","au":["Dimitrios Stamatios Bouras","Sergey Mechatev"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic execution","ghost code","SMT solver","KLEE","logic bombs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/35/x"},{"id":"p01318","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Tracing the Shadows: Automatic Tracking and Analysis of Crypto Money Laundering via Transaction Semantic Analysis","tz":"追踪暗影：基于交易语义分析的加密货币洗钱自动追踪与分析","a":"With the rapid advancement of decentralized finance (DeFi), security incidents related to cryptocurrency have become increasingly prevalent. After such incidents, attackers typically attempt to rapidly move stolen assets, concealing the origin of illicit funds and ultimately converting them into fiat currency. However, existing anti-money laundering (AML) methods struggle to cope with the semantic complexity of DeFi transactions. They either rely heavily on low-level token transfers, or perform protocol-agnostic money flow analysis, failing to capture the high-level intent of transactions. This limitation results in misleading tracing paths with substantial noise and fails when laundering activities span multiple blockchains. In this paper, we propose AMLGuard, a semantic-aware AML framework for account-based blockchains. AMLGuard tracks illicit fund flows from known malicious addresses by performing semantic analysis on complex DeFi transactions, enabling accurate and continuous laundering tracking. Given a complex transaction, AMLGuard combines static rule-based analysis with retrieval-augmented large language model (LLM) reasoning to infer implicit DeFi semantics, transforming raw transaction data into high-level semantic representations. Furthermore, for cross-chain transactions where laundering intent is not explicitly exposed, AMLGuard parses transaction parameters and performs argument parsing to recover cross-chain semantics, enabling seamless tracking across ledgers. Based on the inferred semantics, AMLGuard abstracts each transaction into a DeFi Semantic Unit (DSU). These DSUs are analyzed and composed iteratively to update account states, expand the tracing frontier, and ultimately construct the illicit fund-flow topology. We evaluate the effectiveness of AMLGuard on 82 real-world laundering cases, involving illicit assets worth over $1 billion. Specifically, AMLGuard reconstructs compact illicit fund-flow topologies with destination precision of 94.4% and 87.6%, while achieving the highest address recall of 98.4% and 95.8% and destination recall of 94.1% and 93.8% on single-chain and cross-chain datasets. Furthermore, a case study demonstrates that AMLGuard can assist real-world AML investigation, substantially reducing analysis time and effort.","az":"随着去中心化金融（DeFi）的快速发展，与加密货币相关的安全事件日益频发。此类事件发生后，攻击者通常会试图迅速转移被盗资产，掩盖非法资金的来源，并最终将其兑换为法定货币。然而，现有的反洗钱（AML）方法难以应对 DeFi 交易的语义复杂性。它们要么严重依赖底层的代币转账，要么执行与协议无关的资金流分析，无法捕捉交易的高层意图。这一局限导致追踪路径带有大量噪声且具有误导性，并在洗钱活动跨越多条区块链时失效。本文提出 AMLGuard，一个面向账户型区块链的语义感知反洗钱框架。AMLGuard 通过对复杂 DeFi 交易执行语义分析，从已知恶意地址出发追踪非法资金流，实现准确且连续的洗钱追踪。给定一笔复杂交易，AMLGuard 结合基于静态规则的分析与检索增强的大语言模型（LLM）推理来推断隐含的 DeFi 语义，把原始交易数据转换为高层语义表示。此外，对于洗钱意图未被显式暴露的跨链交易，AMLGuard 解析交易参数并进行参数解析以恢复跨链语义，从而实现跨账本的无缝追踪。基于推断出的语义，AMLGuard 把每笔交易抽象为一个 DeFi 语义单元（DSU）。这些 DSU 被迭代地分析与组合，以更新账户状态、扩展追踪前沿，并最终构建出非法资金流拓扑。我们在 82 个真实洗钱案例上评估 AMLGuard 的有效性，涉及价值超过 10 亿美元的非法资产。具体而言，AMLGuard 重建出紧凑的非法资金流拓扑，在单链与跨链数据集上目的地精确率分别为 94.4% 与 87.6%，同时取得最高的地址召回率 98.4% 与 95.8%，以及目的地召回率 94.1% 与 93.8%。此外，案例研究表明 AMLGuard 能够辅助真实世界的反洗钱调查，大幅减少分析所需的时间与精力。","tl":"用规则加检索增强 LLM 推断 DeFi 语义单元，实现跨链洗钱追踪。","au":["Hao Wu","Haijun Wang","Shangwang Li","Yin Wu","Ming Fan","Ting Liu","Xiapu Luo"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["anti-money laundering","DeFi transaction semantics","cross-chain tracing","retrieval-augmented LLM","fund flow topology"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/36/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18869"},{"id":"p01319","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PropCov: Effective Coverage Reporting for Property-Based Testing","tz":"PropCov：面向基于属性测试的有效覆盖率报告","a":"Property-base testing (PBT), introduced by Haskell’s Quickcheck, is becoming more popular with successful ports for other languages, such as Java’s junit-quickcheck. With PBT, developers write a property test and a data generator. The data generator takes a source of non-determinism and uses it to output well-formed data. The property test exercises the System Under Test (SUT) using the random well-formed data from the generator to ensure a particular property always holds (e.g., data serialized and deserialized should be equal to the original data). The PBT framework then performs many trials, each generating fresh data and executing the property test. A test failure shows a bug to developers, typically in edge-cases. A passing test gives some assurance on the quality of the SUT with regards to the property being tested. Unfortunately, well-known test coverage tools that are instrumental for understanding unit testing work poorly for PBT. In this paper, we present PropCov, a tool for understanding coverage in PBT that also provides suggestions for coverage improvement. PropCov employs a novel combination of static analysis with PBT to approximate the maximum possible coverage, providing an effective measure of the PBT coverage and making suggestions to developers of where to improve existing tests. PropCov features an easily extensible architecture that can support new languages, build systems, and PBT frameworks. We evaluated PropCov using 25 Java projects using junit-quickcheck or jqwik, totaling 293 properties, and found that existing tools report missed coverage that is impossible to reach (86% of lines that JaCoCo reports as not covered), which leads developers to consider hundreds of extra lines of code (2910). Unlike existing coverage tools, PropCov results are accurate — only 7.5% of all properties contain unfeasible code, and PropCov only misses 4% of reachable code. Using PropCov’s suggestions, we increased the coverage of 42 tests over 7 projects and found 4 new bugs in 4 projects.","az":"基于属性的测试（PBT）由 Haskell 的 QuickCheck 引入，随着在 Java 的 junit-quickcheck 等其他语言中的成功移植而日益流行。在 PBT 中，开发者编写一个属性测试和一个数据生成器。数据生成器接收一个非确定性来源，并用它输出格式良好的数据。属性测试使用生成器产生的随机良构数据来执行被测系统（SUT），以确保某个属性始终成立（例如，序列化后再反序列化的数据应与原数据相等）。PBT 框架随后执行多次试验，每次生成新的数据并执行属性测试。测试失败向开发者揭示一个缺陷，通常位于边界情形；测试通过则就所测属性给出被测系统质量的一定保证。遗憾的是，那些对理解单元测试极为关键的知名测试覆盖率工具，在 PBT 上表现很差。本文提出 PropCov，一个用于理解 PBT 覆盖率并同时给出覆盖率改进建议的工具。PropCov 采用了静态分析与 PBT 的新颖结合来逼近可能达到的最大覆盖率，从而提供对 PBT 覆盖率的有效度量，并向开发者建议在何处改进既有测试。PropCov 具有易于扩展的架构，可支持新的语言、构建系统和 PBT 框架。我们使用 25 个采用 junit-quickcheck 或 jqwik 的 Java 项目（共 293 个属性）评估 PropCov，发现现有工具报告的未覆盖部分中有大量是根本不可能到达的（JaCoCo 报告为未覆盖的行中有 86%），这会误导开发者去考虑数百行多余代码（2,910 行）。与现有覆盖率工具不同，PropCov 的结果是准确的——所有属性中只有 7.5% 含有不可行代码，且 PropCov 仅漏报 4% 的可达代码。借助 PropCov 的建议，我们提升了 7 个项目中 42 个测试的覆盖率，并在 4 个项目中发现了 4 个新缺陷。","tl":"结合静态分析逼近 PBT 的可达最大覆盖，纠正传统覆盖工具的误报。","au":["Jesse Coultas","Joseph Wiseman","Luís Pina"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["property-based testing","coverage reporting","static analysis","junit-quickcheck","unreachable code"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/37/x"},{"id":"p01320","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Uniting Bounded Verification and Transformer-Based Learning for Proactive IoT Security","tz":"融合有界验证与基于 Transformer 的学习实现主动式 IoT 安全","a":"The proliferation of Internet-of-Things (IoT) ecosystems has introduced sophisticated interaction threats that emerge from unintended coordination between multiple applications, evading traditional single-app analysis. While formal verification provides soundness guarantees for interaction threats detection, it suffers from scalability limitations when analyzing large-scale deployments with hundreds of interacting applications. We present VeriWeave, a framework that synergistically combines bounded exhaustive formal verification, automated dynamic validation, and specialized transformer-based machine learning to detect interaction threats across application boundaries. VeriWeave employs static analysis to extract behavioral models from applications, uses bounded model checking to exhaustively enumerate potential interaction threat scenarios, at a static-derived scope obtained directly from the extracted models, and automatically validates these scenarios in instrumented environments to generate high-precision ground-truth labels. The validated results train specialized transformer models to predict exploitable interaction threats directly from code, achieving millisecond-scale predictions compared to several hours or days for formal analysis. Our evaluation on 3,732 real-world IoT applications together with a held-out benchmark of 4,000 additional applications (7,732 in total) demonstrates that VeriWeave reduces analysis time by 92% compared to pure formal methods while maintaining superior interaction threats detection accuracy. We validate cross-platform applicability on different ecosystems, confirming generalization. VeriWeave represents the first framework to bridge formal methods rigor with machine learning efficiency for interaction threats detection, enabling proactive vulnerability detection at scale through specialized models trained on validated interaction patterns.","az":"物联网（IoT）生态的普及带来了复杂的交互威胁，它们源自多个应用之间意料之外的协同作用，能够规避传统的单应用分析。虽然形式化验证为交互威胁检测提供了可靠性保证，但在分析包含数百个相互作用应用的大规模部署时存在可扩展性瓶颈。我们提出 VeriWeave，一个协同结合有界穷尽形式化验证、自动化动态验证与专用的基于 Transformer 的机器学习的框架，用于检测跨应用边界的交互威胁。VeriWeave 使用静态分析从应用中提取行为模型，使用有界模型检验在由所提取模型直接得到的静态推导范围内穷尽枚举潜在的交互威胁场景，并在插桩环境中自动验证这些场景以生成高精度的真值标签。经验证的结果用于训练专用的 Transformer 模型，使其能够直接从代码预测可利用的交互威胁，实现毫秒级预测，而形式化分析则需数小时甚至数天。我们在 3,732 个真实 IoT 应用以及另外 4,000 个应用构成的留出基准（共 7,732 个）上的评估表明，VeriWeave 相较纯形式化方法把分析时间减少了 92%，同时保持更优的交互威胁检测准确率。我们在不同生态上验证了跨平台适用性，确认了其泛化能力。VeriWeave 是首个把形式化方法的严谨性与机器学习的效率相桥接、用于交互威胁检测的框架，通过在已验证交互模式上训练的专用模型实现大规模的主动漏洞检测。","tl":"有界模型检验产出真值标签，训练 Transformer 毫秒级预测 IoT 交互威胁。","au":["Md Rashedul Hasan","Hamid Bagheri"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["IoT interaction threats","bounded model checking","transformer classifier","cross-app analysis","proactive vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/38/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/38/Uniting-Bounded-Verification-and-Transformer-Based-Learning-for-Proactive-IoT-Securit"},{"id":"p01321","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Don’t Use a Cannon to Kill a Fly: Lightweight Model Editing for LLMs to Correct Deprecated API Recommendations","tz":"别用大炮打苍蝇：用轻量模型编辑纠正 LLM 的已弃用 API 推荐","a":"Pre-trained or fine-tuned on large code corpora, Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated strong performance in code completion tasks. However, their embedded knowledge is constrained by the timeliness of training data, which often includes code using deprecated APIs. Consequently, LLMs frequently generate deprecated APIs that will no longer be supported in future versions of third-party libraries. While retraining LLMs on updated codebases could refresh their API knowledge, this approach is computationally expensive. Recently, lightweight model editing methods have emerged to efficiently correct specific knowledge in LLMs. However, it remains unclear whether these methods can effectively update deprecated API knowledge and enable edited models to generate up-to-date APIs. To address this gap, we conduct the first systematic study applying 10 state-of-the-art model editing techniques to update deprecated API knowledge in three LLMs: Qwen2.5-Coder, CodeGemma, and DeepSeek-Coder. We introduce EDAPIBench, a dedicated benchmark featuring over 70 deprecated APIs from 8 popular Python libraries, with more than 3,000 editing instances. Our results show that the parameter-efficient fine-tuning method AdaLoRA achieves the best performance in enabling edited models to generate correct, up-to-date APIs, but falls short in Specificity (i.e., the editing influences untargeted knowledge). To resolve this, we propose AdaLoRA-L, which defines Common API Layers'' (layers within the LLMs with high importance across all APIs, storing general knowledge and excluded from editing) and restricts edits exclusively to Specific API Layers'' (layers with high importance only for the target API, storing the API-specific knowledge). Experimental results demonstrate that AdaLoRA-L significantly improves Specificity while maintaining comparable performance across other evaluation metrics.","az":"在大规模代码语料上预训练或微调后，大语言模型（LLM）在代码补全任务上展现出强劲性能。然而，其内嵌知识受训练数据时效性的限制，而这些数据常常包含使用已弃用 API 的代码。因此，LLM 经常生成在第三方库未来版本中不再被支持的已弃用 API。虽然在更新后的代码库上重新训练 LLM 可以刷新其 API 知识，但这种做法计算代价高昂。近来，轻量级模型编辑方法被提出，用以高效地纠正 LLM 中的特定知识。然而，这些方法能否有效更新已弃用 API 知识、并使编辑后的模型生成最新 API，仍不明确。为填补这一空白，我们开展了首个系统性研究，将 10 种最先进的模型编辑技术应用于更新三个 LLM（Qwen2.5-Coder、CodeGemma 和 DeepSeek-Coder）中的已弃用 API 知识。我们引入了 EDAPIBench，一个专门的基准，涵盖来自 8 个流行 Python 库的 70 多个已弃用 API，包含 3,000 多个编辑实例。结果显示，参数高效微调方法 AdaLoRA 在使编辑后模型生成正确、最新的 API 方面表现最佳，但在特异性（Specificity，即编辑会影响非目标知识）上有所欠缺。为解决这一问题，我们提出 AdaLoRA-L，它定义了“通用 API 层”（LLM 中对所有 API 都具有高重要性、存储通用知识且被排除在编辑之外的层），并把编辑严格限制在“特定 API 层”（仅对目标 API 具有高重要性、存储该 API 专属知识的层）。实验结果表明，AdaLoRA-L 显著提升了特异性，同时在其他评测指标上保持相当的表现。","tl":"首次系统评测模型编辑更新弃用 API，并提出按层定位的 AdaLoRA-L。","au":["Guancheng Lin","Xiao Yu","Jacky Keung","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Alex X. Liu"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["model editing","deprecated API","AdaLoRA","code completion","EDAPIBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/39/x"},{"id":"p01322","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ScratchNet: A Multi-modal Benchmark for Evaluating and Advancing LLMs on Scratch Programming Tasks","tz":"ScratchNet：面向 Scratch 编程任务评测与推进 LLM 的多模态基准","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have achieved impressive performance on text-based programming tasks, yet they remain unreliable for block-based languages like Scratch. Scratch programs feature deeply nested, non-linear structures, event-driven concurrency across multiple sprites, and tight coupling between code and multimedia assets, properties that are fundamentally different from those of textual code. As a result, LLMs frequently misinterpret Scratch semantics and propose large, invasive edits that are syntactically valid yet semantically misaligned when repairing buggy programs. We introduce ScratchNet, the first executable benchmark designed to systematically evaluate and advance LLM-based repair methods for Scratch programs, spanning program understanding, debugging, analysis, and repair. The benchmark comprises 100 carefully curated Scratch projects from the public repository, each chosen for high structural and semantic complexity. Every project is paired with executable test suites, bug descriptions and corresponding fixes, block-level edit constraints that define minimal semantically correct repairs, and associated multimedia assets. We construct the benchmark via a human-in-the-loop pipeline that combines automated project mining with expert validation of trigger mechanism–outcome semantics and representative bug patterns, with particular focus on event ordering, concurrency, and state management. To enable rigorous and reproducible evaluation, we propose a three-layer, executable protocol that measures functional correctness via VM-level execution, repair quality in terms of minimality and semantic fidelity using block-level edit distance and behavioral trajectory comparisons, and explanation quality through structured rubrics assessing alignment between the model’s reasoning and its patch. Using this benchmark, we investigate fundamental research questions such as the impact of domain-specific fine-tuning on repair success, the effectiveness of different training data sources, and the ability of models to generalize to unseen bug types. Our benchmark establishes a reproducible foundation and a closed-loop framework for evaluating and post-training LLMs on block-based programming tasks.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在基于文本的编程任务上取得了令人印象深刻的表现，但在 Scratch 这类块式语言上仍不可靠。Scratch 程序具有深度嵌套的非线性结构、跨多个角色（sprite）的事件驱动并发，以及代码与多媒体资源之间的紧耦合，这些性质与文本代码有本质不同。因此，LLM 经常误解 Scratch 语义，在修复有缺陷程序时提出大规模、侵入性的编辑——语法上有效，语义上却并不对齐。我们提出 ScratchNet，首个可执行基准，旨在系统性地评测并推进面向 Scratch 程序的基于 LLM 的修复方法，涵盖程序理解、调试、分析与修复。该基准由 100 个从公共仓库中精心挑选的 Scratch 项目组成，每个项目都因其高度的结构与语义复杂性而入选。每个项目都配有可执行的测试套件、缺陷描述及相应修复、定义最小语义正确修复的块级编辑约束，以及相关的多媒体资源。我们通过人在回路的流水线构建该基准，把自动化项目挖掘与专家对触发机制—结果语义和代表性缺陷模式的验证相结合，尤其关注事件顺序、并发与状态管理。为实现严格且可复现的评测，我们提出了一个三层的可执行协议：通过虚拟机级执行度量功能正确性；用块级编辑距离与行为轨迹比较从最小性与语义保真度上度量修复质量；并通过结构化评分量表评估模型推理与其补丁之间的一致性，以衡量解释质量。基于该基准，我们研究了若干基础研究问题，例如领域专用微调对修复成功率的影响、不同训练数据来源的有效性，以及模型对未见缺陷类型的泛化能力。我们的基准为在块式编程任务上评测与后训练 LLM 建立了可复现的基础与闭环框架。","tl":"首个可执行的 Scratch 块式编程基准，含块级编辑约束与三层评测协议。","au":["Yuan Si","Simeng Han","Daming Li","Hanyuan Shi","Jialu Zhang"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["multimodal","llm-based","low-resource-or-non-english"],"kw":["Scratch programming","block-based language","executable benchmark","program repair","multimodal assets"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/40/x"},{"id":"p01323","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"MG-Fuzz: Model-Guided Fuzzing for Unsafe Scenario Discovery in Autonomous Driving Systems","tz":"MG-Fuzz：面向自动驾驶系统不安全场景发现的模型引导模糊测试","a":"As autonomous driving systems (ADS) are increasingly deployed in real-world environments, discovering diverse unsafe driving scenarios remains a fundamental yet difficult problem. Existing scenario generation and testing approaches often rely on black-box exploration or externally-observed heuristic feedback, which struggle to effectively guide the search toward high-risk scenarios induced by complex decision-making behaviors. A key difficulty stems from the fact that unsafe behaviors in ADS often arise from internal decision-making logic, which can induce structured and discontinuous responses that are hard to effectively explore using purely black-box guidance. Consequently, current tools tend to repeatedly discover a narrow set of similar unsafe scenario types, limiting their ability to expose diverse and previously unseen failure modes. In this paper, we propose MG-Fuzz, a model-guided, multi-objective fuzzing framework for unsafe scenario discovery in autonomous driving systems. Our approach extracts an automaton model that captures the core control logic of the ADS decision-making component, and leverages this model as structured guidance for search-based scenario exploration. To systematically drive the exploration process, MG-Fuzz integrates model-based metrics derived from the automaton with complementary safety metrics, enabling effective evaluation and prioritization of generated driving scenarios across diverse unsafe behavior types. MG-Fuzz has been developed and thoroughly evaluated through extensive experiments on autonomous driving systems. Experimental evidence indicates that MG-Fuzz successfully detects 18 distinct types of unsafe driving scenarios, marking a substantial improvement in detection breadth relative to current state-of-the-art tools.","az":"随着自动驾驶系统（ADS）越来越多地部署到真实环境中，发现多样化的不安全驾驶场景仍是一个基础却困难的问题。现有的场景生成与测试方法通常依赖黑盒探索或外部观测到的启发式反馈，难以有效地把搜索引导到由复杂决策行为所诱发的高风险场景。一个关键难点在于，ADS 中的不安全行为往往源自内部决策逻辑，它会引发结构化且不连续的响应，仅靠纯黑盒引导难以有效探索。因此，当前工具往往反复发现一小类相似的不安全场景类型，限制了其暴露多样且此前未见失效模式的能力。本文提出 MG-Fuzz，一个模型引导的多目标模糊测试框架，用于自动驾驶系统的不安全场景发现。我们的方法抽取一个刻画 ADS 决策组件核心控制逻辑的自动机模型，并把该模型作为结构化引导用于基于搜索的场景探索。为系统性地驱动探索过程，MG-Fuzz 把从自动机导出的基于模型的指标与互补的安全性指标相结合，从而能够跨多种不安全行为类型对生成的驾驶场景进行有效评估与优先级排序。MG-Fuzz 已在自动驾驶系统上开发并通过大量实验充分评估。实验证据表明，MG-Fuzz 成功检测出 18 种不同类型的不安全驾驶场景，相较当前最先进工具在检测广度上有实质性提升。","tl":"抽取 ADS 决策自动机作为结构化引导，显著拓宽不安全场景的发现广度。","au":["Yulong Lyu","Ruiqi Hong","Jiawan Wang","Jun Sun","Lei Bu"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving systems","scenario-based testing","model-guided fuzzing","automaton model","multi-objective search"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/41/x"},{"id":"p01324","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Mind the Gap: An Empirical Study of Synchronization Gaps, Delays, and Missed Opportunities in Software Forks","tz":"注意缺口：软件分叉中同步缺口、延迟与错失机会的实证研究","a":"Fork-based development enables parallel evolution of software, but unsynchronized contributions create persistent divergence: security patches, bug fixes, and quality improvements often fail to propagate across fork families, leaving downstream users exposed to known vulnerabilities or bugs and missing massive opportunities to improve the other repositories in the family. We present the first large-scale empirical study of fork synchronization, analyzing popular GitHub fork families with 3,820 actively maintained forks, and developed a monitoring platform to mine the valuable commits and promote their swift merging. Our findings reveal a synchronization paradox: while 90% of submitted pull requests are merged, only 6.92% of fork commits ever appear in PRs, leaving massive fork development permanently unsynchronized across the families. Synchronization delay is pervasive and structurally uneven where fork propagation accounts for 72.9% of end-to-end commit lifecycle delay. Contrary to common assumptions, PR rejection is rarely caused by technical incorrectness; instead, 65% of rejections stem from superseded contributions, process violations, or maintainer policy decisions. Based on these insights, we develop a three-stage syncability assessment pipeline that identifies fork-local commits that are both sync-worthy (broadly beneficial) and sync-eligible (technically and policy-compatibly portable). Applied to 0.5 million fork-local commits, our pipeline surfaces 12,284 sync-ready commit–repository pairs, demonstrating that our approach identifies practically valuable changes. To further validate the security impact, we manually reviewed 153 security-related commit–repository pairs and confirmed 83 as potential 1-day vulnerabilities, for which we produced 35 proof-of-concept demonstrations and filed issues to the affected repositories. Our monitoring platform enables continuous, near-real-time detection of synchronization opportunities across fork families, improving the sustainability of fork-based open-source ecosystems.","az":"基于分叉的开发使软件得以并行演化，但未同步的贡献会造成持续的分歧：安全补丁、缺陷修复和质量改进往往无法在分叉家族之间传播，使下游用户暴露于已知漏洞或缺陷之下，并错失改进家族中其他仓库的大量机会。我们提出首个关于分叉同步的大规模实证研究，分析了包含 3,820 个活跃维护分叉的热门 GitHub 分叉家族，并开发了一个监控平台来挖掘有价值的提交并推动其快速合并。我们的发现揭示了一个同步悖论：虽然 90% 提交的拉取请求（PR）会被合并，但只有 6.92% 的分叉提交曾出现在 PR 中，导致大量分叉开发在家族之间永久不同步。同步延迟普遍存在且在结构上分布不均，其中分叉传播占端到端提交生命周期延迟的 72.9%。与常见假设相反，PR 被拒绝很少是由技术上的不正确造成的；相反，65% 的拒绝源于贡献被取代、流程违规或维护者的策略决定。基于这些洞见，我们开发了一条三阶段的可同步性评估流水线，用以识别既值得同步（具有广泛益处）又符合同步条件（在技术与策略上可移植）的分叉本地提交。将其应用于 50 万条分叉本地提交后，我们的流水线筛出 12,284 对可同步的提交—仓库配对，表明我们的方法能识别出具有实际价值的变更。为进一步验证安全影响，我们人工审阅了 153 对与安全相关的提交—仓库配对，确认其中 83 个为潜在的 1-day 漏洞，为此我们制作了 35 个概念验证演示并向受影响的仓库提交了 issue。我们的监控平台能够跨分叉家族持续、近实时地检测同步机会，提升了基于分叉的开源生态的可持续性。","tl":"揭示分叉同步悖论，并用三阶段流水线筛出可同步提交与 1-day 漏洞。","au":["Jiaying Zhu","Lyuye Zhang","Wu Jiahui","CHENGYUE LIU","Yang Liu"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","security"],"kw":["fork synchronization","pull request analysis","commit propagation","1-day vulnerabilities","GitHub mining"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/42/x"},{"id":"p01325","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PoCE: Automated Proof-of-Concept Synthesis using Large Language Models for Robust Validation","tz":"PoCE：使用大语言模型自动合成概念验证以实现稳健验证","a":"Vulnerability reports play a critical role in software repair, with Proof-of-Concept (PoC) exploits serving as one of their most essential components. PoC exploits enable software developers to reliably reproduce reported vulnerabilities and subsequently deploy patches. However, generating effective PoCs is costly, expertise-intensive, and increasingly challenging due to the diversity of modern software ecosystems and their complex dependencies. Inadequate or incorrect PoCs can significantly delay patch deployment, thereby increasing the window of exposure to attacks. Prior work on automated PoC generation struggles to produce comprehensive and reliable exploits. In this work, we present an automated PoC generation framework, PoCE, capable of generating PoCs across diverse software systems by handling varied input formats and complex execution contexts using large language models. PoCE integrates structured in-context learning, retrieval-augmented generation, and iterative chain-of-thought reasoning to expand an initial exploitable PoC into multiple validated variants. These variants are executed in controlled environments to confirm exploitability. We evaluate PoCE on eleven widely used software projects, including TensorFlow, Yasm, Zlib, Liblouis, Cflow, TCPDUMP, Fig2dev, Binutils, libsndfile, LibTIFF, and libsixel. Our approach achieves an exploitation success rate of 78.1% and generates multiple exploit variants for most vulnerable cases, uncovering alternative exploit paths and edge conditions. We discover 57 zero-day PoCs and identify 26 previously unknown zero-day vulnerabilities in cross-layer software.","az":"漏洞报告在软件修复中起着关键作用，其中概念验证（PoC）利用是最重要的组成部分之一。PoC 利用使软件开发者能够可靠地复现所报告的漏洞，并随后部署补丁。然而，生成有效的 PoC 代价高昂、依赖专业经验，并且由于现代软件生态的多样性及其复杂的依赖关系而日益困难。不充分或不正确的 PoC 会显著延迟补丁部署，从而扩大受攻击暴露的时间窗口。以往关于自动 PoC 生成的工作难以产出全面且可靠的利用。在本工作中，我们提出自动化 PoC 生成框架 PoCE，它能够利用大语言模型处理多样的输入格式和复杂的执行上下文，从而在各类软件系统上生成 PoC。PoCE 集成了结构化的上下文学习、检索增强生成和迭代式思维链推理，把一个初始的可利用 PoC 扩展为多个经过验证的变体。这些变体在受控环境中执行以确认可利用性。我们在十一个广泛使用的软件项目上评估 PoCE，包括 TensorFlow、Yasm、Zlib、Liblouis、Cflow、TCPDUMP、Fig2dev、Binutils、libsndfile、LibTIFF 和 libsixel。我们的方法取得了 78.1% 的利用成功率，并为大多数脆弱案例生成了多个利用变体，揭示出替代的利用路径与边界条件。我们发现了 57 个零日 PoC，并在跨层软件中识别出 26 个此前未知的零日漏洞。","tl":"用 LLM 把单个 PoC 扩展为多个经执行验证的利用变体，挖出 26 个零日漏洞。","au":["Tanusree Das Tithy","Lamia Hasan Rodoshi","Ayman Rafid Azahar","Amlan Abhidarshi","Tabassum Faruk","Fahmid Al Rifat","Faysal Hossain Shezan"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["proof-of-concept generation","exploit synthesis","retrieval-augmented generation","zero-day vulnerabilities","vulnerability reproduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/43/x"},{"id":"p01326","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Branch-Level Fault Localization in ADS Planning via Temporal Coverage Analysis","tz":"基于时序覆盖分析的 ADS 规划模块分支级缺陷定位","a":"Planning failures in Automated Driving Systems (ADS) are increasingly detected through simulation-based testing, yet localizing their root causes within planning code remains a major challenge. Planning modules execute complex rule-based decision logic over hundreds of frames in a closed-loop interaction with the environment, where faults trigger observable failures only after temporal gaps and under specific execution contexts. These characteristics make traditional spectrum-based fault localization ineffective, as faulty behavior is obscured by execution-level coverage aggregation and limited test diversity. In this paper, we study the problem of debugging planning failures and present a temporal coverage analysis approach for localizing faults in rule-based planning modules. Our key insight is that, while execution-aggregated coverage masks fault behavior, frame-level execution dynamics reveal distinctive temporal signatures that indicate when and how faulty branches activate. Leveraging this insight, our approach first identifies a suspicious frame using planning semantics, and then ranks candidate branches by analyzing their execution behavior within a localized temporal window. We evaluate our approach on 221 reproducible planning failures drawn from a publicly available Apollo planning failure dataset. Our results show that temporal coverage analysis enables accurate suspicious-frame identification and substantially reduces branch inspection effort compared to baseline heuristics, effectively localizing faults from a single failing execution. We further analyze failure cases that lack observable execution signals to clarify the fundamental limits of execution-based localization. Overall, this work demonstrates that temporal execution analysis provides a practical and effective foundation for debugging planning failures in rule-based ADS planning modules.","az":"自动驾驶系统（ADS）的规划失败越来越多地通过基于仿真的测试被发现，但在规划代码中定位其根因仍是一大挑战。规划模块会在与环境的闭环交互中、跨数百帧执行复杂的基于规则的决策逻辑，其中的故障只有在存在时间间隔且处于特定执行上下文时才会触发可观测的失败。这些特性使传统的基于频谱的缺陷定位失效，因为故障行为被执行级的覆盖聚合以及有限的测试多样性所掩盖。本文研究规划失败的调试问题，提出一种用于定位基于规则的规划模块中故障的时序覆盖分析方法。我们的关键洞见是：虽然执行聚合后的覆盖会掩盖故障行为，但帧级的执行动态会显现出独特的时序特征，指示故障分支何时以及如何被激活。基于该洞见，我们的方法首先利用规划语义识别出一个可疑帧，然后通过分析候选分支在局部时间窗口内的执行行为对其排序。我们在取自公开 Apollo 规划失败数据集的 221 个可复现规划失败上评估了该方法。结果表明，时序覆盖分析能够准确识别可疑帧，并相比基线启发式方法大幅降低分支检查工作量，可从单次失败执行中有效定位故障。我们还进一步分析了缺乏可观测执行信号的失败案例，以厘清基于执行的定位方法的根本局限。总体而言，本工作表明时序执行分析为调试基于规则的 ADS 规划模块中的规划失败提供了实用而有效的基础。","tl":"用帧级时序覆盖特征替代聚合覆盖，实现单次失败即可定位规划分支故障。","au":["Sangmin Woo","Dohyun Kim","Donghwan Shin","Yongdae Kim"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["fault localization","autonomous driving system","temporal coverage","planning failure","spectrum-based localization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/44/x"},{"id":"p01327","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Better Call Grep: Evaluating and Improving Grep-Like Lexical Retrieval for Repository-Level Code Completion","tz":"Better Call Grep：评估并改进面向仓库级代码补全的类 Grep 词法检索","a":"Repository-level code completion remains challenging for large language models (LLMs), as it requires reasoning over cross-file dependencies while under limited context windows. To address this challenge, prior work has adopted Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) frameworks based on semantic indexing or structure-aware graph analysis. Although effective, these approaches introduce substantial computational overhead for index construction and maintenance, which hinders their practicality in real-world development. Motivated by common developer workflows that rely on lightweight search utilities (e.g., ripgrep) to locate relevant code, we revisit a fundamental yet underexplored question: how far can simple, index-free lexical retrieval go in supporting repository-level code completion before more complex retrieval mechanisms become necessary? To answer this question, we systematically explore the potential of lightweight, index-free, intent-aware lexical retrieval through extensive empirical analysis. We first introduce Naive GrepRAG, a baseline framework where LLMs autonomously generate ripgrep commands to localize relevant context. Our preliminary experiments show that even this basic implementation achieves performance comparable to sophisticated graph-based baselines. Further analysis reveals that its effectiveness stems from retrieving code fragments that are lexically precise and spatially closer to the completion site. However, we identify key limitations of this approach, including sensitivity to noisy matches caused by high-frequency ambiguous keywords and context fragmentation due to rigid truncation boundaries. To address these issues, we propose GrepRAG, which augments lexical retrieval with a lightweight post-processing pipeline featuring identifier-weighted re-ranking and structure-aware deduplication. Extensive evaluation on CrossCodeEval and RepoEval_Updated demonstrates that GrepRAG consistently outperforms state-of-the-art (SOTA) methods. In particular, on CrossCodeEval, GrepRAG achieves 7.04–15.58% relative improvement in code exact match (EM) over the best baseline.","az":"仓库级代码补全对大语言模型（LLM）而言仍具挑战性，因为它要求在受限上下文窗口下对跨文件依赖进行推理。为应对这一挑战，已有工作采用了基于语义索引或结构感知图分析的检索增强生成（RAG）框架。这些方法虽然有效，却为索引构建与维护带来了可观的计算开销，阻碍了其在真实开发中的实用性。受到开发者常依赖轻量搜索工具（如 ripgrep）来定位相关代码这一常见工作流的启发，我们重新审视一个基本却少被探索的问题：在更复杂的检索机制变得必要之前，简单、无索引的词法检索在支撑仓库级代码补全上究竟能走多远？为回答该问题，我们通过大量实证分析系统地探索了轻量、无索引、意图感知的词法检索的潜力。我们首先提出 Naive GrepRAG，一个让 LLM 自主生成 ripgrep 命令以定位相关上下文的基线框架。初步实验表明，即使这一基础实现也能取得与复杂的基于图的基线相当的性能。进一步分析显示，其有效性源于检索到的代码片段在词法上更精确，且在空间位置上更接近补全点。然而，我们也识别出该方法的关键局限，包括对高频歧义关键词导致的噪声匹配的敏感性，以及僵硬截断边界带来的上下文碎片化。为解决这些问题，我们提出 GrepRAG，它为词法检索增加了一条轻量的后处理流水线，包含标识符加权重排序与结构感知去重。在 CrossCodeEval 与 RepoEval_Updated 上的大量评估表明，GrepRAG 持续优于最新方法（SOTA）。特别是在 CrossCodeEval 上，GrepRAG 相较最佳基线在代码精确匹配（EM）上取得 7.04–15.58% 的相对提升。","tl":"证明无索引 ripgrep 词法检索加轻量重排即可超越图检索基线。","au":["baoyi wang","Xingliang Wang","Guochang Li","Chen Zhi","Junxiao Han","Xinkui Zhao","Nan Wang","Shuiguang Deng","Jianwei Yin"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["repository-level code completion","lexical retrieval","ripgrep","retrieval-augmented generation","cross-file context"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/45/x"},{"id":"p01328","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Beyond the Surface: Towards Feature-Driven Fuzzing on the Chrome Browser","tz":"超越表层：面向 Chrome 浏览器的特性驱动模糊测试","a":"Modern web browsers constitute complex software systems responsible for processing and rendering diverse web content. Despite extensive testing and security measures implemented by browser vendors and the community, the inherent complexity of these systems makes the complete elimination of vulnerabilities practically infeasible. Existing DOM and API fuzzing techniques inadequately address the expanded attack surface introduced by modern browser features and extensions, resulting in a substantial number of elusive vulnerabilities remaining undetected. This paper presents Feazzer, an efficient feature-driven browser fuzzing framework designed to detect elusive vulnerabilities introduced by browser features. Our approach leverages hybrid programs comprising HTML and browser extensions with systematically clustered feature options to explore deep browser states that existing fuzzers fail to reach. We introduce a message-guided fuzzing mechanism that reduces feature conflicts and enhances the semantic quality of generated test cases. Our comprehensive evaluation across multiple Chromium versions demonstrates that Feazzer achieves up to 231.1% improvement in code coverage compared to state-of-the-art fuzzers. Feazzer has discovered 39 previously unknown bugs in Chromium, with 6 assigned CVEs and acknowledgment of over $55,000 in bug bounties from the vendor. Notably, 2 bugs are rated as critical and 27 as high severity, demonstrating the effectiveness of Feazzer in discovering impactful bugs.","az":"现代 Web 浏览器是负责处理与渲染多样化 Web 内容的复杂软件系统。尽管浏览器厂商与社区实施了大量测试与安全措施，这些系统固有的复杂性使得彻底消除漏洞在实践中不可行。现有的 DOM 与 API 模糊测试技术难以覆盖现代浏览器特性与扩展所引入的扩大攻击面，导致大量难以触发的漏洞仍未被发现。本文提出 Feazzer，一个高效的特性驱动浏览器模糊测试框架，用于检测由浏览器特性引入的难以触发的漏洞。我们的方法利用由 HTML 与浏览器扩展构成的混合程序，并对特性选项进行系统化聚类，以探索现有模糊器无法到达的深层浏览器状态。我们引入一种消息引导的模糊测试机制，以减少特性冲突并提升生成测试用例的语义质量。在多个 Chromium 版本上的全面评估表明，Feazzer 相较最新模糊器在代码覆盖率上最高提升 231.1%。Feazzer 已在 Chromium 中发现 39 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 6 个被分配了 CVE，并获得厂商超过 55,000 美元的漏洞赏金致谢。值得注意的是，其中 2 个缺陷被评为严重级、27 个为高危级，表明 Feazzer 在发现高影响缺陷方面的有效性。","tl":"用 HTML 与扩展构成的混合程序按特性聚类驱动浏览器深层状态探索。","au":["Chaoyuan Peng","Muhui Jiang","Yajin Zhou","Lei Wu"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["security","tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["browser fuzzing","Chromium","browser extensions","feature-driven testing","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/46/x"},{"id":"p01329","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SemantiX: A Compatibility Checker between Applications and Compositions of Distributed Systems","tz":"SemantiX：应用与分布式系统组合之间的兼容性检查器","a":"Modern distributed applications compose multiple services with different consistency guarantees. Mismatches between application requirements and chosen system semantics can introduce subtle bugs, but verifying compatibility across complex applications is both challenging and time-consuming. In particular, existing approaches on testing or rigorous formal verification lack flexibility and cannot promptly provide correctness guarantees on multi-semantic compositions. We present SemantiX, a framework for checking semantic compatibility between applications and compositions of distributed systems with heterogeneous consistency models. SemantiX embeds formally defined distributed system modules of consistency semantics which include the first formal definition of visibility constraints. SemantiX introduces the AppGraph approach for systematically modeling complex applications. Applications modeled using AppGraphs can be checked for their compatibility against a combination of distributed system modules. Alternatively, SemantiX can search for combinations of modules compatible to the application. We present three case studies on a movie streaming service, an e-commerce platform, and a cross-service causal distributed storage service. We demonstrate that SemantiX can capture complex service compositions with minimal encoding effort and quickly check compositional compatibility with underlying systems or find the compatible system sets. SemantiX enables developers to efficiently verify distributed application designs and explore alternative consistency configurations, supporting more agile development.","az":"现代分布式应用会组合多个具有不同一致性保证的服务。应用需求与所选系统语义之间的不匹配会引入微妙的缺陷，但在复杂应用上验证兼容性既困难又耗时。特别是，现有的测试或严格形式化验证方法缺乏灵活性，无法及时为多语义组合提供正确性保证。我们提出 SemantiX，一个用于检查应用与具有异构一致性模型的分布式系统组合之间语义兼容性的框架。SemantiX 内嵌了形式化定义的一致性语义分布式系统模块，其中包含首个对可见性约束的形式化定义。SemantiX 引入 AppGraph 方法来系统化地建模复杂应用。用 AppGraph 建模的应用可以针对分布式系统模块的组合进行兼容性检查。此外，SemantiX 也可以搜索与该应用兼容的模块组合。我们给出三个案例研究：一个影视流媒体服务、一个电商平台以及一个跨服务因果一致的分布式存储服务。我们证明 SemantiX 能以极小的编码代价刻画复杂的服务组合，并快速检查其与底层系统的组合兼容性或找出兼容的系统集合。SemantiX 使开发者能够高效验证分布式应用设计并探索备选的一致性配置，从而支持更敏捷的开发。","tl":"首次形式化可见性约束，并用 AppGraph 检查应用与一致性模块组合的兼容性。","au":["Yifei Sun","Ji-Yong Shin"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["distributed systems","consistency models","compatibility checking","visibility constraints","AppGraph"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/47/x"},{"id":"p01330","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"On the Role of Large Language Models in Robustness-Guided Requirement Falsification","tz":"论大语言模型在鲁棒性引导的需求证伪中的作用","a":"Robustness-guided falsification supports the validation of cyber-physical systems by searching for system traces that violate formal temporal requirements. Existing falsification methods typically treat candidate generation as numerical search over an input space, guided by quantitative robustness feedback. This paper studies a different mechanism: a guarded advisory proposer that uses a Large Language Model to generate candidate inputs. The LLM-based proposer suggests candidates inputs using the following information: the requirement to validate, the interface of the system under test, and previously evaluated robustness history. Admission gates ensure that only valid candidate inputs are considered for execution. We evaluate this approach on 19 falsification requirements from the ARCH-COMP 2024 CPS benchmark and on five synthetic problems. The results show that LLM-based proposing is sensitive to model choice and context representation. Among the tested variants, GPT-P, which uses a GPT model with the plain context representation, is the most reliable representative variant. On ARCH-COMP, GPT-P reaches perfect falsification on 16 of 19 requirements, obtains at least one falsification on all 19 requirements, and, on 8 requirements, uses the fewest executions among the reported tools that also achieve perfect falsification. However, its performance is heterogeneous. We explain this behavior through three classes of falsification problems: informative context cues, ambiguous context cues with strong robustness gradient, and ambiguous context cues with weak robustness gradient. Synthetic benchmark problems reproduce these classes under controlled mechanisms. Overall, GPT-P performs best on the informative-context-cue class, where the requirement and SUT interface expose useful candidate hypotheses that the LLM can exploit before extensive robustness-feedback search is needed. To our knowledge, this use of semantic context cues for candidate input proposal is not supported by existing robustness-guided falsification methods.","az":"鲁棒性引导的证伪通过搜索违反形式化时序需求的系统轨迹，支撑信息物理系统的验证。现有证伪方法通常将候选生成视为在输入空间上的数值搜索，由定量的鲁棒性反馈引导。本文研究一种不同的机制：一种使用大语言模型生成候选输入的受控建议器（guarded advisory proposer）。基于 LLM 的建议器利用以下信息给出候选输入：待验证的需求、被测系统的接口，以及此前评估过的鲁棒性历史。准入门控确保只有有效的候选输入才会被执行。我们在 ARCH-COMP 2024 CPS 基准的 19 条证伪需求以及五个合成问题上评估该方法。结果表明，基于 LLM 的建议对模型选择与上下文表示较为敏感。在测试的各变体中，使用 GPT 模型加纯文本上下文表示的 GPT-P 是最可靠的代表性变体。在 ARCH-COMP 上，GPT-P 在 19 条需求中的 16 条达到完美证伪，在全部 19 条需求上至少获得一次证伪，并在 8 条需求上以最少的执行次数超过其他同样达成完美证伪的工具。然而其表现并不均衡。我们用三类证伪问题来解释这一行为：具有信息量的上下文线索、上下文线索模糊但鲁棒性梯度强、上下文线索模糊且鲁棒性梯度弱。合成基准问题在受控机制下复现了这三类情形。总体而言，GPT-P 在具有信息量上下文线索的一类问题上表现最佳——此时需求与被测系统接口暴露出有用的候选假设，LLM 可在需要大量鲁棒性反馈搜索之前加以利用。据我们所知，这种将语义上下文线索用于候选输入建议的做法在现有鲁棒性引导证伪方法中尚不被支持。","tl":"首次让 LLM 利用需求与接口的语义线索提出证伪候选输入。","au":["Ali Kaya","Ivan Porres"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["falsification","cyber-physical systems","temporal requirements","LLM proposer","ARCH-COMP"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/48/x"},{"id":"p01331","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Secrets Unlocked: Evaluating LLMs for Secrets Detection in Android Apps","tz":"Secrets Unlocked：评估 LLM 在 Android 应用密钥检测中的能力","a":"Mobile apps frequently embed sensitive secrets, such as API keys, access tokens, client secrets, and private keys that support internal functionality or enable integration with external systems and third-party services. Developers frequently embed these secrets into Android apps, which allows attackers to extract them through reverse engineering. Once exposed, attackers can exploit them to access sensitive data, manipulate resources, or abuse APIs, resulting in severe security and potential financial risks. In this paper, we present the first large-scale empirical evidence that off-the-shelf large language models (LLMs) can automatically identify secrets in Android apps without any domain-specific prior knowledge, thereby substantially lowering the barrier for attackers. On a benchmark of 5135 Android apps from prior work, LLMs rediscovered 93% of previously known secrets and identified 4361 additional valid credentials (+195%). Extending our analysis to 50 000 Google Play apps collected between August and October 2025, we conducted the largest-scale study to date on secret detection in Android apps, identifying secrets in 17 590 apps (35%). Among the 18 908 detected secrets, 1802 remained active at discovery, including, among others, critical credentials such as Stripe payment keys, OpenAI API keys, and GitHub personal access tokens. We responsibly contacted all the affected developers, of whom 170 confirmed the issues and updated their apps accordingly. Our findings empirically demonstrate the reality of vibe hacking: anyone can now leverage publicly accessible AI models to perform complex offensive security tasks with minimal expertise.","az":"移动应用常常内嵌敏感密钥，例如 API key、访问令牌、客户端密钥与私钥，用于支撑内部功能或实现与外部系统和第三方服务的集成。开发者频繁将这些密钥嵌入 Android 应用，使攻击者可以通过逆向工程提取它们。一旦泄露，攻击者便可利用其访问敏感数据、操纵资源或滥用 API，造成严重的安全与潜在财务风险。本文给出首个大规模实证证据，表明现成的大语言模型（LLM）无需任何领域先验知识即可自动识别 Android 应用中的密钥，从而大幅降低了攻击者的门槛。在取自已有工作的 5135 个 Android 应用基准上，LLM 重新发现了 93% 的已知密钥，并额外识别出 4361 个有效凭据（+195%）。将分析扩展到 2025 年 8 月至 10 月间收集的 50,000 个 Google Play 应用后，我们开展了迄今规模最大的 Android 应用密钥检测研究，在 17,590 个应用（35%）中发现了密钥。在检测到的 18,908 个密钥中，1802 个在发现时仍然有效，其中包括 Stripe 支付密钥、OpenAI API 密钥与 GitHub 个人访问令牌等关键凭据。我们负责任地联系了所有受影响的开发者，其中 170 位确认了问题并相应更新了应用。我们的发现实证展示了“氛围黑客（vibe hacking）”的现实性：任何人如今都可以借助可公开访问的 AI 模型，以极少的专业知识完成复杂的攻击性安全任务。","tl":"首次大规模证明现成 LLM 可零门槛挖出五万应用中的有效凭据。","au":["Marco Alecci","Jordan Samhi","Tegawendé F. Bissyandé","Jacques Klein"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["secrets detection","Android apps","hardcoded credentials","large language models","large-scale study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/49/x"},{"id":"p01332","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SAGE: Signal-Amplified Guided Embeddings for Vulnerability Detection","tz":"SAGE：面向漏洞检测的信号放大引导嵌入","a":"While Large Language Models (LLMs) have achieved milestones in automated software engineering, their application to vulnerability detection remains constrained by a notable sensitivity barrier. Despite advancements in graph-based analysis and supervised fine-tuning, existing paradigms frequently struggle to isolate the fine-grained, sparse semantic deviations characteristic of vulnerabilities from the dominant background of functional logic. We argue that this limitation stems from a notable architectural phenomenon we term Signal Submersion. Our analysis reveals that while vulnerability-relevant features are activated in intermediate layers, these sparse signals occupy a disproportionately small magnitude and are substantially diminished by global semantic representations. To address this, we propose SAGE (Signal-Amplified Guided Embeddings), a framework that transitions from passive inference to active signal amplification. SAGE employs a task-conditional Sparse Autoencoder (SAE) to project entangled representations onto a high-dimensional sparse manifold, mechanistically decoupling and resurfacing faint vulnerability signals. Extensive evaluations on BigVul, PrimeVul, and the zero-day benchmark PreciseBugs demonstrate that SAGE establishes new state-of-the-art performance. Notably, SAGE achieves relative MCC gains of up to 318% on unseen distributions and enables a 7B model to outperform 34B generalist baselines, validating that mechanistic disentanglement is a more efficient path to security than simply increasing model size.","az":"尽管大语言模型（LLM）在自动化软件工程中取得了里程碑式进展，它们在漏洞检测上的应用仍受到显著的敏感性瓶颈制约。尽管基于图的分析与有监督微调不断进步，现有范式仍常常难以将漏洞特有的细粒度、稀疏语义偏差从占主导地位的功能逻辑背景中分离出来。我们认为，这一局限源于一种我们称之为“信号淹没（Signal Submersion）”的显著架构现象。我们的分析表明，虽然与漏洞相关的特征在中间层被激活，但这些稀疏信号所占的幅值极小，并被全局语义表示大幅削弱。为此，我们提出 SAGE（Signal-Amplified Guided Embeddings），一个从被动推理转向主动信号放大的框架。SAGE 采用任务条件化的稀疏自编码器（SAE），将纠缠的表示投影到高维稀疏流形上，从机制上解耦并重新凸显微弱的漏洞信号。在 BigVul、PrimeVul 以及零日基准 PreciseBugs 上的大量评估表明，SAGE 取得了新的最佳性能。值得注意的是，SAGE 在未见分布上取得高达 318% 的 MCC 相对提升，并使一个 7B 模型超越 34B 通用基线，验证了机制性解耦比单纯扩大模型规模是通往安全性的更高效路径。","tl":"用稀疏自编码器解耦中间层表示，放大被淹没的漏洞稀疏信号。","au":["Zhengyang Shan","QianXu","Jiayun Xin","Minghui Xu","Yue Zhang","Zhen Yang","Hao Wu","Xiuzhen Cheng"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","sparse autoencoder","representation disentanglement","PrimeVul","signal submersion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/50/x"},{"id":"p01333","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LogicHunter: Testing LLM Agent Frameworks with an Agentic Oracle","tz":"LogicHunter：用智能体式预言测试 LLM 智能体框架","a":"Large Language Model (LLM) agent frameworks such as LangChain, LlamaIndex, and CrewAI have become critical infrastructure powering production AI systems, yet they remain severely under-tested due to fundamental challenges in automated testing. Unlike traditional software, where crashes serve as reliable oracles, defects in these pure Python frameworks manifest as ordinary exceptions or silent semantic failures, creating profound oracle ambiguity. This problem is exacerbated by strict type governance through Pydantic schemas and complex protocol requirements that cause existing fuzzers to generate overwhelming invalid inputs, while traditional test generators produce only trivial cases with weak regression assertions. We present LogicHunter, a fuzzing framework that addresses both the generation and oracle challenges through active specification-aware testing. LogicHunter employs specification-driven generation that systematically fuses formal type constraints with authentic usage patterns from real-world repositories, synthesizing inputs that are valid by construction yet semantically extreme, equipped with behavioral probes to expose silent failures. To resolve oracle ambiguity, we introduce the Agentic Oracle, which transcends passive classification by actively retrieving documentation, navigating source code, and inspecting runtime states through a ReAct-based architecture with Dual-Layer State Management and Dual-Stream Memory. Evaluated on three widely deployed frameworks, LogicHunter discovered 40 previously unknown bugs with 30 confirmed and 26 fixed by developers, while state-of-the-art baselines found none. The Agentic Oracle achieves 90.9% precision, surpassing the best passive approach at 27.9% by 63 percentage points.","az":"LangChain、LlamaIndex、CrewAI 等大语言模型（LLM）智能体框架已成为支撑生产级 AI 系统的关键基础设施，但由于自动化测试中的根本性挑战，它们仍严重缺乏测试。与崩溃可作为可靠预言的传统软件不同，这些纯 Python 框架中的缺陷表现为普通异常或静默的语义失败，造成严重的预言歧义。该问题又被 Pydantic 模式带来的严格类型治理与复杂的协议要求所加剧：现有模糊器会生成大量无效输入，而传统测试生成器只能产出带有弱回归断言的平凡用例。我们提出 LogicHunter，一个通过主动的规约感知测试同时应对生成与预言两大挑战的模糊测试框架。LogicHunter 采用规约驱动的生成方式，系统性地将形式化类型约束与来自真实仓库的真实使用模式融合，合成构造上有效但语义上极端的输入，并配以行为探针来暴露静默失败。为解决预言歧义，我们引入智能体式预言（Agentic Oracle），它超越被动分类，通过基于 ReAct 的架构并结合双层状态管理与双流记忆，主动检索文档、浏览源代码并检查运行时状态。在三个被广泛部署的框架上评估，LogicHunter 发现了 40 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 30 个被确认、26 个已被开发者修复，而最新基线方法一个也没有发现。智能体式预言达到 90.9% 的精确率，比最佳被动方法的 27.9% 高出 63 个百分点。","tl":"用 ReAct 智能体充当测试预言，捕获智能体框架的静默语义失败。","au":["Minghui Long","Yanjie Zhao","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["agent framework testing","fuzzing","agentic oracle","LangChain","silent semantic failure"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/51/x"},{"id":"p01334","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Temporal Reasoning Benchmarking Framework for LRMs via Difficulty-controlled and Dynamic Test Generation","tz":"面向大推理模型的时序推理基准框架：难度可控与动态测试生成","a":"Defining the reasoning boundaries and ensuring the reliability of Large Reasoning Models (LRMs) remains a critical challenge. Current benchmarks primarily rely on static datasets susceptible to data contamination or synthetic tasks lacking fine-grained difficulty control. Furthermore, standard outcome-based evaluations often conceal reasoning flaws by neglecting the reasoning process. To address these limitations, we introduce TRACE, a testing framework that models temporal reasoning as constraint satisfaction problems via Allen’s Interval Algebra. This approach enables precise regulation of logical complexity and incorporates a Trace-Based Verification Oracle to validate reasoning faithfulness. Using this framework, we construct TRACEBench, an extensive benchmark comprising 1,200 synthesized test instances across graded difficulty levels. We employ TRACE to evaluate six widely used LRMs on TRACEBench. The results confirm a strong negative correlation between model performance and our difficulty metric (Pearson’s 𝑟 ≈ −0.97), validating the effectiveness of our difficulty control mechanism. Moreover, our trace-based analysis exposes significant discrepancies between reasoning validity and final answers, revealing a high spurious guessing rate of approximately 28% in mid-sized models. In addition, we diagnose scale-dependent failure modes, ranging from Degenerative Loops in small models to Reasoning Explosion in advanced architectures. TRACE thus provides a robust, automated platform for benchmarking the true temporal reasoning capabilities of LRMs.","az":"界定推理边界并确保大推理模型（LRM）的可靠性仍是关键挑战。当前基准主要依赖易受数据污染影响的静态数据集，或缺乏细粒度难度控制的合成任务。此外，标准的基于结果的评估往往忽略推理过程，从而掩盖了推理缺陷。为解决这些局限，我们提出 TRACE，一个通过 Allen 区间代数将时序推理建模为约束满足问题的测试框架。该方法可精确调控逻辑复杂度，并引入基于轨迹的验证预言（Trace-Based Verification Oracle）来校验推理的忠实性。基于该框架，我们构建了 TRACEBench，一个包含 1,200 个分级难度合成测试实例的大型基准。我们使用 TRACE 在 TRACEBench 上评估了六个被广泛使用的 LRM。结果确认模型性能与我们的难度度量之间存在强负相关（Pearson r ≈ −0.97），验证了难度控制机制的有效性。而且，基于轨迹的分析揭示了推理有效性与最终答案之间的显著不一致，显示中等规模模型中约 28% 的高虚假猜测率。此外，我们诊断出依赖模型规模的失效模式：从小模型中的退化循环（Degenerative Loops）到先进架构中的推理爆炸（Reasoning Explosion）。因此，TRACE 为评测 LRM 真实的时序推理能力提供了稳健、自动化的平台。","tl":"用区间代数做难度可控的动态生成，并以轨迹预言查验推理忠实性。","au":["shide zhou","Kailong Wang","Ling Shi","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"llm-reasoning-and-test-time-scaling","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["cross-track-bridge","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["temporal reasoning","large reasoning models","difficulty control","trace-based verification","dynamic benchmark"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/52/x"},{"id":"p01335","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Comprehensive Empirical Analysis of Patch Presence Testing: Capabilities, Limitations, and Paths Forward","tz":"补丁存在性检测的全面实证分析：能力、局限与前进路径","a":"Patch presence testing determines whether a binary incorporates the security fixes associated with a known vulnerability and has become increasingly important in software supply-chain security. However, despite numerous proposed techniques, the field still lacks a comprehensive understanding of the practical capabilities and limitations of existing approaches. Fundamental questions remain unanswered, including how well current tools perform in real-world settings, which vulnerability or patch characteristics shape detection accuracy, and what underlying factors limit the effectiveness of all existing tools. To address these issues, we conduct the first systematic and in-depth empirical study of patch presence testing for C/C++ binaries. We construct a high-fidelity benchmark comprising 561 CVEs across ten widely used projects, compiled under diverse configurations. Using this dataset, we perform an extensive evaluation of five state-of-the-art tools representing both syntactic and semantic methodologies. Our findings show that: (1) accuracy reported in prior work reflects only cases where tools successfully generate outputs, whereas in practice many tools frequently fail to produce any result; (2) patch semantics, code scale, and compiler options exert strong influence on accuracy, whereas CWE categories provide little predictive value; (3) common failures fall into two major categories: algorithmic limitations, such as the inability to detect subtle or evolved patches, and engineering deficiencies, such as failures triggered by function level structural modifications or symbol duplication. Building on these findings, we develop two improvement strategies and integrate them into state-of-the-art tools, resulting in notable gains in both accuracy and overall reliability for patch detection.","az":"补丁存在性检测用于判断一个二进制是否包含与某个已知漏洞相关的安全修复，在软件供应链安全中日益重要。然而，尽管已有大量技术被提出，该领域仍缺乏对现有方法实际能力与局限的全面认识。一些根本问题仍未解答，包括当前工具在真实场景中的表现如何、哪些漏洞或补丁特征影响检测准确率，以及哪些底层因素限制了所有现有工具的有效性。为此，我们开展了首个针对 C/C++ 二进制补丁存在性检测的系统性深入实证研究。我们构建了一个高保真基准，涵盖十个广泛使用项目中的 561 个 CVE，并在多种配置下编译。基于该数据集，我们对代表句法与语义两类方法的五个最新工具进行了广泛评估。我们的发现表明：(1) 已有工作报告的准确率只反映了工具成功产生输出的情形，而在实践中许多工具常常无法给出任何结果；(2) 补丁语义、代码规模与编译器选项对准确率有强烈影响，而 CWE 类别几乎没有预测价值；(3) 常见失败可归为两大类：算法性局限，例如无法检测细微或演化后的补丁；以及工程性缺陷，例如由函数级结构修改或符号重复触发的失败。基于这些发现，我们提出两种改进策略并将其集成到最新工具中，使补丁检测在准确率与整体可靠性上都获得显著提升。","tl":"揭示补丁存在性工具常常无输出，并指出编译选项与补丁语义才是主因。","au":["Xiaobei Zhang","Yaowen Zheng","Wu Luo","Shijun Zhao","Yongsheng Tao","Dan Meng","Rui Hou"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset","security"],"kw":["patch presence testing","binary analysis","CVE benchmark","empirical evaluation","supply chain security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/53/x"},{"id":"p01336","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"An Empirical Study of Speculative Decoding on Software Engineering Tasks","tz":"推测解码在软件工程任务上的实证研究","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have become widely used for Software Engineering (SE) tasks, spanning from function-level code generation to complex repository-level workflows. However, the high latency of autoregressive inference remains a significant bottleneck, hindering their deployment in interactive environments. While Speculative Decoding (SD) offers a promising technique for lossless acceleration, prior research on long-context repository-level tasks and complex agentic interactions remains limited. To bridge this gap, we present the first systematic empirical study to evaluate the effectiveness of SD in SE tasks. We systematically benchmark a comprehensive spectrum of strategies, encompassing both model-based and model-free methods, across representative generation, editing, and repair scenarios. Our empirical results indicate that SD demonstrates clear potential for accelerating inference, particularly for smaller models that achieve higher speedups than those of their larger counterparts. We find that the effectiveness of SD methods varies across different task scenarios. Model-based approaches are well-suited for code generation, whereas model-free methods are better adapted to repository-level repair and editing scenarios. Furthermore, we observe that the repetitiveness of SE tasks improves the performance of model-free methods. In contrast to natural language tasks, the higher predictability of SE tasks allows for more aggressive hyperparameters. Our findings are summarized as guidelines to help increase inference efficiency for SE scenarios.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）已被广泛用于软件工程（SE）任务，覆盖从函数级代码生成到复杂的仓库级工作流。然而，自回归推理的高延迟仍是显著瓶颈，阻碍其在交互式环境中的部署。虽然推测解码（Speculative Decoding, SD）提供了一种有前景的无损加速技术，但针对长上下文仓库级任务与复杂智能体交互的既有研究仍然有限。为弥合这一空白，我们给出首个系统性实证研究，评估 SD 在 SE 任务中的有效性。我们在具有代表性的生成、编辑与修复场景下，系统地基准测试了涵盖基于模型与无模型两类方法的完整策略谱系。我们的实证结果表明，SD 在加速推理方面具有明显潜力，尤其对较小模型，其加速比高于更大的模型。我们发现 SD 方法的有效性在不同任务场景间存在差异：基于模型的方法更适合代码生成，而无模型方法更适应仓库级修复与编辑场景。此外，我们观察到 SE 任务的重复性提升了无模型方法的表现。与自然语言任务相比，SE 任务更高的可预测性允许采用更激进的超参数。我们将发现总结为指南，以帮助提升 SE 场景下的推理效率。","tl":"首次系统测度推测解码在生成/编辑/修复三类 SE 场景的适用边界。","au":["Yijia Li","Junkai Chen","Xing Hu","Xin Xia"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["speculative decoding","inference latency","software engineering tasks","empirical study","repository-level tasks"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/54/x"},{"id":"p01337","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Lookahead-then-Verify: Reliable Constrained Decoding for Diffusion LLMs under Context-Free Grammars","tz":"先前瞻再验证：上下文无关文法下扩散式大语言模型的可靠受约束解码","a":"Diffusion Large Language Models (dLLMs) have demonstrated promising generative capabilities and are increasingly used to produce formal languages defined by context-free grammars, such as source code and chemical expressions. However, as probabilistic models, they still struggle to generate syntactically valid outputs reliably. A natural and promising direction to address this issue is to adapt constrained decoding techniques to enforce grammatical correctness during generation. However, applying these techniques faces two primary obstacles. On the one hand, the non-autoregressive nature of dLLMs renders most existing constrained decoding approaches inapplicable. On the other hand, current approaches specifically designed for dLLMs may allow intermediate outputs that are impossible to complete into valid sentences, which significantly limits their reliability in practice. To address these challenges, we present LAVE, a constrained decoding approach specifically designed for dLLMs. Our approach leverages a key property of dLLMs, namely their ability to predict token distributions for all positions in parallel during each forward pass. Whenever a new token is proposed by model, LAVE performs lookahead using these distributions to efficiently and reliably verify the validity of the proposed token. This design ensures reliable constraints by reliably preserving the potential for intermediate outputs to be extended into valid sentences. Extensive experiments across four widely used dLLMs and three representative benchmarks demonstrate that LAVE consistently outperforms existing baselines and achieves substantial improvements in syntactic correctness, while incurring negligible runtime overhead.","az":"扩散式大语言模型（dLLM）已展现出可观的生成能力，并越来越多地被用于生成由上下文无关文法定义的形式语言，例如源代码与化学表达式。然而，作为概率模型，它们仍难以可靠地生成语法有效的输出。解决该问题的一个自然且有前景的方向是改造受约束解码技术，以在生成过程中强制文法正确性。但应用这些技术面临两个主要障碍。一方面，dLLM 的非自回归特性使大多数现有受约束解码方法不再适用。另一方面，当前专为 dLLM 设计的方法可能允许出现无法补全为合法句子的中间输出，这在实践中显著限制了其可靠性。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 LAVE，一种专为 dLLM 设计的受约束解码方法。我们的方法利用 dLLM 的一个关键性质，即它们能在每次前向传播中并行预测所有位置上的 token 分布。每当模型提出一个新 token，LAVE 便利用这些分布进行前瞻，以高效且可靠地验证所提 token 的有效性。该设计通过可靠地保持中间输出可被扩展为合法句子的可能性，确保了约束的可靠性。在四个被广泛使用的 dLLM 与三个代表性基准上的大量实验表明，LAVE 持续优于现有基线，在语法正确性上取得显著提升，同时运行时开销可忽略不计。","tl":"利用 dLLM 并行分布做前瞻验证，确保中间输出仍可补全为合法句。","au":["Yitong Zhang","Yongmin Li","Yuetong Liu","Jia Li","Xiaoran Jia","Zherui Li","Ge Li"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"model-architectures-moe-and-diffusion-lms","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["diffusion LLM","constrained decoding","context-free grammar","syntactic validity","lookahead verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/55/x"},{"id":"p01338","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ChromaEyes: Detecting Inconsistencies of User Interface Elements between Light and Dark Modes of Web Applications","tz":"ChromaEyes：检测 Web 应用明暗模式间用户界面元素的不一致","a":"Dark mode interfaces in web applications have gained widespread adoption because of improved user comfort and reduced power consumption. While these interfaces can be implemented through built-in support or browser extensions that convert light mode layouts, inconsistencies frequently arise during the conversion process, including invisible UI elements, misplaced components, and incorrect color mappings. Despite the prevalence of these issues, no existing approaches systematically detect such inconsistencies between light and dark mode interfaces. Our preliminary study shows that popular commercial vision language models and accessibility issue detectors are ineffective for this task. This paper presents ChromaEyes, a novel approach to automatically detecting inconsistencies of graphical user interface elements between light and dark mode layouts of web applications. Detecting such inconsistencies is inherently challenging given that, since mode conversion intentionally changes colors and contrast, UI elements in light and dark modes are expected to look different. Thus, pixel-wise or visual comparison cannot distinguish intentional adaptations from actual errors. ChromaEyes addresses this challenge by analyzing semantic roles and functional meanings of UI elements, enabling accurate correspondence detection between visually distinct but functionally equivalent components. We evaluate our approach on 2,009 screenshot pairs captured from 196 real web applications (147 with native dark mode support and 49 with browser extension-based conversion). ChromaEyes achieves 96.19% accuracy at the screenshot level and 97.95% at the application level, significantly outperforming vision-language models (e.g., GPT-4o) and state-of-the-art accessibility issue detectors (e.g., OwlEye, axe DevTools).","az":"Web 应用中的深色模式界面因提升用户舒适度与降低功耗而被广泛采用。虽然这类界面可以通过内置支持或将浅色模式布局转换的浏览器扩展来实现，但转换过程中常出现不一致，包括不可见的 UI 元素、错位的组件以及错误的颜色映射。尽管这些问题普遍存在，目前尚无方法能够系统地检测浅色与深色模式界面之间的此类不一致。我们的初步研究表明，流行的商用视觉语言模型与无障碍问题检测器在该任务上并不有效。本文提出 ChromaEyes，一种自动检测 Web 应用浅色与深色模式布局之间图形用户界面元素不一致的新方法。检测此类不一致本身就极具挑战：由于模式转换会有意改变颜色与对比度，浅色与深色模式下的 UI 元素本就应当看起来不同，因此逐像素或视觉比较无法区分有意的适配与真正的错误。ChromaEyes 通过分析 UI 元素的语义角色与功能含义来应对这一挑战，从而能够在视觉上不同但功能等价的组件之间准确建立对应关系。我们在从 196 个真实 Web 应用（147 个具备原生深色模式支持，49 个通过浏览器扩展转换）中截取的 2,009 对截图上评估该方法。ChromaEyes 在截图级别达到 96.19% 的准确率，在应用级别达到 97.95%，显著优于视觉语言模型（如 GPT-4o）与最新的无障碍问题检测器（如 OwlEye、axe DevTools）。","tl":"以语义角色建立明暗模式元素对应，区分有意换色与真实缺陷。","au":["K C Shweta","Byungchul Tak","Tegawendé F. Bissyandé","Dongsun Kim"],"top":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["dark mode","UI inconsistency detection","web applications","semantic role analysis","screenshot comparison"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/56/x"},{"id":"p01339","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Environmental Injection Attacks against GUI Agents in Realistic Dynamic Environments","tz":"真实动态环境下针对 GUI 智能体的环境注入攻击","a":"Graphical User Interface (GUI) agents are increasingly deployed to interact with online web services, yet their exposure to open-world content renders them vulnerable to Environmental Injection Attacks (EIAs). In these attacks, an attacker can inject crafted triggers into website to manipulate the behavior of GUI agents used by other users. In this paper, we find that most existing EIA studies fall short of realism. In particular, they fail to capture the dynamic nature of real-world web content, often assuming that a trigger’s on-screen position and surrounding visual context remain largely consistent between training and testing. To better reflect practice, we introduce a realistic dynamic-environment threat model in which the attacker is a regular user and the trigger is embedded within a dynamically changing environment. Under this threat model, existing approaches largely fail, suggesting that their effectiveness in exposing GUI agent vulnerabilities has been substantially overestimated. To expose the hidden vulnerabilities of existing GUI agents effectively, we propose Chameleon, an attack framework with two key novelties designed for dynamic environments. (1) To synthesize more realistic training data, we introduce LLM-Driven Environment Simulation, which automatically generates diverse, high-fidelity webpage simulations that mimic the variability of real-world dynamic environments. (2) To optimize the trigger more effectively, we introduce Attention Black Hole, which converts attention weights into explicit supervisory signals. This mechanism encourages the agent to remain insensitive to irrelevant surrounding content, thereby improving robustness in dynamic environments. We evaluate Chameleon on six realistic websites and four representative LVLM-powered GUI agents, where it significantly outperforms existing methods. Ablation studies confirm that both novelties are critical to performance, and a closed-loop sandbox experiment further demonstrates that Chameleon can successfully hijack agent behavior in conditions that closely mirror real-world usage. Our results uncover a critical, previously underexplored vulnerability of GUI agents in realistic dynamic environments and establish a robust foundation for future research on defense in open-world GUI agent systems.","az":"图形用户界面（GUI）智能体正被越来越多地部署以与在线 Web 服务交互，但其对开放世界内容的暴露使其易受环境注入攻击（EIA）影响。在此类攻击中，攻击者可将精心构造的触发器注入网站，从而操纵其他用户所用 GUI 智能体的行为。本文发现，现有的大多数 EIA 研究在真实性上存在不足。特别是，它们未能刻画真实 Web 内容的动态特性，常假设触发器的屏幕位置与周围视觉上下文在训练与测试之间基本保持一致。为更贴近实践，我们引入一种真实的动态环境威胁模型，其中攻击者是普通用户，且触发器被嵌入在动态变化的环境中。在该威胁模型下，现有方法大多失效，表明它们在暴露 GUI 智能体漏洞方面的有效性被大幅高估。为有效揭示现有 GUI 智能体的隐藏漏洞，我们提出 Chameleon，一个为动态环境设计、具有两项关键创新的攻击框架。(1) 为合成更真实的训练数据，我们引入 LLM 驱动的环境仿真，自动生成多样、高保真的网页仿真，以模拟真实世界动态环境的变化性。(2) 为更有效地优化触发器，我们引入注意力黑洞（Attention Black Hole），将注意力权重转化为显式的监督信号。该机制促使智能体对无关的周边内容保持不敏感，从而提升在动态环境中的鲁棒性。我们在六个真实网站与四个代表性的 LVLM 驱动 GUI 智能体上评估 Chameleon，其显著优于现有方法。消融实验确认两项创新对性能都至关重要，而闭环沙箱实验进一步表明 Chameleon 能在高度贴近真实使用的条件下成功劫持智能体行为。我们的结果揭示了 GUI 智能体在真实动态环境中一个关键且此前未被充分探索的漏洞，并为未来开放世界 GUI 智能体系统的防御研究奠定了坚实基础。","tl":"提出动态环境威胁模型，用环境仿真与注意力黑洞优化可迁移触发器。","au":["Yitong Zhang","Ximo Li","Liyi Cai","Jia Li"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"gui-computer-use-agents","tg":["security","agentic","multimodal"],"kw":["environmental injection attack","GUI agents","dynamic web environment","attention optimization","LVLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/57/x"},{"id":"p01340","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AttnCompress: Dynamic Attention-Guided Trajectory Compression for Software Engineering Agents","tz":"AttnCompress：面向软件工程智能体的动态注意力引导轨迹压缩","a":"The transition from human-centric assistance to Autonomous Software Engineering (ASE) agents has enabled the resolution of complex real-world SE tasks. However, the trial-and-error nature of these agents generates lengthy interaction trajectories, creating severe bottlenecks in terms of context window limits and cost. While context compression offers a potential remedy, prior approaches suffer from static pruning strategies and granularity mismatches, often failing to preserve the semantic dependencies and syntactic details crucial for SE tasks. To strictly preserve critical task evidence while reducing context length, we introduce AttnCompress, a dynamic attention-guided trajectory compression framework. Unlike existing approaches, AttnCompress bridges the gap between semantic integrity and dynamic adaptability through three key mechanisms: (1) structure-aware segmentation via perplexity (PPL) spikes to preserve the syntactic structure of code and logs; (2) relevance estimation using proxy attention weights to quantify the precise relevance of historical blocks to the agent’s current reasoning; and (3) a dynamic rolling window to re-evaluate and recall historical context as the task evolves. Extensive evaluation on SWE-Bench-Verified and Multi-SWE-Bench demonstrates that AttnCompress achieves a pass rate of 53.17%, outperforming prior state-of-the-art baselines while reducing token consumption by 26.1% and total costs by 35.1%. The framework proves to be model-agnostic and generalizes effectively across diverse programming languages.","az":"从以人为中心的辅助向自主软件工程（ASE）智能体的转变，使得复杂的真实 SE 任务得以被解决。然而，这类智能体试错式的运行方式会产生冗长的交互轨迹，在上下文窗口限制与成本方面造成严重瓶颈。虽然上下文压缩提供了一种潜在补救手段，已有方法却受制于静态剪枝策略与粒度不匹配，常常无法保留对 SE 任务至关重要的语义依赖与语法细节。为在缩减上下文长度的同时严格保留关键任务证据，我们提出 AttnCompress，一个动态的注意力引导轨迹压缩框架。与已有方法不同，AttnCompress 通过三项关键机制弥合语义完整性与动态适应性之间的鸿沟：(1) 通过困惑度（PPL）尖峰进行结构感知分段，以保留代码与日志的语法结构；(2) 使用代理注意力权重进行相关性估计，以精确量化历史块与智能体当前推理的相关程度；(3) 采用动态滚动窗口，随任务演进重新评估并召回历史上下文。在 SWE-Bench-Verified 与 Multi-SWE-Bench 上的大量评估表明，AttnCompress 达到 53.17% 的通过率，优于此前最新基线，同时减少 26.1% 的 token 消耗与 35.1% 的总成本。该框架被证明与模型无关，并能在多种编程语言上有效泛化。","tl":"用困惑度分段加代理注意力动态召回，压缩轨迹同时提高解决率。","au":["Zhengran Zeng","Yixin Li","Rui Xie","Wei Ye","Shikun Zhang"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["trajectory compression","SWE agents","context compression","attention weights","SWE-bench Verified"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/58/x"},{"id":"p01341","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Draft to Precision: Iterative Agentic Framework for Intent-Aware Code Summarization","tz":"从草稿到精确：面向意图感知代码摘要的迭代式智能体框架","a":"Code summarization aims to generate natural language (NL) descriptions for code snippets to assist de- velopers in understanding and maintaining programs. Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have substantially improved the quality of automatic code summarization. In real-world projects, code com- ments are written to serve different developer intents, which has motivated the development of intent-aware summarization methods. However, existing intent-aware methods still struggle to fully capture developer intent, often producing incomplete or misaligned summaries. Our empirical study reveals that real-world comments are typically refined through multiple rounds of developer revision, which we believe is key to achieving high quality. However, current methods typically overlook this iterative refinement. To bridge this gap, we propose an agentic framework that improves code summarization through iterative revision. It integrates two collaborating agents: a Generator that produces and revises summaries, and a Reviewer that assesses the generated summary and drafts targeted revision plans to guide subsequent edits using available contextual information. By iteratively refining summaries with revision plans and contextual information, our framework yields summaries that are more accurate, complete, and better aligned with developer intent. Extensive experiments on an intent-annotated CSN-Java benchmark demonstrate the effectiveness of our method. On automatic metrics, our method achieves a 28.75% improvement over the state-of-the-art baseline methods across all intents. Besides, in human studies, our framework yields average gains of over 20% in usefulness, adequacy, and intent alignment. It also achieves the highest Top-1 preference (over 40% across all intents), underscoring its practical advantage for developers.","az":"代码摘要旨在为代码片段生成自然语言（NL）描述，以帮助开发者理解与维护程序。大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展显著提升了自动代码摘要的质量。在真实项目中，代码注释是为服务不同的开发者意图而撰写的，这推动了意图感知摘要方法的发展。然而，现有的意图感知方法仍难以完整捕捉开发者意图，常产生不完整或不对齐的摘要。我们的实证研究揭示，真实世界的注释通常是经过开发者多轮修订打磨而成的，我们认为这正是达成高质量的关键。然而，当前方法通常忽视了这种迭代精化过程。为弥合这一差距，我们提出一个通过迭代修订改进代码摘要的智能体框架。它集成了两个协作的智能体：生成器（Generator）负责产出并修订摘要，评审器（Reviewer）负责评估所生成的摘要，并利用可用的上下文信息起草有针对性的修订计划以指导后续编辑。通过借助修订计划与上下文信息迭代地精化摘要，我们的框架产出的摘要更准确、更完整，也更契合开发者意图。在带意图标注的 CSN-Java 基准上的大量实验证明了该方法的有效性。在自动指标上，我们的方法在所有意图上相较最新基线方法提升了 28.75%。此外，在人工研究中，我们的框架在有用性、充分性与意图对齐上平均提升超过 20%，并取得最高的 Top-1 偏好率（所有意图上均超过 40%），凸显了其对开发者的实际优势。","tl":"把注释的多轮人工修订过程建模为生成器-评审器迭代修订循环。","au":["Yifei Ge","Chunrong Fang","Zhenyu Chen","Juan Zhai"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","human-study"],"kw":["code summarization","developer intent","iterative refinement","agent framework","CSN-Java"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/59/x"},{"id":"p01342","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards Explorative IRBL: Combining Semantic Retrieval with LLM-driven Iterative Code Exploration","tz":"迈向探索式 IRBL：结合语义检索与 LLM 驱动的迭代代码探索","a":"Information Retrieval-based Bug Localization (IRBL) aims to identify buggy source files for a given bug report. Traditional and deep learning-based IRBL techniques often suffer from vocabulary mismatch and dependence on project-specific metadata. In contrast, recent Large Language Model (LLM)-based approaches struggle to provide appropriate context to the model: they either restrict analysis to a fixed set of candidate files, overwhelm the model with repository-wide information, or rely on explicit bug report cues to guide context collection. To address these issues, we propose GenLoc, a technique that combines semantic retrieval with LLM-driven code-exploration functions to iteratively analyze the code base and identify buggy files. We evaluate GenLoc on three complementary benchmarks, including large-scale and recent Java datasets as well as the Python based SWE-bench Lite dataset. Results demonstrate that GenLoc substantially outperforms traditional IRBL, deep learning-based approaches and recent LLM-based methods, while also localizing bugs that other techniques fail to detect.","az":"基于信息检索的缺陷定位（IRBL）旨在为给定的缺陷报告识别出有缺陷的源文件。传统与基于深度学习的 IRBL 技术常受词汇不匹配以及对项目特定元数据的依赖所困。相比之下，近期基于大语言模型（LLM）的方法难以为模型提供合适的上下文：它们要么将分析限制在固定的候选文件集合上，要么用整个仓库的信息淹没模型，要么依赖缺陷报告中显式的线索来引导上下文收集。为解决这些问题，我们提出 GenLoc，一种将语义检索与 LLM 驱动的代码探索函数相结合、迭代分析代码库以识别缺陷文件的技术。我们在三个互补的基准上评估 GenLoc，包括大规模且较新的 Java 数据集以及基于 Python 的 SWE-bench Lite 数据集。结果表明，GenLoc 大幅优于传统 IRBL、基于深度学习的方法以及近期基于 LLM 的方法，同时还能定位到其他技术无法发现的缺陷。","tl":"让 LLM 用探索函数迭代浏览代码库，摆脱固定候选集与报告线索依赖。","au":["Moumita Asad","Rafed Muhammad Yasir","Sam Malek"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["bug localization","information retrieval","LLM code exploration","semantic retrieval","SWE-bench Lite"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/60/x"},{"id":"p01343","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"WASCII: Bridging WebAssembly Specifications and Implementations through LLM-Enhanced Validation","tz":"WASCII：以 LLM 增强的验证弥合 WebAssembly 规范与实现","a":"The rapid evolution of WebAssembly (Wasm) has led to significant implementation inconsistencies between its specification and the behavior of various Wasm runtimes, posing critical threats to application reliability and security. Verifying that a runtime’s implementation adheres to the natural-language specification is a profound challenge. While Large Language Models (LLMs) offer a promising way to bridge the semantic gap between specification text and source code, their inherent fallibility makes them untrustworthy for direct verification. In this paper, we introduce WASCII, a novel framework for bridging specification and implementation with execution-based validation. Our approach first constructs a Check Tree from the natural-language specification, which captures the validation rules that runtimes must enforce. We then align runtime code to the Check Tree, and employ a Clean Room design with execution-based validation to ensure the correctness of the bridging. The validated test cases are then used for cross-runtime differential testing to identify behavioral inconsistencies. Evaluated on seven major Wasm runtimes, WASCII identified 209 differential behaviors, among which 33 are confirmed as previously unknown specification conformance issues, with 18 already fixed by developers. These results demonstrate that our approach is a highly effective strategy for discovering subtle yet critical bugs in complex systems.","az":"WebAssembly（Wasm）的快速演进导致其规范与各类 Wasm 运行时行为之间出现显著的实现不一致，对应用的可靠性与安全性构成严重威胁。验证某个运行时的实现是否遵循自然语言规范是一项艰巨挑战。虽然大语言模型（LLM）为弥合规范文本与源代码之间的语义鸿沟提供了有前景的途径，但其固有的易错性使其不可直接用于验证。本文提出 WASCII，一个通过基于执行的验证来弥合规范与实现的新框架。我们的方法首先从自然语言规范构建检查树（Check Tree），刻画运行时必须强制执行的校验规则。随后我们将运行时代码与检查树对齐，并采用洁净室（Clean Room）设计与基于执行的验证来确保这一桥接的正确性。经过验证的测试用例随后被用于跨运行时差分测试，以识别行为不一致。在七个主流 Wasm 运行时上的评估中，WASCII 识别出 209 个差分行为，其中 33 个被确认为此前未知的规范一致性问题，18 个已被开发者修复。这些结果表明我们的方法是发现复杂系统中细微但关键缺陷的高效策略。","tl":"从自然语言规范构建检查树并用洁净室执行验证驱动跨运行时差分。","au":["Yeqi Fu","Kaihang Ji","Yuanpeng Wang","Zong Cao","Jiahao Liu","Ding Li","Yao Guo","Zhenkai Liang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["WebAssembly runtime","specification conformance","differential testing","LLM-enhanced validation","check tree"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/61/x"},{"id":"p01344","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Type-IV Clone Generation via LLMs and Deterministic Validation","tz":"通过 LLM 与确定性验证自动生成 Type-IV 代码克隆","a":"Detecting Type-IV code clones, functionally equivalent fragments with different syntax, remains a major challenge for quality assurance. Existing datasets are limited in supporting semantic clone detection due to class imbalance, lack of verified functional equivalence, and data redundancy. We present an automated approach for generating Type-IV clones by leveraging large language models (LLMs) with deterministic testing and filtering. The approach normalizes input code, produces diverse clone candidates through customizable prompts and refactorings, and ensures semantic equivalence via automated testing and syntactic diversity through CodeBLEU-based filtering. Representative unique clones are then selected by clustering. We evaluate the extent to which LLMs generate diverse Python Type-IV clones, how prompt and generation factors affect quality and efficiency, the retention of only Type-IV clones at the final dataset, and the usefulness of the resulting dataset for fine-tuning embedding models. Results show that the generated clones improve Type-IV clone detection across different programming languages.","az":"检测 Type-IV 代码克隆——语法不同但功能等价的代码片段——仍是质量保障中的一大挑战。现有数据集因类别不平衡、缺乏经过验证的功能等价性以及数据冗余，难以支撑语义克隆检测。我们提出一种利用大语言模型（LLM）结合确定性测试与过滤来生成 Type-IV 克隆的自动化方法。该方法对输入代码进行规范化，通过可定制的提示与重构产生多样的克隆候选，并通过自动化测试确保语义等价、通过基于 CodeBLEU 的过滤确保语法多样性。随后通过聚类选出具有代表性的唯一克隆。我们评估了以下方面：LLM 在多大程度上能生成多样的 Python Type-IV 克隆、提示与生成因素如何影响质量与效率、最终数据集中仅保留 Type-IV 克隆的程度，以及所得数据集对微调嵌入模型的有用性。结果表明，生成的克隆能提升跨不同编程语言的 Type-IV 克隆检测效果。","tl":"用 LLM 生成加确定性测试与 CodeBLEU 过滤，造出可验证的语义克隆集。","au":["Luciano Marchezan","Eugene Syriani","Kévin Delcourt","Houari Sahraoui"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["Type-IV clones","semantic clone detection","dataset generation","CodeBLEU filtering","embedding fine-tuning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/62/x"},{"id":"p01345","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Signal Denoising based Kill Matrix Refinement for Mutation-based Fault Localization","tz":"面向基于变异的缺陷定位的信号去噪式杀死矩阵精化","a":"Software debugging is a critical and time-consuming aspect of software development, with fault localization being a fundamental step that significantly impacts debugging efficiency. Mutation-Based Fault Localization (MBFL) has gained prominence due to its robust theoretical foundations and fine-grained analysis capabilities. However, recent studies have identified a critical challenge: noise phenomena, specifically the false kill relationships between mutants and tests, which significantly degrade localization effectiveness. While several approaches have been proposed to rectify the final localization results, they do not directly address the underlying noise. In this paper, we propose a novel approach to refine the kill matrix, a core data structure capturing mutant-test relationships in MBFL, by treating it as a signal that contains both meaningful fault-related patterns and high-frequency noise. Inspired by signal processing theory, we introduce DKMR (Denoising-based Kill Matrix Refinement), which employs two key stages: (1) signal enhancement through hybrid matrix construction to improve the signal-to-noise ratio for better denoising, and (2) signal denoising via frequency domain filtering to suppress noise while preserving fault-related patterns. Building on this foundation, we develop MBFL-DKMR, a fault localization framework that utilizes the refined matrix with continuous values for suspiciousness calculation. Our evaluation on Defects4J v2.0.0 demonstrates that MBFL-DKMR effectively mitigates the noise and outperforms the state-of-the-art MBFL techniques. Specifically, MBFL-DKMR achieves 129 faults localized at Top-1 compared to 85 for BLMu and 103 for Delta4Ms, with negligible additional computational overhead (0.11 seconds, 0.001% of total time). This work highlights the potential of signal processing techniques to enhance the effectiveness of MBFL by refining the kill matrix.","az":"软件调试是软件开发中关键且耗时的环节，其中缺陷定位是显著影响调试效率的基础步骤。基于变异的缺陷定位（MBFL）因其坚实的理论基础与细粒度分析能力而备受关注。然而，近期研究识别出一个关键挑战：噪声现象，具体表现为变异体与测试之间的虚假杀死关系，会显著降低定位效果。虽然已有若干方法被提出以修正最终的定位结果，但它们并未直接处理底层噪声。本文提出一种精化杀死矩阵（MBFL 中刻画变异体—测试关系的核心数据结构）的新方法，将其视为同时包含有意义的与故障相关模式以及高频噪声的信号。受信号处理理论启发，我们提出 DKMR（基于去噪的杀死矩阵精化），包含两个关键阶段：(1) 通过混合矩阵构建进行信号增强，以提高信噪比从而更好地去噪；(2) 通过频域滤波进行信号去噪，在抑制噪声的同时保留与故障相关的模式。在此基础上，我们开发了 MBFL-DKMR 缺陷定位框架，利用带连续值的精化矩阵计算可疑度。我们在 Defects4J v2.0.0 上的评估表明，MBFL-DKMR 有效缓解了噪声并优于最新的 MBFL 技术。具体而言，MBFL-DKMR 在 Top-1 上定位了 129 个故障，而 BLMu 为 85 个、Delta4Ms 为 103 个，且额外计算开销可忽略（0.11 秒，占总时间的 0.001%）。本工作凸显了信号处理技术通过精化杀死矩阵提升 MBFL 有效性的潜力。","tl":"把杀死矩阵当信号，用频域滤波去除虚假杀死关系噪声。","au":["Hengyuan Liu","Xia Song","Yong Liu","Zheng Li"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["mutation-based fault localization","kill matrix","signal denoising","frequency domain filtering","Defects4J"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/63/x"},{"id":"p01346","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AutoHIL: LLM-Based ECU Functional Test Generation through Domain Knowledge Augmentation","tz":"AutoHIL：通过领域知识增强的 LLM 驱动 ECU 功能测试生成","a":"System functional testing is a critical step before the production release of automotive electronic control units (ECUs), especially for safety-critical functions. It is typically performed on hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) benches, and engineers translate functional requirements in natural language into executable test scripts using bench-specific APIs (or test harness primitives (THPs)). Existing research either focuses on generating abstract test cases that lack execution capability, or relies on bench-specific solutions that cannot be generalized. Consequently, industrial practice remains labor-intensive, and is hindered by three main challenges, i.e., the high learning cost of THPs, the incompleteness of functional requirements due to missing tacit domain knowledge (e.g., power management dependencies or system wake-up sequences), and the limited automation. To address these challenges, we propose AUTOHIL, an LLM-based, domain-knowledge-augmented framework for requirement-driven ECU functional test generation on HIL benches. AUTOHIL automatically constructs a THP knowledge base to understand bench operations, extracts tacit domain knowledge from AUTOSAR ECU source code and configuration to augment requirements, and generates test scripts for the augmented requirements based on the THP knowledge base. We evaluate AUTOHIL on two industrial ECUs, i.e., an Airbag Control Unit (ACU) on an in-house bench and an Active Safety Domain Master (ASDM) on a dSPACE platform. AUTOHIL achieves test script executability of 90.33% on ACU and 81.31% on ASDM. We also manually evaluate the functional equivalence between generated scripts and manual scripts, and AUTOHIL reaches a functional correctness of 89.69% on ACU and 84.00% on ASDM. We discover 39 and 25 new functional defects in ACU and ASDM, which have been patched by technicians from the supplier.","az":"系统功能测试是汽车电子控制单元（ECU）量产发布前的关键步骤，尤其对安全关键功能而言。它通常在硬件在环（HIL）台架上进行，工程师需要使用台架专用 API（或测试台架原语，THP）将自然语言的功能需求翻译为可执行的测试脚本。现有研究要么专注于生成缺乏执行能力的抽象测试用例，要么依赖无法泛化的台架专用方案。因此，工业实践仍然高度依赖人力，并受三大挑战阻碍：THP 的学习成本高、由于缺失隐性领域知识（如电源管理依赖或系统唤醒时序）导致功能需求不完整，以及自动化程度有限。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 AUTOHIL，一个基于 LLM、由领域知识增强、面向 HIL 台架的需求驱动 ECU 功能测试生成框架。AUTOHIL 自动构建 THP 知识库以理解台架操作，从 AUTOSAR ECU 源代码与配置中提取隐性领域知识以增强需求，并基于 THP 知识库为增强后的需求生成测试脚本。我们在两个工业 ECU 上评估 AUTOHIL，即自有台架上的安全气囊控制单元（ACU）与 dSPACE 平台上的主动安全域控制器（ASDM）。AUTOHIL 在 ACU 上达到 90.33% 的测试脚本可执行率，在 ASDM 上达到 81.31%。我们还人工评估了生成脚本与人工脚本之间的功能等价性，AUTOHIL 在 ACU 上达到 89.69%、在 ASDM 上达到 84.00% 的功能正确率。我们在 ACU 与 ASDM 中分别发现了 39 个和 25 个新的功能缺陷，供应商技术人员已对其进行修复。","tl":"从 AUTOSAR 源码抽取隐性领域知识补全需求，再生成可执行 HIL 脚本。","au":["Sichen Gong","Qicai Chen","Bihuan Chen","Wenzhuo Zhang","Yukun Gao","Xin Peng"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["ECU functional testing","hardware-in-the-loop","test script generation","domain knowledge augmentation","AUTOSAR"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/64/x"},{"id":"p01347","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Atropos: Improving Cost-Benefit Trade-off of LLM-based Agents under Self-Consistency with Early Termination and Model Hotswap","tz":"Atropos：以早停与模型热切换改善自一致性下 LLM 智能体的成本收益权衡","a":"Open-weight Small Language Models(SLMs) can provide faster local inference at lower financial cost, but may not achieve the same performance level as commercial Large Language Models (LLMs) that are orders of magnitudes larger. Consequently, many of the latest applications of LLMs, such as software engineering agents, tend to be evaluated on larger models only, leaving the issue of improving the cost-benefit trade-off of such applications neglected. This paper proposes Atropos1, a predictive early-termination analysis and hotswap technique that aims to improve the cost-benefit trade-off for LLM-based agents that use self-consistency. The core component of Atropos is a predictive model based on structural properties of LLM inferences: after merging multiple agentic inference paths into a graph representation, Atropos uses Graph Convolutional Network (GCN) to predict whether an ongoing inference will eventually succeed or not. If an agentic task instance running on the source LLM is predicted to fail, Atropos subsequently performs hotswapping, i.e., migrating the on-going inference context onto the more capable target LLM: this is feasible because LLM contexts are stateless. An empirical evaluation of Atropos using three recent LLM-based agents shows that Atropos can predict early termination of eventually failing inferences with the accuracy of 0.85 at the midpoint of the inference. Hotswapping LLMs for such inferences can convert up to 27.57% of them to be successful. Consequently, Atropos achieves 74.35% of the performance of closed LLMs with as low as only 23.9% of the cost.","az":"开放权重的小语言模型（SLM）能以更低的经济成本提供更快的本地推理，但可能达不到规模大若干数量级的商用大语言模型（LLM）的性能水平。因此，LLM 的许多最新应用（如软件工程智能体）往往只在更大的模型上评估，使得改善此类应用的成本收益权衡问题被忽视。本文提出 Atropos，一种预测式早停分析与热切换技术，旨在改善使用自一致性的 LLM 智能体的成本收益权衡。Atropos 的核心组件是一个基于 LLM 推理结构性质的预测模型：在将多条智能体推理路径合并为图表示后，Atropos 使用图卷积网络（GCN）预测一次进行中的推理最终是否会成功。如果某个运行在源 LLM 上的智能体任务实例被预测为会失败，Atropos 随后执行热切换，即把进行中的推理上下文迁移到能力更强的目标 LLM 上；由于 LLM 上下文是无状态的，这一做法是可行的。使用三个最新的基于 LLM 的智能体对 Atropos 进行的实证评估表明，Atropos 能在推理中点以 0.85 的准确率预测出最终会失败的推理并提前终止。对这些推理进行 LLM 热切换可将其中最多 27.57% 转化为成功。因此，Atropos 以最低仅 23.9% 的成本实现了闭源 LLM 74.35% 的性能。","tl":"用 GCN 中途预测推理成败，失败者热切换到强模型以省钱。","au":["Naryeong Kim","Shin Yoo"],"top":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["early termination","model hotswap","self-consistency","cost-benefit trade-off","graph convolutional network"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/65/x"},{"id":"p01348","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"On the Feasibility of Deduplicating Compiler Bugs with Bisection","tz":"论用二分定位去重编译器缺陷的可行性","a":"Random testing has proven to be an effective technique for compiler validation. However, the debugging of bugs identified through random testing presents a significant challenge due to the frequent occurrence of duplicate test programs that expose identical compiler bugs. The process to identify duplicates is a practical research problem known as bug deduplication. Prior methodologies for compiler bug deduplication primarily rely on program analysis to extract bug-related features for duplicate identification, which can result in substantial computational overhead and limited generalizability. This paper investigates the feasibility of employing bisection, a standard debugging procedure largely overlooked in prior research on compiler bug deduplication, for this purpose. Our study demonstrates that the utilization of bisection to locate failure-inducing commits provides a valuable criterion for deduplication, albeit one that requires supplementary techniques for more accurate identification. Building on these results, we introduce BugLens, a novel deduplication method that primarily uses bisection, enhanced by the identification of bug-triggering optimizations to minimize false negatives. Empirical evaluations conducted on four real-world datasets demonstrate that BugLens significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art analysis-based methodologies Tamer and D3 by saving an average of 26.98% and 9.64% human effort to identify the same number of distinct bugs. Given the inherent simplicity and generalizability of bisection, it presents a highly practical solution for compiler bug deduplication in real-world applications.","az":"随机测试已被证明是编译器验证的有效技术。然而，由于频繁出现暴露相同编译器缺陷的重复测试程序，对随机测试所发现缺陷的调试面临显著挑战。识别重复项的过程是一个被称为缺陷去重的实际研究问题。以往的编译器缺陷去重方法主要依赖程序分析提取与缺陷相关的特征来识别重复，这可能带来可观的计算开销与有限的泛化能力。本文研究采用二分定位（bisection）这一在以往编译器缺陷去重研究中很大程度被忽视的标准调试流程来完成该任务的可行性。我们的研究表明，利用二分定位找到触发失败的提交为去重提供了有价值的判据，尽管这一判据需要辅助技术才能更准确地识别。基于这些结果，我们提出 BugLens，一种主要使用二分定位、并通过识别触发缺陷的优化选项来减少漏判的新型去重方法。在四个真实数据集上的实证评估表明，BugLens 显著优于最新的基于分析的方法 Tamer 与 D3，在识别相同数量的不同缺陷时平均节省 26.98% 与 9.64% 的人工工作量。鉴于二分定位固有的简洁性与泛化能力，它为真实应用中的编译器缺陷去重提供了高度实用的解决方案。","tl":"首次证明二分定位失败提交可作为编译器缺陷去重的有效判据。","au":["Xintong Zhou","Zhenyang Xu","Yongqiang Tian","Chengnian Sun"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["compiler bug deduplication","bisection","failure-inducing commit","random testing","BugLens"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/66/x"},{"id":"p01349","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Intrusion Models for Security Assessment: Methodology and Case Study on Xen","tz":"用于安全评估的入侵模型：方法论与 Xen 案例研究","a":"As cyberattacks become increasingly automated and amplified by emerging technologies, particularly Artificial Intelligence (AI), reliably assessing the security resilience of software systems becomes crucial. However, traditional methods that rely on known vulnerabilities provide limited insight into the potential impact of attacks. Intrusion Injection is an emerging approach that leverages Intrusion Models (IMs) to inject exploitable states, representative of real intrusions, providing deeper insight into system resilience beyond known vulnerabilities. This paper contributes to the formalization of Intrusion Models (IMs) and proposes a structured methodology for their instantiation and injection into software systems. Grounded in fault-injection concepts, IMs define explicit abusive functionalities and the resulting erroneous states, which, when injected, enable systematic analysis of software reliability under security threats. To demonstrate feasibility, we apply our approach to the Xen hypervisor, targeting memory and virtualization management components with an injector prototype that allows security researchers and engineers to assess Xen-based systems against potential security-related failures. Our study indicates that intrusion injection driven by IMs can support repeatable, exploit-agnostic security assessments across platforms.","az":"随着网络攻击日益自动化并被人工智能（AI）等新兴技术放大，可靠评估软件系统的安全韧性变得至关重要。然而，依赖已知漏洞的传统方法对攻击潜在影响的洞察有限。入侵注入是一种新兴方法，它利用入侵模型（IM）注入代表真实入侵的可利用状态，从而在已知漏洞之外提供对系统韧性的更深入洞察。本文推动了入侵模型（IM）的形式化，并提出一套结构化的方法论，用于其实例化与向软件系统中的注入。基于故障注入的概念，IM 显式定义了滥用功能及其导致的错误状态；当这些被注入后，可以系统地分析软件在安全威胁下的可靠性。为展示可行性，我们将该方法应用于 Xen 虚拟机管理程序，针对内存与虚拟化管理组件构建了一个注入器原型，使安全研究人员与工程师能够评估基于 Xen 的系统面对潜在安全相关失效时的表现。我们的研究表明，由 IM 驱动的入侵注入可以支持跨平台的、可重复的、与具体漏洞利用无关的安全评估。","tl":"形式化入侵模型并注入可利用状态，实现与漏洞无关的韧性评估。","au":["Charles Gonçalves","Marco Vieira"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["intrusion injection","intrusion models","security assessment","Xen hypervisor","fault injection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/67/x"},{"id":"p01350","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Toward Secure Code Generation: Bridging Correctness and Security via Task-Adaptive Vulnerability Modeling and Execution-Based Benchmarking","tz":"迈向安全的代码生成：通过任务自适应漏洞建模与基于执行的基准测试弥合正确性与安全性","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used for program synthesis, yet they often generate code that is functionally plausible but insecure. Progress in secure code generation has been hindered by benchmarks that are small, non-executable, leak mitigation details, or rely on noisy analyzers and subjective judgments, making it difficult to measure whether security improves without sacrificing correctness. We address these gaps with CodeSecEval, an execution-based benchmark for secure code generation, comprising 255 Python tasks spanning 77 CWE categories. Each task provides paired insecure and secure implementations together with executable functional and vulnerability-targeted security tests, enabling precise and reproducible evaluation of secure code generation and insecure-code repair. Building on CodeSecEval, we propose SecAwareCoder, an agent-based framework that shifts code generation toward secure-by-construction synthesis. SecAwareCoder performs task-adaptive threat modeling to identify security-sensitive regions and derive task-grounded vulnerability hypotheses, uses these hypotheses to guide both constraint-aware code generation and security-aware test synthesis, and leverages execution feedback for targeted refinement. Experiments across multiple LLM backbones show that SecAwareCoder consistently improves Pass@1 and security robustness over prompting and analyzer-driven baselines, narrowing the security–correctness gap in LLM code generation.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）越来越多地被用于程序合成，但它们生成的代码常常在功能上看似合理却并不安全。安全代码生成领域的进展一直受制于这样一些基准：规模小、不可执行、泄露缓解细节，或依赖有噪声的分析器与主观判断，使人难以衡量安全性是否在不牺牲正确性的前提下得到提升。我们通过 CodeSecEval 弥补这些空白——一个基于执行的安全代码生成基准，包含 255 个 Python 任务，覆盖 77 个 CWE 类别。每个任务都提供成对的不安全与安全实现，并配有可执行的功能测试与针对漏洞的安全测试，从而实现对安全代码生成与不安全代码修复的精确、可复现评估。在 CodeSecEval 的基础上，我们提出 SecAwareCoder，一个基于智能体的框架，将代码生成推向“构造即安全”的合成方式。SecAwareCoder 执行任务自适应的威胁建模以识别安全敏感区域并推导出基于任务的漏洞假设，利用这些假设同时引导约束感知的代码生成与安全感知的测试合成，并借助执行反馈进行有针对性的精化。跨多个 LLM 主干的实验表明，SecAwareCoder 相较提示式与分析器驱动的基线持续提升 Pass@1 与安全鲁棒性，缩小了 LLM 代码生成中的安全—正确性差距。","tl":"提出可执行的安全基准，并以任务自适应威胁建模引导安全生成。","au":["Jiexin Wang","Liuwen Cao","Xitong Luo","Yang Cao","Zhenghao Li","Yunyi Xiao","Mengchen Zhao","Adam Jatowt","Yi Cai"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","agentic"],"kw":["secure code generation","CodeSecEval","execution-based benchmark","threat modeling","CWE"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/68/x"},{"id":"p01351","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fuzzing FPGA Synthesis and Simulation Tools via LLM-Generated Syntax-Valid HDL Codes","tz":"通过 LLM 生成语法有效的 HDL 代码对 FPGA 综合与仿真工具进行模糊测试","a":"Field-Programmable Gate Array (FPGA) synthesis and simulation tools, such as Vivado, Quartus, Yosys, and Icarus Verilog, are key components of Electronic Design Automation (EDA) toolchains, translating high-level Hardware Description Language (HDL) codes into low-level gate netlists. However, defects in these compilers can propagate into the synthesized netlists, leading to crashes and functionally incorrect or even insecure hardware implementations and posing significant security risks. Existing fuzz testing approaches face several challenges, including limited diversity in primitive-cell types and a lack of feedback-guided exploration. These issues restrict their ability to thoroughly exercise the compilers and expose deep-seated defects. To address these challenges, we propose PolyHDL, which leverages the prompting Large Language Models (LLMs) for generating valid HDL codes to detect compiler defects in FPGA synthesis and simulation tools. By leveraging prompt learning and integrating feedback-driven guidance from primitive-cell diversity, PolyHDL generates semantically valid HDL codes with diverse primitive-cell combinations, thereby addressing the aforementioned challenges. Furthermore, through equivalence check, PolyHDL effectively reveals potential compiler defects in FPGA synthesis and simulation tools. Experimental results demonstrate that PolyHDL successfully identified and reported 18 valid defects in widely used toolchains, including Vivado, Yosys, Icarus Verilog, and Quartus within one month, 16 of which were confirmed by the official technical support, and achieved a 13.1%–13.4% improvement in code coverage over the SOTA approach.","az":"现场可编程门阵列（FPGA）的综合与仿真工具，如 Vivado、Quartus、Yosys 和 Icarus Verilog，是电子设计自动化（EDA）工具链的关键组成部分，负责把高层硬件描述语言（HDL）代码翻译为底层门级网表。然而，这些编译器中的缺陷会传播到综合出的网表中，导致崩溃以及功能错误甚至不安全的硬件实现，带来显著的安全风险。现有模糊测试方法面临若干挑战，包括原语单元类型多样性有限、缺乏反馈引导的探索。这些问题限制了它们充分激发编译器行为、暴露深层缺陷的能力。为解决这些挑战，我们提出 PolyHDL，利用提示大语言模型（LLM）生成有效的 HDL 代码，以检测 FPGA 综合与仿真工具中的编译器缺陷。通过利用提示学习并融入来自原语单元多样性的反馈驱动引导，PolyHDL 能生成语义有效、原语单元组合多样的 HDL 代码，从而应对上述挑战。此外，PolyHDL 通过等价性检查有效揭示 FPGA 综合与仿真工具中潜在的编译器缺陷。实验结果表明，PolyHDL 在一个月内于 Vivado、Yosys、Icarus Verilog 和 Quartus 等广泛使用的工具链中成功发现并报告了 18 个有效缺陷，其中 16 个已获官方技术支持确认，并在代码覆盖率上比 SOTA 方法提升了 13.1%–13.4%。","tl":"用 LLM 生成多样原语的合法 HDL 并以等价检查测出 EDA 工具缺陷","au":["He Jiang","Wen Zhao","Shikai Guo","Zhihao Xu","Xiaochen Li","Rubing Huang"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","security"],"kw":["FPGA synthesis tools","HDL generation","compiler fuzzing","LLM prompting","equivalence checking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/69/x"},{"id":"p01352","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AutoCodeSherpa: Symbolic Explanations in AI Coding Agents","tz":"AutoCodeSherpa：AI 编程智能体中的符号化解释","a":"Large language model (LLM) agents integrate external tools with one or more LLMs to accomplish specific tasks. Agents have rapidly been adopted by developers, and they are starting to be deployed in industrial workflows, such as their use to fix static analysis issues from the widely used SonarQube static analyzer. However, the growing importance of agents means their actions carry greater impact and potential risk. Thus, to use them at scale, an additional layer of trust and evidence is necessary. This work presents AutoCodeSherpa, a technique that provides explanations of software issues in the form of symbolic formulae. Inspired by the reachability, infection, and propagation model of software faults, the explanations are composed of input, infection, and output conditions, collectively providing a specification of the issue. In practice, the symbolic explanation is implemented as a combination of a property-based test (PBT) and program-internal symbolic expressions. Critically, this means our symbolic explanations are executable and can be automatically evaluated, unlike natural language explanations. Experiments show the generated conditions are highly accurate. For example, input conditions from AutoCodeSherpa had an accuracy of 85.7%. This high accuracy makes symbolic explanations particularly useful in two scenarios. First, the explanations can be used in automated issue resolution environments to decide whether to accept or reject patches from issue resolution agents; AutoCodeSherpa could reject 2x as many incorrect patches as baselines did. Secondly, as agentic AI approaches continue to develop, program analysis driven explanations like ours can be provided to other LLM-based repair techniques which do not employ analysis to improve their output. In our experiments, our symbolic explanations could improve the plausible patch generation rate of the Agentless technique by 60%.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）智能体把外部工具与一个或多个 LLM 结合起来完成特定任务。智能体已被开发者迅速采用，并开始部署到工业工作流中，例如用于修复广泛使用的 SonarQube 静态分析器报出的问题。然而，智能体日益重要意味着其动作带来更大的影响与潜在风险。因此，要大规模使用它们，需要额外的一层信任与证据。本文提出 AutoCodeSherpa，一种以符号公式形式给出软件问题解释的技术。受软件故障的可达性、感染与传播模型启发，这些解释由输入条件、感染条件和输出条件构成，共同给出该问题的一份规约。在实现上，符号化解释由基于性质的测试（PBT）与程序内部符号表达式组合而成。关键在于，这意味着我们的符号化解释是可执行、可自动评估的，不同于自然语言解释。实验表明所生成的条件高度准确，例如 AutoCodeSherpa 的输入条件准确率达 85.7%。这一高准确率使符号化解释在两个场景中尤为有用。第一，这些解释可用于自动化问题求解环境中，判定是否接受或拒绝来自 issue 求解智能体的补丁；AutoCodeSherpa 拒绝的错误补丁数量是基线的 2 倍。第二，随着智能体式 AI 方法不断发展，像我们这样由程序分析驱动的解释可以提供给其他不使用分析的基于 LLM 的修复技术，以改进其输出。在我们的实验中，符号化解释使 Agentless 技术的貌似正确补丁生成率提升了 60%。","tl":"用可执行符号条件解释缺陷并据此拒绝智能体的错误补丁","au":["Sungmin Kang","Haifeng Ruan","Abhik Roychoudhury"],"top":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["symbolic explanation","property-based testing","patch validation","coding agents","issue resolution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/70/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.22414"},{"id":"p01353","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Greedy Steps to Global Optimization: Learning Sequential Test Suite Generation","tz":"从贪心步骤到全局优化：学习序列化的测试套件生成","a":"With the rapid evolution of Large Language Models (LLMs), automated software testing is witnessing a paradigm shift. While proprietary models like GPT-4o demonstrate impressive capabilities, their high deployment costs and data privacy concerns make open-source LLMs the practical imperative for many academic and industrial scenarios. In the field of automated test generation, it has evolved to iterative workflows to construct test suites based on LLMs. When utilizing open-source LLMs, we empirically observe they lack a suite-level perspective, suffering from structural myopia—failing to generate new tests with large marginal gain based on the current covered status. In this paper, from the perspective of sequences, we formalize test suite generation as a Markov Decision Process (MDP) and demonstrate that its objective exhibits monotone submodularity, which enables an effective relaxation of this NP-hard global optimization into a tractable step-wise greedy procedure. Guided by this insight, we propose TestDecision, which transforms LLMs into neural greedy experts. TestDecision consists of two synergistic components: (1) an inference framework which implements test suite construction following a step-wise greedy strategy; and (2) a training pipeline of reinforcement learning which equips the base LLM with sequential test generation ability to maximize marginal gain. Comprehensive evaluations on the ULT benchmark demonstrate that TestDecision significantly outperforms existing advanced methods. It brings an improvement between 38.15-52.37% in branch coverage and 298.22-558.88% in execution pass rate over all base models, achieving a comparable performance on 7B backbone with a much larger proprietary LLM GPT-5.2. Furthermore, TestDecision can find 58.43-95.45% more bugs than vanilla base LLMs and exhibit superior generalization on LiveCodeBench, proving its capability to construct high-quality test suites.","az":"随着大语言模型（LLM）的快速演进，自动化软件测试正经历范式转变。尽管 GPT-4o 等专有模型展现出令人印象深刻的能力，但其高昂的部署成本与数据隐私顾虑使开源 LLM 成为许多学术与工业场景中的现实选择。在自动测试生成领域，已经演化为基于 LLM 的迭代式工作流来构建测试套件。在使用开源 LLM 时，我们经验性地观察到它们缺乏套件级视角，存在“结构性近视”——无法基于当前已覆盖状态生成具有较大边际增益的新测试。本文从序列视角出发，把测试套件生成形式化为马尔可夫决策过程（MDP），并证明其目标函数具有单调次模性，这使得这一 NP 难的全局优化可以有效松弛为可处理的逐步贪心过程。在该洞见指导下，我们提出 TestDecision，将 LLM 转化为神经贪心专家。TestDecision 由两个协同组件构成：（1）一个按逐步贪心策略构建测试套件的推理框架；（2）一条强化学习训练流水线，赋予基座 LLM 最大化边际增益的序列化测试生成能力。在 ULT 基准上的全面评估表明，TestDecision 显著优于现有先进方法：在所有基座模型上带来 38.15–52.37% 的分支覆盖率提升和 298.22–558.88% 的执行通过率提升，7B 骨干模型即可取得与远更大的专有模型 GPT-5.2 相当的性能。此外，TestDecision 比原始基座 LLM 多发现 58.43–95.45% 的缺陷，并在 LiveCodeBench 上展现出更好的泛化性，证明其构建高质量测试套件的能力。","tl":"把测试套件生成建模为次模 MDP，用 RL 训练 LLM 逐步最大化边际增益","au":["Guoqing Wang","Chengran Yang","Xiaoxuan Zhou","Zeyu Sun","Bo Wang","David Lo","Dan Hao"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["test suite generation","submodularity","Markov decision process","reinforcement learning","branch coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/71/x"},{"id":"p01354","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SymWeb: Feedback-Driven Context Exploration and Context-Aware Symbolic Execution for Browser-Embedded WebAssembly Vulnerability Detection","tz":"SymWeb：面向浏览器内嵌 WebAssembly 漏洞检测的反馈驱动上下文探索与上下文感知符号执行","a":"Browser-deployed WebAssembly (wasm) modules often inherit memory-safety bugs from C and C++-style code, yet exploiting, and even reaching, these bugs in the Web threat model is fundamentally context-dependent. JavaScript (JS) controls the exported-call schedule and constructs the wasm entry state, including arguments, globals, and linear-memory layouts, from attacker-influenced web inputs. This makes both wasm-only analysis, which assumes static initial states, and prior browser-based testing such as Wemby ineffective. Wemby generates a fixed, wasm-agnostic context pool and then only mutates wasm parameters, which limits its ability to systematically reach deeper, wasm-relevant contexts and gated behaviors. We present SymWeb, a feedback-guided closed-loop system that links external inputs to browser-reachable JS-induced wasm contexts and then to context-aware wasm symbolic execution. SymWeb couples an Feedback-driven Context Generator with an Context-aware Wasm Symbolic Executor. The context generator performs binary rewriting for ASan-like checks and observability, collects contexts in the browser, and applies influence-guided input mutation. The symbolic executor clusters and symbolizes contexts, performs coverage-guided symbolic execution under reachable entry states, and returns actionable constraints to steer the next online round. We evaluate SymWeb on 30 real-world wasm-enabled websites. Under our Web threat model, SymWeb verifies 17 exploitable vulnerabilities and achieves 72.8% average wasm basic-block coverage. Compared to the browser-based baseline Wemby, SymWeb finds 8 more verified vulnerabilities and improves coverage by 19.9 percentage points. Compared to the wasm-only baseline WASEM, SymWeb finds 14 more verified vulnerabilities and improves coverage by 40.4 percentage points. Overall, these results show that closing the loop between browser-reachable context generation and context-aware wasm analysis substantially improves both vulnerability-finding effectiveness and exploration depth in real Web environments.","az":"浏览器中部署的 WebAssembly（wasm）模块常常继承来自 C/C++ 风格代码的内存安全缺陷，然而在 Web 威胁模型下利用甚至仅仅触达这些缺陷本质上是依赖上下文的。JavaScript（JS）控制导出函数的调用时序，并基于受攻击者影响的 Web 输入构造 wasm 的入口状态，包括参数、全局变量和线性内存布局。这使得假设静态初始状态的纯 wasm 分析，以及既有的基于浏览器的测试（如 Wemby）都不奏效。Wemby 生成固定的、与 wasm 无关的上下文池，随后只变异 wasm 参数，这限制了它系统地触达更深层、与 wasm 相关的上下文和受门控行为的能力。我们提出 SymWeb，一个反馈引导的闭环系统，将外部输入与浏览器可达的、由 JS 诱导的 wasm 上下文相连接，再进一步连接到上下文感知的 wasm 符号执行。SymWeb 将“反馈驱动上下文生成器”与“上下文感知 wasm 符号执行器”耦合在一起。上下文生成器通过二进制重写插入类 ASan 检查与可观测性，在浏览器中收集上下文，并施加影响力引导的输入变异。符号执行器对上下文进行聚类与符号化，在可达入口状态下执行覆盖引导的符号执行，并返回可操作的约束以引导下一轮在线探索。我们在 30 个真实的启用 wasm 的网站上评估 SymWeb。在我们的 Web 威胁模型下，SymWeb 验证了 17 个可利用漏洞，并达到 72.8% 的平均 wasm 基本块覆盖率。与基于浏览器的基线 Wemby 相比，SymWeb 多发现 8 个已验证漏洞，覆盖率提高 19.9 个百分点；与纯 wasm 基线 WASEM 相比，多发现 14 个已验证漏洞，覆盖率提高 40.4 个百分点。总体而言，这些结果表明，把浏览器可达的上下文生成与上下文感知的 wasm 分析闭环起来，能显著提升真实 Web 环境中的漏洞发现效果与探索深度。","tl":"闭环生成浏览器可达上下文再做符号执行，验证 wasm 可利用漏洞","au":["Yuanpeng Wang","Yeqi Fu","Zhineng Zhong","Zhenkai Liang","Ding Li","Yao Guo","Xiangqun Chen"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["WebAssembly","browser context","symbolic execution","memory safety","exploitability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/72/x"},{"id":"p01355","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"The Unseen Delta: Characterizing the Compiler Optimization Landscape via Top-Down Differential Analysis","tz":"看不见的差距：通过自顶向下差分分析刻画编译器优化格局","a":"Compiler optimizations are essential for achieving high performance in modern software. However, recent studies highlight the persistence of performance bugs, i.e., subtle defects where the compiler generates functionally correct but computationally inefficient code, leading to significant performance degradation. Existing detection and testing methods typically employ a bottom-up approach, focusing on specific low-level code properties and remaining confined to known optimization rules. Consequently, they struggle to quantify the holistic impact of identified issues and often overlook critical microarchitectural inefficiencies. We observe a key indicator of untapped potential: different compilers often produce binaries with significant performance differences for identical source code. However, the root causes of these discrepancies remain largely unexplored and difficult to pinpoint using current techniques. To bridge this gap, we introduce a top-down differential analysis methodology. This approach calibrates compiler optimization differences with fine-grained, hierarchical microarchitectural metrics, offering a comprehensive view of runtime behavior. Using a sampling-based approach, this method efficiently pinpoints the critical code snippets responsible for performance differences, enabling targeted root cause analysis. Our empirical evaluation uncovers substantial and often surprising performance differences between binaries generated by GCC and Clang. A categorization of root causes reveals systemic challenges in compiler optimizations. To quantitatively validate our findings and demonstrate practical impact, we developed a binary patching framework that fixes identified performance issues by transplanting superior code sequences from competing compilers. This work provides a novel lens for understanding and analyzing optimization defects.","az":"编译器优化对于现代软件获得高性能至关重要。然而近期研究表明性能缺陷长期存在，即编译器生成功能正确但计算低效的代码这类细微缺陷，会导致显著的性能下降。现有检测与测试方法通常采用自底向上的思路，聚焦于特定的底层代码属性，并局限于已知的优化规则。因此，它们难以量化所发现问题的整体影响，且常常忽略关键的微架构低效。我们观察到一个揭示未开发潜力的关键指标：不同编译器对相同源代码生成的二进制往往存在显著性能差异。然而这些差异的根因在很大程度上仍未被探究，用现有技术也难以定位。为弥合这一空白，我们提出一种自顶向下的差分分析方法。该方法用细粒度、分层的微架构指标来标定编译器优化差异，提供对运行时行为的全面视图。借助基于采样的方式，该方法能高效定位造成性能差异的关键代码片段，从而支持有针对性的根因分析。我们的实证评估揭示了 GCC 与 Clang 生成的二进制之间大量且常常出人意料的性能差异。对根因的分类揭示了编译器优化中的系统性挑战。为了定量验证我们的发现并展示实际影响，我们开发了一个二进制补丁框架，通过移植竞争编译器中更优的代码序列来修复所发现的性能问题。本工作为理解和分析优化缺陷提供了新的视角。","tl":"自顶向下微架构差分定位 GCC/Clang 性能差异根因并移植修复","au":["Zhibo Liu","Huaijin Wang","Shuai Wang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["compiler optimization","performance bugs","differential analysis","microarchitectural metrics","binary patching"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/73/x"},{"id":"p01356","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AgentBreaker: Evaluating Context-Aware Indirect Prompt Injection Risks in Modern Web Agents","tz":"AgentBreaker：评估现代 Web 智能体中上下文感知的间接提示注入风险","a":"Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have enabled autonomous web agents to perform complex user tasks by leveraging their adaptive decision-making capabilities. Despite their growing use in crawling the Web, their security implications under indirect prompt injection (IPI) attacks remain largely understudied. Prior studies have compiled static benchmarks or proposed dynamic frameworks that generate adversarial phrases aimed at deceiving a single LLM within a target agent. However, by ignoring the agent’s operating context, these approaches yield suboptimal IPI attacks against modern web agents leveraging multiple, specialized LLMs. In this paper, we study the vulnerability in web agents to malicious phrases embedded as HTML elements. To assess the security risks posed by this vulnerability, we present AgentBreaker, an IPI attack framework that autonomously composes adversarial phrases tailored to page-specific context. When processed by web agents, these DOM-embedded phrases induce adversarial behaviors, such as clicking attacker-designated HTML elements, posting attacker-provided text, and disclosing internal agent secrets. In our evaluation against five state-of-the-art web agents, AgentBreaker achieves an attack success rate of 71.7%–100% across 60 webpages sampled from Online-Mind2Web. We then propose practical defenses that not only mitigate observed threats but also address potential adaptive attacks. Our defenses reduce the attack success rate down to 1.7%. By conducting context-aware injection, AgentBreaker outperforms existing IPI frameworks, thereby accurately evaluating web agents’ susceptibility to IPI and providing stepping stones for countering this emerging threat.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展使自主 Web 智能体能够凭借自适应决策能力完成复杂的用户任务。尽管它们在爬取 Web 方面的应用日益增多，其在间接提示注入（IPI）攻击下的安全影响仍缺乏研究。此前工作要么编制静态基准，要么提出动态框架生成旨在欺骗目标智能体中单个 LLM 的对抗短语。然而，由于忽略了智能体的运行上下文，这些方法对使用多个专用 LLM 的现代 Web 智能体只能产生次优的 IPI 攻击。本文研究 Web 智能体面对嵌入在 HTML 元素中的恶意短语时的脆弱性。为评估该脆弱性带来的安全风险，我们提出 AgentBreaker，一个能自主组合针对页面特定上下文定制的对抗短语的 IPI 攻击框架。当被 Web 智能体处理时，这些嵌入 DOM 的短语会诱发对抗行为，例如点击攻击者指定的 HTML 元素、发布攻击者提供的文本，以及泄露智能体的内部机密。在针对五个最先进 Web 智能体的评估中，AgentBreaker 在取自 Online-Mind2Web 的 60 个网页上取得了 71.7%–100% 的攻击成功率。随后我们提出了实用防御方案，不仅缓解已观察到的威胁，还应对潜在的自适应攻击，将攻击成功率降至 1.7%。通过进行上下文感知的注入，AgentBreaker 优于现有 IPI 框架，从而能准确评估 Web 智能体对 IPI 的易感性，并为应对这一新兴威胁提供了基础。","tl":"按页面上下文自动生成 DOM 注入短语，攻破多 LLM Web 智能体","au":["Yongbi Son","Changoo Lee","Dongwon Shin","Byoungyoung Lee","Sanghyun Hong","Sooel Son"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"gui-computer-use-agents","tg":["security","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["indirect prompt injection","web agents","DOM injection","attack success rate","defenses"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/74/x"},{"id":"p01357","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Modernization of Machine Learning Engineering Notebooks for Reproducibility","tz":"面向可复现性的机器学习工程笔记本自动现代化","a":"Interactive computational notebooks (e.g., Jupyter notebooks) are widely used in machine learning engineering (MLE) to program and share end-to-end pipelines, from data preparation to model training and evaluation. However, environmental erosion—the rapid evolution of hardware and software ecosystems for machine learning—has rendered many published MLE notebooks non-reproducible in contemporary environments, hindering code reuse and scientific progress. To quantify this gap, we study 12,106 notebooks selected from 75 popular Kaggle competitions: only 26% remain reproducible today. Crucially, we find that environment backporting, i.e., downgrading dependencies to match the submission time, does not improve reproducibility (decreased to 12%) but rather introduces additional failure modes. To address environmental erosion, we design and implement MLEModernizer, an LLM-driven agentic framework that treats the contemporary environment as a fixed constraint and modernizes notebook code to restore reproducibility. MLEModernizer iteratively executes notebooks, collects execution feedback, and applies three types of targeted fixes: error-repair, runtime-reduction, and score-calibration. Evaluated on 8,210 notebooks that are non-reproducible under the baseline environment, MLEModernizer makes 3,292 (40.1%, GPT-5.2) and 3,683 (44.9%, GPT-OSS-120b) notebooks reproducible. MLEModernizer presents a best-effort automated recovery and modernization technique that can improve reproducibility for a subset of notebooks. Practitioners can leverage MLEModernizer to validate, reuse, and maintain MLE artifacts as the hardware and software ecosystems continue to evolve.","az":"交互式计算笔记本（如 Jupyter notebook）在机器学习工程（MLE）中被广泛用于编写和共享从数据准备到模型训练与评估的端到端流水线。然而，环境侵蚀——机器学习硬件与软件生态的快速演进——已使许多已发布的 MLE 笔记本在当代环境中无法复现，阻碍了代码复用与科学进步。为量化这一差距，我们研究了取自 75 个热门 Kaggle 竞赛的 12,106 个笔记本：今天仅有 26% 仍可复现。关键地，我们发现环境回溯（即把依赖降级以匹配提交时的版本）并不能改善可复现性（反而降至 12%），还引入了额外的失败模式。为应对环境侵蚀，我们设计并实现了 MLEModernizer，一个由 LLM 驱动的智能体框架，它把当代环境视为固定约束，并现代化笔记本代码以恢复可复现性。MLEModernizer 迭代执行笔记本、收集执行反馈，并施加三类有针对性的修复：错误修复、运行时缩减和分数校准。在基线环境下不可复现的 8,210 个笔记本上评估，MLEModernizer 使 3,292 个（40.1%，GPT-5.2）和 3,683 个（44.9%，GPT-OSS-120b）笔记本恢复可复现。MLEModernizer 提供了一种尽力而为的自动恢复与现代化技术，可为部分笔记本改善可复现性。从业者可利用 MLEModernizer 在硬件与软件生态持续演进的过程中验证、复用和维护 MLE 制品。","tl":"以当代环境为约束，用智能体改写老笔记本代码恢复可复现","au":["Bihui Jin","Kaiyuan Wang","Pengyu Nie"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["llm-based","agentic","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["computational notebooks","reproducibility","environmental erosion","LLM agent","code modernization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/75/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.07195"},{"id":"p01358","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Seeing is Coding: On the Effectiveness of Vision Language Models in Code Understanding","tz":"看即是写：论视觉语言模型在代码理解中的有效性","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have achieved remarkable success in source code understanding, yet as software systems grow in scale, computational efficiency has become a critical bottleneck. Currently, these models rely on a text-based paradigm that treats source code as a linear sequence of tokens, which leads to a linear increase in context length and associated computational costs. The rapid advancement of Multimodal LLMs (MLLMs) introduces an opportunity to optimize efficiency by representing source code as rendered images. Unlike text, which is difficult to compress without losing semantic meaning, the image modality is inherently suitable for compression. By adjusting resolution, images can be scaled to a fraction of their original token cost while remaining recognizable to vision-capable models. To explore the feasibility of this approach, we conduct the first systematic study on the effectiveness of MLLMs for code understanding. Our experiments reveal that: (1) MLLMs can effectively understand code with substantial token reduction, achieving up to 8x compression; (2) MLLMs can effectively leverage visual cues such as syntax highlighting, improving code completion performance under 4x compression; and (3) Code-understanding tasks like clone detection exhibit exceptional resilience to visual compression, with some compression ratios even slightly outperforming raw text inputs. Our findings highlight both the potential and current limitations of MLLMs in code understanding, which points out a shift toward image-modality code representation as a pathway to more efficient inference.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在源代码理解上取得了显著成功，但随着软件系统规模增长，计算效率已成为关键瓶颈。目前这些模型依赖基于文本的范式，把源代码视为线性的 token 序列，导致上下文长度与相应计算成本线性增长。多模态大语言模型（MLLM）的快速发展带来了通过把源代码表示为渲染图像来优化效率的机会。与难以在不损失语义的情况下压缩的文本不同，图像模态天然适合压缩：通过调整分辨率，图像可被缩放到原始 token 成本的一小部分，同时仍能被具备视觉能力的模型识别。为探索该方法的可行性，我们开展了首个关于 MLLM 用于代码理解有效性的系统研究。实验揭示：（1）MLLM 能在大幅减少 token 的情况下有效理解代码，最高实现 8 倍压缩；（2）MLLM 能有效利用语法高亮等视觉线索，在 4 倍压缩下提升代码补全性能；（3）克隆检测等代码理解任务对视觉压缩表现出异常的鲁棒性，在某些压缩比下甚至略优于原始文本输入。我们的发现同时凸显了 MLLM 在代码理解中的潜力与当前局限，指出向图像模态代码表示转变可能是通往更高效推理的路径。","tl":"把代码渲染成图像喂给多模态模型，8 倍压缩仍能理解代码","au":["Yuling Shi","Chaoxiang Xie","Zhensu Sun","Yeheng Chen","Chenxu Zhang","Longfei Yun","Chengcheng Wan","Hongyu Zhang","David Lo","Xiaodong Gu"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["multimodal","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["multimodal LLM","code understanding","image-modality code","token compression","clone detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/76/x"},{"id":"p01359","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ConFL: Explainable Concurrent Fault Localization via Hierarchy-Guided LLM Reasoning","tz":"ConFL：基于层次引导 LLM 推理的可解释并发缺陷定位","a":"Localizing concurrent bugs from bug reports alone is challenging due to incomplete information, misleading program-entity mentions, and complex cross-thread interactions, causing existing LLM-based approaches to suffer from unstable reasoning and limited explainability. We propose ConFL, an explainable concurrent fault localization framework that augments LLM reasoning with structured concurrency knowledge. ConFL constructs a Concurrent Knowledge Base (CKB) from source code and performs LLM-guided hierarchical retrieval to progressively narrow the search space from components to interaction-level concurrency contexts. An interaction-level DSL explicitly encodes cross-thread interactions over shared resources, enabling focused reasoning without traversing deep call chains. Experiments on real-world concurrent bugs from eight large-scale Java projects show that ConFL significantly outperforms state-of-the-art IR-based and LLM-based baselines, achieving an MRR of 0.503 and a MAP of 0.486, while remaining robust to noisy bug reports, unseen bugs, and different LLM backbones.","az":"仅凭缺陷报告定位并发缺陷颇具挑战，原因在于信息不完整、程序实体提及具有误导性以及复杂的跨线程交互，这使得现有基于 LLM 的方法推理不稳定、可解释性有限。我们提出 ConFL，一个可解释的并发缺陷定位框架，用结构化的并发知识增强 LLM 推理。ConFL 从源代码构建并发知识库（CKB），并执行 LLM 引导的层次化检索，从组件层面逐步收窄到交互级并发上下文。一种交互级 DSL 显式编码共享资源上的跨线程交互，使推理能够聚焦而无需遍历深层调用链。在来自八个大型 Java 项目的真实并发缺陷上的实验表明，ConFL 显著优于最先进的基于信息检索和基于 LLM 的基线，取得 0.503 的 MRR 和 0.486 的 MAP，同时对噪声缺陷报告、未见缺陷和不同 LLM 骨干保持鲁棒。","tl":"构建并发知识库与交互级 DSL，层次检索引导 LLM 定位并发缺陷","au":["Shuai Shao","Dingbang Wang","Yiming Zeng","Tingting Yu"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["concurrency bugs","fault localization","bug reports","knowledge base","hierarchical retrieval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/77/x"},{"id":"p01360","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Belobog: Move Language Fuzzing Framework For Real-World Smart Contracts","tz":"Belobog：面向真实世界智能合约的 Move 语言模糊测试框架","a":"Move is a research-oriented programming language designed for secure and verifiable smart contract development and has been widely used in managing billions of digital assets in blockchains, such as Sui and Aptos. Move features a strong static type system and explicit resource semantics to enforce safety properties such as the prevention of data races, invalid asset transfers, and entry vulnerabilities. However, smart contracts written in Move may still contain certain vulnerabilities that are beyond the reach of its type system. It is thus essential to validate Move smart contracts. Unfortunately, due to its strong type system, existing smart contract fuzzers are ineffective in producing syntactically or semantically valid transactions to test Move smart contracts. This paper introduces the first fuzzing framework, Belobog, for Move smart contracts. Belobog is type-aware and ensures that all generated and mutated transactions are well-typed. More specifically, for a target Move smart contract, Belobog first constructs a type graph based on Move’s type system, and then generates or mutates a transaction based on the graph trace derived from the type graph. In order to overcome the complex checks in Move smart contracts, we further design and implement a concolic executor in Belobog. We evaluated Belobog on 109 real-world Move smart contract projects. The experimental results show that Belobog is able to detect 100% critical and 79% major vulnerabilities manually audited by human experts. We further selected two recent notorious incidents in the Move ecosystem, i.e., Cetus and Nemo. Belobog successfully reproduced full exploits for both of them, without any prior knowledge. Moreover, we applied Belobog on three ongoing auditing projects and found 2 critical, 2 major, and 3 medium new vulnerabilities, all acknowledged by the project developers.","az":"Move 是一门面向研究的编程语言，旨在支持安全且可验证的智能合约开发，已被广泛用于 Sui、Aptos 等区块链中管理数十亿数字资产。Move 具备强静态类型系统和显式的资源语义，以强制实施诸如防止数据竞争、非法资产转移和入口漏洞等安全属性。然而，用 Move 编写的智能合约仍可能包含其类型系统无法覆盖的漏洞，因此验证 Move 智能合约十分必要。遗憾的是，由于其强类型系统，现有智能合约模糊测试工具难以生成语法或语义上有效的交易来测试 Move 智能合约。本文提出首个面向 Move 智能合约的模糊测试框架 Belobog。Belobog 是类型感知的，确保所有生成和变异的交易都是良类型的。具体而言，对于目标 Move 智能合约，Belobog 首先基于 Move 的类型系统构建类型图，然后依据从类型图导出的图轨迹生成或变异交易。为克服 Move 智能合约中复杂的检查，我们进一步在 Belobog 中设计并实现了一个混合符号（concolic）执行器。我们在 109 个真实 Move 智能合约项目上评估 Belobog。实验结果表明，Belobog 能检测出人工专家审计的 100% 严重漏洞和 79% 主要漏洞。我们进一步选取了 Move 生态中两起近期臭名昭著的事件，即 Cetus 和 Nemo，Belobog 在无任何先验知识的情况下成功复现了二者的完整利用。此外，我们将 Belobog 应用于三个正在进行的审计项目，发现了 2 个严重、2 个主要和 3 个中等级别的新漏洞，全部获得项目开发者确认。","tl":"类型图加 concolic 执行，首个能生成良类型交易的 Move 合约 fuzzer","au":["Ziqiao Kong","Wanxu Xia","Zhengwei Li","Yi Lu","Pan Li","Liqun Yang","Yang Liu","Xiapu Luo","Shaohua Li"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Move language","smart contract fuzzing","type-aware generation","concolic execution","vulnerability detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/78/x"},{"id":"p01361","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Insecure Coding Preferences in Long-Term Memory: Security Risks for LLM-based Code Generation","tz":"长期记忆中的不安全编码偏好：基于 LLM 的代码生成的安全风险","a":"LLM-based systems are increasingly incorporating long-term memory to improve cross-session continuity and output consistency. However, the persistence of long-term memory may introduce additional risks in security-sensitive code generation: once insecure coding preferences are stored, they may silently and persistently influence security-critical choices in subsequent generations. In this study, we conduct the first systematic empirical study to evaluate the impact of insecure coding preferences stored in long-term memory on the security of LLM-based code generation. We study two widely used commercial LLMs (i.e., ChatGPT and Gemini) and examine the impact of long-term memory from multiple perspectives. Our results show that insecure coding preferences stored in long-term memory significantly increase the risk of generating vulnerable code by 11.3%–13.8%. Moreover, they reduce the likelihood that models proactively issue security warnings when producing vulnerable code, leading to a 5.4–14.5 percentage-point decrease. Further analysis reveals that these insecure memory entries are difficult to overwrite through normal interactions and can broadly influence model outputs even when prompts are phrased differently. Finally, we evaluate a mitigation strategy based on explicit security requirements, which reduces vulnerability rates by 19.7%–33.6% but may incur a functional performance drop of up to 15.9%. Based on these findings, we provide actionable suggestions to improve the security of long-term memory in LLM-based code generation.","az":"基于 LLM 的系统正越来越多地引入长期记忆，以改善跨会话连续性与输出一致性。然而，长期记忆的持久性可能在安全敏感的代码生成中带来额外风险：一旦不安全的编码偏好被存储，它们可能悄无声息且持续地影响后续生成中的安全关键选择。本研究首次系统性地实证评估存储于长期记忆中的不安全编码偏好对基于 LLM 的代码生成安全性的影响。我们研究了两个广泛使用的商业 LLM（即 ChatGPT 和 Gemini），并从多个角度考察长期记忆的影响。结果表明，存储在长期记忆中的不安全编码偏好使生成脆弱代码的风险显著上升 11.3%–13.8%。此外，它们降低了模型在生成脆弱代码时主动发出安全警告的可能性，导致 5.4–14.5 个百分点的下降。进一步分析显示，这些不安全的记忆条目难以通过正常交互被覆盖，即使提示措辞不同也能广泛影响模型输出。最后，我们评估了一种基于显式安全需求的缓解策略，它将漏洞率降低了 19.7%–33.6%，但可能带来最高 15.9% 的功能性能下降。基于这些发现，我们给出可操作的建议，以提升基于 LLM 的代码生成中长期记忆的安全性。","tl":"首次量化长期记忆里的不安全编码偏好会持续拉高漏洞率","au":["Yuchen Chen","Wei Cheng","Yuan Xiao","Zhou Yang","Weifeng Sun","Chunrong Fang","Xiang Chen","Baowen Xu","David Lo","Zhenyu Chen"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"agent-memory-context-and-retrieval","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["long-term memory","insecure coding preference","code generation security","ChatGPT","Gemini"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/79/x"},{"id":"p01362","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TraceDev: A Traceability-Driven Multi-Agent Framework for Requirement-to-Code Development","tz":"TraceDev：面向需求到代码开发的可追溯性驱动多智能体框架","a":"In modern software development, the rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs) has made the end-to-end transformation of Natural Language Requirements (NLRs) into executable repository-level code increasingly feasible. However, existing approaches typically rely on simplified instructions (e.g., single-sentence descriptions), failing to reflect complex software development scenarios. Moreover, they lack explicit requirement traceability mechanisms, making it difficult to precisely align and validate generated code against original requirements. To address these limitations, we propose TraceDev, a multi-agent framework for automated software development grounded in use cases that contain multiple functional points and complex semantics. TraceDev employs five role-specific agents, including a Requirement Refiner, Designer, Developer, Tester, and Validator. Notably, the Validator Agent constructs and maintains a heterogeneous traceability graph that links requirements, design models, and code artifacts for interacting with the preceding four agents. The traceability graph maintains consistency across various artifacts and serves as a structured context for efficient memory management, supporting reliable repository-level code generation. We evaluate TraceDev on two widely used datasets (including 125 use cases) compared with two state-of-the-art approaches. On the ETOUR dataset, TraceDev achieves a success rate of 53.63%, outperforming baseline approaches by up to 186.63%. A similar trend is observed on the SMOS dataset, where TraceDev attains a success rate of 56.82%, exceeding baseline approaches by up to 340.80%. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of TraceDev in repository-level code generation from requirements. The code and data are available at URL .","az":"在现代软件开发中，大语言模型（LLM）的快速发展使得把自然语言需求（NLR）端到端转化为可执行的仓库级代码日益可行。然而，现有方法通常依赖简化的指令（如单句描述），无法反映复杂的软件开发场景。此外，它们缺乏显式的需求可追溯机制，难以将生成代码与原始需求精确对齐和验证。为解决这些局限，我们提出 TraceDev，一个以包含多个功能点和复杂语义的用例为基础的自动化软件开发多智能体框架。TraceDev 使用五个角色化智能体，包括需求精炼者、设计者、开发者、测试者和验证者。值得注意的是，验证者智能体构建并维护一张异构可追溯图，把需求、设计模型和代码制品链接起来，并与前述四个智能体交互。该可追溯图在各类制品间保持一致性，并作为结构化上下文用于高效的记忆管理，支撑可靠的仓库级代码生成。我们在两个广泛使用的数据集（共 125 个用例）上将 TraceDev 与两种最先进方法比较。在 ETOUR 数据集上，TraceDev 取得 53.63% 的成功率，最高超过基线 186.63%；在 SMOS 数据集上也观察到类似趋势，TraceDev 取得 56.82% 的成功率，最高超过基线 340.80%。这些结果表明 TraceDev 在从需求生成仓库级代码方面的有效性。代码与数据已公开。","tl":"用异构需求-设计-代码可追溯图协调五角色智能体做仓库级开发","au":["Mingyu Chen","Yakun Zhang","Zihao Xie","Yixing Luo","Jinrui Xu","Cuiyun Gao","Kaiqi Zhao","Yunming Ye"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["requirement-to-code","multi-agent framework","traceability graph","repository-level generation","use cases"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/80/x"},{"id":"p01363","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Efficient Grammar-Constrained Decoding via Parser Stack Classification","tz":"通过解析器栈分类实现高效的语法约束解码","a":"LLMs are widely used to generate structured output like source code or JSON. Grammar-constrained decoding (GCD) can guarantee the syntactic validity of the generated output, by masking out tokens that violate rules specified by a context-free grammar. However, the online computational overhead of existing GCD methods, with latency typically scaling linearly with vocabulary size, limits the throughput of LLMs, especially for models with large vocabularies. To address this issue, we propose PSC, a novel grammar-constrained decoding method. By combining acceptance conditions of all vocabulary tokens into a single classifier of the parser stack during preprocessing, PSC can compute the complete vocabulary mask by checking the parser stack exactly once per decoding step, with time complexity independent of the vocabulary size. Experiments show that PSC computes masks up to 700× faster than baselines on complex programming language grammars, and up to 30× faster for schema-conformant JSON; end-to-end LLM throughput with PSC approaches that of unconstrained decoding.","az":"LLM 被广泛用于生成源代码或 JSON 等结构化输出。语法约束解码（GCD）通过屏蔽违反上下文无关文法规则的 token，可以保证生成输出的语法有效性。然而，现有 GCD 方法的在线计算开销（其延迟通常随词表大小线性增长）限制了 LLM 的吞吐量，对于词表很大的模型尤为明显。为解决该问题，我们提出 PSC，一种新的语法约束解码方法。通过在预处理阶段把所有词表 token 的接受条件合并为对解析器栈的单一分类器，PSC 在每个解码步只需检查解析器栈一次即可计算出完整的词表掩码，时间复杂度与词表大小无关。实验表明，在复杂的编程语言文法上，PSC 计算掩码的速度最高比基线快 700 倍；在符合 schema 的 JSON 上最高快 30 倍；使用 PSC 的端到端 LLM 吞吐量接近无约束解码。","tl":"把 token 接受条件编成解析器栈分类器，掩码计算与词表规模无关","au":["Yongmin Li","Yihong Dong","Jia Li","Ge Li"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"efficient-inference-quantization-and-ml-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["grammar-constrained decoding","parser stack","vocabulary mask","structured output","throughput"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/81/x"},{"id":"p01364","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"MoT: Modularization-of-Thought Prompting for Effective Code Generation","tz":"MoT：面向高效代码生成的思维模块化提示","a":"Large Language Models are transforming software development by automatically generating code. Current prompting techniques such as Chain-of-Thought (CoT) suggest tasks step by step and the reasoning process follows a linear structure, which hampers the understanding of complex programming problems, particularly those requiring hierarchical solutions. Inspired by the principle of modularization in software development, in this work, we propose a novel prompting technique called MoT (Modularization of Thought), to enhance the code generation performance of LLMs. First, MoT exploits modularization principles to decompose complex programming problems into smaller, independent reasoning steps, enabling a more structured and interpretable problem-solving process. This hierarchical structure improves the LLMs‘ ability to comprehend complex programming problems. Then, it structures the reasoning process using an MLR Graph (Multi-Level Reasoning Graph), which hierarchically organizes reasoning steps. This approach enhances modular understanding and ensures better alignment between reasoning steps and the generated code, significantly improving code generation performance. Our experiments on two advanced LLMs (GPT-4o-mini and DeepSeek-R1), comparing MoT to six baseline prompting techniques across six widely used datasets, demonstrate that MoT significantly outperforms existing baselines (e.g., CoT and SCoT), achieving Pass@1 scores ranging from 58.1% to 95.1%.","az":"大语言模型正通过自动生成代码改变软件开发。当前的提示技术如思维链（CoT）逐步提示任务，其推理过程遵循线性结构，这妨碍了对复杂编程问题（尤其是需要层次化解法的问题）的理解。受软件开发中模块化原则的启发，本文提出一种新的提示技术 MoT（Modularization of Thought，思维模块化），以提升 LLM 的代码生成性能。首先，MoT 利用模块化原则把复杂编程问题分解为更小的、相互独立的推理步骤，使问题求解过程更结构化、更可解释。这种层次结构提升了 LLM 理解复杂编程问题的能力。随后，它使用 MLR 图（Multi-Level Reasoning Graph，多层推理图）来组织推理过程，按层次结构组织推理步骤。该方法增强了模块化理解，确保推理步骤与生成代码之间更好地对齐，显著提升代码生成性能。我们在两个先进 LLM（GPT-4o-mini 和 DeepSeek-R1）上开展实验，在六个广泛使用的数据集上将 MoT 与六种基线提示技术比较，结果表明 MoT 显著优于现有基线（如 CoT 和 SCoT），Pass@1 分数在 58.1% 到 95.1% 之间。","tl":"借鉴软件模块化，用多层推理图组织代码生成的推理步骤","au":["Ruwei Pan","Hongyu Zhang"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based"],"kw":["prompting technique","modularization of thought","multi-level reasoning graph","code generation","Pass@1"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/82/x"},{"id":"p01365","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AgentInspect: Diagnosing Behavioral Failures in Artificial Intelligence Agents","tz":"AgentInspect：诊断人工智能智能体的行为性失效","a":"Effectively testing Artificial Intelligence (AI) agents remains a fundamental challenge due to their stochastic reasoning, vast and diverse input space, reliance on external tools, and operation in dynamic execution environments; factors that demand new testing methodologies explicitly tailored to the complex and interactive nature of agent-based systems. This work presents a novel methodology for testing AI agents, with a particular focus on assessing their behavioral robustness under varied operational conditions. Our approach relies on following key technical innovations: (1) a coverage-guided test input generation strategy based on agent-specific coverage criteria, (2) a capture-and-simulate mechanism that systematically emulates abnormal tool behaviors to mimic real-world execution failures, and (3) a deterministic behavioral failure detection approach that enables consistent identification of failures across different test inputs. We developed AgentInspect, a framework that automatically detects six categories of behavioral failures in LangChain-based AI agents by analyzing their execution trajectories across two evaluation settings: a baseline setting using real tool responses and a simulated setting incorporating synthetic tool responses. To evaluate our approach, we curated a benchmark of 35 AI agents obtained from GitHub. Our results show that AgentInspect consistently identifies different behavioral failures with high precision and recall across both baseline and simulated execution settings. In particular, the simulated setting exposes failure modes that do not emerge during baseline execution with real tool responses, thereby enabling a more comprehensive assessment of agent robustness. Our findings highlight AgentInspect’s effectiveness in revealing critical failures and its practical utility for systematic robustness evaluation of AI agents.","az":"由于智能体具有随机性推理、庞大多样的输入空间、对外部工具的依赖以及在动态执行环境中运行等特点，有效测试人工智能（AI）智能体仍是一项根本性挑战；这些因素要求专门针对基于智能体的系统的复杂交互本质设计新的测试方法。本文提出一种测试 AI 智能体的新方法，尤其关注评估其在多变运行条件下的行为鲁棒性。我们的方法依赖以下关键技术创新：（1）基于智能体专用覆盖准则的覆盖引导测试输入生成策略；（2）一种捕获-模拟机制，系统性地仿真异常工具行为以模仿真实执行失败；（3）一种确定性的行为失效检测方法，能够在不同测试输入间一致地识别失效。我们开发了 AgentInspect 框架，通过分析基于 LangChain 的 AI 智能体在两种评估设置（使用真实工具响应的基线设置和引入合成工具响应的模拟设置）下的执行轨迹，自动检测六类行为性失效。为评估该方法，我们整理了一个包含从 GitHub 获取的 35 个 AI 智能体的基准。结果表明，AgentInspect 在基线与模拟两种执行设置下都能以高精确率和高召回率一致地识别各类行为性失效。特别地，模拟设置暴露出在使用真实工具响应的基线执行中不会出现的失效模式，从而支持对智能体鲁棒性更全面的评估。我们的发现凸显了 AgentInspect 在揭示关键失效方面的有效性及其在系统化鲁棒性评估中的实用价值。","tl":"覆盖引导输入加模拟异常工具响应，自动查出六类智能体行为失效","au":["Ruchira Manke","Mohammad Wardat","Foutse Khomh","Hridesh Rajan"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["agentic","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["AI agent testing","behavioral failures","coverage-guided input generation","tool response simulation","LangChain"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/83/x"},{"id":"p01366","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Hidden Licensing Risks in the PTMware Ecosystem","tz":"PTMware 生态中隐藏的许可证风险","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have been increasingly integrated into software systems, giving rise to a new class of software referred to as LLMware. In addition to traditional software components composed solely of source code, LLMware also embeds or interacts with LLMs that depend on other models and datasets, forming complex supply chains involving open-source software (OSS) libraries, LLMs, and datasets. However, the licensing issues arising from these intertwined dependencies remain largely unexplored. Leveraging GitHub and Hugging Face, two premier hubs for code and models, we curate a large- scale dataset capturing the supply chains of LLMware. Our dataset comprises 12,180 OSS repositories from GitHub, 3,988 LLMs, and 708 datasets from Hugging Face. We analyze license distributions in the LLMware ecosystem and find that licensing practices differ markedly from those in traditional OSS communities. We further examine license-related issues and identify license selection and maintenance as the primary pain points, with 84% of cases involving discussions about adding appropriate licenses or resolving conflicts in existing ones. We then study license incompatibility in LLMware and evaluate the state-of-the-art approaches, finding that they perform poorly in this setting and achieve only 58% and 76% F1 scores, respectively. These results motivate us to propose LiAgent, which explores the potential of LLM-based agents for ecosystem-level license compatibility analysis, achieves an F1 score of 87%, and improves performance by 14 percentage points over prior approaches. We submit 60 license incompatibility issues detected by LiAgent, of which 11 have been confirmed by developers. Two LLMs with license conflicts have more than 107 million and 5 million downloads on Hugging Face, respectively, suggesting the issues may impact a large number of downstream applications. We conclude by discussing implications and providing recommendations to support the healthy growth of the LLMware ecosystem.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）正越来越多地被集成进软件系统，催生出被称为 LLMware 的新一类软件。除了仅由源代码构成的传统软件组件外，LLMware 还嵌入或与依赖其他模型和数据集的 LLM 交互，形成涉及开源软件（OSS）库、LLM 和数据集的复杂供应链。然而，这些交织依赖所引发的许可证问题在很大程度上仍未被探究。借助代码与模型两大枢纽 GitHub 和 Hugging Face，我们整理了一个刻画 LLMware 供应链的大规模数据集，包含来自 GitHub 的 12,180 个 OSS 仓库，以及来自 Hugging Face 的 3,988 个 LLM 和 708 个数据集。我们分析了 LLMware 生态中的许可证分布，发现其许可实践与传统 OSS 社区明显不同。我们进一步考察与许可证相关的 issue，识别出许可证的选择与维护是主要痛点，84% 的案例涉及关于添加合适许可证或解决既有许可证冲突的讨论。随后我们研究 LLMware 中的许可证不兼容问题，并评估最先进的方法，发现它们在此场景中表现不佳，F1 分数分别仅为 58% 和 76%。这促使我们提出 LiAgent，探索基于 LLM 的智能体进行生态级许可证兼容性分析的潜力，取得 87% 的 F1 分数，比既有方法提升 14 个百分点。我们提交了 LiAgent 检出的 60 个许可证不兼容问题，其中 11 个已被开发者确认。两个存在许可证冲突的 LLM 在 Hugging Face 上的下载量分别超过 1.07 亿次和 500 万次，说明这些问题可能影响大量下游应用。最后我们讨论了启示并给出建议，以支持 LLMware 生态的健康成长。","tl":"首次刻画 LLMware 许可证生态，并用 LLM 智能体做生态级兼容性分析","au":["Bo Wang","Yueyang Chen","Jieke Shi","Minghui Li","Yunbo Lyu","Yinan Wu","Youfang Lin","Zhou Yang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["license incompatibility","LLMware supply chain","Hugging Face","open source licensing","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/84/x"},{"id":"p01367","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Finding and Understanding Missed Optimizations in WebAssembly Optimizer (Experience Paper)","tz":"发现并理解 WebAssembly 优化器中的漏优化（经验论文）","a":"As WebAssembly (Wasm) expands from web applications to high-performance domains, the standard optimizer, wasm-opt, is critical but frequently suffers from missed optimizations (MOs). This paper presents an experience report on detecting MOs in wasm-opt and understanding their root cause through the lens of Wasm’s tree-structured intermediate representation (tree IR). To this end, we adapt an established marker-based technique from C compilers, overcoming the constraints of Wasm’s structured control flow via a novel structure-aware instrumentation strategy. Complementing this, we design a cross-optimization differential testing strategy leveraging the monotonicity of optimization levels as an oracle. Together, these strategies enable the systematic identification of fine-grained MOs that are overlooked by existing cross-architecture methods. Our evaluation uncovered 24 distinct MOs (20 fixed), demonstrating the high actionability and effectiveness of our approach. Beyond detection, our root cause analysis reveals how wasm-opt’s tree IR and other design choices constrain its optimization potential. We conclude with architectural considerations and future directions for wasm-opt and similar optimizers.","az":"随着 WebAssembly（Wasm）从 Web 应用扩展到高性能领域，标准优化器 wasm-opt 变得至关重要，但它频繁出现漏优化（MO）。本文给出一份经验报告，介绍如何检测 wasm-opt 中的漏优化，并通过 Wasm 的树形中间表示（tree IR）视角理解其根因。为此，我们改造了源自 C 编译器的成熟标记（marker）技术，借助一种新颖的结构感知插桩策略克服了 Wasm 结构化控制流带来的限制。作为补充，我们设计了一种跨优化差分测试策略，利用优化级别的单调性作为测试预言。二者结合可系统性地识别现有跨架构方法所忽略的细粒度漏优化。我们的评估发现了 24 个不同的漏优化（其中 20 个已修复），表明该方法高度可操作且有效。除检测之外，我们的根因分析揭示了 wasm-opt 的树形 IR 及其他设计选择如何限制其优化潜力。最后我们给出了针对 wasm-opt 及类似优化器的架构性思考与未来方向。","tl":"结构感知插桩加优化级单调性差分，挖出 wasm-opt 的 24 个漏优化","au":["Ruiyang Xu","Zetao Fan","Shan Huang","Ting Su"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["WebAssembly","missed optimization","wasm-opt","differential testing","tree IR"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/85/x"},{"id":"p01368","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Are We Stuck? Modeling and Detecting Deadlocks in Multi-Autonomous Vehicle Systems","tz":"我们卡住了吗？多自动驾驶车辆系统中死锁的建模与检测","a":"Autonomous driving system (ADS) testing is essential to ensure the safety and reliability of autonomous vehicles (AVs) prior to deployment. As ADSs are increasingly deployed in multi-AV traffic environments, it becomes crucial to assess their cooperative performance, particularly with respect to deadlock, a fundamental liveness issue in concurrent systems that can lead to traffic congestion and prolonged stalling. However, the analysis and testing of ADSs’ cooperative capabilities with respect to deadlock remain largely underexplored. In this work, we present the first systematic study of deadlock in multi-AV systems. We formalize deadlock in autonomous driving using a time-indexed wait-for relation grounded in vehicles’ planned trajectories and road-region occupancy. Building on this formalization, we propose WaitWatch, a wait-for–oriented testing framework that steers scenario generation via spatio-temporal intersection alignment of executed trajectories to induce circular wait patterns. WaitWatch integrates a Deadlock Judge, Intersection Alignment Feedback, and Intersection Oriented Mutation to efficiently uncover latent deadlock scenarios. We conduct an extensive evaluation on three representative ADSs. Experimental results show that, on average, WaitWatch generates 2.28×more deadlock scenarios (DLSs) than the best-performing baseline. By shifting the focus from single-AV evaluation to multi-AV cooperation, our approach identifies a range of previously unknown deadlock behaviors, revealing significant limitations in the cooperative and liveness capabilities of current ADSs. Our findings highlight a fundamental safety–liveness trade-off in deadlock resolution and emonstrate the need for systematic deadlock-aware testing in the development and validation of autonomous driving systems.","az":"自动驾驶系统（ADS）测试对于在部署前确保自动驾驶车辆（AV）的安全性与可靠性至关重要。随着 ADS 越来越多地部署在多 AV 交通环境中，评估其协同性能变得尤为关键，特别是关于死锁——并发系统中一种基本的活性问题，可能导致交通拥堵和长时间停滞。然而，针对 ADS 协同能力在死锁方面的分析与测试仍基本未被探索。本文首次系统研究多 AV 系统中的死锁。我们基于车辆规划轨迹与道路区域占用，用带时间索引的等待关系形式化自动驾驶中的死锁。在此形式化基础上，我们提出 WaitWatch，一个面向等待关系的测试框架，通过对已执行轨迹进行时空交叉对齐来引导场景生成，以诱发循环等待模式。WaitWatch 集成了死锁判定器、交叉对齐反馈和面向交叉的变异，以高效发掘潜在的死锁场景。我们在三个代表性 ADS 上开展了广泛评估。实验结果表明，WaitWatch 平均比表现最好的基线多生成 2.28 倍的死锁场景。通过把关注点从单 AV 评估转向多 AV 协同，我们的方法识别出一系列此前未知的死锁行为，揭示了当前 ADS 在协同与活性能力上的显著局限。我们的发现凸显了死锁消解中根本性的安全—活性权衡，并表明在自动驾驶系统的开发与验证中亟需系统化的死锁感知测试。","tl":"用时间索引等待关系形式化多车死锁并引导场景变异触发它","au":["Mingfei Cheng","Xiaofei Xie","Lili Quan","Yuan Zhou"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving system","deadlock","multi-AV cooperation","scenario-based testing","liveness"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/86/x"},{"id":"p01369","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"StateTree: A Tree-Based Modeling Approach for Fault Detection in Recurrent Neural Networks","tz":"StateTree：面向循环神经网络故障检测的树型建模方法","a":"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) have become a core component of modern intelligent software due to their strong ability to model temporal dependencies. As RNNs are increasingly deployed in safety-critical domains, ensuring their reliability is crucial. However, most existing testing techniques are designed for feedforward networks and struggle with RNNs. The stateful nature, recurrent feedback, and long-term dependencies of RNNs make it difficult for existing testing methods to capture decision logic and temporal behaviors, which in turn makes detecting fault-inducing behaviors that emerge through temporal decision evolution challenging. To address these challenges, we propose StateTree, a tree-based abstract modeling approach for systematic testing of RNN-based systems. StateTree constructs an Abstract State Tree (AST) that captures major RNN decision behaviors, where each root-to-leaf path represents an abstract decision for intuitive interpretation and structured exploration. Using the AST, StateTree guides the testing process toward both major and previously unseen paths to reveal erroneous behaviors. Experiments show that StateTree accurately abstracts RNN decisions, detects hundreds of faults, and retraining with its identified test cases improves robustness beyond existing RNN coverage methods, demonstrating its effectiveness in both fault detection and model performance enhancement.","az":"循环神经网络（RNN）凭借对时序依赖的强建模能力，已成为现代智能软件的核心组件。随着 RNN 越来越多地部署于安全攸关领域，确保其可靠性至关重要。然而，现有多数测试技术针对前馈网络设计，难以应对 RNN。RNN 的有状态性、循环反馈和长期依赖使得现有测试方法难以刻画其决策逻辑与时序行为，这又使得检测那些在时序决策演化中出现的诱发故障行为变得困难。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 StateTree，一种用于系统测试基于 RNN 系统的树型抽象建模方法。StateTree 构建抽象状态树（AST）以刻画 RNN 的主要决策行为，其中每条从根到叶的路径代表一次抽象决策，便于直观解释与结构化探索。借助 AST，StateTree 将测试过程引向主要路径以及此前未见的路径，以揭示错误行为。实验表明，StateTree 能准确抽象 RNN 的决策，检测出数百个故障，并且用其识别出的测试用例进行再训练可以提升鲁棒性，超越现有的 RNN 覆盖率方法，证明了它在故障检测与模型性能提升上的有效性。","tl":"用抽象状态树刻画 RNN 时序决策并据此引导测试找故障","au":["Xinyu Gao","Shuoxiao Zhang","Minghui Wei","Xiao Zhang","An Guo","Enyi Tang"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["recurrent neural networks","abstract state tree","fault detection","DNN testing","coverage guidance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/87/x"},{"id":"p01370","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Poirot: Automatic Root Cause Analysis of Safety Violations in ADS Simulation Testing via Hypothetical Reasoning","tz":"Poirot：通过假设性推理自动分析 ADS 仿真测试中安全违规的根因","a":"With the rapid development of autonomous driving systems (ADSs), it has become critical to ensure their operational safety, leading to the widespread adoption of simulation testing. While existing scenario-based simulation testing approaches have demonstrated effectiveness in detecting safety violations, they often fall short in providing insight into the underlying causes of these violations, which is an essential capability for improving the safety and reliability of ADSs. To address this limitation, we propose a two-phase novel framework, Poirot, for root cause analysis in simulation testing via hypothetical reasoning. Given a reproducible violation scenario, in the module-level analysis phase, Poirot replays the violation scenario and identifies the faulty module by iteratively replacing an actual module with an idealized module and checking whether the violation persists. In the component-level analysis phase, depending on the identified faulty module, Poirot further applies either hypothetical reasoning with a suspicion-guided search strategy or causal analysis to narrow the fault space and pinpoint the faulty component. We evaluate Poirot with two ADSs, e.g., Apollo and Autoware, on a comprehensive benchmark that includes a total of 80 real and injected faults along with their triggering scenarios. Compared with the state-of-the-art root cause analysis approaches, e.g., ACAV and Rocas, Poirot improves the module-level accuracy by 187.29% on average, and identifies the faulty components at a finer granularity, achieving component-level accuracy of 90.62%. Our ablation study shows that our suspicion-guided search strategy in Poirot efficiently reduces the exploration of the fault space by 58.77%, leading to a 65.41% reduction in the time for fault localization. Finally, applied to two scenario-based simulation testing methods, i.e., AvFuzzer and MoDitector, Poirot attributes 425 violation scenarios to 8 faults, cutting debugging time by 96.89% compared to manual analysis in practice.","az":"随着自动驾驶系统（ADS）的快速发展，确保其运行安全变得至关重要，这促使仿真测试被广泛采用。尽管现有基于场景的仿真测试方法在检测安全违规方面已展现出有效性，它们往往无法揭示这些违规的底层原因，而这正是提升 ADS 安全性与可靠性的关键能力。为解决这一局限，我们提出两阶段的新框架 Poirot，通过假设性推理进行仿真测试中的根因分析。给定一个可复现的违规场景，在模块级分析阶段，Poirot 重放该违规场景，并通过迭代地用理想化模块替换实际模块、检查违规是否仍然存在，来识别故障模块。在组件级分析阶段，依据所识别的故障模块，Poirot 进一步采用带有怀疑度引导搜索策略的假设性推理或因果分析，以缩小故障空间并定位故障组件。我们在两个 ADS（如 Apollo 与 Autoware）上评估 Poirot，使用一个包含共 80 个真实与注入故障及其触发场景的综合基准。与最先进的根因分析方法（如 ACAV 与 Rocas）相比，Poirot 将模块级准确率平均提升 187.29%，并以更细粒度识别故障组件，达到 90.62% 的组件级准确率。消融实验表明，Poirot 中的怀疑度引导搜索策略将故障空间的探索有效减少 58.77%，使故障定位时间减少 65.41%。最后，应用于两种基于场景的仿真测试方法（即 AvFuzzer 与 MoDitector）时，Poirot 将 425 个违规场景归因到 8 个故障，与实践中的人工分析相比把调试时间削减了 96.89%。","tl":"用理想化模块替换与怀疑度引导搜索定位 ADS 违规的故障组件","au":["You Lu","Dingji Wang","Kun Zhang","Bihuan Chen","Jiyan Zhang","Xin Peng"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving","root cause analysis","simulation testing","hypothetical reasoning","fault localization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/88/x"},{"id":"p01371","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Deprecated but Not Abandoned: A Large-Scale Empirical Study on Growing-user-demand Deprecated NPM Packages","tz":"已弃用但未被抛弃：关于用户需求持续增长的已弃用 NPM 包的大规模实证研究","a":"Package deprecation in ecosystems like NPM signals the termination of maintenance, and continued use of such packages poses potential sustainability and security risks to dependent projects. We observe a counter-intuitive phenomenon among widely-used deprecated packages whose user demand continues to grow after deprecation; we define these as Growing-user-demand Deprecated NPM Packages (GDNPs). Despite this clear contradiction between deprecation and growing user demand, the community engagement, reasons, and challenges of GDNPs have not been systematically examined. To bridge this gap, we conduct a mixed-method empirical study that identifies and analyzes 864 GDNPs from 4,011 widely-used deprecated packages, alongside surveys of 76 maintainers and 67 users. We find that GDNPs grow on average by 14.5% per month after deprecation, yet repository-level community engagement eventually drops significantly, revealing an expanding maintenance gap. Quantitatively, GDNPs contribute to over 124 million monthly exposures to high-severity vulnerabilities. Surveys indicate that continued reliance stems primarily from the complexity of the dependency tree and user inertia, leading to reactive maintenance and the accumulation of technical debt. Furthermore, topic modeling of post-deprecation discussions of GDNP repositories shows that community discussions heavily prioritize functional errors while seldom discussing security vulnerabilities, highlighting a misalignment between perceived and actual risk. Based on the results, we provide actionable implications that can facilitate future research and assist stakeholders in improving the maintenance of GDNPs.","az":"在 NPM 这类生态中，包的弃用标志着维护的终止，继续使用这类包会给依赖项目带来潜在的可持续性与安全风险。我们观察到一个反直觉现象：一些被广泛使用的已弃用包在弃用后用户需求仍持续增长；我们将其定义为“用户需求增长型已弃用 NPM 包”（GDNP）。尽管弃用与用户需求增长之间存在明显矛盾，GDNP 的社区参与情况、成因与挑战尚未被系统考察。为弥合这一空白，我们开展了一项混合方法实证研究，从 4,011 个广泛使用的已弃用包中识别并分析了 864 个 GDNP，并对 76 名维护者和 67 名用户进行了问卷调查。我们发现 GDNP 在弃用后平均每月增长 14.5%，但仓库级社区参与度最终显著下降，暴露出不断扩大的维护缺口。定量来看，GDNP 每月造成超过 1.24 亿次对高危漏洞的暴露。调查表明，持续依赖主要源于依赖树的复杂性与用户惯性，导致被动式维护与技术债的累积。此外，对 GDNP 仓库弃用后讨论的主题建模显示，社区讨论高度集中于功能性错误，而很少讨论安全漏洞，凸显了感知风险与实际风险之间的错位。基于这些结果，我们给出可操作的启示，以助力未来研究并帮助利益相关方改善 GDNP 的维护。","tl":"发现并刻画弃用后需求反增的 NPM 包及其维护缺口与风险错位","au":["Zezhou Tang","Yang Zhang","Xinjun Mao","Tanghaoran Zhang","Changrong Xie","Wenyu Xu","Simeng Yao","Yiwen Wu"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","tg":["empirical-study","human-study","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["package deprecation","NPM ecosystem","dependency maintenance","empirical study","developer survey"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/89/x"},{"id":"p01372","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Generating Project-Specific Test Cases with Requirement Validation Intention","tz":"基于需求验证意图生成项目专用测试用例","a":"Test cases are valuable assets for maintaining software quality. State-of-the-art automated test generation techniques typically focus on maximizing program branch coverage or translating focal methods into test code. However, in contrast to branch coverage or code-to-test translation, practical tests are written out of the need to validate whether a requirement has been fulfilled. Specifically, each test usually reflects a developer’s validation intention for a program function, regarding (1) what is the test scenario of a program function? and (2) what is expected behavior under such a scenario? Without taking such intention into account, generated tests are less likely to be adopted in practice. In this work, we propose IntentionTest, which generates project-specific tests given the description of validation intention. The design is motivated by two insights: (1) rationale insight: the description of validation intention regarding scenario description and behavioral expectation, compared to coverage and focal code, carries more crucial information about {what to test}; and (2) technical insight: practical test code exhibits high duplication, indicating that existing tests are highly reusable for {how to test}. Therefore, IntentionTest adopts a retrieval-and-edit manner. First, given a focal code and a description of validation intention consisting of a test objective with test precondition and expected results, IntentionTest retrieves a reusable test in the project as the test reference. Then, IntentionTest edits the test reference with an LLM regarding the validation intention toward the target test. To guarantee that the target test can have a project-specific test prefix and a relevant test assertion, IntentionTest further explores the software project to identify crucial code facts (i.e., relevant API/code to call and global variables to refer to in the test) as important context for the test generation. We extensively evaluate IntentionTest against four baselines (TELPA, DA, ChatTester, and EvoSuite) on 3,680 test cases from 12 open-source projects. Compared to state-of-the-art baselines, with a given validation intention, IntentionTest can (1) generate tests far more semantically relevant to ground-truth tests by (i) killing 28.1% to 37.6% more common mutants and (ii) sharing 16.9% to 23.9% more common coverage; and (2) generate 23.7% to 49.0% more successful passing tests.","az":"测试用例是维护软件质量的宝贵资产。最先进的自动测试生成技术通常聚焦于最大化程序分支覆盖率，或把焦点方法翻译成测试代码。然而，与分支覆盖或代码到测试的翻译不同，实际测试是出于验证某项需求是否被满足的需要而编写的。具体而言，每个测试通常反映开发者对某个程序功能的“验证意图”，涉及两点：（1）该程序功能的测试场景是什么？（2）在该场景下的预期行为是什么？若不考虑这种意图，生成的测试在实践中不太可能被采纳。本文提出 IntentionTest，在给定验证意图描述的情况下生成项目专用的测试。该设计由两点洞见驱动：（1）原理洞见：相比覆盖率和焦点代码，关于场景描述与行为预期的验证意图描述携带了更关键的“测什么”的信息；（2）技术洞见：实际测试代码高度重复，说明既有测试对于“怎么测”具有很高的可复用性。因此，IntentionTest 采用检索并编辑的方式。首先，给定焦点代码以及由测试目标、测试前置条件和预期结果构成的验证意图描述，IntentionTest 在项目中检索一个可复用的测试作为测试参考。然后，IntentionTest 用 LLM 依据验证意图把该测试参考编辑为目标测试。为保证目标测试能拥有项目专用的测试前缀和相关的测试断言，IntentionTest 进一步探索软件项目以识别“关键代码事实”（即测试中需要调用的相关 API/代码以及需要引用的全局变量），作为测试生成的重要上下文。我们在来自 12 个开源项目的 3,680 个测试用例上，将 IntentionTest 与四个基线（TELPA、DA、ChatTester 和 EvoSuite）进行了广泛评估。与最先进基线相比，在给定验证意图的情况下，IntentionTest 能够（1）生成语义上与真实测试更相关的测试，表现为（i）多杀死 28.1% 至 37.6% 的共同变异体，（ii）多共享 16.9% 至 23.9% 的共同覆盖；并且（2）多生成 23.7% 至 49.0% 的成功通过测试。","tl":"以验证意图为输入，检索并编辑项目内既有测试生成专用用例","au":["Binhang Qi","Yun Lin","Xinyi Weng","Yuhuan Huang","Chenyan Liu","Hailong Sun","Zhi Jin","Jin Song Dong"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["validation intention","project-specific test generation","retrieve-and-edit","crucial code facts","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/90/x"},{"id":"p01373","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Self-Adaptive Code Representation: Grammar-Guided or Token-Based?","tz":"自适应代码表示：语法引导还是基于 token？","a":"Recent advances in code intelligence are largely driven by large language models (LLMs), which represent code as token sequences and achieve strong results on many software engineering tasks. However, standard token-based approaches often struggle to capture the inherent structural regularities of programming languages. While grammar-guided approaches can alleviate this limitation by modeling syntax more explicitly, they may sacrifice flexibility. In this work, we propose the Self-Adaptive Code Representation (SACR) framework, which enables models to dynamically select between token-based and grammar-guided representations depending on the problem context. SACR operates in two stages: first, the model is jointly trained on both representations to learn their respective strengths; second, an adaptive mechanism quantifies the generation difficulty for each sample and selects the model’s preferred code representation for training. We implement SACR in three versions of SacrCoder with parameter sizes of 0.5B, 1.3B, and 3B, and evaluate their effectiveness across a range of code generation and code repair benchmarks. Through empirical analysis, we first demonstrate that token-based and grammar-guided code representations exhibit complementary strengths. Building on this observation, SACR selectively exploits these complementary representations during training to improve overall performance. Experimental results show that SacrCoder consistently achieves state-of-the-art performance. For example, the 3B model obtains a Pass@1 of 84.1% on HumanEval and 30.3% on APPS, corresponding to relative improvements of 9.5% and 32.3% over grammar-only and dual-format baselines, respectively. Further ablation studies confirm that the effectiveness of SACR in leveraging complementary code representations.","az":"代码智能的最新进展主要由大语言模型（LLM）驱动，它们把代码表示为 token 序列，并在许多软件工程任务上取得了强劲结果。然而，标准的基于 token 的方法往往难以捕捉编程语言固有的结构规律。虽然语法引导的方法能通过更显式地建模语法来缓解这一局限，但可能牺牲灵活性。本文提出自适应代码表示（SACR）框架，使模型能够依据问题上下文动态地在基于 token 与语法引导的表示之间进行选择。SACR 分两个阶段运行：首先，模型在两种表示上联合训练以学习各自的优势；其次，一种自适应机制量化每个样本的生成难度，并为训练选择模型偏好的代码表示。我们以 0.5B、1.3B 和 3B 三种参数规模实现了 SacrCoder，并在一系列代码生成与代码修复基准上评估其效果。通过实证分析，我们首先证明基于 token 与语法引导的代码表示具有互补优势；在此观察基础上，SACR 在训练期间有选择地利用这些互补表示以提升整体性能。实验结果表明 SacrCoder 持续取得最先进性能，例如 3B 模型在 HumanEval 上获得 84.1% 的 Pass@1，在 APPS 上为 30.3%，相对仅语法基线和双格式基线分别提升 9.5% 和 32.3%。进一步的消融实验证实了 SACR 在利用互补代码表示上的有效性。","tl":"按样本生成难度自适应在 token 与语法表示间切换训练代码模型","au":["Qingyuan Liang","Zhao Zhang","Chen Liu","Zeyu Sun","Zheng Lin","Yueyi Xiao","Haotian Zhang","Yingfei Xiong","Lu Zhang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code representation","grammar-guided generation","adaptive training","SacrCoder","code repair"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/91/x"},{"id":"p01374","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Test Case Prioritization for DNNs via Neural Collapse Instability","tz":"基于神经坍缩不稳定性的 DNN 测试用例优先级排序","a":"With the widespread deployment of deep neural networks (DNNs) in safety-critical domains, reducing the cost of model validation under limited testing budgets has become increasingly important. Existing test case prioritization techniques often rely on single-checkpoint confidence signals derived from output probabilities. However, DNNs can be confidently wrong, and the confidence margin between the predicted and competing classes is frequently small, which weakens early fault discovery. To address this limitation, we propose a Neural-Collapse-Inspired Prioritization (NCIP) framework that replaces absolute confidence with cross-checkpoint consistency in the terminal training regime, where model geometry becomes highly structured. NCIP introduces two key components. First, it selects a coherent set of late training checkpoints by measuring the equiangularity of classifier weights, quantified as the standard deviation of pairwise cosine similarities among class weight vectors. Second, it prioritizes test inputs by their prediction variability across the selected checkpoints, surfacing boundary-adjacent and failure-prone samples that are unstable under checkpoint-induced decision boundary shifts. Extensive experiments across multiple datasets and architectures show that NCIP consistently improves early fault discovery over strong baselines, achieving 2.34%–13.57% RAUC gains and 4.61%–31.77% RAUC-500 gains under the same testing budget. NCIP further attains the best average performance across all dataset model pairs.","az":"随着深度神经网络（DNN）在安全攸关领域的广泛部署，在有限测试预算下降低模型验证成本变得日益重要。现有测试用例优先级排序技术通常依赖从输出概率导出的单检查点置信度信号。然而，DNN 可能自信地出错，且预测类与竞争类之间的置信度间隔往往很小，这削弱了早期故障发现能力。为解决这一局限，我们提出受神经坍缩启发的优先级排序框架（NCIP），在模型几何结构高度规整的训练末期阶段，用跨检查点一致性取代绝对置信度。NCIP 引入两个关键组件。第一，它通过度量分类器权重的等角性（量化为类权重向量两两余弦相似度的标准差）来选取一组连贯的训练后期检查点。第二，它按测试输入在所选检查点间的预测变异性进行优先级排序，从而浮现出邻近决策边界、易于触发失败的样本，这些样本在检查点引起的决策边界漂移下并不稳定。跨多个数据集与架构的大量实验表明，在相同测试预算下 NCIP 相较强基线持续改善早期故障发现，取得 2.34%–13.57% 的 RAUC 提升与 4.61%–31.77% 的 RAUC-500 提升，并在所有数据集—模型组合上取得最佳平均性能。","tl":"用训练末期跨检查点预测不稳定性替代置信度做测试排序","au":["Chunyu Liu","Mingyuan Li","Yang LI","Wenmin Li","Fei Gao","Tengfei Tu","Su-Juan Qin"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical"],"kw":["test case prioritization","neural collapse","DNN testing","checkpoint consistency","fault discovery"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/92/x"},{"id":"p01375","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Evaluating the Impact of Explainable AI on Trust in AI-Assisted Code Review","tz":"评估可解释 AI 对 AI 辅助代码评审中信任的影响","a":"Background: The use of large language models (LLMs) for automated code review has brought significant change to a time-consuming part of software engineering. Prior work has shown that LLM-based code tools can improve code quality and enable more robust software development processes. As the tools get more powerful, the explanations behind their decisions remain hard to understand. Developers struggle to assess the validity of LLM-generated code reviews, making it difficult to gauge how much trust they should place in them. While the application of automated code review with LLMs has been extensively researched, the inclusion of Explainable AI (XAI) for transparency in code reviews and its impact on trust are yet to be explored. Objective: We aim to address this research gap by collecting empirical evidence on the influence of XAI on the trust of software developers in AI-assisted code reviews. Method: We conducted a within-subjects user study with 34 participants from diverse programming backgrounds, comparing three experimental LLM-based automated code review systems with varying levels of XAI support: Condition A (detailed explanation and review feedback), Condition B (review feedback only), and Condition C (no explanations). Participants were shown a series of real-world code change requests along with the AI-generated code reviews. During the study, we measured trust perceptions for each system using a questionnaire, agreement with the AI recommendation, the reasoning for accepting or rejecting the code change, and the time taken to review the code change. Results: Our quantitative results show that the level of explanation significantly influences both the level of trust of software developers and their agreement with AI recommendations, but in different ways. Full explanations (Condition A) yield the highest perceived trust (M = 3.99/5) but not the highest agreement with AI recommendations, whereas moderate explanations (Condition B) achieve the highest AI agreement (89.22%). This could suggest that more explanations prompt developers to question AI recommendations more frequently. In contrast, providing no explanations (Condition C) results in the lowest levels of trust and agreement. We also find that the level of explanation did not significantly impact the time taken to accept or reject a code change. Across all conditions, the most commonly cited reasons for code change decisions were changes in code readability and the correctness of the implementation. Conclusion: Overall, these findings indicate that incorporating XAI into the code review process significantly changes the trust perceptions and agreement with AI recommendations for software developers. These results provide insights for the design and evaluation of trustworthy AI-based code review systems, and support researchers in the design of studies on the human factors of AI-assisted software development.","az":"背景：使用大语言模型（LLM）进行自动化代码评审，为软件工程中这一耗时环节带来了显著变化。既有工作表明，基于 LLM 的代码工具可以提升代码质量并支撑更稳健的软件开发流程。随着工具能力增强，其决策背后的解释仍然难以理解。开发者难以评估 LLM 生成的代码评审的有效性，因而难以判断应对其给予多少信任。尽管用 LLM 做自动化代码评审已被广泛研究，把可解释 AI（XAI）引入代码评审以提升透明度及其对信任的影响仍待探索。目标：我们旨在通过收集实证证据来填补这一研究空白，考察 XAI 对软件开发者在 AI 辅助代码评审中信任度的影响。方法：我们开展了一项被试内用户研究，招募了 34 名具有多样编程背景的参与者，比较三种具有不同 XAI 支持程度的实验性基于 LLM 的自动化代码评审系统：条件 A（详细解释与评审反馈）、条件 B（仅评审反馈）、条件 C（无解释）。参与者会看到一系列真实世界的代码变更请求以及 AI 生成的代码评审。研究过程中，我们用问卷测量对每个系统的信任感知、与 AI 建议的一致程度、接受或拒绝代码变更的理由，以及评审该代码变更所花的时间。结果：定量结果显示，解释水平显著影响软件开发者的信任度及其与 AI 建议的一致程度，但影响方式不同。完整解释（条件 A）带来最高的感知信任（M = 3.99/5），但并未带来最高的 AI 建议一致率；而适中解释（条件 B）取得最高的 AI 一致率（89.22%）。这可能说明更多解释会促使开发者更频繁地质疑 AI 建议。相反，不提供解释（条件 C）导致最低的信任与一致水平。我们还发现解释水平对接受或拒绝代码变更所花的时间没有显著影响。在所有条件下，代码变更决策最常被提及的理由是代码可读性的变化与实现的正确性。结论：总体而言，这些发现表明把 XAI 纳入代码评审过程会显著改变软件开发者的信任感知及其与 AI 建议的一致程度。这些结果为可信 AI 代码评审系统的设计与评估提供了洞见，并支持研究者设计关于 AI 辅助软件开发中人因问题的研究。","tl":"34 人实验显示解释越多信任越高但与 AI 建议一致率反而下降","au":["Zhenhan Gao","Marvin Muñoz Barón","Umm-e Habiba","Daniel Graziotin","Stefan Wagner"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","tg":["human-study","llm-based"],"kw":["explainable AI","code review","trust","within-subjects user study","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/93/x"},{"id":"p01376","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RESTOR: Automated Test Oracle Generation for RESTful APIs via Reinforcement Learning","tz":"RESTOR：基于强化学习的 RESTful API 自动化测试预言生成","a":"Automated testing for REST APIs has witnessed rapid advancements, yet existing techniques often rely heavily on formal specifications or massive execution logs, rendering them ineffective in agile industrial environments characterized by cold-start features and isolated traffic samples. In this paper, we present RESTOR, a framework that utilizes Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) to fine-tune a lightweight Large Language Model for generating executable test assertions from single request-response pairs. By employing a novel data augmentation pipeline that constructs semantic constraints and valid/invalid logic variations, RESTOR enables the model to internalize testing common sense and distinguish business logic from dynamic noise. Comprehensive evaluations on industrial datasets demonstrate that RESTOR significantly outperforms large-scale generalist models (e.g., DeepSeek-V3.1). Specifically, it achieves a superior F1-score of 85.42% in key field identification by maintaining a high Precision of 81.30%, effectively mitigating the over-generation issues observed in baselines. Moreover, expert reviews confirm its reliability, showing that RESTOR produces the highest volume of semantically Exact Match assertions while minimizing factual errors on noisy data. Finally, deployment in a production environment at a large-scale technology company validates its practical impact: the system raised the automated test case adoption rate from 74.1% to over 90% in core business lines, substantially reducing manual QA effort in high-frequency CI/CD workflows.","az":"面向 REST API 的自动化测试近年来发展迅速，但现有技术往往严重依赖形式化规约或海量执行日志，使其在以冷启动特性和孤立流量样本为特征的敏捷工业环境中失效。本文提出 RESTOR，一个利用组相对策略优化（GRPO）微调轻量级大语言模型、从单个请求-响应对生成可执行测试断言的框架。通过采用一种新颖的数据增强流水线来构造语义约束以及有效/无效的逻辑变体，RESTOR 使模型能够内化测试常识，并将业务逻辑与动态噪声区分开来。在工业数据集上的全面评测表明，RESTOR 显著优于大规模通用模型（例如 DeepSeek-V3.1）。具体而言，它在关键字段识别上取得了 85.42% 的更优 F1 分数，同时保持 81.30% 的高精确率，有效缓解了基线方法中观察到的过度生成问题。此外，专家评审确认了其可靠性：RESTOR 产生了数量最多的语义完全匹配（Exact Match）断言，同时在噪声数据上把事实性错误降到最低。最后，在一家大型科技公司的生产环境中部署验证了其实际影响：该系统将核心业务线的自动化测试用例采纳率从 74.1% 提升到 90% 以上，大幅减少了高频 CI/CD 工作流中的人工 QA 投入。","tl":"用 GRPO 微调小模型，从单个请求-响应对直接生成可执行断言。","au":["Xun Zhou","Zhen Dong","Mingyu Ren","Qiang Li","JunJie Li","Sifan Wang","Xiaolong Yu","Chaofeng Sha","Xin Peng"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["REST API testing","test oracle generation","GRPO","assertion generation","industrial deployment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/94/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/94/RESTOR-Automated-Test-Oracle-Generation-for-RESTful-APIs-via-Reinforcement-Learning"},{"id":"p01377","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"You are deceived in the pocket: Intrusive Advertisements in Mobile Applications: An Exploratory Study","tz":"口袋中的欺骗：移动应用中的侵入式广告探索性研究","a":"Mobile advertising has become the primary monetization module for the Android ecosystem. However, this growth is accompanied by increasingly complex intrusive advertisements that undermine user agency through sophisticated behavioral interference. Current detection research remains confined to the web context, failing to address the unique in-app characteristics of mobile intrusive ads. Existing ad analysis tools struggle to distinguish voluntary human actions from forced interactions due to the absence of intent-aware modeling. Furthermore, existing marketplace policies and legal frameworks lack unified terminology and enforceable rules, leading to inconsistent oversight. In this paper, we conduct an exploratory study to systematically investigate and model these behaviors. We propose a formal taxonomy grounded in state-transition logic and develop an automated tool to identify intrusive patterns. Our analysis of more than 6,000 apps confirms the prevalence of mobile intrusive ads. Additionally, we perform a comparative analysis of mainstream regulations, uncovering significant misalignments in policy standards across different jurisdictions. Our study establishes a critical theoretical and practical foundation for ecosystem governance, enabling more effective detection and evidence-based policy refinement.","az":"移动广告已成为 Android 生态系统的主要变现模块。然而，这一增长也伴随着日益复杂的侵入式广告，它们通过精巧的行为干扰手段削弱了用户的自主权。当前的检测研究仍局限于 Web 场景，无法应对移动应用内广告的独特特征。由于缺乏意图感知建模，现有的广告分析工具难以区分用户自愿的操作与被迫的交互。此外，现有的应用市场政策与法律框架缺乏统一术语和可执行规则，导致监管标准不一致。本文开展了一项探索性研究，系统地调查并建模这些行为。我们提出了一个基于状态转移逻辑的形式化分类体系，并开发了一款自动化工具来识别侵入式模式。我们对 6000 多个应用的分析证实了移动侵入式广告的普遍性。此外，我们对主流法规进行了比较分析，揭示了不同司法辖区之间政策标准的显著错位。我们的研究为生态治理奠定了关键的理论与实践基础，使更有效的检测和基于证据的政策完善成为可能。","tl":"首次用状态转移逻辑给应用内侵入式广告建模并大规模自动检测。","au":["Miaoying Cai","Dongsun Kim","Lingling Fan","Xiangyu Zhang","Sen Chen"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["intrusive advertisements","Android","taxonomy","state-transition logic","policy compliance"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/95/x"},{"id":"p01378","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Is \"Knowing It's Malicious'' Enough? Evaluating LLMs for Fine-Grained Malware Behavior Auditing","tz":"仅仅知道它是恶意的就够了吗？评测大语言模型的细粒度恶意软件行为审计能力","a":"Automated malware classifiers achieve strong detection performance, but auditing requires more than flagging a sample: analysts must explain malicious behaviors and justify them with concrete code evidence, a requirement that traditional signature-based methods and learning-based XAI often fail to satisfy in a human-interpretable manner. Large Language Models (LLMs) appear well-suited for this task due to their code reasoning and summarization ability, yet it is unclear whether their reasoning capabilities are up to the auditing. In particular, evaluating them faces three hurdles: (1) the lack of detailed, human-written behavior ground truth for reliable benchmarking; (2) the scale of real-world applications’ codebases typically exceed the context limits of current models, which cannot be fully processed at once; and (3) the absence of reliable mechanisms to verify whether LLM-generated behavioral claims are faithfully supported by concrete code evidence. Together, these obstacles make benchmarking LLM-based auditing non-trivial, leaving their true capabilities and failure modes opaque. To bridge this gap, we introduce MalEval, an evaluation framework for systematically measuring the reasoning fidelity of LLMs in malware auditing. We pair real-world application codebases with expert-written audit reports to obtain fine-grained, behavior-level ground truth. Large codebases are compressed into unified behavior-relevant program contexts via a context-driven intermediate representation that preserves essential call relations. Both expert reports and model outputs are then mapped, through constrained reasoning, into structured evidence chains linking code-level facts to high-level behaviors in a common, comparable space. Built on this foundation, MalEval decomposes auditing into 4 stage-wise auditing tasks, allowing each intermediate judgment to be independently verified under limited context windows. We leverage MalEval to evaluate seven widely used LLMs and uncover clear capability boundaries: models rely on surface cues over verifiable evidence, struggle to compose dispersed facts into coherent attack chains, and are highly sensitive to context formulation. These findings shift the focus from optimizing isolated outputs to designing LLM and agentic workflows that can reliably support malware auditing.","az":"自动化恶意软件分类器已经取得了很强的检测性能，但审计所需的远不止给样本打标签：分析人员必须解释恶意行为，并用具体的代码证据加以佐证，而传统的基于签名的方法和基于学习的可解释 AI（XAI）往往无法以人类可理解的方式满足这一要求。大语言模型（LLM）凭借其代码推理与摘要能力，看起来很适合这一任务，但其推理能力是否胜任审计仍不清楚。特别是，评测它们面临三重障碍：（1）缺乏详尽的、人工撰写的行为基准真值，难以进行可靠的基准测试；（2）真实应用的代码库规模通常超出当前模型的上下文限制，无法一次性完整处理；（3）缺乏可靠机制来验证 LLM 生成的行为论断是否真的被具体代码证据所支持。这些障碍共同使得对基于 LLM 的审计进行基准测试变得非常困难，其真实能力与失败模式也因此不透明。为弥合这一空白，我们提出 MalEval，一个系统性度量 LLM 在恶意软件审计中推理保真度的评测框架。我们将真实应用代码库与专家撰写的审计报告配对，从而获得细粒度的、行为级的基准真值。大型代码库通过一种保留关键调用关系的、上下文驱动的中间表示，被压缩为统一的行为相关程序上下文。随后，专家报告与模型输出都通过受约束的推理被映射为结构化证据链，在一个共同的、可比较的空间中把代码级事实与高层行为联系起来。在此基础上，MalEval 将审计分解为 4 个阶段性审计任务，使每个中间判断都能在有限上下文窗口下被独立验证。我们利用 MalEval 评测了七个广泛使用的 LLM，揭示出清晰的能力边界：模型依赖表面线索而非可验证证据，难以把分散的事实组合成连贯的攻击链，并且对上下文的组织方式高度敏感。这些发现将关注点从优化孤立输出，转向设计能够可靠支撑恶意软件审计的 LLM 与智能体工作流。","tl":"提出 MalEval，用证据链把恶意行为审计拆成四阶段可验证任务。","au":["Xinran Zheng","Xingzhi Qian","Yiling He","Shuo Yang","Lorenzo Cavallaro"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["malware auditing","LLM evaluation","evidence chain","reasoning fidelity","MalEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/96/x"},{"id":"p01379","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Answer is Cheap, Show Me the Evidence! Augmenting Automated Vulnerability Assessment with Evidence","tz":"答案很廉价，把证据亮出来！用证据增强自动化漏洞评估","a":"Software Vulnerability (SV) assessment is a vital phase in SV management, which characterizes discovered SVs to locate hot spots and prioritize their remediation. To reduce the overhead and latency of manual assessment, prior works have explored automatically predicting assessment results from SV reports (SVRs). However, existing approaches fail to process the information conveyed by the rich text content (e.g., screenshots and code snippets) embedded in SVRs and miss information about vulnerable projects. More importantly, they primarily focus on assessment accuracy while neglecting to provide explanations or evidence supporting their predictions. As a result, these approaches remain impractical in real-world settings, where imperfect accuracy necessitates manual validation. LLMs offer a promising opportunity to address this limitation by performing SV assessment while simultaneously providing supporting evidence. Nevertheless, our extensive evaluation reveals that mainstream LLMs perform poorly on SV assessment tasks, largely due to a lack of assessment-specific knowledge. To address the above challenges, we propose EAVA, a novel framework that effectively leverages LLMs to perform SV assessment and provide supporting evidence. EAVA employs specialized LLM agents to process rich text content in SVRs and incorporate information about vulnerable projects. EAVA builds a dedicated assessment LLM by injecting assessment-specific knowledge through finetuning. Specifically, we enable large-scale reasoning trajectory annotation using off-the-shelf LLMs and adopt a two-stage training paradigm, i.e., supervised instruction tuning to inject domain knowledge, followed by reinforcement learning to enhance the model’s intrinsic reasoning capability. Evaluations on a newly collected SVR dataset demonstrate that EAVA outperforms the best-performing baseline by 5.3%-35.2% across multiple evaluation metrics. Ablation studies validate the effectiveness of our design choices for both assessment-specific model training and SV information enrichment. Finally, a user study with security experts confirms that the evidence provided by EAVA is useful and practical for real-world SV assessment.","az":"软件漏洞（SV）评估是漏洞管理中的关键环节，它刻画已发现漏洞的特征，以定位热点并对修复进行优先级排序。为降低人工评估的开销与延迟，已有工作探索了从漏洞报告（SVR）自动预测评估结果。然而，现有方法无法处理 SVR 中嵌入的丰富文本内容（如截图和代码片段）所传递的信息，也遗漏了有关受影响项目的信息。更重要的是，它们主要关注评估准确率，却忽视了为预测提供解释或证据。因此，这些方法在真实场景中仍不实用，因为不完美的准确率必然需要人工验证。LLM 提供了一个有前景的机会：在进行漏洞评估的同时提供支撑证据。然而，我们的大量评测显示，主流 LLM 在漏洞评估任务上表现不佳，主要是因为缺乏评估领域的专门知识。为应对上述挑战，我们提出 EAVA，一个有效利用 LLM 执行漏洞评估并提供支撑证据的新框架。EAVA 采用专门的 LLM 智能体处理 SVR 中的富文本内容，并纳入受影响项目的信息。EAVA 通过微调注入评估专属知识，构建了一个专用的评估 LLM。具体而言，我们利用现成 LLM 实现大规模推理轨迹标注，并采用两阶段训练范式，即先用有监督指令微调注入领域知识，再用强化学习增强模型的内在推理能力。在新收集的 SVR 数据集上的评测表明，EAVA 在多项评价指标上比最佳基线高出 5.3%–35.2%。消融实验验证了我们在评估专用模型训练与漏洞信息增强两方面设计选择的有效性。最后，一项面向安全专家的用户研究确认，EAVA 提供的证据对真实世界的漏洞评估是有用且实用的。","tl":"让漏洞评估同时输出可核查证据，并用 SFT+RL 注入评估知识。","au":["Shengyi Pan","Zelong Zheng","Jiayuan Zhou","Xing Hu","Xin Xia","Shanping Li"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","agentic","human-study"],"kw":["vulnerability assessment","supporting evidence","LLM agents","reinforcement learning","security reports"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/97/x"},{"id":"p01380","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Bridging User Feedback and System Diagnosis: Reproducing Mobile Performance Issues from Reviews","tz":"连接用户反馈与系统诊断：从应用评论复现移动性能问题","a":"Mobile application performance is a vital factor for user experience. Yet, performance issues are notoriously difficult to detect in development environments, where they often manifest less conspicuously, making their diagnosis more challenging. In this setting, app reviews from users with diverse device configurations can provide timely and context-rich information about emerging performance issues. However, unlike structured bug reports, app reviews are written by end-users and tend to be more ambiguous, with individual reviews often providing only partial descriptions of the underlying issue. To bridge this gap, we present RevPerf, the first approach to automatically reproduce mobile application performance issues by leveraging and synthesizing information from app reviews. RevPerf retrieves complementary reviews via semantic retrieval and uses prompt engineering to integrate them, enriching the original review with performance issue details. An execution agent is then employed to generate and execute commands to reproduce the issue. After executing all necessary steps, the system incorporates multifaceted detection methods to identify performance issues by monitoring Android logs, GUI changes, and system resource utilization during the reproduction process. Experimental results demonstrate that our proposed framework achieves a 72.73% success rate in reproducing performance issues on the constructed dataset, outperforming the best baseline by 27.28%.","az":"移动应用性能是用户体验的关键因素。然而，性能问题在开发环境中往往难以察觉，其表现不够明显，使诊断更加困难。在这种情况下，来自具有多样设备配置的用户的应用评论，可以及时提供有上下文的、关于新出现性能问题的信息。但与结构化的缺陷报告不同，应用评论由终端用户撰写，往往更加含糊，单条评论通常只提供对底层问题的部分描述。为弥合这一鸿沟，我们提出 RevPerf，这是首个通过利用并综合应用评论中的信息来自动复现移动应用性能问题的方法。RevPerf 通过语义检索获取互补的评论，并使用提示工程将它们整合起来，用性能问题细节丰富原始评论。随后，一个执行智能体被用来生成并执行命令以复现该问题。在执行完所有必要步骤后，系统结合多方面的检测方法，通过在复现过程中监控 Android 日志、GUI 变化和系统资源利用率来识别性能问题。实验结果表明，我们提出的框架在构建的数据集上取得了 72.73% 的复现成功率，比最佳基线高出 27.28%。","tl":"首次把零散用户评论合成为可执行步骤复现性能缺陷。","au":["Zhengquan Li","Zhenhao Li","Sidong Feng","Cuiyun Gao","Tao Zhang","Zishuo Ding"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["performance issue reproduction","app reviews","execution agent","Android","semantic retrieval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/98/x"},{"id":"p01381","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Vbox: Efficient Black-Box Serializability Verification","tz":"Vbox：高效的黑盒可串行化验证","a":"Verifying the serializability of transaction histories is essential for assessing whether a database management system (DBMS) correctly enforces the claimed serializable isolation level. Black-box serializability verification provides a practical means for such validation without relying on internal system details. Existing approaches often suffer from limitations including incomplete anomaly detection, high verification overhead, excessive memory consumption, or dependence on specific concurrency control protocols. This paper presents Vbox, a black-box serializability verification method that incorporates support for predicate database operations, systematic use of transaction timing information, and a satisfiability (SAT)-based formulation with an efficient solver. Both theoretical analysis and experimental evaluation show that Vbox is correct and efficient, detects a broader range of data anomalies, and does not rely on any particular concurrency control protocol.","az":"验证事务历史的可串行化，对于评估数据库管理系统（DBMS）是否正确实施其宣称的可串行化隔离级别至关重要。黑盒可串行化验证提供了一种无需依赖系统内部细节的实用验证手段。现有方法常常存在诸多局限，包括异常检测不完整、验证开销高、内存消耗过大，或依赖特定的并发控制协议。本文提出 Vbox，一种黑盒可串行化验证方法，它支持谓词数据库操作，系统性地利用事务时间信息，并采用基于可满足性（SAT）的形式化建模与高效求解器。理论分析与实验评测均表明，Vbox 是正确且高效的，能够检测更广泛的数据异常，且不依赖任何特定的并发控制协议。","tl":"用事务时序信息加 SAT 建模，做更全面且高效的可串行化验证。","au":["Weihua Sun","Zhaonian Zou"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["serializability verification","black-box","DBMS","SAT solving","transaction anomalies"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/99/x"},{"id":"p01382","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Dependency Optimization for Artifact-Based Build Systems","tz":"面向基于制品的构建系统的自动化依赖优化","a":"As projects grow, the maintenance of intra- and inter-project dependencies declarations becomes increasingly complex. If dependency maintenance is lax, redundant dependencies may accrue, inflating incremental build and test latencies. The heterogeneity of language- and tool-specific dependency expressions and the complexity of the dependency graphs that they specify exacerbate the challenge of identifying and removing redundant dependencies. To address these challenges, this paper introduces DepReduce, a dependency optimization approach designed to be language-agnostic and compatible with all languages supported by the underlying build system. We formalized the dependency optimization objective as minimizing rebuild cost. To achieve this objective, DepReduce performs dependency lifting and dependency flattening operations on the dependency graph in a topological order, and we proved that DepReduce is both correct and optimal. To empirically evaluate the approach, we implemented BazelDepReduce, an automated dependency optimization tool for Bazel. Bazel is a modern build system with native support for multiple programming languages. We evaluated BazelDepReduce on 14 open-source projects written in five programming languages, with eleven of them achieving reductions in rebuild cost. In total, BazelDepReduce identified and removed 250 redundant dependencies, which we used to produce eleven Pull Requests (PRs). Nine PRs have been merged by the target projects, including Angular and Apache RocketMQ. These contributions affected up to 57.6% of subsequent commits, with a median of 26.3%. The two other PRs remain open, awaiting a response from project maintainers. We also adapted BazelDepReduce to support Buck and Cargo, further demonstrating the generalizability of our approach. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach in optimizing dependencies across projects with different programming languages.","az":"随着项目规模增长，项目内与项目间依赖声明的维护变得日益复杂。如果依赖维护不严格，冗余依赖会不断累积，抬高增量构建与测试的延迟。依赖表达方式在语言和工具层面的异构性，以及它们所刻画的依赖图的复杂性，进一步加剧了识别与移除冗余依赖的难度。为应对这些挑战，本文提出 DepReduce，一种与语言无关、兼容底层构建系统所支持的所有语言的依赖优化方法。我们将依赖优化目标形式化为最小化重构建成本。为实现该目标，DepReduce 按拓扑顺序对依赖图执行依赖提升（lifting）与依赖展平（flattening）操作，并且我们证明了 DepReduce 既正确又最优。为了对该方法进行实证评估，我们实现了 BazelDepReduce，一个面向 Bazel 的自动化依赖优化工具。Bazel 是一个原生支持多种编程语言的现代构建系统。我们在用五种编程语言编写的 14 个开源项目上评估了 BazelDepReduce，其中 11 个项目实现了重构建成本的下降。BazelDepReduce 总共识别并移除了 250 个冗余依赖，我们据此提交了 11 个 Pull Request（PR）。其中 9 个 PR 已被目标项目合并，包括 Angular 和 Apache RocketMQ。这些贡献影响了后续至多 57.6% 的提交，中位数为 26.3%。另外 2 个 PR 仍处于开放状态，等待项目维护者回应。我们还将 BazelDepReduce 适配到 Buck 和 Cargo，进一步展示了方法的普适性。这些结果表明，我们的方法在跨不同编程语言的项目中优化依赖方面是有效的。","tl":"把依赖精简形式化为最小化重构建成本，并证明算法最优。","au":["Hongxu Xu","Zhenyang Xu","Shane McIntosh","Chengnian Sun"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["build systems","dependency optimization","Bazel","redundant dependencies","incremental build"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/100/x","pu":"https://xuhongxu.com/issta26-depreduce.pdf"},{"id":"p01383","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Uncovering Business Logic Bugs via Semantics-Driven Unit Test Generation (Experience Paper)","tz":"通过语义驱动的单元测试生成揭示业务逻辑缺陷（经验论文）","a":"Business logic bugs violate intended business semantics and are particularly prevalent in enterprise software. Yet most existing unit test generation techniques are code-centric, making such bugs difficult to expose. We present SeGa, a semantics-driven unit test generation technique for uncovering business logic bugs. SeGa constructs a semantic knowledge base from product requirement documents, represented as a set of functionality entries that group related requirements under a common business intent. Given a focal method, SeGa retrieves the relevant functionality entries and derives fine-grained business scenarios with explicit preconditions, triggering actions, expected outcomes, and semantic constraints to guide LLM-based test generation. We evaluate SeGa on four industrial Go projects containing 60 real-world business logic bugs. SeGa detects 22~25 more bugs than four state-of-the-art LLM-based techniques and improves precision by 26.9%~34.3%. Deployment across 6 production repositories further uncovers 16 previously unknown business logic bugs that were confirmed and fixed by developers, demonstrating SeGa’s practical value. From our industrial study, we summarize a series of lessons and suggestions for practical use and future research.","az":"业务逻辑缺陷违背了预期的业务语义，在企业软件中尤为普遍。然而，现有大多数单元测试生成技术都是以代码为中心的，导致此类缺陷难以暴露。我们提出 SeGa，一种以语义驱动的单元测试生成技术，用于揭示业务逻辑缺陷。SeGa 从产品需求文档中构建语义知识库，表示为一组功能条目，将相关需求归并到共同的业务意图之下。给定一个待测方法，SeGa 检索相关的功能条目，并推导出具有明确前置条件、触发动作、预期结果和语义约束的细粒度业务场景，以指导基于 LLM 的测试生成。我们在四个包含 60 个真实业务逻辑缺陷的工业级 Go 项目上评估了 SeGa。相比四种最先进的基于 LLM 的技术，SeGa 多检测出 22~25 个缺陷，并将精确率提升了 26.9%~34.3%。在 6 个生产仓库上的部署进一步发现了 16 个此前未知的业务逻辑缺陷，均已被开发者确认并修复，展示了 SeGa 的实用价值。基于这项工业研究，我们总结了一系列面向实践应用与未来研究的经验与建议。","tl":"用需求文档构建的业务语义知识库来指导单测生成。","au":["Chen Yang","Junjie Chen"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["business logic bugs","unit test generation","requirement documents","LLM","industrial Go projects"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/101/x"},{"id":"p01384","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Just Old Wine in a New Bottle: Improving Vulnerability Repair Robustness to Combat Homologous but Heterogeneous Vulnerabilities","tz":"换汤不换药：提升漏洞修复对同源异构漏洞的鲁棒性","a":"Collaborative development practices, such as forking and branching, enable parallel development and rapid iteration but significantly complicate vulnerability management. A major challenge is the propagation of homologous but heterogeneous vulnerabilities, where the same vulnerability appears within evolved code contexts that differ structurally and contextually across divergent branches or forks. Existing Automated Vulnerability Repair (AVR) approaches often fail in these scenarios due to their limited ability to generalize across structural and contextual variations. To address this problem, we propose EvoRepair, a robust AVR framework tailored for code evolution contexts. Our approach leverages a Retrieval-Augmented Generation based Evolution Specialist to synthesize code evolution variants, enriching the training data with diverse code contexts. We then employ Chain-of-Thought reasoning and curriculum learning to train a Repair Specialist, enabling it to capture invariant repair logic during structural and contextual changes. We evaluate EvoRepair on two datasets representing cross-branch and cross-fork scenarios. Evaluation results demonstrate that EvoRepair successfully repaired 35.33% of the vulnerabilities on average in evolution scenarios, outperforming the state-of-the-art baseline Vul-R2 by 42.12%. Furthermore, EvoRepair also demonstrates superior generalizability in non-evolution scenarios, achieving state-of-the-art performance on the PrimeVul dataset by fixing 25.75% of the vulnerabilities, surpassing the best baseline by 21.75%.","az":"分叉（fork）和分支（branch）等协作开发实践支持并行开发与快速迭代，却也显著增加了漏洞管理的复杂度。一个主要挑战是同源但异构漏洞的传播：同一个漏洞出现在演化后的代码上下文中，而这些上下文在不同分支或分叉之间在结构和语境上存在差异。现有的自动化漏洞修复（AVR）方法在这些场景中常常失效，因为它们跨结构与语境变化的泛化能力有限。为解决该问题，我们提出 EvoRepair，一个面向代码演化场景的鲁棒 AVR 框架。我们的方法利用基于检索增强生成（RAG）的演化专家模块来合成代码演化变体，用多样化的代码上下文丰富训练数据。随后，我们采用思维链推理与课程学习来训练修复专家模块，使其能够在结构与语境变化中捕捉不变的修复逻辑。我们在代表跨分支与跨分叉场景的两个数据集上评估 EvoRepair。评测结果表明，EvoRepair 在演化场景中平均成功修复了 35.33% 的漏洞，比最先进的基线 Vul-R2 高出 42.12%。此外，EvoRepair 在非演化场景中也展现出更强的泛化性，在 PrimeVul 数据集上修复了 25.75% 的漏洞，达到最先进水平，比最佳基线高出 21.75%。","tl":"合成代码演化变体训练修复模型，捕捉不变的修复逻辑。","au":["Xin Peng","Bo Lin","Yihao Qin","Jing Wang","Xin Zhao","Xiaoling Li","Jun Ma","Xiaoguang Mao","Shangwen Wang"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","security"],"kw":["automated vulnerability repair","homologous vulnerabilities","code evolution","curriculum learning","retrieval-augmented generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/102/x"},{"id":"p01385","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SpectraDL: A Historical Issue-Driven, Test Specification-Assisted Transfer Testing Approach for Deep Learning Frameworks via LLMs","tz":"SpectraDL：由历史 Issue 驱动、测试规约辅助的深度学习框架 LLM 迁移测试方法","a":"Deep learning (DL) frameworks provide diverse fundamental algorithmic units as operators, which are critical infrastructure for constructing various intelligent software. Due to the fact that open source development paradigm is widely adopted by mainstream frameworks, bugs may repeatedly occur across operators and even frameworks. Although some efforts have been reported that large language models (LLMs) are leveraged to exploit historical issues to generate test cases for cross-framework testing, existing approaches suffer from the following limitations: 1) the generated test cases have low fault detection capability since they mainly rely on inputs or contexts from historical issues without considering the underlying root causes; 2) an effective mechanism is missing to determine the appropriate scope in a targeted framework for applying generated test cases. To overcome these limitations, we propose SpectraDL, a historical issue-driven, test specification-assisted transfer testing approach for DL frameworks. SpectraDL first extracts rigorous test specifications for each operator from official documentation, and then extracts and transforms historical issues and associated pull requests into structured fault representations (i.e., bug patterns). A dual retrieval mechanism based on semantic intent and structural input-space features is designed to transfer these bug patterns for testing related operators across frameworks. We evaluated SpectraDL with four mainstream DL frameworks, and experimental results have shown that SpectraDL successfully detected 125 previously unknown bugs, with 107 confirmed by developers. The results confirm that SpectraDL delivers a promising transfer testing approach for DL frameworks.","az":"深度学习（DL）框架以算子的形式提供多样的基础算法单元，是构建各类智能软件的关键基础设施。由于主流框架广泛采用开源开发范式，缺陷可能在不同算子之间乃至不同框架之间反复出现。尽管已有一些工作报告利用大语言模型（LLM）挖掘历史 Issue 来生成跨框架测试的测试用例，但现有方法存在以下局限：1）生成的测试用例故障检测能力低，因为它们主要依赖历史 Issue 中的输入或上下文，而没有考虑其底层根因；2）缺乏有效机制来确定在目标框架中应用所生成测试用例的合适范围。为克服这些局限，我们提出 SpectraDL，一种由历史 Issue 驱动、测试规约辅助的深度学习框架迁移测试方法。SpectraDL 首先从官方文档中为每个算子抽取严格的测试规约，然后将历史 Issue 及其关联的 Pull Request 抽取并转换为结构化的故障表示（即缺陷模式）。我们设计了一种基于语义意图与结构输入空间特征的双重检索机制，将这些缺陷模式迁移到跨框架的相关算子测试中。我们在四个主流 DL 框架上评估了 SpectraDL，实验结果表明 SpectraDL 成功检测出 125 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 107 个已被开发者确认。结果证实，SpectraDL 为 DL 框架提供了一种有前景的迁移测试方法。","tl":"把历史 Issue 抽成缺陷模式并按规约双重检索迁移到同类算子。","au":["Shifan Liu","Chang-ai Sun","Fulei Wu","Wing-Kwong Chan"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["deep learning frameworks","transfer testing","historical issues","test specification","operator bugs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/103/x"},{"id":"p01386","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"BCaLLM: Call Graph-Guided Python Breaking Change Detection with Large Language Models","tz":"BCaLLM：调用图引导、结合大语言模型的 Python 破坏性变更检测","a":"Software libraries frequently evolve, introducing breaking changes that disrupt client applications. Existing detection approaches primarily target static programming languages or focus on syntactic changes, leaving behavioral breaking changes in dynamic languages such as Python underexplored. This task is particularly challenging due to two critical factors often overlooked in existing Python-centric research: side effects and call relationships, which implicitly alter API behaviors and propagate change impact. To address these challenges, we propose a generalized taxonomy of function API breaking changes. Grounded in Hyrum’s Law, our taxonomy is defined from the client’s perspective of observable behaviors and unifies both syntactic and behavioral categories in a multi‑label formulation. Furthermore, we present BCaLLM, a novel framework to detect fine-grained breaking changes in Python packages by leveraging call graphs and large language models (LLMs). BCaLLM constructs a fused call graph to scope change impact, prunes compatible APIs and code context via memory‑based heuristics, and employs an LLM to detect specific breaking changes. We construct PyBCEval, a manually annotated benchmark of 588 APIs from 27 version pairs of 19 widely used Python packages. Experiments with diverse LLMs show that BCaLLM outperforms text-based baselines by 3.71%-10.16% and LLM-based baselines by 1.60%-4.83% in F1-score.","az":"软件库频繁演化，引入破坏性变更从而影响客户端应用。现有检测方法主要针对静态类型语言，或只关注语法层面的变更，使得 Python 等动态语言中的行为性破坏变更研究不足。这项任务尤为困难，原因在于现有以 Python 为中心的研究常常忽视两个关键因素：副作用与调用关系，它们会隐式地改变 API 行为并传播变更影响。为应对这些挑战，我们提出了一个通用的函数 API 破坏性变更分类体系。该分类体系以海勒姆定律（Hyrum's Law）为基础，从客户端可观察行为的视角定义，并以多标签形式统一了语法与行为两类类别。此外，我们提出 BCaLLM，一个利用调用图和大语言模型（LLM）检测 Python 包中细粒度破坏性变更的新框架。BCaLLM 构建融合调用图以界定变更影响范围，通过基于记忆的启发式规则剪除兼容的 API 与代码上下文，并使用 LLM 检测具体的破坏性变更。我们构建了 PyBCEval，一个人工标注的基准，包含来自 19 个广泛使用的 Python 包的 27 个版本对中的 588 个 API。在多种 LLM 上的实验表明，BCaLLM 在 F1 分数上比基于文本的基线高 3.71%–10.16%，比基于 LLM 的基线高 1.60%–4.83%。","tl":"用融合调用图界定影响范围，检测 Python 行为性破坏变更。","au":["Wei Cheng","Chen Shen","Huan Zhang","Yuhan Wu","Jingyue Yang","Wei Hu"],"top":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["breaking changes","Python packages","call graph","Hyrum's Law","PyBCEval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/104/x"},{"id":"p01387","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Compiling Large Multi-Modal Requirement Documents into Runnable Software Systems: From an Agentic Test-Driven Perspective","tz":"把大型多模态需求文档编译成可运行的软件系统：一种智能体测试驱动视角","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have significantly improved programming efficiency by parsing natural language into code snippets. However, their performance degrades significantly as requirements scale; when faced with multi-modal documents containing hundreds of scenarios, LLMs often produce incorrect implemen- tations or omit crucial constraints. Observing LLMs’ ever-evolving capability and their persistent stochastic hallucination, we raise a question, i.e., whether it is possible to make LLM-based agentic programming go beyond code generation to requirement compilation, i.e., programmers can have a runnable system by only accomplishing (non-trivial) requirement documents? In this work, we make a first step by proposing ARC (Agentic Requirement Compilation) technique to parse a multi-modal requirement document, describing hundreds of scenarios in a DSL format, to a runnable web system. In addition to the source code, ARC also generates software engineering artifacts including (1) a modular design that spans the user interface, API interface, and database, (2) enriched test cases for each interface (including unit tests, modular tests, and integration tests), and (3) detailed traceability across all artifacts for software maintenance. Our approach employs a bidirectional test-driven agentic loop: (1) a top-down architecture phase that decomposes requirements into UI, API, and database interfaces, each of which is equipped with verifiable test suites, and (2) a bottom-up implementation phase where agents generate code that must satisfy the generated tests. Throughout this process, ARC maintains strict traceability across requirements, design, and code to facilitate intelligent asset reuse and follow-up maintenance. We evaluate ARC by generating 6 runnable web systems, from the multi-modal documents spanning over 50-200 multi-modal requirement scenarios. Compared to adopting the state-of-the-art LLM-based baselines, the generated web system can pass on average 50.6% more GUI tests. In addition, our user study consisting of 21 participants shows that even novice users can successfully write different DSL-based documents consisting of from 50 to 174 scenarios, within on average 5.6 hours, to generate a runnable system such as a real-world ticket-booking system of around 10K lines of code with maintainable architecture.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）通过将自然语言解析为代码片段，显著提升了编程效率。然而，随着需求规模扩大，它们的表现急剧下降；当面对包含数百个场景的多模态文档时，LLM 常常产生错误实现或遗漏关键约束。观察到 LLM 能力不断演进却又持续存在随机性幻觉，我们提出一个问题：能否让基于 LLM 的智能体编程超越代码生成，走向需求编译，即程序员只需完成（并不平凡的）需求文档就能获得一个可运行的系统？在本工作中，我们迈出第一步，提出 ARC（Agentic Requirement Compilation，智能体需求编译）技术，将以 DSL 格式描述数百个场景的多模态需求文档解析为可运行的 Web 系统。除源代码之外，ARC 还生成软件工程制品，包括：（1）跨越用户界面、API 接口与数据库的模块化设计；（2）为每个接口丰富的测试用例（包括单元测试、模块测试与集成测试）；（3）覆盖所有制品的详细可追溯性以支持软件维护。我们的方法采用双向测试驱动的智能体循环：（1）自顶向下的架构阶段，将需求分解为 UI、API 与数据库接口，每个接口都配备可验证的测试套件；（2）自底向上的实现阶段，智能体生成必须满足所生成测试的代码。在整个过程中，ARC 保持需求、设计与代码之间的严格可追溯性，以促进智能资产复用与后续维护。我们通过从涵盖 50–200 个多模态需求场景的文档生成 6 个可运行 Web 系统来评估 ARC。与采用最先进的基于 LLM 的基线相比，生成的 Web 系统平均多通过 50.6% 的 GUI 测试。此外，我们进行的包含 21 名参与者的用户研究表明，即使是新手用户也能在平均 5.6 小时内成功编写包含 50 到 174 个场景的不同 DSL 文档，从而生成如真实世界订票系统这样约 10K 行代码、具备可维护架构的可运行系统。","tl":"提出需求编译范式：双向测试驱动智能体循环产出可运行系统。","au":["Weiyu Kong","Yun Lin","Xiwen Teoh","Duc-Minh Nguyen","Ruofei Ren","Jiaxin Chang","Haoxu Hu","Haoyu Chen"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"requirements-architecture-and-design","tg":["agentic","llm-based","human-study"],"kw":["requirement compilation","agentic test-driven development","multi-modal requirements","traceability","web system generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/105/x"},{"id":"p01388","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"COEUR : COhesion and Exhaustiveness of User stories Representations","tz":"COEUR：用户故事表示的内聚性与穷尽性","a":"User Stories are key artifacts in Requirement and Software Engineering. Despite their wide adoption, their writing in industrial contexts tends to diverge from the principles initially stated in Agile methodologies. In this context, sets of metrics such as INVEST or QUS emerged to qualify these items. In this paper, we argue that the said sets of metrics are only partially efficient at capturing the quality of user stories contextualized in a project, and that their actual adoption in business contexts is limited due to multiple aspects: their unfitness to specific contexts, the difficulty of implementation requiring human intervention, the absence of reproducibility or their misalignment with actual quality of user stories. Such limitations, prevent practitioners from efficiently applying them for downstream tasks such as LLM-based user story generation. To address these challenges, we introduce COEUR , a framework comprising two metrics: Cohesion and Exhaustiveness . These metrics are designed to mirror core Product Owner responsibilities. Specifically, Cohesion evaluates the structural organization and logical grouping of the backlog, while Exhaustiveness monitors the semantic alignment between the elicited needs and the proposed technical solutions. Aditionnaly, they are quantitative, reproducible, and automatically computable. To evaluate COEUR , we conduct four empirical experiments organized into two validation tracks. The first track utilizes two noising-based experiments to assess our metrics sensitivity to requirement degradation. The second track evaluates their performance in generative contexts through two standard learning paradigms for LLM: In-Context Learning (ICL) and Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT), both applied to our user story generation task. Subsequently, COEUR provides a turnkey measurement of Product Backlog’s quality for both project monitoring by human experts and LLM benchmarking applied to automatic user stories generation.","az":"用户故事是需求工程与软件工程中的关键制品。尽管被广泛采用，它们在工业环境中的书写方式往往偏离敏捷方法最初提出的原则。在此背景下，INVEST 或 QUS 等指标集应运而生，用以评判这些条目。本文认为，上述指标集只能部分有效地刻画项目语境下用户故事的质量，且由于多方面原因，它们在业务环境中的实际采用相当有限：不适配特定语境、实施困难且需要人工介入、缺乏可复现性，或与用户故事的实际质量不一致。这些局限阻碍了从业者高效地将它们用于下游任务，例如基于 LLM 的用户故事生成。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 COEUR，一个包含两项度量的框架：内聚性（Cohesion）与穷尽性（Exhaustiveness）。这些度量旨在映射产品负责人的核心职责。具体而言，内聚性评估待办列表的结构组织与逻辑分组，而穷尽性监测所抽取的需求与所提出技术方案之间的语义一致性。此外，它们是定量的、可复现的、可自动计算的。为评估 COEUR，我们开展了四项实证实验，分为两条验证路线。第一条路线利用两个基于加噪的实验，评估我们的度量对需求退化的敏感性。第二条路线通过两种标准的 LLM 学习范式——上下文学习（ICL）与有监督微调（SFT）——在我们的用户故事生成任务上评估其表现。最终，COEUR 为产品待办列表的质量提供了一种开箱即用的测量手段，既可用于人类专家的项目监控，也可用于自动用户故事生成的 LLM 基准测试。","tl":"提出可自动计算的内聚性与穷尽性两项用户故事质量度量。","au":["Marius Ortega","Hassan Imhah","Nédra Mellouli","Christophe Rodrigues","Nicolas Travers"],"top":"requirements-architecture-and-design","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["user stories","requirements quality metrics","cohesion","exhaustiveness","product backlog"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/106/x","pu":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/106/COEUR-COhesion-and-Exhaustiveness-of-User-stories-Representations"},{"id":"p01389","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Ghosts in the Memory: Detecting Unintended Sensitive Data in Android Apps","tz":"内存中的幽灵：检测 Android 应用中非预期的敏感数据","a":"Android apps often retain sensitive information such as co-users’ data, authentication tokens, and encryption keys in memory, leaving them vulnerable to unauthorized access. Existing dynamic analysis tools struggle to detect such memory-resident leaks because of three fundamental challenges: (i) runtime application self-protection (RASP) and other anti-analysis mechanisms actively detect and block conventional instrumentation; (ii) the semantic gap between high-level data types and their raw memory representations obscures sensitive content; and (iii) the transient nature of memory-resident data causes snapshot-based methods to miss critical exposures. We present ANDROID-MRI, an OS-level analysis tool that embeds tracing directly into the Android kernel to detect unintended sensitive data leakage through memory while remaining invisible to application-layer defenses. ANDROID-MRI provides instruction-granular monitoring to track the propagation of sensitive data in memory, surfacing the full context of unintended persistence. In an evaluation of 50 popular apps (≥1M installs), ANDROID-MRI bypassed 97.6% of RASP protections (vs. 52.4% for Frida) and revealed 17 previously unknown memory disclosures. These included leaks of profile PINs, subscription-only content, and cryptographic keys. 12 vendors confirmed the issues; 4 have patched them, and 3 (Netflix, Smule, and Delivery Express) acknowledged them via bug bounty programs.","az":"Android 应用常常在内存中保留诸如共同使用者数据、认证令牌和加密密钥等敏感信息，使其易遭未授权访问。现有的动态分析工具难以检测此类驻留内存的泄露，原因有三个根本性挑战：(i) 运行时应用自我保护（RASP）及其他反分析机制会主动检测并阻断常规插桩；(ii) 高层数据类型与其原始内存表示之间的语义鸿沟掩盖了敏感内容；(iii) 驻留内存数据的瞬态特性导致基于快照的方法会遗漏关键暴露。我们提出 ANDROID-MRI，一种操作系统级分析工具，它将追踪直接嵌入 Android 内核，以检测通过内存发生的非预期敏感数据泄露，同时对应用层防御保持不可见。ANDROID-MRI 提供指令粒度的监控，以追踪敏感数据在内存中的传播，呈现非预期持久化的完整上下文。在对 50 个流行应用（安装量 ≥100 万）的评估中，ANDROID-MRI 绕过了 97.6% 的 RASP 防护（Frida 为 52.4%），并揭示了 17 个此前未知的内存泄露。其中包括个人资料 PIN、仅限订阅内容以及加密密钥的泄露。12 家厂商确认了这些问题；4 家已修复，3 家（Netflix、Smule 和 Delivery Express）通过漏洞赏金计划予以确认。","tl":"把追踪下沉到 Android 内核，绕过 RASP 做指令级内存泄露检测。","au":["Seonghyeon Song","Taeyoung Kim","Woojoo Kim","Seojin Park","Sungjae Hwang","Hyoungshick Kim"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["Android memory leakage","sensitive data","RASP bypass","kernel-level tracing","dynamic analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/107/x"},{"id":"p01390","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PAGENT: Program Analysis Guided LLM Agent for Proof-of-Concept Generation","tz":"PAGENT：程序分析引导的 LLM 智能体用于概念验证生成","a":"Software developers frequently receive vulnerability reports that require them to reproduce the vulnerability in a reliable manner by generating a proof-of-concept (PoC) input that triggers it. Given the source code for a software project and a specific code location for a potential vulnerability, automatically generating a PoC for the given vulnerability has been a challenging research problem. Symbolic execution and fuzzing techniques require expert guidance and manual steps and face scalability challenges for PoC generation. Although recent advances in LLMs have increased the level of automation and scalability, the success rate of PoC generation with LLMs remains quite low. In this paper, we present a novel approach called Program Analysis Guided proof of concept generation agENT (PAGENT) that is scalable and significantly improves the success rate of automated PoC generation compared to prior results. PAGENT integrates lightweight and rule-based static analysis phases for providing static analysis guidance and sanitizer-based profiling and coverage information for providing dynamic analysis guidance with a PoC generation agent. Our experiments demonstrate that the resulting hybrid approach significantly outperforms the prior top-performing agentic approach by 132% for the PoC generation task.","az":"软件开发者常常收到漏洞报告，要求他们以可靠的方式复现漏洞，即生成能够触发该漏洞的概念验证（PoC）输入。给定某个软件项目的源代码以及潜在漏洞的具体代码位置，自动为该漏洞生成 PoC 一直是一个具有挑战性的研究问题。符号执行与模糊测试技术需要专家指导和人工步骤，且在 PoC 生成上面临可扩展性挑战。尽管近期 LLM 的进展提升了自动化程度与可扩展性，基于 LLM 的 PoC 生成成功率仍然相当低。本文提出一种名为 PAGENT（Program Analysis Guided proof of concept generation agENT）的新方法，它具备可扩展性，并相比先前结果显著提高了自动 PoC 生成的成功率。PAGENT 将轻量级、基于规则的静态分析阶段（提供静态分析引导）与基于消毒器（sanitizer）的剖析和覆盖率信息（提供动态分析引导）集成到一个 PoC 生成智能体中。我们的实验表明，所得到的混合方法在 PoC 生成任务上比先前表现最好的智能体方法高出 132%。","tl":"用静态规则与 sanitizer 覆盖信息双重引导 PoC 生成智能体。","au":["Achintya Desai","Md Shafiuzzaman","Wenbo Guo","Tevfik Bultan"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["agentic","llm-based","security"],"kw":["proof-of-concept generation","program analysis","LLM agent","sanitizer profiling","vulnerability reproduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/108/x"},{"id":"p01391","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Steering Tree-of-Thought Reasoning via Deductive Verification","tz":"通过演绎验证引导思维树推理","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated great potential in code reasoning tasks, but their reasoning processes lack reliable verification mechanisms, making it difficult to ensure logical correctness. The Tree of Thoughts (ToT) framework improves reasoning by exploring multiple paths and employing backtracking, yet its path selection relies entirely on LLM-based self-evaluation—a heuristic and error-prone mechanism—leading to frequent erroneous pruning and unproductive exploration. We identify a key insight: LLMs’ encoding capability is stronger than their reasoning capability—translating code semantics into formal constraints is a pattern-matching task that LLMs can perform reliably, while verification should be delegated to SMT solvers. Based on this insight, we propose Deductive Steering, a mechanism that integrates SMT solver verification into Tree of Thoughts exploration. It consists of four core components: (1) Candidate Generator produces candidate reasoning steps, each comprising a natural language thought t and its SMT constraint encoding ; (2) Deductive Evaluator verifies whether a candidate constraint is a logical consequence of the accumulated constraint by checking the unsatisfiability of ; (3) Counterexample Refinement uses counterexample to guide the LLM in correcting its reasoning when verification fails; (4) Exploration and Backtracking Strategy manages path exploration and backtracks to alternative candidates when verification fails. Experiments on five benchmarks covering fault localization, program synthesis, and loop invariant generation show that Deductive Steering improves accuracy by 11.4–17.2 percentage points while reducing token consumption by 27–45%. The method generalizes across different LLMs and extends to mathematical reasoning, demonstrating broad applicability to domains where reasoning can be encoded as formal constraints.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在代码推理任务中展现出巨大潜力，但其推理过程缺乏可靠的验证机制，难以保证逻辑正确性。思维树（Tree of Thoughts, ToT）框架通过探索多条路径并采用回溯来改进推理，但其路径选择完全依赖基于 LLM 的自我评估——一种启发式且易出错的机制——导致频繁的错误剪枝和无效探索。我们发现一个关键洞见：LLM 的编码能力强于其推理能力——把代码语义翻译为形式化约束是一项 LLM 能够可靠完成的模式匹配任务，而验证则应交给 SMT 求解器。基于这一洞见，我们提出演绎引导（Deductive Steering），一种将 SMT 求解器验证集成进思维树探索的机制。它由四个核心组件构成：(1) 候选生成器产生候选推理步骤，每一步包含一个自然语言思维 t 及其 SMT 约束编码 φ；(2) 演绎评估器通过检查 Φ ∧ ¬φ 的不可满足性，验证候选约束 φ 是否为累积约束 Φ 的逻辑推论；(3) 反例精化在验证失败时利用反例引导 LLM 修正其推理；(4) 探索与回溯策略管理路径探索，并在验证失败时回溯到备选候选。在涵盖缺陷定位、程序合成与循环不变量生成的五个基准上的实验表明，演绎引导将准确率提升了 11.4–17.2 个百分点，同时将 token 消耗降低 27–45%。该方法可泛化到不同的 LLM，并可扩展到数学推理，展示了其在推理可编码为形式化约束的领域中的广泛适用性。","tl":"把 ToT 的自评换成 SMT 演绎验证并用反例回溯纠错。","au":["Haoliang Cheng","Enyi Tang","Shuoxiao Zhang","Jiahe Mao","Yanling Fu","Zhiyuan Ma","Keyu Cui","Yuchuan Liu","Yu Tian","Xinyu Gao","Haibin Wang"],"top":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","alt":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Tree of Thoughts","SMT solver","deductive verification","code reasoning","counterexample refinement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/109/x"},{"id":"p01392","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"HELO-APR: Enhancing Low-Resource Program Repair through Cross-Lingual Knowledge Transfer","tz":"HELO-APR：通过跨语言知识迁移增强低资源程序修复","a":"Large Language Models (LLMs) perform well on automatic program repair (APR) for high-resource programming languages (HRPLs), but their effectiveness drops sharply in low-resource programming languages (LRPLs), due to a lack of sufficient verified buggy-fixed pairs for APR training. To address this challenge, we propose HELO-APR (High-resource Enabled LOw-resource APR), a two-stage APR framework that enables cross-lingual transfer of repair knowledge from HRPLs to LRPLs. HELO-APR (1) constructs high-quality LRPL training data by synthesizing LRPL buggy-fixed pairs from HRPL counterparts, preserving defect type consistency while ensuring the synthesized code is idiomatic, and then (2) adopts a curriculum learning strategy that progressively performs HRPL repair learning, cross-lingual repair alignment, and LRPL repair adaptation, improving repair effectiveness in LRPLs. Using C++ as the source HRPL and Ruby and Rust as the target LRPLs, experiments on xCodeEval show that HELO-APR achieves the best macro-average Pass@k results and outperforms strong baselines in most settings, increasing Pass@1 from 31.17% to 48.65% on DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B and from 1.67% to 11.97% on CodeLlama-7B, while improving syntactic validity by raising the macro-average target compilation rate on CodeLlama from 49.77% to 91.98%. On Defects4Ruby, HELO-APR increases BLEU-4 from 61.20 to 66.79 and ROUGE-1 from 76.76 to 83.59 on CodeLlama-7B, indicating higher similarity to developer patches in real-world settings. Finally, we conduct ablation studies to assess the necessity of each core component. These results suggest that verified cross-lingual supervision provides a reusable approach for improving LLM-based repair in low-resource languages.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）在高资源编程语言（HRPL）的自动程序修复（APR）上表现良好，但在低资源编程语言（LRPL）上效果急剧下降，原因是缺乏足够的、经过验证的缺陷-修复配对用于 APR 训练。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 HELO-APR（High-resource Enabled LOw-resource APR），一个两阶段 APR 框架，实现修复知识从 HRPL 到 LRPL 的跨语言迁移。HELO-APR：(1) 通过从 HRPL 对应样本合成 LRPL 缺陷-修复配对来构建高质量的 LRPL 训练数据，在保持缺陷类型一致性的同时确保合成代码符合语言习惯；(2) 采用课程学习策略，逐步进行 HRPL 修复学习、跨语言修复对齐和 LRPL 修复适配，从而提升在 LRPL 上的修复效果。以 C++ 作为源 HRPL、Ruby 和 Rust 作为目标 LRPL，在 xCodeEval 上的实验表明，HELO-APR 取得了最佳的宏平均 Pass@k 结果，并在大多数设置下超越了强基线：在 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上将 Pass@1 从 31.17% 提升到 48.65%，在 CodeLlama-7B 上从 1.67% 提升到 11.97%；同时提升了语法有效性，将 CodeLlama 上的宏平均目标编译通过率从 49.77% 提升到 91.98%。在 Defects4Ruby 上，HELO-APR 将 CodeLlama-7B 的 BLEU-4 从 61.20 提升到 66.79，ROUGE-1 从 76.76 提升到 83.59，表明与开发者补丁在真实场景下有更高的相似度。最后，我们进行了消融实验以评估各核心组件的必要性。这些结果表明，经过验证的跨语言监督为改进低资源语言中基于 LLM 的修复提供了一种可复用的方法。","tl":"从高资源语言合成低资源缺陷对，用课程学习做跨语言修复迁移。","au":["Zhipeng Wang","Boyang Yang","Yidong Wan","Liuye Guo","You Lv","Tao Zheng","Zhuowei Wang","Tieke He"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","low-resource-or-non-english"],"kw":["low-resource program repair","cross-lingual transfer","curriculum learning","xCodeEval","data synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/110/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.17016"},{"id":"p01393","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Do Large Language Models Understand Code like Humans?","tz":"大语言模型像人一样理解代码吗？","a":"Code understandability is a critical aspect of software quality. Prior research has largely focused on this attribute from a human-centric perspective, while it should be viewed as a relational property arising from the interaction between a reader and the code. With the increasing adoption of large language models (LLMs) in software engineering, we posit that the notion of “reader” should be generalized to encompass both humans and models. Building on this relational perspective, we extend the concept of code understandability to distinguish between human and model code understandability, aiming to investigate the alignment between the two. To this end, we use a dataset from a prior study containing human-rated judgments of understandability across diverse participant groups, and evaluate multiple open and closed-source LLMs. To operationalize model code understandability, we introduce four proxies: P0, based on program comprehension-focused question answering; and P1–P3, based on program intent summarization (derived from our proposed semantic self-consistency). Our findings show that LLMs exhibit stronger alignment with general human code understandability than previously used shallow machine learning baselines. Stratified analyses further reveal that model code understandability aligns most closely with professional developers, but significantly less with other student groups. Role-conditioned prompting does not improve the alignment for the latter, suggesting that current LLMs cannot accurately mimic the perspectives of human readers with varying expertise. Finally, we demonstrate that semantic self-consistency is a reliable and extensible measure for quantifying model code understandability, with broad implications in both software engineering research and practice.","az":"代码可理解性是软件质量的关键方面。已有研究主要从以人为中心的视角关注这一属性，但它其实应被视为一种关系性属性，产生于阅读者与代码之间的交互。随着大语言模型（LLM）在软件工程中的广泛应用，我们认为阅读者这一概念应当被推广为同时涵盖人类与模型。基于这一关系性视角，我们扩展了代码可理解性的概念，以区分人类代码可理解性与模型代码可理解性，旨在研究两者之间的一致性。为此，我们使用了一项先前研究的数据集，其中包含来自不同参与者群体的、对可理解性的人工评分判断，并评测了多个开源与闭源 LLM。为了将模型代码可理解性可操作化，我们引入四种代理指标：P0，基于以程序理解为核心的问答；以及 P1–P3，基于程序意图摘要（由我们提出的语义自一致性推导而来）。我们的发现表明，LLM 与一般人类代码可理解性的一致程度高于此前使用的浅层机器学习基线。分层分析进一步揭示，模型代码可理解性与专业开发者的一致性最高，而与其他学生群体的一致性显著更低。角色条件化提示并未改善后者的一致性，这表明当前的 LLM 无法准确模拟具有不同专业水平的人类阅读者的视角。最后，我们证明语义自一致性是一种可靠且可扩展的度量，用于量化模型代码可理解性，对软件工程研究与实践都具有广泛意义。","tl":"提出语义自一致性代理，量化模型与人类代码可理解性的对齐。","au":["Xiaokai Rong","Aashish Yadavally","Hridya Dhulipala","Anh H. N. Nguyen","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["code understandability","human-model alignment","semantic self-consistency","program comprehension","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/111/x"},{"id":"p01394","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"FuncDroid: Towards Inter-Functional Flows for Comprehensive Mobile App GUI Testing","tz":"FuncDroid：面向功能间流的全面移动应用 GUI 测试","a":"As mobile application (app) functionalities grow increasingly complex and their iterations accelerate, ensuring high reliability presents significant challenges. While functionality-oriented GUI testing has attracted growing research attention, existing approaches largely overlook interactions across functionalities, making them ineffective at uncovering deep bugs hidden in inter-functional behaviors. To fill this gap, we first design a Functional Flow Graph (FFG), a behavioral model that explicitly captures an app’s functional units and their inter-functional interactions. Based on the FFG, we further introduce an inter-functional-flow-oriented GUI testing approach with the dual goals of precise model construction and deep bug detection. This approach is realized through a long–short-term-view-guided testing process. By combining two complementary test-generation views, it can adaptively refine functional boundaries and systematically explore inter-functional flows under diverse triggering conditions. We implement our approach in a tool called FuncDroid, and evaluate it on two benchmarks: (1) a widely‑used open‑source benchmark with 50 reproducible crash bugs and (2) a diverse set of 52 popular commercial apps. Experimental results demonstrate that FuncDroid significantly outperforms state‑of‑the‑art baselines in both coverage (+28%) and bug detection number (+107%). Moreover, FuncDroid successfully uncovers 18 previously unknown non‑crash functional bugs in commercial apps, confirming its practical effectiveness.","az":"随着移动应用（app）功能日益复杂、迭代不断加速，确保高可靠性带来了巨大挑战。尽管面向功能的 GUI 测试已引起越来越多的研究关注，但现有方法大多忽视了跨功能之间的交互，使其难以发现隐藏在功能间行为中的深层缺陷。为填补这一空白，我们首先设计了功能流图（Functional Flow Graph, FFG），一种显式刻画应用功能单元及其功能间交互的行为模型。基于 FFG，我们进一步提出一种面向功能间流的 GUI 测试方法，兼顾精确模型构建与深层缺陷检测两个目标。该方法通过长短视角引导的测试过程来实现：通过结合两种互补的测试生成视角，它能够自适应地细化功能边界，并在多样的触发条件下系统地探索功能间流。我们在名为 FuncDroid 的工具中实现了该方法，并在两个基准上进行评估：(1) 一个包含 50 个可复现崩溃缺陷的广泛使用的开源基准；(2) 一组包含 52 个流行商业应用的多样化集合。实验结果表明，FuncDroid 在覆盖率（+28%）和缺陷检测数量（+107%）上都显著优于最先进的基线。此外，FuncDroid 在商业应用中成功发现了 18 个此前未知的非崩溃功能性缺陷，证实了其实际有效性。","tl":"用功能流图显式建模功能间交互以挖掘深层 GUI 缺陷。","au":["Jinlong He","xiachangwei","Binru Huang","Jiwei Yan","Jun Yan","Jian Zhang"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["GUI testing","functional flow graph","Android apps","inter-functional interaction","bug detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/112/x"},{"id":"p01395","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Evaluating and Mitigating the Misguidance Effect of Buggy Code in LLM-Generated Unit Tests","tz":"评估并缓解缺陷代码对 LLM 生成单元测试的误导效应","a":"While Large Language Models (LLMs) show great promise for automating unit test generation, recent studies suggest that the quality of generated tests can be negatively impacted when models are prompted with buggy code. This paper presents a new metric to quantitatively measure the “misguidance effect,” a phenomenon where buggy code steers LLMs toward generating tests that validate its erroneous behavior rather than expose it. Our analysis reveals that prompting LLMs with buggy code has a severe, twofold impact: it significantly increases “misguided tests” that assert incorrect behavior while simultaneously suppressing the generation of effective, bug-finding tests. We further corroborate this effect from a model-internal perspective, showing that buggy code skews LLMs’ preference toward tests that assert the same erroneous behavior. To counter this, we introduce and validate a specification-based unit test generation paradigm that replaces the code under test in the prompt with an LLM-generated specification docstring. Our results show that this paradigm effectively reduces misguided tests while substantially increasing effective tests, improves multi-round, feedback-driven test generation pipelines, and remains applicable to both buggy and bug-free code. Overall, these results suggest that specification-based prompting is a promising strategy for mitigating misguidance from buggy code in LLM-generated unit tests.","az":"尽管大语言模型（LLM）在自动化单元测试生成方面展现出巨大前景，近期研究表明，当模型以含缺陷的代码作为提示时，所生成测试的质量会受到负面影响。本文提出一种新的度量，用以定量测量误导效应，即含缺陷代码引导 LLM 生成验证其错误行为、而非暴露该错误的测试的现象。我们的分析揭示，用缺陷代码提示 LLM 会带来严重的双重影响：它显著增加了断言错误行为的被误导测试，同时抑制了有效的、能发现缺陷的测试的生成。我们进一步从模型内部视角佐证了这一效应，表明缺陷代码会使 LLM 的偏好偏向那些断言同样错误行为的测试。为应对这一问题，我们提出并验证了一种基于规约的单元测试生成范式，它用 LLM 生成的规约文档字符串（docstring）替换提示中的被测代码。我们的结果显示，该范式有效减少了被误导测试，同时大幅增加了有效测试，改善了多轮反馈驱动的测试生成流水线，并且对含缺陷代码与无缺陷代码同样适用。总体而言，这些结果表明，基于规约的提示是缓解 LLM 生成单元测试中缺陷代码误导问题的一种有前景的策略。","tl":"提出误导效应度量，并用规约 docstring 替代被测代码来缓解。","au":["Junda Zhao","Shurui Zhou","Eldan Cohen"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["unit test generation","misguidance effect","buggy code","specification-based prompting","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/113/x"},{"id":"p01396","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fuzzing the Boundary Between Models and Code in Hybrid AI-enabled Systems","tz":"对混合 AI 系统中模型与代码边界的模糊测试","a":"Deep learning (DL) techniques are increasingly integrated into traditional software systems, giving rise to hybrid AI-enabled systems that combine neural models with program logic. While these systems exhibit remarkable capabilities, their complex and heterogeneous architectures pose significant challenges for reliability and testing, particularly in safety-critical domains such as autonomous driving. Existing testing approaches either target traditional code or isolate neural networks, overlooking failures arising from their interactions. In this paper, we present Neude, a lightweight and extensible coverage-guided fuzzing framework specifically designed for hybrid AI-enabled systems. Unlike existing tools, Neude combines observations of program execution and neural model coverage to guide input mutations toward unexplored state spaces, enabling systematic evaluation of the entire hybrid pipeline. Moreover, Neude employs domain-aware mutation operators coupled with metamorphic relations, allowing automated bug detection without manual assertions. We evaluate Neude on Pylot, a complex autonomous driving system with tightly coupled neural and program components. Experimental results show that Neude uncovers diverse faults, and further analysis reveals how model uncertainty propagates through deterministic program logic to trigger downstream module failures. Our findings highlight the fragility of current hybrid architectures, calling for a paradigm shift from model-centric testing to system-centric quality assurance that accounts for the intricate interplay between neural and procedural components.","az":"深度学习（DL）技术正日益被集成进传统软件系统，催生了将神经模型与程序逻辑相结合的混合 AI 系统。尽管这些系统展现出卓越的能力，其复杂且异构的架构给可靠性与测试带来了重大挑战，在自动驾驶等安全攸关领域尤为突出。现有测试方法要么针对传统代码，要么孤立地测试神经网络，忽视了两者交互所引发的失效。本文提出 Neude，一个专为混合 AI 系统设计的轻量、可扩展的覆盖引导模糊测试框架。与现有工具不同，Neude 结合对程序执行和神经模型覆盖率的观测来引导输入变异，导向尚未探索的状态空间，从而实现对整个混合流水线的系统性评估。此外，Neude 采用领域感知的变异算子并结合蜕变关系，无需人工断言即可自动检测缺陷。我们在 Pylot 上评估 Neude，这是一个神经组件与程序组件紧密耦合的复杂自动驾驶系统。实验结果表明，Neude 发现了多样的故障，进一步分析揭示了模型不确定性如何通过确定性的程序逻辑传播，从而触发下游模块失效。我们的发现凸显了当前混合架构的脆弱性，呼吁从以模型为中心的测试，转向考虑神经与程序组件之间复杂交互的、以系统为中心的质量保障。","tl":"同时用程序执行与神经覆盖引导变异，测试模型-代码交互边界。","au":["Xinyu Gao","Yang Feng","Yuchen Lu","Zhenqian Liu","Zhenyu Chen","Baowen Xu"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["hybrid AI-enabled systems","coverage-guided fuzzing","autonomous driving","metamorphic relations","Pylot"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/114/x"},{"id":"p01397","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Unpacking AI Agent Participation in Issue-Centered Collaboration in Open-Source Software Development","tz":"解读 AI 智能体在开源软件开发中以 Issue 为中心的协作参与","a":"The increasing participation of AI agents in open-source software development raises questions about their role in collaborative processes. This paper investigates how AI agent participation relates to the structure and outcomes of issue-centered collaboration in open-source software projects. We adopt a process-level perspective by modeling issue handling as sequences of events and extending dynamic issue entropy to distinguish between agent-related and non-agent-related contributions. Using large-scale issue event data from 83 GitHub repositories, we construct a project–month panel dataset and analyze associations between collaboration complexity and development outcomes. Our results show that agent-related collaboration complexity is more strongly associated with development output than human-only collaboration complexity, and is associated with fewer newly introduced defects. In contrast, its relationship with issue resolution efficiency is highly context-dependent. These findings highlight the importance of considering collaboration structure when evaluating the impact of AI agents in open-source software development.","az":"AI 智能体在开源软件开发中日益增多的参与，引发了关于其在协作过程中角色的疑问。本文研究 AI 智能体的参与如何与开源软件项目中以 Issue 为中心的协作结构和结果相关联。我们采取过程层面的视角，将 Issue 处理建模为事件序列，并扩展动态 Issue 熵以区分与智能体相关和与智能体无关的贡献。利用来自 83 个 GitHub 仓库的大规模 Issue 事件数据，我们构建了项目-月份面板数据集，并分析协作复杂度与开发结果之间的关联。我们的结果表明，与智能体相关的协作复杂度同开发产出的关联强于纯人类协作复杂度，并且与更少的新引入缺陷相关联。相比之下，它与 Issue 解决效率之间的关系高度依赖于具体情境。这些发现凸显了在评估 AI 智能体对开源软件开发的影响时，考虑协作结构的重要性。","tl":"扩展动态 Issue 熵，量化智能体参与对开源协作产出的影响。","au":["Kaiwen Zhi","Guisheng Fan","Wentao Chen"],"top":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","agentic"],"kw":["AI agents in OSS","issue collaboration","dynamic issue entropy","panel data","GitHub mining"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/115/x"},{"id":"p01398","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Checked-In Secret Detection: Strings are All You Need","tz":"签入式密钥检测：你只需要字符串","a":"Hardcoded secrets in source code pose critical security vulnerabilities which can be easily exploited by malicious adversaries. Existing regex-based detection approaches suffer from fundamental limitations, as secrets often lack identifiable patterns, resulting in poor precision and recall. Recent studies have explored context-aware detection methods, as surrounding code can reveal the purpose of candidate strings. However, these methods confront three key challenges: (1) obfuscation robustness where models over-rely on easily obfuscated identifiers, (2) cross-language generalization difficulties due to uneven training data distribution, and (3) lengthy and noisy context that introduces excessive irrelevant tokens and slows inference. We observe that strings serve as a critical information source for code semantics, offering superior contextual density, obfuscation robustness, and language independence. Based on this insight, we propose StringGroup, a novel context extraction algorithm that mines strings surrounding potential secrets. With only 33.2% of the original context, it preserves over 80% of semantic information and significantly improves the signal-to-noise ratio for secret detection. We further design a context-aware secret detection tool, Secretron, based on StringGroup methods and Transformer model. Evaluation on the SecretBench dataset demonstrates high accuracy with 98.74% F1-score and strong robustness under obfuscation and cross-language scenarios, outperforming state-of-the-art LLM-based baselines. We deploy our tool in real-world environments and successfully detect 48 previously unknown secret keys from 26 applications, demonstrating the practical effectiveness of our approach.","az":"源代码中的硬编码密钥构成关键的安全漏洞，很容易被恶意攻击者利用。现有基于正则表达式的检测方法存在根本性局限，因为密钥往往缺乏可识别的模式，导致精确率与召回率都很差。近期研究探索了上下文感知的检测方法，因为周围代码可以揭示候选字符串的用途。然而，这些方法面临三个关键挑战：(1) 抗混淆鲁棒性问题，模型过度依赖易被混淆的标识符；(2) 由于训练数据分布不均带来的跨语言泛化困难；(3) 冗长嘈杂的上下文引入过多无关 token 并拖慢推理。我们观察到，字符串是代码语义的关键信息来源，具有更高的上下文密度、抗混淆鲁棒性和语言无关性。基于这一洞见，我们提出 StringGroup，一种挖掘潜在密钥周围字符串的新型上下文抽取算法。它仅使用原始上下文的 33.2%，却保留了超过 80% 的语义信息，并显著提升了密钥检测的信噪比。我们进一步基于 StringGroup 方法与 Transformer 模型设计了上下文感知的密钥检测工具 Secretron。在 SecretBench 数据集上的评测表明，其准确率很高，F1 分数达 98.74%，在混淆与跨语言场景下鲁棒性强，优于最先进的基于 LLM 的基线。我们将该工具部署到真实环境中，从 26 个应用中成功检测出 48 个此前未知的密钥，展示了方法的实际有效性。","tl":"只用周围字符串作上下文，抗混淆且跨语言地检测硬编码密钥。","au":["Zhengdong Huang","Kevin Li","Jinqiu Yang","Yepang Liu","Lili Wei"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["hardcoded secret detection","StringGroup","context extraction","obfuscation robustness","SecretBench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/116/x"},{"id":"p01399","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Testing Retrieval-Augmented Generation Systems with Chunk Coverage","tz":"用块覆盖率测试检索增强生成系统","a":"Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)-based systems are increasingly deployed in high-stakes settings where correct behaviour depends not only on the language model but also on the retrieval component that selects external documents at inference time. While existing RAG evaluation metrics assess retrieval and generation quality on a per-query basis, typically relying on query-level test oracles such as reference answers or relevance annotations, they provide limited insight into whether a test suite adequately exercises the retrieval behaviour of the system as a whole. In this paper, we introduce Chunk Coverage (CC), an oracle-independent test adequacy criterion for testing the retrieval component of RAG systems. CC measures the fraction of corpus chunks that are retrieved at least once across a test suite, providing a structural view of which parts of the retrieval space have been exercised. We further show how CC can be used to guide test selection and generation by prioritising queries that expand coverage of previously unexercised retrieval regions. We evaluate CC on clinical and financial RAG system scenarios. CC-guided testing reaches 50% of attainable coverage up to 1.9 times faster than random selection and up to 6.9 times faster than redundancy-biased strategies. Moreover, CC improves fault detection effectiveness (APFD) by 10% to 25% over random, indicating earlier discovery of distinct retrieval faults. These results show that CC captures retrieval diversity relevant to effective testing without requiring test oracles.","az":"基于检索增强生成（RAG）的系统正越来越多地部署于高风险场景，其正确行为不仅取决于语言模型，也取决于在推理时选择外部文档的检索组件。现有的 RAG 评测指标在逐查询的基础上评估检索与生成质量，通常依赖查询级的测试预言，如参考答案或相关性标注，但它们几乎无法说明某个测试套件是否充分地激发了整个系统的检索行为。本文提出块覆盖率（Chunk Coverage, CC），一种与预言无关的测试充分性准则，用于测试 RAG 系统的检索组件。CC 度量在整个测试套件中至少被检索到一次的语料块所占比例，从而提供检索空间中哪些部分已被激发的结构性视图。我们进一步展示了如何利用 CC 来指导测试选择与生成，方法是优先选择能扩展此前未被激发的检索区域覆盖的查询。我们在临床与金融 RAG 系统场景上评估 CC。CC 引导的测试达到可达成覆盖率 50% 的速度，比随机选择快至多 1.9 倍，比偏向冗余的策略快至多 6.9 倍。此外，CC 将故障检测有效性（APFD）相比随机提升 10% 至 25%，表明能更早发现互不相同的检索故障。这些结果表明，CC 无需测试预言即可刻画与有效测试相关的检索多样性。","tl":"提出块覆盖率：无需预言即可衡量 RAG 检索测试充分性。","au":["Jinhan Kim","Samuele Pasini","Paolo Tonella"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["RAG testing","chunk coverage","test adequacy","oracle-independent","test prioritization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/117/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18155"},{"id":"p01400","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Function Calling as a Flexible LLM Defense Add-On: Capability and Application Exploration","tz":"把函数调用当作灵活的 LLM 防御插件：能力与应用探索","a":"Large language models (LLMs) exhibit impressive capabilities but are susceptible to adversarial attacks that induce harmful outputs. Although various defenses have been proposed, their practicality is restricted by substantial runtime overhead or degraded model helpfulness. Moreover, LLM applications typically have diverse and evolving security requirements that cannot be fully anticipated during the design of static defenses. These limitations call for a flexible, low-overhead defense mechanism that can be easily customized to meet task-specific needs. In this paper, we explore function calling (FC)—a built-in mechanism in modern LLMs for invoking custom tools—as a lightweight and adaptable defense add-on. We show that by defining functions representing malicious actions, LLMs equipped with FC can intercept harmful prompts by triggering these function calls instead of generating unsafe content. Extensive experiments across mainstream LLMs demonstrate that FC substantially improves defense effectiveness with minimal impact on model helpfulness. To further assess FC’s practical utility, we also introduce DSPEC, a new dataset reflecting real-world LLM applications with specific defense requirements. Our evaluations on DSPEC show that FC substantially outperforms existing defenses in this realistic setting. Besides, we also explore the practical applications of FC in various scenarios, including universal defense frameworks and multi-agent systems, further demonstrating its versatility and effectiveness in enhancing LLM security.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）展现出令人印象深刻的能力，但容易受到诱导其产生有害输出的对抗攻击。尽管已有多种防御被提出，它们的实用性受限于巨大的运行时开销或模型有用性的下降。此外，LLM 应用通常具有多样且不断演变的安全需求，无法在设计静态防御时被完全预见。这些局限呼唤一种灵活、低开销、易于定制以满足任务特定需求的防御机制。本文探索将函数调用（FC）——现代 LLM 中用于调用自定义工具的内置机制——作为一种轻量且可适配的防御插件。我们表明，通过定义表示恶意行为的函数，配备 FC 的 LLM 可以通过触发这些函数调用来拦截有害提示，而不是生成不安全内容。在主流 LLM 上的大量实验表明，FC 显著提升了防御有效性，同时对模型有用性的影响极小。为进一步评估 FC 的实用价值，我们还引入了 DSPEC，一个反映具有特定防御需求的真实 LLM 应用的新数据集。我们在 DSPEC 上的评测显示，在这一贴近现实的设定中，FC 大幅优于现有防御。此外，我们还探索了 FC 在多种场景中的实际应用，包括通用防御框架与多智能体系统，进一步展示了其在增强 LLM 安全性方面的多功能性与有效性。","tl":"用函数调用声明恶意行为，让模型以调用代替生成来拦截攻击。","au":["Zhenlan Ji","Daoyuan Wu","Wenxuan Wang","Pingchuan Ma","Shuai Wang","Lei Ma","Juergen Rahmel"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","tg":["security","benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["function calling","LLM defense","adversarial prompts","DSPEC","multi-agent systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/118/x"},{"id":"p01401","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Custom Logic to APIs: Understanding and Recommending API Replacement Refactorings","tz":"从自定义逻辑到 API：理解并推荐 API 替换型重构","a":"Software refactoring is essential for maintaining code quality. However, API replacement refactoring, which replaces custom logic with API calls, remains less underexplored. Existing refactoring tools often fail to detect such opportunities due to their reliance on rigid templates and their inability to capture complex, multi-statement semantic equivalents. To bridge this gap, we conduct the first empirical study of API replacement refactorings, analyzing 166,299 commits across six open-source Java projects to quantify their occurrence and to characterize their scope, categories, and recurring patterns. Based on these insights, we propose AKIRA (Adaptive Knowledge Discovery and Retrieval), a hybrid framework that integrates pattern-deterministic heuristics with a refactoring-aware knowledge base to assess the practical feasibility of recommending API replacement refactorings. Our evaluation shows that AKIRA achieves 90% recall and 88% precision on a manually curated dataset. Furthermore, on the external RETIWA dataset, AKIRA significantly improves the state of the art by increasing recall from 21% to 81% and precision from 40% to 78%. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of combining static pattern matching with semantic reasoning to support the automation of recommending complex API replacement refactorings.","az":"软件重构对维持代码质量至关重要。然而，将自定义逻辑替换为 API 调用的 API 替换型重构仍然缺乏探索。现有重构工具往往由于依赖僵化的模板、且无法刻画复杂的多语句语义等价物，而无法检测此类重构机会。为弥补这一空白，我们开展了首个针对 API 替换型重构的实证研究，分析了六个开源 Java 项目中的 166,299 个提交，以量化其发生情况并刻画其作用范围、类别与反复出现的模式。基于这些洞见，我们提出了 AKIRA（自适应知识发现与检索），这是一个混合框架，它将模式确定性启发式规则与具备重构感知能力的知识库相结合，以评估推荐 API 替换型重构的实际可行性。我们的评估表明，AKIRA 在人工整理的数据集上取得了 90% 的召回率和 88% 的精确率。此外，在外部 RETIWA 数据集上，AKIRA 显著超越了现有最优方法，将召回率从 21% 提升到 81%，将精确率从 40% 提升到 78%。这些结果表明，将静态模式匹配与语义推理相结合，能够有效支持复杂 API 替换型重构推荐的自动化。","tl":"首次实证刻画 API 替换重构并用混合知识库自动推荐。","au":["Bridget Nyirongo","Yanjie Jiang","Yuxia Zhang","Hui Liu"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["API replacement refactoring","refactoring recommendation","empirical study","knowledge base","static pattern matching"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/119/x"},{"id":"p01402","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"IterTestQ: Assembly-Level, Cross-Platform Testing of Quantum Computing Platforms","tz":"IterTestQ：面向量子计算平台的汇编级跨平台测试","a":"Quantum computing platforms are susceptible to quantum-specific bugs, such as incorrectly ordering qubits or incorrectly implementing quantum abstractions. These bugs are difficult to detect and require specialized expertise. The field faces challenges due to a fragmented landscape of platforms and rapid development cycles that often prioritize new features over thorough testing, severely hindering the reliability of quantum software. To address these challenges, we present IterTestQ, the first cross-platform testing approach for quantum computing platforms. The key technical contribution is our novel ITE process, which generates equivalent quantum programs by iteratively (I)mporting them into platform-specific representations, (T)ransforming the program via optimizations and gate conversions, and (E)xporting the program again. To transfer programs across platforms and test cross-platform consistency, IterTestQ leverages QASM, an assembly-level representation supported by most platforms. The approach uses a crash oracle to detect failures during cross-platform transformations and an equivalence oracle to validate the semantic consistency of the generated assembly programs, which are expected to be equivalent by construction. We evaluate IterTestQ on four widely-used quantum computing platforms: Qiskit, PennyLane, Pytket, and BQSKit, revealing 18 bugs, 15 of which are already confirmed or fixed. Our results also demonstrate that IterTestQ complements existing quantum fuzzers (covering tens of thousands of otherwise uncovered lines), is efficient (with 0.00089 seconds per generated program), and that the ITE process is crucial for its effectiveness.","az":"量子计算平台容易出现量子特有的缺陷，例如错误地排列量子比特顺序或错误地实现量子抽象。这些缺陷难以检测，且需要专门的专业知识。该领域面临的挑战在于平台格局碎片化，以及快速的开发周期常常将新特性置于充分测试之上，严重阻碍了量子软件的可靠性。为应对这些挑战，我们提出了 IterTestQ，这是首个面向量子计算平台的跨平台测试方法。其核心技术贡献是我们新颖的 ITE 流程：通过迭代地将程序（I）导入到平台特定表示、（T）经由优化与门转换对程序进行变换、再（E）导出程序，从而生成等价的量子程序。为在平台间迁移程序并测试跨平台一致性，IterTestQ 利用了大多数平台都支持的汇编级表示 QASM。该方法使用崩溃预言来检测跨平台变换过程中的失败，并使用等价性预言来验证所生成的、按构造应当等价的汇编程序的语义一致性。我们在四个被广泛使用的量子计算平台上评估了 IterTestQ：Qiskit、PennyLane、Pytket 和 BQSKit，发现了 18 个缺陷，其中 15 个已被确认或修复。我们的结果还表明，IterTestQ 与现有的量子模糊测试工具互补（覆盖了数万行原本未被覆盖的代码），效率很高（每生成一个程序耗时 0.00089 秒），并且 ITE 流程对其有效性至关重要。","tl":"用 QASM 导入-变换-导出迭代生成等价量子程序做跨平台测试。","au":["Matteo Paltenghi","Michael Pradel"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["quantum platform testing","cross-platform testing","QASM","equivalence oracle","Qiskit"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/120/x"},{"id":"p01403","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Integrating Multiple Features for Weakly-Supervised False-Passing Products Detection in Software Product Lines","tz":"融合多种特征的软件产品线假通过产品弱监督检测","a":"Software Product Lines (SPL) enable the efficient development of configurable systems through feature modularization. However, the inherent configurability of software introduces significant challenges for fault localization within these systems. A key challenge among these is the problem of false-passing products, configurable products that contain faulty code yet coincidentally pass all their associated tests, thereby masking faults and misleading diagnosis efforts. To mitigate the negative impact of false-passing products. Supervised detection approaches are often impractical due to their reliance on complete labels, which are unavailable during early testing phases. To address this, we propose PULP, a label-agnostic detection approach that exploits the execution similarity between failing and false-passing products. PULP extracts five categories of features and employs a weakly-supervised learning algorithm to identify false-passing products without pre-labeled data. Evaluated on 823 buggy versions from six real-world SPL systems, PULP achieves superior detection performance, with best accuracy of 90.33% and precision of 94.93% for false-passing products and consistently enhances fault localization rankings after eliminating the negative impact of false-passing product. This method offers a practical tool for SPL testing and debugging in label-incomplete environments.","az":"软件产品线（SPL）通过特征模块化实现了可配置系统的高效开发。然而，软件固有的可配置性给这类系统中的缺陷定位带来了重大挑战。其中一个关键挑战是假通过产品问题：这些可配置产品包含有缺陷的代码，却恰好通过了与之相关的所有测试，从而掩盖了缺陷并误导诊断工作。为缓解假通过产品的负面影响——有监督的检测方法往往不切实际，因为它们依赖完整标签，而这些标签在测试早期阶段是不可得的。为此，我们提出了 PULP，一种与标签无关的检测方法，利用失败产品与假通过产品之间的执行相似性。PULP 提取五类特征，并采用弱监督学习算法，在没有预先标注数据的情况下识别假通过产品。在来自六个真实世界 SPL 系统的 823 个含缺陷版本上进行评估，PULP 取得了优越的检测性能，对假通过产品的最佳准确率为 90.33%、精确率为 94.93%，并且在消除假通过产品的负面影响后持续提升了缺陷定位排名。该方法为标签不完整环境下的 SPL 测试与调试提供了实用工具。","tl":"用弱监督执行相似性识别 SPL 中掩盖缺陷的假通过产品。","au":["Tao Zhang","Yan Lei","Haoran Xia","Huan Xie","Chunyan Liu"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","empirical-study"],"kw":["software product lines","false-passing products","fault localization","weakly-supervised learning","configurable systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/121/x"},{"id":"p01404","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Applying System Call Filtering to Real-World Binaries (Experience Paper)","tz":"将系统调用过滤应用于真实世界二进制程序（经验论文）","a":"System call filtering restricts applications to the system calls they require, but inferring accurate syscall sets for binary-only programs remains challenging. A central difficulty lies in recovering precise control-flow information from binaries: over-approximation leads to overly permissive syscall filters, while missed control-flow edges result in unsound policies. Although many techniques have been proposed to improve control-flow recovery in binaries, their practical impact on syscall inference remains poorly understood. In this work, we conduct an empirical study of syscall inference from binaries using multiple off-the-shelf binary analysis tools. We evaluate how different control-flow refinement techniques affect inferred syscall sets in practice. Our experiments on real-world applications show that refinements targeting individual control- flow transfers (e.g., call-site and callee argument matching) substantially improve per-call target precision but often do not reduce the overall syscall set. In contrast, techniques that reduce the global set of address-taken functions—such as leveraging relocation information to accurately identify code pointers—yield the most significant syscall reductions. Finally, we identify a practical lower bound on syscall reduction achievable via sound static binary analysis alone, and show that further improvements are likely to require configuration or workload-aware specialization.","az":"系统调用过滤将应用程序限制在其所需的系统调用集合内，但为仅有二进制的程序推断准确的系统调用集合仍然困难。核心难点在于从二进制中恢复精确的控制流信息：过度近似会导致过于宽松的系统调用过滤器，而遗漏控制流边则会产生不健全的策略。尽管已有许多技术被提出以改进二进制中的控制流恢复，但它们对系统调用推断的实际影响仍然缺乏理解。在本工作中，我们使用多种现成的二进制分析工具，对从二进制推断系统调用开展了实证研究。我们评估了不同的控制流精化技术在实践中如何影响推断出的系统调用集合。我们在真实世界应用上的实验表明，针对单个控制流转移的精化（例如调用点与被调用者参数匹配）显著提升了逐个调用点的目标精度，但往往并不能缩减整体的系统调用集合。相反，那些缩减全局取址函数集合的技术——例如利用重定位信息来准确识别代码指针——带来了最显著的系统调用缩减。最后，我们确定了仅靠健全的静态二进制分析所能达到的系统调用缩减的实际下界，并表明进一步的改进很可能需要面向配置或负载的特化。","tl":"实测各类控制流精化对二进制系统调用过滤的真实收益与下界。","au":["Soumyakant Priyadarshan","Seyedhamed Ghavamnia"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["empirical-study","security","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["system call filtering","binary analysis","control-flow recovery","attack surface reduction","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/122/x"},{"id":"p01405","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards More Realistic Assertion Generation under Mixed-Assertion Scenario","tz":"迈向混合断言场景下更真实的断言生成","a":"Unit testing is essential for software quality assurance, where a test case typically consists of a test prefix and an oracle, expressed as assertions. In practice, crafting high-quality assertions is non-trivial and time-consuming, as it requires developers to reason carefully about program states and expected behaviors. While recent advances in Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown promise for automating assertion generation (AG), current AG methods often rely on two unrealistic assumptions: (1) the Single-Assertion Formulation (A1), which assumes tests contain only one assertion, and (2) the Known-Position Formulation (A2), which treats AG as a “fill-in-the-blanks” task with pre-defined insertion points. Despite being widely adopted, the realism and implications of these assumptions have not been systematically examined. This paper revisits AG under a realistic Mixed-Assertion Scenario, where tests may contain one or multiple assertions and insertion positions are unavailable at inference time. To examine A1, we first conduct a large-scale empirical study of 358,117 developer-written tests from 7,061 projects. The results show that multi-assertion tests are prevalent, accounting for 40.32% of all tests and appearing in 92.87% of projects. Through manual analysis, we derive a taxonomy comprising ten fine-grained assertion patterns, showing that assertions in multi-assertion tests are rarely independent checks (4.69%) and instead coordinate to validate a unified test objective. To examine A2, we remove ground-truth insertion cues and observe substantial performance degradation, with Exact Match dropping by 11.80%-23.18% overall. This suggests that position cues affect not only where assertions are placed, but also the quality of what to assert. Motivated by these findings, we propose DA-AG, a two-stage framework designed for the realistic Mixed-Assertion Scenario with unknown insertion positions. In the first stage, it predicts assertion insertion positions to construct an assertion skeleton with explicit insertion cues. In the second stage, it generates assertion content conditioned on the resulting skeleton and retrieved exemplar assertion sequences. Extensive experiments across 13 diverse LLMs show that DA-AG consistently outperforms the corresponding one-stage baselines, which directly generate the completed test from the focal method and raw test prefix. DA-AG improves Exact Match by 32.24%-78.08% and CodeBLEU by 2.80%-8.63%, and further increases bug exposure on Defects4J by 6-39 exposed bugs and 7-23 unique exposed bugs. Moreover, DA-AG outperforms representative closed-source LLMs (e.g., GPT-4o and Claude-3.5) in both generation quality and bug-finding effectiveness under the realistic setting.","az":"单元测试对软件质量保障至关重要，其中一个测试用例通常由测试前缀和以断言形式表达的预言组成。在实践中，编写高质量断言并不容易且耗时，因为它要求开发者仔细推理程序状态与预期行为。尽管大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展在自动化断言生成（AG）方面展现出潜力，当前的 AG 方法往往依赖两个不切实际的假设：（1）单断言形式化（A1），假定测试只包含一个断言；（2）已知位置形式化（A2），将 AG 视为具有预定义插入点的“填空”任务。尽管这两个假设被广泛采用，它们的真实性与影响却尚未被系统检验。本文在更真实的混合断言场景下重新审视 AG，其中测试可能包含一个或多个断言，且推理时无法获知插入位置。为检验 A1，我们首先对来自 7,061 个项目的 358,117 个开发者编写的测试开展了大规模实证研究。结果显示多断言测试十分普遍，占全部测试的 40.32%，并出现在 92.87% 的项目中。通过人工分析，我们归纳出包含十种细粒度断言模式的分类体系，表明多断言测试中的断言很少是相互独立的检查（仅 4.69%），而是协同验证一个统一的测试目标。为检验 A2，我们移除了真实插入位置线索，观察到性能大幅下降，整体精确匹配率下降了 11.80%–23.18%。这表明位置线索不仅影响断言被放在哪里，也影响断言内容的质量。受这些发现启发，我们提出 DA-AG，一个面向插入位置未知的真实混合断言场景的两阶段框架。第一阶段预测断言插入位置，构建带有显式插入线索的断言骨架；第二阶段以该骨架和检索到的示例断言序列为条件生成断言内容。在 13 个不同 LLM 上的大量实验表明，DA-AG 一致优于相应的一阶段基线（后者直接从焦点方法和原始测试前缀生成完整测试）。DA-AG 将精确匹配率提升 32.24%–78.08%，CodeBLEU 提升 2.80%–8.63%，并在 Defects4J 上额外暴露 6–39 个缺陷以及 7–23 个独有缺陷。此外，在该真实设定下，DA-AG 在生成质量和查错效果上均优于具有代表性的闭源 LLM（如 GPT-4o 与 Claude-3.5）。","tl":"揭穿单断言与已知位置假设，提出先定位后生成的两阶段断言生成。","au":["Hongyan Li","Kunpeng E","Weifeng Sun","Quanjun Zhang","Meng Yan"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["assertion generation","test oracle","multi-assertion tests","Defects4J","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/123/x"},{"id":"p01406","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"OptiMine: Scalable and Precise Code Optimization for Android Apps via LLM-Driven Semantic Analysis","tz":"OptiMine：通过 LLM 驱动的语义分析实现 Android 应用可扩展且精确的代码优化","a":"As Android applications grow in scale, latent performance issues increasingly degrade user experience and business outcomes, yet systematically identifying optimization opportunities in large codebases remains challenging. We present OptiMine, a hybrid knowledge-to-code framework that integrates large language models (LLMs) with static program analysis to automatically uncover actionable performance optimizations. OptiMine systematically transforms unstructured expert knowledge from documents, commit diffs, and reports into structured Optimization Signatures, enabling reproducible and context-aware program reasoning. These signatures drive scalable candidate retrieval via declarative Datalog queries, while LLM-guided semantic validation performs precise applicability checking, side-effect analysis, and impact aware ranking. We evaluate OptiMine on a public benchmark and a large industrial Android codebase. The results show that OptiMine achieves higher precision and broader coverage than heuristic- and pattern-based baselines, while scaling effectively to industrial settings. Overall, OptiMine enables reliable and scalable performance auditing, bridging expert knowledge and actionable performance improvements in real-world mobile systems.","az":"随着 Android 应用规模不断增长，潜在的性能问题日益损害用户体验与业务结果，然而在大型代码库中系统性地识别优化机会仍然困难。我们提出 OptiMine，一个将大语言模型（LLM）与静态程序分析相结合的“知识到代码”混合框架，用于自动发现可落地的性能优化。OptiMine 系统性地将来自文档、提交差异和报告的非结构化专家知识转化为结构化的优化签名（Optimization Signatures），从而实现可复现且具备上下文感知的程序推理。这些签名通过声明式 Datalog 查询驱动可扩展的候选检索，同时由 LLM 引导的语义验证执行精确的适用性检查、副作用分析以及影响感知的排序。我们在一个公开基准和一个大型工业级 Android 代码库上评估了 OptiMine。结果表明，OptiMine 相比基于启发式和基于模式的基线取得了更高的精确率和更广的覆盖，同时能够有效扩展到工业场景。总体而言，OptiMine 实现了可靠且可扩展的性能审计，在专家知识与可落地的性能改进之间架起桥梁，服务于真实世界的移动系统。","tl":"把专家性能知识转成优化签名，用 Datalog 检索加 LLM 验证。","au":["Pengbo Du","Qiuping Yi","Liangzheng Zhang","Hongliang Liang"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["Android performance","code optimization","static analysis","Datalog","LLM semantic validation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/124/x"},{"id":"p01407","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Dataset of Reproducible Flaky-Test Failures","tz":"一个可复现的不稳定测试失败数据集","a":"Flaky tests pass and fail non-deterministically when run on the same version of code. Previous research proposed techniques to detect, debug, and repair different categories of flaky tests. However, reproducing the flaky-test failures remains a major challenge due to their inherent non-determinism. Reliably reproducing flaky-test failures is essential for helping both developers and automatic techniques to debug and repair flaky tests. Many datasets related to flaky tests exist to help researchers study them, but these datasets are often composed of disjoint information, where each dataset provides some unique information over the others, such as flaky tests of many different categories, failure logs of flaky tests, or flaky tests reported by developers vs. flaky tests found by automated tools. Furthermore, several of them are missing the key aspect of providing a means to reliably reproduce the flaky-test failures. In this work, we aim to create a dataset of flaky tests, where each test’s failure is reproducible and there is a comprehensive set of information for the flaky test. Compared to prior flaky-test datasets, our dataset is the first to provide (1) an environment to compile the code for running the flaky tests, (2) scripts to run the tests to reproduce the flaky-test failures, (3) scripts to automatically apply flaky-test fixes and check that the test is no longer flaky, and (4) execution logs of the flaky test both passing and failing. We present ReproFlake, a dataset of 1115 flaky tests, spread across four different flaky-test categories. We also publish the guideline we developed to construct our dataset so others can contribute to this dataset by collecting the same information. We also study the categories of flaky tests in ReproFlake, the location and size of flaky-test fixes, and the code coverage of flaky tests before and after they are fixed. Our study highlights promising future flaky-test research directions, which our dataset helps enable.","az":"不稳定测试（flaky test）在同一版本代码上运行时会非确定性地时而通过、时而失败。已有研究提出了检测、调试和修复不同类别不稳定测试的技术。然而，由于其固有的非确定性，复现不稳定测试的失败仍是一大难题。可靠地复现不稳定测试失败，对于帮助开发者和自动化技术调试与修复不稳定测试至关重要。目前存在许多与不稳定测试相关的数据集以帮助研究者开展研究，但这些数据集往往由互不相交的信息构成，每个数据集相对其他数据集提供一些独有信息，例如涵盖多种类别的不稳定测试、不稳定测试的失败日志，或是开发者报告的不稳定测试与自动化工具发现的不稳定测试之别。此外，其中若干数据集缺少一个关键方面：提供可靠复现不稳定测试失败的手段。在本工作中，我们旨在构建一个不稳定测试数据集，其中每个测试的失败都是可复现的，并且为该不稳定测试提供了全面的信息集合。与以往的不稳定测试数据集相比，我们的数据集首次提供了：（1）用于编译代码以运行不稳定测试的环境；（2）运行测试以复现不稳定测试失败的脚本；（3）自动应用不稳定测试修复并检查该测试是否不再不稳定的脚本；（4）不稳定测试通过与失败两种情形下的执行日志。我们提出 ReproFlake，一个包含 1,115 个不稳定测试、覆盖四种不同不稳定测试类别的数据集。我们还公开了构建该数据集所制定的指南，以便他人通过收集同样的信息为该数据集做出贡献。我们还研究了 ReproFlake 中不稳定测试的类别、不稳定测试修复的位置与规模，以及不稳定测试在修复前后的代码覆盖率。我们的研究指出了若干有前景的未来不稳定测试研究方向，而我们的数据集有助于推动这些方向。","tl":"首个提供环境、复现与修复脚本及日志的不稳定测试数据集。","au":["Suzzana Rafi","MAHBUB-UL-HOQUE SUMON","Md Erfan","Maruf Morshed Khan","August Shi","Wing Lam"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["flaky tests","reproducible failures","dataset","test repair","code coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/125/x","pu":"https://people.cs.gmu.edu/~winglam/publications/2026/RafiETAL26ReproFlake.pdf"},{"id":"p01408","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"MuMuTestUp: Mutation-based Multi-Agent Test Case Update","tz":"MuMuTestUp：基于变异的多智能体测试用例更新","a":"Modern software systems evolve rapidly under continuous integration and deployment (CI/CD) practices, in which tests act as critical gatekeepers of software quality. However, when substantial code changes are introduced, existing test cases may become obsolete, leading to compilation failures, erroneous test behaviors, or inadequate regression coverage. Such issues can disrupt CI/CD pipelines, degrade development productivity, and ultimately undermine overall software quality. Many efforts are devoted to designing automatic test case update methods to address these issues. The most recent approaches rely on large language models (LLMs) to iteratively refine test cases using execution feedback from compilation errors or coverage reports, and on context retrieved via exact-matching approaches. They also prioritize test executability and line coverage to quickly build executable, correct test cases from the original broken test cases. Despite their correctness, current approaches face three limitations: (1) they focus on executabilty but overlook the adequacy of test assertions, which lowers the capability of test cases to detect faults; (2) they utilize only coarse line coverage singals instead of specific information about uncovered lines and branches; (3) they use exact-matching context retrieval approaches, which fails to provide accurate context given potential hallucinated queries from LLMs. To address these challenges, we propose MuMuTestUp, a Mutation-guided, Multi-agent framework for automated test case updating. MuMuTestUp integrates three specialized agents: (1) a Mutation Analysis agent that leverages surviving mutants as indicators of weak or missing test assertions and generates individual repair instructions to strengthen or synthesize assertions for each surviving mutant, (2) a Coverage Analysis agent generates individual repair instructions for each uncovered line, uncovered branch rather than exposing raw coverage signals to the LLM, and (3) a Semantic Retrieval agent that uses semantic-similarity search to handle unavailable or hallucinated symbols. Additionally, we construct Prbench, a pull-request–level dataset of 571 samples from 10 open-source Java projects that considered cross-commit update scenarios, validated through three rounds of execution following prior studies to detect outdated tests. We evaluate MuMuTestUp against state-of-the-art baselines using both open-source and closed-source LLMs (Deepseek-V3.2 and GPT-4.1). With GPT-4.1, MuMuTestUp achieves a line coverage of 88.94%, branch coverage of 63.36%, and mutation score of 72.39%, outperforming the best baseline by 5.33%, 19.93%, and 16.66%, respectively.","az":"现代软件系统在持续集成与持续部署（CI/CD）实践下快速演化，其中测试充当软件质量的关键守门人。然而，当引入大量代码变更时，已有测试用例可能变得过时，导致编译失败、错误的测试行为或不足的回归覆盖。这些问题会中断 CI/CD 流水线、降低开发效率，并最终损害整体软件质量。许多工作致力于设计自动化的测试用例更新方法来解决这些问题。最新的方法依赖大语言模型（LLM），利用来自编译错误或覆盖率报告的执行反馈迭代精化测试用例，并通过精确匹配方法检索上下文。它们还优先考虑测试的可执行性与行覆盖率，以便从原始损坏的测试用例快速构建可执行、正确的测试用例。尽管这些方法保证了正确性，但当前方法面临三个局限：（1）它们关注可执行性却忽视了测试断言的充分性，从而降低了测试用例检测缺陷的能力；（2）它们仅使用粗粒度的行覆盖率信号，而非关于未覆盖行与分支的具体信息；（3）它们使用精确匹配的上下文检索方法，在 LLM 可能产生幻觉查询时无法提供准确上下文。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 MuMuTestUp，一个由变异引导的多智能体自动化测试用例更新框架。MuMuTestUp 集成了三个专门的智能体：（1）变异分析智能体，利用存活变异体作为断言薄弱或缺失的指示，并为每个存活变异体生成单独的修复指令，以强化或合成断言；（2）覆盖分析智能体，为每一条未覆盖行、未覆盖分支生成单独的修复指令，而不是把原始覆盖率信号直接暴露给 LLM；（3）语义检索智能体，使用语义相似度搜索来处理不可用或幻觉产生的符号。此外，我们构建了 Prbench，一个拉取请求级别的数据集，包含来自 10 个开源 Java 项目、考虑跨提交更新场景的 571 个样本，并遵循已有研究经过三轮执行验证以识别过时测试。我们使用开源与闭源 LLM（Deepseek-V3.2 与 GPT-4.1）将 MuMuTestUp 与最先进的基线进行了对比评估。在使用 GPT-4.1 时，MuMuTestUp 取得了 88.94% 的行覆盖率、63.36% 的分支覆盖率和 72.39% 的变异得分，分别比最佳基线高出 5.33%、19.93% 和 16.66%。","tl":"用存活变异体指导多智能体更新过时测试，补强断言而非只求可执行。","au":["Dawei Tian","Jiakun Liu","Yun Peng","Yichen Zhang","Jianlei Chi","Jun Sun","Xiaohong Su"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","agentic","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["test case update","mutation testing","multi-agent","CI/CD","regression coverage"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/126/x"},{"id":"p01409","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Names Are All You Need: Effective and Safe Regression Test Selection for Python","tz":"名字就够了：面向 Python 的有效且安全的回归测试选择","a":"Regression test selection (RTS) reduces the cost of regression testing by executing only those tests affected by a code change. Despite extensive study of RTS in statically typed languages such as Java, achieving effective and safe RTS in Python is challenging. Python’s dynamic typing makes precise call-graph construction difficult, which can cause call-graph-based RTS to miss affected tests, and hence, compromise safety. Python’s eager importing mechanism, in contrast, renders file-level dependency analysis overly conservative. This paper presents NameRTS, the first Python RTS approach based on fine-grained dependency analysis. NameRTS models a Python program as a bipartite graph of code element nodes (e.g., classes, functions, global variables) and name nodes (i.e., identifiers used to reference code elements), with edges capturing definitions and references. RTS is formulated as a reachability problem on this graph: a test is selected if any modified code element is reachable from the names used in that test. This design avoids call-graph construction, enabling a conservative analysis amenable to safety. To control dependency cascades introduced by coarse name matching, NameRTS applies two pruning strategies that leverage prior test executions and context information to refine name matching. To evaluate NameRTS, we construct the first Python RTS dataset with a ground truth indicating which test files are affected by each commit. It includes 500 commits drawn from 10 real-world Python projects. We compare NameRTS with the best-performing baseline, BabelRTS, an RTS technique based on coarse file-level dependencies. On this benchmark, NameRTS skips 69.90% of test files on average, outperforming BabelRTS by 146.5%. It also reduces end-to-end testing time by 45.59%, yielding a 107.7% improvement over BabelRTS. In terms of safety, NameRTS selects all affected tests for 99.6% of commits, with only rare misses in exceptional cases. In contrast, BabelRTS is safe for 76.6% of commits. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of NameRTS, paving the way for more efficient regression testing in Python.","az":"回归测试选择（RTS）通过仅执行受代码变更影响的测试来降低回归测试成本。尽管 RTS 在 Java 等静态类型语言中已被广泛研究，但在 Python 中实现有效且安全的 RTS 仍具挑战。Python 的动态类型使精确构建调用图变得困难，这可能导致基于调用图的 RTS 漏选受影响的测试，从而损害安全性；而 Python 的急切导入机制又使得文件级依赖分析过于保守。本文提出 NameRTS，首个基于细粒度依赖分析的 Python RTS 方法。NameRTS 将 Python 程序建模为由代码元素节点（如类、函数、全局变量）与名字节点（即用于引用代码元素的标识符）构成的二部图，边刻画定义与引用关系。RTS 被形式化为该图上的可达性问题：若某个被修改的代码元素可从某测试所使用的名字到达，则选择该测试。该设计避免了调用图构建，实现了有利于安全性的保守分析。为控制粗粒度名字匹配引入的依赖级联，NameRTS 应用两种剪枝策略，利用先前的测试执行信息与上下文信息来精化名字匹配。为评估 NameRTS，我们构建了首个 Python RTS 数据集，其中包含指示每个提交影响了哪些测试文件的真值标注。它包含取自 10 个真实世界 Python 项目的 500 个提交。我们将 NameRTS 与表现最好的基线 BabelRTS（一种基于粗粒度文件级依赖的 RTS 技术）进行比较。在该基准上，NameRTS 平均跳过 69.90% 的测试文件，比 BabelRTS 高出 146.5%；它还将端到端测试时间减少 45.59%，相比 BabelRTS 提升 107.7%。在安全性方面，NameRTS 在 99.6% 的提交上选中了全部受影响的测试，仅在极少数特殊情况下有遗漏；相比之下，BabelRTS 仅在 76.6% 的提交上是安全的。这些结果证明了 NameRTS 的有效性，为 Python 中更高效的回归测试铺平了道路。","tl":"用标识符二部图可达性替代调用图，实现安全的 Python 测试选择。","au":["You Wang","Michael Pradel","Zhongxin Liu"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["regression test selection","Python","dependency analysis","bipartite graph","safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/127/x"},{"id":"p01410","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"From Static to Dynamic: Benchmarking Real-world Code Review with MCR-bench","tz":"从静态到动态：用 MCR-bench 对真实世界代码评审进行基准测试","a":"In real-world software development, code review typically involves iterative interactions between developers and reviewers to improve software quality, making the process costly and time-consuming. Although recent work explores large language models (LLMs) for automated code review, most approaches oversimplify code review into a single-round, static decision task, which fails to capture the multi-round interactive nature and the complex problem-solving processes inherent in realistic review scenarios. To bridge this gap, we introduce MCR-bench, the first defect state–aware benchmark designed for realistic multi-round code review. MCR-bench covers five commonly-used programming languages and consists of 2,269 real-world multi-round code review tasks. each of which annotated with fine-grained defect information and cross-round state labels. Each task in MCR-bench is equipped with fine-grained defect metadata (e.g., description, type, severity) alongside dynamic state annotations, capturing the complete evolutionary trajectory of a defect throughout the multi-round process. We obtain several findings through extensive experiments on MCR-bench with mainstream LLMs. (1) Limited overall capability: experiments reveal that mainstreaming LLMs exhibit limited overall performance in defect detection and defect lifecycle state tracking, with performance degrading significantly as the number of interaction rounds increases; (2) Defect-sensitive performance: LLMs’ performance varies substantially across different defect types and severity levels, with semantically complex or low-salience defects being significantly more likely to be missed; (3) Underlying Failure Mechanisms: our in-depth error analysis dissects the distinct drivers of false positives and false negatives, revealing critical weaknesses such as cross-round temporal misalignment and the inadequate long-range memory.","az":"在真实世界的软件开发中，代码评审通常涉及开发者与评审者之间的迭代交互以改进软件质量，这使该过程既昂贵又耗时。尽管近期工作探索了用大语言模型（LLM）实现自动化代码评审，但大多数方法把代码评审过度简化为单轮、静态的决策任务，无法刻画真实评审场景中固有的多轮交互特性与复杂的问题求解过程。为弥补这一差距，我们提出 MCR-bench，首个面向真实多轮代码评审、具备缺陷状态感知的基准。MCR-bench 覆盖五种常用编程语言，包含 2,269 个真实世界的多轮代码评审任务，每个任务都标注了细粒度的缺陷信息与跨轮次的状态标签。MCR-bench 中的每个任务都配有细粒度的缺陷元数据（如描述、类型、严重程度）以及动态状态标注，刻画了缺陷在多轮过程中的完整演化轨迹。我们在 MCR-bench 上对主流 LLM 进行了大量实验，得到若干发现。(1) 整体能力有限：实验显示主流 LLM 在缺陷检测与缺陷生命周期状态跟踪上的整体表现有限，且随着交互轮数增加性能显著下降；(2) 对缺陷敏感的表现：LLM 的表现在不同缺陷类型与严重程度上差异显著，语义复杂或显著性低的缺陷更容易被漏检；(3) 潜在失效机制：我们深入的错误分析剖析了误报与漏报各自的驱动因素，揭示了诸如跨轮次时间错位与长程记忆不足等关键弱点。","tl":"首个带缺陷状态标注的多轮代码评审基准，暴露 LLM 跨轮退化。","au":["Dewu Zheng","Yanlin Wang","Xiwen Wang","Kefeng Duan","Hongyu Zhang","Xilin Liu","Yuchi Ma","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based"],"kw":["code review","multi-round interaction","benchmark","defect state tracking","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/128/x"},{"id":"p01411","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Rust's Type Checker Implementation is Unsound: An Empirical Study on Soundness Bugs in rustc","tz":"Rust 的类型检查器实现并不健全：对 rustc 健全性缺陷的实证研究","a":"Rust is claimed to be a type-sound language capable of preventing various undesirable behaviors, including memory bugs. However, rustc , the official Rust compiler, is not immune to defects; it contains soundness bugs , where the compiler accepts programs that should be rejected during type checking. In this work, we present an empirical study of 23 issues that report potential soundness bugs in rustc , collected from the GitHub issue tracker between January 1, 2022 and September 1, 2025. We analyze each issue in depth, focusing on its affected feature , symptom (how the feature is mishandled), consequence (the resulting undesirable behavior), triggering features , community consensus regarding whether it is a bug, and lifecycle , including introduction, discovery, and fix. Furthermore, we investigate existing artifacts, including implementations such as Miri, Chalk, and a-mir-formality, alongside documentation such as the Rust Reference, the FLS, and Rust RFCs to assess their potential as oracles for testing the type soundness of rustc . Our key findings indicate that: (1) Certain soundness bugs, typically triggered by implied bounds or trait objects , compromise memory safety. (2) Sound type checking is challenged by edge cases involving associated types and the interaction between lifetimes and traits . (3) Most bugs persist from the initial introduction of the relevant features and require significant time to be discovered. (4) While Miri can detect soundness bugs that lead to memory bugs, a-mir-formality and Chalk are currently immature despite their potential to identify other bug categories. (5) Existing documentation frequently fails to provide precise explanations of the language semantics.","az":"Rust 被宣称是一种类型健全的语言，能够防止各种不良行为，包括内存缺陷。然而，官方 Rust 编译器 rustc 并非没有缺陷；它存在健全性缺陷，即编译器接受了本应在类型检查阶段被拒绝的程序。在本工作中，我们对 2022 年 1 月 1 日至 2025 年 9 月 1 日期间从 GitHub issue 跟踪器收集的 23 个报告潜在健全性缺陷的 issue 开展了实证研究。我们深入分析每个 issue，重点关注其受影响的语言特性、症状（该特性被如何错误处理）、后果（由此产生的不良行为）、触发特性、社区对其是否为缺陷的共识，以及生命周期（包括引入、发现与修复）。此外，我们考察了现有制品，包括 Miri、Chalk 和 a-mir-formality 等实现，以及 Rust Reference、FLS 和 Rust RFC 等文档，以评估它们作为测试 rustc 类型健全性的预言的潜力。我们的主要发现表明：(1) 某些健全性缺陷，通常由隐含边界（implied bounds）或 trait 对象触发，会破坏内存安全；(2) 健全的类型检查受到涉及关联类型、以及生命周期与 trait 之间交互的边界情形的挑战；(3) 大多数缺陷自相关特性最初引入时就存在，并需要相当长时间才被发现；(4) 尽管 Miri 能够检测导致内存缺陷的健全性缺陷，a-mir-formality 与 Chalk 虽有识别其他缺陷类别的潜力，但目前仍不成熟；(5) 现有文档常常无法对语言语义给出精确解释。","tl":"系统剖析 rustc 23 个类型健全性缺陷及现有预言的可用性。","au":["Yusung Sim","Sukyoung Ryu","Jaemin Hong"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Rust","type soundness bugs","rustc","empirical study","test oracle"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/129/x"},{"id":"p01412","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Solving String Split Constraints via Structural Relaxation","tz":"通过结构松弛求解字符串 split 约束","a":"String operations are integral to program analysis, yet reasoning about the ubiquitous split operation remains a challenge. SMT solvers have difficulty with split because it transforms a string into a variable-length sequence, creating a structural mismatch that leads to uninterpreted abstractions or unsound bounded approximations. In this paper, we bridge this gap with a precise, SMT-LIB-compliant encoding. Our key insight is structural relaxation: exploiting the sparsity of real-world constraints, we decouple the split structure from strict length requirements, materializing segments only on demand. We further introduce position-aware constraints to handle complex regex-based delimiters without overlaps. We evaluated our framework on 580 benchmarks using four leading string solvers. Our encoding enables off-the-shelf solvers to handle split constraints, solving 157 out of 168 real-world benchmarks and outperforming current baselines. Notably, our framework involves complex string operations, thereby revealing 12 previously unknown implementation bugs in mainstream solvers.","az":"字符串操作是程序分析不可或缺的一部分，然而对无处不在的 split 操作进行推理仍然困难。SMT 求解器难以处理 split，因为它将一个字符串转换为变长序列，造成结构上的不匹配，从而导致未解释的抽象或不健全的有界近似。本文通过一种精确且符合 SMT-LIB 规范的编码弥合了这一差距。我们的关键洞见是结构松弛：利用真实世界约束的稀疏性，我们将 split 结构与严格的长度要求解耦，仅按需物化各个片段。我们进一步引入位置感知约束，以处理复杂的基于正则表达式的分隔符而不产生重叠。我们使用四款领先的字符串求解器在 580 个基准上评估了我们的框架。我们的编码使现成的求解器能够处理 split 约束，在 168 个真实世界基准中求解了 157 个，优于当前基线。值得注意的是，我们的框架涉及复杂的字符串操作，因而揭示了主流求解器中 12 个此前未知的实现缺陷。","tl":"结构松弛加按需物化，让现成 SMT 求解器精确处理 split 约束。","au":["Rui Han","Ziheng Wang","Baoquan Cui","Yuhang Dong","Fuqi Jia","Feifei Ma","Jian Zhang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["string constraints","split operation","SMT solving","structural relaxation","SMT-LIB encoding"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/130/x"},{"id":"p01413","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Augmenting Multi-Technique Static Analysis with Large Language Models: A Neuro-Symbolic Approach to Smart Contract Vulnerability Detection","tz":"用大语言模型增强多技术静态分析：面向智能合约漏洞检测的神经符号方法","a":"Smart contracts facilitate and enforce agreements between untrusted parties without trusted intermediaries, but vulnerabilities within contracts can cause severe damage once exploited. Various analysis techniques have been proposed for vulnerability detection, but they are typically limited to specific vulnerability types. While recent frameworks employ aggregation to broaden detection capacity, they often accumulate false positives due to loose integration that fails to resolve underlying conflicts. Meanwhile, the semantic reasoning capacity of large language models (LLMs) has shown promise in detecting vulnerabilities, despite inherent reasoning bottlenecks and hallucinations. Recognizing these challenges, in this work, we propose a novel neuro-symbolic approach, named Ensemble LLM-assisted Static Analysis (ELSA). ELSA comprises two key modules, namely, LLM-assisted static analysis and analyzer ensemble (the ensemble of multiple LLM-assisted static analyzers), each incorporating two distinct strategies. The LLM-assisted static analysis augments individual analysis techniques with constraint-guided neural semantic reasoning, while the analyzer ensemble resolves conflicting outputs to distill a robust consensus. We evaluate ELSA on a comprehensive benchmark, including three open-source datasets and additional self-constructed Zero-Knowledge Proof-based smart contracts whose complexity poses unique challenges to static analysis. Experimental results demonstrate that our approach significantly outperforms baselines and advanced mainstream approaches, effectively bridging semantic gaps and synergizing the complementary advantages of different analyzers. Furthermore, an ablation study and fine-grained analysis are conducted to investigate the key factors contributing to overall performance gains.","az":"智能合约无需可信中介即可在互不信任的各方之间促成并强制执行协议，但合约中的漏洞一旦被利用就可能造成严重损失。已有多种分析技术被提出用于漏洞检测，但它们通常局限于特定漏洞类型。尽管近期一些框架采用聚合来拓宽检测能力，但由于松散集成无法解决底层冲突，它们往往累积误报。与此同时，大语言模型（LLM）的语义推理能力在漏洞检测上展现出潜力，尽管存在固有的推理瓶颈与幻觉问题。认识到这些挑战，我们在本工作中提出一种新颖的神经符号方法，名为集成 LLM 辅助静态分析（ELSA）。ELSA 包含两个关键模块，即 LLM 辅助静态分析与分析器集成（多个 LLM 辅助静态分析器的集成），每个模块各自包含两种不同策略。LLM 辅助静态分析以约束引导的神经语义推理增强单个分析技术，而分析器集成则解决相互冲突的输出以提炼出稳健的共识。我们在一个综合基准上评估 ELSA，该基准包括三个开源数据集，以及额外自建的、其复杂性给静态分析带来独特挑战的基于零知识证明的智能合约。实验结果表明，我们的方法显著优于基线与先进的主流方法，有效弥合了语义鸿沟并协同发挥了不同分析器的互补优势。此外，我们还开展了消融实验与细粒度分析，以探究带来整体性能提升的关键因素。","tl":"用约束引导的 LLM 推理增强并集成多种静态分析器消解冲突。","au":["Junxiang Wang","Fu Song","Miaomiao Zhang","Bowen Du","Rongcan Pei"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract vulnerability detection","neuro-symbolic","static analysis ensemble","LLM reasoning","zero-knowledge proof contracts"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/131/x"},{"id":"p01414","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Rethinking Mixture-of-Experts for Vulnerability Detection: An Empirical Study and Improved Design","tz":"反思用于漏洞检测的专家混合模型：一项实证研究与改进设计","a":"Deep learning–based vulnerability detection (DLVD) has recently adopted the Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) paradigm to address vulnerability heterogeneity and the long-tailed distribution of Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) categories. A representative framework, MoEVD, builds CWE-specific experts and a router for expert selection, but its assumptions about expert specialization and routing reliability remain underexplored. We reproduce MoEVD under the same dataset, splits, backbone, and evaluation protocol, and conduct a fine-grained empirical study of expert behavior and routing decisions. We find that CWE-based experts do not consistently develop stable or exclusive specialization, and their effectiveness is highly sensitive to non-target vulnerabilities, while router misassignment is non-negligible and disproportionately routes non-vulnerable samples to a few experts, increasing false positives. These results reveal structural limitations in the original design. Guided by these insights, we relax strict CWE-based expert binding to enable more abstract specialization and replace fixed top-k routing with probability-mass-based top-p selection and an OR-style voting rule. On BigVul, the combined design improves F1 from 0.38 to 0.42 and recall from 0.32 to 0.39 without sacrificing precision, showing that principled adjustments to expert construction and routing can outperform the original MoEVD framework.","az":"基于深度学习的漏洞检测（DLVD）近来采用专家混合（MoE）范式来应对漏洞的异质性以及常见缺陷枚举（CWE）类别的长尾分布。一个代表性框架 MoEVD 构建了 CWE 专用的专家和用于专家选择的路由器，但其关于专家专精化与路由可靠性的假设仍缺乏探究。我们在相同的数据集、划分、骨干模型和评估协议下复现了 MoEVD，并对专家行为与路由决策开展了细粒度的实证研究。我们发现，基于 CWE 的专家并不能持续形成稳定或排他的专精化，其有效性对非目标漏洞高度敏感；同时路由器的错误分配不可忽视，并且不成比例地把非漏洞样本路由到少数几个专家，从而增加误报。这些结果揭示了原始设计中的结构性局限。在这些洞见指导下，我们放松了严格的基于 CWE 的专家绑定以支持更抽象的专精化，并用基于概率质量的 top-p 选择与 OR 式投票规则替换固定的 top-k 路由。在 BigVul 上，组合后的设计将 F1 从 0.38 提升到 0.42、召回率从 0.32 提升到 0.39，且未牺牲精确率，表明对专家构建与路由的有原则的调整可以超越原始的 MoEVD 框架。","tl":"复现揭示 CWE 专家未真正专精，改用 top-p 路由与投票提升 F1。","au":["Rongze Jiang","Chaofeng Sha","Xin Peng"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["reproducibility-replication","empirical-study"],"kw":["vulnerability detection","Mixture-of-Experts","routing","CWE","replication"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/132/x"},{"id":"p01415","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RecurIC3: Exploiting Structural Lemma Reuse to Accelerate IC3","tz":"RecurIC3：利用结构性引理复用加速 IC3","a":"IC3/PDR has become a widely adopted technique for safety model checking due to its high efficiency. Despite its success, the algorithm often suffers from redundant exploration due to the lack of a cross-level memory mechanism. This results in the repetitive discovery of highly similar CTIs (Counterexamples to Induction), forcing the solver to waste computational effort traversing overlapping blocking chains. We propose RecurIC3, a framework that alleviates this bottleneck via structural reuse. RecurIC3 maintains a Bad State Tree (G {bad}) that persistently records CTIs together with their level-aligned predecessor–successor links along blocking chains, turning the blocking phase into a history-aware process. To reduce solver calls, RecurIC3 first retrieves and rechecks lightweight candidates from G {bad}, and falls back to solver queries only when reuse is exhausted.This approach can significantly reduce the search space, thereby enhancing the verification efficiency of IC3. We implemented RecurIC3 in the state-of-the-art model checker Kind2 and evaluated it on the official benchmark suite. On instances where reuse is triggered, RecurIC3 reduces the number of explored tree nodes by 27%, achieves a 1.42 cumulative speedup, and solves 16 additional instances (13 safe and 3 unsafe) within the same timeout. These results suggest that structural reuse can substantially accelerate IC3.","az":"由于效率高，IC3/PDR 已成为被广泛采用的安全性模型检验技术。尽管取得了成功，该算法常因缺乏跨层记忆机制而遭受冗余探索之苦。这导致高度相似的 CTI（归纳反例）被反复发现，迫使求解器在遍历相互重叠的阻塞链上浪费计算资源。我们提出 RecurIC3，一个通过结构复用缓解这一瓶颈的框架。RecurIC3 维护一棵坏状态树（G_bad），持久记录 CTI 及其沿阻塞链的层级对齐的前驱—后继链接，把阻塞阶段转变为一个具有历史感知的过程。为减少求解器调用，RecurIC3 首先从 G_bad 中检索并重新检查轻量级候选，仅在复用耗尽时才回退到求解器查询。该方法可显著缩减搜索空间，从而提升 IC3 的验证效率。我们在最先进的模型检验器 Kind2 中实现了 RecurIC3，并在官方基准套件上进行了评估。在触发复用的实例上，RecurIC3 将探索的树节点数量减少 27%，取得 1.42 倍的累计加速，并在相同超时限制内多求解 16 个实例（13 个安全、3 个不安全）。这些结果表明，结构复用可以显著加速 IC3。","tl":"用坏状态树记录 CTI 实现跨层引理复用，显著加速 IC3。","au":["Yuhan Li","Liangze Yin","Xinyi Gong","Liu Minghao","Tun Li","Wei Dong","Ji Wang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["IC3 / PDR","model checking","lemma reuse","counterexample to induction","Kind2"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/133/x"},{"id":"p01416","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CausalRepair: Bridging the Causality Gap in Large Language Model-based Automated Program Repair via Dual-Slicing","tz":"CausalRepair：通过双重切片弥合基于大语言模型的自动程序修复中的因果性鸿沟","a":"Automated Program Repair (APR) aims to automatically fix buggy programs. In recent years, with the rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs), LLM-based APR techniques have achieved significant progress. Despite their potential, the effectiveness of LLMs relies heavily on the quality of the provided repair context. However, existing LLM-based APR approaches suffer from a causality gap when constructing such contexts. Specifically, on the test side, existing methods struggle with test context ambiguity arising from noise interference or dependency absence; meanwhile, on the source side, existing retrieval-augmented methods primarily rely on static analysis inevitably introduce static over-approximation, resulting in contexts filled with unexecuted code and noise. Consequently, these contexts mislead LLMs, hindering them from identifying the true root cause and leading to incorrect fixes. To bridge this gap, we introduce the concept of minimal causal context, defined as the essential set of dependencies required to explain a specific failure. Based on this, we propose CausalRepair, a novel conversation-driven APR framework that instantiates this concept through a synergistic dual-slicing strategy. Specifically, CausalRepair employs context-aware static slicing on the test side to purify test semantics, and utilizes execution-trace-based dynamic slicing on the source side to capture precise runtime dependencies. This constructs a high-quality context causally relevant to the bug, which filters out irrelevant code and guides the iterative repair process. We evaluate CausalRepair on the widely used Defects4J (V1.2 and V2.0) and the latest Defects4J-Trans benchmarks. To ensure a fair comparison, we unify the backbone model as DeepSeek-V3 in all experiments. The results demonstrate that CausalRepair correctly fixes 313 bugs on Defects4J, significantly outperforming state-of-the-art approaches such as ReinFix and TSAPR, while reducing the average repair cost to $0.029 per bug, achieving a dual optimization of effectiveness and efficiency.","az":"自动程序修复（APR）旨在自动修复有缺陷的程序。近年来，随着大语言模型（LLM）的迅速发展，基于 LLM 的 APR 技术取得了显著进展。尽管潜力巨大，LLM 的有效性严重依赖所提供修复上下文的质量。然而，现有基于 LLM 的 APR 方法在构建此类上下文时存在因果性鸿沟。具体而言，在测试一侧，现有方法难以应对由噪声干扰或依赖缺失所引起的测试上下文歧义；同时在源码一侧，现有的检索增强方法主要依赖静态分析，不可避免地引入静态过近似，导致上下文中充满未被执行的代码与噪声。因此，这些上下文会误导 LLM，妨碍其识别真正的根因，从而导致错误修复。为弥合这一鸿沟，我们引入最小因果上下文的概念，将其定义为解释某个特定失败所需的本质依赖集合。基于此，我们提出 CausalRepair，一个新颖的、由对话驱动的 APR 框架，通过协同的双重切片策略实例化该概念。具体而言，CausalRepair 在测试一侧采用上下文感知的静态切片以净化测试语义，并在源码一侧利用基于执行轨迹的动态切片以捕获精确的运行时依赖。这构建出与缺陷因果相关的高质量上下文，过滤掉无关代码并指导迭代修复过程。我们在广泛使用的 Defects4J（V1.2 与 V2.0）以及最新的 Defects4J-Trans 基准上评估 CausalRepair。为确保公平比较，所有实验中我们统一以 DeepSeek-V3 作为骨干模型。结果表明，CausalRepair 在 Defects4J 上正确修复了 313 个缺陷，显著优于 ReinFix 和 TSAPR 等最先进方法，同时将平均修复成本降至每个缺陷 0.029 美元，实现了效果与效率的双重优化。","tl":"静态加动态双重切片构建最小因果修复上下文，修复 313 个缺陷。","au":["Linhao Wu","Yizhou Chen","Zhen Yang","Pengyu Xue","Dan Hao"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["automated program repair","program slicing","execution trace","Defects4J","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/134/x"},{"id":"p01417","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards Understanding the Bugs in Verilator, a Hardware Description Language Compiler","tz":"理解硬件描述语言编译器 Verilator 中的缺陷","a":"Verilator is the premier open-source Hardware Description Language (HDL) compiler. It transforms Verilog and SystemVerilog designs into optimized C++ or SystemC models, enabling high-speed, cycle-accurate simulation prior to large-scale production. As a cornerstone of the hardware verification ecosystem, the correctness of Verilator is paramount; compiler faults can lead to silent simulation errors or unexpected failures, undermining the integrity of the hardware development lifecycle. Unlike traditional software compilers, HDL compilers manage unique concurrency and synthesis semantics, potentially introducing distinct bug patterns and complexities. However, while prior research has explored testing techniques for HDL toolchains, there remains a lack of systematic empirical studies characterizing the specific nature of bugs in Verilator. This knowledge gap hinders the development of targeted improvements in compiler robustness and testing strategies. To address this, we present the first comprehensive empirical study of Verilator bugs. We manually collected, analyzed, and categorized a dataset of 488 confirmed bugs from the official repository over three years. Our study investigates bug symptoms, root causes, and the characteristics of triggering test cases, while also evaluating the effectiveness of existing testing techniques. Based on our findings, we provide actionable guidance for developers to enhance Verilator’s reliability and for researchers to design more effective automated testing methodologies for HDL compilers.","az":"Verilator 是最主要的开源硬件描述语言（HDL）编译器。它将 Verilog 与 SystemVerilog 设计转换为优化的 C++ 或 SystemC 模型，从而在大规模量产前实现高速、周期精确的仿真。作为硬件验证生态的基石，Verilator 的正确性至关重要；编译器故障可能导致静默的仿真错误或意外失败，破坏硬件开发生命周期的完整性。与传统软件编译器不同，HDL 编译器需要处理独特的并发与综合语义，可能引入不同的缺陷模式与复杂性。然而，尽管已有研究探索了 HDL 工具链的测试技术，仍缺乏系统性的实证研究来刻画 Verilator 中缺陷的具体性质。这一知识空白阻碍了针对性地提升编译器健壮性与测试策略。为此，我们呈现首个关于 Verilator 缺陷的全面实证研究。我们从官方仓库中人工收集、分析并归类了三年间 488 个已确认的缺陷。我们的研究考察了缺陷症状、根本原因以及触发测试用例的特征，同时评估了现有测试技术的有效性。基于我们的发现，我们为开发者提供了增强 Verilator 可靠性的可操作指导，也为研究者设计更有效的 HDL 编译器自动化测试方法提供了参考。","tl":"首个 Verilator 488 个缺陷的症状与根因分类实证研究。","au":["Songyan Jiang","Maolin Sun","Kang Chen","Qingyang Li","Yibiao Yang","Yuming Zhou"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["empirical-study","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["Verilator","HDL compiler bugs","empirical study","bug taxonomy","compiler testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/135/x"},{"id":"p01418","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DeepSCA: Dependency-Aware Software Composition Analysis for C/C++ Based on a Curated Code Feature Database","tz":"DeepSCA：基于精选代码特征数据库的依赖感知 C/C++ 软件成分分析","a":"Software Composition Analysis (SCA) identifies reused third-party libraries (TPLs) and their dependencies, forming the basis of Software Bills of Materials (SBOMs) for securing software supply chain. Current C/C++ SCA techniques extract code features and match them against a TPL feature database. However, detection recall is limited by feature database coverage, and two key challenges remain: (1) Coverage-Precision Trade-off: Feature databases built from a single repository (e.g., GitHub) often yield high false negatives, as C/C++ TPLs are inherently distributed across diverse hosting platforms (e.g., Debian, ArchLinux, and Xrepo), each offering partially overlapping yet distinct sets of TPLs. Although a multi-repository feature database improves TPL coverage, it inevitably introduces numerous shared functions (e.g., cross-TPL code clones) that map to a broader set of candidate origins. When coupled with the limitations of existing SCA techniques in tracing provenance, this ambiguity further increases false positives. (2) Neglected Dependency Context: Existing SCA techniques primarily focus on detecting reused TPLs but often overlook their inter-dependencies. However, license compatibility constraints are inherently determined by directed dependency relationships among TPLs. DeepSCA addresses Challenge 1 by constructing a feature database with 66,143,596 functions extracted from 33,100 C/C++ TPLs, covering nine mainstream hosting repositories. To reduce false positives from shared functions, DeepSCA groups TPLs with shared code, and uses uniqueness scores to trace functions to their origins—ensuring high precision without sacrificing recall. To overcome Challenge 2, DeepSCA generates the dependency graph from the detected TPLs. it resolves filename ambiguity by simulating compiler header search paths and mitigates symbol ambiguity via namespace-aware resolution, enabling accurate file-level dependency mapping to TPLs. Evaluated on a ground-truth dataset of 335 OpenHarmony projects (10,583 TPLs, 64,200 dependencies), DeepSCA achieves 85.6% precision and 87.3% recall for TPL detection, outperforming state-of-the-art tools (e.g., 16.8% precision and 21.1% recall improvement over TPLite). Its dependency graphs reach 91.8% precision, surpassing Cneps by 11.3%. Moreover, the dependency graph generated by DeepSCA uncovers previously hidden combinations of license incompatibility issues in real-world projects.","az":"软件成分分析（SCA）识别被复用的第三方库（TPL）及其依赖关系，构成了保障软件供应链安全的软件物料清单（SBOM）的基础。当前的 C/C++ SCA 技术提取代码特征并与 TPL 特征数据库进行匹配。然而，检测召回率受限于特征数据库的覆盖范围，并且仍存在两个关键挑战：（1）覆盖率—精确率权衡：由单一仓库（如 GitHub）构建的特征数据库常常产生大量漏报，因为 C/C++ 的 TPL 本质上分散在多样的托管平台（如 Debian、ArchLinux 和 Xrepo）上，每个平台提供部分重叠但又各不相同的 TPL 集合。尽管多仓库特征数据库提升了 TPL 覆盖率，它不可避免地引入大量共享函数（如跨 TPL 代码克隆），这些函数会映射到更广泛的候选来源集合。再加上现有 SCA 技术在追溯来源方面的局限，这种歧义进一步增加了误报。（2）被忽视的依赖上下文：现有 SCA 技术主要关注检测被复用的 TPL，却常常忽视它们之间的相互依赖关系。然而，许可证兼容性约束本质上由 TPL 之间的有向依赖关系决定。DeepSCA 通过构建一个特征数据库来应对挑战 1，该数据库从覆盖九个主流托管仓库的 33,100 个 C/C++ TPL 中提取了 66,143,596 个函数。为减少由共享函数带来的误报，DeepSCA 将具有共享代码的 TPL 分组，并使用唯一性得分将函数追溯到其来源——在不牺牲召回率的前提下确保高精确率。为克服挑战 2，DeepSCA 从检测到的 TPL 生成依赖图；它通过模拟编译器头文件搜索路径解决文件名歧义，并通过命名空间感知的解析缓解符号歧义，从而实现准确的文件级到 TPL 的依赖映射。在包含 335 个 OpenHarmony 项目（10,583 个 TPL、64,200 条依赖）的真值数据集上评估，DeepSCA 在 TPL 检测上取得 85.6% 的精确率和 87.3% 的召回率，优于最先进工具（例如相比 TPLite 精确率提升 16.8%、召回率提升 21.1%）。其依赖图达到 91.8% 的精确率，超过 Cneps 11.3%。此外，DeepSCA 生成的依赖图揭示了真实项目中此前隐藏的许可证不兼容组合问题。","tl":"跨九个仓库建库加唯一性溯源与依赖图，提升 C/C++ SCA 精度。","au":["Meiqiu Xu","Xibin Zhao","Wenxuan Yu","Zhiliang Zhu","Li Li","Heqing Huang","Ying Wang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["software composition analysis","third-party libraries","SBOM","dependency graph","license compatibility"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/136/x"},{"id":"p01419","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"MalTotal: Cost-Effective and Language-Agnostic Malicious Code Poisoning Detection for Millions of Repositories","tz":"MalTotal：面向百万级仓库的高性价比且语言无关的恶意代码投毒检测","a":"The widespread adoption of open source software (OSS) has revolutionized modern application development, but has also introduced significant security challenges. Malicious code poisoning attacks have escalated in both frequency and sophistication, targeting public package registries and open-source platforms like GitHub. Existing detection methods, including heuristic-based, learning-based, and LLM-based approaches, face key limitations such as reliance on language-specific designs, poor generalization, and high computational costs, which make them unsuitable for large-scale and multi-language analysis. To address these gaps, we propose MalTotal, a scalable and cost-effective framework for language-agnostic malicious code detection. By leveraging LLM-assisted semantic reasoning, MalTotal identifies sensitive API in built-in and third-party libraries, performs hybrid semantic slicing to reconstruct malicious behavior contexts, and significantly reduces token consumption for large-scale analysis. Extensive evaluations demonstrate that MalTotal outperforms 8 state-of-the-art baselines, achieving an average F1-score of 93.1% across 5 mainstream programming languages. Furthermore, MalTotal’s hybrid slicing strategy reduces LLM token consumption by 94.0%, lowering the cost of analysis from $86.25 to $5.19 on 2,168 repositories. In a large-scale study of 120K GitHub repositories containing over 7.3 million files, MalTotal identified 564 previously unknown malicious repositories across multiple languages at a total cost of just $338. These results demonstrate MalTotal’s effectiveness, scalability, and cost-efficiency, highlighting its potential to mitigate code poisoning attacks in large-scale codebases.","az":"开源软件（OSS）的广泛采用变革了现代应用开发，但也带来了重大的安全挑战。恶意代码投毒攻击在频率和复杂度上均不断升级，瞄准公共包注册中心和 GitHub 等开源平台。现有检测方法（包括基于启发式、基于学习和基于 LLM 的方法）面临关键局限，例如依赖语言特定的设计、泛化能力差以及计算成本高，这些使它们不适用于大规模、多语言分析。为弥补这些空白，我们提出 MalTotal，一个可扩展且高性价比的语言无关恶意代码检测框架。通过利用 LLM 辅助的语义推理，MalTotal 识别内置库与第三方库中的敏感 API，执行混合语义切片以重建恶意行为上下文，并显著降低大规模分析的 token 消耗。大量评估表明，MalTotal 优于 8 个最先进基线，在 5 种主流编程语言上取得 93.1% 的平均 F1 分数。此外，MalTotal 的混合切片策略将 LLM token 消耗降低 94.0%，把在 2,168 个仓库上的分析成本从 86.25 美元降至 5.19 美元。在对包含超过 730 万个文件的 12 万个 GitHub 仓库的大规模研究中，MalTotal 以仅 338 美元的总成本，跨多种语言识别出 564 个此前未知的恶意仓库。这些结果证明了 MalTotal 的有效性、可扩展性与成本效率，凸显了其缓解大规模代码库中代码投毒攻击的潜力。","tl":"混合语义切片把 LLM 成本降 94%，在 12 万仓库中挖出 564 个恶意库。","au":["Jian Zhao","Shenao Wang","Qingyang Wu","Yanjie Zhao","Xiao Cheng","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["malicious code detection","code poisoning","software supply chain","semantic slicing","language-agnostic"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/137/x"},{"id":"p01420","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Repair-Driven Greybox Fuzzing","tz":"修复驱动的灰盒模糊测试","a":"We present repair-driven greybox fuzzing, a new approach to greybox fuzzing that combines the strengths of unstructured, byte-level input mutation and grammar-guided input generation. By increasing input diversity while preserving input validity, repair-driven fuzzing promises to improve bug-finding ability for systems under test such as programming language interpreters that consume highly structured inputs. Our idea is to first mutate an input using a standard byte-level mutator, typically leading to an invalid input, and then repair the input using a grammar. Aggressively breaking and then repairing an input provides an effective way to reach parts of the input space that would be left unexplored by both byte-level and idiomatic grammar-based mutations. We put this idea into practice via RepairFuzz, a new greybox fuzzer based on AFL++, leveraging the byte level mutations of AFL++ and using the CPCT+ error recovery algorithm for input repair. We present a large experimental evaluation applying RepairFuzz to six SUTs covering four different programming language input formats (Lua, PHP, JavaScript and Ruby), and present an experimental comparison with AFL++, Nautilus, and Grammarinator, the state-of-the-art in standard greybox fuzzing and grammar-guided fuzzing. Our evaluation shows that RepairFuzz was able to find 10 confirmed bugs that were previously-unknown, including 9 that could not be found using Nautilus, Grammarinator, or AFL++ directly or in combination. Further, RepairFuzz yields absolute increases in code coverage for several SUTs and substantial complementary code coverage across all.","az":"我们提出修复驱动的灰盒模糊测试，这是一种将非结构化的字节级输入变异与语法引导的输入生成二者优势相结合的新型灰盒模糊测试方法。通过在保持输入有效性的同时提升输入多样性，修复驱动的模糊测试有望提升对消费高度结构化输入的被测系统（如编程语言解释器）的查错能力。我们的想法是：先用标准的字节级变异器对输入进行变异（这通常会产生无效输入），然后使用语法对该输入进行修复。激进地破坏再修复输入，提供了一种有效方式去触达那些字节级变异与惯常的基于语法的变异都无法探索的输入空间区域。我们通过 RepairFuzz 将这一想法付诸实践，这是一个基于 AFL++ 的新型灰盒模糊测试工具，利用 AFL++ 的字节级变异，并使用 CPCT+ 错误恢复算法进行输入修复。我们开展了大规模实验评估，将 RepairFuzz 应用于覆盖四种不同编程语言输入格式（Lua、PHP、JavaScript 和 Ruby）的六个被测系统，并与标准灰盒模糊测试和语法引导模糊测试的最先进工具 AFL++、Nautilus 和 Grammarinator 进行了实验比较。我们的评估表明，RepairFuzz 能够发现 10 个已确认的此前未知缺陷，其中 9 个无法被 Nautilus、Grammarinator 或 AFL++ 单独或组合使用发现。此外，RepairFuzz 在若干被测系统上带来了代码覆盖率的绝对提升，并在所有被测系统上带来了可观的互补覆盖。","tl":"先字节变异打碎输入再按语法修复，兼得多样性与有效性。","au":["Bachir Bendrissou","Alastair F. Donaldson","Cristian Cadar"],"top":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["greybox fuzzing","grammar-based repair","input mutation","AFL++","language interpreters"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/138/x"},{"id":"p01421","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CLIR: Liveness-Driven and Structure-Aware Fuzzing for the Cranelift Compiler","tz":"CLIR：面向 Cranelift 编译器的活跃性驱动与结构感知模糊测试","a":"Modern compilers are complex software systems that must correctly translate high-level programming languages into machine code across multiple architectures. Cranelift, a fast and modern compiler backend originally developed for WebAssembly and recently adopted as an experimental backend for Rust, has gained increasing importance due to its superior compilation speed compared to LLVM and comprehensive multi-architecture support, including x86-64, AArch64, s390x, and RISCV64. However, despite decades of development in compiler testing, testing Cranelift still illustrates unique challenges, i.e., (1) constructing valid IR under the strict enforcement of SSA form, (2) generating sequences with sufficient computational density to stress backend components, and (3) balancing broad backend coverage with efficient root cause analysis across heterogeneous architectures. To address these challenges, we propose CLIR, a differential testing framework that integrates a syntax-preserving hierarchical generation strategy to guarantee SSA validity, a liveness-guided instruction refinement mechanism to maximize computational density, and a diagnosis-guided cross-architecture adaptation scheme to facilitate efficient root cause analysis across heterogeneous backends. Our comprehensive evaluation demonstrates that CLIR significantly outperforms existing state-of-the-art baselines, detecting 8×, 24×, and 8× more unique bugs than them, i.e., cranelift-fuzzgen, wasm-smith, and WASMaker, respectively, while RustSmith even uncovered zero bugs. Consequently, within 72 hours of testing, CLIR discovered 24 bugs, with 21 confirmed and 9 fixed spanning all target architectures.","az":"现代编译器是复杂的软件系统，必须在多种架构上正确地把高级编程语言翻译为机器码。Cranelift 是一个快速、现代的编译器后端，最初为 WebAssembly 开发，近期被采纳为 Rust 的实验性后端；由于其相比 LLVM 更优的编译速度以及对多架构（包括 x86-64、AArch64、s390x 和 RISCV64）的全面支持，它的重要性日益提升。然而，尽管编译器测试已有数十年的发展，测试 Cranelift 仍存在独特挑战，即：(1) 在 SSA 形式被严格强制的前提下构造有效的 IR；(2) 生成具有足够计算密度以对后端组件施加压力的指令序列；(3) 在广泛的后端覆盖与跨异构架构的高效根因分析之间取得平衡。为应对这些挑战，我们提出 CLIR，一个差分测试框架，它集成了保持语法的层次化生成策略以确保 SSA 有效性、活跃性引导的指令精化机制以最大化计算密度，以及诊断引导的跨架构适配方案以促进在异构后端上的高效根因分析。我们的全面评估表明，CLIR 显著优于现有最先进基线，分别比 cranelift-fuzzgen、wasm-smith 和 WASMaker 多检测出 8 倍、24 倍和 8 倍的独特缺陷，而 RustSmith 甚至未发现任何缺陷。因此，在 72 小时的测试中，CLIR 发现了 24 个缺陷，其中 21 个已确认、9 个已修复，覆盖所有目标架构。","tl":"活跃性引导生成高计算密度 SSA IR，72 小时挖出 Cranelift 24 个缺陷。","au":["Shangtong Cao","Tianlei Song","Qiuping Yi","Tianyu Chen","Guoai Xu","Ningyu He","Haoyu Wang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Cranelift","compiler testing","differential testing","SSA IR generation","liveness-guided refinement"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/139/x"},{"id":"p01422","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Testing Static Taint Analyzers with Equivalence Modulo Taint","tz":"用“污点模等价”测试静态污点分析器","a":"Static taint analyzers are widely used to detect security vulnerabilities, yet their complexity makes them prone to soundness and precision bugs. Validating these analyzers is challenging because ground-truth taint flows are rarely available and differential testing requires multiple comparable tools. To address this challenge, we introduce Equivalence Modulo Taint (EMT), a testing oracle for static taint analysis that defines program equivalence in terms of preserved source-sink flows rather than full program semantics. EMT enables testing a single analyzer without ground-truth labels by checking consistency of reported flows across equivalent-modulo-taint program variants. Based on EMT, we present TaintCC, a framework that generates equivalent-modulo-taint variants through semantically equivalent, taint-oblivious, and taint-aware transformations targeting common sources of taint-analysis bugs. We evaluate TaintCC on four widely used analyzers—FlowDroid, Mariana Trench, Pysa, and Semgrep—and discover 16 unique bugs, demonstrating that even mature analyzers, whether academic or industrial, remain susceptible to reliability issues.","az":"静态污点分析器被广泛用于检测安全漏洞，但其复杂性使其容易出现健全性与精确性缺陷。验证这些分析器颇具挑战，因为真值污点流很少可得，而差分测试又需要多个可比较的工具。为应对这一挑战，我们引入污点模等价（Equivalence Modulo Taint，EMT），一种用于静态污点分析的测试预言：它以保持源—汇流为标准来定义程序等价，而非要求完整的程序语义等价。EMT 使得在没有真值标签的情况下也能测试单个分析器，方法是检查其在污点模等价的程序变体之间所报告流的一致性。基于 EMT，我们提出 TaintCC，一个通过语义等价的、污点无关的以及污点感知的变换来生成污点模等价变体的框架，这些变换针对污点分析缺陷的常见来源。我们在四款被广泛使用的分析器——FlowDroid、Mariana Trench、Pysa 和 Semgrep——上评估了 TaintCC，发现了 16 个独特缺陷，表明即便是成熟的分析器（无论学术界还是工业界）仍然存在可靠性问题。","tl":"提出污点模等价预言，无需真值即可测出污点分析器 16 个缺陷。","au":["Maria Christakis","Anastasia Isychev","Samuel Pilz","Florian Tesarek","Valentin Wüstholz"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["static taint analysis","testing analyzers","equivalence modulo taint","metamorphic oracle","FlowDroid"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/140/x","pu":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/ISSTA-2026.pdf"},{"id":"p01423","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"How Does Killing Surviving Mutants Help Detect Real Bugs with Assertion Generation? A Controlled Experiment","tz":"杀死存活变异体如何借助断言生成帮助发现真实缺陷？一项受控实验","a":"Killing surviving mutants is a central activity of mutation testing. This activity is motivated by the coupling-effect hypothesis: tests that expose simple artificial faults can also detect more complex, previously unseen real bugs. Despite these claimed benefits, automated studies have not directly measured the causal impact of mutant killing on real-bug detection. This limitation stems from open-ended mutant-killing strategies and a fundamental evaluation asymmetry that obscures causal attribution. In this work, we present the first large-scale controlled experiment that directly measures whether killing surviving mutants, without knowledge of future real bugs, would have enabled their detection. We model mutant killing as a selective, incremental process under realistic budget constraints, and we restrict test improvements to assertion augmentation. This restriction enables precise attribution of each test augmentation to a specific mutant-killing action. To support the experiment, we design a fully automated, fault-based assertion-augmentation technique that operates uniformly on mutants and real bugs and integrate it into Defects4J. Our controlled experiment yields several key empirical insights: (1) Across 642 Defects4J bugs, we find that 104 bugs would become detectable by adding an additional assertion to an existing passing, non-triggering test. (2) When coupling exists, a real bug is, on average, coupled with 21 surviving mutants, through which mutant killing can produce triggering tests. This number is substantially higher than the average of two mutants reported in prior studies. In those studies, coupling is inferred solely from documented bug-fixing tests rather than from tests derived via mutant killing. (3) Among these bugs, 63 of the 104 are detectable through principled mutant-killing (test augmentation) process. Notably, killing a randomly selected 30% of relevant surviving mutants, using only one assertion per mutant, suffices to detect 84.5% of these bugs. (4) By substituting mutants with real bugs and comparing their resulting assertion augmentation outputs, we find that real bugs induce broader behavioral effects than mutants, affecting more memory state locations, variables, and tests. (5) When mutation-derived assertions detect real bugs, they validate program outputs that overlap with, and are often strict subsets of, those affected by the real bugs. This offers a mechanistic explanation for why killing simple mutants can enable the detection of more complex real bugs.","az":"杀死存活变异体是变异测试的核心活动。这一活动由耦合效应假设所驱动：能够暴露简单人工故障的测试也能检测更复杂、此前未见的真实缺陷。尽管宣称有这些益处，自动化研究尚未直接测量杀死变异体对发现真实缺陷的因果影响。这一局限源于开放式的变异体杀死策略，以及一种根本性的评估不对称性，后者掩盖了因果归因。在本工作中，我们提出首个大规模受控实验，直接测量在不知晓未来真实缺陷的前提下杀死存活变异体是否本可以使这些缺陷被检测出来。我们将变异体杀死建模为在现实预算约束下的一种选择性、增量式过程，并将测试改进限制为断言增强。这一限制使得每一次测试增强都能被精确归因于某个具体的变异体杀死动作。为支撑该实验，我们设计了一种完全自动化的、基于故障的断言增强技术，它对变异体和真实缺陷一视同仁地运作，并将其集成到 Defects4J 中。我们的受控实验得出若干关键实证洞见：(1) 在 642 个 Defects4J 缺陷中，我们发现有 104 个缺陷只需向一个已有的、通过且未触发失败的测试中添加一条额外断言即可被检测出来。(2) 当耦合存在时，一个真实缺陷平均与 21 个存活变异体耦合，通过这些变异体，杀死变异体可以产生触发失败的测试。这一数字远高于以往研究报告的平均 2 个变异体。在那些研究中，耦合仅从有记录的缺陷修复测试推断，而非从通过杀死变异体导出的测试推断。(3) 在这些缺陷中，104 个里有 63 个可以通过有原则的变异体杀死（测试增强）过程被检测出来。值得注意的是，随机选取 30% 的相关存活变异体并对每个变异体仅使用一条断言加以杀死，就足以检测出这些缺陷中的 84.5%。(4) 通过用真实缺陷替换变异体并比较由此产生的断言增强输出，我们发现真实缺陷引发的行为影响比变异体更广，影响更多的内存状态位置、变量和测试。(5) 当由变异导出的断言检测到真实缺陷时，它们所校验的程序输出与真实缺陷所影响的输出存在重叠，且往往是后者的严格子集。这为“杀死简单变异体为何能促成更复杂真实缺陷的检测”提供了机制性解释。","tl":"受控实验首次因果量化杀变异体与真实缺陷检测的耦合机制。","au":["Hang Du","Vijay Krishna Palepu","James Jones"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["mutation testing","coupling effect","assertion augmentation","Defects4J","controlled experiment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/141/x"},{"id":"p01424","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"The Illusion of Success: Learning-Based Android Malware Detectors (Replicability Study)","tz":"成功的假象：基于学习的 Android 恶意软件检测器（可复现性研究）","a":"Machine learning (ML) approaches have shown impressive performance in Android malware detection and have become the scalable alternatives to signature and heuristic-based methods. ML-based detectors typically collect large amounts of benign and malware applications from popular data sources, split the collected dataset into training and testing subsets, train a binary classifier, and report test set performance. While these tools report 95%+ recall, several recent works have shed light on flaws in experiment setup or evaluation methods questioning the trustworthiness of their results. In an effort to further understand the true performance of the tools, we conduct a systematic literature review of tools and design large-scale longitudinal evaluation using widely used datasets and detection approaches. Even after carefully accounting for the known biases in experiment setup and evaluation, we observe that tools achieve significantly diverging classification performance (ranging from 56% to 94% recall) even on different subsets of the same dataset. Surprisingly, we also find that a deliberately flawed classifier that uses unreliable class package names as features performs nearly as good, sometimes better, than the set of tools we evaluated on these datasets, showing the untrustworthiness of tool-reported results. Our results further establish that there is still much room for improvement in ML-based AMD towards creating semantic-aware detectors and more reliable evaluation methodologies.","az":"机器学习（ML）方法在 Android 恶意软件检测中展现出令人印象深刻的性能，并已成为基于签名和启发式方法的可扩展替代方案。基于 ML 的检测器通常从流行数据源收集大量良性与恶意应用，将收集到的数据集划分为训练集与测试集，训练一个二分类器，并报告测试集性能。尽管这些工具报告了 95% 以上的召回率，近期若干工作揭示了其实验设置或评估方法中的缺陷，质疑其结果的可信度。为进一步理解这些工具的真实性能，我们开展了对相关工具的系统文献综述，并使用广泛使用的数据集与检测方法设计了大规模纵向评估。即便在仔细考虑了实验设置与评估中的已知偏差之后，我们仍观察到这些工具即使在同一数据集的不同子集上也取得了显著分化的分类性能（召回率从 56% 到 94% 不等）。令人惊讶的是，我们还发现一个故意设计得有缺陷的分类器——它使用不可靠的类包名作为特征——在这些数据集上的表现几乎与我们评估的这组工具一样好，有时甚至更好，显示出工具自报结果的不可信。我们的结果进一步表明，基于 ML 的 Android 恶意软件检测在构建语义感知检测器和更可靠的评估方法方面仍有很大改进空间。","tl":"纵向复现显示恶意软件检测器性能大幅波动，劣质特征也能打平。","au":["Michael Tegegn","Julia Rubin"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["reproducibility-replication","empirical-study","security"],"kw":["Android malware detection","machine learning","replicability study","evaluation bias","longitudinal evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/142/x"},{"id":"p01425","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"No One-Size-Fits-All: Adaptive Code Editing with Feature-Based Strategy Selection","tz":"没有万能方案：基于特征的策略选择实现自适应代码编辑","a":"Large language models have shown strong potential in automating code editing (CE) tasks, yet most existing systems rely on a fixed CE strategy (i.e., one-step, search-replace, and plan-apply) across diverse scenarios. In practice, CE tasks vary widely in code context, edit locality, and semantic complexity, causing no single strategy to perform consistently well. Moreover, systematic studies on the relationship between strategies and CE tasks remain scarce, limiting further optimization of LLM-based code editing strategies. To address this gap, we construct CEBench, comprising 500 real-world CE tasks curated from SWE-bench. Then we compare three representative CE strategies (one-step, search-replace, plan-apply). Our study reveals two key findings: (1) each strategy exhibits distinct advantages for specific CE tasks, with no universal optimality; (2) strategy effectiveness is significantly influenced by four core task features: total lines of code, modification type, modification scope, and task type. Motivated by these findings, we propose ACE, an adaptive code editing framework that dynamically selects optimal CE strategies based on task features. Unlike classifier-based or instruction-prompting approaches, Ace employs a fine-tuned LLM that learns feature-strategy mappings from empirical data to recommend strategies with interpretable rationales. Extensive experiments on our CEBench-verified show that ACE outperforms state-of-the-art baselines: it boosts Pass@1 by 15.2% while reducing token consumption by 26.3% compared to the best baseline (AutoCodeRover). Our strategy selector achieves 73.1% selection accuracy with 70.4% rationale accuracy (Cohen’s Kappa=0.802), providing transparent and trustworthy decision-making for developers.","az":"大语言模型在自动化代码编辑（CE）任务方面展现出强大潜力，然而大多数现有系统在各种场景下都依赖一种固定的 CE 策略（即一步式、搜索—替换、计划—应用）。实际上，CE 任务在代码上下文、编辑局部性和语义复杂度上差异很大，导致没有任何单一策略能够始终表现良好。此外，关于策略与 CE 任务之间关系的系统性研究仍然稀缺，限制了基于 LLM 的代码编辑策略的进一步优化。为填补这一空白，我们构建了 CEBench，包含从 SWE-bench 精选出的 500 个真实世界 CE 任务。随后我们比较了三种有代表性的 CE 策略（一步式、搜索—替换、计划—应用）。我们的研究揭示了两个关键发现：(1) 每种策略在特定 CE 任务上都表现出独特优势，不存在普适的最优；(2) 策略的有效性显著受四个核心任务特征影响：代码总行数、修改类型、修改范围和任务类型。受这些发现启发，我们提出 ACE，一个基于任务特征动态选择最优 CE 策略的自适应代码编辑框架。与基于分类器或指令提示的方法不同，ACE 采用一个微调后的 LLM，从经验数据中学习特征—策略映射，从而给出带有可解释理由的策略推荐。在我们的 CEBench-verified 上的大量实验表明，ACE 优于最先进基线：相比最佳基线（AutoCodeRover），它将 Pass@1 提升 15.2%，同时将 token 消耗降低 26.3%。我们的策略选择器达到 73.1% 的选择准确率和 70.4% 的理由准确率（Cohen's Kappa = 0.802），为开发者提供了透明且可信的决策。","tl":"按任务特征自适应选择代码编辑策略，提升 Pass@1 并省 token。","au":["Jun Wan","Zhongxin Liu","Dajun Chen","Wei Jiang","Yong Li","Xiaoxue Ren"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["code editing","strategy selection","CEBench","SWE-bench","adaptive framework"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/143/x"},{"id":"p01426","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"When Optimizations Backfire: The Paradox of Plaintext Optimizations in Privacy-Preserving ML Compilers","tz":"当优化适得其反：隐私保护机器学习编译器中明文优化的悖论","a":"Growing concerns about data security and privacy have fueled the widespread adoption of Privacy-Preserving Machine Learning (PPML). Cryptography-based PPML, which allows computation directly on encrypted data, significantly mitigates data leakage risks. To facilitate its adoption, Ciphertext Machine Learning Compilers (CMLCs) automate the translation of high-level ML procedures into low-level circuits for encrypted data. Recently, CMLCs have increasingly adopted infrastructure from Plaintext Machine Learning Compilers (PMLCs). While integrating Plaintext-Domain Optimization Passes (PDOPs) into CMLCs offers potential performance, usability, and extensibility benefits, our study shows it can also lead to severe performance regressions — a risk that has been largely overlooked. To address this, we introduce Hopta, a hybrid domain optimization defects tester and analyzer, aiming to find optimization bugs that can degrade the performance of compiled circuits from CMLCs. We carefully design two core components: (1) an optimization pipeline mutation mechanism to detect optimization defects by selectively enabling/disabling PDOPs, and (2) a profile-guided code reduction tool that efficiently simplifies defect-triggering programs to isolate optimization defects and facilitate debugging. Applying Hopta to SecretFlow-SPU, a production-grade CMLC, we identified 11 optimization defects (spanning matrix indexing, arithmetic/boolean conversion, and cost model deviation) that led to substantial performance regressions, with compiled circuits incurring up to 310.2% increased cost. Our comprehensive analysis provides empirical insights into fundamental differences between plaintext and ciphertext domain optimization strategies, offering crucial guidance for future CMLC development. We conclude with a brief discussion of extensions to other hybrid ML compilers, underscoring the methodology’s compiler-agnostic nature. This work establishes a new research direction for enhancing CMLC performance and the practical deployment of privacy-preserving ML systems.","az":"对数据安全与隐私日益增长的关注推动了隐私保护机器学习（PPML）的广泛采用。基于密码学的 PPML 允许直接在加密数据上计算，显著降低了数据泄露风险。为促进其落地，密文机器学习编译器（CMLC）自动将高层 ML 过程翻译为面向加密数据的底层电路。近来，CMLC 越来越多地复用明文机器学习编译器（PMLC）的基础设施。虽然把明文域优化遍（PDOP）集成进 CMLC 在性能、易用性和可扩展性上有潜在收益，但我们的研究表明它也会导致严重的性能回退——这一风险此前基本被忽视。为此，我们提出 Hopta，一个混合域优化缺陷的测试与分析工具，旨在发现会降低 CMLC 所编译电路性能的优化缺陷。我们精心设计了两个核心组件：(1) 通过选择性启用/禁用 PDOP 来检测优化缺陷的优化流水线变异机制；(2) 一个性能剖析引导的代码规约工具，可高效简化触发缺陷的程序，以隔离优化缺陷并便于调试。将 Hopta 应用于工业级 CMLC SecretFlow-SPU，我们识别出 11 个优化缺陷（涉及矩阵索引、算术/布尔转换以及代价模型偏差），它们导致了显著的性能回退，编译出的电路开销最高增加 310.2%。我们的全面分析提供了关于明文域与密文域优化策略根本差异的实证洞见，为未来 CMLC 的开发提供了关键指导。最后我们简要讨论了向其他混合 ML 编译器的扩展，强调该方法与具体编译器无关的特性。本工作为提升 CMLC 性能以及隐私保护 ML 系统的实际部署确立了一个新的研究方向。","tl":"首次系统揭示并自动检测明文优化遍在密文 ML 编译器中引发的性能回退缺陷。","au":["Yichen Li","Jin Tan","Dongwei Xiao","Yiteng Peng","Pingchuan Ma","Junming Ma","Shoumeng Yan","Shuai Wang","Fengwei Zhang"],"top":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","alt":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["privacy-preserving ML compiler","optimization defects","compiler testing","code reduction","SecretFlow-SPU"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/144/x"},{"id":"p01427","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Test Case Selection for Deep Neural Networks: A Replication Study on LLMs for Code (Replicability Study)","tz":"面向深度神经网络的测试用例选择：在代码大模型上的复现研究（可复现性研究）","a":"Test case selection (TCS) techniques have been widely studied to support the operational evaluation of deep neural networks (DNNs) under limited testing budgets, where labeling cost is a primary concern and uncovering model failures early is a key objective. Although prior studies report promising results, existing empirical evaluations focus almost exclusively on vision-based DNNs and datasets. As observed in recent surveys, models and datasets specifically designed for software engineering tasks have not been considered, leaving it unclear whether prior findings generalize to LLM code models. This paper presents a large-scale replication study of TCS techniques in the context of LLM code models. We re-examine established TCS strategies originally proposed for DNNs and complement them with statistical sampling strategies that have not previously been evaluated for TCS. We assess their effectiveness on three code-related classification tasks: clone detection, vulnerability detection, and technical debt prediction. The study spans 17 fine-tuned language models, 7 predictive features, and 13 selection strategies, and evaluates performance along two dimensions: operational accuracy estimation and early failure discovery. The results indicate that only a subset of findings reported for vision-based DNNs generalize when TCS is applied to LLMs for code. In particular, feature-driven uncertainty measures consistently outperform entropy-based baselines, and statistical sampling strategies improve robustness without sacrificing accuracy estimation or failure discovery. At the same time, performance varies substantially across tasks and models, indicating that the effectiveness of TCS techniques is context-dependent. Overall, this study provides empirical evidence on the replicability of TCS techniques beyond vision-based deep learning and offers insights into their use for the operational evaluation of LLMs for code.","az":"测试用例选择（TCS）技术已被广泛研究，用于在有限测试预算下支持深度神经网络（DNN）的运行时评估，其中标注成本是主要顾虑，尽早发现模型失效是关键目标。尽管已有研究报告了令人鼓舞的结果，现有实证评估几乎全部集中在基于视觉的 DNN 与数据集上。正如近期综述所指出的，专门为软件工程任务设计的模型与数据集尚未被纳入考量，因此先前结论能否推广到代码大模型仍不清楚。本文在代码大模型场景下开展了一项大规模的 TCS 技术复现研究。我们重新审视了最初为 DNN 提出的成熟 TCS 策略，并补充了此前从未在 TCS 中评估过的统计抽样策略。我们在三个与代码相关的分类任务上评估其有效性：克隆检测、漏洞检测与技术债预测。该研究涵盖 17 个微调后的语言模型、7 种预测特征和 13 种选择策略，并从两个维度评估性能：运行时准确率估计与早期失效发现。结果表明，只有一部分在基于视觉的 DNN 上报告的结论能推广到代码大模型的 TCS 场景。特别地，基于特征的不确定性度量持续优于基于熵的基线，而统计抽样策略在不牺牲准确率估计与失效发现的前提下提升了鲁棒性。同时，性能在不同任务和模型间差异很大，说明 TCS 技术的有效性依赖于具体上下文。总体而言，本研究提供了 TCS 技术在视觉深度学习之外可复现性的实证证据，并为其用于代码大模型的运行时评估提供了洞见。","tl":"首次在代码 LLM 上复现 TCS 技术，发现视觉领域结论仅部分成立。","au":["Ali Asgari","Mitchell Olsthoorn","Annibale Panichella"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["reproducibility-replication","empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["test case selection","replication study","code LLMs","uncertainty metrics","statistical sampling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/145/x"},{"id":"p01428","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CAST: A Compiler-Based Framework for Systematically Testing LLM Compositional Safety","tz":"CAST：一个基于编译器思想的 LLM 组合式安全系统化测试框架","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used in software pipelines, raising concerns about harmful behaviors in security-critical domains. Existing safety evaluations predominantly probe models with single prompts or short interactions, and therefore do not capture how safety behaves under multi-step workflows where individual requests are composed into complex behavior. This paper introduces compositional safety, the property that an LLM remains safe not only against isolated malicious prompts, but also under structured, long-horizon decompositions of harmful intents. we propose CAST, a systematic testing framework designed to evaluate the compositional safety of LLMs in the domain of malicious code. Drawing inspiration from modern compiler infrastructures, CAST decouples test case generation from test execution using a novel intermediate representation, CAIR. This architecture allows the framework to automatically refine high-level testing intents into granular sub-tasks that serve as unit tests for the model’s alignment. These components are subsequently instantiated by the System Under Test (SUT) and reassembled to verify if the model can be driven to realize the original harmful goal. We evaluate CAST on four state-of-the-art LLMs across three security-critical testbeds. Our results demonstrate that CAST systematically exposes severe safety violations in strongly aligned models that resist conventional red-teaming, achieving up to a 365% increase in successful test cases compared to baseline testing strategies.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）越来越多地被用于软件流水线中，这引发了对其在安全关键领域产生有害行为的担忧。现有的安全评估主要以单条提示或短交互来探测模型，因而无法刻画在多步工作流中——即把单个请求组合成复杂行为时——安全性的表现。本文提出了组合式安全（compositional safety）这一属性，即 LLM 不仅要在面对孤立的恶意提示时保持安全，也要在有害意图被结构化、长程分解后仍然安全。我们提出 CAST，一个系统化测试框架，用于评估 LLM 在恶意代码领域的组合式安全性。受现代编译器基础设施启发，CAST 通过一种新颖的中间表示 CAIR 将测试用例生成与测试执行解耦。该架构使框架能够自动把高层测试意图细化为细粒度子任务，作为对模型对齐性的单元测试。这些组件随后由被测系统（SUT）实例化并重新组装，以验证模型是否能被驱动去实现最初的有害目标。我们在三个安全关键测试床上对四个最先进的 LLM 评估了 CAST。结果表明，CAST 能系统性地暴露出强对齐模型中那些可抵御传统红队测试的严重安全违规，相比基线测试策略成功测试用例数最多提升 365%。","tl":"用编译器式中间表示分解有害意图，系统暴露 LLM 的组合式安全漏洞。","au":["Lu Yan","Zhuo Zhang","Xiangzhe Xu","Shengwei An","Guangyu Shen","Zhou Xuan","Xuan Chen","Xiangyu Zhang"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","tg":["security","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["compositional safety","malicious code","LLM red-teaming","intermediate representation","systematic testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/146/x"},{"id":"p01429","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CAM: A Causality-based Analysis Framework for Multi-Agent Code Generation Systems","tz":"CAM：面向多智能体代码生成系统的因果分析框架","a":"Despite the remarkable success that Multi-Agent Code Generation Systems (MACGS) have achieved, the inherent complexity of multi-agent architectures produces substantial volumes of intermediate outputs. To date, the individual importance of these intermediate outputs to the system correctness remains opaque, which impedes targeted optimization of MACGS designs. To address this challenge, we propose CAM, the first Causality-based Analysis framework for MACGS that systematically quantifies the contribution of different intermediate features for system correctness. By comprehensively categorizing intermediate outputs and systematically simulating realistic errors on intermediate features, we identify the important features for system correctness and aggregate their importance rankings, facilitating comprehensive analysis of MACGS. We instantiate CAM on representative MACGS across multiple backend LLMs and datasets and conduct extensive empirical analysis on the identified importance rankings. Our analysis reveals intriguing findings: first, we uncover context-dependent features features whose importance emerges mainly through interactions with other features, revealing that quality assurance for MACGS should move beyond module-level validation to incorporate cross-feature consistency checks; second, we reveal that hybrid backend MACGS with different backend LLMs assigned according to their relative strength achieves up to 7.2% Pass@1 improvement, underscoring hybrid architectures as a promising direction for future MACGS design. We further demonstrate CAM’s practical utility through two applications: (1) failure repair which achieves a 73.3% success rate by optimizing top-3 importance-ranked features and (2) feature pruning that reduces up to 66.8% intermediate token consumption while maintaining generation performance by pruning low-importance features. Our work provides actionable insights for MACGS design and deployment, establishing causality analysis as a powerful approach for understanding and improving MACGS.","az":"尽管多智能体代码生成系统（MACGS）已取得显著成功，多智能体架构固有的复杂性会产生大量中间输出。迄今为止，这些中间输出各自对系统正确性的重要性仍不透明，阻碍了对 MACGS 设计的针对性优化。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 CAM，首个面向 MACGS 的基于因果的分析框架，系统性地量化不同中间特征对系统正确性的贡献。通过全面地对中间输出进行分类并系统地在中间特征上模拟真实错误，我们识别出对系统正确性重要的特征并聚合其重要性排名，从而支持对 MACGS 的全面分析。我们在多种后端 LLM 与数据集上，将 CAM 实例化到具有代表性的 MACGS 上，并围绕识别出的重要性排名开展了广泛的实证分析。我们的分析揭示了有趣的发现：第一，我们发现了上下文依赖型特征——其重要性主要通过与其他特征的交互才显现，这说明 MACGS 的质量保障应超越模块级验证，纳入跨特征一致性检查；第二，我们发现按各后端 LLM 的相对强项进行分配的混合后端 MACGS 可带来最高 7.2% 的 Pass@1 提升，凸显混合架构是未来 MACGS 设计的有前景方向。我们进一步通过两个应用展示 CAM 的实用价值：(1) 失败修复，通过优化重要性排名前三的特征达到 73.3% 的成功率；(2) 特征剪枝，通过剪除低重要性特征，在保持生成性能的同时最多减少 66.8% 的中间 token 消耗。我们的工作为 MACGS 的设计与部署提供了可操作的洞见，确立了因果分析作为理解和改进 MACGS 的有力方法。","tl":"首次用因果分析量化多智能体代码系统各中间产物的重要性。","au":["LYU ZONGYI","Zhenlan Ji","Songqiang Chen","Liwen Wang","Yuheng Huang","Shuai Wang","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","empirical-study"],"kw":["multi-agent code generation","causality analysis","feature importance","failure repair","token pruning"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/147/x"},{"id":"p01430","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"KaPilot: LLM-Assisted Generation of Kani Specifications for Unsafe Rust Verification","tz":"KaPilot：LLM 辅助生成用于 unsafe Rust 验证的 Kani 规约","a":"Rust’s ownership and type system provide strong memory safety guarantees, but unsafe code still presents memory safety risks. Formal verification is crucial for ensuring memory safety, but writing precise specifications for unsafe Rust is challenging and largely manual. Large language models (LLMs) have shown promise in generating formal specifications but are often code-centric, prone to inheriting implementation flaws, and lack systematic quality assessment. In this paper, we present KaPilot, a multi-agent framework for automatically generating specifications to verify unsafe Rust memory safety using Kani. The process begins with lightweight program analysis and proof harness generation. The SafetyReq agent extracts a concise, refined list of safety requirements from the target Rust function’s documentation, which guides the SpecGen agent in producing initial specifications that specify memory safety concerns. Then, the specifications are iteratively refined through a generate–precheck–verify loop involving SpecGen, SpecPrecheck, and SpecVerify agents, which assess quality and feed errors back. By executing this loop multiple times, KaPilot generates a set of candidate specifications. Finally, the shuffle-and-implication strategy is applied to systematically determine the best specification from these candidates. We evaluated KaPilot on 54 unsafe Rust functions with ground truth and 44 without. KaPilot achieved 88.9% and 69.2% specification generation success, respectively, with 57.4% of generated specifications equivalent to or stronger than the ground truth. Compared with AutoSpec, KaPilot produces 14.8% more verifiable specifications and 25.9% more equivalent-or-better specifications.","az":"Rust 的所有权与类型系统提供了强内存安全保证，但 unsafe 代码仍存在内存安全风险。形式化验证对于确保内存安全至关重要，但为 unsafe Rust 编写精确规约颇具挑战且基本靠人工。大语言模型（LLM）在生成形式化规约方面已展现潜力，但往往以代码为中心、容易继承实现中的缺陷，且缺乏系统性的质量评估。本文提出 KaPilot，一个多智能体框架，用于自动生成规约，以使用 Kani 验证 unsafe Rust 的内存安全。该流程首先进行轻量级程序分析与证明桩（proof harness）生成。SafetyReq 智能体从目标 Rust 函数的文档中提取一份简明、精炼的安全需求清单，用以指导 SpecGen 智能体产生刻画内存安全关注点的初始规约。随后，规约通过一个由 SpecGen、SpecPrecheck 和 SpecVerify 智能体构成的“生成—预检—验证”循环迭代精化，这些智能体评估质量并反馈错误。通过多次执行该循环，KaPilot 生成一组候选规约。最后，采用“打乱与蕴含”（shuffle-and-implication）策略从这些候选中系统性地确定最佳规约。我们在 54 个有基准答案的 unsafe Rust 函数和 44 个无基准答案的函数上评估了 KaPilot。KaPilot 的规约生成成功率分别达到 88.9% 和 69.2%，其中 57.4% 的生成规约与基准答案等价或更强。与 AutoSpec 相比，KaPilot 多产生 14.8% 的可验证规约和 25.9% 的等价或更优规约。","tl":"多智能体“生成-预检-验证”循环自动产出可验证的 unsafe Rust 安全规约。","au":["Minghua Wang","Yuxi Ling","Mingzhi Gao","Yuwei Liu","Lin Huang"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["specification generation","unsafe Rust","Kani verification","multi-agent LLM","memory safety"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/148/x"},{"id":"p01431","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RippleGUItester: Change-Aware Exploratory Testing","tz":"RippleGUItester：变更感知的探索式测试","a":"Software systems evolve continuously through frequent code changes, yet such changes often introduce unintended bugs despite extensive testing and code review. Existing testing approaches are largely constrained to predefined execution paths or rely on unguided exploration, leaving many change-induced issues undetected. To address this challenge, we present RippleGUItester, a change-driven testing system that treats a code change as the epicenter of a ripple effect and explores its broader, user-visible impacts via the GUI. Given a code change, RippleGUItester performs LLM-based change-impact analysis to generate and enrich realistic test scenarios, executes these scenarios on both pre-change and post-change versions of the system, and applies differential analysis to identify behavioral differences. Crucially, RippleGUItester employs multimodal bug detection, comparing visual GUI changes and interpreting them in the context of natural-language change intents to distinguish unintended bugs from intended behavioral updates. We evaluate our approach on hundreds of real-world code changes across four widely used software systems: Firefox, Zettlr, JabRef, and Godot. Our results show that the proposed approach uncovers bugs introduced by code changes that were missed by existing test suites, CI pipelines, and code review. In total, we identify 26 previously unknown bugs that still exist in the latest versions of the evaluated systems. After reporting, 16 bugs have been fixed, 2 have been confirmed, 6 are still under discussion, and 2 were marked as intended. We envision RippleGUItester being applied before or shortly after a code change is merged, enabling earlier detection of regressions.","az":"软件系统通过频繁的代码变更持续演进，但即便有大量测试和代码评审，这些变更仍常引入意料之外的缺陷。现有测试方法大多局限于预定义的执行路径，或依赖无引导的探索，导致许多由变更引起的问题未被发现。为应对这一挑战，我们提出 RippleGUItester，一个变更驱动的测试系统，它把一次代码变更视为涟漪效应的震中，并通过 GUI 探索其更广泛的、用户可见的影响。给定一次代码变更，RippleGUItester 执行基于 LLM 的变更影响分析，生成并丰富真实的测试场景，在系统的变更前与变更后版本上执行这些场景，并应用差分分析识别行为差异。关键在于，RippleGUItester 采用多模态缺陷检测，比较可见的 GUI 变化并结合自然语言描述的变更意图进行解释，从而区分非预期缺陷与有意的行为更新。我们在四个广泛使用的软件系统（Firefox、Zettlr、JabRef 和 Godot）上针对数百个真实代码变更评估了该方法。结果表明，所提方法能发现由代码变更引入、且被现有测试套件、CI 流水线和代码评审漏掉的缺陷。我们总共识别出 26 个此前未知、且在被评估系统最新版本中仍然存在的缺陷。在上报后，16 个已修复，2 个已确认，6 个仍在讨论中，2 个被标记为有意行为。我们设想 RippleGUItester 可在代码变更合并之前或之后不久使用，从而更早地发现回归。","tl":"以代码变更为震中做 GUI 差分探索，多模态识别非预期回归缺陷。","au":["Yanqi Su","Michael Pradel","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["change-impact analysis","GUI testing","differential testing","regression detection","multimodal bug detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/149/x"},{"id":"p01432","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Gleaner: A Semantically-Rich and Efficient Online Sampler for Microservice Diagnostics","tz":"Gleaner：面向微服务诊断的语义丰富且高效的在线采样器","a":"Distributed tracing in microservices is critical for diagnostics but generates overwhelming data volumes, necessitating intelligent sampling. To maximize fidelity, state-of-the-art (SOTA) tail-based samplers analyze complete (or even log-enriched) traces by modeling them as graphs. However, this reliance on computationally expensive graph analysis creates a performance bottleneck that prohibits their use in online settings. To this end, we propose Gleaner, an online tail-sampling framework that breaks this trade-off. It is founded on the key insight that explicit graph structures are unnecessary for high-fidelity trace grouping. Instead, Gleaner represents each trace as a “bag-of-edges” augmented with log semantics, replacing slow graph algorithms with highly efficient set-based operations. It also employs an alarm-driven quota and a diversity-preserving strategy to prioritize anomalous and rare traces for downstream Root Cause Analysis (RCA). Experimentally, Gleaner processes traces at 0.74ms each, improving Trace Pattern Coverage by up to 128.7% and Shannon Entropy by up to 32.9% over baselines. At just a 1% sampling rate, Gleaner improves RCA accuracy by 42%-107% over the next-best sampler. Moreover, RCA on Gleaner’s sampled data is more accurate than with the entire, unsampled dataset. This result reframes intelligent sampling from a data reduction technique to a powerful signal enhancement paradigm for automated operations.","az":"微服务中的分布式追踪对诊断至关重要，但会产生海量数据，因而必须进行智能采样。为最大化保真度，最先进（SOTA）的尾部采样器把完整（甚至日志增强）的追踪建模为图来分析。然而，这种对计算代价高昂的图分析的依赖造成了性能瓶颈，使其无法用于在线场景。为此，我们提出 Gleaner，一个打破该权衡的在线尾部采样框架。它的关键洞见是：高保真的追踪分组并不需要显式的图结构。相反，Gleaner 将每条追踪表示为带日志语义增强的“边袋”（bag-of-edges），用高效的集合操作替代缓慢的图算法。它还采用告警驱动的配额机制与保持多样性的策略，优先保留异常与稀有的追踪供下游根因分析（RCA）使用。实验表明，Gleaner 处理每条追踪仅需 0.74ms，相比基线将追踪模式覆盖率最多提升 128.7%，香农熵最多提升 32.9%。在仅 1% 的采样率下，Gleaner 相比次优采样器将 RCA 准确率提升 42%–107%。此外，在 Gleaner 采样数据上做 RCA 甚至比使用完整未采样数据集更准确。这一结果把智能采样从一种数据缩减技术重新定位为面向自动化运维的强大信号增强范式。","tl":"用“边袋+日志语义”替代图分析，实现高保真在线尾采样并提升 RCA。","au":["Yifan Yang","Aoyang Fang","Songhan Zhang","Pinjia He"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","non-llm-classical","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["distributed tracing","tail-based sampling","microservices","root cause analysis","online sampler"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/150/x"},{"id":"p01433","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Context Matters: Improving the Practical Reliability of LLM-Based Unit Test Generation (Experience Paper)","tz":"上下文很重要：提升基于 LLM 的单元测试生成在实践中的可靠性（经验论文）","a":"Automated unit test generation has recently benefited from advances in large language models (LLMs), yet our industrial deployments reveal a persistent gap between promising research results and practical usability. In real-world projects with complex frameworks and cross-file dependencies, LLM-generated tests frequently fail to compile, require costly manual repair, or provide unstable coverage improvements. This paper reports our experience in designing, deploying, and evaluating CATGen, a context-aware workflow for LLM-based unit test generation, informed by repeated industrial failures and refinements. Rather than relying on LLMs to infer incomplete project context, we found that compilation robustness critically depends on making project-level dependencies explicit, stabilizing test class scaffolding, and replacing iterative LLM-based repair with lightweight static analysis. These experience-driven insights shaped CATGen’s multi-stage design, which combines structured context retrieval, deterministic test skeleton construction, and program analytics–based post-processing. We evaluate CATGen on real-world complex focal methods from proprietary industrial projects and additionally on the Defects4J benchmark to assess generalizability. Across both settings, CATGen substantially improves compilation success and structural coverage while significantly reducing generation time and token consumption compared to existing LLM-based approaches. Our results demonstrate that reliable LLM-based unit test generation in practice depends less on prompt engineering alone and more on systematic engineering support grounded in real-world development constraints.","az":"自动化单元测试生成近来受益于大语言模型（LLM）的进展，但我们的工业部署揭示了研究成果与实际可用性之间持续存在的鸿沟。在具有复杂框架和跨文件依赖的真实项目中，LLM 生成的测试经常无法编译、需要昂贵的人工修复，或带来不稳定的覆盖率提升。本文报告了我们设计、部署与评估 CATGen 的经验——一个面向 LLM 单元测试生成的上下文感知工作流，其设计源自反复的工业失败与迭代改进。我们发现，与其依赖 LLM 去推断不完整的项目上下文，编译健壮性关键取决于显式化项目级依赖、稳定测试类脚手架，以及用轻量级静态分析替代迭代式的 LLM 修复。这些源自实践的洞见塑造了 CATGen 的多阶段设计，它结合了结构化上下文检索、确定性的测试骨架构建和基于程序分析的后处理。我们在来自专有工业项目的真实复杂焦点方法上评估 CATGen，并额外在 Defects4J 基准上评估其泛化性。在两种设置下，CATGen 都显著提升了编译成功率与结构覆盖率，同时相比现有基于 LLM 的方法大幅降低了生成时间与 token 消耗。我们的结果表明，实践中可靠的基于 LLM 的单元测试生成较少依赖提示工程本身，而更依赖扎根于真实开发约束的系统化工程支撑。","tl":"工业经验表明：显式项目上下文与静态分析后处理胜过提示工程。","au":["Junjie Chen","Ziqi Wang","Lin Yang","Chen Yang","Xiao Chu","Jianyi Zhou","Guangtai Liang","Qianxiang Wang","Dong Wang"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unit test generation","context-aware workflow","compilation success","industrial deployment","static analysis post-processing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/151/x"},{"id":"p01434","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Inferring 1-Minimal Trigger Configurations for Assessing Linux Kernel CVE Triggerability","tz":"推断 1-极小触发配置以评估 Linux 内核 CVE 的可触发性","a":"Vendors assessing Linux kernel CVEs need to know whether a bug is triggerable under production-tailored configurations, not merely whether a version is affected, yet upstream reproducers and vulnerability databases rarely provide configuration-level context. We study minimal trigger-configuration inference: given a CVE entry and a target kernel version (optionally a baseline .config), we synthesize a Kconfig-satisfiable option set that remains effective after make olddefconfig and, when a reproducer is available, still triggers under a specified evaluation protocol; we then prune it to a 1-minimal (subset-minimal) boundary for evaluation. Our framework FCC links vulnerability cues to build-system symbols to mine candidates, completes implicit prerequisites under olddefconfig feedback to avoid silent rollback, and performs runtime-validated minimization guided by the inferred dependency topology. We evaluate on KernJC (32 CVEs) and KernelCTF (56 CVEs), totaling 88 CVEs across multiple kernel versions. On the 88-CVE set, FCC improves the post-make olddefconfig configuration success rate from 62.5% (55/88) to 96.6% (85/88) over an olddef-only injection baseline; on the KernJC set, FCC reduces the average candidate set size by 78.7% compared to KernJC (Avg.14.72 vs. 69.00 options per CVE). By returning an effective and auditable 1-minimal configuration boundary, FCC helps vendors scope triggerability against their deployment configurations with a clear, tool-supported decision line.","az":"评估 Linux 内核 CVE 的厂商需要知道某个缺陷在面向生产环境定制的配置下是否可触发，而不仅仅是某个版本是否受影响；然而上游复现器与漏洞数据库很少提供配置级别的上下文。我们研究最小触发配置推断问题：给定一个 CVE 条目和目标内核版本（可选地还有一个基线 .config），我们合成一个满足 Kconfig 约束的选项集合，使其在执行 make olddefconfig 之后仍然有效，并且在有复现器可用时，仍能在指定的评估协议下触发漏洞；随后我们将其剪枝到 1-极小（子集极小）边界以供评估。我们的框架 FCC 将漏洞线索与构建系统符号关联以挖掘候选项，在 olddefconfig 反馈下补全隐含前提以避免静默回滚，并在推断出的依赖拓扑指导下执行经运行时验证的最小化。我们在 KernJC（32 个 CVE）和 KernelCTF（56 个 CVE）上评估，覆盖多个内核版本共 88 个 CVE。在这 88 个 CVE 的集合上，相比仅使用 olddef 注入的基线，FCC 把 make olddefconfig 之后的配置成功率从 62.5%（55/88）提升到 96.6%（85/88）；在 KernJC 集合上，FCC 相比 KernJC 将平均候选集合规模减少 78.7%（每个 CVE 平均 14.72 个选项对比 69.00 个）。通过返回一个有效且可审计的 1-极小配置边界，FCC 帮助厂商依据其部署配置界定可触发性，提供清晰的、有工具支撑的决策依据。","tl":"自动合成并极小化触发内核 CVE 所需的 Kconfig 配置集合。","au":["Tongjie Wei","Peng Zhang","Zhiwen Hu","Xupu Hu","Chen Lyu","Gangyan Zeng"],"top":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","alt":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Linux kernel CVE","trigger configuration","Kconfig","1-minimal set","triggerability assessment"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/152/x"},{"id":"p01435","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"The Discreet Charm of the Bugeoisie: A First Look at Bug Reports Created by Researchers","tz":"Bug 资产阶级的隐秘魅力：对研究者创建的缺陷报告的首次考察","a":"Many ISSTA papers present automated tools to find bugs in software, including in open-source projects. Some researchers create public bug reports for the bugs they deem worth reporting, e.g., new bugs found by the tools. We focus on studying bug reports created by researchers and coin the term Bugeoisie to refer to such bug reports. We collect the Bugeoisie for ISSTA 2025 by reading the papers, examining the artifacts, and contacting the authors, while trying to “chase” bug report links. This process turns out to be surprisingly challenging because only a few authors make such links readily available. We then analyze the Bugeoisie to understand when the bug reports were created and how they were resolved up until now. For most papers that make claims about the number of bugs found, reported, or confirmed, independently checking those claims is again surprisingly challenging. Our findings point out to the important changes that conference organizers and reviewers may want to require for the Bugeoisie. We also provide some suggestions for paper authors to prepare and describe their Bugeoisie in their papers and artifacts.","az":"许多 ISSTA 论文提出自动化工具，用于在软件（包括开源项目）中发现缺陷。一些研究者会为他们认为值得上报的缺陷（例如工具新发现的缺陷）创建公开的缺陷报告。我们聚焦于研究由研究者创建的缺陷报告，并创造术语 Bugeoisie 来指代这类缺陷报告。我们通过阅读论文、检查制品、联系作者并尝试“追踪”缺陷报告链接，收集了 ISSTA 2025 的 Bugeoisie。这一过程出人意料地困难，因为只有少数作者会方便地提供此类链接。随后我们分析 Bugeoisie，以了解这些缺陷报告是何时创建的、迄今为止是如何被处理的。对于大多数宣称发现、上报或确认了若干缺陷数量的论文，独立核验这些宣称同样出人意料地困难。我们的发现指出了会议组织者与评审人可能需要对 Bugeoisie 提出的重要变更。我们也为论文作者如何在论文与制品中准备和描述其 Bugeoisie 提供了一些建议。","tl":"首次实证核查论文所报缺陷的可追溯性，发现绝大多数难以独立验证。","au":["Ji young Kim","Jana Dragovic","Alessandro Botta","T. M. Rithwanul Islam","Alaa Mohamad","Karim Sharaf","Sejuti Sharmin Siddiqui","Divyanshi Joshi","Harini Anand","Nurjemal Saryyeva","Shubham Chapagain","Saad Nasir","Darko Marinov","Bogdan Alexandru Stoica"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication","position-vision"],"kw":["bug reports","research artifacts","verifiability","ISSTA study","open science"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/153/x"},{"id":"p01436","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"BinRAG: An RAG-Based Decompilation Framework Fusing Name Prediction and Calling Context","tz":"BinRAG：融合名称预测与调用上下文的基于 RAG 的反编译框架","a":"Decompiling stripped binaries to assist human reverse engineers remains a critical yet highly challenging task in software security. Prior work has developed various neural networks and even dedicated large language models (LLMs) to improve function and variable name recovery in decompiled code. Nonetheless, these approaches alone fall short of enabling a generic LLM-based decompilation pipeline that can reliably enhance the readability and semantic clarity of decompiled outputs. In this paper, we propose BinRAG, a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) based decompilation framework designed to enhance the decompilation of stripped binaries. Building upon name prediction models, BinRAG features three novel designs: (1) it first utilizes name prediction models to transform raw decompiled outputs into enriched, source-like queries for RAG retrieval; (2) it further enhances these queries by fine-tuning a specialized LLM that jointly considers predicted variable names and binary optimization levels, enabling more accurate retrieval from a curated example database; (3) it then integrates these retrieved examples with the target’s calling context, employing a general-purpose LLM to synthesize high-fidelity, human-readable decompiled code. Evaluation on 3,200 functions from real-world software repositories demonstrates that BinRAG achieves 9% and 16% improvements in semantic precision and readability compared to state-of-the-art approaches. Our results show that BinRAG effectively scales to large codebases and significantly reduces manual effort in reverse engineering tasks.","az":"对被剥离符号的二进制进行反编译以辅助人类逆向工程师，仍是软件安全中一项关键而极具挑战的任务。已有工作开发了各种神经网络甚至专门的大语言模型（LLM），以改进反编译代码中函数名与变量名的恢复。然而，仅靠这些方法还不足以构建一个通用的、基于 LLM 的反编译流水线来可靠地提升反编译输出的可读性与语义清晰度。本文提出 BinRAG，一个基于检索增强生成（RAG）的反编译框架，旨在增强对被剥离二进制的反编译。BinRAG 在名称预测模型之上具有三项新设计：(1) 首先利用名称预测模型把原始反编译输出转化为信息更丰富、类似源码的查询以供 RAG 检索；(2) 进一步通过微调一个同时考虑预测变量名与二进制优化级别的专用 LLM 来增强这些查询，从而能从精心构建的示例数据库中更准确地检索；(3) 随后把检索到的示例与目标的调用上下文整合，使用通用 LLM 合成高保真、人类可读的反编译代码。在来自真实软件仓库的 3,200 个函数上的评估表明，BinRAG 在语义精度与可读性上相比最先进方法分别提升 9% 与 16%。结果显示 BinRAG 能有效扩展到大型代码库，并显著减少逆向工程任务中的人工投入。","tl":"用名称预测构造查询做 RAG，再融合调用上下文合成可读反编译代码。","au":["Wai Kin Wong","Daoyuan Wu","Zhibo Liu","Huaijin Wang","Li Zongjie","Shuai Wang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","tg":["llm-based","security","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["decompilation","retrieval-augmented generation","stripped binaries","name prediction","calling context"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/154/x"},{"id":"p01437","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Exploiting Ethereum Rollback Semantics: Profit-Driven Attack Synthesis and Off-Chain Misinterpretation Testing","tz":"利用以太坊回滚语义：以盈利为导向的攻击合成与链下误解析测试","a":"The Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) enforces atomic execution through rollback, reverting all state changes when execution fails. While necessary for correctness, rollback semantics introduce a distinct attack surface affecting both on-chain execution and off-chain infrastructures. On-chain, attackers can use conditional failure to filter executions, committing only profitable outcomes while rolling back unprofitable attempts. Off-chain, systems such as explorers, token trackers, and RPC providers may misinterpret aborted executions as successful, leading to inconsistent records or unintended transfers. Existing tools largely treat rollback as an execution endpoint, providing limited support for profit-driven attack synthesis or off-chain misinterpretation testing. To address this gap, we formalize two rollback attack models and develop RollGain, a unified framework for rollback-aware analysis. For on-chain attacks, RollGain models contract structure and value flows, validates candidate executions symbolically, and replays on a forked chain to rank profitability. For off-chain testing, RollGain conducts call tree analysis on 3.08 billion Ethereum transactions to characterize rollback patterns and exercises rollback-inducing execution vectors against external services. On our evaluation datasets, RollGain achieves 95.3% recall with zero false positives, and uncovers 20 rollback misinterpretation vulnerabilities across 18 off-chain systems, of which 18 have been confirmed, 16 fixed, and 5 assigned CVE identifiers.","az":"以太坊虚拟机（EVM）通过回滚强制原子执行，在执行失败时撤销所有状态变更。虽然回滚语义对正确性是必要的，但它引入了一个独特的攻击面，影响链上执行与链下基础设施两方面。在链上，攻击者可以利用条件失败来筛选执行，仅提交有利可图的结果而回滚无利可图的尝试。在链下，诸如区块浏览器、代币追踪器和 RPC 提供方等系统可能把被中止的执行误判为成功，导致记录不一致或非预期的转账。现有工具大多把回滚视为执行终点，对以盈利为导向的攻击合成或链下误解析测试支持有限。为填补这一空白，我们形式化了两种回滚攻击模型，并开发了 RollGain，一个用于回滚感知分析的统一框架。对于链上攻击，RollGain 对合约结构与价值流建模，符号化地验证候选执行，并在分叉链上重放以按盈利能力排序。对于链下测试，RollGain 对 30.8 亿条以太坊交易进行调用树分析以刻画回滚模式，并针对外部服务施加可诱发回滚的执行向量。在我们的评估数据集上，RollGain 达到 95.3% 的召回率且零误报，并在 18 个链下系统中发现了 20 个回滚误解析漏洞，其中 18 个已确认，16 个已修复，5 个获得了 CVE 编号。","tl":"首次系统刻画 EVM 回滚语义攻击面，合成盈利攻击并挖出 20 个链下漏洞。","au":["Yixuan Liu","Xinlei Li","Yi Li"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["Ethereum rollback","attack synthesis","off-chain misinterpretation","symbolic validation","EVM security"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/155/x","pu":"https://liyiweb.com/files/Liu2026EER.pdf"},{"id":"p01438","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Enhancing LLM-based Bug Reproduction via Code Entity Retrieval and Test Case Repair","tz":"通过代码实体检索与测试用例修复增强基于 LLM 的缺陷复现","a":"Automated bug reproduction from bug reports is a critical yet challenging step in software debugging. While LLM-based bug reproduction shows promise, its effectiveness is often hampered by insufficient contextual awareness of the relevant codebase and a tendency to produce invalid test cases. To address these limitations, we propose a novel approach, called LTER, that enhances LLM-based bug reproduction through fine-grained code entity retrieval and a feedback-driven dynamic repair loop. LTER first identifies specific code entities within bug reports to automatically extract precise contexts, including class definitions, constructors, and method logic. The extracted contexts are then used to guide the LLM in generating reproduced test cases. To further ensure executability, LTER employs an iterative repair mechanism to resolve complex dependencies. Specifically, upon injecting a generated test case into the project, if a compilation failure occurs, the framework forwards the error messages to the LLM for an initial repair. Should this initial repair fail, it empowers the LLM to analyze diagnostic messages to recognize missing context and retrieve indispensable dependencies, subsequently regenerating the test case with the supplemented data. Finally, LTER employs a hybrid cascade ranking strategy to accurately select the most effective reproduction test case from the generated candidates. The experimental results on the widely-used Defects4J benchmark show that LTER substantially outperforms the best performance in automated bug reproduction, increasing the reproduction success rate to 47.1% with successfully identifying a valid reproduction test as the top candidate in 39.9% of the cases. Furthermore, LTER demonstrates strong generalization capability, delivering robust performance on the GHRB dataset containing recent bugs previously unseen by the LLM.","az":"从缺陷报告自动复现缺陷是软件调试中关键而困难的一步。虽然基于 LLM 的缺陷复现展现出潜力，但其效果常受限于对相关代码库的上下文感知不足以及倾向于产生无效测试用例。为解决这些局限，我们提出一种新方法 LTER，通过细粒度的代码实体检索和反馈驱动的动态修复循环来增强基于 LLM 的缺陷复现。LTER 首先识别缺陷报告中的具体代码实体，以自动抽取精确的上下文，包括类定义、构造函数和方法逻辑。抽取到的上下文随后用于指导 LLM 生成复现测试用例。为进一步确保可执行性，LTER 采用迭代式修复机制来解决复杂依赖。具体而言，在把生成的测试用例注入项目后，若发生编译失败，框架会把错误信息转发给 LLM 进行初次修复；若初次修复失败，则让 LLM 分析诊断信息以识别缺失的上下文并检索必需的依赖，随后利用补充的数据重新生成测试用例。最后，LTER 采用混合级联排序策略，从生成的候选中准确挑选最有效的复现测试用例。在广泛使用的 Defects4J 基准上的实验结果表明，LTER 大幅超越自动缺陷复现的最佳性能，将复现成功率提升至 47.1%，并在 39.9% 的情形中成功地把有效复现测试排在首位。此外，LTER 展现出很强的泛化能力，在包含 LLM 此前未见过的新近缺陷的 GHRB 数据集上依然表现稳健。","tl":"细粒度代码实体检索加编译错误驱动修复，把缺陷复现率提到 47.1%。","au":["Hao Ding","Yanjie Jiang","Yuxia Zhang","Hui Liu"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["bug reproduction","code entity retrieval","test case repair","Defects4J","cascade ranking"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/156/x"},{"id":"p01439","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"DocPrism: Multi-Lingual Detection of Incorrectness Inconsistencies Between Code and Documentation","tz":"DocPrism：多语言检测代码与文档间的错误性不一致","a":"Code-documentation inconsistencies are common and undesirable: they can lead to developer misunderstandings and software defects. This paper introduces DocCo, a lightweight multi-language, code-documentation inconsistency detection tool. DocCo uses a standard large language model (LLM) to analyze and explain inconsistencies, and focuses on outputting incorrectness inconsistencies. Plain use of LLMs for this task yields unacceptably high inconsistency flag rates—i.e., over 90% of functions are flagged as inconsistent with their documentation. One substantial reason is that LLMs identify natural gaps between high-level documentation and code as incompleteness inconsistencies. We introduce and apply the Local Categorization, External Filtering (LCEF) methodology: LCEF uses an LLM’s local completion skills, rather than its long-term reasoning skills, to focus on reporting incorrectness inconsistencies. In our ablation study, LCEF reduces DocCo’s inconsistency flag rate from 98% to 14%, and increases F1 score from 0.22 to 0.77, compared to standard prompting techniques. On a broad evaluation across Python, TypeScript, C++, and Java, DocCo maintains a low flag rate of 17%, and achieves a precision of 0.63 without performing any fine-tuning. We also establish a conservative lower bound across four programming languages showing that inconsistency errors are present in 11% of code-documentation pairs.","az":"代码与文档的不一致很常见且有害：它们会导致开发者误解与软件缺陷。本文介绍 DocCo，一个轻量级的多语言代码-文档不一致检测工具。DocCo 使用标准大语言模型（LLM）来分析并解释不一致，并专注于输出错误性（incorrectness）不一致。直接使用 LLM 完成该任务会产生高得无法接受的不一致标记率——即超过 90% 的函数被标记为与其文档不一致。一个重要原因是 LLM 会把高层文档与代码之间的自然差距识别为不完整性不一致。我们提出并应用了“局部分类、外部过滤”（LCEF）方法：LCEF 利用 LLM 的局部补全能力而非其长程推理能力，从而专注于报告错误性不一致。在我们的消融实验中，相比标准提示技术，LCEF 把 DocCo 的不一致标记率从 98% 降到 14%，并把 F1 分数从 0.22 提升到 0.77。在涵盖 Python、TypeScript、C++ 和 Java 的广泛评估中，DocCo 保持了 17% 的低标记率，并在完全不做微调的情况下取得 0.63 的精度。我们还在四种编程语言上建立了一个保守下界，表明 11% 的代码-文档对中存在不一致错误。","tl":"用局部补全加外部过滤把 LLM 的文档不一致误报率从 98% 降到 14%。","au":["Xiaomeng Xu","Zahin Wahab","Reid Holmes","Caroline Lemieux"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["code-documentation inconsistency","LLM detection","local categorization external filtering","multi-language","false positive reduction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/157/x"},{"id":"p01440","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"NCFuzz: Configuration-guided Network Service Fuzzing","tz":"NCFuzz：配置引导的网络服务模糊测试","a":"Network services like FTP and DNS are critical components of modern dependable cyberspace infrastructure. Software fuzzing, especially network protocol fuzzing, is widely used to uncover flaws in these systems. However, conventional fuzzers focus on network messages, overlook one critical dimension, service configurations. Incorporating configurations into fuzzing is challenging due to complex semantics, trigger conditions, and resulting enlarged search space. We tackle the problem of finding bugs under non-default configurations, termed ConfBug, by designing a new fuzzer called NCFuzz. NCFuzz leverages two key observations: 1) software documentation contains rich information about configurations; 2) interactions between configuration and network messages can be tracked through code instrumentation and data-flow analysis. Using these insights, NCFuzz uses configuration knowledge and configuration-network-message relation to guide fuzzer towards new software states. Evaluations on six network service implementations show NCFuzz achieves higher coverage than baseline fuzzers. Five ConfBug were discovered during fuzzing.","az":"FTP、DNS 等网络服务是现代可信赖网络空间基础设施的关键组件。软件模糊测试，尤其是网络协议模糊测试，被广泛用于发现这些系统中的缺陷。然而，传统模糊器聚焦于网络报文，忽视了一个关键维度：服务配置。由于语义复杂、触发条件苛刻以及由此带来的搜索空间膨胀，把配置纳入模糊测试颇具挑战。我们针对在非默认配置下寻找缺陷的问题（称为 ConfBug），设计了新的模糊器 NCFuzz。NCFuzz 利用两个关键观察：1) 软件文档中包含关于配置的丰富信息；2) 配置与网络报文之间的交互可以通过代码插桩与数据流分析来追踪。基于这些洞见，NCFuzz 利用配置知识以及配置-网络报文关系来引导模糊器进入新的软件状态。在六个网络服务实现上的评估表明，NCFuzz 取得了高于基线模糊器的覆盖率，并在模糊测试过程中发现了五个 ConfBug。","tl":"首次把服务配置维度纳入网络协议模糊测试并发现非默认配置下的缺陷。","au":["Xuesong Bai","Hengkai Ye","Shenghan Zheng","Fenglu Zhang","Hong Hu","Zhou Li"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["network service fuzzing","configuration-guided","ConfBug","data-flow analysis","protocol testing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/158/x"},{"id":"p01441","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Re-evaluating Detection of Equivalent Mutants Using LLMs: We Should Properly Measure How Far We Are","tz":"重新评估使用 LLM 检测等价变异体：我们应当正确衡量自己究竟走到了哪一步","a":"Mutation testing is a widely used approach for measuring quality of test suites. Equivalent mutant detection (EMD), i.e., determining if a mutant semantically behaves the same as the original code despite some syntactic differences, is a critical problem in mutation testing. A recent study has shown the great promise of LLM-based EMD techniques, reporting substantial improvements over traditional compiler- and machine-learning–based approaches. In this work, we revisit prior results and evaluate the generalization capabilities of LLM-based EMD techniques across two new datasets that differ from the original dataset in mutation operators, programming languages, and source projects. Contrary to prior findings, all studied LLM-based EMD techniques suffer substantial performance degradation on the new datasets. Through extensive analysis, we identify original-method–level data leakage in the original dataset as a key factor inflating earlier results and show that LLMs often rely on a method-wise majority-voting shortcut rather than reasoning about the semantic effects of individual mutations. Based on these findings, we call for the adoption of realistic cross-method evaluation settings and the development of mutation-centric semantic reasoning in future LLM-based EMD research.","az":"变异测试是衡量测试套件质量的广泛使用的方法。等价变异体检测（EMD），即判断某个变异体是否在语义上与原始代码行为相同（尽管存在语法差异），是变异测试中的关键问题。近期一项研究显示了基于 LLM 的 EMD 技术的巨大潜力，报告其相比传统基于编译器和机器学习的方法有显著提升。在本工作中，我们重新审视先前结果，并在两个与原始数据集在变异算子、编程语言和来源项目上均不同的新数据集上评估基于 LLM 的 EMD 技术的泛化能力。与先前发现相反，所有被研究的基于 LLM 的 EMD 技术在新数据集上都出现了大幅性能下降。通过广泛分析，我们指出原始数据集中存在原始方法级别的数据泄漏，这是抬高早先结果的关键因素，并表明 LLM 常常依赖方法级多数投票的捷径，而非真正推理单个变异的语义效果。基于这些发现，我们呼吁采用真实的跨方法评测设置，并在未来基于 LLM 的 EMD 研究中发展以变异为中心的语义推理。","tl":"揭示 LLM 等价变异体检测的高分源于方法级数据泄漏与多数投票捷径。","au":["Arjun Tandon","Mehmet Fırat Dündar","Milkiyas Gebremichael Gebru","Darko Marinov","Yiling Lou","Wenxi Wang"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["reproducibility-replication","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["equivalent mutant detection","data leakage","LLM evaluation","mutation testing","generalization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/159/x"},{"id":"p01442","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CID: Clean-Seed-Free Backdoor Defense via Counterfactual Invariance for Neural Code Models","tz":"CID：面向神经代码模型的基于反事实不变性的免干净种子后门防御","a":"Neural code models, which automate foundational software engineering tasks such as code classification and generation, are critically vulnerable to backdoor attacks. Yet, existing defenses face a dual failure: they struggle with sophisticated threats spanning injection-based and semantically-equivalent transformation (SET-based) backdoor attacks, and they rely on a restrictive assumption—a trusted, pre-verified in-distribution clean seed set—that can be costly and difficult to obtain and audit in practice. This paper introduces Counterfactual Invariance-based Defense (CID), a clean-seed-free backdoor defense—requiring no a priori trusted in-distribution clean data—grounded in operational counterfactual invariance tests. CID’s core insight is that clean and poisoned samples exhibit asymmetric counterfactual behavior: clean predictions degrade under semantic context corruption (semantic sufficiency), whereas backdoor predictions change when a localized trigger is neutralized (trigger necessity). Accordingly, CID applies two orthogonal probes—a contextual intervention to test semantic sufficiency and a structural neutralization test guided by a gradient-based probe to test trigger necessity—to extract a high-purity clean seed set directly from a mixed dataset. This seed set then enables Mahalanobis-based clustering in representation space to partition the full dataset. Evaluated across four software engineering tasks and three model architectures, and further validated on multilingual code summarization, CID achieves strong poison detection performance among evaluated baselines while keeping false positives low in most settings. By eliminating reliance on a priori trusted in-distribution clean seed data, CID provides a practical pathway toward more secure deployment of neural code models.","az":"神经代码模型自动化了代码分类与生成等基础软件工程任务，但它们极易受到后门攻击。然而现有防御面临双重失败：它们难以应对跨越注入式与语义等价变换式（SET-based）后门攻击的复杂威胁，并且依赖一个限制性的假设——一个可信的、预先验证过的同分布干净种子集，而这在实践中获取与审计的代价高昂且困难。本文提出基于反事实不变性的防御（CID），一种无需干净种子的后门防御——不需要任何先验可信的同分布干净数据——其基础是可操作的反事实不变性检验。CID 的核心洞见是：干净样本与被投毒样本表现出不对称的反事实行为：干净样本的预测在语义上下文被破坏时会退化（语义充分性），而后门样本的预测在局部触发器被中和时会改变（触发器必要性）。据此，CID 应用两个正交探针——用上下文干预检验语义充分性，用梯度探针引导的结构中和检验触发器必要性——直接从混合数据集中提取高纯度的干净种子集。该种子集随后支持在表示空间中进行基于马氏距离的聚类，以划分整个数据集。在四项软件工程任务与三种模型架构上评估，并在多语言代码摘要上进一步验证，CID 在所评估的基线中取得了强劲的投毒检测性能，同时在多数设置下保持较低的误报率。通过消除对先验可信同分布干净种子数据的依赖，CID 为神经代码模型更安全的部署提供了一条实用路径。","tl":"用反事实不变性自动提纯干净种子，实现免种子假设的代码模型后门防御。","au":["Junyao Ye","Zhen Li","Xi Tang","Shulin Li","Shi Liang","Deqing Zou","Hai Jin"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["backdoor defense","neural code models","counterfactual invariance","poison detection","clean-seed-free"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/160/x"},{"id":"p01443","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Provably Lossless Acceleration of DNN Mutation Testing via Memoization","tz":"通过记忆化对 DNN 变异测试进行可证明无损的加速","a":"Mutation analysis has recently reemerged in the context of deep neural networks (DNNs) as a promising, but notoriously costly, approach for assessing test dataset adequacy. Existing techniques speed up DNN mutation testing through lossy approximations that trade efficiency for mutation score accuracy. This paper introduces Mure, the first provably lossless framework for accelerating DNN mutation testing via memoization. Mure is based on the idea that DNN mutants and the original model share substantial redundant computation, so during mutation testing, it executes only the mutated suffixes of each mutant and reuses the common prefix from the original model, which is computed only once. We give a formal account of memoized mutation testing, and prove that Mure is sound, i.e., it produces results equivalent to exhaustive vanilla mutation testing, and identify basic conditions under which speed-up is guaranteed. We have implemented Mure and evaluated it on 15 DNN models of various architectures, complexities, and sizes ranging from a few thousands to millions of parameters. This provides empirical evidence that Mure reduces the computational cost of mutation testing by 44.54%, on average. We also observed that while state-of-the-art techniques tend to yield higher acceleration (up to 88.97%, on average), they come at the cost of some error in mutation score. We further analyze the effect of mutation generation selection ratio on the effectiveness of Mure and observed predictable reductions in memoization opportunities with increasing the percentage of mutated neurons. We observed that Mure offers more than 20% speed-up even when as high as 5% of the neurons are mutated.","az":"变异分析近来在深度神经网络（DNN）背景下重新兴起，成为评估测试数据集充分性的有前景但出了名昂贵的方法。现有技术通过有损近似加速 DNN 变异测试，以变异分数准确性换取效率。本文提出 Mure，首个通过记忆化（memoization）加速 DNN 变异测试的可证明无损框架。Mure 基于这样一个想法：DNN 变异体与原始模型共享大量冗余计算，因此在变异测试期间，它只执行每个变异体被修改的后缀部分，并复用只需计算一次的原始模型公共前缀。我们给出了记忆化变异测试的形式化描述，并证明 Mure 是可靠的，即其产生的结果与穷举式的朴素变异测试等价，同时识别出保证加速的基本条件。我们实现了 Mure，并在 15 个架构、复杂度和规模各异（参数量从数千到数百万）的 DNN 模型上进行评估。这提供了实证证据：Mure 平均将变异测试的计算成本降低 44.54%。我们还观察到，虽然最先进技术往往能带来更高的加速（平均最高 88.97%），但代价是变异分数存在一定误差。我们进一步分析了变异生成选择比例对 Mure 有效性的影响，观察到随着被变异神经元比例增加，记忆化机会出现可预测的下降。我们发现，即使高达 5% 的神经元被变异，Mure 仍能提供超过 20% 的加速。","tl":"首个可证明无损的 DNN 变异测试加速框架，复用公共前缀计算。","au":["Ali Ghanbari","Ben Greenman","Sasan Tavakkol","Shibbir Ahmed"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mutation testing","memoization","DNN testing","lossless acceleration","test adequacy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/161/x"},{"id":"p01444","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Profiling-Guided Bayesian Optimization of JVM Configurations","tz":"性能剖析引导的 JVM 配置贝叶斯优化","a":"Regression testing is essential for maintaining software quality but often incurs substantial time costs. While regression testing time can often be reduced by selectively running fewer tests, prior work has demonstrated that tuning Java Virtual Machine (JVM) configuration flags can also reduce testing time in Java projects, even while running all tests and preserving original testing outcomes. However, finding effective flag combinations remains challenging due to the vast configuration space and complex interactions between flags. Random search and direct modeling approaches that map flag configurations to testing time have shown limited effectiveness in navigating this complex optimization landscape. We present PROBO (PROfiling-Guided Bayesian Optimization), an iterative approach that leverages JVM runtime metrics (e.g., garbage collection frequency, just-in-time (JIT) compilation rates, and memory allocation) to guide Bayesian optimization for testing time reduction. Unlike prior work using Bayesian inference that directly models the relationship from flag configurations to testing time, PROBO decomposes the prediction problem through observable runtime behaviors: a metrics model predicts how flag configurations affect runtime metrics, and a performance model predicts how those metrics affect testing time. PROBO collects 44 runtime metrics using a profiler during test execution, and propagates feature importance scores through both models to identify which flags most strongly influence testing time-predictive metrics. Finally, PROBO generates candidate flag configurations through three complementary strategies guided by expected testing time improvement. We evaluate PROBO on 16 open-source Java projects, comparing against random search and BOCA (a Bayesian optimization baseline). PROBO achieves an average testing time reduction of 10.7% across all projects when evaluating 20 configurations per project, outperforming random search (5.8%) by 1.85× and BOCA (4.3%) by 2.49×. PROBO successfully generates configurations that substantially reduce testing time for all 16 projects, with reductions ranging up to 27.4%. With a one-hour time budget for search, PROBO maintains its advantage with 8.0% average reduction, demonstrating practical applicability. PROBO-generated configurations remain effective across software evolution, maintaining 8.8% average reduction over an average of 88 future commits per project. Our analysis reveals that metrics related to JIT compilation, particularly Total Compilation Rate (methods compiled per second) and C1 Compilation Rate (first-tier JIT compilation rate), are the strongest predictors of testing time, accounting for 67.2% of consistently important metrics across projects.","az":"回归测试对维持软件质量至关重要，但往往带来大量时间开销。虽然回归测试时间常可通过选择性地运行更少的测试来缩短，先前工作已表明，调优 Java 虚拟机（JVM）配置标志同样可以在运行全部测试并保持原有测试结果的前提下减少 Java 项目的测试时间。然而，由于配置空间巨大以及标志之间复杂的交互作用，寻找有效的标志组合仍然困难。随机搜索以及把标志配置直接映射到测试时间的直接建模方法，在这一复杂优化地形中被证明效果有限。我们提出 PROBO（性能剖析引导的贝叶斯优化），一种迭代方法，利用 JVM 运行时指标（如垃圾回收频率、即时（JIT）编译速率和内存分配）来引导贝叶斯优化以缩短测试时间。与先前使用贝叶斯推断直接建模“标志配置到测试时间”关系的工作不同，PROBO 通过可观测的运行时行为分解预测问题：一个指标模型预测标志配置如何影响运行时指标，一个性能模型预测这些指标如何影响测试时间。PROBO 在测试执行期间使用性能剖析器收集 44 个运行时指标，并在两个模型间传播特征重要性分数，以识别哪些标志对预测测试时间的指标影响最强。最后，PROBO 通过三种互补策略、以期望的测试时间改进为指导生成候选标志配置。我们在 16 个开源 Java 项目上评估 PROBO，与随机搜索和 BOCA（贝叶斯优化基线）比较。在每个项目评估 20 个配置的条件下，PROBO 在所有项目上实现平均 10.7% 的测试时间缩减，比随机搜索（5.8%）高 1.85 倍，比 BOCA（4.3%）高 2.49 倍。PROBO 成功地为全部 16 个项目生成了能大幅缩短测试时间的配置，缩减幅度最高达 27.4%。在一小时搜索预算下，PROBO 仍保持优势，平均缩减 8.0%，显示了实际可用性。PROBO 生成的配置在软件演进中依然有效，在每个项目平均 88 次后续提交上保持 8.8% 的平均缩减。我们的分析显示，与 JIT 编译相关的指标，尤其是总编译速率（每秒编译方法数）和 C1 编译速率（第一层 JIT 编译速率），是测试时间最强的预测因子，占各项目中一贯重要指标的 67.2%。","tl":"用运行时指标解耦建模引导贝叶斯优化，显著优于直接建模的 JVM 调优。","au":["Abdelrahman Baz","Wing Lam","August Shi"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["JVM configuration tuning","Bayesian optimization","regression testing time","runtime profiling metrics","JIT compilation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/162/x","pu":"https://people.cs.gmu.edu/~winglam/publications/2026/BazETAL26Probo.pdf"},{"id":"p01445","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding and Improving Model Editing for Secure Code Generation","tz":"理解并改进面向安全代码生成的模型编辑","a":"Large language models (LLMs) are widely used for code generation, yet they can reproduce vulnerable code implementations learned from insecure patterns in training data. Prior work has primarily explored inference-time hardening to reduce insecure generations without updating the target model. While effective, this paradigm couples security behavior to the auxiliary component and incurs additional runtime overhead. This paper presents the first systematic empirical study of applying model editing as the model-level hardening mechanism for secure code generation. Unlike inference-time interventions, model editing updates a small subset of parameters to inject security-relevant knowledge directly into the target LLM. We evaluate 3 state-of-the-art editing methods across diverse LLM families and compare them with CoSec, a representative inference-time hardening approach, focusing on: (i) security effectiveness and robustness, (ii) generalization to unseen vulnerabilities, and (iii) functional correctness on general programming tasks. Our results show that model editing yields substantially larger security gains than CoSec on seen vulnerability types, improving security ratios by 15%–25% over vanilla models, and these gains remain stable under prompt perturbations. However, security improvements do not always transfer reliably to unseen vulnerabilities and induce functional regressions on general programming tasks, even for UltraEdit, the best-performing editing method in our evaluation. To mitigate this side effect, we propose SafeEdit, an effective post-edit refinement method that combines functional tuning with edit-aware regularization, which improves Pass@1 by 44.40%–156.07% over UltraEdit and largely preserves (and even improves) security. Moreover, SafeEdit and CoSec are complementary: combining them can further improve security under stochastic decoding while maintaining strong functional correctness. Finally, we analyze efficiency and key design factors, showing that model editing is more efficient than CoSec and sensitive to editing depth, parameter location, and injected context. Overall, our work provides evidence-backed guidance for applying model editing to secure code generation.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）被广泛用于代码生成，但它们可能复现从训练数据中不安全模式学到的脆弱代码实现。先前工作主要探索推理时加固，在不更新目标模型的前提下减少不安全生成。这种范式虽然有效，却把安全行为耦合到辅助组件上，并带来额外的运行时开销。本文首次系统性地实证研究了把模型编辑作为模型级加固机制用于安全代码生成。与推理时干预不同，模型编辑更新一小部分参数，把与安全相关的知识直接注入目标 LLM。我们在多个 LLM 家族上评估了 3 种最先进的编辑方法，并与代表性的推理时加固方法 CoSec 比较，聚焦于：(i) 安全有效性与鲁棒性；(ii) 对未见漏洞的泛化性；(iii) 在通用编程任务上的功能正确性。结果表明，在已见漏洞类型上，模型编辑带来的安全收益远大于 CoSec，相比原始模型将安全比例提升 15%–25%，并且这些收益在提示扰动下保持稳定。然而，安全改进并不总能可靠地迁移到未见漏洞，并且会在通用编程任务上引起功能回退，即便对我们评估中表现最好的编辑方法 UltraEdit 也是如此。为缓解这一副作用，我们提出 SafeEdit，一种有效的编辑后精化方法，它把功能微调与编辑感知正则化结合起来，相比 UltraEdit 将 Pass@1 提升 44.40%–156.07%，并在很大程度上保持（甚至提升）安全性。此外，SafeEdit 与 CoSec 是互补的：将二者结合可在随机解码下进一步提升安全性，同时保持强的功能正确性。最后，我们分析了效率与关键设计因素，表明模型编辑比 CoSec 更高效，并且对编辑深度、参数位置和注入上下文敏感。总体而言，我们的工作为把模型编辑应用于安全代码生成提供了有证据支撑的指导。","tl":"首次系统评估模型编辑用于安全代码生成，并提出 SafeEdit 弥补功能回退。","au":["Weifeng Sun","Quanjun Zhang","Yuchen Chen","Chengran Yang","Gou Tan","David Lo"],"top":"secure-code-generation","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["security","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["model editing","secure code generation","inference-time hardening","SafeEdit","functional regression"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/163/x"},{"id":"p01446","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Multi-Stage On-Demand Program Slicing for Modular Analysis of Multi-Threaded Programs","tz":"面向多线程程序模块化分析的多阶段按需程序切片","a":"Precise analysis of multi-threaded programs requires combining flow-sensitive pointer analysis (FSPTA) with interleaving and lock analysis (ILA) to reason about cross-thread value flows under feasible concurrent executions. ILA computes may-happen-in-parallel (MHP) relations and lock-release spans to determine when shared accesses can occur concurrently. Unfortunately, these analyses are both expensive and tightly coupled: FSPTA needs ILA to rule out infeasible inter-thread def-use relations, while ILA needs alias information to identify interference-relevant interactions. As a result, whole-program analyses often spend most of their time on code that is irrelevant to the client query. We present MSli, an on-demand slicing framework for modular analysis of multi-threaded programs. It extracts compact, query-relevant program slices while preserving the answers of downstream analyses. Unlike single-pass slicing over a unified dependence graph, MSli performs multi-stage slicing with analysis-specific criteria. Concretely, a lightweight pre-analysis establishes an over-approximation of inter-thread value flows and performs ILA slicing source extraction to identify the MHP and lock-span queries required later for ILA slicing. The refined main-phase ILA results then enable reconstruction of a thread-aware value-flow graph to guide FSPTA slicing, supporting modular analysis and downstream clients. We implement MSli in SVF and evaluate it on ten large real-world projects with data race detection as a representative client. Compared with the unsliced baseline (FSAM), MSli reduces the analyzed ICFG to 5.4% (ILA) and 25.7% (FSPTA), reduces ILA/FSPTA runtimes to 4.7%/18.3%, and cuts total analysis time to 20.8% on average, while producing identical query outcomes and race alarms.","az":"对多线程程序的精确分析需要把流敏感指针分析（FSPTA）与交错及锁分析（ILA）结合，以在可行的并发执行下推理跨线程的值流。ILA 计算可能并行发生（MHP）关系与锁释放跨度，以确定共享访问何时可能并发发生。不幸的是，这两类分析既昂贵又紧密耦合：FSPTA 需要 ILA 来排除不可行的线程间定义-使用关系，而 ILA 又需要别名信息来识别与干扰相关的交互。结果，整程序分析往往把大部分时间花在与客户查询无关的代码上。我们提出 MSli，一个面向多线程程序模块化分析的按需切片框架。它抽取紧凑的、与查询相关的程序切片，同时保持下游分析的答案不变。与在统一依赖图上做单趟切片不同，MSli 采用带有分析特定准则的多阶段切片。具体而言，一个轻量级预分析建立线程间值流的过近似，并执行 ILA 切片源抽取，以识别后续 ILA 切片所需的 MHP 与锁跨度查询。精化后的主阶段 ILA 结果随后支持重建线程感知的值流图，以指导 FSPTA 切片，从而支持模块化分析与下游客户。我们在 SVF 中实现 MSli，并在十个大型真实项目上以数据竞争检测作为代表性客户进行评估。与未切片的基线（FSAM）相比，MSli 把被分析的 ICFG 缩减到 5.4%（ILA）和 25.7%（FSPTA），把 ILA/FSPTA 运行时间分别降到 4.7%/18.3%，总分析时间平均降至 20.8%，同时产生完全相同的查询结果与竞争告警。","tl":"多阶段按需切片解耦 ILA 与指针分析，5 倍加速且结果完全一致。","au":["Jiawei Yang","Xiao Cheng","Jiawei Wang","Xiapu Luo","Yulei Sui"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["program slicing","flow-sensitive pointer analysis","may-happen-in-parallel","multi-threaded analysis","data race detection"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/164/x"},{"id":"p01447","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ProgSCA: Software Composition Analysis via Program-Level Modeling","tz":"ProgSCA：基于程序级建模的软件成分分析","a":"Software composition analysis (SCA) aims to identify third-party dependencies in programs, which plays a critical role in ensuring software supply chain security. Existing approaches largely follow a rule-based paradigm: they first compute function-level similarities, then aggregate these results using handcrafted heuristics to determine which third-party libraries (TPLs) the target program depends on. However, such rules require substantial manual effort and expert knowledge to design, tune, and maintain. To address this, we present ProgSCA, an SCA framework based on a two-stage strategy and program-level rather than function-level modeling. ProgSCA formulates SCA as a retrieval problem, first employing lightweight methods to quickly filter out irrelevant libraries from numerous candidate TPLs, then using a model trained at the program level to directly predict dependency between programs. Comprehensive evaluations show that ProgSCA achieves state-of-the-art performance in SCA tasks, improving F1 scores over existing methods by 174% and 100% in two mainstream scenarios, respectively. Moreover, ProgSCA proves effective in the downstream task of function similarity matching, further demonstrating the practical value of our approach.","az":"软件成分分析（SCA）旨在识别程序中的第三方依赖，对保障软件供应链安全起着关键作用。现有方法大多遵循基于规则的范式：先计算函数级相似度，再用手工启发式规则聚合这些结果，以判定目标程序依赖哪些第三方库（TPL）。然而，这类规则的设计、调优与维护需要大量人工投入与专家知识。为此，我们提出 ProgSCA，一个基于两阶段策略、以程序级而非函数级建模的 SCA 框架。ProgSCA 把 SCA 形式化为一个检索问题：先用轻量级方法从众多候选 TPL 中快速过滤掉无关库，再使用在程序级训练的模型直接预测程序之间的依赖关系。全面评估表明，ProgSCA 在 SCA 任务上达到了最先进的性能，在两种主流场景下相比现有方法将 F1 分数分别提升 174% 与 100%。此外，ProgSCA 在下游的函数相似度匹配任务中同样有效，进一步验证了本方法的实用价值。","tl":"把软件成分分析建模为程序级检索问题，摆脱手工启发式规则。","au":["Peihong Li","Cheng Li","guyuchen","Yanzhe Hu","Liheng Chen","Zeyu Gao","Hao Wang","Chao Zhang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["security","non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["software composition analysis","third-party library detection","program-level modeling","supply chain security","retrieval"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/165/x"},{"id":"p01448","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SmartDecompiler-R1: Enhancing Faithful and Explainable Smart Contract Bytecode Decompilation with Reinforcement Learning","tz":"SmartDecompiler-R1：用强化学习增强忠实且可解释的智能合约字节码反编译","a":"Understanding EVM bytecode is critical for smart contract security analysis. Existing decompilers typically rely on heuristic rules or leverage large language models (LLMs) to generate source code after bytecode analysis. However, heuristic-based approaches often produce pseudocode that is difficult for humans to interpret, while LLM-based methods also face several problems. LLMs have little experience with low-level bytecode, which weakens their reasoning and causes inaccurate results. Additionally, their tendency to auto-correct code breaks faithfulness to the original program. A general lack of clarity in these approaches also hinders effective auditing and interpretation. In this paper, we propose SmartDecompiler-R1, an end-to-end decompilation framework that translates Three-Address Code (TAC), a register-based representation of EVM bytecode, into source code using reinforcement learning. SmartDecompiler-R1 significantly improves both the accuracy and consistency of decompiled code, while additionally providing human-readable explanations for the bytecode-to-source generation process. To the best of our knowledge, we are the first to design a benchmark equipped with well-defined test cases and a systematic evaluation framework for smart contract decompilation. Experimental results on this benchmark demonstrate that SmartDecompiler-R1 substantially outperforms existing decompilers on execution consistency by 46.23%. In particular, compared with LLM-based approaches, SmartDecompiler-R1 achieves a significant improvement in preserving vulnerability consistency between the original and decompiled contracts. Furthermore, we conduct extensive ablation studies to validate the effectiveness of individual components of SmartDecompiler-R1, and design targeted experiments to demonstrate the interpretability and readability of the generated explanations.","az":"理解 EVM 字节码对智能合约安全分析至关重要。现有反编译器通常依赖启发式规则，或在字节码分析后利用大语言模型（LLM）生成源代码。然而，基于启发式的方法往往产生人类难以理解的伪代码，而基于 LLM 的方法也面临若干问题：LLM 对底层字节码经验很少，这削弱了其推理能力并导致结果不准确；此外，它们倾向于自动“纠正”代码，破坏了对原程序的忠实性。这些方法普遍缺乏清晰性，也妨碍了有效的审计与解读。本文提出 SmartDecompiler-R1，一个端到端的反编译框架，使用强化学习把三地址码（TAC，一种基于寄存器的 EVM 字节码表示）翻译为源代码。SmartDecompiler-R1 显著提升了反编译代码的准确性与一致性，并额外为字节码到源码的生成过程提供人类可读的解释。据我们所知，我们是首个为智能合约反编译设计配备良定义测试用例与系统性评估框架的基准。在该基准上的实验结果表明，SmartDecompiler-R1 在执行一致性上大幅超越现有反编译器 46.23%。特别是，与基于 LLM 的方法相比，SmartDecompiler-R1 在保持原合约与反编译合约之间漏洞一致性方面取得了显著改进。此外，我们开展了广泛的消融实验以验证 SmartDecompiler-R1 各组件的有效性，并设计了针对性实验来展示所生成解释的可解释性与可读性。","tl":"用强化学习从 TAC 端到端反编译合约，兼顾忠实性与可解释性。","au":["Yilun Ma","Lingxiao Tang","Li Lin","Zhipeng Gao","Jiachi Chen","Xin Xia","Lingfeng Bao"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","tg":["llm-based","benchmark-dataset","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["smart contract decompilation","EVM bytecode","reinforcement learning","three-address code","execution consistency"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/166/x"},{"id":"p01449","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Revisiting Graph Representations for ML-based Binary Code Similarity Detection: A Systematic Study","tz":"重新审视基于机器学习的二进制代码相似度检测中的图表示：一项系统性研究","a":"Binary Code Similarity Detection (BCSD) is a foundational capability in software security, underpinning critical applications ranging from vulnerability detection to malware analysis. While recent tools based on Machine Learning (ML) have achieved significant performance improvements, their efficacy is heavily contingent upon the underlying code representation. Through a systematic literature review of ML-based BCSD papers, we find that existing approaches typically leverage linear sequences or adopt graph-based representations, with the latter constituting the majority (77%). Despite this prevalence, there is no consensus on which graph representation yields superior effectiveness. Existing works usually couple graph construction with customized learning backbones and evaluate them on inconsistent benchmarks. This makes isolating the representation’s impact difficult. Consequently, determining which graph topology truly captures the robust semantics of binary code remains an unsolved problem. In this paper, we present the first systematic study of graph representations for ML-based BCSD to bridge this gap. Specifically, we implement a modular evaluation framework that decouples graph construction from model training. Using this framework, we systematically evaluate seven representative graph representations, finding that no single representation is universally dominant, as distinct topologies exhibit unique strengths depending on the evaluation scenario. We further investigate their combination effectiveness in N-day vulnerability detection and employ a tailored interpretability tool, which demonstrates that models trained on data-centric representations primarily focus on sparse semantic cores while those learning from control-centric graphs depend on global connectivity.","az":"二进制代码相似度检测（BCSD）是软件安全中的基础能力，支撑着从漏洞检测到恶意软件分析等关键应用。尽管近期基于机器学习（ML）的工具取得了显著的性能提升，其效果高度依赖于底层的代码表示。通过对基于 ML 的 BCSD 论文进行系统性文献综述，我们发现现有方法通常利用线性序列，或采用基于图的表示，后者占多数（77%）。尽管图表示如此普遍，对于哪种图表示能带来更好的效果仍无共识。现有工作通常把图构造与定制化的学习骨干网络耦合在一起，并在不一致的基准上评估，这使得孤立地分析表示本身的影响变得困难。因此，究竟哪种图拓扑真正捕捉了二进制代码的鲁棒语义，仍是一个未解问题。本文首次对基于 ML 的 BCSD 的图表示开展系统性研究以填补这一空白。具体而言，我们实现了一个模块化评估框架，把图构造与模型训练解耦。利用该框架，我们系统评估了七种有代表性的图表示，发现没有任何单一表示能普遍占优，不同拓扑依评估场景展现出各自独特的优势。我们进一步考察了它们在 N-day 漏洞检测中的组合效果，并使用定制的可解释性工具，表明在以数据为中心的表示上训练的模型主要关注稀疏的语义核心，而从以控制流为中心的图中学习的模型则依赖全局连通性。","tl":"解耦图构造与模型训练，首次公平比较七种 BCSD 图表示。","au":["Tengteng Yang","Yikun Hu","jican zhang","Lei Xue","Ming Fan","Liang Zhang"],"top":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","alt":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical","security"],"kw":["binary code similarity detection","graph representation","systematic study","modular evaluation","interpretability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/167/x"},{"id":"p01450","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"SEDCoT: Enhancing LLM-Based COBOL Code Translation via Symbolic Execution and Delta Debugging","tz":"SEDCoT：通过符号执行与增量调试增强基于 LLM 的 COBOL 代码翻译","a":"COBOL, as a representative legacy programming language, has been widely adopted in sectors such as banking, insurance, and government infrastructure. Maintaining COBOL code has become increasingly challenging due to outdated technologies, sparse documentation, and the retirement of original developers, which creates a pressing need to translate COBOL code into mainstream programming languages such as C. However, the unique grammar and semantics of COBOL make rule-based translation difficult to understand and maintain. Furthermore, translation performance using large language models (LLMs) is suboptimal compared to other programming languages, as COBOL is low-resource and exhibits distinct logical and behavioral patterns. To address these challenges, we propose a novel COBOL translation framework, SEDCoT. In SEDCoT, we first leverage large language models (LLMs) to translate COBOL code into the target programming language. Next, we employ a combination of symbolic execution and LLMs to generate test cases for the translated code and to repair any errors detected. Finally, we apply delta debugging to simplify test cases that are difficult to fix, thereby guiding LLMs to perform more effective code repairs. We conduct a comprehensive evaluation of SEDCoT on a public COBOL-to-C dataset. The experimental results show that SEDCoT outperforms state-of-the-art methods by at least 12%, demonstrating its effectiveness. Furthermore, our readability evaluation indicates that code translated by SEDCoT exhibits substantially higher readability compared to rule-based translation methods.","az":"COBOL 作为具有代表性的遗留编程语言，已在银行、保险和政府基础设施等领域被广泛采用。由于技术过时、文档稀缺以及原始开发者的退休，维护 COBOL 代码变得越来越困难，这带来了把 COBOL 代码翻译为 C 等主流编程语言的迫切需求。然而，COBOL 独特的语法与语义使得基于规则的翻译难以理解和维护。此外，由于 COBOL 是低资源语言且展现出独特的逻辑与行为模式，使用大语言模型（LLM）的翻译性能相比其他编程语言并不理想。为应对这些挑战，我们提出一个新颖的 COBOL 翻译框架 SEDCoT。在 SEDCoT 中，我们首先利用大语言模型（LLM）把 COBOL 代码翻译为目标编程语言；接着，我们结合符号执行与 LLM 为翻译后的代码生成测试用例，并修复检测到的任何错误；最后，我们应用增量调试（delta debugging）简化那些难以修复的测试用例，从而引导 LLM 执行更有效的代码修复。我们在一个公开的 COBOL 到 C 数据集上对 SEDCoT 进行了全面评估。实验结果表明，SEDCoT 至少比最先进方法高出 12%，验证了其有效性。此外，我们的可读性评估表明，相比基于规则的翻译方法，SEDCoT 翻译出的代码具有显著更高的可读性。","tl":"用符号执行生成测试加增量调试引导 LLM 修复 COBOL 翻译错误。","au":["Phillip Entin","Wenchao Gu","Alexander Knapp","Chunyang Chen"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["llm-based","low-resource-or-non-english","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["COBOL translation","symbolic execution","delta debugging","legacy modernization","LLM code translation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/168/x"},{"id":"p01451","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ConUT: Condition-Aware Test Generation for Complex Java Code","tz":"ConUT：面向复杂 Java 代码的条件感知测试生成","a":"Automatically generating high-coverage unit tests for complex Java methods remains a formidable challenge, particularly when execution paths are guarded by intricate control-flow nesting and cross-class state dependencies. Existing LLM-based approaches predominantly follow a goal-driven paradigm, relying on unguided code synthesis within a vast search space to satisfy coverage objectives. Lacking explicit guidance on how to construct the precise object states required for complex predicates, these methods suffer from a construction-reachability gap, ultimately resulting in insufficient coverage for complex methods. This paper introduces ConUT, a condition-aware unit test generation framework centered on the paradigm of Configuration-Driven Guidance, which is a strategy that bridges the gap between abstract branch targets and concrete code realization by providing the LLM with structured instantiation recipes. Our core insight is that the implicit causal chain leading to a target branch can be explicitly manifested via static analysis and distilled into structured guidance. ConUT utilizes Backward Dependency Tracing (BDT) to identify the fields and method calls that influence predicates, and distills these findings into structured Configuration Templates (C_{cfg}). These templates serve as a ``semantic roadmap,'' pruning the LLM’s search space and transitioning it from a stochastic generator into a guided logic realizer. We evaluate ConUT on eight real-world Java projects characterized by high-complexity ``logic hotspots''. Experimental results demonstrate that ConUT significantly outperforms state-of-the-art baselines, achieving an average branch coverage of 72.84% and line coverage of 83.87%. Notably, ConUT exceeds the best baseline by 11.94% branch coverage improvement while utilizing 67% fewer test cases. These findings prove ConUT’s effectiveness in bridging the gap between program analysis and LLM synthesis through explicit causal-chain manifestation.","az":"为复杂的 Java 方法自动生成高覆盖率的单元测试仍然是一项艰巨的挑战，尤其是当执行路径被错综复杂的嵌套控制流和跨类状态依赖所守护时。现有基于大语言模型的方法大多遵循一种“目标驱动范式”，依赖在巨大搜索空间内无引导的代码合成来满足覆盖率目标。由于缺乏关于“如何”构造复杂谓词所需的精确对象状态的显式指导，这些方法存在构造—可达性鸿沟，最终导致对复杂方法的覆盖不足。本文提出 ConUT，一个以“配置驱动引导”范式为核心的条件感知单元测试生成框架，该策略通过向大语言模型提供结构化的实例化配方，弥合抽象分支目标与具体代码实现之间的鸿沟。我们的核心洞见是：通向目标分支的隐式因果链可以通过静态分析显式呈现出来，并提炼为结构化的引导信息。ConUT 利用“反向依赖追踪”（Backward Dependency Tracing，BDT）识别影响谓词的字段与方法调用，并将这些发现提炼为结构化的配置模板（$C_{cfg}$）。这些模板充当“语义路线图”，裁剪大语言模型的搜索空间，使其从随机生成器转变为受引导的逻辑实现者。我们在八个具有高复杂度“逻辑热点”的真实 Java 项目上评估 ConUT。实验结果表明，ConUT 显著优于当前最先进的基线方法，平均分支覆盖率达到 72.84%，行覆盖率达到 83.87%。值得注意的是，ConUT 在分支覆盖率上比最佳基线高出 11.94%，同时使用的测试用例数量减少了 67%。这些发现证明了 ConUT 通过显式的因果链呈现，有效弥合了程序分析与大语言模型合成之间的鸿沟。","tl":"用静态反向依赖追踪产出配置模板来引导 LLM 覆盖复杂分支。","au":["RuiGuo Yu","ruiqi dong","Xi Xiao","Xiaogang Zhu","Shaohua Wang","Sheng Wen","Qingli"],"top":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["unit test generation","branch coverage","backward dependency tracing","static analysis guidance","LLM"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/169/x"},{"id":"p01452","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Testing Method Relocation Algorithms via Template-Based Systematic Structural Traversal and Precondition Filtering","tz":"通过基于模板的系统性结构遍历与前置条件过滤测试方法重定位算法","a":"Method relocation refactorings, primarily Move Method and Pull Up/Push Down Method, are indispensable for reducing coupling and enhancing cohesion. Despite their widespread automation in modern refactoring engines, these algorithms remain notoriously error-prone, posing significant risks to software reliability. A primary challenge in testing them lies in the vast search space of complex program structures and the intricate preconditions required for safe method relocation. To address this, we propose RelocTest, a comprehensive testing framework that combines template-driven structural traversal with automated precondition filtering. RelocTest systematically explores the input space by populating program templates specially designed for method relocation through a two-stage generation process: (1) Skeleton Synthesis, which systematically traverses diverse syntactic structures, and (2) LLM-Guided Completion, which leverages Large Language Models to inject diverse, executable code into these skeletons. This hybrid strategy ensures high structural coverage while maintaining test case validity. Furthermore, to optimize testing efficiency, we introduce an LLM-based Precondition Extractor that analyzes the implementation of method relocation algorithms to identify and prune test cases destined for rejection. We evaluated RelocTest on 7 mainstream refactoring engines. Our approach successfully uncovered 56 previously unknown bugs, with 19 already confirmed by tool vendors, demonstrating its effectiveness in hardening industrial-strength refactoring tools.","az":"方法重定位重构，主要是 Move Method 和 Pull Up/Push Down Method，对于降低耦合、提升内聚是不可或缺的。尽管现代重构引擎已广泛实现其自动化，这些算法仍然出了名地容易出错，给软件可靠性带来重大风险。测试它们的主要挑战在于复杂程序结构的巨大搜索空间，以及安全进行方法重定位所需的错综复杂的前置条件。为此，我们提出 RelocTest，一个将模板驱动的结构遍历与自动化前置条件过滤相结合的综合测试框架。RelocTest 通过两阶段生成过程填充专为方法重定位设计的程序模板，系统性地探索输入空间：(1) 骨架合成（Skeleton Synthesis），系统性地遍历多样的语法结构；(2) LLM 引导的补全（LLM-Guided Completion），利用大语言模型向这些骨架中注入多样且可执行的代码。这一混合策略在保持测试用例有效性的同时确保了高结构覆盖率。此外，为优化测试效率，我们引入一个基于大语言模型的前置条件提取器，它分析方法重定位算法的实现，识别并剪除注定会被拒绝的测试用例。我们在 7 个主流重构引擎上评估了 RelocTest。我们的方法成功发现了 56 个此前未知的缺陷，其中 19 个已被工具厂商确认，证明了其在加固工业级重构工具方面的有效性。","tl":"模板骨架加 LLM 补全，系统测出重构引擎 56 个新缺陷。","au":["Chunhao Dong","Yanjie Jiang","Yang Zhang","Hui Liu"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["refactoring engine testing","move method","program template generation","precondition filtering","LLM-guided completion"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/170/x"},{"id":"p01453","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"E2WR: An Effective and Efficient Reduction Framework for WebAssembly Binaries","tz":"E2WR：一个高效有效的 WebAssembly 二进制归约框架","a":"WebAssembly (Wasm) is a prominent programming language enabling high-performance execution across diverse computing environments. However, bugs in Wasm runtimes, which execute Wasm binaries, can lead to severe security breaches and system failures. Manually debugging Wasm binaries that trigger such runtime bugs is exceedingly difficult due to their poor human readability, stemming from low-level stack-based instructions, complex control flow structures, and extraordinary length, often containing millions of instructions. Thus, there is a critical need for automated reduction techniques that minimize Wasm binaries while preserving the ability to trigger the original bug. However, existing reducers often suffer from significant limitations in effectiveness and efficiency: language-agnostic reducers frequently generate invalid variants without Wasm validation awareness, while Wasm-specific reducers still lack efficient delta-debugging-style intra-function instruction-sequence reduction and reduce non-function definitions inefficiently. To address these challenges, we propose E^2WR, an effective and efficient reduction framework for Wasm binaries. E^2WR introduces a two-stage approach for intra-function instruction-sequence reduction, consisting of operand-dependency guided instruction reduction and combinational redundancy elimination to enable efficient delta debugging while avoiding unnecessary padding instructions, and a non-function-oriented reduction approach that combines static analysis with delta-debugging-guided trials to remove property-irrelevant non-function definitions efficiently. Compared with Wasm-Shrink and Wasm-Reduce, E^2WR produces binaries that are 95.4% and 63.9% smaller, respectively, and achieves reduction speed improvement of 11.1 and 5.1 , respectively.","az":"WebAssembly（Wasm）是一种重要的编程语言，能够在多样的计算环境中实现高性能执行。然而，执行 Wasm 二进制的 Wasm 运行时中的缺陷可能导致严重的安全漏洞和系统故障。手工调试触发此类运行时缺陷的 Wasm 二进制极其困难，因为它们可读性很差，源于底层的基于栈的指令、复杂的控制流结构以及极长的长度（往往包含数百万条指令）。因此，迫切需要在保留触发原始缺陷能力的前提下最小化 Wasm 二进制的自动化归约技术。然而，现有归约器在有效性和效率上往往存在显著局限：语言无关的归约器由于缺乏 Wasm 验证意识，经常生成无效变体；而 Wasm 专用归约器仍缺乏高效的、delta 调试式的函数内指令序列归约，并且在归约非函数定义时效率低下。为解决这些挑战，我们提出 E$^2$WR，一个有效且高效的 Wasm 二进制归约框架。E$^2$WR 为函数内指令序列归约引入了两阶段方法，包括操作数依赖引导的指令归约与组合式冗余消除，从而在避免不必要填充指令的同时实现高效的 delta 调试；并提出一种面向非函数的归约方法，将静态分析与 delta 调试引导的试探相结合，高效移除与性质无关的非函数定义。与 Wasm-Shrink 和 Wasm-Reduce 相比，E$^2$WR 产出的二进制分别小 95.4% 和 63.9%，归约速度分别提升 11.1 倍和 5.1 倍。","tl":"首次为 Wasm 二进制做依赖引导的函数内与非函数归约。","au":["Shiyao Zhou","Ningyu He","David Lo","Xiapu Luo"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["WebAssembly","test case reduction","delta debugging","runtime bugs","binary minimization"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/171/x"},{"id":"p01454","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"LogNexus: Effective Log Compression via Unified Redundancy Encoding","tz":"LogNexus：基于统一冗余编码的高效日志压缩","a":"State-of-the-art log compressors typically rely on a decoupled “parse-then-compress” workflow, where parsing is optimized for semantic accuracy (i.e., event identification) rather than storage efficiency. Through a comprehensive empirical study, we reveal that this architectural decoupling prevents the exploitation of deep correlations between static templates and dynamic variables. To address it, we propose LogNexus based on the principle of unified redundancy encoding, a new log compression paradigm that co-designs structural extraction and variable encoding. LogNexus constructs a Unified Redundancy Tree (URT) using a hierarchical strategy that progressively mines frequent “structure+variable” patterns in logs. Such a design captures deep contextual redundancies ignored by traditional methods while minimizing computational overhead by pre-emptively encoding dominant patterns. Extensive evaluation on 16 benchmark datasets demonstrates that LogNexus establishes a new state-of-the-art. It achieves the highest compression ratio on 14 datasets (outperforming baselines by 9.48% to 89.13%) and the fastest speed (1.51× to 40.06× faster than competitors). Furthermore, when configured in non-chunked mode to maximize global pattern discovery, LogNexus boosts its compression ratio by 285.13%, which is 27.08% higher than the best baseline, while retaining a 2.43× speed advantage. The decompression audit further shows that LogNexus successfully restores every token on all 16 datasets.","az":"当前最先进的日志压缩器通常依赖解耦的“先解析再压缩”工作流，其中解析是为语义准确性（即事件识别）而优化的，而非为存储效率。通过一项全面的实证研究，我们揭示这种架构上的解耦阻碍了对静态模板与动态变量之间深层关联的利用。为解决这一问题，我们基于统一冗余编码原则提出 LogNexus，一种协同设计结构提取与变量编码的新型日志压缩范式。LogNexus 采用分层策略构建统一冗余树（Unified Redundancy Tree，URT），逐步挖掘日志中频繁出现的“结构+变量”模式。这一设计捕捉了传统方法忽视的深层上下文冗余，同时通过预先编码主导模式来最小化计算开销。在 16 个基准数据集上的大量评估表明，LogNexus 确立了新的最先进水平。它在 14 个数据集上取得了最高压缩率（比基线高出 9.48% 至 89.13%），并且速度最快（比竞争者快 1.51 倍至 40.06 倍）。此外，当配置为非分块模式以最大化全局模式发现时，LogNexus 将其压缩率提升了 285.13%，比最佳基线高 27.08%，同时仍保持 2.43 倍的速度优势。解压审计进一步表明，LogNexus 在全部 16 个数据集上都成功还原了每一个 token。","tl":"用统一冗余树把日志解析与变量编码协同设计以提升压缩率。","au":["Yang Liu","Kaiming Zhang","Zhuangbin Chen","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"operations-observability-and-performance","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["log compression","unified redundancy tree","log parsing","compression ratio","observability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/172/x"},{"id":"p01455","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Paired Code Smells and Test Smells: A Fine-Grained Longitudinal Empirical Study","tz":"成对的代码坏味与测试坏味：一项细粒度的纵向实证研究","a":"As software systems grow in complexity, ensuring maintainability is essential, but often hindered by various quality issues. Among them, code smells and test smells are widely recognized indicators of technical debt that degrade system quality. While production code and test suites are intrinsically coupled and evolve together, existing research predominantly studies code smells and test smells in isolation, ignoring their underlying connection over time. To bridge this gap, this paper presents a fine-grained longitudinal study on the co-evolutionary dynamics of “paired smells”, which refer to cases where code and test smells exist concurrently in linked production and test code. By analyzing 128,417 commits across 19 long-lived open-source Java repositories, we investigate the statistical associations, survival lifespans, and removal motivations of these paired flaws. As a result, we identify 30 statistically significant rules where specific test smells imply the presence of underlying production code smells and our survival analysis reveals that in most of repositories, paired smells have relatively shorter lifespans than unpaired ones. To explain this phenomenon, our manual inspection reveals that paired smells often signal deeper structural issues, prompting explicit risk-driven refactoring. Finally, we discuss the implications of these results for code quality analysis and continuous integration tools, suggesting that they should link related smell findings between production and test code and guide synchronized refactoring.","az":"随着软件系统日益复杂，确保可维护性至关重要，但常常受到各种质量问题的阻碍。其中，代码坏味与测试坏味是公认的技术债指标，会降低系统质量。尽管生产代码与测试套件本质上相互耦合、共同演化，现有研究大多孤立地研究代码坏味与测试坏味，忽视了它们随时间推移的内在关联。为弥补这一空白，本文对“成对坏味”的共演化动态开展了一项细粒度的纵向研究，成对坏味指代码坏味与测试坏味同时存在于相互关联的生产代码与测试代码中的情形。通过分析 19 个长期维护的开源 Java 仓库中的 128,417 次提交，我们考察这些成对缺陷的统计关联、存活时长与移除动机。结果表明，我们识别出 30 条统计显著的规则，其中特定的测试坏味意味着底层生产代码坏味的存在；我们的生存分析显示，在大多数仓库中，成对坏味的存活时长相对短于非成对坏味。为解释这一现象，我们的人工检查发现，成对坏味往往预示更深层的结构性问题，从而促使开发者进行明确的风险驱动重构。最后，我们讨论了这些结果对代码质量分析与持续集成工具的启示，建议它们应将生产代码与测试代码中相关的坏味发现关联起来，并引导同步重构。","tl":"首次量化代码坏味与测试坏味成对出现的关联与更短存活期。","au":["Ziwen Cai"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["code smells","test smells","co-evolution","survival analysis","technical debt"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/173/x"},{"id":"p01456","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fixed-Point Guided ADS Scenario Generation via Multi-Modal LLM Reasoning and Software Testing","tz":"由不动点引导的自动驾驶场景生成：结合多模态 LLM 推理与软件测试","a":"Robust scenario generation is essential for systematically testing Autonomous Driving Systems (ADS) under rare and safety-critical conditions. However, existing methods face a dilemma: search-based approaches often lack semantic guidance, while specification-based methods rely on unscalable manual rules. Current LLM-driven techniques, meanwhile, primarily act as surface-level scene translators without explicit behavioral grounding. We present InvarGen, a framework that bridges these gaps by utilizing multi-modal LLMs as parametric specification generators. Central to InvarGen is the concept of Scenario Fixed Points—dynamic safety invariants (e.g., context-aware headway thresholds) automatically extracted and formalized from unstructured accident videos. Unlike static templates, these fixed points adaptively constrain the search space, guiding a hybrid evolutionary process: Intelligent Fuzzing exploits boundary parameters to trigger specific violations, while Structural Mutation ensures the global exploration of diverse environmental contexts. Evaluation across 1,400 synthesized scenarios based on 200 real-world accidents demonstrates that InvarGen outperforms LLM-driven and traditional search-based baselines in multiple dimensions. It discovers up to 37.5% more unique violation types than the best baseline, achieves a 30% fixed-point violation rate, and improves semantic diversity by 25%. It also maintains 100% compatibility with OpenX standards, ensuring cross-platform simulation on Carla and Panosim. Ablation studies confirm that all components are statistically essential. These results highlight the promise of fixed-point semantics as a principled bridge between unstructured LLM reasoning and rigorous robustness testing.","az":"稳健的场景生成对于在罕见且安全关键的条件下系统性测试自动驾驶系统（ADS）至关重要。然而，现有方法面临两难：基于搜索的方法往往缺乏语义引导，而基于规约的方法依赖难以扩展的人工规则。与此同时，当前由大语言模型驱动的技术主要充当表层的场景翻译器，缺乏明确的行为基础。我们提出 InvarGen 框架，通过将多模态大语言模型用作参数化规约生成器来弥合这些差距。InvarGen 的核心是“场景不动点”（Scenario Fixed Points）概念——即从非结构化事故视频中自动提取并形式化的动态安全不变量（例如上下文感知的车头时距阈值）。与静态模板不同，这些不动点自适应地约束搜索空间，引导一个混合演化过程：智能模糊测试（Intelligent Fuzzing）利用边界参数来触发特定违规，而结构变异（Structural Mutation）确保对多样环境上下文的全局探索。基于 200 起真实事故合成的 1,400 个场景上的评估表明，InvarGen 在多个维度上优于基于 LLM 的和传统基于搜索的基线。它比最佳基线多发现最多 37.5% 的独特违规类型，达到 30% 的不动点违规率，并将语义多样性提升 25%。它还保持与 OpenX 标准 100% 的兼容性，确保在 Carla 与 Panosim 上的跨平台仿真。消融实验确认所有组件在统计上都是必要的。这些结果凸显了不动点语义作为连接非结构化 LLM 推理与严格鲁棒性测试的原则性桥梁的前景。","tl":"从事故视频提取动态安全不变量作为场景搜索的约束不动点。","au":["xudong zhang","Shihao Zhu","Yan Cai"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","multimodal","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["autonomous driving systems","scenario generation","safety invariants","multi-modal LLM","evolutionary fuzzing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/174/x"},{"id":"p01457","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"ARQ: A Mixed-Precision Quantization Framework for Accurate and Certifiably Robust DNNs","tz":"ARQ：面向高精度与可认证鲁棒 DNN 的混合精度量化框架","a":"Mixed precision quantization has become an important technique for optimizing the execution of deep neural networks (DNNs). Certified robustness, which provides provable guarantees about a model’s ability to withstand different adversarial perturbations, has rarely been addressed in quantization due to the unacceptably high cost of certifying robustness. This paper introduces ARQ, an innovative mixed-precision quantization method that not only preserves the clean accuracy of the smoothed classifiers, but also maintains their certified robustness. ARQ uses reinforcement learning to find accurate and robust DNN quantization, while efficiently leveraging randomized smoothing, a popular class of statistical DNN verification algorithms. ARQ consistently performs better than multiple state-of-the-art quantization techniques across all the benchmarks and the input perturbation levels. The performance of ARQ quantized networks reaches that of the original DNN with floating-point weights, while with only$~1.5%$ instructions and the highest certified radius. ARQ code is available at https://anonymous.4open.science/r/ARQ-35CB .","az":"混合精度量化已成为优化深度神经网络（DNN）执行的重要技术。可认证鲁棒性为模型抵御各种对抗扰动的能力提供可证明的保证，但由于认证鲁棒性的代价高得难以接受，在量化中很少被涉及。本文提出 ARQ，一种创新的混合精度量化方法，它不仅保持了平滑分类器的干净准确率，还维持了它们的可认证鲁棒性。ARQ 使用强化学习来寻找准确且鲁棒的 DNN 量化方案，同时高效利用随机平滑（randomized smoothing）这一流行的统计式 DNN 验证算法。在所有基准和输入扰动水平上，ARQ 始终优于多种最先进的量化技术。ARQ 量化后的网络性能达到了具有浮点权重的原始 DNN 的水平，同时仅需约 1.5% 的指令，并具有最高的认证半径。ARQ 代码可在 https://anonymous.4open.science/r/ARQ-35CB 获取。","tl":"用强化学习搜索既保精度又保认证鲁棒性的混合精度量化。","au":["Yuchen Yang","Yifan Zhao","Shubham Ugare","Gagandeep Singh","Sasa Misailovic"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"efficient-inference-quantization-and-ml-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["mixed-precision quantization","certified robustness","randomized smoothing","reinforcement learning","DNN verification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/175/x"},{"id":"p01458","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Red-Teaming Coding Agents from a Tool-Invocation Perspective: An Empirical Security Assessment","tz":"从工具调用视角红队测试编程智能体：一项实证安全评估","a":"Coding agents powered by large language models are becoming central modules of modern IDEs. They help users to perform various complex coding tasks by invoking tools. Although powerful, tool-invocation operation in coding agents opens a substantial attack surface for adversaries.Prior work has demonstrated attacks against both general-purpose LLM agents and domain-specific agents. However, to our knowledge, no previous works focus on the security risks of tool-invocation in coding agents. To fill this gap, we conduct the first systematic, in-depth red-teaming from a tool-invocation perspective in six popular real-world coding agents: Cursor, Claude Code, Copilot, Windsurf, Cline, and Trae. Our red-teaming proceeds in two phases. In Phase 1, we conduct a prompt leakage as reconnaissance to recover system prompts and related context. Specifically, we identify a mode gap between chat generation and tool-call argument generation: during schema-driven argument completion, the model behaves as if it is performing benign structured filling and may copy hidden agent context into tool-call arguments. We instantiate this gap as ToolLeak, which exfiltrates agent-internal prompts (e.g., system prompts and tool metadata) via required tool parameters. In Phase 2, we hijack the tool-invocation behavior of the coding agent with a novel two-channel prompt injection in the tool description and the tool return. Our hijacking achieves remote code execution (RCE) on major real-world coding agents. We adaptively construct the malicious payload using leaked security information in Phase 1. Our evaluation shows that ToolLeak substantially outperforms strong prompt-leak baselines in both emulated and real-world settings. In the emulated setting, ToolLeak achieves the best overall prompt-exfiltration performance across all six simulated coding agents. On real-world coding agents, ToolLeak achieves the best pseudo-recall on 18 of 25 evaluated agent-LLM pairs. Furthermore, our red-teaming successfully hijacks all six real-world coding agents for RCE and consistently yields higher attack success rates than baseline attacks. Lastly, we present two case studies on Cursor and Claude Code to demonstrate the real-world impact of our red-teaming.","az":"由大语言模型驱动的编程智能体正成为现代 IDE 的核心模块。它们通过调用工具帮助用户完成各种复杂的编程任务。虽然功能强大，编程智能体中的工具调用操作却为攻击者打开了相当大的攻击面。已有工作展示了针对通用 LLM 智能体和领域专用智能体的攻击。然而据我们所知，此前没有工作聚焦于编程智能体中工具调用的安全风险。为填补这一空白，我们在六个流行的真实编程智能体（Cursor、Claude Code、Copilot、Windsurf、Cline 和 Trae）上开展了首个系统、深入的工具调用视角红队测试。我们的红队测试分两个阶段进行。第一阶段，我们进行提示泄露作为侦察，以恢复系统提示及相关上下文。具体而言，我们识别出聊天生成与工具调用参数生成之间的模式差异：在由 schema 驱动的参数补全过程中，模型表现得像是在进行良性的结构化填充，可能会把隐藏的智能体上下文复制进工具调用参数。我们将这一差异实例化为 ToolLeak，它通过必填的工具参数窃取智能体内部提示（例如系统提示与工具元数据）。第二阶段，我们用一种新颖的双通道提示注入（在工具描述与工具返回值中）劫持编程智能体的工具调用行为。我们的劫持在主流真实编程智能体上实现了远程代码执行（RCE）。我们利用第一阶段泄露的安全信息自适应地构造恶意载荷。评估显示，在模拟与真实环境中，ToolLeak 都显著优于强提示泄露基线。在模拟环境中，ToolLeak 在全部六个被模拟的编程智能体上取得了最佳的整体提示窃取表现。在真实编程智能体上，ToolLeak 在 25 个被评估的智能体—LLM 组合中的 18 个上取得了最佳的伪召回率。此外，我们的红队测试成功劫持了全部六个真实编程智能体实现 RCE，并且攻击成功率持续高于基线攻击。最后，我们给出针对 Cursor 和 Claude Code 的两个案例研究，展示红队测试的真实世界影响。","tl":"利用工具参数填充模式差异窃取系统提示并双通道注入实现 RCE。","au":["Yuchong Xie","Mingyu Luo","Zesen Liu","Zhixiang Zhang","Kaikai Zhang","Yu Liu","Ci Tao","Changhui Wang","Zongjie Li","Ping Chen","Shuai Wang","Dongdong She"],"top":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","alt":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","tg":["security","agentic","empirical-study"],"kw":["coding agents","tool invocation","prompt leakage","prompt injection","remote code execution"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/176/x"},{"id":"p01459","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"How Safe is Your Screen? Understanding and Detecting Privacy Leaks in Sensitive Activities","tz":"你的屏幕安全吗？理解并检测敏感 Activity 中的隐私泄露","a":"Android apps handle sensitive data, often displayed on screens (i.e., Activities), and protecting these activities is vital for ensuring user privacy. Several studies have demonstrated the risk of private data leakage via screen capture and identified malware exploiting this vulnerability. To mitigate such threats, Google introduced FLAG_SECURE, an activity-level security feature that protects an Activity when set by blocking screen capture and restricting display on non-secure devices. Proper usage of this security feature could significantly reduce data leakage risks. However, to the best of our knowledge, its adoption across diverse Android apps has not been systematically studied. In this work, we present a large-scale empirical study of screenshot-based vulnerabilities in Android apps using a systematic static analysis pipeline, ASSA. The pipeline automatically constructs UI models of activities and fragments by leveraging a customized version of Frontmatter, and combines them with a Large Language Model (LLM) to infer runtime context and identify sensitive user data rendered on screens. We apply ASSA to 5,667 popular real-world Android apps and find that 19.8% contain at least one activity that displays sensitive information without screen-capture protection, while 87.2% of apps do not apply FLAG_SECURE to any activity, exposing credentials, financial information, and location data to screenshot attacks. Beyond quantifying prevalence, we analyze FLAG_SECURE usage patterns and establish a taxonomy that captures diverse factors influencing developers’ decisions to adopt or omit screen protection, including intentional privacy protection, intellectual property safeguarding, and unintentional inheritance from base activities. To assess real-world impact, we further conduct in-depth case studies on 200 vulnerable apps and responsibly disclose our findings to the affected vendors, receiving 6 confirmed patches and 18 acknowledgments, including 10 vendors who reported ongoing efforts toward mitigation. These findings indicate that screenshot-based vulnerabilities are not only widespread but also systematically overlooked in practice, highlighting the need for greater awareness and more careful handling of sensitive on-screen information by developers.","az":"Android 应用处理敏感数据，这些数据常常显示在屏幕（即 Activity）上，保护这些 Activity 对于确保用户隐私至关重要。多项研究已证明通过屏幕捕获导致私密数据泄露的风险，并发现了利用该漏洞的恶意软件。为缓解此类威胁，Google 引入了 FLAG_SECURE，这是一项 Activity 级别的安全特性，设置后会阻止屏幕捕获并限制在非安全设备上显示，从而保护该 Activity。正确使用这一安全特性可显著降低数据泄露风险。然而据我们所知，其在各类 Android 应用中的采用情况尚未被系统研究。在本工作中，我们使用系统化的静态分析流水线 ASSA，对 Android 应用中基于截屏的漏洞开展了一项大规模实证研究。该流水线利用定制版 Frontmatter 自动构建 Activity 与 Fragment 的 UI 模型，并将其与大语言模型结合，以推断运行时上下文并识别屏幕上渲染的敏感用户数据。我们将 ASSA 应用于 5,667 个流行的真实 Android 应用，发现 19.8% 的应用至少包含一个显示敏感信息却没有屏幕捕获保护的 Activity，而 87.2% 的应用没有对任何 Activity 使用 FLAG_SECURE，使凭证、金融信息和位置数据暴露于截屏攻击。除量化普遍性之外，我们还分析了 FLAG_SECURE 的使用模式，并建立了一个分类法，刻画影响开发者采用或忽略屏幕保护的多种因素，包括有意的隐私保护、知识产权保护，以及从基类 Activity 无意继承。为评估真实世界影响，我们进一步对 200 个存在漏洞的应用开展深入案例研究，并负责任地向受影响厂商披露我们的发现，获得 6 个已确认的补丁和 18 次致谢，其中 10 家厂商报告正在推进缓解工作。这些发现表明，基于截屏的漏洞不仅广泛存在，而且在实践中被系统性忽视，凸显了开发者需要提高意识并更谨慎地处理屏幕上的敏感信息。","tl":"首次大规模测量 Android 中 FLAG_SECURE 缺失导致的截屏泄露。","au":["Youngseok Kim","Sungho Lee","Sungjae Hwang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["empirical-study","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["Android privacy","FLAG_SECURE","screen capture leakage","static analysis","UI model"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/177/x"},{"id":"p01460","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Cracking Query Bottlenecks: Towards Efficiency-Oriented Text-to-SQL Generation","tz":"破解查询瓶颈：面向效率的 Text-to-SQL 生成","a":"Text-to-SQL models translate natural language questions into SQL, enabling non-technical users to access databases. However, most existing research focuses on correctness, neglecting query efficiency. In this paper, we address the challenge of evaluating the execution efficiency of generated SQL in Text-to-SQL by introducing EESQLBench, a novel benchmark designed to assess both correctness and efficiency. EESQLBench pairs each natural language question with an expert-optimized SQL query, providing a reliable efficiency baseline. We evaluate six representative large language models (LLMs), including four open-source models (SQLCoder, CodeLlama, DeepSeek-Coder, and DeepSeek-R1) and two closed-source models (GPT-5.2 and Gemini-2.5-Pro), using cost-based metrics including Cost Reachability (CR) and Acceptable Reachability at $k$ (AR@$k$). Our results reveal that current LLMs, despite achieving high correctness, struggle to produce efficient queries. We observe substantial efficiency gaps between models and emphasize that semantic correctness alone does not guarantee query efficiency. Furthermore, we provide insights into common inefficiency patterns in LLM-generated SQL queries, such as missing access pruning and inefficient subquery logic.","az":"Text-to-SQL 模型将自然语言问题翻译为 SQL，使非技术用户也能访问数据库。然而，现有研究大多关注正确性，忽视了查询效率。本文通过引入 EESQLBench 来应对评估 Text-to-SQL 中所生成 SQL 执行效率的挑战，这是一个旨在同时评估正确性与效率的新基准。EESQLBench 为每个自然语言问题配备一条专家优化的 SQL 查询，提供可靠的效率基线。我们使用基于代价的指标（包括代价可达性 CR 与 k 处可接受可达性 AR@k）评估了六个具有代表性的大语言模型，包括四个开源模型（SQLCoder、CodeLlama、DeepSeek-Coder 和 DeepSeek-R1）以及两个闭源模型（GPT-5.2 和 Gemini-2.5-Pro）。结果显示，当前的大语言模型尽管取得了很高的正确率，却难以生成高效的查询。我们观察到模型之间存在显著的效率差距，并强调仅有语义正确性并不能保证查询效率。此外，我们还给出了 LLM 生成的 SQL 中常见低效模式的洞见，例如缺失访问剪枝和低效的子查询逻辑。","tl":"提出同时衡量 SQL 正确性与执行代价效率的新基准。","au":["Li Lin","Yunfeng Shen","Lingfeng Bao","Rongxin Wu","Yang Liu"],"top":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["text-to-SQL","query efficiency","benchmark","cost-based metrics","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/178/x"},{"id":"p01461","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Lingxi: Repository-Level Issue Resolution Framework Enhanced by Procedural Knowledge Guided Scaling","tz":"Lingxi：由过程性知识引导扩展增强的仓库级 Issue 求解框架","a":"Driven by the advancements of Large Language Models (LLMs), LLM-powered agents are making significant improvements in software engineering tasks, yet struggle with complex, repository-level issue resolution. Existing agent-based methods have two key limitations. First, they lack of procedural knowledge (i.e., how an issue is fixed step-by-step and rationales behind it) to learn and leverage for issue resolution. Second, they rely on massive computational power to blindly explore the solution space. To address those limitations, we propose Lingxi, an issue resolution framework that leverages procedural knowledge extracted from historical issue-fixing data to guide agents in solving repository-level issues. Lingxi first constructs this knowledge offline through a hierarchical abstraction mechanism, enabling agents to learn the how and why behind a fix, not just the final solution. During online application, it employs a knowledge-driven scaling method that leverages the procedural knowledge of similar issues to intelligently analyze the target issue from multiple perspectives, in sharp contrast to undirected, brute-force exploration. Lingxi successfully resolves 74.6% of bugs on the SWE-bench Verified benchmark in Past@1 setting, outperforming five state-of-the-art techniques by a significant margin (5.4% to 14.9%). Our comprehensive ablation study confirmed that the success of Lingxi comes directly from its use of procedural knowledge. Without it, the performance gains from scaling alone is negligible. Our qualitative study further shows that the ‘‘design patterns & coding practices’’ is the most critical knowledge aspect, and that the roles of different knowledge aspects switch across different stages (i.e., analysis, planning, and fixing).","az":"在大语言模型（LLM）进展的推动下，LLM 驱动的智能体在软件工程任务上取得了显著提升，但在复杂的仓库级 issue 求解上仍显吃力。现有基于智能体的方法有两个关键局限。第一，它们缺乏可供学习和利用的过程性知识（即一个 issue 是如何被一步步修复的以及其背后的原理）。第二，它们依赖巨量算力盲目地探索解空间。为解决这些局限，我们提出 Lingxi，一个利用从历史 issue 修复数据中提取的过程性知识来引导智能体求解仓库级 issue 的框架。Lingxi 首先通过分层抽象机制离线构建这类知识，使智能体能够学习修复背后的“如何做”和“为什么”，而不仅仅是最终解。在线应用时，它采用一种知识驱动的扩展方法，利用相似 issue 的过程性知识从多个视角智能地分析目标 issue，与无引导的暴力探索形成鲜明对比。Lingxi 在 SWE-bench Verified 基准的 Pass@1 设定下成功解决了 74.6% 的缺陷，以显著幅度（5.4% 至 14.9%）超越五种最先进技术。我们全面的消融实验证实，Lingxi 的成功直接来自其对过程性知识的使用；若没有它，仅靠扩展带来的性能提升微乎其微。我们的定性研究进一步表明，“设计模式与编码实践”是最关键的知识方面，且不同知识方面的作用会在不同阶段（即分析、规划与修复）之间切换。","tl":"把历史修复的过程性知识分层抽象后驱动智能体的推理扩展。","au":["Xu Yang","Jiayuan Zhou","Michael Pacheco","Wenhan Zhu","Pengfei He","Shaowei Wang","Kui Liu","Ruiqi Pan"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["issue resolution","procedural knowledge","SWE-bench Verified","LLM agent","knowledge-driven scaling"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/179/x"},{"id":"p01462","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Characterizing Real-World Bugs in Tile Programs for Automated Bug Detection","tz":"刻画 Tile 程序中的真实世界缺陷以支持自动化缺陷检测","a":"Tile-based programming frameworks are increasingly adopted to write high-performance GPU kernels in domains such as deep learning and scientific computing. While these frameworks enhance productivity and hardware utilization, their multi-stage compilation pipelines introduce distinct code generation bugs that are tightly coupled to input shapes, data types, and backend targets. These bugs often manifest as silent correctness or performance issues, making them difficult to detect using existing compiler testing tools. Additionally, the unique programming conventions of tile domain specific languages complicate root cause identification, while fixing such bugs demands specialized knowledge of tile abstractions and compilation pipelines. Despite the growing adoption of tile-based systems, their code generation bugs remain largely unexplored. This paper presents the first systematic study of tile-program code generation bugs. We analyze 301 real-world bug reports from GitHub and categorize their root causes, symptoms, input patterns, test oracles that trigger these bugs and the strategies used to fix them. Our study provides foundational insights for building debugging, testing, and repair tools tailored to tile-based compiler infrastructures.","az":"基于 tile 的编程框架在深度学习和科学计算等领域被越来越多地用于编写高性能 GPU 内核。虽然这些框架提升了生产力与硬件利用率，但其多阶段编译流水线引入了与输入形状、数据类型和后端目标紧密耦合的独特代码生成缺陷。这些缺陷往往表现为静默的正确性或性能问题，使用现有编译器测试工具难以检测。此外，tile 领域专用语言独特的编程约定使根因识别变得复杂，而修复此类缺陷需要关于 tile 抽象与编译流水线的专门知识。尽管基于 tile 的系统采用日益广泛，其代码生成缺陷在很大程度上仍未被探索。本文提出了首个关于 tile 程序代码生成缺陷的系统性研究。我们分析了来自 GitHub 的 301 份真实缺陷报告，并对其根本原因、症状、输入模式、触发这些缺陷的测试预言以及所用的修复策略进行了归类。我们的研究为构建针对基于 tile 的编译器基础设施的调试、测试与修复工具提供了基础性洞见。","tl":"首次系统归类 tile 编程框架的代码生成缺陷根因与修复策略。","au":["Ravishka Rathnasuriya","Zihe Song","Nidhi Majoju","Tingxi Li","Aaryaa Moharir","Wei Yang","Tao Xie"],"top":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["empirical-study","non-llm-classical"],"kw":["tile programming","GPU kernel","code generation bugs","compiler pipeline","empirical bug study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/180/x"},{"id":"p01463","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Automated Program Repair for UI-centric Android Bugs: How Far are We?","tz":"面向 UI 中心 Android 缺陷的自动程序修复：我们走到哪一步了？","a":"Substantial research effort has been devoted to developing techniques for automated program repair (APR) that suggest patches for localized buggy code – and more recent techniques have begun to leverage the capabilities of code-centric large language models (LLMs). However, the scope and diversity of bugs to which these techniques have historically been applied is limited. In particular, the research community currently lacks a comprehensive understanding of the performance of APR techniques on bugs that arise in UI-centric programs, such as mobile apps. Bugs in UI centric programs carry with them unique challenges, including (i) the need to reason across interconnected subroutines that connect presentation and program logic, (ii) event driven programming paradigms, and (iii) the need to reason about program state through cues in the UI. In this paper, we investigate the effectiveness of existing APR techniques when applied to fix bugs in UI-centric programs – specifically Android applications. To explore this phenomenon, we conduct a comprehensive empirical study with five existing program repair techniques (including those that utilize LLMs) on a hybrid dataset including 46 synthetic bugs, generated via an Android-specific mutation tool, and 25 real bugs systematically mined from issue reports of 13 popular Android applications. Our findings illustrate important current limitations in resolving UI-related issues in mobile apps. We synthesize these results to form a taxonomy of the limitations of existing program repair techniques. This taxonomy details important limitations and can inform future research efforts in designing automated program repair tools for UI-centric bugs in mobile apps.","az":"大量研究致力于开发为已定位的缺陷代码建议补丁的自动程序修复（APR）技术，近期的技术已开始利用以代码为中心的大语言模型（LLM）的能力。然而，这些技术历来所应用的缺陷的范围与多样性是有限的。特别地，研究社区目前缺乏对 APR 技术在 UI 中心程序（如移动应用）中出现的缺陷上表现的全面理解。UI 中心程序中的缺陷带来独特挑战，包括：(i) 需要跨越连接表示层与程序逻辑的相互关联的子例程进行推理；(ii) 事件驱动的编程范式；(iii) 需要通过 UI 中的线索来推断程序状态。本文研究现有 APR 技术在修复 UI 中心程序（具体而言是 Android 应用）缺陷时的有效性。为探究这一现象，我们对五种现有程序修复技术（包括使用 LLM 的技术）在一个混合数据集上开展了全面的实证研究，该数据集包含由 Android 专用变异工具生成的 46 个合成缺陷，以及从 13 个流行 Android 应用的 issue 报告中系统挖掘的 25 个真实缺陷。我们的发现说明了在解决移动应用中 UI 相关问题上的重要现存局限。我们综合这些结果，形成了现有程序修复技术局限性的分类法。该分类法详述了重要的局限，可为未来设计面向移动应用 UI 中心缺陷的自动程序修复工具的研究提供指导。","tl":"首次系统评估 APR 在 UI 中心 Android 缺陷上的失效并给出局限分类法。","au":["Junayed Mahmud","Sparsh Pandey","Nadeeshan De Silva","Atish Kumar Dipongkor","Jingjing Wu","Oscar Chaparro","Mattia Fazzini","Kevin Moran"],"top":"automated-program-repair","alt":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["automated program repair","Android UI bugs","empirical evaluation","LLM-based repair","limitation taxonomy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/181/x"},{"id":"p01464","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"EventSpec: Defining and Detecting Event-Semantic Issues in Blockchain Ecosystems","tz":"EventSpec：定义并检测区块链生态中的事件语义问题","a":"In recent years, smart contracts have become the backbone of decentralized applications (DApps), and off-chain systems such as bridges, wallets, and indexers rely heavily on event logs to track contract execution and state changes. However, the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) does not validate or enforce event semantics, so logs can diverge from on-chain state, misleading off-chain systems into accepting incorrect state transitions. Existing smart contract vulnerability detection tools focus on logic bugs, with limited support for detecting event-semantic defects. To address this gap, we collect audit reports and incident cases and apply open card sorting to define five classes of event-semantic defects: event collision, state-event mismatch, unauthorized event emission, event emission mismatch, and event parameter mismatch. We propose EventSpec, which infers event specifications from a contract corpus via behavior inference and semantic-constraint extraction and applies differential checking to identify event-semantic defects in target contracts. We run EventSpec on 6,552 real-world contracts and evaluate detection effectiveness based on manually labeled results; EventSpec achieves an overall comprehensive precision of 90.17%. We further provide an off-chain evaluation harness that reproduces two off-chain attack vectors on any EVM-compatible chain: event origin confusion caused by unintended emitters and event–state desynchronization where events lack matching state updates. Using this harness, we demonstrate the feasibility of these attacks on bridge relayers, blockchain explorers, and NFT marketplaces, and report six wallet issues, four of which were confirmed (including a $600 bounty), with two remaining pending.","az":"近年来，智能合约已成为去中心化应用（DApp）的支柱，而跨链桥、钱包和索引器等链下系统高度依赖事件日志来跟踪合约执行与状态变化。然而，以太坊虚拟机（EVM）并不校验或强制事件语义，因此日志可能与链上状态发生偏离，误导链下系统接受错误的状态转移。现有智能合约漏洞检测工具聚焦逻辑缺陷，对事件语义缺陷的支持有限。为填补这一空白，我们收集审计报告与事故案例，并运用开放式卡片分类法定义了五类事件语义缺陷：事件冲突、状态—事件不匹配、未授权事件发射、事件发射不匹配以及事件参数不匹配。我们提出 EventSpec，它通过行为推断与语义约束提取从合约语料中推断事件规约，并应用差分检查来识别目标合约中的事件语义缺陷。我们在 6,552 个真实合约上运行 EventSpec，并基于人工标注结果评估检测效果；EventSpec 取得了 90.17% 的整体综合精确率。我们进一步提供了一个链下评估测试床，可在任意 EVM 兼容链上复现两种链下攻击向量：由非预期发射者导致的事件来源混淆，以及事件缺少对应状态更新导致的事件—状态失同步。利用这一测试床，我们在跨链桥中继器、区块链浏览器和 NFT 市场上论证了这些攻击的可行性，并报告了六个钱包问题，其中四个已被确认（包括一笔 600 美元赏金），另两个仍在处理中。","tl":"首次定义五类事件语义缺陷并用规约差分检测真实合约。","au":["Yixuan Liu","Yuxin Dong","Ye Liu","Yin Wu","Chengxuan Zhang","Xiapu Luo","Yi Li"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","tg":["tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["smart contract","event semantics","specification inference","differential checking","off-chain systems"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/182/x","pu":"https://liyiweb.com/files/Liu2026EDD.pdf"},{"id":"p01465","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"avaCGs: Version-Aware Call Graphs for Efficient Version-Range Queries","tz":"avaCGs：面向高效版本范围查询的版本感知调用图","a":"Developers employ version ranges to specify a range of valid versions for software libraries their projects depend on. While this can yield benefits like automatic adoption of library updates, it complicates method reachability analysis: a sound whole-program analysis must consider method invocations of every library release within that range. Such releases might themselves introduce transitive ranged dependencies to a project, leading to a combinatorial blow-up in the number of configurations to analyze. If developers wanted to soundly determine whether a critical method might be reachable via a ranged library dependency, they would have to build the individual call graphs for every release within that range, and perform reachability analysis on each one of them. As call-graph construction is an expensive operation, this approach is rarely practical. To enable direct version-range queries, we introduce artifact version-aware call graphs (avaCGs) that comprise call graph information about all versions of a software artifact in a single graph structure. Further, we propose a novel approach that incrementally computes call graphs based on Rapid Type Analysis (RTA) , implement it for the JVM platform, and show that it yields identical results to full RTA call-graph builds. Our evaluation shows that on our benchmarks, avaCGs can improve the performance of reachability queries by up to 9.58x, while our incremental construction is up to 79% faster compared to full builds for each release. We also observe that for real-world libraries hosted on Maven Central, almost 80% of all releases do not change the RTA call graph compared to their previous release, further justifying the use of incremental approaches.","az":"开发者使用版本范围来指定其项目所依赖软件库的有效版本区间。虽然这能带来诸如自动采用库更新之类的好处，却使方法可达性分析变得复杂：健全的全程序分析必须考虑该范围内每一个库发布版本的方法调用。这些发布版本本身又可能为项目引入传递性的范围依赖，导致需要分析的配置数量组合爆炸。如果开发者想要健全地判定某个关键方法是否可能经由带版本范围的库依赖而可达，他们就必须为该范围内的每个发布版本构建单独的调用图，并在每一个上执行可达性分析。由于调用图构建是一项昂贵的操作，这种做法很少切实可行。为支持直接的版本范围查询，我们引入了制品版本感知调用图（avaCGs），它在单一图结构中包含某软件制品所有版本的调用图信息。此外，我们提出一种基于快速类型分析（Rapid Type Analysis，RTA）增量计算调用图的新方法，在 JVM 平台上实现，并证明它产生与完整 RTA 调用图构建相同的结果。我们的评估显示，在我们的基准上，avaCGs 可将可达性查询性能提升最高 9.58 倍，而我们的增量构建相比为每个发布版本做完整构建最快可提升 79%。我们还观察到，对于托管在 Maven Central 上的真实库，几乎 80% 的发布版本相较其前一版本并未改变 RTA 调用图，这进一步佐证了使用增量方法的合理性。","tl":"把一个制品所有版本的调用图合并为单一可增量构建的图结构。","au":["Johannes Düsing","Dominik Helm","Ben Hermann"],"top":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["call graph","version ranges","reachability analysis","Rapid Type Analysis","incremental analysis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/183/x","pu":"https://www.iste.uni-stuttgart.de/documents/documents-ese/issta2026-avacg-dhh.pdf"},{"id":"p01466","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"What Makes In-Context Examples Effective for Code Generation?","tz":"是什么让上下文示例对代码生成有效？","a":"In-Context Learning (ICL) has emerged as a promising solution to enhance the code generation capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs) by incorporating code examples inside the prompt to let LLMs learn from demonstrations. However, despite their effectiveness gains, it remains unclear which specific properties of ICL-provided code examples (e.g., solution insight, essential contextual information, identifier naming styles, code formatting) drive these gains. This paper systematically investigates the impact of different sources and internal features of code examples on ICL for code generation through controlled experiments on contest-style programming questions and repository-level tasks. Our results show that while LLMs struggle to extract generalizable problem-solving insights from provided solutions to similar questions or repository snippets, their retrieval-augmented ICL performance can significantly benefit from explicit contextual information, such as input/output demonstrations, required helper functions, and namespace information. Through targeted mutation operators, we further find that identifier naming is substantially more critical than code formatting or low-level implementation details, with the elimination of descriptive variable names causing performance drops of up to 30 percentage points. Finally, we demonstrate that LLMs significantly prefer semantically meaningful identifier names and that adherence to surface-level naming conventions is far less important than semantic clarity. These findings provide practical guidelines for constructing effective ICL code examples and highlight challenges in reflection-based learning for code generation.","az":"上下文学习（ICL）通过在提示中加入代码示例让大语言模型（LLM）从演示中学习，已成为增强其代码生成能力的一种有前景的方案。然而，尽管有效性有所提升，ICL 所提供代码示例的哪些具体属性（例如解题思路、必要的上下文信息、标识符命名风格、代码格式）驱动了这些收益，仍不清楚。本文通过在竞赛式编程题目和仓库级任务上的受控实验，系统性地考察代码示例的不同来源与内部特征对代码生成 ICL 的影响。结果表明，虽然 LLM 难以从相似题目的解答或仓库片段中提取可泛化的解题洞见，但其检索增强的 ICL 性能可以显著受益于显式的上下文信息，例如输入/输出演示、所需的辅助函数以及命名空间信息。通过有针对性的变异算子，我们进一步发现标识符命名远比代码格式或底层实现细节更为关键，去除描述性变量名会造成最多 30 个百分点的性能下降。最后，我们证明 LLM 显著偏好语义上有意义的标识符名称，而遵循表层命名规范的重要性远低于语义清晰度。这些发现为构建有效的 ICL 代码示例提供了实用指南，并凸显了代码生成中基于反思的学习所面临的挑战。","tl":"受控实验表明标识符语义清晰度比格式与解题示例更决定 ICL 收益。","au":["Dongze Li","Songqiang Chen","Jialun Cao","Shing-Chi Cheung"],"top":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["in-context learning","code generation","identifier naming","controlled experiment","retrieval-augmented prompting"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/184/x"},{"id":"p01467","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Code-MUE: Measuring Code LLM' Uncertainty through Execution-based Semantic Interaction Graphs","tz":"Code-MUE：通过基于执行的语义交互图度量代码大模型的不确定性","a":"As Code Large Language Models (LLMs) become central to modern software engineering, their inherent stochasticity poses significant real-world risks, where even minor errors can lead to severe functional, security, or safety consequences. Reliable automation, therefore, demands the ability to distinguish between confident, well-supported predictions and stochastic guessing. However, existing uncertainty estimation methods face a critical gap: white and grey-box techniques are often inapplicable to closed-source models, while standard “black-box” text metrics fail to capture the unique fragility of code, where syntactic variation does not always imply semantic divergence. To bridge this syntax-semantics gap, we introduce Code-MUE, a purely black-box framework that measures uncertainty through execution-based Semantic Interaction Graphs. Unlike prior approaches that rely on superficial textual similarity, Code-MUE grounds uncertainty in observable runtime behavior, calculating the Von Neumann entropy of the solution space to quantify global semantic diversity. A large-scale empirical study across eight state-of-the-art LLMs demonstrates that Code-MUE achieves a strong negative correlation with functional correctness (Spearman’s correlation up to -0.98), significantly outperforming lexical and embedding-based baselines while enabling robust risk detection and selective prediction in practical workflows.","az":"随着代码大语言模型（LLM）成为现代软件工程的核心，其固有的随机性带来了重大的现实风险，即便微小的错误也可能导致严重的功能、安全或安全性后果。因此，可靠的自动化要求能够区分自信、有充分支撑的预测与随机猜测。然而，现有的不确定性估计方法面临一个关键空白：白盒与灰盒技术往往无法用于闭源模型，而标准的“黑盒”文本指标又无法刻画代码特有的脆弱性——语法上的变化并不总是意味着语义上的分歧。为弥合这一语法—语义鸿沟，我们提出 Code-MUE，一个纯黑盒框架，通过基于执行的语义交互图来度量不确定性。与依赖表层文本相似度的既有方法不同，Code-MUE 将不确定性建立在可观察的运行时行为之上，通过计算解空间的冯·诺依曼熵来量化全局语义多样性。一项跨越八个最先进 LLM 的大规模实证研究表明，Code-MUE 与功能正确性呈现强负相关（Spearman 相关系数高达 -0.98），显著优于基于词法与嵌入的基线，并能在实际工作流中实现稳健的风险检测与选择性预测。","tl":"用执行行为构图并取冯·诺依曼熵作为黑盒代码不确定性度量。","au":["xiaoning ren","Yinxing Xue","Lei Ma","Yuheng Huang"],"top":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","alt":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["uncertainty estimation","code LLM","semantic interaction graph","execution-based","selective prediction"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/185/x"},{"id":"p01468","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"RICE: Harnessing LLMs and Historical Issues to Discover Internal Rust Compiler Errors","tz":"RICE：利用大语言模型与历史 Issue 发现 Rust 编译器内部错误","a":"Rust is a modern system-level programming language that emphasizes safety, concurrency, and performance. Ensuring the reliability of the Rust compiler is critical, as undetected compiler defects, particularly internal compiler errors (ICEs), can lead to runtime crashes or undefined behavior in system software. Existing compiler testing methods, including generation-based, mutation-based, and recent LLM-driven approaches, are limited in their ability to systematically uncover ICEs triggered by advanced language features or complex code interactions. In this paper, we propose RICE, an LLM-assisted Rust compiler testing approach that generates test cases by adapting defect-prone patterns extracted from historical ICE issues to diverse code contexts in the official test suite. RICE features simplification-guided identification of defect-prone patterns and context-aware adaptation of patterns to maintain compilability and meaningful semantic interactions. Applied to multiple recent Rust compiler releases, RICE discovered 37 ICEs, including 15 previously unknown zero-day bugs, outperforming existing testing tools in code coverage and ICE discovery. Our results demonstrate that systematically leveraging historical defect-prone patterns enables more effective testing, accelerates bug fixing, and enhances regression testing in Rust compilers.","az":"Rust 是一种强调安全性、并发性与性能的现代系统级编程语言。确保 Rust 编译器的可靠性至关重要，因为未被发现的编译器缺陷——尤其是内部编译器错误（ICE）——可能导致系统软件的运行时崩溃或未定义行为。现有的编译器测试方法，包括基于生成的、基于变异的以及近期基于大语言模型的方法，在系统性地发现由高级语言特性或复杂代码交互触发的 ICE 方面能力有限。本文提出 RICE，一种由大语言模型辅助的 Rust 编译器测试方法，它通过将从历史 ICE issue 中提取的易致缺陷模式适配到官方测试套件中多样的代码上下文来生成测试用例。RICE 的特点是以简化为引导识别易致缺陷模式，以及上下文感知地适配这些模式以保持可编译性和有意义的语义交互。将 RICE 应用于多个近期 Rust 编译器版本，它发现了 37 个 ICE，其中包括 15 个此前未知的零日缺陷，在代码覆盖率与 ICE 发现数量上都优于现有测试工具。我们的结果表明，系统性地利用历史易致缺陷模式能够实现更有效的测试，加速缺陷修复，并增强 Rust 编译器的回归测试。","tl":"把历史 ICE issue 的易错模式移植到官方测试上下文生成新用例。","au":["Langyi Lu","Wei You","Bin Liang","Jianjun Huang"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["Rust compiler testing","internal compiler error","defect-prone patterns","LLM-assisted test generation","zero-day bugs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/186/x"},{"id":"p01469","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Efficient Predictive Monitoring of Message Passing Interface Programs","tz":"消息传递接口（MPI）程序的高效预测性监控","a":"The Message Passing Interface (MPI) is the standard programming model for high-performance computing, yet nondeterministic scheduling in concurrent executions makes reliability assurance highly challenging. Beyond deadlocks, property-related bugs such as modifying a send buffer before a nonblocking send completes or accessing a freed RMA window are often hard to reproduce and validate, as they typically manifest only under rare event interleavings and can be both latent and catastrophic. Existing dynamic checkers usually cover only the observed schedule of a single execution; dynamic verification largely focuses on deadlocks; and static techniques scale poorly to medium-to-large programs, often timing out or running out of memory. Overall, existing techniques do not support scalable analysis of temporal properties in large MPI programs. To address these limitations, we propose the first efficient predictive monitoring approach for temporal properties in MPI programs. From a single execution, we collect an event trace and use trace equivalence to predict the set of legal equivalent executions under the same input. We then check whether any predicted execution satisfies the target property. To make this process sound, we formalize three correctness criteria for MPI trace reordering and enforce them through MPI-semantics-driven dependency extraction, tracked with vector clocks. To improve efficiency, we exploit the bounded length of a pattern language and reduce long-trace reordering to reordering short patterns. We implement our approach in MPI-PRV, instantiate ten representative MPI bug properties, and evaluate it on 13 real-world MPI applications with 38 configurations. MPI-PRV successfully and correctly analyzes all $38$ tasks, whereas MPI-SV and MUST analyze only $14$ and $11$ tasks, respectively. MPI-PRV also achieves orders-of-magnitude reductions in runtime and memory usage, demonstrating strong efficiency and scalability for large MPI programs.","az":"消息传递接口（MPI）是高性能计算的标准编程模型，但并发执行中的非确定性调度使可靠性保障极具挑战。除死锁之外，诸如在非阻塞发送完成前修改发送缓冲区、或访问已释放的 RMA 窗口这类与性质相关的缺陷往往难以复现和验证，因为它们通常只在罕见的事件交错下显现，既可能潜伏又可能是灾难性的。现有的动态检查器通常只覆盖单次执行所观察到的调度；动态验证主要聚焦死锁；而静态技术在中大型程序上扩展性很差，常常超时或耗尽内存。总体而言，现有技术不支持对大型 MPI 程序中时序性质的可扩展分析。为解决这些局限，我们提出首个针对 MPI 程序时序性质的高效预测性监控方法。我们从单次执行中收集事件轨迹，并利用轨迹等价性预测同一输入下所有合法的等价执行集合，然后检查是否存在某个被预测的执行满足目标性质。为使该过程健全，我们形式化了 MPI 轨迹重排的三条正确性准则，并通过由 MPI 语义驱动的依赖提取（以向量时钟跟踪）加以强制。为提升效率，我们利用模式语言的有界长度，将长轨迹的重排归约为短模式的重排。我们在 MPI-PRV 中实现了该方法，实例化了十个有代表性的 MPI 缺陷性质，并在 13 个真实 MPI 应用的 38 种配置上进行评估。MPI-PRV 成功且正确地分析了全部 38 个任务，而 MPI-SV 和 MUST 分别只能分析 14 个和 11 个。MPI-PRV 在运行时间与内存使用上还实现了数量级的削减，展示了对大型 MPI 程序的强大效率与可扩展性。","tl":"由单次轨迹预测等价执行以健全高效检查 MPI 时序性质。","au":["Jiaqiang Yao","Haocheng Geng","Zhenbang Chen"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["MPI","predictive monitoring","temporal properties","trace equivalence","vector clocks"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/187/x"},{"id":"p01470","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Contamination Means Overestimation? A Fine-grained Empirical Study in Code Intelligence","tz":"污染就意味着高估吗？代码智能中的细粒度实证研究","a":"In recent years, code intelligence has gained increasing importance in the field of automated software engineering. Meanwhile, the widespread adoption of Pretrained Language Models (PLMs) and Large Language Models (LLMs) has raised concerns regarding data contamination and its potential impact on model performance evaluation. Previous studies mainly focused on sample-level contamination, ignoring partial contamination scenarios that are pervasive in code intelligence. This paper fills this gap and presents a systematic empirical study to investigate the fine-grained data contamination on mainstream code tasks. Our study involves diverse representative PLMs: RoBERTa and GPT-2, and LLMs: LLaMA and StarCoder, covering three major tasks: code translation, code generation, and code summarization, across two Programming Languages (PLs): Java and Python. We categorize contamination scenarios into four types according to the code intelligence practice, namely input-only, output-only, unpaired, and paired contamination settings, and construct corresponding experimental and control groups for exploration. Experimental results show that, under the pre-training, fine-tuning, and inference paradigm adopted by PLMs, even deliberately injecting paired contamination does not lead to significant performance overestimation. But direct inference or small-scale fine-tuning uncovers the contamination effects. In contrast, LLMs with pre-training and inference paradigm are significantly affected by the paired contamination. Apart from the above, other contamination scenarios have no impact on both PLMs and LLMs. Our findings challenge the conventional belief that contamination inevitably leads to performance overestimation, providing new insights into the evaluation and deployment of code intelligence models.","az":"近年来，代码智能在自动化软件工程领域的重要性日益上升。与此同时，预训练语言模型（PLM）与大语言模型（LLM）的广泛采用引发了对数据污染及其对模型性能评估潜在影响的担忧。以往研究主要关注样本级污染，忽视了在代码智能中普遍存在的部分污染场景。本文填补这一空白，开展了一项系统的实证研究，考察主流代码任务上的细粒度数据污染。我们的研究涵盖多种有代表性的 PLM：RoBERTa 和 GPT-2，以及 LLM：LLaMA 和 StarCoder，覆盖三大任务：代码翻译、代码生成和代码摘要，跨越两种编程语言（PL）：Java 和 Python。我们依据代码智能实践把污染场景分为四类，即仅输入污染、仅输出污染、非配对污染和配对污染，并构建相应的实验组与对照组进行探究。实验结果显示，在 PLM 所采用的预训练、微调、推理范式下，即便刻意注入配对污染也不会导致显著的性能高估；但直接推理或小规模微调会暴露污染效应。相比之下，采用预训练加推理范式的 LLM 受配对污染的影响显著。除上述之外，其他污染场景对 PLM 和 LLM 都没有影响。我们的发现挑战了“污染必然导致性能高估”的传统认知，为代码智能模型的评估与部署提供了新的洞见。","tl":"实证表明只有配对污染在 LLM 范式下才造成显著高估。","au":["Zhen Yang","Hongyi Lin","Yifan He","Junqi Wang","Zeyu Sun","Shuo Liu","Jie Xu","Pengpeng Wang","Zhongxing Yu","Qingyuan Liang"],"top":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based"],"kw":["data contamination","code intelligence","performance overestimation","PLM vs LLM","empirical study"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/188/x"},{"id":"p01471","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"A Closer Look at the Use of Reinforcement Learning for Speeding Up Runtime Verification of Software Tests (Experience Paper)","tz":"再看用强化学习加速软件测试运行时验证（经验论文）","a":"Runtime verification (RV) found many bugs by monitoring passing tests against formal specifications (specs), but it is slow. Researchers have recently shown that reinforcement learning (RL) can be used to speed up by RV during testing—by up to 551.5x, finding 99.6% of spec violations. We call this approach, “RL-based RV”; it aims to probabilistically monitor most unique traces—sequences of events like method calls—and monitor fewer redundant ones. But, there was no detailed study to understand remaining challenges in RL-based RV, towards finding insights and opportunities for improvement. We conduct the first in-depth study of RL-based RV. In particular, we focus on the only RL-based RV technique, Valg, and answer five main questions, using 58 Java projects. (i) How much slower is Valg than two optimal baselines? Up to 323.8x, or 3.2 hours (vs. running tests without RV), and up to 9.6x, or 25.3 minutes (vs. a theoretically optimal baseline that monitors only unique traces). (ii) Where does Valg spend its time? 48.6% (or 1.9 hours) is spent on monitoring, and 24.1% (or, 48.5 minutes) is also spent on signaling events to monitors. (iii) What characterizes code where Valg monitors too many redundant traces or misses unique ones? Across 100 code locations, at least 67.8% of redundant traces are due to limitations of the convergence heuristic, and 41.3% of missed unique traces occur when Valg’s assumption do not hold. (iv) How much do test non-determinism and the stochasticity of RL algorithm affect unique trace preservation? We see up to 95.5pp swings in the rate of unique trace preservation on the same project. (v) How do other off-the shelf RL algorithms compare with Valg? Only two of 11 RL algorithms that we survey are feasible in continuous integration; both are slower than Valg and miss more unique traces. So, custom RL algorithms for RV are needed. Overall, RL-based RV is promising, but there is plenty of room to improve it. We highlight several exciting directions for future research on doing so.","az":"运行时验证（RV）通过依据形式化规约（specs）监控通过的测试发现了许多缺陷，但它很慢。研究者近期表明，强化学习（RL）可用于在测试期间加速 RV——最高可达 551.5 倍，并能发现 99.6% 的规约违规。我们称这一方法为“基于 RL 的 RV”；它旨在以概率方式监控大多数独特轨迹（即方法调用等事件序列），而较少监控冗余轨迹。然而，此前没有详细研究来理解基于 RL 的 RV 中遗留的挑战，从而找出洞见与改进机会。我们开展了首个关于基于 RL 的 RV 的深入研究。具体而言，我们聚焦于唯一的基于 RL 的 RV 技术 Valg，使用 58 个 Java 项目回答五个主要问题。(i) Valg 比两个最优基线慢多少？相较不做 RV 地运行测试，最多慢 323.8 倍，即 3.2 小时；相较一个只监控独特轨迹的理论最优基线，最多慢 9.6 倍，即 25.3 分钟。(ii) Valg 的时间花在哪里？48.6%（或 1.9 小时）花在监控上，另有 24.1%（或 48.5 分钟）花在向监控器发送事件信号上。(iii) Valg 监控过多冗余轨迹或漏掉独特轨迹的代码有什么特征？在 100 个代码位置中，至少 67.8% 的冗余轨迹源于收敛启发式的局限，41.3% 的遗漏独特轨迹发生在 Valg 的假设不成立时。(iv) 测试的非确定性与 RL 算法的随机性对独特轨迹保留率影响多大？我们在同一项目上观察到独特轨迹保留率最多有 95.5 个百分点的波动。(v) 其他现成的 RL 算法与 Valg 相比如何？我们调研的 11 个 RL 算法中只有两个在持续集成中可行；二者都比 Valg 更慢且漏掉更多独特轨迹。因此，需要为 RV 定制 RL 算法。总体而言，基于 RL 的 RV 前景可期，但仍有大量改进空间。我们指出了若干激动人心的未来研究方向。","tl":"首次深入剖析 RL 加速运行时验证的开销来源与失效条件。","au":["Shinhae Kim","Saikat Dutta","Owolabi Legunsen"],"top":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["empirical-study","reproducibility-replication"],"kw":["runtime verification","reinforcement learning","unique traces","monitoring overhead","experience paper"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/189/x"},{"id":"p01472","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"WITFuzz: Validity-Preserving Greybox Fuzzing for WebAssembly Interface Type Binding Generators","tz":"WITFuzz：面向 WebAssembly 接口类型绑定生成器的保持有效性灰盒模糊测试","a":"In the WebAssembly component model, interfaces written in WebAssembly Interface Types (WIT) are packaged and consumed as build-time dependencies, and binding generators (bindgens) translate them into language-specific bindings. Although a WIT package can be spec-valid, it can still break builds—by crashing or timing out during bindgen execution (Phase I), or by causing downstream toolchains to reject the generated bindings after generation appears to succeed (Phase II). Testing bindgens at scale is challenging because WIT is strongly typed and constraint-rich, and Phase II failures require language-specific checking. We present WITFuzz, a validity-preserving greybox fuzzer for WIT bindgens. WITFuzz mutates resolved WIT abstract syntax trees via structure-aware rewrites expressed in a small domain-specific language, and propagates correlated updates to maintain WIT validity. To overcome coverage plateaus, WITFuzz expands its strategy pool online using coverage-guided, LLM-assisted synthesis, admitting only strategies that pass local validation. WITFuzz further uses a build-aware, multi-layer oracle that combines in-loop checks with selective asynchronous compilation/typechecking of generated bindings to capture non-crashing build breakers. Across 12 bindgens, WITFuzz achieves the highest coverage and uncovers 40 previously unknown Phase I and Phase II build-breaking bugs, including 35 missed by all baselines.","az":"在 WebAssembly 组件模型中，用 WebAssembly 接口类型（WIT）编写的接口被打包并作为构建期依赖使用，绑定生成器（bindgen）将其翻译为特定语言的绑定。尽管一个 WIT 包可能符合规范，它仍可能破坏构建——或是在 bindgen 执行期间崩溃或超时（第一阶段），或是在生成看似成功之后导致下游工具链拒绝所生成的绑定（第二阶段）。大规模测试 bindgen 很有挑战，因为 WIT 是强类型且约束丰富的，而第二阶段的失败需要特定语言的检查。我们提出 WITFuzz，一个面向 WIT bindgen 的保持有效性的灰盒模糊测试器。WITFuzz 通过以一种小型领域专用语言表达的结构感知重写来变异已解析的 WIT 抽象语法树，并传播相关联的更新以维持 WIT 的有效性。为克服覆盖率停滞，WITFuzz 使用覆盖率引导、LLM 辅助的合成在线扩充其策略池，只接纳通过本地验证的策略。WITFuzz 还使用一个构建感知的多层预言，将循环内检查与对所生成绑定的选择性异步编译/类型检查相结合，以捕获不导致崩溃的构建破坏者。在 12 个 bindgen 上，WITFuzz 取得了最高覆盖率，并发现了 40 个此前未知的第一阶段与第二阶段构建破坏缺陷，其中 35 个被所有基线漏掉。","tl":"结构感知变异加 LLM 在线扩策略，测出 bindgen 的构建破坏缺陷。","au":["Hanqin Guan","Ningyu He","Shangtong Cao","Yifeng Cai","Yao Guo","Ding Li"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["WebAssembly Interface Types","binding generator","greybox fuzzing","structure-aware mutation","build-breaking bugs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/190/x"},{"id":"p01473","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"On the Evaluation of Large Language Models in Unit Test Evolution (Experience Paper)","tz":"关于大语言模型在单元测试演化中的评估（经验论文）","a":"Large language models (LLMs) have recently shown promising potential in automating unit test updates for evolving software systems. However, the effectiveness of LLMs in unit test evolution remains insufficiently understood, particularly with respect to prompt design choices, in-context learning (ICL) strategies, and different types of test evolution. In this paper, we present the first comprehensive empirical study to evaluate LLMs for unit test evolution. We systematically assess nine open-source code LLMs with parameter sizes ranging from 3B to 34B, along with three state-of-the-art commercial models, under diverse prompt designs and ICL methods. To support robust and execution-based evaluation, we construct a new benchmark consisting of 530 real-world focal method–test co-evolution instances collected from seven actively maintained open-source projects. Our evaluation employs a suite of compilation, execution, and coverage-based metrics. Extensive experimental results reveal that prompt design and ICL methods play a critical role. However, different LLMs and evolution types should adopt different prompt design strategies and ICL methods in the unit test evolution. Based on our findings, we derive actionable insights to guide future research and practical adoption of LLM-based techniques for unit test evolution.","az":"大语言模型（LLM）近期在为不断演化的软件系统自动更新单元测试方面展现出可观潜力。然而，LLM 在单元测试演化中的有效性仍未被充分理解，尤其是在提示设计选择、上下文学习（ICL）策略以及不同类型的测试演化方面。本文提出首个全面的实证研究来评估用于单元测试演化的 LLM。我们在多样的提示设计与 ICL 方法下，系统评估了参数规模从 3B 到 34B 的九个开源代码 LLM，以及三个最先进的商用模型。为支持稳健的、基于执行的评估，我们构建了一个新基准，包含从七个活跃维护的开源项目中收集的 530 个真实焦点方法—测试共演化实例。我们的评估采用了一套基于编译、执行与覆盖率的指标。大量实验结果表明，提示设计与 ICL 方法起着关键作用；然而，不同的 LLM 与不同的演化类型在单元测试演化中应当采用不同的提示设计策略与 ICL 方法。基于这些发现，我们给出了可操作的洞见，以指导未来研究以及基于 LLM 的单元测试演化技术的实际采用。","tl":"首个单元测试演化的 LLM 评测基准与提示/ICL 策略实证。","au":["Weichang Liu","Junwei Zhang","Yuqing Niu","Bo Zhou"],"top":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["unit test evolution","in-context learning","prompt design","benchmark","code LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/191/x"},{"id":"p01474","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"STARS: Static Analysis-guided Assertion Synthesis Using Large Language Models","tz":"STARS：由静态分析引导的大语言模型断言合成","a":"Automated unit test generation promises to reduce the cost of software quality assurance, and hence, is attracting attention from both academia and industry. Yet, generating assertions that are executable, meaningful to developers, and able to catch faults remains an unsolved challenge. Existing approaches either randomly enumerate assertions that are plausible based on static program analysis without considering whether they naturally fit the test prefix or query an LLM to generate assertions based on local context only, such as the test prefix and the focal method. However, we observe that local context alone is insufficient for LLMs to generate high-quality assertions because many desirable assertions are built from components that are almost impossible to guess for an LLM, such as sequences of multiple method calls. This paper presents STARS, a novel test assertion generation technique that combines the benefits of static program analysis and LLM-based synthesis. The key idea is to first gather a set of assertion components based on static program analysis and to then combine, concretize, prioritize, and improve them with an LLM. The resulting assertions go beyond what an LLM alone could realistically guess based on the test prefix and focal method, and they naturally fit the given test case. Empirical results show that STARS consistently outperforms the state-of-the-art baseline in five evaluation metrics: STARS achieves an exact-match rate of at most 66.2%, and its mutation score nearly triples that of the baseline (10.97% vs. 3.97%), approaching that of developer-written assertions, while consuming 24.75% fewer tokens and 30.6% fewer LLM queries","az":"自动化单元测试生成有望降低软件质量保障的成本，因而正吸引学术界与工业界的关注。然而，生成既可执行、对开发者有意义、又能捕获故障的断言仍是一个未解的挑战。现有方法要么基于静态程序分析随机枚举看似合理的断言，而不考虑它们是否自然契合测试前缀；要么仅基于局部上下文（例如测试前缀与焦点方法）查询大语言模型生成断言。然而我们观察到，仅靠局部上下文不足以让 LLM 生成高质量断言，因为许多理想的断言由 LLM 几乎不可能猜出的成分构成，例如多个方法调用的序列。本文提出 STARS，一种新颖的测试断言生成技术，它结合了静态程序分析与基于 LLM 的合成的优势。其核心思想是先基于静态程序分析收集一组断言成分，然后用 LLM 对它们进行组合、具体化、排序与改进。由此得到的断言超出了 LLM 仅凭测试前缀与焦点方法所能实际猜测的范围，并且自然契合给定的测试用例。实证结果表明，STARS 在五项评估指标上持续优于最先进的基线：STARS 的精确匹配率最高达 66.2%，其变异得分几乎是基线的三倍（10.97% 对 3.97%），接近开发者手写断言的水平，同时消耗的 token 减少 24.75%，LLM 查询次数减少 30.6%。","tl":"先用静态分析收集断言成分，再让 LLM 组合具体化并排序。","au":["Jialun Cao","Haoyu Wang","Haoran Yan","Ming Wen","Michael Pradel"],"top":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","alt":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["assertion generation","test oracle","static program analysis","mutation score","LLM synthesis"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/192/x"},{"id":"p01475","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AdaptAgent: A Multi-agent, Domain-Guided Reasoning Framework for Code Adaptation","tz":"AdaptAgent：面向代码适配的多智能体领域引导推理框架","a":"Developers often reuse code snippets from online forums (e.g., Stack Overflow). However, integrating them into an existing repository remains challenging in a manual process. A successful integration typically requires more than copying code, as a user must produce correct adapting changes at a designated location in the target repository. We formalize this as the code adaptation problem: given a snippet, functional intent, a target repository, and an adaptation location, generate a patch that adapts the snippet into the repository. We present AdaptAgent, a multi-agent, domain-guided reasoning framework for code adaptation. Rather than relying on single-shot prompting, AdaptAgent decomposes adaptation into specialized agents that communicate via typed artifacts: an Intent Summarizer extracts adaptation goals from Q&A text; a Policy Agent derives domain policies from six adaptation categories; a Domain Planner generates a self-ordered plan; a Context Miner distills sibling-method semantics from the target codebase; and a Code Adapter realizes the plan as a minimal unified diff, iteratively refined using a compiler-based Verifier. This division of labor enables robust, policy-aligned adaptations and supports adapting online snippets into a project. On a real-world dataset, AdaptAgent outperforms strong baselines in semantic correctness and produces patches that mirror developers’ actual adaptation patterns. Our ablation study shows each agent’s necessity, especially planning for code-hardening and exception-handling, and intent for logic customization.","az":"开发者经常复用来自在线论坛（例如 Stack Overflow）的代码片段。然而，将它们整合进现有仓库在人工流程中仍然充满挑战。成功的整合通常不只是复制代码，因为用户必须在目标仓库的指定位置产出正确的适配性改动。我们将其形式化为代码适配问题：给定一个片段、功能意图、一个目标仓库以及一个适配位置，生成一个将该片段适配进仓库的补丁。我们提出 AdaptAgent，一个面向代码适配的多智能体、领域引导推理框架。AdaptAgent 不依赖单次提示，而是将适配分解为通过带类型制品通信的专门智能体：意图摘要器从问答文本中提取适配目标；策略智能体从六类适配类别中导出领域策略；领域规划器生成一个自排序的计划；上下文挖掘器从目标代码库中提炼兄弟方法的语义；代码适配器将计划实现为最小的统一 diff，并借助基于编译器的验证器迭代精化。这种分工使得适配稳健且与策略一致，并支持将在线片段适配进项目。在一个真实数据集上，AdaptAgent 在语义正确性上优于强基线，并产出与开发者实际适配模式相符的补丁。我们的消融研究表明每个智能体都是必要的，尤其是用于代码加固与异常处理的规划，以及用于逻辑定制的意图。","tl":"把代码片段复用形式化为适配问题并用分工智能体产出最小补丁。","au":["Xiaokai Rong","Hridya Dhulipala","Aashish Yadavally","Tien N. Nguyen"],"top":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","alt":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","tg":["llm-based","agentic","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["code adaptation","code reuse","multi-agent framework","Stack Overflow snippets","patch generation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/193/x"},{"id":"p01476","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Understanding Automated Program Repair Agents Through the Lens of Traceability: An Empirical Study","tz":"从可追溯性视角理解自动程序修复智能体：一项实证研究","a":"Automated Program Repair (APR) agents leverage large language models (LLMs) to autonomously diagnose and patch software bugs using planning, reasoning, and tools. Although these agents show strong performance on leaderboards such as SWE-bench, little is understood about how they take actions, where they fail, and how their behavior compares to human developers. In this paper, we present the first systematic analysis of these limitations using 5 state-of-the-art APR agents. We trace the full decision-making pipelines of the 5 APR agents across 500 real-world repair tasks, from issue description to patch validation. Our study reveals that, while agents excel at simple fixes, they struggle with logic-intensive bugs, often generating verbose, overfitted patches that pass existing test suites without solving the root cause. Test generation and regression test selection remain major bottlenecks, as agents fail to reproduce issues or run relevant regression tests. Moreover, many agents operate with primitive tooling (e.g. bash scripts) and do not have access to debuggers or program analysis tools. These findings highlight key limitations of current APR systems and motivate several directions for next-generation APR design, including but not limited to: (1) a shift-left approach emphasizing early, high-quality test generation and validation to reduce spurious fixes and improve semantic correctness; (2) richer, more integrated tool ecosystems; (3) diversified agent architectures that combine complementary strengths; and (4) benchmarks that prioritize semantic repair quality and test-generation fidelity over surface-level success metrics.","az":"自动程序修复（APR）智能体利用大语言模型（LLM），通过规划、推理和工具自主地诊断并修补软件缺陷。尽管这些智能体在 SWE-bench 等排行榜上表现强劲，但人们对它们如何采取行动、在哪里失败、以及其行为与人类开发者相比如何，所知甚少。本文利用 5 个最先进的 APR 智能体，首次对这些局限性进行了系统分析。我们在 500 个真实世界的修复任务上追踪了这 5 个 APR 智能体从 issue 描述到补丁验证的完整决策流水线。我们的研究表明：虽然智能体擅长简单修复，但在逻辑密集型缺陷上举步维艰，常常生成冗长、过拟合的补丁——这些补丁能通过已有测试套件，却没有解决根因。测试生成与回归测试选择仍是主要瓶颈，智能体往往无法复现 issue，也无法运行相关的回归测试。此外，许多智能体只使用原始的工具（例如 bash 脚本），无法访问调试器或程序分析工具。这些发现凸显了当前 APR 系统的关键局限，并启发了下一代 APR 设计的若干方向，包括但不限于：（1）采用“左移”思路，强调早期、高质量的测试生成与验证，以减少虚假修复并提升语义正确性；（2）更丰富、更一体化的工具生态；（3）多样化的智能体架构，以组合互补的优势；（4）优先考察语义修复质量与测试生成保真度、而非表层成功率指标的基准测试。","tl":"首次全链路追踪5个APR智能体在500任务上的决策与失败点","au":["Ira Ceka","Hailie Mitchell","Saurabh Pujar","Luca Buratti","Shyam Ramji","Junfeng Yang","Gail Kaiser","Baishakhi Ray"],"top":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["empirical-study","agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["APR agents","traceability","empirical study","patch overfitting","SWE-bench"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/194/x"},{"id":"p01477","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CONCUR: Benchmarking LLMs for Concurrent Code Generation","tz":"CONCUR：面向并发代码生成的 LLM 基准测试","a":"Leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) for code generation has increasingly emerged as a common practice in the domain of software engineering. Relevant benchmarks have been established to evaluate the code generation capabilities of LLMs. However, existing benchmarks focus primarily on sequential code, lacking the ability to effectively evaluate LLMs on concurrent code generation. Compared to sequential code, concurrent code exhibits greater complexity and possesses unique types of bugs, such as deadlocks and race conditions, that do not occur in sequential code. Therefore, a benchmark for evaluating sequential code generation cannot be useful for evaluating concurrent code generation with LLMs. To address this gap, we designed a benchmark CONCUR specifically aimed at evaluating the capability of LLMs to generate concurrent code. CONCUR consists of a base set of 43 concurrency problems derived from a standard concurrency textbook, together with 72 validated mutant variants, resulting in 115 total problems. The base problems serve as the semantic core of the benchmark, while the mutants expand linguistic and structural diversity. We conducted an evaluation of a range of LLMs on CONCUR, highlighting limitations of current models. Overall, our work provides a novel direction for evaluating the capability of LLMs to generate code with focus on concurrency.","az":"利用大语言模型（LLM）进行代码生成已日益成为软件工程领域的常见实践。相关基准测试已被建立起来以评估 LLM 的代码生成能力。然而，现有基准主要聚焦于顺序代码，无法有效评估 LLM 的并发代码生成能力。与顺序代码相比，并发代码复杂度更高，并且具有顺序代码中不会出现的独特缺陷类型，例如死锁和竞态条件。因此，用于评估顺序代码生成的基准无法有效评估 LLM 的并发代码生成。为填补这一空白，我们设计了 CONCUR 基准，专门用于评估 LLM 生成并发代码的能力。CONCUR 包含一个由标准并发教材衍生出的 43 个并发问题的基础集，以及 72 个经过验证的变异体变体，共计 115 个问题。基础问题构成该基准的语义内核，而变异体则扩展了语言层面与结构层面的多样性。我们在 CONCUR 上评估了一系列 LLM，凸显了当前模型的局限。总体而言，我们的工作为评估 LLM 在并发场景下的代码生成能力提供了一个新方向。","tl":"首个专测LLM并发代码生成的基准，含43题与72变异体","au":["Jue Huang","Tarek Mahmud","Corina S. Păsăreanu","Guowei Yang"],"top":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","alt":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["concurrent code generation","benchmark","deadlock","race condition","LLM evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/195/x"},{"id":"p01478","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"PatchPorter: LLM-Driven Security Patch Porting via Version Tracing and Context Selection for NPM","tz":"PatchPorter：面向 NPM 的 LLM 驱动安全补丁移植——基于版本溯源与上下文选择","a":"Third-Party Libraries are widely used in modern software development, yet their vulnerabilities pose serious security risks. This issue is particularly severe in the NPM ecosystem, where high-risk 1-day vulnerabilities can remain unpatched for extended periods. Although upgrading to the latest patched version is commonly recommended, it often causes major compatibility issues. Patch porting offers an effective solution to this challenge. However, existing patch porting methods are mainly designed for C and have two limitations when applied to NPM. First, they can be brittle in precisely localizing fix locations when substantial semantic gaps exist across versions. Second, they rely on either excessive or insufficient context for patch adaptation, which may introduce redundant information and increase the risk of hallucination. This paper introduces PatchPorter, a patch porting method for NPM that builds on Large Language Models (LLMs). PatchPorter addresses these limitations through two modules. The localization module leverages LLM semantic understanding and code evolution analysis over version histories maintained by version control systems to identify fix locations. The context selection module analyzes patch dependencies to select minimal yet sufficient context around the localized fix location. The selected context is used as input for the LLM to generate the patch. We construct a dataset of 112 NPM vulnerabilities with Proof-of-Concepts for automated dynamic validation. Experimental results show that PatchPorter significantly surpasses other methods in accuracy, achieving a 26.2% improvement over the best-performing baseline and a 70.6% increase on the most difficult tasks. Its ability to handle various vulnerability types highlights its practical value. Additional results confirm that both of its main modules also outperform alternative approaches.","az":"第三方库在现代软件开发中被广泛使用，但其漏洞带来了严重的安全风险。这一问题在 NPM 生态中尤为严重，高危的 1-day 漏洞可能长期得不到修补。虽然升级到最新的已修补版本是常见建议，但往往会引发严重的兼容性问题。补丁移植为这一挑战提供了有效的解决方案。然而，现有的补丁移植方法主要针对 C 语言设计，应用到 NPM 时存在两点局限。第一，当版本之间存在较大的语义鸿沟时，它们在精确定位修复位置上会很脆弱。第二，它们在补丁适配时依赖过多或过少的上下文，可能引入冗余信息并增加幻觉风险。本文提出 PatchPorter，一种基于大语言模型（LLM）的 NPM 补丁移植方法。PatchPorter 通过两个模块来解决上述局限。定位模块利用 LLM 的语义理解能力，并结合对版本控制系统所维护的版本历史进行代码演化分析，以识别修复位置。上下文选择模块分析补丁依赖，在已定位的修复位置周围选取最小但充分的上下文。所选上下文作为 LLM 的输入用于生成补丁。我们构建了一个包含 112 个 NPM 漏洞及其 Proof-of-Concept 的数据集，用于自动化动态验证。实验结果表明，PatchPorter 在准确率上显著超越其他方法，相对最佳基线提升 26.2%，在最困难的任务上提升 70.6%。它处理多种漏洞类型的能力凸显了其实用价值。补充实验进一步确认，其两个主要模块也都优于替代方案。","tl":"用版本演化溯源定位+最小充分上下文，实现NPM安全补丁移植","au":["Zeliang Yu","Ming Wen","Zichao Wei","Yulun Wu","Deqing Zou","Hai Jin"],"top":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","alt":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release","benchmark-dataset"],"kw":["patch porting","NPM","1-day vulnerability","context selection","version tracing"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/196/x"},{"id":"p01479","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"AsyncLeakBench: A Curated Benchmark of Asynchronous Resource Leaks in Open-Source Java Projects","tz":"AsyncLeakBench：开源 Java 项目中异步资源泄漏的精选基准","a":"Asynchronous programming has become a core execution model in modern Java software, powering server-side processing, network I/O, reactive streams, task scheduling, and RPC communication. In such asynchronous executions, resource creation and release are no longer confined to a single call stack; instead, they are distributed across heterogeneous execution contexts such as callbacks, Future/Promise chains, and scheduler boundaries. As a result, a resource lifecycle can be determined non-deterministically by events such as execution ordering, races, cancellation, and timeouts, making resource leaks a critical source of performance degradation and failures. However, prior research and public datasets on resource leaks have largely focused on synchronous settings, where defects typically manifest as missing close calls or omitted exceptional paths. In synchronous programs, release logic is often located within the same thread and call stack, allowing leaks to be defined and analyzed by tracking close invocations along normal and exceptional control-flow paths. In contrast, in asynchronous environments, resource release depends on the execution of callbacks on different threads, Future completion events, or scheduler decisions, and the release path itself may vary under cancellation, timeouts, or changes in execution order. Therefore, existing synchronous leak datasets fail to adequately represent the conditions and repair strategies of asynchronous resource leaks, hindering quantitative and fair evaluation of detection and automated repair techniques. To bridge this gap, we present AsyncLeakBench, a public benchmark that systematically curates real-world asynchronous resource leak defects that have been fixed in open-source Java projects. We collect 572 defect–patch pairs from 18 representative projects via a semi-automatic workflow, and refine them into high-quality ground truth through iterative filtering and manual validation. We further categorize the collected cases into 11 categories, summarizing key triggers and repair strategies driven by asynchronous events such as cancellation, timeouts, and scheduler boundaries. Moreover, an initial evaluation on existing resource leak detectors confirms that their detection performance is limited, particularly for leak patterns activated by asynchronous events such as cancellation and timeouts, highlighting the need for a dedicated benchmark for this defect class. AsyncLeakBench provides a realistic and reproducible evaluation basis for asynchronous resource leak detection and automated repair, static and dynamic analysis, fault localization, and LLM-based debugging. By establishing asynchronous resource leaks as a distinct defect class and offering a standardized benchmark for systematic study, this work contributes to advancing future research in software analysis and testing.","az":"异步编程已成为现代 Java 软件的核心执行模型，支撑着服务端处理、网络 I/O、响应式流、任务调度和 RPC 通信。在这类异步执行中，资源的创建与释放不再局限于单个调用栈，而是分散在回调、Future/Promise 链以及调度器边界等异构执行上下文中。因此，资源生命周期可能由执行顺序、竞态、取消和超时等事件非确定性地决定，使资源泄漏成为性能退化与故障的关键来源。然而，以往关于资源泄漏的研究与公开数据集大多聚焦于同步场景，其中缺陷通常表现为缺失 \\texttt{close} 调用或遗漏异常路径。在同步程序中，释放逻辑通常位于同一线程和调用栈内，因此可以通过沿正常与异常控制流路径追踪 \\texttt{close} 调用来定义和分析泄漏。相比之下，在异步环境中，资源释放依赖于在不同线程上执行的回调、Future 完成事件或调度器决策，而释放路径本身还可能随取消、超时或执行顺序变化而改变。因此，现有的同步泄漏数据集无法充分表征异步资源泄漏的触发条件与修复策略，阻碍了对检测与自动修复技术的定量且公平的评估。为弥合这一空白，我们提出 \\textbf{AsyncLeakBench}，一个系统性整理了开源 Java 项目中已修复的真实异步资源泄漏缺陷的公开基准。我们通过半自动工作流，从 \\textbf{18} 个代表性项目中收集了 \\textbf{572} 个缺陷—补丁对，并通过迭代筛选与人工验证将其精炼为高质量的 ground truth。我们进一步将收集到的案例划分为 \\textbf{11} 个类别，总结了由取消、超时和调度器边界等异步事件驱动的关键触发条件与修复策略。此外，对现有资源泄漏检测器的初步评估确认，它们的检测性能有限，尤其是对由取消和超时等异步事件激活的泄漏模式，凸显了为这一缺陷类别建立专门基准的必要性。AsyncLeakBench 为异步资源泄漏的检测与自动修复、静态与动态分析、缺陷定位以及基于 LLM 的调试提供了真实且可复现的评估基础。通过将异步资源泄漏确立为一个独立的缺陷类别并提供标准化基准以支持系统研究，本工作推动了软件分析与测试领域的后续研究。","tl":"首个异步资源泄漏基准：572缺陷补丁对、11类触发与修复模式","au":["Jinyoung Kim","Jinseok Heo","Dongwook Choi","Eunseok Lee"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["asynchronous resource leak","Java","benchmark","defect-patch pairs","leak detector evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/197/x"},{"id":"p01480","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Systematically Cover SQL Syntactic Structures via k-Sequence","tz":"通过 k-序列系统性覆盖 SQL 语法结构","a":"Testing Relational Database Management Systems (RDBMSs) is inherently challenging because SQL, the primary language for interacting with RDBMSs, exhibits a vast and highly complex grammar with hundreds of interdependent production rules in the Extended Backus–Naur Form. While existing grammar-based testing techniques have made progress in covering SQL syntactic structures, they predominantly focus on parent-child relationships in derivation paths, which capture vertical expansions from a non-terminal to its alternatives. However, they overlook an equally critical dimension, sibling-like relationships, which capture co-occurring alternatives across derivation paths. This oversight results in insufficient coverage of intricate syntactic interactions that may trigger unique behaviors or latent bugs in RDBMSs. In this work, we propose k-sequence, a novel coverage criterion that characterizes syntactic structures as ordered sequences of k alternatives encountered during derivation. By simultaneously capturing both vertical parent-child and horizontal sibling-like relationships in the SQL syntactic structures, k-sequence provides a unified framework for comprehensive SQL syntactic coverage. Based on this criterion, we develop KSeqFuzz, a directed fuzzing approach that systematically generates SQL statements to explore previously unseen k-sequences, achieving deeper and broader testing coverage. We implement and evaluate KSeqFuzz on four widely-deployed RDBMSs, i.e., MySQL, MariaDB, TiDB, and OceanBase. In total, KSeqFuzz detects 58 new unique bugs, including 6 critical crashes. Evaluation results demonstrate that KSeqFuzz outperforms state-of-the-art baselines, detecting 26% more unique bugs during 24-hour testing campaigns.","az":"测试关系型数据库管理系统（RDBMS）本质上具有挑战性，因为与 RDBMS 交互的主要语言 SQL 拥有庞大且高度复杂的文法，在扩展巴科斯范式（EBNF）中包含数百条相互依赖的产生式规则。虽然现有基于文法的测试技术在覆盖 SQL 语法结构方面取得了进展，但它们主要关注推导路径中的\\textit{父子关系}，即从一个非终结符到其候选式的\\textit{纵向}展开。然而，它们忽略了同样关键的另一维度——\\textit{兄弟式关系}，即跨推导路径共现的候选式。这一疏漏导致对复杂语法交互的覆盖不足，而这些交互可能触发 RDBMS 中独特的行为或潜藏的缺陷。在本工作中，我们提出 \\textit{k-sequence}，一种新的覆盖准则，它将语法结构刻画为推导过程中所遇到的 $k$ 个候选式的有序序列。通过同时捕捉 SQL 语法结构中的\\textit{纵向父子}关系与\\textit{横向兄弟式}关系，\\textit{k-sequence} 为全面的 SQL 语法覆盖提供了统一框架。基于该准则，我们开发了 KSeqFuzz，一种定向模糊测试方法，系统性地生成 SQL 语句以探索此前未见的 \\textit{k-sequence}，从而实现更深更广的测试覆盖。我们在四个广泛部署的 RDBMS 上实现并评估了 KSeqFuzz，即 MySQL、MariaDB、TiDB 和 OceanBase。总计而言，KSeqFuzz 检测到 58 个新的独特缺陷，其中包括 6 个严重崩溃。评估结果表明，KSeqFuzz 优于最先进的基线方法，在 24 小时测试活动中多检测出 26% 的独特缺陷。","tl":"提出k-序列覆盖准则，兼顾语法的父子与兄弟关系来测数据库","au":["Hongtao Zhou","Yingying Zheng","Yu Gao","Jiansen Song","Xudong Xie","Rui Yang","Ziyu Cui","Wensheng Dou","Jun Wei"],"top":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["SQL grammar coverage","k-sequence","directed fuzzing","RDBMS testing","KSeqFuzz"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/198/x"},{"id":"p01481","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"IssueExec: A Test-Driven Approach for Localizing Software Engineering Issues","tz":"IssueExec：一种测试驱动的软件工程 Issue 定位方法","a":"Issue localization, which identifies code locations requiring modification from issue descriptions, is a critical step in automated software maintenance. Existing approaches predominantly attempt to directly align issue descriptions with code elements, yet often struggle due to the inherent abstraction gap between the issue description and code implementation. Seeking alternative signals, our theoretical analysis suggests that test suites can serve as executable proxies for requirements, reducing localization uncertainty by 2.01 bits on average. A large-scale empirical study on 18 repositories validates this premise: existing tests cover 96.98% of ground-truth files, and the two-hop pathway yields stronger semantic connectivity than direct matching in 82.4% of cases. Despite their potential, leveraging tests for localization faces two key challenges: the semantic gap separating issue descriptions from test identifiers, and the substantial noise in execution traces from infrastructure code. To address these, we propose IssueExec, which bridges the semantic gap through domain-knowledge-enhanced test representations and filters noise via hierarchical trace analysis. Experiments on SWE-bench Lite show that IssueExec achieves state-of-the-art performance, improving function-level Recall@1 by 41.57% over the strongest baseline. When integrated into the Agentless pipeline, IssueExec resolves 17.72% more issues, demonstrating practical downstream benefits.","az":"Issue 定位，即从 issue 描述中识别需要修改的代码位置，是自动化软件维护中的关键一步。现有方法大多试图将 issue 描述与代码元素直接对齐，但由于 issue 描述与代码实现之间固有的抽象鸿沟，往往效果不佳。为寻找替代信号，我们的理论分析表明，测试套件可以作为需求的可执行代理，平均可将定位的不确定性降低 2.01 比特。在 18 个仓库上的大规模实证研究验证了这一前提：已有测试覆盖了 96.98% 的 ground-truth 文件，并且在 82.4% 的案例中，两跳路径比直接匹配具有更强的语义连通性。尽管潜力可观，利用测试进行定位仍面临两大挑战：issue 描述与测试标识符之间的语义鸿沟，以及执行轨迹中来自基础设施代码的大量噪声。为此，我们提出 IssueExec，通过领域知识增强的测试表示来弥合语义鸿沟，并通过分层轨迹分析过滤噪声。在 SWE-bench Lite 上的实验表明，IssueExec 取得了最先进的性能，函数级 Recall@1 相比最强基线提升 41.57%。当集成到 Agentless 流水线中时，IssueExec 多解决了 17.72% 的 issue，展示了实际的下游收益。","tl":"把测试套件当作需求的可执行代理来做issue定位","au":["Jiawei Liu","Yun Lin","Chenyan Liu","Yu Qian","Liu Yiming","Jiaxin Chang","Weinan Zhang","Linpeng Huang"],"top":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","empirical-study"],"kw":["issue localization","test-driven","execution trace","SWE-bench Lite","Agentless"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/199/x"},{"id":"p01482","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Mathematically-Guided Detection of Floating-Point Errors","tz":"数学引导的浮点误差检测","a":"Floating-point computations are important for modern scientific and engineering software, especially for safety-critical systems, yet only a small subset of inputs typically trigger substantial numerical errors. Detecting such error-inducing inputs and the underlying bugs is therefore essential for improving their security and reliability. Existing techniques commonly rely on either oracle-driven exploration that repeatedly compares against high-precision references or search-driven heuristics. Despite the improvements made, they remain limited by (1) Expensive computation of high-precision oracles and (2) Lack of long-range convergence, which often requires dense probing near narrow error-inducing regions and expensive computation. We propose MGDE (Mathematically-Guided Detection of floating-point Errors), a method that replaces trial-and-error exploration with mathematically defined targets and directed convergence. MGDE first uses condition-number theory to identify numerically unstable atomic operations without invoking expensive high-precision oracles during exploration. MDGE exploits the observation that extreme condition numbers occur near structured boundaries (e.g., cancellation points and singularities), reformulating detection as a numerical root-finding problem. By solving the resulting objectives with the Newton–Raphson method, MGDE can steer inputs toward error-prone regions from far-away initializations. We evaluate MGDE on GNU Scientific Library (GSL) functions and compare against two state-of-the-art baselines, ATOMU and FPCC, using triggered bugs as the primary metric. On 88 single-input functions, MGDE triggers 80 bugs across 47 functions, outperforming ATOMU (70 bugs in 46 functions) and FPCC (53 bugs in 42 functions). MGDE is also faster: ATOMU and FPCC require 41.71 and 10.17 more time, respectively. The advantage is even more significant for multi-input functions, where MGDE triggers nine bugs while FPCC triggers none, and achieves an average runtime of 0.6443 seconds per function compared to FPCC’s 100-second budget. Overall, MGDE substantially advances the state of the art in both effectiveness and efficiency, and we report 16 previously unknown GSL bugs, which have been confirmed by the GSL community.","az":"浮点计算对现代科学与工程软件十分重要，尤其是对安全攸关系统，但通常只有一小部分输入会触发显著的数值误差。因此，检测这类诱发误差的输入及其背后的缺陷，对提升其安全性与可靠性至关重要。现有技术通常依赖于反复与高精度参考值比较的预言驱动探索，或依赖搜索驱动的启发式方法。尽管已有改进，它们仍受限于 \\textbf{(1) 高精度预言的计算代价高昂} 和 \\textbf{(2) 缺乏长程收敛能力}，后者往往需要在狭窄的诱发误差区域附近进行密集探测和昂贵计算。我们提出 MGDE（\\textbf{M}athematically-\\textbf{G}uided \\textbf{D}etection of floating-point \\textbf{E}rrors），一种以数学定义的目标和定向收敛取代试错式探索的方法。MGDE 首先利用条件数理论来识别数值不稳定的原子运算，无需在探索过程中调用昂贵的高精度预言。MGDE 利用了“极端条件数出现在结构化边界附近（例如相消点与奇点）”这一观察，将检测重新表述为一个数值求根问题。通过用牛顿–拉夫森方法求解由此得到的目标函数，MGDE 能够从远离的初始点将输入引导至易出错区域。我们在 GNU 科学库（GSL）函数上评估 MGDE，并以触发的缺陷数作为主要指标，与两个最先进的基线 ATOMU 和 FPCC 比较。在 88 个单输入函数上，MGDE 在 47 个函数中触发了 80 个缺陷，优于 ATOMU（46 个函数中 70 个缺陷）和 FPCC（42 个函数中 53 个缺陷）。MGDE 也更快：ATOMU 和 FPCC 分别需要多出 41.71$\\times$ 和 10.17$\\times$ 的时间。在多输入函数上优势更为显著，MGDE 触发了 9 个缺陷而 FPCC 一个也没有，且每个函数的平均运行时间为 0.6443 秒，而 FPCC 的预算为 100 秒。总体而言，MGDE 在有效性和效率上都大幅推进了当前最先进水平，我们报告了 16 个此前未知的 GSL 缺陷，并已获得 GSL 社区确认。","tl":"用条件数理论+牛顿求根定向找浮点误差输入，免去高精度预言","au":["Youshuai Tan","Zhanwei Zhang","Haonan Zhang","Lianyu Zheng","Zishuo Ding","Jinfu Chen","Weiyi Shang"],"top":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","alt":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["floating-point error","condition number","Newton-Raphson","GSL","error-inducing inputs"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/200/x"},{"id":"p01483","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"TracePilot: Self-verifiable Framework for Decentralized Applications Fault Localization across Transactions","tz":"TracePilot：跨交易的去中心化应用故障定位自验证框架","a":"Decentralized Applications (DApps) serve as a critical technical underpinning for business logic and user interaction within the blockchain-powered Web3 ecosystem. However, DApps are prone to faults, and localizing these faults within their intricate and often interconnected logic is a particularly time-consuming process, frequently taking tens of hours and leading to substantial economic losses for developers. Existing state-of-the-art DApp fault localization methods, e.g., FaultSeeker, cannot capture cross-transaction fault logic and produce verifiable diagnostic reports. Therefore, security experts have to spend substantial time manually verifying results and devising fixes. In this paper, we present TracePilot, a large language model (LLM)-based framework that automates DApp fault localization in two phases: distilling global fault insights from transaction sequences and then performing focused trace exploration to isolate the faulty logic. Crucially, we propose a patch verification mechanism that treats attack-blocking patches as executable evidence for fault localization while flagging potential overfitting risks for expert review. This mechanism improves result trustworthiness and reduces manual verification costs. Evaluated on a dataset of 149 real-world cases, TracePilot achieves a 71.14% Top-1 Recall. In the single-transaction fair comparison, it achieves 72.73%, substantially outperforming the state-of-the-art method at 32.23%. On cross-transaction cases, TracePilot achieves a 64.29% Top-1 Recall. The proposed algorithm is being integrated into the contract security agent developed by Ant Digital Technologies. Moreover, to facilitate further research, our code and dataset are publicly available online: https://github.com/feiqiuaaaa/TracePilot .","az":"去中心化应用（DApp）是区块链驱动的 Web3 生态中业务逻辑与用户交互的关键技术支撑。然而，DApp 容易出现故障，而在其错综复杂、往往相互关联的逻辑中定位这些故障是一个特别耗时的过程，常常需要数十小时，并给开发者带来重大经济损失。现有最先进的 DApp 故障定位方法（例如 FaultSeeker）无法捕捉跨交易的故障逻辑，也无法产出可验证的诊断报告。因此，安全专家不得不花费大量时间手工验证结果并设计修复方案。本文提出 TracePilot，一个基于大语言模型（LLM）的框架，通过两个阶段自动化 DApp 故障定位：先从交易序列中提炼全局故障洞见，再进行聚焦的轨迹探索以隔离出有问题的逻辑。关键在于，我们提出了一种补丁验证机制，将“能阻断攻击的补丁”视为故障定位的可执行证据，同时标记潜在的过拟合风险以供专家复核。该机制提升了结果的可信度并降低了人工验证成本。在包含 149 个真实案例的数据集上评估，TracePilot 达到 71.14% 的 Top-1 Recall。在单交易的公平比较中，它达到 72.73%，大幅优于最先进方法的 32.23%。在跨交易案例上，TracePilot 达到 64.29% 的 Top-1 Recall。该算法正在被集成到蚂蚁数科开发的合约安全智能体中。此外，为便利后续研究，我们的代码与数据集已公开：https://github.com/feiqiuaaaa/TracePilot 。","tl":"用攻击阻断补丁作可执行证据，实现跨交易DApp故障自验证定位","au":["Xuanyu Zhu","Zhiying Wu","Tao Wang","Ying Yan","Wei Zhou","Jiajing Wu","Zigui Jiang","Zibin Zheng"],"top":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","alt":"fault-localization-and-debugging","tg":["llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale","agentic"],"kw":["DApp fault localization","cross-transaction","patch verification","LLM agent","Web3"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/201/x"},{"id":"p01484","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Empowering Lightweight Language Models for Security Code Review via Context-Aware Distillation","tz":"通过上下文感知蒸馏赋能轻量语言模型进行安全代码评审","a":"Security code review, which specifically examines software from a security perspective, is indispensable for preempting vulnerabilities and bolstering software reliability. However, existing automated approaches face a dilemma. They either rely on large language models with prohibitive deployment costs, or employ lightweight models that struggle with complex reasoning and global contextual understanding. In this paper, we propose LSCR, a context-aware distillation framework that empowers lightweight language models for security code review by distilling static-analysis–style security rationale from powerful teacher models. Rather than directly transferring final review outputs, LSCR guides student models to internalize how high-level security judgments are systematically derived from low-level code evidence, leveraging repository-level context during training. By embedding this evidence-driven analysis paradigm into lightweight models, LSCR enables more reliable security code reviews under constrained model capacity. When compared with competitive lightweight baselines, LSCR attains an average improvement of over 12% in security issue classification accuracy and more than 13.3% gains in BLEU score for review generation. Human evaluation reveals that LSCR increases the proportion of instrumental reviews by 52.6% on average over state-of-the-art baselines, while reducing misleading feedback by 22.6%. LSCR effectively narrows the performance gap between small-scale and large-scale models, making on-premise security code review more feasible in practice.","az":"安全代码评审专门从安全视角审查软件，对于预先排除漏洞、增强软件可靠性不可或缺。然而，现有自动化方法面临两难：它们要么依赖部署成本高昂的大语言模型，要么采用难以进行复杂推理和全局上下文理解的轻量模型。本文提出 \\textbf{LSCR}，一个上下文感知的蒸馏框架，通过从强大的教师模型中蒸馏出“静态分析式”的安全推理依据，赋能轻量语言模型完成安全代码评审。LSCR 并非直接迁移最终的评审输出，而是引导学生模型内化“高层安全判断如何系统性地从低层代码证据中推导出来”，并在训练中利用仓库级上下文。通过将这种证据驱动的分析范式嵌入轻量模型，LSCR 使受限模型容量下的安全代码评审更为可靠。与有竞争力的轻量基线相比，LSCR 在安全问题分类准确率上平均提升超过 \\textbf{12%}，在评审生成的 BLEU 分数上提升超过 \\textbf{13.3%}。人工评估显示，LSCR 相比最先进基线平均将“有实际帮助的评审”比例提高了 \\textbf{52.6%}，同时将误导性反馈减少了 \\textbf{22.6%}。LSCR 有效缩小了小规模模型与大规模模型之间的性能差距，使本地私有化部署的安全代码评审在实践中更为可行。","tl":"蒸馏静态分析式安全推理依据，让小模型做可靠安全评审","au":["Zixiao Zhao","Yanjie Jiang","Hui Liu","Lu Zhang"],"top":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","security","human-study"],"kw":["security code review","knowledge distillation","lightweight LLM","repository-level context","security rationale"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/202/x"},{"id":"p01485","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"EvidenT: An Evidence-Preserving Framework for Iterative System-Level Package Repair","tz":"EvidenT：面向迭代式系统级软件包修复的证据保留框架","a":"Frequent toolchain updates and the expanding diversity of instruction set architectures (ISAs) have made large-scale system-level software package repair a critical task. Diagnosing and repairing build failures remains challenging due to heterogeneous failure evidence, complex dependency constraints, and architecture-specific build conventions. While recent LLM-based repair methods have shown promise for project-level source code fixes, they struggle with system-level repair where failures involve multi-language artifacts (e.g., build recipes, scripts, and source archives) and require iterative validation through external build services. In this paper, we first conduct a systematic empirical study of real-world system-level build failures. Our findings reveal that 72% of failures stem from dependency and environment misconfigurations rather than isolated code defects, suggesting that effective repair must prioritize packaging logic and iterative feedback. Motivated by these insights, we propose EvidenT, an evidence-preserving repair framework that decouples iteration-aware evidence management from tool execution. EvidenT comprises (1) an external Build Service for reproducible build execution and feedback; (2) an Evidence-Preserving Repair Controller that performs cross-modal fusion of repair history, knowledge context, and build artifacts; and (3) an automated Repair Orchestrator that executes a suite of modular tools for failure localization and system-level repair actions within a closed-loop validation environment. We evaluate EvidenT on a benchmark of 219 real-world RISC-V package build failures. EvidenT successfully repairs 118 packages (53.88%), substantially outperforming state-of-the-art agentic baselines (20.55%) and direct LLM-based repair (1.83%). To demonstrate its architectural generality, we extend EvidenT to legacy ISAs by updating only ISA-specific knowledge context. In preliminary experiments, it achieves success rates of 41.77% on aarch64 and 46.99% on x86_64, showcasing its robustness across diverse hardware ecosystems.","az":"频繁的工具链更新以及指令集架构（ISA）日益多样化，使大规模系统级软件包修复成为一项关键任务。由于失败证据异构、依赖约束复杂以及架构特定的构建约定，诊断和修复构建失败仍然困难重重。虽然近期基于 LLM 的修复方法在项目级源码修复上展现了潜力，但它们在系统级修复上举步维艰——此类失败涉及多语言制品（例如构建配方、脚本和源码归档），并且需要通过外部构建服务进行迭代验证。本文首先对真实世界的系统级构建失败进行了系统的实证研究。我们的发现表明，72% 的失败源于依赖与环境的错误配置，而非孤立的代码缺陷，这说明有效的修复必须优先关注打包逻辑与迭代反馈。受这些洞见启发，我们提出 EvidenT，一个证据保留的修复框架，将“迭代感知的证据管理”与“工具执行”解耦。EvidenT 包含：（1）一个外部构建服务，用于可复现的构建执行与反馈；（2）一个证据保留修复控制器，对修复历史、知识上下文和构建制品进行跨模态融合；（3）一个自动化修复编排器，在闭环验证环境中执行一套模块化工具，完成失败定位与系统级修复动作。我们在包含 219 个真实 RISC-V 软件包构建失败的基准上评估 EvidenT。EvidenT 成功修复了 118 个软件包（53.88%），大幅优于最先进的智能体基线（20.55%）和直接使用 LLM 的修复（1.83%）。为展示其架构通用性，我们仅通过更新 ISA 特定的知识上下文，就将 EvidenT 扩展到了传统 ISA。在初步实验中，它在 aarch64 上达到 41.77%、在 x86_64 上达到 46.99% 的成功率，展现了在多样硬件生态中的鲁棒性。","tl":"证据管理与工具执行解耦，闭环修复RISC-V系统级构建失败","au":["Chenyu Zhao","Minghua Ma","Shenglin Zhang","Zeshun Huang","Yongqian Sun","Chetan Bansal","Saravan Rajmohan","Dan Pei"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"automated-program-repair","tg":["agentic","llm-based","industrial-or-large-scale"],"kw":["build failure repair","system-level package","RISC-V","evidence preservation","LLM agent"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/203/x","pu":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.08621"},{"id":"p01486","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"CARE: Cascading Impact-Aware Compliance Test Suite Evolution under Regulatory Changes","tz":"CARE：法规变更下级联影响感知的合规测试套件演化","a":"In response to frequent changes in regulatory rules, this paper proposes CARE, a cascading impact-aware framework for automated compliance testing evolution. Existing approaches often suffer from over-reuse or missed updates because they treat rule changes in isolation and ignore complex interdependencies across testing artifacts. CARE addresses this issue by constructing a unified four-layer cascading relation model spanning Rule-Requirement-Scenario-Test Case, enabling fine-grained traceability across abstraction levels. By explicitly modeling how rule changes propagate and amplify along this chain, the framework precisely identifies impacted scenarios and test cases that need updating, while safely maximizing the reuse of unaffected ones. Experiments conducted on real-world compliance testing tasks across multiple domains show that CARE achieves an average F1 of 90.3% on updated test suites, outperforming existing methods by up to 164% and approaching expert-level effectiveness. Ablation studies further demonstrate that explicit cascading impact modeling and handling are key contributors to these improvements. In addition, CARE substantially reduces manual effort and improves test maintenance efficiency, and indicates strong cross-domain generalization. This work highlights cascading impact propagation as a central challenge in regulation-driven test maintenance and shows that shifting from isolated rule handling to cascading impact-aware evolution is essential for achieving both high test quality and maintenance efficiency.","az":"针对监管规则频繁变更的问题，本文提出 CARE，一个用于自动化合规测试演化的级联影响感知框架。现有方法常因孤立地处理规则变更、忽视测试制品之间复杂的相互依赖，而出现过度复用或漏更新的问题。CARE 通过构建一个横跨“规则—需求—场景—测试用例”的统一四层级联关系模型来解决这一问题，实现跨抽象层级的细粒度可追溯性。通过显式建模规则变更如何沿该链条传播与放大，该框架能够精确识别需要更新的受影响场景与测试用例，同时安全地最大化复用未受影响的部分。在多个领域的真实合规测试任务上开展的实验表明，CARE 在更新后的测试套件上取得平均 90.3% 的 F1，比现有方法最高高出 164%，接近专家级效果。消融实验进一步表明，显式的级联影响建模与处理是这些提升的关键贡献因素。此外，CARE 大幅减少了人工工作量并提升了测试维护效率，还展现出很强的跨领域泛化能力。本工作凸显了级联影响传播是法规驱动的测试维护中的核心挑战，并表明从孤立的规则处理转向级联影响感知的演化，对于同时实现高测试质量与维护效率至关重要。","tl":"四层级联关系模型刻画法规变更传播，精准演化合规测试套件","au":["Zhiyi Xue","Xiaohong Chen","Min Zhang"],"top":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["compliance testing","regulatory change","test suite evolution","cascading impact","traceability"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/204/x"},{"id":"p01487","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Fine-Grained Privacy Leakage Detection in OpenHarmony Apps","tz":"OpenHarmony 应用中的细粒度隐私泄露检测","a":"In recent years, the distributed operating system OpenHarmony has gained significant popularity. As the number of OpenHarmony apps grows rapidly, privacy abuse and data leakage have emerged as critical concerns. However, the untyped and highly flexible nature of Ark bytecode poses substantial challenges. We propose HScope, a novel fine-grained program analysis framework designed to directly analyze OpenHarmony app bytecode and identify privacy risks. HScope employs abstract interpretation to model the dynamic behaviors of OpenHarmony apps, enabling precise resolution of indirect calls and the complex inter-component communication mechanisms. We evaluate HScope on a dataset of 300 real-world OpenHarmony apps. The results demonstrate that HScope is both effective and comprehensive, successfully uncovering 39 previously unknown privacy issues (corresponding to 27 apps). These findings highlight HScope’s potential as a practical and scalable solution for securing the evolving OpenHarmony ecosystem.","az":"近年来，分布式操作系统 OpenHarmony 迅速流行。随着 OpenHarmony 应用数量的快速增长，隐私滥用与数据泄露已成为关键隐患。然而，Ark 字节码无类型且高度灵活的特性带来了巨大挑战。我们提出 HScope，一个新颖的细粒度程序分析框架，旨在直接分析 OpenHarmony 应用字节码并识别隐私风险。HScope 采用抽象解释来建模 OpenHarmony 应用的动态行为，从而精确解析间接调用以及复杂的组件间通信机制。我们在包含 300 个真实 OpenHarmony 应用的数据集上评估 HScope。结果表明 HScope 既有效又全面，成功发现了 39 个此前未知的隐私问题（涉及 27 个应用）。这些发现凸显了 HScope 作为保障不断演进的 OpenHarmony 生态安全的实用且可扩展方案的潜力。","tl":"首个直接分析Ark字节码的抽象解释隐私泄露检测框架","au":["AOHAN MEI","Guangliang Yang","Xinming Guo","Yi Wang","Fuan Gui","Min Yang"],"top":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["non-llm-classical","tool-or-artifact-release","empirical-study"],"kw":["OpenHarmony","Ark bytecode","privacy leakage","abstract interpretation","inter-component communication"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/205/x"},{"id":"p01488","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"An Empirical Study and Benchmark of Kubernetes Misconfiguration Scanners","tz":"Kubernetes 错误配置扫描器的实证研究与基准","a":"Kubernetes is a widely adopted container orchestration framework, yet misconfigurations remain a leading cause of cloud security incidents and a major challenge for practitioners. Automated security scanners are commonly used to detect such misconfigurations, but their effectiveness has not been systematically evaluated. As a result, it remains unclear which tools can be trusted, what misconfigurations they reliably detect, and to what extent they improve Kubernetes security. This paper presents the first systematic investigation of ten prominent Kubernetes security scanners that are actively used in practice. We begin by examining the misconfigurations that each scanner claims to detect. Although scanners provide documentation of their coverage, these descriptions are written in natural language and are often ambiguous, making it unclear what is actually detected. To address this issue, we manually analyze scanner implementations to identify their precise detection targets and validate them through dynamic testing. Our analysis reveals that scanners frequently adopt different criteria for the same documented misconfiguration, exposing significant inconsistencies caused by ambiguous specifications. Building on these results, we introduce the first comprehensive benchmark for Kubernetes misconfigurations, covering all misconfigurations targeted by the ten scanners. The benchmark includes 4,109 misconfiguration files for static and dynamic analysis and 144 shell scripts for dynamic analysis, encompassing 281 unique misconfigurations. Using this benchmark, we conducted an empirical evaluation of ten scanners. Our results show that, in static scanning, Kubescape achieves the highest accuracy (43.8%), and it also performs best in dynamic analysis with an accuracy of 62.3%. We further analyze the strengths and limitations of each scanner, identifying coverage gaps that significantly affect detection effectiveness. Our findings provide practical guidance for practitioners selecting Kubernetes security scanners and highlight key challenges that should be addressed by the software engineering community. Moreover, the proposed benchmark establishes a foundation for future research on Kubernetes security.","az":"Kubernetes 是被广泛采用的容器编排框架，但错误配置仍是云安全事件的主要成因，也是从业者面临的重大挑战。自动化安全扫描器常被用于检测此类错误配置，但其有效性尚未得到系统评估。因此，哪些工具值得信赖、它们能可靠检测哪些错误配置、以及它们在多大程度上改善了 Kubernetes 安全，仍不明确。本文首次系统考察了十款在实践中被积极使用的主流 Kubernetes 安全扫描器。我们首先考察每款扫描器声称能检测的错误配置。虽然扫描器提供了覆盖范围的文档，但这些描述以自然语言写成且常含歧义，使其真正检测的内容并不清晰。为解决该问题，我们人工分析了扫描器的实现，以确定其精确的检测目标，并通过动态测试加以验证。我们的分析表明，扫描器对同一份被记录的错误配置往往采用不同的判定标准，暴露出由规格歧义造成的显著不一致。基于这些结果，我们引入了首个全面的 Kubernetes 错误配置基准，覆盖十款扫描器所针对的全部错误配置。该基准包含 4,109 个用于静态与动态分析的错误配置文件，以及 144 个用于动态分析的 shell 脚本，共涵盖 281 种独特的错误配置。利用该基准，我们对十款扫描器进行了实证评估。结果显示，在静态扫描中 Kubescape 取得最高准确率（43.8%），在动态分析中同样表现最佳，准确率为 62.3%。我们进一步分析了每款扫描器的优势与局限，识别出显著影响检测效果的覆盖缺口。我们的发现为从业者选择 Kubernetes 安全扫描器提供了实用指导，并凸显了软件工程社区应当解决的关键挑战。此外，所提出的基准为未来的 Kubernetes 安全研究奠定了基础。","tl":"首个K8s错误配置基准，揭示十款扫描器判定标准严重不一致","au":["Haeun Eom","Bohyun Suk","Sungjae Hwang"],"top":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","alt":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","tg":["benchmark-dataset","empirical-study","security"],"kw":["Kubernetes","misconfiguration scanner","benchmark","cloud security","empirical evaluation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/206/x"},{"id":"p01489","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Towards Iterative End-to-End Software Development: A Feature-Driven Multi-Agent Framework","tz":"迈向迭代式端到端软件开发：一个特性驱动的多智能体框架","a":"Recent advances in large language model agents offer the promise of automating end-to-end software development from natural language requirements. However, existing approaches largely adopt linear, waterfall-style pipelines, which oversimplify the iterative nature of real-world development and struggle with complex, larger-scale projects. To address these limitations, we propose EvoDev, an iterative software development framework inspired by feature-driven development. EvoDev decomposes user requirements into a set of user-valued features and constructs a Feature Map, a directed acyclic graph that explicitly models dependencies between features. Each feature node in the feature map maintains multi-layer contexts, including business logic, software design, and code implementation, which are propagated along dependencies to provide context for subsequent development iterations. We evaluate EvoDev on challenging Android development tasks and show that it outperforms the best-performing baseline, Claude Code, by 57.3%, while improving single-agent performance by 16.0%–58.5% across different base LLMs, highlighting the importance of feature decomposition, dependency modeling, context propagation, and workflow-aware agent design for end-to-end software development. Moreover, our work summarizes practical insights for designing iterative, LLM-driven development frameworks and informs future training of base LLMs to better support iterative software development.","az":"大语言模型智能体的最新进展带来了从自然语言需求自动化完成端到端软件开发的希望。然而，现有方法大多采用线性的瀑布式流水线，过度简化了真实开发的迭代本质，在复杂的大规模项目上难以胜任。为解决这些局限，我们提出 EvoDev，一个受特性驱动开发启发的迭代式软件开发框架。EvoDev 将用户需求分解为一组对用户有价值的特性，并构建 Feature Map——一个显式建模特性间依赖关系的有向无环图。特性图中的每个特性节点都维护多层上下文，包括业务逻辑、软件设计和代码实现，这些上下文沿依赖关系传播，为后续开发迭代提供上下文。我们在具有挑战性的 Android 开发任务上评估 EvoDev，结果显示它比表现最好的基线 Claude Code 高出 57.3%，并在不同基座 LLM 上将单智能体性能提升 16.0%–58.5%，凸显了特性分解、依赖建模、上下文传播和工作流感知的智能体设计对端到端软件开发的重要性。此外，我们的工作总结了设计迭代式 LLM 驱动开发框架的实用洞见，并为未来基座 LLM 的训练如何更好支持迭代式软件开发提供了启示。","tl":"用特性依赖DAG与多层上下文传播替代瀑布式端到端开发流水线","au":["Junwei Liu","Chen Xu","Chong Wang","Tong Bai","Weitong Chen","Kaseng Wong","Yiling Lou","Xin Peng"],"top":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","alt":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","tg":["agentic","llm-based"],"kw":["end-to-end software development","feature-driven development","multi-agent","feature map","context propagation"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/207/x"},{"id":"p01490","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Silence of Commit Messages: An Empirical Study for Vulnerability Commit Message Generation using Large Language Models","tz":"提交信息的沉默：使用大语言模型生成漏洞提交信息的实证研究","a":"The vulnerability commit message serves as crucial metadata for maintaining software within version control systems. Nonetheless, manually crafted vulnerability commit messages often lack detail or exhibit inconsistent formatting. Recently, the growing application of Large Language Models (LLMs) for code and natural language comprehension has opened avenues for automating the crafting of these messages. This paper systematically and thoroughly explores the generation of security patch commit messages in the context of LLMs, delving into topics such as dataset construction, evaluation method design, and the relationship between vulnerability types and submission structure. First, we explore the elements of commit messages using LLM and integrate a questionnaire survey to pinpoint four essential types of information: summary, background, impact, and fix, which are essential for developers. This aims to establish a structured dataset of bug submissions and assess its quality. Next, we examine general automated evaluation techniques for assessing LLM-generated commit messages and find that GPT-3.5’s evaluation methods align more closely with human judgment. Then, we conduct an organized investigation into how LLM generation effects vary across three principal vulnerability types, uncovering that LLMs’ adaptability differs across vulnerabilities. Furthermore, we perform an exhaustive examination of generation quality across various components and find that LLMs excel at generating summaries but struggle to produce impact details. In particular, the smallest DeepSeek-Coder shows a semantic retention advantage in crafting backgrounds, whereas DeepSeek-V3 struggles with impact aspects. Lastly, we investigate the effects of different prompting strategies (e.g., zero-shot, few-shot prompts) and parameter settings (e.g., temperature and top_p) on the quality of commit message generation, finding that prompt and parameter configurations critically influence output quality, with model sensitivity varying.","az":"漏洞提交信息是在版本控制系统中维护软件的关键元数据。然而，人工撰写的漏洞提交信息往往缺乏细节或格式不一致。近来，大语言模型（LLM）在代码与自然语言理解方面的应用日益增多，为自动撰写此类信息开辟了途径。本文系统而深入地探索了在 LLM 语境下安全补丁提交信息的生成，涉及数据集构建、评估方法设计，以及漏洞类型与提交结构之间关系等议题。首先，我们使用 LLM 探究提交信息的构成要素，并结合问卷调查确定了对开发者至关重要的四类核心信息：摘要（summary）、背景（background）、影响（impact）与修复（fix）。这旨在建立一个结构化的缺陷提交数据集并评估其质量。接着，我们考察了用于评估 LLM 生成的提交信息的通用自动化评价技术，发现 GPT-3.5 的评估方法与人类判断更为一致。随后，我们对三类主要漏洞类型下 LLM 生成效果的差异进行了系统性考察，发现 LLM 的适应能力因漏洞类型而异。此外，我们对各组成部分的生成质量进行了详尽检验，发现 LLM 擅长生成摘要，却难以产出影响细节。特别地，体量最小的 DeepSeek-Coder 在撰写背景时展现出语义保留优势，而 DeepSeek-V3 在影响方面表现欠佳。最后，我们研究了不同提示策略（例如零样本、少样本提示）和参数设置（例如 temperature 与 top_p）对提交信息生成质量的影响，发现提示与参数配置对输出质量有决定性影响，且模型的敏感度各不相同。","tl":"系统研究LLM生成漏洞提交信息：四要素数据集、评估法与分项质量","au":["Hao Shen","Ming Hu","JiayeLi","Xiaofei Xie","Mingsong Chen"],"top":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","alt":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","tg":["empirical-study","llm-based","security"],"kw":["vulnerability commit message","commit message generation","LLM evaluation","security patch","prompting strategy"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/208/x"},{"id":"p01491","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Characterizing and Repairing Obsolete Android GUI Tests under UI Evolution","tz":"UI 演化下过时 Android GUI 测试的特征刻画与修复","a":"Graphical user interface (GUI) tests are widely used in regression testing of mobile applications (apps) to validate app behavior from the user’s perspective. However, frequent app evolution, such as UI redesigns and feature updates, often renders existing GUI tests obsolete, even when underlying functionality remains unchanged. Automatically repairing such tests is critical for maintaining test suites and reducing substantial manual effort. Despite the practical importance, there is still a lack of a systematic understanding of the characteristics of obsolete GUI tests and a publicly available benchmark to support their study. To fill this gap, we construct a benchmark comprising 736 obsolete GUI tests collected from 36 real-world mobile apps across 668 historical versions. We then conduct a large-scale empirical study that reveals two major challenges in repairing obsolete GUI tests: First, identifying the intended target widget is difficult because widget attributes are frequently missing or unstable, and visually similar widgets may correspond to different functionalities. Second, the target widget is often no longer directly reachable from the failure state, as it may be hidden behind additional UI interactions or relocated to another screen. To address these challenges, we further propose GUIRevive, an automated GUI test repair approach that addresses semantic ambiguity in widget identification and target unreachability under UI evolution by integrating semantic-aware reasoning, functionality-preserving validation, and goal-guided UI exploration. Our evaluation shows that GUIRevive successfully repairs 86.4% of obsolete GUI tests and significantly outperforms state-of-the-art repair techniques by up to 220%. Moreover, GUIRevive has been deployed in industrial settings, achieving a 93% repair success rate on industrial mobile apps.","az":"图形用户界面（GUI）测试被广泛用于移动应用的回归测试，以从用户视角验证应用行为。然而，频繁的应用演化（例如 UI 重设计和功能更新）常常使已有的 GUI 测试过时，即便底层功能并未改变。自动修复此类测试对于维护测试套件、减少大量人工工作至关重要。尽管具有重要的实践意义，学界仍缺乏对过时 GUI 测试特征的系统理解，也缺乏支持相关研究的公开基准。为填补这一空白，我们构建了一个基准，包含从 36 个真实移动应用的 668 个历史版本中收集的 736 个过时 GUI 测试。随后我们开展了一项大规模实证研究，揭示了修复过时 GUI 测试的两大挑战：第一，识别原本想要操作的目标控件很困难，因为控件属性经常缺失或不稳定，且视觉上相似的控件可能对应不同功能。第二，目标控件往往无法从失败状态直接到达，因为它可能被隐藏在额外的 UI 交互之后，或被迁移到了另一个界面。为应对这些挑战，我们进一步提出 GUIRevive，一种自动化 GUI 测试修复方法，通过整合语义感知推理、功能保持验证和目标引导的 UI 探索，解决控件识别中的语义歧义以及 UI 演化下目标不可达的问题。我们的评估表明，GUIRevive 成功修复了 86.4% 的过时 GUI 测试，显著优于最先进的修复技术，最高高出 220%。此外，GUIRevive 已部署于工业环境，在工业移动应用上达到 93% 的修复成功率。","tl":"构建736例过时GUI测试基准，并用目标引导探索修复不可达控件","au":["Shiwen Song","Yiheng Xiong","Wenbo Guo","Manqi Sun","Jiaolong Kong","Xiaofei Xie"],"top":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","alt":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","tg":["benchmark-dataset","industrial-or-large-scale","llm-based"],"kw":["obsolete GUI tests","test repair","UI evolution","Android","widget identification"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/209/x"},{"id":"p01492","v":"ISSTA 2026","k":"Research Papers","t":"Project-Scale Statement-Level Fault Localization via Multi-View Semantic Learning and Pairwise Reranking","tz":"基于多视图语义学习与成对重排序的项目级语句级缺陷定位","a":"Statement-level fault localization (FL) is critical for effective software debugging, as it enables developers to precisely identify faulty lines of code. While traditional spectrum-based, mutation-based, and deep learning-based FL techniques have achieved notable progress, they remain limited in modeling rich fault semantics. Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) offer new opportunities for FL due to their strong capacity for semantic understanding and reasoning over bugs. However, existing LLM-based FL approaches largely treat fault localization as isolated, code-centric prediction, limiting their ability to perform the holistic fault reasoning required for precise statement-level localization. In this paper, we propose FaultScape, a novel LLM-based framework for project-scale, statement-level FL that formulates FL as a multi-view semantic learning and reasoning problem. FaultScape addresses the limitations of existing approaches through three key components. First, we introduce a joint contrastive fine-tuning strategy that trains LLMs on large-scale bug-fix data to explicitly learn fault semantics from multiple complementary views. View-specific fault semantics, including fault type, root cause, and repair intent, are learned via supervised binary classification, while cross-view semantic consistency is enforced through contrastive learning. These two objectives are jointly optimized within a unified training loss. The fine-tuned models extract multi-view fault likelihoods as semantic features for each suspicious statement. Second, we adopt a dynamic feature integration module that combines these semantic features with spectrum-based and mutation-based execution features, producing an initial suspiciousness statement ranking. Third, we design a test-guided pairwise re-ranking strategy based on LLM that explicitly compares highly suspicious statements among candidates under failing-test contexts. By estimating relative fault likelihoods through pairwise comparison rather than independent scoring, the model produces a refined project-scale ranking. We evaluate FaultScape on Defects4J v1.2.0, where it localizes 112/171/196 bugs at Top-1/3/5 out of 395, outperforming state-of-the-art DL-based and LLM-based baselines. On leakage-free benchmarks, FaultScape further localizes 11/18/20 bugs at Top-1/3/5 on ConDefects (31 bugs) and 12/21/22 bugs on GHRB (34 bugs), demonstrating strong generalization to unseen projects. These results show that combining multi-view fault semantics with contrastive, failure-guided reasoning substantially advances the effectiveness and robustness of statement-level fault localization.","az":"语句级缺陷定位（FL）对高效的软件调试至关重要，因为它能让开发者精确识别出错的代码行。尽管传统的基于频谱、基于变异和基于深度学习的 FL 技术已取得显著进展，它们在建模丰富的缺陷语义方面仍有局限。大语言模型（LLM）的最新进展凭借其对缺陷的强大语义理解与推理能力，为 FL 提供了新机会。然而，现有基于 LLM 的 FL 方法大多将缺陷定位视为孤立的、以代码为中心的预测任务，限制了它们进行精确语句级定位所需的整体性缺陷推理。本文提出 FaultScape，一个用于项目级、语句级 FL 的新型 LLM 框架，将 FL 表述为一个多视图语义学习与推理问题。FaultScape 通过三个关键组件解决现有方法的局限。第一，我们引入联合对比微调策略，在大规模缺陷—修复数据上训练 LLM，从多个互补视图显式学习缺陷语义。视图特定的缺陷语义（包括缺陷类型、根因和修复意图）通过有监督的二分类学习，同时通过对比学习强制跨视图语义一致性。这两个目标在统一的训练损失中联合优化。微调后的模型为每条可疑语句抽取多视图缺陷似然作为语义特征。第二，我们采用动态特征融合模块，将这些语义特征与基于频谱和基于变异的执行特征相结合，产生初始的可疑语句排序。第三，我们设计了基于 LLM 的测试引导成对重排序策略，在失败测试的上下文下显式比较候选中的高可疑语句。通过成对比较估计相对缺陷似然、而非独立打分，模型产生更精细的项目级排序。我们在 Defects4J v1.2.0 上评估 FaultScape，在全部 395 个缺陷中，它在 Top-1/3/5 分别定位了 112/171/196 个缺陷，优于最先进的基于深度学习和基于 LLM 的基线。在无泄漏基准上，FaultScape 在 ConDefects（31 个缺陷）上 Top-1/3/5 进一步定位了 11/18/20 个缺陷，在 GHRB（34 个缺陷）上定位了 12/21/22 个，展现出对未见项目的强泛化能力。这些结果表明，将多视图缺陷语义与对比式、失败引导的推理相结合，能显著提升语句级缺陷定位的有效性与鲁棒性。","tl":"多视图对比微调加测试引导成对重排，做项目级语句定位","au":["Hongwei Yu","Xu Wang","Jian Zhang","Xiangxin Meng","lijiarui","Yang Liu","Chunming Hu"],"top":"fault-localization-and-debugging","alt":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","tg":["llm-based","tool-or-artifact-release"],"kw":["statement-level fault localization","contrastive fine-tuning","multi-view semantics","pairwise reranking","Defects4J"],"u":"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/210/x"}],"themes":[{"id":"code-generation-and-code-llms","en":"Code Generation & Code LLMs","zh":"代码生成与代码大模型","blurb":"把代码模型本身当作研究对象：生成前往哪里取上下文、推理与解码怎么做、面向什么领域、写出的代码是否安全、以及如何训练与剖析模型。SE 与 AI 两条线在这里正面相遇——ICSE/FSE/ASE/ISSTA 的 LLM4SE 工作与 ICLR/ICML/NeurIPS 的代码模型工作并排陈列。","scope":"both","topics":[{"id":"repo-context-and-retrieval-for-code","en":"Repository Context & Retrieval for Code Generation","zh":"仓库级上下文工程与代码检索增强","def":"贡献在于“生成之前往哪里取上下文”的论文：跨文件与仓库级上下文选择、调用链/依赖图上下文、面向代码生成的检索增强(RAG)、补全用的词法与语义检索、单次生成调用前的上下文内联与压缩、以及 IDE 补全在延迟与窗口预算下的取舍。","kw":["repository-level code generation","cross-file context","context engineering","retrieval-augmented code generation","call chain context","dependency graph context","code completion","context inlining"]},{"id":"codegen-reasoning-prompting-and-decoding","en":"Reasoning, Prompting & Decoding for Code Generation","zh":"代码生成的推理、提示与解码控制","def":"通过改变“模型怎么想、怎么解码”来提升生成代码质量的论文，以及生成前的意图/需求对齐：思维链与模块化思维、自我改进与自我调试、候选采样/重排/集成、面向代码的 LLM-as-judge 选择、文法约束解码与前瞻解码、token 重加权、投机解码等单次调用推理加速，以及模糊、矛盾或不完整需求的处理。","kw":["chain-of-thought","modularization-of-thought","prompting strategy","self-refinement","self-debugging","ensemble selection","reranking candidates","LLM-as-a-judge for code"]},{"id":"domain-specific-and-multimodal-code-generation","en":"Domain-Specific & Multimodal Code Generation","zh":"领域专用与多模态代码生成","def":"以目标语言或平台的约束为核心贡献的代码生成：HDL/Verilog、GPU/Triton/CUDA 算子、基础设施即代码(Dockerfile、Kubernetes、Terraform)、SQL 与 text-to-SQL、UI/GUI 代码与截图转代码、Simulink 与嵌入式代码、Notebook 与数据科学流水线、Bash、智能合约生成、三维/场景代码、ORM 模式，以及低资源与遗留目标(HarmonyOS/ArkTS、COBOL、小众语言)。","kw":["Verilog / HDL generation","GPU kernel / Triton / CUDA generation","Infrastructure-as-Code","Dockerfile generation","text-to-SQL","UI code generation","screenshot-to-code","Simulink / embedded code"]},{"id":"secure-code-generation","en":"Secure & Compliant Code Generation","zh":"安全与合规的代码生成","def":"以“模型写出的代码是否安全/合规/运行安全”为评价目标的论文：安全代码生成的基准与防御、安全性-可用性权衡、生成代码中的 CWE、MISRA 等编码规范合规、软件包与依赖幻觉及其解码期防御、记忆或微调中携带的不安全编码偏好，以及诱导代码模型产出恶意代码的越狱攻击。","kw":["secure code generation","CWE in generated code","MISRA compliance","security-utility trade-off","package hallucination","guarded decoding defence","insecure coding preference","secure code benchmark"]},{"id":"code-model-training-alignment-and-internals","en":"Code Model Training, Adaptation & Internals","zh":"代码模型的训练、适配与内部机制","def":"针对非智能体代码任务，修改或剖析代码模型本身的论文：预训练/SFT/继续训练、偏好优化与 GRPO/DPO/RLVR、训练数据合成与清洗、噪声标签过滤、蒸馏、模型融合、模型编辑与机器遗忘、量化压缩与把代码模型编译为轻量可执行体、端云级联；以及模型的可靠性信号与完整性——注意力/神经元探针、正确性的内部表征、不确定性与校准、记忆化、对扰动与混淆的鲁棒性、后门与数据投毒、数据集水印、成员推断、AI 生成代码检测。","kw":["fine-tuning code LLM","GRPO / DPO for code","training data synthesis","knowledge distillation","model merging","model editing","machine unlearning","quantization & compression"]}]},{"id":"coding-and-swe-agents","en":"Coding & Software-Engineering Agents","zh":"编程与软件工程智能体","blurb":"智能体本身就是研究对象：从 issue 到补丁的端到端求解、多智能体协作与整套软件的生成、智能体的训练与成本控制、失效诊断，以及围绕智能体长出来的新制品生态(框架、Skill/MCP、AGENTS.md 类配置、LLM 应用与推理服务)。这是本用户 ICSE27 访谈工作的正对口区域。","scope":"both","topics":[{"id":"swe-agents-issue-resolution","en":"Repository-Level Issue Resolution & SWE Agents","zh":"仓库级 Issue 求解与 SWE 智能体","def":"输入是真实仓库中“未定位”的自然语言 issue、缺陷报告或特性请求，系统必须自己找到目标代码并产出经验证的变更：SWE-bench 式 issue 求解、为该流水线服务的 issue/缺陷定位智能体、仓库级迁移智能体、特性新增、以程序性知识扩展智能体循环，以及对抗式/竞技场式 issue 求解设定。","kw":["issue resolution","issue localization","SWE-bench","repository-level issue","autonomous patch","feature addition","agent scaffold","issue-to-code"]},{"id":"multi-agent-and-end-to-end-software-development","en":"Multi-Agent Collaboration & End-to-End Software Development","zh":"多智能体协作与端到端软件开发","def":"贡献在于面向软件工程的多智能体拓扑或协作协议(角色分工、辩论、协调者-提议者、自组织团队、KV-Cache 通信)，或从需求经设计、编码到测试构建整套应用的流水线：全栈/Web 应用生成、需求到代码的可追溯流水线、端到端评估的 agentic IDE，以及跨多个 SE 任务评估的多智能体框架。","kw":["multi-agent framework","role-playing agents","agent debate","coordinator-proposer","self-organizing agents","end-to-end software development","full-stack app generation","requirement-to-code pipeline"]},{"id":"se-agent-training-cost-and-context-efficiency","en":"SE Agent Training, Cost & Trajectory/Context Efficiency","zh":"SE 智能体的训练、成本与轨迹上下文效率","def":"对 SE 智能体策略做后训练的论文(轨迹 SFT、基于执行反馈的 RL/RLVR/GRPO、工具交互与调试器使用训练、智能体对齐、合成 SWE 轨迹数据)，以及在保持成功率前提下降低 token/轮次/成本的论文(轨迹削减与注意力引导压缩、跨轮上下文压缩、轮次控制与步数预算、提前终止、模型热替换与路由、循环中执行代码的成本收益分析)。","kw":["agentic training","RLVR for SE agents","trajectory learning","SWE trajectory data","tool-interactive training","trajectory compression","context compression across turns","turn control"]},{"id":"agent-behavior-and-failure-analysis","en":"Agent Behaviour, Plan Following & Failure Diagnosis","zh":"智能体行为、计划遵循与失效诊断","def":"刻画编程/SE 智能体“怎么做、为什么决策失败”的实证与诊断论文：过程导向的错误分类、计划遵循度、确定性锚定与智能体需要多少静态结构、智能体动作的可追溯性、多智能体运行中的失效归因、智能体行为的符号化解释、agentic 助手的运行安全失效、智能体产出改动的可维护性与坏味，以及多轮编程会话的质量退化。","kw":["process-oriented error analysis","plan following","failure attribution","agent traceability","behavioral failures","deterministic anchoring","agent-generated code quality","maintainability of agent edits"]},{"id":"llm-app-and-agent-infrastructure-ecosystem","en":"LLM Application & Agent Infrastructure Ecosystem","zh":"LLM 应用与智能体基础设施生态","def":"以 LLM 应用与智能体赖以运行的底座及其制品生态(或其安全性)为对象的论文：agentic 框架的缺陷与测试实践、面向智能体系统的混沌工程与故障注入、Agent Skill/MCP 工具包(复用、克隆、恶意性、凭据泄露)、提交进仓库的 AI 配置制品与模型配置安全坏味、LLM 原生 IDE 的安全隐私、模型卡与预训练模型仓库制品、RAG 系统测试与 LLM 集成应用缺陷、面向智能体动作的运行时护栏与强制执行、针对编程/Web/GUI 智能体的提示注入与环境注入红队，以及 LLM 服务/LMaaS 管理与推理栈的跨层根因分析。","kw":["agentic framework bugs","agent skills / MCP","committed AI configuration","LLM-native IDE security","RAG system testing","LLM-integrated application","runtime enforcement & guardrail","prompt injection"]}]},{"id":"agent-mechanisms-and-environments","en":"Agent Mechanisms, Training & Environments","zh":"智能体机制、训练与运行环境","blurb":"AI 社区“怎么把智能体做得更好”的机制层：记忆与检索、规划与长程推理、工具使用与函数调用、多智能体协作与自进化、面向智能体的强化学习与训练环境、GUI/计算机操作智能体。这些是设计 SE 智能体时最可迁移的一手材料；配套的长上下文、测试时扩展见主题 llm-core，验证器与基准见主题 evaluation。","scope":"AI","topics":[{"id":"agent-memory-context-and-retrieval","en":"Agent Memory, Context Management & Retrieval","zh":"智能体记忆、上下文管理与检索","def":"核心机制是“智能体在长回合或多轮中存什么、压什么、取什么、忘什么”的论文：显式记忆模块与记忆智能体、面向通用策略的记忆基准、作为智能体记忆使用的 KV-Cache 与思维自适应缓存压缩、多轮对话状态，以及把外部知识取进工作上下文的检索——检索器训练、多步与图检索、RAG 流水线、以及面向文档集合的 agentic/深度研究式搜索。","kw":["agent memory","memory module","memory benchmark","KV cache compression as memory","multi-turn state","retrieval-augmented generation","retriever training","multi-step retrieval"]},{"id":"agent-tool-use-and-function-calling","en":"Tool Use & Function Calling","zh":"工具使用与函数调用","def":"贡献在于智能体如何调用外部工具或 API、以及由此解锁的能力：工具集成推理、函数调用的可靠性与 schema 设计、以工具使用实现长度泛化、用投机或并行动作执行压缩“行动-观察”循环的延迟，以及把函数调用改造为防御或控制面。","kw":["tool use","tool-integrated reasoning","function calling","API invocation","tool schema","speculative actions","parallel action execution","agent latency"]},{"id":"gui-computer-use-agents","en":"GUI & Computer-Use Agents","zh":"GUI 与计算机操作智能体","def":"通过图形界面行动的智能体：桌面操作系统、浏览器或移动应用，依靠截图与 UI 动作操作——计算机操作智能体模型及其跨平台训练数据、屏幕定位(grounding)、带能力诊断的移动 GUI 智能体，以及界面与环境变化下 UI 智能体的可靠性。","kw":["computer-use agent","GUI agent","mobile GUI agent","screen grounding","cross-platform UI data","OSWorld / WebArena","UI automation","environment variation"]}]},{"id":"evaluation-benchmarks-and-empirical-evidence","en":"Benchmarks, Evaluation & Empirical Evidence","zh":"基准、评测方法与实证证据","blurb":"“我们怎么知道它真的有用”——两个赛道共享的一层。代码与智能体基准(SWE-bench 类、Gaia2/τ²-bench/AstaBench 类)、评测有效性与数据污染、验证器与奖励模型，以及以人为证据的研究(开发者实验、访谈、眼动、IDE 遥测，以及 AI 会议上的从业者与生产部署调研)。","scope":"both","topics":[{"id":"code-and-agent-benchmarks","en":"Code, SE & Agent Benchmarks","zh":"代码、软件工程与智能体基准","def":"主要产出是可复用评测制品或评测协议的论文：代码与仓库级基准、多领域多语言代码评测集、SE 任务基准数据集、动态或竞技场式评测协议、智能体基准与仿真评测世界(动态/异步环境、双向控制对话基准、智能家居与科研智能体套件、网络安全智能体基准)，以及带能力诊断的排行榜。","kw":["benchmark construction","dataset construction","repo-level benchmark","multilingual code benchmark","agent benchmark","simulated environment benchmark","dual-control benchmark","arena-style evaluation"]},{"id":"evaluation-validity-contamination-and-reproducibility","en":"Evaluation Validity, Contamination & Reproducibility","zh":"评测有效性、数据污染与可复现性","def":"关于“我们怎么测量”而非某项能力的元研究：指标偏置与构念效度、数据污染与泄漏、基准标注质量与 SWE-bench 类数据中 PR-Issue 不匹配、测量结果的随机性与非确定性、微基准可靠性与模型排名稳定性、对既有技术的复现与重评估、开放科学与制品可得性，以及基于 LLM 的实证研究的可复现性。","kw":["metric validity","surface bias","data contamination","benchmark label quality","measurement randomness","nondeterminism of scores","micro-benchmark reliability","model ranking stability"]},{"id":"verifiers-judges-and-reward-models","en":"Verifiers, Judges & Reward Models","zh":"验证器、评判模型与奖励模型","def":"贡献在于“给另一个模型的输出打分、检查或筛选”的模型或方法：验证器与批评者、LLM-as-judge 与生成式/全模态奖励模型、推理期自验证与基于反思的拒绝、编程助手的信任与置信评估、面向自我纠错生成的执行一致性可靠性估计，以及对模型输入的测试充分性检查。","kw":["verifier","critic model","LLM-as-a-judge","generative reward model","self-verification","reflection and rejection","trust assessment","confidence estimation"]},{"id":"human-studies-of-ai-assisted-work","en":"Human, Practitioner & Adoption Studies of AI-Assisted Work","zh":"AI 辅助工作的人因、从业者与采纳研究","def":"证据来自人、或来自人的行为痕迹而非基准分数的论文：面向开发者的对照实验、访谈、问卷、扎根理论与眼动研究；信任、生产力、认知偏差与建议接受度；大规模 IDE 与对话遥测；仓库层面对 AI 工具与智能体采纳的度量；经验证的心理测量量表；人机行为对比；以及 AI 会议上关于“生产中的智能体是怎么造、怎么评的”从业者访谈与调研。","kw":["developer study","controlled experiment","interview & survey","eye tracking","grounded theory","trust in AI","productivity","cognitive bias"]}]},{"id":"software-testing-and-fuzzing","en":"Software Testing & Fuzzing","zh":"软件测试与模糊测试","blurb":"经典且最大的 SE 板块。按“产出什么”(测试输入、预言、套件)与“被测系统是什么”(界面、编译器/数据库/内核)切分；被测系统优先于技术——编译器的 fuzzer 归编译器测试，合约的 fuzzer 归区块链安全，DNN 的 fuzzer 归 ML 系统质量。","scope":"SE","topics":[{"id":"unit-integration-and-api-test-generation","en":"Unit, Integration & API Test Generation","zh":"单元、集成与 API 测试生成","def":"为普通应用代码与服务自动产出可执行测试用例、测试套件或测试桩的论文，目标是覆盖率或发现缺陷：基于 LLM 与程序分析的单元测试生成、项目与条件感知的测试、测试切分(carving)、服务级与集成测试、REST/HTTP 与 GraphQL API 测试生成、由自然语言描述生成测试，以及测试生成流水线的工业实践经验。","kw":["unit test generation","test case generation","integration test","service-level test","coverage-driven generation","test carving","harness for unit tests","REST API testing"]},{"id":"test-oracles-assertions-and-metamorphic-testing","en":"Test Oracles, Assertions & Metamorphic Testing","zh":"测试预言、断言与蜕变测试","def":"贡献在于“判定对错”而非“造输入”的论文：测试预言的推断与生成、断言生成与断言质量、异常预言、从文档或代码导出的性质(property-based)、蜕变关系构造与蜕变式提示、差分关系、基于不变式的预言，以及由自然语言意图驱动的行为回归预言。","kw":["test oracle generation","assertion generation","exception oracle","metamorphic relation","metamorphic testing","property-based testing","invariant oracle","differential oracle"]},{"id":"test-suite-analysis-mutation-coverage-and-flakiness","en":"Test-Suite Analysis: Mutation, Coverage, Selection & Flakiness","zh":"测试套件分析：变异、覆盖、用例选择与不稳定测试","def":"研究已有测试套件随时间演化而非生成新套件的论文：变异测试、变异体生成与等价变异体检测、变异分数加速、覆盖准则与新的充分性度量、组合覆盖与覆盖数组、回归测试的选择/优先级/最小化与范围界定、测试套件演化、过时测试的修复与迁移、测试坏味，以及不稳定(flaky)测试的检测、复现与刻画。","kw":["mutation testing","equivalent mutants","mutation score acceleration","coverage criterion","test adequacy","covering array","regression test selection","test prioritization"]},{"id":"gui-mobile-web-and-xr-testing","en":"GUI, Mobile, Web & XR Testing","zh":"GUI、移动、Web 与扩展现实测试","def":"通过用户界面驱动或验证软件的论文：Android/iOS 的 GUI 探索与跨应用测试、Web 与浏览器端到端测试、XR/AR/VR 应用测试与 GUI 元素定位、众包测试与录制回放、UI 演化下 GUI 测试脚本的修复与迁移、UI 层缺陷检测与移动测试失败归类。","kw":["GUI testing","Android app testing","GUI exploration","web end-to-end testing","XR / AR testing","GUI grounding","record and replay","crowdsourced testing"]},{"id":"greybox-directed-fuzzing-and-input-generation","en":"Greybox/Directed Fuzzing & Structured Input Generation","zh":"灰盒/定向模糊测试与结构化输入生成","def":"与目标无关的模糊测试机制与输入合成：灰盒与定向模糊测试算法、种子调度与种子-工作者并行、变异调度与能量调度、覆盖反馈与平台期突破、定向性的距离度量、混合/混合符号执行式模糊测试、fuzz 桩生成与桩退化、模糊测试的评估方法与基准随机性；以及文法推断、基于文法与结构感知的输入生成、输入生成器合成、输入归约与尺寸调整。","kw":["greybox fuzzing","directed fuzzing","seed scheduling","mutation scheduling","coverage feedback","fuzzing plateau","hybrid fuzzing","harness generation"]},{"id":"compiler-runtime-database-and-kernel-testing","en":"Compiler, Runtime, Database & Kernel Testing","zh":"编译器、运行时、数据库与内核测试","def":"被测系统是基础设施或面向开发者的软件：编译器、解释器、JIT 与语言运行时、JVM 与 WebAssembly 引擎、DBMS、查询与 DataFrame 引擎、向量数据库、SMT/SAT/CHC/MIP 求解器、作为被测对象的静态分析器与代码检查器、操作系统内核、网络与无线协议实现、固件、重构引擎，以及分布式系统正确性检查(可串行化、跨系统组合兼容性)——含其模糊测试器、差分/蜕变/组合式测试程序合成，以及编译器缺陷隔离与去重。","kw":["compiler testing","differential testing","DBMS testing","query engine testing","interpreter & runtime testing","WebAssembly engine","JVM implementation bugs","solver testing"]}]},{"id":"program-analysis-debugging-and-repair","en":"Program Analysis, Debugging, Repair & Verification","zh":"程序分析、调试、修复与形式化验证","blurb":"缺陷出现之后的经典链路，加上语义优先的分析与证明机制：定位、修复、复现与缺陷刻画，静态分析算法与告警治理，符号执行、求解与形式化验证/规约。与测试主题的区别在于输入是已知失败或程序语义，而不是生成的输入。","scope":"SE","topics":[{"id":"fault-localization-and-debugging","en":"Fault Localization & Debugging","zh":"缺陷定位与调试","def":"定位或解释已观察失败的原因、并支持调试过程的论文：谱/变异/学习式缺陷定位、语句与分支级定位、基于缺陷报告的检索式定位、面向回归失败的切片、Delta Debugging 与输入最小化、崩溃去重与失败索引聚类、交互式与追问式调试器、面向调试的执行感知日志、轨迹抽象、带高效动态分析的调试智能体，以及专业调试实践的实证研究。","kw":["fault localization","spectrum-based localization","bug localization from reports","delta debugging","crash deduplication","failure indexing","interactive debugger","slicing for debugging"]},{"id":"automated-program-repair","en":"Automated Program Repair","zh":"自动程序修复","def":"针对“已定位”的功能性缺陷(失败测试、Defects4J 条目、类型或空值错误、崩溃栈、编译诊断)生成并验证补丁的论文：基于 LLM 与搜索的补丁生成、修复素材检索、多 hunk 与仓库级修复、轨迹与执行反馈引导的修复、带记忆与多智能体的修复循环、内存安全与资源泄漏修复、补丁正确性与过拟合评估、低资源与跨语言修复，以及修复基准。","kw":["automated program repair","patch generation","repair ingredients","multi-hunk repair","trace-guided repair","patch validation","patch overfitting","memory-safety repair"]},{"id":"bug-reproduction-defect-detection-and-bug-studies","en":"Bug Reproduction, Defect-Class Detection & Empirical Bug Studies","zh":"缺陷复现、特定缺陷类检测与缺陷实证研究","def":"三类紧密相连的非安全缺陷活动：(a) 把缺陷报告、视频、issue 或崩溃变成可执行复现或 fail-to-pass 测试；(b) 检测特定的非安全缺陷类——数据竞争、死锁、资源与内存泄漏、API 与线程池误用、代码-注释不一致、引入回归的变更、业务逻辑与浮点误差；(c) 预测或实证刻画缺陷——JIT 缺陷预测、变更风险评分、CI 失败分诊、引入缺陷提交识别(SZZ)、特定技术的缺陷分类与根因研究、缺陷报告挖掘。","kw":["bug reproduction","reproducing test","crash reproduction","video-based bug report","data race detection","resource leak detection","API misuse","code-comment inconsistency"]},{"id":"static-analysis-warnings-and-type-systems","en":"Static Analysis, Warning Management & Type Systems","zh":"静态分析、告警治理与类型系统","def":"静态分析的核心机制及其工程化使用：指针/别名与值流分析、污点与数据流分析、调用图构建与剪枝、程序切片与变更影响分析、抽象解释与 CFL 可达性、增量/稀疏与 GPU/SIMD 加速分析、终止性与循环摘要、Datalog 与多面体分析；类型推断、类型标注、类型混淆与类型检查器健全性；以及面向工具的一侧——可执行告警推荐、误报过滤、SAST/Linter 评估与配置、告警修复与自定义检查器编写、神经符号与 LLM 增强分析。","kw":["pointer analysis","value-flow analysis","taint analysis","call graph","program slicing","abstract interpretation","incremental analysis","type inference"]},{"id":"symbolic-execution-verification-and-formal-specifications","en":"Symbolic Execution, Solving, Verification & Formal Specifications","zh":"符号执行、约束求解、形式化验证与规约","def":"以语义为先的程序推理：符号与混合执行引擎、路径爆炸与状态剪枝、ghost code 与参数自配置；SMT/SAT/CHC/MIP 求解、字符串/浮点/堆约束、解的多样化；演绎验证与神经/LLM 引导的定理证明、证明自动化与精化、循环不变式与引理发现、验证桩合成、有界与统计模型检验、IC3/PDR、运行时与预测式验证(含 MPI 程序)；以及形式化制品本身——规约与 typestate 推断、API/REST 规约生成、协议状态机抽取、自然语言到 LTL、TLA+/Event-B/Alloy 建模、行为模型生成与修复、时序性质精化、控制器与策略合成。","kw":["symbolic execution","concolic execution","SMT / SAT solving","string & floating-point constraints","deductive verification","theorem proving","loop invariant","verification harness"]}]},{"id":"software-security-and-supply-chain","en":"Software Security, Vulnerabilities & Supply Chain","zh":"软件安全、漏洞与供应链","blurb":"按安全对象组织：源码漏洞的检测/评估/可利用性、安全补丁的生命周期、链上软件、二进制与恶意软件(含检测器自身的对抗鲁棒性)，以及生态与平台层面的供应链、隐私合规与系统加固。","scope":"SE","topics":[{"id":"vulnerability-detection-assessment-and-exploitability","en":"Vulnerability Detection, Assessment & Exploitability","zh":"漏洞检测、评估与可利用性","def":"判断通用源码是否含漏洞、判定发现的严重性与真实性、或证明其可达可利用的论文：LLM/agentic 与学习式漏洞检测及根因推理、仓库级检测、安全规约与安全预言、CWE/Top-25 覆盖与分布外泛化、安全发现的误报过滤、严重性与证据驱动评估、推理轨迹忠实性、漏洞数据集构建，以及 PoC/利用合成、跨版本利用迁移、可达性与残余风险分析、ReDoS 与整数溢出分诊。","kw":["vulnerability detection","CWE / Top-25","agentic vulnerability reasoning","repository-level detection","security specification","false positive filtering","severity assessment","reasoning-trace faithfulness"]},{"id":"vulnerability-repair-and-patch-management","en":"Vulnerability Repair & Security Patch Management","zh":"漏洞修复与安全补丁治理","def":"修复安全缺陷、或跨版本/分支/发行版管理安全补丁的论文：自动漏洞修复与修复模式/意图建模、以 PoC 为中心的有界验证、面向同源变体的修复鲁棒性、安全补丁检测与静默修复识别、补丁存在性检测(含混淆二进制)、补丁移植与回移及其基准、反打补丁分析、一个 CVE 多个补丁、跨发行版补丁共享，以及 CVE 生态的实践研究。","kw":["vulnerability repair","security patch detection","silent fix","patch presence testing","patch backporting","patch porting","unpatching","multiple patches per CVE"]},{"id":"smart-contract-and-blockchain-security","en":"Smart Contract, Blockchain Security, Forensics & Economics","zh":"智能合约与区块链：安全、取证与经济","def":"以链上软件为对象的论文：智能合约漏洞检测、验证与信息流策略合成、合约模糊测试与符号执行、DeFi 攻击分析与价格操纵/逐利型利用合成、合约控制流完整性、合约字节码反编译、共识客户端与 RPC 实现、Move/Solidity 语言工具链、钱包与浏览器扩展测试、代币骗局与陷阱代币检测、链上交易取证(含洗钱追踪与机器人指纹)，以及矿工 Gas 收益等区块链经济学。","kw":["smart contract vulnerability","Solidity / Move","Ethereum / Solana","DeFi attack","price manipulation exploit","contract fuzzing","contract decompilation","consensus client"]},{"id":"binary-analysis-reverse-engineering-and-malware","en":"Binary Analysis, Reverse Engineering & Malware","zh":"二进制分析、逆向工程与恶意软件","def":"输入为编译后、去符号或混淆制品的论文：反编译与伪代码恢复、函数名/类型/类结构恢复、二进制代码相似性与源码-二进制匹配、反混淆与不透明谓词消解、固件二进制的控制流重建、二进制插桩与重写、二进制优化与体积缩减；恶意软件分类、行为审计与投毒检测；以及这些检测器自身的对抗鲁棒性——对杀毒引擎与二进制相似性模型的语义保持规避，及学习式恶意软件检测器的可复现性。","kw":["decompilation","pseudocode recovery","function name recovery","binary code similarity","deobfuscation","opaque predicate","firmware control-flow reconstruction","binary instrumentation"]},{"id":"supply-chain-privacy-and-platform-security","en":"Supply Chain, Privacy, Compliance & Platform Hardening","zh":"供应链、隐私合规与平台加固","def":"存在于生态层或应用层之下的风险：恶意与混淆包、抢注、仓库级投毒检测、软件成分分析与第三方库/版本识别、SBOM 与溯源(含零知识 SBOM 共享)、许可证与合规风险、脆弱依赖可达性、AI/模型与预训练模型供应链、刷星与流行度操纵；应用中的个人与敏感数据泄露、硬编码密钥与凭据检测、隐私政策与法规合规、权限与云 IAM/访问控制实践；以及平台加固——瘦身(debloating)、系统调用过滤、TEE/SGX 可信基裁剪与分区、控制流完整性、微架构侧信道(Spectre)检测、工控/PLC 防护、软件签名与密钥保护。","kw":["software supply chain","malicious package","npm / PyPI registry","package confusion","SBOM & provenance","software composition analysis","third-party library detection","license compliance"]}]},{"id":"software-evolution-and-repositories","en":"Software Evolution, Repositories & Engineering Process","zh":"软件演化、仓库挖掘与工程过程","blurb":"已经存在的软件如何被评审、理解、检索、重构、翻译、升级，以及围绕它的需求、架构、社区与研究方法。这是用户关心的 MSR 主线；AI 辅助开发的人因证据放在主题 evaluation 的 human-studies 里，此处收录不以 AI 工具为对象的社会技术与方法学研究。","scope":"SE","topics":[{"id":"code-review-and-change-history-analysis","en":"Code Review & Change/Commit History Analysis","zh":"代码评审与变更/提交历史分析","def":"围绕“评审变更”与“挖掘变更历史”的论文：代码评审自动化与评审意见生成、评审者推荐及其对人员流失与知识分布的影响、评审决策与文件排序效应、安全代码评审数据集与轻量安全评审模型、Pull Request 分析与修订恢复、Issue-Commit 链接恢复、提交解缠、方法级历史生成、代码差异比对、cherry-pick/补丁应用，以及依赖约束操作历史上的选择性撤销/重做。","kw":["code review automation","review comment generation","reviewer recommendation","pull request analysis","issue-commit link","commit untangling","code differencing","method-level history"]},{"id":"code-comprehension-semantics-search-and-documentation","en":"Code Comprehension, Program-Semantics Reasoning, Search & Documentation","zh":"代码理解、程序语义推理、检索与文档","def":"帮助人或模型理解既有代码、以及检索匹配代码的论文：代码摘要及其幻觉、提交信息与变更摘要生成、文档与 API 文档生成、代码-注释/代码-文档不一致(含多语言)、可读性与理解代理指标、代码解释质量；评估或提升模型“理解代码在做什么”的能力——模拟/部分执行、Hoare 式正确性推理、仓库级代码推理、与人类理解的对比、视觉语言模型的代码理解；以及语义代码检索、跨语言检索、克隆检测与代码相似性/表示学习、抄袭与重构攻击抵抗。","kw":["code summarization","commit message generation","documentation generation","code-comment inconsistency","readability & comprehension","code execution reasoning","Hoare-style reasoning","repository-level reasoning"]},{"id":"refactoring-translation-and-modernization","en":"Refactoring, Code Quality, Translation & Modernization","zh":"重构、代码质量、翻译与现代化","def":"在保持行为的前提下变换既有代码、或度量治理其内部质量的论文：自动化与智能体驱动的重构、代码与架构坏味(含 LLM 生成代码的坏味)、可维护性与技术债、设计规则违规修复、自适应与级联式代码编辑策略；以及跨语言/跨平台翻译——C 转 Rust、COBOL 现代化、SQL 方言翻译、UI 框架转译、反编译伪代码转源码、宏翻译、仓库级翻译智能体、执行对齐验证与翻译基准。","kw":["automated refactoring","code smell","architectural smell","maintainability","technical debt","design rule violation","code translation","C-to-Rust"]},{"id":"dependency-library-and-api-evolution","en":"Dependency, Library & API Evolution","zh":"依赖、库与 API 演化","def":"从非安全视角维持项目第三方依赖健康的论文：依赖升级自动化与状态路径探索、破坏性变更与不兼容的检测与修复、弃用与废弃信号、API 演化与迁移、面向特定库的适配、版本范围与冲突求解、版本感知调用图、技术滞后与冗余、隐藏与条件依赖、生态成熟度与语言特性使用研究，以及面向维护者的生态分析。","kw":["dependency upgrade","breaking change detection","incompatibility fixing","deprecated API","library migration","version range resolution","version-aware call graph","technical lag"]},{"id":"requirements-architecture-and-design","en":"Requirements, Architecture & Design","zh":"需求工程、软件架构与设计","def":"实现之前的上游制品与系统级结构：需求获取、用户故事自动补全与分解、需求验证/证伪与修复、性能需求量化、情感与非功能需求、需求到代码的可追溯、把应用评论与终端用户反馈作为需求来源、LLM 时代“规格说明到底是什么”的实证；以及架构恢复与精化、微服务拆分、模型驱动开发与基于 DSL 的设计、系统结构的特征/设计建模、仓库级架构理解。","kw":["requirements elicitation","user story decomposition","requirements validation","requirement repair","traceability","non-functional requirements","app review mining","architecture recovery"]},{"id":"oss-communities-governance-and-se-research","en":"OSS Communities, Governance, Education & SE Research","zh":"开源社区、治理、教育与软件工程研究反思","def":"软件工程的社会组织与元研究一侧，且研究对象不是 AI 工具：贡献者留存、流失与脱离、性别同质性与多样性、职业路径与软件岗位市场、毒性与对话恶化、行为准则与 GenAI 贡献政策、项目流行度与社区分析、团队效能与换位思考、开源可持续性预测；软件工程教育与课程经验；以及对领域自身的反思——效度讨论、开放科学与制品实践、文献筛选方法、科研软件复现工具，以及立场、愿景与挑战类论文。","kw":["contributor retention","turnover & disengagement","gender & diversity","toxicity","code of conduct","GenAI contribution policy","community analytics","team effectiveness"]}]},{"id":"systems-operations-and-domain-software","en":"Systems, Operations & Domain Software Engineering","zh":"系统、运维与领域软件工程","blurb":"部署之后与特定领域之内的软件工程：可观测性与性能、配置与交付流水线、机器学习系统与数据质量、信息物理/机器人/嵌入式与受监管关键领域、前端与无障碍质量，以及量子与密码学等新兴计算载体。","scope":"SE","topics":[{"id":"operations-observability-and-performance","en":"Operations, Observability, Root-Cause Analysis & Performance","zh":"运维可观测性、根因分析与性能","def":"关于运行中的系统及其非功能行为的论文：日志解析与压缩、日志语句生成、基于日志的异常检测与故障诊断、分布式追踪与采样、微服务与云原生根因分析及故障传播基准、事故诊断与分诊、排障指南自动化、弹性伸缩与服务时序监控；以及性能工程——性能缺陷与回归检测、微基准生成与可检测性驱动的基准、剖析与关键路径分析、代码与应用的速度优化、能耗/功率建模与碳感知绿色工程、内存与资源效率、GPU/CUDA/HPC 性能刻画与部署。","kw":["log parsing","log anomaly detection","distributed tracing","microservice root cause analysis","incident diagnosis","AIOps","autoscaling","performance regression"]},{"id":"configuration-build-and-deployment-engineering","en":"Configuration, Variability, Build, CI/CD & Deployment","zh":"配置、可变性、构建、CI/CD 与部署","def":"软件的配置空间与交付流水线：配置性能学习、调优与采样策略、性能模型的不确定性、错误配置检测与配置可诊断性、配置感知测试与配置测试套件生成；软件产品线、特征模型及其求解、可变性感知分析、误通过产品检测、配置空间上的组合交互测试与覆盖数组；构建系统、增量与跨配置构建的正确性与调度、构建依赖验证与优化、CI 失败处理、容器镜像与 Dockerfile 重构、Kubernetes 错配扫描器、IaC 对账与操作系统兼容性、无服务器与部署调度；以及发布计划等搜索式项目决策。","kw":["configuration performance learning","configuration tuning","sampling strategy","misconfiguration detection","software product line","feature model","variability-aware analysis","combinatorial interaction testing"]},{"id":"ml-systems-dl-frameworks-and-data-quality","en":"ML Systems, DL Frameworks, Model Quality & Data Engineering","zh":"机器学习系统、深度学习框架、模型质量与数据工程","def":"制品是学习型系统、其基础设施或其数据的软件工程：深度学习库/框架/算子/编译器的测试(含车载与数组、DataFrame 栈)、配置引起的预测不稳定、DL 框架中的 GPU 优化实践；DNN 模型测试、测试输入优先级与选择、神经元/分布覆盖及其批判性重评估、DNN 变异测试加速、模型修复、网络模块化、鲁棒性与结构性验证、量化下的可认证鲁棒性、强化学习智能体测试、标注与数据标签的故障定位；以及机器学习数据/流水线工程——Notebook、数据泄漏、数据质量与数据修复、为可复现而做的 Notebook 现代化、ML 赋能系统的质量。","kw":["DL library testing","DL compiler testing","operator fuzzing","DNN testing","test input prioritization","neuron coverage","DNN mutation testing","model repair"]},{"id":"cps-robotics-embedded-and-safety-critical-domains","en":"CPS, Autonomous Driving, Robotics, Embedded & Safety-Critical Domains","zh":"信息物理系统、自动驾驶、机器人、嵌入式与安全关键领域","def":"系统具有物理实体、嵌入式属性、或绑定受监管/关键任务领域的论文：自动驾驶场景生成、危险场景搜索、失当行为预测、扰动测试、ADS 缺陷定位与安全违规根因、多车死锁与互感知；无人机规划器与集群、机器人与 ROS 生态、Isaac Sim 等仿真器、里程计与多目标跟踪、多智能体路径规划、晶圆搬运与工业自动化、硬件在环 ECU 测试；嵌入式与固件工程，含 MCU 外设模型合成、固件重宿主模糊测试、PLC 虚拟化冗余、Simulink 与硬件特定代码，以及 EDA 工具链质量(HDL 编译器/仿真器缺陷、FPGA 综合与仿真工具模糊测试)；物联网与智能家居集成；具有平衡性预言的游戏与仿真类软件；以及受监管或关键任务软件——法律/税务关键系统、医学影像流水线、卫星与航天软件、法规变更下的合规测试套件演化。","kw":["autonomous driving testing","scenario generation","misbehavior prediction","UAV / drone","robotics & ROS","Isaac Sim","multi-object tracking","hardware-in-the-loop ECU"]},{"id":"ui-frontend-quality-and-accessibility","en":"UI/Frontend Quality, Accessibility & Inclusive Software Engineering","zh":"前端界面质量、无障碍与包容性软件工程","def":"质量属性落在“用户看到什么、能不能用”上、且不以测试生成为框架的论文：无障碍缺陷检测(屏幕阅读器/WCAG)与自动无障碍修复、从业者对应用无障碍的看法、用多模态模型推荐可用性改进、终端用户提交的界面改进建议；以及 Web/前端平台质量——冗余渲染与 React 重渲染、IFrame 渲染缺陷、响应式布局回流、明暗模式界面不一致、从语言规范抽取 JavaScript Polyfill、浏览器与 Node.js 中的 WebAssembly 使用、生成式 GUI 代码的可玩性与视觉保真。","kw":["accessibility issue detection","screen reader","WCAG repair","usability improvement","UI improvement suggestion","superfluous re-rendering","iframe rendering","responsive layout reflow"]},{"id":"quantum-cryptographic-and-emerging-substrate-se","en":"Quantum, Cryptographic & Emerging-Substrate Software Engineering","zh":"量子、密码学与新兴计算载体的软件工程","def":"面向非经典或密码学执行载体的软件工程：量子程序测试与探针式测试、量子库模糊测试、量子神经网络变异测试、量子可测试性度量、跨平台量子执行与量子缺陷生命周期研究；全同态加密库测试、安全多方计算编译器测试、隐私保护机器学习编译器的正确性、零知识虚拟机的安全与可用性；以及密码软件工具链——TLS 证书校验与 CRL 解析器测试、基于 LLM 的密码方案形式化分析、开源生态的后量子密码就绪度评估。","kw":["quantum program testing","quantum library fuzzing","quantum testability metric","quantum bug lifecycle","fully homomorphic encryption","MPC compiler testing","privacy-preserving ML compiler","zero-knowledge VM"]}]},{"id":"llm-core-reasoning-training-and-efficiency","en":"LLM Core: Reasoning, Training & Efficiency","zh":"大模型内核：推理、训练与高效部署","blurb":"AI 赛道的发动机舱，决定了任何 SE 智能体运行的成本与能力上限：推理与测试时扩展、RL 后训练与偏好优化、预训练数据与缩放律、架构与扩散语言模型、高效推理与 ML 系统软件、长上下文与上下文学习。","scope":"AI","topics":[{"id":"llm-reasoning-and-test-time-scaling","en":"Reasoning, Chain-of-Thought & Test-Time Scaling","zh":"推理、思维链与测试时扩展","def":"在权重冻结的前提下塑造、压缩或扩展模型推理过程的论文：思维链结构与层次化思考、过度思考抑制与推理强度控制、从基座模型采样以获得推理、并行推理线程与自适应线程化、best-of-n 等测试时计算、无超参的解码与采样规则、在参数化或扰动问题上的推理鲁棒性、能量式思考，以及把 LLM 当作推理引擎去设计或配置非 LLM 算法。","kw":["chain-of-thought","hierarchical thinking","overthinking reduction","reasoning effort","test-time compute","parallel reasoning","sampling strategy","decoding hyperparameters"]},{"id":"model-architectures-moe-and-diffusion-lms","en":"Sequence Architectures, Mixture-of-Experts & Diffusion Language Models","zh":"序列架构、专家混合与扩散语言模型","def":"骨干网络本身：状态空间模型与 Mamba 系列设计、线性与门控注意力、无 attention-sink 的表述、循环网络与非线性 RNN 的并行训练、混合堆叠与表达力-效率权衡、层循环与 program-of-layers、位置编码与旋转位置编码变体、把记忆做进架构的设计；专家混合的路由、辅助损失、最优稀疏度、专家专精与稠密-MoE 对比、MoE 的模式连通性；以及非自回归文本生成——掩码与任意顺序扩散语言模型、去掩码策略、规划器感知路径学习、解码顺序与扩散 LM 的快速推理及其推理能力。","kw":["state space model","Mamba","linear / gated attention","hybrid architecture","positional embedding / RoPE","expressivity-efficiency tradeoff","mixture-of-experts","expert routing & specialization"]},{"id":"efficient-inference-quantization-and-ml-systems","en":"Efficient Inference, Quantization & ML Systems Software","zh":"高效推理、量化与机器学习系统软件","def":"让训练好的模型跑得便宜，以及承载它的软件：投机与多草稿解码、KV 缓存压缩与查询无关的缓存重建、token 合并与跳层/提前退出、服务系统、高并发吞吐与弹性多模态并行、扩散 Transformer 的特征缓存；训练后量化与量化感知训练、三值与 4 比特格式、低秩与自压缩网络、面向部署的蒸馏、边缘与模拟/类脑执行；以及机器学习系统软件本身——算子 DSL 与 tile 级语言、GPU 内核协同设计、张量记号与 API 设计、自动微分库，以及推理栈的数值确定性与可复现性。","kw":["speculative decoding","KV cache compression","token merging","early exit","serving system","throughput & concurrency","post-training quantization","4-bit / ternary"]}]},{"id":"trustworthy-ai-safety-and-model-integrity","en":"Trustworthy AI: Safety, Interpretability & Model Integrity","zh":"可信 AI：安全、可解释性与模型完整性","blurb":"两个赛道共享：模型与智能体被攻击、被对齐、被审计、被打开看内部，以及训练数据会不会漏出来。SE 会议上关于越狱、公平性、代码模型记忆与水印的工作在这里与 AI 会议的同类工作并列。","scope":"both","topics":[{"id":"ai-safety-jailbreaks-alignment-and-values","en":"Safety, Jailbreaks, Alignment, Values & Governance","zh":"安全、越狱、对齐、价值观与治理","def":"攻击或防御模型的安全行为、并引导其价值取向：越狱提示合成与语言感知的越狱模糊测试、恶意与休眠式微调、隐写与视觉中心攻击、对计算机操作智能体的对抗测试、可复现攻击框架、防御与拒答控制及过度拒答测试；价值对齐——价值基准与测量、多元与可调对齐、良性提示下的诚实性与欺骗、思维链可监控性与弱到强监控、隐式奖励作弊检测；公平性、社会偏见与伦理，含公平性测试与修复、反事实公平、生成代码与推理中的偏见、毒性与认知偏差；以及 AI 政策、监管、同行评议与科研社区立场论文。","kw":["jailbreak","red teaming","malicious finetuning","adversarial prompt","guardrail & refusal control","overrefusal testing","value alignment benchmark","pluralistic alignment"]},{"id":"interpretability-and-model-internals","en":"Interpretability, Model Internals & Trust Signals","zh":"可解释性、模型内部机制与可信信号","def":"打开模型并读取其置信度：稀疏自编码器与特征分裂/吸收、时序 SAE、电路与归因图、面向推理的多 token 归因、机制式数据归因、神经元与激活解释及激活预言机、对表征的因果干预、潜空间动力学与表征几何、神经元的组合式解释、视觉语言模型中的符号机制、权重中的记忆痕迹；以及可信信号——校准与不确定性估计、幻觉检测及其显著性/信息流解释、弃答，以及面向决策的共形鲁棒性控制。","kw":["sparse autoencoder","feature absorption","circuit analysis","attribution graph","multi-token attribution","neuron explanation","activation steering","causal intervention"]},{"id":"privacy-memorization-watermarking-and-unlearning","en":"Privacy, Memorization, Watermarking & Unlearning","zh":"隐私、记忆化、水印与机器遗忘","def":"模型记住了什么数据、谁能证明、以及那是谁的数据：记忆化度量与专供研究的模型套件、成员推断与数据抽取、面向适配与 LoRA 的差分隐私、经验隐私保护基准；模型与输出水印、语义条件水印、抗伪造签名、指纹与模型血缘追踪、版权保护与概念擦除；机器遗忘及其边界与政策含义；以及被部署系统采集到的数据主体的隐私——驾驶语料中的行人、监控视频中的个体、隐私轨迹生成，还有部署中的 RAG 系统内专有知识库的产权保护。","kw":["memorization measurement","membership inference","data extraction","differential privacy","DP LoRA","watermarking","model fingerprinting","model lineage"]}]},{"id":"ai-foundations-multimodal-and-science","en":"AI Foundations, Multimodal & Science","zh":"AI 基础、多模态与科学智能","blurb":"与软件工程没有直接交集、但必须有归属才能覆盖全部语料的 AI 部分：生成与多模态模型、学习理论与优化、图/时序/因果/经典强化学习与科学智能。给它们粗粒度的容身之处，方便一键过滤。","scope":"AI","topics":[{"id":"generative-and-multimodal-models","en":"Generative, Vision, Multimodal, Speech & Embodied Models","zh":"生成式、视觉、多模态、语音与具身模型","def":"贡献在于连续信号的生成机制或非文本模态的论文：扩散与流匹配目标、采样器与求解器、引导、蒸馏与一步生成、扩散的奖励对齐，以及扩散为何泛化或记忆的理论；图像/视频/三维生成与编辑、视觉自回归、像素与视频分词器、新视角合成、逆渲染与高斯表示、世界模型与第一人称模拟器、动作与人体/手部合成；经典视觉任务——深度与法线估计、光流、检测与分割、复原、融合与事件相机；视觉语言模型与多模态推理、空间智能、多模态检索与嵌入；语音、音频与音乐模型及其基准；深度伪造与生成媒体取证；以及具身智能——视觉-语言-动作模型、机器人操作策略与导航。","kw":["diffusion & flow matching","sampler / solver","one-step generation","image & video generation","3D scene & novel view","visual tokenizer","world model","depth / optical flow / segmentation"]}]}],"tags":[{"id":"benchmark-dataset","en":"Benchmark / Dataset","zh":"基准与数据集"},{"id":"empirical-study","en":"Empirical Study","zh":"实证研究"},{"id":"human-study","en":"Human-Subject Study","zh":"人类被试研究"},{"id":"industrial-or-large-scale","en":"Industrial / Large-Scale","zh":"工业实践与大规模"},{"id":"security","en":"Security & Privacy","zh":"安全与隐私"},{"id":"llm-based","en":"LLM-Based","zh":"基于大模型"},{"id":"agentic","en":"Agentic","zh":"智能体式"},{"id":"non-llm-classical","en":"Non-LLM / Classical Method","zh":"非大模型的经典方法"},{"id":"reproducibility-replication","en":"Reproducibility / Replication","zh":"可复现与复现研究"},{"id":"position-vision","en":"Position / Vision / Challenge","zh":"立场、愿景与挑战论文"},{"id":"tool-or-artifact-release","en":"Tool / Framework Release","zh":"工具与框架发布"},{"id":"multimodal","en":"Multimodal","zh":"多模态"},{"id":"low-resource-or-non-english","en":"Low-Resource / Non-English / Legacy","zh":"低资源、非英语与遗留生态"},{"id":"accessibility-inclusion","en":"Accessibility & Inclusion","zh":"无障碍与包容性"},{"id":"cross-track-bridge","en":"Cross-Track Bridge","zh":"跨赛道桥接"}]};